_number\":253,\"content\":\"export type { Prop } from './world/props/prop';\"},{\"line_number\":254,\"content\":\"export type { PropDefinition } from './world/props/prop';\"},{\"line_number\":255,\"content\":\"export type { PropPart } from './world/props/prop';\"},{\"line_number\":256,\"content\":\"export type { PropTouch } from './world/props/prop';\"},{\"line_number\":257,\"content\":\"export type { PropKnock } from './world/props/prop';\"},{\"line_number\":261,\"content\":\"export type { PropPlacement } from './world/props/place';\"},{\"line_number\":262,\"content\":\"export type { PropBody } from './world/props/place';\"},{\"line_number\":263,\"content\":\"export type { PropPose } from './world/props/place';\"},{\"line_number\":271,\"content\":\"export type { ScenePropComponent } from './sim/props';\"},{\"line_number\":272,\"content\":\"export type { ScenePropComponents } from './sim/props';\"},{\"line_number\":282,\"content\":\"export type { ClipsSpec } from './sim/actorClips';\"},{\"line_number\":288,\"content\":\"export type { PuppetComponent } from './sim/actors';\"},{\"line_number\":311,\"content\":\"export type { StepGait } from './world/footsteps';\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"0cefe367-7467-40d4-b361-e0713b655ae6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a large engine. I need to build a complete game.\n\nI am reviewing specific engine APIs for scenes, audio, terrain, and input. I will check existing box examples to find the most efficient implementation path.\n\nI am trimming the scope to a compact but complete game. I will use engine puppets and HTML HUD rather than hundreds of custom props. Several activities are being cut entirely: Great Tilt step 3 counterweights, Expert variants, Hoop Patrol, Reps Hall, Island Jog race, Cliff Plunge, and Step Class. The remaining required activities include Morning Check.\n\nPose Class will use eight poses: nothing, chair, heron, archer, comma, napkin, bridge, and lighthouse. Still Pond, The Line, Paddle Glide, Sand Garden, and Group Class are also required. The remaining activities are Pose Class B, Still Pond, and The Line. Day 1 pairs Morning Check with Pose Class A, Still Pond, and a walk to the noticeboard. Day 2 adds Sand Garden and Pose Class B. Day 3 adds Paddle Glide and The Line.\n\nThe original three-day plan cannot fit the remaining activities. Day 2 needs three activities but only has two. Day 3 needs three poses but only has one. The schedule must be reflowed to five days.\n\nDay 4 will pair Morning Check with Pose C and Still Pond. Activities may be replayed after their first completion.\n\nDay 4 will pair Morning Check with Pose C and either a second Sand Garden or Still Pond. The auto-playthrough must visit every shipped day, activity, and finale step.\n\nDay 4 will pair Morning Check with Pose C and Still Pond. Day 5 will pair Morning Check with Group Class and Great Tilt. This schedule assigns every required activity exactly once.\n\nScoring bots must hit bands on ten seeds for every activity. The director must start each one.\n\nThe scoring targets are strict. A perfect bot needs at least 750 points. A human-like bot needs at least 550. A sloppy bot needs at least 300. Idle and random play must not throw errors. Idle self-ends and scores stay between zero and one thousand with no NaN. Teardown leaves no stray bodies.\n\nThe wobble model was tested. It scored 38 percent without input. Human performance scored 90 percent. Sloppy performance scored 72 percent. Perfect performance scored 100 percent.\n\nTime-in-ring will naturally separate bot scores if the target is center and the ring radius is about 0.22. Off-center seats up to 0.5 may be too difficult for sloppy bots, so activities need tuning to keep shipped bots passing. The perfect bot uses a proportional controller with no delay and gain three, reading the current center-of-balance to reach the activity target.\n\nThe wobble physics model uses a slew target clamped to the disc, with gain 14, instability 3, damping 5, noise 3.5, noise rate 0.15, and reach 0.9. The perfect bot drives the stick to match this slew target exactly, counteracting noise when the desired seat is zero.\n\nThe bot stick command is now defined as `clamp(gain_bot * error + jitter)`, where error is desired seat minus delayed center-of-balance. The plan specifies four bot tiers: perfect with no delay and gain 3, human-like with 250 ms delay and gain 1.2, sloppy with 350 ms delay and gain 0.8, and idle with no input.\n\nThe stick command is slewed at four units per second and then multiplied by reach 0.9. For a center hold the perfect bot drives the stick to negative gain times the delayed center-of-balance, creating an equilibrium that fights noise and instability.\n\nI will implement the wobble model exactly and verify ring occupancy against the idle, human-like, and sloppy benchmarks before designing scores.\n\nMorning Check scoring is now defined as 45 percent share inside a 0.22 ring, 30 percent time-to-six-targets, and 25 percent one-foot balance. Idle performance is expected near 38 percent inside the 0.22 ring.\n\nIdle Morning Check scores about 185 points. Human-like performance is harder to pin down because the human thumb holds off-center at 0.35 with 87 percent success, yet targets sit at radius 0.5. The human bot gain of 1.2 may struggle to hold that far out.\n\nI will simulate the wobble model mathematically in a Node script before coding. The current proportional bot may not reach targets at radius 0.5, so I might need to tune the bot or the targets to guarantee human-like scores hit the 550-point threshold.\n\nThe tests must call the shipped balance step, so I will prototype the wobble model in scratch to tune score bands before porting the math into the shipped code. I also derived the steady-state target formula for pose holds: target equals seat minus instability times seat plus noise, all divided by gain.\n\nThe steady-state target for pose holds is now quantified: it equals roughly 78.6 percent of the seat radius minus one-fourteenth of the noise amplitude. Maximum noise acceleration reaches about 5.1, which would offset the center-of-balance by roughly 0.46 units, though slow oscillation at 0.15 Hz lets the controller track it. The perfect bot command is simply three times the error between desired and delayed center-of-balance.\n\nThe stick command is slewed at four units per second, so the wobble model receives a smoothed input rather than an instantaneous jump. I need to check how the engine passes custom intents to the step function and whether the activity system reads bot components directly when auto-play is enabled.\n\nTests will call each activity's own bot function to generate seat input, feed that intent into the shipped balance step, and then score the resulting world state. This means the test manually steps the simulation while the activity system handles its own setup, step, and scoring.\n\nThe wobble physics will be a pure function exported for tests and registered as a system. The data layer will split into scenes/breath.ts, scenes/data/days.ts, poses.ts, lures.ts, trays.ts, and courses.ts.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4481b938-8db4-4325-8e07-d1a1ec925aa0-26","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"when: 'now'","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine","glob":"*.ts","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4481b938-8db4-4325-8e07-d1a1ec925aa0-27","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"export function defineActionMap|export function defineScene|actions\\?:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine","glob":"*.ts","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4481b938-8db4-4325-8e07-d1a1ec925aa0-28","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"virtual\\.axis|game:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/docs/API.md","head_limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7345,"output_tokens":3691,"cache_read_input_tokens":70144,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"81bcfbd5-577a-4cce-b396-25cc660dba6c"}
