ath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/core/settings.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":185,\"content\":\"export function defineSettings(fields: Record<string, Field>, registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): Entry[] {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/anim/clip/clipsets.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":106,\"content\":\"export function defineClipSet(input: ClipSet | string | object, options: { registry?: Registry } = {}): ClipSetEntry {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/intents.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":195,\"content\":\"export function held(intents: Intents, button: string): boolean {\"},{\"line_number\":200,\"content\":\"export function pressed(intents: Intents, button: string): boolean {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/actorClips.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":129,\"content\":\"export function playClip<C extends object>(world: World<C>, id: number, clip: string, play?: ClipPlay): ClipLayerState {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/actors.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":228,\"content\":\"export function spawnActor<C extends object>(world: World<C>, spec: ActorSpec): number {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/physics/character.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":153,\"content\":\"export function createCharacter(spec: Record<string, unknown> = {}, registry?: Registry): Character {\"},{\"line_number\":186,\"content\":\"export function createCharacterState(): CharacterState {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/codes.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":115,\"content\":\"export function heldBase(code: string): string | null {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"2eb469c0-6b28-407c-9117-e4e8e79839d7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_22","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The engine model is now clear.\n\nI am reviewing key engine APIs and small examples to prepare for structured game development.\n\nI will prototype the wobble model as a pure function first to verify bot scores. The simulation will be the source of truth with a thin page wrapper. I am designing the Wobble type with position, velocity, slewed stick, and state fields.\n\nThe Wobble type now includes body-part positions, a breath phase, and hold values. The `stepWobble` function will be the single pure update path for both the system and tests. Activities will be modeled as state machines on one `act` component instead of multiple entity types.\n\nEach activity module will export setup, step, score, teardown, and bot helpers. The scene step dispatches to the active activity. An auto director system will play through days automatically when game.auto is enabled. It uses a perfect internal bot to finish and may be driven by tests.\n\nA full playthrough spans roughly 1600 seconds, or about 96,000 steps. Time boxes on every activity prevent softlocks even during idle play.\n\nA dedicated `game:bench` test scene will isolate wobble and activities without terrain or physics. This keeps activity tests fast and avoids heavy physics during the auto director.\n\nThe setup function will be shared between the island scene and the bench scene. Character physics is the main bottleneck, but the starter game already runs ten seeds in five seconds. Activity tests that only score points can skip spawning actors entirely, since Pose scrub writes clip slots only when an actor exists.\n\nReal steps are required for time boxes, so time scaling is ruled out. Shortening activity durations via game settings would not satisfy the shipped auto path requirement. The auto playthrough must therefore run real activities at their intended lengths.\n\nThe director must use the real day table, so activity durations stay unchanged. To keep the auto playthrough fast, activities will run as pure state on components without physics. During node verification, the island scene may disable physics entirely and rely only on kinematic props.\n\nSliding props will be handled by sim-side kinematic positions updated by tilt, avoiding Rapier entirely. This makes the island scene faster and more deterministic, though it may require a README note. I am checking whether spawnActor requires the physics world; if so, the island scene must keep physics enabled, but one character during the auto test should remain fast enough.\n\nI will benchmark character step cost to confirm whether physics is required for the auto director. The visual scope is now defined: a title screen over a simple scene, an island with terrain and stations, activities with balance HUDs and scrubbing clips, and HTML menus.\n\nOnly key props will be custom defineProp instances; generic items will use engine props to save time. The WebGPU boot must display the title and game state, so the island scene must stay lightweight. The hub scene will be minimal, containing only a pavilion. The round scene for group class will reuse the same round module. Audio will use defineSong and defineSfx, with music volume set to 0.1 and tests verifying non-silent output.\n\nA conflict surfaced in the UI requirements. The pause menu contains eight items, but the acceptance criterion limits menus to six rows. I must resolve this discrepancy before proceeding.\n\nThe pause menu will be split into two pages to keep every visible menu under six rows. Settings will also be paginated into groups of at most six items.\n\nDev mode sliders must also respect the six-row limit. Each menu instance will contain at most six items, with paging controls to keep visible rows under the cap.\n\nInput priority is set: PlayStation first, then Xbox, then keyboard, then mouse. The attract mode will idle for ten seconds on the front-end menus and exit on any key, click, or pad press without writing a save. Touch support will use CSS media queries and JavaScript detection, defaulting to off with an option to enable it. If WebGPU is unavailable, the engine must display a plain error message rather than crash. The global `window.__game` object will expose screen state, attract mode, last device, glyph set, volumes, day, event, focus, and title. Save keys will be prefixed with `thumb-yoga:` to avoid collisions.\n\nThe save file will store day, results, pebbles, finds, outfits, bests, and settings. In-game confirmation prompts will be removed. The title screen will display \"Thumb Yoga\". The word \"Wii\" is restricted to the source line and hub source field. Weight, BMI, calorie, and body-size scoring are banned; Tare's seed lines about weighing people are explicitly included in the plan.\n\nThe seed lines that mention weight are narrative only. They describe the scale refusing to weigh people, not active scoring. This satisfies both the plan's explicit inclusion and the acceptance criterion that bans weight, BMI, calorie, and body-size scoring.\n\nI will avoid banned names such as Fit Age, Fit Credits, and Body Test. The exit interview must match the About screen exactly in order. PROGRESS.md will track the running tally. Code must pass prettier and eslint with no any types, enums, or Math.pow. I will replace play.ts with the new scenes and update npm tests; the old gem game golden replay will fail.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e220f10a-254a-46b7-af2e-fb49cdf37075-32","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/package.json"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e220f10a-254a-46b7-af2e-fb49cdf37075-33","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wi