{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5dc680d5-5636-4f98-9b1a-bfd67bfd1b62-45","content":"{\"type\":\"Bash\",\"output\":[50,10,46,47,108,97,98,115,47,103,97,109,101,47,98,101,115,116,46,116,101,115,116,46,116,115,10,46,47,108,97,98,115,47,103,97,109,101,47,115,99,101,110,101,115,47,112,108,97,121,46,116,101,115,116,46,116,115,10],\"output_for_prompt\":\"exit: 0\\n2\\n./labs/game/best.test.ts\\n./labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"cd \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656\\\" && find . -name '*.test.ts' -not -path './node_modules/*' | wc -l && find . -name '*.test.ts' -not -path './node_modules/*' | head -40\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Count test files shipped in the game workspace\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc%2Fwork/01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc/terminal/call-5dc680d5-5636-4f98-9b1a-bfd67bfd1b62-45.log\",\"total_bytes\":59}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"a43f3791-0129-455b-8da8-abf35a1cb807"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_27","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Only two test files exist. npm test runs the game.\n\n`npm run check` validates the full engine and takes 22 seconds. Engine files must not be broken. Vitest loads `tests/setup/adviceTrap.ts`. The wobble implementation will be prototyped in a scratch script first, then moved into `wobble.ts` with a quick tsx test. The simulation swaps `Math.sin` during steps, so math portability needs care.\n\nstepWobble will use the portable Math.sin during active simulation steps. Tests calling it outside a step will use native Math, but acceptance tests run it inside a fresh simulation step. Sway phases will be drawn once per seat from w.rng('sway'). Component fields must be schema types, so phases may need to be stored as separate number fields rather than arrays.\n\nTopple mechanics are now defined: a seat wobbles for six steps when its radius exceeds one, then recovers over sixty steps until the cob returns to center.\n\nBreath mechanics are being drafted. The guide ring will pulse with a period, and lung capacity will fill when both feet are held while emptying when released. A running match between lungs and guide will raise calm.\n\nA concrete breathing model is being sketched using sine or phase-based interpolation.\n\nLung capacity fills over half the period when both feet are held and empties otherwise. Sync is a running average of the match between lungs and guide. Calm drifts toward sync when match is high, decaying when it is low. Score equals composure multiplied by half plus half of sync. Doing nothing risks a low score because lungs stay empty while the guide oscillates.\n\nThe breathing score formula conflicts with the plan. A no-input run yields a match of 0.5 and a score near 750, which is Composed rather than the required Adequate range of 300–550. The no-input result must be capped to hit that target.\n\nThe no-input score is fixed at exactly 500. Sync will be zero when lungs are idle, yielding a score of 1000 times 0.5. This lands in the Adequate band at 300–549. Human performance must exceed 500 and reach at least 550. Perfect breathing scores will hit 750 or higher.\n\nThe running average of match still yields a score near 750 when lungs are idle, because the guide ring averages 0.5 while lungs stay at zero. Sync must therefore be zero when the player never breathes, or measured as correlation between lung velocity and guide velocity so a flat lungs line scores zero.\n\nA step-by-step sync metric was considered: the player scores a point for holding both feet during the guide's rise and releasing during its fall. Even with this rule, an idle run still yields a 0.5 sync, which is too high. The plan's description of sync as a running match between lungs and guide is being revisited.\n\nSync will only rise when the player is actively breathing, defined as holding both feet or having lungs above 0.05. Otherwise it decays toward zero. This guarantees a no-input score of exactly 500 and a perfect score of 1000.\n\nCalm rises toward sync at a rate of dt / 2. The default calmEffect of 0.5 halves sway when full calm is reached. Sway phases are drawn once per seat from the RNG. Stick input is clamped and slewed toward raw values at four units per second.\n\nThe target vector is clamped to the unit disc. Acceleration blends the stick target, instability, noise, and disturbance, then integrates velocity and position with damping. During recovery, input may be ignored.\n\nA full lean with reach 0.9 confirms the seat will topple, since equilibrium exceeds radius 1. The no-input ring position of 0.22 will be verified with a script after implementation. The bot will use a history buffer of cob positions for its delay, compute stick output from desired versus seen position plus small jitter drawn from its own RNG stream.\n\nThe bot's gain of 3 is internal and separate from the physics gain of 14. The equilibrium math is too messy to verify by hand, so a scratch benchmark will be written to simulate it. A pure function in `scenes/wobble.ts` can be imported by a test script without pulling in heavy simulation dependencies.\n\nI will write the real implementation files and a Vitest test instead of a scratch script. I need to look up defineSong, createAudio, sky, terrain, ui.createMenu, WebGPU failure detection, and session client fetch patterns. Core files will stay under 400 lines.\n\nThe file plan is now concrete. It covers settings, the wobble physics model, components, bot profiles, data tables for days, poses, lures, trays, and courses, plus event handlers for morning, pose, pond, and line.\n\nThe file plan now includes event handlers for paddle, garden, tilt, and group, plus a scene registry, day flow machine, director, pilot, island, round, score, cast clips, and rest.json. The size of rest.json is being checked to see if it can be copied directly or must be split.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9b939ba4-190c-41ce-8022-c7d9ac2971e6-46","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656\" && find data/anim -name '_set.json' | head -20 && python3 - << 'PY'\nimport os\nfor root, dirs, files in os.walk('data/anim'):\n    for f in files:\n        if f.endswith('_set.json') or 'rest' in f.lower():\n            p=os.path.join(root,f)\n            print(os.path.getsize(p), p)\nPY","description":"Locate animation rest pose JSON size"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9b939ba4-190c-41ce-8022-c7d9ac2971e6-47","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"export function defineSong|export function defineSfx|export function createAudio","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine","glob":"*.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":237,"output_tokens":3157,"cache_read_input_tokens":98816,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"ac652b0f-68fb-489c-8f54-865080f7849c"}
