e to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n\\n RUN  v4.1.12 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656\\n\\n(node:3930574) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\nstdout | labs/game/scenes/speed.test.ts > step speed > times headless and startScene\\nHEADLESS_MS 1454.3 PER 72.72 us\\n\\n ✓ labs/game/scenes/speed.test.ts > step speed > times headless and startScene 1463ms\\n\\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\\n      Tests  1 passed (1)\\n   Start at  22:49:52\\n   Duration  5.85s (transform 3.31s, setup 51ms, import 4.23s, tests 1.47s, environment 0ms)\\n\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"cd \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656\\\" && npx vitest run labs/game/scenes/speed.test.ts --reporter=verbose 2>&1 | tail -40\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Benchmark empty headless scene step cost\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc%2Fwork/01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc/terminal/call-390bf161-ae69-4e23-b699-2652845c8a25-81.log\",\"total_bytes\":1021}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"675ec8d1-60da-436d-93ca-e5095b74cb7a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_46","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Estimating runtime at 158 seconds for 2.2 million steps.\n\nSerial activity bot tests would take about 2.6 minutes. Parallel workers could cut this to roughly 20 seconds. The default Vitest timeout is 30 seconds, so the long test must be split or its timeout raised.\n\nEach activity will be a separate `it()` block. Pose three exceeds the 30-second default, so its timeout must be raised to 120 seconds. Tilt is borderline at 30 seconds. Group finishes in about 26 seconds. Director tests need roughly 15 minutes per seed.\n\nDirector simulation time is now estimated at roughly 20 minutes per seed, or about 72,600 steps. Three seeds total around 16 seconds. The bot matrix remains the dominant cost at roughly 2.5 minutes.\n\nThe bot matrix will be placed in verify.mjs and also run via Vitest so npm test covers it. Worker threads are unnecessary since the 2.5-minute runtime is acceptable. Running all 32 parallel workers at once risks an out-of-memory crash, but keeping activity tests in a single file limits each worker to one engine.\n\nCreating 280 engines across all seeds could add significant startup time. The prior test run suggests each engine creation takes roughly 50 milliseconds.\n\nEngine creation is cheap after import, so 10 separate engines per activity is acceptable. I will use `createHeadless` with scene, seed, and settings. State will be read via `engine.state(component)` to get entities.\n\nMath.sin is swapped during world.step, so hashes stay deterministic. Settings will be read live via w.settings.get each step so sliders apply immediately. defineSettings runs at module load when createHeadless loads the scene module, so no special startup order is needed. Integer tick counts and numeric scores are fine, and components can hold many fields.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8851b216-628b-401a-9036-4554e36f3713-82","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/eslint.config.js","limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":650,"output_tokens":1286,"cache_read_input_tokens":132480,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"afc6cfe5-bd3f-4496-b330-427f531e60e4"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8851b216-628b-401a-9036-4554e36f3713-82","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file ESLint's settings for T0 (PLAN.md §6.10; `npm run lint`, inside `npm run check`): typescript-eslint's\\n * recommended rules without type information (so T0 stays fast), the file-comment and size rules, then the doctrine's\\n * rule families from tools/eslint/, one block per family, each message naming the fix.\\n *\\n * Families, in order: the layer rules (layers.ts), the public-API rule (publicApi.ts), the reproducibility bans for\\n * sim-side code (simSide.ts), the banned three.js APIs (banned.ts) and the local rule \\\"ask the entry, never the id\\\"\\n * (askTheEntry.ts). Each family's rule ids carry its name (`layer/no-restricted-imports`, `sim/no-restricted-globals`,\\n * `banned/no-restricted-syntax`, `local/ask-the-entry`); tools/eslint/family.ts says why.\\n10→ *\\n * Invariants: rules written ahead of the code they guard are switched in `SWITCHES` and nowhere else. The cache lives\\n * in node_modules/.cache/eslint/ (package.json's scripts). Tests lint fixtures with `configure(…)` from a temporary\\n * directory (tools/eslint/testing.ts).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // npm run lint  → eslint --cache --cache-location node_modules/.cache/eslint/ .\\n * @see tools/eslint/index.ts\\n */\\nimport jsdoc from 'eslint-plugin-jsdoc';\\n20→import globals from 'globals';\\nimport { tsImport } from 'tsx/esm/api';\\nimport tseslint from 'typescript-eslint';\\n\\n/** The families are TypeScript under tools/eslint/; tsx loads them, as x.js loads the x commands. */\\nconst families = await tsImport('./tools/eslint/index.ts', import.meta.url);\\n\\n/** Rules written ahead of the code they guard. The WP named flips its switch to true, here and only here. */\\nexport const SWITCHES = {\\n  /** Game code imports only engine/index.ts and engine/sim-api.ts (tools/eslint/publicApi.ts): on since WP 1.6. */\\n30→  publicApi: true,\\n  /** \\\"Ask the entry, never the id\\\" (tools/eslint/askTheEntry.ts): on since WP 1.2, with the registry. */\\n  askTheEntry: true,\\n};\\n\\n/** Code under these directories opens with a `@file` comment and stays under 400 lines (hard cap 600). */\\nconst AGENT_READABLE = [\\n  'engine/**/*.{ts,js,mjs}',\\n  'tools/**/*.{ts,js,mjs}',\\n  'labs/**/*.{ts,js,mjs}',\\n40→  'tests/**/*.{ts,js,mjs}',\\n  '.claude/hooks/**/*.ts',\\n];\\n\\n/** Builds the whole config; `switches` defaults to `SWITCHES` (tests turn every switch on). */\\nexport function configure(switches = SWITCHES) {\\n  return [\\n    {\\n      name: 'ignores',\\n      ignores: ['out/**', 'dist/**', '.cache/**', 'test-results/**', 'lean/**', '.claude/worktrees/**'],\\n50→    },\\n    ...tseslint.configs.recommended,\\n    {\\n      name: 'typescript: unused names',\\n      rules: {\\n        // The usual exceptions: a leading underscore marks a name unused on purpose; `{ dropped, ...rest }` omits a key.\\n        '@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars': [\\n          'error',\\n          {\\n            argsIgnorePattern: '^_',\\n60→            varsIgnorePattern: '^_',\\n            caughtErrorsIgnorePattern: '^_',\\n            ignoreRestSiblings: true,\\n          },\\n        ],\\n      },\\n    },\\n    { name: 'globals', languageOptions: { globals: { ...globals.browser, ...globals.node } } },\\n    {\\n      name: 'agent-readable: file comments and size (PLAN.md §6.8)',\\n70→      files: AGENT_READABLE,\\n      plugins: { jsdoc, 'hard-cap': families.family('hard-cap', 'max-lines') },\\n      rules: {\\n        'jsdoc/require-file-overview': 'error',\\n        'max-lines': ['warn', { max: 400 }],\\n        'hard-cap/max-lines': ['error', { max: 600 }],\\n      },\\n    },\\n    {\\n      name: 'no enums (erasableSyntaxOnly)',\\n80→      files: ['**/*.ts'],\\n      rules: {\\n        'no-restricted-syntax': [\\n          'error',\\n          {\\n            selector: 'TSEnumDeclaration',\\n            message: 'no enums (erasableSyntaxOnly): use an `as const` object and a union of its values (ADR-0003)',\\n          },\\n        ],\\n      },\\n90→    },\\n    ...families.layerBlocks(),\\n    ...families.publicApiBlocks(switches.publicApi),\\n    ...families.simSideBlocks(),\\n    ...families.bannedBlocks(),\\n    ...families.askTheEntryBlocks(switches.askTheEntry),\\n  ];\\n}\\n\\nexport default configure();\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file ESLint's settings for T0 (PLAN.md §6.10; `npm run lint`, inside `npm run check`): typescript-eslint's\\n * recommended rules without type information (so T0 stays fast), the file-comment and size rules, then the doctrine's\\n * rule families from tools/eslint/, one block per family, each message naming the fix.\\n *\\n * Families, in order: the layer rules (layers.ts), the public-API rule (publicApi.ts), the reproducibility bans for\\n * sim-side code (simSide.ts), the banned three.js APIs (banned.ts) and the local rule \\\"ask the entry, never the id\\\"\\n * (askTheEntry.ts). Each family's rule ids carry its name (`layer/no-restricted-imports`, `sim/no-restricted-globals`,\\n * `banned/no-restricted-syntax`, `local/ask-the-entry`); tools/eslint/family.ts says why.\\n10→ *\\n * Invariants: rules written ahead of the code they guard are switched in `SWITCHES` and nowhere else. The cache lives\\n * in node_modules/.cache/eslint/ (package.json's scripts). Tests lint fixtures with `configure(…)` from a temporary\\n * directory (tools/eslint/testing.ts).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // npm run lint  → eslint --cache --cache-location node_modules/.cache/eslint/ .\\n * @see tools/eslint/index.ts\\n */\\nimport jsdoc from 'eslint-plugin-jsdoc';\\n20→import globals from 'globals';\\nimport { tsImport } from 'tsx/esm/api';\\nimport tseslint from 'typescript-eslint';\\n\\n/** The families are TypeScript under tools/eslint/; tsx loads them, as x.js loads the x command