Escape').ok; // false: reserved for pause\"},{\"line_number\":91,\"content\":\"  rebind(action: string, code: string, options?: { replace?: string }): RebindResult;\"},{\"line_number\":142,\"content\":\"    rebind(action, code, { replace } = {}) {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"c1fc283d-5f53-451f-8b7a-dcad1010f772"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_60","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Starting to write the code. The starter play files and speed test will be deleted as they are replaced.\n\nPlanning to split the implementation into focused scene files: settings, wobble physics, bot thumb, state flow, and score logic. Correctness of the simulation comes first.\n\nExpanding the file plan to include data modules for days, poses, trays, course gates, and lures. Adding event handlers for kit, morning, pose, pond, line, paddle, garden, tilt, and group activities. Also adding a catalog registry, driver for step flow and actions, and an island scene.\n\nAdding `scenes/round.ts` and `scenes/play.test.ts` to the file plan. Each module will be roughly 150–350 lines.\n\nDefining shared `act` component fields for activity state: phase, tick, step accumulators, pose or gate index, flags, and generic numeric fields.\n\nAdding physics and pose fields to the shared `act` component: heading, velocity, foot state, debounce, composure, and goal coordinates. Also defining a `hist` component to store 24 cob capture samples as arrays.\n\nThe engine's World is generic, so I'll use loose component typing with casts. Actor is defined globally even when unused in scenes like the bench. I'm defining a local `Ent` type to bundle flow, wobble, and act components for cleaner queries.\n\nGroup wobbles will be handled by querying all seats, with seat 0 as the player.\n\nThe driver step order is now defined. Scene step reads live settings into a config. For event or group modes it determines input from auto/bot or intents, steps balance for each seat, then runs the activity step. If the activity finishes it tears down and advances to results. The director advances script for results, evening, or title modes. In roam mode the pilot writes actor intents during the ai phase, which runs after scene step in the intents phase.\n\nThe pilot system in the ai phase will write actor.intents. In roam mode it copies the step intents into actor.intents. Otherwise it writes a zero move. Scene step does not need to write intents directly.\n\nScene step will stash raw intents in a `pad` component every frame. The pilot reads this pad for roam moves, and the activity reads it for balance. Balance logic runs directly inside scene step where intents are available. Test bots pass intents each step.\n\nThe test will call the shipped bot and pass its result as step intents. The director will set a `flow.bot` flag so the scene step ignores those external intents and calls the bot itself. This avoids double-calling the bot while satisfying the verification requirement.\n\nThe test harness will call `game.start` to reset each activity into a fresh state before running it. Scene step will use the intents passed directly from the test bot, not the internal director bot, unless `flow.auto` is enabled.\n\nThe director will call the same setup function internally rather than using an external game.start action. A two-second golden replay of a still ring with no input will be recorded and verified by the test harness. The starter bot.replay.json will be deleted and replaced with a fresh recording generated via node x replay after the scene is stable. The npm test suite will include play.test.ts, which will contain the replay verification.\n\nThe replay golden must be recorded last because any engine change invalidates it. The island scene with terrain and seven actors will be tested for boot speed; the round scene is separate and small. A retreat looks module will be defined in labs/game/looks/retreat.ts.\n\nThe page sets `post.look=look:retreat` as a scene query. `defineSky` will be page-side, and its fields can be copied from `sky:noon`. Platform, cairn pebble, plaque, and mat props will use `defineProp` with physics enabled for `spawnProp`. The bench scene disables physics and skips actor spawning to keep node tests fast; activities spawn only lightweight `made` entities that are invisible when the view is off. The island scene will instead spawn the full visual cast.\n\nActivity setup will not spawn actors. The bench scene calls the same setup, so it must remain physics-free. A separate `present(w)` on the island will spawn visuals when an activity starts. Tests will verify teardown by checking for stray `made` entities. Any physics bodies created during setup must be removed to satisfy the acceptance criteria that no stray bodies remain.\n\nScrub clips will drive guest actor animation on the island. During the rules phase, if the mode is event and pose progress or cob data exists, each clip slot’s time is updated from those values.\n\nThe scrub function will live in the pose activity step. It queries all actors with clips and updates their slot times from the current pose progress and COB values. Morning leans will also use this logic.\n\nThe scrub function will also advance the active pose clip by its progress value. Actor clips cannot be played during setup because that throws an error; instead, lean and pose clips will be triggered on the first step tick.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-59509fac-ae65-4f9e-92c5-7cbc05dc97af-102","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/anim/clip/clipsets.ts","offset":90,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":452,"output_tokens":2751,"cache_read_input_tokens":160896,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"a55923ce-97d0-4206-a9e6-4adca579abc1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-59509fac-ae65-4f9e-92c5-7cbc05dc97af-102","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"90→    fields: CLIPSET_FIELDS,\\n    defineWith:\\n      \\\"defineClipSet({ set: 'NAME', sources: { … }, clips: { … } }) with a set's _set.json and its clip files\\\",\\n  });\\n}\\nclipSetKind(sharedRegistry);\\n\\n/** The id a set registers under: `clipset:` and its name in lower case (`clipset:style100_back`). */\\nexport function clipSetId(name: string): string {\\n  return `clipset:${name.toLowerCase()}`;\\n100→}\\n\\n/**\\n * Parses `input` (a set's text or object, `parseClipSet`) and registers it on `registry` as `clipSetId(set)`; a set\\n * registered already is returned when it is the same, and refused (`CORE_DUPLICATE_ID`) when it differs.\\n */\\nexport function defineClipSet(input: ClipSet | string | object, options: { registry?: Registry } = {}): ClipSetEntry {\\n  const registry = options.registry ?? sharedRegistry;\\n  clipSetKind(registry);\\n  const set = parseClipSet(input);\\n110→  const id = clipSetId(set.set);\\n  if (registry.has('clipset', id)) {\\n    const kept = registry.get('clipset', id) as unknown as ClipSetEntry;\\n    if (Object.entries(set).every(([key, value]) => sameValue(value, kept[key as keyof ClipSetEntry]))) return kept;\\n  }\\n  return registry.def('clipset', id, set as unknown as Record<string, unknown>) as unknown as ClipSetEntry;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * A set directory's files (`_set.json` and one `.json` file a clip, by file name; others ignored) as one set\\n120→ * (`parseClipSet`), its clips in its `fit`'s order, then by file name, as tools/anim/repack.ts `joinSet` gives it:\\n * what a page registers from the text `import.meta.glob` loads. `where` names the directory in errors.\\n */\\nexport function clipSetFromFiles(files: Readonly<Record<string, string>>, where = 'the set'): ClipSet {\\n  const { [SET_FILE]: head, ...rest } = files;\\n  if (head === undefined) throw codeError('ANIM_CLIP_BAD_HEADER', { where, field: SET_FILE, value: 'missing', shape: 'the set’s header' }); // prettier-ignore\\n  let raw: object;\\n  try {\\n    raw = JSON.parse(head) as object;\\n  } catch (error) {\",\"content_concise\":\"90→    fields: CLIPSET_FIELDS,\\n    defineWith:\\n      \\\"defineClipSet({ set: 'NAME', sources: { … }, clips: { … } }) with a set's _set.json and its clip files\\\",\\n  });\\n}\\nclipSetKind(sharedRegistry);\\n\\n/** The id a set registers under: `clipset:` and its name in lower case (`clipset:style100_back`). */\\nexport function clipSetId(name: string): string {\\n  return `clipset:${name.toLowerCase()}`;\\n100→}\\n\\n/**\\n * Parses `input` (a set's text or object, `parseClipSet`) and registers it on `registry` as `clipSetId(set)`; a set\\n * registered already is returned when it is the same, and refused (`CORE_DUPLICATE_ID`) when it differs.\\n */\\nexport function defineClipSet(input: ClipSet | string | object, options: { registry?: Registry } = {}): ClipSetEntry {\\n  const registry = options.registry ?? sharedRegistry;\\n  clipSetKind(registry);\\n  const set = parseClipSet(input);\\n110→  const id = clipSetId(set.set);\\n  if (registry.has('clipset', id)) {\\n    const kept = registry.get('clipset', id) as unknown as ClipSetEntry;\\n    if (Object.entries(set).every(([key, value]) => sameValue(value, kept[key as keyof ClipSetEntry]))) return kept;\\n  }\\n  return registry.def('clipset', id, set as unknown as Record<string, unknown>) as unknown as ClipSetEntry;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * A set directory's files (`_set.json` and one `.json` file a clip, by file name; others ignored) as one set\\n120→ * (`parseClipSet`), its clips in its `fit`'s order, then by file name, as tools/anim/repack.ts `joinSet` gives it:\\n * what a page registers from the text `import.meta.glob` loads. `where` names the directory in errors.\\n */\\nexport function clipSetFromFiles(files: Readonly<Record<string, string>>, where = 'the set'): ClipSet {\\n  const { [SET_FILE]: head, ...rest } = files;\\n  if (head === undefined) throw codeError('ANIM_CLIP_BAD_HEADER', { where, field: SET_FILE, value: 'missing', shape: 'the set’s header' }); // prettier-ignore\\n  let raw: object;\\n  try {\\n    raw = JSON.parse(head) as object;\\n  } catch (error) {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/anim/clip/clipsets.ts\",\"offset\":90,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"    fields: CLIPSET_FIELDS,\\n    defineWith:\\n      \\\"defineClipSet({ set: 'NAME', sources: { … }, clips: { … } }) with a set's _set.json and its clip files\\\",\\n  });\\n}\\nclipSetKind(sharedRegistry);\\n\\n/** The id a set registers under: `clipset:` and its name in lower case (`clipset:style100_back`). */\\nexport function clipSetId(name: string): string {\\n  return `clipset:${name.toLowerCase()}`;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Parses `input` (a set's text or object, `parseClipSet`) and registers it on `registry` as `clipSetId(set)`; a set\\n * registered already is returned when it is the same, and refused (`CORE_DUPLICATE_ID`) when it differs.\\n */\\nexport function defineClipSet(input: ClipSet | string | object, options: { registry?: Registry } = {}): ClipSetEntry {\\n  const registry = options.registry ?? sharedRegistry;\\n  clipSetKind(registry);\\n  const set = parseClipSet(input);\\n  const id = clipSetId(set.set);\\n  if (registry.has('clipset', id)) {\\n    const kept = registry.get('clipset', id) as unknown as ClipSetEntry;\\n    if (Object.entries(set).every(([key, value]) => sameValue(value, kept[key as keyof ClipSetEntry]))) return kept;\\n  }\\n  return registry.def('clipset', id, set as unknown as Record<string, unknown>) as unknown as ClipSetEntry;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * A set directory's files (`_set.json` and one `.json` file a clip, by file name; others ignored) as one set\\n * (`parse