ode. The presets are registered on the\\n * shared registry when this module loads.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:670-693` (`Input.DEFAULT`, `PLATFORMER`, `SHMUP`, `MENU_KEYS`) with 3D\\n * movement, and shardfall's layer that is never rebound (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:131-161`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * const map = getActionMap('actionMap:thirdPerson');\\n * map.actions.jump; // ['Space', 'PadSouth']\\n * map.move; // ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right']\\n * SYSTEM_ACTIONS.pause; // ['Escape', 'PadStart']\\n * listActionMaps().map((entry) => entry.id); // ['actionMap:firstPerson', 'actionMap:platformer', …]\\n * @see engine/input/bindings.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\\nimport { show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\\nimport { AIM_RULES, type AimRule } from './aim';\\nimport { isCode } from './codes';\\n\\n/** The system layer: action → codes. Always active, never rebound, never in the intents. */\\nexport const SYSTEM_ACTIONS: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>> = Object.freeze({\\n  pause: ['Escape', 'PadStart'],\\n  uiAccept: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Space', 'PadSouth'],\\n  uiCancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'PadEast'],\\n  uiUp: ['ArrowUp', 'PadUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\\n  uiDown: ['ArrowDown', 'PadDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\\n  uiLeft: ['ArrowLeft', 'PadLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\\n  uiRight: ['ArrowRight', 'PadRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\\n});\\n\\n/** Codes no action map binds: the pause buttons, and keys the browser or the system keeps. */\\nexport const RESERVED_CODES: readonly string[] = Object.freeze([\\n  'Escape',\\n  'PadStart',\\n  'PadHome',\\n  'F5',\\n  'F11',\\n  'F12',\\n  'MetaLeft',\\n  'MetaRight',\\n]);\\n\\n/** The fields of an `actionMap` entry. */\\nconst ACTION_MAP_FIELDS = {\\n  description: { type: 'string', default: '', description: 'What the map is for, in plain words.' },\\n  actions: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    required: true,\\n    description:\\n      'Action name → the codes bound to it (KeyboardEvent.code, MouseLeft…, PadSouth…, PadLeftStickUp…): held actions are the intents b, pressed ones p.',\\n  },\\n  move: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right'],\\n    description: 'The four actions that walk, as forward, back, left, right: their strengths make the move axes.',\\n  },\\n  values: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: {},\\n    description:\\n      'Custom intent key (\\\"game:throttle\\\") → action: its analog strength (0 to 1, a trigger) is that intent.',\\n  },\\n  look: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n    default: false,\\n    description: \\\"True for first person and the shooter: the intents carry look = [the camera's yaw, its pitch].\\\",\\n  },\\n  aimWith: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: AIM_RULES,\\n    default: 'none',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"What the intents' aim holds: none; centre, the point the screen centre's ray meets (first person, the shooter); pointer, the pointer's ray onto the player's floor or a right stick's push (isometric, top-down).\\\",\\n  },\\n  lock: {\\n\",\"total_lines\":275}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"4d4a8725-9312-4f2e-9ac8-ecb04de38e86"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_68","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"uiAccept includes Space and PadSouth.\n\nSpace is bound to both feet in the balance map. The system layer keeps it separate as uiAccept. The simulation reads these as button intents. Holding Space activates both feet.\n\nSpace triggers uiAccept during Still Pond. A fake pause menu would intercept this input and waste composure. The fake menu must not listen to uiAccept. Tests confirm a lure is not a real pause.\n\nEnter is both uiAccept and an act button. It would trigger menu accept and count as a pond movement.\n\nSpace is excluded from the act list, so it cannot trigger pond penalties. PadSouth serves as both uiAccept and act, correctly penalizing Cross presses in Still Pond. The roam map will use forward, back, left, and right intents to generate a move vector; the pilot copies this into actor.intents.move, and the scene step saves the values on pad.mx and pad.mz.\n\nActivities will not use move for balance.\n\nPage reads gamepads and sends game:seats. Single-player tests will map seat 0 to the balance values.\n\nThe next step is writing code. Characters, terrain, and HTML labels for stations will be placed first. Props can wait if time runs short.\n\nA sea component will be spawned as a large box at the origin with a sea material.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d49fead9-4760-4b38-9fb9-179a7724a2a3-113","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"defineProp\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/box","glob":"*.ts","head_limit":5}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d49fead9-4760-4b38-9fb9-179a7724a2a3-114","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/world/props/prop.ts","offset":1,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6017,"output_tokens":970,"cache_read_input_tokens":170752,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"704b4dd4-5064-4ddd-922e-7c26410e03ba"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d49fead9-4760-4b38-9fb9-179a7724a2a3-113","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d49fead9-4760-4b38-9fb9-179a7724a2a3-114","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The prop registry (PLAN.md WP 4.5, §6.6): the registry kind `prop`, one entry per kind of thing that stands\\n * in a level, as data: the meshes it is drawn with (geometry and material by id, §6.1: `world` names them, `gfx`\\n * builds them, engine/gfx/props.ts), its body (a shape and a material for the physics world), an optional light\\n * spot, where a level places it, and its interaction hooks. The engine's props are the crate, the barrel, the\\n * brazier's fire and the pillar (engine/world/props/catalog.ts), the library's sconce, banner, chest, door, table,\\n * bench, statue, lantern and chair (library.ts, WP 10.3, the chair WP 13.16's) and the house's fittings, the pane,\\n * the switch, the lamp and the garage door (fittings.ts, WP 13.16); a game adds its own with `defineProp`\\n * (`x new prop`). WP 13.16's fields: a `kinematic` body the sim drives, `health` and what breaking leaves (`breaks`),\\n10→ * a `prompt` for its own `use`, and parts `lit` only while the prop is on; a hook's touch also names the world, the\\n * entity and its user.\\n *\\n * A prop's frame: its base, where it stands, is the origin, +Y up, and its parts stand on it as the geometry kit's\\n * shapes stand on the ground. Its body's shape stands on the base too, so the body's origin, the prop's centre, is\\n * `propCentre(prop)` above it: what a body's pose (`readBody`) and `propPose` give, and what the meshes are drawn\\n * at. A part with `flame.tongues` above 0 is drawn as that many flame tongues dancing round its origin (its geometry\\n * a cone one metre high, stretched each frame), the 2D hall's flames. The hooks: `hit` (a swing, a blast) knocks a\\n * dynamic prop away and leaves the others; `use` does nothing; shared code calls them and never compares ids.\\n *\\n20→ * Carried: the idea of my-3d2dge's 2D prop catalog (`src/starter/*`, `src/emberdeep/51-themes.js`): kinds of props\\n * as data with their light metadata (a colour, a reach and a flicker beside the drawing).\\n *\\n * Invariants: an entry is plain data plus its two hooks, every field filled with its default; a part's name is\\n * unique in its prop; colours are hex; vectors have three numbers; a body's shape has a size above 0; spawn names\\n * and light tags are words. Geometry and material ids are gfx's to resolve (a missing one draws its kind's fallback,\\n * and `node x qa geo tex --only prop:` reports it). Problems raise `CORE_BAD_SPEC` naming each; a missing id gets\\n * `prop:crate` after a warning (`CORE_UNKNOWN_ID`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n30→ * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n * defineProp('prop:stool', { parts: [{ geometry: 'geometry:frustum', params: { radiusBottom: 0.2, radiusTop: 0.2, height: 0.45 }, material: 'material:planks' }], body: { type: 'dynamic', shape: 'cylinder', radius: 0.2, height: 0.45 } }, reg);\\n * propCentre(getProp('prop:stool', reg)); // 0.225: half its height\\n * getProp('prop:crate', reg).body.type; // 'dynamic': the engine's props come with the kind\\n * @see engine/world/props/prop.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { galleryField } from '../../core/gallery';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\\nimport type { EntryOf, Schema } from '../../core/schema';\\n40→import type { Point3 } from '../level/types';\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The prop registry (PLAN.md WP 4.5, §6.6): the registry kind `prop`, one entry per kind of thing that stands\\n * in a level, as data: the meshes it is drawn with (geometry and material by id, §6.1: `world` names them, `gfx`\\n * builds them, engine/gfx/props.ts), its body (a shape and a material for the physics world), an optional light\\n * spot, where a level places it, and its interaction hooks. The engine's props are the crate, the barrel, the\\n * brazier's fire and the pillar (engine/world/props/catalog.ts), the library's sconce, banner, chest, door, table,\\n * bench, statue, lantern and chair (library.ts, WP 10.3, the chair WP 13.16's) and the house's fittings, the pane,\\n * the switch, the lamp and the garage door (fittings.ts, WP 13.16); a game adds its own with `defineProp`\\n * (`x new prop`). WP 13.16's fields: a `kinematic` body the sim drives, `health` and what breaking leaves (`breaks`),\\n10→ * a `prompt` for its own `use`, and parts `lit` only while the prop is on; a hook's touch also names the world, the\\n * entity and its user.\\n *\\n * A prop's frame: its base, where it stands, is the origin, +Y up, and its parts stand on it as the geometry kit's\\n * shapes stand on the ground. Its body's shape stands on the base too, so the body's origin, the prop's centre, is\\n * `propCentre(prop)` above it: what a body's pose (`readBody`) and `propPose` give, and what the meshes are drawn\\n * at. A part with `flame.tongues` above 0 is drawn as that many flame tongues dancing round its origin (its geometry\\n * a cone one metre high, stretched each frame), the 2D hall's flames. The hooks: `hit` (a swing, a blast) knocks a\\n * dynamic prop away and leaves the others; `use` does nothing; shared code calls them and never compares ids.\\n *\\n20→ * Carried: the idea of my-3d2dge's 2D prop catalog (`src/starter/*`, `src/emberdeep/51-themes.js`): kinds of props\\n * as data with their light metadata (a colour, a reach and a flicker beside the drawing).\\n *\\n * Invariants: an entry is plain data plus its two hooks, every field filled with its default; a part's name is\\n * unique in its prop; colours are hex; vectors have three numbers; a body's shape has a size above 0; spawn names\\n * and light tags are words. Geometry and material ids are gfx's to resolve (a missing one draws its kind's fallback,\\n * and `node x qa geo tex --only prop:` reports it). Problems raise `CORE_BAD_SPEC` naming each; a missing id gets\\n * `prop:crate` after a warning (`CORE_UNKNOWN_ID`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n30→ * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n * defineProp('prop:stool', { parts: [{ geometry: 'geometry:frustum', params: { radiusBottom: 0.2, radiusTop: 0.2, height: 0.45 }, material: 'material:planks' }], body: { type: 'dynamic', shape: 'cylinder', radius: 0.2, height: 0.45 } }, reg);\\n * propCentre(getProp('prop:stool', reg)); // 0.225: half its height\\n * getProp('prop:crate', reg).body.type; // 'dynamic': the engine's props come with the kind\\n * @see engine/world/props/prop.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { galleryField } from '../../core/gallery';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\\nimport type { EntryOf, Schema } from '../../core/schema';\\n40→import type { Point3 } from '../level/types';\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/world/props/prop.ts\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The prop registry (PLAN.md WP 4.5, §6.6): the registry kind `prop`, one entry per kind of thing that stands\\n * in a level, as data: the meshes it is drawn with (geometry and material by id, §6.1: `world` names them, `gfx`\\n * builds them, engine/gfx/props.ts), its body (a shape and a material for the physics world), an optional light\\n * spot, where a level places it, and its interaction hooks. The engine's props are the crate, the barrel, the\\n * brazier's fire and the pillar (engine/world/props/catalog.ts), the library's sconce, banner, chest, door, table,\\n * bench, statue, lantern and chair (library.ts, WP 10.3, the chair WP 13.16's) and the house's fittings, the pane,\\n * the switch, the lamp and the garage door (fittings.ts, WP 13.16); a game adds its own with `defineProp`\\n * (`x new prop`). WP 13.16's fields: a `kinematic` body the sim drives, `health` and what breaking leaves (`breaks`),\\n * a `prompt` for its own `use`, and parts `lit` only while the prop is on; a hook's touch also names the world, the\\n * entity and its user.\\n *\\n * A prop's frame: its base, where it stands, is the origin, +Y up, and its parts stand on it as the geometry kit's\\n * shapes stand on the ground. Its body's shape stands on the base too, so the body's origin, the prop's centre, is\\n * `propCentre(prop)` above it: what a body's pose (`readBody`) and `propPose` give, and what the meshes are drawn\\n * at. A part with `flame.tongues` above 0 is drawn as that many flame tongues dancing round its origin (its geometry\\n * a cone one metre high, stretched each frame), the 2D hall's flames. The hooks: `hit` (a swing, a blast) knocks a\\n * dynamic prop away and leaves the others; `use` does nothing; shared code calls them and never compares ids.\\n *\\n * Carried: the idea of my-3d2dge's 2D prop catalog (`src/starter/*`, `src/emberdeep/51-themes.js`): kinds of props\\n * as data with their light metadata (a colour, a reach and a flicker beside the drawing).\\n *\\n * Invariants: an entry is plain data plus its two hooks, every field filled with its default; a part's name is\\n * unique in its prop; colours are hex; vectors have three numbers; a body's shape has a size above 0; spawn names\\n * and light tags are words. Geometry and material ids are gfx's to resolve (a missing one draws its kind's fallback,\\n * and `node x qa geo tex --only prop:` reports it). Problems raise `CORE_BAD_SPEC` naming each; a missing id gets\\n * `prop:crate` after a warning (`CORE_UNKNOWN_ID`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n * defineProp('prop:stool', { parts: [{ geometry: 'geometry:frustum', params: { radiusBottom: 0.2, radiusTop: 0.2, height: 0.45 }, material: 'material:planks' }], body: { type: 'dynamic', shape: 'cylinder', radius: 0.2, height: 0.45 } }, reg);\\n * propCentre(getProp('prop:stool', reg)); // 0.225: half its height\\n * getProp('prop:crate', reg).body.type; // 'dynamic': the engine's props come with the kind\\n * @see engine/world/props/prop.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { galleryField } from '../../core/gallery';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\\nimport type { EntryOf, Schema } from '../../core/schema';\\nimport type { Point3 } from '../level/types';\\n\",\"total_lines\":373}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"c1dd7987-56b0-4d85-acc2-dcdc2bcbdf2a"}
