{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1b03eab3-b5a5-41f7-80be-8dd1968632f4-118","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"40→  /** A stream from `seed` (any number; normalised with `| 0`, as my-3d2dge's `E.rng` does). */\\n  constructor(seed: number) {\\n    this.#state = seed | 0;\\n  }\\n\\n  /** The next number in [0, 1). */\\n  next(): number {\\n    const s = (this.#state + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0;\\n    this.#state = s;\\n    let t = Math.imul(s ^ (s >>> 15), 1 | s);\\n50→    t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;\\n    return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / TWO_32;\\n  }\\n\\n  /** A number in [min, max). */\\n  range(min: number, max: number): number {\\n    return min + this.next() * (max - min);\\n  }\\n\\n  /** An integer from `min` to `max`, both included. */\\n60→  int(min: number, max: number): number {\\n    return Math.floor(min + this.next() * (max - min + 1));\\n  }\\n\\n  /** True with probability `p`. */\\n  chance(p: number): boolean {\\n    return this.next() < p;\\n  }\\n\\n  /** One element of `list`, uniformly; undefined when it is empty. */\\n70→  pick<T>(list: readonly T[]): T {\\n    return list[Math.floor(this.next() * list.length)];\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Shuffles `list` in place (Fisher–Yates) and returns it. */\\n  shuffle<T>(list: T[]): T[] {\\n    for (let i = list.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {\\n      const j = Math.floor(this.next() * (i + 1));\\n      [list[i], list[j]] = [list[j], list[i]];\\n    }\",\"content_concise\":\"40→  /** A stream from `seed` (any number; normalised with `| 0`, as my-3d2dge's `E.rng` does). */\\n  constructor(seed: number) {\\n    this.#state = seed | 0;\\n  }\\n\\n  /** The next number in [0, 1). */\\n  next(): number {\\n    const s = (this.#state + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0;\\n    this.#state = s;\\n    let t = Math.imul(s ^ (s >>> 15), 1 | s);\\n50→    t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;\\n    return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / TWO_32;\\n  }\\n\\n  /** A number in [min, max). */\\n  range(min: number, max: number): number {\\n    return min + this.next() * (max - min);\\n  }\\n\\n  /** An integer from `min` to `max`, both included. */\\n60→  int(min: number, max: number): number {\\n    return Math.floor(min + this.next() * (max - min + 1));\\n  }\\n\\n  /** True with probability `p`. */\\n  chance(p: number): boolean {\\n    return this.next() < p;\\n  }\\n\\n  /** One element of `list`, uniformly; undefined when it is empty. */\\n70→  pick<T>(list: readonly T[]): T {\\n    return list[Math.floor(this.next() * list.length)];\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Shuffles `list` in place (Fisher–Yates) and returns it. */\\n  shuffle<T>(list: T[]): T[] {\\n    for (let i = list.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {\\n      const j = Math.floor(this.next() * (i + 1));\\n      [list[i], list[j]] = [list[j], list[i]];\\n    }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/core/rng.ts\",\"offset\":40,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"  /** A stream from `seed` (any number; normalised with `| 0`, as my-3d2dge's `E.rng` does). */\\n  constructor(seed: number) {\\n    this.#state = seed | 0;\\n  }\\n\\n  /** The next number in [0, 1). */\\n  next(): number {\\n    const s = (this.#state + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0;\\n    this.#state = s;\\n    let t = Math.imul(s ^ (s >>> 15), 1 | s);\\n    t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;\\n    return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / TWO_32;\\n  }\\n\\n  /** A number in [min, max). */\\n  range(min: number, max: number): number {\\n    return min + this.next() * (max - min);\\n  }\\n\\n  /** An integer from `min` to `max`, both included. */\\n  int(min: number, max: number): number {\\n    return Math.floor(min + this.next() * (max - min + 1));\\n  }\\n\\n  /** True with probability `p`. */\\n  chance(p: number): boolean {\\n    return this.next() < p;\\n  }\\n\\n  /** One element of `list`, uniformly; undefined when it is empty. */\\n  pick<T>(list: readonly T[]): T {\\n    return list[Math.floor(this.next() * list.length)];\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Shuffles `list` in place (Fisher–Yates) and returns it. */\\n  shuffle<T>(list: T[]): T[] {\\n    for (let i = list.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {\\n      const j = Math.floor(this.next() * (i + 1));\\n      [list[i], list[j]] = [list[j], list[i]];\\n    }\\n\",\"total_lines\":257}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"fd7448db-a280-4b26-83a7-fd2ddbb69de3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_73","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Math.imul and the unsigned right shift operator are acceptable.\n\nThe simulation swaps Math during each step, so internal RNG calls remain valid. Deterministic setup should run inside steps rather than outside them. Components will be defined once at module load to avoid duplicate definitions. Scene actions execute between steps and can spawn or reset objects before the next step begins.\n\nThe test will import and invoke setup, step, score, and bot directly from the source module. The simulation engine will also call the same functions internally when a bot argument is provided.\n\nThe test will run a headless engine, invoke the morning setup action, then loop over bot intents and step calls. It will assert scores and inspect entities directly. The snapshot must expose enough world state for the bot function. I need to verify whether createHeadless exposes the raw world or only a state snapshot.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-470b0719-0989-4010-8ef0-fc97e212126c-119","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"defineMember\\('state'","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/dev","glob":"*.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":656,"output_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_tokens":180096,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"8b470101-25b5-4dc9-8105-0486e74d16d7"}
