{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b9d8a537-a746-4b1b-afa7-3bd4deb57407-125","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"170→      return next;\\n    },\\n    set(path, value) {\\n      sync();\\n      const change = settings.set(path, value);\\n      sync();\\n      return change;\\n    },\\n    act(name, args) {\\n      const actions = run.scene.actions as Record<string, (w: unknown, a: unknown) => void>;\\n180→      const own = Object.hasOwn(actions, name) && typeof actions[name] === 'function' ? actions[name] : undefined;\\n      const engine = own ? undefined : findDevAction(registry, name);\\n      if (!own && !engine) {\\n        const names = [...new Set([...Object.keys(actions), ...listDevActions(registry).map((a) => a.id)])].sort();\\n        const near = didYouMean(name, names).trim().slice(1, -1);\\n        const suggestion = near || (names.length ? `its actions: ${names.map(show).join(', ')}` : 'it has none');\\n        throw codeError('SIM_NO_ACTION', { scene: run.scene.id, name: show(name), suggestion });\\n      }\\n      const text = args === undefined ? undefined : serialize(args as Canonical);\\n      const given = () => (text === undefined ? undefined : deserialize(text));\\n190→      const checked = engine ? devArgs(engine, given(), name) : {}; // before anything changes\\n      sync();\\n      const before = world.capture(); // the sim and its recorded settings: a throw puts both back\\n      try {\\n        for (const [path, value] of Object.entries(engine?.settings(checked) ?? {})) settings.set(path, value);\\n        if (own) world.run((w) => own(w, given()));\\n        else if (engine && changesSim(engine)) world.run((w) => engine.run(w as never, checked));\\n      } catch (error) {\\n        world.restore(before);\\n        throw error;\\n200→      }\\n      sync();\\n      if (!own && !changesSim(engine!)) return; // settings alone: recorded as set (view ones never)\\n      Object.assign(pointFor('dev'), { dev: name }, text === undefined ? {} : { args: deserialize(text) });\\n    },\\n    capture() {\\n      sync();\\n      const capture = world.capture();\\n      const text = serialize(inputs as unknown as Canonical);\\n      marks.set(capture, { steps, inputs: text, last, seen, hash: digest(capture) });\",\"content_concise\":\"170→      return next;\\n    },\\n    set(path, value) {\\n      sync();\\n      const change = settings.set(path, value);\\n      sync();\\n      return change;\\n    },\\n    act(name, args) {\\n      const actions = run.scene.actions as Record<string, (w: unknown, a: unknown) => void>;\\n180→      const own = Object.hasOwn(actions, name) && typeof actions[name] === 'function' ? actions[name] : undefined;\\n      const engine = own ? undefined : findDevAction(registry, name);\\n      if (!own && !engine) {\\n        const names = [...new Set([...Object.keys(actions), ...listDevActions(registry).map((a) => a.id)])].sort();\\n        const near = didYouMean(name, names).trim().slice(1, -1);\\n        const suggestion = near || (names.length ? `its actions: ${names.map(show).join(', ')}` : 'it has none');\\n        throw codeError('SIM_NO_ACTION', { scene: run.scene.id, name: show(name), suggestion });\\n      }\\n      const text = args === undefined ? undefined : serialize(args as Canonical);\\n      const given = () => (text === undefined ? undefined : deserialize(text));\\n190→      const checked = engine ? devArgs(engine, given(), name) : {}; // before anything changes\\n      sync();\\n      const before = world.capture(); // the sim and its recorded settings: a throw puts both back\\n      try {\\n        for (const [path, value] of Object.entries(engine?.settings(checked) ?? {})) settings.set(path, value);\\n        if (own) world.run((w) => own(w, given()));\\n        else if (engine && changesSim(engine)) world.run((w) => engine.run(w as never, checked));\\n      } catch (error) {\\n        world.restore(before);\\n        throw error;\\n200→      }\\n      sync();\\n      if (!own && !changesSim(engine!)) return; // settings alone: recorded as set (view ones never)\\n      Object.assign(pointFor('dev'), { dev: name }, text === undefined ? {} : { args: deserialize(text) });\\n    },\\n    capture() {\\n      sync();\\n      const capture = world.capture();\\n      const text = serialize(inputs as unknown as Canonical);\\n      marks.set(capture, { steps, inputs: text, last, seen, hash: digest(capture) });\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/session.ts\",\"offset\":170,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"      return next;\\n    },\\n    set(path, value) {\\n      sync();\\n      const change = settings.set(path, value);\\n      sync();\\n      return change;\\n    },\\n    act(name, args) {\\n      const actions = run.scene.actions as Record<string, (w: unknown, a: unknown) => void>;\\n      const own = Object.hasOwn(actions, name) && typeof actions[name] === 'function' ? actions[name] : undefined;\\n      const engine = own ? undefined : findDevAction(registry, name);\\n      if (!own && !engine) {\\n        const names = [...new Set([...Object.keys(actions), ...listDevActions(registry).map((a) => a.id)])].sort();\\n        const near = didYouMean(name, names).trim().slice(1, -1);\\n        const suggestion = near || (names.length ? `its actions: ${names.map(show).join(', ')}` : 'it has none');\\n        throw codeError('SIM_NO_ACTION', { scene: run.scene.id, name: show(name), suggestion });\\n      }\\n      const text = args === undefined ? undefined : serialize(args as Canonical);\\n      const given = () => (text === undefined ? undefined : deserialize(text));\\n      const checked = engine ? devArgs(engine, given(), name) : {}; // before anything changes\\n      sync();\\n      const before = world.capture(); // the sim and its recorded settings: a throw puts both back\\n      try {\\n        for (const [path, value] of Object.entries(engine?.settings(checked) ?? {})) settings.set(path, value);\\n        if (own) world.run((w) => own(w, given()));\\n        else if (engine && changesSim(engine)) world.run((w) => engine.run(w as never, checked));\\n      } catch (error) {\\n        world.restore(before);\\n        throw error;\\n      }\\n      sync();\\n      if (!own && !changesSim(engine!)) return; // settings alone: recorded as set (view ones never)\\n      Object.assign(pointFor('dev'), { dev: name }, text === undefined ? {} : { args: deserialize(text) });\\n    },\\n    capture() {\\n      sync();\\n      const capture = world.capture();\\n      const text = serialize(inputs as unknown as Canonical);\\n      marks.set(capture, { steps, inputs: text, last, seen, hash: digest(capture) });\\n\",\"total_lines\":240}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"3dc40b96-381e-4283-b7fb-e9b95072d74f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_80","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Scene actions receive arguments as deserialized plain data.\n\nWriting simulation code now. Scene and activity steps will not overlap. Wobble components default on spawn then initialize sway from random state. Considering whether to use separate entities or one entity with all components.\n\nSettled on the entity layout. Flow, act, and pad will live on a single session entity. Each seat gets its own wobble and history entity. History arrays will be 24 zeros at spawn to avoid shared default references.\n\nThe driver script index will be stored on the flow component. The programme is built dynamically from DAYS inside the simulation, so the test can verify visited activities against the exported days.ts table without duplicating the day table.\n\nThe seen string will be roughly 200 characters. Repeated visits are fine because the test checks that every required activity ID appears at least once. Finale steps will be recorded as `tilt:storm`, `east`, `stone`, and `dawn`. The group activity will appear once in the seen list.\n\nCredits mode will be recorded as `credits` in the seen list. The director will enforce a hard step limit to prevent softlocks. Random input tests will use finite stick and button values only, avoiding NaN or invalid keys that could trigger intent errors.\n\nModel tests will verify wobble physics. A 20-second still probe will confirm the share stays between 0.15 and 0.5, proving sway exists without being dominant. Held full stick will be tested for toppling. Calm mode will be validated by comparing variance or outside-ring time. An internal `ring` activity may be added to support these probes.\n\nThe balance probe will use a dedicated `hold` activity that only steps wobble and records the inside-share value. The test will invoke this through the scene so the swapped `Math.sin` is active, satisfying the acceptance requirement to call the shipped balance step.\n\nThe scene step will always invoke `stepBalance`. This satisfies the acceptance requirement to call the shipped balance function while ensuring the simulation's swapped `Math` is active.\n\nThe test will assert that `stepBalance` is the exact function imported from the module. Sim results will be checked directly, since the swapped `Math` inside the simulation is what matters.\n\nA test helper will manually step the engine through an activity to verify the shipped balance function is invoked. The scene still triggers the activity step.\n\nThe test harness cannot call `activity.setup` directly because the world object is not exposed. Scene actions trigger setup automatically, and the public API only provides headless creation, so manual activity invocation remains impossible.\n\nThe test will drive the real engine step directly. It will read the current world state, call the activity bot to generate intents, step the engine once, and verify that the activity tick incremented by exactly one. This confirms the shipped scene path is actually being exercised.\n\nThe test will verify setup by checking that `act.id` changes after the `game.start` action. Only `game.start` will serve as the setup entry point, eliminating any duplicate setup path.\n\nThe code will be split into separate files per activity to avoid a single oversized module. The first batch covers settings, wobble physics, bot logic, state management, scoring, day tables, poses, catalog types, and then the activities themselves. History arrays will follow the gem component pattern of numeric arrays. Shared default references are avoided by assigning fresh arrays during spawn.\n\nThe `stepBalance` signature is now fixed. It takes a wobble state, a sway coefficient object, a stick input, configuration, and time. Sway coefficients will be stored directly on the wobble component to avoid a separate entity.\n\nThe wobble component will hold thirty numeric fields. Settings will be read on demand via a `cfgOf` helper that takes a getter function. Activities will set `act.goalX` and `act.goalY` before the balance step, and the bot will read those goals plus history to produce stick input.\n\nThe scene step order is now fixed: prepare goals and disturbances, read input, step balance, advance score and phase, then record history. A one-step delay between the test bot and the simulation is intentional because the human bot already has a delay.\n\nThe step order is refined so goals are updated at the end of the previous step. At the start of each step, the bot reads the already-set goals, produces stick input, and the balance step applies that input before advance updates the next goals. This keeps the test's intent generation and simulation state perfectly aligned.\n\nAn `intentsOf` helper will map stick axes into directional intent keys. It splits horizontal and vertical inputs into left, right, forward, and back buttons, then maps the foot buttons directly.\n\nIntent encoding now covers both foot buttons, gentle mode, and mouse deltas. Scene actions default missing keys to zero. The activity interface is defined with setup, step, teardown, and score methods.\n\nThe activity `step` method no longer takes intents because the scene driver applies them to the wobble component directly. Activities will read the wobble state instead.\n\nA new `made` component is defined for bodies spawned by activities. It tracks position and kind, and teardown despawns all made entities.\n\nAn `island` component will track tilt angles and day state. The centre stone sets `tiltX` from its position. The title list will be copied into the dev folder as `titles.json`. A `PROGRESS.md` will be written at the work root. The plan checklist item will be marked complete once progress and titles are saved.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c6fa19a9-606d-4732-a4ba-2123eb394550-126","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"scene","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/app/routes.ts","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":772,"output_tokens":3323,"cache_read_input_tokens":184064,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"f9dd76e1-90f2-4bbe-9642-394973a8d4ef"}
