{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-60f10da8-00af-4484-bc23-63c4558c8901-132","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"50→/** A hold lasts at least this long (s) … */\\nexport const HOLD_TIME = 0.32;\\n/** … and is seen by at least this many frames, so a slow frame never turns a tap into a hold. */\\nexport const HOLD_FRAMES = 2;\\n/** The mouse ends touch mode once it moves more than this (CSS px) from the last pointer. */\\nexport const MOUSE_SLOP = 2;\\n\\n/** The `touch` setting: touch mode as detected (`auto`), or forced `on` or `off`. */\\nexport type TouchSetting = 'auto' | 'on' | 'off';\\n\\n60→/** The touch settings: view settings, never in the hash. */\\nexport const TOUCH_SETTINGS = {\\n  touch: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: ['auto', 'on', 'off'],\\n    default: 'auto',\\n    view: true,\\n    description:\\n      \\\"Touch mode, which shows the touch controls and the phone defaults: 'auto' follows the screen (a coarse pointer or a first touch on, the mouse off), 'on' and 'off' force it.\\\",\\n  },\\n70→} as const satisfies Record<string, Field>;\\ndefineSettings(TOUCH_SETTINGS);\\n\\n/** Where the touch device listens. */\\nexport interface TouchTargets {\\n  /** The game's element (the canvas): the stick and taps on the game. */\\n  element: EventTarget;\\n  /** Where pointer events arrive, wherever they land (the window). */\\n  target: EventTarget;\\n}\",\"content_concise\":\"50→/** A hold lasts at least this long (s) … */\\nexport const HOLD_TIME = 0.32;\\n/** … and is seen by at least this many frames, so a slow frame never turns a tap into a hold. */\\nexport const HOLD_FRAMES = 2;\\n/** The mouse ends touch mode once it moves more than this (CSS px) from the last pointer. */\\nexport const MOUSE_SLOP = 2;\\n\\n/** The `touch` setting: touch mode as detected (`auto`), or forced `on` or `off`. */\\nexport type TouchSetting = 'auto' | 'on' | 'off';\\n\\n60→/** The touch settings: view settings, never in the hash. */\\nexport const TOUCH_SETTINGS = {\\n  touch: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: ['auto', 'on', 'off'],\\n    default: 'auto',\\n    view: true,\\n    description:\\n      \\\"Touch mode, which shows the touch controls and the phone defaults: 'auto' follows the screen (a coarse pointer or a first touch on, the mouse off), 'on' and 'off' force it.\\\",\\n  },\\n70→} as const satisfies Record<string, Field>;\\ndefineSettings(TOUCH_SETTINGS);\\n\\n/** Where the touch device listens. */\\nexport interface TouchTargets {\\n  /** The game's element (the canvas): the stick and taps on the game. */\\n  element: EventTarget;\\n  /** Where pointer events arrive, wherever they land (the window). */\\n  target: EventTarget;\\n}\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/devices/touch.ts\",\"offset\":50,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"/** A hold lasts at least this long (s) … */\\nexport const HOLD_TIME = 0.32;\\n/** … and is seen by at least this many frames, so a slow frame never turns a tap into a hold. */\\nexport const HOLD_FRAMES = 2;\\n/** The mouse ends touch mode once it moves more than this (CSS px) from the last pointer. */\\nexport const MOUSE_SLOP = 2;\\n\\n/** The `touch` setting: touch mode as detected (`auto`), or forced `on` or `off`. */\\nexport type TouchSetting = 'auto' | 'on' | 'off';\\n\\n/** The touch settings: view settings, never in the hash. */\\nexport const TOUCH_SETTINGS = {\\n  touch: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: ['auto', 'on', 'off'],\\n    default: 'auto',\\n    view: true,\\n    description:\\n      \\\"Touch mode, which shows the touch controls and the phone defaults: 'auto' follows the screen (a coarse pointer or a first touch on, the mouse off), 'on' and 'off' force it.\\\",\\n  },\\n} as const satisfies Record<string, Field>;\\ndefineSettings(TOUCH_SETTINGS);\\n\\n/** Where the touch device listens. */\\nexport interface TouchTargets {\\n  /** The game's element (the canvas): the stick and taps on the game. */\\n  element: EventTarget;\\n  /** Where pointer events arrive, wherever they land (the window). */\\n  target: EventTarget;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":299}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"7f99f5b5-5142-489e-93c9-cf14b9578f0c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_87","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `touch=off` query parameter works.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c87dd9ce-7e07-4813-9d4e-1fac1d1737e5-133","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/tools/eslint/askTheEntry.ts","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":432,"output_tokens":162,"cache_read_input_tokens":191616,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"53dea6b2-214a-4963-893d-5ac61dbc3117"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c87dd9ce-7e07-4813-9d4e-1fac1d1737e5-133","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The local rule \\\"ask the entry, never the id\\\" (PLAN.md §6.6, ADR-0012): shared code reads an entry's hooks and\\n * fields, each with a default on the kind's schema, and never compares a registered id, so new content works without\\n * editing the code that uses it. No stock rule expresses this.\\n *\\n * It reports, in `engine/` outside `*.test.ts`:\\n * - `===`, `!==`, `==` and `!=` between a string and either an id-shaped string (`'move:slash'`: a kind, a colon, a\\n *   name) or an id (`id`, `x.id`, `targetId`, `x.ownerId`);\\n * - `switch` on an id, or with an id-shaped `case`;\\n10→ * - `[…].includes(x.id)` or `.indexOf(…)` over listed strings, and `x.id.startsWith('…')`, `.endsWith('…')`.\\n * Comparing two variables (`entry.id === id`, a registry lookup) is fine, and so is an event or message type\\n * (`e.type === 'hit:start'`, `eventType`), whose colon strings are not ids.\\n *\\n * Invariants: written now, switched on by WP 1.2 with the registry (`SWITCHES.askTheEntry` in eslint.config.js).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // engine/anim/react.ts: if (move.id === 'move:slash') flinch();\\n * // → local/ask-the-entry: Ask the entry, never the id: … give the kind a hook with a default …\\n * @see tools/eslint/askTheEntry.test.ts\\n20→ */\\nimport type { Rule } from 'eslint';\\nimport type { Node as EsNode } from 'estree';\\n\\n/** A registered id: a kind, a colon, a name (`move:slash`, `prop:crate`; PLAN.md §6.3). */\\nexport const ID_SHAPE = /^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*:[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$/;\\n\\n/** An identifier that holds an id: `id`, or a name ending in `Id`. */\\nconst ID_NAME = /^(id|[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*Id)$/;\\n\\n30→/** Any node; ESLint's own types use estree's (installed with ESLint). */\\ntype Node = Rule.Node | EsNode;\\n\\n/** The string a literal or an expression-free template holds, else undefined. */\\nfunction stringOf(node: Node | null | undefined): string | undefined {\\n  if (!node) return undefined;\\n  if (node.type === 'Literal' && typeof node.value === 'string') return node.value;\\n  if (node.type === 'TemplateLiteral' && node.expressions.length === 0) return node.quasis[0].value.cooked ?? undefined;\\n  return undefined;\\n}\\n40→\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The local rule \\\"ask the entry, never the id\\\" (PLAN.md §6.6, ADR-0012): shared code reads an entry's hooks and\\n * fields, each with a default on the kind's schema, and never compares a registered id, so new content works without\\n * editing the code that uses it. No stock rule expresses this.\\n *\\n * It reports, in `engine/` outside `*.test.ts`:\\n * - `===`, `!==`, `==` and `!=` between a string and either an id-shaped string (`'move:slash'`: a kind, a colon, a\\n *   name) or an id (`id`, `x.id`, `targetId`, `x.ownerId`);\\n * - `switch` on an id, or with an id-shaped `case`;\\n10→ * - `[…].includes(x.id)` or `.indexOf(…)` over listed strings, and `x.id.startsWith('…')`, `.endsWith('…')`.\\n * Comparing two variables (`entry.id === id`, a registry lookup) is fine, and so is an event or message type\\n * (`e.type === 'hit:start'`, `eventType`), whose colon strings are not ids.\\n *\\n * Invariants: written now, switched on by WP 1.2 with the registry (`SWITCHES.askTheEntry` in eslint.config.js).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // engine/anim/react.ts: if (move.id === 'move:slash') flinch();\\n * // → local/ask-the-entry: Ask the entry, never the id: … give the kind a hook with a default …\\n * @see tools/eslint/askTheEntry.test.ts\\n20→ */\\nimport type { Rule } from 'eslint';\\nimport type { Node as EsNode } from 'estree';\\n\\n/** A registered id: a kind, a colon, a name (`move:slash`, `prop:crate`; PLAN.md §6.3). */\\nexport const ID_SHAPE = /^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*:[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$/;\\n\\n/** An identifier that holds an id: `id`, or a name ending in `Id`. */\\nconst ID_NAME = /^(id|[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*Id)$/;\\n\\n30→/** Any node; ESLint's own types use estree's (installed with ESLint). */\\ntype Node = Rule.Node | EsNode;\\n\\n/** The string a literal or an expression-free template holds, else undefined. */\\nfunction stringOf(node: Node | null | undefined): string | undefined {\\n  if (!node) return undefined;\\n  if (node.type === 'Literal' && typeof node.value === 'string') return node.value;\\n  if (node.type === 'TemplateLiteral' && node.expressions.length === 0) return node.quasis[0].value.cooked ?? undefined;\\n  return undefined;\\n}\\n40→\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/tools/eslint/askTheEntry.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The local rule \\\"ask the entry, never the id\\\" (PLAN.md §6.6, ADR-0012): shared code reads an entry's hooks and\\n * fields, each with a default on the kind's schema, and never compares a registered id, so new content works without\\n * editing the code that uses it. No stock rule expresses this.\\n *\\n * It reports, in `engine/` outside `*.test.ts`:\\n * - `===`, `!==`, `==` and `!=` between a string and either an id-shaped string (`'move:slash'`: a kind, a colon, a\\n *   name) or an id (`id`, `x.id`, `targetId`, `x.ownerId`);\\n * - `switch` on an id, or with an id-shaped `case`;\\n * - `[…].includes(x.id)` or `.indexOf(…)` over listed strings, and `x.id.startsWith('…')`, `.endsWith('…')`.\\n * Comparing two variables (`entry.id === id`, a registry lookup) is fine, and so is an event or message type\\n * (`e.type === 'hit:start'`, `eventType`), whose colon strings are not ids.\\n *\\n * Invariants: written now, switched on by WP 1.2 with the registry (`SWITCHES.askTheEntry` in eslint.config.js).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // engine/anim/react.ts: if (move.id === 'move:slash') flinch();\\n * // → local/ask-the-entry: Ask the entry, never the id: … give the kind a hook with a default …\\n * @see tools/eslint/askTheEntry.test.ts\\n */\\nimport type { Rule } from 'eslint';\\nimport type { Node as EsNode } from 'estree';\\n\\n/** A registered id: a kind, a colon, a name (`move:slash`, `prop:crate`; PLAN.md §6.3). */\\nexport const ID_SHAPE = /^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*:[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$/;\\n\\n/** An identifier that holds an id: `id`, or a name ending in `Id`. */\\nconst ID_NAME = /^(id|[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*Id)$/;\\n\\n/** Any node; ESLint's own types use estree's (installed with ESLint). */\\ntype Node = Rule.Node | EsNode;\\n\\n/** The string a literal or an expression-free template holds, else undefined. */\\nfunction stringOf(node: Node | null | undefined): string | undefined {\\n  if (!node) return undefined;\\n  if (node.type === 'Literal' && typeof node.value === 'string') return node.value;\\n  if (node.type === 'TemplateLiteral' && node.expressions.length === 0) return node.quasis[0].value.cooked ?? undefined;\\n  return undefined;\\n}\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":111}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"c9d545be-efd2-49c8-a8fd-81c5585e2e3b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_88","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The rule applies only to the engine/ directory, not labs/game.\n\nI will compare IDs in the game code. I plan to write files in parallel batches and add a `clamp` helper to math.ts. I am designing a director programme with a `DayPlan` interface to prevent softlocks.\n\nThe director programme now defines five days with specific event sequences and poses. It generates a flat list of events, marking the finale when the event is 'tilt'.\n\nThe programme now appends an evening event after each day except the last. Day 5 ends with the tilt finale rather than a separate evening. After credits, the sequence enters free play. The final morning is the last Morning Check. The manual player flow begins at the title screen and proceeds to day one.\n\nThe flow script index advances after each activity or sleep action. The programme menu will let the player jump to today's next activity. Sleep at the hut ends the day. The auto director simply runs the programme list without waiting. A `flow.cursor` field tracks the current position. The title screen starts at cursor zero, and Begin sets it to zero before launching the first event. After credits, the game enters a credits mode where the ferry does not return. Free play shows a noticeboard with all activities, and the morning check can be started again.\n\nSave data will persist day, pebbles, age, cursor, and finds. On load, game.begin passes this state to the simulation. The page will listen for events to update the store. Lines will emit as 'line' events with an ID. Activity completion will emit a 'score' event so the page can display results. The simulation will be the source of truth for screen mode. The page will mirror flow.mode into __game.screen unless a menu is open.\n\nPause menus will not pause the simulation in hub sessions. The attract mode will trigger after ten seconds of idle time on front-end screens, looping short director slices instead of the full campaign. When attract exits, the page will disable auto mode and reseed to a fresh title without writing to the store.\n\nThe inspector seed function preserves settings, so disabling auto mode before seeding correctly resets the scene to the title screen. Seed does not touch the page store, leaving saves untouched. A dev slider for live noise adjustment will be exposed via inspector.set, allowing tests to observe cob changes in real time.\n\nThe dev slider test will verify live behaviour by setting a multiplier such as `game.pebbles.mult`. The simulation will apply this value to pebble awards, and the page will mirror the setting in `__game.pebbleMult` each frame. A simple proof is to set the multiplier to maximum and compare sway before and after.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d7398a2f-3838-4d7a-8920-d3a588ac4799-134","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"describe\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/dev","glob":"*.ts","head_limit":15}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":866,"output_tokens":1379,"cache_read_input_tokens":192000,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"3cf70441-125b-4aa7-add9-5a6c6d99c3b4"}
