{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-cd0bbb0a-a0f1-410a-a646-f8018847f03e-139","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file What the clip layer plays and keeps (PLAN.md §10.4, WP 8.4; engine/anim/clip/layer.ts plays it): a play's\\n * options (`ClipPlay`: my-3d2dge's moment fields), a slot (a clip playing, its time and weight), the layer's plain\\n * state (`ClipLayerState`, which the sim saves, hashes and captures), its events, what a step is told\\n * (`ClipStepInput`), its timings (`CLIP_LAYER`) and what it is made with (`ClipLayerOptions`). Split from layer.ts at\\n * its line cap.\\n *\\n * Invariants: data only, plain numbers, strings and arrays; times in seconds, speeds in m/s.\\n *\\n10→ * @example\\n * CLIP_LAYER.fade; // 0.12: a clip fades in over 0.12 s unless its play says otherwise\\n * @see engine/anim/clip/layer.test.ts\\n */\\nimport type { Build } from '../builds';\\nimport type { JointName, MaskName } from '../skeleton';\\nimport type { ClipLibrary } from './library';\\n\\n/** How a clip plays (see the file comment). */\\nexport interface ClipPlay {\\n20→  /** Playback rate, 1 as captured. */\\n  speed?: number;\\n  /** Seconds it fades in over what plays now (0.12; 0 at once). */\\n  fade?: number;\\n  /** Seconds it fades out when stopped or ended (0.2). */\\n  out?: number;\\n  /** Clip seconds it starts from (0). */\\n  at?: number;\\n  /** The joints it plays: a preset, or joints and presets (`boneMask`). */\\n  mask?: MaskName | readonly (JointName | MaskName | 'root')[];\\n30→  /** Loops, or not, whatever the clip says. */\\n  loop?: boolean;\\n  /** Added to the pose under it (its change from its first frame), not laid over it. */\\n  additive?: boolean;\\n  /** Left and right swapped. */\\n  mirror?: boolean;\\n  /** Moving or a flinch does not cancel it. */\\n  walk?: boolean;\\n  /** A one-shot keeps its last pose until stopped. */\\n  hold?: boolean;\\n40→  /** The clip that follows when this one ends. */\\n  next?: string;\\n  /** Clip seconds by which a fall is down: a `landed` event, and `down()` from then. */\\n  landed?: number;\\n  /** Played as an attack: a `hit` event at its `hit` event, else at its strike time. */\\n  attack?: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/** A slot: a playing clip and where it is. Plain data. */\\nexport interface ClipSlot {\\n50→  /** `SET/Clip`. */\\n  clip: string;\\n  /** Clip seconds (a loop's run on; sampling wraps them). */\\n  t: number;\\n  /** Its fade, 0–1. */\\n  w: number;\\n  /** The last tick's rate. */\\n  rate: number;\\n  /** Seconds of the fade out under way; 0 while it plays on. */\\n  stopping: number;\\n60→  /** Picked by `locomote`. */\\n  loco: boolean;\\n  play: ClipPlay;\\n}\\n\\n/** The layer's state, plain data: what `step` changes and `save` copies. */\\nexport interface ClipLayerState {\\n  /** The clips playing, bottom first: the last is the current one. */\\n  slots: ClipSlot[];\\n  /** The loops `locomote` picks from, by ground speed. */\\n70→  moving: { idle?: string; walk: string; run?: string } | null;\\n  /** Whether the run plays (the walk–run switch's side). */\\n  running: boolean;\\n  /** The last tick's ground speed, m/s. */\\n  ground: number;\\n  /** The last tick's root motion `[x, z]`, metres in the character's frame. */\\n  root: [number, number];\\n}\\n\\n/** An event of the tick `step` took. */\\n80→export type ClipLayerEvent =\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file What the clip layer plays and keeps (PLAN.md §10.4, WP 8.4; engine/anim/clip/layer.ts plays it): a play's\\n * options (`ClipPlay`: my-3d2dge's moment fields), a slot (a clip playing, its time and weight), the layer's plain\\n * state (`ClipLayerState`, which the sim saves, hashes and captures), its events, what a step is told\\n * (`ClipStepInput`), its timings (`CLIP_LAYER`) and what it is made with (`ClipLayerOptions`). Split from layer.ts at\\n * its line cap.\\n *\\n * Invariants: data only, plain numbers, strings and arrays; times in seconds, speeds in m/s.\\n *\\n10→ * @example\\n * CLIP_LAYER.fade; // 0.12: a clip fades in over 0.12 s unless its play says otherwise\\n * @see engine/anim/clip/layer.test.ts\\n */\\nimport type { Build } from '../builds';\\nimport type { JointName, MaskName } from '../skeleton';\\nimport type { ClipLibrary } from './library';\\n\\n/** How a clip plays (see the file comment). */\\nexport interface ClipPlay {\\n20→  /** Playback rate, 1 as captured. */\\n  speed?: number;\\n  /** Seconds it fades in over what plays now (0.12; 0 at once). */\\n  fade?: number;\\n  /** Seconds it fades out when stopped or ended (0.2). */\\n  out?: number;\\n  /** Clip seconds it starts from (0). */\\n  at?: number;\\n  /** The joints it plays: a preset, or joints and presets (`boneMask`). */\\n  mask?: MaskName | readonly (JointName | MaskName | 'root')[];\\n30→  /** Loops, or not, whatever the clip says. */\\n  loop?: boolean;\\n  /** Added to the pose under it (its change from its first frame), not laid over it. */\\n  additive?: boolean;\\n  /** Left and right swapped. */\\n  mirror?: boolean;\\n  /** Moving or a flinch does not cancel it. */\\n  walk?: boolean;\\n  /** A one-shot keeps its last pose until stopped. */\\n  hold?: boolean;\\n40→  /** The clip that follows when this one ends. */\\n  next?: string;\\n  /** Clip seconds by which a fall is down: a `landed` event, and `down()` from then. */\\n  landed?: number;\\n  /** Played as an attack: a `hit` event at its `hit` event, else at its strike time. */\\n  attack?: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/** A slot: a playing clip and where it is. Plain data. */\\nexport interface ClipSlot {\\n50→  /** `SET/Clip`. */\\n  clip: string;\\n  /** Clip seconds (a loop's run on; sampling wraps them). */\\n  t: number;\\n  /** Its fade, 0–1. */\\n  w: number;\\n  /** The last tick's rate. */\\n  rate: number;\\n  /** Seconds of the fade out under way; 0 while it plays on. */\\n  stopping: number;\\n60→  /** Picked by `locomote`. */\\n  loco: boolean;\\n  play: ClipPlay;\\n}\\n\\n/** The layer's state, plain data: what `step` changes and `save` copies. */\\nexport interface ClipLayerState {\\n  /** The clips playing, bottom first: the last is the current one. */\\n  slots: ClipSlot[];\\n  /** The loops `locomote` picks from, by ground speed. */\\n70→  moving: { idle?: string; walk: string; run?: string } | null;\\n  /** Whether the run plays (the walk–run switch's side). */\\n  running: boolean;\\n  /** The last tick's ground speed, m/s. */\\n  ground: number;\\n  /** The last tick's root motion `[x, z]`, metres in the character's frame. */\\n  root: [number, number];\\n}\\n\\n/** An event of the tick `step` took. */\\n80→export type ClipLayerEvent =\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/anim/clip/layerData.ts\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file What the clip layer plays and keeps (PLAN.md §10.4, WP 8.4; engine/anim/clip/layer.ts plays it): a play's\\n * options (`ClipPlay`: my-3d2dge's moment fields), a slot (a clip playing, its time and weight), the layer's plain\\n * state (`ClipLayerState`, which the sim saves, hashes and captures), its events, what a step is told\\n * (`ClipStepInput`), its timings (`CLIP_LAYER`) and what it is made with (`ClipLayerOptions`). Split from layer.ts at\\n * its line cap.\\n *\\n * Invariants: data only, plain numbers, strings and arrays; times in seconds, speeds in m/s.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * CLIP_LAYER.fade; // 0.12: a clip fades in over 0.12 s unless its play says otherwise\\n * @see engine/anim/clip/layer.test.ts\\n */\\nimport type { Build } from '../builds';\\nimport type { JointName, MaskName } from '../skeleton';\\nimport type { ClipLibrary } from './library';\\n\\n/** How a clip plays (see the file comment). */\\nexport interface ClipPlay {\\n  /** Playback rate, 1 as captured. */\\n  speed?: number;\\n  /** Seconds it fades in over what plays now (0.12; 0 at once). */\\n  fade?: number;\\n  /** Seconds it fades out when stopped or ended (0.2). */\\n  out?: number;\\n  /** Clip seconds it starts from (0). */\\n  at?: number;\\n  /** The joints it plays: a preset, or joints and presets (`boneMask`). */\\n  mask?: MaskName | readonly (JointName | MaskName | 'root')[];\\n  /** Loops, or not, whatever the clip says. */\\n  loop?: boolean;\\n  /** Added to the pose under it (its change from its first frame), not laid over it. */\\n  additive?: boolean;\\n  /** Left and right swapped. */\\n  mirror?: boolean;\\n  /** Moving or a flinch does not cancel it. */\\n  walk?: boolean;\\n  /** A one-shot keeps its last pose until stopped. */\\n  hold?: boolean;\\n  /** The clip that follows when this one ends. */\\n  next?: string;\\n  /** Clip seconds by which a fall is down: a `landed` event, and `down()` from then. */\\n  landed?: number;\\n  /** Played as an attack: a `hit` event at its `hit` event, else at its strike time. */\\n  attack?: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/** A slot: a playing clip and where it is. Plain data. */\\nexport interface ClipSlot {\\n  /** `SET/Clip`. */\\n  clip: string;\\n  /** Clip seconds (a loop's run on; sampling wraps them). */\\n  t: number;\\n  /** Its fade, 0–1. */\\n  w: number;\\n  /** The last tick's rate. */\\n  rate: number;\\n  /** Seconds of the fade out under way; 0 while it plays on. */\\n  stopping: number;\\n  /** Picked by `locomote`. */\\n  loco: boolean;\\n  play: ClipPlay;\\n}\\n\\n/** The layer's state, plain data: what `step` changes and `save` copies. */\\nexport interface ClipLayerState {\\n  /** The clips playing, bottom first: the last is the current one. */\\n  slots: ClipSlot[];\\n  /** The loops `locomote` picks from, by ground speed. */\\n  moving: { idle?: string; walk: string; run?: string } | null;\\n  /** Whether the run plays (the walk–run switch's side). */\\n  running: boolean;\\n  /** The last tick's ground speed, m/s. */\\n  ground: number;\\n  /** The last tick's root motion `[x, z]`, metres in the character's frame. */\\n  root: [number, number];\\n}\\n\\n/** An event of the tick `step` took. */\\nexport type ClipLayerEvent =\\n\",\"total_lines\":112}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"182fd120-1ad8-4d92-a8d1-eac3ad396da6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_94","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Speed is set to zero. Hold and walk are enabled. Leans use additive blending.\n\nConfirmed the animation timing order. The clips system steps the layer and may overwrite t based on speed. With speed at zero, t stays unchanged. Setting t in the intents phase after the anim phase prevents overwriting. The next step loads state and steps with speed zero again, but the value remains correct.\n\nA `game.scrub` system will be added in the rules phase to set t last. Speed zero is being attempted, with a tiny speed fallback if rejected. Files will be written in large batches.\n\nOld starter files will be deleted once the new main exists to prevent typecheck errors. The vitest test imports createHeadless and passes, confirming WebGPU loads correctly. The `hist` component field will use `type: 'array'`, with empty arrays filled at spawn if hashing issues arise. The `tick` field must be an integer.\n\nScore will be stored as a number type to allow floats. The flow.seen string may grow long but that is acceptable.\n\nA shared types file will be created for activities to import. Import chains were checked and no circular dependencies exist between state, driver, catalog, and activities.\n\nbot.ts will import wobble and state types. The activity bot will import bot.ts for thumb().\n\nThe View interface will be placed in state.ts.\n\nThe View interface now includes `hist` and `cfg`. The `Hist` component stores a 24-point circular buffer of x and y coordinates. A `remember` function appends new points or overwrites the oldest entry when full. A `recall` function will retrieve past positions by delay.\n\nThe `recall` function will return zero coordinates when the history is empty. It clamps delay to the buffer length minus one.\n\nA hidden `ring` activity is being considered for the balance model test. The morning phase already covers the full lean topple scenario. Running it directly may be sufficient.\n\nA probe activity using `flow.event === 'probe'` was considered to test balance for a fixed duration. It would be started via `game.start` and kept out of menus. The director might exclude it from the catalog. A simpler alternative is to drive the existing morning still phase with full lean input and verify topples within 20 seconds.\n\nNo probe activity is needed. Morning will be tested directly. Zero input for twenty seconds lets the still phase record inside share on act.a at step twelve. Full right input for five seconds should trigger topples. Calm will be verified by comparing two twenty-second runs: one with synchronized breathing and one without. The test expects higher inside share when breathing is active.\n\nThe still-phase inside share will be frozen in `act.a` after twelve seconds. A custom scene step will call `stepBalance` directly, and a dedicated \"stand\" activity will run for twenty seconds to score the ring.\n\nA `game.probe` flag and `probeSeconds` setting were considered as a test hook inside the shipped driver. This approach was rejected as too ugly. The cleaner path is to define the test scene directly in the test file, then call the shipped `stepBalance` function from within a scene step.\n\nThe verification rules permit calling the real shipped function directly. A `game:probe` scene will spawn a fresh simulation and invoke `stepBalance` from its step, avoiding any reimplementation or past-setup mocking. Activity tests will continue to use `game:bench`.\n\n`freshWobble` will be placed in `wobble.ts` so the test scene and game share it. Sway will be seeded inside that function. Files will be written carefully and kept short. `node-verify` will be added after tests pass. Titles will be copied into the dev folder and `PROGRESS.md` written now. A shell script will extract `rest.json` while code files are composed. The cuts deviation will be added when the plan is updated. The `createAudio` volume API needs checking before writing audio.\n\nThe sim core will be written first, followed by model tests and then activities. Given the turn budget, as much as possible will be written now.\n\nGroup class short forms are 45 seconds each. Still ring score is inside share multiplied by 1000. Heron is pose score. Pond is pond score. Mean is group score.\n\nThe group bot reuses the same bots per class but switches desired goals. Grouping three sub-activities into one activity risks act field conflicts when calling their step functions directly.\n\nShort group activities will duplicate scoring rules briefly by calling shared helpers. A `track` function for the ring tracker will be placed in `kit.ts`. ESLint unused-variable warnings need fixing. The World type will use a loose interface or default generic to avoid casting.\n\nThe `World` type will be imported directly from `sim-api`. A `FlowEnt` helper will query the flow entity and cast it safely. Permanent entities will be spawned in the scene setup rather than inside actions, because `game.start` resets state without respawning the flow component.\n\nThe reset function zeroes all wobble state except sway coefficients, preserving the per-seat seed value across activities. Topples are reset per activity so each pose score reflects only that activity's count.\n\nThe history buffer will be cleared at the start of each activity to prevent stale coordinates from corrupting pose scoring. The old speed.test.ts will be deleted in this turn. A PoseDef interface is being drafted for pose data, defining clip names, seat positions, sway and instability multipliers, and ring radius.\n\nPoseDef now includes `breath`, `bothFeet`, `foot`, and `gull` flags. The pose catalog is grouped into three sets: a, b, and c. Hold times default to 12 seconds per pose, except comma which overrides to 8 seconds.\n\nPose definitions will use 0 for hold time to inherit the global setting. Lighthouse overrides its ring radius to 0.14 and its sway to 1.2. Nothing uses sway 0.5 and breath 0.6. Chair sway scales from base 1 upward by phase. Heron has instability 1.5 and left foot required. Archer has instability 1.2. Comma spans two seats. Napkin sits at 0, 0.5 with a gull disturbance. Bridge uses breath 0.7. Enter phase lerps the guide from origin to seat over four seconds along a slight arc. Progress scrubs from 0 to 1 and advances only when within 0.18 of the seat.\n\nThe enter phase is a scrub; if ten seconds pass without following the guide, the pose advances to hold anyway. The score counts only the hold phase for in-ring and sync accuracy, while topples accumulate across the entire pose. Release lasts two seconds plus rest before the next pose begins. Class mean will be computed at the end, so a weak hold on one pose will pull the average down.\n\nChair pose will score using feet-hold share instead of sync, since it requires no breath. The default score weights are 0.7 for in-ring and 0.3 for sync. Nothing uses 0.4 and 0.6. Bridge uses 0.3 and 0.7.\n\nHeron pose will require the standing foot to remain on the ground for the ring check to count, mirroring the morning one-foot drain. The pose.ts module is expected to be about three hundred fifty lines. A Tray interface is being drafted for sand trays with marbles, holes, and ridge segments. Tilt physics will use the slewed stick target rather than the noisy cob.\n\nTilt is derived from the stick target’s x coordinate scaled by a tilt degree constant. Marbles accelerate downward under gravity, tuned so a moderate lean sinks one in about four seconds across a two-unit tray width. Friction reduces speed by forty percent per second. A marble enters a hole only when its distance to the hole center is below radius and its speed is low enough to sink. Ridge segments block the normal component of motion if they cross the marble’s path.\n\nBots will steer the cob toward each hole scaled to 0.6 so they do not topple; with zero noise the feedforward bot stays stable and no topples occur. The sand activity uses five trays and lasts ninety seconds total, advancing when all marbles are sunk or after ninety seconds. The score is eight hundred times the fraction of marbles sunk plus two hundred times the bonus for finishing early.\n\nTray holes will sit downhill from each marble with a clear path, and the time limit is generous, so the activity should be easy enough for sloppy sinks to reach roughly forty percent and human runs to hit about seventy percent.\n\nThe paddle course will generate twelve gate points on a circle from the seed during setup. Each gate will spawn as a made entity with x and z coordinates for the bot to read; these entities are removed on teardown.\n\nThe line activity needs no complex geometry.\n\nTwelve guest made entities will be spawned on the island, positioned at the terrace initially and updated by the bot during the activity. Their coordinates are stored in act.hx and act.hz. Plaques and hidden pebbles will be permanent components on the island only, spawned during island setup and persisting across activities.\n\nRelic components will persist across activities because they use a `relic` tag rather than the standard teardown path. Each relic stores its base x, z, kind, found flag, and creep value. Plaques will shift left by 0.4 units per day via a `shift` field updated each step from `flow.day`. The full design is now complete and ready to be written out.\n\nI will create the files now using shell commands and direct writes. I checked that `defineSettings` and `defineScene` are safe from duplicate calls because Vitest isolates modules and does not re-evaluate them. The bench, island, round, and probe scenes are all defined, with probe placed in the test file and bench exported from the scene files.\n\nThe simulation will be written first and tested before the page. Twenty hundred lines of dialogue, data, and songs are planned for the page. The todo list will also be updated.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The balance sim has to be real and fast enough to score every activity. I’m putting that model in first, then the retreat around it."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b5cf2730-a90a-48af-b04c-3e94cc9c2c2c-140","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"DEV=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656\"\nmkdir -p \"$DEV/labs/game/scenes/events\" \"$DEV/labs/game/scenes/data\" \"$DEV/labs/game/cast\" \"$DEV/labs/game/ui/screens\" \"$DEV/labs/game/ui/lines\" \"$DEV/labs/game/audio\" \"$DEV/labs/game/sounds\" \"$DEV/labs/game/looks\" \"$DEV/labs/game/props\" \"$DEV/labs/game/tools\" \"$DEV/labs/game/replays\"\nnode -e '\nconst fs=require(\"fs\");\nconst s=require(\"./data/anim/sets/mesh2motion/_set.json\");\nfs.writeFileSync(\"labs/game/cast/rest.json\", JSON.stringify(s.sources.M2M_ANIMATED.rest, null, 2)+\"\\n\");\n' \n# titles\ncp /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/title-pick.json \"$DEV/titles.json\"\nrm -f \"$DEV/labs/game/scenes/speed.test.ts\"\necho done\nls labs/game/cast/rest.json\nwc -c labs/game/cast/rest.json","description":"Make game folders, copy rest pose and title pick","block_until_ms":15000}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":992,"output_tokens":4854,"cache_read_input_tokens":197120,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"13ff0410-7f12-4894-81fe-058adf10693d"}
