-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/main.ts\\n/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json\\n/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts\\n/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/play.ts\\n/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/bot.ts\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"DEV=\\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656\\\"\\nfind \\\"$DEV/labs/game\\\" -type f | head -50\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"List current game source files\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc%2Fwork/01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc/terminal/call-9be50788-dbbf-4a8a-8611-c48069011201-142.log\",\"total_bytes\":2343}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"99775ff0-e850-4345-b516-29b6930e1986"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_97","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"play.ts exists. The earlier listing was confusing because of a head command and two directories.\n\nDrafting the core source files: wobble.ts, settings.ts, state.ts, and bot.ts. Component descriptions are required. Seat values will be integers. Settings read via `w.settings.get` update every step. Pose hold times convert seconds to steps using `Math.round(seconds * w.hz)`.\n\nA `steps()` helper converts seconds to steps. `clamp` and `slew` utilities are defined for bounds and rate limiting. Now writing the core source files.\n\nEach source file will stay under 400 lines. settings.ts will export a shared TUNABLES array for the dev panel and simulator. Default values live in defineSettings. Activity durations will be constants inside each activity file. Driver auto is next.\n\nThe game auto mode now controls the initial state. Director mode skips the title and starts the programme immediately. Attract mode starts the attract loop. Off mode shows the title. Tests call game.start which overrides the mode to event regardless of auto. The start method accepts an event name and an optional pose. Unknown events throw a plain Error so tests catch them. A visit append is also being added.\n\nThe `visit` helper appends activity IDs to a comma-separated seen list. Credits end sets mode to credits and records the visit. Director auto advances through title, event, results, evening, credits, and roam states. Results and evening each last 30 steps before advancing.\n\nThe attract loop will cycle through eight activities, each capped at 15 seconds. The planned sequence is pose, pond, line, paddle, garden, tilt stone, and repeat. Activities that use the quick flag will run in these shortened time boxes.\n\nThe bot will cheat perfectly. Scores do not matter.\n\nActivities self-end normally unless the quick flag is set.\n\nAfter results the human must press game.carry to advance. Programme \"Go\" starts an event. game.sleep advances to evening and the next day.\n\nThe director auto test runs inside the simulator without page actions. It only steps forward.\n\nThe programme script is built once from DAYS at module load.\n\nThe `beginNext` function advances the programme cursor through the script. It starts an evening or credits event directly, or launches a normal activity. When an activity ends, the cursor increments. In auto mode the flow moves to results briefly before advancing; otherwise it stays on results until the human presses carry. The day field updates from the current script item. The final morning is included in the script.\n\nGroup and tilt are activities in the script. The idle bot finishes by checking its time box inside activity.step and setting act.done, which triggers driver teardown and results. Scores are clamped to 0–1000 with a finite guard. A rankOf helper maps scores to Unsettling, Serene, or Composed.\n\n`pebblesOf` scales a base pebble count from 1 to 5 based on the score rank, multiplied by a factor and clamped to at least 1. `wobbleAge` maps a normalized value to an age between 18 and 82 using a power curve.\n\nThe wobbleAge bounds are confirmed: 18 at s=1 and 82 at s=0. The simulator will avoid exponentiation operators. Large tests will use a 180-second timeout. Random test inputs will cover both axes and buttons to prevent crashes. A NaN guard will be added to stepBalance so non-finite values default to zero.\n\nThe bench scene will be implemented first so terrain bugs do not block scoring. The island scene is for the page and shares the same driver setup. A `bootSession` helper spawns the initial flow, activity, and pad entities.\n\nBalance is moved out of the rules phase and into the scene step, where it receives intents directly. The pilot system is registered in the ai phase.\n\nThe scrub system is registered in the rules phase. Scene step now runs drive first to handle balance and activities, then the ai pilot moves actors, followed by physics and scrub. The pad component receives movement intents as pad.mx and pad.mz. The pilot logic begins with a check for the roam mode.\n\nThe pilot assigns movement intents to the actor based on pad input. During the finale, the score uses act.hx and act.hz as its reference point rather than the actor's visual position.\n\nThe actor will be teleported to the simulation position during activities using `placeActor` so the body stands on the mat. Roam mode will leave the actor to the controller. The chase camera will follow the feet.\n\nThe actor will remain at spawn during activities so the camera stays fixed and the HUD disc is visible. The pilot will hold movement intents to zero while the guest is at a station. A `game.go` action will teleport the actor to the station when the activity starts. The exact `placeActor` signature will be verified during compilation.\n\nCore files, morning, pond, and a test will be written together first. The driver will be kept complete enough for all activities so it does not need rewriting later. Activities can be added to the catalog as they are written. A single test run will validate the entire suite.\n\nAll activities will be written before testing to save time. Array mutations are confirmed safe because the engine copies state on capture. Empty arrays will be passed explicitly at spawn to avoid schema defaults. Ready to write.\n\nA `zeroWobble` helper will zero dynamics while preserving sway. Initial sway magnitude is drawn from 0.8 to 1.25. The `guide` field stores the balance target for the HUD and pond. Breathing requires both feet together; a single foot counts as a stray.\n\nA stray foot penalty triggers only when exactly one foot is active, not when both are held. Stick input uses raw stick magnitude above 0.25, while mouse movement uses a 0.02 threshold on the scaled delta. The act button maps to game:act above 0.5 and feeds into intents for pond checks. A 60-step debounce applies to inputs. Lure IDs cycle every 6–10 seconds.\n\nLures will cycle through a table in data/lures.ts. The fake pause lure id `lure.pause` triggers a page menu while the simulation keeps stepping. Tests verify the tick advances and mode stays event. Ready to write files.\n\nThe scene step will run the drive function directly. Tests must call the `game.start` action before stepping, since setup already boots the session at tick zero. `createHeadless` runs setup before returning. It accepts a seed and settings object. Pose set arguments like `pose: 'a'` are passed as game.start parameters rather than settings.\n\nTests will log the minimum score per bot on failure to help tuning. Estimated runtime is 60–90 seconds across all activities, so a 180-second timeout is planned.\n\nEach activity test will use a 120-second timeout. Reusing one engine across runs is being considered to avoid repeated Rapier initialization overhead, though reseeding would restart setup and reset sway cleanly.\n\nOne engine per activity will be reused across all ten seeds. `engine.seed(n)` restarts the scene and resets sway cleanly while preserving settings. This avoids repeated Rapier initialization overhead.\n\nThe headless engine object exposes `actions.run` through the dev/actions import, so tests can dispatch actions after reseeding. The type is loose and may need a cast.\n\nThe bench scene needs no actors. The island scene will import the driver and catalog, then define its step as drive and register actions. The activity catalog must list every activity before the driver imports it. No circular imports exist between catalog, activities, and driver.\n\nA single `game:retreat` scene will serve both the page and tests. Tests pass `{ 'game.presentation': 0 }` to skip terrain and actors for speed, while the page omits the setting to build the full island. If a test forgets the setting, it defaults to 1 and runs correctly but slowly.\n\nThe scene spec cannot toggle physics dynamically, so two separate scenes are required. `game:bench` will run without physics for fast tests, while `game:island` keeps terrain and physics for the page. Both share the same driver, boot sequence, and actions.\n\nThe bench scene will use a 15-line `attach` helper that calls `bootSession`. The island scene will reuse that helper and add `dress`. I need to check whether `defineScene` with terrain automatically adds the body.\n\nThe scene may need both the terrain field and an explicit addTerrainBody call, so I will verify this against a box example. Tests will not load island.ts, so they do not need terrain bodies; only the page imports that module. A separate round scene will handle the group round for hub visuals, while bench tests can start the group directly via game.start.\n\nThe round scene will be minimal: flat ground, four props, plumb, no terrain, and a single physics floor body so it boots quickly. The hub test requires ghost entities present as simulation components updated from the game:ghosts intent.\n\nThe page will forward hub messages into the simulation as virtual axis inputs. Node tests do not cover the harness; only the browser harness does. For node group tests, one local player is enough to score. Ghost entities carry seat, position, pose, score, and an on flag. The page sends packed arrays of ghost data, and the simulation updates those entities. When on is zero, the ghost is hidden from the page. Tests verify that a ghost entity exists in the simulation.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The workspace is ready. Next I’ll add the balance model and the activity sim that the tests will drive directly."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-198c2a4d-6b41-4389-8d0a-0a8ca16d36c0-143","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/settings.ts","new_string":"/**\n * @file Tunables for the retreat (`game.*`). Every one applies at once (`when: 'now'`) so Dev Mode sliders and\n * replays change the live balance step. Cut activities have no settings here, so their names do not linger.\n */\nimport { defineSettings } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\n\n/** One slider: the setting path and the range Dev Mode offers. */\nexport interface Tunable {\n  path: string;\n  min: number;\n  max: number;\n  step: number;\n}\n\n/** The numeric settings Dev Mode lists, in the order the panel pages through them. */\nexport const TUNABLES: readonly Tunable[] = [\n  { path: 'game.wobble.gain', min: 4, max: 30, step: 0.5 },\n  { path: 'game.wobble.instability', min: 0, max: 10, step: 0.1 },\n  { path: 'game.wobble.damping', min: 1, max: 12, step: 0.1 },\n  { path: 'game.wobble.noise', min: 0, max: 8, step: 0.1 },\n  { path: 'game.wobble.noiseRate', min: 0.05, max: 0.4, step: 0.01 },\n  { path: 'game.wobble.reach', min: 0.5, max: 1, step: 0.01 },\n  { path: 'game.breath.period', min: 4, max: 14, step: 0.1 },\n  { path: 'game.breath.calmEffect', min: 0, max: 1, step: 0.01 },\n  { path: 'game.age.k', min: 0.5, max: 3, step: 0.05 },\n  { path: 'game.pose.hold', min: 4, max: 30, step: 0.5 },\n  { path: 'game.pose.ring', min: 0.08, max: 0.45, step: 0.01 },\n  { path: 'game.pond.penalty', min: 10, max: 200, step: 5 },\n  { path: 'game.line.stepKick', min: 0, max: 1, step: 0.01 },\n  { path: 'game.line.gust', min: 0, max: 1.5, step: 0.05 },\n  { path: 'game.paddle.speed', min: 1, max: 14, step: 0.1 },\n  { path: 'game.garden.tilt', min: 2, max: 25, step: 0.5 },\n  { path: 'game.garden.gravity', min: 1, max: 30, step: 0.5 },\n  { path: 'game.garden.sink', min: 0.05, max: 4, step: 0.05 },\n  { path: 'game.tilt.rate', min: 0, max: 2, step: 0.01 },\n  { path: 'game.pebbles.mult', min: 0.2, max: 3, step: 0.1 },\n];\n\nconst num = (def: number, min: number, max: number, unit: string, description: string) =>\n  ({ type: 'number' as const, default: def, minimum: min, maximum: max, unit, when: 'now' as const, description });\n\n/** Registers every retreat setting. Imported once, from the scenes. */\nexport const GAME_SETTINGS = defineSettings({\n  'game.wobble.gain': num(14, 4, 30, '1/s^2', 'How fast weight follows the thumb.'),\n  'game.wobble.instability': num(3, 0, 10, '1/s^2', 'How hard the body falls away from the centre.'),\n  'game.wobble.damping': num(5, 1, 12, '1/s', 'How heavy the body feels.'),\n  'game.wobble.noise': num(3.5, 0, 8, '1/s^2', 'Sway strength.'),\n  'game.wobble.noiseRate': num(0.15, 0.05, 0.4, 'Hz', 'Sway speed. Kept slow so a late thumb can lean against it.'),\n  'game.wobble.reach': num(0.9, 0.5, 1, '1', 'Full stick target. A held full stick topples on purpose.'),\n  'game.breath.period': num(8, 4, 14, 's', 'One breath: half in, half out.'),\n  'game.breath.calmEffect': num(0.5, 0, 1, '1', 'How much full calm quiets the sway.'),\n  'game.age.k': num(1.3, 0.5, 3, '1', 'How sharply Wobble Age falls as the morning check improves.'),\n  'game.pose.hold': num(12, 4, 30, 's', 'How long a pose is held.'),\n  'game.pose.ring': num(0.2, 0.08, 0.45, '1', 'The seat ring a pose is held inside.'),\n  'game.pond.penalty': num(80, 10, 200, '1', 'Composure lost when the pond is disturbed.'),\n  'game.line.stepKick': num(0.35, 0, 1, '1', 'Sideways kick of one step on the line.'),\n  'game.line.gust': num(0.55, 0, 1.5, '1', 'How hard a gust shoves the line.'),\n  'game.paddle.speed': num(6, 1, 14, 'm/s', 'Board speed at a full forward lean.'),\n  'game.garden.tilt': num(12, 2, 25, 'deg', 'How far a full lean tilts a tray.'),\n  'game.garden.gravity': num(9, 1, 30, 'm/s^2', 'How fast marbles run downhill.'),\n  'game.garden.sink': num(1.2, 0.05, 4, 'm/s', 'A marble slower than this is caught by a hole.'),\n  'game.tilt.rate': num(0.15, 0, 2, 'deg/s', 'How fast the storm leans the island before a deed takes some off.'),\n  'game.pebbles.mult': num(1, 0.2, 3, '1', 'Scales pebbles earned from a rank.'),\n  'game.mouse.sens': num(0.0025, 0.0004, 0.02, '1/px', 'How far pointer movement leans.'),\n});\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-198c2a4d-6b41-4389-8d0a-0a8ca16d36c0-144","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/wobble.ts","new_string":"/**\n * @file The one verb. Centre of balance is a point in the unit disc. Each step slews the stick, then\n * accelerates toward it with instability, slow sway and breath. Past the rim for six steps the body topples,\n * stumbles, and recentres. It is never a game over.\n */\nimport { defineComponent, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\n\n/** Numbers the balance step reads. Sliders change them between steps. */\nexport interface BalanceCfg {\n  gain: number;\n  instability: number;\n  damping: number;\n  noise: number;\n  noiseRate: number;\n  reach: number;\n  calmEffect: number;\n  period: number;\n  sens: number;\n}\n\n/** What the thumb, the feet and the activity are doing this step. */\nexport interface Stick {\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n  gentle: boolean;\n  both: boolean;\n  mdx: number;\n  mdy: number;\n  disturbX: number;\n  disturbY: number;\n  noiseScale: number;\n  instabilityScale: number;\n}\n\n/** The centre of balance and the sway drawn once for the seat. */\nexport interface Wobble {\n  seat: number;\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n  vx: number;\n  vy: number;\n  sx: number;\n  sy: number;\n  mx: number;\n  my: number;\n  calm: number;\n  lungs: number;\n  sync: number;\n  over: number;\n  recover: number;\n  topples: number;\n  guide: number;\n  m1: number;\n  m2: number;\n  m3: number;\n  p1: number;\n  p2: number;\n  p3: number;\n  n1: number;\n  n2: number;\n  n3: number;\n  q1: number;\n  q2: number;\n  q3: number;\n}\n\n/** A ring buffer of recent centres, so a late thumb sees an old one. */\nexport interface Hist {\n  i: number;\n  n: number;\n  xs: number[];\n  ys: number[];\n}\n\nconst field = (description: string, unit = '1') =>\n  ({ type: 'number' as const, default: 0, unit, description });\n\n/** The component `wobble`: one balancing body. */\nexport const WOBBLE = defineComponent('wobble', {\n  description: 'A seat’s centre of balance, its breath and the sway drawn for it.',\n  fields: {\n    seat: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Which mat this body stands on.' },\n    x: field('Centre of balance, left to right. Past 1 is the rim.'),\n    y: field('Centre of balance, back to forward.'),\n    vx: field('Velocity along x.', '1/s'),\n    vy: field('Velocity along y.', '1/s'),\n    sx: field('The stick after the slew, left to right.'),\n    sy: field('The stick after the slew, back to forward.'),\n    mx: field('Mouse lean, decaying.'),\n    my: field('Mouse lean, decaying.'),\n    calm: field('How settled the breath is, 0 to 1.'),\n    lungs: field('How full the breath is, 0 to 1.'),\n    sync: field('How well the breath matches the guide, 0 to 1.'),\n    over: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Steps in a row spent outside the disc.' },\n    recover: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Steps left in a topple’s recentre.' },\n    topples: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Topples since the count was cleared.' },\n    guide: field('The breath guide, 0 empty to 1 full.'),\n    m1: field('Sway rate ratio, x, first voice.'),\n    m2: field('Sway rate ratio, x, second voice.'),\n    m3: field('Sway rate ratio, x, third voice.'),\n    p1: field('Sway phase, x, first voice.', 'rad'),\n    p2: field('Sway phase, x, second voice.', 'rad'),\n    p3: field('Sway phase, x, third voice.', 'rad'),\n    n1: field('Sway rate ratio, y, first voice.'),\n    n2: field('Sway rate ratio, y, second voice.'),\n    n3: field('Sway rate ratio, y, third voice.'),\n    q1: field('Sway phase, y, first voice.', 'rad'),\n    q2: field('Sway phase, y, second voice.', 'rad'),\n    q3: field('Sway phase, y, third voice.', 'rad'),\n  },\n});\n\n/** The component `hist`: the centres a delayed thumb can still see. */\nexport const HIST = defineComponent('hist', {\n  description: 'Recent centres of balance for one seat, oldest first in the ring.',\n  fields: {\n    i: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Where the next sample is written once the ring is full.' },\n    n: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'How many samples have been kept.' },\n    xs: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Recent centres, left to right.' },\n    ys: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Recent centres, back to forward.' },\n  },\n});\n\n/** A number kept between lo and hi. */\nexport function clamp(n: number, lo: number, hi: number): number {\n  return Math.max(lo, Math.min(hi, n));\n}\n\n/** Moves `current` toward `target` by at most `maxDelta`. */\nexport function slew(current: number, target: number, maxDelta: number): number {\n  const d = target - current;\n  if (Math.abs(d) <= maxDelta) return target;\n  return current + Math.sign(d) * maxDelta;\n}\n\n/** The slow sway on one axis. Phases come from the seat, never from Math.random. */\nexport function swayNoise(t: number, rate: number, m1: number, m2: number, m3: number, p1: number, p2: number, p3: number): number {\n  const a = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * m1 * t + p1);\n  const b = 0.6 * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * 1.7 * m2 * t + p2);\n  const c = 0.3 * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * 3.1 * m3 * t + p3);\n  return (a + b + c) / 1.3;\n}\n\n/** Draws the six ratios and phases for a seat from the stream `sway`. */\nexport function drawSway(w: World): void {\n  const rng = w.rng('sway');\n  const ratio = () => rng.range(0.8, 1.25);\n  const phase = () => rng.range(0, Math.PI * 2);\n  const body = w.spawn({\n    wobble: {\n      m1: ratio(), m2: ratio(), m3: ratio(), p1: phase(), p2: phase(), p3: phase(),\n      n1: ratio(), n2: ratio(), n3: ratio(), q1: phase(), q2: phase(), q3: phase(),\n    },\n    hist: { xs: [], ys: [] },\n  });\n  void body;\n}\n\n/** Clears the motion and the breath, and keeps the sway. A new activity starts here. */\nexport function resetBalance(b: Wobble, hist: Hist): void {\n  b.x = 0; b.y = 0; b.vx = 0; b.vy = 0; b.sx = 0; b.sy = 0; b.mx = 0; b.my = 0;\n  b.calm = 0; b.lungs = 0; b.sync = 0; b.over = 0; b.recover = 0; b.topples = 0; b.guide = 0;\n  hist.i = 0; hist.n = 0; hist.xs.length = 0; hist.ys.length = 0;\n}\n\n/** Remembers a centre. The ring holds 24, which covers the sloppy thumb’s delay. */\nexport function remember(hist: Hist, x: number, y: number): void {\n  const cap = 24;\n  if (hist.xs.length < cap) {\n    hist.xs.push(x);\n    hist.ys.push(y);\n  } else {\n    hist.xs[hist.i] = x;\n    hist.ys[hist.i] = y;\n    hist.i = (hist.i + 1) % cap;\n  }\n  hist.n += 1;\n}\n\n/** The centre `delay` steps ago, or the oldest one we have. */\nexport function recall(hist: Hist, delay: number): { x: number; y: number } {\n  const len = hist.xs.length;\n  if (len === 0) return { x: 0, y: 0 };\n  const age = Math.min(Math.max(0, delay), len - 1);\n  const newest = len < 24 ? len - 1 : (hist.i + 24 - 1) % 24;\n  const at = (newest - age + len) % len;\n  return { x: hist.xs[at] ?? 0, y: hist.ys[at] ?? 0 };\n}\n\n/** One balance step. `t` and `dt` are sim time. A topple recentres over one second and counts once. */\nexport function stepBalance(b: Wobble, stick: Stick, cfg: BalanceCfg, t: number, dt: number): void {\n  const period = Math.max(0.25, cfg.period);\n  const phase = (t % period) / period;\n  const rising = phase < 0.5;\n  b.guide = rising ? phase * 2 : (1 - phase) * 2;\n  const fill = dt / (period * 0.5);\n  if (stick.both) b.lungs = Math.min(1, b.lungs + fill);\n  else b.lungs = Math.max(0, b.lungs - fill);\n  const instant = 1 - Math.abs(b.lungs - b.guide);\n  const participating = stick.both || b.lungs > 0.04;\n  const toward = participating ? instant : 0;\n  const blend = Math.min(1, dt / (participating ? 0.6 : 2));\n  b.sync += (toward - b.sync) * blend;\n  b.calm += (b.sync - b.calm) * Math.min(1, dt / 1.2);\n\n  if (b.recover > 0) {\n    const left = b.recover;\n    b.x *= (left - 1) / left;\n    b.y *= (left - 1) / left;\n    b.vx = 0;\n    b.vy = 0;\n    b.recover -= 1;\n    b.over = 0;\n    return;\n  }\n\n  const decay = Math.exp(-dt / 0.6);\n  b.mx = (b.mx + stick.mdx) * decay;\n  b.my = (b.my + stick.mdy) * decay;\n  const rawX = clamp(stick.x + b.mx, -1, 1);\n  const rawY = clamp(stick.y + b.my, -1, 1);\n  b.sx = slew(b.sx, rawX, 4 * dt);\n  b.sy = slew(b.sy, rawY, 4 * dt);\n  const scale = (stick.gentle ? 0.4 : 1) * cfg.reach;\n  let tx = b.sx * scale;\n  let ty = b.sy * scale;\n  const len = Math.hypot(tx, ty);\n  if (len > 1) {\n    tx /= len;\n    ty /= len;\n  }\n  const quiet = 1 - cfg.calmEffect * clamp(b.calm, 0, 1);\n  const amp = cfg.noise * stick.noiseScale * quiet;\n  const nx = swayNoise(t, cfg.noiseRate, b.m1, b.m2, b.m3, b.p1, b.p2, b.p3) * amp + stick.disturbX;\n  const ny = swayNoise(t, cfg.noiseRate, b.n1, b.n2, b.n3, b.q1, b.q2, b.q3) * amp + stick.disturbY;\n  const inst = cfg.instability * stick.instabilityScale;\n  const ax = cfg.gain * (tx - b.x) + inst * b.x + nx;\n  const ay = cfg.gain * (ty - b.y) + inst * b.y + ny;\n  b.vx += ax * dt;\n  b.vy += ay * dt;\n  const damp = Math.exp(-cfg.damping * dt);\n  b.vx *= damp;\n  b.vy *= damp;\n  b.x += b.vx * dt;\n  b.y += b.vy * dt;\n  if (Math.hypot(b.x, b.y) > 1) b.over += 1;\n  else b.over = 0;\n  if (b.over >= 6) {\n    b.topples += 1;\n    b.recover = 60;\n    b.over = 0;\n  }\n}\n\n/** True when the centre sits inside a ring of `radius`. */\nexport function inRing(b: Wobble, radius: number): boolean {\n  return Math.hypot(b.x, b.y) <= radius;\n}\n","old_string":""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1433,"output_tokens":10185,"cache_read_input_tokens":203776,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"b5571209-2d5c-4547-bc95-960f5bc140bf"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-198c2a4d-6b41-4389-8d0a-0a8ca16d36c0-143","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file Tunables for the retreat (`game.*`). Every one applies at once (`when: 'now'`) so Dev Mode sliders and\\n * replays change the live balance step. Cut activities have no settings here, so their names do not linger.\\n */\\nimport { defineSettings } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\n\\n/** One slider: the setting path and the range Dev Mode offers. */\\nexport interface Tunable {\\n  path: string;\\n  min: number;\\n  max: number;\\n  step: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** The numeric settings Dev Mode lists, in the order the panel pages through them. */\\nexport const TUNABLES: readonly Tunable[] = [\\n  { path: 'game.wobble.gain', min: 4, max: 30, step: 0.5 },\\n  { path: 'game.wobble.instability', min: 0, max: 10, step: 0.1 },\\n  { path: 'game.wobble.damping', min: 1, max: 12, step: 0.1 },\\n  { path: 'game.wobble.noise', min: 0, max: 8, step: 0.1 },\\n  { path: 'game.wobble.noiseRate', min: 0.05, max: 0.4, step: 0.01 },\\n  { path: 'game.wobble.reach', min: 0.5, max: 1, step: 0.01 },\\n  { path: 'game.breath.period', min: 4, max: 14, step: 0.1 },\\n  { path: 'game.breath.calmEffect', min: 0, max: 1, step: 0.01 },\\n  { path: 'game.age.k', min: 0.5, max: 3, step: 0.05 },\\n  { path: 'game.pose.hold', min: 4, max: 30, step: 0.5 },\\n  { path: 'game.pose.ring', min: 0.08, max: 0.45, step: 0.01 },\\n  { path: 'game.pond.penalty', min: 10, max: 200, step: 5 },\\n  { path: 'game.line.stepKick', min: 0, max: 1, step: 0.01 },\\n  { path: 'game.line.gust', min: 0, max: 1.5, step: 0.05 },\\n  { path: 'game.paddle.speed', min: 1, max: 14, step: 0.1 },\\n  { path: 'game.garden.tilt', min: 2, max: 25, step: 0.5 },\\n  { path: 'game.garden.gravity', min: 1, max: 30, step: 0.5 },\\n  { path: 'game.garden.sink', min: 0.05, max: 4, step: 0.05 },\\n  { path: 'game.tilt.rate', min: 0, max: 2, step: 0.01 },\\n  { path: 'game.pebbles.mult', min: 0.2, max: 3, step: 0.1 },\\n];\\n\\nconst num = (def: number, min: number, max: number, unit: string, description: string) =>\\n  ({ type: 'number' as const, default: def, minimum: min, maximum: max, unit, when: 'now' as const, description });\\n\\n/** Registers every retreat setting. Imported once, from the scenes. */\\nexport const GAME_SETTINGS = defineSettings({\\n  'game.wobble.gain': num(14, 4, 30, '1/s^2', 'How fast weight follows the thumb.'),\\n  'game.wobble.instability': num(3, 0, 10, '1/s^2', 'How hard the body falls away from the centre.'),\\n  'game.wobble.damping': num(5, 1, 12, '1/s', 'How heavy the body feels.'),\\n  'game.wobble.noise': num(3.5, 0, 8, '1/s^2', 'Sway strength.'),\\n  'game.wobble.noiseRate': num(0.15, 0.05, 0.4, 'Hz', 'Sway speed. Kept slow so a late thumb can lean against it.'),\\n  'game.wobble.reach': num(0.9, 0.5, 1, '1', 'Full stick target. A held full stick topples on purpose.'),\\n  'game.breath.period': num(8, 4, 14, 's', 'One breath: half in, half out.'),\\n  'game.breath.calmEffect': num(0.5, 0, 1, '1', 'How much full calm quiets the sway.'),\\n  'game.age.k': num(1.3, 0.5, 3, '1', 'How sharply Wobble Age falls as the morning check improves.'),\\n  'game.pose.hold': num(12, 4, 30, 's', 'How long a pose is held.'),\\n  'game.pose.ring': num(0.2, 0.08, 0.45, '1', 'The seat ring a pose is held inside.'),\\n  'game.pond.penalty': num(80, 10, 200, '1', 'Composure lost when the pond is disturbed.'),\\n  'game.line.stepKick': num(0.35, 0, 1, '1', 'Sideways kick of one step on the line.'),\\n  'game.line.gust': num(0.55, 0, 1.5, '1', 'How hard a gust shoves the line.'),\\n  'game.paddle.speed': num(6, 1, 14, 'm/s', 'Board speed at a full forward lean.'),\\n  'game.garden.tilt': num(12, 2, 25, 'deg', 'How far a full lean tilts a tray.'),\\n  'game.garden.gravity': num(9, 1, 30, 'm/s^2', 'How fast marbles run downhill.'),\\n  'game.garden.sink': num(1.2, 0.05, 4, 'm/s', 'A marble slower than this is caught by a hole.'),\\n  'game.tilt.rate': num(0.15, 0, 2, 'deg/s', 'How fast the storm leans the island before a deed takes some off.'),\\n  'game.pebbles.mult': num(1, 0.2, 3, '1', 'Scales pebbles earned from a rank.'),\\n  'game.mouse.sens': num(0.0025, 0.0004, 0.02, '1/px', 'How far pointer movement leans.'),\\n});\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/settings.ts has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/settings.ts has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/settings.ts\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file Tunables for the retreat (`game.*`). Every one applies at once (`when: 'now'`) so Dev Mode sliders and\\n * replays change the live balance step. Cut activities have no settings here, so their names do not linger.\\n */\\nimport { defineSettings } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\n\\n/** One slider: the setting path and the range Dev Mode offers. */\\nexport interface Tunable {\\n  path: string;\\n  min: number;\\n  max: number;\\n  step: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** The numeric settings Dev Mode lists, in the order the panel pages through them. */\\nexport const TUNABLES: readonly Tunable[] = [\\n  { path: 'game.wobble.gain', min: 4, max: 30, step: 0.5 },\\n  { path: 'game.wobble.instability', min: 0, max: 10, step: 0.1 },\\n  { path: 'game.wobble.damping', min: 1, max: 12, step: 0.1 },\\n  { path: 'game.wobble.noise', min: 0, max: 8, step: 0.1 },\\n  { path: 'game.wobble.noiseRate', min: 0.05, max: 0.4, step: 0.01 },\\n  { path: 'game.wobble.reach', min: 0.5, max: 1, step: 0.01 },\\n  { path: 'game.breath.period', min: 4, max: 14, step: 0.1 },\\n  { path: 'game.breath.calmEffect', min: 0, max: 1, step: 0.01 },\\n  { path: 'game.age.k', min: 0.5, max: 3, step: 0.05 },\\n  { path: 'game.pose.hold', min: 4, max: 30, step: 0.5 },\\n  { path: 'game.pose.ring', min: 0.08, max: 0.45, step: 0.01 },\\n  { path: 'game.pond.penalty', min: 10, max: 200, step: 5 },\\n  { path: 'game.line.stepKick', min: 0, max: 1, step: 0.01 },\\n  { path: 'game.line.gust', min: 0, max: 1.5, step: 0.05 },\\n  { path: 'game.paddle.speed', min: 1, max: 14, step: 0.1 },\\n  { path: 'game.garden.tilt', min: 2, max: 25, step: 0.5 },\\n  { path: 'game.garden.gravity', min: 1, max: 30, step: 0.5 },\\n  { path: 'game.garden.sink', min: 0.05, max: 4, step: 0.05 },\\n  { path: 'game.tilt.rate', min: 0, max: 2, step: 0.01 },\\n  { path: 'game.pebbles.mult', min: 0.2, max: 3, step: 0.1 },\\n];\\n\\nconst num = (def: number, min: number, max: number, unit: string, description: string) =>\\n  ({ type: 'number' as const, default: def, minimum: min, maximum: max, unit, when: 'now' as const, description });\\n\\n/** Registers every retreat setting. Imported once, from the scenes. */\\nexport const GAME_SETTINGS = defineSettings({\\n  'game.wobble.gain': num(14, 4, 30, '1/s^2', 'How fast weight follows the thumb.'),\\n  'game.wobble.instability': num(3, 0, 10, '1/s^2', 'How hard the body falls away from the centre.'),\\n  'game.wobble.damping': num(5, 1, 12, '1/s', 'How heavy the body feels.'),\\n  'game.wobble.noise': num(3.5, 0, 8, '1/s^2', 'Sway strength.'),\\n  'game.wobble.noiseRate': num(0.15, 0.05, 0.4, 'Hz', 'Sway speed. Kept slow so a late thumb can lean against it.'),\\n  'game.wobble.reach': num(0.9, 0.5, 1, '1', 'Full stick target. A held full stick topples on purpose.'),\\n  'game.breath.period': num(8, 4, 14, 's', 'One breath: half in, half out.'),\\n  'game.breath.calmEffect': num(0.5, 0, 1, '1', 'How much full calm quiets the sway.'),\\n  'game.age.k': num(1.3, 0.5, 3, '1', 'How sharply Wobble Age falls as the morning check improves.'),\\n  'game.pose.hold': num(12, 4, 30, 's', 'How long a pose is held.'),\\n  'game.pose.ring': num(0.2, 0.08, 0.45, '1', 'The seat ring a pose is held inside.'),\\n  'game.pond.penalty': num(80, 10, 200, '1', 'Composure lost when the pond is disturbed.'),\\n  'game.line.stepKick': num(0.35, 0, 1, '1', 'Sideways kick of one step on the line.'),\\n  'game.line.gust': num(0.55, 0, 1.5, '1', 'How hard a gust shoves the line.'),\\n  'game.paddle.speed': num(6, 1, 14, 'm/s', 'Board speed at a full forward lean.'),\\n  'game.garden.tilt': num(12, 2, 25, 'deg', 'How far a full lean tilts a tray.'),\\n  'game.garden.gravity': num(9, 1, 30, 'm/s^2', 'How fast marbles run downhill.'),\\n  'game.garden.sink': num(1.2, 0.05, 4, 'm/s', 'A marble slower than this is caught by a hole.'),\\n  'game.tilt.rate': num(0.15, 0, 2, 'deg/s', 'How fast the storm leans the island before a deed takes some off.'),\\n  'game.pebbles.mult': num(1, 0.2, 3, '1', 'Scales pebbles earned from a rank.'),\\n  'game.mouse.sens': num(0.0025, 0.0004, 0.02, '1/px', 'How far pointer movement leans.'),\\n});\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-198c2a4d-6b41-4389-8d0a-0a8ca16d36c0-144","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file The one verb. Centre of balance is a point in the unit disc. Each step slews the stick, then\\n * accelerates toward it with instability, slow sway and breath. Past the rim for six steps the body topples,\\n * stumbles, and recentres. It is never a game over.\\n */\\nimport { defineComponent, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\n\\n/** Numbers the balance step reads. Sliders change them between steps. */\\nexport interface BalanceCfg {\\n  gain: number;\\n  instability: number;\\n  damping: number;\\n  noise: number;\\n  noiseRate: number;\\n  reach: number;\\n  calmEffect: number;\\n  period: number;\\n  sens: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** What the thumb, the feet and the activity are doing this step. */\\nexport interface Stick {\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  gentle: boolean;\\n  both: boolean;\\n  mdx: number;\\n  mdy: number;\\n  disturbX: number;\\n  disturbY: number;\\n  noiseScale: number;\\n  instabilityScale: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** The centre of balance and the sway drawn once for the seat. */\\nexport interface Wobble {\\n  seat: number;\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  vx: number;\\n  vy: number;\\n  sx: number;\\n  sy: number;\\n  mx: number;\\n  my: number;\\n  calm: number;\\n  lungs: number;\\n  sync: number;\\n  over: number;\\n  recover: number;\\n  topples: number;\\n  guide: number;\\n  m1: number;\\n  m2: number;\\n  m3: number;\\n  p1: number;\\n  p2: number;\\n  p3: number;\\n  n1: number;\\n  n2: number;\\n  n3: number;\\n  q1: number;\\n  q2: number;\\n  q3: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** A ring buffer of recent centres, so a late thumb sees an old one. */\\nexport interface Hist {\\n  i: number;\\n  n: number;\\n  xs: number[];\\n  ys: number[];\\n}\\n\\nconst field = (description: string, unit = '1') =>\\n  ({ type: 'number' as const, default: 0, unit, description });\\n\\n/** The component `wobble`: one balancing body. */\\nexport const WOBBLE = defineComponent('wobble', {\\n  description: 'A seat’s centre of balance, its breath and the sway drawn for it.',\\n  fields: {\\n    seat: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Which mat this body stands on.' },\\n    x: field('Centre of balance, left to right. Past 1 is the rim.'),\\n    y: field('Centre of balance, back to forward.'),\\n    vx: field('Velocity along x.', '1/s'),\\n    vy: field('Velocity along y.', '1/s'),\\n    sx: field('The stick after the slew, left to right.'),\\n    sy: field('The stick after the slew, back to forward.'),\\n    mx: field('Mouse lean, decaying.'),\\n    my: field('Mouse lean, decaying.'),\\n    calm: field('How settled the breath is, 0 to 1.'),\\n    lungs: field('How full the breath is, 0 to 1.'),\\n    sync: field('How well the breath matches the guide, 0 to 1.'),\\n    over: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Steps in a row spent outside the disc.' },\\n    recover: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Steps left in a topple’s recentre.' },\\n    topples: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Topples since the count was cleared.' },\\n    guide: field('The breath guide, 0 empty to 1 full.'),\\n    m1: field('Sway rate ratio, x, first voice.'),\\n    m2: field('Sway rate ratio, x, second voice.'),\\n    m3: field('Sway rate ratio, x, third voice.'),\\n    p1: field('Sway phase, x, first voice.', 'rad'),\\n    p2: field('Sway phase, x, second voice.', 'rad'),\\n    p3: field('Sway phase, x, third voice.', 'rad'),\\n    n1: field('Sway rate ratio, y, first voice.'),\\n    n2: field('Sway rate ratio, y, second voice.'),\\n    n3: field('Sway rate ratio, y, third voice.'),\\n    q1: field('Sway phase, y, first voice.', 'rad'),\\n    q2: field('Sway phase, y, second voice.', 'rad'),\\n    q3: field('Sway phase, y, third voice.', 'rad'),\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** The component `hist`: the centres a delayed thumb can still see. */\\nexport const HIST = defineComponent('hist', {\\n  description: 'Recent centres of balance for one seat, oldest first in the ring.',\\n  fields: {\\n    i: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Where the next sample is written once the ring is full.' },\\n    n: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'How many samples have been kept.' },\\n    xs: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Recent centres, left to right.' },\\n    ys: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Recent centres, back to forward.' },\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** A number kept between lo and hi. */\\nexport function clamp(n: number, lo: number, hi: number): number {\\n  return Math.max(lo, Math.min(hi, n));\\n}\\n\\n/** Moves `current` toward `target` by at most `maxDelta`. */\\nexport function slew(current: number, target: number, maxDelta: number): number {\\n  const d = target - current;\\n  if (Math.abs(d) <= maxDelta) return target;\\n  return current + Math.sign(d) * maxDelta;\\n}\\n\\n/** The slow sway on one axis. Phases come from the seat, never from Math.random. */\\nexport function swayNoise(t: number, rate: number, m1: number, m2: number, m3: number, p1: number, p2: number, p3: number): number {\\n  const a = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * m1 * t + p1);\\n  const b = 0.6 * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * 1.7 * m2 * t + p2);\\n  const c = 0.3 * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * 3.1 * m3 * t + p3);\\n  return (a + b + c) / 1.3;\\n}\\n\\n/** Draws the six ratios and phases for a seat from the stream `sway`. */\\nexport function drawSway(w: World): void {\\n  const rng = w.rng('sway');\\n  const ratio = () => rng.range(0.8, 1.25);\\n  const phase = () => rng.range(0, Math.PI * 2);\\n  const body = w.spawn({\\n    wobble: {\\n      m1: ratio(), m2: ratio(), m3: ratio(), p1: phase(), p2: phase(), p3: phase(),\\n      n1: ratio(), n2: ratio(), n3: ratio(), q1: phase(), q2: phase(), q3: phase(),\\n    },\\n    hist: { xs: [], ys: [] },\\n  });\\n  void body;\\n}\\n\\n/** Clears the motion and the breath, and keeps the sway. A new activity starts here. */\\nexport function resetBalance(b: Wobble, hist: Hist): void {\\n  b.x = 0; b.y = 0; b.vx = 0; b.vy = 0; b.sx = 0; b.sy = 0; b.mx = 0; b.my = 0;\\n  b.calm = 0; b.lungs = 0; b.sync = 0; b.over = 0; b.recover = 0; b.topples = 0; b.guide = 0;\\n  hist.i = 0; hist.n = 0; hist.xs.length = 0; hist.ys.length = 0;\\n}\\n\\n/** Remembers a centre. The ring holds 24, which covers the sloppy thumb’s delay. */\\nexport function remember(hist: Hist, x: number, y: number): void {\\n  const cap = 24;\\n  if (hist.xs.length < cap) {\\n    hist.xs.push(x);\\n    hist.ys.push(y);\\n  } else {\\n    hist.xs[hist.i] = x;\\n    hist.ys[hist.i] = y;\\n    hist.i = (hist.i + 1) % cap;\\n  }\\n  hist.n += 1;\\n}\\n\\n/** The centre `delay` steps ago, or the oldest one we have. */\\nexport function recall(hist: Hist, delay: number): { x: number; y: number } {\\n  const len = hist.xs.length;\\n  if (len === 0) return { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n  const age = Math.min(Math.max(0, delay), len - 1);\\n  const newest = len < 24 ? len - 1 : (hist.i + 24 - 1) % 24;\\n  const at = (newest - age + len) % len;\\n  return { x: hist.xs[at] ?? 0, y: hist.ys[at] ?? 0 };\\n}\\n\\n/** One balance step. `t` and `dt` are sim time. A topple recentres over one second and counts once. */\\nexport function stepBalance(b: Wobble, stick: Stick, cfg: BalanceCfg, t: number, dt: number): void {\\n  const period = Math.max(0.25, cfg.period);\\n  const phase = (t % period) / period;\\n  const rising = phase < 0.5;\\n  b.guide = rising ? phase * 2 : (1 - phase) * 2;\\n  const fill = dt / (period * 0.5);\\n  if (stick.both) b.lungs = Math.min(1, b.lungs + fill);\\n  else b.lungs = Math.max(0, b.lungs - fill);\\n  const instant = 1 - Math.abs(b.lungs - b.guide);\\n  const participating = stick.both || b.lungs > 0.04;\\n  const toward = participating ? instant : 0;\\n  const blend = Math.min(1, dt / (participating ? 0.6 : 2));\\n  b.sync += (toward - b.sync) * blend;\\n  b.calm += (b.sync - b.calm) * Math.min(1, dt / 1.2);\\n\\n  if (b.recover > 0) {\\n    const left = b.recover;\\n    b.x *= (left - 1) / left;\\n    b.y *= (left - 1) / left;\\n    b.vx = 0;\\n    b.vy = 0;\\n    b.recover -= 1;\\n    b.over = 0;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n\\n  const decay = Math.exp(-dt / 0.6);\\n  b.mx = (b.mx + stick.mdx) * decay;\\n  b.my = (b.my + stick.mdy) * decay;\\n  const rawX = clamp(stick.x + b.mx, -1, 1);\\n  const rawY = clamp(stick.y + b.my, -1, 1);\\n  b.sx = slew(b.sx, rawX, 4 * dt);\\n  b.sy = slew(b.sy, rawY, 4 * dt);\\n  const scale = (stick.gentle ? 0.4 : 1) * cfg.reach;\\n  let tx = b.sx * scale;\\n  let ty = b.sy * scale;\\n  const len = Math.hypot(tx, ty);\\n  if (len > 1) {\\n    tx /= len;\\n    ty /= len;\\n  }\\n  const quiet = 1 - cfg.calmEffect * clamp(b.calm, 0, 1);\\n  const amp = cfg.noise * stick.noiseScale * quiet;\\n  const nx = swayNoise(t, cfg.noiseRate, b.m1, b.m2, b.m3, b.p1, b.p2, b.p3) * amp + stick.disturbX;\\n  const ny = swayNoise(t, cfg.noiseRate, b.n1, b.n2, b.n3, b.q1, b.q2, b.q3) * amp + stick.disturbY;\\n  const inst = cfg.instability * stick.instabilityScale;\\n  const ax = cfg.gain * (tx - b.x) + inst * b.x + nx;\\n  const ay = cfg.gain * (ty - b.y) + inst * b.y + ny;\\n  b.vx += ax * dt;\\n  b.vy += ay * dt;\\n  const damp = Math.exp(-cfg.damping * dt);\\n  b.vx *= damp;\\n  b.vy *= damp;\\n  b.x += b.vx * dt;\\n  b.y += b.vy * dt;\\n  if (Math.hypot(b.x, b.y) > 1) b.over += 1;\\n  else b.over = 0;\\n  if (b.over >= 6) {\\n    b.topples += 1;\\n    b.recover = 60;\\n    b.over = 0;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** True when the centre sits inside a ring of `radius`. */\\nexport function inRing(b: Wobble, radius: number): boolean {\\n  return Math.hypot(b.x, b.y) <= radius;\\n}\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/wobble.ts has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/wobble.ts has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/wobble.ts\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file The one verb. Centre of balance is a point in the unit disc. Each step slews the stick, then\\n * accelerates toward it with instability, slow sway and breath. Past the rim for six steps the body topples,\\n * stumbles, and recentres. It is never a game over.\\n */\\nimport { defineComponent, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\n\\n/** Numbers the balance step reads. Sliders change them between steps. */\\nexport interface BalanceCfg {\\n  gain: number;\\n  instability: number;\\n  damping: number;\\n  noise: number;\\n  noiseRate: number;\\n  reach: number;\\n  calmEffect: number;\\n  period: number;\\n  sens: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** What the thumb, the feet and the activity are doing this step. */\\nexport interface Stick {\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  gentle: boolean;\\n  both: boolean;\\n  mdx: number;\\n  mdy: number;\\n  disturbX: number;\\n  disturbY: number;\\n  noiseScale: number;\\n  instabilityScale: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** The centre of balance and the sway drawn once for the seat. */\\nexport interface Wobble {\\n  seat: number;\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  vx: number;\\n  vy: number;\\n  sx: number;\\n  sy: number;\\n  mx: number;\\n  my: number;\\n  calm: number;\\n  lungs: number;\\n  sync: number;\\n  over: number;\\n  recover: number;\\n  topples: number;\\n  guide: number;\\n  m1: number;\\n  m2: number;\\n  m3: number;\\n  p1: number;\\n  p2: number;\\n  p3: number;\\n  n1: number;\\n  n2: number;\\n  n3: number;\\n  q1: number;\\n  q2: number;\\n  q3: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** A ring buffer of recent centres, so a late thumb sees an old one. */\\nexport interface Hist {\\n  i: number;\\n  n: number;\\n  xs: number[];\\n  ys: number[];\\n}\\n\\nconst field = (description: string, unit = '1') =>\\n  ({ type: 'number' as const, default: 0, unit, description });\\n\\n/** The component `wobble`: one balancing body. */\\nexport const WOBBLE = defineComponent('wobble', {\\n  description: 'A seat’s centre of balance, its breath and the sway drawn for it.',\\n  fields: {\\n    seat: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Which mat this body stands on.' },\\n    x: field('Centre of balance, left to right. Past 1 is the rim.'),\\n    y: field('Centre of balance, back to forward.'),\\n    vx: field('Velocity along x.', '1/s'),\\n    vy: field('Velocity along y.', '1/s'),\\n    sx: field('The stick after the slew, left to right.'),\\n    sy: field('The stick after the slew, back to forward.'),\\n    mx: field('Mouse lean, decaying.'),\\n    my: field('Mouse lean, decaying.'),\\n    calm: field('How settled the breath is, 0 to 1.'),\\n    lungs: field('How full the breath is, 0 to 1.'),\\n    sync: field('How well the breath matches the guide, 0 to 1.'),\\n    over: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Steps in a row spent outside the disc.' },\\n    recover: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Steps left in a topple’s recentre.' },\\n    topples: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Topples since the count was cleared.' },\\n    guide: field('The breath guide, 0 empty to 1 full.'),\\n    m1: field('Sway rate ratio, x, first voice.'),\\n    m2: field('Sway rate ratio, x, second voice.'),\\n    m3: field('Sway rate ratio, x, third voice.'),\\n    p1: field('Sway phase, x, first voice.', 'rad'),\\n    p2: field('Sway phase, x, second voice.', 'rad'),\\n    p3: field('Sway phase, x, third voice.', 'rad'),\\n    n1: field('Sway rate ratio, y, first voice.'),\\n    n2: field('Sway rate ratio, y, second voice.'),\\n    n3: field('Sway rate ratio, y, third voice.'),\\n    q1: field('Sway phase, y, first voice.', 'rad'),\\n    q2: field('Sway phase, y, second voice.', 'rad'),\\n    q3: field('Sway phase, y, third voice.', 'rad'),\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** The component `hist`: the centres a delayed thumb can still see. */\\nexport const HIST = defineComponent('hist', {\\n  description: 'Recent centres of balance for one seat, oldest first in the ring.',\\n  fields: {\\n    i: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Where the next sample is written once the ring is full.' },\\n    n: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'How many samples have been kept.' },\\n    xs: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Recent centres, left to right.' },\\n    ys: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Recent centres, back to forward.' },\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** A number kept between lo and hi. */\\nexport function clamp(n: number, lo: number, hi: number): number {\\n  return Math.max(lo, Math.min(hi, n));\\n}\\n\\n/** Moves `current` toward `target` by at most `maxDelta`. */\\nexport function slew(current: number, target: number, maxDelta: number): number {\\n  const d = target - current;\\n  if (Math.abs(d) <= maxDelta) return target;\\n  return current + Math.sign(d) * maxDelta;\\n}\\n\\n/** The slow sway on one axis. Phases come from the seat, never from Math.random. */\\nexport function swayNoise(t: number, rate: number, m1: number, m2: number, m3: number, p1: number, p2: number, p3: number): number {\\n  const a = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * m1 * t + p1);\\n  const b = 0.6 * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * 1.7 * m2 * t + p2);\\n  const c = 0.3 * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * 3.1 * m3 * t + p3);\\n  return (a + b + c) / 1.3;\\n}\\n\\n/** Draws the six ratios and phases for a seat from the stream `sway`. */\\nexport function drawSway(w: World): void {\\n  const rng = w.rng('sway');\\n  const ratio = () => rng.range(0.8, 1.25);\\n  const phase = () => rng.range(0, Math.PI * 2);\\n  const body = w.spawn({\\n    wobble: {\\n      m1: ratio(), m2: ratio(), m3: ratio(), p1: phase(), p2: phase(), p3: phase(),\\n      n1: ratio(), n2: ratio(), n3: ratio(), q1: phase(), q2: phase(), q3: phase(),\\n    },\\n    hist: { xs: [], ys: [] },\\n  });\\n  void body;\\n}\\n\\n/** Clears the motion and the breath, and keeps the sway. A new activity starts here. */\\nexport function resetBalance(b: Wobble, hist: Hist): void {\\n  b.x = 0; b.y = 0; b.vx = 0; b.vy = 0; b.sx = 0; b.sy = 0; b.mx = 0; b.my = 0;\\n  b.calm = 0; b.lungs = 0; b.sync = 0; b.over = 0; b.recover = 0; b.topples = 0; b.guide = 0;\\n  hist.i = 0; hist.n = 0; hist.xs.length = 0; hist.ys.length = 0;\\n}\\n\\n/** Remembers a centre. The ring holds 24, which covers the sloppy thumb’s delay. */\\nexport function remember(hist: Hist, x: number, y: number): void {\\n  const cap = 24;\\n  if (hist.xs.length < cap) {\\n    hist.xs.push(x);\\n    hist.ys.push(y);\\n  } else {\\n    hist.xs[hist.i] = x;\\n    hist.ys[hist.i] = y;\\n    hist.i = (hist.i + 1) % cap;\\n  }\\n  hist.n += 1;\\n}\\n\\n/** The centre `delay` steps ago, or the oldest one we have. */\\nexport function recall(hist: Hist, delay: number): { x: number; y: number } {\\n  const len = hist.xs.length;\\n  if (len === 0) return { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n  const age = Math.min(Math.max(0, delay), len - 1);\\n  const newest = len < 24 ? len - 1 : (hist.i + 24 - 1) % 24;\\n  const at = (newest - age + len) % len;\\n  return { x: hist.xs[at] ?? 0, y: hist.ys[at] ?? 0 };\\n}\\n\\n/** One balance step. `t` and `dt` are sim time. A topple recentres over one second and counts once. */\\nexport function stepBalance(b: Wobble, stick: Stick, cfg: BalanceCfg, t: number, dt: number): void {\\n  const period = Math.max(0.25, cfg.period);\\n  const phase = (t % period) / period;\\n  const rising = phase < 0.5;\\n  b.guide = rising ? phase * 2 : (1 - phase) * 2;\\n  const fill = dt / (period * 0.5);\\n  if (stick.both) b.lungs = Math.min(1, b.lungs + fill);\\n  else b.lungs = Math.max(0, b.lungs - fill);\\n  const instant = 1 - Math.abs(b.lungs - b.guide);\\n  const participating = stick.both || b.lungs > 0.04;\\n  const toward = participating ? instant : 0;\\n  const blend = Math.min(1, dt / (participating ? 0.6 : 2));\\n  b.sync += (toward - b.sync) * blend;\\n  b.calm += (b.sync - b.calm) * Math.min(1, dt / 1.2);\\n\\n  if (b.recover > 0) {\\n    const left = b.recover;\\n    b.x *= (left - 1) / left;\\n    b.y *= (left - 1) / left;\\n    b.vx = 0;\\n    b.vy = 0;\\n    b.recover -= 1;\\n    b.over = 0;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n\\n  const decay = Math.exp(-dt / 0.6);\\n  b.mx = (b.mx + stick.mdx) * decay;\\n  b.my = (b.my + stick.mdy) * decay;\\n  const rawX = clamp(stick.x + b.mx, -1, 1);\\n  const rawY = clamp(stick.y + b.my, -1, 1);\\n  b.sx = slew(b.sx, rawX, 4 * dt);\\n  b.sy = slew(b.sy, rawY, 4 * dt);\\n  const scale = (stick.gentle ? 0.4 : 1) * cfg.reach;\\n  let tx = b.sx * scale;\\n  let ty = b.sy * scale;\\n  const len = Math.hypot(tx, ty);\\n  if (len > 1) {\\n    tx /= len;\\n    ty /= len;\\n  }\\n  const quiet = 1 - cfg.calmEffect * clamp(b.calm, 0, 1);\\n  const amp = cfg.noise * stick.noiseScale * quiet;\\n  const nx = swayNoise(t, cfg.noiseRate, b.m1, b.m2, b.m3, b.p1, b.p2, b.p3) * amp + stick.disturbX;\\n  const ny = swayNoise(t, cfg.noiseRate, b.n1, b.n2, b.n3, b.q1, b.q2, b.q3) * amp + stick.disturbY;\\n  const inst = cfg.instability * stick.instabilityScale;\\n  const ax = cfg.gain * (tx - b.x) + inst * b.x + nx;\\n  const ay = cfg.gain * (ty - b.y) + inst * b.y + ny;\\n  b.vx += ax * dt;\\n  b.vy += ay * dt;\\n  const damp = Math.exp(-cfg.damping * dt);\\n  b.vx *= damp;\\n  b.vy *= damp;\\n  b.x += b.vx * dt;\\n  b.y += b.vy * dt;\\n  if (Math.hypot(b.x, b.y) > 1) b.over += 1;\\n  else b.over = 0;\\n  if (b.over >= 6) {\\n    b.topples += 1;\\n    b.recover = 60;\\n    b.over = 0;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** True when the centre sits inside a ring of `radius`. */\\nexport function inRing(b: Wobble, radius: number): boolean {\\n  return Math.hypot(b.x, b.y) <= radius;\\n}\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"708402be-5fa2-4ac4-b233-98a23233a685"}
