{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fd732a93-a17b-46c1-b54c-df2b43ea273c-0","content":"{\"type\":\"Todo\",\"TodosUpdated\":{\"summary_for_prompt\":\"- [in_progress] ac1: ac1: Hand-in, title, and records (PROGRESS, exit-interview, HTML, RNG title)\\n- [pending] ac2: ac2: One balance verb, every shipped activity with score bands and bots\\n- [pending] ac3: ac3: Five-day retreat: island, cast, saves, 200+ lines, code audio\\n- [pending] ac4: ac4: 10-foot shell: pad/keyboard/mouse, pause, attract, touch, WebGPU fallback\\n- [pending] ac5: ac5: Couch Group Class and AI Hub ghost sessions with harness\\n- [pending] verify: verify: Run verification plan and save proof under scratch\\n\",\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"ac1: Hand-in, title, and records (PROGRESS, exit-interview, HTML, RNG title)\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},{\"content\":\"ac2: One balance verb, every shipped activity with score bands and bots\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"ac3: Five-day retreat: island, cast, saves, 200+ lines, code audio\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"ac4: 10-foot shell: pad/keyboard/mouse, pause, attract, touch, WebGPU fallback\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"ac5: Couch Group Class and AI Hub ghost sessions with harness\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"verify: Run verification plan and save proof under scratch\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"}],\"state\":{\"todos\":{\"ac1\":{\"content\":\"ac1: Hand-in, title, and records (PROGRESS, exit-interview, HTML, RNG title)\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},\"ac2\":{\"content\":\"ac2: One balance verb, every shipped activity with score bands and bots\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},\"ac3\":{\"content\":\"ac3: Five-day retreat: island, cast, saves, 200+ lines, code audio\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},\"ac4\":{\"content\":\"ac4: 10-foot shell: pad/keyboard/mouse, pause, attract, touch, WebGPU fallback\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},\"ac5\":{\"content\":\"ac5: Couch Group Class and AI Hub ghost sessions with harness\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},\"verify\":{\"content\":\"verify: Run verification plan and save proof under scratch\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"}}}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fd732a93-a17b-46c1-b54c-df2b43ea273c-1","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The one verb. Centre of balance is a point in the unit disc. Each step slews the stick, then\\n * accelerates toward it with instability, slow sway and breath. Past the rim for six steps the body topples,\\n * stumbles, and recentres. It is never a game over.\\n */\\nimport { defineComponent, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\n\\n/** Numbers the balance step reads. Sliders change them between steps. */\\nexport interface BalanceCfg {\\n10→  gain: number;\\n  instability: number;\\n  damping: number;\\n  noise: number;\\n  noiseRate: number;\\n  reach: number;\\n  calmEffect: number;\\n  period: number;\\n  sens: number;\\n}\\n20→\\n/** What the thumb, the feet and the activity are doing this step. */\\nexport interface Stick {\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  gentle: boolean;\\n  both: boolean;\\n  mdx: number;\\n  mdy: number;\\n  disturbX: number;\\n30→  disturbY: number;\\n  noiseScale: number;\\n  instabilityScale: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** The centre of balance and the sway drawn once for the seat. */\\nexport interface Wobble {\\n  seat: number;\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n40→  vx: number;\\n  vy: number;\\n  sx: number;\\n  sy: number;\\n  mx: number;\\n  my: number;\\n  calm: number;\\n  lungs: number;\\n  sync: number;\\n  over: number;\\n50→  recover: number;\\n  topples: number;\\n  guide: number;\\n  m1: number;\\n  m2: number;\\n  m3: number;\\n  p1: number;\\n  p2: number;\\n  p3: number;\\n  n1: number;\\n60→  n2: number;\\n  n3: number;\\n  q1: number;\\n  q2: number;\\n  q3: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** A ring buffer of recent centres, so a late thumb sees an old one. */\\nexport interface Hist {\\n  i: number;\\n70→  n: number;\\n  xs: number[];\\n  ys: number[];\\n}\\n\\nconst field = (description: string, unit = '1') =>\\n  ({ type: 'number' as const, default: 0, unit, description });\\n\\n/** The component `wobble`: one balancing body. */\\nexport const WOBBLE = defineComponent('wobble', {\\n80→  description: 'A seat’s centre of balance, its breath and the sway drawn for it.',\\n  fields: {\\n    seat: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Which mat this body stands on.' },\\n    x: field('Centre of balance, left to right. Past 1 is the rim.'),\\n    y: field('Centre of balance, back to forward.'),\\n    vx: field('Velocity along x.', '1/s'),\\n    vy: field('Velocity along y.', '1/s'),\\n    sx: field('The stick after the slew, left to right.'),\\n    sy: field('The stick after the slew, back to forward.'),\\n    mx: field('Mouse lean, decaying.'),\\n90→    my: field('Mouse lean, decaying.'),\\n    calm: field('How settled the breath is, 0 to 1.'),\\n    lungs: field('How full the breath is, 0 to 1.'),\\n    sync: field('How well the breath matches the guide, 0 to 1.'),\\n    over: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Steps in a row spent outside the disc.' },\\n    recover: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Steps left in a topple’s recentre.' },\\n    topples: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Topples since the count was cleared.' },\\n    guide: field('The breath guide, 0 empty to 1 full.'),\\n    m1: field('Sway rate ratio, x, first voice.'),\\n    m2: field('Sway rate ratio, x, second voice.'),\\n100→    m3: field('Sway rate ratio, x, third voice.'),\\n    p1: field('Sway phase, x, first voice.', 'rad'),\\n    p2: field('Sway phase, x, second voice.', 'rad'),\\n    p3: field('Sway phase, x, third voice.', 'rad'),\\n    n1: field('Sway rate ratio, y, first voice.'),\\n    n2: field('Sway rate ratio, y, second voice.'),\\n    n3: field('Sway rate ratio, y, third voice.'),\\n    q1: field('Sway phase, y, first voice.', 'rad'),\\n    q2: field('Sway phase, y, second voice.', 'rad'),\\n    q3: field('Sway phase, y, third voice.', 'rad'),\\n110→  },\\n});\\n\\n/** The component `hist`: the centres a delayed thumb can still see. */\\nexport const HIST = defineComponent('hist', {\\n  description: 'Recent centres of balance for one seat, oldest first in the ring.',\\n  fields: {\\n    i: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Where the next sample is written once the ring is full.' },\\n    n: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'How many samples have been kept.' },\\n    xs: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Recent centres, left to right.' },\\n120→    ys: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Recent centres, back to forward.' },\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** A number kept between lo and hi. */\\nexport function clamp(n: number, lo: number, hi: number): number {\\n  return Math.max(lo, Math.min(hi, n));\\n}\\n\\n/** Moves `current` toward `target` by at most `maxDelta`. */\\n130→export function slew(current: number, target: number, maxDelta: number): number {\\n  const d = target - current;\\n  if (Math.abs(d) <= maxDelta) return target;\\n  return current + Math.sign(d) * maxDelta;\\n}\\n\\n/** The slow sway on one axis. Phases come from the seat, never from Math.random. */\\nexport function swayNoise(t: number, rate: number, m1: number, m2: number, m3: number, p1: number, p2: number, p3: number): number {\\n  const a = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * m1 * t + p1);\\n  const b = 0.6 * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * 1.7 * m2 * t + p2);\\n140→  const c = 0.3 * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * 3.1 * m3 * t + p3);\\n  return (a + b + c) / 1.3;\\n}\\n\\n/** Draws the six ratios and phases for a seat from the stream `sway`. */\\nexport function drawSway(w: World): void {\\n  const rng = w.rng('sway');\\n  const ratio = () => rng.range(0.8, 1.25);\\n  const phase = () => rng.range(0, Math.PI * 2);\\n  const body = w.spawn({\\n150→    wobble: {\\n      m1: ratio(), m2: ratio(), m3: ratio(), p1: phase(), p2: phase(), p3: phase(),\\n      n1: ratio(), n2: ratio(), n3: ratio(), q1: phase(), q2: phase(), q3: phase(),\\n    },\\n    hist: { xs: [], ys: [] },\\n  });\\n  void body;\\n}\\n\\n/** Clears the motion and the breath, and keeps the sway. A new activity starts here. */\\n160→export function resetBalance(b: Wobble, hist: Hist): void {\\n  b.x = 0; b.y = 0; b.vx = 0; b.vy = 0; b.sx = 0; b.sy = 0; b.mx = 0; b.my = 0;\\n  b.calm = 0; b.lungs = 0; b.sync = 0; b.over = 0; b.recover = 0; b.topples = 0; b.guide = 0;\\n  hist.i = 0; hist.n = 0; hist.xs.length = 0; hist.ys.length = 0;\\n}\\n\\n/** Remembers a centre. The ring holds 24, which covers the sloppy thumb’s delay. */\\nexport function remember(hist: Hist, x: number, y: number): void {\\n  const cap = 24;\\n  if (hist.xs.length < cap) {\\n170→    hist.xs.push(x);\\n    hist.ys.push(y);\\n  } else {\\n    hist.xs[hist.i] = x;\\n    hist.ys[hist.i] = y;\\n    hist.i = (hist.i + 1) % cap;\\n  }\\n  hist.n += 1;\\n}\\n\\n180→/** The centre `delay` steps ago, or the oldest one we have. */\\nexport function recall(hist: Hist, delay: number): { x: number; y: number } {\\n  const len = hist.xs.length;\\n  if (len === 0) return { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n  const age = Math.min(Math.max(0, delay), len - 1);\\n  const newest = len < 24 ? len - 1 : (hist.i + 24 - 1) % 24;\\n  const at = (newest - age + len) % len;\\n  return { x: hist.xs[at] ?? 0, y: hist.ys[at] ?? 0 };\\n}\\n\\n190→/** One balance step. `t` and `dt` are sim time. A topple recentres over one second and counts once. */\\nexport function stepBalance(b: Wobble, stick: Stick, cfg: BalanceCfg, t: number, dt: number): void {\\n  const period = Math.max(0.25, cfg.period);\\n  const phase = (t % period) / period;\\n  const rising = phase < 0.5;\\n  b.guide = rising ? phase * 2 : (1 - phase) * 2;\\n  const fill = dt / (period * 0.5);\\n  if (stick.both) b.lungs = Math.min(1, b.lungs + fill);\\n  else b.lungs = Math.max(0, b.lungs - fill);\\n  const instant = 1 - Math.abs(b.lungs - b.guide);\\n200→  const participating = stick.both || b.lungs > 0.04;\\n  const toward = participating ? instant : 0;\\n  const blend = Math.min(1, dt / (participating ? 0.6 : 2));\\n  b.sync += (toward - b.sync) * blend;\\n  b.calm += (b.sync - b.calm) * Math.min(1, dt / 1.2);\\n\\n  if (b.recover > 0) {\\n    const left = b.recover;\\n    b.x *= (left - 1) / left;\\n    b.y *= (left - 1) / left;\\n210→    b.vx = 0;\\n    b.vy = 0;\\n    b.recover -= 1;\\n    b.over = 0;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n\\n  const decay = Math.exp(-dt / 0.6);\\n  b.mx = (b.mx + stick.mdx) * decay;\\n  b.my = (b.my + stick.mdy) * decay;\\n220→  const rawX = clamp(stick.x + b.mx, -1, 1);\\n  const rawY = clamp(stick.y + b.my, -1, 1);\\n  b.sx = slew(b.sx, rawX, 4 * dt);\\n  b.sy = slew(b.sy, rawY, 4 * dt);\\n  const scale = (stick.gentle ? 0.4 : 1) * cfg.reach;\\n  let tx = b.sx * scale;\\n  let ty = b.sy * scale;\\n  const len = Math.hypot(tx, ty);\\n  if (len > 1) {\\n    tx /= len;\\n230→    ty /= len;\\n  }\\n  const quiet = 1 - cfg.calmEffect * clamp(b.calm, 0, 1);\\n  const amp = cfg.noise * stick.noiseScale * quiet;\\n  const nx = swayNoise(t, cfg.noiseRate, b.m1, b.m2, b.m3, b.p1, b.p2, b.p3) * amp + stick.disturbX;\\n  const ny = swayNoise(t, cfg.noiseRate, b.n1, b.n2, b.n3, b.q1, b.q2, b.q3) * amp + stick.disturbY;\\n  const inst = cfg.instability * stick.instabilityScale;\\n  const ax = cfg.gain * (tx - b.x) + inst * b.x + nx;\\n  const ay = cfg.gain * (ty - b.y) + inst * b.y + ny;\\n  b.vx += ax * dt;\\n240→  b.vy += ay * dt;\\n  const damp = Math.exp(-cfg.damping * dt);\\n  b.vx *= damp;\\n  b.vy *= damp;\\n  b.x += b.vx * dt;\\n  b.y += b.vy * dt;\\n  if (Math.hypot(b.x, b.y) > 1) b.over += 1;\\n  else b.over = 0;\\n  if (b.over >= 6) {\\n    b.topples += 1;\\n250→    b.recover = 60;\\n    b.over = 0;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** True when the centre sits inside a ring of `radius`. */\\nexport function inRing(b: Wobble, radius: number): boolean {\\n  return Math.hypot(b.x, b.y) <= radius;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The one verb. Centre of balance is a point in the unit disc. Each step slews the stick, then\\n * accelerates toward it with instability, slow sway and breath. Past the rim for six steps the body topples,\\n * stumbles, and recentres. It is never a game over.\\n */\\nimport { defineComponent, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\n\\n/** Numbers the balance step reads. Sliders change them between steps. */\\nexport interface BalanceCfg {\\n10→  gain: number;\\n  instability: number;\\n  damping: number;\\n  noise: number;\\n  noiseRate: number;\\n  reach: number;\\n  calmEffect: number;\\n  period: number;\\n  sens: number;\\n}\\n20→\\n/** What the thumb, the feet and the activity are doing this step. */\\nexport interface Stick {\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  gentle: boolean;\\n  both: boolean;\\n  mdx: number;\\n  mdy: number;\\n  disturbX: number;\\n30→  disturbY: number;\\n  noiseScale: number;\\n  instabilityScale: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** The centre of balance and the sway drawn once for the seat. */\\nexport interface Wobble {\\n  seat: number;\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n40→  vx: number;\\n  vy: number;\\n  sx: number;\\n  sy: number;\\n  mx: number;\\n  my: number;\\n  calm: number;\\n  lungs: number;\\n  sync: number;\\n  over: number;\\n50→  recover: number;\\n  topples: number;\\n  guide: number;\\n  m1: number;\\n  m2: number;\\n  m3: number;\\n  p1: number;\\n  p2: number;\\n  p3: number;\\n  n1: number;\\n60→  n2: number;\\n  n3: number;\\n  q1: number;\\n  q2: number;\\n  q3: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** A ring buffer of recent centres, so a late thumb sees an old one. */\\nexport interface Hist {\\n  i: number;\\n70→  n: number;\\n  xs: number[];\\n  ys: number[];\\n}\\n\\nconst field = (description: string, unit = '1') =>\\n  ({ type: 'number' as const, default: 0, unit, description });\\n\\n/** The component `wobble`: one balancing body. */\\nexport const WOBBLE = defineComponent('wobble', {\\n80→  description: 'A seat’s centre of balance, its breath and the sway drawn for it.',\\n  fields: {\\n    seat: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Which mat this body stands on.' },\\n    x: field('Centre of balance, left to right. Past 1 is the rim.'),\\n    y: field('Centre of balance, back to forward.'),\\n    vx: field('Velocity along x.', '1/s'),\\n    vy: field('Velocity along y.', '1/s'),\\n    sx: field('The stick after the slew, left to right.'),\\n    sy: field('The stick after the slew, back to forward.'),\\n    mx: field('Mouse lean, decaying.'),\\n90→    my: field('Mouse lean, decaying.'),\\n    calm: field('How settled the breath is, 0 to 1.'),\\n    lungs: field('How full the breath is, 0 to 1.'),\\n    sync: field('How well the breath matches the guide, 0 to 1.'),\\n    over: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Steps in a row spent outside the disc.' },\\n    recover: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Steps left in a topple’s recentre.' },\\n    topples: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Topples since the count was cleared.' },\\n    guide: field('The breath guide, 0 empty to 1 full.'),\\n    m1: field('Sway rate ratio, x, first voice.'),\\n    m2: field('Sway rate ratio, x, second voice.'),\\n100→    m3: field('Sway rate ratio, x, third voice.'),\\n    p1: field('Sway phase, x, first voice.', 'rad'),\\n    p2: field('Sway phase, x, second voice.', 'rad'),\\n    p3: field('Sway phase, x, third voice.', 'rad'),\\n    n1: field('Sway rate ratio, y, first voice.'),\\n    n2: field('Sway rate ratio, y, second voice.'),\\n    n3: field('Sway rate ratio, y, third voice.'),\\n    q1: field('Sway phase, y, first voice.', 'rad'),\\n    q2: field('Sway phase, y, second voice.', 'rad'),\\n    q3: field('Sway phase, y, third voice.', 'rad'),\\n110→  },\\n});\\n\\n/** The component `hist`: the centres a delayed thumb can still see. */\\nexport const HIST = defineComponent('hist', {\\n  description: 'Recent centres of balance for one seat, oldest first in the ring.',\\n  fields: {\\n    i: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Where the next sample is written once the ring is full.' },\\n    n: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'How many samples have been kept.' },\\n    xs: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Recent centres, left to right.' },\\n120→    ys: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Recent centres, back to forward.' },\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** A number kept between lo and hi. */\\nexport function clamp(n: number, lo: number, hi: number): number {\\n  return Math.max(lo, Math.min(hi, n));\\n}\\n\\n/** Moves `current` toward `target` by at most `maxDelta`. */\\n130→export function slew(current: number, target: number, maxDelta: number): number {\\n  const d = target - current;\\n  if (Math.abs(d) <= maxDelta) return target;\\n  return current + Math.sign(d) * maxDelta;\\n}\\n\\n/** The slow sway on one axis. Phases come from the seat, never from Math.random. */\\nexport function swayNoise(t: number, rate: number, m1: number, m2: number, m3: number, p1: number, p2: number, p3: number): number {\\n  const a = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * m1 * t + p1);\\n  const b = 0.6 * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * 1.7 * m2 * t + p2);\\n140→  const c = 0.3 * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * 3.1 * m3 * t + p3);\\n  return (a + b + c) / 1.3;\\n}\\n\\n/** Draws the six ratios and phases for a seat from the stream `sway`. */\\nexport function drawSway(w: World): void {\\n  const rng = w.rng('sway');\\n  const ratio = () => rng.range(0.8, 1.25);\\n  const phase = () => rng.range(0, Math.PI * 2);\\n  const body = w.spawn({\\n150→    wobble: {\\n      m1: ratio(), m2: ratio(), m3: ratio(), p1: phase(), p2: phase(), p3: phase(),\\n      n1: ratio(), n2: ratio(), n3: ratio(), q1: phase(), q2: phase(), q3: phase(),\\n    },\\n    hist: { xs: [], ys: [] },\\n  });\\n  void body;\\n}\\n\\n/** Clears the motion and the breath, and keeps the sway. A new activity starts here. */\\n160→export function resetBalance(b: Wobble, hist: Hist): void {\\n  b.x = 0; b.y = 0; b.vx = 0; b.vy = 0; b.sx = 0; b.sy = 0; b.mx = 0; b.my = 0;\\n  b.calm = 0; b.lungs = 0; b.sync = 0; b.over = 0; b.recover = 0; b.topples = 0; b.guide = 0;\\n  hist.i = 0; hist.n = 0; hist.xs.length = 0; hist.ys.length = 0;\\n}\\n\\n/** Remembers a centre. The ring holds 24, which covers the sloppy thumb’s delay. */\\nexport function remember(hist: Hist, x: number, y: number): void {\\n  const cap = 24;\\n  if (hist.xs.length < cap) {\\n170→    hist.xs.push(x);\\n    hist.ys.push(y);\\n  } else {\\n    hist.xs[hist.i] = x;\\n    hist.ys[hist.i] = y;\\n    hist.i = (hist.i + 1) % cap;\\n  }\\n  hist.n += 1;\\n}\\n\\n180→/** The centre `delay` steps ago, or the oldest one we have. */\\nexport function recall(hist: Hist, delay: number): { x: number; y: number } {\\n  const len = hist.xs.length;\\n  if (len === 0) return { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n  const age = Math.min(Math.max(0, delay), len - 1);\\n  const newest = len < 24 ? len - 1 : (hist.i + 24 - 1) % 24;\\n  const at = (newest - age + len) % len;\\n  return { x: hist.xs[at] ?? 0, y: hist.ys[at] ?? 0 };\\n}\\n\\n190→/** One balance step. `t` and `dt` are sim time. A topple recentres over one second and counts once. */\\nexport function stepBalance(b: Wobble, stick: Stick, cfg: BalanceCfg, t: number, dt: number): void {\\n  const period = Math.max(0.25, cfg.period);\\n  const phase = (t % period) / period;\\n  const rising = phase < 0.5;\\n  b.guide = rising ? phase * 2 : (1 - phase) * 2;\\n  const fill = dt / (period * 0.5);\\n  if (stick.both) b.lungs = Math.min(1, b.lungs + fill);\\n  else b.lungs = Math.max(0, b.lungs - fill);\\n  const instant = 1 - Math.abs(b.lungs - b.guide);\\n200→  const participating = stick.both || b.lungs > 0.04;\\n  const toward = participating ? instant : 0;\\n  const blend = Math.min(1, dt / (participating ? 0.6 : 2));\\n  b.sync += (toward - b.sync) * blend;\\n  b.calm += (b.sync - b.calm) * Math.min(1, dt / 1.2);\\n\\n  if (b.recover > 0) {\\n    const left = b.recover;\\n    b.x *= (left - 1) / left;\\n    b.y *= (left - 1) / left;\\n210→    b.vx = 0;\\n    b.vy = 0;\\n    b.recover -= 1;\\n    b.over = 0;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n\\n  const decay = Math.exp(-dt / 0.6);\\n  b.mx = (b.mx + stick.mdx) * decay;\\n  b.my = (b.my + stick.mdy) * decay;\\n220→  const rawX = clamp(stick.x + b.mx, -1, 1);\\n  const rawY = clamp(stick.y + b.my, -1, 1);\\n  b.sx = slew(b.sx, rawX, 4 * dt);\\n  b.sy = slew(b.sy, rawY, 4 * dt);\\n  const scale = (stick.gentle ? 0.4 : 1) * cfg.reach;\\n  let tx = b.sx * scale;\\n  let ty = b.sy * scale;\\n  const len = Math.hypot(tx, ty);\\n  if (len > 1) {\\n    tx /= len;\\n230→    ty /= len;\\n  }\\n  const quiet = 1 - cfg.calmEffect * clamp(b.calm, 0, 1);\\n  const amp = cfg.noise * stick.noiseScale * quiet;\\n  const nx = swayNoise(t, cfg.noiseRate, b.m1, b.m2, b.m3, b.p1, b.p2, b.p3) * amp + stick.disturbX;\\n  const ny = swayNoise(t, cfg.noiseRate, b.n1, b.n2, b.n3, b.q1, b.q2, b.q3) * amp + stick.disturbY;\\n  const inst = cfg.instability * stick.instabilityScale;\\n  const ax = cfg.gain * (tx - b.x) + inst * b.x + nx;\\n  const ay = cfg.gain * (ty - b.y) + inst * b.y + ny;\\n  b.vx += ax * dt;\\n240→  b.vy += ay * dt;\\n  const damp = Math.exp(-cfg.damping * dt);\\n  b.vx *= damp;\\n  b.vy *= damp;\\n  b.x += b.vx * dt;\\n  b.y += b.vy * dt;\\n  if (Math.hypot(b.x, b.y) > 1) b.over += 1;\\n  else b.over = 0;\\n  if (b.over >= 6) {\\n    b.topples += 1;\\n250→    b.recover = 60;\\n    b.over = 0;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** True when the centre sits inside a ring of `radius`. */\\nexport function inRing(b: Wobble, radius: number): boolean {\\n  return Math.hypot(b.x, b.y) <= radius;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/wobble.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The one verb. Centre of balance is a point in the unit disc. Each step slews the stick, then\\n * accelerates toward it with instability, slow sway and breath. Past the rim for six steps the body topples,\\n * stumbles, and recentres. It is never a game over.\\n */\\nimport { defineComponent, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\n\\n/** Numbers the balance step reads. Sliders change them between steps. */\\nexport interface BalanceCfg {\\n  gain: number;\\n  instability: number;\\n  damping: number;\\n  noise: number;\\n  noiseRate: number;\\n  reach: number;\\n  calmEffect: number;\\n  period: number;\\n  sens: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** What the thumb, the feet and the activity are doing this step. */\\nexport interface Stick {\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  gentle: boolean;\\n  both: boolean;\\n  mdx: number;\\n  mdy: number;\\n  disturbX: number;\\n  disturbY: number;\\n  noiseScale: number;\\n  instabilityScale: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** The centre of balance and the sway drawn once for the seat. */\\nexport interface Wobble {\\n  seat: number;\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  vx: number;\\n  vy: number;\\n  sx: number;\\n  sy: number;\\n  mx: number;\\n  my: number;\\n  calm: number;\\n  lungs: number;\\n  sync: number;\\n  over: number;\\n  recover: number;\\n  topples: number;\\n  guide: number;\\n  m1: number;\\n  m2: number;\\n  m3: number;\\n  p1: number;\\n  p2: number;\\n  p3: number;\\n  n1: number;\\n  n2: number;\\n  n3: number;\\n  q1: number;\\n  q2: number;\\n  q3: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** A ring buffer of recent centres, so a late thumb sees an old one. */\\nexport interface Hist {\\n  i: number;\\n  n: number;\\n  xs: number[];\\n  ys: number[];\\n}\\n\\nconst field = (description: string, unit = '1') =>\\n  ({ type: 'number' as const, default: 0, unit, description });\\n\\n/** The component `wobble`: one balancing body. */\\nexport const WOBBLE = defineComponent('wobble', {\\n  description: 'A seat’s centre of balance, its breath and the sway drawn for it.',\\n  fields: {\\n    seat: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Which mat this body stands on.' },\\n    x: field('Centre of balance, left to right. Past 1 is the rim.'),\\n    y: field('Centre of balance, back to forward.'),\\n    vx: field('Velocity along x.', '1/s'),\\n    vy: field('Velocity along y.', '1/s'),\\n    sx: field('The stick after the slew, left to right.'),\\n    sy: field('The stick after the slew, back to forward.'),\\n    mx: field('Mouse lean, decaying.'),\\n    my: field('Mouse lean, decaying.'),\\n    calm: field('How settled the breath is, 0 to 1.'),\\n    lungs: field('How full the breath is, 0 to 1.'),\\n    sync: field('How well the breath matches the guide, 0 to 1.'),\\n    over: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Steps in a row spent outside the disc.' },\\n    recover: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Steps left in a topple’s recentre.' },\\n    topples: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Topples since the count was cleared.' },\\n    guide: field('The breath guide, 0 empty to 1 full.'),\\n    m1: field('Sway rate ratio, x, first voice.'),\\n    m2: field('Sway rate ratio, x, second voice.'),\\n    m3: field('Sway rate ratio, x, third voice.'),\\n    p1: field('Sway phase, x, first voice.', 'rad'),\\n    p2: field('Sway phase, x, second voice.', 'rad'),\\n    p3: field('Sway phase, x, third voice.', 'rad'),\\n    n1: field('Sway rate ratio, y, first voice.'),\\n    n2: field('Sway rate ratio, y, second voice.'),\\n    n3: field('Sway rate ratio, y, third voice.'),\\n    q1: field('Sway phase, y, first voice.', 'rad'),\\n    q2: field('Sway phase, y, second voice.', 'rad'),\\n    q3: field('Sway phase, y, third voice.', 'rad'),\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** The component `hist`: the centres a delayed thumb can still see. */\\nexport const HIST = defineComponent('hist', {\\n  description: 'Recent centres of balance for one seat, oldest first in the ring.',\\n  fields: {\\n    i: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Where the next sample is written once the ring is full.' },\\n    n: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'How many samples have been kept.' },\\n    xs: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Recent centres, left to right.' },\\n    ys: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Recent centres, back to forward.' },\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** A number kept between lo and hi. */\\nexport function clamp(n: number, lo: number, hi: number): number {\\n  return Math.max(lo, Math.min(hi, n));\\n}\\n\\n/** Moves `current` toward `target` by at most `maxDelta`. */\\nexport function slew(current: number, target: number, maxDelta: number): number {\\n  const d = target - current;\\n  if (Math.abs(d) <= maxDelta) return target;\\n  return current + Math.sign(d) * maxDelta;\\n}\\n\\n/** The slow sway on one axis. Phases come from the seat, never from Math.random. */\\nexport function swayNoise(t: number, rate: number, m1: number, m2: number, m3: number, p1: number, p2: number, p3: number): number {\\n  const a = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * m1 * t + p1);\\n  const b = 0.6 * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * 1.7 * m2 * t + p2);\\n  const c = 0.3 * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * 3.1 * m3 * t + p3);\\n  return (a + b + c) / 1.3;\\n}\\n\\n/** Draws the six ratios and phases for a seat from the stream `sway`. */\\nexport function drawSway(w: World): void {\\n  const rng = w.rng('sway');\\n  const ratio = () => rng.range(0.8, 1.25);\\n  const phase = () => rng.range(0, Math.PI * 2);\\n  const body = w.spawn({\\n    wobble: {\\n      m1: ratio(), m2: ratio(), m3: ratio(), p1: phase(), p2: phase(), p3: phase(),\\n      n1: ratio(), n2: ratio(), n3: ratio(), q1: phase(), q2: phase(), q3: phase(),\\n    },\\n    hist: { xs: [], ys: [] },\\n  });\\n  void body;\\n}\\n\\n/** Clears the motion and the breath, and keeps the sway. A new activity starts here. */\\nexport function resetBalance(b: Wobble, hist: Hist): void {\\n  b.x = 0; b.y = 0; b.vx = 0; b.vy = 0; b.sx = 0; b.sy = 0; b.mx = 0; b.my = 0;\\n  b.calm = 0; b.lungs = 0; b.sync = 0; b.over = 0; b.recover = 0; b.topples = 0; b.guide = 0;\\n  hist.i = 0; hist.n = 0; hist.xs.length = 0; hist.ys.length = 0;\\n}\\n\\n/** Remembers a centre. The ring holds 24, which covers the sloppy thumb’s delay. */\\nexport function remember(hist: Hist, x: number, y: number): void {\\n  const cap = 24;\\n  if (hist.xs.length < cap) {\\n    hist.xs.push(x);\\n    hist.ys.push(y);\\n  } else {\\n    hist.xs[hist.i] = x;\\n    hist.ys[hist.i] = y;\\n    hist.i = (hist.i + 1) % cap;\\n  }\\n  hist.n += 1;\\n}\\n\\n/** The centre `delay` steps ago, or the oldest one we have. */\\nexport function recall(hist: Hist, delay: number): { x: number; y: number } {\\n  const len = hist.xs.length;\\n  if (len === 0) return { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n  const age = Math.min(Math.max(0, delay), len - 1);\\n  const newest = len < 24 ? len - 1 : (hist.i + 24 - 1) % 24;\\n  const at = (newest - age + len) % len;\\n  return { x: hist.xs[at] ?? 0, y: hist.ys[at] ?? 0 };\\n}\\n\\n/** One balance step. `t` and `dt` are sim time. A topple recentres over one second and counts once. */\\nexport function stepBalance(b: Wobble, stick: Stick, cfg: BalanceCfg, t: number, dt: number): void {\\n  const period = Math.max(0.25, cfg.period);\\n  const phase = (t % period) / period;\\n  const rising = phase < 0.5;\\n  b.guide = rising ? phase * 2 : (1 - phase) * 2;\\n  const fill = dt / (period * 0.5);\\n  if (stick.both) b.lungs = Math.min(1, b.lungs + fill);\\n  else b.lungs = Math.max(0, b.lungs - fill);\\n  const instant = 1 - Math.abs(b.lungs - b.guide);\\n  const participating = stick.both || b.lungs > 0.04;\\n  const toward = participating ? instant : 0;\\n  const blend = Math.min(1, dt / (participating ? 0.6 : 2));\\n  b.sync += (toward - b.sync) * blend;\\n  b.calm += (b.sync - b.calm) * Math.min(1, dt / 1.2);\\n\\n  if (b.recover > 0) {\\n    const left = b.recover;\\n    b.x *= (left - 1) / left;\\n    b.y *= (left - 1) / left;\\n    b.vx = 0;\\n    b.vy = 0;\\n    b.recover -= 1;\\n    b.over = 0;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n\\n  const decay = Math.exp(-dt / 0.6);\\n  b.mx = (b.mx + stick.mdx) * decay;\\n  b.my = (b.my + stick.mdy) * decay;\\n  const rawX = clamp(stick.x + b.mx, -1, 1);\\n  const rawY = clamp(stick.y + b.my, -1, 1);\\n  b.sx = slew(b.sx, rawX, 4 * dt);\\n  b.sy = slew(b.sy, rawY, 4 * dt);\\n  const scale = (stick.gentle ? 0.4 : 1) * cfg.reach;\\n  let tx = b.sx * scale;\\n  let ty = b.sy * scale;\\n  const len = Math.hypot(tx, ty);\\n  if (len > 1) {\\n    tx /= len;\\n    ty /= len;\\n  }\\n  const quiet = 1 - cfg.calmEffect * clamp(b.calm, 0, 1);\\n  const amp = cfg.noise * stick.noiseScale * quiet;\\n  const nx = swayNoise(t, cfg.noiseRate, b.m1, b.m2, b.m3, b.p1, b.p2, b.p3) * amp + stick.disturbX;\\n  const ny = swayNoise(t, cfg.noiseRate, b.n1, b.n2, b.n3, b.q1, b.q2, b.q3) * amp + stick.disturbY;\\n  const inst = cfg.instability * stick.instabilityScale;\\n  const ax = cfg.gain * (tx - b.x) + inst * b.x + nx;\\n  const ay = cfg.gain * (ty - b.y) + inst * b.y + ny;\\n  b.vx += ax * dt;\\n  b.vy += ay * dt;\\n  const damp = Math.exp(-cfg.damping * dt);\\n  b.vx *= damp;\\n  b.vy *= damp;\\n  b.x += b.vx * dt;\\n  b.y += b.vy * dt;\\n  if (Math.hypot(b.x, b.y) > 1) b.over += 1;\\n  else b.over = 0;\\n  if (b.over >= 6) {\\n    b.topples += 1;\\n    b.recover = 60;\\n    b.over = 0;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** True when the centre sits inside a ring of `radius`. */\\nexport function inRing(b: Wobble, radius: number): boolean {\\n  return Math.hypot(b.x, b.y) <= radius;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":258}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fd732a93-a17b-46c1-b54c-df2b43ea273c-2","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Game plan: a balance-and-wellness game inspired by Wii Fit\\n\\nYou build this without the director. This plan is complete: follow it, and where it is silent use your judgment and\\nwrite the call in `labs/game/README.md`. Your own TASK.md still rules: it holds the file and folder names, the title\\nrule, and the reports. Every path below is relative to your dev folder.\\n\\n**[tested]** marks what was actually run on this machine on 2026-11-04, against my-3dge at commit e7a1243. **[source]**\\nmarks what was read in that commit's code but not run. Trust both over your memory of three.js or the engine. Anything\\nunmarked is design: yours to tune.\\n10→\\nContents: 1 The game · 2 World and cast · 3 The one verb · 4 Controls · 5 Structure · 6 Activities · 7 The finale ·\\n8 Screens · 9 Multiplayer · 10 Art · 11 Animation · 12 Audio · 13 Writing · 14 Tech · 15 Engine traps · 16 Testing ·\\n17 Build order · 18 Done · 19 Reports · 20 Brief-to-plan map\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. The game\\n\\n**Pitch.** You are a guest at the Little Fulcrum Wellness Retreat, a spotless island run by a retired bathroom scale\\n20→who stopped weighing people and now measures only how much you wobble. Every activity (poses, reps, step class,\\npaddling, a slackline, a tilting sand garden, sitting perfectly still while a frog judges you) is played through one\\nverb: keep your centre of balance where it should be. Over five days the deadpan gets stranger. The plaques move.\\nMarbles roll by themselves. The staff keep asking you to stand further east. Little Fulcrum is balanced on a single\\nrock. On the last night the storm comes, the island tips, and in the finale your thumb's balance *is* the island's.\\n\\n**Genre:** a 3D sports and wellness anthology of balance activities around a small walkable island, with a daily-ritual\\nmeta game and a comedy story. **Perspective:** third person throughout: a chase camera on the island, and a purpose-built\\ncamera for each activity (the table in section 6). **Hub genre:** Sports.\\n\\n30→**Pillars**, for every decision:\\n\\n1. **One verb, many bodies.** The left stick is your weight. A new activity changes what your weight moves, never how\\n   you move it. Fifteen seconds with any activity teaches the next one.\\n2. **Your thumb is the exercise.** The character's limbs follow the input directly, by scrubbing animation (section 11).\\n   Nothing plays \\\"a squat\\\" at you. You do the squat.\\n3. **Deadpan kindness.** Nobody shouts, nothing is a game over. The game is polite, slightly invasive, and proud of you\\n   in a way that worries you.\\n4. **The daily ritual.** A morning check, one big number, a stamp, a growing stack of pebbles. Coming back is the game.\\n5. **A small joke grows into the world.** The tilt starts as a sign that says \\\"Please keep to the centre\\\". It ends with\\n40→   a storm and a whole island on your thumb.\\n6. **A class, not a match.** Other people are on the next mat, wobbling. You can see them. It is enough.\\n\\n**Take from the source (feel and mechanics):** the centre-of-balance dot; holding still as a skill; lean-steered\\nminigames; breathing; rhythm stepping; rep counting; a daily test that yields an \\\"age\\\"; a talking fitness peripheral\\nwith personal questions; a serene instructor; earning time-based currency in a plaza; passive-aggressive encouragement.\\n\\n**Never take (this is an original game, not a recreation):** the word \\\"Wii\\\" anywhere in the game except the About\\nscreen's Source line and the hub's source field; \\\"Fit Age\\\", \\\"Fit Credits\\\", \\\"Fit Piggy Bank\\\", \\\"Body Test\\\"; the source's\\ntrainer look; the Balance Board's shape or lines; Mii-like avatars; Wuhu Island; the source's minigame names, course\\n50→layouts, menus, logo, fonts, jingles or melodies.\\n\\n**Never do, ever:** weight, BMI, calorie or body-size talk or numbers. All judgement is of *wobble*. That is also the\\ngame's best running joke: the scale refuses to weigh anyone.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. World and cast\\n\\n**Little Fulcrum**: a green and sand island about 200 m across, one low summit, a clean white retreat scattered on it,\\n60→open sea to every horizon. It looks like a brochure. Everything is very slightly too tidy.\\n\\nStation layout, in metres (x east, z south, island centre at 0,0; tune by eye, keep the relations):\\n\\n| Place | Around | Holds |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Ferry Pier and Beach | (0, 100) | Arrival, the ferry; the south shore |\\n| The Plaza | (0, 34), flat, y≈8 | Tare's Platform (Morning Check), Noticeboard, your Cairn |\\n| Pose Pavilion | (-52, 18), flat | Pose Class, Group Class: four mats, white floor, pale curtains, open sides |\\n| Still Pond | (-70, -12), a hollow | Still Pond |\\n70→| The Annex | (52, 22), flat | Reps Hall and Step Class under one long open roof, a mirror wall |\\n| Guest Huts | (64, 52) | Your hut: sleep ends the day |\\n| South-West Lagoon | (-60, 85) | The Line (headland to rock), Paddle Glide launch |\\n| Sand Terrace | (30, -48) | Sand Garden |\\n| North Cliff | (0, -88), 14 m drop | Cliff Plunge |\\n| Hoop Beach | (62, 84) | Hoop Patrol |\\n| Lighthouse | (84, -60) | Landmark; the storm's beam |\\n| East Terrace | (74, 8) | The \\\"high side\\\" in the finale |\\n| Centre Stone | (0, 0), the summit | A plain stone with a brass plate reading \\\"Do not\\\". The finale ends here |\\n\\n80→**Cast** (all original, pronouns as given):\\n\\n- **Tare** (it): the mascot and guide. A squat round dial bathroom scale on two stubby legs, face in the dial. Retired\\n  from weighing. Hops beside you. Chirpy, nosy, secretly sad. Keeps the secret of the rock badly.\\n- **Instructor Plumb** (they): head instructor. Tall, narrow, utterly vertical. Pale mint tracksuit, eyes always closed\\n  in two calm arcs, one very long straight plait that has never once moved. Speaks slowly and flatly. In the storm the\\n  plait swings for the first time, and that is the most frightening moment in the game. At dawn Plumb opens their eyes,\\n  once.\\n- **Gerald** (he): a retired guest with immense calves, always already there, always finished. Says only \\\"Morning.\\\"\\n  until Day 4.\\n90→- **Bex** (they): a bored teenager sent here by a parent, holding a phone-shaped stone, annoyingly excellent.\\n- **Old Nan** (she): 91, Wobble Age 19. Stands where you left her. Nobody has seen her arrive.\\n- **The Gull** and **the Frog** (it): recurring menaces. The Gull lands on you at the worst moment. The Frog just looks.\\n- **You**: \\\"Guest\\\". Pick one of three looks and a tracksuit colour at the pier. No name entry.\\n\\n**The five-day story** (delivered in one-liners, never in walls of text):\\n\\n| Day | Beat |\\n|---|---|\\n| 1 Arrival | Ferry leaves. Tare greets you. First Wobble Age is terrible. Sign: \\\"Please keep to the centre.\\\" |\\n100→| 2 The Mat | Plaques have moved. \\\"Guests are reminded to distribute themselves evenly.\\\" |\\n| 3 The Water | Drinks slide along tables. A notice calls this \\\"a feature of the drink\\\". |\\n| 4 The Sand | Marbles in the Sand Garden roll with nobody there. Gerald speaks. At night Tare confesses: the island sits on one rock. \\\"We don't mention it to guests. You're a guest. I didn't mention it.\\\" |\\n| 5 The Tilt | Group Class. Then the storm, The Great Tilt (section 7), dawn, the last Morning Check, credits. |\\n| After | \\\"You may stay as long as you like. The ferry does not return.\\\" Free Play, and a fresh Morning Check every in-game day. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. The one verb: the Wobble Model\\n\\n110→This is the game's core. Build it first, tune it in dev mode, and reuse it everywhere. It lives in the sim as a\\ncomponent `wobble` on each balancing body, one per seat.\\n\\n**The centre of balance (CoB)** is a point in a unit disc: `x` left to right, `y` back to forward. `r = 1` is the edge:\\npast it you topple.\\n\\nEach step (1/60 s), for each axis:\\n\\n```\\ntarget  = slew(stick + mouse, 4 units/s) × (gentle ? 0.4 : 1) × reach      // clamped to the disc\\n120→accel   = gain × (target − cob) + instability × cob + noise(t) × (1 − calmEffect × calm) + disturbance\\nvel    += accel × dt;   vel *= exp(−damping × dt);   cob += vel × dt\\n```\\n\\n| Setting | Default | Range | What it does |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `game.wobble.gain` | 14 /s² | 4–30 | How fast your weight follows your thumb |\\n| `game.wobble.instability` | 3 /s² | 0–10 | How hard you fall away from the centre |\\n| `game.wobble.damping` | 5 /s | 1–12 | How heavy the body feels |\\n| `game.wobble.noise` | 3.5 /s² | 0–8 | Sway strength |\\n130→| `game.wobble.noiseRate` | 0.15 Hz | 0.05–0.4 | Sway speed: a slow push you lean against |\\n| `game.wobble.reach` | 0.9 | 0.5–1 | Full stick's target; a held full stick topples, on purpose |\\n| `game.breath.period` | 8 s | 4–14 | One breath, half in, half out |\\n| `game.breath.calmEffect` | 0.5 | 0–1 | How much full calm quiets the sway |\\n\\nSway per axis, phases and small rate ratios `m` drawn once per seat from a named stream (`w.rng('sway')`), never\\n`Math.random`, and written with plain `Math.sin` so the sim's math swap reaches it:\\n\\n```\\nnoise(t) = ( sin(2π·rate·m1·t + p1) + 0.6·sin(2π·rate·1.7·m2·t + p2) + 0.3·sin(2π·rate·3.1·m3·t + p3) ) / 1.3      // mi in 0.8–1.25\\n140→```\\n\\n**These numbers are modelled, and the slow sway matters [tested in a small simulation of this exact model, 20 s, 10 seeds,\\nstaying in a ring of 0.22]:** no input 38%; a human-like thumb (250 ms reaction, proportional gain 1.2, a little jitter) 90%;\\na sloppy thumb (350 ms, gain 0.8) 72%; a no-delay bot 100%. A ring of 0.16 drops the thumb to 65%. Off-centre seats out to\\n0.35 hold at 87%, and 0.6 starts to topple (so keep seats within 0.5). **At the 0.45 Hz sway first tried, doing nothing beat\\nthe human thumb,** because a 250 ms reaction turns correction into amplification, so keep the sway slow. Nobody can play by\\nhand here: the delayed-thumb bot (section 16) is how you judge feel.\\n\\nThe universal 4 units/s slew is what makes keyboard feel analog: a quick tap is a small nudge, a held key is a full lean.\\n150→Sticks barely notice it. Mouse adds its own target with a slow decay (section 4).\\n\\n**Topple.** `r > 1` for 6 steps: the body stumbles (`reactTo` flinch, a stumble clip, a creak), the activity decides the\\nprice, and the CoB returns to centre over a second. It is never a game over.\\n\\n**Breath.** The third input is both feet held. A guide ring swells and shrinks with `breath.period`. Holding both feet\\nfills `lungs`; letting go empties them. `sync` is a running match between your lungs and the guide. Good sync raises\\n`calm` (0–1), which quiets the sway, warms the picture slightly, softens the sound, and pays a bonus. Breath is used in\\nstill activities and is the charge mechanic in fast ones. Being out of sync has no penalty beyond losing the help.\\n\\n160→**Feet.** Left and right foot are the two triggers (analog) or shoulders. Used for steps, rhythm, paddling, jogging and\\none-leg holds. Both together is breath, or a jump in Step Class. That is every input the activities need: **Lean, Left\\nFoot, Right Foot, Both Feet.**\\n\\n**Scoring.** Every activity yields 0–1000 and a rank: 0 **Present**, 300 **Adequate**, 550 **Composed**, 750 **Serene**,\\n900 **Unsettling**. Pebbles earned: 1 to 5 by rank.\\n\\n**No softlocks.** Every activity and every finale step ends by itself: each step has a time box, after which it moves on with\\na remark (\\\"We will call that a start.\\\"). A player who puts the pad down reaches the results screen.\\n\\n170→**Balance targets the tests enforce** (section 16) on 10 seeds at default settings, in every activity: the perfect bot\\nscores ≥ 750, the human-like delayed thumb ≥ 550, the sloppy thumb ≥ 300, no input at all ≤ 500 and below the human-like\\nthumb. Random mashing never crashes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Controls\\n\\nThe DualSense on a TV is the design target. Keyboard and mouse are native, not stand-ins.\\n\\n180→| Verb | DualSense | Keyboard | Mouse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Lean (activities) | Left stick (D-pad too) | WASD or arrows; Shift is gentle | Move: pointer-locked movement leans |\\n| Left foot / Right foot | L2 / R2 (L1 / R1 too) | Q / E | Left button / Right button |\\n| Both feet (breathe, jump) | L2 + R2 | Space | Both buttons |\\n| Pause | Options | Esc | |\\n| Walk (island) | Left stick | WASD; Shift walks slowly | |\\n| Look (island) | Right stick | | Move (pointer lock) |\\n| Talk, use, enter | Cross | E or Enter | Left button at the thing in view |\\n| Hop | Square | Space | |\\n190→| Programme (today's list) | Triangle | Tab | |\\n| Wave | Circle | C | |\\n| Menus | D-pad or stick, Cross, Circle | Arrows, Enter or Space, Esc | Hover moves focus, click picks |\\n\\nActivity-specific mouse feel: in Sand Garden the pointer's place on the tray is the tilt; in Hoop Patrol you circle the\\nmouse; Step Class is left and right click on the beat. On the island the thing at the centre of the screen gets a highlight\\nand its prompt, and left click uses it.\\n\\n**Prompts** follow the input used last (`input.lastDevice`), switching the same frame. Pad: PlayStation glyphs (Cross,\\nCircle, Square, Triangle, L1, R1, L2, R2, sticks) drawn as inline SVG. Settings has \\\"Button icons: PlayStation / Xbox\\\"\\n200→(A B X Y, LB RB LT RT). Keyboard and mouse: key caps and a mouse icon with the button lit. Never rely on the engine's\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Game plan: a balance-and-wellness game inspired by Wii Fit\\n\\nYou build this without the director. This plan is complete: follow it, and where it is silent use your judgment and\\nwrite the call in `labs/game/README.md`. Your own TASK.md still rules: it holds the file and folder names, the title\\nrule, and the reports. Every path below is relative to your dev folder.\\n\\n**[tested]** marks what was actually run on this machine on 2026-11-04, against my-3dge at commit e7a1243. **[source]**\\nmarks what was read in that commit's code but not run. Trust both over your memory of three.js or the engine. Anything\\nunmarked is design: yours to tune.\\n10→\\nContents: 1 The game · 2 World and cast · 3 The one verb · 4 Controls · 5 Structure · 6 Activities · 7 The finale ·\\n8 Screens · 9 Multiplayer · 10 Art · 11 Animation · 12 Audio · 13 Writing · 14 Tech · 15 Engine traps · 16 Testing ·\\n17 Build order · 18 Done · 19 Reports · 20 Brief-to-plan map\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. The game\\n\\n**Pitch.** You are a guest at the Little Fulcrum Wellness Retreat, a spotless island run by a retired bathroom scale\\n20→who stopped weighing people and now measures only how much you wobble. Every activity (poses, reps, step class,\\npaddling, a slackline, a tilting sand garden, sitting perfectly still while a frog judges you) is played through one\\nverb: keep your centre of balance where it should be. Over five days the deadpan gets stranger. The plaques move.\\nMarbles roll by themselves. The staff keep asking you to stand further east. Little Fulcrum is balanced on a single\\nrock. On the last night the storm comes, the island tips, and in the finale your thumb's balance *is* the island's.\\n\\n**Genre:** a 3D sports and wellness anthology of balance activities around a small walkable island, with a daily-ritual\\nmeta game and a comedy story. **Perspective:** third person throughout: a chase camera on the island, and a purpose-built\\ncamera for each activity (the table in section 6). **Hub genre:** Sports.\\n\\n30→**Pillars**, for every decision:\\n\\n1. **One verb, many bodies.** The left stick is your weight. A new activity changes what your weight moves, never how\\n   you move it. Fifteen seconds with any activity teaches the next one.\\n2. **Your thumb is the exercise.** The character's limbs follow the input directly, by scrubbing animation (section 11).\\n   Nothing plays \\\"a squat\\\" at you. You do the squat.\\n3. **Deadpan kindness.** Nobody shouts, nothing is a game over. The game is polite, slightly invasive, and proud of you\\n   in a way that worries you.\\n4. **The daily ritual.** A morning check, one big number, a stamp, a growing stack of pebbles. Coming back is the game.\\n5. **A small joke grows into the world.** The tilt starts as a sign that says \\\"Please keep to the centre\\\". It ends with\\n40→   a storm and a whole island on your thumb.\\n6. **A class, not a match.** Other people are on the next mat, wobbling. You can see them. It is enough.\\n\\n**Take from the source (feel and mechanics):** the centre-of-balance dot; holding still as a skill; lean-steered\\nminigames; breathing; rhythm stepping; rep counting; a daily test that yields an \\\"age\\\"; a talking fitness peripheral\\nwith personal questions; a serene instructor; earning time-based currency in a plaza; passive-aggressive encouragement.\\n\\n**Never take (this is an original game, not a recreation):** the word \\\"Wii\\\" anywhere in the game except the About\\nscreen's Source line and the hub's source field; \\\"Fit Age\\\", \\\"Fit Credits\\\", \\\"Fit Piggy Bank\\\", \\\"Body Test\\\"; the source's\\ntrainer look; the Balance Board's shape or lines; Mii-like avatars; Wuhu Island; the source's minigame names, course\\n50→layouts, menus, logo, fonts, jingles or melodies.\\n\\n**Never do, ever:** weight, BMI, calorie or body-size talk or numbers. All judgement is of *wobble*. That is also the\\ngame's best running joke: the scale refuses to weigh anyone.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. World and cast\\n\\n**Little Fulcrum**: a green and sand island about 200 m across, one low summit, a clean white retreat scattered on it,\\n60→open sea to every horizon. It looks like a brochure. Everything is very slightly too tidy.\\n\\nStation layout, in metres (x east, z south, island centre at 0,0; tune by eye, keep the relations):\\n\\n| Place | Around | Holds |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Ferry Pier and Beach | (0, 100) | Arrival, the ferry; the south shore |\\n| The Plaza | (0, 34), flat, y≈8 | Tare's Platform (Morning Check), Noticeboard, your Cairn |\\n| Pose Pavilion | (-52, 18), flat | Pose Class, Group Class: four mats, white floor, pale curtains, open sides |\\n| Still Pond | (-70, -12), a hollow | Still Pond |\\n70→| The Annex | (52, 22), flat | Reps Hall and Step Class under one long open roof, a mirror wall |\\n| Guest Huts | (64, 52) | Your hut: sleep ends the day |\\n| South-West Lagoon | (-60, 85) | The Line (headland to rock), Paddle Glide launch |\\n| Sand Terrace | (30, -48) | Sand Garden |\\n| North Cliff | (0, -88), 14 m drop | Cliff Plunge |\\n| Hoop Beach | (62, 84) | Hoop Patrol |\\n| Lighthouse | (84, -60) | Landmark; the storm's beam |\\n| East Terrace | (74, 8) | The \\\"high side\\\" in the finale |\\n| Centre Stone | (0, 0), the summit | A plain stone with a brass plate reading \\\"Do not\\\". The finale ends here |\\n\\n80→**Cast** (all original, pronouns as given):\\n\\n- **Tare** (it): the mascot and guide. A squat round dial bathroom scale on two stubby legs, face in the dial. Retired\\n  from weighing. Hops beside you. Chirpy, nosy, secretly sad. Keeps the secret of the rock badly.\\n- **Instructor Plumb** (they): head instructor. Tall, narrow, utterly vertical. Pale mint tracksuit, eyes always closed\\n  in two calm arcs, one very long straight plait that has never once moved. Speaks slowly and flatly. In the storm the\\n  plait swings for the first time, and that is the most frightening moment in the game. At dawn Plumb opens their eyes,\\n  once.\\n- **Gerald** (he): a retired guest with immense calves, always already there, always finished. Says only \\\"Morning.\\\"\\n  until Day 4.\\n90→- **Bex** (they): a bored teenager sent here by a parent, holding a phone-shaped stone, annoyingly excellent.\\n- **Old Nan** (she): 91, Wobble Age 19. Stands where you left her. Nobody has seen her arrive.\\n- **The Gull** and **the Frog** (it): recurring menaces. The Gull lands on you at the worst moment. The Frog just looks.\\n- **You**: \\\"Guest\\\". Pick one of three looks and a tracksuit colour at the pier. No name entry.\\n\\n**The five-day story** (delivered in one-liners, never in walls of text):\\n\\n| Day | Beat |\\n|---|---|\\n| 1 Arrival | Ferry leaves. Tare greets you. First Wobble Age is terrible. Sign: \\\"Please keep to the centre.\\\" |\\n100→| 2 The Mat | Plaques have moved. \\\"Guests are reminded to distribute themselves evenly.\\\" |\\n| 3 The Water | Drinks slide along tables. A notice calls this \\\"a feature of the drink\\\". |\\n| 4 The Sand | Marbles in the Sand Garden roll with nobody there. Gerald speaks. At night Tare confesses: the island sits on one rock. \\\"We don't mention it to guests. You're a guest. I didn't mention it.\\\" |\\n| 5 The Tilt | Group Class. Then the storm, The Great Tilt (section 7), dawn, the last Morning Check, credits. |\\n| After | \\\"You may stay as long as you like. The ferry does not return.\\\" Free Play, and a fresh Morning Check every in-game day. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. The one verb: the Wobble Model\\n\\n110→This is the game's core. Build it first, tune it in dev mode, and reuse it everywhere. It lives in the sim as a\\ncomponent `wobble` on each balancing body, one per seat.\\n\\n**The centre of balance (CoB)** is a point in a unit disc: `x` left to right, `y` back to forward. `r = 1` is the edge:\\npast it you topple.\\n\\nEach step (1/60 s), for each axis:\\n\\n```\\ntarget  = slew(stick + mouse, 4 units/s) × (gentle ? 0.4 : 1) × reach      // clamped to the disc\\n120→accel   = gain × (target − cob) + instability × cob + noise(t) × (1 − calmEffect × calm) + disturbance\\nvel    += accel × dt;   vel *= exp(−damping × dt);   cob += vel × dt\\n```\\n\\n| Setting | Default | Range | What it does |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `game.wobble.gain` | 14 /s² | 4–30 | How fast your weight follows your thumb |\\n| `game.wobble.instability` | 3 /s² | 0–10 | How hard you fall away from the centre |\\n| `game.wobble.damping` | 5 /s | 1–12 | How heavy the body feels |\\n| `game.wobble.noise` | 3.5 /s² | 0–8 | Sway strength |\\n130→| `game.wobble.noiseRate` | 0.15 Hz | 0.05–0.4 | Sway speed: a slow push you lean against |\\n| `game.wobble.reach` | 0.9 | 0.5–1 | Full stick's target; a held full stick topples, on purpose |\\n| `game.breath.period` | 8 s | 4–14 | One breath, half in, half out |\\n| `game.breath.calmEffect` | 0.5 | 0–1 | How much full calm quiets the sway |\\n\\nSway per axis, phases and small rate ratios `m` drawn once per seat from a named stream (`w.rng('sway')`), never\\n`Math.random`, and written with plain `Math.sin` so the sim's math swap reaches it:\\n\\n```\\nnoise(t) = ( sin(2π·rate·m1·t + p1) + 0.6·sin(2π·rate·1.7·m2·t + p2) + 0.3·sin(2π·rate·3.1·m3·t + p3) ) / 1.3      // mi in 0.8–1.25\\n140→```\\n\\n**These numbers are modelled, and the slow sway matters [tested in a small simulation of this exact model, 20 s, 10 seeds,\\nstaying in a ring of 0.22]:** no input 38%; a human-like thumb (250 ms reaction, proportional gain 1.2, a little jitter) 90%;\\na sloppy thumb (350 ms, gain 0.8) 72%; a no-delay bot 100%. A ring of 0.16 drops the thumb to 65%. Off-centre seats out to\\n0.35 hold at 87%, and 0.6 starts to topple (so keep seats within 0.5). **At the 0.45 Hz sway first tried, doing nothing beat\\nthe human thumb,** because a 250 ms reaction turns correction into amplification, so keep the sway slow. Nobody can play by\\nhand here: the delayed-thumb bot (section 16) is how you judge feel.\\n\\nThe universal 4 units/s slew is what makes keyboard feel analog: a quick tap is a small nudge, a held key is a full lean.\\n150→Sticks barely notice it. Mouse adds its own target with a slow decay (section 4).\\n\\n**Topple.** `r > 1` for 6 steps: the body stumbles (`reactTo` flinch, a stumble clip, a creak), the activity decides the\\nprice, and the CoB returns to centre over a second. It is never a game over.\\n\\n**Breath.** The third input is both feet held. A guide ring swells and shrinks with `breath.period`. Holding both feet\\nfills `lungs`; letting go empties them. `sync` is a running match between your lungs and the guide. Good sync raises\\n`calm` (0–1), which quiets the sway, warms the picture slightly, softens the sound, and pays a bonus. Breath is used in\\nstill activities and is the charge mechanic in fast ones. Being out of sync has no penalty beyond losing the help.\\n\\n160→**Feet.** Left and right foot are the two triggers (analog) or shoulders. Used for steps, rhythm, paddling, jogging and\\none-leg holds. Both together is breath, or a jump in Step Class. That is every input the activities need: **Lean, Left\\nFoot, Right Foot, Both Feet.**\\n\\n**Scoring.** Every activity yields 0–1000 and a rank: 0 **Present**, 300 **Adequate**, 550 **Composed**, 750 **Serene**,\\n900 **Unsettling**. Pebbles earned: 1 to 5 by rank.\\n\\n**No softlocks.** Every activity and every finale step ends by itself: each step has a time box, after which it moves on with\\na remark (\\\"We will call that a start.\\\"). A player who puts the pad down reaches the results screen.\\n\\n170→**Balance targets the tests enforce** (section 16) on 10 seeds at default settings, in every activity: the perfect bot\\nscores ≥ 750, the human-like delayed thumb ≥ 550, the sloppy thumb ≥ 300, no input at all ≤ 500 and below the human-like\\nthumb. Random mashing never crashes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Controls\\n\\nThe DualSense on a TV is the design target. Keyboard and mouse are native, not stand-ins.\\n\\n180→| Verb | DualSense | Keyboard | Mouse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Lean (activities) | Left stick (D-pad too) | WASD or arrows; Shift is gentle | Move: pointer-locked movement leans |\\n| Left foot / Right foot | L2 / R2 (L1 / R1 too) | Q / E | Left button / Right button |\\n| Both feet (breathe, jump) | L2 + R2 | Space | Both buttons |\\n| Pause | Options | Esc | |\\n| Walk (island) | Left stick | WASD; Shift walks slowly | |\\n| Look (island) | Right stick | | Move (pointer lock) |\\n| Talk, use, enter | Cross | E or Enter | Left button at the thing in view |\\n| Hop | Square | Space | |\\n190→| Programme (today's list) | Triangle | Tab | |\\n| Wave | Circle | C | |\\n| Menus | D-pad or stick, Cross, Circle | Arrows, Enter or Space, Esc | Hover moves focus, click picks |\\n\\nActivity-specific mouse feel: in Sand Garden the pointer's place on the tray is the tilt; in Hoop Patrol you circle the\\nmouse; Step Class is left and right click on the beat. On the island the thing at the centre of the screen gets a highlight\\nand its prompt, and left click uses it.\\n\\n**Prompts** follow the input used last (`input.lastDevice`), switching the same frame. Pad: PlayStation glyphs (Cross,\\nCircle, Square, Triangle, L1, R1, L2, R2, sticks) drawn as inline SVG. Settings has \\\"Button icons: PlayStation / Xbox\\\"\\n200→(A B X Y, LB RB LT RT). Keyboard and mouse: key caps and a mouse icon with the button lit. Never rely on the engine's\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":200,\"raw_output\":\"# Game plan: a balance-and-wellness game inspired by Wii Fit\\n\\nYou build this without the director. This plan is complete: follow it, and where it is silent use your judgment and\\nwrite the call in `labs/game/README.md`. Your own TASK.md still rules: it holds the file and folder names, the title\\nrule, and the reports. Every path below is relative to your dev folder.\\n\\n**[tested]** marks what was actually run on this machine on 2026-11-04, against my-3dge at commit e7a1243. **[source]**\\nmarks what was read in that commit's code but not run. Trust both over your memory of three.js or the engine. Anything\\nunmarked is design: yours to tune.\\n\\nContents: 1 The game · 2 World and cast · 3 The one verb · 4 Controls · 5 Structure · 6 Activities · 7 The finale ·\\n8 Screens · 9 Multiplayer · 10 Art · 11 Animation · 12 Audio · 13 Writing · 14 Tech · 15 Engine traps · 16 Testing ·\\n17 Build order · 18 Done · 19 Reports · 20 Brief-to-plan map\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. The game\\n\\n**Pitch.** You are a guest at the Little Fulcrum Wellness Retreat, a spotless island run by a retired bathroom scale\\nwho stopped weighing people and now measures only how much you wobble. Every activity (poses, reps, step class,\\npaddling, a slackline, a tilting sand garden, sitting perfectly still while a frog judges you) is played through one\\nverb: keep your centre of balance where it should be. Over five days the deadpan gets stranger. The plaques move.\\nMarbles roll by themselves. The staff keep asking you to stand further east. Little Fulcrum is balanced on a single\\nrock. On the last night the storm comes, the island tips, and in the finale your thumb's balance *is* the island's.\\n\\n**Genre:** a 3D sports and wellness anthology of balance activities around a small walkable island, with a daily-ritual\\nmeta game and a comedy story. **Perspective:** third person throughout: a chase camera on the island, and a purpose-built\\ncamera for each activity (the table in section 6). **Hub genre:** Sports.\\n\\n**Pillars**, for every decision:\\n\\n1. **One verb, many bodies.** The left stick is your weight. A new activity changes what your weight moves, never how\\n   you move it. Fifteen seconds with any activity teaches the next one.\\n2. **Your thumb is the exercise.** The character's limbs follow the input directly, by scrubbing animation (section 11).\\n   Nothing plays \\\"a squat\\\" at you. You do the squat.\\n3. **Deadpan kindness.** Nobody shouts, nothing is a game over. The game is polite, slightly invasive, and proud of you\\n   in a way that worries you.\\n4. **The daily ritual.** A morning check, one big number, a stamp, a growing stack of pebbles. Coming back is the game.\\n5. **A small joke grows into the world.** The tilt starts as a sign that says \\\"Please keep to the centre\\\". It ends with\\n   a storm and a whole island on your thumb.\\n6. **A class, not a match.** Other people are on the next mat, wobbling. You can see them. It is enough.\\n\\n**Take from the source (feel and mechanics):** the centre-of-balance dot; holding still as a skill; lean-steered\\nminigames; breathing; rhythm stepping; rep counting; a daily test that yields an \\\"age\\\"; a talking fitness peripheral\\nwith personal questions; a serene instructor; earning time-based currency in a plaza; passive-aggressive encouragement.\\n\\n**Never take (this is an original game, not a recreation):** the word \\\"Wii\\\" anywhere in the game except the About\\nscreen's Source line and the hub's source field; \\\"Fit Age\\\", \\\"Fit Credits\\\", \\\"Fit Piggy Bank\\\", \\\"Body Test\\\"; the source's\\ntrainer look; the Balance Board's shape or lines; Mii-like avatars; Wuhu Island; the source's minigame names, course\\nlayouts, menus, logo, fonts, jingles or melodies.\\n\\n**Never do, ever:** weight, BMI, calorie or body-size talk or numbers. All judgement is of *wobble*. That is also the\\ngame's best running joke: the scale refuses to weigh anyone.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. World and cast\\n\\n**Little Fulcrum**: a green and sand island about 200 m across, one low summit, a clean white retreat scattered on it,\\nopen sea to every horizon. It looks like a brochure. Everything is very slightly too tidy.\\n\\nStation layout, in metres (x east, z south, island centre at 0,0; tune by eye, keep the relations):\\n\\n| Place | Around | Holds |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Ferry Pier and Beach | (0, 100) | Arrival, the ferry; the south shore |\\n| The Plaza | (0, 34), flat, y≈8 | Tare's Platform (Morning Check), Noticeboard, your Cairn |\\n| Pose Pavilion | (-52, 18), flat | Pose Class, Group Class: four mats, white floor, pale curtains, open sides |\\n| Still Pond | (-70, -12), a hollow | Still Pond |\\n| The Annex | (52, 22), flat | Reps Hall and Step Class under one long open roof, a mirror wall |\\n| Guest Huts | (64, 52) | Your hut: sleep ends the day |\\n| South-West Lagoon | (-60, 85) | The Line (headland to rock), Paddle Glide launch |\\n| Sand Terrace | (30, -48) | Sand Garden |\\n| North Cliff | (0, -88), 14 m drop | Cliff Plunge |\\n| Hoop Beach | (62, 84) | Hoop Patrol |\\n| Lighthouse | (84, -60) | Landmark; the storm's beam |\\n| East Terrace | (74, 8) | The \\\"high side\\\" in the finale |\\n| Centre Stone | (0, 0), the summit | A plain stone with a brass plate reading \\\"Do not\\\". The finale ends here |\\n\\n**Cast** (all original, pronouns as given):\\n\\n- **Tare** (it): the mascot and guide. A squat round dial bathroom scale on two stubby legs, face in the dial. Retired\\n  from weighing. Hops beside you. Chirpy, nosy, secretly sad. Keeps the secret of the rock badly.\\n- **Instructor Plumb** (they): head instructor. Tall, narrow, utterly vertical. Pale mint tracksuit, eyes always closed\\n  in two calm arcs, one very long straight plait that has never once moved. Speaks slowly and flatly. In the storm the\\n  plait swings for the first time, and that is the most frightening moment in the game. At dawn Plumb opens their eyes,\\n  once.\\n- **Gerald** (he): a retired guest with immense calves, always already there, always finished. Says only \\\"Morning.\\\"\\n  until Day 4.\\n- **Bex** (they): a bored teenager sent here by a parent, holding a phone-shaped stone, annoyingly excellent.\\n- **Old Nan** (she): 91, Wobble Age 19. Stands where you left her. Nobody has seen her arrive.\\n- **The Gull** and **the Frog** (it): recurring menaces. The Gull lands on you at the worst moment. The Frog just looks.\\n- **You**: \\\"Guest\\\". Pick one of three looks and a tracksuit colour at the pier. No name entry.\\n\\n**The five-day story** (delivered in one-liners, never in walls of text):\\n\\n| Day | Beat |\\n|---|---|\\n| 1 Arrival | Ferry leaves. Tare greets you. First Wobble Age is terrible. Sign: \\\"Please keep to the centre.\\\" |\\n| 2 The Mat | Plaques have moved. \\\"Guests are reminded to distribute themselves evenly.\\\" |\\n| 3 The Water | Drinks slide along tables. A notice calls this \\\"a feature of the drink\\\". |\\n| 4 The Sand | Marbles in the Sand Garden roll with nobody there. Gerald speaks. At night Tare confesses: the island sits on one rock. \\\"We don't mention it to guests. You're a guest. I didn't mention it.\\\" |\\n| 5 The Tilt | Group Class. Then the storm, The Great Tilt (section 7), dawn, the last Morning Check, credits. |\\n| After | \\\"You may stay as long as you like. The ferry does not return.\\\" Free Play, and a fresh Morning Check every in-game day. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. The one verb: the Wobble Model\\n\\nThis is the game's core. Build it first, tune it in dev mode, and reuse it everywhere. It lives in the sim as a\\ncomponent `wobble` on each balancing body, one per seat.\\n\\n**The centre of balance (CoB)** is a point in a unit disc: `x` left to right, `y` back to forward. `r = 1` is the edge:\\npast it you topple.\\n\\nEach step (1/60 s), for each axis:\\n\\n```\\ntarget  = slew(stick + mouse, 4 units/s) × (gentle ? 0.4 : 1) × reach      // clamped to the disc\\naccel   = gain × (target − cob) + instability × cob + noise(t) × (1 − calmEffect × calm) + disturbance\\nvel    += accel × dt;   vel *= exp(−damping × dt);   cob += vel × dt\\n```\\n\\n| Setting | Default | Range | What it does |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `game.wobble.gain` | 14 /s² | 4–30 | How fast your weight follows your thumb |\\n| `game.wobble.instability` | 3 /s² | 0–10 | How hard you fall away from the centre |\\n| `game.wobble.damping` | 5 /s | 1–12 | How heavy the body feels |\\n| `game.wobble.noise` | 3.5 /s² | 0–8 | Sway strength |\\n| `game.wobble.noiseRate` | 0.15 Hz | 0.05–0.4 | Sway speed: a slow push you lean against |\\n| `game.wobble.reach` | 0.9 | 0.5–1 | Full stick's target; a held full stick topples, on purpose |\\n| `game.breath.period` | 8 s | 4–14 | One breath, half in, half out |\\n| `game.breath.calmEffect` | 0.5 | 0–1 | How much full calm quiets the sway |\\n\\nSway per axis, phases and small rate ratios `m` drawn once per seat from a named stream (`w.rng('sway')`), never\\n`Math.random`, and written with plain `Math.sin` so the sim's math swap reaches it:\\n\\n```\\nnoise(t) = ( sin(2π·rate·m1·t + p1) + 0.6·sin(2π·rate·1.7·m2·t + p2) + 0.3·sin(2π·rate·3.1·m3·t + p3) ) / 1.3      // mi in 0.8–1.25\\n```\\n\\n**These numbers are modelled, and the slow sway matters [tested in a small simulation of this exact model, 20 s, 10 seeds,\\nstaying in a ring of 0.22]:** no input 38%; a human-like thumb (250 ms reaction, proportional gain 1.2, a little jitter) 90%;\\na sloppy thumb (350 ms, gain 0.8) 72%; a no-delay bot 100%. A ring of 0.16 drops the thumb to 65%. Off-centre seats out to\\n0.35 hold at 87%, and 0.6 starts to topple (so keep seats within 0.5). **At the 0.45 Hz sway first tried, doing nothing beat\\nthe human thumb,** because a 250 ms reaction turns correction into amplification, so keep the sway slow. Nobody can play by\\nhand here: the delayed-thumb bot (section 16) is how you judge feel.\\n\\nThe universal 4 units/s slew is what makes keyboard feel analog: a quick tap is a small nudge, a held key is a full lean.\\nSticks barely notice it. Mouse adds its own target with a slow decay (section 4).\\n\\n**Topple.** `r > 1` for 6 steps: the body stumbles (`reactTo` flinch, a stumble clip, a creak), the activity decides the\\nprice, and the CoB returns to centre over a second. It is never a game over.\\n\\n**Breath.** The third input is both feet held. A guide ring swells and shrinks with `breath.period`. Holding both feet\\nfills `lungs`; letting go empties them. `sync` is a running match between your lungs and the guide. Good sync raises\\n`calm` (0–1), which quiets the sway, warms the picture slightly, softens the sound, and pays a bonus. Breath is used in\\nstill activities and is the charge mechanic in fast ones. Being out of sync has no penalty beyond losing the help.\\n\\n**Feet.** Left and right foot are the two triggers (analog) or shoulders. Used for steps, rhythm, paddling, jogging and\\none-leg holds. Both together is breath, or a jump in Step Class. That is every input the activities need: **Lean, Left\\nFoot, Right Foot, Both Feet.**\\n\\n**Scoring.** Every activity yields 0–1000 and a rank: 0 **Present**, 300 **Adequate**, 550 **Composed**, 750 **Serene**,\\n900 **Unsettling**. Pebbles earned: 1 to 5 by rank.\\n\\n**No softlocks.** Every activity and every finale step ends by itself: each step has a time box, after which it moves on with\\na remark (\\\"We will call that a start.\\\"). A player who puts the pad down reaches the results screen.\\n\\n**Balance targets the tests enforce** (section 16) on 10 seeds at default settings, in every activity: the perfect bot\\nscores ≥ 750, the human-like delayed thumb ≥ 550, the sloppy thumb ≥ 300, no input at all ≤ 500 and below the human-like\\nthumb. Random mashing never crashes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Controls\\n\\nThe DualSense on a TV is the design target. Keyboard and mouse are native, not stand-ins.\\n\\n| Verb | DualSense | Keyboard | Mouse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Lean (activities) | Left stick (D-pad too) | WASD or arrows; Shift is gentle | Move: pointer-locked movement leans |\\n| Left foot / Right foot | L2 / R2 (L1 / R1 too) | Q / E | Left button / Right button |\\n| Both feet (breathe, jump) | L2 + R2 | Space | Both buttons |\\n| Pause | Options | Esc | |\\n| Walk (island) | Left stick | WASD; Shift walks slowly | |\\n| Look (island) | Right stick | | Move (pointer lock) |\\n| Talk, use, enter | Cross | E or Enter | Left button at the thing in view |\\n| Hop | Square | Space | |\\n| Programme (today's list) | Triangle | Tab | |\\n| Wave | Circle | C | |\\n| Menus | D-pad or stick, Cross, Circle | Arrows, Enter or Space, Esc | Hover moves focus, click picks |\\n\\nActivity-specific mouse feel: in Sand Garden the pointer's place on the tray is the tilt; in Hoop Patrol you circle the\\nmouse; Step Class is left and right click on the beat. On the island the thing at the centre of the screen gets a highlight\\nand its prompt, and left click uses it.\\n\\n**Prompts** follow the input used last (`input.lastDevice`), switching the same frame. Pad: PlayStation glyphs (Cross,\\nCircle, Square, Triangle, L1, R1, L2, R2, sticks) drawn as inline SVG. Settings has \\\"Button icons: PlayStation / Xbox\\\"\\n(A B X Y, LB RB LT RT). Keyboard and mouse: key caps and a mouse icon with the button lit. Never rely on the engine's\\n\",\"total_lines\":1059}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fd732a93-a17b-46c1-b54c-df2b43ea273c-3","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,48,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,47,84,104,117,109,98,32,89,111,103,97,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,115,1