{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_102","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have a solid plan. The scope is large, so I will write code efficiently.\n\nI will check the data formats and settings first. The bench scene will use physics-free component logic for scoring tests. The island scene keeps actors for presentation. Activities step through the scene without physics.\n\nI will spawn and despawn entities during setup and teardown to keep the world clean. I am drafting a shared scene driver with boot and drive functions. The driver queries flow and act components to run the active activity.\n\nThe driver will check game.auto and act.band to decide whether to call the activity bot or use player intents. Tests pass intents directly from bot(), so the scene must not override them. Director mode triggers internal bot calls.\n\nThe director test will step with empty intents and verify credits and the days.ts programme. To test activity.step directly, I will define a probe scene inside the test file that calls morning.step.\n\nThe probe scene will call the shipped morning.step, which delegates to stepBalance. A unit test will instead invoke stepBalance directly on a spawned wobble through a minimal scene. The activity step signature takes World so it can read settings and components. The bot function returns an intents object and score returns a number. Tests will import morning from the events module.\n\nI drafted a headless test loop that runs the morning activity until completion. I realized the engine state is a copy, so bot() cannot access the real world. I need to import headlessHost from the engine app to get the actual world. I am checking whether that path is publicly available for game tests.\n\nExisting game tests already import from `../../../engine` and `../../../engine/sim-api`, so the public API restriction likely does not apply to test files. I am checking whether `headlessHost` is exported from `engine/index`. If it is, the test can retrieve the real world via `headlessHost(engine)` and pass it directly to `bot(w)`. The scene's `game.start` triggers `morning.setup`, while the test independently calls `morning.bot` and `morning.score`.\n\nThe test will not call `morning.step` directly on the host world. Instead it will generate intents with `activity.bot`, pass them to `engine.step`, and let the scene driver invoke `activity.step`. The test will then read the score. The scene's `game.start` already handles setup.\n\nI am weighing whether to call `morning.setup` directly on the host world before stepping, rather than through the `game.start` action. If the test invokes `morning.step` without `engine.step`, the simulation clock will not advance, which could break time-dependent logic. I am reviewing the World API to find the cleanest approach that satisfies the auditor.\n\nThe bench scene step will delegate to a `drive` function that selects the active activity from the flow component and invokes its `step`. The test will validate both paths: it will define a probe scene inside the test file that calls `morning.step` directly, and it will also run through the `game:bench` scene via `game.start` to exercise the shipped driver.\n\nThe auditor requires tests to drive the shipped code on the real path. A probe scene inside the test file that calls the shipped functions satisfies this. The bench scene will serve as the real game simulation without terrain, and the island scene will reuse the same driver. Tests will exercise the full path through `game:bench`, `actions.run('game.start')`, `bot()`, `engine.step`, and `score()`.\n\nI rejected the idea of asserting that `morning.step` equals the catalog function, since that would be a trivial test. Instead, the test loop will drive the shipped functions through `bot()` and `engine.step`, and an explicit test will verify the wiring. I am also considering exporting the shared `drive` function so tests can import and invoke the step functions directly.\n\nI will write a `play` helper that creates a fresh headless engine and calls the activity's setup, step, score, and bot directly. This ensures the test source literally invokes each function, satisfying the auditor's requirement to drive the shipped code without reimplementing or mocking.\n\nI realized that calling `activity.step` directly inside the test loop would double-apply the activity step if the bench scene also invokes it. I am now weighing whether to suppress the scene's automatic step when the test drives it manually, and how the shipped scene path should still function.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0c6bd2a8-a170-4c74-8e75-25a34323418d-14","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"step\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/world.ts","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0c6bd2a8-a170-4c74-8e75-25a34323418d-15","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"tick|settings","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/world.ts","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0c6bd2a8-a170-4c74-8e75-25a34323418d-16","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/scene.ts","offset":1,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5178,"output_tokens":2426,"cache_read_input_tokens":74496,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"8059fafc-58b9-4393-976b-1c1c5ae1d8a2"}
