\":\" * (`jump`, `skill2`) and none is a system action, `move` names four actions of the map and `view` others, `values` keys\"},{\"line_number\":82,\"content\":\"  values: {\"},{\"line_number\":126,\"content\":\"  readonly values: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;\"},{\"line_number\":161,\"content\":\"  for (const [key, action] of Object.entries(map.values)) {\"},{\"line_number\":162,\"content\":\"    if (!/^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*:[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$/.test(key)) problems.push(`values key ${show(key)} must be \\\"game:name\\\"`);\"},{\"line_number\":164,\"content\":\"      problems.push(`values.${key} names ${show(action)}, which actions lacks`);\"},{\"line_number\":188,\"content\":\"  values?: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8c46c9a4-756a-457a-8647-1de44dbe3535-63","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Action maps and presets (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24; doctrine: Common ground): the registry kind `actionMap`, a set\\n * of named actions with the physical codes bound to each (engine/input/codes.ts), as Unity's action maps and Godot's\\n * InputMap hold them; the presets; and the system layer, which no player rebinds.\\n *\\n * An action is a button the sim reads: held actions arrive as the intents' `b`, pressed ones as `p`\\n * (engine/input/intents.ts). The four actions a map names in `move` (forward, back, left, right) are not buttons:\\n * their strengths make the move axes `[right − left, forward − back]`, so keys walk at full speed and a half-pushed\\n * stick at half, and `fromCamera` turns the axes into a world direction. `values` writes an action's analog strength\\n10→ * (a trigger) as a custom intent. `look: true` (first person, the shooter) adds the camera's view direction as `look`,\\n * `aimWith` names the rule that gives the intents' `aim` its point (engine/input/aim.ts: the screen centre's ray, the\\n * pointer's onto the floor, or none; the action `aim`, where a map has one, raises the sights), and `lock: true` takes\\n * the pointer lock on a click so the mouse turns the view (with the cursor free, it points and aims). The actions a\\n * map names in `view` (a camera switch, a view's turn) are the page's: bound and rebound like the others, never\\n * buttons in the intents (`createEngine({ onView })`). A game with several camera modes gives each its own map\\n * (`createEngine({ actionMap })`, WP 13.9).\\n *\\n * The system layer (`SYSTEM_ACTIONS`): pause, and the menu's accept, cancel and directions. It is always active\\n * beside the map, never rebound, and never part of the intents: the app and the UI read it (`input.pressed('pause')`),\\n20→ * so remapping movement never breaks a menu (the lesson of `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md`). `RESERVED_CODES` (the\\n * pause buttons, and keys the browser or system keeps) and a map's own `reserved` codes are refused by rebinding.\\n *\\n * Invariants (`CORE_BAD_SPEC` when broken): every code is valid (`isCode`), action names are lower-case words\\n * (`jump`, `skill2`) and none is a system action, `move` names four actions of the map and `view` others, `values` keys\\n * are namespaced custom intents naming actions of the map, and no action binds a reserved code. The presets are registered on the\\n * shared registry when this module loads.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:670-693` (`Input.DEFAULT`, `PLATFORMER`, `SHMUP`, `MENU_KEYS`) with 3D\\n * movement, and shardfall's layer that is never rebound (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:131-161`).\\n30→ *\\n * @example\\n * const map = getActionMap('actionMap:thirdPerson');\\n * map.actions.jump; // ['Space', 'PadSouth']\\n * map.move; // ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right']\\n * SYSTEM_ACTIONS.pause; // ['Escape', 'PadStart']\\n * listActionMaps().map((entry) => entry.id); // ['actionMap:firstPerson', 'actionMap:platformer', …]\\n * @see engine/input/bindings.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\\n40→import { show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\\nimport { AIM_RULES, type AimRule } from './aim';\\nimport { isCode } from './codes';\\n\\n/** The system layer: action → codes. Always active, never rebound, never in the intents. */\\nexport const SYSTEM_ACTIONS: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>> = Object.freeze({\\n  pause: ['Escape', 'PadStart'],\\n  uiAccept: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Space', 'PadSouth'],\\n  uiCancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'PadEast'],\\n  uiUp: ['ArrowUp', 'PadUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\\n50→  uiDown: ['ArrowDown', 'PadDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\\n  uiLeft: ['ArrowLeft', 'PadLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\\n  uiRight: ['ArrowRight', 'PadRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\\n});\\n\\n/** Codes no action map binds: the pause buttons, and keys the browser or the system keeps. */\\nexport const RESERVED_CODES: readonly string[] = Object.freeze([\\n  'Escape',\\n  'PadStart',\\n  'PadHome',\\n60→  'F5',\\n  'F11',\\n  'F12',\\n  'MetaLeft',\\n  'MetaRight',\\n]);\\n\\n/** The fields of an `actionMap` entry. */\\nconst ACTION_MAP_FIELDS = {\\n  description: { type: 'string', default: '', description: 'What the map is for, in plain words.' },\\n70→  actions: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    required: true,\\n    description:\\n      'Action name → the codes bound to it (KeyboardEvent.code, MouseLeft…, PadSouth…, PadLeftStickUp…): held actions are the intents b, pressed ones p.',\\n  },\\n  move: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right'],\\n80→    description: 'The four actions that walk, as forward, back, left, right: their strengths make the move axes.',\\n  },\\n  values: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: {},\\n    description:\\n      'Custom intent key (\\\"game:throttle\\\") → action: its analog strength (0 to 1, a trigger) is that intent.',\\n  },\\n  look: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n90→    default: false,\\n    description: \\\"True for first person and the shooter: the intents carry look = [the camera's yaw, its pitch].\\\",\\n  },\\n  aimWith: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: AIM_RULES,\\n    default: 'none',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"What the intents' aim holds: none; centre, the point the screen centre's ray meets (first person, the shooter); pointer, the pointer's ray onto the player's floor or a right stick's push (isometric, top-down).\\\",\\n  },\\n100→  lock: {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Action maps and presets (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24; doctrine: Common ground): the registry kind `actionMap`, a set\\n * of named actions with the physical codes bound to each (engine/input/codes.ts), as Unity's action maps and Godot's\\n * InputMap hold them; the presets; and the system layer, which no player rebinds.\\n *\\n * An action is a button the sim reads: held actions arrive as the intents' `b`, pressed ones as `p`\\n * (engine/input/intents.ts). The four actions a map names in `move` (forward, back, left, right) are not buttons:\\n * their strengths make the move axes `[right − left, forward − back]`, so keys walk at full speed and a half-pushed\\n * stick at half, and `fromCamera` turns the axes into a world direction. `values` writes an action's analog strength\\n10→ * (a trigger) as a custom intent. `look: true` (first person, the shooter) adds the camera's view direction as `look`,\\n * `aimWith` names the rule that gives the intents' `aim` its point (engine/input/aim.ts: the screen centre's ray, the\\n * pointer's onto the floor, or none; the action `aim`, where a map has one, raises the sights), and `lock: true` takes\\n * the pointer lock on a click so the mouse turns the view (with the cursor free, it points and aims). The actions a\\n * map names in `view` (a camera switch, a view's turn) are the page's: bound and rebound like the others, never\\n * buttons in the intents (`createEngine({ onView })`). A game with several camera modes gives each its own map\\n * (`createEngine({ actionMap })`, WP 13.9).\\n *\\n * The system layer (`SYSTEM_ACTIONS`): pause, and the menu's accept, cancel and directions. It is always active\\n * beside the map, never rebound, and never part of the intents: the app and the UI read it (`input.pressed('pause')`),\\n20→ * so remapping movement never breaks a menu (the lesson of `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md`). `RESERVED_CODES` (the\\n * pause buttons, and keys the browser or system keeps) and a map's own `reserved` codes are refused by rebinding.\\n *\\n * Invariants (`CORE_BAD_SPEC` when broken): every code is valid (`isCode`), action names are lower-case words\\n * (`jump`, `skill2`) and none is a system action, `move` names four actions of the map and `view` others, `values` keys\\n * are namespaced custom intents naming actions of the map, and no action binds a reserved code. The presets are registered on the\\n * shared registry when this module loads.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:670-693` (`Input.DEFAULT`, `PLATFORMER`, `SHMUP`, `MENU_KEYS`) with 3D\\n * movement, and shardfall's layer that is never rebound (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:131-161`).\\n30→ *\\n * @example\\n * const map = getActionMap('actionMap:thirdPerson');\\n * map.actions.jump; // ['Space', 'PadSouth']\\n * map.move; // ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right']\\n * SYSTEM_ACTIONS.pause; // ['Escape', 'PadStart']\\n * listActionMaps().map((entry) => entry.id); // ['actionMap:firstPerson', 'actionMap:platformer', …]\\n * @see engine/input/bindings.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\\n40→import { show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\\nimport { AIM_RULES, type AimRule } from './aim';\\nimport { isCode } from './codes';\\n\\n/** The system layer: action → codes. Always active, never rebound, never in the intents. */\\nexport const SYSTEM_ACTIONS: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>> = Object.freeze({\\n  pause: ['Escape', 'PadStart'],\\n  uiAccept: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Space', 'PadSouth'],\\n  uiCancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'PadEast'],\\n  uiUp: ['ArrowUp', 'PadUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\\n50→  uiDown: ['ArrowDown', 'PadDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\\n  uiLeft: ['ArrowLeft', 'PadLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\\n  uiRight: ['ArrowRight', 'PadRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\\n});\\n\\n/** Codes no action map binds: the pause buttons, and keys the browser or the system keeps. */\\nexport const RESERVED_CODES: readonly string[] = Object.freeze([\\n  'Escape',\\n  'PadStart',\\n  'PadHome',\\n60→  'F5',\\n  'F11',\\n  'F12',\\n  'MetaLeft',\\n  'MetaRight',\\n]);\\n\\n/** The fields of an `actionMap` entry. */\\nconst ACTION_MAP_FIELDS = {\\n  description: { type: 'string', default: '', description: 'What the map is for, in plain words.' },\\n70→  actions: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    required: true,\\n    description:\\n      'Action name → the codes bound to it (KeyboardEvent.code, MouseLeft…, PadSouth…, PadLeftStickUp…): held actions are the intents b, pressed ones p.',\\n  },\\n  move: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right'],\\n80→    description: 'The four actions that walk, as forward, back, left, right: their strengths make the move axes.',\\n  },\\n  values: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: {},\\n    description:\\n      'Custom intent key (\\\"game:throttle\\\") → action: its analog strength (0 to 1, a trigger) is that intent.',\\n  },\\n  look: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n90→    default: false,\\n    description: \\\"True for first person and the shooter: the intents carry look = [the camera's yaw, its pitch].\\\",\\n  },\\n  aimWith: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: AIM_RULES,\\n    default: 'none',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"What the intents' aim holds: none; centre, the point the screen centre's ray meets (first person, the shooter); pointer, the pointer's ray onto the player's floor or a right stick's push (isometric, top-down).\\\",\\n  },\\n100→  lock: {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/actionMaps.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":100,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file Action maps and presets (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24; doctrine: Common ground): the registry kind `actionMap`, a set\\n * of named actions with the physical codes bound to each (engine/input/codes.ts), as Unity's action maps and Godot's\\n * InputMap hold them; the presets; and the system layer, which no player rebinds.\\n *\\n * An action is a button the sim reads: held actions arrive as the intents' `b`, pressed ones as `p`\\n * (engine/input/intents.ts). The four actions a map names in `move` (forward, back, left, right) are not buttons:\\n * their strengths make the move axes `[right − left, forward − back]`, so keys walk at full speed and a half-pushed\\n * stick at half, and `fromCamera` turns the axes into a world direction. `values` writes an action's analog strength\\n * (a trigger) as a custom intent. `look: true` (first person, the shooter) adds the camera's view direction as `look`,\\n * `aimWith` names the rule that gives the intents' `aim` its point (engine/input/aim.ts: the screen centre's ray, the\\n * pointer's onto the floor, or none; the action `aim`, where a map has one, raises the sights), and `lock: true` takes\\n * the pointer lock on a click so the mouse turns the view (with the cursor free, it points and aims). The actions a\\n * map names in `view` (a camera switch, a view's turn) are the page's: bound and rebound like the others, never\\n * buttons in the intents (`createEngine({ onView })`). A game with several camera modes gives each its own map\\n * (`createEngine({ actionMap })`, WP 13.9).\\n *\\n * The system layer (`SYSTEM_ACTIONS`): pause, and the menu's accept, cancel and directions. It is always active\\n * beside the map, never rebound, and never part of the intents: the app and the UI read it (`input.pressed('pause')`),\\n * so remapping movement never breaks a menu (the lesson of `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md`). `RESERVED_CODES` (the\\n * pause buttons, and keys the browser or system keeps) and a map's own `reserved` codes are refused by rebinding.\\n *\\n * Invariants (`CORE_BAD_SPEC` when broken): every code is valid (`isCode`), action names are lower-case words\\n * (`jump`, `skill2`) and none is a system action, `move` names four actions of the map and `view` others, `values` keys\\n * are namespaced custom intents naming actions of the map, and no action binds a reserved code. The presets are registered on the\\n * shared registry when this module loads.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:670-693` (`Input.DEFAULT`, `PLATFORMER`, `SHMUP`, `MENU_KEYS`) with 3D\\n * movement, and shardfall's layer that is never rebound (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:131-161`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * const map = getActionMap('actionMap:thirdPerson');\\n * map.actions.jump; // ['Space', 'PadSouth']\\n * map.move; // ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right']\\n * SYSTEM_ACTIONS.pause; // ['Escape', 'PadStart']\\n * listActionMaps().map((entry) => entry.id); // ['actionMap:firstPerson', 'actionMap:platformer', …]\\n * @see engine/input/bindings.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\\nimport { show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\\nimport { AIM_RULES, type AimRule } from './aim';\\nimport { isCode } from './codes';\\n\\n/** The system layer: action → codes. Always active, never rebound, never in the intents. */\\nexport const SYSTEM_ACTIONS: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>> = Object.freeze({\\n  pause: ['Escape', 'PadStart'],\\n  uiAccept: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Space', 'PadSouth'],\\n  uiCancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'PadEast'],\\n  uiUp: ['ArrowUp', 'PadUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\\n  uiDown: ['ArrowDown', 'PadDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\\n  uiLeft: ['ArrowLeft', 'PadLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\\n  uiRight: ['ArrowRight', 'PadRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\\n});\\n\\n/** Codes no action map binds: the pause buttons, and keys the browser or the system keeps. */\\nexport const RESERVED_CODES: readonly string[] = Object.freeze([\\n  'Escape',\\n  'PadStart',\\n  'PadHome',\\n  'F5',\\n  'F11',\\n  'F12',\\n  'MetaLeft',\\n  'MetaRight',\\n]);\\n\\n/** The fields of an `actionMap` entry. */\\nconst ACTION_MAP_FIELDS = {\\n  description: { type: 'string', default: '', description: 'What the map is for, in plain words.' },\\n  actions: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    required: true,\\n    description:\\n      'Action name → the codes bound to it (KeyboardEvent.code, MouseLeft…, PadSouth…, PadLeftStickUp…): held actions are the intents b, pressed ones p.',\\n  },\\n  move: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right'],\\n    description: 'The four actions that walk, as forward, back, left, right: their strengths make the move axes.',\\n  },\\n  values: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: {},\\n    description:\\n      'Custom intent key (\\\"game:throttle\\\") → action: its analog strength (0 to 1, a trigger) is that intent.',\\n  },\\n  look: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n    default: false,\\n    description: \\\"True for first person and the shooter: the intents carry look = [the camera's yaw, its pitch].\\\",\\n  },\\n  aimWith: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: AIM_RULES,\\n    default: 'none',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"What the intents' aim holds: none; centre, the point the screen centre's ray meets (first person, the shooter); pointer, the pointer's ray onto the player's floor or a right stick's push (isometric, top-down).\\\",\\n  },\\n  lock: {\\n\",\"total_lines\":275}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f