{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_128","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Held actions arrive as intents.\n\nLean is read from values, not move. Feet are analog values and may appear as held buttons. Act is not in values; it appears in b when held. Tests should pass `b: ['act']` or `game:act: 1`. Space is on both feet.\n\nSpace is uiAccept and is not in intents. PadSouth is act and costs composure in the pond. Mouse buttons map to footl and footr; mouse movement is a virtual axis. Gentle is shift and appears as the held action `gentle`. A `held` helper checks `intents.b` for the given name.\n\nRandom mash will use only known game:* keys and valid action names in b. Custom keys must pass normalizeIntents and match the `game:name` pattern. Arrays are plain data.\n\nStarter files will be deleted once new scenes exist to prevent test failures on old ones. A new golden replay will be recorded after the game works, replacing the old bot.replay.json with --update. npm test runs all **/*.test.ts files.\n\nHeavy tests will be consolidated into a single file to avoid memory exhaustion from parallel workers. Tests within that file run sequentially by default.\n\nThe 600-line hard cap applies to all labs files including tests. Band matrix and director tests will share one file. They will only be split if the file exceeds that limit.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-72c856a0-b1fd-4a84-984c-41d71c604b70-64","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/tools/eslint/simSide.ts","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2897,"output_tokens":879,"cache_read_input_tokens":141568,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"24554871-a6be-4b8b-a888-a40c5fb810eb"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-72c856a0-b1fd-4a84-984c-41d71c604b70-64","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The reproducibility bans for sim-side code (PLAN.md §6.5, Appendix B; doctrine: Reproducible): no clocks, no\\n * unseeded randomness, no DOM, no Web Audio, no three.js, so identical inputs and seeds give identical play in Node\\n * and in Chromium.\\n *\\n * Sim-side means `engine/{core,sim,physics,anim,world}`, `engine/input/intents.ts`, `engine/audio/{dsp,data}`,\\n * `engine/dev/bot.ts` and the gallery's scene (`engine/dev/galleryScene.ts`), every lab's scenes and cast (the box's,\\n * the starter game's, a game's own), the box's and the playground's sound events (labs/box/sounds/events.ts,\\n * labs/playground/sounds/{events,ground}.ts: the scenes' `sounds`), and the fixture scenes; `*.test.ts` files are\\n10→ * exempt. The standard `Math` stays allowed, `Math.sin` and `Math.cos` included:\\n * the sim swaps in fdlibm ports while it steps (§6.5). `core/math.ts` alone imports three.js, for its math\\n * classes (layers.ts limits it to them).\\n *\\n * Beyond Appendix B's list, the same holes in other spellings are closed too: `setImmediate`,\\n * `requestIdleCallback`, `crypto`, `process`, Node's `Buffer`, `location` and Web Storage, all of `performance`\\n * (`timeOrigin` is a wall-clock timestamp), `globalThis.Date`, `self['Date']` and `const { Date } = globalThis`, and\\n * Node built-ins with or without `node:` (sim-side code runs in Chromium as well). Dynamic `import()` is banned\\n * outright, whatever its source: it resolves at a wall-clock moment, and no import rule (layer, three.js, Node) sees\\n * it. No swap reaches an operator or an alias, so `**` and `**=` are banned (write `Math.pow`), and so are `Math`\\n20→ * destructured and a swapped function (engine/core/simMath.ts's `SIM_MATH_NAMES`) held in a variable (ADR-0006\\n * amendment 1).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // engine/sim/spawn.ts: const roll = Math.random();\\n * // → sim/no-restricted-properties: use a named seeded stream: rng('<stream>') …\\n * @see tools/eslint/simSide.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { builtinModules } from 'node:module';\\nimport type { ESLint, Linter } from 'eslint';\\n30→import { SIM_MATH_NAMES } from '../../engine/core/simMath';\\nimport { family } from './family';\\n\\n/** The plugin the sim-side blocks use: core's restriction rules as `sim/<rule>`. */\\nexport const simPlugin: ESLint.Plugin = family(\\n  'sim',\\n  'no-restricted-globals',\\n  'no-restricted-properties',\\n  'no-restricted-syntax',\\n  'no-restricted-imports',\\n40→);\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The reproducibility bans for sim-side code (PLAN.md §6.5, Appendix B; doctrine: Reproducible): no clocks, no\\n * unseeded randomness, no DOM, no Web Audio, no three.js, so identical inputs and seeds give identical play in Node\\n * and in Chromium.\\n *\\n * Sim-side means `engine/{core,sim,physics,anim,world}`, `engine/input/intents.ts`, `engine/audio/{dsp,data}`,\\n * `engine/dev/bot.ts` and the gallery's scene (`engine/dev/galleryScene.ts`), every lab's scenes and cast (the box's,\\n * the starter game's, a game's own), the box's and the playground's sound events (labs/box/sounds/events.ts,\\n * labs/playground/sounds/{events,ground}.ts: the scenes' `sounds`), and the fixture scenes; `*.test.ts` files are\\n10→ * exempt. The standard `Math` stays allowed, `Math.sin` and `Math.cos` included:\\n * the sim swaps in fdlibm ports while it steps (§6.5). `core/math.ts` alone imports three.js, for its math\\n * classes (layers.ts limits it to them).\\n *\\n * Beyond Appendix B's list, the same holes in other spellings are closed too: `setImmediate`,\\n * `requestIdleCallback`, `crypto`, `process`, Node's `Buffer`, `location` and Web Storage, all of `performance`\\n * (`timeOrigin` is a wall-clock timestamp), `globalThis.Date`, `self['Date']` and `const { Date } = globalThis`, and\\n * Node built-ins with or without `node:` (sim-side code runs in Chromium as well). Dynamic `import()` is banned\\n * outright, whatever its source: it resolves at a wall-clock moment, and no import rule (layer, three.js, Node) sees\\n * it. No swap reaches an operator or an alias, so `**` and `**=` are banned (write `Math.pow`), and so are `Math`\\n20→ * destructured and a swapped function (engine/core/simMath.ts's `SIM_MATH_NAMES`) held in a variable (ADR-0006\\n * amendment 1).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // engine/sim/spawn.ts: const roll = Math.random();\\n * // → sim/no-restricted-properties: use a named seeded stream: rng('<stream>') …\\n * @see tools/eslint/simSide.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { builtinModules } from 'node:module';\\nimport type { ESLint, Linter } from 'eslint';\\n30→import { SIM_MATH_NAMES } from '../../engine/core/simMath';\\nimport { family } from './family';\\n\\n/** The plugin the sim-side blocks use: core's restriction rules as `sim/<rule>`. */\\nexport const simPlugin: ESLint.Plugin = family(\\n  'sim',\\n  'no-restricted-globals',\\n  'no-restricted-properties',\\n  'no-restricted-syntax',\\n  'no-restricted-imports',\\n40→);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/tools/eslint/simSide.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The reproducibility bans for sim-side code (PLAN.md §6.5, Appendix B; doctrine: Reproducible): no clocks, no\\n * unseeded randomness, no DOM, no Web Audio, no three.js, so identical inputs and seeds give identical play in Node\\n * and in Chromium.\\n *\\n * Sim-side means `engine/{core,sim,physics,anim,world}`, `engine/input/intents.ts`, `engine/audio/{dsp,data}`,\\n * `engine/dev/bot.ts` and the gallery's scene (`engine/dev/galleryScene.ts`), every lab's scenes and cast (the box's,\\n * the starter game's, a game's own), the box's and the playground's sound events (labs/box/sounds/events.ts,\\n * labs/playground/sounds/{events,ground}.ts: the scenes' `sounds`), and the fixture scenes; `*.test.ts` files are\\n * exempt. The standard `Math` stays allowed, `Math.sin` and `Math.cos` included:\\n * the sim swaps in fdlibm ports while it steps (§6.5). `core/math.ts` alone imports three.js, for its math\\n * classes (layers.ts limits it to them).\\n *\\n * Beyond Appendix B's list, the same holes in other spellings are closed too: `setImmediate`,\\n * `requestIdleCallback`, `crypto`, `process`, Node's `Buffer`, `location` and Web Storage, all of `performance`\\n * (`timeOrigin` is a wall-clock timestamp), `globalThis.Date`, `self['Date']` and `const { Date } = globalThis`, and\\n * Node built-ins with or without `node:` (sim-side code runs in Chromium as well). Dynamic `import()` is banned\\n * outright, whatever its source: it resolves at a wall-clock moment, and no import rule (layer, three.js, Node) sees\\n * it. No swap reaches an operator or an alias, so `**` and `**=` are banned (write `Math.pow`), and so are `Math`\\n * destructured and a swapped function (engine/core/simMath.ts's `SIM_MATH_NAMES`) held in a variable (ADR-0006\\n * amendment 1).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // engine/sim/spawn.ts: const roll = Math.random();\\n * // → sim/no-restricted-properties: use a named seeded stream: rng('<stream>') …\\n * @see tools/eslint/simSide.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { builtinModules } from 'node:module';\\nimport type { ESLint, Linter } from 'eslint';\\nimport { SIM_MATH_NAMES } from '../../engine/core/simMath';\\nimport { family } from './family';\\n\\n/** The plugin the sim-side blocks use: core's restriction rules as `sim/<rule>`. */\\nexport const simPlugin: ESLint.Plugin = family(\\n  'sim',\\n  'no-restricted-globals',\\n  'no-restricted-properties',\\n  'no-restricted-syntax',\\n  'no-restricted-imports',\\n);\\n\",\"total_lines\":172}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"88101a51-2f10-4084-8378-2defb67ced78"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_129","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The simulation code must not use ** or Math.random.\n\nTests are exempt from the restrictions. Math methods will be fully qualified, and `Math.pow` will replace `**` in both simulation and page code. The driver will run scene steps first in the intents phase, then activity steps call `stepBalance` and `remember`, and finish if done. `w.tick` starts at 1 during a step and is 0 before any step.\n\nThe bot sees the previous step's tick between steps, while the director sees the current tick during a step. This one-step timing difference is negligible.\n\nThe activity will store the instability scale on the stick each step. The bot will read that scale from pose data to compute holds.\n\nThe morning reach activity will store its generated targets in an array field `goals` on the activity object. Setup writes coordinate pairs into this array, and mutation during the step is permitted.\n\nFresh `goals` arrays will be passed at spawn to avoid sharing defaults. `clearAct` resets both `goals` and `ring` arrays. Garden holes are drawn from fixed data tables, so they do not need random generation.\n\nA `note` string field will store the current pose or lure identifier. The schema can accommodate many fields. Entity IDs from `w.query` will be used for despawning. The teardown test spawns three entities: flow, act, and island, plus one wobble and one history entity.\n\nTeardown despawns all entities tagged `made` and any wobble seats above zero. Group activities spawn seats 1–3 with the `made` tag, but seat 0 is excluded. Ghosts on the round scene use a `ghost` component and persist independently of the `made` tag. The activity score clamps to 0–1000, so NaN is avoided.\n\nThe pond score formula is `calm * (0.5 + 0.5 * sync)`. Idle calm stays at 1000, so the base score is exactly 500. The sync term is gated by a `breathed` flag to prevent floating-point noise from breaking exact equality.\n\nPenalty values are integers, so the score stays exact even when calm drops. Flags are set only when both is held. A 60-step debounce counts down via act.wait. Lure events fire at random 6–10 second intervals; setup precomputes these step numbers into the goals array. During a step, a matching tick sets the text to the lure id for three seconds before clearing. The fake pause uses the id 'menu' and still increments the tick. Pressing during a lure triggers a penalty if act exceeds 0.5 or the stick passes threshold.\n\nA real pause sends no intents, so the test path steps with empty intents while the menu text persists, the calm score stays unchanged, and the tick still increments. Penalties are skipped for gentle or breath inputs. Stick thresholds use raw values: stick magnitude above 0.25, mouse delta above 0.02, act above 0.5 or held, and a stray foot when left and right foot states differ. Mouse deltas come from the raw game:mouse array; pond checks the un-decayed value this step. Island terrain spans 120 cells at two meters each, giving a 240-meter width, with origin at [-120, y, -120] to center it at zero.\n\nIsland terrain is centered at zero with a 240-meter span. Only hills are generated; ridges are zero and one dome sits at height 11. The plaza is flattened to y≈8. Actors spawn at their feet height, which the placement logic will drop to the ground.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-efec20e4-31e2-4216-a3da-cf49a5e9e240-65","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/siteApi.ts","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1656,"output_tokens":1851,"cache_read_input_tokens":144384,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"9d60ee01-31c1-43f1-b7a5-1b9306c06b99"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-efec20e4-31e2-4216-a3da-cf49a5e9e240-65","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The site part of the public sim API (PLAN.md §6.1, Phase 13, WP 13.13, WP 10.5): every name sim-side game code\\n * takes for levels written as storeys (their 3D queries) and for outdoor ground (the terrain kind, its queries, its\\n * body and its navigation), re-exported whole by engine/sim-api.ts, so that file stays under its line cap, as\\n * engine/sim/movementApi.ts does for movement (ADR-0025 amendment 7). Game code imports these names from\\n * engine/sim-api.ts (or engine/index.ts), never from here: the public-API rule rejects any other engine path.\\n *\\n * Invariants: the same as engine/sim-api.ts's: a flat list of `export … from` lines, one name per line, grouped by\\n * area and append-only; WP 13.15 appends the sites' names. Only sim-side modules are re-exported, and each name is\\n10→ * documented where it is declared.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // labs/playground/scenes/hill.ts\\n * // import { addTerrainBody, defineTerrain, getTerrain } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\n * @see engine/sim-api.ts\\n */\\n\\n// Storeys (WP 13.13): format 2, levels written as storeys, read a storey at a time or in 3D: the highest surface at or\\n// under a point, its storey (by height, or by that surface) and its room.\\n20→export { LEVEL_FORMAT_2 } from '../world/level/types';\\nexport { storeyView } from '../world/level/storeys';\\nexport { floorBelow } from '../world/level/heights';\\nexport { surfaceBelow } from '../world/level/heights';\\nexport { storeyAt } from '../world/level/heights';\\nexport { storeyBelow } from '../world/level/heights';\\nexport { roomAt } from '../world/level/heights';\\nexport type { StoreyDescriptor } from '../world/level/types';\\nexport type { RoomDescriptor } from '../world/level/types';\\nexport type { OpeningDescriptor } from '../world/level/types';\\n30→export type { RoofDescriptor } from '../world/level/types';\\n\\n// Terrain (WP 10.5): the registry kind `terrain`, a seeded heightfield, its queries, its body and its navigation.\\nexport { defineTerrain } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { getTerrain } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { makeTerrain } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { terrainProblems } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { TERRAIN_FIELDS } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport type { Terrain } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport type { TerrainSpec } from '../world/terrain';\\n40→export type { TerrainEntry } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport type { TerrainHill } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport type { TerrainFlat } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { terrainHeight } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { terrainGradient } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { terrainNormal } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { terrainGrade } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { terrainSurface } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { scatterTerrain } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport type { ScatterRule } from '../world/terrain';\\n50→export type { TerrainPlace } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { addTerrainBody } from './levelBodies';\\nexport { terrainNavGrid } from '../world/terrainNav';\\nexport { terrainNavSurface } from '../world/terrainNav';\\nexport type { TerrainNavOptions } from '../world/terrainNav';\\nexport type { NavSurface } from '../world/nav';\\nexport type { NavSource } from '../world/nav';\\n\\n// Sites (WP 13.15): levels standing on a terrain, each placed and turned in quarter turns, the terrain cut under\\n// them; the queries over all of it, the bodies, the ladders and the navigation over every storey and the terrain.\\n60→export { defineSite } from '../world/site';\\nexport { getSite } from '../world/site';\\nexport { makeSite } from '../world/site';\\nexport { SITE_FIELDS } from '../world/site';\\nexport { toWorld } from '../world/site';\\nexport { toLocal } from '../world/site';\\nexport type { Site } from '../world/site';\\nexport type { SiteSpec } from '../world/site';\\nexport type { SiteStructure } from '../world/site';\\nexport type { StructureSpec } from '../world/site';\\n70→export { siteFloorBelow } from '../world/siteQueries';\\nexport { siteSurfaceBelow } from '../world/siteQueries';\\nexport { siteStructureAt } from '../world/siteQueries';\\nexport { siteSolidAt } from '../world/siteQueries';\\nexport { siteClearSight } from '../world/siteQueries';\\nexport { siteRescueGrid } from '../world/siteQueries';\\nexport type { SiteRescueGrid } from '../world/siteQueries';\\nexport { createSiteNav } from '../world/siteNav';\\nexport type { SiteNav } from '../world/siteNav';\\nexport type { SiteNavOptions } from '../world/siteNav';\\n80→export { addSiteBodies } from './levelBodies';\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The site part of the public sim API (PLAN.md §6.1, Phase 13, WP 13.13, WP 10.5): every name sim-side game code\\n * takes for levels written as storeys (their 3D queries) and for outdoor ground (the terrain kind, its queries, its\\n * body and its navigation), re-exported whole by engine/sim-api.ts, so that file stays under its line cap, as\\n * engine/sim/movementApi.ts does for movement (ADR-0025 amendment 7). Game code imports these names from\\n * engine/sim-api.ts (or engine/index.ts), never from here: the public-API rule rejects any other engine path.\\n *\\n * Invariants: the same as engine/sim-api.ts's: a flat list of `export … from` lines, one name per line, grouped by\\n * area and append-only; WP 13.15 appends the sites' names. Only sim-side modules are re-exported, and each name is\\n10→ * documented where it is declared.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // labs/playground/scenes/hill.ts\\n * // import { addTerrainBody, defineTerrain, getTerrain } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\n * @see engine/sim-api.ts\\n */\\n\\n// Storeys (WP 13.13): format 2, levels written as storeys, read a storey at a time or in 3D: the highest surface at or\\n// under a point, its storey (by height, or by that surface) and its room.\\n20→export { LEVEL_FORMAT_2 } from '../world/level/types';\\nexport { storeyView } from '../world/level/storeys';\\nexport { floorBelow } from '../world/level/heights';\\nexport { surfaceBelow } from '../world/level/heights';\\nexport { storeyAt } from '../world/level/heights';\\nexport { storeyBelow } from '../world/level/heights';\\nexport { roomAt } from '../world/level/heights';\\nexport type { StoreyDescriptor } from '../world/level/types';\\nexport type { RoomDescriptor } from '../world/level/types';\\nexport type { OpeningDescriptor } from '../world/level/types';\\n30→export type { RoofDescriptor } from '../world/level/types';\\n\\n// Terrain (WP 10.5): the registry kind `terrain`, a seeded heightfield, its queries, its body and its navigation.\\nexport { defineTerrain } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { getTerrain } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { makeTerrain } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { terrainProblems } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { TERRAIN_FIELDS } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport type { Terrain } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport type { TerrainSpec } from '../world/terrain';\\n40→export type { TerrainEntry } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport type { TerrainHill } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport type { TerrainFlat } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { terrainHeight } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { terrainGradient } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { terrainNormal } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { terrainGrade } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { terrainSurface } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { scatterTerrain } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport type { ScatterRule } from '../world/terrain';\\n50→export type { TerrainPlace } from '../world/terrain';\\nexport { addTerrainBody } from './levelBodies';\\nexport { terrainNavGrid } from '../world/terrainNav';\\nexport { terrainNavSurface } from '../world/terrainNav';\\nexpor