icha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/events/morning.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":96,\"content\":\"export function score(w: World): number {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/events/pose.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":138,\"content\":\"export function score(w: World): number {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/events/group.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":139,\"content\":\"export function score(w: World): number {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/events/line.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":100,\"content\":\"export function score(w: World): number {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/events/paddle.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":74,\"content\":\"export function score(w: World): number {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/events/pond.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":72,\"content\":\"export function score(w: World): number {\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a17f1e37-23cd-430a-bb25-13f93eeabf9b-40","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The sim world (PLAN.md §6.4, §6.5, Q13, WP 1.4, I-03; doctrines: Reproducible, Common ground): entities as\\n * plain objects with monotonic ids, components as plain-data properties of declared kinds (`e.position`), systems\\n * as functions in a fixed order (engine/sim/systems.ts), spawn, despawn and event queues that apply at step\\n * boundaries, named seeded RNG streams, sim-time timers, and the state, hash, trace, capture and restore of all of\\n * it (engine/sim/state.ts, engine/sim/capture.ts). It runs in Node and in a page alike; no ECS framework.\\n *\\n * Entry points: `step(intents)` (the systems of the phase `ai` skipped while the setting `ai.frozen` is on: the dev\\n * action `freeze`), `run(fn)` (setup, dev actions), and `spawn`, `despawn` and `emit` called between steps. Each runs\\n10→ * synchronously inside `withSimMath` (engine/core/simMath.ts), as do `capture`, `restore`, `state`, `hash` and\\n * `trace`: `Math.sin` in a system, timer or listener is the fdlibm port, native again afterwards. Events reach\\n * listeners only through `w.emit` (`w.events` lists, never emits); a step's intents are a frozen copy.\\n *\\n * Invariants (the ordered world, §6.5 item 4): ids count up from 1, never reused in a timeline (a restore rewinds them\\n * with the rest). Entities iterate in id order (engine/sim/entityTable.ts). During an entry point, `spawn`, `despawn` and `emit` queue; at its end (the boundary) the spawns join in id\\n * order, the despawns leave, then the events reach their listeners in emit order, repeated while listeners queue\\n * more (1,000 rounds at most: `SIM_EVENT_STORM`), so a system sees the entities the step began with. `add` and\\n * `remove` act at once; spawn and `add` copy their values and keep components in name order (engine/sim/entities.ts).\\n * During step k (from 1) every phase, timer and listener sees `tick` k, and a timer made in any of them is due from\\n20→ * step k + 1. `hz` is fixed when the world is made (the `time.hz` setting then). A despawned entity's `rng.entity`\\n * streams are dropped (asking again is `SIM_NO_ENTITY`); `fxRng` streams are never hashed or captured. A system that\\n * throws stops the step, which drops what it queued and counts only if its timers stage has run (a throw before it\\n * leaves `tick` as it was and fires no timer).\\n *\\n * Gameplay state lives in components, settings, timers or RNG streams, never in closure or module variables: those\\n * are neither hashed nor captured, so a restore would leave them behind. Hold ids, not entity objects, across steps:\\n * a restore makes new objects; and an id (an entity's or a timer's) kept from a timeline a restore abandoned may name\\n * a new object of the restored one. RNG handles stay valid across restores (engine/core/rng.ts).\\n *\\n30→ * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\\n * import { defineComponent } from './state';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n * defineComponent('position', { description: 'Where.', fields: { x: { type: 'number', default: 0, description: 'East.' } } }, reg);\\n * const w = createWorld<{ position: { x: number } }>({ seed: 1, registry: reg });\\n * w.systems.add('drift', (w) => w.query('position').forEach((e) => (e.position.x += Math.sin(w.time) * w.dt)));\\n * const id = w.spawn({ position: { x: 2 } }); // between steps: it joins at once\\n * w.step({}); // w.get(id)?.position?.x is 2.000…, and w.hash() 16 hex digits, the same on every run\\n * @see engine/sim/world.test.ts\\n40→ */\\nimport { createEvents, type EventMap, type Events } from '../core/events';\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, log as sharedLog, type Log } from '../core/log';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\\nimport { derive, RngStreams, type Rng } from '../core/rng';\\nimport { copyValue, freezeValue, isPlainObject, show } from '../core/schema';\\nimport { createSettings, type Settings, type SimSettings } from '../core/settings';\\nimport { withSimMath } from '../core/simMath';\\nimport { SIM_HZ } from '../core/time';\\nimport { createTimers, type Timers } from '../core/timers';\\n50→import { cloneData, makeCapture, readCapture, scheduleOf, type WorldCapture } from './capture';\\nimport { makeEntity, placeComponent, type LiveEntity } from './entities';\\nimport { createEntityTable } from './entityTable';\\nimport { componentTable, hashState, traceState } from './state';\\nimport type { AnyComponents, Entity, PhysicsHook, SpawnSpec, StateView, With, WorldState, WorldTrace } from './state';\\nimport {\\n  AI_FROZEN,\\n  createSystems,\\n  phaseIndex,\\n  type Intents,\\n60→  type Phase,\\n  type SystemSpec,\\n  type Systems,\\n} from './systems';\\n\\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\\nexport const WORLD_CODES = defineCodes('sim', {\\n  SIM_NO_ENTITY: {\\n    template: 'there is no entity {id}{why}',\\n    fix: 'use an id spawn() returned while its entity lives (w.has(id) tells): a spawned entity joins the world at the end of the step that spawned it, so give it its components in spawn(); a despawned one leaves at the end of its step',\\n70→  },\\n  SIM_BUSY: {\\n    template: '{what} was called during a step',\\n    fix: 'call step(), run(), capture() and restore() between steps; inside a system, change the world directly (spawn, despawn and emit queue to the end of the step)',\\n  },\\n  SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT: {\\n    template: '{where} got {value}',\\n    fix: 'pass {expected}',\\n    doc: 'Raised by the world (engine/sim/world.ts) for a seed or step rate that is not a number of the right kind, a spawn that is not a plain object of components, or an `id` given among the components.',\\n  },\\n80→  SIM_EVENT_STORM: {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The sim world (PLAN.md §6.4, §6.5, Q13, WP 1.4, I-03; doctrines: Reproducible, Common ground): entities as\\n * plain objects with monotonic ids, components as plain-data properties of declared kinds (`e.position`), systems\\n * as functions in a fixed order (engine/sim/systems.ts), spawn, despawn and event queues that apply at step\\n * boundaries, named seeded RNG streams, sim-time timers, and the state, hash, trace, capture and restore of all of\\n * it (engine/sim/state.ts, engine/sim/capture.ts). It runs in Node and in a page alike; no ECS framework.\\n *\\n * Entry points: `step(intents)` (the systems of the phase `ai` skipped while the setting `ai.frozen` is on: the dev\\n * action `freeze`), `run(fn)` (setup, dev actions), and `spawn`, `despawn` and `emit` called between steps. Each runs\\n10→ * synchronously inside `withSimMath` (engine/core/simMath.ts), as do `capture`, `restore`, `state`, `hash` and\\n * `trace`: `Math.sin` in a system, timer or listener is the fdlibm port, native again afterwards. Events reach\\n * listeners only through `w.emit` (`w.events` lists, never emits); a step's intents are a frozen copy.\\n *\\n * Invariants (the ordered world, §6.5 item 4): ids count up from 1, never reused in a timeline (a restore rewinds them\\n * with the rest). Entities iterate in id order (engine/sim/entityTable.ts). During an entry point, `spawn`, `despawn` and `emit` queue; at its end (the boundary) the spawns join in id\\n * order, the despawns leave, then the events reach their listeners in emit order, repeated while listeners queue\\n * more (1,000 rounds at most: `SIM_EVENT_STORM`), so a system sees the entities the step began with. `add` and\\n * `remove` act at once; spawn and `add` copy their values and keep components in name order (engine/sim/entities.ts).\\n * During step k (from 1) every phase, timer and listener sees `tick` k, and a timer made in any of them is due from\\n20→ * step k + 1. `hz` is fixed when the world is made (the `time.hz` setting then). A despawned entity's `rng.entity`\\n * streams are dropped (asking again is `SIM_NO_ENTITY`); `fxRng` streams are never hashed or captured. A system that\\n * throws stops the step, which drops what it queued and counts only if its timers stage has run (a throw before it\\n * leaves `tick` as it was and fires no timer).\\n *\\n * Gameplay state lives in components, settings, timers or RNG streams, never in closure or module variables: those\\n * are neither hashed nor captured, so a restore would leave them behind. Hold ids, not entity objects, across steps:\\n * a restore makes new objects; and an id (an entity's or a timer's) kept from a timeline a restore abandoned may name\\n * a new object of the restored one. RNG handles stay valid across restores (engine/core/rng.ts).\\n *\\n30→ * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\\n * import { defineComponent } from './state';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n * defineComponent('position', { description: 'Where.', fields: { x: { type: 'number', default: 0, description: 'East.' } } }, reg);\\n * const w = createWorld<{ position: { x: number } }>({ seed: 1, registry: reg });\\n * w.systems.add('drift', (w) => w.query('position').forEach((e) => (e.position.x += Math.sin(w.time) * w.dt)));\\n * const id = w.spawn({ position: { x: 2 } }); // between steps: it joins at once\\n * w.step({}); // w.get(id)?.position?.x is 2.000…, and w.hash() 16 hex digits, the same on every run\\n * @see engine/sim/world.test.ts\\n40→ */\\nimport { createEvents, type EventMap, type Events } from '../core/events';\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, log as sharedLog, type Log } from '../core/log';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\\nimport { derive, RngStreams, type Rng } from '../core/rng';\\nimport { copyValue, freezeValue, isPlainObject, show } from '../core/schema';\\nimport { createSettings, type Settings, type SimSettings } from '../core/settings';\\nimport { withSimMath } from '../core/simMath';\\nimport { SIM_HZ } from '../core/time';\\nimport { createTimers, type Timers } from '../core/timers';\\n50→import { cloneData, makeCapture, readCapture, scheduleOf, type WorldCapture } from './capture';\\nimport { makeEntity, placeComponent, type LiveEntity } from './entities';\\nimport { createEntityTable } from './entityTable';\\nimport { componentTable, hashState, traceState } from './state';\\nimport type { AnyComponents, Entity, PhysicsHook, SpawnSpec, StateView, With, WorldState, WorldTrace } from './state';\\nimport {\\n  AI_FROZEN,\\n  createSystems,\\n  phaseIndex,\\n  type Intents,\\n60→  type Phase,\\n  type SystemSpec,\\n  type Systems,\\n} from './systems';\\n\\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\\nexport const WORLD_CODES = defineCodes('sim', {\\n  SIM_NO_ENTITY: {\\n    template: 'there is no entity {id}{why}',\\n    fix: 'use an id spawn() returned while its entity lives (w.has(id) tells): a spawned entity joins the world at the end of the step that spawned it, so give it its components in spawn(); a despawned one leaves at the end of its step',\\n70→  },\\n  SIM_BUSY: {\\n    template: '{what} was called during a step',\\n    fix: 'call step(), run(), capture() and restore() between steps; inside a system, change the world directly (spawn, despawn and emit queue to the end of the step)',\\n  },\\n  SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT: {\\n    template: '{where} got {value}',\\n    fix: 'pass {expected}',\\n    doc: 'Raised by the world (engine/sim/world.ts) for a seed or step rate that is not a number of the right kind, a spawn that is not a plain object of components, or an `id` given among the components.',\\n  },\\n80→  SIM_EVENT_STORM: {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/world.ts\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The sim world (PLAN.md §6.4, §6.5, Q13, WP 1.4, I-03; doctrines: Reproducible, Common ground): entities as\\n * plain objects with monotonic ids, components as plain-data properties of declared kinds (`e.position`), systems\\n * as functions in a fixed order (engine/sim/systems.ts), spawn, despawn and event queues that apply at step\\n * boundaries, named seeded RNG streams, sim-time timers, and the state, hash, trace, capture and restore of all of\\n * it (engine/sim/state.ts, engine/sim/capture.ts). It runs in Node and in a page alike; no ECS framework.\\n *\\n * Entry points: `step(intents)` (the systems of the phase `ai` skipped while the setting `ai.frozen` is on: the dev\\n * action `freeze`), `run(fn)` (setup, dev actions), and `spawn`, `despawn` and `emit` called between steps. Each runs\\n * synchronously inside `withSimMath` (engine/core/simMath.ts), as do `capture`, `restore`, `state`, `hash` and\\n * `trace`: `Math.sin` in a system, timer or listener is the fdlibm port, native again afterwards. Events reach\\n * listeners only through `w.emit` (`w.events` lists, never emits); a step's intents are a frozen copy.\\n *\\n * Invariants (the ordered world, §6.5 item 4): ids count up from 1, never reused in a timeline (a restore rewinds them\\n * with the rest). Entities iterate in id order (engine/sim/entityTable.ts). During an entry point, `spawn`, `despawn` and `emit` queue; at its end (the boundary) the spawns join in id\\n * order, the despawns leave, then the events reach their listeners in emit order, repeated while listeners queue\\n * more (1,000 rounds at most: `SIM_EVENT_STORM`), so a system sees the entities the step began with. `add` and\\n * `remove` act at once; spawn and `add` copy their values and keep components in name order (engine/sim/entities.ts).\\n * During step k (from 1) every phase, timer and listener sees `tick` k, and a timer made in any of them is due from\\n * step k + 1. `hz` is fixed when the world is made (the `time.hz` setting then). A despawned entity's `rng.entity`\\n * streams are dropped (asking again is `SIM_NO_ENTITY`); `fxRng` streams are never hashed or captured. A system that\\n * throws stops the step, which drops what it queued and counts only if its timers stage has run (a throw before it\\n * leaves `tick` as it was and fires no timer).\\n *\\n * Gameplay state lives in components, settings, timers or RNG streams, never in closure or module variables: those\\n * are neither hashed nor captured, so a restore would leave them behind. Hold ids, not entity objects, across steps:\\n * a restore makes new objects; and an id (an entity's or a timer's) kept from a timeline a restore abandoned may name\\n * a new object of the restored one. RNG handles stay valid across restores (engine/core/rng.ts).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\\n * import { defineComponent } from './state';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n * defineComponent('position', { description: 'Where.', fields: { x: { type: 'number', default: 0, description: 'East.' } } }, reg);\\n * const w = createWorld<{ position: { x: number } }>({ seed: 1, registry: reg });\\n * w.systems.add('drift', (w) => w.query('position').forEach((e) => (e.position.x += Math.sin(w.time) * w.dt)));\\n * const id = w.spawn({ position: { x: 2 } }); // between steps: it joins at once\\n * w.step({}); // w.get(id)?.position?.x is 2.000…, and w.hash() 16 hex digits, the same on every run\\n * @see engine/sim/world.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { createEvents, type EventMap, type Events } from '../core/events';\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, log as sharedLog, type Log } from '../core/log';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\\nimport { derive, RngStreams, type Rng } from '../core/rng';\\nimport { copyValue, freezeValue, isPlainObject, show } from '../core/schema';\\nimport { createSettings, type Settings, type SimSettings } from '../core/settings';\\nimport { withSimMath } from '../core/simMath';\\nimport { SIM_HZ } from '../core/time';\\nimport { createTimers, type Timers } from '../core/timers';\\nimport { cloneData, makeCapture, readCapture, scheduleOf, type WorldCapture } from './capture';\\nimport { makeEntity, placeComponent, type LiveEntity } from './entities';\\nimport { createEntityTable } from './entityTable';\\nimport { componentTable, hashState, traceState } from './state';\\nimport type { AnyComponents, Entity, PhysicsHook, SpawnSpec, StateView, With, WorldState, WorldTrace } from './state';\\nimport {\\n  AI_FROZEN,\\n  createSystems,\\n  phaseIndex,\\n  type Intents,\\n  type Phase,\\n  type SystemSpec,\\n  type Systems,\\n} from './systems';\\n\\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\\nexport const WORLD_CODES = defineCodes('sim', {\\n  SIM_NO_ENTITY: {\\n    template: 'there is no entity {id}{why}',\\n    fix: 'use an id spawn() returned while its entity lives (w.has(id) tells): a spawned entity joins the world at the end of the step that spawned it, so give it its components in spawn(); a despawned one leaves at the end of its step',\\n  },\\n  SIM_BUSY: {\\n    template: '{what} was called during a step',\\n    fix: 'call step(), run(), capture() and restore() between steps; inside a system, change the world directly (spawn, despawn and emit queue to the end of the step)',\\n  },\\n  SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT: {\\n    template: '{where} got {value}',\\n    fix: 'pass {expected}',\\n    doc: 'Raised by the world (engine/sim/world.ts) for a seed or step rate that is not a number of the right kind, a spawn that is not a plain object of components, or an `id` given among the components.',\\n  },\\n  SIM_EVENT_STORM: {\\n\",\"total_lines\":394}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"7ce84771-10f3-46c2-8d85-5e756e201284"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_157","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Score depends on tick for line, garden, and paddle.\n\nI'll use `flow` for the results timer. `act.vx` might be unused in garden. I won't use `prior` or `wait`.\n\n`act.wait` is safe for the results countdown. It will be set to 0 at finish and incremented each results frame. `tick` will not be reset.\n\nI need to confirm that `w.time` exists on World. Between steps, `w.tick` holds the last completed step, which matches bot behavior.\n\ndrawSway spawns wobble without a seat field, defaulting to 0. Group setup re-seeds sway for CPU seats after boot, so the order remains deterministic.\n\nstartEvent must run between steps, but finishEvent triggers it during a step. Spawns inside startEvent queue to the boundary and appear at the end of that step.\n\nfinishEvent teardown despawns entities during the step. startEvent spawns new ones in the same step. Both queue to the boundary, so despawn and spawn may apply together.\n\nWorld comments confirm despawns leave and spawns join in id order. A step's query sees only entities present at its start, so teardown sweeps old guests without touching new ones. This cleanly separates old and new entities.\n\n`world.run` is an entry point, so spawns inside it queue until the end of `run()`. The first group step therefore sees CPU seats 1–3 only after setup completes.\n\nI'll add a `cfgOf` attract cheat. I'm defining a `BeginArgs` interface for `game.begin` with fields like day, cursor, pebbles, age, prior, seen, credits, rank, and result.\n\nIf credits is 1, the game enters free-roam mode without restarting the story. A new daily check still runs via `game.start` morning. If a cursor is provided, the game starts that programme item unless it is evening or credits.\n\nA director test script runs the full cycle from morning through credits. It verifies that every activity is visited, including all tilt steps, both pose classes, evening, and the final morning. The test checks seen flags and credits after the credits screen stops. Island base state updates on sleep.\n\nHuman play will start with auto off, so `game.begin` immediately triggers the first activity and the pad reaches credits without walking. The results screen waits for `game.carry`, while evening waits for `game.sleep`; the page will call these from menus. A human test can also enable auto director. If a saved cursor points to pose-a, `begin` starts that activity directly.\n\nThe `begin` function maps each `BeginArgs` field directly onto the flow state.\n\n`begin` derives the island base from `flow.day` and sets both `base` and `tiltX`. If credits are active it enters free-roam mode. Otherwise it resolves the programme item at the cursor and opens evening, credits, or starts the event. I also began writing `game.start`.\n\n`game.start` accepts an optional event argument and calls `startEvent` without advancing the cursor. It handles evening and credits events directly, while unknown IDs throw.\n\n`openAttract` sets mode to event, resets the cursor to zero, and starts the first slice.\n\nThe page triggers attract by setting `game.auto` and calling `inspector.seed`, which reboots the world. The boot sequence should detect `auto === 'attract'` and begin the loop.\n\nBoot auto-starting director or attract would double-start if `game.begin` also runs. The test sets `auto` in headless settings and calls `begin`, so either boot-on-auto or begin is acceptable for the shipped path.\n\nBoot will auto-start the director programme when `game.auto` is set to director, letting tests step directly without calling `begin`. `game.begin` remains for human play and save restoration. A real player sees the title screen because auto is off by default.\n\nBoot auto-starts the director programme from item 0 or the attract slice when `game.auto` is set to director or attract. Spawns during scene setup queue until setup ends, so drawSway, the flow entity, and activity spawns all exist before step 1. The order of queued spawns is preserved. However, calling startEvent during boot triggers rowOf, which queries wobble.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-236e9c64-0f85-4cb2-8d02-a6df75548adb-41","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"scene\\.setup|world\\.run","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/session.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-236e9c64-0f85-4cb2-8d02-a6df75548adb-42","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"setup\\(world|scene\\.setup","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim","glob":"**/*.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9751,"output_tokens":2553,"cache_read_input_tokens":86656,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"95ac1922-5b3c-4b94-833d-3eedae5014f3"}
