'game:charge'`). Devices (WP 3.3) make intents; the sim only reads them.\"},{\"line_number\":44,\"content\":\"  INPUT_BAD_INTENTS: {\"},{\"line_number\":46,\"content\":\"    fix: 'give intents as { move: [x, z], cam, aim: [x, y, z], look: [yaw, pitch], b: [held buttons], p: [pressed buttons] } with finite numbers, plus custom keys namespaced \\\"game:key\\\" holding plain data (engine/input/intents.ts); null or a missing key means not given',\"},{\"line_number\":54,\"content\":\"/** A namespaced key for game code's own intents: `'game:charge'`. */\"},{\"line_number\":92,\"content\":\"/** A namespaced key: a lower-case word, a colon, a name. */\"},{\"line_number\":95,\"content\":\"/** The namespaced key a bad one most likely means: `'Game:x'` → `'game:x'`, `'charge'` → `'game:charge'`. */\"},{\"line_number\":153,\"content\":\" * `INPUT_BAD_INTENTS` listing every problem. `null` and `undefined` values mean \\\"not given\\\".\"},{\"line_number\":157,\"content\":\"    throw codeError('INPUT_BAD_INTENTS', { where, problems: `they are ${show(raw)}; intents are an object` });\"},{\"line_number\":168,\"content\":\"        `unknown key ${show(key)}${didYouMean(key, Object.keys(INTENT_KEYS))} (custom keys are namespaced: \\\"${customKey(key)}\\\")`,\"},{\"line_number\":182,\"content\":\"  if (problems.length) throw codeError('INPUT_BAD_INTENTS', { where, problems: problems.join('; ') });\"},{\"line_number\":252,\"content\":\" * as the step before, so `p` is the change's presses plus the new edges of `b`. Throws `INPUT_BAD_INTENTS`.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"a9bc52a9-4d3c-4e18-913a-591476a3e5d2"}
