{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_184","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Vitest ran from the workspace root instead of the dev folder because the shell's current directory is the workspace.\n\nTests passed in 9 seconds from the work root. Morning bands scored correctly across 10 seeds. The installed vitest version is 4.1.12 but v5.1.0 executed.\n\nThe test passed functionally. The workspace path is the work root, so vitest resolved from a parent directory. I should run from the dev folder to use the project's vitest 4 and its config. The 9-second runtime equals roughly 85 microseconds per step.\n\nThe full matrix would take roughly 3.5 to 8 minutes. Tilt and group tests may be slower due to queries. I will run from the dev folder so node resolution uses its node_modules and vite config.\n\nRelative imports resolved correctly from the work root. Morning bands passed across all categories including idle scoring below human baseline. I will run the remaining band tests from the dev folder next, excluding director for now.\n\nDirector tests may take about a minute. I will run the band tests first, then director. The command targets bands with verbose reporter and includes morning again. Total runtime could be 4 to 8 minutes. I will check the skill for long jobs before proceeding.\n\nI will wait up to ten minutes for the tests to finish in this call. I will run bands, mash, Wobble, setup calls, and balance together in one vitest process to avoid memory issues. Director is excluded.\n\nI will launch the band suite in the background with block_until_ms set to zero so I can keep reading activity code while it runs. I need to read the skill before starting this long background job.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Morning Check clears every band. Next I’ll run the other activities on the same sim and fix whatever falls short."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-973dc215-a5dc-4069-b2dc-61c3a303e6d2-79","