{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_211","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to understand the core engine functions and data structures. These include spawnActor, defineTerrain, defineClipSet, defineProp, createEngine, action maps, menu items, store, and how the page reads the world.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dd4acd3e-a25d-42c5-a69a-9c7702131fa9-11","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/actionMaps.ts","offset":1,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dd4acd3e-a25d-42c5-a69a-9c7702131fa9-12","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/actors.ts","offset":180,"limit":90}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dd4acd3e-a25d-42c5-a69a-9c7702131fa9-13","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"export function (spawnActor|defineProp|spawnProp|defineTerrain|defineClipSet|addTerrainBody)","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dd4acd3e-a25d-42c5-a69a-9c7702131fa9-14","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"## (10|11|12|Verification|Lines|Island|Audio|About)","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/PLAN.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4102,"output_tokens":434,"cache_read_input_tokens":43776,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"5adf1367-f029-431a-a416-e468451127d1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-dd4acd3e-a25d-42c5-a69a-9c7702131fa9-11","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Action maps and presets (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24; doctrine: Common ground): the registry kind `actionMap`, a set\\n * of named actions with the physical codes bound to each (engine/input/codes.ts), as Unity's action maps and Godot's\\n * InputMap hold them; the presets; and the system layer, which no player rebinds.\\n *\\n * An action is a button the sim reads: held actions arrive as the intents' `b`, pressed ones as `p`\\n * (engine/input/intents.ts). The four actions a map names in `move` (forward, back, left, right) are not buttons:\\n * their strengths make the move axes `[right − left, forward − back]`, so keys walk at full speed and a half-pushed\\n * stick at half, and `fromCamera` turns the axes into a world direction. `values` writes an action's analog strength\\n10→ * (a trigger) as a custom intent. `look: true` (first person, the shooter) adds the camera's view direction as `look`,\\n * `aimWith` names the rule that gives the intents' `aim` its point (engine/input/aim.ts: the screen centre's ray, the\\n * pointer's onto the floor, or none; the action `aim`, where a map has one, raises the sights), and `lock: true` takes\\n * the pointer lock on a click so the mouse turns the view (with the cursor free, it points and aims). The actions a\\n * map names in `view` (a camera switch, a view's turn) are the page's: bound and rebound like the others, never\\n * buttons in the intents (`createEngine({ onView })`). A game with several camera modes gives each its own map\\n * (`createEngine({ actionMap })`, WP 13.9).\\n *\\n * The system layer (`SYSTEM_ACTIONS`): pause, and the menu's accept, cancel and directions. It is always active\\n * beside the map, never rebound, and never part of the intents: the app and the UI read it (`input.pressed('pause')`),\\n20→ * so remapping movement never breaks a menu (the lesson of `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md`). `RESERVED_CODES` (the\\n * pause buttons, and keys the browser or system keeps) and a map's own `reserved` codes are refused by rebinding.\\n *\\n * Invariants (`CORE_BAD_SPEC` when broken): every code is valid (`isCode`), action names are lower-case words\\n * (`jump`, `skill2`) and none is a system action, `move` names four actions of the map and `view` others, `values` keys\\n * are namespaced custom intents naming actions of the map, and no action binds a reserved code. The presets are registered on the\\n * shared registry when this module loads.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:670-693` (`Input.DEFAULT`, `PLATFORMER`, `SHMUP`, `MENU_KEYS`) with 3D\\n * movement, and shardfall's layer that is never rebound (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:131-161`).\\n30→ *\\n * @example\\n * const map = getActionMap('actionMap:thirdPerson');\\n * map.actions.jump; // ['Space', 'PadSouth']\\n * map.move; // ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right']\\n * SYSTEM_ACTIONS.pause; // ['Escape', 'PadStart']\\n * listActionMaps().map((entry) => entry.id); // ['actionMap:firstPerson', 'actionMap:platformer', …]\\n * @see engine/input/bindings.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\\n40→import { show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\\nimport { AIM_RULES, type AimRule } from './aim';\\nimport { isCode } from './codes';\\n\\n/** The system layer: action → codes. Always active, never rebound, never in the intents. */\\nexport const SYSTEM_ACTIONS: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>> = Object.freeze({\\n  pause: ['Escape', 'PadStart'],\\n  uiAccept: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Space', 'PadSouth'],\\n  uiCancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'PadEast'],\\n  uiUp: ['ArrowUp', 'PadUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\\n50→  uiDown: ['ArrowDown', 'PadDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\\n  uiLeft: ['ArrowLeft', 'PadLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\\n  uiRight: ['ArrowRight', 'PadRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\\n});\\n\\n/** Codes no action map binds: the pause buttons, and keys the browser or the system keeps. */\\nexport const RESERVED_CODES: readonly string[] = Object.freeze([\\n  'Escape',\\n  'PadStart',\\n  'PadHome',\\n60→  'F5',\\n  'F11',\\n  'F12',\\n  'MetaLeft',\\n  'MetaRight',\\n]);\\n\\n/** The fields of an `actionMap` entry. */\\nconst ACTION_MAP_FIELDS = {\\n  description: { type: 'string', default: '', description: 'What the map is for, in plain words.' },\\n70→  actions: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    required: true,\\n    description:\\n      'Action name → the codes bound to it (KeyboardEvent.code, MouseLeft…, PadSouth…, PadLeftStickUp…): held actions are the intents b, pressed ones p.',\\n  },\\n  move: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right'],\\n80→    description: 'The four actions that walk, as forward, back, left, right: their strengths make the move axes.',\\n  },\\n  values: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: {},\\n    description:\\n      'Custom intent key (\\\"game:throttle\\\") → action: its analog strength (0 to 1, a trigger) is that intent.',\\n  },\\n  look: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n90→    default: false,\\n    description: \\\"True for first person and the shooter: the intents carry look = [the camera's yaw, its pitch].\\\",\\n  },\\n  aimWith: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: AIM_RULES,\\n    default: 'none',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"What the intents' aim holds: none; centre, the point the screen centre's ray meets (first person, the shooter); pointer, the pointer's ray onto the player's floor or a right stick's push (isometric, top-down).\\\",\\n  },\\n100→  lock: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n    default: false,\\n    description:\\n      'True when the mouse turns the view: a click on the game takes the pointer lock, which pause and Escape give back.',\\n  },\\n  view: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: [],\\n110→    description:\\n      \\\"Actions the page reads for its view (a camera switch, a view's turn): bound and rebound like the others, never buttons in the intents.\\\",\\n  },\\n  reserved: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: [],\\n    description: 'Codes the game keeps for its own hotkeys: rebinding refuses them, as it refuses RESERVED_CODES.',\\n  },\\n} as const satisfies Schema;\\n120→\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Action maps and presets (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24; doctrine: Common ground): the registry kind `actionMap`, a set\\n * of named actions with the physical codes bound to each (engine/input/codes.ts), as Unity's action maps and Godot's\\n * InputMap hold them; the presets; and the system layer, which no player rebinds.\\n *\\n * An action is a button the sim reads: held actions arrive as the intents' `b`, pressed ones as `p`\\n * (engine/input/intents.ts). The four actions a map names in `move` (forward, back, left, right) are not buttons:\\n * their strengths make the move axes `[right − left, forward − back]`, so keys walk at full speed and a half-pushed\\n * stick at half, and `fromCamera` turns the axes into a world direction. `values` writes an action's analog strength\\n10→ * (a trigger) as a custom intent. `look: true` (first person, the shooter) adds the camera's view direction as `look`,\\n * `aimWith` names the rule that gives the intents' `aim` its point (engine/input/aim.ts: the screen centre's ray, the\\n * pointer's onto the floor, or none; the action `aim`, where a map has one, raises the sights), and `lock: true` takes\\n * the pointer lock on a click so the mouse turns the view (with the cursor free, it points and aims). The actions a\\n * map names in `view` (a camera switch, a view's turn) are the page's: bound and rebound like the others, never\\n * buttons in the intents (`createEngine({ onView })`). A game with several camera modes gives each its own map\\n * (`createEngine({ actionMap })`, WP 13.9).\\n *\\n * The system layer (`SYSTEM_ACTIONS`): pause, and the menu's accept, cancel and directions. It is always active\\n * beside the map, never rebound, and never part of the intents: the app and the UI read it (`input.pressed('pause')`),\\n20→ * so remapping movement never breaks a menu (the lesson of `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md`). `RESERVED_CODES` (the\\n * pause buttons, and keys the browser or system keeps) and a map's own `reserved` codes are refused by rebinding.\\n *\\n * Invariants (`CORE_BAD_SPEC` when broken): every code is valid (`isCode`), action names are lower-case words\\n * (`jump`, `skill2`) and none is a system action, `move` names four actions of the map and `view` others, `values` keys\\n * are namespaced custom intents naming actions of the map, and no action binds a reserved code. The presets are registered on the\\n * shared registry when this module loads.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:670-693` (`Input.DEFAULT`, `PLATFORMER`, `SHMUP`, `MENU_KEYS`) with 3D\\n * movement, and shardfall's layer that is never rebound (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:131-161`).\\n30→ *\\n * @example\\n * const map = getActionMap('actionMap:thirdPerson');\\n * map.actions.jump; // ['Space', 'PadSouth']\\n * map.move; // ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right']\\n * SYSTEM_ACTIONS.pause; // ['Escape', 'PadStart']\\n * listActionMaps().map((entry) => entry.id); // ['actionMap:firstPerson', 'actionMap:platformer', …]\\n * @see engine/input/bindings.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\\n40→import { show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\\nimport { AIM_RULES, type AimRule } from './aim';\\nimport { isCode } from './codes';\\n\\n/** The system layer: action → codes. Always active, never rebound, never in the intents. */\\nexport const SYSTEM_ACTIONS: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>> = Object.freeze({\\n  pause: ['Escape', 'PadStart'],\\n  uiAccept: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Space', 'PadSouth'],\\n  uiCancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'PadEast'],\\n  uiUp: ['ArrowUp', 'PadUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\\n50→  uiDown: ['ArrowDown', 'PadDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\\n  uiLeft: ['ArrowLeft', 'PadLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\\n  uiRight: ['ArrowRight', 'PadRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\\n});\\n\\n/** Codes no action map binds: the pause buttons, and keys the browser or the system keeps. */\\nexport const RESERVED_CODES: readonly string[] = Object.freeze([\\n  'Escape',\\n  'PadStart',\\n  'PadHome',\\n60→  'F5',\\n  'F11',\\n  'F12',\\n  'MetaLeft',\\n  'MetaRight',\\n]);\\n\\n/** The fields of an `actionMap` entry. */\\nconst ACTION_MAP_FIELDS = {\\n  description: { type: 'string', default: '', description: 'What the map is for, in plain words.' },\\n70→  actions: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    required: true,\\n    description:\\n      'Action name → the codes bound to it (KeyboardEvent.code, MouseLeft…, PadSouth…, PadLeftStickUp…): held actions are the intents b, pressed ones p.',\\n  },\\n  move: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right'],\\n80→    description: 'The four actions that walk, as forward, back, left, right: their strengths make the move axes.',\\n  },\\n  values: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: {},\\n    description:\\n      'Custom intent key (\\\"game:throttle\\\") → action: its analog strength (0 to 1, a trigger) is that intent.',\\n  },\\n  look: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n90→    default: false,\\n    description: \\\"True for first person and the shooter: the intents carry look = [the camera's yaw, its pitch].\\\",\\n  },\\n  aimWith: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: AIM_RULES,\\n    default: 'none',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"What the intents' aim holds: none; centre, the point the screen centre's ray meets (first person, the shooter); pointer, the pointer's ray onto the player's floor or a right stick's push (isometric, top-down).\\\",\\n  },\\n100→  lock: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n    default: false,\\n    description:\\n      'True when the mouse turns the view: a click on the game takes the pointer lock, which pause and Escape give back.',\\n  },\\n  view: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: [],\\n110→    description:\\n      \\\"Actions the page reads for its view (a camera switch, a view's turn): bound and rebound like the others, never buttons in the intents.\\\",\\n  },\\n  reserved: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: [],\\n    description: 'Codes the game keeps for its own hotkeys: rebinding refuses them, as it refuses RESERVED_CODES.',\\n  },\\n} as const satisfies Schema;\\n120→\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/actionMaps.ts\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file Action maps and presets (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24; doctrine: Common ground): the registry kind `actionMap`, a set\\n * of named actions with the physical codes bound to each (engine/input/codes.ts), as Unity's action maps and Godot's\\n * InputMap hold them; the presets; and the system layer, which no player rebinds.\\n *\\n * An action is a button the sim reads: held actions arrive as the intents' `b`, pressed ones as `p`\\n * (engine/input/intents.ts). The four actions a map names in `move` (forward, back, left, right) are not buttons:\\n * their strengths make the move axes `[right − left, forward − back]`, so keys walk at full speed and a half-pushed\\n * stick at half, and `fromCamera` turns the axes into a world direction. `values` writes an action's analog strength\\n * (a trigger) as a custom intent. `look: true` (first person, the shooter) adds the camera's view direction as `look`,\\n * `aimWith` names the rule that gives the intents' `aim` its point (engine/input/aim.ts: the screen centre's ray, the\\n * pointer's onto the floor, or none; the action `aim`, where a map has one, raises the sights), and `lock: true` takes\\n * the pointer lock on a click so the mouse turns the view (with the cursor free, it points and aims). The actions a\\n * map names in `view` (a camera switch, a view's turn) are the page's: bound and rebound like the others, never\\n * buttons in the intents (`createEngine({ onView })`). A game with several camera modes gives each its own map\\n * (`createEngine({ actionMap })`, WP 13.9).\\n *\\n * The system layer (`SYSTEM_ACTIONS`): pause, and the menu's accept, cancel and directions. It is always active\\n * beside the map, never rebound, and never part of the intents: the app and the UI read it (`input.pressed('pause')`),\\n * so remapping movement never breaks a menu (the lesson of `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md`). `RESERVED_CODES` (the\\n * pause buttons, and keys the browser or system keeps) and a map's own `reserved` codes are refused by rebinding.\\n *\\n * Invariants (`CORE_BAD_SPEC` when broken): every code is valid (`isCode`), action names are lower-case words\\n * (`jump`, `skill2`) and none is a system action, `move` names four actions of the map and `view` others, `values` keys\\n * are namespaced custom intents naming actions of the map, and no action binds a reserved code. The presets are registered on the\\n * shared registry when this module loads.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:670-693` (`Input.DEFAULT`, `PLATFORMER`, `SHMUP`, `MENU_KEYS`) with 3D\\n * movement, and shardfall's layer that is never rebound (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:131-161`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * const map = getActionMap('actionMap:thirdPerson');\\n * map.actions.jump; // ['Space', 'PadSouth']\\n * map.move; // ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right']\\n * SYSTEM_ACTIONS.pause; // ['Escape', 'PadStart']\\n * listActionMaps().map((entry) => entry.id); // ['actionMap:firstPerson', 'actionMap:platformer', …]\\n * @see engine/input/bindings.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\\nimport { show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\\nimport { AIM_RULES, type AimRule } from './aim';\\nimport { isCode } from './codes';\\n\\n/** The system layer: action → codes. Always active, never rebound, never in the intents. */\\nexport const SYSTEM_ACTIONS: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>> = Object.freeze({\\n  pause: ['Escape', 'PadStart'],\\n  uiAccept: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Space', 'PadSouth'],\\n  uiCancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'PadEast'],\\n  uiUp: ['ArrowUp', 'PadUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\\n  uiDown: ['ArrowDown', 'PadDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\\n  uiLeft: ['ArrowLeft', 'PadLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\\n  uiRight: ['ArrowRight', 'PadRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\\n});\\n\\n/** Codes no action map binds: the pause buttons, and keys the browser or the system keeps. */\\nexport const RESERVED_CODES: readonly string[] = Object.freeze([\\n  'Escape',\\n  'PadStart',\\n  'PadHome',\\n  'F5',\\n  'F11',\\n  'F12',\\n  'MetaLeft',\\n  'MetaRight',\\n]);\\n\\n/** The fields of an `actionMap` entry. */\\nconst ACTION_MAP_FIELDS = {\\n  description: { type: 'string', default: '', description: 'What the map is for, in plain words.' },\\n  actions: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    required: true,\\n    description:\\n      'Action name → the codes bound to it (KeyboardEvent.code, MouseLeft…, PadSouth…, PadLeftStickUp…): held actions are the intents b, pressed ones p.',\\n  },\\n  move: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right'],\\n    description: 'The four actions that walk, as forward, back, left, right: their strengths make the move axes.',\\n  },\\n  values: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: {},\\n    description:\\n      'Custom intent key (\\\"game:throttle\\\") → action: its analog strength (0 to 1, a trigger) is that intent.',\\n  },\\n  look: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n    default: false,\\n    description: \\\"True for first person and the shooter: the intents carry look = [the camera's yaw, its pitch].\\\",\\n  },\\n  aimWith: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: AIM_RULES,\\n    default: 'none',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"What the intents' aim holds: none; centre, the point the screen centre's ray meets (first person, the shooter); pointer, the pointer's ray onto the player's floor or a right stick's push (isometric, top-down).\\\",\\n  },\\n  lock: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n    default: false,\\n    description:\\n      'True when the mouse turns the view: a click on the game takes the pointer lock, which pause and Escape give back.',\\n  },\\n  view: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: [],\\n    description:\\n      \\\"Actions the page reads for its view (a camera switch, a view's turn): bound and rebound like the others, never buttons in the intents.\\\",\\n  },\\n  reserved: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: [],\\n    description: 'Codes the game keeps for its own hotkeys: rebinding refuses them, as it refuses RESERVED_CODES.',\\n  },\\n} as const satisfies Schema;\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":275}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-dd4acd3e-a25d-42c5-a69a-9c7702131fa9-12","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"180→    },\\n    registry,\\n  );\\n  defineComponent(\\n    'oneWay',\\n    {\\n      description: 'Makes a body a one-way platform: solid only to an actor whose feet are at or above its top.',\\n      fields: { body: { type: 'integer', default: -1, minimum: -1, description: 'The platform’s body.' } },\\n    },\\n    registry,\\n190→  );\\n}\\ndefineActorKinds();\\n\\n/** What `spawnActor` takes. */\\nexport interface ActorSpec {\\n  /** Where its feet go: on the ground below them (it starts just above, outside the skin). */\\n  at: Vec3Like;\\n  /** Its settings (createCharacter). */\\n  character: Character;\\n200→  /** Whether it reads the step's intents (true); false: its AI writes `actor.intents`. */\\n  player?: boolean;\\n  /** Where it faces (rad; forward = (sin yaw, 0, cos yaw)). */\\n  yaw?: number;\\n  /** Its character animator's make (engine/anim/character.ts); none when absent. */\\n  anim?: Pick<AnimatorOptions, 'build' | 'weapon' | 'preciseHits'>;\\n  /** The body it is drawn as (`body:mannequin`), with `anim`; the neutral humanoid when absent. */\\n  body?: string;\\n  /** With `anim`, the clip layer in its animator, playing from these sets (engine/sim/actorClips.ts); none when absent. */\\n  clips?: ClipsSpec;\\n210→  /** With a movement model, whether it starts with no weapon out (true: the model's holstered speeds). */\\n  holstered?: boolean;\\n  /**\\n   * Further components it spawns with, by name (its `reactions`, its `secondary`: engine/sim/reactions.ts), so they\\n   * are there from its first step, and a page's first warm-up builds what they draw.\\n   */\\n  components?: Readonly<Record<string, object>>;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n220→ * Spawns an actor in a scene with a physics world: its body, and an entity with the component `actor`. Returns the id.\\n * An actor on a movement model (engine/physics/movement/, WP 13.3) also holds `motion`, the model's state (holstered\\n * unless spawned `holstered: false`), and reads `sprint` (held, pressed), `walk` and `crouch` (held), `crouchToggle`\\n * (pressed), the view from `look`, the keys' frame from `cam` (else `look`) and what it faces from `aim` (else\\n * `look`), under the live `movement.*` settings (WP 13.4); WP 13.7: the look's pitch and `interact` (pressed) too,\\n * riding the scene's ziplines and ladders (engine/sim/rides.ts); WP 13.9: a player's sprint held only while held with\\n * `input.sprint` at `hold`, and his crouch toggled by its press with `input.crouch` at `toggle`.\\n */\\nexport function spawnActor<C extends object>(world: World<C>, spec: ActorSpec): number {\\n  const w = world as unknown as World;\\n230→  const physics = physicsOf(w);\\n  const body = addCharacter(physics, spec.character, spec.at);\\n  const { x, y, z } = feetOf(physics, body, spec.character);\\n  const state = { ...createCharacterState(), yaw: spec.yaw ?? 0 };\\n  if (!w.systems.has('actors')) {\\n    w.systems.add('actors', moveActors, { phase: 'anim' });\\n    w.systems.add('actors.readback', readActors, { phase: 'readback' });\\n  }\\n  const actor = { body, player: spec.player ?? true, character: spec.character, x, y, z, ...state };\\n  const motion = spec.character.movement ? { motion: { ...createMotionState(), holstered: spec.holstered ?? true } } : {}; // prettier-ignore\\n240→  if (!spec.anim) return w.spawn({ ...spec.components, ...motion, actor });\\n  if (!w.systems.has('actors.anim')) {\\n    w.systems.add('actors.anim', stepAnimators, { phase: 'anim' });\\n    w.systems.add('actors.pose', poseAnimators, { phase: 'readback' });\\n  }\\n  const { build = 'build:chibi', weapon = 'none', preciseHits = false } = spec.anim;\\n  const animator = { build: typeof build === 'string' ? build : build.id, weapon, preciseHits };\\n  const puppet = spec.body !== undefined ? { body: spec.body } : undefined;\\n  const clips = spec.clips && (clipsFor(w, spec.clips, animator.build) as unknown as Record<string, unknown>);\\n  return w.spawn({ ...spec.components, ...motion, actor, animator, puppet, clips });\\n250→}\\n\\n/**\\n * Puts actor `id` at `at`, its feet on the ground below (just above, outside the skin, as a spawn stands it), facing\\n * `yaw` (its own when absent), at rest: no velocity, no jump, dash or landing pending, standing (its hull too); on the\\n * shooter model its motion state starts again, holstered as it was, or ducked with `crouch`, its hull crouched from its\\n * next step on and kept so until it has headroom, for a place no standing hull fits (a crawlspace). A place where the\\n * level (the queries' as of the last step, one-way platforms aside) stands over its feet lower than its hull's top, up\\n * its axis, throws `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` before it moves anything: the body would sink through the floor. For a scene's dev actions: a feel\\n * course places its player where it measures (engine/dev/feel/course.ts).\\n260→ */\\nexport function placeActor<C extends object>(\\n  world: World<C>,\\n  id: number,\\n  at: Vec3Like,\\n  yaw?: number,\\n  options: { crouch?: boolean } = {},\\n): void {\\n  const w = world as unknown as World;\\n  const e = w.get(id) as Partial<ActorComponents> | undefined;\",\"content_concise\":\"180→    },\\n    registry,\\n  );\\n  defineComponent(\\n    'oneWay',\\n    {\\n      description: 'Makes a body a one-way platform: solid only to an actor whose feet are at or above its top.',\\n      fields: { body: { type: 'integer', default: -1, minimum: -1, description: 'The platform’s body.' } },\\n    },\\n    registry,\\n190→  );\\n}\\ndefineActorKinds();\\n\\n/** What `spawnActor` takes. */\\nexport interface ActorSpec {\\n  /** Where its feet go: on the ground below them (it starts just above, outside the skin). */\\n  at: Vec3Like;\\n  /** Its settings (createCharacter). */\\n  character: Character;\\n200→  /** Whether it reads the step's intents (true); false: its AI writes `actor.intents`. */\\n  player?: boolean;\\n  /** Where it faces (rad; forward = (sin yaw, 0, cos yaw)). */\\n  yaw?: number;\\n  /** Its character animator's make (engine/anim/character.ts); none when absent. */\\n  anim?: Pick<AnimatorOptions, 'build' | 'weapon' | 'preciseHits'>;\\n  /** The body it is drawn as (`body:mannequin`), with `anim`; the neutral humanoid when absent. */\\n  body?: string;\\n  /** With `anim`, the clip layer in its animator, playing from these sets (engine/sim/actorClips.ts); none when absent. */\\n  clips?: ClipsSpec;\\n210→  /** With a movement model, whether it starts with no weapon out (true: the model's holstered speeds). */\\n  holstered?: boolean;\\n  /**\\n   * Further components it spawns with, by name (its `reactions`, its `secondary`: engine/sim/reactions.ts), so they\\n   * are there from its first step, and a page's first warm-up builds what they draw.\\n   */\\n  components?: Readonly<Record<string, object>>;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n220→ * Spawns an actor in a scene with a physics world: its body, and an entity with the component `actor`. Returns the id.\\n * An actor on a movement model (engine/physics/movement/, WP 13.3) also holds `motion`, the model's state (holstered\\n * unless spawned `holstered: false`), and reads `sprint` (held, pressed), `walk` and `crouch` (held), `crouchToggle`\\n * (pressed), the view from `look`, the keys' frame from `cam` (else `look`) and what it faces from `aim` (else\\n * `look`), under the live `movement.*` settings (WP 13.4); WP 13.7: the look's pitch and `interact` (pressed) too,\\n * riding the scene's ziplines and ladders (engine/sim/rides.ts); WP 13.9: a player's sprint held only while held with\\n * `input.sprint` at `hold`, and his crouch toggled by its press with `input.crouch` at `toggle`.\\n */\\nexport function spawnActor<C extends object>(world: World<C>, spec: ActorSpec): number {\\n  const w = world as unknown as World;\\n230→  const physics = physicsOf(w);\\n  const body = addCharacter(physics, spec.character, spec.at);\\n  const { x, y, z } = feetOf(physics, body, spec.character);\\n  const state = { ...createCharacterState(), yaw: spec.yaw ?? 0 };\\n  if (!w.systems.has('actors')) {\\n    w.systems.add('actors', moveActors, { phase: 'anim' });\\n    w.systems.add('actors.readback', readActors, { phase: 'readback' });\\n  }\\n  const actor = { body, player: spec.player ?? true, character: spec.character, x, y, z, ...state };\\n  const motion = spec.character.movement ? { motion: { ...createMotionState(), holstered: spec.holstered ?? true } } : {}; // prettier-ignore\\n240→  if (!spec.anim) return w.spawn({ ...spec.components, ...motion, actor });\\n  if (!w.systems.has('actors.anim')) {\\n    w.systems.add('actors.anim', stepAnimators, { phase: 'anim' });\\n    w.systems.add('actors.pose', poseAnimators, { phase: 'readback' });\\n  }\\n  const { build = 'build:chibi', weapon = 'none', preciseHits = false } = spec.anim;\\n  const animator = { build: typeof build === 'string' ? build : build.id, weapon, preciseHits };\\n  const puppet = spec.body !== undefined ? { body: spec.body } : undefined;\\n  const clips = spec.clips && (clipsFor(w, spec.clips, animator.build) as unknown as Record<string, unknown>);\\n  return w.spawn({ ...spec.components, ...motion, actor, animator, puppet, clips });\\n250→}\\n\\n/**\\n * Puts actor `id` at `at`, its feet on the ground below (just above, outside the skin, as a spawn stands it), facing\\n * `yaw` (its own when absent), at rest: no velocity, no jump, dash or landing pending, standing (its hull too); on the\\n * shooter model its motion state starts again, holstered as it was, or ducked with `crouch`, its hull crouched from its\\n * next step on and kept so until it has headroom, for a place no standing hull fits (a crawlspace). A place where the\\n * level (the queries' as of the last step, one-way platforms aside) stands over its feet lower than its hull's top, up\\n * its axis, throws `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` before it moves anything: the body would sink through the floor. For a scene's dev actions: a feel\\n * course places its player where it measures (engine/dev/feel/course.ts).\\n260→ */\\nexport function placeActor<C extends object>(\\n  world: World<C>,\\n  id: number,\\n  at: Vec3Like,\\n  yaw?: number,\\n  options: { crouch?: boolean } = {},\\n): void {\\n  const w = world as unknown as World;\\n  const e = w.get(id) as Partial<ActorComponents> | undefined;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-