{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_212","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A full island terrain scene would be too heavy and error-prone. A simpler approach is preferable.\n\nI will check how defineScene handles terrain and review PLAN sections 10-12, the verification plan, and TASK.md requirements. The remaining work breaks down into six songs, over two hundred lines, about data, cast clips, and a modest island scene booting the driver with terrain.\n\nThe island scene will use marks instead of physics actors for pebbles, plaques, and sea. A small round scene with ghosts and mats is also planned. main.ts must check WebGPU, strip the aihub query, connect the hub, create the engine, set audio volume, configure action maps, menus, attract mode, saves, glyphs, dev sliders, and touch gating. This is a large codebase.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-94ca9882-7b4f-4308-9fda-743cfc3b1a07-15","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/main.ts","limit":250}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-94ca9882-7b4f-4308-9fda-743cfc3b1a07-16","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"export (async )?function createEngine|export interface EngineOptions|cameraInput|actionMap|onFrame|modal","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/app/engine.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-94ca9882-7b4f-4308-9fda-743cfc3b1a07-17","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/ui/menu.ts","offset":1,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-94ca9882-7b4f-4308-9fda-743cfc3b1a07-18","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/PLAN.md","offset":630,"limit":220}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4334,"output_tokens":742,"cache_read_input_tokens":47872,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"f8c04326-6258-481e-9028-09f31a01de54"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-94ca9882-7b4f-4308-9fda-743cfc3b1a07-15","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The starter game's page (labs/game/index.html): it starts the engine (`createEngine`, engine/app/engine.ts) on\\n * the scene `game:play` (labs/game/scenes/play.ts) with the arena's text registered for the view, offers the bot's\\n * replay to `?replay=bot`, and shows the round each drawn frame in the HTML/CSS overlay's HUD: the gems, the clock,\\n * the controls, the best round kept across sessions (labs/game/best.ts, through the engine's store) and, when the\\n * round ends, how it ended. Enter then starts a new round on the next seed. Escape (or the pad's Start) pauses the\\n * round under a menu (`createMenu`: Resume, New round), which keeps its keys out of play while it is open\\n * (`createEngine({ modal })`); the store keeps the best round and any keys rebound (`createEngine({ store })`). The\\n * camera is the chase camera unless the URL names one (`?cam=iso`, `?cam3=orbit`).\\n10→ *\\n * Everything else a page does (routes, the renderer, the frame loop, the devices, `window.__engine`, the error\\n * overlay, the touch controls) is the engine's, so this file is the game's own presentation only. It reads the run\\n * and never changes it: the HUD cannot change the hash.\\n *\\n * Game code: it imports only the engine's public API (engine/index.ts) and the game's own files.\\n *\\n * Open it at http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (`npm run dev`): `?seed=7&game.gems=20` plays another round,\\n * `?replay=bot` the bot's, `?cam=iso` another camera. Headless, `node x shot labs/game` reports what it draws.\\n */\\n20→/// <reference types=\\\"vite/client\\\" />\\nimport { createEngine, createMenu, createStore, type Engine, type EngineFrame, type Menu } from '../../engine';\\nimport { bestOf, recordBest } from './best';\\nimport { ARENA_TEXT, play, type Round } from './scenes/play';\\n\\n/** The page's query, with the chase camera when it names none: it follows the player round the arena. */\\nconst search = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\nif (!search.has('cam') && !search.has('cam3')) search.set('cam3', 'chase');\\n\\n/** The game's replays, by name (`?replay=bot`), as text loaded on demand. */\\n30→const replays = { bot: () => import('./replays/bot.replay.json?raw').then((module) => module.default) };\\n\\n/** The started engine; null until `createEngine` resolves (its first frames are drawn before that). */\\nlet engine: Engine | null = null;\\n\\n/** Whether the round on screen has ended, so Enter starts the next. */\\nlet ended = false;\\n\\n/** The game's store: its best round across sessions; a replay's page plays in its demo mode, so it sets none. */\\nconst store = createStore({ prefix: 'my3dge-game:', mode: search.has('replay') ? 'demo' : 'play' });\\n40→\\n/** The fastest won round kept (s), and the run whose clock the page saw running, with the steps it started with. */\\nlet best = bestOf(store);\\nlet seen: { world: object; steps: number } | null = null;\\n\\n/** The pause menu while it is open; null while the round plays. */\\nlet paused: Menu | null = null;\\n\\n/** Opens the pause menu over the paused round, or reads it a frame: Resume (or Escape again), New round. */\\nfunction pauseMenu(dt: number): void {\\n50→  const [inspector, ui, input] = [engine?.inspector, engine?.ui, engine?.input];\\n  if (!inspector || !ui || !input) return;\\n  const close = () => {\\n    paused?.remove();\\n    paused = null;\\n    inspector.resume();\\n  };\\n  if (paused) return void paused.update(dt);\\n  if (!input.pressed('pause')) return;\\n  inspector.pause();\\n60→  const items = [\\n    { label: 'Resume', id: 'resume' },\\n    { label: 'New round', id: 'new' },\\n  ];\\n  paused = createMenu(ui.root, items, { input, id: 'pause', title: 'Paused', onCancel: close, onPick: (_i, item) => {\\n    if (typeof item === 'object' && item.id === 'new') inspector.seed(inspector.seed() + 1);\\n    close();\\n  } }); // prettier-ignore\\n}\\n\\n70→/** Shows the round in the HUD: the gems, the clock, the controls, and how the round ended. */\\nfunction showRound({ world }: EngineFrame): void {\\n  const ui = engine?.ui;\\n  const entity = world.query('round')[0] as unknown as { round: Round } | undefined;\\n  if (!ui || !entity) return;\\n  const { gems, collected, left, state } = entity.round;\\n  if (seen?.world !== world) seen = state === 'playing' ? { world, steps: left + world.tick } : null;\\n  const was = ended;\\n  ui.hud('gems', `Gems ${collected} / ${gems}`, { at: 'top-left' });\\n  ui.hud('clock', `${Math.ceil(left / world.hz)} s`, { at: 'top-right', color: left < 10 * world.hz ? '#ff8f6b' : '' });\\n80→  ui.hud('keys', 'WASD: run · Space: jump · Shift: dash · Esc: pause', { at: 'bottom', keys: true });\\n  ended = state !== 'playing';\\n  if (ended && !was && state === 'won' && seen) best = recordBest(store, (seen.steps - left) / world.hz);\\n  ui.hud('best', best === null ? null : `Best ${best.toFixed(1)} s`, { at: 'top-left' });\\n  const end = state === 'won' ? 'Every gem! Enter: play again' : 'Time! Enter: play again';\\n  ui.hud('end', ended ? end : null, { at: 'top' });\\n}\\n\\nengine = await createEngine({\\n  canvas: document.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('#view')!,\\n90→  scenes: [play.id],\\n  levels: { 'level:arena': { text: ARENA_TEXT, file: 'labs/game/scenes/play.ts' } },\\n  replays,\\n  search: `?${search}`,\\n  store,\\n  modal: () => paused !== null,\\n  onFrame: (frame) => {\\n    pauseMenu(frame.dt);\\n    showRound(frame);\\n  },\\n100→});\\n\\naddEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\\n  const inspector = engine?.inspector;\\n  if (event.code === 'Enter' && ended && inspector) inspector.seed(inspector.seed() + 1);\\n});\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The starter game's page (labs/game/index.html): it starts the engine (`createEngine`, engine/app/engine.ts) on\\n * the scene `game:play` (labs/game/scenes/play.ts) with the arena's text registered for the view, offers the bot's\\n * replay to `?replay=bot`, and shows the round each drawn frame in the HTML/CSS overlay's HUD: the gems, the clock,\\n * the controls, the best round kept across sessions (labs/game/best.ts, through the engine's store) and, when the\\n * round ends, how it ended. Enter then starts a new round on the next seed. Escape (or the pad's Start) pauses the\\n * round under a menu (`createMenu`: Resume, New round), which keeps its keys out of play while it is open\\n * (`createEngine({ modal })`); the store keeps the best round and any keys rebound (`createEngine({ store })`). The\\n * camera is the chase camera unless the URL names one (`?cam=iso`, `?cam3=orbit`).\\n10→ *\\n * Everything else a page does (routes, the renderer, the frame loop, the devices, `window.__engine`, the error\\n * overlay, the touch controls) is the engine's, so this file is the game's own presentation only. It reads the run\\n * and never changes it: the HUD cannot change the hash.\\n *\\n * Game code: it imports only the engine's public API (engine/index.ts) and the game's own files.\\n *\\n * Open it at http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (`npm run dev`): `?seed=7&game.gems=20` plays another round,\\n * `?replay=bot` the bot's, `?cam=iso` another camera. Headless, `node x shot labs/game` reports what it draws.\\n */\\n20→/// <reference types=\\\"vite/client\\\" />\\nimport { createEngine, createMenu, createStore, type Engine, type EngineFrame, type Menu } from '../../engine';\\nimport { bestOf, recordBest } from './best';\\nimport { ARENA_TEXT, play, type Round } from './scenes/play';\\n\\n/** The page's query, with the chase camera when it names none: it follows the player round the arena. */\\nconst search = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\nif (!search.has('cam') && !search.has('cam3')) search.set('cam3', 'chase');\\n\\n/** The game's replays, by name (`?replay=bot`), as text loaded on demand. */\\n30→const replays = { bot: () => import('./replays/bot.replay.json?raw').then((module) => module.default) };\\n\\n/** The started engine; null until `createEngine` resolves (its first frames are drawn before that). */\\nlet engine: Engine | null = null;\\n\\n/** Whether the round on screen has ended, so Enter starts the next. */\\nlet ended = false;\\n\\n/** The game's store: its best round across sessions; a replay's page plays in its demo mode, so it sets none. */\\nconst store = createStore({ prefix: 'my3dge-game:', mode: search.has('replay') ? 'demo' : 'play' });\\n40→\\n/** The fastest won round kept (s), and the run whose clock the page saw running, with the steps it started with. */\\nlet best = bestOf(store);\\nlet seen: { world: object; steps: number } | null = null;\\n\\n/** The pause menu while it is open; null while the round plays. */\\nlet paused: Menu | null = null;\\n\\n/** Opens the pause menu over the paused round, or reads it a frame: Resume (or Escape again), New round. */\\nfunction pauseMenu(dt: number): void {\\n50→  const [inspector, ui, input] = [engine?.inspector, engine?.ui, engine?.input];\\n  if (!inspector || !ui || !input) return;\\n  const close = () => {\\n    paused?.remove();\\n    paused = null;\\n    inspector.resume();\\n  };\\n  if (paused) return void paused.update(dt);\\n  if (!input.pressed('pause')) return;\\n  inspector.pause();\\n60→  const items = [\\n    { label: 'Resume', id: 'resume' },\\n    { label: 'New round', id: 'new' },\\n  ];\\n  paused = createMenu(ui.root, items, { input, id: 'pause', title: 'Paused', onCancel: close, onPick: (_i, item) => {\\n    if (typeof item === 'object' && item.id === 'new') inspector.seed(inspector.seed() + 1);\\n    close();\\n  } }); // prettier-ignore\\n}\\n\\n70→/** Shows the round in the HUD: the gems, the clock, the controls, and how the round ended. */\\nfunction showRound({ world }: EngineFrame): void {\\n  const ui = engine?.ui;\\n  const entity = world.query('round')[0] as unknown as { round: Round } | undefined;\\n  if (!ui || !entity) return;\\n  const { gems, collected, left, state } = entity.round;\\n  if (seen?.world !== world) seen = state === 'playing' ? { world, steps: left + world.tick } : null;\\n  const was = ended;\\n  ui.hud('gems', `Gems ${collected} / ${gems}`, { at: 'top-left' });\\n  ui.hud('clock', `${Math.ceil(left / world.hz)} s`, { at: 'top-right', color: left < 10 * world.hz ? '#ff8f6b' : '' });\\n80→  ui.hud('keys', 'WASD: run · Space: jump · Shift: dash · Esc: pause', { at: 'bottom', keys: true });\\n  ended = state !== 'playing';\\n  if (ended && !was && state === 'won' && seen) best = recordBest(store, (seen.steps - left) / world.hz);\\n  ui.hud('best', best === null ? null : `Best ${best.toFixed(1)} s`, { at: 'top-left' });\\n  const end = state === 'won' ? 'Every gem! Enter: play again' : 'Time! Enter: play again';\\n  ui.hud('end', ended ? end : null, { at: 'top' });\\n}\\n\\nengine = await createEngine({\\n  canvas: document.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('#view')!,\\n90→  scenes: [play.id],\\n  levels: { 'level:arena': { text: ARENA_TEXT, file: 'labs/game/scenes/play.ts' } },\\n  replays,\\n  search: `?${search}`,\\n  store,\\n  modal: () => paused !== null,\\n  onFrame: (frame) => {\\n    pauseMenu(frame.dt);\\n    showRound(frame);\\n  },\\n100→});\\n\\naddEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\\n  const inspector = engine?.inspector;\\n  if (event.code === 'Enter' && ended && inspector) inspector.seed(inspector.seed() + 1);\\n});\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/main.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":250,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The starter game's page (labs/game/index.html): it starts the engine (`createEngine`, engine/app/engine.ts) on\\n * the scene `game:play` (labs/game/scenes/play.ts) with the arena's text registered for the view, offers the bot's\\n * replay to `?replay=bot`, and shows the round each drawn frame in the HTML/CSS overlay's HUD: the gems, the clock,\\n * the controls, the best round kept across sessions (labs/game/best.ts, through the engine's store) and, when the\\n * round ends, how it ended. Enter then starts a new round on the next seed. Escape (or the pad's Start) pauses the\\n * round under a menu (`createMenu`: Resume, New round), which keeps its keys out of play while it is open\\n * (`createEngine({ modal })`); the store keeps the best round and any keys rebound (`createEngine({ store })`). The\\n * camera is the chase camera unless the URL names one (`?cam=iso`, `?cam3=orbit`).\\n *\\n * Everything else a page does (routes, the renderer, the frame loop, the devices, `window.__engine`, the error\\n * overlay, the touch controls) is the engine's, so this file is the game's own presentation only. It reads the run\\n * and never changes it: the HUD cannot change the hash.\\n *\\n * Game code: it imports only the engine's public API (engine/index.ts) and the game's own files.\\n *\\n * Open it at http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (`npm run dev`): `?seed=7&game.gems=20` plays another round,\\n * `?replay=bot` the bot's, `?cam=iso` another camera. Headless, `node x shot labs/game` reports what it draws.\\n */\\n/// <reference types=\\\"vite/client\\\" />\\nimport { createEngine, createMenu, createStore, type Engine, type EngineFrame, type Menu } from '../../engine';\\nimport { bestOf, recordBest } from './best';\\nimport { ARENA_TEXT, play, type Round } from './scenes/play';\\n\\n/** The page's query, with the chase camera when it names none: it follows the player round the arena. */\\nconst search = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\nif (!search.has('cam') && !search.has('cam3')) search.set('cam3', 'chase');\\n\\n/** The game's replays, by name (`?replay=bot`), as text loaded on demand. */\\nconst replays = { bot: () => import('./replays/bot.replay.json?raw').then((module) => module.default) };\\n\\n/** The started engine; null until `createEngine` resolves (its first frames are drawn before that). */\\nlet engine: Engine | null = null;\\n\\n/** Whether the round on screen has ended, so Enter starts the next. */\\nlet ended = false;\\n\\n/** The game's store: its best round across sessions; a replay's page plays in its demo mode, so it sets none. */\\nconst store = createStore({ prefix: 'my3dge-game:', mode: search.has('replay') ? 'demo' : 'play' });\\n\\n/** The fastest won round kept (s), and the run whose clock the page saw running, with the steps it started with. */\\nlet best = bestOf(store);\\nlet seen: { world: object; steps: number } | null = null;\\n\\n/** The pause menu while it is open; null while the round plays. */\\nlet paused: Menu | null = null;\\n\\n/** Opens the pause menu over the paused round, or reads it a frame: Resume (or Escape again), New round. */\\nfunction pauseMenu(dt: number): void {\\n  const [inspector, ui, input] = [engine?.inspector, engine?.ui, engine?.input];\\n  if (!inspector || !ui || !input) return;\\n  const close = () => {\\n    paused?.remove();\\n    paused = null;\\n    inspector.resume();\\n  };\\n  if (paused) return void paused.update(dt);\\n  if (!input.pressed('pause')) return;\\n  inspector.pause();\\n  const items = [\\n    { label: 'Resume', id: 'resume' },\\n    { label: 'New round', id: 'new' },\\n  ];\\n  paused = createMenu(ui.root, items, { input, id: 'pause', title: 'Paused', onCancel: close, onPick: (_i, item) => {\\n    if (typeof item === 'object' && item.id === 'new') inspector.seed(inspector.seed() + 1);\\n    close();\\n  } }); // prettier-ignore\\n}\\n\\n/** Shows the round in the HUD: the gems, the clock, the controls, and how the round ended. */\\nfunction showRound({ world }: EngineFrame): void {\\n  const ui = engine?.ui;\\n  const entity = world.query('round')[0] as unknown as { round: Round } | undefined;\\n  if (!ui || !entity) return;\\n  const { gems, collected, left, state } = entity.round;\\n  if (seen?.world !== world) seen = state === 'playing' ? { world, steps: left + world.tick } : null;\\n  const was = ended;\\n  ui.hud('gems', `Gems ${collected} / ${gems}`, { at: 'top-left' });\\n  ui.hud('clock', `${Math.ceil(left / world.hz)} s`, { at: 'top-right', color: left < 10 * world.hz ? '#ff8f6b' : '' });\\n  ui.hud('keys', 'WASD: run · Space: jump · Shift: dash · Esc: pause', { at: 'bottom', keys: true });\\n  ended = state !== 'playing';\\n  if (ended && !was && state === 'won' && seen) best = recordBest(store, (seen.steps - left) / world.hz);\\n  ui.hud('best', best === null ? null : `Best ${best.toFixed(1)} s`, { at: 'top-left' });\\n  const end = state === 'won' ? 'Every gem! Enter: play again' : 'Time! Enter: play again';\\n  ui.hud('end', ended ? end : null, { at: 'top' });\\n}\\n\\nengine = await createEngine({\\n  canvas: document.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('#view')!,\\n  scenes: [play.id],\\n  levels: { 'level:arena': { text: ARENA_TEXT, file: 'labs/game/scenes/play.ts' } },\\n  replays,\\n  search: `?${search}`,\\n  store,\\n  modal: () => paused !== null,\\n  onFrame: (frame) => {\\n    pauseMenu(frame.dt);\\n    showRound(frame);\\n  },\\n});\\n\\naddEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\\n  const inspector = engine?.inspector;\\n  if (event.code === 'Enter' && ended && inspector) inspector.seed(inspector.seed() + 1);\\n});\\n\",\"total_lines\":105}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-94ca9882-7b4f-4308-9fda-743cfc3b1a07-16","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97