.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/input.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":19,\"content\":\" * `bindingsFor(map)`, another map's bindings, unswitched, for a controls screen (WP 13.25). A code a held binding waits\"},{\"line_number\":23,\"content\":\" * nothing stays held after alt-tab; a gamepad that disconnects lets go of its own. `listen(device)` serves rebinding.\"},{\"line_number\":104,\"content\":\"  /** The bindings of the map in use: rebind, reset, labels. */\"},{\"line_number\":109,\"content\":\"  bindingsFor(map: string): Bindings;\"},{\"line_number\":137,\"content\":\"  /** The next code pressed on `device`'s family, swallowed; null when Escape cancels or another listen starts. */\"},{\"line_number\":138,\"content\":\"  listen(device: 'keyboard' | 'gamepad'): Promise<string | null>;\"},{\"line_number\":141,\"content\":\"  /** Removes every listener. */\"},{\"line_number\":166,\"content\":\"  let listening: { family: 'keyboard' | 'gamepad'; resolve: (code: string | null) => void } | null = null;\"},{\"line_number\":196,\"content\":\"    const wait = listening;\"},{\"line_number\":197,\"content\":\"    listening = null;\"},{\"line_number\":204,\"content\":\"      if (listening && code === 'Escape') return hear(null);\"},{\"line_number\":207,\"content\":\"      if (listening?.family === family && (family === 'keyboard' || PAD_BUTTONS.includes(code as never))) {\"},{\"line_number\":285,\"content\":\"    bindingsFor(map) {\"},{\"line_number\":375,\"content\":\"    listen(device) {\"},{\"line_number\":377,\"content\":\"      return new Promise((resolve) => (listening = { family: device, resolve }));\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/codes.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":14,\"content\":\" * lists one and no player rebinds one; a button names its action with `data-action` (engine/input/devices/touch.ts).\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/bindings.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":3,\"content\":\" * player's changes on top, as engine data. `rebind` puts a code on an action, refusing reserved codes and codes\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-cbc8ed1f-4449-4655-ae13-ff199e5c51cb-55","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"c9700c37-3351-499b-b3a3-a01da07ff0a1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_223","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have enough information to write the game.\n\nI will write the game in batches of under 600 lines each. The planned files cover clips, island and round scenes, audio, UI book, glyphs, shell, main.ts, and index.html.\n\nThe plan now includes retreat.ts for materials and sky, plus maps.ts for action maps. Tools onefile.mjs and verify.mjs will be added. The hub tags page and starter files will be deleted. README, ENGINE-FEEDBACK, PROGRESS, and exit-interview will be written. Songs, voice, lines, and action maps are page-side. The engine will only define the balance lock for play and the roam lock for island walking.\n\nThe engine will use a single action map for both balance and roam. During activities, the pilot will keep the actor standing by not writing move intents.\n\nThe action map will switch between two states. During play it locks the pointer for mouse lean. On front-end screens it stays unlocked so clicks pass through menus. The map binds left and right keys to the actor's movement.\n\nForward and back keys are added to the action map. Left and right foot buttons are mapped to Q, E, and the left and right bumpers. Space is bound to breathe, but modal menus suppress intents so it still works as uiAccept. The act button uses F, Enter, and all four D-pad directions.\n\nGentle is bound to Shift and the left bumper. Programme is bound to Tab and the D-pad north. The move axis maps forward, back, left, and right. Values map game:r, game:l, game:f, game:b, game:fl, game:fr, and game:g to their respective controls. Space will serve as both uiAccept and breathe. Act will not use Space.\n\nPadSouth will serve as both act and uiAccept. During play it costs composure in the pond, while menus still pass clicks through because modal drops intents.\n\nSpace is mapped to the breathe action, but readSeat currently checks game:fl/fr and footl/footr buttons instead. I may need to update readSeat so a held breathe input registers as both feet.\n\nI will update readSeat in kit.ts to treat a held breathe input as both feet. This avoids virtual axis conflicts and keeps existing tests passing.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-15478cd6-8bea-45c8-aaa3-5703156252db-56","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/events/kit.ts","offset":80,"limit":90}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-15478cd6-8bea-45c8-aaa3-5703156252db-57","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/score.ts","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-15478cd6-8bea-45c8-aaa3-5703156252db-58","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/data/days.ts","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1551,"output_tokens":1687,"cache_read_input_tokens":101760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"ee25edda-b256-4867-bbab-effdf39d2349"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-15478cd6-8bea-45c8-aaa3-5703156252db-56","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"80→    py: pointer.y,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** The balance numbers, including steadier hands. Attract mode quiets the sway so the demo can cheat. */\\nexport function cfgOf(w: World): BalanceCfg {\\n  const g = (path: string) => Number(w.settings.get(path));\\n  const assist = g('game.assist') > 0.5 ? 0.5 : 1;\\n  const cheat = String(w.settings.get('game.auto')) === 'attract' ? 0.25 : 1;\\n  return {\\n90→    gain: g('game.wobble.gain'),\\n    instability: g('game.wobble.instability'),\\n    damping: g('game.wobble.damping'),\\n    noise: g('game.wobble.noise') * assist * cheat,\\n    noiseRate: g('game.wobble.noiseRate'),\\n    reach: g('game.wobble.reach'),\\n    calmEffect: g('game.breath.calmEffect'),\\n    period: g('game.breath.period'),\\n    sens: g('game.mouse.sens'),\\n  };\\n100→}\\n\\n/** The wobble and its history for a seat. */\\nexport function rowOf(w: World, seat: number): { wobble: Wobble; hist: Hist } {\\n  const rows = w.query('wobble') as unknown as { wobble: Wobble; hist: Hist }[];\\n  for (const row of rows) if (row.wobble.seat === seat && row.hist) return row;\\n  throw new Error(`no seat ${seat}`);\\n}\\n\\n/** Extra forces an activity adds for one step. */\\n110→export interface Push {\\n  noise?: number;\\n  inst?: number;\\n  dx?: number;\\n  dy?: number;\\n  seat?: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** One balance step for a seat, then the centre is remembered for a late thumb. */\\nexport function apply(w: World, intents: Intents, push: Push = {}): { body: Wobble; seat: Seat } {\\n120→  const seatIndex = push.seat ?? 0;\\n  const row = rowOf(w, seatIndex);\\n  const seat = readSeat(intents, seatIndex);\\n  const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n  const stick: Stick = {\\n    x: seat.x,\\n    y: seat.y,\\n    gentle: seat.gentle,\\n    both: seat.both,\\n    mdx: seat.mdx * cfg.sens,\\n130→    mdy: seat.mdy * cfg.sens,\\n    disturbX: push.dx ?? 0,\\n    disturbY: push.dy ?? 0,\\n    noiseScale: push.noise ?? 1,\\n    instabilityScale: push.inst ?? 1,\\n  };\\n  stepBalance(row.wobble, stick, cfg, w.time, w.dt);\\n  remember(row.hist, row.wobble.x, row.wobble.y);\\n  return { body: row.wobble, seat };\\n}\\n140→\\n/** The flow entity. */\\nexport function flowOf(w: World): Flow {\\n  return part<Flow>(w, 'flow');\\n}\\n\\n/** The activity board. */\\nexport function actOf(w: World): Act {\\n  return part<Act>(w, 'act');\\n}\\n150→\\n/** Removes every entity an activity marked. */\\nexport function sweep(w: World): void {\\n  for (const row of w.query('made') as unknown as { id: number }[]) w.despawn(row.id);\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"80→    py: pointer.y,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** The balance numbers, including steadier hands. Attract mode quiets the sway so the demo can cheat. */\\nexport function cfgOf(w: World): BalanceCfg {\\n  const g = (path: string) => Number(w.settings.get(path));\\n  const assist = g('game.assist') > 0.5 ? 0.5 : 1;\\n  const cheat = String(w.settings.get('game.auto')) === 'attract' ? 0.25 : 1;\\n  return {\\n90→    gain: g('game.wobble.gain'),\\n    instability: g('game.wobble.instability'),\\n    damping: g('game.wobble.damping'),\\n    noise: g('game.wobble.noise') * assist * cheat,\\n    noiseRate: g('game.wobble.noiseRate'),\\n    reach: g('game.wobble.reach'),\\n    calmEffect: g('game.breath.calmEffect'),\\n    period: g('game.breath.period'),\\n    sens: g('game.mouse.sens'),\\n  };\\n100→}\\n\\n/** The wobble and its history for a seat. */\\nexport function rowOf(w: World, seat: number): { wobble: Wobble; hist: Hist } {\\n  const rows = w.query('wobble') as unknown as { wobble: Wobble; hist: Hist }[];\\n  for (const row of rows) if (row.wobble.seat === seat && row.hist) return row;\\n  throw new Error(`no seat ${seat}`);\\n}\\n\\n/** Extra forces an activity adds for one step. */\\n110→export interface Push {\\n  noise?: number;\\n  inst?: number;\\n  dx?: number;\\n  dy?: number;\\n  seat?: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** One balance step for a seat, then the centre is remembered for a late thumb. */\\nexport function apply(w: World, intents: Intents, push: Push = {}): { body: Wobble; seat: Seat } {\\n120→  const seatIndex = push.seat ?? 0;\\n  const row = rowOf(w, seatIndex);\\n  const seat = readSeat(intents, seatIndex);\\n  const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n  const stick: Stick = {\\n    x: seat.x,\\n    y: seat.y,\\n    gentle: seat.gentle,\\n    both: seat.both,\\n    mdx: seat.mdx * cfg.sens,\\n130→    mdy: seat.mdy * cfg.sens,\\n    disturbX: push.dx ?? 0,\\n    disturbY: push.dy ?? 0,\\n    noiseScale: push.noise ?? 1,\\n    instabilityScale: push.inst ?? 1,\\n  };\\n  stepBalance(row.wobble, stick, cfg, w.time, w.dt);\\n  remember(row.hist, row.wobble.x, row.wobble.y);\\n  return { body: row.wobble, seat };\\n}\\n140→\\n/** The flow entity. */\\nexport function flowOf(w: World): Flow {\\n  return part<Flow>(w, 'flow');\\n}\\n\\n/** The activity board. */\\nexport function actOf(w: World): Act {\\n  return part<Act>(w, 'act');\\n}\\n150→\\n/** Removes every entity an activity marked. */\\nexport function sweep(w: World): void {\\n  for (const row of w.query('made') as unknown as { id: number }[]) w.despawn(row.id);\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/events/kit.ts\",\"offset\":80,\"limit\":90,\"raw_output\":\"    py: pointer.y,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** The balance numbers, including steadier hands. Attract mode quiets the sway so the demo can cheat. */\\nexport function cfgOf(w: World): BalanceCfg {\\n  const g = (path: string) => Number(w.settings.get(path));\\n  const assist = g('game.assist') > 0.5 ? 0.5 : 1;\\n  const cheat = String(w.settings.get('game.auto')) === 'attract' ? 0.25 : 1;\\n  return {\\n    gain: g('game.wobble.gain'),\\n    instability: g('game.wobble.instability'),\\n    damping: g('game.wobble.damping'),\\n    noise: g('game.wobble.noise') * assist * cheat,\\n    noiseRate: g('game.wobble.noiseRate'),\\n    reach: g('game.wobble.reach'),\\n    calmEffect: g('game.breath.calmEffect'),\\n    period: g('game.breath.period'),\\n    sens: g('game.mouse.sens'),\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** The wobble and its history for a seat. */\\nexport function rowOf(w: World, seat: number): { wobble: Wobble; hist: Hist } {\\n  const rows = w.query('wobble') as unknown as { wobble: Wobble; hist: Hist }[];\\n  for (const row of rows) if (row.wobble.seat === seat && row.hist) return row;\\n  throw new Error(`no seat ${seat}`);\\n}\\n\\n/** Extra forces an activity adds for one step. */\\nexport interface Push {\\n  noise?: number;\\n  inst?: number;\\n  dx?: number;\\n  dy?: number;\\n  seat?: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** One balance step for a seat, then the centre is remembered for a late thumb. */\\nexport function apply(w: World, intents: Intents, push: Push = {}): { body: Wobble; seat: Seat } {\\n  const seatIndex = push.seat ?? 0;\\n  const row = rowOf(w, seatIndex);\\n  const seat = readSeat(intents, seatIndex);\\n  const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n  const stick: Stick = {\\n    x: seat.x,\\n    y: seat.y,\\n    gentle: seat.gentle,\\n    both: seat.both,\\n    mdx: seat.mdx * cfg.sens,\\n    mdy: seat.mdy * cfg.sens,\\n    disturbX: push.dx ?? 0,\\n    disturbY: push.dy ?? 0,\\n    noiseScale: push.noise ?? 1,\\n    instabilityScale: push.inst ?? 1,\\n  };\\n  stepBalance(row.wobble, stick, cfg, w.time, w.dt);\\n  remember(row.hist, row.wobble.x, row.wobble.y);\\n  return { body: row.wobble, seat };\\n}\\n\\n/** The flow entity. */\\nexport function flowOf(w: World): Flow {\\n  return part<Flow>(w, 'flow');\\n}\\n\\n/** The activity board. */\\nexport function actOf(w: World): Act {\\n  return part<Act>(w, 'act');\\n}\\n\\n/** Removes every entity an activity marked. */\\nexport function sweep(w: World): void {\\n  for (const row of w.query('made') as unknown as { id: number }[]) w.despawn(row.id);\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":154}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-15478cd6-8bea-45c8-aaa3-5703156252db-57","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Ranks, pebbles and Wobble Age. Every activity ends as a number from 0 to 1000. The words and the\\n * pebbles hang off that number. Age is the morning check only, and it never talks about a body.\\n */\\nimport { clamp } from './wobble';\\n\\n/** The rank words, from a quiet morning to a result the staff will not discuss. */\\nexport const RANKS = ['Present', 'Adequate', 'Composed', 'Serene', 'Unsettling'] as const;\\n\\n10→/** Pebbles a rank is worth before the multiplier. One is the least. Five is the most. */\\nconst PEBBLES: Readonly<Record<string, number>> = {\\n  Present: 1,\\n  Adequate: 2,\\n  Composed: 3,\\n  Serene: 4,\\n  Unsettling: 5,\\n};\\n\\n/** A score kept inside 0 to 1000. Anything that is not a finite number becomes 0. */\\n20→export function clampScore(n: number): number {\\n  if (!Number.isFinite(n)) return 0;\\n  return clamp(n, 0, 1000);\\n}\\n\\n/** The rank word for a score. Thresholds are 300, 550, 750 and 900. */\\nexport function rankOf(score: number): string {\\n  const s = clampScore(score);\\n  if (s >= 900) return 'Unsettling';\\n  if (s >= 750) return 'Serene';\\n30→  if (s >= 550) return 'Composed';\\n  if (s >= 300) return 'Adequate';\\n  return 'Present';\\n}\\n\\n/** Pebbles for a rank, scaled, and never fewer than one. They are not spent. */\\nexport function pebblesOf(rank: string, mult: number): number {\\n  const base = PEBBLES[rank] ?? 1;\\n  const m = Number.isFinite(mult) ? mult : 1;\\n  return Math.max(1, Math.round(base * m));\\n40→}\\n\\n/**\\n * Wobble Age from a morning share `s` (0 to 1). `k` is `game.age.k`.\\n * A perfect morning is 18. A morning with no share is 82.\\n */\\nexport function wobbleAge(s: number, k: number): number {\\n  const t = clamp(Number.isFinite(s) ? s : 0, 0, 1);\\n  const exp = Number.isFinite(k) ? k : 1.3;\\n  return Math.round(18 + 64 * Math.pow(1 - t, exp));\\n50→}\\n\\n/** How today's age sits next to yesterday. The same number is still news. */\\nexport function ageRemark(today: number, yesterday: number): string {\\n  if (!(yesterday > 0)) return 'Your first Wobble Age. We will pretend to be surprised tomorrow.';\\n  const d = yesterday - today;\\n  if (d > 0) return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Yesterday it was ${yesterday}. You stood still and time went backwards.`;\\n  if (d < 0) return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Yesterday it was ${yesterday}. The island has noted the difference.`;\\n  return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Yesterday it was ${today}. Consistency is a kind of wobble.`;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Ranks, pebbles and Wobble Age. Every activity ends as a number from 0 to 1000. The words and the\\n * pebbles hang off that number. Age is the morning check only, and it never talks about a body.\\n */\\nimport { clamp } from './wobble';\\n\\n/** The rank words, from a quiet morning to a result the staff will not discuss. */\\nexport const RANKS = ['Present', 'Adequate', 'Composed', 'Serene', 'Unsettling'] as const;\\n\\n10→/** Pebbles a rank is worth before the multiplier. One is the least. Five is the most. */\\nconst PEBBLES: Readonly<Record<string, number>> = {\\n  Present: 1,\\n  Adequate: 2,\\n  Composed: 3,\\n  Serene: 4,\\n  Unsettling: 5,\\n};\\n\\n/** A score kept inside 0 to 1000. Anything that is not a finite number becomes 0. */\\n20→export function clampScore(n: number): number {\\n  if (!Number.isFinite(n)) return 0;\\n  return clamp(n, 0, 1000);\\n}\\n\\n/** The rank word for a score. Thresholds are 300, 550, 750 and 900. */\\nexport function rankOf(score: number): string {\\n  const s = clampScore(score);\\n  if (s >= 900) return 'Unsettling';\\n  if (s >= 750) return 'Serene';\\n30→  if (s >= 550) return 'Composed';\\n  if (s >= 300) return 'Adequate';\\n  return 'Present';\\n}\\n\\n/** Pebbles for a rank, scaled, and never fewer than one. They are not spent. */\\nexport function pebblesOf(rank: string, mult: number): number {\\n  const base = PEBBLES[rank] ?? 1;\\n  const m = Number.isFinite(mult) ? mult : 1;\\n  return Math.max(1, Math.round(base * m));\\n40→}\\n\\n/**\\n * Wobble Age from a morning share `s` (0 to 1). `k` is `game.age.k`.\\n * A perfect morning is 18. A morning with no share is 82.\\n */\\nexport function wobbleAge(s: number, k: number): number {\\n  const t = clamp(Number.isFinite(s) ? s : 0, 0, 1);\\n  const exp = Number.isFinite(k) ? k : 1.3;\\n  return Math.round(18 + 64 * Math.pow(1 - t, exp));\\n50→}\\n\\n/** How today's age sits next to yesterday. The same number is still news. */\\nexport function ageRemark(today: number, yesterday: number): string {\\n  if (!(yesterday > 0)) return 'Your first Wobble Age. We will pretend to be surprised tomorrow.';\\n  const d = yesterday - today;\\n  if (d > 0) return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Yesterday it was ${yesterday}. You stood still and time went backwards.`;\\n  if (d < 0) return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Yesterday it was ${yesterday}. The island has noted the difference.`;\\n  return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Yesterday it was ${today}. Consistency is a kind of wobble.`;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/score.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file Ranks, pebbles and Wobble Age. Every activity ends as a number from 0 to 1000. The words and the\\n * pebbles hang off that number. Age is the morning check only, and it never talks about a body.\\n */\\nimport { clamp } from './wobble';\\n\\n/** The rank words, from a quiet morning to a result the staff will not discuss. */\\nexport const RANKS = ['Present', 'Adequate', 'Composed', 'Serene', 'Unsettling'] as const;\\n\\n/** Pebbles a rank is worth before the multiplier. One is the least. Five is the most. */\\nconst PEBBLES: Readonly<Record<string, number>> = {\\n  Present: 1,\\n  Adequate: 2,\\n  Composed: 3,\\n  Serene: 4,\\n  Unsettling: 5,\\n};\\n\\n/** A score kept inside 0 to 1000. Anything that is not a finite number becomes 0. */\\nexport function clampScore(n: number): number {\\n  if (!Number.isFinite(n)) return 0;\\n  return clamp(n, 0, 1000);\\n}\\n\\n/** The rank word for a score. Thresholds are 300, 550, 750 and 900. */\\nexport function rankOf(score: number): string {\\n  const s = clampScore(score);\\n  if (s >= 900) return 'Unsettling';\\n  if (s >= 750) return 'Serene';\\n  if (s >= 550) return 'Composed';\\n  if (s >= 300) return 'Adequate';\\n  return 'Present';\\n}\\n\\n/** Pebbles for a rank, scaled, and never fewer than one. They are not spent. */\\nexport function pebblesOf(rank: string, mult: number): number {\\n  const base = PEBBLES[rank] ?? 1;\\n  const m = Number.isFinite(mult) ? mult : 1;\\n  return Math.max(1, Math.round(base * m));\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Wobble Age from a morning share `s` (0 to 1). `k` is `game.age.k`.\\n * A perfect morning is 18. A morning with no share is 82.\\n */\\nexport function wobbleAge(s: number, k: number): number {\\n  const t = clamp(Number.isFinite(s) ? s : 0, 0, 1);\\n  const exp = Number.isFinite(k) ? k : 1.3;\\n  return Math.round(18 + 64 * Math.pow(1 - t, exp));\\n}\\n\\n/** How today's age sits next to yesterday. The same number is still news. */\\nexport function ageRemark(today: number, yesterday: number): string {\\n  if (!(yesterday > 0)) return 'Your first Wobble Age. We will pretend to be surprised tomorrow.';\\n  const d = yesterday - today;\\n  if (d > 0) return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Yesterday it was ${yesterday}. You stood still and time went backwards.`;\\n  if (d < 0) return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Yesterday it was ${yesterday}. The island has noted the difference.`;\\n  return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Yesterday it was ${today}. Consistency is a kind of wobble.`;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":59}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-15478cd6-8bea-45c8-aaa3-5703156252db-58","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The five days, and the only programme the director walks. Evening sits between days.\\n * The last morning comes after the fifth evening. Then the credits. The ferry does not return.\\n */\\n\\n/** One residency day and the activities on it, in order. */\\nexport interface DayPlan {\\n  day: number;\\n  events: readonly string[];\\n10→}\\n\\n/** What a new guest does. Free play later offers the same ids from the noticeboard. */\\nexport const DAYS: readonly DayPlan[] = [\\n  { day: 1, events: ['morning', 'pose-a', 'pond'] },\\n  { day: 2, events: ['morning', 'pose-b', 'garden'] },\\n  { day: 3, events: ['morning', 'paddle', 'line'] },\\n  { day: 4, events: ['morning', 'pose-c'] },\\n  { day: 5, events: ['morning', 'group', 'tilt'] },\\n];\\n20→\\n/** One stop on the programme, including evenings, the last morning and the credits. */\\nexport interface ProgrammeItem {\\n  day: number;\\n  event: string;\\n}\\n\\n/** The whole residency in order. Tests and the director both read this. There is no second copy. */\\nexport function programme(): ProgrammeItem[] {\\n  const out: ProgrammeItem[] = [];\\n30→  for (const day of DAYS) {\\n    for (const event of day.events) out.push({ day: day.day, event });\\n    out.push({ day: day.day, event: 'evening' });\\n  }\\n  out.push({ day: 5, event: 'morning' });\\n  out.push({ day: 5, event: 'credits' });\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The five days, and the only programme the director walks. Evening sits between days.\\n * The last morning comes after the fifth evening. Then the credits. The ferry does not return.\\n */\\n\\n/** One residency day and the activities on it, in order. */\\nexport interface DayPlan {\\n  day: number;\\n  events: readonly string[];\\n10→}\\n\\n/** What a new guest does. Free play later offers the same ids from the noticeboard. */\\nexport const DAYS: readonly DayPlan[] = [\\n  { day: 1, events: ['morning', 'pose-a', 'pond'] },\\n  { day: 2, events: ['morning', 'pose-b', 'garden'] },\\n  { day: 3, events: ['morning', 'paddle', 'line'] },\\n  { day: 4, events: ['morning', 'pose-c'] },\\n  { day: 5, events: ['morning', 'group', 'tilt'] },\\n];\\n20→\\n/** One stop on the programme, including evenings, the last morning and the credits. */\\nexport interface ProgrammeItem {\\n  day: number;\\n  event: string;\\n}\\n\\n/** The whole residency in order. Tests and the director both read this. There is no second copy. */\\nexport function programme(): ProgrammeItem[] {\\n  const out: ProgrammeItem[] = [];\\n30→  for (const day of DAYS) {\\n    for (const event of day.events) out.push({ day: day.day, event });\\n    out.push({ day: day.day, event: 'evening' });\\n  }\\n  out.push({ day: 5, event: 'morning' });\\n  out.push({ day: 5, event: 'credits' });\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/data/days.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The five days, and the only programme the director walks. Evening sits between days.\\n * The last morning comes after the fifth evening. Then the credits. The ferry does not return.\\n */\\n\\n/** One residency day and the activities on it, in order. */\\nexport interface DayPlan {\\n  day: number;\\n  events: readonly string[];\\n}\\n\\n/** What a new guest does. Free play later offers the same ids from the noticeboard. */\\nexport const DAYS: readonly DayPlan[] = [\\n  { day: 1, events: ['morning', 'pose-a', 'pond'] },\\n  { day: 2, events: ['morning', 'pose-b', 'garden'] },\\n  { day: 3, events: ['morning', 'paddle', 'line'] },\\n  { day: 4, events: ['morning', 'pose-c'] },\\n  { day: 5, events: ['morning', 'group', 'tilt'] },\\n];\\n\\n/** One stop on the programme, including evenings, the last morning and the credits. */\\nexport interface ProgrammeItem {\\n  day: number;\\n  event: string;\\n}\\n\\n/** The whole residency in order. Tests and the director both read this. There is no second copy. */\\nexport function programme(): ProgrammeItem[] {\\n  const out: ProgrammeItem[] = [];\\n  for (const day of DAYS) {\\n    for (const event of day.events) out.push({ day: day.day, event });\\n    out.push({ day: day.day, event: 'evening' });\\n  }\\n  out.push({ day: 5, event: 'morning' });\\n  out.push({ day: 5, event: 'credits' });\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":37}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"7c1df43b-ed7c-4386-9195-92a87c6e9df8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_224","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"pond.ts needs to be checked. It uses raw mdx before sens.\n\nBreathe handling will be added to readSeat. Code will follow strict formatting rules: 120-character line limits, no `any` types or enums, no `Math.random` in the simulation, and no `**` operators there. The page may use `performance.now` and `Math`. The island group class starts on the game start event. The hub round scene starts its group automatically when the session begins. round.ts will use physics with a small size and no terrain.\n\nRound.ts spawns four mat marks and ghost components. Each step applies ghosts from intents. In single-player mode the island scene loads first, not round. In hub mode the scene becomes game:round and boots title mode. The page triggers the group start after the AIHub start. Title mode waits for game.begin or game.start when auto is off. Round.step reads game:ghosts.\n\nGhost data is an array of five-number groups: seat, x, y, pose, and on. The page sends this format. Mark entities will render ghost positions, with their x and z updated each step. Local player wobble uses seat 0; ghosts are other seats and do not affect balance. For the hub ready scene, terrain is removed and actors are minimized to keep startup fast. Actor physics initialization is acceptable for a small set. Clip definitions should be loaded only at island import, not round.\n\nRound.ts will not import clips or island terrain. It imports driver, state, and catalog for group activity. The terrain spec is defined in island.ts but remains unbuilt during round setup. Main imports island unconditionally, so the clip set parses at import time without cost. createEngine loads only the active scene, so island setup does not run when game:round is active.\n\nrest.json is a single object. clips will import REST from rest.ts to avoid duplication. defineClipSet requires the rest object inside sources. parseClipSet may validate the shape, but the plan already tested this. If clips fail, island can spawn actors without animation. Song files will be defined at page import. Tracks must fill whole bars. Song specs default steps and beats.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e52a091c-ca4f-4769-9362-d3c721e3bcb7-59","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"play\\(id","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/audio/runtime/audio.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e52a091c-ca4f-4769-9362-d3c721e3bcb7-60","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/audio/data/song.ts","offset":80,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e52a091c-ca4f-4769-9362-d3c721e3bcb7-61","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"volume\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/audio/runtime/audio.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3625,"output_tokens":1126,"cache_read_input_tokens":103296,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"d21b286e-f669-42a2-b39e-45c2cecf7ca6"}
