{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_228","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have a clear picture. I will write the files.\n\nBatching file writes. Updating readSeat for breathing. Island camera will follow the guest actor's feet, switching to the mat origin during events. Mapping island layout coordinates and engine axis conventions.\n\nFinalized island coordinates: cove at z=-50, x=0; pond at 24,18. Stations mapped to specific marks with text prompts. Hidden pebbles placed at odd spots. Roaming pilot logic copies intents.move onto actor.intents.\n\nPilot intents are set to move, b, and p arrays. Default walk speed is used for the character. Near a station, pressing act triggers startEvent, which queues activity spawning until the entry phase ends. This between-step timing is intentional.\n\nEvents will not be triggered from inside the scene step. The pilot will only move and set a \"near\" component that the page reads between frames. Adding a new field to the flow entity is difficult without schema changes, so act.text during roam mode may serve as the prompt indicator.\n\nThe page will read act.text to detect the nearest station and trigger game.start. Stations are marks carrying a text activity ID. A \"Go\" button on the programme menu also starts events.\n\nSave data is stored as JSON under the key 'save'. The game loads this object on begin. It writes the save after results, evening, credits, and pebble changes unless in attract or demo mode. Erasing uses an in-game confirm menu to remove the store entry and seed.\n\nAttract mode will only trigger on front-end screens. Title, settings, about, and controls are included. Play and results are excluded. A ten-second idle timer starts when the screen is not in play. The implementation tracks screen state, an attract flag, and the last input time.\n\nFront-end screens trigger attract mode after ten seconds of idle time. The game seeds a new random value and locks the auto flag. Any input during attract mode disables it, reseeds the game, and returns to the title screen. Dev mode exits attract mode first.\n\nGlyphs capture window pointerdown, keydown, and gamepad events each frame before paint. The default icon set is PlayStation. Xbox uses the 'xbox' icon set. Keyboard and mouse inputs switch the set to 'keys' or 'mouse'.\n\nThe icon set is stored in a 'icons' setting as 'playstation' or 'xbox'. UI font size will be injected via CSS at max(28px, 2.6vh). Menus are capped at six items; the pause menu paginates its eight entries across two pages. The hub pause screen omits dev mode and does not pause the simulation. The title menu lists Begin, Continue, Free Play, Group Class, Settings, and About.\n\nFree Play opens the noticeboard of activities. The Results overlay shows rank, score, sentence, Again, and Carry on. Evening mode has a Sleep button. Credits mode displays text and returns to roam when the user leaves.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-70861b86-af37-4438-af52-cc3d6e6c85ca-67","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"describe\\(kind|function describe|default:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/app","glob":"*.ts","head_limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-70861b86-af37-4438-af52-cc3d6e6c85ca-68","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"describe\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/session.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2228,"output_tokens":1736,"cache_read_input_tokens":111360,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"0f3636c2-ebf5-4834-8f43-c87d2bc70879"}
