d, spawn, travel) and by the bot (engine/dev/bot.ts) when the id given is no live actor, or none is given and the scene has no player actor. Nothing has changed.\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":62,\"content\":\"  /** What it does, one line: `__engine.actions.list()` shows it. */\"},{\"line_number\":82,\"content\":\"  help: { type: 'string', required: true, description: 'What it does, one line: __engine.actions.list() shows it.' },\"},{\"line_number\":141,\"content\":\"/** The engine's dev actions (see the file comment). */\"},{\"line_number\":224,\"content\":\" * the setting `ai.frozen` (engine/sim/systems.ts), and the engine's five actions (see the file comment).\"},{\"line_number\":230,\"content\":\"      'Dev actions: changes made to a running scene between steps (god mode, freeze, spawn, travel, time scale), recorded in replays.',\"},{\"line_number\":260,\"content\":\"/** The dev actions on `registry`, by name. */\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fa04a484-42a7-4d66-b9bc-f0546ed51de5-78","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"04513ed3-14e4-4489-8edf-15165c7c9236"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_235","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"engine/dev/actions.ts contains __engine.","signature":"bUcwYqgAw1oLHXGrL72o3Iq7y3+yJlTogSeSP3FnGJ+LEnre2mzjVYIPY8zBRb8z6IoMeTwadT1LhVccWJiIaUks6S7ZMvxko4QwvkoAS+Mbb06a9ldTdMAk274j5sNTqkGZjJd/ZcJ0Rh+Vj5wMllXz46Cj2mjvAtLNXS4r+nI6PghFTfuhoCo"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e84ba9b0-cb36-4ebb-bff5-a06300f19f72-79","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/dev/actions.ts","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":803,"output_tokens":111,"cache_read_input_tokens":121472,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"f698ecf2-c582-4928-a5fa-af2d7f9282af"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e84ba9b0-cb36-4ebb-bff5-a06300f19f72-79","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file `__engine.actions` and `__engine.bot` (PLAN.md §8.3, WP 5.6; doctrine: Agent-operable): the developer's tools\\n * on the inspector, registered from this file as `inspectorMember` entries (engine/dev/members.ts), so a page\\n * (`x eval \\\"__engine.actions.run('travel', { at: [3, 0, 5] })\\\"`) and `createHeadless` reach the same calls.\\n *\\n * - `actions.list()`: the dev actions this run has, the scene's own (engine/sim/scene.ts `actions`) and then the\\n *   engine's (engine/sim/devActions.ts: god, freeze, spawn, travel, timeScale, and any `defineDevAction` added), each\\n *   with what it changes: `sim` (recorded as a dev action) or `settings` alone (recorded as set, view ones never).\\n * - `actions.run(name, args)`: runs one between steps through the session (`session.act`: the args checked, its\\n10→ *   settings set, then its change to the sim, all or nothing), so the replay holds it; the view snaps to the world.\\n * - `bot(plan)`: plays the player with the bot (engine/dev/bot.ts) over the scene's level: the goals `to`, a `tour`,\\n *   `back`, the stop condition `until` (`component.field`), `steps`, a `trace`, its options; through `step`, so each\\n *   step is recorded (`input.record()` replays it). With `seeds` (`1-20`, `5`, `3,7,9`), a sweep from fresh sessions\\n *   of the scene with this run's recorded settings instead, the run itself left alone: one row, a run per seed.\\n *\\n * Invariants: members change the sim only through the session's recorded operations (engine/dev/members.ts); this\\n * module registers them when it loads (engine/app/headless.ts loads it, so every engine has them).\\n *\\n * @example\\n20→ * import { createHeadless } from '../app/headless';\\n * import { defineScene } from '../sim/scene';\\n * const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: defineScene('dev-actions-demo', { setup: () => {} }) });\\n * const actions = engine.actions as { list(): { name: string }[] };\\n * actions.list().map((action) => action.name); // ['freeze', 'god', 'spawn', 'timeScale', 'travel']: none of its own\\n * @see engine/dev/actions.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError } from '../core/log';\\nimport type { Field, Schema } from '../core/schema';\\nimport { changesSim, listDevActions } from '../sim/devActions';\\n30→import { getLevel } from '../world/level/level';\\nimport { getSite } from '../world/site';\\nimport { runBot, type BotPlan } from './bot';\\nimport { sweepBot } from './botSweep';\\nimport { defineMember } from './members';\\n\\n/** One dev action as `actions.list()` shows it. */\\nexport interface ActionRow {\\n  name: string;\\n  /** Whose it is: the scene's own, or the engine's. */\\n40→  from: 'scene' | 'engine';\\n  /** What it changes: `sim` (recorded as a dev action), or `settings` alone (recorded as set, but view ones). */\\n  changes: 'sim' | 'settings';\\n  /** Its help line and its arguments (`at, yaw?, id?`), the engine's only. */\\n  help?: string;\\n  args?: string;\\n}\\n\\n/** An action's arguments as a list reads them: `at, yaw?, id?`, defaults shown. */\\nconst argsLine = (args: Schema) =>\\n50→  Object.entries(args)\\n    .map(([key, field]: [string, Field]) =>\\n      field.required ? key : field.default === undefined ? `${key}?` : `${key} = ${JSON.stringify(field.default)}`,\\n    ) // prettier-ignore\\n    .join(', ');\\n\\ndefineMember('actions.list', {\\n  help: \\\"Lists the run's dev actions: the scene's own, then the engine's (god, freeze, spawn, travel, timeScale).\\\",\\n  impl(h): ActionRow[] {\\n    const own = Object.keys(h.session.scene.actions ?? {}).sort();\\n60→    const scene = own.map((name): ActionRow => ({ name, from: 'scene', changes: 'sim' }));\\n    const engine = listDevActions(h.registry)\\n      .filter((action) => !own.includes(action.id))\\n      .map((action): ActionRow => ({ name: action.id, from: 'engine', changes: changesSim(action) ? 'sim' : 'settings', help: action.help, args: argsLine(action.args) })); // prettier-ignore\\n    return [...scene, ...engine];\\n  },\\n});\\n\\ndefineMember('actions.run', {\\n  help: \\\"Runs a dev action between steps, recorded in the replay: actions.run('travel', { at: [3, 0, 5] }).\\\",\\n70→  args: {\\n    name: { type: 'string', required: true, description: 'Its name, as actions.list() shows it.' },\\n    args: { type: 'object', description: 'Its arguments, as actions.list() names them.' },\\n  },\\n  impl(h, name: string, args?: Record<string, unknown>) {\\n    h.session.act(name, args);\\n    return { name, tick: h.session.world.tick };\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n80→defineMember('bot', {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file `__engine.actions` and `__engine.bot` (PLAN.md §8.3, WP 5.6; doctrine: Agent-operable): the developer's tools\\n * on the inspector, registered from this file as `inspectorMember` entries (engine/dev/members.ts), so a page\\n * (`x eval \\\"__engine.actions.run('travel', { at: [3, 0, 5] })\\\"`) and `createHeadless` reach the same calls.\\n *\\n * - `actions.list()`: the dev actions this run has, the scene's own (engine/sim/scene.ts `actions`) and then the\\n *   engine's (engine/sim/devActions.ts: god, freeze, spawn, travel, timeScale, and any `defineDevAction` added), each\\n *   with what it changes: `sim` (recorded as a dev action) or `settings` alone (recorded as set, view ones never).\\n * - `actions.run(name, args)`: runs one between steps through the session (`session.act`: the args checked, its\\n10→ *   settings set, then its change to the sim, all or nothing), so the replay holds it; the view snaps to the world.\\n * - `bot(plan)`: plays the player with the bot (engine/dev/bot.ts) over the scene's level: the goals `to`, a `tour`,\\n *   `back`, the stop condition `until` (`component.field`), `steps`, a `trace`, its options; through `step`, so each\\n *   step is recorded (`input.record()` replays it). With `seeds` (`1-20`, `5`, `3,7,9`), a sweep from fresh sessions\\n *   of the scene with this run's recorded settings instead, the run itself left alone: one row, a run per seed.\\n *\\n * Invariants: members change the sim only through the session's recorded operations (engine/dev/members.ts); this\\n * module registers them when it loads (engine/app/headless.ts loads it, so every engine has them).\\n *\\n * @example\\n20→ * import { createHeadless } from '../app/headless';\\n * import { defineScene } from '../sim/scene';\\n * const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: defineScene('dev-actions-demo', { setup: () => {} }) });\\n * const actions = engine.actions as { list(): { name: string }[] };\\n * actions.list().map((action) => action.name); // ['freeze', 'god', 'spawn', 'timeScale', 'travel']: none of its own\\n * @see engine/dev/actions.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError } from '../core/log';\\nimport type { Field, Schema } from '../core/schema';\\nimport { changesSim, listDevActions } from '../sim/devActions';\\n30→import { getLevel } from '../world/level/level';\\nimport { getSite } from '../world/site';\\nimport { runBot, type BotPlan } from './bot';\\nimport { sweepBot } from './botSweep';\\nimport { defineMember } from './members';\\n\\n/** One dev action as `actions.list()` shows it. */\\nexport interface ActionRow {\\n  name: string;\\n  /** Whose it is: the scene's own, or the engine's. */\\n40→  from: 'scene' | 'engine';\\n  /** What it changes: `sim` (recorded as a dev action), or `settings` alone (recorded as set, but view ones). */\\n  changes: 'sim' | 'settings';\\n  /** Its help line and its arguments (`at, yaw?, id?`), the engine's only. */\\n  help?: string;\\n  args?: string;\\n}\\n\\n/** An action's arguments as a list reads them: `at, yaw?, id?`, defaults shown. */\\nconst argsLine = (args: Schema) =>\\n50→  Object.entries(args)\\n    .map(([key, field]: [string, Field]) =>\\n      field.required ? key : field.default === undefined ? `${key}?` : `${key} = ${JSON.stringify(field.default)}`,\\n    ) // prettier-ignore\\n    .join(', ');\\n\\ndefineMember('actions.list', {\\n  help: \\\"Lists the run's dev actions: the scene's own, then the engine's (god, freeze, spawn, travel, timeScale).\\\",\\n  impl(h): ActionRow[] {\\n    const own = Object.keys(h.session.scene.actions ?? {}).sort();\\n60→    const scene = own.map((name): ActionRow => ({ name, from: 'scene', changes: 'sim' }));\\n    const engine = listDevActions(h.registry)\\n      .filter((action) => !own.includes(action.id))\\n      .map((action): ActionRow => ({ name: action.id, from: 'engine', changes: changesSim(action) ? 'sim' : 'settings', help: action.help, args: argsLine(action.args) })); // prettier-ignore\\n    return [...scene, ...engine];\\n  },\\n});\\n\\ndefineMember('actions.run', {\\n  help: \\\"Runs a dev action between steps, recorded in the replay: actions.run('travel', { at: [3, 0, 5] }).\\\",\\n70→  args: {\\n    name: { type: 'string', required: true, description: 'Its name, as actions.list() shows it.' },\\n    args: { type: 'object', description: 'Its arguments, as actions.list() names them.' },\\n  },\\n  impl(h, name: string, args?: Record<string, unknown>) {\\n    h.session.act(name, args);\\n    return { name, tick: h.session.world.tick };\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n80→defineMember('bot', {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/dev/actions.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file `__engine.actions` and `__engine.bot` (PLAN.md §8.3, WP 5.6; doctrine: Agent-operable): the developer's tools\\n * on the inspector, registered from this file as `inspectorMember` entries (engine/dev/members.ts), so a page\\n * (`x eval \\\"__engine.actions.run('travel', { at: [3, 0, 5] })\\\"`) and `createHeadless` reach the same calls.\\n *\\n * - `actions.list()`: the dev actions this run has, the scene's own (engine/sim/scene.ts `actions`) and then the\\n *   engine's (engine/sim/devActions.ts: god, freeze, spawn, travel, timeScale, and any `defineDevAction` added), each\\n *   with what it changes: `sim` (recorded as a dev action) or `settings` alone (recorded as set, view ones never).\\n * - `actions.run(name, args)`: runs one between steps through the session (`session.act`: the args checked, its\\n *   settings set, then its change to the sim, all or nothing), so the replay holds it; the view snaps to the world.\\n * - `bot(plan)`: plays the player with the bot (engine/dev/bot.ts) over the scene's level: the goals `to`, a `tour`,\\n *   `back`, the stop condition `until` (`component.field`), `steps`, a `trace`, its options; through `step`, so each\\n *   step is recorded (`input.record()` replays it). With `seeds` (`1-20`, `5`, `3,7,9`), a sweep from fresh sessions\\n *   of the scene with this run's recorded settings instead, the run itself left alone: one row, a run per seed.\\n *\\n * Invariants: members change the sim only through the session's recorded operations (engine/dev/members.ts); this\\n * module registers them when it loads (engine/app/headless.ts loads it, so every engine has them).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createHeadless } from '../app/headless';\\n * import { defineScene } from '../sim/scene';\\n * const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: defineScene('dev-actions-demo', { setup: () => {} }) });\\n * const actions = engine.actions as { list(): { name: string }[] };\\n * actions.list().map((action) => action.name); // ['freeze', 'god', 'spawn', 'timeScale', 'travel']: none of its own\\n * @see engine/dev/actions.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError } from '../core/log';\\nimport type { Field, Schema } from '../core/schema';\\nimport { changesSim, listDevActions } from '../sim/devActions';\\nimport { getLevel } from '../world/level/level';\\nimport { getSite } from '../world/site';\\nimport { runBot, type BotPlan } from './bot';\\nimport { sweepBot } from './botSweep';\\nimport { defineMember } from './members';\\n\\n/** One dev action as `actions.list()` shows it. */\\nexport interface ActionRow {\\n  name: string;\\n  /** Whose it is: the scene's own, or the engine's. */\\n  from: 'scene' | 'engine';\\n  /** What it changes: `sim` (recorded as a dev action), or `settings` alone (recorded as set, but view ones). */\\n  changes: 'sim' | 'settings';\\n  /** Its help line and its arguments (`at, yaw?, id?`), the engine's only. */\\n  help?: string;\\n  args?: string;\\n}\\n\\n/** An action's arguments as a list reads them: `at, yaw?, id?`, defaults shown. */\\nconst argsLine = (args: Schema) =>\\n  Object.entries(args)\\n    .map(([key, field]: [string, Field]) =>\\n      field.required ? key : field.default === undefined ? `${key}?` : `${key} = ${JSON.stringify(field.default)}`,\\n    ) // prettier-ignore\\n    .join(', ');\\n\\ndefineMember('actions.list', {\\n  help: \\\"Lists the run's dev actions: the scene's own, then the engine's (god, freeze, spawn, travel, timeScale).\\\",\\n  impl(h): ActionRow[] {\\n    const own = Object.keys(h.session.scene.actions ?? {}).sort();\\n    const scene = own.map((name): ActionRow => ({ name, from: 'scene', changes: 'sim' }));\\n    const engine = listDevActions(h.registry)\\n      .filter((action) => !own.includes(action.id))\\n      .map((action): ActionRow => ({ name: action.id, from: 'engine', changes: changesSim(action) ? 'sim' : 'settings', help: action.help, args: argsLine(action.args) })); // prettier-ignore\\n    return [...scene, ...engine];\\n  },\\n});\\n\\ndefineMember('actions.run', {\\n  help: \\\"Runs a dev action between steps, recorded in the replay: actions.run('travel', { at: [3, 0, 5] }).\\\",\\n  args: {\\n    name: { type: 'string', required: true, description: 'Its name, as actions.list() shows it.' },\\n    args: { type: 'object', description: 'Its arguments, as actions.list() names them.' },\\n  },\\n  impl(h, name: string, args?: Record<string, unknown>) {\\n    h.session.act(name, args);\\n    return { name, tick: h.session.world.tick };\\n  },\\n});\\n\\ndefineMember('bot', {\\n\",\"total_lines\":101}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"1d00d925-59e3-437f-a2e7-01a9c28aa1ab"}
