{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-11c9f865-7912-47e3-9f7d-01f55e6e3fbc-110","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"90→\\n  /** mulberry32: numbers in [0, 1), the same sequence everywhere for the same 32-bit start. */\\n  function generator(a) {\\n    return function () {\\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\\n      var t = a;\\n      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\\n    };\\n100→  }\\n\\n  // A fair start: in a session the game gets an empty storage of its own, so\\n  // every round starts as a first launch (no saved unlocks, upgrades or runs),\\n  // and nothing the round saves touches the player's own saves.\\n  if (hub.active) {\\n    for (var s = 0, stores = ['localStorage', 'sessionStorage']; s < stores.length; s++) {\\n      try {\\n        Object.defineProperty(root, stores[s], { configurable: true, value: memoryStorage() });\\n      } catch (e) {\\n110→        warn('could not give the game a fresh ' + stores[s]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\\n  // a generator seeded by the hub, so every copy builds the same start.\\n  var realRandom = Math.random;\\n  var seededRandom = null;\\n  if (hub.active && seedArg) {\\n120→    Math.random = seededRandom = generator(Number(seedArg[1]) >>> 0);\\n    hub.seeded = true;\\n  }\\n\\n  // In a session the hub owns fullscreen: a game that asks for it gets the\\n  // hub's whole page, so the scoreboard and the hub's cards stay on top. The\\n  // hub says when its page goes in and out, so the game's own toggle and its\\n  // fullscreenchange listeners work as they always did.\\n  var fullscreenOn = false;\\n  if (hub.active && root.Element && root.document) {\",\"content_concise\":\"90→\\n  /** mulberry32: numbers in [0, 1), the same sequence everywhere for the same 32-bit start. */\\n  function generator(a) {\\n    return function () {\\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\\n      var t = a;\\n      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\\n    };\\n100→  }\\n\\n  // A fair start: in a session the game gets an empty storage of its own, so\\n  // every round starts as a first launch (no saved unlocks, upgrades or runs),\\n  // and nothing the round saves touches the player's own saves.\\n  if (hub.active) {\\n    for (var s = 0, stores = ['localStorage', 'sessionStorage']; s < stores.length; s++) {\\n      try {\\n        Object.defineProperty(root, stores[s], { configurable: true, value: memoryStorage() });\\n      } catch (e) {\\n110→        warn('could not give the game a fresh ' + stores[s]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\\n  // a generator seeded by the hub, so every copy builds the same start.\\n  var realRandom = Math.random;\\n  var seededRandom = null;\\n  if (hub.active && seedArg) {\\n120→    Math.random = seededRandom = generator(Number(seedArg[1]) >>> 0);\\n    hub.seeded = true;\\n  }\\n\\n  // In a session the hub owns fullscreen: a game that asks for it gets the\\n  // hub's whole page, so the scoreboard and the hub's cards stay on top. The\\n  // hub says when its page goes in and out, so the game's own toggle and its\\n  // fullscreenchange listeners work as they always did.\\n  var fullscreenOn = false;\\n  if (hub.active && root.Element && root.document) {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/hub/session-client.txt\",\"offset\":90,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"\\n  /** mulberry32: numbers in [0, 1), the same sequence everywhere for the same 32-bit start. */\\n  function generator(a) {\\n    return function () {\\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\\n      var t = a;\\n      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  // A fair start: in a session the game gets an empty storage of its own, so\\n  // every round starts as a first launch (no saved unlocks, upgrades or runs),\\n  // and nothing the round saves touches the player's own saves.\\n  if (hub.active) {\\n    for (var s = 0, stores = ['localStorage', 'sessionStorage']; s < stores.length; s++) {\\n      try {\\n        Object.defineProperty(root, stores[s], { configurable: true, value: memoryStorage() });\\n      } catch (e) {\\n        warn('could not give the game a fresh ' + stores[s]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\\n  // a generator seeded by the hub, so every copy builds the same start.\\n  var realRandom = Math.random;\\n  var seededRandom = null;\\n  if (hub.active && seedArg) {\\n    Math.random = seededRandom = generator(Number(seedArg[1]) >>> 0);\\n    hub.seeded = true;\\n  }\\n\\n  // In a session the hub owns fullscreen: a game that asks for it gets the\\n  // hub's whole page, so the scoreboard and the hub's cards stay on top. The\\n  // hub says when its page goes in and out, so the game's own toggle and its\\n  // fullscreenchange listeners work as they always did.\\n  var fullscreenOn = false;\\n  if (hub.active && root.Element && root.document) {\\n\",\"total_lines\":488}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"d5b3dd4d-308f-4fce-b698-7d1628311bce"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_258","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"AIHub.rng('card') returns a function that yields a random number between 0 and 1.\n\nThe card will use the RNG for decorative numbers only. Gameplay uses w.rng instead.\n\nThe client script is always present in the HTML. I will only call connect if AIHub.active is true. Otherwise the client stays inactive and Math.random remains unseeded. Standalone tests verify this behavior.\n\nI am ready to write the code.\n\nA lines test will verify the book's length and sentence count. Node tests can import book.ts directly since it is pure. voice.ts and songs.ts define audio at import time, but tests will not import main so they avoid side effects. A Node script for audio verification is blocked because Node cannot import TypeScript without a bundler.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b74a35bd-ffb6-4018-8ee7-ddde0bd6f3df-111","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"labs/game/(scenes/play|best|bot)","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656","glob":"*.{ts,mjs,json}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":698,"output_tokens":514,"cache_read_input_tokens":144512,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"4aed73b3-0b70-4e38-a8df-cd9baed31275"}
