{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_270","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Running the retreat test for band \"survives a mash\" to verify the kit change.\n\nWriting the remaining code now. Keeping clip objects small. Fixing wobble spawn logic so drawSway spawns seat 0 and groups handle extra spawns, while island avoids extra wobbles. Assigning move intents to actors using Partial<Intents> types.\n\nConfirmed that live actor queries return mutable components during simulation steps. Will implement island walking in the scene step. Sea bobbing will use a sine wave on sceneProp.y, oscillating with Math.sin(w.time * 0.4).\n\nConfirmed that fixed props without bodies draw from component x, y, z. Adding hidden pebble logic and defining the STATIONS array with coordinates and text labels.\n\nFinished the STATIONS array with the remaining entries. The noticeboard is page UI, not a station. A mark at 6, -8 shows notice.board text and opens the programme on act when near or via Tab. The pilot sets act.text to the station ID within 3.5m in roam mode. Pressing an actor starts the game only if the text is a known activity ID; plaque lines are ignored.\n\nPlaque text uses line IDs like 'plaque.lean'. The page starts a station event only when the actor is near a station and in roam mode; the simulation writes act.text during roam but leaves it alone while an activity runs. Pebbles are collectible marks: within 1.4 units of a free pebble, the actor takes it, increments the pebble count, and sets the line to 'find.pebble'. Spawn positions will be cast onto the flat ground.\n\nGuest actors will use a build animation and a zero-speed hold clip. The set build is defined at module level after the clip set. Other cast members without animations may lack puppet meshes but still receive physics bodies.\n\nActors without animations will render as plain capsule entities, which is acceptable. The set build must be defined before any animated spawn to prevent import-time errors from a missing REST body. The role component is already registered in state.ts through the driver boot chain, so island can safely spawn it. I will now write the clip definitions and run a quick vitest node test.\n\nImporting the cast clips module before island spawns so the set build exists at import time. The shell will listen for card events to capture remaining seconds.\n\nIf no card event arrives, the shell will show a 10-second countdown and \"Get ready\". Enter and Space confirm readiness; Triangle or T requests more time. The harness fires synthetic Enter events without blocking them when no card is active. During play, Enter still acts as an actor command. Standalone mode handles repeated Enter presses safely even without a hub. On the title screen, Enter triggers uiAccept to select Begin.\n\nThe standalone test only requires the client to remain inactive and the screen to render, so starting the game via Enter is acceptable as long as no errors occur. The keydown handler must be guarded against throwing when no hub exists. Math.random will not be reseeded. The index error handler should avoid recording APP_START for harmless failures. A no-webgpu fallback path will be written before createEngine so the engine never downgrades.\n\nThe WebGPU fallback shows a \"WebGPU required\" message and returns early. The shell must still publish a minimal `__game` object so tests can read the error text. The iPhone touch test checks for a controller line, settings tap, no touch stick, and attract mode. Touch detection uses a matchMedia query for coarse pointers without hover. The settings button is type=button with id=touch-settings and must be visible and sized for Playwright to tap it.\n\nThe touch overlay stays on screen during attract mode. Taps do not start play; only the settings button opens the menu. Entering attract mode seeds the scene via inspector.set and inspector.seed, which restarts the simulation while preserving the settings overlay. Exiting attract mode turns off auto and returns to the title screen. The save routine is skipped before entering attract.\n\nThe idle clock resets on key, mouse, pad, and touch input. Tapping the settings button should not reset attract mode; taps must reach only Settings and never start play.\n\nPointer events on touch devices will not exit attract mode, while keyboard and pad input still do. The idle timeout is set to 10000 ms.\n\nThe attract timer starts once the frame loop reaches 10000 ms, so the test at 10.5 s should catch it. Front-end menus such as title, settings, controls, about, programme, and erase will not block attract mode; if a menu is open when attract begins, the system closes it and shows the demo banner. Play screen remains locked out of attract.\n\nThe screen state will be 'title' initially and switch to 'play', 'results', 'evening', or 'credits' during the flow, unless a menu is open. During attract mode, the screen will be set to 'attract' so tests can observe the demo activities. Dev mode will be hidden when hubInfo is present. The pause overlay in the hub will not call inspector.pause().\n\nWiring song selection into the frame loop. The active track switches based on flow state: lobby for title and roam, stillness for morning and pose, water for line and paddle, rake for garden, tilt for storm, dawn for credits, and a single stamp for results. Audio intensity scales with the day cycle. Voice lines trigger whenever the flow line changes.\n\nSpeaker roles are mapped from line ID prefixes: ask and tare for ask/tare, pose plumb for pose, line tare for line, tilt plumb for tilt, group plumb for group, evening tare for evening, credits tare for credits, and plaque tare for the noticeboard. The say() function will use the audio module, and silent playback before a user gesture is acceptable since tests render offline. The engine index exports renderSong and renderSfx so audio tests can import them directly. Scene tests remain simulation-side and are not subject to public-API restrictions.\n\nAudio tests can import the engine directly because they sit outside the scenes directory. Voice lines will be kept to two sentences or fewer, with no ellipsis and no exclamation marks. A simple FNV-1a hash function is being added to the say module for deterministic playback.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ca09a475-71c2-4c13-a203-4d9ad82d1388-125","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"filter: \\{ type: 'bandpass'","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/audio","glob":"*.ts","head_limit":5}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1824,"output_tokens":3019,"cache_read_input_tokens":156800,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"17c85b08-4a3a-4fd9-8dfa-666e6a0388e0"}
