{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5e49c3d6-64e6-43b4-be05-0f7cc12fc1ed-69","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Action maps and presets (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24; doctrine: Common ground): the registry kind `actionMap`, a set\\n * of named actions with the physical codes bound to each (engine/input/codes.ts), as Unity's action maps and Godot's\\n * InputMap hold them; the presets; and the system layer, which no player rebinds.\\n *\\n * An action is a button the sim reads: held actions arrive as the intents' `b`, pressed ones as `p`\\n * (engine/input/intents.ts). The four actions a map names in `move` (forward, back, left, right) are not buttons:\\n * their strengths make the move axes `[right − left, forward − back]`, so keys walk at full speed and a half-pushed\\n * stick at half, and `fromCamera` turns the axes into a world direction. `values` writes an action's analog strength\\n10→ * (a trigger) as a custom intent. `look: true` (first person, the shooter) adds the camera's view direction as `look`,\\n * `aimWith` names the rule that gives the intents' `aim` its point (engine/input/aim.ts: the screen centre's ray, the\\n * pointer's onto the floor, or none; the action `aim`, where a map has one, raises the sights), and `lock: true` takes\\n * the pointer lock on a click so the mouse turns the view (with the cursor free, it points and aims). The actions a\\n * map names in `view` (a camera switch, a view's turn) are the page's: bound and rebound like the others, never\\n * buttons in the intents (`createEngine({ onView })`). A game with several camera modes gives each its own map\\n * (`createEngine({ actionMap })`, WP 13.9).\\n *\\n * The system layer (`SYSTEM_ACTIONS`): pause, and the menu's accept, cancel and directions. It is always active\\n * beside the map, never rebound, and never part of the intents: the app and the UI read it (`input.pressed('pause')`),\\n20→ * so remapping movement never breaks a menu (the lesson of `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md`). `RESERVED_CODES` (the\\n * pause buttons, and keys the browser or system keeps) and a map's own `reserved` codes are refused by rebinding.\\n *\\n * Invariants (`CORE_BAD_SPEC` when broken): every code is valid (`isCode`), action names are lower-case words\\n * (`jump`, `skill2`) and none is a system action, `move` names four actions of the map and `view` others, `values` keys\\n * are namespaced custom intents naming actions of the map, and no action binds a reserved code. The presets are registered on the\\n * shared registry when this module loads.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:670-693` (`Input.DEFAULT`, `PLATFORMER`, `SHMUP`, `MENU_KEYS`) with 3D\\n * movement, and shardfall's layer that is never rebound (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:131-161`).\\n30→ *\\n * @example\\n * const map = getActionMap('actionMap:thirdPerson');\\n * map.actions.jump; // ['Space', 'PadSouth']\\n * map.move; // ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right']\\n * SYSTEM_ACTIONS.pause; // ['Escape', 'PadStart']\\n * listActionMaps().map((entry) => entry.id); // ['actionMap:firstPerson', 'actionMap:platformer', …]\\n * @see engine/input/bindings.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\\n40→import { show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\\nimport { AIM_RULES, type AimRule } from './aim';\\nimport { isCode } from './codes';\\n\\n/** The system layer: action → codes. Always active, never rebound, never in the intents. */\\nexport const SYSTEM_ACTIONS: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>> = Object.freeze({\\n  pause: ['Escape', 'PadStart'],\\n  uiAccept: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Space', 'PadSouth'],\\n  uiCancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'PadEast'],\\n  uiUp: ['ArrowUp', 'PadUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\\n50→  uiDown: ['ArrowDown', 'PadDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\\n  uiLeft: ['ArrowLeft', 'PadLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\\n  uiRight: ['ArrowRight', 'PadRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\\n});\\n\\n/** Codes no action map binds: the pause buttons, and keys the browser or the system keeps. */\\nexport const RESERVED_CODES: readonly string[] = Object.freeze([\\n  'Escape',\\n  'PadStart',\\n  'PadHome',\\n60→  'F5',\\n  'F11',\\n  'F12',\\n  'MetaLeft',\\n  'MetaRight',\\n]);\\n\\n/** The fields of an `actionMap` entry. */\\nconst ACTION_MAP_FIELDS = {\\n  description: { type: 'string', default: '', description: 'What the map is for, in plain words.' },\\n70→  actions: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    required: true,\\n    description:\\n      'Action name → the codes bound to it (KeyboardEvent.code, MouseLeft…, PadSouth…, PadLeftStickUp…): held actions are the intents b, pressed ones p.',\\n  },\\n  move: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right'],\\n80→    description: 'The four actions that walk, as forward, back, left, right: their strengths make the move axes.',\\n  },\\n  values: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: {},\\n    description:\\n      'Custom intent key (\\\"game:throttle\\\") → action: its analog strength (0 to 1, a trigger) is that intent.',\\n  },\\n  look: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n90→    default: false,\\n    description: \\\"True for first person and the shooter: the intents carry look = [the camera's yaw, its pitch].\\\",\\n  },\\n  aimWith: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: AIM_RULES,\\n    default: 'none',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"What the intents' aim holds: none; centre, the point the screen centre's ray meets (first person, the shooter); pointer, the pointer's ray onto the player's floor or a right stick's push (isometric, top-down).\\\",\\n  },\\n100→  lock: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n    default: false,\\n    description:\\n      'True when the mouse turns the view: a click on the game takes the pointer lock, which pause and Escape give back.',\\n  },\\n  view: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: [],\\n110→    description:\\n      \\\"Actions the page reads for its view (a camera switch, a view's turn): bound and rebound like the others, never buttons in the intents.\\\",\\n  },\\n  reserved: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: [],\\n    description: 'Codes the game keeps for its own hotkeys: rebinding refuses them, as it refuses RESERVED_CODES.',\\n  },\\n} as const satisfies Schema;\\n120→\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Action maps and presets (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24; doctrine: Common ground): the registry kind `actionMap`, a set\\n * of named actions with the physical codes bound to each (engine/input/codes.ts), as Unity's action maps and Godot's\\n * InputMap hold them; the presets; and the system layer, which no player rebinds.\\n *\\n * An action is a button the sim reads: held actions arrive as the intents' `b`, pressed ones as `p`\\n * (engine/input/intents.ts). The four actions a map names in `move` (forward, back, left, right) are not buttons:\\n * their strengths make the move axes `[right − left, forward − back]`, so keys walk at full speed and a half-pushed\\n * stick at half, and `fromCamera` turns the axes into a world direction. `values` writes an action's analog strength\\n10→ * (a trigger) as a custom intent. `look: true` (first person, the shooter) adds the camera's view direction as `look`,\\n * `aimWith` names the rule that gives the intents' `aim` its point (engine/input/aim.ts: the screen centre's ray, the\\n * pointer's onto the floor, or none; the action `aim`, where a map has one, raises the sights), and `lock: true` takes\\n * the pointer lock on a click so the mouse turns the view (with the cursor free, it points and aims). The actions a\\n * map names in `view` (a camera switch, a view's turn) are the page's: bound and rebound like the others, never\\n * buttons in the intents (`createEngine({ onView })`). A game with several camera modes gives each its own map\\n * (`createEngine({ actionMap })`, WP 13.9).\\n *\\n * The system layer (`SYSTEM_ACTIONS`): pause, and the menu's accept, cancel and directions. It is always active\\n * beside the map, never rebound, and never part of the intents: the app and the UI read it (`input.pressed('pause')`),\\n20→ * so remapping movement never breaks a menu (the lesson of `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md`). `RESERVED_CODES` (the\\n * pause buttons, and keys the browser or system keeps) and a map's own `reserved` codes are refused by rebinding.\\n *\\n * Invariants (`CORE_BAD_SPEC` when broken): every code is valid (`isCode`), action names are lower-case words\\n * (`jump`, `skill2`) and none is a system action, `move` names four actions of the map and `view` others, `values` keys\\n * are namespaced custom intents naming actions of the map, and no action binds a reserved code. The presets are registered on the\\n * shared registry when this module loads.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:670-693` (`Input.DEFAULT`, `PLATFORMER`, `SHMUP`, `MENU_KEYS`) with 3D\\n * movement, and shardfall's layer that is never rebound (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:131-161`).\\n30→ *\\n * @example\\n * const map = getActionMap('actionMap:thirdPerson');\\n * map.actions.jump; // ['Space', 'PadSouth']\\n * map.move; // ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right']\\n * SYSTEM_ACTIONS.pause; // ['Escape', 'PadStart']\\n * listActionMaps().map((entry) => entry.id); // ['actionMap:firstPerson', 'actionMap:platformer', …]\\n * @see engine/input/bindings.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\\n40→import { show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\\nimport { AIM_RULES, type AimRule } from './aim';\\nimport { isCode } from './codes';\\n\\n/** The system layer: action → codes. Always active, never rebound, never in the intents. */\\nexport const SYSTEM_ACTIONS: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>> = Object.freeze({\\n  pause: ['Escape', 'PadStart'],\\n  uiAccept: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Space', 'PadSouth'],\\n  uiCancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'PadEast'],\\n  uiUp: ['ArrowUp', 'PadUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\\n50→  uiDown: ['ArrowDown', 'PadDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\\n  uiLeft: ['ArrowLeft', 'PadLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\\n  uiRight: ['ArrowRight', 'PadRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\\n});\\n\\n/** Codes no action map binds: the pause buttons, and keys the browser or the system keeps. */\\nexport const RESERVED_CODES: readonly string[] = Object.freeze([\\n  'Escape',\\n  'PadStart',\\n  'PadHome',\\n60→  'F5',\\n  'F11',\\n  'F12',\\n  'MetaLeft',\\n  'MetaRight',\\n]);\\n\\n/** The fields of an `actionMap` entry. */\\nconst ACTION_MAP_FIELDS = {\\n  description: { type: 'string', default: '', description: 'What the map is for, in plain words.' },\\n70→  actions: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    required: true,\\n    description:\\n      'Action name → the codes bound to it (KeyboardEvent.code, MouseLeft…, PadSouth…, PadLeftStickUp…): held actions are the intents b, pressed ones p.',\\n  },\\n  move: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right'],\\n80→    description: 'The four actions that walk, as forward, back, left, right: their strengths make the move axes.',\\n  },\\n  values: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: {},\\n    description:\\n      'Custom intent key (\\\"game:throttle\\\") → action: its analog strength (0 to 1, a trigger) is that intent.',\\n  },\\n  look: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n90→    default: false,\\n    description: \\\"True for first person and the shooter: the intents carry look = [the camera's yaw, its pitch].\\\",\\n  },\\n  aimWith: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: AIM_RULES,\\n    default: 'none',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"What the intents' aim holds: none; centre, the point the screen centre's ray meets (first person, the shooter); pointer, the pointer's ray onto the player's floor or a right stick's push (isometric, top-down).\\\",\\n  },\\n100→  lock: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n    default: false,\\n    description:\\n      'True when the mouse turns the view: a click on the game takes the pointer lock, which pause and Escape give back.',\\n  },\\n  view: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: [],\\n110→    description:\\n      \\\"Actions the page reads for its view (a camera switch, a view's turn): bound and rebound like the others, never buttons in the intents.\\\",\\n  },\\n  reserved: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: [],\\n    description: 'Codes the game keeps for its own hotkeys: rebinding refuses them, as it refuses RESERVED_CODES.',\\n  },\\n} as const satisfies Schema;\\n120→\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/actionMaps.ts\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file Action maps and presets (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24; doctrine: Common ground): the registry kind `actionMap`, a set\\n * of named actions with the physical codes bound to each (engine/input/codes.ts), as Unity's action maps and Godot's\\n * InputMap hold them; the presets; and the system layer, which no player rebinds.\\n *\\n * An action is a button the sim reads: held actions arrive as the intents' `b`, pressed ones as `p`\\n * (engine/input/intents.ts). The four actions a map names in `move` (forward, back, left, right) are not buttons:\\n * their strengths make the move axes `[right − left, forward − back]`, so keys walk at full speed and a half-pushed\\n * stick at half, and `fromCamera` turns the axes into a world direction. `values` writes an action's analog strength\\n * (a trigger) as a custom intent. `look: true` (first person, the shooter) adds the camera's view direction as `look`,\\n * `aimWith` names the rule that gives the intents' `aim` its point (engine/input/aim.ts: the screen centre's ray, the\\n * pointer's onto the floor, or none; the action `aim`, where a map has one, raises the sights), and `lock: true` takes\\n * the pointer lock on a click so the mouse turns the view (with the cursor free, it points and aims). The actions a\\n * map names in `view` (a camera switch, a view's turn) are the page's: bound and rebound like the others, never\\n * buttons in the intents (`createEngine({ onView })`). A game with several camera modes gives each its own map\\n * (`createEngine({ actionMap })`, WP 13.9).\\n *\\n * The system layer (`SYSTEM_ACTIONS`): pause, and the menu's accept, cancel and directions. It is always active\\n * beside the map, never rebound, and never part of the intents: the app and the UI read it (`input.pressed('pause')`),\\n * so remapping movement never breaks a menu (the lesson of `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md`). `RESERVED_CODES` (the\\n * pause buttons, and keys the browser or system keeps) and a map's own `reserved` codes are refused by rebinding.\\n *\\n * Invariants (`CORE_BAD_SPEC` when broken): every code is valid (`isCode`), action names are lower-case words\\n * (`jump`, `skill2`) and none is a system action, `move` names four actions of the map and `view` others, `values` keys\\n * are namespaced custom intents naming actions of the map, and no action binds a reserved code. The presets are registered on the\\n * shared registry when this module loads.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:670-693` (`Input.DEFAULT`, `PLATFORMER`, `SHMUP`, `MENU_KEYS`) with 3D\\n * movement, and shardfall's layer that is never rebound (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:131-161`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * const map = getActionMap('actionMap:thirdPerson');\\n * map.actions.jump; // ['Space', 'PadSouth']\\n * map.move; // ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right']\\n * SYSTEM_ACTIONS.pause; // ['Escape', 'PadStart']\\n * listActionMaps().map((entry) => entry.id); // ['actionMap:firstPerson', 'actionMap:platformer', …]\\n * @see engine/input/bindings.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\\nimport { show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\\nimport { AIM_RULES, type AimRule } from './aim';\\nimport { isCode } from './codes';\\n\\n/** The system layer: action → codes. Always active, never rebound, never in the intents. */\\nexport const SYSTEM_ACTIONS: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>> = Object.freeze({\\n  pause: ['Escape', 'PadStart'],\\n  uiAccept: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Space', 'PadSouth'],\\n  uiCancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'PadEast'],\\n  uiUp: ['ArrowUp', 'PadUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\\n  uiDown: ['ArrowDown', 'PadDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\\n  uiLeft: ['ArrowLeft', 'PadLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\\n  uiRight: ['ArrowRight', 'PadRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\\n});\\n\\n/** Codes no action map binds: the pause buttons, and keys the browser or the system keeps. */\\nexport const RESERVED_CODES: readonly string[] = Object.freeze([\\n  'Escape',\\n  'PadStart',\\n  'PadHome',\\n  'F5',\\n  'F11',\\n  'F12',\\n  'MetaLeft',\\n  'MetaRight',\\n]);\\n\\n/** The fields of an `actionMap` entry. */\\nconst ACTION_MAP_FIELDS = {\\n  description: { type: 'string', default: '', description: 'What the map is for, in plain words.' },\\n  actions: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    required: true,\\n    description:\\n      'Action name → the codes bound to it (KeyboardEvent.code, MouseLeft…, PadSouth…, PadLeftStickUp…): held actions are the intents b, pressed ones p.',\\n  },\\n  move: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right'],\\n    description: 'The four actions that walk, as forward, back, left, right: their strengths make the move axes.',\\n  },\\n  values: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: {},\\n    description:\\n      'Custom intent key (\\\"game:throttle\\\") → action: its analog strength (0 to 1, a trigger) is that intent.',\\n  },\\n  look: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n    default: false,\\n    description: \\\"True for first person and the shooter: the intents carry look = [the camera's yaw, its pitch].\\\",\\n  },\\n  aimWith: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: AIM_RULES,\\n    default: 'none',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"What the intents' aim holds: none; centre, the point the screen centre's ray meets (first person, the shooter); pointer, the pointer's ray onto the player's floor or a right stick's push (isometric, top-down).\\\",\\n  },\\n  lock: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n    default: false,\\n    description:\\n      'True when the mouse turns the view: a click on the game takes the pointer lock, which pause and Escape give back.',\\n  },\\n  view: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: [],\\n    description:\\n      \\\"Actions the page reads for its view (a camera switch, a view's turn): bound and rebound like the others, never buttons in the intents.\\\",\\n  },\\n  reserved: {\\n    type: 'array',\\n    items: { type: 'string' },\\n    default: [],\\n    description: 'Codes the game keeps for its own hotkeys: rebinding refuses them, as it refuses RESERVED_CODES.',\\n  },\\n} as const satisfies Schema;\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":275}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5e49c3d6-64e6-43b4-be05-0f7cc12fc1ed-70","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The menu (PLAN.md §6.7, WP 10.6, I-50): a list with a cursor, for title screens, pause menus, settings and\\n * shops, as HTML/CSS over the overlay. `createMenu(parent, items, { input, sound, title, place, onPick, onCancel,\\n * onMove, send })` makes it open; `update(dt)` each frame reads the page's input and returns true when it picked or\\n * cancelled.\\n *\\n * `uiUp` and `uiDown` (keys, the pad's D-pad and left stick; held, they repeat: engine/ui/widgets.ts `createRepeat`)\\n * move the cursor over the items, round the ends, past disabled ones; `uiAccept` picks the item under it, `uiCancel`\\n * calls `onCancel` when there is one; a pointer moving over an item moves the cursor there (a menu opening under a still\\n10→ * pointer, or rows shifting under it, moves none), a click picks it. A gamepad drives the menu with its buttons, and any\\n * other panel through the pad's cursor (`createPadCursor`).\\n *\\n * Picks that change play: the system layer never enters the intents (engine/input/actionMaps.ts), so a menu never\\n * reaches the sim itself. An item with an `id` is handed to `send(id)` when picked, which the page turns into input\\n * the session records (a dev action, `__engine.actions.run`, or a custom intent for the next step), so the replay\\n * holds the pick; `onPick` hears every pick, for what only the page changes (a look, a panel).\\n *\\n * Elements: `[data-ui=menu]` (`data-id`, `data-value` the cursor's index; `data-place`), its `[data-ui=menu-title]`,\\n * and a `[data-ui=item]` per item (`data-id` its id or index, `data-value` `selected`, `disabled` or empty). Cues: `move`,\\n20→ * `pick`, `cancel`. Invariants: presentation only; `active: false` reads no input; the cursor never rests on a disabled\\n * item while another is enabled. Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:4288-4330` (`Menu`: items, disabled ones\\n * skipped, onPick, onCancel, onMove) and shardfall's rule that menu actions reach the game as input (§5.8).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // browser: the menu needs a page\\n * // const pause = createMenu(ui.root, ['Resume', { label: 'Restart', id: 'restart' }], {\\n * //   input, title: 'Paused', onCancel: () => pause.remove(), send: (id) => engine.actions.run(id) });\\n * // pause.update(dt); // each frame\\n * @see engine/ui/menu.test.ts\\n30→ * @see tests/e2e/ui.spec.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes } from '../core/log';\\nimport { createRepeat, setText, uiElement, widgetStyle, type UiInput, type UiSound } from './widgets';\\n\\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\\nexport const MENU_CODES = defineCodes('ui', {\\n  UI_BAD_MENU: {\\n    template: 'menu: {problem}',\\n    fix: \\\"give items as strings or { label, id?, disabled? }, and update(dt) the frame's seconds, 0 or more\\\",\\n40→    doc: 'Raised by the menu (engine/ui/menu.ts) for an item that is neither a string nor `{ label, id?, disabled? }`, or a frame time that is not a number of seconds from 0.',\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** One menu item: its label, or `{ label, id, disabled }` (an `id` is sent when picked). */\\nexport type MenuItem = string | { readonly label: string; readonly id?: string; readonly disabled?: boolean };\\n\\n/** Where the menu stands. */\\nexport type MenuPlace = 'center' | 'top' | 'bottom';\\n\\n50→/** How a menu is made. */\\nexport interface MenuOptions {\\n  input: UiInput;\\n  sound?: UiSound;\\n  /** Its id (`data-id`). */\\n  id?: string;\\n  title?: string;\\n  /** Where it stands (`center`). */\\n  place?: MenuPlace;\\n  onPick?(index: number, item: MenuItem): void;\\n60→  onCancel?(): void;\\n  onMove?(index: number, item: MenuItem): void;\\n  /** Hands a picked item's id to the page, which records it as input (see the file comment). */\\n  send?(id: string): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** The menu (see the file comment). */\\nexport interface Menu {\\n  readonly el: HTMLElement;\\n  /** The cursor's index, and its item. */\\n70→  readonly index: number;\\n  readonly selected: MenuItem | undefined;\\n  /** False: it reads no input (another menu over it has the input). */\\n  active: boolean;\\n  /** Reads the input for a frame of `dt` s; true when it picked or cancelled. Throws `UI_BAD_MENU`. */\\n  update(dt: number): boolean;\\n  /** Moves the cursor to `index` (a disabled item: the next enabled one after it). */\\n  select(index: number): void;\\n  /** Picks the item under the cursor, as accept does; false when it is disabled. */\\n  pick(): boolean;\\n80→  /** Replaces the items, keeping the cursor where it can. Throws `UI_BAD_MENU`. */\\n  setItems(items: readonly MenuItem[]): void;\\n  remove(): void;\\n}\\n\\nconst labelOf = (item: MenuItem) => (typeof item === 'string' ? item : item.label);\\nconst off = (item: MenuItem | undefined) => typeof item === 'object' && item.disabled === true;\\n\\n/** Makes an open menu of `items` in `parent` (see the file comment). */\\nexport function createMenu(parent: HTMLElement, items: readonly MenuItem[], options: MenuOptions): Menu {\\n90→  widgetStyle(parent.ownerDocument);\\n  const { input, sound = () => {} } = options;\\n  const el = uiElement(parent, 'ui-panel ui-menu', 'menu', options.id);\\n  el.dataset.place = options.place ?? 'center';\\n  if (options.title) el.append(Object.assign(uiElement(el, 'ui-menu-title', 'menu-title'), { textContent: options.title })); // prettier-ignore\\n  parent.append(el);\\n  const repeat = createRepeat();\\n  let list: MenuItem[] = [];\\n  let rows: HTMLElement[] = [];\\n  let index = 0;\\n100→\\n  /** `index` stepped by `dir` until an enabled item (or all the way round). */\\n  const skip = (from: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\\n    let at = from;\\n    for (let k = 0; k < list.length && off(list[at]); k++) at = (at + dir + list.length) % list.length;\\n    return at;\\n  };\\n  const draw = () => {\\n    if (el.dataset.value !== String(index)) el.dataset.value = String(index);\\n    rows.forEach((row, i) => {\\n110→      const value = off(list[i]) ? 'disabled' : i === index ? 'selected' : '';\\n      if (row.dataset.value !== value) row.dataset.value = value;\\n    });\\n  };\\n  const move = (to: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\\n    if (!list.length) return;\\n    const next = skip(((to % list.length) + list.length) % list.length, dir);\\n    if (next === index) return;\\n    index = next;\\n    sound('move');\\n120→    draw();\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The menu (PLAN.md §6.7, WP 10.6, I-50): a list with a cursor, for title screens, pause menus, settings and\\n * shops, as HTML/CSS over the overlay. `createMenu(parent, items, { input, sound, title, place, onPick, onCancel,\\n * onMove, send })` makes it open; `update(dt)` each frame reads the page's input and returns true when it picked or\\n * cancelled.\\n *\\n * `uiUp` and `uiDown` (keys, the pad's D-pad and left stick; held, they repeat: engine/ui/widgets.ts `createRepeat`)\\n * move the cursor over the items, round the ends, past disabled ones; `uiAccept` picks the item under it, `uiCancel`\\n * calls `onCancel` when there is one; a pointer moving over an item moves the cursor there (a menu opening under a still\\n10→ * pointer, or rows shifting under it, moves none), a click picks it. A gamepad drives the menu with its buttons, and any\\n * other panel through the pad's cursor (`createPadCursor`).\\n *\\n * Picks that change play: the system layer never enters the intents (engine/input/actionMaps.ts), so a menu never\\n * reaches the sim itself. An item with an `id` is handed to `send(id)` when picked, which the page turns into input\\n * the session records (a dev action, `__engine.actions.run`, or a custom intent for the next step), so the replay\\n * holds the pick; `onPick` hears every pick, for what only the page changes (a look, a panel).\\n *\\n * Elements: `[data-ui=menu]` (`data-id`, `data-value` the cursor's index; `data-place`), its `[data-ui=menu-title]`,\\n * and a `[data-ui=item]` per item (`data-id` its id or index, `data-value` `selected`, `disabled` or empty). Cues: `move`,\\n20→ * `pick`, `cancel`. Invariants: presentation only; `active: false` reads no input; the cursor never rests on a disabled\\n * item while another is enabled. Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:4288-4330` (`Menu`: items, disabled ones\\n * skipped, onPick, onCancel, onMove) and shardfall's rule that menu actions reach the game as input (§5.8).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // browser: the menu needs a page\\n * // const pause = createMenu(ui.root, ['Resume', { label: 'Restart', id: 'restart' }], {\\n * //   input, title: 'Paused', onCancel: () => pause.remove(), send: (id) => engine.actions.run(id) });\\n * // pause.update(dt); // each frame\\n * @see engine/ui/menu.test.ts\\n30→ * @see tests/e2e/ui.spec.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes } from '../core/log';\\nimport { createRepeat, setText, uiElement, widgetStyle, type UiInput, type UiSound } from './widgets';\\n\\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\\nexport const MENU_CODES = defineCodes('ui', {\\n  UI_BAD_MENU: {\\n    template: 'menu: {problem}',\\n    fix: \\\"give items as strings or { label, id?, disabled? }, and update(dt) the frame's seconds, 0 or more\\\",\\n40→    doc: 'Raised by the menu (engine/ui/menu.ts) for an item that is neither a string nor `{ label, id?, disabled? }`, or a frame time that is not a number of seconds from 0.',\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** One menu item: its label, or `{ label, id, disabled }` (an `id` is sent when picked). */\\nexport type MenuItem = string | { readonly label: string; readonly id?: string; readonly disabled?: boolean };\\n\\n/** Where the menu stands. */\\nexport type MenuPlace = 'center' | 'top' | 'bottom';\\n\\n50→/** How a menu is made. */\\nexport interface MenuOptions {\\n  input: UiInput;\\n  sound?: UiSound;\\n  /** Its id (`data-id`). */\\n  id?: string;\\n  title?: string;\\n  /** Where it stands (`center`). */\\n  place?: MenuPlace;\\n  onPick?(index: number, item: MenuItem): void;\\n60→  onCancel?(): void;\\n  onMove?(index: number, item: MenuItem): void;\\n  /** Hands a picked item's id to the page, which records it as input (see the file comment). */\\n  send?(id: string): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** The menu (see the file comment). */\\nexport interface Menu {\\n  readonly el: HTMLElement;\\n  /** The cursor's index, and its item. */\\n70→  readonly index: number;\\n  readonly selected: MenuItem | undefined;\\n  /** False: it reads no input (another menu over it has the input). */\\n  active: boolean;\\n  /** Reads the input for a frame of `dt` s; true when it picked or cancelled. Throws `UI_BAD_MENU`. */\\n  update(dt: number): boolean;\\n  /** Moves the cursor to `index` (a disabled item: the next enabled one after it). */\\n  select(index: number): void;\\n  /** Picks the item under the cursor, as accept does; false when it is disabled. */\\n  pick(): boolean;\\n80→  /** Replaces the items, keeping the cursor where it can. Throws `UI_BAD_MENU`. */\\n  setItems(items: readonly MenuItem[]): void;\\n  remove(): void;\\n}\\n\\nconst labelOf = (item: MenuItem) => (typeof item === 'string' ? item : item.label);\\nconst off = (item: MenuItem | undefined) => typeof item === 'object' && item.disabled === true;\\n\\n/** Makes an open menu of `items` in `parent` (see the file comment). */\\nexport function createMenu(parent: HTMLElement, items: readonly MenuItem[], options: MenuOptions): Menu {\\n90→  widgetStyle(parent.ownerDocument);\\n  const { input, sound = () => {} } = options;\\n  const el = uiElement(parent, 'ui-panel ui-menu', 'menu', options.id);\\n  el.dataset.place = options.place ?? 'center';\\n  if (options.title) el.append(Object.assign(uiElement(el, 'ui-menu-title', 'menu-title'), { textContent: options.title })); // prettier-ignore\\n  parent.append(el);\\n  const repeat = createRepeat();\\n  let list: MenuItem[] = [];\\n  let rows: HTMLElement[] = [];\\n  let index = 0;\\n100→\\n  /** `index` stepped by `dir` until an enabled item (or all the way round). */\\n  const skip = (from: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\\n    let at = from;\\n    for (let k = 0; k < list.length && off(list[at]); k++) at = (at + dir + list.length) % list.length;\\n    return at;\\n  };\\n  const draw = () => {\\n    if (el.dataset.value !== String(index)) el.dataset.value = String(index);\\n    rows.forEach((row, i) => {\\n110→      const value = off(list[i]) ? 'disabled' : i === index ? 'selected' : '';\\n      if (row.dataset.value !== value) row.dataset.value = value;\\n    });\\n  };\\n  const move = (to: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\\n    if (!list.length) return;\\n    const next = skip(((to % list.length) + list.length) % list.length, dir);\\n    if (next === index) return;\\n    index = next;\\n    sound('move');\\n120→    draw();\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/ui/menu.ts\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The menu (PLAN.md §6.7, WP 10.6, I-50): a list with a cursor, for title screens, pause menus, settings and\\n * shops, as HTML/CSS over the overlay. `createMenu(parent, items, { input, sound, title, place, onPick, onCancel,\\n * onMove, send })` makes it open; `update(dt)` each frame reads the page's input and returns true when it picked or\\n * cancelled.\\n *\\n * `uiUp` and `uiDown` (keys, the pad's D-pad and left stick; held, they repeat: engine/ui/widgets.ts `createRepeat`)\\n * move the cursor over the items, round the ends, past disabled ones; `uiAccept` picks the item under it, `uiCancel`\\n * calls `onCancel` when there is one; a pointer moving over an item moves the cursor there (a menu opening under a still\\n * pointer, or rows shifting under it, moves none), a click picks it. A gamepad drives the menu with its buttons, and any\\n * other panel through the pad's cursor (`createPadCursor`).\\n *\\n * Picks that change play: the system layer never enters the intents (engine/input/actionMaps.ts), so a menu never\\n * reaches the sim itself. An item with an `id` is handed to `send(id)` when picked, which the page turns into input\\n * the session records (a dev action, `__engine.actions.run`, or a custom intent for the next step), so the replay\\n * holds the pick; `onPick` hears every pick, for what only the page changes (a look, a panel).\\n *\\n * Elements: `[data-ui=menu]` (`data-id`, `data-value` the cursor's index; `data-place`), its `[data-ui=menu-title]`,\\n * and a `[data-ui=item]` per item (`data-id` its id or index, `data-value` `selected`, `disabled` or empty). Cues: `move`,\\n * `pick`, `cancel`. Invariants: presentation only; `active: false` reads no input; the cursor never rests on a disabled\\n * item while another is enabled. Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:4288-4330` (`Menu`: items, disabled ones\\n * skipped, onPick, onCancel, onMove) and shardfall's rule that menu actions reach the game as input (§5.8).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // browser: the menu needs a page\\n * // const pause = createMenu(ui.root, ['Resume', { label: 'Restart', id: 'restart' }], {\\n * //   input, title: 'Paused', onCancel: () => pause.remove(), send: (id) => engine.actions.run(id) });\\n * // pause.update(dt); // each frame\\n * @see engine/ui/menu.test.ts\\n * @see tests/e2e/ui.spec.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes } from '../core/log';\\nimport { createRepeat, setText, uiElement, widgetStyle, type UiInput, type UiSound } from './widgets';\\n\\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\\nexport const MENU_CODES = defineCodes('ui', {\\n  UI_BAD_MENU: {\\n    template: 'menu: {problem}',\\n    fix: \\\"give items as strings or { label, id?, disabled? }, and update(dt) the frame's seconds, 0 or more\\\",\\n    doc: 'Raised by the menu (engine/ui/menu.ts) for an item that is neither a string nor `{ label, id?, disabled? }`, or a frame time that is not a number of seconds from 0.',\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** One menu item: its label, or `{ label, id, disabled }` (an `id` is sent when picked). */\\nexport type MenuItem = string | { readonly label: string; readonly id?: string; readonly disabled?: boolean };\\n\\n/** Where the menu stands. */\\nexport type MenuPlace = 'center' | 'top' | 'bottom';\\n\\n/** How a menu is made. */\\nexport interface MenuOptions {\\n  input: UiInput;\\n  sound?: UiSound;\\n  /** Its id (`data-id`). */\\n  id?: string;\\n  title?: string;\\n  /** Where it stands (`center`). */\\n  place?: MenuPlace;\\n  onPick?(index: number, item: MenuItem): void;\\n  onCancel?(): void;\\n  onMove?(index: number, item: MenuItem): void;\\n  /** Hands a picked item's id to the page, which records it as input (see the file comment). */\\n  send?(id: string): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** The menu (see the file comment). */\\nexport interface Menu {\\n  readonly el: HTMLElement;\\n  /** The cursor's index, and its item. */\\n  readonly index: number;\\n  readonly selected: MenuItem | undefined;\\n  /** False: it reads no input (another menu over it has the input). */\\n  active: boolean;\\n  /** Reads the input for a frame of `dt` s; true when it picked or cancelled. Throws `UI_BAD_MENU`. */\\n  update(dt: number): boolean;\\n  /** Moves the cursor to `index` (a disabled item: the next enabled one after it). */\\n  select(index: number): void;\\n  /** Picks the item under the cursor, as accept does; false when it is disabled. */\\n  pick(): boolean;\\n  /** Replaces the items, keeping the cursor where it can. Throws `UI_BAD_MENU`. */\\n  setItems(items: readonly MenuItem[]): void;\\n  remove(): void;\\n}\\n\\nconst labelOf = (item: MenuItem) => (typeof item === 'string' ? item : item.label);\\nconst off = (item: MenuItem | undefined) => typeof item === 'object' && item.disabled === true;\\n\\n/** Makes an open menu of `items` in `parent` (see the file comment). */\\nexport function createMenu(parent: HTMLElement, items: readonly MenuItem[], options: MenuOptions): Menu {\\n  widgetStyle(parent.ownerDocument);\\n  const { input, sound = () => {} } = options;\\n  const el = uiElement(parent, 'ui-panel ui-menu', 'menu', options.id);\\n  el.dataset.place = options.place ?? 'center';\\n  if (options.title) el.append(Object.assign(uiElement(el, 'ui-menu-title', 'menu-title'), { textContent: options.title })); // prettier-ignore\\n  parent.append(el);\\n  const repeat = createRepeat();\\n  let list: MenuItem[] = [];\\n  let rows: HTMLElement[] = [];\\n  let index = 0;\\n\\n  /** `index` stepped by `dir` until an enabled item (or all the way round). */\\n  const skip = (from: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\\n    let at = from;\\n    for (let k = 0; k < list.length && off(list[at]); k++) at = (at + dir + list.length) % list.length;\\n    return at;\\n  };\\n  const draw = () => {\\n    if (el.dataset.value !== String(index)) el.dataset.value = String(index);\\n    rows.forEach((row, i) => {\\n      const value = off(list[i]) ? 'disabled' : i === index ? 'selected' : '';\\n      if (row.dataset.value !== value) row.dataset.value = value;\\n    });\\n  };\\n  const move = (to: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\\n    if (!list.length) return;\\n    const next = skip(((to % list.length) + list.length) % list.length, dir);\\n    if (next === index) return;\\n    index = next;\\n    sound('move');\\n    draw();\\n\",\"total_lines\":187}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5e49c3d6-64e6-43b4-be05-0f7cc12fc1ed-71","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Looks (PLAN.md WP 7.4, §6.6 kind `look`): a material style (WP 7.2, engine/gfx/materials/styles.ts) plus a\\n * filter chain (engine/gfx/post/filters.ts), as data, and the sky that lights the scene (WP 7.8, a `sky` id,\\n * engine/gfx/sky.ts). A look names what it changes; every filter it leaves out is off, and a style or sky of `''`\\n * keeps the scene's own. The chain draws the look the setting `post.look` names (engine/gfx/post/chain.ts); switching\\n * looks writes uniforms and re-points materials to styles the warm-up has already compiled, so it builds no\\n * pipeline. A look's sky is shown by the pages `createEngine` starts (engine/app/look.ts): the stage's lights give way\\n * to it (engine/gfx/stageSky.ts), which changes the shader key, so a look with another sky warms up before it draws.\\n * WP 13.24 adds the toon style's `shade` and `dither`, what a look asks of the stage (`shells`, outline shells round\\n10→ * its props and bodies, engine/gfx/stageShells.ts; `skyGradient`, the dome as a clean gradient) and its variant for\\n * perspective cameras (`perspective`, a look id whose filters and toon numbers the chain draws there). WP 13.30 adds\\n * what it asks of the whole picture: `resolution`, the mode drawn while `gfx.resolution` is `auto`\\n * (engine/gfx/resolution.ts), and `textures`, every material's maps filtered `smooth` or `pixel`\\n * (engine/gfx/materials/library.ts `filter`); the page's look applies both (engine/app/look.ts), building nothing.\\n *\\n * The entries are seeded from shardfall's tuned presets (`shardfall:crates/pav_view/src/looks.toml`, with\\n * `look.rs:100-353`), keys renamed: its whole looks are here (`look:hd-2d`, `look:game-boy`…), and its one-section\\n * presets are looks of their own, grouped by the filter they set (`look:palette/game-boy`, `look:stylize/oil-paint`,\\n * engine/gfx/post/presets.ts). Its \\\"objects\\\" (characters and objects) is the scope `characters+objects`. Its air and\\n20→ * bounce light came with WP 11.5 (the `air` and `gi` sections, engine/gfx/post/shading.ts): the looks Sunbeams and\\n * Lamplit fog, and their presets. Left out: styles that differ by part and the knobs WP 7.2's styles lack\\n * (`flat_shadow`, `specular`, `exposure`), so four looks keep the scene's style where shardfall styled the parts\\n * apart. One rename for the lesson: \\\"64 colours\\\" posterized to 4 levels, which shifts the hue of dull colours, so it\\n * is `look:palette/512-colours`, at 8. WP 13.31 and 13.32 add Style Lab's presets and looks made by combining them\\n * (engine/gfx/post/presetsMore.ts), and every look's `combine` and `strength` (engine/gfx/post/combine.ts): the looks\\n * it lays on, how much of each and which of its filters, and how much of the whole look shows.\\n *\\n * Invariants: every look's levels are 0 or 8 and more (the kind's check); a missing id falls back to `look:clean`\\n * with a warning naming the closest ids; looks read their fields, never their ids. A game's own look is scaffolded by\\n30→ * `node x new look labs/<lab>/looks/<name>` (tools/templates/look/).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\\n * const registry = createRegistry();\\n * defineLooks(registry);\\n * registry.get('look', 'look:game-boy').filters.palette.palette; // 'gameboy'\\n * registry.list('look').length; // 137\\n * @see engine/gfx/post/looks.test.ts\\n * @see tests/e2e/post.spec.ts\\n40→ */\\nimport { galleryField } from '../../core/gallery';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\\nimport type { EntryOf, Schema } from '../../core/schema';\\nimport { MATERIAL_STYLES } from '../materials/styles';\\nimport { TOON_LOOK } from '../materials/toon';\\nimport { RESOLUTION_MODES } from '../resolution';\\nimport { TEXTURE_LOOKS } from '../textures/types';\\nimport { COMBINE_FIELD, STRENGTH_FIELD, type CombineLayer } from './combine';\\nimport { colorFields, colorProblem, FILTER_FIELDS, FILTER_NAMES, levelsProblem, type FilterSpec } from './filters';\\n50→import { PRESETS } from './presets';\\nimport { COMBINED_LOOKS, STYLE_PRESETS } from './presetsMore';\\n\\n/** Where a menu lists a look: `look` for a whole look, else the filter it presets, or `shading` for a style. */\\nexport const LOOK_GROUPS = ['look', 'shading', ...FILTER_NAMES] as const;\\n\\n/** The default of every filter: all of them off. */\\nconst OFF = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(FILTER_FIELDS).map(([name, field]) => [name, field.default]));\\n\\n/** The fields of a `look` entry; see the file comment. */\\n60→export const LOOK_FIELDS = {\\n  description: { type: 'string', default: '', description: 'What it looks like, in plain sentences.' },\\n  group: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: LOOK_GROUPS,\\n    default: 'look',\\n    description: \\\"Where a menu lists it: 'look' for a whole look, else the filter it presets ('shading' for a style).\\\",\\n  },\\n  style: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n70→    enum: ['', ...MATERIAL_STYLES],\\n    default: '',\\n    description: \\\"The material style everything is drawn in (lambert, toon, flat, pbr); '' keeps the scene's own.\\\",\\n  },\\n  sky: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    default: '',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"The sky preset that lights the scene (a 'sky' id: sky:hall, the torch-lit hall); '' keeps the scene's own lights.\\\",\\n  },\\n80→  toon: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: { ...TOON_LOOK },\\n    description: \\\"The toon style's bands, rim, shade and dither, used when the style is 'toon'.\\\",\\n    properties: {\\n      bands: { type: 'integer', default: TOON_LOOK.bands, minimum: 2, maximum: 8, description: 'Bands of light.' },\\n      rim: { type: 'number', default: TOON_LOOK.rim, minimum: 0, maximum: 1, description: \\\"The rim light's strength.\\\" },\\n      shade: {\\n        type: 'number',\\n        default: TOON_LOOK.shade,\\n90→        minimum: 0,\\n        maximum: 1,\\n        description: \\\"How far each material's shadows shift in hue (cooler, more saturated) from its colour darkened.\\\",\\n      },\\n      dither: {\\n        type: 'number',\\n        default: TOON_LOOK.dither,\\n        minimum: 0,\\n        maximum: 1,\\n        description:\\n100→          \\\"The share of each band's step mixed by an ordered dither fixed to the world, edges hard; 0 smooths.\\\",\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Looks (PLAN.md WP 7.4, §6.6 kind `look`): a material style (WP 7.2, engine/gfx/materials/styles.ts) plus a\\n * filter chain (engine/gfx/post/filters.ts), as data, and the sky that lights the scene (WP 7.8, a `sky` id,\\n * engine/gfx/sky.ts). A look names what it changes; every filter it leaves out is off, and a style or sky of `''`\\n * keeps the scene's own. The chain draws the look the setting `post.look` names (engine/gfx/post/chain.ts); switching\\n * looks writes uniforms and re-points materials to styles the warm-up has already compiled, so it builds no\\n * pipeline. A look's sky is shown by the pages `createEngine` starts (engine/app/look.ts): the stage's lights give way\\n * to it (engine/gfx/stageSky.ts), which changes the shader key, so a look with another sky warms up before it draws.\\n * WP 13.24 adds the toon style's `shade` and `dither`, what a look asks of the stage (`shells`, outline shells round\\n10→ * its props and bodies, engine/gfx/stageShells.ts; `skyGradient`, the dome as a clean gradient) and its variant for\\n * perspective cameras (`perspective`, a look id whose filters and toon numbers the chain draws there). WP 13.30 adds\\n * what it asks of the whole picture: `resolution`, the mode drawn while `gfx.resolution` is `auto`\\n * (engine/gfx/resolution.ts), and `textures`, every material's maps filtered `smooth` or `pixel`\\n * (engine/gfx/materials/library.ts `filter`); the page's look applies both (engine/app/look.ts), building nothing.\\n *\\n * The entries are seeded from shardfall's tuned presets (`shardfall:crates/pav_view/src/looks.toml`, with\\n * `look.rs:100-353`), keys renamed: its whole looks are here (`look:hd-2d`, `look:game-boy`…), and its one-section\\n * presets are looks of their own, grouped by the filter they set (`look:palette/game-boy`, `look:stylize/oil-paint`,\\n * engine/gfx/post/presets.ts). Its \\\"objects\\\" (characters and objects) is the scope `characters+objects`. Its air and\\n20→ * bounce light came with WP 11.5 (the `air` and `gi` sections, engine/gfx/post/shading.ts): the looks Sunbeams and\\n * Lamplit fog, and their presets. Left out: styles that differ by part and the knobs WP 7.2's styles lack\\n * (`flat_shadow`, `specular`, `exposure`), so four looks keep the scene's style where shardfall styled the parts\\n * apart. One rename for the lesson: \\\"64 colours\\\" posterized to 4 levels, which shifts the hue of dull colours, so it\\n * is `look:palette/512-colours`, at 8. WP 13.31 and 13.32 add Style Lab's presets and looks made by combining them\\n * (engine/gfx/post/presetsMore.ts), and every look's `combine` and `strength` (engine/gfx/post/combine.ts): the looks\\n * it lays on, how much of each and which of its filters, and how much of the whole look shows.\\n *\\n * Invariants: every look's levels are 0 or 8 and more (the kind's check); a missing id falls back to `look:clean`\\n * with a warning naming the closest ids; looks read their fields, never their ids. A game's own look is scaffolded by\\n30→ * `node x new look labs/<lab>/looks/<name>` (tools/templates/look/).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\\n * const registry = createRegistry();\\n * defineLooks(registry);\\n * registry.get('look', 'look:game-boy').filters.palette.palette; // 'gameboy'\\n * registry.list('look').length; // 137\\n * @see engine/gfx/post/looks.test.ts\\n * @see tests/e2e/post.spec.ts\\n40→ */\\nimport { galleryField } from '../../core/gallery';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\\nimport type { EntryOf, Schema } from '../../core/schema';\\nimport { MATERIAL_STYLES } from '../materials/styles';\\nimport { TOON_LOOK } from '../materials/toon';\\nimport { RESOLUTION_MODES } from '../resolution';\\nimport { TEXTURE_LOOKS } from '../textures/types';\\nimport { COMBINE_FIELD, STRENGTH_FIELD, type CombineLayer } from './combine';\\nimport { colorFields, colorProblem, FILTER_FIELDS, FILTER_NAMES, levelsProblem, type FilterSpec } from './filters';\\n50→import { PRESETS } from './presets';\\nimport { COMBINED_LOOKS, STYLE_PRESETS } from './presetsMore';\\n\\n/** Where a menu lists a look: `look` for a whole look, else the filter it presets, or `shading` for a style. */\\nexport const LOOK_GROUPS = ['look', 'shading', ...FILTER_NAMES] as const;\\n\\n/** The default of every filter: all of them off. */\\nconst OFF = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(FILTER_FIELDS).map(([name, field]) => [name, field.default]));\\n\\n/** The fields of a `look` entry; see the file comment. */\\n60→export const LOOK_FIELDS = {\\n  description: { type: 'string', default: '', description: 'What it looks like, in plain sentences.' },\\n  group: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: LOOK_GROUPS,\\n    default: 'look',\\n    description: \\\"Where a menu lists it: 'look' for a whole look, else the filter it presets ('shading' for a style).\\\",\\n  },\\n  style: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n70→    enum: ['', ...MATERIAL_STYLES],\\n    default: '',\\n    description: \\\"The material style everything is drawn in (lambert, toon, flat, pbr); '' keeps the scene's own.\\\",\\n  },\\n  sky: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    default: '',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"The sky preset that lights the scene (a 'sky' id: sky:hall, the torch-lit hall); '' keeps the scene's own lights.\\\",\\n  },\\n80→  toon: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: { ...TOON_LOOK },\\n    description: \\\"The toon style's bands, rim, shade and dither, used when the style is 'toon'.\\\",\\n    properties: {\\n      bands: { type: 'integer', default: TOON_LOOK.bands, minimum: 2, maximum: 8, description: 'Bands of light.' },\\n      rim: { type: 'number', default: TOON_LOOK.rim, minimum: 0, maximum: 1, description: \\\"The rim light's strength.\\\" },\\n      shade: {\\n        type: 'number',\\n        default: TOON_LOOK.shade,\\n90→        minimum: 0,\\n        maximum: 1,\\n        description: \\\"How far each material's shadows shift in hue (cooler, more saturated) from its colour darkened.\\\",\\n      },\\n      dither: {\\n        type: 'number',\\n        default: TOON_LOOK.dither,\\n        minimum: 0,\\n        maximum: 1,\\n        description:\\n100→          \\\"The share of each band's step mixed by an ordered dither fixed to the world, edges hard; 0 smooths.\\\",\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/gfx/post/looks.ts\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":100,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file Looks (PLAN.md WP 7.4, §6.6 kind `look`): a material style (WP 7.2, engine/gfx/materials/styles.ts) plus a\\n * filter chain (engine/gfx/post/filters.ts), as data, and the sky that lights the scene (WP 7.8, a `sky` id,\\n * engine/gfx/sky.ts). A look names what it changes; every filter it leaves out is off, and a style or sky of `''`\\n * keeps the scene's own. The chain draws the look the setting `post.look` names (engine/gfx/post/chain.ts); switching\\n * looks writes uniforms and re-points materials to styles the warm-up has already compiled, so it builds no\\n * pipeline. A look's sky is shown by the pages `createEngine` starts (engine/app/look.ts): the stage's lights give way\\n * to it (engine/gfx/stageSky.ts), which changes the shader key, so a look with another sky warms up before it draws.\\n * WP 13.24 adds the toon style's `shade` and `dither`, what a look asks of the stage (`shells`, outline shells round\\n * its props and bodies, engine/gfx/stageShells.ts; `skyGradient`, the dome as a clean gradient) and its variant for\\n * perspective cameras (`perspective`, a look id whose filters and toon numbers the chain draws there). WP 13.30 adds\\n * what it asks of the whole picture: `resolution`, the mode drawn while `gfx.resolution` is `auto`\\n * (engine/gfx/resolution.ts), and `textures`, every material's maps filtered `smooth` or `pixel`\\n * (engine/gfx/materials/library.ts `filter`); the page's look applies both (engine/app/look.ts), building nothing.\\n *\\n * The entries are seeded from shardfall's tuned presets (`shardfall:crates/pav_view/src/looks.toml`, with\\n * `look.rs:100-353`), keys renamed: its whole looks are here (`look:hd-2d`, `look:game-boy`…), and its one-section\\n * presets are looks of their own, grouped by the filter they set (`look:palette/game-boy`, `look:stylize/oil-paint`,\\n * engine/gfx/post/presets.ts). Its \\\"objects\\\" (characters and objects) is the scope `characters+objects`. Its air and\\n * bounce light came with WP 11.5 (the `air` and `gi` sections, engine/gfx/post/shading.ts): the looks Sunbeams and\\n * Lamplit fog, and their presets. Left out: styles that differ by part and the knobs WP 7.2's styles lack\\n * (`flat_shadow`, `specular`, `exposure`), so four looks keep the scene's style where shardfall styled the parts\\n * apart. One rename for the lesson: \\\"64 colours\\\" posterized to 4 levels, which shifts the hue of dull colours, so it\\n * is `look:palette/512-colours`, at 8. WP 13.31 and 13.32 add Style Lab's presets and looks made by combining them\\n * (engine/gfx/post/presetsMore.ts), and every look's `combine` and `strength` (engine/gfx/post/combine.ts): the looks\\n * it lays on, how much of each and which of its filters, and how much of the whole look shows.\\n *\\n * Invariants: every look's levels are 0 or 8 and more (the kind's check); a missing id falls back to `look:clean`\\n * with a warning naming the closest ids; looks read their fields, never their ids. A game's own look is scaffolded by\\n * `node x new look labs/<lab>/looks/<name>` (tools/templates/look/).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\\n * const registry = createRegistry();\\n * defineLooks(registry);\\n * registry.get('look', 'look:game-boy').filters.palette.palette; // 'gameboy'\\n * registry.list('look').length; // 137\\n * @see engine/gfx/post/looks.test.ts\\n * @see tests/e2e/post.spec.ts\\n */\\nimport { galleryField } from '../../core/gallery';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\\nimport type { EntryOf, Schema } from '../../core/schema';\\nimport { MATERIAL_STYLES } from '../materials/styles';\\nimport { TOON_LOOK } from '../materials/toon';\\nimport { RESOLUTION_MODES } from '../resolution';\\nimport { TEXTURE_LOOKS } from '../textures/types';\\nimport { COMBINE_FIELD, STRENGTH_FIELD, type CombineLayer } from './combine';\\nimport { colorFields, colorProblem, FILTER_FIELDS, FILTER_NAMES, levelsProblem, type FilterSpec } from './filters';\\nimport { PRESETS } from './presets';\\nimport { COMBINED_LOOKS, STYLE_PRESETS } from './presetsMore';\\n\\n/** Where a menu lists a look: `look` for a whole look, else the filter it presets, or `shading` for a style. */\\nexport const LOOK_GROUPS = ['look', 'shading', ...FILTER_NAMES] as const;\\n\\n/** The default of every filter: all of them off. */\\nconst OFF = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(FILTER_FIELDS).map(([name, field]) => [name, field.default]));\\n\\n/** The fields of a `look` entry; see the file comment. */\\nexport const LOOK_FIELDS = {\\n  description: { type: 'string', default: '', description: 'What it looks like, in plain sentences.' },\\n  group: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: LOOK_GROUPS,\\n    default: 'look',\\n    description: \\\"Where a menu lists it: 'look' for a whole look, else the filter it presets ('shading' for a style).\\\",\\n  },\\n  style: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: ['', ...MATERIAL_STYLES],\\n    default: '',\\n    description: \\\"The material style everything is drawn in (lambert, toon, flat, pbr); '' keeps the scene's own.\\\",\\n  },\\n  sky: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    default: '',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"The sky preset that lights the scene (a 'sky' id: sky:hall, the torch-lit hall); '' keeps the scene's own lights.\\\",\\n  },\\n  toon: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: { ...TOON_LOOK },\\n    description: \\\"The toon style's bands, rim, shade and dither, used when the style is 'toon'.\\\",\\n    properties: {\\n      bands: { type: 'integer', default: TOON_LOOK.bands, minimum: 2, maximum: 8, description: 'Bands of light.' },\\n      rim: { type: 'number', default: TOON_LOOK.rim, minimum: 0, maximum: 1, description: \\\"The rim light's strength.\\\" },\\n      shade: {\\n        type: 'number',\\n        default: TOON_LOOK.shade,\\n        minimum: 0,\\n        maximum: 1,\\n        description: \\\"How far each material's shadows shift in hue (cooler, more saturated) from its colour darkened.\\\",\\n      },\\n      dither: {\\n        type: 'number',\\n        default: TOON_LOOK.dither,\\n        minimum: 0,\\n        maximum: 1,\\n        description:\\n          \\\"The share of each band's step mixed by an ordered dither fixed to the world, edges hard; 0 smooths.\\\",\\n\",\"total_lines\":363}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5e49c3d6-64e6-43b4-be05-0f7cc12fc1ed-72","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The kind `sky` (PLAN.md WP 7.1, §6.6): its fields (`SKY_FIELDS`: the background colour, the dome, the sun, the\\n * ambient light, the fog, the backdrop's layers and how bright the light pool's point lights shine), `defineSky` for\\n * a preset, and the built-in presets, declared on the shared registry when this module loads: `sky:hall`, the\\n * torch-lit hall (dark, torches, fog past the focus), and `sky:daylight`, a plain day for fixtures. Others arrive\\n * when a scene needs one. engine/gfx/sky.ts's `createSky` puts a preset on a scene. Split from sky.ts at its line cap.\\n *\\n * Invariants: data only, nothing drawn; every object field's default holds its properties' defaults, so a preset may\\n * leave a whole object out. Angles in radians, lengths in metres.\\n10→ *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n * defineSkies(reg); // the kind and its presets, sky:hall and sky:daylight\\n * defineSky('sky:dusk', { background: '#402030', sun: { intensity: 1, elevation: 0.1 } }, reg).sun.azimuth; // 0: as the field's default\\n * @see engine/gfx/sky.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\\nimport type { Schema } from '../core/schema';\\n20→import { AMBIENT_FIELDS, FOG_FIELDS } from './atmosphere';\\nimport { BACKDROP_KINDS } from './backdrop';\\n\\nconst text = (description: string, value: string) => ({ type: 'string', default: value, description }) as const;\\nconst num = (description: string, value: number, minimum = 0, maximum?: number, unit?: string) =>\\n  ({ type: 'number', default: value, minimum, ...(maximum === undefined ? {} : { maximum }), ...(unit ? { unit } : {}), description }) as const; // prettier-ignore\\n/** An object field whose default holds every property's default, so a preset may leave the whole object out. */\\nconst group = <const P extends Schema>(description: string, properties: P) => {\\n  const defaults = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(properties).map(([key, field]) => [key, field.default]));\\n  return { type: 'object', default: defaults, description, properties } as const;\\n30→};\\n\\n/** The fields of a `sky` entry; see the file comment. Angles in radians, lengths in metres. */\\nexport const SKY_FIELDS = {\\n  description: text('What it looks like, in plain sentences.', ''),\\n  background: text('The colour behind everything, hex, where neither dome nor backdrop is drawn.', '#06050b'),\\n  pointLights: num(\\\"A multiplier on the light pool's intensities: 1 as the light kinds say, 0 puts them out.\\\", 1),\\n  dome: group(\\\"The sky dome: three.js's SkyMesh (the Preetham daylight model), lit by the sun's direction.\\\", {\\n    show: { type: 'boolean', default: false, description: 'Whether the dome is drawn.' },\\n    turbidity: num('Haze in the air (SkyMesh turbidity): 2 is clear, 10 is hazy.', 2),\\n40→    rayleigh: num('Rayleigh scattering (SkyMesh rayleigh): more is bluer, then redder.', 1),\\n    mieCoefficient: num('Mie scattering (SkyMesh mieCoefficient): the glow round the sun.', 0.005),\\n    mieDirectionalG: num('How tight the glow round the sun is (SkyMesh mieDirectionalG), 0 to 1.', 0.8, 0, 1),\\n    exposure: num('A multiplier on its colour: the frame has no tone mapping, so a clear day wants about 0.5.', 1),\\n  }),\\n  sun: group(\\\"The sun: three.js's DirectionalLight, shining from its azimuth and elevation; intensity 0 for none.\\\", {\\n    color: text('Its colour, hex.', '#fff0d8'),\\n    intensity: num('How bright it is (DirectionalLight intensity); 0 for no sun.', 0),\\n    azimuth: num('Where it stands round the level, from +Z toward +X.', 0, -7, 7, 'rad'),\\n    elevation: num('How high it stands above the horizon.', 0.9, 0, 1.5708, 'rad'),\\n50→  }),\\n  ambient: group(\\n    \\\"The ambient light: three.js's HemisphereLight, one colour from above and one from below.\\\",\\n    AMBIENT_FIELDS,\\n  ),\\n  fog: group(\\n    'Range fog past the focus plus height fog on the floor (engine/gfx/atmosphere.ts); amount 0 for none.',\\n    FOG_FIELDS,\\n  ),\\n  backdrop: group('Silhouettes round the horizon, far layers first; no layers draws no backdrop.', {\\n60→    haze: text('The colour hazed layers fade toward, hex.', '#c8e4f8'),\\n    tint: text('A colour the silhouettes are drawn through, hex: white as baked; the night darkens them.', '#ffffff'),\\n    layers: {\\n      type: 'array',\\n      default: [],\\n      description: 'The layers, far to near.',\\n      items: {\\n        type: 'object',\\n        properties: {\\n          kind: { type: 'string', enum: BACKDROP_KINDS, required: true, description: 'Its silhouette.' },\\n70→          color: text('Its colour, hex.', '#5aa060'),\\n          height: num('Its tallest point, as a share of the backdrop band.', 0.5, 0, 1),\\n          haze: num('How far it fades toward the haze colour, 0 to 1.', 0, 0, 1),\\n          seed: { type: 'integer', default: 1, description: 'Its seed: another seed, another skyline.' },\\n        },\\n      },\\n    },\\n  }),\\n} as const satisfies Schema;\\n\\n80→/** A `sky` entry. */\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The kind `sky` (PLAN.md WP 7.1, §6.6): its fields (`SKY_FIELDS`: the background colour, the dome, the sun, the\\n * ambient light, the fog, the backdrop's layers and how bright the light pool's point lights shine), `defineSky` for\\n * a preset, and the built-in presets, declared on the shared registry when this module loads: `sky:hall`, the\\n * torch-lit hall (dark, torches, fog past the focus), and `sky:daylight`, a plain day for fixtures. Others arrive\\n * when a scene needs one. engine/gfx/sky.ts's `createSky` puts a preset on a scene. Split from sky.ts at its line cap.\\n *\\n * Invariants: data only, nothing drawn; every object field's default holds its properties' defaults, so a preset may\\n * leave a whole object out. Angles in radians, lengths in metres.\\n10→ *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n * defineSkies(reg); // the kind and its presets, sky:hall and sky:daylight\\n * defineSky('sky:dusk', { background: '#402030', sun: { intensity: 1, elevation: 0.1 } }, reg).sun.azimuth; // 0: as the field's default\\n * @see engine/gfx/sky.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\\nimport type { Schema } from '../core/schema';\\n20→import { AMBIENT_FIELDS, FOG_FIELDS } from './atmosphere';\\nimport { BACKDROP_KINDS } from './backdrop';\\n\\nconst text = (description: string, value: string) => ({ type: 'string', default: value, description }) as const;\\nconst num = (description: string, value: number, minimum = 0, maximum?: number, unit?: string) =>\\n  ({ type: 'number', default: value, minimum, ...(maximum === undefined ? {} : { maximum }), ...(unit ? { unit } : {}), description }) as const; // prettier-ignore\\n/** An object field whose default holds every property's default, so a preset may leave the whole object out. */\\nconst group = <const P extends Schema>(description: string, properties: P) => {\\n  const defaults = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(properties).map(([key, field]) => [key, field.default]));\\n  return { type: 'object', default: defaults, description, properties } as const;\\n30→};\\n\\n/** The fields of a `sky` entry; see the file comment. Angles in radians, lengths in metres. */\\nexport const SKY_FIELDS = {\\n  description: text('What it looks like, in plain sentences.', ''),\\n  background: text('The colour behind everything, hex, where neither dome nor backdrop is drawn.', '#06050b'),\\n  pointLights: num(\\\"A multiplier on the light pool's intensities: 1 as the light kinds say, 0 puts them out.\\\", 1),\\n  dome: group(\\\"The sky dome: three.js's SkyMesh (the Preetham daylight model), lit by the sun's direction.\\\", {\\n    show: { type: 'boolean', default: false, description: 'Whether the dome is drawn.' },\\n    turbidity: num('Haze in the air (SkyMesh turbidity): 2 is clear, 10 is hazy.', 2),\\n40→    rayleigh: num('Rayleigh scattering (SkyMesh rayleigh): more is bluer, then redder.', 1),\\n    mieCoefficient: num('Mie scattering (SkyMesh mieCoefficient): the glow round the sun.', 0.005),\\n    mieDirectionalG: num('How tight the glow round the sun is (SkyMesh mieDirectionalG), 0 to 1.', 0.8, 0, 1),\\n    exposure: num('A multiplier on its colour: the frame has no tone mapping, so a clear day wants about 0.5.', 1),\\n  }),\\n  sun: group(\\\"The sun: three.js's DirectionalLight, shining from its azimuth and elevation; intensity 0 for none.\\\", {\\n    color: text('Its colour, hex.', '#fff0d8'),\\n    intensity: num('How bright it is (DirectionalLight intensity); 0 for no sun.', 0),\\n    azimuth: num('Where it stands round the level, from +Z toward +X.', 0, -7, 7, 'rad'),\\n    elevation: num('How high it stands above the horizon.', 0.9, 0, 1.5708, 'rad'),\\n50→  }),\\n  ambient: group(\\n    \\\"The ambient light: three.js's HemisphereLight, one colour from above and one from below.\\\",\\n    AMBIENT_FIELDS,\\n  ),\\n  fog: group(\\n    'Range fog past the focus plus height fog on the floor (engine/gfx/atmosphere.ts); amount 0 for none.',\\n    FOG_FIELDS,\\n  ),\\n  backdrop: group('Silhouettes round the horizon, far layers first; no layers draws no backdrop.', {\\n60→    haze: text('The colour hazed layers fade toward, hex.', '#c8e4f8'),\\n    tint: text('A colour the silhouettes are drawn through, hex: white as baked; the night darkens them.', '#ffffff'),\\n    layers: {\\n      type: 'array',\\n      default: [],\\n      description: 'The layers, far to near.',\\n      items: {\\n        type: 'object',\\n        properties: {\\n          kind: { type: 'string', enum: BACKDROP_KINDS, required: true, description: 'Its silhouette.' },\\n70→          color: text('Its colour, hex.', '#5aa060'),\\n          height: num('Its tallest point, as a share of the backdrop band.', 0.5, 0, 1),\\n          haze: num('How far it fades toward the haze colour, 0 to 1.', 0, 0, 1),\\n          seed: { type: 'integer', default: 1, description: 'Its seed: another seed, another skyline.' },\\n        },\\n      },\\n    },\\n  }),\\n} as const satisfies Schema;\\n\\n80→/** A `sky` entry. */\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/gfx/skyKind.ts\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The kind `sky` (PLAN.md WP 7.1, §6.6): its fields (`SKY_FIELDS`: the background colour, the dome, the sun, the\\n * ambient light, the fog, the backdrop's layers and how bright the light pool's point lights shine), `defineSky` for\\n * a preset, and the built-in presets, declared on the shared registry when this module loads: `sky:hall`, the\\n * torch-lit hall (dark, torches, fog past the focus), and `sky:daylight`, a plain day for fixtures. Others arrive\\n * when a scene needs one. engine/gfx/sky.ts's `createSky` puts a preset on a scene. Split from sky.ts at its line cap.\\n *\\n * Invariants: data only, nothing drawn; every object field's default holds its properties' defaults, so a preset may\\n * leave a whole object out. Angles in radians, lengths in metres.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n * defineSkies(reg); // the kind and its presets, sky:hall and sky:daylight\\n * defineSky('sky:dusk', { background: '#402030', sun: { intensity: 1, elevation: 0.1 } }, reg).sun.azimuth; // 0: as the field's default\\n * @see engine/gfx/sky.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\\nimport type { Schema } from '../core/schema';\\nimport { AMBIENT_FIELDS, FOG_FIELDS } from './atmosphere';\\nimport { BACKDROP_KINDS } from './backdrop';\\n\\nconst text = (description: string, value: string) => ({ type: 'string', default: value, description }) as const;\\nconst num = (description: string, value: number, minimum = 0, maximum?: number, unit?: string) =>\\n  ({ type: 'number', default: value, minimum, ...(maximum === undefined ? {} : { maximum }), ...(unit ? { unit } : {}), description }) as const; // prettier-ignore\\n/** An object field whose default holds every property's default, so a preset may leave the whole object out. */\\nconst group = <const P extends Schema>(description: string, properties: P) => {\\n  const defaults = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(properties).map(([key, field]) => [key, field.default]));\\n  return { type: 'object', default: defaults, description, properties } as const;\\n};\\n\\n/** The fields of a `sky` entry; see the file comment. Angles in radians, lengths in metres. */\\nexport const SKY_FIELDS = {\\n  description: text('What it looks like, in plain sentences.', ''),\\n  background: text('The colour behind everything, hex, where neither dome nor backdrop is drawn.', '#06050b'),\\n  pointLights: num(\\\"A multiplier on the light pool's intensities: 1 as the light kinds say, 0 puts them out.\\\", 1),\\n  dome: group(\\\"The sky dome: three.js's SkyMesh (the Preetham daylight model), lit by the sun's direction.\\\", {\\n    show: { type: 'boolean', default: false, description: 'Whether the dome is drawn.' },\\n    turbidity: num('Haze in the air (SkyMesh turbidity): 2 is clear, 10 is hazy.', 2),\\n    rayleigh: num('Rayleigh scattering (SkyMesh rayleigh): more is bluer, then redder.', 1),\\n    mieCoefficient: num('Mie scattering (SkyMesh mieCoefficient): the glow round the sun.', 0.005),\\n    mieDirectionalG: num('How tight the glow round the sun is (SkyMesh mieDirectionalG), 0 to 1.', 0.8, 0, 1),\\n    exposure: num('A multiplier on its colour: the frame has no tone mapping, so a clear day wants about 0.5.', 1),\\n  }),\\n  sun: group(\\\"The sun: three.js's DirectionalLight, shining from its azimuth and elevation; intensity 0 for none.\\\", {\\n    color: text('Its colour, hex.', '#fff0d8'),\\n    intensity: num('How bright it is (DirectionalLight intensity); 0 for no sun.', 0),\\n    azimuth: num('Where it stands round the level, from +Z toward +X.', 0, -7, 7, 'rad'),\\n    elevation: num('How high it stands above the horizon.', 0.9, 0, 1.5708, 'rad'),\\n  }),\\n  ambient: group(\\n    \\\"The ambient light: three.js's HemisphereLight, one colour from above and one from below.\\\",\\n    AMBIENT_FIELDS,\\n  ),\\n  fog: group(\\n    'Range fog past the focus plus height fog on the floor (engine/gfx/atmosphere.ts); amount 0 for none.',\\n    FOG_FIELDS,\\n  ),\\n  backdrop: group('Silhouettes round the horizon, far layers first; no layers draws no backdrop.', {\\n    haze: text('The colour hazed layers fade toward, hex.', '#c8e4f8'),\\n    tint: text('A colour the silhouettes are drawn through, hex: white as baked; the night darkens them.', '#ffffff'),\\n    layers: {\\n      type: 'array',\\n      default: [],\\n      description: 'The layers, far to near.',\\n      items: {\\n        type: 'object',\\n        properties: {\\n          kind: { type: 'string', enum: BACKDROP_KINDS, required: true, description: 'Its silhouette.' },\\n          color: text('Its colour, hex.', '#5aa060'),\\n          height: num('Its tallest poin