{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_342","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The score during play is the average of a, b, and c. Those values may only be filled at class end.\n\nI'll send flow.result when available, otherwise a running estimate. A finite score is enough for progress. I'll compute the score from act if a, b, and c are readable, defaulting to zero at class start and updating later. Class index maps to act.phase and pose id to act.pose as a number. I'm now writing all files and will retest the island while writing.\n\nAbout-data.ts will contain the full interview content. Each answer must be two short sentences or fewer. I'll count issues as I draft and update totals at the end.\n\nCritical issues include island NaN yaw, missing settings, line length, and early bot bands. The most helpful fix is retreat bot bands; pixel screenshots under headless are least helpful.\n\nEngine feedback: liked scene actions, settings, and headless host. Stuck on playClip in setup, yaw requirements, frozen recorded world, hub query keys, and music at 0.5. Built balance model, director, voices, and songs. Hardest were hub ready deadlines versus terrain and the input/modal split. One change requested: a public way to add a mesh or default music to 0.1.\n\nPrompt liked clear acceptance numbers and cut line.\n\nConfusing prompt feedback includes a score range mismatch, seed lines longer than two sentences, and hub hash pinning versus fetching. The hardest part was combining one file with a hub harness and bot bands. The fix is to use one score definition and ship the client hash that matches the fetched file.\n\nThe usage string must exactly read \"added on import\". Player count uses an en dash: \"1–4\". Tags are 3d, sports, third-person, comedy, and co-op. Source is Wii Fit. The word Wii appears only in the About source line and hub source field.\n\nGenre is Sports and perspective is third-person. The date is 2026-11-04 22:36:56. I will check eslint max-lines and prettier printWidth before writing files. A shell test is unnecessary because verify.mjs drives the browser directly; the island test serves as the simulation boot. verify.mjs will run npm run check and the game tests, then print failures and a count.\n\nverify.mjs will run the game vitest files directly so director proof is captured in verify.log. npm test and npm check will be logged separately to npm-test.log and npm-check.log. The script must exit 0 with a final count line of zero failures.\n\nverify.mjs will spawn npm run check and fail if it exits nonzero. It will then run the retreat, island, and audio vitest tests directly. Browser stages are included in the full verify but skipped under --quick. A static grep may be added. The script prints failures and a final zero-count line.\n\nBrowser checks will live inside verify.mjs. If Chromium fails to launch, the script writes launch-error.txt and falls back to node and static checks. A started page with ready false is not that fallback. Two boots must agree, and verify will enforce that. The file stays under 600 lines because tools/ is linted.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-acf55be2-f1c3-4cb8-ada3-49d4950e912f-166","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"replay","glob":"**/tools/**/*replay*"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-acf55be2-f1c3-4cb8-ada3-49d4950e912f-167","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"labs/game/replays|replay","glob":"**/package.json"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1514,"output_tokens":1298,"cache_read_input_tokens":147328,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"570f3932-ebdf-4e69-985e-6e3ac784d72a"}
