{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_344","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Planning to write a small script using createAppHost and step through it.\n\nChecking if createAppHost records inputs. Will write the page first, then record a replay after the page works. Need to add @file for eslint on mjs files. Will retest island in the background while writing code.\n\nNavigating to the dev build directory. Checking the defineLook schema for valid bloom fields and required filter shapes.\n\nMapping controller inputs to game actions. Space triggers breathing but is blocked by open menus. Enter handles both action and menu acceptance. PadSouth serves as both action and menu confirmation.\n\nCross serves as both action and menu selection. Mouse buttons map to feet; clicks select menus while open and act as left foot during play. Pointer lock is manual, requested only on canvas click when playing and no modal is active.\n\nChecking whether the action map ID must be `actionMap:retreat`. The shell will use a single state object. Five files are planned: about-data.ts, retreat.ts, actions.ts, glyphs.ts, and save.ts.\n\nThe file plan now includes present.ts, hub.ts, main.ts, index.html, hub/tags.html, tools/onefile.mjs, tools/verify.mjs, README.md, and ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md. The page presenter will be the largest file and must stay under 500 lines by keeping menus data-driven. It will expose a bootPage function that returns a Page object with onFrame and publishes __game.\n\nModal input blocking is being defined. It will be active during open menus, the touch-only title gate, and results screens to prevent stick drift and unwanted actions. It will remain off during attract, play, and roam.\n\nModal can remain true during attract mode. The driver overwrites empty intents with bot commands inside the scene step, so the attract simulation still runs correctly.\n\nThe idle clock will trigger attract mode after ten seconds of no input while a modal menu is open. The Settings button is both a real HTML element and a createMenu item so it works on touchscreens.\n\nA large Settings button with `data-ui=\"touch-settings\"` will be added for touchscreen tapping. Touch stick layout is omitted because `touch=off` is in the query string. The WebGPU compatibility check must run before `createEngine`, so the failure message needs to be present in the DOM early enough for the script to reveal it.\n\nAn inline script in the HTML head will check for WebGPU support and set the failure message before main.ts runs. If main.ts also finds no GPU, it returns early so the message stays visible.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0c2e1224-6f8d-4789-9853-9ab558341335-170","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"font-size|fontSize","glob":"**/engine/ui/widgets.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1216,"output_tokens":1758,"cache_read_input_tokens":152704,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"4f3bce84-a86d-421c-8ca4-8292cf2bc96a"}
