{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-084e0816-9bd9-4593-9ac2-3317e2f92607-171","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"40→  strength(action: string): number;\\n  /** The device used last: the pad's cursor shows only for `gamepad`. */\\n  readonly lastDevice: string;\\n}\\n\\n/** A cue a widget asks the page to play. */\\nexport type UiCue = 'move' | 'pick' | 'cancel' | 'type';\\n\\n/** Plays a cue (the page's audio); widgets without one stay silent. */\\nexport type UiSound = (cue: UiCue) => void;\\n50→\\n/** A widget made by this module: its element, an update and its removal. */\\nexport interface Widget<T> {\\n  readonly el: HTMLElement;\\n  set(value: T): void;\\n  remove(): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** The stylesheet's element id. */\\nconst STYLE_ID = 'ui-widgets-style';\\n60→\\n/** The widgets' stylesheet: the bar, the hearts, the box, the dialog, the menu and the pad's cursor. */\\nconst STYLE = `\\n.ui-bar { position: relative; width: 12em; height: 1em; border: 1px solid #140b12; border-radius: 2px;\\n  background: #3a1a26; box-shadow: 0 1px 2px #0b0814; overflow: hidden; }\\n.ui-bar-fill { position: absolute; inset: 0; transform-origin: left; transform: scaleX(var(--ui-fill, 0));\\n  background: linear-gradient(rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35), transparent 40%), var(--ui-color, #e0463c); }\\n.ui-bar-text { position: absolute; inset: 0; font-size: 0.7em; line-height: 1.45; text-align: center;\\n  text-shadow: 0 1px 1px #0b0814; }\\n.ui-hearts { display: flex; gap: 0.1em; font-size: 1.15em; line-height: 1; text-shadow: 0 1px 1px #0b0814; }\\n70→.ui-heart { color: #3a1826; }\\n.ui-heart[data-fill='full'] { color: #e8384a; }\\n.ui-heart[data-fill='half'] { color: transparent; background: linear-gradient(90deg, #e8384a 50%, #3a1826 50%);\\n  -webkit-background-clip: text; background-clip: text; }\\n.ui-box, .ui-dialog, .ui-menu, .ui-dialog-choices { background: linear-gradient(#2a3266, #10143a);\\n  border: 2px solid #e8e4ff; border-radius: 6px; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #05040a; color: #ffffff; }\\n.ui-box { padding: 0.45em 0.7em; }\\n.ui-box-title, .ui-menu-title, .ui-dialog-name { color: #ffd36a; }\\n.ui-box-title { font-size: 0.85em; margin-bottom: 0.25em; }\\n.ui-panel { position: absolute; pointer-events: auto; white-space: normal; }\",\"content_concise\":\"40→  strength(action: string): number;\\n  /** The device used last: the pad's cursor shows only for `gamepad`. */\\n  readonly lastDevice: string;\\n}\\n\\n/** A cue a widget asks the page to play. */\\nexport type UiCue = 'move' | 'pick' | 'cancel' | 'type';\\n\\n/** Plays a cue (the page's audio); widgets without one stay silent. */\\nexport type UiSound = (cue: UiCue) => void;\\n50→\\n/** A widget made by this module: its element, an update and its removal. */\\nexport interface Widget<T> {\\n  readonly el: HTMLElement;\\n  set(value: T): void;\\n  remove(): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** The stylesheet's element id. */\\nconst STYLE_ID = 'ui-widgets-style';\\n60→\\n/** The widgets' stylesheet: the bar, the hearts, the box, the dialog, the menu and the pad's cursor. */\\nconst STYLE = `\\n.ui-bar { position: relative; width: 12em; height: 1em; border: 1px solid #140b12; border-radius: 2px;\\n  background: #3a1a26; box-shadow: 0 1px 2px #0b0814; overflow: hidden; }\\n.ui-bar-fill { position: absolute; inset: 0; transform-origin: left; transform: scaleX(var(--ui-fill, 0));\\n  background: linear-gradient(rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35), transparent 40%), var(--ui-color, #e0463c); }\\n.ui-bar-text { position: absolute; inset: 0; font-size: 0.7em; line-height: 1.45; text-align: center;\\n  text-shadow: 0 1px 1px #0b0814; }\\n.ui-hearts { display: flex; gap: 0.1em; font-size: 1.15em; line-height: 1; text-shadow: 0 1px 1px #0b0814; }\\n70→.ui-heart { color: #3a1826; }\\n.ui-heart[data-fill='full'] { color: #e8384a; }\\n.ui-heart[data-fill='half'] { color: transparent; background: linear-gradient(90deg, #e8384a 50%, #3a1826 50%);\\n  -webkit-background-clip: text; background-clip: text; }\\n.ui-box, .ui-dialog, .ui-menu, .ui-dialog-choices { background: linear-gradient(#2a3266, #10143a);\\n  border: 2px solid #e8e4ff; border-radius: 6px; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #05040a; color: #ffffff; }\\n.ui-box { padding: 0.45em 0.7em; }\\n.ui-box-title, .ui-menu-title, .ui-dialog-name { color: #ffd36a; }\\n.ui-box-title { font-size: 0.85em; margin-bottom: 0.25em; }\\n.ui-panel { position: absolute; pointer-events: auto; white-space: normal; }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/ui/widgets.ts\",\"offset\":40,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"  strength(action: string): number;\\n  /** The device used last: the pad's cursor shows only for `gamepad`. */\\n  readonly lastDevice: string;\\n}\\n\\n/** A cue a widget asks the page to play. */\\nexport type UiCue = 'move' | 'pick' | 'cancel' | 'type';\\n\\n/** Plays a cue (the page's audio); widgets without one stay silent. */\\nexport type UiSound = (cue: UiCue) => void;\\n\\n/** A widget made by this module: its element, an update and its removal. */\\nexport interface Widget<T> {\\n  readonly el: HTMLElement;\\n  set(value: T): void;\\n  remove(): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** The stylesheet's element id. */\\nconst STYLE_ID = 'ui-widgets-style';\\n\\n/** The widgets' stylesheet: the bar, the hearts, the box, the dialog, the menu and the pad's cursor. */\\nconst STYLE = `\\n.ui-bar { position: relative; width: 12em; height: 1em; border: 1px solid #140b12; border-radius: 2px;\\n  background: #3a1a26; box-shadow: 0 1px 2px #0b0814; overflow: hidden; }\\n.ui-bar-fill { position: absolute; inset: 0; transform-origin: left; transform: scaleX(var(--ui-fill, 0));\\n  background: linear-gradient(rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35), transparent 40%), var(--ui-color, #e0463c); }\\n.ui-bar-text { position: absolute; inset: 0; font-size: 0.7em; line-height: 1.45; text-align: center;\\n  text-shadow: 0 1px 1px #0b0814; }\\n.ui-hearts { display: flex; gap: 0.1em; font-size: 1.15em; line-height: 1; text-shadow: 0 1px 1px #0b0814; }\\n.ui-heart { color: #3a1826; }\\n.ui-heart[data-fill='full'] { color: #e8384a; }\\n.ui-heart[data-fill='half'] { color: transparent; background: linear-gradient(90deg, #e8384a 50%, #3a1826 50%);\\n  -webkit-background-clip: text; background-clip: text; }\\n.ui-box, .ui-dialog, .ui-menu, .ui-dialog-choices { background: linear-gradient(#2a3266, #10143a);\\n  border: 2px solid #e8e4ff; border-radius: 6px; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #05040a; color: #ffffff; }\\n.ui-box { padding: 0.45em 0.7em; }\\n.ui-box-title, .ui-menu-title, .ui-dialog-name { color: #ffd36a; }\\n.ui-box-title { font-size: 0.85em; margin-bottom: 0.25em; }\\n.ui-panel { position: absolute; pointer-events: auto; white-space: normal; }\\n\",\"total_lines\":276}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"e16b04ca-9915-4850-a7fb-2c4b633db43a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_346","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The root font might be on the overlay.\n\nAll widget text must be forced to 28px via CSS. Using em units on a parent that is smaller than 28px would still fail the size check, so every element needs an explicit font-size override.\n\nThe clinical palette is chosen: light panels, slate text, and coral focus. Menu and panel backgrounds will be #F7FAFC with slate text and coral borders. Selected items will use the same coral background and slate text. A disc SVG will be sized to 30vh.\n\nA custom #shell element will be appended to the body so CSS can be fully controlled. Menus will be created inside #shell instead of the engine overlay. The engine overlay will be bypassed entirely for the HUD. Touch input is disabled to prevent the engine's touch stick from appearing.\n\nThe engine canvas must exist before createEngine runs. The query string will include touch=off, post.look=look:retreat, and cam3=chase. Unknown keys are stripped, so only valid settings are passed. The default scene is game:island.\n\nThe seed will come from the hub. Replays will not be included in the page, so passing ?replay= would error. Demo mode activates when a replay or hub is present. Music volume is set immediately after createAudio. Songs and voice imports must run before createAudio because the audio registry is checked at playback time.\n\nThe startup sequence is now fixed. GPU checks run first. Then side-effect imports load looks, songs, voice, scenes, and the action map. The search string is stripped next. If a hub is active, it connects. Then the store and audio are created with volume at 0.1. The engine starts last. Scene registration happens during those imports.\n\nA `run` helper will wrap `inspector.actions.run`. The engine inspector actions are typed as `unknown` because of an index signature, so a `Run` interface cast is used instead of `any`. An `EntryDescription` interface is also being defined.\n\nThe `EntryDescription` interface now defines a `fields` array of objects with `key`, `value`, and `differs` properties. A `settingDefault` helper will query the inspector for a setting path, locate the field whose key is `'default'`, and return its numeric value or zero if absent. The schema confirms that default values are included in the description output.\n\nThe dev jump system covers days one through five, ten activities, and a finale with four tilt states. Results will be paginated four per page with next and back buttons. A reset-all-tunables button will also be added.\n\nThe slider will display four tunables at once. Pressing up or down will step the selection, and pressing left or right will adjust the value directly. The menu consumes uiUp, uiDown, uiAccept, and uiCancel, so uiLeft may still be available for slider input.\n\nThe slider will use the `pressed` edge instead of held input to avoid rapid repetition. Attract mode exits on keydown, mouse movement, pointerdown, and gamepad button presses; touch taps will not trigger exit.\n\nAttract mode will not write to the save store. The seed restarts without persisting attract changes. Settings modified during attract remain in memory but are not saved to disk. A snapshot of the current state will be taken before entering attract.\n\nSave writes will trigger on begin, carry, sleep, pebble line changes, settings, and erase. Pebble finds are recorded when flow.line equals find.pebble. Best scores update only if the current result beats the stored record. The Heron clip is optional and will be skipped for now. Non-null assertions will be avoided.\n\nPrettier will use single quotes and a 120-character print width. The audio test passed, and the game.auto import is now in place. The island retest is running in parallel with the current edits. A guest spawned at y=40 should drop properly once the physics terrain body exists. The previous failure was caused by settings, so the engine should boot correctly after that fix. The heightfield is small enough to avoid heavy terrain issues.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ffb31258-774e-4994-9a71-88cb9a8d3b30-172","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/core/settings.ts","offset":180,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ffb31258-774e-4994-9a71-88cb9a8d3b30-173","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/play.ts","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":926,"output_tokens":2142,"cache_read_input_tokens":155904,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"ad692920-4d30-4bad-9ae4-49b8489a63fa"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ffb31258-774e-4994-9a71-88cb9a8d3b30-172","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"180→  });\\n}\\nsettingKind(sharedRegistry);\\n\\n/** Declares settings, path → field, on `registry` (the shared one by default). Throws `CORE_BAD_SPEC` for a bad field. */\\nexport function defineSettings(fields: Record<string, Field>, registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): Entry[] {\\n  settingKind(registry);\\n  return Object.entries(fields).map(([path, field]) => {\\n    if (!/^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*(\\\\.[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*)*$/.test(path)) {\\n      const problems = `the path ${show(path)} must be words joined by dots, such as hero.runSpeed`;\\n190→      throw codeError('CORE_BAD_SPEC', { where: 'defineSettings', problems });\\n    }\\n    return registry.def('setting', path, field as unknown as Record<string, unknown>);\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/** Text from a URL or the command line as a value of `field`'s type; undefined when it cannot be. */\\nfunction fromText(field: Field, text: string): unknown {\\n  switch (field.type) {\\n    case 'number':\\n200→    case 'integer':\\n      return text.trim() === '' ? undefined : Number(text);\\n    case 'boolean':\\n      return text === '' || text === 'true' || text === '1' ? true : text === 'false' || text === '0' ? false : text;\\n    case 'string':\\n      return text;\\n    default:\\n      try {\\n        return JSON.parse(text);\\n      } catch {\\n210→        return field.type === 'any' ? text : undefined;\\n      }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** How a store is made: the registry whose `setting` entries it serves (the shared one by default). */\\nexport interface SettingsOptions {\\n  registry?: Registry;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"180→  });\\n}\\nsettingKind(sharedRegistry);\\n\\n/** Declares settings, path → field, on `registry` (the shared one by default). Throws `CORE_BAD_SPEC` for a bad field. */\\nexport function defineSettings(fields: Record<string, Field>, registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): Entry[] {\\n  settingKind(registry);\\n  return Object.entries(fields).map(([path, field]) => {\\n    if (!/^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*(\\\\.[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*)*$/.test(path)) {\\n      const problems = `the path ${show(path)} must be words joined by dots, such as hero.runSpeed`;\\n190→      throw codeError('CORE_BAD_SPEC', { where: 'defineSettings', problems });\\n    }\\n    return registry.def('setting', path, field as unknown as Record<string, unknown>);\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/** Text from a URL or the command line as a value of `field`'s type; undefined when it cannot be. */\\nfunction fromText(field: Field, text: string): unknown {\\n  switch (field.type) {\\n    case 'number':\\n200→    case 'integer':\\n      return text.trim() === '' ? undefined : Number(text);\\n    case 'boolean':\\n      return text === '' || text === 'true' || text === '1' ? true : text === 'false' || text === '0' ? false : text;\\n    case 'string':\\n      return text;\\n    default:\\n      try {\\n        return JSON.parse(text);\\n      } catch {\\n210→        return field.type === 'any' ? text : undefined;\\n      }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** How a store is made: the registry whose `setting` entries it serves (the shared one by default). */\\nexport interface SettingsOptions {\\n  registry?: Registry;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/core/settings.ts\",\"offset\":180,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"  });\\n}\\nsettingKind(sharedRegistry);\\n\\n/** Declares settings, path → field, on `registry` (the shared one by default). Throws `CORE_BAD_SPEC` for a bad field. */\\nexport function defineSettings(fields: Record<string, Field>, registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): Entry[] {\\n  settingKind(registry);\\n  return Object.entries(fields).map(([path, field]) => {\\n    if (!/^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*(\\\\.[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*)*$/.test(path)) {\\n      const problems = `the path ${show(path)} must be words joined by dots, such as hero.runSpeed`;\\n      throw codeError('CORE_BAD_SPEC', { where: 'defineSettings', problems });\\n    }\\n    return registry.def('setting', path, field as unknown as Record<string, unknown>);\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/** Text from a URL or the command line as a value of `field`'s type; undefined when it cannot be. */\\nfunction fromText(field: Field, text: string): unknown {\\n  switch (field.type) {\\n    case 'number':\\n    case 'integer':\\n      return text.trim() === '' ? undefined : Number(text);\\n    case 'boolean':\\n      return text === '' || text === 'true' || text === '1' ? true : text === 'false' || text === '0' ? false : text;\\n    case 'string':\\n      return text;\\n    default:\\n      try {\\n        return JSON.parse(text);\\n      } catch {\\n        return field.type === 'any' ? text : undefined;\\n      }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** How a store is made: the registry whose `setting` entries it serves (the shared one by default). */\\nexport interface SettingsOptions {\\n  registry?: Registry;\\n}\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":382}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ffb31258-774e-4994-9a71-88cb9a8d3b30-173","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The starter game's scene `game:play`: every new game begins as this one (tools/game/new-game.mjs copies\\n * labs/game/ into it), so it is small, plays, and shows the parts a game is made of. The player, a humanoid on the\\n * character controller, runs round the arena (`ARENA_TEXT` below: walls, two pillars, two low walls to jump) collecting\\n * the gems the seed scatters, before the clock runs out. All the gems: won; the clock at 0: lost.\\n *\\n * The parts: a level as text, compiled for its physics bodies; settings (`game.*`, read when the scene starts, so they\\n * change play and go in replays); components (`gem`, drawn as a small glowing box because it declares `x` and `z` in\\n * metres; `round`, the score and the clock); the player (labs/game/cast/player.ts, an actor that reads the step's\\n10→ * intents: `move`, `jump`, `dash`); systems in the phase `rules`, after the actors' feet are read back; a named random\\n * stream (`gems`); events (`gem`, `won`, `lost`) that pages, sounds and tests hear. The page is labs/game/main.ts, the\\n * bot labs/game/bot.ts.\\n *\\n * The level's text lives here, not in a .txt file, since sim-side code reads no files; the page registers the same\\n * text for the view (labs/game/main.ts).\\n *\\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts, so `node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts` runs it in Node.\\n *\\n * @example\\n20→ * // node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --steps 600\\n * // node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --set game.gems=3 --seed 7\\n * ARENA.spawns.find((spawn) => spawn.name === 'hero')?.position; // [3.5, 0, 2.5]\\n * @see labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts\\n */\\nimport {\\n  addLevelBodies,\\n  compileLevel,\\n  defineComponent,\\n  defineScene,\\n30→  defineSettings,\\n  physicsOf,\\n  type ActorComponent,\\n  type World,\\n} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { spawnPlayer } from '../cast/player';\\n\\n/** The arena: 18 × 14 m inside walls 3 m high, two 2 × 2 m pillars, two low walls (0.75 m) to jump, the spawn `@`. */\\nexport const ARENA_TEXT = `---\\ndescription: The starter game's arena. 18 × 14 m inside walls 3 m high, two 2 × 2 m pillars, two low walls 0.75 m high that the player jumps, and the player's spawn.\\n40→---\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The starter game's scene `game:play`: every new game begins as this one (tools/game/new-game.mjs copies\\n * labs/game/ into it), so it is small, plays, and shows the parts a game is made of. The player, a humanoid on the\\n * character controller, runs round the arena (`ARENA_TEXT` below: walls, two pillars, two low walls to jump) collecting\\n * the gems the seed scatters, before the clock runs out. All the gems: won; the clock at 0: lost.\\n *\\n * The parts: a level as text, compiled for its physics bodies; settings (`game.*`, read when the scene starts, so they\\n * change play and go in replays); components (`gem`, drawn as a small glowing box because it declares `x` and `z` in\\n * metres; `round`, the score and the clock); the player (labs/game/cast/player.ts, an actor that reads the step's\\n10→ * intents: `move`, `jump`, `dash`); systems in the phase `rules`, after the actors' feet are read back; a named random\\n * stream (`gems`); events (`gem`, `won`, `lost`) that pages, sounds and tests hear. The page is labs/game/main.ts, the\\n * bot labs/game/bot.ts.\\n *\\n * The level's text lives here, not in a .txt file, since sim-side code reads no files; the page registers the same\\n * text for the view (labs/game/main.ts).\\n *\\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts, so `node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts` runs it in Node.\\n *\\n * @example\\n20→ * // node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --steps 600\\n * // node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --set game.gems=3 --seed 7\\n * ARENA.spawns.find((spawn) => spawn.name === 'hero')?.position; // [3.5, 0, 2.5]\\n * @see labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts\\n */\\nimport {\\n  addLevelBodies,\\n  compileLevel,\\n  defineComponent,\\n  defineScene,\\n30→  defineSettings,\\n  physicsOf,\\n  type ActorComponent,\\n  type World,\\n} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { spawnPlayer } from '../cast/player';\\n\\n/** The arena: 18 × 14 m inside walls 3 m high, two 2 × 2 m pillars, two low walls (0.75 m) to jump, the spawn `@`. */\\nexport const ARENA_TEXT = `---\\ndescription: The starter game's arena. 18 × 14 m inside walls 3 m high, two 2 × 2 m pillars, two low walls 0.75 m high that the player jumps, and the player's spawn.\\n40→---\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/play.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The starter game's scene `game:play`: every new game begins as this one (tools/game/new-game.mjs copies\\n * labs/game/ into it), so it is small, plays, and shows the parts a game is made of. The player, a humanoid on the\\n * character controller, runs round the arena (`ARENA_TEXT` below: walls, two pillars, two low walls to jump) collecting\\n * the gems the seed scatters, before the clock runs out. All the gems: won; the clock at 0: lost.\\n *\\n * The parts: a level as text, compiled for its physics bodies; settings (`game.*`, read when the scene starts, so they\\n * change play and go in replays); components (`gem`, drawn as a small glowing box because it declares `x` and `z` in\\n * metres; `round`, the score and the clock); the player (labs/game/cast/player.ts, an actor that reads the step's\\n * intents: `move`, `jump`, `dash`); systems in the phase `rules`, after the actors' feet are read back; a named random\\n * stream (`gems`); events (`gem`, `won`, `lost`) that pages, sounds and tests hear. The page is labs/game/main.ts, the\\n * bot labs/game/bot.ts.\\n *\\n * The level's text lives here, not in a .txt file, since sim-side code reads no files; the page registers the same\\n * text for the view (labs/game/main.ts).\\n *\\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts, so `node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts` runs it in Node.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --steps 600\\n * // node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --set game.gems=3 --seed 7\\n * ARENA.spawns.find((spawn) => spawn.name === 'hero')?.position; // [3.5, 0, 2.5]\\n * @see labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts\\n */\\nimport {\\n  addLevelBodies,\\n  compileLevel,\\n  defineComponent,\\n  defineScene,\\n  defineSettings,\\n  physicsOf,\\n  type ActorComponent,\\n  type World,\\n} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { spawnPlayer } from '../cast/player';\\n\\n/** The arena: 18 × 14 m inside walls 3 m high, two 2 × 2 m pillars, two low walls (0.75 m) to jump, the spawn `@`. */\\nexport const ARENA_TEXT = `---\\ndescription: The starter game's arena. 18 × 14 m inside walls 3 m high, two 2 × 2 m pillars, two low walls 0.75 m high that the player jumps, and the player's spawn.\\n---\\n\",\"total_lines\":212}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"12501859-0403-409a-a90c-9ff1123d4d05"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_347","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Defining game settings in play.ts.\n\nVitest isolates test files by default, so play and retreat settings won't conflict. play still needs to be deleted to avoid starter test failures. checkAll importing all scenes is safe as long as paths don't duplicate.\n\nRetreat settings don't overlap with play. Deleting play is safe since check won't import it anyway. I'll add window.__game and AIHub types to hub.ts, verify pad button 8 maps to Select, and start writing present.ts.\n\nDefined PAD glyph mappings for PlayStation, Xbox, keyboard, and mouse. These will drive the prompt line. Now moving on to song pick.\n\nDrafted the `songFor` function to select background music based on game flow. It routes attract, title, and roam to lobby; morning and pose to stillness; line and paddle to water; garden to rake; tilt before phase 3 to tilt; tilt dawn and credits to dawn; results to stamp; evening to lobby. Will verify in songs.ts that the stamp song loops false.\n\nMusic will only restart when the song ID changes, not every frame. The stamp song plays once on entering results. Voice lines trigger when flow.line changes, looking up act.text for lures via LINES['lure.'+id]. The book stays clean without exclamation marks. Disc reads wobble seat 0 x,y.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9c6bce9e-0c57-4a10-9939-afd93281d5e4-174","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"defineSong\\('song:","glob":"**/songs.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9c6bce9e-0c57-4a10-9939-afd93281d5e4-175","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656\" && npx vitest run labs/game/island.test.ts --reporter=verbose","description":"Retest island and pavilion boot"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3241,"output_tokens":1008,"cache_read_input_tokens":156800,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"c69f7d96-dd68-4574-ac7e-50307b117307"}
