]?.[0] ?? 0;\\n      row.mark.z = (MATS[row.ghost.seat]?.[1] ?? 0) + row.ghost.x;\\n      row.mark.y = 1 + row.ghost.y;\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\",\"new_line\":39,\"context_before\":\"function applyGhosts(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const raw = (intents as Record<string, unknown>)['game:ghosts'];\\n  const packed = Array.isArray(raw) ? raw : [];\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\\n/** Starts the class. The page calls this when a hub round begins, and when a sofa picks Group Class. */\\nfunction go(w: World): void {\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"790ba3cb-f365-4555-b7e5-61be9e79b2f1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_350","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing all page files in parallel.\n\nDrafting the about-data page with two-sentence answers. Testing counts will be updated after the full test run.\n\nEight test issues surfaced before the build. Four are critical: bot bands, island spawn NaN yaw, missing game.auto registration, and line book length. The four-bot score bands on ten seeds were most helpful.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9739226f-9e60-439e-bd61-e46089033959-178","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/sounds/songs.ts","offset":60,"limit":25}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1436,"output_tokens":488,"cache_read_input_tokens":162432,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"682363f9-2263-4247-988c-afd74131336d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9739226f-9e60-439e-bd61-e46089033959-178","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"60→/** The ending. The theme, alone. */\\nexport const dawn = defineSong('song:dawn', {\\n  bpm: 72,\\n  tracks: [\\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.18, notes: bars('C4 - - - E4 - - - G4 - - - B4 - - -', 'A4 - - - G4 - - - E4 - - - C4 - - -') },\\n    { wave: 'square', vol: 0.05, notes: bars('E5 . . . G5 . . . . . . . B5 . . .', 'A5 . . . G5 . . . E5 . . . . . . .') },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\n/** One stamp. It does not loop. */\\n70→export const stamp = defineSong('song:stamp', {\\n  bpm: 120,\\n  loop: false,\\n  tracks: [{ wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.22, notes: 'C5 E5 G5 C6 . . . . G5 . E5 . C5 . . .' }],\\n});\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"60→/** The ending. The theme, alone. */\\nexport const dawn = defineSong('song:dawn', {\\n  bpm: 72,\\n  tracks: [\\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.18, notes: bars('C4 - - - E4 - - - G4 - - - B4 - - -', 'A4 - - - G4 - - - E4 - - - C4 - - -') },\\n    { wave: 'square', vol: 0.05, notes: bars('E5 . . . G5 . . . . . . . B5 . . .', 'A5 . . . G5 . . . E5 . . . . . . .') },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\n/** One stamp. It does not loop. */\\n70→export const stamp = defineSong('song:stamp', {\\n  bpm: 120,\\n  loop: false,\\n  tracks: [{ wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.22, notes: 'C5 E5 G5 C6 . . . . G5 . E5 . C5 . . .' }],\\n});\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/sounds/songs.ts\",\"offset\":60,\"limit\":25,\"raw_output\":\"/** The ending. The theme, alone. */\\nexport const dawn = defineSong('song:dawn', {\\n  bpm: 72,\\n  tracks: [\\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.18, notes: bars('C4 - - - E4 - - - G4 - - - B4 - - -', 'A4 - - - G4 - - - E4 - - - C4 - - -') },\\n    { wave: 'square', vol: 0.05, notes: bars('E5 . . . G5 . . . . . . . B5 . . .', 'A5 . . . G5 . . . E5 . . . . . . .') },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\n/** One stamp. It does not loop. */\\nexport const stamp = defineSong('song:stamp', {\\n  bpm: 120,\\n  loop: false,\\n  tracks: [{ wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.22, notes: 'C5 E5 G5 C6 . . . . G5 . E5 . C5 . . .' }],\\n});\\n\",\"total_lines\":74}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"3480cd11-7b19-409e-88c0-8217dba0a31c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_351","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing all source files.\n\nThe About screen will page through long text using a More button. Only Back and More will appear as menu items, keeping the menu under six rows.\n\nAll About text will be rendered in a single scrollable panel. Every Source Information field and feedback answer will be present in the DOM, since \"on the screen\" likely means present in the document rather than visible without scrolling.\n\nThe About panel will be scrollable with a 70vh max-height. The Touch Settings button will be large and tappable. The title menu focus string will be stored.\n\nThe window.__game update function will be called from event listeners and the onFrame loop. Keydown exits attract mode and sets the last device to keyboard. Pointerdown exits attract for mouse input but not touch. Pointermove exits attract on mouse movement. Gamepad buttons are polled in onFrame to set the last device and exit attract.\n\nThe keydown listener updates the game state immediately rather than waiting for the next frame. The icons setting defaults to PlayStation glyphs and switches to Xbox after a device switch; it is stored in save settings.icons. Glyph selection maps keyboard input to keys, mouse clicks to mouse, and all other devices to the current icon set.\n\nInitial lastDevice is set to gamepad. The Button icons setting toggles between PlayStation and Xbox glyphs, updating the glyph only when the last device is gamepad. Music volume defaults to 0.1, effects to 1, and voices to 1 on a fresh save; existing saves apply their stored volumes on boot. The store reads and writes a Save object keyed by 'save'. A pre-existing save enables Continue.\n\nSave writes are suppressed during attract mode and the hub. The erase flow asks Yes/No, then removes the save entry and seeds a fresh one. Settings for assist and CPU are stored in the save object; on continue they are applied via inspector.set before game.begin. Changing assist updates the inspector live and persists the value. Dev sliders modify the inspector directly and optionally save, with reset restoring defaults through describe.\n\nDev sliders will not be persisted in save files. Only assist, CPU, volumes, and icons are saved as user settings.\n\nThe present.ts overlay type now covers title, pause, settings, controls, dev, about, erase, results, evening, credits, programme, card, and none. The active screen derives from hub state and flow mode.\n\nThe title screen will show a touch-only gate when no real input has been detected yet. It displays a message and a Settings button, but hides the Begin option. Once a key or other real input is received, the gate lifts and the normal title menu appears.\n\nAn attract flag keeps a banner at the top of the title screen unless settings are open. Opening settings during attract mode does not clear the attract state.\n\nClosing settings returns to the attract banner. Starting attract mode sets the auto inspector to 'attract', seeds the inspector, and restarts the simulation. The page menus survive this reset because they are page DOM. If attract starts from the title screen, the title menu closes and the banner appears. If settings are open when idle triggers, they remain visible behind the attract mode. The idle timer resets on any input.\n\nThe idle timer counts only front-end menus as active input. Pause and play are excluded from this check, so attract mode cannot trigger during gameplay. If the user leaves the controller while in a paused state, the ten-second idle countdown continues until attract begins behind the pause screen.\n\nAttract mode only activates on the title, settings, about, controls, and programme screens while the flow is in title or roam mode. It does not trigger during island roaming. Exiting attract mode resets the auto inspector to off, seeds the simulation, and returns to the title screen without writing a save file. The pause menu opens only when the pause button is pressed while the hub is inactive, no modal menu is open, and attract mode is not running.\n\nThe hub pause overlay appears when the pause button is pressed without holding button 8. It shows Resume, Volume, and Button icons. The simulation never pauses. Restarting an activity resumes it. Returning to the island leaves the event and resumes. Quitting saves the game if not in attract mode, seeds a fresh title screen, and resumes.\n\nOpening the dev menu will resume the paused simulation so live sliders affect the running game. The pause menu closes when entering dev.\n\nThe Dev screen will have a Back button that returns to the running game, not the pause menu. The Pause menu will include a Dev Mode option so tests can reach it. Tunable sliders will render as `<input type=\"range\">` elements with a `data-ui=\"slider\"` attribute; changing them calls `inspector.set`.\n\nThe Dev menu will stay under six rows by keeping only four items: Next, Reset, Jumps, and Back. Each tunable will appear as both a menu row and a range input so keyboard-only tests can reach it.\n\nThe Dev menu will page through 18 tunables in groups of four. A Reset button restores defaults, and keyboard input on the range sliders triggers the change immediately.\n\nThe Jumps submenu splits into four pages: Days, Morning/Pose/Pond/Garden, Paddle/Line/Group/Tilt storm, and East/Stone/Dawn/Finish Serene. The Finish submenu offers six ranks—Present, Adequate, Composed, Serene, Unsettling, Back—and calls game.finish with the chosen rank.\n\nA time-scale menu item will cycle through 0.25, 1, and 4 using inspector.timeScale.\n\nRebinding controls will use a five-action-per-page menu with a \"Listen on pad\" option; keyboard input is captured via input.listen and applied with input.bindings.rebind. If the capture fails, the error appears in the status line instead of an alert.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e23cc545-2dd4-4ca4-9214-f9d0991fd3f7-179","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/events/kit.ts","offset":115,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e23cc545-2dd4-4ca4-9214-f9d0991fd3f7-180","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/events/group.ts","offset":40,"limit":100}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":768,"output_tokens":2907,"cache_read_input_tokens":163840,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"fdaf0542-3a66-49a8-9635-f91f65b52357"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e23cc545-2dd4-4ca4-9214-f9d0991fd3f7-179","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"115→  dy?: number;\\n  seat?: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** One balance step for a seat, then the centre is remembered for a late thumb. */\\n120→export function apply(w: World, intents: Intents, push: Push = {}): { body: Wobble; seat: Seat } {\\n  const seatIndex = push.seat ?? 0;\\n  const row = rowOf(w, seatIndex);\\n  const seat = readSeat(intents, seatIndex);\\n  const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n  const stick: Stick = {\\n    x: seat.x,\\n    y: seat.y,\\n    gentle: seat.gentle,\\n    both: seat.both,\\n130→    mdx: seat.mdx * cfg.sens,\\n    mdy: seat.mdy * cfg.sens,\\n    disturbX: push.dx ?? 0,\\n    disturbY: push.dy ?? 0,\\n    noiseScale: push.noise ?? 1,\\n    instabilityScale: push.inst ?? 1,\\n  };\\n  stepBalance(row.wobble, stick, cfg, w.time, w.dt);\\n  remember(row.hist, row.wobble.x, row.wobble.y);\\n  return { body: row.wobble, seat };\\n140→}\\n\\n/** The flow entity. */\\nexport function flowOf(w: World): Flow {\\n  return part<Flow>(w, 'flow');\\n}\\n\\n/** The activity board. */\\nexport function actOf(w: World): Act {\\n  return part<Act>(w, 'act');\\n150→}\\n\\n/** Removes every entity an activity marked. */\\nexport function sweep(w: World): void {\\n  for (const row of w.query('made') as unknown as { id: number }[]) w.despawn(row.id);\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"115→  dy?: number;\\n  seat?: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** One balance step for a seat, then the centre is remembered for a late thumb. */\\n120→export function apply(w: World, intents: Intents, push: Push = {}): { body: Wobble; seat: Seat } {\\n  const seatIndex = push.seat ?? 0;\\n  const row = rowOf(w, seatIndex);\\n  const seat = readSeat(intents, seatIndex);\\n  const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n  const stick: Stick = {\\n    x: seat.x,\\n    y: seat.y,\\n    gentle: seat.gentle,\\n    both: seat.both,\\n130→    mdx: seat.mdx * cfg.sens,\\n    mdy: seat.mdy * cfg.sens,\\n    disturbX: push.dx ?? 0,\\n    disturbY: push.dy ?? 0,\\n    noiseScale: push.noise ?? 1,\\n    instabilityScale: push.inst ?? 1,\\n  };\\n  stepBalance(row.wobble, stick, cfg, w.time, w.dt);\\n  remember(row.hist, row.wobble.x, row.wobble.y);\\n  return { body: row.wobble, seat };\\n140→}\\n\\n/** The flow entity. */\\nexport function flowOf(w: World): Flow {\\n  return part<Flow>(w, 'flow');\\n}\\n\\n/** The activity board. */\\nexport function actOf(w: World): Act {\\n  return part<Act>(w, 'act');\\n150→}\\n\\n/** Removes every entity an activity marked. */\\nexport function sweep(w: World): void {\\n  for (const row of w.query('made') as unknown as { id: number }[]) w.despawn(row.id);\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/events/kit.ts\",\"offset\":115,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"  dy?: number;\\n  seat?: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** One balance step for a seat, then the centre is remembered for a late thumb. */\\nexport function apply(w: World, intents: Intents, push: Push = {}): { body: Wobble; seat: Seat } {\\n  const seatIndex = push.seat ?? 0;\\n  const row = rowOf(w, seatIndex);\\n  const seat = readSeat(intents, seatIndex);\\n  const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n  const stick: Stick = {\\n    x: seat.x,\\n    y: seat.y,\\n    gentle: seat.gentle,\\n    both: seat.both,\\n    mdx: seat.mdx * cfg.sens,\\n    mdy: seat.mdy * cfg.sens,\\n    disturbX: push.dx ?? 0,\\n    disturbY: push.dy ?? 0,\\n    noiseScale: push.noise ?? 1,\\n    instabilityScale: push.inst ?? 1,\\n  };\\n  stepBalance(row.wobble, stick, cfg, w.time, w.dt);\\n  remember(row.hist, row.wobble.x, row.wobble.y);\\n  return { body: row.wobble, seat };\\n}\\n\\n/** The flow entity. */\\nexport function flowOf(w: World): Flow {\\n  return part<Flow>(w, 'flow');\\n}\\n\\n/** The activity board. */\\nexport function actOf(w: World): Act {\\n  return part<Act>(w, 'act');\\n}\\n\\n/** Removes every entity an activity marked. */\\nexport function sweep(w: World): void {\\n  for (const row of w.query('made') as unknown as { id: number }[]) w.despawn(row.id);\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":155}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e23cc545-2dd4-4ca4-9214-f9d0991fd3f7-180","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"40→        },\\n      });\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Steps the CPU mats. They do not change your score. */\\nfunction cpus(w: World): void {\\n  const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n  const packed: number[] = [];\\n50→  for (let seat = 0; seat <= 3; seat++) packed.push(0, 0, 0, 0);\\n  for (let seat = 1; seat <= 3; seat++) {\\n    let row: ReturnType<typeof rowOf> | undefined;\\n    try {\\n      row = rowOf(w, seat);\\n    } catch {\\n      row = undefined;\\n    }\\n    if (!row) continue;\\n    const stick = seek('human', 0, 0, row.wobble, row.hist, cfg, w.tick, 1);\\n60→    const both = wantBreath('human', w.time, cfg.period) ? 1 : 0;\\n    packed[seat * 4] = stick.x;\\n    packed[seat * 4 + 1] = stick.y;\\n    packed[seat * 4 + 2] = both;\\n    packed[seat * 4 + 3] = both;\\n  }\\n  const intents = { 'game:seats': packed } as Intents;\\n  for (let seat = 1; seat <= 3; seat++) {\\n    try {\\n      rowOf(w, seat);\\n70→    } catch {\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    apply(w, intents, { seat, noise: 1.35 });\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Lead-in, then the class. Phase 0 still, 1 heron, 2 pond. */\\nexport function step(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n80→  if (act.done) return;\\n  if (act.phase === 2) {\\n    const savedA = act.a;\\n    const savedB = act.b;\\n    const clock = act.hold;\\n    act.tick = clock;\\n    pondStep(w, intents);\\n    act.hold = act.tick;\\n    act.a = savedA;\\n    act.b = savedB;\\n90→    act.phase = 2;\\n    if (act.done || act.hold >= 45 * 60) {\\n      act.c = pondScore(w);\\n      act.a = savedA;\\n      act.b = savedB;\\n      act.done = 1;\\n    } else act.done = 0;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  act.tick += 1;\\n100→  act.left += 1;\\n  const pose = poseById('heron');\\n  const { body, seat } = apply(w, intents, { inst: act.phase === 1 ? pose.instability : 1, noise: act.phase === 1 ? 1 : 1 });\\n  cpus(w);\\n  if (act.left < LEAD) return;\\n  const scoring = act.left - LEAD;\\n  if (act.phase === 0) {\\n    act.samples += 1;\\n    if (Math.hypot(body.x, body.y) <= 0.22) act.acc += 1;\\n    if (scoring >= CLASS) {\\n110→      act.a = 1000 * (act.samples ? act.acc / act.samples : 0);\\n      act.phase = 1;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n      act.samples = 0;\\n      act.acc = 0;\\n      flowOf(w).line = 'group.heron';\\n    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  const down = seat.fl > 0.5;\\n120→  act.samples += 1;\\n  if (down && Math.hypot(body.x, body.y) <= 0.2) act.acc += 1;\\n  act.acc2 += body.sync;\\n  if (scoring >= CLASS) {\\n    const inShare = act.samples ? act.acc / act.samples : 0;\\n    const sync = act.samples ? act.acc2 / act.samples : 0;\\n    const savedA = act.a;\\n    const savedB = clampScore(1000 * (0.7 * inShare + 0.3 * sync));\\n    pondSetup(w, 45);\\n    act.a = savedA;\\n130→    act.b = savedB;\\n    act.phase = 2;\\n    act.hold = 0;\\n    act.done = 0;\\n    flowOf(w).line = 'group.pond';\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** The mean of the three classes, so a rank still fits in 0 to 1000. */\\nexport function score(w: World): number {\",\"content_concise\":\"40→        },\\n      });\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Steps the CPU mats. They do not change your score. */\\nfunction cpus(w: World): void {\\n  const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n  const packed: number[] = [];\\n50→  for (let seat = 0; seat <= 3; seat++) packed.push(0, 0, 0, 0);\\n  for (let seat = 1; seat <= 3; seat++) {\\n    let row: ReturnType<typeof rowOf> | undefined;\\n    try {\\n      row = rowOf(w, seat);\\n    } catch {\\n      row = undefined;\\n    }\\n    if (!row) continue;\\n    const stick = seek('human', 0, 0, row.wobble, row.hist, cfg, w.tick, 1);\\n60→    const both = wantBreath('human', w.time, cfg.period) ? 1 : 0;\\n    packed[seat * 4] = stick.x;\\n    packed[seat * 4 + 1] = stick.y;\\n    packed[seat * 4 + 2] = both;\\n    packed[seat * 4 + 3] = both;\\n  }\\n  const intents = { 'game:seats': packed } as Intents;\\n  for (let seat = 1; seat <= 3; seat++) {\\n    try {\\n      rowOf(w, seat);\\n70→    } catch {\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    apply(w, intents, { seat, noise: 1.35 });\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Lead-in, then the class. Phase 0 still, 1 heron, 2 pond. */\\nexport function step(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n80→  if (act.done) return;\\n  if (act.phase === 2) {\\n    const savedA = act.a;\\n    const savedB = act.b;\\n    const clock = act.hold;\\n    act.tick = clock;\\n    pondStep(w, intents);\\n    act.hold = act.tick;\\n    act.a = savedA;\\n    act.b = savedB;\\n90→    act.phase = 2;\\n    if (act.done || act.hold >= 45 * 60) {\\n      act.c = pondScore(w);\\n      act.a = savedA;\\n      act.b = savedB;\\n      act.done = 1;\\n    } else act.done = 0;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  act.tick += 1;\\n100→  act.left += 1;\\n  const pose = poseById('heron');\\n  const { body, seat } = apply(w, intents, { inst: act.phase === 1 ? pose.instability : 1, noise: act.phase === 1 ? 1 : 1 });\\n  cpus(w);\\n  if (act.left < LEAD) return;\\n  const scoring = act.left - LEAD;\\n  if (act.phase === 0) {\\n    act.samples += 1;\\n    if (Math.hypot(body.x, body.y) <= 0.22) act.acc += 1;\\n    if (scoring >= CLASS) {\\n110→      act.a = 1000 * (act.samples ? act.acc / act.samples : 0);\\n      act.phase = 1;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n      act.samples = 0;\\n      act.acc = 0;\\n      flowOf(w).line = 'group.heron';\\n    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  const down = seat.fl > 0.5;\\n120→  act.samples += 1;\\n  if (down && Math.hypot(body.x, body.y) <= 0.2) act.acc += 1;\\n  act.acc2 += body.sync;\\n  if (scoring >= CLASS) {\\n    const inShare = act.samples ? act.acc / act.samples : 0;\\n    const sync = act.samples ? act.acc2 / act.samples : 0;\\n    const savedA = act.a;\\n    const savedB = clampScore(1000 * (0.7 * inShare + 0.3 * sync));\\n    pondSetup(w, 45);\\n    act.a = savedA;\\n130→    act.b = savedB;\\n    act.phase = 2;\\n    act.hold = 0;\\n    act.done = 0;\\n    flowOf(w).line = 'group.pond';\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** The mean of the three classes, so a rank still fits in 0 to 1000. */\\nexport function score(w: World): number {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/events/group.ts\",\"offset\":40,\"limit\":100,\"raw_output\":\"        },\\n      });\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Steps the CPU mats. They do not change your score. */\\nfunction cpus(w: World): void {\\n  const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n  const packed: number[] = [];\\n  for (let seat = 0; seat <= 3; seat++) packed.push(0, 0, 0, 0);\\n  for (let seat = 1; seat <= 3; seat++) {\\n    let row: ReturnType<typeof rowOf> | undefined;\\n    try {\\n      row = rowOf(w, seat);\\n    } catch {\\n      row = undefined;\\n    }\\n    if (!row) continue;\\n    const stick = seek('human', 0, 0, row.wobble, row.hist, cfg, w.tick, 1);\\n    const both = wantBreath('human', w.time, cfg.period) ? 1 : 0;\\n    packed[seat * 4] = stick.x;\\n    packed[seat * 4 + 1] = stick.y;\\n    packed[seat * 4 + 2] = both;\\n    packed[seat * 4 + 3] = both;\\n  }\\n  const intents = { 'game:seats': packed } as Intents;\\n  for (let seat = 1; seat <= 3; seat++) {\\n    try {\\n      rowOf(w, seat);\\n    } catch {\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    apply(w, intents, { seat, noise: 1.35 });\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Lead-in, then the class. Phase 0 still, 1 heron, 2 pond. */\\nexport function step(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  if (act.done) return;\\n  if (act.phase === 2) {\\n    const savedA = act.a;\\n    const savedB = act.b;\\n    const clock = act.hold;\\n    act.tick = clock;\\n    pondStep(w, intents);\\n    act.hold = act.tick;\\n    act.a = savedA;\\n    act.b = savedB;\\n    act.phase = 2;\\n    if (act.done || act.hold >= 45 * 60) {\\n      act.c = pondScore(w);\\n      act.a = savedA;\\n      act.b = savedB;\\n      act.done = 1;\\n    } else act.done = 0;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  act.tick += 1;\\n  act.left += 1;\\n  const pose = poseById('heron');\\n  const { body, seat } = apply(w, intents, { inst: act.phase === 1 ? pose.instability : 1, noise: act.phase === 1 ? 1 : 1 });\\n  cpus(w);\\n  if (act.left < LEAD) return;\\n  const scoring = act.left - LEAD;\\n  if (act.phase === 0) {\\n    act.samples += 1;\\n    if (Math.hypot(body.x, body.y) <= 0.22) act.acc += 1;\\n    if (scoring >= CLASS) {\\n      act.a = 1000 * (act.samples ? act.acc / act.samples : 0);\\n      act.phase = 1;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n      act.samples = 0;\\n      act.acc = 0;\\n      flowOf(w).line = 'group.heron';\\n    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  const down = seat.fl > 0.5;\\n  act.samples += 1;\\n  if (down && Math.hypot(body.x, body.y) <= 0.2) act.acc += 1;\\n  act.acc2 += body.sync;\\n  if (scoring >= CLASS) {\\n    const inShare = act.samples ? act.acc / act.samples : 0;\\n    const sync = act.samples ? act.acc2 / act.samples : 0;\\n    const savedA = act.a;\\n    const savedB = clampScore(1000 * (0.7 * inShare + 0.3 * sync));\\n    pondSetup(w, 45);\\n    act.a = savedA;\\n    act.b = savedB;\\n    act.phase = 2;\\n    act.hold = 0;\\n    act.done = 0;\\n    flowOf(w).line = 'group.pond';\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** The mean of the three classes, so a rank still fits in 0 to 1000. */\\nexport function score(w: World): number {\\n\",\"total_lines\":177}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"5e3904da-69fa-4620-a336-ab94f0a4c9a6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_352","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The CPU writes game:seats internally by constructing intents locally. It does not read the page's game:seats for the CPU.\n\nThe page's game:seats are ignored by cpus(). Extra pads do not affect CPU seats. The plan requires page pads to override CPU for local multiplayer.\n\ncpus() currently ignores step intents entirely. It should instead read incoming game:seats and use them for seats marked human by the page. This preserves bot behavior when no page data arrives.\n\ncpus() will read step intents and use page game:seats for claimed seats. The page must not send zeros, or it would zero the CPU.\n\nThe page will send a `game:claim` array marking human seats. The sim reads this alongside `game:seats` and uses the page values only when a seat is claimed. Tests omit `game:claim`, so CPU behavior stays unchanged.\n\nThis change is small and preserves existing scores. It adds local pad support without retuning. The page sends signed stick axes from -1 to 1, which align with the sim's seek() output. A new `claimed()` helper will check the `game:claim` array to decide whether to use page game:seats for a seat.\n\nThe page will send `game:claim` and `game:seats` via `virtual.axis` every frame during group play. These values clear when group mode ends. The modal stays false during group so virtual axes are not dropped.\n\n`group.ts` needs its `cpus` signature and call updated to pass step intents. Page pad axes map directly to sim sticks, with y inverted for forward motion. The file is about 170 lines, so adding the new logic fits within the line limit.\n\nAbout-data answers will stay two sentences. The exit interview reuses those same strings. sourceInformation.usage must read exactly \"added on import\". Player count uses an en-dash: \"1–4\". Controls fit on one line. defineLook is imported from the engine. A sea material with texture water is being defined.\n\nSand and lawn materials are defined with their own colors. The sea material uses a water texture with seed 2 and base color #6fd0e8. Sky looks for retreat, dawn, dusk, and storm are registered. The page will set post.look to look:retreat by default. It can switch to look:storm during tilt storms.\n\nThe page will set the storm sky look inside a try/catch block to avoid boot failures. It will only query for that look once, and otherwise keep the default retreat look. Camera follow for the guest seat is also being considered, though the exact timing of cameraInput relative to onFrame is uncertain.\n\nA module-level feet variable will be updated in onFrame and read by cameraInput. The guest starts at [0, 40, 6] and falls to [0, 1.2, 6]. The code will query world entities for the actor with role guest and update the follow target once that actor is found.\n\nMouse deltas will be accumulated in module-level variables during canvas pointermove events. Each onFrame will write those values to the virtual game:mouse axis and then zero the accumulators. Because sampling happens before onFrame, this creates a one-frame delay. When no movement occurs, the axis is explicitly set to [0, 0] so it does not stick.\n\nPointer lock will be triggered by a canvas click during play, but only when the modal is closed. Song and voice will be handled inside onFrame. Save writes will be debounced to fire once when entering result, evening, or credits modes, or when pebble counts change.\n\nA composite key of mode, event, result, pebbles, and cursor will trigger a save write only when it changes. Title, attract, and hub modes are excluded. The erase action removes the save key, and begin writes a fresh save after game.start. Because actions.run runs between steps, the next onFrame will see the updated state before saving.\n\nFree play is gated by the save file, not the live flow. The title screen always shows day one until the player begins a game. Free play only unlocks after the save records day greater than one or credits. The exact sequence of begin and leave during pick is being checked to avoid stamping an unwanted state.\n\nFree play after day one will call begin then leave. This starts the current event and immediately tears it down without results. Credits free play simply calls begin. Group play from title uses startEvent directly with no mode check.\n\nThe programme menu during roam lists the current day's events plus a Go option. It reads from flow.day and calls game.start for each item.\n\nDuring roam, pressing act triggers game.start using act.text as the event id. The HUD shows press act when near a station.\n\nResults menu options are Again, which restarts the current event; Carry, which calls game.carry; and Sleep, which calls game.sleep.\n\nEvening mode uses Sleep to enter sleep. Credits mode uses Walk to leave and Morning check to start the morning event.\n\nThe HUD will display line text from LINES[flow.line].\n\nThe sim imports LURES from data/lures.ts to show a pond lure panel when act.text matches a lure id. The panel renders as a div with data-ui=\"lure\". If the id is menu, it displays a fake Resume button made of a div with role=\"button\" instead of a real button. Clicking this div counts as pointer input and disturbs the pond.\n\nThe fake pause button will not intercept Escape or real pause. Pressing Enter on the menu lure still triggers act and disturbs the pond. The hub card HTML is drafted with placeholders for player count and time, and decorative numbers may come from AIHub.rng.\n\nThe hub card will use AIHub.rng('card') for all random numbers and avoid Math.random entirely. The countdown timer will come from the card event's `left` value. Card names will be drawn from hub.players. When the card is visible, pressing Enter will signal ready via AIHub.answer('ready').\n\nReady input will use Enter, PadSouth, and click or tap on the hub card. Space is not used for ready. PadNorth may serve as an extra ready button. The start event will set a started flag.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-51bea5b2-76c3-49c7-a2e9-e85315742a85-181","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"players|color|welcome","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/hub/round.js","head_limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4354,"output_tokens":3238,"cache_read_input_tokens":164608,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"12e351d8-7321-4d5e-95c2-c7655676b425"}
