{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_356","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Tracing the pond phase's CPU call chain through apply, rowOf, and stepBalance.\n\nConfirmed pondStep handles seat 0 and cpus handles seats 1-3. Verified apply leaves act untouched. Now writing UI files in large chunks. Will check group.ts stays under 200 lines. Designing a Page API with modal() and frame() methods for present.ts.\n\nFinalized the Page API with a `feet()` method and `createPage` factory. The UI will be split into three files: `ui/copy.ts` for line lookups, `ui/shell.ts` for menus and DOM, and `ui/play.ts` for frame logic. Hub wiring will live inside `createPage`. Now starting to write individual files.\n\nDrafting the About screen's shared data file. It will contain SOURCE, TESTING, ENGINE, PROMPT, AI_HUB, and EXIT sections matching the exit-interview.json keys. Each answer is limited to two short sentences.\n\nFleshing out the About screen's data file with concrete answers. The technical stack is my-3dge e7a1243, three.js r182 WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite 7.3, and TypeScript. Art direction uses native toon puppets on a bright retreat lawn, sand, and sea. Animation relies on an engine clip layer with a small original pose set scrubbed from the balance step; the rest pose credits Mesh2Motion. Audio combines tracker songs, code-made effects, and gibberish syllable voices, with fresh-save music as a tenth. Online features include AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode plus same-screen Group Class. Testing covers bot bands on ten seeds, a three-seed director, and browser checks of the built file. Research is none.\n\nThe About data file now includes environment, model, and usage fields. Testing caught eight issues before hand-in: score bands, a NaN prop yaw, a missing boot setting, over-long lines, a ghost pack offset, and three balance misses. Four were critical: three activities scored under their bands and the island would not boot. The four bot bands on ten seeds for every shipped activity was the most helpful test. A headless screenshot was the least helpful because it can be blank while the simulation state is fine.\n\nThe ENGINE section of the About data file is now complete. It explains that scene actions, live settings, and a headless world enabled browser-free testing. It lists four setup blockers: playClip during setup, props needing yaw, a frozen recorded world, and hub query keys read as settings. It credits the balance step, day director, songs, and syllable voices to the game itself. It notes the hardest part was keeping the pavilion small for the hub deadline while the island remained a real place. It states no engine files were changed. It suggests adding a mesh to the page and starting music at a tenth instead of a half.\n\nThe PROMPT section of the About data file is now complete. It credits the acceptance numbers, cut line, and bot bands for making scope checkable. It notes the group score must sum to 3000 while fitting a 0 to 1000 rank, and that several seed lines exceed two sentences. The hardest part was one HTML file that serves as both a full retreat and a ghost session the harness can drive. It suggests stating the group score once and pinning the session client hash to the file the plan tells you to fetch.\n\nThe AI_HUB section is also complete. It names the hub Thumb Yoga with the tagline \"A week of balance at Little Fulcrum\" and the description \"Stand on the disc and keep the dot near the middle.\"\n\nThe AI hub metadata is now complete. Little Fulcrum runs a five-day retreat of pose, pond, water, sand, and a storm. The game is a one-to-four player third-person sports title with controls for leaning, WASD or mouse, and foot buttons. Tags include 3d, sports, third-person, comedy, and co-op. The source field contains only \"Wii Fit\" to satisfy the word limit. Ready to write all files.\n\nAdding a CREDITS array to the About data file with one-sentence entries for each dependency and the original pose clips. Preparing to write the UI files now, including a compact shell. Will replace index.html with the Thumb Yoga title and Calibrating message, and add a hub:session meta tag to tags.html.\n\nAdding hub meta tags to tags.html. The session goal is 42 characters: \"Stay the steadiest across three classes\".\n\nVerifying the hub howto string is within the 80-character limit. Preparing to write onefile.mjs from the plan, using a function-based replacement for the charset meta tag.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-46a2bf83-e11f-4895-a7fd-cc954b80e9b9-186","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"alias|three/webgpu","glob":"**/vite.config.*"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":544,"output_tokens":1905,"cache_read_input_tokens":174592,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"37c3d6f4-2509-4411-9fe7-75cf6d5fc89f"}
