{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_367","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will flip the status flags when everything is actually done, at the end.\n\nAdding a Deviations section to the stage file. Writing a `runAction` helper to safely invoke inspector actions. Checking whether `inspector.actions` needs a type guard.\n\nCasting the `run` function to a specific signature after the type check. Camera.set will use query parameters. Feet tracking will run in onFrame from world. The frozen view should still contain actor and role components.\n\nThe disc will be rendered as a div with SVG. Menus will use a single active Menu state, replacing the previous one when opened. Pause menu pages are planned: page 0 shows Resume, Restart, Back to the island, Settings, Controls, and More; page 1 shows Dev Mode, About, Quit, and Back. The hub pause menu is simpler, showing only Resume, Music, Effects, Voices, Icons, and Back without pausing simulation. Settings have two pages: page 0 lists Music, Effects, Voices, Icons, Assist, and More; page 1 lists CPU guests, Erase save, Controls, and Back. Volume items cycle on selection, and icons toggle.\n\nAssist toggles game.assist and CPU toggles game.cpu. Erase opens a yes/no confirmation menu. Controls rebinds will be shown on a dedicated page. The dev screen adds four ranges in a #sliders div, plus Next, Reset, Jumps, Time, Seed, and Back. Jumps replaces the standard menu. A generic openMenu helper will handle item lists, titles, and callbacks. Continue is disabled without a save, and Free play is disabled without a valid save.\n\nTouch screens will skip the title menu and show a Settings button instead. The title menu appears only after a key is pressed to arm the gate. When attract mode is active, the message stays until a key is pressed. The screen name becomes \"touch\" when the gate is up and no menu is open, or \"settings\" when opened from touch. A controller note line will remain in the DOM while the touch gate is active. Menu items are sliced to six entries. Hover moves focus and click selects items, with a data-value attribute marking the selected row.\n\nFocus will be published each frame from the selected menu label. Menus get IDs for testing: 'title' and 'results'. Speech lines will use the voices volume setting as both a parameter and on the UI bus. Effects volume targets the effects bus, music volume targets the music bus, and song changes happen in the frame loop.\n\nThe results screen will stamp the current song once on entry and track it to avoid repeated calls. Dawn effects for credits and tilt phase 3 require reading act.phase from the frame. A Snap interface is defined for frozen state, and the first flow entity plus wobble seat zero will be read.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dc92d18d-992b-4b47-935e-3b78c12144f2-201","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/events/group.ts","offset":77,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":903,"output_tokens":1339,"cache_read_input_tokens":186752,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"7104bd73-3ead-4857-91ae-bcbb7c2d02b6"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-dc92d18d-992b-4b47-935e-3b78c12144f2-201","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"77→    packed[seat * 4 + 2] = both;\\n    packed[seat * 4 + 3] = both;\\n  }\\n80→  const intents = { 'game:seats': packed } as Intents;\\n  for (let seat = 1; seat <= 3; seat++) {\\n    try {\\n      rowOf(w, seat);\\n    } catch {\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    apply(w, intents, { seat, noise: 1.35 });\\n  }\\n}\\n90→\\n/** Lead-in, then the class. Phase 0 still, 1 heron, 2 pond. */\\nexport function step(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  if (act.done) return;\\n  if (act.phase === 2) {\\n    const savedA = act.a;\\n    const savedB = act.b;\\n    const clock = act.hold;\\n    act.tick = clock;\\n100→    pondStep(w, intents);\\n    cpus(w, intents);\\n    act.hold = act.tick;\\n    act.a = savedA;\\n    act.b = savedB;\\n    act.phase = 2;\\n    if (act.done || act.hold >= 45 * 60) {\",\"content_concise\":\"77→    packed[seat * 4 + 2] = both;\\n    packed[seat * 4 + 3] = both;\\n  }\\n80→  const intents = { 'game:seats': packed } as Intents;\\n  for (let seat = 1; seat <= 3; seat++) {\\n    try {\\n      rowOf(w, seat);\\n    } catch {\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    apply(w, intents, { seat, noise: 1.35 });\\n  }\\n}\\n90→\\n/** Lead-in, then the class. Phase 0 still, 1 heron, 2 pond. */\\nexport function step(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  if (act.done) return;\\n  if (act.phase === 2) {\\n    const savedA = act.a;\\n    const savedB = act.b;\\n    const clock = act.hold;\\n    act.tick = clock;\\n100→    pondStep(w, intents);\\n    cpus(w, intents);\\n    act.hold = act.tick;\\n    act.a = savedA;\\n    act.b = savedB;\\n    act.phase = 2;\\n    if (act.done || act.hold >= 45 * 60) {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/events/group.ts\",\"offset\":77,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"    packed[seat * 4 + 2] = both;\\n    packed[seat * 4 + 3] = both;\\n  }\\n  const intents = { 'game:seats': packed } as Intents;\\n  for (let seat = 1; seat <= 3; seat++) {\\n    try {\\n      rowOf(w, seat);\\n    } catch {\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    apply(w, intents, { seat, noise: 1.35 });\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Lead-in, then the class. Phase 0 still, 1 heron, 2 pond. */\\nexport function step(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  if (act.done) return;\\n  if (act.phase === 2) {\\n    const savedA = act.a;\\n    const savedB = act.b;\\n    const clock = act.hold;\\n    act.tick = clock;\\n    pondStep(w, intents);\\n    cpus(w, intents);\\n    act.hold = act.tick;\\n    act.a = savedA;\\n    act.b = savedB;\\n    act.phase = 2;\\n    if (act.done || act.hold >= 45 * 60) {\\n\",\"total_lines\":192}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"bb35810d-e861-4bcc-b51f-c06c87de243d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_368","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Pond uses real CPU intents, including player breathing.\n\nCPU seats use claim or bot intents. The outer intents object is only used for claim and game:seats. pondStep may set act.done, but cpus ignores it and restores the state. No local variable shadowing occurs. Now writing files, making stage.ts as complete as possible.\n\nThe pond phase is safe because the CPU path uses bot intents, which contain game:seats. The claimed function in group.ts added lines but they are fine. I will write TypeScript directly without Python helpers. index.html will include the 28px rule and shell layout CSS. I am now drafting main.ts.\n\nmain.ts imports the engine, retreat looks, songs, voice audio, UI actions, and both scenes. It checks for WebGPU support and either displays a browser requirement message or proceeds to boot.\n\nThe boot function hides the message element once the engine is ready. A 14-second watchdog will call hub.ready() regardless of whether the engine finishes loading.\n\nA `tellReady` helper will clear the 14-second watchdog and call `hub.ready()` once the engine is ready. It guards against duplicate calls with a `told` flag.\n\nThe card appears after `ready()` because the hub sends it only once `ready` is true. The engine draws before `ready`, so the card is visible when the harness sends Enter.\n\nThe hub flushes pending events for listeners registered before `ready()`, so the card will not be missed. In `main.ts`, `createPage` registers its listeners first, then `createEngine` attaches to the page, and finally `tellReady()` is called.\n\ncreatePage will register hub listeners immediately, before the engine exists. The card UI can render while the engine is still initializing.\n\nattach stores the engine reference and renders any pending card events that arrived before attachment.\n\nThe URL search is cleaned up by removing aihub parameters, setting touch to off, and adding post.look=look:retreat.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The pavilion ghost pack is fixed. Next I am writing the page: look, controls, menus, and the hub card."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dd60ce3c-6f2a-4975-b266-e7c466b64464-202","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/about-data.ts","content":"/**\n * @file The words shared by the About screen and exit-interview.json.\n * Each answer is at most two short sentences. The source name appears only in the source fields.\n */\nexport const SOURCE = {\n  date: '2026-11-04 22:36:56',\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\n  plan: 'PLAN.md',\n  genre: 'Sports',\n  perspective: 'third-person',\n  tech: 'my-3dge at e7a1243, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite 7.3, TypeScript.',\n  artDirection: 'The engine toon style, with a bright lawn, sand shore, and a flat sea.',\n  animation: 'The engine clip layer. Original poses are scrubbed from the balance step. The rest pose is Mesh2Motion.',\n  audio: 'Tracker songs, code-made effects, and gibberish syllable voices. A fresh save plays music at a tenth.',\n  online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, and same-screen Group Class on its own.',\n  testing: 'Bot bands on ten seeds, a three-seed walk to the credits, and browser checks of the built file.',\n  research: 'none',\n  environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\n  model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\n  usage: 'added on import',\n} as const;\n\n/** Testing Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\nexport const TESTING = [\n  'Testing caught eight issues before hand-in. They were score bands, a NaN prop yaw, a missing boot setting, over-long lines, and a ghost pack read at the wrong offset.',\n  'Four were critical. Three activities scored under their band, and the island would not boot.',\n  'The most helpful test was the four bot bands on ten seeds for every shipped activity.',\n  'The least helpful was a headless screenshot. The canvas can be blank while the sim state is fine.',\n] as const;\n\n/** Engine Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\nexport const ENGINE = [\n  'Scene actions, live settings, and a headless world you can step made the week testable without a browser.',\n  'I got stuck on playClip during setup, props that need a yaw, a frozen recorded world, and hub query keys read as settings.',\n  'The balance step, the day director, the songs, and the syllable voices are the game’s own.',\n  'The hardest part was keeping the pavilion small enough for the hub ready deadline while the island stayed a place.',\n  'None. The engine files were not changed.',\n  'I would let a page add a mesh, and I would start the music bus at a tenth instead of a half.',\n] as const;\n\n/** Prompt Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\nexport const PROMPT = [\n  'The acceptance numbers, the cut line, and the bot bands made the scope checkable.',\n  'The group score is described as a sum to 3000 and also has to fit a rank from 0 to 1000. Several seed lines are longer than two sentences.',\n  'The hardest part was one HTML file that is a full retreat and also a ghost session the harness can drive.',\n  'I would state the group score once, and pin the session client hash to the file the plan says to fetch.',\n] as const;\n\n/** Credits shown under the same About screen. */\nexport const CREDITS = [\n  'my-3dge, MIT.',\n  'three.js r182, MIT.',\n  'Rapier 0.21, Apache-2.0.',\n  '@stdlib, Apache-2.0.',\n  'AI Hub session client 1.4.0, pasted unmodified.',\n  'The rest pose follows Mesh2Motion. The pose clips themselves are original.',\n] as const;\n\n/** Catalogue fields. The source name is only here and in SOURCE.source. */\nexport const AI_HUB = {\n  name: 'Thumb Yoga',\n  tagline: 'A week of balance at Little Fulcrum',\n  description: 'Stand on the disc and keep the dot near the middle. Little Fulcrum runs five days of pose, pond, water, sand, and a storm.',\n  type: 'Game',\n  genre: 'Sports',\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\n  series: '',\n  players: '1–4',\n  controls: 'Lean with the left stick, WASD or the mouse. L2 and R2, or Q and E, are the feet. Both feet or Space breathe.',\n  tags: ['3d', 'sports', 'third-person', 'comedy', 'co-op'],\n} as const;\n\n/** The exit-interview object. The screen and the file both read this. */\nexport const EXIT = {\n  sourceInformation: SOURCE,\n  testingFeedback: [...TESTING],\n  engineFeedback: [...ENGINE],\n  promptFeedback: [...PROMPT],\n  aiHub: AI_HUB,\n};\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dd60ce3c-6f2a-4975-b266-e7c466b64464-203","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/looks/retreat.ts","content":"/**\n * @file The retreat look. High-key daylight, a dawn, a dusk, and a drained storm.\n * Materials for the lawn, the shore, and the sea are defined here so the view can find them.\n */\nimport { defineLook, defineMaterial, defineSky } from '../../../engine';\n\ndefineMaterial('material:sand', {\n  description: 'Shore sand and the mats.',\n  color: '#F4E8C8',\n  roughness: 0.9,\n});\n\ndefineMaterial('material:lawn', {\n  description: 'The upland lawn.',\n  color: '#A9D98A',\n  roughness: 0.85,\n});\n\ndefineMaterial('material:sea', {\n  description: 'The sea around the island. The texture is drifted by moving the prop.',\n  color: '#6FD0E8',\n  map: { texture: 'texture:water', seed: 2, params: { base: '#6fd0e8' } },\n});\n\nconst day = {\n  dome: { show: true, turbidity: 2, rayleigh: 1, mieCoefficient: 0.005, mieDirectionalG: 0.8, exposure: 0.5 },\n  sun: { color: '#fff0d8', intensity: 2.6, azimuth: 0.4, elevation: 1.05 },\n  ambient: { sky: '#BFE9FF', ground: '#F4E8C8', intensity: 1.5 },\n  fog: { color: '#c8eaf8', start: 50, end: 240, amount: 0.35 },\n  backdrop: { haze: '#BFE9FF', tint: '#ffffff', layers: [] as [] },\n};\n\ndefineSky('sky:retreat', {\n  description: 'Brochure noon over an empty sea horizon.',\n  background: '#BFE9FF',\n  ...day,\n});\n\ndefineSky('sky:retreatDawn', {\n  description: 'The last morning. The sun is low and the sea is pale.',\n  background: '#f3d2c4',\n  dome: { show: true, turbidity: 6, rayleigh: 2.2, mieCoefficient: 0.01, mieDirectionalG: 0.85, exposure: 0.36 },\n  sun: { color: '#ffc8a0', intensity: 1.7, azimuth: -1.2, elevation: 0.25 },\n  ambient: { sky: '#f0d0c8', ground: '#c8b8a0', intensity: 1.1 },\n  fog: { color: '#f0ddd4', start: 30, end: 200, amount: 0.5 },\n  backdrop: { haze: '#f3d2c4', layers: [] },\n});\n\ndefineSky('sky:retreatDusk', {\n  description: 'Evening on the lawn. The sun sits in the west.',\n  background: '#e7a888',\n  dome: { show: true, turbidity: 5, rayleigh: 2.4, mieCoefficient: 0.01, mieDirectionalG: 0.85, exposure: 0.32 },\n  sun: { color: '#ff9a60', intensity: 1.5, azimuth: 2.4, elevation: 0.2 },\n  ambient: { sky: '#e8c0b0', ground: '#6a5040', intensity: 1 },\n  fog: { color: '#e8c8b8', start: 30, end: 200, amount: 0.45 },\n  backdrop: { haze: '#e7a888', layers: [] },\n});\n\ndefineSky('sky:storm', {\n  description: 'The Great Tilt. The colour drains and the sun is a grey disc.',\n  background: '#9aa8b0',\n  dome: { show: true, turbidity: 10, rayleigh: 0.6, mieCoefficient: 0.02, mieDirectionalG: 0.7, exposure: 0.28 },\n  sun: { color: '#d8dde2', intensity: 0.8, azimuth: 0.2, elevation: 0.6 },\n  ambient: { sky: '#b8c4cc', ground: '#6a7070', intensity: 0.8 },\n  fog: { color: '#aeb8c0', start: 20, end: 140, amount: 0.7 },\n  backdrop: { haze: '#9aa8b0', layers: [] },\n});\n\ndefineLook('look:retreat', {\n  description: 'High-key brochure daylight: soft toon light, a little bloom, a thin ink line.',\n  sky: 'sky:retreat',\n  style: 'toon',\n  filters: {\n    bloom: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.35, threshold: 0.92 },\n    grade: { scope: 'all', brightness: 1.08, saturation: 0.92, lift: 0.03 },\n    outline: { scope: 'characters+objects', width: 1, darken: 0.25 },\n  },\n});\n\ndefineLook('look:storm', {\n  description: 'The same toon line, with the colour pulled toward the storm sky.',\n  sky: 'sky:storm',\n  style: 'toon',\n  filters: {\n    bloom: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.2, threshold: 0.95 },\n    grade: { scope: 'all', brightness: 0.92, saturation: 0.45, lift: 0.02 },\n    outline: { scope: 'characters+objects', width: 1, darken: 0.35 },\n  },\n});\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dd60ce3c-6f2a-4975-b266-e7c466b64464-204","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/actions.ts","content":"/**\n * @file The balance map. Lean is the stick and the keys. The feet are triggers, Q and E, and the mouse buttons.\n * Space breathes. It is not the act button. The pointer stays free on menus.\n */\nimport { defineActionMap } from '../../../engine';\n\ndefineActionMap('actionMap:retreat', {\n  description: 'Lean with the left stick, WASD or the arrows. The feet are L2 and R2, Q and E, or the mouse buttons.',\n  lock: false,\n  actions: {\n    forward: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\n    back: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\n    left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\n    right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\n    footl: ['KeyQ', 'PadL2', 'MouseLeft'],\n    footr: ['KeyE', 'PadR2', 'MouseRight'],\n    breathe: ['Space'],\n    act: ['KeyF', 'Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'PadSouth'],\n    gentle: ['ShiftLeft', 'PadL1'],\n  },\n  move: ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right'],\n  values: {\n    'game:f': 'forward',\n    'game:b': 'back',\n    'game:l': 'left',\n    'game:r': 'right',\n    'game:fl': 'footl',\n    'game:fr': 'footr',\n    'game:g': 'gentle',\n  },\n});\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dd60ce3c-6f2a-4975-b266-e7c466b64464-205","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/glyphs.ts","content":"/**\n * @file Prompts for the device used last. Pads start as PlayStation. Settings can ask for Xbox.\n * Keys and mouse buttons replace the pad marks the frame those devices are used.\n */\nexport type GlyphSet = 'playstation' | 'xbox' | 'keys' | 'mouse';\n\n/** One row of marks for the verbs. */\nconst MARKS: Record<GlyphSet, Record<string, string>> = {\n  playstation: { accept: 'Cross', cancel: 'Circle', lean: 'Left stick', feet: 'L2 and R2', breathe: 'L2 and R2 together', act: 'Cross', pause: 'Options' },\n  xbox: { accept: 'A', cancel: 'B', lean: 'Left stick', feet: 'LT and RT', breathe: 'LT and RT together', act: 'A', pause: 'Menu' },\n  keys: { accept: 'Enter', cancel: 'Esc', lean: 'WASD', feet: 'Q and E', breathe: 'Space', act: 'F', pause: 'Esc' },\n  mouse: { accept: 'Click', cancel: 'Esc', lean: 'Mouse', feet: 'Left and right buttons', breathe: 'Space', act: 'Click', pause: 'Esc' },\n};\n\n/** The mark for one verb on this glyph set. */\nexport function glyph(set: GlyphSet, verb: string): string {\n  return MARKS[set][verb] ?? verb;\n}\n\n/** One prompt line. Two clauses, one sentence. */\nexport function promptLine(set: GlyphSet): string {\n  const row = MARKS[set];\n  return `${row.lean} leans, and ${row.feet} are the feet. ${row.breathe} breathes, and ${row.act} acts.`;\n}\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dd60ce3c-6f2a-4975-b266-e7c466b64464-206","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/save.ts","content":"/**\n * @file The retreat save. The sim never reads the store. The page copies this in through game.begin.\n * Outfits stay an empty list. Pebbles are kept and never spent.\n */\nimport type { Store } from '../../../engine';\n\n/** What the player turned in Settings. */\nexport interface Prefs {\n  music: number;\n  effects: number;\n  voices: number;\n  icons: 'playstation' | 'xbox';\n  assist: number;\n  cpu: number;\n}\n\n/** One saved week. */\nexport interface Save {\n  day: number;\n  cursor: number;\n  pebbles: number;\n  age: number;\n  prior: number;\n  credits: number;\n  result: number;\n  seen: string;\n  rank: string;\n  bests: Record<string, number>;\n  finds: string[];\n  outfits: string[];\n  settings: Prefs;\n}\n\n/** The store key. */\nexport const SAVE_KEY = 'save';\n\n/** Volumes and switches for a guest who has never saved. */\nexport function freshPrefs(): Prefs {\n  return { music: 0.1, effects: 1, voices: 1, icons: 'playstation', assist: 0, cpu: 1 };\n}\n\n/** A week that has not started. */\nexport function freshSave(): Save {\n  return {\n    day: 1, cursor: 0, pebbles: 0, age: 0, prior: 0, credits: 0, result: 0, seen: '', rank: '',\n    bests: {}, finds: [], outfits: [], settings: freshPrefs(),\n  };\n}\n\n/** Reads the save, or null when there is none or it is not a save. */\nexport function readSave(store: Store): Save | null {\n  const raw = store.get(SAVE_KEY, null);\n  if (!raw || typeof raw !== 'object') return null;\n  const row = raw as Partial<Save>;\n  if (typeof row.day !== 'number') return null;\n  const base = freshSave();\n  return {\n    ...base,\n    ...row,\n    bests: row.bests && typeof row.bests === 'object' ? row.bests : {},\n    finds: Array.isArray(row.finds) ? row.finds.filter((id) => typeof id === 'string') : [],\n    outfits: [],\n    settings: { ...base.settings, ...(row.settings ?? {}) },\n  };\n}\n\n/** Writes the save. Callers skip this during attract and during a hub session. */\nexport function writeSave(store: Store, save: Save): void {\n  store.set(SAVE_KEY, { ...save, outfits: [] });\n}\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1636,"output_tokens":6662,"cache_read_input_tokens":187648,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"a7c5fc8d-5bb4-4d70-b47d-a4b3c5fe79d6"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-dd60ce3c-6f2a-4975-b266-e7c466b64464-202","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file The words shared by the About screen and exit-interview.json.\\n * Each answer is at most two short sentences. The source name appears only in the source fields.\\n */\\nexport const SOURCE = {\\n  date: '2026-11-04 22:36:56',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n  perspective: 'third-person',\\n  tech: 'my-3dge at e7a1243, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite 7.3, TypeScript.',\\n  artDirection: 'The engine toon style, with a bright lawn, sand shore, and a flat sea.',\\n  animation: 'The engine clip layer. Original poses are scrubbed from the balance step. The rest pose is Mesh2Motion.',\\n  audio: 'Tracker songs, code-made effects, and gibberish syllable voices. A fresh save plays music at a tenth.',\\n  online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, and same-screen Group Class on its own.',\\n  testing: 'Bot bands on ten seeds, a three-seed walk to the credits, and browser checks of the built file.',\\n  research: 'none',\\n  environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\\n  model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\\n  usage: 'added on import',\\n} as const;\\n\\n/** Testing Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const TESTING = [\\n  'Testing caught eight issues before hand-in. They were score bands, a NaN prop yaw, a missing boot setting, over-long lines, and a ghost pack read at the wrong offset.',\\n  'Four were critical. Three activities scored under their band, and the island would not boot.',\\n  'The most helpful test was the four bot bands on ten seeds for every shipped activity.',\\n  'The least helpful was a headless screenshot. The canvas can be blank while the sim state is fine.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Engine Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const ENGINE = [\\n  'Scene actions, live settings, and a headless world you can step made the week testable without a browser.',\\n  'I got stuck on playClip during setup, props that need a yaw, a frozen recorded world, and hub query keys read as settings.',\\n  'The balance step, the day director, the songs, and the syllable voices are the game’s own.',\\n  'The hardest part was keeping the pavilion small enough for the hub ready deadline while the island stayed a place.',\\n  'None. The engine files were not changed.',\\n  'I would let a page add a mesh, and I would start the music bus at a tenth instead of a half.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Prompt Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const PROMPT = [\\n  'The acceptance numbers, the cut line, and the bot bands made the scope checkable.',\\n  'The group score is described as a sum to 3000 and also has to fit a rank from 0 to 1000. Several seed lines are longer than two sentences.',\\n  'The hardest part was one HTML file that is a full retreat and also a ghost session the harness can drive.',\\n  'I would state the group score once, and pin the session client hash to the file the plan says to fetch.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Credits shown under the same About screen. */\\nexport const CREDITS = [\\n  'my-3dge, MIT.',\\n  'three.js r182, MIT.',\\n  'Rapier 0.21, Apache-2.0.',\\n  '@stdlib, Apache-2.0.',\\n  'AI Hub session client 1.4.0, pasted unmodified.',\\n  'The rest pose follows Mesh2Motion. The pose clips themselves are original.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Catalogue fields. The source name is only here and in SOURCE.source. */\\nexport const AI_HUB = {\\n  name: 'Thumb Yoga',\\n  tagline: 'A week of balance at Little Fulcrum',\\n  description: 'Stand on the disc and keep the dot near the middle. Little Fulcrum runs five days of pose, pond, water, sand, and a storm.',\\n  type: 'Game',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  series: '',\\n  players: '1–4',\\n  controls: 'Lean with the left stick, WASD or the mouse. L2 and R2, or Q and E, are the feet. Both feet or Space breathe.',\\n  tags: ['3d', 'sports', 'third-person', 'comedy', 'co-op'],\\n} as const;\\n\\n/** The exit-interview object. The screen and the file both read this. */\\nexport const EXIT = {\\n  sourceInformation: SOURCE,\\n  testingFeedback: [...TESTING],\\n  engineFeedback: [...ENGINE],\\n  promptFeedback: [...PROMPT],\\n  aiHub: AI_HUB,\\n};\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/about-data.ts has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/about-data.ts has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/about-data.ts\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file The words shared by the About screen and exit-interview.json.\\n * Each answer is at most two short sentences. The source name appears only in the source fields.\\n */\\nexport const SOURCE = {\\n  date: '2026-11-04 22:36:56',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n  perspective: 'third-person',\\n  tech: 'my-3dge at e7a1243, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite 7.3, TypeScript.',\\n  artDirection: 'The engine toon style, with a bright lawn, sand shore, and a flat sea.',\\n  animation: 'The engine clip layer. Original poses are scrubbed from the balance step. The rest pose is Mesh2Motion.',\\n  audio: 'Tracker songs, code-made effects, and gibberish syllable voices. A fresh save plays music at a tenth.',\\n  online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, and same-screen Group Class on its own.',\\n  tes