,115,46,32,65,110,105,109,97,116,105,111,110,58,32,116,104,101,32,101,110,103,105,110,101,39,115,32,99,108,105,112,32,108,97,121,101,114,32,97,110,100,32,104,117,109,97,110,111,105,100,32,119,105,116,104,32,97,32,110,101,119,32,114,101,97,100,97,98,108,101,32,99,108,105,112,32,115,101,116,32,115,99,114,117,98,98,101,100,32,102,114,111,109,32,116,104,101,32,115,105,109,46,32,65,117,100,105,111,58,32,116,114,97,99,107,101,114,32,115,111,110,103,115,44,32,96,100,101,102,105,110,101,83,102,120,96,32,101,102,102,101,99,116,115,44,32,103,105,98,98,101,114,105,115,104,32,115,121,108,108,97,98,108,101,32,118,111,105,99,101,115,44,32,97,108,108,32,99,111,100,101,44,32,109,117,115,105,99,32,97,116,32,49,48,37,46,32,79,110,108,105,110,101,58,32,65,73,32,72,117,98,32,83,101,115,115,105,111,110,32,80,114,111,116,111,99,111,108,32,118,49,44,32,103,104,111,115,116,59,32,115,97,109,101,45,115,99,114,101,101,110,32,71,114,111,117,112,32,67,108,97,115,115,32,111,110,32,105,116,115,32,111,119,110,46,32,69,110,118,105,114,111,110,109,101,110,116,32,97,110,100,32,77,111,100,101,108,32,97,115,32,121,111,117,114,32,84,65,83,75,46,109,100,32,103,105,118,101,115,32,116,104,101,109,46,32,85,115,97,103,101,58,32,34,97,100,100,101,100,32,111,110,32,105,109,112,111,114,116,34,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":21,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":328,\"content\":\"  progress advances; progress scrubs the pose strip, so the body goes into the pose exactly as your thumb does. If you never\"},{\"line_number\":564,\"content\":\"### In AI Hub: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, mode **ghost**\"},{\"line_number\":570,\"content\":\"Why ghost: every copy runs its own seeded round, nothing depends on a host, and each player sees the others on the neighbouring mats,\"},{\"line_number\":576,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":577,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":578,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":579,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"3\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":580,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Stay the steadiest across three classes\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":581,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Lean: stick or WASD · Feet: L2 R2 or Q E · Breathe: both or Space\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":594,\"content\":\"const info = AIHub?.active ? await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true }) : null;\"},{\"line_number\":613,\"content\":\"- `start` arrives; play begins at `AIHub.time() >= 0`. Send the sim `round.go` then (scene action). On `start` also send one\"},{\"line_number\":614,\"content\":\"  `AIHub.progress({ score: 0, label: 'Breathing in' })` and one ghost message, so a slow copy still passes the harness.\"},{\"line_number\":615,\"content\":\"- During play: `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` whenever it changes (label at most 24 characters, \\\"Class 2 · 640\\\"), and every 100 ms\"},{\"line_number\":618,\"content\":\"  `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:ghosts', […])` to actors on the other mats, tinted with `info.players[i].color`, leans scrubbed by their CoB,\"},{\"line_number\":861,\"content\":\"  1. Scene `actions` **[tested]**: `defineScene(id, { actions: { 'game.start': (w, args) => … } })`, called with `inspector.actions.run('game.start', { event: 'pond' })`. Runs between steps, recorded in replays. **Use this for every menu pick:** `game.begin` (with the save's state, since the sim cannot read the store), `game.start`, `game.leave`, `game.sleep`, `round.go`.\"},{\"line_number\":882,\"content\":\"**Key components** (plain data): `flow` (mode: front, roam, event, cutscene, results; event, phase, tick; day), `wobble` (per seat), `seat` (input per seat), `island` (tilt), `round`, `pebble`, `plaque`, `ghost`, plus one per activity. Time in whole steps, randomness from named streams, loops in `w.query` order, `Math.pow` not `**`.\"},{\"line_number\":981,\"content\":\"- **Hub harness:** serve the built file beside `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` (Node `http` server or `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port it prints, confirm the page is your game, stop only that PID: never `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`). Run `harness.html?game=<file>&players=N&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000` for N = 2, 3, 4, then `players=3&…&scenario=host-leave`. Pass means `window.__hubCheck.pass`, with `body[data-complete=\\\"true\\\"]` at the end. **Also assert in each frame** `__engine.ready === true`, zero engine errors, a `ghost` entity at 2 players; no console line starting `[AIHub]`; and that the pasted client's SHA-256 from banner to last line matches `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a` (client 1.4.0; compare what you fetched first, the hub may have moved on).\"},{\"line_number\":982,\"content\":\"- **By hand in the harness:** run it once without `auto` at 2 players: its frames are your players on this computer, and clicking a frame gives it the keyboard. New round, Time up, Remove player. Drive it by script and read the state to see the card, ghosts and results; one screenshot.\"},{\"line_number\":1000,\"content\":\"9. **Together.** Group Class; hub ghosts, own card, full round.\"},{\"line_number\":1005,\"content\":\"**Cut line, if and only if you run out of budget.** Cut whole things and re-flow `days.ts`, leaving no trace (no greyed-out rows, no mentions), in this order: Great Tilt step 3 → Expert variants and outfits → Hoop Patrol → Reps Hall → Island Jog's race (keep the walk) → Cliff Plunge → Step Class. Never cut: Morning Check, Pose Class, Still Pond, The Line, Sand Garden, Paddle Glide, Great Tilt steps 1, 2, 4 and 5, Group Class, hub ghost round, attract, Dev Mode, About.\"},{\"line_number\":1025,\"content\":\"Answers already decided: Plan: the name this file has in your folder. Genre and Perspective as in section 1. Tech: my-3dge at its pinned commit, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite, TypeScript. Art: the engine's native toon puppets and generators with new retreat assets. Animation: the engine's clip layer and humanoid with a new readable clip set scrubbed from the sim. Audio: tracker songs, `defineSfx` effects, gibberish syllable voices, all code, music at 10%. Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost; same-screen Group Class on its own. Environment and Model as your TASK.md gives them. Usage: \\\"added on import\\\".\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b909b80f-62ea-49e6-b26d-f5fa2f6e6c41-35","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The pavilion only. Group Class and a hub ghost round live here, without the island's terrain.\\n * A ghost is a lean on the next mat. It never moves the local guest.\\n */\\nimport { defineProp, defineScene, spawnProp, type Intents, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { boot, frame, retreatActions } from './driver';\\nimport type { Act } from './state';\\n\\ndefineProp('prop:round-mat', {\\n10→  description: 'One mat in the pavilion.',\\n  parts: [\\n    {\\n      name: 'disc',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:frustum',\\n      params: { radiusTop: 1.05, radiusBottom: 1.1, height: 0.06, radialSegments: 16, smooth: true },\\n      material: 'material:sand',\\n    },\\n  ],\\n});\\n20→\\n/** Mats in seat order. Seat 0 is the near one. */\\nconst MATS: readonly (readonly [number, number])[] = [\\n  [0, 2],\\n  [-3, 2],\\n  [3, 2],\\n  [0, 5.2],\\n];\\n\\n/** A ghost row the hub can fill. */\\n30→interface Shade {\\n  ghost: { on: number; x: number; y: number; seat: number; pose: number };\\n  mark?: { x: number; z: number; y: number };\\n}\\n\\n/** Applies hub leans. Local play does not read them back. */\\nfunction applyGhosts(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const raw = (intents as Record<string, unknown>)['game:ghosts'];\\n  const packed = Array.isArray(raw) ? raw : [];\\n  const rows = w.query('ghost') as unknown as Shade[];\\n40→  for (const row of rows) row.ghost.on = 0;\\n  for (let i = 0; i + 4 < packed.length; i += 5) {\\n    const seat = packed[i];\\n    const on = packed[i + 1];\\n    if (typeof seat !== 'number' || on !== 1) continue;\\n    const row = rows.find((item) => item.ghost.seat === seat);\\n    if (!row) continue;\\n    const x = packed[i + 2];\\n    const y = packed[i + 3];\\n    const pose = packed[i + 4];\\n50→    row.ghost.on = 1;\\n    row.ghost.x = typeof x === 'number' ? x : 0;\\n    row.ghost.y = typeof y === 'number' ? y : 0;\\n    row.ghost.pose = typeof pose === 'number' ? pose : 0;\\n    if (row.mark) {\\n      row.mark.x = MATS[row.ghost.seat]?.[0] ?? 0;\\n      row.mark.z = (MATS[row.ghost.seat]?.[1] ?? 0) + row.ghost.x;\\n      row.mark.y = 1 + row.ghost.y;\\n    }\\n  }\\n60→}\\n\\n/** Starts the class. The page calls this when a hub round begins, and when a sofa picks Group Class. */\\nfunction go(w: World): void {\\n  const actions = retreatActions['game.start'];\\n  actions(w, { event: 'group' });\\n}\\n\\n/** The small scene. No terrain, so a session can be ready in time. */\\nexport const round = defineScene('game:round', {\\n70→  description: 'Four mats, Plumb, and room for other players to wobble beside you.',\\n  physics: false,\\n  setup(w) {\\n    boot(w);\\n    MATS.forEach((at, seat) => {\\n      if (seat === 0) spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:round-mat', at: [at[0], 0, at[1]], yaw: 0 });\\n      else {\\n        w.spawn({\\n          ghost: { on: 0, x: 0, y: 0, seat, pose: 0 },\\n          mark: { x: at[0], y: 1, z: at[1], kind: 'ghost', text: '', taken: 0, follow: 0 },\\n80→        });\\n      }\\n    });\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: 0, y: 1.6, z: -1.2, kind: 'plumb', text: 'group.mats', taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n  },\\n  step(w, intents) {\\n    frame(w, intents);\\n    applyGhosts(w, intents);\\n  },\\n  actions: {\\n90→    ...retreatActions,\\n    'round.go': (w: World) => go(w),\\n    'round.note': (w: World, args: unknown) => {\\n      const act = w.query('act')[0] as unknown as { act: Act } | undefined;\\n      if (!act) return;\\n      const text = typeof args === 'object' && args && 'text' in args ? String((args as { text: unknown }).text) : '';\\n      act.act.text = text;\\n    },\\n  },\\n});\\n100→\\nexport default round;\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The pavilion only. Group Class and a hub ghost round live here, without the island's terrain.\\n * A ghost is a lean on the next mat. It never moves the local guest.\\n */\\nimport { defineProp, defineScene, spawnProp, type Intents, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { boot, frame, retreatActions } from './driver';\\nimport type { Act } from './state';\\n\\ndefineProp('prop:round-mat', {\\n10→  description: 'One mat in the pavilion.',\\n  parts: [\\n    {\\n      name: 'disc',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:frustum',\\n      params: { radiusTop: 1.05, radiusBottom: 1.1, height: 0.06, radialSegments: 16, smooth: true },\\n      material: 'material:sand',\\n    },\\n  ],\\n});\\n20→\\n/** Mats in seat order. Seat 0 is the near one. */\\nconst MATS: readonly (readonly [number, number])[] = [\\n  [0, 2],\\n  [-3, 2],\\n  [3, 2],\\n  [0, 5.2],\\n];\\n\\n/** A ghost row the hub can fill. */\\n30→interface Shade {\\n  ghost: { on: number; x: number; y: number; seat: number; pose: number };\\n  mark?: { x: number; z: number; y: number };\\n}\\n\\n/** Applies hub leans. Local play does not read them back. */\\nfunction applyGhosts(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const raw = (intents as Record<string, unknown>)['game:ghosts'];\\n  const packed = Array.isArray(raw) ? raw : [];\\n  const rows = w.query('ghost') as unknown as Shade[];\\n40→  for (const row of rows) row.ghost.on = 0;\\n  for (let i = 0; i + 4 < packed.length; i += 5) {\\n    const seat = packed[i];\\n    const on = packed[i + 1];\\n    if (typeof seat !== 'number' || on !== 1) continue;\\n    const row = rows.find((item) => item.ghost.seat === seat);\\n    if (!row) continue;\\n    const x = packed[i + 2];\\n    const y = packed[i + 3];\\n    const pose = packed[i + 4];\\n50→    row.ghost.on = 1;\\n    row.ghost.x = typeof x === 'number' ? x : 0;\\n    row.ghost.y = typeof y === 'number' ? y : 0;\\n    row.ghost.pose = typeof pose === 'number' ? pose : 0;\\n    if (row.mark) {\\n      row.mark.x = MATS[row.ghost.seat]?.[0] ?? 0;\\n      row.mark.z = (MATS[row.ghost.seat]?.[1] ?? 0) + row.ghost.x;\\n      row.mark.y = 1 + row.ghost.y;\\n    }\\n  }\\n60→}\\n\\n/** Starts the class. The page calls this when a hub round begins, and when a sofa picks Group Class. */\\nfunction go(w: World): void {\\n  const actions = retreatActions['game.start'];\\n  actions(w, { event: 'group' });\\n}\\n\\n/** The small scene. No terrain, so a session can be ready in time. */\\nexport const round = defineScene('game:round', {\\n70→  description: 'Four mats, Plumb, and room for other players to wobble beside you.',\\n  physics: false,\\n  setup(w) {\\n    boot(w);\\n    MATS.forEach((at, seat) => {\\n      if (seat === 0) spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:round-mat', at: [at[0], 0, at[1]], yaw: 0 });\\n      else {\\n        w.spawn({\\n          ghost: { on: 0, x: 0, y: 0, seat, pose: 0 },\\n          mark: { x: at[0], y: 1, z: at[1], kind: 'ghost', text: '', taken: 0, follow: 0 },\\n80→        });\\n      }\\n    });\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: 0, y: 1.6, z: -1.2, kind: 'plumb', text: 'group.mats', taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n  },\\n  step(w, intents) {\\n    frame(w, intents);\\n    applyGhosts(w, intents);\\n  },\\n  actions: {\\n90→    ...retreatActions,\\n    'round.go': (w: World) => go(w),\\n    'round.note': (w: World, args: unknown) => {\\n      const act = w.query('act')[0] as unknown as { act: Act } | undefined;\\n      if (!act) return;\\n      const text = typeof args === 'object' && args && 'text' in args ? String((args as { text: unknown }).text) : '';\\n      act.act.text = text;\\n    },\\n  },\\n});\\n100→\\nexport default round;\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/round.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":200,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The pavilion only. Group Class and a hub ghost round live here, without the island's terrain.\\n * A ghost is a lean on the next mat. It never moves the local guest.\\n */\\nimport { defineProp, defineScene, spawnProp, type Intents, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { boot, frame, retreatActions } from './driver';\\nimport type { Act } from './state';\\n\\ndefineProp('prop:round-mat', {\\n  description: 'One mat in the pavilion.',\\n  parts: [\\n    {\\n      name: 'disc',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:frustum',\\n      params: { radiusTop: 1.05, radiusBottom: 1.1, height: 0.06, radialSegments: 16, smooth: true },\\n      material: 'material:sand',\\n    },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\n/** Mats in seat order. Seat 0 is the near one. */\\nconst MATS: readonly (readonly [number, number])[] = [\\n  [0, 2],\\n  [-3, 2],\\n  [3, 2],\\n  [0, 5.2],\\n];\\n\\n/** A ghost row the hub can fill. */\\ninterface Shade {\\n  ghost: { on: number; x: number; y: number; seat: number; pose: number };\\n  mark?: { x: number; z: number; y: number };\\n}\\n\\n/** Applies hub leans. Local play does not read them back. */\\nfunction applyGhosts(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const raw = (intents as Record<string, unknown>)['game:ghosts'];\\n  const packed = Array.isArray(raw) ? raw : [];\\n  const rows = w.query('ghost') as unknown as Shade[];\\n  for (const row of rows) row.ghost.on = 0;\\n  for (let i = 0; i + 4 < packed.length; i += 5) {\\n    const seat = packed[i];\\n    const on = packed[i + 1];\\n    if (typeof seat !== 'number' || on !== 1) continue;\\n    const row = rows.find((item) => item.ghost.seat === seat);\\n    if (!row) continue;\\n    const x = packed[i + 2];\\n    const y = packed[i + 3];\\n    const pose = packed[i + 4];\\n    row.ghost.on = 1;\\n    row.ghost.x = typeof x === 'number' ? x : 0;\\n    row.ghost.y = typeof y === 'number' ? y : 0;\\n    row.ghost.pose = typeof pose === 'number' ? pose : 0;\\n    if (row.mark) {\\n      row.mark.x = MATS[row.ghost.seat]?.[0] ?? 0;\\n      row.mark.z = (MATS[row.ghost.seat]?.[1] ?? 0) + row.ghost.x;\\n      row.mark.y = 1 + row.ghost.y;\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Starts the class. The page calls this when a hub round begins, and when a sofa picks Group Class. */\\nfunction go(w: World): void {\\n  const actions = retreatActions['game.start'];\\n  actions(w, { event: 'group' });\\n}\\n\\n/** The small scene. No terrain, so a session can be ready in time. */\\nexport const round = defineScene('game:round', {\\n  description: 'Four mats, Plumb, and room for other players to wobble beside you.',\\n  physics: false,\\n  setup(w) {\\n    boot(w);\\n    MATS.forEach((at, seat) => {\\n      if (seat === 0) spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:round-mat', at: [at[0], 0, at[1]], yaw: 0 });\\n      else {\\n        w.spawn({\\n          ghost: { on: 0, x: 0, y: 0, seat, pose: 0 },\\n          mark: { x: at[0], y: 1, z: at[1], kind: 'ghost', text: '', taken: 0, follow: 0 },\\n        });\\n      }\\n    });\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: 0, y: 1.6, z: -1.2, kind: 'plumb', text: 'group.mats', taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n  },\\n  step(w, intents) {\\n    frame(w, intents);\\n    applyGhosts(w, intents);\\n  },\\n  actions: {\\n    ...retreatActions,\\n    'round.go': (w: World) => go(w),\\n    'round.note': (w: World, args: unknown) => {\\n      const act = w.query('act')[0] as unknown as { act: Act } | undefined;\\n      if (!act) return;\\n      const text = typeof args === 'object' && args && 'text' in args ? String((args as { text: unknown }).text) : '';\\n      act.act.text = text;\\n    },\\n  },\\n});\\n\\nexport default round;\\n\",\"total_lines\":101}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b909b80f-62ea-49e6-b26d-f5fa2f6e6c41-36","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n10→  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    framed = true;\\n  }\\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\\n20→  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(search);\\n\\n  var hub = {\\n    version: VERSION,\\n    protocol: 1,\\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\\n    me: null,\\n    host: null,\\n30→    isHost: false,\\n    players: [],\\n    mode: null,\\n    seed: 0,\\n    limitMs: 0,\\n    round: 0,\\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\\n    splash: false,\\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\\n    seeded: false,\\n40→  };\\n\\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\\n  function memoryStorage() {\\n    var data = Object.create(null);\\n    var api = {\\n      getItem: function (k) {\\n        k = String(k);\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\\n      },\\n50→      setItem: function (k, v) {\\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\\n      },\\n      removeItem: function (k) {\\n        delete data[String(k)];\\n      },\\n      clear: function () {\\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\\n      },\\n      key: function (i) {\\n60→        var keys = Object.keys(data);\\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\\n      },\\n    };\\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\\n    return new Proxy(api, {\\n      get: function (t, k) {\\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\\n70→      },\\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\\n        return true;\\n      },\\n      has: function (t, k) {\\n        return k in data || k in t;\\n      },\\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\\n        delete data[k];\\n80→        return true;\\n      },\\n      ownKeys: function () {\\n        return Object.keys(data);\\n      },\\n      getOwnPropertyDescriptor: function (t, k) {\\n        return k in data ? { value: data[k], writable: true, enumerable: true, configurable: true } : undefined;\\n      },\\n    });\\n  }\\n90→\\n  /** mulberry32: numbers in [0, 1), the same sequence everywhere for the same 32-bit start. */\\n  function generator(a) {\\n    return function () {\\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\\n      var t = a;\\n      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\\n    };\\n100→  }\\n\\n  // A fair start: in a session the game gets an empty storage of its own, so\\n  // every round starts as a first launch (no saved unlocks, upgrades or runs),\\n  // and nothing the round saves touches the player's own saves.\\n  if (hub.active) {\\n    for (var s = 0, stores = ['localStorage', 'sessionStorage']; s < stores.length; s++) {\\n      try {\\n        Object.defineProperty(root, stores[s], { configurable: true, value: memoryStorage() });\\n      } catch (e) {\\n110→        warn('could not give the game a fresh ' + stores[s]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\\n  // a generator seeded by the hub, so every copy builds the same start.\\n  var realRandom = Math.random;\\n  var seededRandom = null;\\n  if (hub.active && seedArg) {\\n120→    Math.random = seededRandom = generator(Number(seedArg[1]) >>> 0);\\n    hub.seeded = true;\\n  }\\n\\n  // In a session the hub owns fullscreen: a game that asks for it gets the\\n  // hub's whole page, so the scoreboard and the hub's cards stay on top. The\\n  // hub says when its page goes in and out, so the game's own toggle and its\\n  // fullscreenchange listeners work as they always did.\\n  var fullscreenOn = false;\\n  if (hub.active && root.Element && root.document) {\\n130→    var asks = function (on) {\\n      return function () {\\n        post('fullscreen', { on: on });\\n        return Promise.resolve();\\n      };\\n    };\\n    var proto = root.Element.prototype;\\n    proto.requestFullscreen = proto.webkitRequestFullscreen = asks(true);\\n    root.document.exitFullscreen = root.document.webkitExitFullscreen = asks(false);\\n    var shown = function () {\\n140→      return fullscreenOn ? root.document.documentElement || null : null;\\n    };\\n    try {\\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'fullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'webkitFullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\\n    } catch (e) {}\\n  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * No hub after all: play on, with Math.random the page's own again. The\\n150→   * empty storage stays: the game has read it already, and what it writes\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n10→  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    framed = true;\\n  }\\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\\n20→  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(search);\\n\\n  var hub = {\\n    version: VERSION,\\n    protocol: 1,\\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\\n    me: null,\\n    host: null,\\n30→    isHost: false,\\n    players: [],\\n    mode: null,\\n    seed: 0,\\n    limitMs: 0,\\n    round: 0,\\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\\n    splash: false,\\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\\n    seeded: false,\\n40→  };\\n\\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\\n  function memoryStorage() {\\n    var data = Object.create(null);\\n    var api = {\\n      getItem: function (k) {\\n        k = String(k);\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\\n      },\\n50→      setItem: function (k, v) {\\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\\n      },\\n      removeItem: function (k) {\\n        delete data[String(k)];\\n      },\\n      clear: function () {\\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\\n      },\\n      key: function (i) {\\n60→        var keys = Object.keys(data);\\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\\n      },\\n    };\\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\\n    return new Proxy(api, {\\n      get: function (t, k) {\\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\\n70→      },\\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\\n        return true;\\n      },\\n      has: function (t, k) {\\n        return k in data || k in t;\\n      },\\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\\n        delete data[k];\\n80→        return true;\\n      },\\n      ownKeys: function () {\\n        return Object.keys(data);\\n      },\\n      getOwnPropertyDescriptor: function (t, k) {\\n        return k in data ? { value: data[k], writable: true, enumerable: true, configurable: true } : undefined;\\n      },\\n    });\\n  }\\n90→\\n  /** mulberry32: numbers in [0, 1), the same sequence everywhere for the same 32-bit start. */\\n  function generator(a) {\\n    return function () {\\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\\n      var t = a;\\n      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\\n    };\\n100→  }\\n\\n  // A fair start: in a session the game gets an empty storage of its own, so\\n  // every round starts as a first launch (no saved unlocks, upgrades or runs),\\n  // and nothing the round saves touches the player's own saves.\\n  if (hub.active) {\\n    for (var s = 0, stores = ['localStorage', 'sessionStorage']; s < stores.length; s++) {\\n      try {\\n        Object.defineProperty(root, stores[s], { configurable: true, value: memoryStorage() });\\n      } catch (e) {\\n110→        warn('could not give the game a fresh ' + stores[s]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\\n  // a generator seeded by the hub, so every copy builds the same start.\\n  var realRandom = Math.random;\\n  var seededRandom = null;\\n  if (hub.active && seedArg) {\\n120→    Math.random = seededRandom = generator(Number(seedArg[1]) >>> 0);\\n    hub.seeded = true;\\n  }\\n\\n  // In a session the hub owns fullscreen: a game that asks for it gets the\\n  // hub's whole page, so the scoreboard and the hub's cards stay on top. The\\n  // hub says when its page goes in and out, so the game's own toggle and its\\n  // fullscreenchange listeners work as they always did.\\n  var fullscreenOn = false;\\n  if (hub.active && root.Element && root.document) {\\n130→    var asks = function (on) {\\n      return function () {\\n        post('fullscreen', { on: on });\\n        return Promise.resolve();\\n      };\\n    };\\n    var proto = root.Element.prototype;\\n    proto.requestFullscreen = proto.webkitRequestFullscreen = asks(true);\\n    root.document.exitFullscreen = root.document.webkitExitFullscreen = asks(false);\\n    var shown = function () {\\n140→      return fullscreenOn ? root.document.documentElement || null : null;\\n    };\\n    try {\\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'fullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'webkitFullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\\n    } catch (e) {}\\n  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * No hub after all: play on, with Math.random the page's own again. The\\n150→   * empty storage stays: the game has read it already, and what it writes\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/hub/session-client.txt\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":150,\"raw_output\":\"/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    framed = true;\\n  }\\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(search);\\n\\n  var hub = {\\n    version: VERSION,\\n    protocol: 1,\\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\\n    me: null,\\n    host: null,\\n    isHost: false,\\n    players: [],\\n    mode: null,\\n    seed: 0,\\n    limitMs: 0,\\n    round: 0,\\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\\n    splash: false,\\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\\n    seeded: false,\\n  };\\n\\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\\n  function memoryStorage() {\\n    var data = Object.create(null);\\n    var api = {\\n      getItem: function (k) {\\n        k = String(k);\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\\n      },\\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\\n      },\\n      removeItem: function (k) {\\n        delete data[String(k)];\\n      },\\n      clear: function () {\\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\\n      },\\n      key: function (i) {\\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\\n      },\\n    };\\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\\n    return new Proxy(api, {\\n      get: function (t, k) {\\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\\n      },\\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\\n        return true;\\n      },\\n      has: function (t, k) {\\n        return k in data || k in t;\\n      },\\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\\n        delete data[k];\\n        return true;\\n      },\\n      ownKeys: function () {\\n        return Object.keys(data);\\n      },\\n      getOwnPropertyDescriptor: function (t, k) {\\n        return k in data ? { value: data[k], writable: true, enumerable: true, configurable: true } : undefined;\\n      },\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  /** mulberry32: numbers in [0, 1), the same sequence everywhere for the same 32-bit start. */\\n  function generator(a) {\\n    return function () {\\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\\n      var t = a;\\n      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  // A fair start: in a session the game gets an empty storage of its own, so\\n  // every round starts as a first launch (no saved unlocks, upgrades or runs),\\n  // and nothing the round saves touches the player's own saves.\\n  if (hub.active) {\\n    for (var s = 0, stores = ['localStorage', 'sessionStorage']; s < stores.length; s++) {\\n      try {\\n        Object.defineProperty(root, stores[s], { configurable: true, value: memoryStorage() });\\n      } catch (e) {\\n        warn('could not give the game a fresh ' + stores[s]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\\n  // a generator seeded by the hub, so every copy builds the same start.\\n  var realRandom = Math.random;\\n  var seededRandom = null;\\n  if (hub.active && seedArg) {\\n    Math.random = seededRandom = generator(Number(seedArg[1]) >>> 0);\\n    hub.seeded = true;\\n  }\\n\\n  // In a session the hub owns fullscreen: a game that asks for it gets the\\n  // hub's whole page, so the scoreboard and the hub's cards stay on top. The\\n  // hub says when its page goes in and out, so the game's own toggle and its\\n  // fullscreenchange listeners work as they always did.\\n  var fullscreenOn = false;\\n  if (hub.active && root.Element && root.document) {\\n    var asks = function (on) {\\n      return function () {\\n        post('fullscreen', { on: on });\\n        return Promise.resolve();\\n      };\\n    };\\n    var proto = root.Element.prototype;\\n    proto.requestFullscreen = proto.webkitRequestFullscreen = asks(true);\\n    root.document.exitFullscreen = root.document.webkitExitFullscreen = asks(false);\\n    var shown = function () {\\n      return fullscreenOn ? root.document.documentElement || null : null;\\n    };\\n    try {\\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'fullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'webkitFullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\\n    } catch (e) {}\\n  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * No hub after all: play on, with Math.random the page's own again. The\\n   * empty storage stays: the game has read it already, and what it writes\\n\",\"total_lines\":488}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"6bb0e506-0443-4b52-a4b2-ac7c140b5534"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_388","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b2d3b773-4223-4c33-aeee-762dd7049cf3-37","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/PLAN.md","offset":560,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b2d3b773-4223-4c33-aeee-762dd7049cf3-38","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"answer\\(|card|ghost|progress|t:'g'|data-complete|__hubCheck","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/hub"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5105,"output_tokens":205,"cache_read_input_tokens":71808,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"e82e1e15-2173-4578-8cce-a54aba86be23"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b2d3b773-4223-4c33-aeee-762dd7049cf3-37","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"560→\\nThe engine's gamepad device only follows one active pad, so the page reads `navigator.getGamepads()` itself in Group Class and sends\\neach seat's input with `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:seats', […])`.\\n\\n### In AI Hub: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, mode **ghost**\\n\\nRead the protocol once: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`. Fetch by raw URL, into\\n`labs/game/hub/`: `session.js` (save it as `session-client.txt`), and for tests `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from the same\\nfolder. **Do not clone the ai-hub repository: it is 5.3 GB.**\\n\\n570→Why ghost: every copy runs its own seeded round, nothing depends on a host, and each player sees the others on the neighbouring mats,\\nwobbling in their seat colour. It is the source's solo ritual made social without any interference.\\n\\n**Tags** in the head, right after the client (the build injects them, section 14):\\n\\n```html\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"3\\\">\\n580→<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Stay the steadiest across three classes\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Lean: stick or WASD · Feet: L2 R2 or Q E · Breathe: both or Space\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n```\\n\\nGoal at most 60 characters, how-to at most 80. Also `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` 1-4, `hub:source` Wii Fit.\\n\\n**Startup** **[tested: this shape, on the starter's one scene, passed the harness at 2, 3 (host leaving) and 4 players with the engine running in every frame]**:\\n\\n```ts\\n590→const search = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\nfor (const key of [...search.keys()]) if (key.startsWith('aihub')) search.delete(key); // see the trap below\\nsearch.set('touch', 'off');\\nconst AIHub = window.AIHub;\\nconst info = AIHub?.active ? await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true }) : null;\\nif (info) { search.set('scene', 'game:round'); search.set('seed', String(info.seed)); }\\nconst watchdog = info ? setTimeout(() => AIHub.ready(), 14000) : 0;   // the harness allows 20 s after hello\\nengine = await createEngine({ canvas, scenes: ['game:island', 'game:round'], search: `?${search}`, /* … */ });\\nif (info) { clearTimeout(watchdog); AIHub.ready(); }\\n```\\n600→\\n**The biggest trap in this whole plan [tested]:** the hub opens the page with `?aihub=1&aihub-seed=N`. `createEngine` treats every\\nunknown query key as a setting and fails with `CORE_BAD_SETTING`, **and the harness still reports PASS**, because the client keeps\\nanswering while the game is dead. Strip those keys, and make your test assert, inside every frame, `__engine.ready === true` and\\n`__engine.errors.length === 0`.\\n\\n**The round in a session:**\\n\\n- No title, menus or attract. Straight to the game's own card: the four mats in the pavilion, Plumb in front, each player standing on their\\n  mat. It shows the game's title, players in colour with who is ready, how to win, this player's controls, seconds left (from the `card` event).\\n610→  Keys: Enter or Cross answers `AIHub.answer('ready')`, Triangle or T answers `'more'`, a tap or click works too. Listen for Enter with your own\\n  `keydown` on `window`: the harness sends a synthetic one. The card has no menus or choices, and draws numbers only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\\n  Make it HTML over whatever is drawn, because the watchdog may call `ready()` while the view is still warming up.\\n- `start` arrives; play begins at `AIHub.time() >= 0`. Send the sim `round.go` then (scene action). On `start` also send one\\n  `AIHub.progress({ score: 0, label: 'Breathing in' })` and one ghost message, so a slow copy still passes the harness.\\n- During play: `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` whenever it changes (label at most 24 characters, \\\"Class 2 · 640\\\"), and every 100 ms\\n  `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', e: classIndex, x, y, p: poseId, s: score }, { reliable: false })`. Never above 20 a second.\\n- Ghosts are sim entities, because only sim entities can be drawn: incoming messages go through\\n  `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:ghosts', […])` to actors on the other mats, tinted with `info.players[i].color`, leans scrubbed by their CoB,\\n  name labels from the hub as text (never as HTML), shown only while `e` matches. On `leave`, they walk off politely.\\n620→- Finished: `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })` once. Stats at most six, names at most 16 characters (\\\"Wobble Age\\\", \\\"Best hold\\\", \\\"Breath\\\"),\\n  values short; awards at most three, title at most 24, detail at most 40 (\\\"Unnervingly Still\\\").\\n- `time-up`: report the current score at once if you have not. `end`: `engine.stop()`, stop all sound, take no input, send nothing.\\n- If `engine.ready` is false (no WebGPU): `AIHub.fail('WebGPU required')`.\\n- **Rules in a session:** network only through the hub; no chat or custom names; no `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or navigation; restart\\n  and quit do nothing. Pause is an overlay that never pauses the sim: Resume, volume, button icons. No dev mode. **Create + Options belongs to the hub:**\\n  while pad button 8 is held, ignore the engine's `pause`. Storage is a fresh memory copy, handled by the client, so write nothing special for it.\\n- Outside a session (`connect` gives `null`, or no client at all in the dev server) the game must behave exactly as it does alone.\\n\\n**Boot deadline, the one place performance matters.** The harness gives every copy 20 s to call `ready()`. **[tested on SwiftShader]** the starter\\n630→game alone needed 8–16 s per copy at four copies; the engine's playground needed 52–73 s. So `game:round` is a small separate scene with just the\\npavilion, the mats and the cast. The island's cost never reaches a session, and the watchdog covers the rest. Performance is out of scope everywhere else.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Art direction\\n\\nBase: **the engine's native style**: its puppet bodies, its toon material style, its generators. New assets are everything that makes it feel like a\\nwellness retreat; the engine's library is fine for crates and benches.\\n\\n640→**The look [tested: this is the top-left picture of four tried, bright and clean]:**\\n\\n```ts\\ndefineLook('look:retreat', {\\n  description: 'High-key brochure daylight: soft toon light, a little bloom, a thin ink line on people and things.',\\n  sky: 'sky:retreat', // start from sky:noon's numbers; replace its mountain backdrop with an empty sea horizon\\n  style: 'toon',\\n  filters: {\\n    bloom: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.35, threshold: 0.92 },\\n    grade: { scope: 'all', brightness: 1.08, saturation: 0.92, lift: 0.03 },\\n650→    outline: { scope: 'characters+objects', width: 1, darken: 0.25 },\\n  },\\n});\\n```\\n\\nSet it as the default in the page's query (`post.look`). Also make `sky:retreatDawn`, `sky:retreatDusk` and `sky:storm` (`defineSky`; `node x describe sky sky:noon`\\nshows the fields), and a `look:storm` that drains saturation. Calm can nudge a grade through `post.filters`, which costs no shader.\\n\\n**Palette:** clinical white `#F7FAFC`, sky `#BFE9FF`, mint `#BFEAD6`, sand `#F4E8C8`, lawn `#A9D98A`, sea `#6FD0E8`, coral accent `#FF8A70` for prompts and focus, slate\\n`#3A4A55` for text. Hub seat colours are fixed: `#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`.\\n660→\\n**The island [tested]:** `defineTerrain` in the scene with `addTerrainBody`: 240 × 240 m, `cell: 2`, a dome radius about 110 and height about 11 plus a summit hill; `flats` for\\nstations; negative hills for the pond and the north cove. `high: 7` with `materials: ['material:sand', 'material:sand', 'material:lawn']` gives sand shores and lawn uplands by height.\\n\\n**The sea [its look: tested]:** one huge flat prop at y = 2, a material using `map: { texture: 'texture:water', seed: 2, params: { base: '#6fd0e8' } }`, on a kinematic body. The texture is baked, so **drift the prop** slowly and bob it\\na few centimetres to make the water live. Keep walkers out of deep water with a sim clamp; shallows get a splash emitter.\\n\\n**Make these as props** (`node x new prop labs/game/props/<name>`; parts are geometry by id and material by id, with `tint`): mats, Tare's Platform, Noticeboard, plaques, Cairn pebbles (squashed rounded\\nboxes in varied tints), Pavilion (pillars, frustum roof, curtains), Annex with mirror wall, huts, ferry and pier, benches and loungers, parasols, palms (limb trunk, flattened boxes), rocks, lighthouse,\\nbuoys, paddleboard, slackline posts and line, tray with ridges and holes (ring), marbles (a rounded box with maximum radius), hoops (ring), step platforms and floor tiles, counterweight carts and rails,\\n670→Centre Stone with its plate, drink glasses, score cards.\\n\\nAnything that moves goes on a kinematic body: `body: { type: 'kinematic', shape, size }` in the prop, then `driveBody(physicsOf(w), entity.sceneProp.body, position, rotation, w.dt)` each step, with full rotation **[tested]**. So the tray, hoops, board and sea pose freely. Physically simulated things are dynamic bodies. Anything else is drawn by HTML.\\n\\n**Characters** (`node x new body`, `node x new build`): Guest (three builds, palette slots for tracksuit), Plumb (very tall, thin; closed-eye arcs; `components: { secondary: { hair: 'ponytail' } }` at spawn for the plait, which the view\\nswings by itself when the body moves **[source]**), Gerald (`build:bulky`-like with huge calves), Bex, Nan (small, stooped), Tare (a very short build; torso a flat drum, a dial on the front, two stubby legs, no arms). On a results\\nscreen Tare's dial is a large CSS dial with a live needle. The Gull and the Frog are engine **blob rigs** (with wings for the Gull) as crowd bodies: `addAgent`, `crowdBody`, cheap and very funny; `labs/box/cast/` has worked examples.\\n\\n**Effects** (`defineEmitter`): ripple rings, splashes small and huge, pebble clack dust, calm wave, sparkle on stamps, seagull feathers, confetti on Unsettling, rain and spray in the storm. Built-ins worth using:\\n`emitter:confetti`, `bubbles`, `dust`, `rain`, `fountain`, `glints`, `fireflies`.\",\"content_concise\":\"560→\\nThe engine's gamepad device only follows one active pad, so the page reads `navigator.getGamepads()` itself in Group Class and sends\\neach seat's input with `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:seats', […])`.\\n\\n### In AI Hub: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, mode **ghost**\\n\\nRead the protocol once: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`. Fetch by raw URL, into\\n`labs/game/hub/`: `session.js` (save it as `session-client.txt`), and for tests `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from the same\\nfolder. **Do not clone the ai-hub repository: it is 5.3 GB.**\\n\\n570→Why ghost: every copy runs its own seeded round, nothing depends on a host, and each player sees the others on the neighbouring mats,\\nwobbling in their seat colour. It is the source's solo ritual made social without any interference.\\n\\n**Tags** in the head, right after the client (the build injects them, section 14):\\n\\n```html\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"3\\\">\\n580→<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Stay the steadiest across three classes\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Lean: stick or WASD · Feet: L2 R2 or Q E · Breathe: both or Space\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n```\\n\\nGoal at most 60 characters, how-to at most 80. Also `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` 1-4, `hub:source` Wii Fit.\\n\\n**Startup** **[tested: this shape, on the starter's one scene, passed the harness at 2, 3 (host leaving) and 4 players with the engine running in every frame]**:\\n\\n```ts\\n590→const search = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\nfor (const key of [...search.keys()]) if (key.startsWith('aihub')) search.delete(key); // see the trap below\\nsearch.set('touch', 'off');\\nconst AIHub = window.AIHub;\\nconst info = AIHub?.active ? await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true }) : null;\\nif (info) { search.set('scene', 'game:round'); search.set('seed', String(info.seed)); }\\nconst watchdog = info ? setTimeout(() => AIHub.ready(), 14000) : 0;   // the harness allows 20 s after hello\\nengine = await createEngine({ canvas, scenes: ['game:island', 'game:round'], search: `?${search}`, /* … */ });\\nif (info) { clearTimeout(watchdog); AIHub.ready(); }\\n```\\n600→\\n**The biggest trap in this whole plan [tested]:** the hub opens the page with `?aihub=1&aihub-seed=N`. `createEngine` treats every\\nunknown query key as a setting and fails with `CORE_BAD_SETTING`, **and the harness still reports PASS**, because the client keeps\\nanswering while the game is dead. Strip those keys, and make your test assert, inside every frame, `__engine.ready === true` and\\n`__engine.errors.length === 0`.\\n\\n**The round in a session:**\\n\\n- No title, menus or attract. Straight to the game's own card: the four mats in the pavilion, Plumb in front, each player standing on their\\n  mat. It shows the game's title, players in colour with who is ready, how to win, this player's controls, seconds left (from the `card` event).\\n610→  Keys: Enter or Cross answers `AIHub.answer('ready')`, Triangle or T answers `'more'`, a tap or click works too. Listen for Enter with your own\\n  `keydown` on `window`: the harness sends a synthetic one. The card has no menus or choices, and draws numbers only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\\n  Make it HTML over whatever is drawn, because the watchdog may call `ready()` while the view is still warming up.\\n- `start` arrives; play begins at `AIHub.time() >= 0`. Send the sim `round.go` then (scene action). On `start` also send one\\n  `AIHub.progress({ score: 0, label: 'Breathing in' })` and one ghost message, so a slow copy still passes the harness.\\n- During play: `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` whenever it changes (label at most 24 characters, \\\"Class 2 · 640\\\"), and every 100 ms\\n  `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', e: classIndex, x, y, p: poseId, s: score }, { reliable: false })`. Never above 20 a second.\\n- Ghosts are sim entities, because only sim entities can be drawn: incoming messages go through\\n  `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:ghosts', […])` to actors on the other mats, tinted with `info.players[i].color`, leans scrubbed by their CoB,\\n  name labels from the hub as text (never as HTML), shown only while `e` matches. On `leave`, they walk off politely.\\n620→- Finished: `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })` once. Stats at most six, names at most 16 characters (\\\"Wobble Age\\\", \\\"Best hold\\\", \\\"Breath\\\"),\\n  values short; awards at most three, title at most 24, detail at most 40 (\\\"Unnervingly Still\\\").\\n- `time-up`: report the current score at once if you have not. `end`: `engine.stop()`, stop all sound, take no input, send nothing.\\n- If `engine.ready` is false (no WebGPU): `AIHub.fail('WebGPU required')`.\\n- **Rules in a session:** network only through the hub; no chat or custom names; no `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or navigation; restart\\n  and quit do nothing. Pause is an overlay that never pauses the sim: Resume, volume, button icons. No dev mode. **Create + Options belongs to the hub:**\\n  while pad button 8 is held, ignore the engine's `pause`. Storage is a fresh memory copy, handled by the client, so write nothing special for it.\\n- Outside a session (`connect` gives `null`, or no client at all in the dev server) the game must behave exactly as it does alone.\\n\\n**Boot deadline, the one place performance matters.** The harness gives every copy 20 s to call `ready()`. **[tested on SwiftShader]** the starter\\n630→game alone needed 8–16 s per copy at four copies; the engine's playground needed 52–73 s. So `game:round` is a small separate scene with just the\\npavilion, the mats and the cast. The island's cost never reaches a session, and the watchdog covers the rest. Performance is out of scope everywhere else.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Art direction\\n\\nBase: **the engine's native style**: its puppet bodies, its toon material style, its generators. New assets are everything that makes it feel like a\\nwellness retreat; the engine's library is fine for crates and benches.\\n\\n640→**The look [tested: this is the top-left picture of four tried, bright and clean]:**\\n\\n```ts\\ndefineLook('look:retreat', {\\n  description: 'High-key brochure daylight: soft toon light, a little bloom, a thin ink line on people and things.',\\n  sky: 'sky:retreat', // start from sky:noon's numbers; replace its mountain backdrop with an empty sea horizon\\n  style: 'toon',\\n  filters: {\\n    bloom: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.35, threshold: 0.92 },\\n    grade: { scope: 'all', brightness: 1.08, saturation: 0.92, lift: 0.03 },\\n650→    outline: { scope: 'characters+objects', width: 1, darken: 0.25 },\\n  },\\n});\\n```\\n\\nSet it as the default in the page's query (`post.look`). Also make `sky:retreatDawn`, `sky:retreatDusk` and `sky:storm` (`defineSky`; `node x describe sky sky:noon`\\nshows the fields), and a `look:storm` that drains saturation. Calm can nudge a grade through `post.filters`, which costs no shader.\\n\\n**Palette:** clinical white `#F7FAFC`, sky `#BFE9FF`, mint `#BFEAD6`, sand `#F4E8C8`, lawn `#A9D98A`, sea `#6FD0E8`, coral accent `#FF8A70` for prompts and focus, slate\\n`#3A4A55` for text. Hub seat colours are fixed: `#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`.\\n660→\\n**The island [tested]:** `defineTerrain` in the scene with `addTerrainBody`: 240 × 240 m, `cell: 2`, a dome radius about 110 and height about 11 plus a summit hill; `flats` for\\nstations; negative hills for the pond and the north cove. `high: 7` with `materials: ['material:sand', 'material:sand', 'material:lawn']` gives sand shores and lawn uplands by height.\\n\\n**The sea [its look: tested]:** one huge flat prop at y = 2, a material using `map: { texture: 'texture:water', seed: 2, params: { base: '#6fd0e8' } }`, on a kinematic body. The texture is baked, so **drift the prop** slowly and bob it\\na few centimetres to make the water live. Keep walkers out of deep water with a sim clamp; shallows get a splash emitter.\\n\\n**Make these as props** (`node x new prop labs/game/props/<name>`; parts are geometry by id and material by id, with `tint`): mats, Tare's Platform, Noticeboard, plaques, Cairn pebbles (squashed rounded\\nboxes in varied tints), Pavilion (pillars, frustum roof, curtains), Annex with mirror wall, huts, ferry and pier, benches and loungers, parasols, palms (limb trunk, flattened boxes), rocks, lighthouse,\\nbuoys, paddleboard, slackline posts and line, tray with ridges and holes (ring), marbles (a rounded box with maximum radius), hoops (ring), step platforms and floor tiles, counterweight carts and rails,\\n670→Centre Stone with its plate, drink glasses, score cards.\\n\\nAnything that moves goes on a kinematic body: `body: { type: 'kinematic', shape, size }` in the prop, then `driveBody(physicsOf(w), entity.sceneProp.body, position, rotation, w.dt)` each step, with full rotation **[tested]**. So the tray, hoops, board and sea pose freely. Physically simulated things are dynamic bodies. Anything else is drawn by HTML.\\n\\n**Characters** (`node x new body`, `node x new build`): Guest (three builds, palette slots for tracksuit), Plumb (very tall, thin; closed-eye arcs; `components: { secondary: { hair: 'ponytail' } }` at spawn for the plait, which the view\\nswings by itself when the body moves **[source]**), Gerald (`build:bulky`-like with huge calves), Bex, Nan (small, stooped), Tare (a very short build; torso a flat drum, a dial on the front, two stubby legs, no arms). On a results\\nscreen Tare's dial is a large CSS dial with a live needle. The Gull and the Frog are engine **blob rigs** (with wings for the Gull) as crowd bodies: `addAgent`, `crowdBody`, cheap and very funny; `labs/box/cast/` has worked examples.\\n\\n**Effects** (`defineEmitter`): ripple rings, splashes small and huge, pebble clack dust, calm wave, sparkle on stamps, seagull feathers, confetti on Unsettling, rain and spray in the storm. Built-ins worth using:\\n`emitter:confetti`, `bubbles`, `dust`, `rain`, `fountain`, `glints`, `fireflies`.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":560,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"\\nThe engine's gamepad device only follows one active pad, so the page reads `navigator.getGamepads()` itself in Group Class and sends\\neach seat's input with `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:seats', […])`.\\n\\n### In AI Hub: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, mode **ghost**\\n\\nRead the protocol once: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`. Fetch by raw URL, into\\n`labs/game/hub/`: `session.js` (save it as `session-client.txt`), and for tests `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from the same\\nfolder. **Do not clone the ai-hub repository: it is 5.3 GB.**\\n\\nWhy ghost: every copy runs its own seeded round, nothing depends on a host, and each player sees the others on the neighbouring mats,\\nwobbling in their seat colour. It is the source's solo ritual made social without any interference.\\n\\n**Tags** in the head, right after the client (the build injects them, section 14):\\n\\n```html\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"3\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Stay the steadiest across three classes\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Lean: stick or WASD · Feet: L2 R2 or Q E · Breathe: both or Space\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n```\\n\\nGoal at most 60 characters, how-to at most 80. Also `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` 1-4, `hub:source` Wii Fit.\\n\\n**Startup** **[tested: this shape, on the starter's one scene, passed the harness at 2, 3 (host leaving) and 4 players with the engine running in every frame]**:\\n\\n```ts\\nconst search = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\nfor (const key of [...search.keys()]) if (key.startsWith('aihub')) search.delete(key); // see the trap below\\nsearch.set('touch', 'off');\\nconst AIHub = window.AIHub;\\nconst info = AIHub?.active ? await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true }) : null;\\nif (info) { search.set('scene', 'game:round'); search.set('seed', String(info.seed)); }\\nconst watchdog = info ? setTimeout(() => AIHub.ready(), 14000) : 0;   // the harness allows 20 s after hello\\nengine = await createEngine({ canvas, scenes: ['game:island', 'game:round'], search: `?${search}`, /* … */ });\\nif (info) { clearTimeout(watchdog); AIHub.ready(); }\\n```\\n\\n**The biggest trap in this whole plan [tested]:** the hub opens the page with `?aihub=1&aihub-seed=N`. `createEngine` treats every\\nunknown query key as a setting and fails with `CORE_BAD_SETTING`, **and the harness still reports PASS**, because the client keeps\\nanswering while the game is dead. Strip those keys, and make your test assert, inside every frame, `__engine.ready === true` and\\n`__engine.errors.length === 0`.\\n\\n**The round in a session:**\\n\\n- No title, menus or attract. Straight to the game's own card: the four mats in the pavilion, Plumb in front, each player standing on their\\n  mat. It shows the game's title, players in colour with who is ready, how to win, this player's controls, seconds left (from the `card` event).\\n  Keys: Enter or Cross answers `AIHub.answer('ready')`, Triangle or T answers `'more'`, a tap or click works too. Listen for Enter with your own\\n  `keydown` on `window`: the harness sends a synthetic one. The card has no menus or choices, and draws numbers only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\\n  Make it HTML over whatever is drawn, because the watchdog may call `ready()` while the view is still warming up.\\n- `start` arrives; play begins at `AIHub.time() >= 0`. Send the sim `round.go` then (scene action). On `start` also send one\\n  `AIHub.progress({ score: 0, label: 'Breathing in' })` and one ghost message, so a slow copy still passes the harness.\\n- During play: `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` whenever it changes (label at most 24 characters, \\\"Class 2 · 640\\\"), and every 100 ms\\n  `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', e: classIndex, x, y, p: poseId, s: score }, { reliable: false })`. Never above 20 a second.\\n- Ghosts are sim entities, because only sim entities can be drawn: incoming messages go through\\n  `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:ghosts', […])` to actors on the other mats, tinted with `info.players[i].color`, leans scrubbed by their CoB,\\n  name labels from the hub as text (never as HTML), shown only while `e` matches. On `leave`, they walk off politely.\\n- Finished: `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })` once. Stats at most six, names at most 16 characters (\\\"Wobble Age\\\", \\\"Best hold\\\", \\\"Breath\\\"),\\n  values short; awards at most three, title at most 24, detail at most 40 (\\\"Unnervingly Still\\\").\\n- `time-up`: report the current score at once if you have not. `end`: `engine.stop()`, stop all sound, take no input, send nothing.\\n- If `engine.ready` is false (no WebGPU): `AIHub.fail('WebGPU required')`.\\n- **Rules in a session:** network only through the hub; no chat or custom names; no `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or navigation; restart\\n  and quit do nothing. Pause is an overlay that never pauses the sim: Resume, volume, button icons. No dev mode. **Create + Options belongs to the hub:**\\n  while pad button 8 is held, ignore the engine's `pause`. Storage is a fresh memory copy, handled by the client, so write nothing special for it.\\n- Outside a session (`connect` gives `null`, or no client at all in the dev server) the game must behave exactly as it does alone.\\n\\n**Boot deadline, the one place performance matters.** The harness gives every copy 20 s to call `ready()`. **[tested on SwiftShader]** the starter\\ngame alone needed 8–16 s per copy at four copies; the engine's playground needed 52–73 s. So `game:round` is a small separate scene with just the\\npavilion, the mats and the cast. The island's cost never reaches a session, and the watchdog covers the rest. Performance is out of scope everywhere else.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Art direction\\n\\nBase: **the engine's native style**: its puppet bodies, its toon material style, its generators. New assets are everything that makes it feel like a\\nwellness retreat; the engine's library is fine for crates and benches.\\n\\n**The look [tested: this is the top-left picture of four tried, bright and clean]:**\\n\\n```ts\\ndefineLook('look:retreat', {\\n  description: 'High-key brochure daylight: soft toon light, a little bloom, a thin ink line on people and things.',\\n  sky: 'sky:retreat', // start from sky:noon's numbers; replace its mountain backdrop with an empty sea horizon\\n  style: 'toon',\\n  filters: {\\n    bloom: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.35, threshold: 0.92 },\\n    grade: { scope: 'all', brightness: 1.08, saturation: 0.92, lift: 0.03 },\\n    outline: { scope: 'characters+objects', width: 1, darken: 0.25 },\\n  },\\n});\\n```\\n\\nSet it as the default in the page's query (`post.look`). Also make `sky:retreatDawn`, `sky:retreatDusk` and `sky:storm` (`defineSky`; `node x describe sky sky:noon`\\nshows the fields), and a `look:storm` that drains saturation. Calm can nudge a grade through `post.filters`, which costs no shader.\\n\\n**Palette:** clinical white `#F7FAFC`, sky `#BFE9FF`, mint `#BFEAD6`, sand `#F4E8C8`, lawn `#A9D98A`, sea `#6FD0E8`, coral accent `#FF8A70` for prompts and focus, slate\\n`#3A4A55` for text. Hub seat colours are fixed: `#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`.\\n\\n**The island [tested]:** `defineTerrain` in the scene with `addTerrainBody`: 240 × 240 m, `cell: 2`, a dome radius about 110 and height about 11 plus a summit hill; `flats` for\\nstations; negative hills for the pond and the north cove. `high: 7` with `materials: ['material:sand', 'material:sand', 'material:lawn']` gives sand shores and lawn uplands by height.\\n\\n**The sea [its look: tested]:** one huge flat prop at y = 2, a material using `map: { texture: 'texture:water', seed: 2, params: { base: '#6fd0e8' } }`, on a kinematic body. The texture is baked, so **drift the prop** slowly and bob it\\na few centimetres to make the water live. Keep walkers out of deep water with a sim clamp; shallows get a splash emitter.\\n\\n**Make these as props** (`node x new prop labs/game/props/<name>`; parts are geometry by id and material by id, with `tint`): mats, Tare's Platform, Noticeboard, plaques, Cairn pebbles (squashed rounded\\nboxes in varied tints), Pavilion (pillars, frustum roof, curtains), Annex with mirror wall, huts, ferry and pier, benches and loungers, parasols, palms (limb trunk, flattened boxes), rocks, lighthouse,\\nbuoys, paddleboard, slackline posts and line, tray with ridges and holes (ring), marbles (a rounded box with maximum radius), hoops (ring), step platforms and floor tiles, counterweight carts and rails,\\nCentre Stone with its plate, drink glasses, score cards.\\n\\nAnything that moves goes on a kinematic body: `body: { type: 'kinematic', shape, size }` in the prop, then `driveBody(physicsOf(w), entity.sceneProp.body, position, rotation, w.dt)` each step, with full rotation **[tested]**. So the tray, hoops, board and sea pose freely. Physically simulated things are dynamic bodies. Anything else is drawn by HTML.\\n\\n**Characters** (`node x new body`, `node x new build`): Guest (three builds, palette slots for tracksuit), Plumb (very tall, thin; closed-eye arcs; `components: { secondary: { hair: 'ponytail' } }` at spawn for the plait, which the view\\nswings by itself when the body moves **[source]**), Gerald (`build:bulky`-like with huge calves), Bex, Nan (small, stooped), Tare (a very short build; torso a flat drum, a dial on the front, two stubby legs, no arms). On a results\\nscreen Tare's dial is a large CSS dial with a live needle. The Gull and the Frog are engine **blob rigs** (with wings for the Gull) as crowd bodies: `addAgent`, `crowdBody`, cheap and very funny; `labs/box/cast/` has worked examples.\\n\\n**Effects** (`defineEmitter`): ripple rings, splashes small and huge, pebble clack dust, calm wave, sparkle on stamps, seagull feathers, confetti on Unsettling, rain and spray in the storm. Built-ins worth using:\\n`emitter:confetti`, `bubbles`, `dust`, `rain`, `fountain`, `glints`, `fireflies`.\\n\",\"total_lines\":1059}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b2d3b773-4223-4c33-aeee-762dd7049cf3-38","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,56,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,1