l` or `playwright install-deps`.\\n- The system Python has Playwright and nothing else. For one (Pillow, numpy …), use uv: `uv run --with pillow python script.py`, adding `--with playwright==1.63.0` when the script drives a browser too (a newer Playwright can't find the browsers here).\\n\\n## Goal\\n\\nBuild an original game inspired by the source.\\n\\nScope\\n\\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\\n\\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\\n\\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\\n\\nMultiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\\n\\nNarrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\\n\\n## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\\nDesign the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\\n\\nDo not use overly dense, web-style data screens.\\n\\nTouch-only devices: no touch controls; show \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\\n\\n## Done\\nNo TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\\n\\n## Source Information\\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:36:56\\n- Source: the work it's based on\\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\\n- Art Direction: style used\\n- Animation: system used\\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\\n- Online: network features used, or none\\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\\n- Research: research done, or none\\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\n- Usage: write \\\"added on import\\\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\\n\\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\\n{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\\"date\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"plan\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"genre\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"tech\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"animation\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"audio\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"online\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"testing\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"research\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"environment\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"model\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"},\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"the game's title, as on its title screen\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"a few words to go under the title\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"one or two sentences for the catalogue\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game, Tech demo or Tool\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"the controls, in one line\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\\n\\nTesting Feedback\\n\\n- How many issues did testing catch?\\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\\n\\nEngine Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about the engine?\\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\\n\\nPrompt Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\\n- What was confusing?\\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\\n- What would you change in this prompt?\\n\",\"total_lines\":151}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-470d8887-b30e-4077-b754-ab53d55009f4-47","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The words shared by the About screen and exit-interview.json.\\n * Each answer is at most two short sentences. The source name appears only in the source fields.\\n */\\nexport const SOURCE = {\\n  date: '2026-11-04 22:36:56',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n10→  perspective: 'third-person',\\n  tech: 'my-3dge at e7a1243, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite 7.3, TypeScript.',\\n  artDirection: 'The engine toon style, with a bright lawn, sand shore, and a flat sea.',\\n  animation: 'The engine clip layer. Original poses are scrubbed from the balance step. The rest pose is Mesh2Motion.',\\n  audio: 'Tracker songs, code-made effects, and gibberish syllable voices. A fresh save plays music at a tenth.',\\n  online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, and same-screen Group Class on its own.',\\n  testing: 'Bot bands on ten seeds, a three-seed walk to the credits, and browser checks of the built file.',\\n  research: 'none',\\n  environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\\n  model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\\n20→  usage: 'added on import',\\n} as const;\\n\\n/** Testing Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const TESTING = [\\n  'Testing caught eight issues before hand-in. They were score bands, a NaN prop yaw, a missing boot setting, over-long lines, and a ghost pack read at the wrong offset.',\\n  'Four were critical. Three activities scored under their band, and the island would not boot.',\\n  'The most helpful test was the four bot bands on ten seeds for every shipped activity.',\\n  'The least helpful was a headless screenshot. The canvas can be blank while the sim state is fine.',\\n] as const;\\n30→\\n/** Engine Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const ENGINE = [\\n  'Scene actions, live settings, and a headless world you can step made the week testable without a browser.',\\n  'I got stuck on playClip during setup, props that need a yaw, a frozen recorded world, and hub query keys read as settings.',\\n  'The balance step, the day director, the songs, and the syllable voices are the game’s own.',\\n  'The hardest part was keeping the pavilion small enough for the hub ready deadline while the island stayed a place.',\\n  'None. The engine files were not changed.',\\n  'I would let a page add a mesh, and I would start the music bus at a tenth instead of a half.',\\n] as const;\\n40→\\n/** Prompt Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const PROMPT = [\\n  'The acceptance numbers, the cut line, and the bot bands made the scope checkable.',\\n  'The group score is described as a sum to 3000 and also has to fit a rank from 0 to 1000. Several seed lines are longer than two sentences.',\\n  'The hardest part was one HTML file that is a full retreat and also a ghost session the harness can drive.',\\n  'I would state the group score once, and pin the session client hash to the file the plan says to fetch.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Credits shown under the same About screen. */\\n50→export const CREDITS = [\\n  'my-3dge, MIT.',\\n  'three.js r182, MIT.',\\n  'Rapier 0.21, Apache-2.0.',\\n  '@stdlib, Apache-2.0.',\\n  'AI Hub session client 1.4.0, pasted unmodified.',\\n  'The rest pose follows Mesh2Motion. The pose clips themselves are original.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Catalogue fields. The source name is only here and in SOURCE.source. */\\n60→export const AI_HUB = {\\n  name: 'Thumb Yoga',\\n  tagline: 'A week of balance at Little Fulcrum',\\n  description: 'Stand on the disc and keep the dot near the middle. Little Fulcrum runs five days of pose, pond, water, sand, and a storm.',\\n  type: 'Game',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  series: '',\\n  players: '1–4',\\n  controls: 'Lean with the left stick, WASD or the mouse. L2 and R2, or Q and E, are the feet. Both feet or Space breathe.',\\n70→  tags: ['3d', 'sports', 'third-person', 'comedy', 'co-op'],\\n} as const;\\n\\n/** The exit-interview object. The screen and the file both read this. */\\nexport const EXIT = {\\n  sourceInformation: SOURCE,\\n  testingFeedback: [...TESTING],\\n  engineFeedback: [...ENGINE],\\n  promptFeedback: [...PROMPT],\\n  aiHub: AI_HUB,\\n80→};\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The words shared by the About screen and exit-interview.json.\\n * Each answer is at most two short sentences. The source name appears only in the source fields.\\n */\\nexport const SOURCE = {\\n  date: '2026-11-04 22:36:56',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n10→  perspective: 'third-person',\\n  tech: 'my-3dge at e7a1243, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite 7.3, TypeScript.',\\n  artDirection: 'The engine toon style, with a bright lawn, sand shore, and a flat sea.',\\n  animation: 'The engine clip layer. Original poses are scrubbed from the balance step. The rest pose is Mesh2Motion.',\\n  audio: 'Tracker songs, code-made effects, and gibberish syllable voices. A fresh save plays music at a tenth.',\\n  online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, and same-screen Group Class on its own.',\\n  testing: 'Bot bands on ten seeds, a three-seed walk to the credits, and browser checks of the built file.',\\n  research: 'none',\\n  environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\\n  model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\\n20→  usage: 'added on import',\\n} as const;\\n\\n/** Testing Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const TESTING = [\\n  'Testing caught eight issues before hand-in. They were score bands, a NaN prop yaw, a missing boot setting, over-long lines, and a ghost pack read at the wrong offset.',\\n  'Four were critical. Three activities scored under their band, and the island would not boot.',\\n  'The most helpful test was the four bot bands on ten seeds for every shipped activity.',\\n  'The least helpful was a headless screenshot. The canvas can be blank while the sim state is fine.',\\n] as const;\\n30→\\n/** Engine Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const ENGINE = [\\n  'Scene actions, live settings, and a headless world you can step made the week testable without a browser.',\\n  'I got stuck on playClip during setup, props that need a yaw, a frozen recorded world, and hub query keys read as settings.',\\n  'The balance step, the day director, the songs, and the syllable voices are the game’s own.',\\n  'The hardest part was keeping the pavilion small enough for the hub ready deadline while the island stayed a place.',\\n  'None. The engine files were not changed.',\\n  'I would let a page add a mesh, and I would start the music bus at a tenth instead of a half.',\\n] as const;\\n40→\\n/** Prompt Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const PROMPT = [\\n  'The acceptance numbers, the cut line, and the bot bands made the scope checkable.',\\n  'The group score is described as a sum to 3000 and also has to fit a rank from 0 to 1000. Several seed lines are longer than two sentences.',\\n  'The hardest part was one HTML file that is a full retreat and also a ghost session the harness can drive.',\\n  'I would state the group score once, and pin the session client hash to the file the plan says to fetch.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Credits shown under the same About screen. */\\n50→export const CREDITS = [\\n  'my-3dge, MIT.',\\n  'three.js r182, MIT.',\\n  'Rapier 0.21, Apache-2.0.',\\n  '@stdlib, Apache-2.0.',\\n  'AI Hub session client 1.4.0, pasted unmodified.',\\n  'The rest pose follows Mesh2Motion. The pose clips themselves are original.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Catalogue fields. The source name is only here and in SOURCE.source. */\\n60→export const AI_HUB = {\\n  name: 'Thumb Yoga',\\n  tagline: 'A week of balance at Little Fulcrum',\\n  description: 'Stand on the disc and keep the dot near the middle. Little Fulcrum runs five days of pose, pond, water, sand, and a storm.',\\n  type: 'Game',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  series: '',\\n  players: '1–4',\\n  controls: 'Lean with the left stick, WASD or the mouse. L2 and R2, or Q and E, are the feet. Both feet or Space breathe.',\\n70→  tags: ['3d', 'sports', 'third-person', 'comedy', 'co-op'],\\n} as const;\\n\\n/** The exit-interview object. The screen and the file both read this. */\\nexport const EXIT = {\\n  sourceInformation: SOURCE,\\n  testingFeedback: [...TESTING],\\n  engineFeedback: [...ENGINE],\\n  promptFeedback: [...PROMPT],\\n  aiHub: AI_HUB,\\n80→};\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/about-data.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The words shared by the About screen and exit-interview.json.\\n * Each answer is at most two short sentences. The source name appears only in the source fields.\\n */\\nexport const SOURCE = {\\n  date: '2026-11-04 22:36:56',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n  perspective: 'third-person',\\n  tech: 'my-3dge at e7a1243, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite 7.3, TypeScript.',\\n  artDirection: 'The engine toon style, with a bright lawn, sand shore, and a flat sea.',\\n  animation: 'The engine clip layer. Original poses are scrubbed from the balance step. The rest pose is Mesh2Motion.',\\n  audio: 'Tracker songs, code-made effects, and gibberish syllable voices. A fresh save plays music at a tenth.',\\n  online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, and same-screen Group Class on its own.',\\n  testing: 'Bot bands on ten seeds, a three-seed walk to the credits, and browser checks of the built file.',\\n  research: 'none',\\n  environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\\n  model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\\n  usage: 'added on import',\\n} as const;\\n\\n/** Testing Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const TESTING = [\\n  'Testing caught eight issues before hand-in. They were score bands, a NaN prop yaw, a missing boot setting, over-long lines, and a ghost pack read at the wrong offset.',\\n  'Four were critical. Three activities scored under their band, and the island would not boot.',\\n  'The most helpful test was the four bot bands on ten seeds for every shipped activity.',\\n  'The least helpful was a headless screenshot. The canvas can be blank while the sim state is fine.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Engine Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const ENGINE = [\\n  'Scene actions, live settings, and a headless world you can step made the week testable without a browser.',\\n  'I got stuck on playClip during setup, props that need a yaw, a frozen recorded world, and hub query keys read as settings.',\\n  'The balance step, the day director, the songs, and the syllable voices are the game’s own.',\\n  'The hardest part was keeping the pavilion small enough for the hub ready deadline while the island stayed a place.',\\n  'None. The engine files were not changed.',\\n  'I would let a page add a mesh, and I would start the music bus at a tenth instead of a half.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Prompt Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const PROMPT = [\\n  'The acceptance numbers, the cut line, and the bot bands made the scope checkable.',\\n  'The group score is described as a sum to 3000 and also has to fit a rank from 0 to 1000. Several seed lines are longer than two sentences.',\\n  'The hardest part was one HTML file that is a full retreat and also a ghost session the harness can drive.',\\n  'I would state the group score once, and pin the session client hash to the file the plan says to fetch.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Credits shown under the same About screen. */\\nexport const CREDITS = [\\n  'my-3dge, MIT.',\\n  'three.js r182, MIT.',\\n  'Rapier 0.21, Apache-2.0.',\\n  '@stdlib, Apache-2.0.',\\n  'AI Hub session client 1.4.0, pasted unmodified.',\\n  'The rest pose follows Mesh2Motion. The pose clips themselves are original.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Catalogue fields. The source name is only here and in SOURCE.source. */\\nexport const AI_HUB = {\\n  name: 'Thumb Yoga',\\n  tagline: 'A week of balance at Little Fulcrum',\\n  description: 'Stand on the disc and keep the dot near the middle. Little Fulcrum runs five days of pose, pond, water, sand, and a storm.',\\n  type: 'Game',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  series: '',\\n  players: '1–4',\\n  controls: 'Lean with the left stick, WASD or the mouse. L2 and R2, or Q and E, are the feet. Both feet or Space breathe.',\\n  tags: ['3d', 'sports', 'third-person', 'comedy', 'co-op'],\\n} as const;\\n\\n/** The exit-interview object. The screen and the file both read this. */\\nexport const EXIT = {\\n  sourceInformation: SOURCE,\\n  testingFeedback: [...TESTING],\\n  engineFeedback: [...ENGINE],\\n  promptFeedback: [...PROMPT],\\n  aiHub: AI_HUB,\\n};\\n\",\"total_lines\":80}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-470d8887-b30e-4077-b754-ab53d55009f4-48","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Prompts for the device used last. Pads start as PlayStation. Settings can ask for Xbox.\\n * Keys and mouse buttons replace the pad marks the frame those devices are used.\\n */\\nexport type GlyphSet = 'playstation' | 'xbox' | 'keys' | 'mouse';\\n\\n/** One row of marks for the verbs. */\\nconst MARKS: Record<GlyphSet, Record<string, string>> = {\\n  playstation: { accept: 'Cross', cancel: 'Circle', lean: 'Left stick', feet: 'L2 and R2', breathe: 'L2 and R2 together', act: 'Cross', pause: 'Options' },\\n10→  xbox: { accept: 'A', cancel: 'B', lean: 'Left stick', feet: 'LT and RT', breathe: 'LT and RT together', act: 'A', pause: 'Menu' },\\n  keys: { accept: 'Enter', cancel: 'Esc', lean: 'WASD', feet: 'Q and E', breathe: 'Space', act: 'F', pause: 'Esc' },\\n  mouse: { accept: 'Click', cancel: 'Esc', lean: 'Mouse', feet: 'Left and right buttons', breathe: 'Space', act: 'Click', pause: 'Esc' },\\n};\\n\\n/** The mark for one verb on this glyph set. */\\nexport function glyph(set: GlyphSet, verb: string): string {\\n  return MARKS[set][verb] ?? verb;\\n}\\n\\n20→/** One prompt line. Two clauses, one sentence. */\\nexport function promptLine(set: GlyphSet): string {\\n  const row = MARKS[set];\\n  return `${row.lean} leans, and ${row.feet} are the feet. ${row.breathe} breathes, and ${row.act} acts.`;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Prompts for the device used last. Pads start as PlayStation. Settings can ask for Xbox.\\n * Keys and mouse buttons replace the pad marks the frame those devices are used.\\n */\\nexport type GlyphSet = 'playstation' | 'xbox' | 'keys' | 'mouse';\\n\\n/** One row of marks for the verbs. */\\nconst MARKS: Record<GlyphSet, Record<string, string>> = {\\n  playstation: { accept: 'Cross', cancel: 'Circle', lean: 'Left stick', feet: 'L2 and R2', breathe: 'L2 and R2 together', act: 'Cross', pause: 'Options' },\\n10→  xbox: { accept: 'A', cancel: 'B', lean: 'Left stick', feet: 'LT and RT', breathe: 'LT and RT together', act: 'A', pause: 'Menu' },\\n  keys: { accept: 'Enter', cancel: 'Esc', lean: 'WASD', feet: 'Q and E', breathe: 'Space', act: 'F', pause: 'Esc' },\\n  mouse: { accept: 'Click', cancel: 'Esc', lean: 'Mouse', feet: 'Left and right buttons', breathe: 'Space', act: 'Click', pause: 'Esc' },\\n};\\n\\n/** The mark for one verb on this glyph set. */\\nexport function glyph(set: GlyphSet, verb: string): string {\\n  return MARKS[set][verb] ?? verb;\\n}\\n\\n20→/** One prompt line. Two clauses, one sentence. */\\nexport function promptLine(set: GlyphSet): string {\\n  const row = MARKS[set];\\n  return `${row.lean} leans, and ${row.feet} are the feet. ${row.breathe} breathes, and ${row.act} acts.`;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/glyphs.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file Prompts for the device used last. Pads start as PlayStation. Settings can ask for Xbox.\\n * Keys and mouse buttons replace the pad marks the frame those devices are used.\\n */\\nexport type GlyphSet = 'playstation' | 'xbox' | 'keys' | 'mouse';\\n\\n/** One row of marks for the verbs. */\\nconst MARKS: Record<GlyphSet, Record<string, string>> = {\\n  playstation: { accept: 'Cross', cancel: 'Circle', lean: 'Left stick', feet: 'L2 and R2', breathe: 'L2 and R2 together', act: 'Cross', pause: 'Options' },\\n  xbox: { accept: 'A', cancel: 'B', lean: 'Left stick', feet: 'LT and RT', breathe: 'LT and RT together', act: 'A', pause: 'Menu' },\\n  keys: { accept: 'Enter', cancel: 'Esc', lean: 'WASD', feet: 'Q and E', breathe: 'Space', act: 'F', pause: 'Esc' },\\n  mouse: { accept: 'Click', cancel: 'Esc', lean: 'Mouse', feet: 'Left and right buttons', breathe: 'Space', act: 'Click', pause: 'Esc' },\\n};\\n\\n/** The mark for one verb on this glyph set. */\\nexport function glyph(set: GlyphSet, verb: string): string {\\n  return MARKS[set][verb] ?? verb;\\n}\\n\\n/** One prompt line. Two clauses, one sentence. */\\nexport function promptLine(set: GlyphSet): string {\\n  const row = MARKS[set];\\n  return `${row.lean} leans, and ${row.feet} are the feet. ${row.breathe} breathes, and ${row.act} acts.`;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":24}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-470d8887-b30e-4077-b754-ab53d55009f4-49","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The balance map. Lean is the stick and the keys. The feet are triggers, Q and E, and the mouse buttons.\\n * Space breathes. It is not the act button. The pointer stays free on menus.\\n */\\nimport { defineActionMap } from '../../../engine';\\n\\ndefineActionMap('actionMap:retreat', {\\n  description: 'Lean with the left stick, WASD or the arrows. The feet are L2 and R2, Q and E, or the mouse buttons.',\\n  lock: false,\\n10→  actions: {\\n    forward: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\\n    back: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\\n    left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\\n    right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\\n    footl: ['KeyQ', 'PadL2', 'MouseLeft'],\\n    footr: ['KeyE', 'PadR2', 'MouseRight'],\\n    breathe: ['Space'],\\n    act: ['KeyF', 'Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'PadSouth'],\\n    gentle: ['ShiftLeft', 'PadL1'],\\n20→  },\\n  move: ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right'],\\n  values: {\\n    'game:f': 'forward',\\n    'game:b': 'back',\\n    'game:l': 'left',\\n    'game:r': 'right',\\n    'game:fl': 'footl',\\n    'game:fr': 'footr',\\n    'game:g': 'gentle',\\n30→  },\\n});\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The balance map. Lean is the stick and the keys. The feet are triggers, Q and E, and the mouse buttons.\\n * Space breathes. It is not the act button. The pointer stays free on menus.\\n */\\nimport { defineActionMap } from '../../../engine';\\n\\ndefineActionMap('actionMap:retreat', {\\n  description: 'Lean with the left stick, WASD or the arrows. The feet are L2 and R2, Q and E, or the mouse buttons.',\\n  lock: false,\\n10→  actions: {\\n    forward: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\\n    back: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\\n    left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\\n    right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\\n    footl: ['KeyQ', 'PadL2', 'MouseLeft'],\\n    footr: ['KeyE', 'PadR2', 'MouseRight'],\\n    breathe: ['Space'],\\n    act: ['KeyF', 'Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'PadSouth'],\\n    gentle: ['ShiftLeft', 'PadL1'],\\n20→  },\\n  move: ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right'],\\n  values: {\\n    'game:f': 'forward',\\n    'game:b': 'back',\\n    'game:l': 'left',\\n    'game:r': 'right',\\n    'game:fl': 'footl',\\n    'game:fr': 'footr',\\n    'game:g': 'gentle',\\n30→  },\\n});\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/actions.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":60,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The balance map. Lean is the stick and the keys. The feet are triggers, Q and E, and the mouse buttons.\\n * Space breathes. It is not the act button. The pointer stays free on menus.\\n */\\nimport { defineActionMap } from '../../../engine';\\n\\ndefineActionMap('actionMap:retreat', {\\n  description: 'Lean with the left stick, WASD or the arrows. The feet are L2 and R2, Q and E, or the mouse buttons.',\\n  lock: false,\\n  actions: {\\n    forward: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\\n    back: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\\n    left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\\n    right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\\n    footl: ['KeyQ', 'PadL2', 'MouseLeft'],\\n    footr: ['KeyE', 'PadR2', 'MouseRight'],\\n    breathe: ['Space'],\\n    act: ['KeyF', 'Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'PadSouth'],\\n    gentle: ['ShiftLeft', 'PadL1'],\\n  },\\n  move: ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right'],\\n  values: {\\n    'game:f': 'forward',\\n    'game:b': 'back',\\n    'game:l': 'left',\\n    'game:r': 'right',\\n    'game:fl': 'footl',\\n    'game:fr': 'footr',\\n    'game:g': 'gentle',\\n  },\\n});\\n\",\"total_lines\":31}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"f309e67c-f23e-4534-a93c-984acf5f3f1a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_391","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will rewrite stage.ts into working split files. Then I will write main.ts, index.html, tags, onefile, and tests.\n\nI am checking the engine signature and import patterns for main.ts. I will split stage.ts into snap.ts, hub.ts, menus.ts, and stage.ts. I considered using a Shell class to avoid a large context object, but that would still leave one big file.\n\nA `PageCtx` interface will replace the Shell class. It carries audio, store, hub state, engine, menu, screen, attract mode, armed status, icons, glyph set, device focus, preferences, save data, and a publish method. Menus.ts can call back into stage functions through this context.\n\nThe PageCtx interface is too messy with circular calls. I will keep menus.ts as pure menu builders and pick handlers that return an action union. stage.ts will hold the main loop. A Menus class with callbacks is another option.\n\nI have settled on five compact files: ui/types.ts, ui/snap.ts, ui/menus.ts, ui/hubview.ts, and ui/stage.ts. I am checking MenuItem types and confirming that importing from scenes into ui is allowed.\n\nI realized that importing settings.ts into the page bundle would crash. It calls defineSettings at import time, and if scenes also imports it, registry.def throws CORE_DUPLICATE_ID. Pure data files like days.ts and lures.ts are safe to import.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fb52a598-36aa-421b-8c8e-2558dba3a07c-50","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/sounds/songs.ts","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fb52a598-36aa-421b-8c8e-2558dba3a07c-51","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhig