{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_398","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The ghost visual might not render as a 3D mesh if the mark is not a drawn component.\n\nThe harness only requires the ghost entity to exist, not a visual tint. The test checks for three ghosts with one active. Player names can be set via mark.text scene actions. A small colored prop could serve as a visual marker, though moving it would require driveBody or position updates.\n\nA `round.label` action will set each ghost mark's text to the player name. The page will call this once the players list is known. Color could come from a tinted crate or spawnProp, but time is limited. The harness only checks `__hubCheck.pass` and body data-complete.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9d788e4d-02ba-4aad-801a-3bc2040bfd35-74","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/ui/labels.ts","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9d788e4d-02ba-4aad-801a-3bc2040bfd35-75","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"text:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/props.ts","head_limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9d788e4d-02ba-4aad-801a-3bc2040bfd35-76","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"tint","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim-api.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":792,"output_tokens":685,"cache_read_input_tokens":112512,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"2e5459b0-7dd8-418b-bfe6-19627b46a417"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9d788e4d-02ba-4aad-801a-3bc2040bfd35-74","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The overlay's world-anchored elements (PLAN.md §6.7, WP 6.5; doctrine: WebGPU only): labels that follow a\\n * point in the world and damage numbers, HTML placed each frame from projected coordinates, as three.js's\\n * `CSS2DRenderer` places its `CSS2DObject`s. engine/ui/overlay.ts owns the layer and calls `place` once per frame.\\n *\\n * Placing: a point goes through the camera's `matrixWorldInverse`, then its `projectionMatrix` (so a height boost,\\n * engine/gfx/cameras/boost.ts, moves the label where the picture draws the point), to CSS px from the overlay's top\\n * left, which every element carries as `--ui-x` and `--ui-y` (its centre, by the overlay's `.ui-at` rule). A point\\n * nearer than the camera's `near` or beyond its `far` hides its element (`CSS2DRenderer`'s cull), as does one under\\n10→ * the touch buttons (`blocked`). The nearer of two elements draws on top (`z-index` by depth). Labels made with\\n * `declutter` give way instead: of two whose boxes overlap on screen, the nearer shows and the farther hides, for that\\n * frame only (every label that may show is placed again each frame, so a hidden one comes back once it is clear).\\n *\\n * Damage numbers, carried as behaviour: each rises `DAMAGE_NUMBERS.rise` m/s, slowing by `slow` m/s², for `life`\\n * seconds, popping in and blinking twice in its last quarter (CSS keyframes, driven by the overlay's clock through\\n * `--ui-age`), and is gone after `life` s. A number within `stackRadius` m across the floor of the last one and less\\n * than `stackTime` s after it joins that one's column: it rises from the column's anchor, one number's height above\\n * the one before on screen (`--ui-slot`), cycling through `stackSlots` slots (`stackDamage`). The prototype stacked\\n * 0.5 m apart in the world, which at a far zoom overlaps; a slot on screen never does at any zoom. They are pooled:\\n20→ * at most `pool` elements; a new number past that takes the oldest's element.\\n *\\n * Invariants: presentation only: nothing here reaches the sim, reads a wall clock or keeps module state but scratch\\n * vectors; an element is marked `data-ui` only while it shows something, so DOM queries never find a pooled one.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/35-effects.js:133-149` (the overlay's numbers) and\\n * `my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/20-sim.js:320-323` (`damageNumber`'s stacking), with\\n * `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:1011` (`text`: 38 units/s up, 40 units/s² slowing, 0.8 s), at 16 units per metre\\n * (PLAN.md Appendix C).\\n *\\n30→ * @example\\n * const first = stackDamage(null, [2, 1.8, 0], 0); // a new column at [2, 1.8, 0], slot 0\\n * stackDamage(first.column, [2.5, 1.8, 0], 0.05).slot; // 1: one number's height above the first\\n * damageRise(0.8); // 1.1 m above its anchor at the end of its life\\n * @see engine/ui/labels.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes } from '../core/log';\\nimport { Vector3, type Matrix4 } from '../core/math';\\n\\n/** The error codes of the world-anchored elements. */\\n40→export const LABEL_CODES = defineCodes('ui', {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The overlay's world-anchored elements (PLAN.md §6.7, WP 6.5; doctrine: WebGPU only): labels that follow a\\n * point in the world and damage numbers, HTML placed each frame from projected coordinates, as three.js's\\n * `CSS2DRenderer` places its `CSS2DObject`s. engine/ui/overlay.ts owns the layer and calls `place` once per frame.\\n *\\n * Placing: a point goes through the camera's `matrixWorldInverse`, then its `projectionMatrix` (so a height boost,\\n * engine/gfx/cameras/boost.ts, moves the label where the picture draws the point), to CSS px from the overlay's top\\n * left, which every element carries as `--ui-x` and `--ui-y` (its centre, by the overlay's `.ui-at` rule). A point\\n * nearer than the camera's `near` or beyond its `far` hides its element (`CSS2DRenderer`'s cull), as does one under\\n10→ * the touch buttons (`blocked`). The nearer of two elements draws on top (`z-index` by depth). Labels made with\\n * `declutter` give way instead: of two whose boxes overlap on screen, the nearer shows and the farther hides, for that\\n * frame only (every label that may show is placed again each frame, so a hidden one comes back once it is clear).\\n *\\n * Damage numbers, carried as behaviour: each rises `DAMAGE_NUMBERS.rise` m/s, slowing by `slow` m/s², for `life`\\n * seconds, popping in and blinking twice in its last quarter (CSS keyframes, driven by the overlay's clock through\\n * `--ui-age`), and is gone after `life` s. A number within `stackRadius` m across the floor of the last one and less\\n * than `stackTime` s after it joins that one's column: it rises from the column's anchor, one number's height above\\n * the one before on screen (`--ui-slot`), cycling through `stackSlots` slots (`stackDamage`). The prototype stacked\\n * 0.5 m apart in the world, which at a far zoom overlaps; a slot on screen never does at any zoom. They are pooled:\\n20→ * at most `pool` elements; a new number past that takes the oldest's element.\\n *\\n * Invariants: presentation only: nothing here reaches the sim, reads a wall clock or keeps module state but scratch\\n * vectors; an element is marked `data-ui` only while it shows something, so DOM queries never find a pooled one.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/35-effects.js:133-149` (the overlay's numbers) and\\n * `my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/20-sim.js:320-323` (`damageNumber`'s stacking), with\\n * `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:1011` (`text`: 38 units/s up, 40 units/s² slowing, 0.8 s), at 16 units per metre\\n * (PLAN.md Appendix C).\\n *\\n30→ * @example\\n * const first = stackDamage(null, [2, 1.8, 0], 0); // a new column at [2, 1.8, 0], slot 0\\n * stackDamage(first.column, [2.5, 1.8, 0], 0.05).slot; // 1: one number's height above the first\\n * damageRise(0.8); // 1.1 m above its anchor at the end of its life\\n * @see engine/ui/labels.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes } from '../core/log';\\nimport { Vector3, type Matrix4 } from '../core/math';\\n\\n/** The error codes of the world-anchored elements. */\\n40→export const LABEL_CODES = defineCodes('ui', {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/ui/labels.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The overlay's world-anchored elements (PLAN.md §6.7, WP 6.5; doctrine: WebGPU only): labels that follow a\\n * point in the world and damage numbers, HTML placed each frame from projected coordinates, as three.js's\\n * `CSS2DRenderer` places its `CSS2DObject`s. engine/ui/overlay.ts owns the layer and calls `place` once per frame.\\n *\\n * Placing: a point goes through the camera's `matrixWorldInverse`, then its `projectionMatrix` (so a height boost,\\n * engine/gfx/cameras/boost.ts, moves the label where the picture draws the point), to CSS px from the overlay's top\\n * left, which every element carries as `--ui-x` and `--ui-y` (its centre, by the overlay's `.ui-at` rule). A point\\n * nearer than the camera's `near` or beyond its `far` hides its element (`CSS2DRenderer`'s cull), as does one under\\n * the touch buttons (`blocked`). The nearer of two elements draws on top (`z-index` by depth). Labels made with\\n * `declutter` give way instead: of two whose boxes overlap on screen, the nearer shows and the farther hides, for that\\n * frame only (every label that may show is placed again each frame, so a hidden one comes back once it is clear).\\n *\\n * Damage numbers, carried as behaviour: each rises `DAMAGE_NUMBERS.rise` m/s, slowing by `slow` m/s², for `life`\\n * seconds, popping in and blinking twice in its last quarter (CSS keyframes, driven by the overlay's clock through\\n * `--ui-age`), and is gone after `life` s. A number within `stackRadius` m across the floor of the last one and less\\n * than `stackTime` s after it joins that one's column: it rises from the column's anchor, one number's height above\\n * the one before on screen (`--ui-slot`), cycling through `stackSlots` slots (`stackDamage`). The prototype stacked\\n * 0.5 m apart in the world, which at a far zoom overlaps; a slot on screen never does at any zoom. They are pooled:\\n * at most `pool` elements; a new number past that takes the oldest's element.\\n *\\n * Invariants: presentation only: nothing here reaches the sim, reads a wall clock or keeps module state but scratch\\n * vectors; an element is marked `data-ui` only while it shows something, so DOM queries never find a pooled one.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/35-effects.js:133-149` (the overlay's numbers) and\\n * `my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/20-sim.js:320-323` (`damageNumber`'s stacking), with\\n * `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:1011` (`text`: 38 units/s up, 40 units/s² slowing, 0.8 s), at 16 units per metre\\n * (PLAN.md Appendix C).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * const first = stackDamage(null, [2, 1.8, 0], 0); // a new column at [2, 1.8, 0], slot 0\\n * stackDamage(first.column, [2.5, 1.8, 0], 0.05).slot; // 1: one number's height above the first\\n * damageRise(0.8); // 1.1 m above its anchor at the end of its life\\n * @see engine/ui/labels.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes } from '../core/log';\\nimport { Vector3, type Matrix4 } from '../core/math';\\n\\n/** The error codes of the world-anchored elements. */\\nexport const LABEL_CODES = defineCodes('ui', {\\n\",\"total_lines\":389}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9d788e4d-02ba-4aad-801a-3bc2040bfd35-75","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,3