{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c3fdb320-d195-4365-ab54-88e5bc4111bc-115","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"350→    return engine;\\n  }\\n  const step = (intents: Record<string, unknown>) => {\\n    if (playback && !playback.done) {\\n      playback.step(started.session);\\n      started.stepped(); // its hit-stops reach the clock as in live play\\n    } else {\\n      playback = null;\\n      started.stepOnce(intents);\\n    }\\n360→  };\\n  loop = createLoop({\\n    clock: () => started.clock,\\n    sample,\\n    step,\\n    draw: ({ alpha, dt }) => {\\n      // frozen in a reproducible run: a replay playing, or the governor turned off (engine/dev/governor.ts)\\n      parts.governor!.freeze((playback !== null && !playback.done) || !settingsNow.get<boolean>('gfx.governor'));\\n      if (warming) return;\\n      const report = frame(alpha, dt);\\n370→      if (!report.drawn && report.warming) warming = warmCameras().finally(() => (warming = null));\\n    },\\n    hold: () => started.playing,\\n    cap: () => input.touch?.active ?? false,\\n    onError: (error) => fail(error, 'APP_FRAME'),\\n  });\\n  parts.ready = true;\\n  overlay.hide();\\n  loop.start();\\n  const replay = asked?.playback;\\n380→  if (asked && !replay) fail(asked.error);\\n  else if (replay) {\\n    try {\\n      started.begin(replay.replay);\\n      playback = replay;\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      fail(error);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return engine;\\n390→}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"350→    return engine;\\n  }\\n  const step = (intents: Record<string, unknown>) => {\\n    if (playback && !playback.done) {\\n      playback.step(started.session);\\n      started.stepped(); // its hit-stops reach the clock as in live play\\n    } else {\\n      playback = null;\\n      started.stepOnce(intents);\\n    }\\n360→  };\\n  loop = createLoop({\\n    clock: () => started.clock,\\n    sample,\\n    step,\\n    draw: ({ alpha, dt }) => {\\n      // frozen in a reproducible run: a replay playing, or the governor turned off (engine/dev/governor.ts)\\n      parts.governor!.freeze((playback !== null && !playback.done) || !settingsNow.get<boolean>('gfx.governor'));\\n      if (warming) return;\\n      const report = frame(alpha, dt);\\n370→      if (!report.drawn && report.warming) warming = warmCameras().finally(() => (warming = null));\\n    },\\n    hold: () => started.playing,\\n    cap: () => input.touch?.active ?? false,\\n    onError: (error) => fail(error, 'APP_FRAME'),\\n  });\\n  parts.ready = true;\\n  overlay.hide();\\n  loop.start();\\n  const replay = asked?.playback;\\n380→  if (asked && !replay) fail(asked.error);\\n  else if (replay) {\\n    try {\\n      started.begin(replay.replay);\\n      playback = replay;\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      fail(error);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return engine;\\n390→}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/app/engine.ts\",\"offset\":350,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"    return engine;\\n  }\\n  const step = (intents: Record<string, unknown>) => {\\n    if (playback && !playback.done) {\\n      playback.step(started.session);\\n      started.stepped(); // its hit-stops reach the clock as in live play\\n    } else {\\n      playback = null;\\n      started.stepOnce(intents);\\n    }\\n  };\\n  loop = createLoop({\\n    clock: () => started.clock,\\n    sample,\\n    step,\\n    draw: ({ alpha, dt }) => {\\n      // frozen in a reproducible run: a replay playing, or the governor turned off (engine/dev/governor.ts)\\n      parts.governor!.freeze((playback !== null && !playback.done) || !settingsNow.get<boolean>('gfx.governor'));\\n      if (warming) return;\\n      const report = frame(alpha, dt);\\n      if (!report.drawn && report.warming) warming = warmCameras().finally(() => (warming = null));\\n    },\\n    hold: () => started.playing,\\n    cap: () => input.touch?.active ?? false,\\n    onError: (error) => fail(error, 'APP_FRAME'),\\n  });\\n  parts.ready = true;\\n  overlay.hide();\\n  loop.start();\\n  const replay = asked?.playback;\\n  if (asked && !replay) fail(asked.error);\\n  else if (replay) {\\n    try {\\n      started.begin(replay.replay);\\n      playback = replay;\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      fail(error);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return engine;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":390}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"38b9558a-77e7-46fa-8aef-a4968cd617b8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_428","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`loop.start()` runs before the return statement, and it may trigger a synchronous frame update.\n\nA `held` object will store the engine reference. `createEngine` can run a frame before returning, so the engine is assigned only after creation completes. Input handling waits for `page.bind`, which is acceptable for a couple of frames.\n\nA long boot time can trigger the attract timer before `bind` completes. The idle clock uses construction time as its baseline, so if engine creation takes 15 seconds, the first frame after binding sees an idle duration of 10 seconds and starts attract immediately. This skips the title screen and menu, since `showTitle` only runs during `bind`.\n\nThe boot check requires the title screen to appear. Starting attract before binding would fail this test.\n\n`bind()` will reset `lastInput` to the current time and only then call `showTitle()`. The attract timer will be skipped until the engine is bound, preventing early activation during a long boot.\n\nThe title screen correctly blocks modal input before the menu exists. The hub starts as a card with no attract timer. Shell CSS will fix HUD readability by making the shell fixed and non-interactive, while buttons and inputs keep pointer events.\n\nShell CSS now defines exact positions for the disc, card, touch settings, note, banner, copy, and about panels.\n\nThe about panel will scroll with overflow auto. Slider controls will sit fixed at the bottom left.\n\nMenu items inside the engine overlay will remain interactive despite the overlay's pointer-events-none root.\n\nThe card panel will only render when the current screen is 'card'.\n\nCode will be kept compact to stay under 450 lines.\n\nshowAbout will return to the screen stored in aboutFrom. That value can be 'title', 'pause', 'hub', or 'settings'.\n\nAbout will return to the hub pause screen when opened from there, and to the title screen otherwise. Settings will return to the hub pause screen if the hub is active, to the pause screen for event, roam, or results modes, and to the title screen otherwise.\n\nThe settings slider will read its live value from `state().settings`. Resetting a setting restores the default value returned by `describe`. The time scale cycles through 0.25, 1, and 4. `as` type casts are permitted, but `any` is not.\n\nLive settings values will be read from `state().settings[path]`. View settings are excluded because they are not tunables. If `state()` throws or is slow, the code will fall back to a default value.\n\n`inspector.state()` returns a filtered WorldState copy that includes settings.\n\nFiles will be written in parallel batches.\n\n`applyGhosts` and group intents need name updates.\n\nA small page test may be added, since tests must drive shipped code.\n\nNo DOM tests will be added because Vitest runs in Node without a document. Browser tests are deferred. Island and retreat mash tests will run after compilation. ESLint import type consistency and unused variables will be checked afterward. A shared `ui/host.ts` interface will provide types to `snap.ts`, `menus.ts`, and `hub.ts` to avoid circular dependencies.\n\n`stage.ts` will import all modules and drive the hub from its frame loop. The `frame` method reads a snap, updates live state from it, advances any active menu, and fetches input from the engine.\n\nThe frame loop processes input only when no menu is open and the game has not ended. Pause toggles the hub pause menu or the inspector pause menu. Action presses during roam start the game if text exists and no lure is active. Group presses send seats in normal mode or clear claims and seats in hub mode. The hub view ticks while playing. After input handling, the loop checks for attract, shows results, evening, or credits menus, then paints the scene, hub card, and publishes the frame. When the hub finishes a results round, it calls `hubView.finish(false)`.\n\nMenu input consumes the pause press, so the game does not also toggle pause while a menu is open. The hub card screen uses pad buttons and keydown to answer questions; act presses are ignored there because the modal flag drops intents. Ghosts continue sending even when the hub pause menu is active, since that overlay does not pause the simulation.\n\n`hubView.tick` will run outside the `if (!menu)` block so it keeps updating during hub pause. It can read the simulation's wobble from `snap.ax/ay` instead of raw input, since the simulation continues running while paused. The virtual axis still works for packing ghosts even when modal drops intents this frame.\n\nThe plan explicitly states that pause is an overlay that never pauses the simulation. This means the hub pause menu must not block gameplay input or ghost updates, even though modal drops intents during its open state.\n\nModal input is active only for the title, touch, card, about, and menu screens. During hub play with no menu open, modal stays false so the player can keep leaning while the pause menu is up. The attract screen also keeps modal off.\n\nPlayer input is safely ignored during attract because the bot replaces intents. Exit attract is handled by listeners rather than intents. When settings are open during attract, modal stays true and the demo continues using the bot.\n\nGame ghosts will be cleared outside hub mode. The names axis updates every hub frame. round.go runs once when time() reaches zero or passes it.\n\nAIHub.time during start events is negative until the countdown expires, so the frame loop checks this condition.\n\nA `maybeGo` function guards round start with a `started` flag, ensuring `round.go` runs only once after the countdown completes. The progress label is sliced to 24 characters. A `running` score helper returns the final result in results mode, or the mean of axes a, b, and c otherwise.\n\nThe score helper rounds the mean of axes a, b, and c to an integer. Progress is sent when the rounded score or phase changes. The initial label reads Breathing in with score 0. During play it shows Class X · score. Ghosts are sent immediately on go and every 100 milliseconds after that. Rate limiting is acceptable since the send rate stays under 20 per second.\n\nThe end handler mutes audio and stops the engine. Progress will not be sent after the game ends. A time-up event triggers finish(true) immediately, so results are sent with the current score even if the class has not yet finished.\n\nAwards are only granted when the score reaches at least 900. Stats values are strings. The finish function uses the live score even if results mode is not active. If a host leaves, that copy receives an end event and stops without sending a result; the remaining copies will handle time-up.\n\nThe card screen must draw all decorative numbers from `AIHub.rng('card')` and cannot use `Math.random`. The countdown timer is allowed because it originates from the hub. Muting audio on end is sufficient; no manual volume reset is needed.\n\nA single `rng('card')()` call will generate a decorative mat number for the card screen. This satisfies the rule that all decorative numbers must come from that source. The displayed mat number is skipped because it may not match the actual seat.\n\nThe card screen will list players with colors. A ready set tracks which players have confirmed their seat. The paintCard function hides the card when the screen is not active and skips rendering if the client is missing.\n\nThe card screen renders each player as a colored row showing their name, whether it is the local user, and a Ready or Waiting mark. The countdown timer displays seconds remaining or \"Starting.\" Two buttons, Ready and More time, handle player answers.\n\nCard screen taps and clicks will answer ready. Button click events handle both mouse and touch input. A window pointerdown listener will also catch mouse answers, though double-firing is harmless because the answer function is idempotent.\n\nTouch devices in hub sessions must still support card buttons via click events. Touch pointerdown will not set touchAt or block input, since the card screen is not attract mode. Enter on the card screen is handled by a listener and stays modal, preventing game act presses. Space serves as both breathe and uiAccept; on the title screen it may activate the menu item, but the standalone harness test expects the client to remain inactive while the screen is drawn.\n\nThe standalone harness test only requires the client to stay inactive and the screen to draw without errors. Starting the game with Enter is acceptable as long as no errors occur. The createPage helper must not throw if the document object already exists, since node tests will not import stage. main.ts is imported exclusively by index.html.\n\nTests will not import main.ts, so vitest should not load it. Settings are imported through stage and island, but only one module instance exists in the browser, preventing duplicate defineSettings calls. I am also checking prettier printWidth and trailing comma settings.\n\nI will run prettier on the new files and check line counts against the eslint max-lines limit. I also need to fix a compile error in group.ts where an inner `const intents` shadows the function parameter, which would fail type checking. I am ready to write all files now.\n\nThe Host interface will expose only data and primitives. Menu functions will close over the host object rather than being defined inside it, keeping the interface clean.\n\nThe Host interface now includes methods for publishing, running scripts, opening menus, closing them, applying preferences, resuming, and handling glyphs. The open method is implemented in stage and manages screen transitions, menu state, focus, and publishing. Menus will call host.open and host.run.\n\n`menus` will be stored on the host so stage can call `menus.showPause`. `createMenus(host)` will export the menu factory. `persist()` is added to the Host interface and implemented by stage. The Erase action clears the save, resets preferences, seeds to 1, and returns to the title screen. The inspector's `seed(1)` call restarts to title mode and opens the menu.\n\nContinue passes the full save object to game.begin, but applySave ignores extra keys like bests and outfits. Begin creates a fresh save with empty arguments, so the flow stays on day one and opens the first programme item. Free play checks credits before starting, and group mode launches from title.\n\nI will add CSS to remove exclamation marks from the card and shell screens. The dev slider menu will be limited to six rows by slicing items in open(). Jumps will show four entries plus More and Back. Days will be split into two pages: days one through four on the first page, and day five alone on the second. Events will be chunked into groups of four, with steps set to four and ranks covering the first four days and the last one.\n\nThe menu layout is finalized. Jumps, events, and ranks are split into pages of up to four items each. Each page shows at most six rows: four items plus More and Back. Settings and pause pages fit within that limit.\n\nDev mode and hub pause each fit five rows, while the title screen fits six. Sliders will be hidden outside the dev screen. The dev menu reads live settings and resets to defaults; resetting or changing time and seed reopens the dev menu so sliders update. Restart uses the current live event, which is refreshed every frame before menus read it.\n\nremember() updates the save from a snapshot but leaves the event field untouched, since Save does not include it. The publish payload will use live.event and the day from save.day, which remember() keeps current. __game.screen will hold the screen state. I will write index.html, main.ts, tags, and onefile next, delete the starter files, run a typecheck on the game files, and verify island and group compilation.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-63c2ebff-adf1-446a-98ee-20fdad2d85a2-116","name":"list_dir","input":{"target_directory":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/cast"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":513,"output_tokens":5933,"cache_read_input_tokens":161152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"95f552ba-6469-4f7e-b549-8859ade4e774"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-63c2ebff-adf1-446a-98ee-20fdad2d85a2-116","content":"{\"type\":\"ListDir\",\"Content\":{\"content\":\"- /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/cast/\\n  - clips.ts\\n  - player.ts\\n  - rest.json\\n  - rest.ts\",\"absolute_root_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/cast\"}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"034e33e6-7ee7-431b-9b81-fa472074afe0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_429","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will delete player.ts with the starter.\n\nclips.ts is the real cast. I'll write code following existing import order conventions and avoid non-null assertions. The card ready set will use a filtered array of player IDs, with left possibly null.\n\nI'll write all files now. The pond lure stays hidden during results menus and doesn't block actions. I also fixed a menu edge case where open() always receives at least one item.\n\nI fixed a keydown bug on touch devices. When armed is false, pressing a key now shows the title screen instead of leaving it blank.\n\nThe touch profile test will not send a keypress. It only checks the message and settings tap.\n\nMouse clicks on touch devices are treated as real pointers rather than touch-only input. Showing the title screen in that case is acceptable.\n\nTouch input now records a timestamp and ignores the event. Mouse clicks on touch screens reveal the title screen. The settings button does not set armed state; it opens settings directly, which safely handles a missing engine before binding. Touching settings during attract mode will not exit the attract loop.\n\nThe host will store the last detected device and its glyph set. The publish step will read both values. Audio volumes from preferences will also be published.\n\nI'll add a comment header to the new files. Hub.ts will handle send rate and packing. Stage.ts will serve as the glue layer. I'll place sendSeats in stage because it concerns couch logic, not hub logic. I'll update round.ts and group.ts, delete old files with rm, then run tsc.\n\nI'll run eslint and vitest on the new files first, then prettier. The full TypeScript check is too slow for now. I confirmed the UI directory is included in tsconfig. I'll import the side-effect modules in main.ts so defineLook, songs, voice, and actions initialize properly.\n\nI'll write index.html with a calibrating message in 28px font. The script will hide this element once the engine is ready, or keep it visible if no GPU is found. The shell is created before the engine starts, so both overlays appear during loading.\n\nIf WebGPU is unavailable, the script will skip creating the shell and instead show a no-gpu message and fail the AI hub. I will hardcode that message to avoid pulling in the book module.\n\nI'll import the no-GPU message from the book module so it stays in one source. I'll declare a minimal AIHub interface on window in main.ts. The connect call will use ghost mode with seats 1 and 4 and card enabled. I'll handle null seed and info values. Search parameters will be built from location.search.\n\nThe engine URL builder strips aihub keys and sets touch to off. It forces post.look to retreat and cam3 to chase unless cam or cam3 is already present. Valid keys like scene, seed, and game.auto remain untouched.\n\nThe store mode will be demo when info is present or the URL contains replay. Music volume is set to 0.1 on fresh profiles and may be overridden by saved preferences. Touch devices are detected with a media query for coarse non-hover pointers. The hub flag is set whenever info is present.\n\nIf the AI hub is active but connection fails or times out, the game falls back to normal single-player mode. The connect call only runs when the hub is actually active; otherwise it returns null. A ten-second watchdog timer applies only when info is present. Both scenes are always loaded so solo play can still function.\n\nSolo play will use the island scene, while hub play routes through round. I will defer writing the engine and README until after tests pass. The menus module will be drafted in a single write.\n\nI verified that menus.open will not crash before input binding, since it requires an engine. In bind, the engine is assigned before applyPrefs runs, so settings and volumes are applied safely. The retreat look is registered early enough to be set on the first frame.\n\nThe post.look setter will only run when the look ID changes, and it will disable itself if any call throws. This prevents repeated errors while still switching between storm and dawn.\n\nThe post.look setter now checks for a live inspector before calling set, so it safely retries on the next frame if the inspector is missing. A songOk flag will guard audio.music calls to prevent repeated errors while the audio context is still initializing.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1dbc4830-fcb4-434c-b6d1-7a452c5e4871-117","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/audio/runtime/audio.ts","offset":250,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6030,"output_tokens":2844,"cache_read_input_tokens":161664,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"e1d36bcd-5f5f-4fd6-8f3b-edfa168d8b77"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1dbc4830-fcb4-434c-b6d1-7a452c5e4871-117","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"250→      const sting = bindings.get(type);\\n      if (sting) player?.stinger(sting);\\n      if (typeof payload !== 'object' || payload === null) return null;\\n      const { sfx, vol, variant, position } = payload as Record<string, unknown>;\\n      if (typeof sfx !== 'string') return null;\\n      return play(sfx, { vol, variant, position } as PlayOptions);\\n    },\\n    bind(type, id) {\\n      if (id === null) bindings.delete(type);\\n      else bindings.set(type, checkSound(id));\\n260→    },\\n    music(id, opts = {}) {\\n      if (id !== null) getSong(id, registry);\\n      if (opts.intensity !== undefined) level = opts.intensity;\\n      if (player) player.play(id, opts);\\n      else pending = { id, options: opts };\\n    },\\n    intensity(value, opts) {\\n      level = value;\\n      player?.intensity(value, opts);\\n270→    },\\n    stinger(id, opts) {\\n      checkSound(id); // also while locked, when the player is not there yet\\n      player?.stinger(id, opts);\\n    },\\n    update(next, view) {\\n      if (view) queries = view;\\n      if (next) pose = next;\\n      if (!context || !pose) return;\\n      if (next) placeListener(context.listener, pose, context.currentTime);\\n280→      if (!queries) return;\\n      for (const voice of pool.voices) {\\n        if (!voice.position) continue;\\n        const now = wallsBetween(queries, pose.position, voice.position);\\n        if (now !== voice.walls) voice.occlude(now, true);\\n      }\\n    },\\n    volume(bus, value) {\\n      if (value !== undefined) volumes[bus] = mixer ? mixer.volume(bus, value) : Math.min(1, Math.max(0, value));\\n      return volumes[bus];\\n290→    },\\n    mute(on = !muted) {\\n      muted = on;\\n      mixer?.mute(on);\\n      return muted;\\n    },\\n    duck(on) {\\n      mixer?.duck(on);\\n    },\\n    room(next) {\",\"content_concise\":\"250→      const sting = bindings.get(type);\\n      if (sting) player?.stinger(sting);\\n      if (typeof payload !== 'object' || payload === null) return null;\\n      const { sfx, vol, variant, position } = payload as Record<string, unknown>;\\n      if (typeof sfx !== 'string') return null;\\n      return play(sfx, { vol, variant, position } as PlayOptions);\\n    },\\n    bind(type, id) {\\n      if (id === null) bindings.delete(type);\\n      else bindings.set(type, checkSound(id));\\n260→    },\\n    music(id, opts = {}) {\\n      if (id !== null) getSong(id, registry);\\n      if (opts.intensity !== undefined) level = opts.intensity;\\n      if (player) player.play(id, opts);\\n      else pending = { id, options: opts };\\n    },\\n    intensity(value, opts) {\\n      level = value;\\n      player?.intensity(value, opts);\\n270→    },\\n    stinger(id, opts) {\\n      checkSound(id); // also while locked, when the player is not there yet\\n      player?.stinger(id, opts);\\n    },\\n    update(next, view) {\\n      if (view) queries = view;\\n      if (next) pose = next;\\n      if (!context || !pose) return;\\n      if (next) placeListener(context.listener, pose, context.currentTime);\\n280→      if (!queries) return;\\n      for (const voice of pool.voices) {\\n        if (!voice.position) continue;\\n        const now = wallsBetween(queries, pose.position, voice.position);\\n        if (now !== voice.walls) voice.occlude(now, true);\\n      }\\n    },\\n    volume(bus, value) {\\n      if (value !== undefined) volumes[bus] = mixer ? mixer.volume(bus, value) : Math.min(1, Math.max(0, value));\\n      return volumes[bus];\\n290→    },\\n    mute(on = !muted) {\\n      muted = on;\\n      mixer?.mute(on);\\n      return muted;\\n    },\\n    duck(on) {\\n      mixer?.duck(on);\\n    },\\n    room(next) {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/audio/runtime/audio.ts\",\"offset\":250,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"      const sting = bindings.get(type);\\n      if (sting) player?.stinger(sting);\\n      if (typeof payload !== 'object' || payload === null) return null;\\n      const { sfx, vol, variant, position } = payload as Record<string, unknown>;\\n      if (typeof sfx !== 'string') return null;\\n      return play(sfx, { vol, variant, position } as PlayOptions);\\n    },\\n    bind(type, id) {\\n      if (id === null) bindings.delete(type);\\n      else bindings.set(type, checkSound(id));\\n    },\\n    music(id, opts = {}) {\\n      if (id !== null) getSong(id, registry);\\n      if (opts.intensity !== undefined) level = opts.intensity;\\n      if (player) player.play(id, opts);\\n      else pending = { id, options: opts };\\n    },\\n    intensity(value, opts) {\\n      level = value;\\n      player?.intensity(value, opts);\\n    },\\n    stinger(id, opts) {\\n      checkSound(id); // also while locked, when the player is not there yet\\n      player?.stinger(id, opts);\\n    },\\n    update(next, view) {\\n      if (view) queries = view;\\n      if (next) pose = next;\\n      if (!context || !pose) return;\\n      if (next) placeListener(context.listener, pose, context.currentTime);\\n      if (!queries) return;\\n      for (const voice of pool.voices) {\\n        if (!voice.position) continue;\\n        const now = wallsBetween(queries, pose.position, voice.position);\\n        if (now !== voice.walls) voice.occlude(now, true);\\n      }\\n    },\\n    volume(bus, value) {\\n      if (value !== undefined) volumes[bus] = mixer ? mixer.volume(bus, value) : Math.min(1, Math.max(0, value));\\n      return volumes[bus];\\n    },\\n    mute(on = !muted) {\\n      muted = on;\\n      mixer?.mute(on);\\n      return muted;\\n    },\\n    duck(on) {\\n      mixer?.duck(on);\\n    },\\n    room(next) {\\n\",\"total_lines\":321}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"73619ea7-d220-43d0-b8d9-48c5bceb29a5"}
