{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3af4ac3d-c96b-4463-9aa7-9f160453676f-123","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"35→\\n/** The two projections three.js has: `PerspectiveCamera` and `OrthographicCamera`. */\\nexport type Projection = 'perspective' | 'orthographic';\\n\\n/** Where a camera is, where it looks and its lens, in a frame: plain, frozen data (see the file comment). */\\n40→export interface CameraPose {\\n  /** The camera's position, m. */\\n  readonly position: Vec3;\\n  /** The heading of the view direction, rad (the intents' `cam`). */\\n  readonly yaw: number;\\n  /** Up or down from level, rad: + up, −π/2 straight down. */\\n  readonly pitch: number;\\n  /** A bank about the view direction, rad: + tips the picture's top to the right, as a lean into a right turn. */\\n  readonly roll: number;\\n  readonly projection: Projection;\\n50→  /** Vertical field of view, degrees (`PerspectiveCamera.fov`). */\\n  readonly fov: number;\\n  /** Orthographic: the frustum's height at zoom 1, m (`top − bottom`, three.js's examples' `frustumSize`). */\\n  readonly frustumSize: number;\\n  /** As three.js cameras' `zoom`: 2 shows half as much (a narrower lens, a smaller frustum). */\\n  readonly zoom: number;\\n  readonly near: number;\\n  readonly far: number;\\n  /** Heights (world y) are stretched by this in the picture only; 1 shows true heights. */\\n  readonly boost: number;\\n60→  /** From the position to the point the camera looks at (its target), m. */\\n  readonly distance: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** What the devices give a camera in a frame; every field is optional (orbit and fly turn, fly moves, views zoom). */\",\"content_concise\":\"35→\\n/** The two projections three.js has: `PerspectiveCamera` and `OrthographicCamera`. */\\nexport type Projection = 'perspective' | 'orthographic';\\n\\n/** Where a camera is, where it looks and its lens, in a frame: plain, frozen data (see the file comment). */\\n40→export interface CameraPose {\\n  /** The camera's position, m. */\\n  readonly position: Vec3;\\n  /** The heading of the view direction, rad (the intents' `cam`). */\\n  readonly yaw: number;\\n  /** Up or down from level, rad: + up, −π/2 straight down. */\\n  readonly pitch: number;\\n  /** A bank about the view direction, rad: + tips the picture's top to the right, as a lean into a right turn. */\\n  readonly roll: number;\\n  readonly projection: Projection;\\n50→  /** Vertical field of view, degrees (`PerspectiveCamera.fov`). */\\n  readonly fov: number;\\n  /** Orthographic: the frustum's height at zoom 1, m (`top − bottom`, three.js's examples' `frustumSize`). */\\n  readonly frustumSize: number;\\n  /** As three.js cameras' `zoom`: 2 shows half as much (a narrower lens, a smaller frustum). */\\n  readonly zoom: number;\\n  readonly near: number;\\n  readonly far: number;\\n  /** Heights (world y) are stretched by this in the picture only; 1 shows true heights. */\\n  readonly boost: number;\\n60→  /** From the position to the point the camera looks at (its target), m. */\\n  readonly distance: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** What the devices give a camera in a frame; every field is optional (orbit and fly turn, fly moves, views zoom). */\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/gfx/cameras/pose.ts\",\"offset\":35,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"\\n/** The two projections three.js has: `PerspectiveCamera` and `OrthographicCamera`. */\\nexport type Projection = 'perspective' | 'orthographic';\\n\\n/** Where a camera is, where it looks and its lens, in a frame: plain, frozen data (see the file comment). */\\nexport interface CameraPose {\\n  /** The camera's position, m. */\\n  readonly position: Vec3;\\n  /** The heading of the view direction, rad (the intents' `cam`). */\\n  readonly yaw: number;\\n  /** Up or down from level, rad: + up, −π/2 straight down. */\\n  readonly pitch: number;\\n  /** A bank about the view direction, rad: + tips the picture's top to the right, as a lean into a right turn. */\\n  readonly roll: number;\\n  readonly projection: Projection;\\n  /** Vertical field of view, degrees (`PerspectiveCamera.fov`). */\\n  readonly fov: number;\\n  /** Orthographic: the frustum's height at zoom 1, m (`top − bottom`, three.js's examples' `frustumSize`). */\\n  readonly frustumSize: number;\\n  /** As three.js cameras' `zoom`: 2 shows half as much (a narrower lens, a smaller frustum). */\\n  readonly zoom: number;\\n  readonly near: number;\\n  readonly far: number;\\n  /** Heights (world y) are stretched by this in the picture only; 1 shows true heights. */\\n  readonly boost: number;\\n  /** From the position to the point the camera looks at (its target), m. */\\n  readonly distance: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** What the devices give a camera in a frame; every field is optional (orbit and fly turn, fly moves, views zoom). */\\n\",\"total_lines\":286}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"18fd1fd9-3d95-4500-8119-f40b1c9b25d4"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_434","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"audio.update(frame.camera) works because CameraPose has position, yaw, and pitch.\n\nPassing frame.queries as the second argument to audio.update, falling back to undefined. Will write files carefully and fix group.ts with search_replace while composing.\n\nCard buttons need type button to prevent form submission. Async rebinds will use void with .then to avoid floating promises. The \"already taken\" message omits an exclamation mark.\n\nRebind failures for reserved controls will show the same message. The RebindResult type is not needed; only result.ok is used.\n\nA circular initialization issue was spotted: host methods need menus, but menus needs host. The plan is to declare menus as a let variable and have host methods close over it.\n\nThe circular initialization concern is resolved. Host methods do not need menus during setup, so menus can be assigned before bind. Frame closes over menus later.\n\nFiles will be consolidated: Snap and readSnap go in snap.ts, HubClient in hub.ts, and Host in menus.ts. Stage will import both hub.ts and menus.ts.\n\nHubClient and Menus interfaces are defined. Hub logic will take a small HubEnv. I'll write files now and fix type errors with tsc. Lines wrap at 120 characters. I may use `satisfies`. The group fix and round names will be handled in parallel.\n\nRound name labels will be set only when the name string is non-empty. When a ghost leaves, its text clears so it walks off. The code checks that names is an array before indexing by seat.\n\nSeat labels will be drawn as simulation text when the ghost is active, and cleared when it leaves. The engine's HTML label system will also be used to show seat names anchored at world positions.\n\nThe plan forbids HTML overlays for ghost names. I will use engine.ui.hud to display seat labels at the top-left corner, colored by player, and clear them when a ghost leaves.\n\nThe `const intents` shadow in group.ts is a SyntaxError. The island test passed before this edit, so the cpus change introduced it. Any test that imports group.ts will fail to load.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The page draft cannot compile: it stores live fields on the save, and the ghost send is empty. Group Class also redeclares `intents`, which stops the file from loading. I'll fix those and wire the shell."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-091de0aa-872c-48e5-9a71-496b640c1cf3-124","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/events/group.ts","old_string":"  const intents = { 'game:seats': packed } as Intents;\n  for (let seat = 1; seat <= 3; seat++) {\n    try {\n      rowOf(w, seat);\n    } catch {\n      continue;\n    }\n    apply(w, intents, { seat, noise: 1.35 });\n  }","new_string":"  const fed = { 'game:seats': packed } as Intents;\n  for (let seat = 1; seat <= 3; seat++) {\n    try {\n      rowOf(w, seat);\n    } catch {\n      continue;\n    }\n    apply(w, fed, { seat, noise: 1.35 });\n  }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-091de0aa-872c-48e5-9a71-496b640c1cf3-125","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/round.ts","old_string":"    if (row.mark) {\n      row.mark.x = MATS[row.ghost.seat]?.[0] ?? 0;\n      row.mark.z = (MATS[row.ghost.seat]?.[1] ?? 0) + row.ghost.x;\n      row.mark.y = 1 + row.ghost.y;\n    }\n  }\n}","new_string":"    if (row.mark) {\n      row.mark.x = MATS[row.ghost.seat]?.[0] ?? 0;\n      row.mark.z = (MATS[row.ghost.seat]?.[1] ?? 0) + row.ghost.x;\n      row.mark.y = 1 + row.ghost.y;\n    }\n  }\n  const names = (intents as Record<string, unknown>)['game:names'];\n  if (!Array.isArray(names)) return;\n  for (const row of rows) {\n    const label = names[row.ghost.seat];\n    if (!row.mark || typeof label !== 'string') continue;\n    row.mark.text = row.ghost.on === 1 ? label : '';\n  }\n}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":565,"output_tokens":2005,"cache_read_input_tokens":172800,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"156bcaef-3f54-4dff-82f9-368c90a4c83e"}
