ated ids already visited.'),\\n    credits: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: '1 once the credits have started.' },\\n    line: str('The line id the page should say.'),\\n    result: num('The last score, 0 to 1000.'),\\n    age: num('The last Wobble Age.'),\\n    pebbles: num('Pebbles stacked so far. They are not spent.'),\\n    rank: str('The last rank word.'),\\n    prior: num(\\\"Yesterday's Wobble Age, or 0.\\\"),\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** The component `act`. One entity holds the activity. */\\nexport const ACT = defineComponent('act', {\\n  description: 'Counters for the activity that is running. Cleared when the next one starts.',\\n  fields: {\\n    phase: num('Which part of the activity is playing.'),\\n    tick: num('Steps since this activity started.'),\\n    left: num('Steps left in a box, or steps into the current part.'),\\n    done: num('1 when the activity has ended itself.'),\\n    a: num('Score part A, or a frozen class score.'),\\n    b: num('Score part B.'),\\n    c: num('Score part C.'),\\n    n: num('A count.'),\\n    m: num('Another count.'),\\n    hold: num('Steps the current target has been held.'),\\n    falls: num('Falls, topples or splashes the score counts.'),\\n    dist: num('Metres along a line, or a share.'),\\n    gx: num('Guide or goal, left to right.'),\\n    gy: num('Guide or goal, back to forward.'),\\n    px: num('A board, a marble or a guest, east.'),\\n    py: num('A board, a marble or a guest, south.'),\\n    vx: num('Speed east.'),\\n    vy: num('Speed south.'),\\n    hx: num('Lateral error, or a heading.'),\\n    hz: num('A second heading or a bias.'),\\n    calm: num('Composure, or a stored calm.'),\\n    wait: num('Steps until the next penalty or lure.'),\\n    samples: num('Steps counted toward a share.'),\\n    acc: num('Steps that counted, or a sum.'),\\n    acc2: num('A second sum, usually breath.'),\\n    top0: num('Topples at the start of a hold.'),\\n    pose: num('Which pose or tray is up.'),\\n    flags: num('Small bit flags for the activity.'),\\n    foot: num('The foot in use. 1 left, 2 right.'),\\n    text: str('A lure id, a pose id, or a short note.'),\\n    goals: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Targets and schedules.' },\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** The component `island`. */\\nexport const ISLAND = defineComponent('island', {\\n  description: 'How far the island is leaning. Geometry stays. People and drinks do not.',\\n  fields: {\\n    tiltX: num('Lean toward the west, degrees.'),\\n    tiltZ: num('Lean toward the north, degrees.'),\\n    base: num('The story lean for this day, degrees.'),\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** Something an activity spawned and must remove. */\\nexport const MADE = defineComponent('made', {\\n  description: 'An entity an activity spawned. Teardown removes every one.',\\n  fields: { tag: str('What it was.') },\\n});\\n\\n/** A neighbour's lean, sent by the hub. It never moves the local guest. */\\nexport const GHOST = defineComponent('ghost', {\\n  description: 'Another player on the next mat. Drawn from hub messages. Local play ignores it.',\\n  fields: {\\n    on: num('1 while a message has arrived for this seat.'),\\n    x: num('Their centre, left to right.'),\\n    y: num('Their centre, back to forward.'),\\n    seat: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Their mat.' },\\n    pose: num('Which class they are in.'),\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** Who an actor is. The pilot reads it. */\\nexport const ROLE = defineComponent('role', {\\n  description: 'Which member of the retreat this actor is.',\\n  fields: { who: str('guest, plumb, tare, gerald, bex, nan, gull or frog.') },\\n});\\n\\n/** A guest drifting in the finale, or a plaque, drawn as a small box. */\\nexport const MARK = defineComponent('mark', {\\n  description: 'A placed thing: a hidden pebble, a plaque, a drifting guest or a mat.',\\n  fields: {\\n    x: { type: 'number', default: 0, unit: 'm', description: 'East.' },\\n    y: { type: 'number', default: 0, unit: 'm', description: 'Up.' },\\n    z: { type: 'number', default: 0, unit: 'm', description: 'South.' },\\n    kind: str('pebble, plaque, guest, mat or cairn.'),\\n    text: str('A line id, when it has one.'),\\n    taken: num('1 once a pebble is picked up.'),\\n    follow: num('1 when a finale guest is walking with you.'),\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** A blank activity board with its own array. */\\nexport function emptyAct(): Act {\\n  return {\\n    phase: 0, tick: 0, left: 0, done: 0, a: 0, b: 0, c: 0, n: 0, m: 0, hold: 0, falls: 0,\\n    dist: 0, gx: 0, gy: 0, px: 0, py: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, hx: 0, hz: 0, calm: 0, wait: 0,\\n    samples: 0, acc: 0, acc2: 0, top0: 0, pose: 0, flags: 0, foot: 0, text: '', goals: [],\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** The first entity's component, which boot always spawns. */\\nexport function part<T>(w: World, name: string): T {\\n  const rows = w.query(name as never) as unknown as Record<string, T>[];\\n  const row = rows[0];\\n  if (!row) throw new Error(`missing ${name}`);\\n  return row[name];\\n}\\n\\n/** Records `id` once on the comma list. */\\nexport function visit(flow: Flow, id: string): void {\\n  const parts = flow.seen ? flow.seen.split(',') : [];\\n  if (!parts.includes(id)) parts.push(id);\\n  flow.seen = parts.join(',');\\n}\\n\\n/** Clears the board and keeps the same array object only after replacing it. */\\nexport function resetAct(act: Act): void {\\n  const next = emptyAct();\\n  Object.assign(act, next);\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":201}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6823f3ce-a1af-4eec-a70c-d3378bd9e5d1-36","content":"{\"type\":\"Bash\",\"output\":[101,110,103,105,110,101,47,115,105,109,47,115,116,97,116,101,46,116,115,58,54,48,58,101,120,112,111,114,116,32,116,121,112,101,32,67,111,109,112,111,110,101,110,116,68,97,116,97,32,61,32,82,101,99,111,114,100,60,115,116,114,105,110,103,44,32,117,110,107,110,111,119,110,62,59,10,45,45,45,83,80,65,87,78,45,45,45,10],\"output_for_prompt\":\"exit: 0\\nengine/sim/state.ts:60:export type ComponentData = Record<string, unknown>;\\n---SPAWN---\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"cd \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656\\\" && rg -n \\\"type ComponentData|interface ComponentData\\\" engine --glob '!**/node_modules/**' | head -20 && echo \\\"---SPAWN---\\\" && rg -n \\\"spawn\\\\(spec\\\" engine/sim --glob '*.ts' | head -20\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Find ComponentData and spawn signature\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc%2Fwork/01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc/terminal/call-6823f3ce-a1af-4eec-a70c-d3378bd9e5d1-36.log\",\"total_bytes\":88}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"4a6618f2-95e3-4592-84b9-a037ac199ec7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_472","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"ComponentData is typed as `Record<string, unknown>`.\n\nThe `Act` interface cannot be assigned to `Partial<ComponentData>` because interfaces lack index signatures and their known properties may not be compatible with `unknown`.\n\nThe error is at driver.ts:247. The `w.spawn` call passes `act: emptyAct()` into a parameter typed as `Record<string, unknown>`.\n\nFlow and island are fresh object literals, so TypeScript accepts them against `Partial<ComponentData>`. `emptyAct()` is not a fresh literal, so it fails the excess-property check. Casting to `Partial<ComponentData>` or spreading the result should fix it.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-98313af2-8fa5-404d-89f8-df11519fe517-37","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"spawn\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/state.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-98313af2-8fa5-404d-89f8-df11519fe517-38","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/state.ts","offset":1,"limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2462,"output_tokens":636,"cache_read_input_tokens":61952,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"d867c408-d9ec-4978-b528-2f5189cc1b3d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-98313af2-8fa5-404d-89f8-df11519fe517-37","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-98313af2-8fa5-404d-89f8-df11519fe517-38","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The canonical state and its hash (PLAN.md §6.5 items 4 and 6, WP 1.4, I-05; doctrine: Reproducible):\\n * component kinds declared with their field lists (registry kind `component`), the plain-data form of the sim that\\n * `state()` returns, the one 64-bit FNV-1a hash over everything a capture holds (`hash()`), per-entity digests\\n * (`trace()`), and `diffStates`, which names the fields where two states part.\\n *\\n * What the hash covers, after the format tag (`STATE_FORMAT`), in this order, each part tagged: the seed, the next\\n * entity id and the world's step rate (hz); every entity in id order, its components in name order, each\\n * component's fields in the order its kind declares them; the timers' tick count and timers (engine/core/timers.ts\\n10→ * `state()`); the settings that differ from their defaults, except `view` ones (so declaring another setting, as each\\n * scene module loaded beside this one does, never changes a hash); the state of every sim RNG stream\\n * away from its derived seed (`rng()`, `rng.entity()`); and the physics hook's state (WP 3.1: every body's\\n * translation, rotation and velocities in handle order, never Rapier's snapshot bytes). Visual streams (`fxRng`),\\n * event listeners, systems and view settings are never hashed (captures hold listeners and systems beside the data).\\n *\\n * Components are plain data (ADR-0006 amendment 3; the rules in engine/sim/entities.ts): no class instance or typed\\n * array in a field (`SIM_NOT_DATA`, a declared default included), and every field has a default (or is required), so\\n * every entity holding a kind holds all its fields, in declared order; the hash checks that shape as it reads.\\n *\\n20→ * Invariants: the hash reads no `Map` or `Set` iteration order; entities, components, settings and RNG names come in\\n * sorted order, and fields in declared order. Nothing is skipped silently: a component nobody declared\\n * (`SIM_UNKNOWN_COMPONENT`), a field its kind does not declare (`SIM_UNDECLARED_FIELD`) or a value that is not plain\\n * data (`SIM_NOT_DATA`, naming the entity and field) throws. A component kind's name is the entity's property\\n * (`e.position`), a lower-case word; its fields are schema.ts fields holding data, never hooks.\\n * `hashState(w.state())` equals `w.hash()`.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n30→ * defineComponent('health', { description: 'Hit points.', fields: { hp: { type: 'number', default: 10, description: 'Left.' } } }, reg);\\n * const table = componentTable(reg);\\n * table.make('health', { hp: 7 }, 'a test'); // { hp: 7 }\\n * const view = { seed: 1, nextId: 2, hz: 60, entities: [{ id: 1, health: { hp: 7 } }], timers: { ticks: 0, nextId: 1, timers: [] }, settings: {}, rng: {} };\\n * hashState(view, table) === hashState(structuredClone(view), table); // true\\n * diffStates(view, { ...view, nextId: 3 }); // [{ path: 'nextId', a: 2, b: 3 }]\\n * @see engine/sim/state.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, didYouMean } from '../core/log';\\nimport { Fnv64, TAG, type Canonical } from '../core/hash';\\n40→import { registry as sharedRegistry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\\nimport { checkField, isPlainObject, parse, show, type EntryOf, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\\nimport type { SettingValue } from '../core/settings';\\nimport type { TimersState } from '../core/timers';\\nimport { componentNames, eachField, feedData, notData } from './entities';\\n\\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\\nexport const STATE_CODES = defineCodes('sim', {\\n  SIM_UNKNOWN_COMPONENT: {\\n    template: '{name} is not a component kind{suggestion}',\\n50→    fix: 'declare it with defineComponent({name}, { description, fields }) before an entity holds it (node x describe component lists the declared kinds)',\\n    doc: 'Raised by the world (engine/sim/world.ts) and the hash (engine/sim/state.ts) for an entity property, a `spawn`, `add`, `remove` or `query` name, or a captured component that no `defineComponent` declared: the hash covers declared components only, so an undeclared one is refused rather than skipped.',\\n  },\\n  SIM_UNDECLARED_FIELD: {\\n    template: 'entity {id} has {name}.{field}, a field the component kind {name} does not declare{suggestion}',\\n    fix: 'declare the field in defineComponent({name}, { fields }) or stop writing it: the hash and captures read the declared fields only, so an undeclared one would let two different states match',\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** One component's data: its fields by name, plain data (numbers, strings, booleans, null, arrays, plain objects). */\\n60→export type ComponentData = Record<string, unknown>;\\n\\n/** An entity as plain data: its id and its components by kind name. */\\nexport interface EntityData {\\n  readonly id: number;\\n  readonly [name: string]: unknown;\\n}\\n\\n/** The components of an untyped world: any declared kind, by name. */\\nexport type AnyComponents = Record<string, ComponentData>;\\n70→\\n/** An entity: its id and the components it holds, by kind name (`e.position`). */\\nexport type Entity<C extends object = AnyComponents> = { readonly id: number } & {\\n  [K in Exclude<keyof C, 'id'>]?: C[K];\\n};\\n\\n/** An entity known to hold the components `K` (what `query` returns). */\\nexport type With<C extends object, K extends keyof C> = Entity<C> & { [P in K]: C[P] };\\n\\n/** What `spawn` takes: components by kind name, each with any of its fields (the rest take their defaults). */\\n80→export type SpawnSpec<C extends object> = { [K in Exclude<keyof C, 'id'>]?: Partial<C[K]> };\\n\\n/** The physics part of the world's state, hashed and captured with the rest (WP 3.1 plugs Rapier in; §6.5 items 5–7). */\\nexport interface PhysicsHook {\\n  /** What the hash covers: every body's translation, rotation and velocities in handle order (a Float64Array). */\\n  state(): Canonical;\\n  /** The physics part of a capture: Rapier's snapshot bytes and what else restoring needs. Never hashed. */\\n  capture(): unknown;\\n  /** Puts back what `capture()` returned, so the next step continues exactly. */\\n  restore(data: unknown): void;\\n90→}\\n\\n/** A component kind as `defineComponent` stores it in the registry. */\\nexport interface ComponentKind<S extends Schema = Schema> {\\n  readonly id: string;\\n  readonly kind: 'component';\\n  readonly description: string;\\n  readonly fields: S;\\n}\\n\\n100→/** The data type of a component of kind fields `S`, as `make` returns it: writable, defaults filled. */\\nexport type ComponentOf<S extends Schema> = { -readonly [K in keyof EntryOf<S>]: EntryOf<S>[K] };\\n\\n/**\\n * What the hash reads, live or stored: the ids, entities (in id order), timers, settings, RNG states and the physics\\n * hook's state. `state()` returns one; the world hashes its live parts the same way.\\n */\\nexport interface StateView {\\n  readonly seed: number;\\n  readonly nextId: number;\\n110→  /** The world's step rate, fixed when it is made. */\\n  readonly hz: number;\\n  readonly entities: readonly EntityData[];\\n  readonly timers: TimersState;\\n  readonly settings: Readonly<Record<string, SettingValue>>;\\n  readonly rng: Readonly<Record<string, number>>;\\n  readonly physics?: Canonical;\\n}\\n\\n/** The sim as plain data: what `world.state()` returns and the hash covers. */\\n120→export interface WorldState extends StateView {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The canonical state and its hash (PLAN.md §6.5 items 4 and 6, WP 1.4, I-05; doctrine: Reproducible):\\n * component kinds declared with their field lists (registry kind `component`), the plain-data form of the sim that\\n * `state()` returns, the one 64-bit FNV-1a hash over everything a capture holds (`hash()`), per-entity digests\\n * (`trace()`), and `diffStates`, which names the fields where two states part.\\n *\\n * What the hash covers, after the format tag (`STATE_FORMAT`), in this order, each part tagged: the seed, the next\\n * entity id and the world's step rate (hz); every entity in id order, its components in name order, each\\n * component's fields in the order its kind declares them; the timers' tick count and timers (engine/core/timers.ts\\n10→ * `state()`); the settings that differ from their defaults, except `view` ones (so declaring another setting, as each\\n * scene module loaded beside this one does, never changes a hash); the state of every sim RNG stream\\n * away from its derived seed (`rng()`, `rng.entity()`); and the physics hook's state (WP 3.1: every body's\\n * translation, rotation and velocities in handle order, never Rapier's snapshot bytes). Visual streams (`fxRng`),\\n * event listeners, systems and view settings are never hashed (captures hold listeners and systems beside the data).\\n *\\n * Components are plain data (ADR-0006 amendment 3; the rules in engine/sim/entities.ts): no class instance or typed\\n * array in a field (`SIM_NOT_DATA`, a declared default included), and every field has a default (or is required), so\\n * every entity holding a kind holds all its fields, in declared order; the hash checks that shape as it reads.\\n *\\n20→ * Invariants: the hash reads no `Map` or `Set` iteration order; entities, components, settings and RNG names come in\\n * sorted order, and fields in declared order. Nothing is skipped silently: a component nobody declared\\n * (`SIM_UNKNOWN_COMPONENT`), a field its kind does not declare (`SIM_UNDECLARED_FIELD`) or a value that is not plain\\n * data (`SIM_NOT_DATA`, naming the entity and field) throws. A component kind's name is the entity's property\\n * (`e.position`), a lower-case word; its fields are schema.ts fields holding data, never hooks.\\n * `hashState(w.state())` equals `w.hash()`.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n30→ * defineComponent('health', { description: 'Hit points.', fields: { hp: { type: 'number', default: 10, description: 'Left.' } } }, reg);\\n * const table = componentTable(reg);\\n * table.make('health', { hp: 7 }, 'a test'); // { hp: 7 }\\n * const view = { seed: 1, nextId: 2, hz: 60, entities: [{ id: 1, health: { hp: 7 } }], timers: { ticks: 0, nextId: 1, timers: [] }, settings: {}, rng: {} };\\n * hashState(view, table) === hashState(structuredClone(view), table); // true\\n * diffStates(view, { ...view, nextId: 3 }); // [{ path: 'nextId', a: 2, b: 3 }]\\n * @see engine/sim/state.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, didYouMean } from '../core/log';\\nimport { Fnv64, TAG, type Canonical } from '../core/hash';\\n40→import { registry as sharedRegistry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\\nimport { checkField, isPlainObject, parse, show, type EntryOf, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\\nimport type { SettingValue } from '../core/settings';\\nimport type { TimersState } from '../core/timers';\\nimport { componentNames, eachField, feedData, notData } from './entities';\\n\\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\\nexport const STATE_CODES = defineCodes('sim', {\\n  SIM_UNKNOWN_COMPONENT: {\\n    template: '{name} is not a component kind{suggestion}',\\n50→    fix: 'declare it with defineComponent({name}, { description, fields }) before an entity holds it (node x describe component lists the declared kinds)',\\n    doc: 'Raised by the world (engine/sim/world.ts) and the hash (engine/sim/state.ts) for an entity property, a `spawn`, `add`, `remove` or `query` name, or a captured component that no `defineComponent` declared: the hash covers declared components only, so an undeclared one is refused rather than skipped.',\\n  },\\n  SIM_UNDECLARED_FIELD: {\\n    template: 'entity {id} has {name}.{field}, a field the component kind {name} does not declare{suggestion}',\\n    fix: 'declare the field in defineComponent({name}, { fields }) or stop writing it: the hash and captures read the declared fields only, so an undeclared one would let two different states match',\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** One component's data: its fields by name, plain data (numbers, strings, booleans, null, arrays, plain objects). */\\n60→export type ComponentData = Record<string, unknown>;\\n\\n/** An entity as plain data: its id and its components by kind name. */\\nexport interface EntityData {\\n  readonly id: number;\\n  readonly [name: string]: unknown;\\n}\\n\\n/** The components of an untyped world: any declared kind, by name. */\\nexport type AnyComponents = Record<string, ComponentData>;\\n70→\\n/** An entity: its id and the components it holds, by kind name (`e.position`). */\\nexport type Entity<C extends object = AnyComponents> = { readonly id: number } & {\\n  [K in Exclude<keyof C, 'id'>]?: C[K];\\n};\\n\\n/** An entity known to hold the components `K` (what `query` returns). */\\nexport type With<C extends object, K extends keyof C> = Entity<C> & { [P in K]: C[P] };\\n\\n/** What `spawn` takes: components by kind name, each with any of its fields (the rest take their defaults). */\\n80→export type SpawnSpec<C extends object> = { [K in Exclude<keyof C, 'id'>]?: Partial<C[K]> };\\n\\n/** The physics part of the world's state, hashed and captured with the rest (WP 3.1 plugs Rapier in; §6.5 items 5–7). */\\nexport interface PhysicsHook {\\n  /** What the hash covers: every body's translation, rotation and velocities in handle order (a Float64Array). */\\n  state(): Canonical;\\n  /** The physics part of a capture: Rapier's snapshot bytes and what else restoring needs. Never hashed. */\\n  capture(): unknown;\\n  /** Puts back what `capture()` returned, so the next step continues exactly. */\\n  restore(data: unknown): void;\\n90→}\\n\\n/** A component kind as `defineComponent` stores it in the registry. */\\nexport interface ComponentKind<S extends Schema = Schema> {\\n  readonly id: string;\\n  readonly kind: 'component';\\n  readonly description: string;\\n  readonly fields: S;\\n}\\n\\n100→/** The data type of a component of kind fields `S`, as `make` returns it: writable, defaults filled. */\\nexport type ComponentOf<S extends Schema> = { -readonly [K in keyof EntryOf<S>]: EntryOf<S>[K] };\\n\\n/**\\n * What the hash reads, live or stored: the ids, entities (in id order), timers, settings, RNG states and the physics\\n * hook's state. `state()` returns one; the world hashes its live parts the same way.\\n */\\nexport interface StateView {\\n  readonly seed: number;\\n  readonly nextId: number;\\n110→  /** The world's step rate, fixed when it is made. */\\n  readonly hz: number;\\n  readonly entities: readonly EntityData[];\\n  readonly timers: TimersState;\\n  readonly settings: Readonly<Record<string, SettingValue>>;\\n  readonly rng: Readonly<Record<string, number>>;\\n  readonly physics?: Canonical;\\n}\\n\\n/** The sim as plain data: what `world.state()` returns and the hash covers. */\\n120→export interface WorldState extends StateView {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/state.ts\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The canonical state and its hash (PLAN.md §6.5 items 4 and 6, WP 1.4, I-05; doctrine: Reproducible):\\n * component kinds declared with their field lists (registry kind `component`), the plain-data form of the sim that\\n * `state()` returns, the one 64-bit FNV-1a hash over everything a capture holds (`hash()`), per-entity digests\\n * (`trace()`), and `diffStates`, which names the fields where two states part.\\n *\\n * What the hash covers, after the format tag (`STATE_FORMAT`), in this order, each part tagged: the seed, the next\\n * entity id and the world's step rate (hz); every entity in id order, its components in name order, each\\n * component's fields in the order its kind declares them; the timers' tick count and timers (engine/core/timers.ts\\n * `state()`); the settings that differ from their defaults, except `view` ones (so declaring another setting, as each\\n * scene module loaded beside this one does, never changes a hash); the state of every sim RNG stream\\n * away from its derived seed (`rng()`, `rng.entity()`); and the physics hook's state (WP 3.1: every body's\\n * translation, rotation and velocities in handle order, never Rapier's snapshot bytes). Visual streams (`fxRng`),\\n * event listeners, systems and view settings are never hashed (captures hold listeners and systems beside the data).\\n *\\n * Components are plain data (ADR-0006 amendment 3; the rules in engine/sim/entities.ts): no class instance or typed\\n * array in a field (`SIM_NOT_DATA`, a declared default included), and every field has a default (or is required), so\\n * every entity holding a kind holds all its fields, in declared order; the hash checks that shape as it reads.\\n *\\n * Invariants: the hash reads no `Map` or `Set` iteration order; entities, components, settings and RNG names come in\\n * sorted order, and fields in declared order. Nothing is skipped silently: a component nobody declared\\n * (`SIM_UNKNOWN_COMPONENT`), a field its kind does not declare (`SIM_UNDECLARED_FIELD`) or a value that is not plain\\n * data (`SIM_NOT_DATA`, naming the entity and field) throws. A component kind's name is the entity's property\\n * (`e.position`), a lower-case word; its fields are schema.ts fields holding data, never hooks.\\n * `hashState(w.state())` equals `w.hash()`.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n * defineComponent('health', { description: 'Hit points.', fields: { hp: { type: 'number', default: 10, description: 'Left.' } } }, reg);\\n * const table = componentTable(reg);\\n * table.make('health', { hp: 7 }, 'a test'); // { hp: 7 }\\n * const view = { seed: 1, nextId: 2, hz: 60, entities: [{ id: 1, health: { hp: 7 } }], timers: { ticks: 0, nextId: 1, timers: [] }, settings: {}, rng: {} };\\n * hashState(view, table) === hashState(structuredClone(view), table); // true\\n * diffStates(view, { ...view, nextId: 3 }); // [{ path: 'nextId', a: 2, b: 3 }]\\n * @see engine/sim/state.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, didYouMean } from '../core/log';\\nimport { Fnv64, TAG, type Canonical } from '../core/hash';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\\nimport { checkField, isPlainObject, parse, show, type EntryOf, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\\nimport type { SettingValue } from '../core/settings';\\nimport type { TimersState } from '../core/timers';\\nimport { componentNames, eachField, feedData, notData } from './entities';\\n\\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\\nexport const STATE_CODES = defineCodes('sim', {\\n  SIM_UNKNOWN_COMPONENT: {\\n    template: '{name} is not a component kind{suggestion}',\\n    fix: 'declare it with defineComponent({name}, { description, fields }) before an entity holds it (node x describe component lists the declared kinds)',\\n    doc: 'Raised by the world (engine/sim/world.ts) and the hash (engine/sim/state.ts) for an entity property, a `spawn`, `add`, `remove` or `query` name, or a captured component that no `defineComponent` declared: the hash covers declared components only, so an undeclared one is refused rather than skipped.',\\n  },\\n  SIM_UNDECLARED_FIELD: {\\n    template: 'entity {id} has {name}.{field}, a field the component kind {name} does not declare{suggestion}',\\n    fix: 'declare the field in defineComponent({name}, { fields }) or stop writing it: the hash and captures read the declared fields only, so an undeclared one would let two different states match',\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** One component's data: its fields by name, plain data (numbers, strings, booleans, null, arrays, plain objects). */\\nexport type ComponentData = Record<string, unknown>;\\n\\n/** An entity as plain data: its id and its components by kind name. */\\nexport interface EntityData {\\n  readonly id: number;\\n  readonly [name: string]: unknown;\\n}\\n\\n/** The components of an untyped world: any declared kind, by name. */\\nexport type AnyComponents = Record<string, ComponentData>;\\n\\n/** An entity: its id and the components it holds, by kind name (`e.position`). */\\nexport type Entity<C extends object = AnyComponents> = { readonly id: number } & {\\n  [K in Exclude<keyof C, 'id'>]?: C[K];\\n};\\n\\n/** An entity known to hold the components `K` (what `query` returns). */\\nexport type With<C extends object, K extends keyof C> = Entity<C> & { [P in K]: C[P] };\\n\\n/** What `spawn` takes: components by kind name, each with any of its fields (the rest take their defaults). */\\nexport type SpawnSpec<C extends object> = { [K in Exclude<keyof C, 'id'>]?: Partial<C[K]> };\\n\\n/** The physics part of the world's state, hashed and captured with the rest (WP 3.1 plugs Rapier in; §6.5 items 5–7). */\\nexport interface PhysicsHook {\\n  /** What the hash covers: every body's translation, rotation and velocities in handle order (a Float64Array). */\\n  state(): Canonical;\\n  /** The physics part of a capture: Rapier's snapshot bytes and what else restoring needs. Never hashed. */\\n  capture(): unknown;\\n  /** Puts back what `capture()` returned, so the next step continues exactly. */\\n  restore(data: unknown): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** A component kind as `defineComponent` stores it in the registry. */\\nexport interface ComponentKind<S extends Schema = Schema> {\\n  readonly id: string;\\n  readonly kind: 'component';\\n  readonly description: string;\\n  readonly fields: S;\\n}\\n\\n/** The data type of a component of kind fields `S`, as `make` returns it: writable, defaults filled. */\\nexport type ComponentOf<S extends Schema> = { -readonly [K in keyof EntryOf<S>]: EntryOf<S>[K] };\\n\\n/**\\n * What the hash reads, live or stored: the ids, entities (in id order), timers, settings, RNG states and the physics\\n * hook's state. `state()` returns one; the world hashes its live parts the same way.\\n */\\nexport interface StateView {\\n  readonly seed: number;\\n  readonly nextId: number;\\n  /** The world's step rate, fixed when it is made. */\\n  readonly hz: number;\\n  readonly entities: readonly EntityData[];\\n  readonly timers: TimersState;\\n  readonly settings: Readonly<Record<string, SettingValue>>;\\n  readonly rng: Readonly<Record<string, number>>;\\n  readonly physics?: Canonical;\\n}\\n\\n/** The sim as plain data: what `world.state()` returns and the hash covers. */\\nexport interface WorldState extends StateView {\\n\",\"total_lines\":361}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"13d19fe8-8243-4024-b32c-cb6fb54ad43f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_473","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"World is untyped. C defaults to Record<string, ComponentData>. SpawnSpec becomes a partial mapping of component data.\n\nAct is incompatible with Partial<ComponentData> due to the index signature. Spreading emptyAct() into a fresh object literal looks like the cleanest fix.\n\nSpreading emptyAct() into a fresh object literal still yields type Act, which is not assignable. The simplest fix is casting emptyAct() to Record<string, unknown> directly in driver.ts boot. Only one line triggered the type error.\n\nAll events/*.ts files need their import path corrected from `../../../engine/sim-api` to `../../../../engine/sim-api`. The type errors list garden, group, kit, line, morning, paddle, pond, pose, and tilt. No tsconfig paths are involved; the module resolution is simply wrong.\n\nThe import path errors are puzzling because vitest previously passed. The files may have been correct before and were later corrupted, or a different copy is being checked. Node will verify the actual file paths.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b19810da-49a6-4aca-9f74-a2940c24b698-39","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656\" && ls vitest.config.ts vite.config.ts 2>&1 && echo \"---RESOLVE---\" && node --input-type=module -e \"\nimport { createRequire } from 'module';\nimport { existsSync } from 'fs';\nimport { dirname, resolve } from 'path';\nconst from = resolve('labs/game/scenes/events/morning.ts');\nconst target = resolve(dirname(from), '../../../engine/sim-api.ts');\nconst target4 = resolve(dirname(from), '../../../../engine/sim-api.ts');\nconsole.log('from events 3', target, existsSync(target));\nconsole.log('from events 4', target4, existsSync(target4));\nconst fromScene = resolve('lab