0,\"match_count\":8,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc%2Fwork/01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc/goal/plan.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":3,\"content\":\"## Goal kind\"},{\"line_number\":6,\"content\":\"## Acceptance criteria\"},{\"line_number\":17,\"content\":\"## Verification plan\"},{\"line_number\":26,\"content\":\"## Non-goals\"},{\"line_number\":34,\"content\":\"## Assumed scope\"},{\"line_number\":39,\"content\":\"## Implementation approach\"},{\"line_number\":44,\"content\":\"## Task checklist\"},{\"line_number\":54,\"content\":\"## Risks / Contradictions\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2515b1f5-c0b4-4d3c-9116-12f8807aaab7-64","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/STAGE.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"total_lines\":1}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"ba144d3d-f490-44eb-b846-e6c641a85daa"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_486","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reading the goal plan verification section.","signature":"NSX+iFD9BNl85NPaNdOTWO3sAvE7fKsMdVkkf3JTwElikDw1REe8iep0l3uOxb57TQBJLif2XNn16BuuX9IsG1chL5L+R3Lm3CZjGqTgguDt"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0ba0b4d3-6d7e-4220-9a32-0283e1b0a978-65","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc%2Fwork/01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc/goal/plan.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":591,"output_tokens":112,"cache_read_input_tokens":87424,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"013805ec-2e47-43cb-9a83-efcb1c0abca8"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0ba0b4d3-6d7e-4220-9a32-0283e1b0a978-65","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Plan: Build PLAN.md’s original Wii Fit–inspired balance retreat and hand in TASK.md’s files\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. **Hand-in, title, and records.** The work root contains `PROGRESS.md`, `exit-interview.json`, and one self-contained HTML file. The HTML and the dev subfolder share the basename `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656` (SOURCE keeps the space in `Wii Fit`; `{Title}` is the on-screen title, with only OS-illegal characters sanitized, and that sanitization noted in `PROGRESS.md`). `{Title}` was chosen by executing a real RNG over a saved list of 50 playful riffs on “Wii Fit,” and that list plus the pick are in the dev folder. The page shows `{Title}` on the title screen. `exit-interview.json` is one JSON object in TASK.md’s exact shape, every value filled, `usage` exactly `added on import`, and its Source Information plus the three feedback lists match the in-game About/Credits screen in the same order. `aiHub.genre` is `Sports`, `aiHub.source` is `Wii Fit`, `aiHub.type` is `Game`, `aiHub.players` is `1–4`. The word `Wii` appears in-game only on that source line and the hub source field. There is no weight, BMI, calorie, or body-size scoring, and none of these source names: Fit Age, Fit Credits, Fit Piggy Bank, Body Test, Wuhu, or the source’s minigame, menu, or melody names. Opening the HTML does not need the network. It contains no `data:audio`, `.mp3`, `.wav`, or `.ogg` payload.\\n\\n2. **One balance verb, every shipped activity.** Lean (left stick or D-pad, WASD or arrows, pointer-locked mouse), left foot, right foot, and both feet are the only activity inputs, and a new activity changes what the weight moves, not how it is moved. Centre-of-balance is a point in a unit disc. With no input, time inside radius 0.22 is well under half (sway stays slow). A held full lean topples. Calm from breathing with the guide reduces sway. Topple stumbles and recentres; it is never a game over. Each activity, started from its own fresh state, scores 0–1000, maps to Present / Adequate / Composed / Serene / Unsettling (thresholds 0 / 300 / 550 / 750 / 900), awards 1–5 pebbles by rank, ends itself on a time box if the pad is put down, and leaves no stray bodies. On 10 seeds the perfect bot scores at least 750, the human-like bot (about 250 ms late, gain about 1.2) at least 550, the sloppy bot (about 350 ms, gain about 0.8) at least 300, and idle at most 500 and below the human-like bot. Random input does not throw. These are present and playable: Morning Check (still ring, reach, one-foot, Wobble Age from 18 to 82), Pose Class for Seated Nothing, Patient Chair, Heron, Archer, Sideways Comma, Folded Napkin, Polite Bridge, and Lighthouse (enter, hold, release; the body scrub follows the thumb), Still Pond (only matched breathing is correct; other input costs composure; a lure is not a real pause; doing nothing is Adequate), The Line, Paddle Glide, Sand Garden, and Great Tilt steps storm, everyone-east, centre-stone (island tilt follows centre-of-balance), and dawn. Reps Hall, Step Class, Hoop Patrol, Cliff Plunge, Island Jog’s race, Great Tilt counterweights, expert variants, and outfits are either fully playable or removed in that cut order with the day list reflowed and no leftover mention.\\n10→\\n3. **Five-day retreat you can finish.** A third-person island hub has the stations and the cast Tare, Plumb, Gerald, Bex, Old Nan, the Gull, and the Frog. Walking is allowed, and every programme or noticeboard entry can also “Go” without crossing the island. Five days each do a Morning Check plus their activities, then sleep, stamps, and a short remark. Pebbles are never spent; they stack on a cairn. Hidden pebbles and creeping plaques exist. Saves restore day, results, pebbles, finds, outfits, bests, and settings; erase asks inside the game, not `confirm()`. A shipped auto playthrough from a fresh save, on 3 seeds, visits every shipped day, activity, and finale step and reaches credits without throwing or a softlock. After credits, free play and a new daily check remain, and the ferry does not come back. At least 200 lines, none longer than two short sentences, include PLAN.md’s seed lines; Plumb has no exclamation marks. All music, effects, and voices are code. Fresh-save music volume is 0.1. The same line always babbles the same way. Songs and syllables render non-silent. Pose and lean clips are scrubbed from balance or pose progress, not played as a canned squat at the player.\\n\\n4. **10-foot shell.** The same screens serve a standard-mapped pad, keyboard, and mouse. Prompts follow the last device in the same frame: PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox glyphs (A B X Y, LB RB LT RT) after the Settings switch, key caps and mouse buttons after those inputs. Hover moves menu focus; click selects. Body text at 1920×1080 is at least 28 px; menus have at most six rows; results are one rank, one number, one sentence, not a dense data page. Pause opens Resume, Restart, Back to the island, Settings, Controls, Dev Mode, About/Credits, and Quit. Dev Mode, absent in a hub session, has live sliders for the numeric `game.*` tunables in PLAN.md (including wobble, breath, and pebble multiplier) and a reset to defaults, plus jumps to a day, activity, or finale step. Attract mode starts after 10 seconds without input on a front-end menu, loops through several activities (the driver may cheat), exits on key, click, or pad, and does not write the save. A touch-only profile shows “Controller or keyboard required” and a Settings control that opens by tap, with no on-screen touch play, while attract still runs. Without WebGPU the page shows a plain message naming current Chrome or Edge, not a blank page. Keyboard bindings can be rebound in Controls.\\n\\n5. **Couch Group Class and AI Hub ghost sessions.** Up to four players join mats on one screen (pad, or keyboard and mouse for one seat). Empty seats become CPU guests unless Settings turns them off. A round is three short classes dealt from one seed, then a podium. In AI Hub the mode is ghost: meta tags `hub:session` 1, `hub:session-players` 1-4, `hub:session-mode` ghost, `hub:session-minutes` 3, goal at most 60 characters, how-to at most 80 characters, `hub:webgpu` required, `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` 1-4, `hub:source` Wii Fit. The fetched session client is pasted unmodified and is byte-identical in the HTML. Its SHA-256 is `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a` (client 1.4.0). If the fetched file’s own banner is a newer client, record the new hash in `PROGRESS.md` and still inject those exact bytes. `?aihub` query keys are stripped before engine boot so unknown keys do not kill the engine. A session skips title, attract, and dev mode; pause does not pause the sim; `ready()` is reached with the engine actually running. Ghosts show the other players’ leans and do not affect local play. The hub harness passes for 2, 3, and 4 players and for host-leave: `__hubCheck.pass`, `body[data-complete=\\\"true\\\"]`, every frame `__engine.ready === true` and zero engine errors, a ghost present at 2 players, and no console line starting with `[AIHub]`. With no hub, the game is the full single-player build.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. **gating:** In the dev workspace, add or extend tests that call the shipped balance step and each shipped activity’s own setup, step, score, and bot from a fresh sim. Do not reimplement the model, mock the unit under test, or start past setup. Assert criterion 2’s bands, self-end, age range, Still Pond penalties, teardown, and no `NaN`. Run `node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs` from the dev folder (full run, not only `--quick`) and write stdout to `{SCRATCH}/verify.log`. Pass only if the exit code is 0 and the log has no failure lines and one final count line of zero failures. Also write `{SCRATCH}/npm-test.log` and `{SCRATCH}/npm-check.log` for `npm test` and `npm run check`, both passing. `npm run check` shows the engine matches its lock, or `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` lists the exact engine diff and why.\\n2. **gating:** The same verify command (or a node test it runs) drives the shipped auto/director path from a fresh save on 3 seeds, not a hand-rolled copy of the day table. `{SCRATCH}/verify.log` must show each seed reaching credits. Replay capture/restore of the shipped goldens continues exactly; that result is in the same log.\\n20→3. **gating:** Launch the handed-in HTML twice, from `file://`, in headless Chromium (`CHROMIUM_PATH` = the headless shell, flags `--no-sandbox --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`). Both runs must agree: `__engine.ready === true`, `__engine.errors` empty, no WebGPU downgrade error, `window.__game` (screen, attract, last device, glyph set, volumes, day, event, focus) shows the title screen and `{Title}`, and the music volume is 0.1. The canvas’s drawing width and height equal the requested view and are non-zero. A scripted standard-mapping pad or a key, applied through the real menu path, changes `__game` the same way both times. Save `{SCRATCH}/boot-1.log`, `{SCRATCH}/boot-2.log`, `{SCRATCH}/boot-1.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/boot-2.png`. Primary observable is that state, not the bitmap. If the screenshot is fully blank or uncleared while those state checks pass, write `{SCRATCH}/webgpu-readback.txt` and do not fail the launch for pixels alone (known SwiftShader limit). If a readback shows a partial scene that disagrees with `__game`, that is a failure. If Chromium cannot start, save the error as `{SCRATCH}/launch-error.txt`; node checks in steps 1–2 and the static checks in step 5 are then the bar. A started page with `ready` false or a blank state is never that fallback.\\n4. **gating:** Browser-drive the built page (same Chromium) and record `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`. Must show: PlayStation glyphs before any Xbox setting, Xbox glyphs after the setting, prompts switching to keys and to mouse in the same frame as those inputs, hover moving focus, attract beginning at 10–11 s of idle and leaving on a key, a click, and a pad press with the save unchanged, a dev slider changing live behaviour and Reset restoring the default, About text containing every Source Information field and each feedback answer, and at 1920×1080 every visible text node at least 28 px and no menu over six rows. WebKit (no WebGPU here) shows the Chrome-or-Edge message. An iPhone and a tablet Chromium profile show the controller-or-keyboard line, open Settings by `touchscreen.tap`, draw no touch stick, and still run attract.\\n5. **gating:** Serve the built HTML and the fetched harness files with a single `127.0.0.1` process on an OS-picked port; stop only that PID. Run the harness for `players=2`, `3`, `4`, and `players=3&scenario=host-leave` (latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5). Write `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`. Pass only if each run has `__hubCheck.pass`, `data-complete=\\\"true\\\"`, per-frame engine ready and zero engine errors, a ghost at 2 players, and no `[AIHub]` console line. `{SCRATCH}/hub-client.sha` is the injected client hash and matches criterion 5. A no-session load still reaches the title. Standalone client check: Enter, Space, Enter, Space leaves the client present and inactive, leaves `Math.random` unseeded, draws the screen, and adds no errors.\\n6. **gating:** Static pass on the work root: HTML and folder names, `exit-interview.json` parses and matches About, `PROGRESS.md` exists, game README says what the game is and which judgment calls were made, `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` is specific, and a search of the game sources for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, and `stub` is clean except test wording. Audio proof (song and syllable render, music 0.1) is in `{SCRATCH}/verify.log` or `{SCRATCH}/audio.log`.\\n7. **evidence:** 1920×1080 screenshots under `{SCRATCH}/shots/` of title, island, Pose Class HUD, Still Pond with a lure, The Line, Great Tilt wide shot, results, pause, Dev Mode, and About. Missing shots do not fail when steps 1–6 passed, including an honest launch fallback.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- Recreating Wii Fit’s BMI or weight test, trainer look, Balance Board, Miis, Wuhu Island, Fit Bank, logos, fonts, or melodies.\\n- Frame-rate optimization, except the hub’s 20-second `ready()` deadline.\\n- Cloning the ai-hub repository, adding npm dependencies, or `git init` / commits in the dev folder.\\n30→- Shared-world or more than four players, real gamepads, iOS Safari, and listening tests by ear.\\n- A second desktop-only layout, or touch controls beyond the required message and Settings button.\\n- A half-built cut-line activity left in the menu.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\nWork root is the folder that holds `STAGE.md`, `PLAN.md`, and `TASK.md`. The dev subfolder is a my-3dge full workspace created with that repo’s `new-game` tool (clone only for the generator, then delete it), then `npm ci` only. Game code lives on top of the read-only engine. Hub `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, and `round.js` are fetched from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/`, not from a clone. Deliverables in the work root: the one HTML file, `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`.\\n\\nWii Fit (Nintendo, 2007) was checked against public guides: daily Body Test (weight, BMI, centre-of-balance, Wii Fit Age), yoga holds with a breath guide, strength reps, aerobics (step, hoop, jog), lean-steered balance minigames, a trainer, and a time bank. PLAN.md already maps those into an original wobble game and bans body-size metrics and source names. Do not add activities the plan does not list.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\n40→Follow PLAN.md for design detail. This section is not a second spec: a structure that meets the criteria is acceptable even if file names differ, as long as the engine’s own workspace rules still hold (`labs/game` is where this engine mounts a game).\\n\\nKeep the balance step, activity rules, bots, and day tables as pure sim code with no rendering or DOM, so node tests drive them directly. The page only reads sim state, plays code audio, and sends input or menu choices back through the engine’s recorded channels. One bot writer produces perfect, human-like, sloppy, idle, attract, and CPU-guest input. Days, poses, charts, trays, and lines stay data. Ship a smaller complete loop early (boot, one activity, one-file HTML, hub `ready`) and add activities without breaking that loop. Put the single verify command in front of the node tests, the three-seed auto playthrough, audio renders, and the browser and harness stages. Publish `window.__game` for those checks. Write About copy and `exit-interview.json` from the same answers before the final HTML build.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Save 50 titles, RNG-pick one, create the named dev folder with `new-game`, `npm ci`, and a work-root `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- [ ] One-file HTML build, unmodified hub client and tags, tiny session scene, verify command skeleton, harness green with the engine actually ready.\\n- [ ] Balance model, maps, disc, glyphs, Morning Check, four bots, dev sliders, and the score-band tests.\\n- [ ] Scrubbed clips, Guest and Plumb, Pose Class, code voices, island, flow, saves, results.\\n- [ ] Still Pond, The Line, Paddle Glide, Sand Garden, any later activities not cut, Great Tilt, and the 3-seed auto path to credits.\\n50→- [ ] Same-screen Group Class and hub ghosts; harness 2, 3, 4, and host-leave.\\n- [ ] Attract, settings, controls, About, touch-only and no-WebGPU pages, songs, and 200+ lines.\\n- [ ] `exit-interview.json`, HTML copied to the work root, full verify, and two consistent boots with logs under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- TASK.md says a headless WebGPU screenshot can be blank and to trust game state. A fully blank bitmap with `ready` and a real `__game` screen is that limit, not an automatic fail. A readable but empty or partial frame that disagrees with `__game` is a game bug.\\n- The live client fetched while writing this plan is banner `1.4.0`, matching PLAN.md’s pin. If the upstream file moves, the unmodified fetched bytes win over the old hash, and the new hash goes in `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- The required basename contains a space because SOURCE is `Wii Fit`. That is intentional, not a reason to drop the source token.\\n- PLAN.md forbids `git init` in the dev folder even though the engine guide says to commit. Do not init or commit.\\n- Other agents share ports and memory. Do not bind 5173, do not kill processes you did not start, and do not run more than two browsers. `earlyoom` killing a browser is memory pressure, not a game bug to retry in a loop.\\n60→- Great Tilt’s session scene must stay small: SwiftShader has needed most of the harness’s 20 s just to boot. The island must not load in a hub session.\\n- Firefox has no WebGPU here. Only Chromium can run the game; WebKit is only for the no-WebGPU message.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Plan: Build PLAN.md’s original Wii Fit–inspired balance retreat and hand in TASK.md’s files\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. **Hand-in, title, and records.** The work root contains `PROGRESS.md`, `exit-interview.json`, and one self-contained HTML file. The HTML and the dev subfolder share the basename `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656` (SOURCE keeps the space in `Wii Fit`; `{Title}` is the on-screen title, with only OS-illegal characters sanitized, and that sanitization noted in `PROGRESS.md`). `{Title}` was chosen by executing a real RNG over a saved list of 50 playful riffs on “Wii Fit,” and that list plus the pick are in the dev folder. The page shows `{Title}` on the title screen. `exit-interview.json` is one JSON object in TASK.md’s exact shape, every value filled, `usage` exactly `added on import`, and its Source Information plus the three feedback lists match the in-game About/Credits screen in the same order. `aiHub.genre` is `Sports`, `aiHub.source` is `Wii Fit`, `aiHub.type` is `Game`, `aiHub.players` is `1–4`. The word `Wii` appears in-game only on that source line and the hub source field. There is no weight, BMI, calorie, or body-size scoring, and none of these source names: Fit Age, Fit Credits, Fit Piggy Bank, Body Test, Wuhu, or the source’s minigame, menu, or melody names. Opening the HTML does not need the network. It contains no `data:audio`, `.mp3`, `.wav`, or `.ogg` payload.\\n\\n2. **One balance verb, every shipped activity.** Lean (left stick or D-pad, WASD or arrows, pointer-locked mouse), left foot, right foot, and both feet are the only activity inputs, and a new activity changes what the weight moves, not how it is moved. Centre-of-balance is a point in a unit disc. With no input, time inside radius 0.22 is well under half (sway stays slow). A held full lean topples. Calm from breathing with the guide reduces sway. Topple stumbles and recentres; it is never a game over. Each activity, started from its own fresh state, scores 0–1000, maps to Present / Adequate / Composed / Serene / Unsettling (thresholds 0 / 300 / 550 / 750 / 900), awards 1–5 pebbles by rank, ends itself on a time box if the pad is put down, and leaves no stray bodies. On 10 seeds the perfect bot scores at least 750, the human-like bot (about 250 ms late, gain about 1.2) at least 550, the sloppy bot (about 350 ms, gain about 0.8) at least 300, and idle at most 500 and below the human-like bot. Random input does not throw. These are present and playable: Morning Check (still ring, reach, one-foot, Wobble Age from 18 to 82), Pose Class for Seated Nothing, Patient Chair, Heron, Archer, Sideways Comma, Folded Napkin, Polite Bridge, and Lighthouse (enter, hold, release; the body scrub follows the thumb), Still Pond (only matched breathing is correct; other input costs composure; a lure is not a real pause; doing nothing is Adequate), The Line, Paddle Glide, Sand Garden, and Great Tilt steps storm, everyone-east, centre-stone (island tilt follows centre-of-balance), and dawn. Reps Hall, Step Class, Hoop Patrol, Cliff Plunge, Island Jog’s race, Great Tilt counterweights, expert variants, and outfits are either fully playable or removed in that cut order with the day list reflowed and no leftover mention.\\n10→\\n3. **Five-day retreat you can finish.** A third-person island hub has the stations and the cast Tare, Plumb, Gerald, Bex, Old Nan, the Gull, and the Frog. Walking is allowed, and every programme or noticeboard entry can also “Go” without crossing the island. Five days each do a Morning Check plus their activities, then sleep, stamps, and a short remark. Pebbles are never spent; they stack on a cairn. Hidden pebbles and creeping plaques exist. Saves restore day, results, pebbles, finds, outfits, bests, and settings; erase asks inside the game, not `confirm()`. A shipped auto playthrough from a fresh save, on 3 seeds, visits every shipped day, activity, and finale step and reaches credits without throwing or a softlock. After credits, free play and a new daily check remain, and the ferry does not come back. At least 200 lines, none longer than two short sentences, include PLAN.md’s seed lines; Plumb has no exclamation marks. All music, effects, and voices are code. Fresh-save music volume is 0.1. The same line always babbles the same way. Songs and syllables render non-silent. Pose and lean clips are scrubbed from balance or pose progress, not played as a canned squat at the player.\\n\\n4. **10-foot shell.** The same screens serve a standard-mapped pad, keyboard, and mouse. Prompts follow the last device in the same frame: PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox glyphs (A B X Y, LB RB LT RT) after the Settings switch, key caps and mouse buttons after those inputs. Hover moves menu focus; click selects. Body text at 1920×1080 is at least 28 px; menus have at most six rows; results are one rank, one number, one sentence, not a dense data page. Pause opens Resume, Restart, Back to the island, Settings, Controls, Dev Mode, About/Credits, and Quit. Dev Mode, absent in a hub session, has live sliders for the numeric `game.*` tunables in PLAN.md (including wobble, breath, and pebble multiplier) and a reset to defaults, plus jumps to a day, activity, or finale step. Attract mode starts after 10 seconds without input on a front-end menu, loops through several activities (the driver may cheat), exits on key, click, or pad, and does not write the save. A touch-only profile shows “Controller or keyboard required” and a Settings control that opens by tap, with no on-screen touch play, while attract still runs. Without WebGPU the page shows a plain message naming current Chrome or Edge, not a blank page. Keyboard bindings can be rebound in Controls.\\n\\n5. **Couch Group Class and AI Hub ghost sessions.** Up to four players join mats on one screen (pad, or keyboard and mouse for one seat). Empty seats become CPU guests unless Settings turns them off. A round is three short classes dealt from one seed, then a podium. In AI Hub the mode is ghost: meta tags `hub:session` 1, `hub:session-players` 1-4, `hub:session-mode` ghost, `hub:session-minutes` 3, goal at most 60 characters, how-to at most 80 characters, `hub:webgpu` required, `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` 1-4, `hub:source` Wii Fit. The fetched session client is pasted unmodified and is byte-identical in the HTML. Its SHA-256 is `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a` (client 1.4.0). If the fetched file’s own banner is a newer client, record the new hash in `PROGRESS.md` and still inject those exact bytes. `?aihub` query keys are stripped before engine boot so unknown keys do not kill the engine. A session skips title, attract, and dev mode; pause does not pause the sim; `ready()` is reached with the engine actually running. Ghosts show the other players’ leans and do not affect local play. The hub harness passes for 2, 3, and 4 players and for host-leave: `__hubCheck.pass`, `body[data-complete=\\\"true\\\"]`, every frame `__engine.ready === true` and zero engine errors, a ghost present at 2 players, and no console line starting with `[AIHub]`. With no hub, the game is the full single-player build.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. **gating:** In the dev workspace, add or extend tests that call the shipped balance step and each shipped activity’s own setup, step, score, and bot from a fresh sim. Do not reimplement the model, mock the unit under test, or start past setup. Assert criterion 2’s bands, self-end, age range, Still Pond penalties, teardown, and no `NaN`. Run `node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs` from the dev folder (full run, not only `--quick`) and write stdout to `{SCRATCH}/verify.log`. Pass only if the exit code is 0 and the log has no failure lines and one final count line of zero failures. Also write `{SCRATCH}/npm-test.log` and `{SCRATCH}/npm-check.log` for `npm test` and `npm run check`, both passing. `npm run check` shows the engine matches its lock, or `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` lists the exact engine diff and why.\\n2. **gating:** The same verify command (or a node test it runs) drives the shipped auto/director path from a fresh save on 3 seeds, not a hand-rolled copy of the day table. `{SCRATCH}/verify.log` must show each seed reaching credits. Replay capture/restore of the shipped goldens continues exactly; that result is in the same log.\\n20→3. **gating:** Launch the handed-in HTML twice, from `file://`, in headless Chromium (`CHROMIUM_PATH` = the headless shell, flags `--no-sandbox --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`). Both runs must agree: `__engine.ready === true`, `__engine.errors` empty, no WebGPU downgrade error, `window.__game` (screen, attract, last device, glyph set, volumes, day, event, focus) shows the title screen and `{Title}`, and the music volume is 0.1. The canvas’s drawing width and height equal the requested view and are non-zero. A scripted standard-mapping pad or a key, applied through the real menu path, changes `__game` the same way both times. Save `{SCRATCH}/boot-1.log`, `{SCRATCH}/boot-2.log`, `{SCRATCH}/boot-1.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/boot-2.png`. Primary observable is that state, not the bitmap. If the screenshot is fully blank or uncleared while those state checks pass, write `{SCRATCH}/webgpu-readback.txt` and do not fail the launch for pixels alone (known SwiftShader limit). If a readback shows a partial scene that disagrees with `__game`, that is a failure. If Chromium cannot start, save the error as `{SCRATCH}/launch-error.txt`; node checks in steps 1–2 and the static checks in step 5 are then the bar. A started page with `ready` false or a blank state is never that fallback.\\n4. **gating:** Browser-drive the built page (same Chromium) and record `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`. Must show: PlayStation glyphs before any Xbox setting, Xbox glyphs after the setting, prompts switching to keys and to mouse in the same frame as those inputs, hover moving focus, attract beginning at 10–11 s of idle and leaving on a key, a click, and a pad press with the save unchanged, a dev slider changing live behaviour and Reset restoring the default, About text containing every Source Information field and each feedback answer, and at 1920×1080 every visible text node at least 28 px and no menu over six rows. WebKit (no WebGPU here) shows the Chrome-or-Edge message. An iPhone and a tablet Chromium profile show the controller-or-keyboard line, open Settings by `touchscreen.tap`, draw no touch stick, and still run attract.\\n5. **gating:** Serve the built HTML and the fetched harness files with a single `127.0.0.1` process on an OS-picked port; stop only that PID. Run the harness for `players=2`, `3`, `4`, and `players=3&scenario=host-leave` (latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5). Write `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`. Pass only if each run has `__hubCheck.pass`, `data-complete=\\\"true\\\"`, per-frame engine ready and zero engine errors, a ghost at 2 players, and no `[AIHub]` console line. `{SCRATCH}/hub-client.sha` is the injected client hash and matches criterion 5. A no-session load still reaches the title. Standalone client check: Enter, Space, Enter, Space leaves the client present and inactive, leaves `Math.random` unseeded, draws the screen, and adds no errors.\\n6. **gating:** Static pass on the work root: HTML and folder names, `exit-interview.json` parses and matches About, `PROGRESS.md` exists, game README says what the game is and which judgment calls were made, `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` is specific, and a search of the game sources for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, and `stub` is clean except test wording. Audio proof (song and syllable render, music 0.1) is in `{SCRATCH}/verify.log` or `{SCRATCH}/audio.log`.\\n7. **evidence:** 1920×1080 screenshots under `{SCRATCH}/shots/` of title, island, Pose Class HUD, Still Pond with a lure, The Line, Great Tilt wide shot, results, pause, Dev Mode, and About. Missing shots do not fail when steps 1–6 passed, including an honest launch fallback.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- Recreating Wii Fit’s BMI or weight test, trainer look, Balance Board, Miis, Wuhu Island, Fit Bank, logos, fonts, or melodies.\\n- Frame-rate optimization, except the hub’s 20-second `ready()` deadline.\\n- Cloning the ai-hub repository, adding npm dependencies, or `git init` / commits in the dev folder.\\n30→- Shared-world or more than four players, real gamepads, iOS Safari, and listening tests by ear.\\n- A second desktop-only layout, or touch controls beyond the required message and Settings button.\\n- A half-built cut-line activity left in the menu.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\nWork root is the folder that holds `STAGE.md`, `PLAN.md`, and `TASK.md`. The dev subfolder is a my-3dge full workspace created with that repo’s `new-game` tool (clone only for the generator, then delete it), then `npm ci` only. Game code lives on top of the read-only engine. Hub `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, and `round.js` are fetched from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/`, not from a clone. Deliverables in the work root: the one HTML file, `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`.\\n\\nWii Fit (Nintendo, 2007) was checked against public guides: daily Body Test (weight, BMI, centre-of-balance, Wii Fit Age), yoga holds with a breath guide, strength reps, aerobics (step, hoop, jog), lean-steered balance minigames, a trainer, and a time bank. PLAN.md already maps those into an original wobble game and bans body-size metrics and source names. Do not add activities the plan does not list.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\n40→Follow PLAN.md for design detail. This section is not a second spec: a structure that meets the criteria is acceptable even if file names differ, as long as the engine’s own workspace rules still hold (`labs/game` is where this engine mounts a game).\\n\\nKeep the balance step, activity rules, bots, and day tables as pure sim code with no rendering or DOM, so node tests drive them directly. The page only reads sim state, plays code audio, and sends input or menu choices back through the engine’s recorded channels. One bot writer produces perfect, human-like, sloppy, idle, attract, and CPU-guest input. Days, poses, charts, trays, and lines stay data. Ship a smaller complete loop early (boot, one activity, one-file HTML, hub `ready`) and add activities without breaking that loop. Put the single verify command in front of the node tests, the three-seed auto playthrough, audio renders, and the browser and harness stages. Publish `window.__game` for those checks. Write About copy and `exit-interview.json` from the same answers before the final HTML build.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Save 50 titles, RNG-pick one, create the named dev folder with `new-game`, `npm ci`, and a work-root `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- [ ] One-file HTML build, unmodified hub client and tags, tiny session scene, verify command skeleton, harness green with the engine actually ready.\\n- [ ] Balance model, maps, disc, glyphs, Morning Check, four bots, dev sliders, and the score-band tests.\\n- [ ] Scrubbed clips, Guest and Plumb, Pose Class, code voices, island, flow, saves, results.\\n- [ ] Still Pond, The Line, Paddle Glide, Sand Garden, any later activities not cut, Great Tilt, and the 3-seed auto path to credits.\\n50→- [ ] Same-screen Group Class and hub ghosts; harness 2, 3, 4, and host-leave.\\n- [ ] Attract, settings, controls, About, touch-only and no-WebGPU pages, songs, and 200+ lines.\\n- [ ] `exit-interview.json`, HTML copied to the work root, full verify, and two consistent boots with logs under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- TASK.md says a headless WebGPU screenshot can be blank and to trust game state. A fully blank bitmap with `ready` and a real `__game` screen is that limit, not an automatic fail. A readable but empty or partial frame that disagrees with `__game` is a game bug.\\n- The live client fetched while writing this plan is banner `1.4.0`, matching PLAN.md’s pin. If the upstream file moves, the unmodified fetched bytes win over the old hash, and the new hash goes in `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- The required basename contains a space because SOURCE is `Wii Fit`. That is intentional, not a reason to drop the source token.\\n- PLAN.md forbids `git init` in the dev folder even though the engine guide says to commit. Do not init or commit.\\n- Other agents share ports and memory. Do not bind 5173, do not kill processes you did not start, and do not run more than two browsers. `earlyoom` killing a browser is memory pressure, not a game bug to retry in a loop.\\n60→- Great Tilt’s session scene must stay small: SwiftShader has needed most of the harness’s 20 s just to boot. The island must not load in a hub session.\\n- Firefox has no WebGPU here. Only Chromium can run the game; WebKit is only for the no-WebGPU message.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc%2Fwork/01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc/goal/plan.md\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"# Plan: Build PLAN.md’s original Wii Fit–inspired balance retreat and hand in TASK.md’s files\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. **Hand-in, title, and records.** The work root contains `PROGRESS.md`, `exit-interview.json`, and one self-contained HTML file. The HTML and the dev subfolder share the basename `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656` (SOURCE keeps the space in `Wii Fit`; `{Title}` is the on-screen title, with only OS-illegal characters sanitized, and that sanitization noted in `PROGRESS.md`). `{Title}` was chosen by executing a real RNG over a saved list of 50 playful riffs on “Wii Fit,” and that list plus the pick are in the dev folder. The page shows `{Title}` on the title screen. `exit-interview.json` is one JSON object in TASK.md’s exact shape, every value filled, `usage` exactly `added on import`, and its Source Information plus the three feedback lists match the in-game About/Credits screen in the same order. `aiHub.genre` is `Sports`, `aiHub.source` is `Wii Fit`, `aiHub.type` is `Game`, `aiHub.players` is `1–4`. The word `Wii` appears in-game only on that source line and the hub source field. There is no weight, BMI, calorie, or body-size scoring, and none of these source names: Fit Age, Fit Credits, Fit Piggy Bank, Body Test, Wuhu, or the source’s minigame, menu, or melody names. Opening the HTML does not need the network. It contains no `data:audio`, `.mp3`, `.wav`, or `.ogg` payload.\\n\\n2. **One balance verb, every shipped activity.** Lean (left stick or D-pad, WASD or arrows, pointer-locked mouse), left foot, right foot, and both feet are the only activity inputs, and a new activity changes what the weight moves, not how it is moved. Centre-of-balance is a point in a unit disc. With no input, time inside radius 0.22 is well under half (sway stays slow). A held full lean topples. Calm from breathing with the guide reduces sway. Topple stumbles and recentres; it is never a game over. Each activity, started from its own fresh state, scores 0–1000, maps to Present / Adequate / Composed / Serene / Unsettling (thresholds 0 / 300 / 550 / 750 / 900), awards 1–5 pebbles by rank, ends itself on a time box if the pad is put down, and leaves no stray bodies. On 10 seeds the perfect bot scores at least 750, the human-like bot (about 250 ms late, gain about 1.2) at least 550, the sloppy bot (about 350 ms, gain about 0.8) at least 300, and idle at most 500 and below the human-like bot. Random input does not throw. These are present and playable: Morning Check (still ring, reach, one-foot, Wobble Age from 18 to 82), Pose Class for Seated Nothing, Patient Chair, Heron, Archer, Sideways Comma, Folded Napkin, Polite Bridge, and Lighthouse (enter, hold, release; the body scrub follows the thumb), Still Pond (only matched breathing is correct; other input costs composure; a lure is not a real pause; doing nothing is Adequate), The Line, Paddle Glide, Sand Garden, and Great Tilt steps storm, everyone-east, centre-stone (island tilt follows centre-of-balance), and dawn. Reps Hall, Step Class, Hoop Patrol, Cliff Plunge, Island Jog’s race, Great Tilt counterweights, expert variants, and outfits are either fully playable or removed in that cut order with the day list reflowed and no leftover mention.\\n\\n3. **Five-day retreat you can finish.** A third-person island hub has the stations and the cast Tare, Plumb, Gerald, Bex, Old Nan, the Gull, and the Frog. Walking is allowed, and every programme or noticeboard entry can also “Go” without crossing the island. Five days each do a Morning Check plus their activities, then sleep, stamps, and a short remark. Pebbles are never spent; they stack on a cairn. Hidden pebbles and creeping plaques exist. Saves restore day, results, pebbles, finds, outfits, bests, and settings; erase asks inside the game, not `confirm()`. A shipped auto playthrough from a fresh save, on 3 seeds, visits every shipped day, activity, and finale step and reaches credits without throwing or a softlock. After credits, free play and a new daily check remain, and the ferry does not come back. At least 200 lines, none longer than two short sentences, include PLAN.md’s seed lines; Plumb has no exclamation marks. All music, effects, and voices are code. Fresh-save music volume is 0.1. The same line always babbles the same way. Songs and syllables render non-silent. Pose and lean clips are scrubbed from balance or pose progress, not played as a canned squat at the player.\\n\\n4. **10-foot shell.** The same screens serve a standard-mapped pad, keyboard, and mouse. Prompts follow the last device in the same frame: PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox glyphs (A B X Y, LB RB LT RT) after the Settings switch, key caps and mouse buttons after those inputs. Hover moves menu focus; click selects. Body text at 1920×1080 is at least 28 px; menus have at most six rows; results are one rank, one number, one sentence, not a dense data page. Pause opens Resume, Restart, Back to the island, Settings, Controls, Dev Mode, About/Credits, and Quit. Dev Mode, absent in a hub session, has live sliders for the numeric `game.*` tunables in PLAN.md (including wobble, breath, and pebble multiplier) and a reset to defaults, plus jumps to a day, activity, or finale step. Attract mode starts after 10 seconds without input on a front-end menu, loops through several activities (the driver may cheat), exits on key, click, or pad, and does not write the save. A touch-only profile shows “Controller or keyboard required” and a Settings control that opens by tap, with no on-screen touch play, while attract still runs. Without WebGPU the page shows a plain message naming current Chrome or Edge, not a blank page. Keyboard bindings can be rebound in Controls.\\n\\n5. **Couch Group Class and AI Hub ghost sessions.** Up to four players join mats on one screen (pad, or keyboard and mouse for one seat). Empty seats become CPU guests unless Settings turns them off. A round is three short classes dealt from one seed, then a podium. In AI Hub the mode is ghost: meta tags `hub:session` 1, `hub:session-players` 1-4, `hub:session-mode` ghost, `hub:session-minutes` 3, goal at most 60 characters, how-to at most 80 characters, `hub:webgpu` required, `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` 1-4, `hub:source` Wii Fit. The fetched session client is pasted unmodified and is byte-identical in the HTML. Its SHA-256 is `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a` (client 1.4.0). If the fetched file’s own banner is a newer client, record the new hash in `PROGRESS.md` and still inject those exact bytes. `?aihub` query keys are stripped before engine boot so unknown keys do not kill the engine. A session skips title, attract, and dev mode; pause does not pause the sim; `ready()` is reached with the engine actually running. Ghosts show the other players’ leans and do not affect local play. The hub harness passes for 2, 3, and 4 players and for host-leave: `__hubCheck.pass`, `body[data-complete=\\\"true\\\"]`, every frame `__engine.ready === true` and zero engine errors, a ghost present at 2 players, and no console line starting with `[AIHub]`. With no hub, the game is the full single-player build.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. **gating:** In the dev workspace, add or extend tests that call the shipped balance step and each shipped activity’s own setup, step, score, and bot from a fresh sim. Do not reimplement the model, mock the unit under test, or start past setup. Assert criterion 2’s bands, self-end, age range, Still Pond penalties, teardown, and no `NaN`. Run `node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs` from the dev folder (full run, not only `--quick`) and write stdout to `{SCRATCH}/verify.log`. Pass only if the exit code is 0 and the log has no failure lines and one final count line of zero failures. Also write `{SCRATCH}/npm-test.log` and `{SCRATCH}/npm-check.log` for `npm test` and `npm run check`, both passing. `npm run check` shows the engine matches its lock, or `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` lists the exact engine diff and why.\\n2. **gating:** The same verify command (or a node test it runs) drives the shipped auto/director path from a fresh save on 3 seeds, not a hand-rolled copy of the day table. `{SCRATCH}/verify.log` must show each seed reaching credits. Replay capture/restore of the shipped goldens continues exactly; that result is in the same log.\\n3. **gating:** Launch the handed-in HTML twice, from `file://`, in headless Chromium (`CHROMIUM_PATH` = the headless shell, flags `--no-sandbox --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`). Both runs must agree: `__engine.ready === true`, `__engine.errors` empty, no WebGPU downgrade error, `window.__game` (screen, attract, last device, glyph set, volumes, day, event, focus) shows the title screen and `{Title}`, and the music volume is 0.1. The canvas’s drawing width and height equal the requested view and are non-zero. A scripted standard-mapping pad or a key, applied through the real menu path, changes `__game` the same way both times. Save `{SCRATCH}/boot-1.log`, `{SCRATCH}/boot-2.log`, `{SCRATCH}/boot-1.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/boot-2.png`. Primary observable is that state, not the bitmap. If the screenshot is fully blank or uncleared while those state checks pass, write `{SCRATCH}/webgpu-readback.txt` and do not fail the launch for pixels alone (known SwiftShader limit). If a readback shows a partial scene that disagrees with `__game`, that is a failure. If Chromium cannot start, save the error as `{SCRATCH}/launch-error.txt`; node checks in steps 1–2 and the static checks in step 5 are then the bar. A started page with `ready` false or a blank state is never that fallback.\\n4. **gating:** Browser-drive the built page (same Chromium) and record `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`. Must show: PlayStation glyphs before any Xbox setting, Xbox glyphs after the setting, prompts switching to keys and to mouse in the same frame as those inputs, hover moving focus, attract beginning at 10–11 s of idle and leaving on a key, a click, and a pad press with the save unchanged, a dev slider changing live behaviour and Reset restoring the default, About text containing every Source Information field and each feedback answer, and at 1920×1080 every visible text node at least 28 px and no menu over six rows. WebKit (no WebGPU here) shows the Chrome-or-Edge message. An iPhone and a tablet Chromium profile show the controller-or-keyboard line, open Settings by `touchscreen.tap`, draw no touch stick, and still run attract.\\n5. **gating:** Serve the built HTML and the fetched harness files with a single `127.0.0.1` process on an OS-picked port; stop only that PID. Run the harness for `players=2`, `3`, `4`, and `players=3&scenario=host-leave` (latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5). Write `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`. Pass only if each run has `__hubCheck.pass`, `data-complete=\\\"true\\\"`, per-frame engine ready and zero engine errors, a ghost at 2 players, and no `[AIHub]` console line. `{SCRATCH}/hub-client.sha` is the injected client hash and matches criterion 5. A no-session load still reaches the title. Standalone client check: Enter, Space, Enter, Space leaves the client present and inactive, leaves `Math.random` unseeded, draws the screen, and adds no errors.\\n6. **gating:** Static pass on the work root: HTML and folder names, `exit-interview.json` parses and matches About, `PROGRESS.md` exists, game README says what the game is and which judgment calls were made, `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` is specific, and a search of the game sources for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, and `stub` is clean except test wording. Audio proof (song and syllable render, music 0.1) is in `{SCRATCH}/verify.log` or `{SCRATCH}/audio.log`.\\n7. **evidence:** 1920×1080 screenshots under `{SCRATCH}/shots/` of title, island, Pose Class HUD, Still Pond with a lure, The Line, Great Tilt wide shot, results, pause, Dev Mode, and About. Missing shots do not fail when steps 1–6 passed, including an honest launch fallback.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- Recreating Wii Fit’s BMI or weight test, trainer look, Balance Board, Miis, Wuhu Island, Fit Bank, logos, fonts, or melodies.\\n- Frame-rate optimization, except the hub’s 20-second `ready()` deadline.\\n- Cloning the ai-hub repository, adding npm dependencies, or `git init` / commits in the dev folder.\\n- Shared-world or more than four players, real gamepads, iOS Safari, and listening tests by ear.\\n- A second desktop-only layout, or touch controls beyond the required message and Settings button.\\n- A half-built cut-line activity left in the menu.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\nWork root is the folder that holds `STAGE.md`, `PLAN.md`, and `TASK.md`. The dev subfolder is a my-3dge full workspace created with that repo’s `new-game` tool (clone only for the generator, then delete it), then `npm ci` only. Game code lives on top of the read-only engine. Hub `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, and `round.js` are fetched from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/`, not from a clone. Deliverables in the work root: the one HTML file, `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`.\\n\\nWii Fit (Nintendo, 2007) was checked against public guides: daily Body Test (weight, BMI, centre-of-balance, Wii Fit Age), yoga holds with a breath guide, strength reps, aerobics (step, hoop, jog), lean-steered balance minigames, a trainer, and a time bank. PLAN.md already maps those into an original wobble game and bans body-size metrics and source names. Do not add activities the plan does not list.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nFollow PLAN.md for design detail. This section is not a second spec: a structure that meets the criteria is acceptable even if file names differ, as long as the engine’s own workspace rules still hold (`labs/game` is where this engine mounts a game).\\n\\nKeep the balance step, activity rules, bots, and day tables as pure sim code with no rendering or DOM, so node tests drive them directly. The page only reads sim state, plays code audio, and sends input or menu choices back through the engine’s recorded channels. One bot writer produces perfect, human-like, sloppy, idle, attract, and CPU-guest input. Days, poses, charts, trays, and lines stay data. Ship a smaller complete loop early (boot, one activity, one-file HTML, hub `ready`) and add activities without breaking that loop. Put the single verify command in front of the node tests, the three-seed auto playthrough, audio renders, and the browser and harness stages. Publish `window.__game` for those checks. Write About copy and `exit-interview.json` from the same answers before the final HTML build.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Save 50 titles, RNG-pick one, create the named dev folder with `new-game`, `npm ci`, and a work-root `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- [ ] One-file HTML build, unmodified hub client and tags, tiny session scene, verify command skeleton, harness green with the engine actually ready.\\n- [ ] Balance model, maps, disc, glyphs, Morning Check, four bots, dev sliders, and the score-band tests.\\n- [ ] Scrubbed clips, Guest and Plumb, Pose Class, code voices, island, flow, saves, results.\\n- [ ] Still Pond, The Line, Paddle Glide, Sand Garden, any later activities not cut, Great Tilt, and the 3-seed auto path to credits.\\n- [ ] Same-screen Group Class and hub ghosts; harness 2, 3, 4, and host-leave.\\n- [ ] Attract, settings, controls, About, touch-only and no-WebGPU pages, songs, and 200+ lines.\\n- [ ] `exit-interview.json`, HTML copied to the work root, full verify, and two consistent boots with logs under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- TASK.md says a headless WebGPU screenshot can be blank and to trust game state. A fully blank bitmap with `ready` and a real `__game` screen is that limit, not an automatic fail. A readable but empty or partial frame that disagrees with `__game` is a game bug.\\n- The live client fetched while writing this plan is banner `1.4.0`, matching PLAN.md’s pin. If the upstream file moves, the unmodified fetched bytes win over the old hash, and the new hash goes in `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- The required basename contains a space because SOURCE is `Wii Fit`. That is intentional, not a reason to drop the source token.\\n- PLAN.md forbids `git init` in the dev folder even though the engine guide says to commit. Do not init or commit.\\n- Other agents share ports and memory. Do not bind 5173, do not kill processes you did not start, and do not run more than two browsers. `earlyoom` killing a browser is memory pressure, not a game bug to retry in a loop.\\n- Great Tilt’s session scene must stay small: SwiftShader has needed most of the harness’s 20 s just to boot. The island must not load in a hub session.\\n- Firefox has no WebGPU here. Only Chromium can run the game; WebKit is only for the no-WebGPU message.\\n\",\"total_lines\":61}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"1a0dbf5a-f802-43aa-a692-3493b45d9919"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_487","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a large remaining task.\n\nI need to add `@file` JSDoc comments to bridge.js and round.js to satisfy the eslint file-overview rule. These files were fetched from the hub, so adding the comment should be safe.\n\nI will write verify.mjs to run node tests and print only failures with a count. I need to inspect retreat.test.ts to reuse existing test functions. Then I will record a golden replay, fix page bugs by reading code and testing, build the HTML deliverables, and run all verification.\n\nI realized npm test prints too much output. verify.mjs should run the checks directly and only print failures. The log must end with exactly one count line: \"0 failures\" or \"1 failure\". I need to avoid letting vitest's own output leak into that log.\n\nI must avoid dumping vitest's raw output into verify.log because test names like \"does not fail\" contain the word \"fail\". The script should run the game's test logic directly or parse vitest results cleanly, then print only failures. Director tests also need to be included.\n\nI will run the replay check and audio tests. Browser stages are skipped in quick mode.\n\nThe verify script can invoke vitest with a JSON reporter to extract failure names cleanly.\n\nA critical requirement surfaced: the log must show every seed reaching credits, not just failures.\n\nThe log can include seed credits and replay results alongside the failure count. The full engine test suite will take several minutes to run.\n\nI will run `npm run check` as well. I plan to read the page files—stage.ts, menus.ts, hub.ts, and snap.ts—carefully to catch bugs before running browser tests. I will also inspect retreat.test.ts, island.test.ts, and the director test exports so verify.mjs can invoke existing tests directly rather than reimplementing them.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e024a741-8a55-49e9-bf95-72d52828ed5c-66","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/retreat.test.ts","limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e024a741-8a55-49e9-bf95-72d52828ed5c-67","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/tools/cmd/replay.ts","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e024a741-8a55-49e9-bf95-72d52828ed5c-68","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/stage.ts","offset":40,"limit":250}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4480,"output_tokens":1242,"cache_read_input_tokens":87936,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"ba43e567-c4ea-42d0-905d-ed86e786167f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e024a741-8a55-49e9-bf95-72d52828ed5c-66","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The retreat, driven through the shipped scene. Bands, the balance step, teardown and the director\\n * all call the activities' own setup, step, score and bot. Nothing here reimplements the disc.\\n */\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { createAppHost, type AppRun } from '../../engine/app/headless';\\nimport type { Intents, World } from '../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { bench } from './scenes/bench';\\nimport type { Band } from './scenes/bot';\\n10→import { ACTIVITIES, type Activity } from './scenes/catalog';\\nimport { programme } from './scenes/data/days';\\nimport { actOf, cfgOf, flowOf, rowOf } from './scenes/events/kit';\\nimport { disturbed, pond } from './scenes/events/pond';\\nimport { wobbleAge } from './scenes/score';\\nimport { inRing, resetBalance, stepBalance, type Stick } from './scenes/wobble';\\n\\nconst BANDS: readonly Band[] = ['perfect', 'human', 'sloppy', 'idle'];\\nconst SEEN = [\\n  'morning', 'pose', 'pose-a', 'pose-b', 'pose-c', 'pond', 'garden', 'paddle', 'line', 'group',\\n20→  'tilt:storm', 'tilt:east', 'tilt:stone', 'tilt:dawn', 'evening', 'credits',\\n];\\n\\n/** A live world and the menu actions that drive it. */\\nfunction open(seed: number, settings?: Record<string, unknown>) {\\n  const run = createAppHost({ scene: bench, seed, settings });\\n  const w = run.session.world as World;\\n  const menu = (name: string, args?: unknown) => {\\n    (run.inspector.actions as { run: (action: string, value?: unknown) => void }).run(name, args);\\n  };\\n30→  const reseed = (next: number) => {\\n    (run.inspector.seed as (n?: number) => number)(next);\\n  };\\n  return { run, w, menu, reseed };\\n}\\n\\n/** A stick with every field, so the probe does not invent a second model. */\\nfunction stick(x: number, y: number, both = false): Stick {\\n  return {\\n    x, y, gentle: false, both, mdx: 0, mdy: 0, disturbX: 0, disturbY: 0, noiseScale: 1, instabilityScale: 1,\\n40→  };\\n}\\n\\n/** The world the run is on now. A reseed replaces it. */\\nfunction live(run: AppRun): World {\\n  return run.session.world as World;\\n}\\n\\n/** Plays one activity. The scene calls step. This calls the activity's bot and score. */\\nfunction play(run: AppRun, menu: (name: string, args?: unknown) => void, activity: Activity, band: Band): number {\\n50→  const w = live(run);\\n  const bootCount = w.count;\\n  menu('game.start', { event: activity.id });\\n  const cap = activity.seconds * 60 + 120;\\n  let score = Number.NaN;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < cap; i++) {\\n    const intents = activity.bot(w, band);\\n    run.stepOnce(intents);\\n    if (flowOf(w).mode === 'results') {\\n      score = activity.score(w);\\n60→      break;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  activity.teardown(w);\\n  expect(w.count, `${activity.id} teardown`).toBe(bootCount);\\n  return score;\\n}\\n\\ndescribe('balance', () => {\\n  it('keeps a still thumb inside the 0.22 ring only part of the time', () => {\\n70→    const shares: number[] = [];\\n    for (let seed = 1; seed <= 10; seed++) {\\n      const { w } = open(seed);\\n      const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n      resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n      const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n      let inside = 0;\\n      const steps = 20 * 60;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < steps; i++) {\\n        stepBalance(row.wobble, stick(0, 0), cfg, i / 60, w.dt);\\n80→        if (inRing(row.wobble, 0.22)) inside += 1;\\n      }\\n      shares.push(inside / steps);\\n    }\\n    const mean = shares.reduce((sum, n) => sum + n, 0) / shares.length;\\n    expect(mean).toBeGreaterThan(0.15);\\n    expect(mean).toBeLessThan(0.55);\\n  });\\n\\n  it('topples a held full stick and quiets sway when the breath is calm', () => {\\n90→    const { w } = open(1);\\n    const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n    resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n    const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 180; i++) stepBalance(row.wobble, stick(1, 0), cfg, i / 60, w.dt);\\n    expect(row.wobble.topples).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n    let wild = 0;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 600; i++) {\\n      stepBalance(row.wobble, stick(0, 0), cfg, i / 60, w.dt);\\n100→      wild += Math.abs(row.wobble.x);\\n    }\\n    resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n    let quiet = 0;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 600; i++) {\\n      row.wobble.calm = 1;\\n      stepBalance(row.wobble, stick(0, 0, true), cfg, i / 60, w.dt);\\n      quiet += Math.abs(row.wobble.x);\\n    }\\n    expect(quiet).toBeLessThan(wild);\\n110→  });\\n});\\n\\ndescribe('activities', () => {\\n  it('calls setup, step, score and bot on each activity', () => {\\n    const { w } = open(1);\\n    for (const activity of ACTIVITIES) {\\n      activity.setup(w);\\n      const intents = activity.bot(w, 'idle');\\n      activity.step(w, intents);\\n120→      expect(Number.isFinite(activity.score(w))).toBe(true);\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The retreat, driven through the shipped scene. Bands, the balance step, teardown and the director\\n * all call the activities' own setup, step, score and bot. Nothing here reimplements the disc.\\n */\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { createAppHost, type AppRun } from '../../engine/app/headless';\\nimport type { Intents, World } from '../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { bench } from './scenes/bench';\\nimport type { Band } from './scenes/bot';\\n10→import { ACTIVITIES, type Activity } from './scenes/catalog';\\nimport { programme } from './scenes/data/days';\\nimport { actOf, cfgOf, flowOf, rowOf } from './scenes/events/kit';\\nimport { disturbed, pond } from './scenes/events/pond';\\nimport { wobbleAge } from './scenes/score';\\nimport { inRing, resetBalance, stepBalance, type Stick } from './scenes/wobble';\\n\\nconst BANDS: readonly Band[] = ['perfect', 'human', 'sloppy', 'idle'];\\nconst SEEN = [\\n  'morning', 'pose', 'pose-a', 'pose-b', 'pose-c', 'pond', 'garden', 'paddle', 'line', 'group',\\n20→  'tilt:storm', 'tilt:east', 'tilt:stone', 'tilt:dawn', 'evening', 'credits',\\n];\\n\\n/** A live world and the menu actions that drive it. */\\nfunction open(seed: number, settings?: Record<string, unknown>) {\\n  const run = createAppHost({ scene: bench, seed, settings });\\n  const w = run.session.world as World;\\n  const menu = (name: string, args?: unknown) => {\\n    (run.inspector.actions as { run: (action: string, value?: unknown) => void }).run(name, args);\\n  };\\n30→  const reseed = (next: number) => {\\n    (run.inspector.seed as (n?: number) => number)(next);\\n  };\\n  return { run, w, menu, reseed };\\n}\\n\\n/** A stick with every field, so the probe does not invent a second model. */\\nfunction stick(x: number, y: number, both = false): Stick {\\n  return {\\n    x, y, gentle: false, both, mdx: 0, mdy: 0, disturbX: 0, disturbY: 0, noiseScale: 1, instabilityScale: 1,\\n40→  };\\n}\\n\\n/** The world the run is on now. A reseed replaces it. */\\nfunction live(run: AppRun): World {\\n  return run.session.world as World;\\n}\\n\\n/** Plays one activity. The scene calls step. This calls the activity's bot and score. */\\nfunction play(run: AppRun, menu: (name: string, args?: unknown) => void, activity: Activity, band: Band): number {\\n50→  const w = live(run);\\n  const bootCount = w.count;\\n  menu('game.start', { event: activity.id });\\n  const cap = activity.seconds * 60 + 120;\\n  let score = Number.NaN;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < cap; i++) {\\n    const intents = activity.bot(w, band);\\n    run.stepOnce(intents);\\n    if (flowOf(w).mode === 'results') {\\n      score = activity.score(w);\\n60→      break;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  activity.teardown(w);\\n  expect(w.count, `${activity.id} teardown`).toBe(bootCount);\\n  return score;\\n}\\n\\ndescribe('balance', () => {\\n  it('keeps a still thumb inside the 0.22 ring only part of the time', () => {\\n70→    const shares: number[] = [];\\n    for (let seed = 1; seed <= 10; seed++) {\\n      const { w } = open(seed);\\n      const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n      resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n      const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n      let inside = 0;\\n      const steps = 20 * 60;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < steps; i++) {\\n        stepBalance(row.wobble, stick(0, 0), cfg, i / 60, w.dt);\\n80→        if (inRing(row.wobble, 0.22)) inside += 1;\\n      }\\n      shares.push(inside / steps);\\n    }\\n    const mean = shares.reduce((sum, n) => sum + n, 0) / shares.length;\\n    expect(mean).toBeGreaterThan(0.15);\\n    expect(mean).toBeLessThan(0.55);\\n  });\\n\\n  it('topples a held full stick and quiets sway when the breath is calm', () => {\\n90→    const { w } = open(1);\\n    const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n    resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n    const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 180; i++) stepBalance(row.wobble, stick(1, 0), cfg, i / 60, w.dt);\\n    expect(row.wobble.topples).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n    let wild = 0;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 600; i++) {\\n      stepBalance(row.wobble, stick(0, 0), cfg, i / 60, w.dt);\\n100→      wild += Math.abs(row.wobble.x);\\n    }\\n    resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n    let quiet = 0;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 600; i++) {\\n      row.wobble.calm = 1;\\n      stepBalance(row.wobble, stick(0, 0, true), cfg, i / 60, w.dt);\\n      quiet += Math.abs(row.wobble.x);\\n    }\\n    expect(quiet).toBeLessThan(wild);\\n110→  });\\n});\\n\\ndescribe('activities', () => {\\n  it('calls setup, step, score and bot on each activity', () => {\\n    const { w } = open(1);\\n    for (const activity of ACTIVITIES) {\\n      activity.setup(w);\\n      const intents = activity.bot(w, 'idle');\\n      activity.step(w, intents);\\n120→      expect(Number.isFinite(activity.score(w))).toBe(true);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/retreat.test.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The retreat, driven through the shipped scene. Bands, the balance step, teardown and the director\\n * all call the activities' own setup, step, score and bot. Nothing here reimplements the disc.\\n */\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { createAppHost, type AppRun } from '../../engine/app/headless';\\nimport type { Intents, World } from '../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { bench } from './scenes/bench';\\nimport type { Band } from './scenes/bot';\\nimport { ACTIVITIES, type Activity } from './scenes/catalog';\\nimport { programme } from './scenes/data/days';\\nimport { actOf, cfgOf, flowOf, rowOf } from './scenes/events/kit';\\nimport { disturbed, pond } from './scenes/events/pond';\\nimport { wobbleAge } from './scenes/score';\\nimport { inRing, resetBalance, stepBalance, type Stick } from './scenes/wobble';\\n\\nconst BANDS: readonly Band[] = ['perfect', 'human', 'sloppy', 'idle'];\\nconst SEEN = [\\n  'morning', 'pose', 'pose-a', 'pose-b', 'pose-c', 'pond', 'garden', 'paddle', 'line', 'group',\\n  'tilt:storm', 'tilt:east', 'tilt:stone', 'tilt:dawn', 'evening', 'credits',\\n];\\n\\n/** A live world and the menu actions that drive it. */\\nfunction open(seed: number, settings?: Record<string, unknown>) {\\n  const run = createAppHost({ scene: bench, seed, settings });\\n  const w = run.session.world as World;\\n  const menu = (name: string, args?: unknown) => {\\n    (run.inspector.actions as { run: (action: string, value?: unknown) => void }).run(name, args);\\n  };\\n  const reseed = (next: number) => {\\n    (run.inspector.seed as (n?: number) => number)(next);\\n  };\\n  return { run, w, menu, reseed };\\n}\\n\\n/** A stick with every field, so the probe does not invent a second model. */\\nfunction stick(x: number, y: number, both = false): Stick {\\n  return {\\n    x, y, gentle: false, both, mdx: 0, mdy: 0, disturbX: 0, disturbY: 0, noiseScale: 1, instabilityScale: 1,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** The world the run is on now. A reseed replaces it. */\\nfunction live(run: AppRun): World {\\n  return run.session.world as World;\\n}\\n\\n/** Plays one activity. The scene calls step. This calls the activity's bot and score. */\\nfunction play(run: AppRun, menu: (name: string, args?: unknown) => void, activity: Activity, band: Band): number {\\n  const w = live(run);\\n  const bootCount = w.count;\\n  menu('game.start', { event: activity.id });\\n  const cap = activity.seconds * 60 + 120;\\n  let score = Number.NaN;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < cap; i++) {\\n    const intents = activity.bot(w, band);\\n    run.stepOnce(intents);\\n    if (flowOf(w).mode === 'results') {\\n      score = activity.score(w);\\n      break;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  activity.teardown(w);\\n  expect(w.count, `${activity.id} teardown`).toBe(bootCount);\\n  return score;\\n}\\n\\ndescribe('balance', () => {\\n  it('keeps a still thumb inside the 0.22 ring only part of the time', () => {\\n    const shares: number[] = [];\\n    for (let seed = 1; seed <= 10; seed++) {\\n      const { w } = open(seed);\\n      const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n      resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n      const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n      let inside = 0;\\n      const steps = 20 * 60;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < steps; i++) {\\n        stepBalance(row.wobble, stick(0, 0), cfg, i / 60, w.dt);\\n        if (inRing(row.wobble, 0.22)) inside += 1;\\n      }\\n      shares.push(inside / steps);\\n    }\\n    const mean = shares.reduce((sum, n) => sum + n, 0) / shares.length;\\n    expect(mean).toBeGreaterThan(0.15);\\n    expect(mean).toBeLessThan(0.55);\\n  });\\n\\n  it('topples a held full stick and quiets sway when the breath is calm', () => {\\n    const { w } = open(1);\\n    const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n    resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n    const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 180; i++) stepBalance(row.wobble, stick(1, 0), cfg, i / 60, w.dt);\\n    expect(row.wobble.topples).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n    let wild = 0;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 600; i++) {\\n      stepBalance(row.wobble, stick(0, 0), cfg, i / 60, w.dt);\\n      wild += Math.abs(row.wobble.x);\\n    }\\n    resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n    let quiet = 0;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 600; i++) {\\n      row.wobble.calm = 1;\\n      stepBalance(row.wobble, stick(0, 0, true), cfg, i / 60, w.dt);\\n      quiet += Math.abs(row.wobble.x);\\n    }\\n    expect(quiet).toBeLessThan(wild);\\n  });\\n});\\n\\ndescribe('activities', () => {\\n  it('calls setup, step, score and bot on each activity', () => {\\n    const { w } = open(1);\\n    for (const activity of ACTIVITIES) {\\n      activity.setup(w);\\n      const intents = activity.bot(w, 'idle');\\n      activity.step(w, intents);\\n      expect(Number.isFinite(activity.score(w))).toBe(true);\\n\",\"total_lines\":222}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e024a741-8a55-49e9-bf95-72d52828ed5c-67","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Replays against their golden hashes (PLAN.md §8.4, §6.5 items 8–9, WPs 1.5 and 2.7). Usage: node x replay\\n * <file|dir…> [--update] [--browser sim|page] [--bisect] [--runs n] [--swap names] [--state] [--until n]. Exit 0 when\\n * every replay gives its goldens in every run (or, recorded elsewhere, agrees with itself; or was recorded), 1\\n * otherwise, 2 on a usage error. The verdict never says \\\"match\\\" unless this platform's goldens were compared.\\n *\\n * `--state` writes the state a replay ends in, as Node plays it: its canonical state and event trace, as `x sim`\\n * writes its own, to `out/replay/<name>/state.json` (`<name>`: the file's, without `.replay.json`); `--until n` (it\\n * implies `--state`) writes the state after step n instead. So an agent reads where a run left its bodies, its props\\n10→ * and its components without a page or a probe of its own (tools/lib/replayState.ts).\\n *\\n * Each `*.replay.json` (a directory means every one under it) plays from step 0 in Node, `--runs` times (3), and with\\n * `--browser sim` as often again in Chromium, in tests/pages/replay.html: the sim in a page, no renderer, through the\\n * same player (engine/sim/replay.ts). Every run must give the goldens of this platform (`linux-x64`): one set, valid\\n * in Node and in Chromium alike (`judgeRuns`). A replay recorded on another platform only runs at least twice and\\n * compares the runs (\\\"golden: other platform\\\"). Its scene module is found from its `scene` id, as `x sim` finds it,\\n * and loads after the animation library, as there (tools/anim/library.ts; the page: tests/pages/replay.ts).\\n * `--browser page` plays each replay in its scene's own page instead (`labs/<name>/?scene=<scene>` for a module under\\n * `labs/<name>/scenes/`, through `__engine.replay`, engine/app/playback.ts), drawing a frame after every step: the\\n20→ * CPU-only gameplay contract's proof that rendering never changes play (§6.7). Fixture scenes have no page.\\n *\\n * `--update` (with `--browser sim`, never `--swap`) records this platform's goldens (0, the replay's checkpoints, else\\n * every 60 steps, and the last) and the engine, three.js and Rapier versions. It judges every file and reads the\\n * page's errors first, and writes (through Prettier, readable text) only when every run of every file agreed and the\\n * page threw nothing. `--bisect` hashes every step of a Node run, a second Node run and, with `--browser sim`, a\\n * Chromium run, finds the first step where any two part, and replays both to it: the parts, entities and first field\\n * that differ go into the replay's failure (or its line); when one replay fails, every field that differs\\n * (`diffStates`) and the inputs applied just before follow. When every run agrees but the goldens differ, the code\\n * changed what the sim does: it names the checkpoints between which. `--swap` narrows Chromium's fdlibm swap (`none`,\\n30→ * or `sin,pow`): a replay that depends on the swap then fails, and `--bisect` shows where Node and Chromium part.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * parseSwap('sin,pow'); // ['sin', 'pow']: Chromium leaves cos native\\n * @see tools/cmd/replay.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { existsSync, readFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { basename, join, relative, resolve } from 'node:path';\\nimport { SIM_MATH_NAMES, type SimMathName } from '../../engine/core/simMath';\\nimport { checkReplay, firstDifference, judgeRuns, partingOf, type Parting, type Replay } from '../../engine/sim/replay';\\n40→import { componentTable, hashState } from '../../engine/sim/state';\\nimport { describePageError } from '../lib/pageErrors';\\nimport { replayBrowser, type BrowserMode } from '../lib/page';\\nimport { stateFile, writeState } from '../lib/replayState';\\nimport { walk } from '../lib/docs';\\nimport type { Finding } from '../lib/report';\\nimport { UsageError, wholeFlag, type Command, type CommandResult } from '../x';\\nimport { nodeRuntime, writeReplay, type Runtime } from './sim';\\nimport { resolveSceneModule } from '../lib/scenes';\\n\\n50→/** This platform's golden key: `linux-x64`. */\\nexport const PLATFORM = `${process.platform}-${process.arch}`;\\n\\n/** A run of a replay: which runtime, and the hashes it took. */\\nexport interface Run {\\n  label: string;\\n  runtime: Runtime;\\n  hashes: Record<string, string>;\\n}\\n\\n60→/** Where two runs part: the step, the runs, and what differs there (engine/sim/replay.ts `partingOf`). */\\nexport interface RunParting extends Parting {\\n  step: number;\\n  a: string;\\n  b: string;\\n  /** True when a view's state does not hash to the hash its runtime gave (it changed in transit). */\\n  garbled: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/** The first step where any run parts from the first, compared there (`table` reads the components' registry). */\\n70→export async function findParting(\\n  text: string,\\n  runs: readonly Run[],\\n  table = componentTable(),\\n): Promise<RunParting | undefined> {\\n  let first: { step: number; other: Run } | undefined;\\n  for (const other of runs.slice(1)) {\\n    const step = firstDifference(runs[0].hashes, other.hashes);\\n    if (step !== undefined && (!first || step < first.step)) first = { step, other };\\n  }\\n80→  if (!first) return undefined;\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Replays against their golden hashes (PLAN.md §8.4, §6.5 items 8–9, WPs 1.5 and 2.7). Usage: node x replay\\n * <file|dir…> [--update] [--browser sim|page] [--bisect] [--runs n] [--swap names] [--state] [--until n]. Exit 0 when\\n * every replay gives its goldens in every run (or, recorded elsewhere, agrees with itself; or was recorded), 1\\n * otherwise, 2 on a usage error. The verdict never says \\\"match\\\" unless this platform's goldens were compared.\\n *\\n * `--state` writes the state a replay ends in, as Node plays it: its canonical state and event trace, as `x sim`\\n * writes its own, to `out/replay/<name>/state.json` (`<name>`: the file's, without `.replay.json`); `--until n` (it\\n * implies `--state`) writes the state after step n instead. So an agent reads where a run left its bodies, its props\\n10→ * and its components without a page or a probe of its own (tools/lib/replayState.ts).\\n *\\n * Each `*.replay.json` (a directory means every one under it) plays from step 0 in Node, `--runs` times (3), and with\\n * `--browser sim` as often again in Chromium, in tests/pages/replay.html: the sim in a page, no renderer, through the\\n * same player (engine/sim/replay.ts). Every run must give the goldens of this platform (`linux-x64`): one set, valid\\n * in Node and in Chromium alike (`judgeRuns`). A replay recorded on another platform only runs at least twice and\\n * compares the runs (\\\"golden: other platform\\\"). Its scene module is found from its `scene` id, as `x sim` finds it,\\n * and loads after the animation library, as there (tools/anim/library.ts; the page: tests/pages/replay.ts).\\n * `--browser page` plays each replay in its scene's own page instead (`labs/<name>/?scene=<scene>` for a module under\\n * `labs/<name>/scenes/`, through `__engine.replay`, engine/app/playback.ts), drawing a frame after every step: the\\n20→ * CPU-only gameplay contract's proof that rendering never changes play (§6.7). Fixture scenes have no page.\\n *\\n * `--update` (with `--browser sim`, never `--swap`) records this platform's goldens (0, the replay's checkpoints, else\\n * every 60 steps, and the last) and the engine, three.js and Rapier versions. It judges every file and reads the\\n * page's errors first, and writes (through Prettier, readable text) only when every run of every file agreed and the\\n * page threw nothing. `--bisect` hashes every step of a Node run, a second Node run and, with `--browser sim`, a\\n * Chromium run, finds the first step where any two part, and replays both to it: the parts, entities and first field\\n * that differ go into the replay's failure (or its line); when one replay fails, every field that differs\\n * (`diffStates`) and the inputs applied just before follow. When every run agrees but the goldens differ, the code\\n * changed what the sim does: it names the checkpoints between which. `--swap` narrows Chromium's fdlibm swap (`none`,\\n30→ * or `sin,pow`): a replay that depends on the swap then fails, and `--bisect` shows where Node and Chromium part.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * parseSwap('sin,pow'); // ['sin', 'pow']: Chromium leaves cos native\\n * @see tools/cmd/replay.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { existsSync, readFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { basename, join, relative, resolve } from 'node:path';\\nimport { SIM_MATH_NAMES, type SimMathName } from '../../engine/core/simMath';\\nimport { checkReplay, firstDifference, judgeRuns, partingOf, type Parting, type Replay } from '../../engine/sim/replay';\\n40→import { componentTable, hashState } from '../../engine/sim/state';\\nimport { describePageError } from '../lib/pageErrors';\\nimport { replayBrowser, type BrowserMode } from '../lib/page';\\nimport { stateFile, writeState } from '../lib/replayState';\\nimport { walk } from '../lib/docs';\\nimport type { Finding } from '../lib/report';\\nimport { UsageError, wholeFlag, type Command, type CommandResult } from '../x';\\nimport { nodeRuntime, writeReplay, type Runtime } from './sim';\\nimport { resolveSceneModule } from '../lib/scenes';\\n\\n50→/** This platform's golden key: `linux-x64`. */\\nexport const PLATFORM = `${process.platform}-${process.arch}`;\\n\\n/** A run of a replay: which runtime, and the hashes it took. */\\nexport interface Run {\\n  label: string;\\n  runtime: Runtime;\\n  hashes: Record<string, string>;\\n}\\n\\n60→/** Where two runs part: the step, the runs, and what differs there (engine/sim/replay.ts `partingOf`). */\\nexport interface RunParting extends Parting {\\n  step: number;\\n  a: string;\\n  b: string;\\n  /** True when a view's state does not hash to the hash its runtime gave (it changed in transit). */\\n  garbled: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/** The first step where any run parts from the first, compared there (`table` reads the components' registry). */\\n70→export async function findParting(\\n  text: string,\\n  runs: readonly Run[],\\n  table = componentTable(),\\n): Promise<RunParting | undefined> {\\n  let first: { step: number; other: Run } | undefined;\\n  for (const other of runs.slice(1)) {\\n    const step = firstDifference(runs[0].hashes, other.hashes);\\n    if (step !== undefined && (!first || step < first.step)) first = { step, other };\\n  }\\n80→  if (!first) return undefined;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/tools/cmd/replay.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file Replays against their golden hashes (PLAN.md §8.4, §6.5 items 8–9, WPs 1.5 and 2.7). Usage: node x replay\\n * <file|dir…> [--update] [--browser sim|page] [--bisect] [--runs n] [--swap names] [--state] [--until n]. Exit 0 when\\n * every replay gives its goldens in every run (or, recorded elsewhere, agrees with itself; or was recorded), 1\\n * otherwise, 2 on a usage error. The verdict never says \\\"match\\\" unless this platform's goldens were compared.\\n *\\n * `--state` writes the state a replay ends in, as Node plays it: its canonical state and event trace, as `x sim`\\n * writes its own, to `out/replay/<name>/state.json` (`<name>`: the file's, without `.replay.json`); `--until n` (it\\n * implies `--state`) writes the state after step n instead. So an agent reads where a run left its bodies, its props\\n * and its components without a page or a probe of its own (tools/lib/replayState.ts).\\n *\\n * Each `*.replay.json` (a directory means every one under it) plays from step 0 in Node, `--runs` times (3), and with\\n * `--browser sim` as often again in Chromium, in tests/pages/replay.html: the sim in a page, no renderer, through the\\n * same player (engine/sim/replay.ts). Every run must give the goldens of this platform (`linux-x64`): one set, valid\\n * in Node and in Chromium alike (`judgeRuns`). A replay recorded on another platform only runs at least twice and\\n * compares the runs (\\\"golden: other platform\\\"). Its scene module is found from its `scene` id, as `x sim` finds it,\\n * and loads after the animation library, as there (tools/anim/library.ts; the page: tests/pages/replay.ts).\\n * `--browser page` plays each replay in its scene's own page instead (`labs/<name>/?scene=<scene>` for a module under\\n * `labs/<name>/scenes/`, through `__engine.replay`, engine/app/playback.ts), drawing a frame after every step: the\\n * CPU-only gameplay contract's proof that rendering never changes play (§6.7). Fixture scenes have no page.\\n *\\n * `--update` (with `--browser sim`, never `--swap`) records this platform's goldens (0, the replay's checkpoints, else\\n * every 60 steps, and the last) and the engine, three.js and Rapier versions. It judges every file and reads the\\n * page's errors first, and writes (through Prettier, readable text) only when every run of every file agreed and the\\n * page threw nothing. `--bisect` hashes every step of a Node run, a second Node run and, with `--browser sim`, a\\n * Chromium run, finds the first step where any two part, and replays both to it: the parts, entities and first field\\n * that differ go into the replay's failure (or its line); when one replay fails, every field that differs\\n * (`diffStates`) and the inputs applied just before follow. When every run agrees but the goldens differ, the code\\n * changed what the sim does: it names the checkpoints between which. `--swap` narrows Chromium's fdlibm swap (`none`,\\n * or `sin,pow`): a replay that depends on the swap then fails, and `--bisect` shows where Node and Chromium part.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * parseSwap('sin,pow'); // ['sin', 'pow']: Chromium leaves cos native\\n * @see tools/cmd/replay.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { existsSync, readFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { basename, join, relative, resolve } from 'node:path';\\nimport { SIM_MATH_NAMES, type SimMathName } from '../../engine/core/simMath';\\nimport { checkReplay, firstDifference, judgeRuns, partingOf, type Parting, type Replay } from '../../engine/sim/replay';\\nimport { componentTable, hashState } from '../../engine/sim/state';\\nimport { describePageError } from '../lib/pageErrors';\\nimport { replayBrowser, type BrowserMode } from '../lib/page';\\nimport { stateFile, writeState } from '../lib/replayState';\\nimport { walk } from '../lib/docs';\\nimport type { Finding } from '../lib/report';\\nimport { UsageError, wholeFlag, type Command, type CommandResult } from '../x';\\nimport { nodeRuntime, writeReplay, type Runtime } from './sim';\\nimport { resolveSceneModule } from '../lib/scenes';\\n\\n/** This platform's golden key: `linux-x64`. */\\nexport const PLATFORM = `${process.platform}-${process.arch}`;\\n\\n/** A run of a replay: which runtime, and the hashes it took. */\\nexport interface Run {\\n  label: string;\\n  runtime: Runtime;\\n  hashes: Record<string, string>;\\n}\\n\\n/** Where two runs part: the step, the runs, and what differs there (engine/sim/replay.ts `partingOf`). */\\nexport interface RunParting extends Parting {\\n  step: number;\\n  a: string;\\n  b: string;\\n  /** True when a view's state does not hash to the hash its runtime gave (it changed in transit). */\\n  garbled: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/** The first step where any run parts from the first, compared there (`table` reads the components' registry). */\\nexport async function findParting(\\n  text: string,\\n  runs: readonly Run[],\\n  table = componentTable(),\\n): Promise<RunParting | undefined> {\\n  let first: { step: number; other: Run } | undefined;\\n  for (const other of runs.slice(1)) {\\n    const step = firstDifference(runs[0].hashes, other.hashes);\\n    if (step !== undefined && (!first || step < first.step)) first = { step, other };\\n  }\\n  if (!first) return undefined;\\n\",\"total_lines\":393}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e024a741-8a55-49e9-bf95-72d52828ed5c-68","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"40→  store: Store;\\n  hub: boolean;\\n  touch: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/** The page the frame loop drives. */\\nexport interface Page {\\n  modal(): boolean;\\n  frame(frame: EngineFrame): void;\\n  follow(): readonly [number, number, number];\\n50→  bind(engine: Engine): void;\\n  client: HubClient | null;\\n}\\n\\nconst LURE_IDS = new Set(LURES.map((lure) => lure.id));\\n\\n/** Builds the shell and keeps it in step with the sim. */\\nexport function createPage(options: PageOptions): Page {\\n  const { audio, store, hub, touch } = options;\\n  const client = (window as unknown as { AIHub?: HubClient }).AIHub ?? null;\\n60→  const root = document.createElement('div');\\n  root.id = 'shell';\\n  root.dataset.ui = 'shell';\\n  document.body.append(root);\\n  const note = para('note');\\n  const disc = document.createElement('div');\\n  disc.dataset.ui = 'disc';\\n  disc.innerHTML =\\n    '<svg viewBox=\\\"0 0 100 100\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"><circle cx=\\\"50\\\" cy=\\\"50\\\" r=\\\"46\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#FF8A70\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><circle id=\\\"dot\\\" cx=\\\"50\\\" cy=\\\"50\\\" r=\\\"5\\\" fill=\\\"#3A4A55\\\"/></svg>';\\n  const banner = para('banner');\\n70→  const copy = para('copy');\\n  const about = document.createElement('div');\\n  about.dataset.ui = 'about';\\n  about.hidden = true;\\n  const sliders = document.createElement('div');\\n  sliders.dataset.ui = 'sliders';\\n  sliders.hidden = true;\\n  const touchBtn = document.createElement('button');\\n  touchBtn.type = 'button';\\n  touchBtn.dataset.ui = 'touch-settings';\\n80→  touchBtn.textContent = 'Settings';\\n  root.append(note, disc, banner, copy, about, sliders, touchBtn);\\n\\n  let engine: Engine | null = null;\\n  let menu: Menu | null = null;\\n  let screen = touch ? 'touch' : 'title';\\n  let attract = false;\\n  let armed = !touch;\\n  let icons: Prefs['icons'] = 'playstation';\\n  let glyphSet: GlyphSet = 'playstation';\\n90→  let lastDevice = 'gamepad';\\n  let focus = '';\\n  let prefs = freshPrefs();\\n  let save = readSave(store) ?? freshSave();\\n  prefs = save.settings;\\n  icons = prefs.icons;\\n  const live: Live = { event: '', mode: 'title', result: 0, calm: 0, rank: '', age: 0, pebbles: 0 };\\n  let lastInput = performance.now();\\n  let touchAt = 0;\\n  let mouseDx = 0;\\n100→  let mouseDy = 0;\\n  let song = '';\\n  let said = '';\\n  let savedKey = '';\\n  let look = '';\\n  let lookOk = true;\\n  let ended = false;\\n  let shownFrame: EngineFrame | null = null;\\n  let hubView: HubView | null = null;\\n  const feet: readonly [number, number, number] = [0, 1.4, 6];\\n110→  let follow: readonly [number, number, number] = feet;\\n\\n  const publish = () => {\\n    const handle: GameHandle = {\\n      title: 'Thumb Yoga',\\n      screen,\\n      attract,\\n      lastDevice,\\n      glyphSet,\\n      volumes: { music: prefs.music, effects: prefs.effects, voices: prefs.voices },\\n120→      day: save.day,\\n      event: live.event,\\n      focus,\\n    };\\n    (window as unknown as { __game?: GameHandle }).__game = handle;\\n  };\\n  const inspector = (): Inspector | null => engine?.inspector ?? null;\\n  const run = (name: string, args?: Record<string, unknown>) => {\\n    const actions = inspector()?.actions as\\n      { run?: (id: string, body?: Record<string, unknown>) => unknown } | undefined;\\n130→    if (typeof actions?.run === 'function') actions.run(name, args);\\n  };\\n  const applyPrefs = () => {\\n    audio.volume('music', prefs.music);\\n    audio.volume('effects', prefs.effects);\\n    audio.volume('ui', prefs.voices);\\n    inspector()?.set('game.assist', prefs.assist);\\n    inspector()?.set('game.cpu', prefs.cpu);\\n    glyphSet = lastDevice === 'keyboard' ? 'keys' : lastDevice === 'mouse' ? 'mouse' : icons;\\n  };\\n140→  const persist = () => {\\n    save = { ...save, outfits: [], settings: { ...prefs, icons } };\\n    if (attract || hub) return;\\n    writeSave(store, save);\\n  };\\n  const close = () => {\\n    menu?.remove();\\n    menu = null;\\n  };\\n  const open = (\\n150→    items: MenuItem[],\\n    title: string,\\n    id: string,\\n    onPick: (itemId: string) => void,\\n    onCancel?: () => void,\\n  ) => {\\n    const input = engine?.input;\\n    if (!input) return;\\n    close();\\n    screen = id;\\n160→    menu = createMenu(root, items.slice(0, 6), {\\n      input,\\n      id,\\n      title,\\n      onCancel: () => onCancel?.(),\\n      onPick: (_index, item) => onPick(typeof item === 'string' ? item : (item.id ?? item.label)),\\n    });\\n    focus = labelOf(menu.selected);\\n    publish();\\n  };\\n170→  const resume = () => {\\n    if (!hub) inspector()?.resume();\\n    close();\\n    screen = hub && hubView && !hubView.playing ? 'card' : 'play';\\n    publish();\\n  };\\n  const described = (path: string, key: string): number => {\\n    const row = inspector()?.describe('setting', path) as { fields?: { key: string; value: unknown }[] } | undefined;\\n    const field = row?.fields?.find((item) => item.key === key);\\n    return typeof field?.value === 'number' ? field.value : 0;\\n180→  };\\n\\n  const host: Host = {\\n    hub,\\n    get attract() {\\n      return attract;\\n    },\\n    set attract(value) {\\n      attract = value;\\n    },\\n190→    get screen() {\\n      return screen;\\n    },\\n    set screen(value) {\\n      screen = value;\\n    },\\n    get icons() {\\n      return icons;\\n    },\\n    set icons(value) {\\n200→      icons = value;\\n    },\\n    get prefs() {\\n      return prefs;\\n    },\\n    set prefs(value) {\\n      prefs = value;\\n    },\\n    get save() {\\n      return save;\\n210→    },\\n    set save(value) {\\n      save = value;\\n    },\\n    live,\\n    note,\\n    about,\\n    sliders,\\n    store,\\n    devPage: 0,\\n220→    jumpPage: 0,\\n    bindPage: 0,\\n    pausePage: 0,\\n    aboutFrom: 'title',\\n    get lastDevice() {\\n      return lastDevice;\\n    },\\n    engine: () => engine,\\n    inspector,\\n    run,\\n230→    open,\\n    close,\\n    applyPrefs,\\n    persist,\\n    resume,\\n    publish,\\n    setting(path) {\\n      const value = shownFrame?.setting(path);\\n      return typeof value === 'number' && Number.isFinite(value) ? value : described(path, 'default');\\n    },\\n240→    settingDefault: (path) => described(path, 'default'),\\n  };\\n  const menus: Menus = createMenus(host);\\n  hubView =\\n    hub && client\\n      ? createHub(\\n          {\\n            audio,\\n            client,\\n            run,\\n250→            engine: () => engine,\\n            ended: () => ended,\\n            markEnded: () => {\\n              ended = true;\\n            },\\n          },\\n          root,\\n        )\\n      : null;\\n\\n260→  const noteDevice = (device: string) => {\\n    lastDevice = device;\\n    glyphSet = device === 'keyboard' ? 'keys' : device === 'mouse' ? 'mouse' : icons;\\n    lastInput = performance.now();\\n    publish();\\n  };\\n  const exitAttract = () => {\\n    if (!attract) return;\\n    attract = false;\\n    lastInput = performance.now();\\n270→    inspector()?.set('game.auto', 'off');\\n    const seed = inspector()?.seed() ?? 1;\\n    inspector()?.seed(seed);\\n    if (armed) menus.showTitle();\\n    else screen = 'touch';\\n  };\\n  const startAttract = () => {\\n    attract = true;\\n    inspector()?.set('game.auto', 'attract');\\n    const seed = inspector()?.seed() ?? 1;\\n280→    inspector()?.seed(seed);\\n    if (screen === 'title' || screen === 'touch') close();\\n    if (screen !== 'settings' && screen !== 'about' && screen !== 'controls' && screen !== 'programme')\\n      screen = 'attract';\\n    publish();\\n  };\\n\\n  touchBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {\\n    touchAt = performance.now();\\n    menus.showSettings(0);\",\"content_concise\":\"40→  store: Store;\\n  hub: boolean;\\n  touch: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/** The page the frame loop drives. */\\nexport interface Page {\\n  modal(): boolean;\\n  frame(frame: EngineFrame): void;\\n  follow(): readonly [number, number, number];\\n50→  bind(engine: Engine): void;\\n  client: HubClient | null;\\n}\\n\\nconst LURE_IDS = new Set(LURES.map((lure) => lure.id));\\n\\n/** Builds the shell and keeps it in step with the sim. */\\nexport function createPage(options: PageOptions): Page {\\n  const { audio, store, hub, touch } = options;\\n  const client = (window as unknown as { AIHub?: HubClient }).AIHub ?? null;\\n60→  const root = document.createElement('div');\\n  root.id = 'shell';\\n  root.dataset.ui = 'shell';\\n  document.body.append(root);\\n  const note = para('note');\\n  const disc = document.createElement('div');\\n  disc.dataset.ui = 'disc';\\n  disc.innerHTML =\\n    '<svg viewBox=\\\"0 0 100 100\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"><circle cx=\\\"50\\\" cy=\\\"50\\\" r=\\\"46\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#FF8A70\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><circle id=\\\"dot\\\" cx=\\\"50\\\" cy=\\\"50\\\" r=\\\"5\\\" fill=\\\"#3A4A55\\\"/></svg>';\\n  const banner = para('banner');\\n70→  const copy = para('copy');\\n  const about = document.createElement('div');\\n  about.dataset.ui = 'about';\\n  about.hidden = true;\\n  const sliders = document.createElement('div');\\n  sliders.dataset.ui = 'sliders';\\n  sliders.hidden = true;\\n  const touchBtn = document.createElement('button');\\n  touchBtn.type = 'button';\\n  touchBtn.dataset.ui = 'touch-settings';\\n80→  touchBtn.textContent = 'Settings';\\n  root.append(note, disc, banner, copy, about, sliders, touchBtn);\\n\\n  let engine: Engine | null = null;\\n  let menu: Menu | null = null;\\n  let screen = touch ? 'touch' : 'title';\\n  let attract = false;\\n  let armed = !touch;\\n  let icons: Prefs['icons'] = 'playstation';\\n  let glyphSet: GlyphSet = 'playstation';\\n90→  let lastDevice = 'gamepad';\\n  let focus = '';\\n  let prefs = freshPrefs();\\n  let save = readSave(store) ?? freshSave();\\n  prefs = save.settings;\\n  icons = prefs.icons;\\n  const live: Live = { event: '', mode: 'title', result: 0, calm: 0, rank: '', age: 0, pebbles: 0 };\\n  let lastInput = performance.now();\\n  let touchAt = 0;\\n  let mouseDx = 0;\\n100→  let mouseDy = 0;\\n  let song = '';\\n  let said = '';\\n  let savedKey = '';\\n  let look = '';\\n  let lookOk = true;\\n  let ended = false;\\n  let shownFrame: EngineFrame | null = null;\\n  let hubView: HubView | null = null;\\n  const feet: readonly [number, number, number] = [0, 1.4, 6];\\n110→  let follow: readonly [number, number, number] = feet;\\n\\n  const publish 