nd shore, and a flat sea.',\\n  animation: 'The engine clip layer. Original poses are scrubbed from the balance step. The rest pose is Mesh2Motion.',\\n  audio: 'Tracker songs, code-made effects, and gibberish syllable voices. A fresh save plays music at a tenth.',\\n  online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, and same-screen Group Class on its own.',\\n  testing: 'Bot bands on ten seeds, a three-seed walk to the credits, and browser checks of the built file.',\\n  research: 'none',\\n  environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\\n  model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\\n  usage: 'added on import',\\n} as const;\\n\\n/** Testing Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const TESTING = [\\n  'Testing caught eight issues before hand-in. They were score bands, a NaN prop yaw, a missing boot setting, over-long lines, and a ghost pack read at the wrong offset.',\\n  'Four were critical. Three activities scored under their band, and the island would not boot.',\\n  'The most helpful test was the four bot bands on ten seeds for every shipped activity.',\\n  'The least helpful was a headless screenshot. The canvas can be blank while the sim state is fine.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Engine Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const ENGINE = [\\n  'Scene actions, live settings, and a headless world you can step made the week testable without a browser.',\\n  'I got stuck on playClip during setup, props that need a yaw, a frozen recorded world, and hub query keys read as settings.',\\n  'The balance step, the day director, the songs, and the syllable voices are the game’s own.',\\n  'The hardest part was keeping the pavilion small enough for the hub ready deadline while the island stayed a place.',\\n  'None. The engine files were not changed.',\\n  'I would let a page add a mesh, and I would start the music bus at a tenth instead of a half.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Prompt Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const PROMPT = [\\n  'The acceptance numbers, the cut line, and the bot bands made the scope checkable.',\\n  'The group score is described as a sum to 3000 and also has to fit a rank from 0 to 1000. Several seed lines are longer than two sentences.',\\n  'The hardest part was one HTML file that is a full retreat and also a ghost session the harness can drive.',\\n  'I would state the group score once, and pin the session client hash to the file the plan says to fetch.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Credits shown under the same About screen. */\\nexport const CREDITS = [\\n  'my-3dge, MIT.',\\n  'three.js r182, MIT.',\\n  'Rapier 0.21, Apache-2.0.',\\n  '@stdlib, Apache-2.0.',\\n  'AI Hub session client 1.4.0, pasted unmodified.',\\n  'The rest pose follows Mesh2Motion. The pose clips themselves are original.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Catalogue fields. The source name is only here and in SOURCE.source. */\\nexport const AI_HUB = {\\n  name: 'Thumb Yoga',\\n  tagline: 'A week of balance at Little Fulcrum',\\n  description: 'Stand on the disc and keep the dot near the middle. Little Fulcrum runs five days of pose, pond, water, sand, and a storm.',\\n  type: 'Game',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  series: '',\\n  players: '1–4',\\n  controls: 'Lean with the left stick, WASD or the mouse. L2 and R2, or Q and E, are the feet. Both feet or Space breathe.',\\n  tags: ['3d', 'sports', 'third-person', 'comedy', 'co-op'],\\n} as const;\\n\\n/** The exit-interview object. The screen and the file both read this. */\\nexport const EXIT = {\\n  sourceInformation: SOURCE,\\n  testingFeedback: [...TESTING],\\n  engineFeedback: [...ENGINE],\\n  promptFeedback: [...PROMPT],\\n  aiHub: AI_HUB,\\n};\\n\",\"total_lines\":80}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"82564e24-616a-4517-af81-88933fd1c09f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_501","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"TESTING answers claim eight issues and four critical items, yet only list five.\n\nI will correct the issue count later once I know the true tally. The ghost pack, bands, NaN yaw, missing setting, and long lines are confirmed. I may add the import path bug and unused sunkNow. Next steps are adding @file directives to bridge.js and round.js, adding overlay font CSS, and adding console logs for seeds in the director test.\n\nI will write a comprehensive verify.mjs script and run a fast island test to confirm loading before the full suite. The prompt lines are two short sentences each, satisfying the plan. I also noticed the prompt uses LT and RT instead of LB and RB, which may not match the test's expected glyphs.\n\nThe prompt must include the full Xbox glyph set—A, B, X, Y, LB, RB, LT, RT—when the gamepad is set to Xbox or PlayStation. The test searches visible text for these names after the Settings switch. I will add them to the prompt line while keeping it within two short sentences.\n\nAdding the full Xbox glyph set to the prompt line might exceed the two-sentence limit. When a menu is open, the note element is not updated to the prompt text, so it may remain empty or show leftover content. The test checks both the internal glyphSet and the visible prompt text.\n\nThe default glyphSet is 'playstation'. The test expects prompts to switch to keys and mouse in the same frame. I will ensure the note text remains visible even when a menu is open so the test can read it.\n\nI am refining the paint function to show prompt text on the note element even when a menu is open, while preserving existing lure sentences. The exact conditional logic is being finalized.\n\nThe paint function will show the prompt line on the note element whenever a menu is open, while still displaying activity sentences during play. The prompt text itself is being rewritten to include the full set of Xbox glyphs—A, B, X, Y, LB, RB, LT, and RT—so the test can read them in both the PlayStation and Xbox variants.\n\nThe prompt lines are finalized at two sentences each. The keys and mouse variants use Enter, WASD, Click, and Mouse to satisfy the test. I am also verifying that the pause menu includes all required items across both pages.\n\nThe pause menu contains all required items across both pages, with no page exceeding six entries. Dev Mode is correctly absent from the hub pause screen. The attract-mode timeout uses performance.now() and resets on input, so it behaves properly. I am checking the engine loop timing: the loop starts before bind resolves, but frame() only drives the engine once bind sets it, so attract mode cannot begin until then.\n\nThe audio volume is set to 0.1 before createPage, and applyPrefs restores it from preferences. A leftover save in localStorage could override that value on the next boot.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-882fb39f-8255-404c-a86b-614b26a8dc3f-93","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"game\\.begin|function begin|autoOf","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/driver.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2885,"output_tokens":1898,"cache_read_input_tokens":121856,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"91b88ab1-b2b3-497d-8047-c5c318f6dcc7"}
