{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_507","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll generate a replay using `node x sim`.\n\nI'll run `node x sim` with 120 steps to generate the replay file. I'll check the REPLAY_FORMAT value and add a director console.log before the expect statement. I'll also verify whether `out/` is gitignored.\n\nI'll add a non-silent audio check and update glyph prompts. I'll add an overlay font rule to CSS and include the @file directive in hub.js. I'll write verify.mjs, draft PROGRESS.md, and generate exit-interview.json from the EXIT data.\n\nI'm tallying the actual bugs to match the testing answers. Seven issues are critical and four are not. The critical ones include score band failures, NaN prop yaw, missing game.auto, ghost pack offset, group.ts const redeclaration, and wrong import depth.\n\nThe import path bug may have been hidden by TypeScript path mapping or Vitest's Vite resolver. The filesystem path was never correct.\n\nThe import path bug likely caused tests to fail, not pass. The summary's claim of a last green run is probably stale. I'll fix the counts honestly without inflating them.\n\nTesting caught six issues before hand-in. Three were critical: score bands, the missing boot setting, and the wrong import depth.\n\nI'll update about-data before the HTML build so the files stay in sync. Research is set to \"none\" per the plan. I need to verify titles.json exists and check that ESLint warnings won't fail.\n\nThe `@file` tag will be added to the JSDoc block in bridge.js. ESLint requires this tag for the check to pass, and the plan permits editing fetched files.\n\nI cannot modify the engine's eslint.config.js because that would break the engine lock. Adding @file to the game files is safe since labs/game is outside the engine scope. I'll run prettier --write on the edited files afterward.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f341ed0b-6111-4974-9ff0-50076