   if (asking() && (repeat(input, 'uiDown', dt) || repeat(input, 'uiRight', dt))) mark(choice + 1);\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/ui/menu.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":7,\"content\":\" * `uiUp` and `uiDown` (keys, the pad's D-pad and left stick; held, they repeat: engine/ui/widgets.ts `createRepeat`)\"},{\"line_number\":173,\"content\":\"      if (repeat(input, 'uiDown', dt)) move(index + 1, 1);\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/ui/widgets.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":16,\"content\":\" * `lastDevice`, over the system layer's `uiAccept`, `uiCancel` and `uiUp`/`uiDown`/`uiLeft`/`uiRight`, which never enter\"},{\"line_number\":262,\"content\":\"      const stick = [input.strength('uiRight') - input.strength('uiLeft'), input.strength('uiDown') - input.strength('uiUp')]; // prettier-ignore\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/actionMaps.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":50,\"content\":\"  uiDown: ['ArrowDown', 'PadDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"1a46b0e7-f04f-464d-94dd-d92adb3f542c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_516","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Updating menus on each frame based on input.\n\nPlaywright keyboard presses should trigger the engine's keydown listener. Hovering menu items may not generate movement events, so I'll dispatch a pointermove with movementX if needed. Clicks will select rows through the existing handler.\n\nAttract mode requires three separate exits to test key, click, and pad inputs. This will take over 30 seconds. The save key in localStorage is thumb-yoga:save.\n\nAttract mode won't write to localStorage, so the save key should remain absent before and after. The attract test must run on the title screen before any begin press. I'll use separate pages or a single long script for the dev slider test.\n\nFont size checks will skip hidden elements. The title screen has six visible menu items. WebKit launches the page and expects a Chrome or Edge message, since it lacks WebGPU support.\n\nThree.js imports may throw before the GPU check in WebKit. The current error handler only shows a generic message. I'll add an inline script before the module to display the Chrome or Edge text if navigator.gpu is missing.\n\nThe inline script will be placed right after the #msg element in the body so it reliably sets the WebGPU message before any module imports run. The iPhone profile uses hover:none and pointer:coarse, which correctly marks touch as true.\n\nTouch screens enter attract mode after ten seconds without input, even though the touch button is hidden while armed. The settings button remains visible on touch devices.\n\nTapping the settings button on a touch screen does not set armed, so the touch button stays visible. The attract timer continues running while the settings screen is open; it only switches to attract mode when the user exits settings.\n\nI'll verify the engine does not add a .touch-stick class when touch is disabled. The font size formula should keep text at least 28 pixels even on an iPhone viewport. I'll implement all tests and run a comprehensive Python browser script from verify.mjs.\n\nBrowser checks will live in labs/game/tools/browser.mjs. Playwright from the project's node_modules will be tried first, falling back to Python if the shell cannot launch it. Chromium executable paths should work across minor versions. I'll verify the playwright import later.\n\nPython will handle browser automation to avoid Playwright version mismatches. The script lives in labs/game/tools/browse.py and is invoked by verify.mjs. I will tee the runner's stdout into scratch/verify.log. Boot logs and screenshots should be written to SCRATCH.\n\nThe Python browser script will accept an output directory argument. verify.mjs will pass the scratch path via VERIFY_SCRATCH or argv. Hardcoding the session-specific scratch path inside the game repository is acceptable.\n\nI'll use VERIFY_OUT to route boot logs and screenshots into the scratch directory. npm test and npm check logs are handled separately. I also need to inspect how the engine sets canvas width.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b693f6c0-41cc-4e4c-babc-26c7bce495fc-115","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"canvas\\.width|devicePixelRatio|drawingBuffer","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/gfx","glob":"**/*.ts","head_limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":748,"output_tokens":1922,"cache_read_input_tokens":150400,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"72dd2fe3-4768-4dbc-8e6b-0bf8a95fcc2e"}
