01,115,116,32,70,105,108,101,115,32,32,50,32,112,97,115,115,101,100,32,40,50,41,10,32,32,32,32,32,32,84,101,115,116,115,32,32,53,32,112,97,115,115,101,100,32,40,53,41,10,32,32,32,83,116,97,114,116,32,97,116,32,32,48,49,58,48,48,58,51,57,10,32,32,32,68,117,114,97,116,105,111,110,32,32,54,46,49,51,115,32,40,116,114,97,110,115,102,111,114,109,32,56,46,48,48,115,44,32,115,101,116,117,112,32,49,52,49,109,115,44,32,105,109,112,111,114,116,32,49,48,46,56,52,115,44,32,116,101,115,116,115,32,51,48,57,109,115,44,32,101,110,118,105,114,111,110,109,101,110,116,32,48,109,115,41,10,10],\"output_for_prompt\":\"exit: 0\\n(node:84115) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n(node:84129) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n\\n RUN  v4.1.12 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656\\n\\n(node:84155) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n(node:84156) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n ✓ labs/game/island.test.ts > places > boots the island and walks a step 99ms\\n ✓ labs/game/island.test.ts > places > boots the pavilion and keeps a ghost seat 3ms\\n ✓ labs/game/audio.test.ts > sound and lines > renders every song with samples 187ms\\n ✓ labs/game/audio.test.ts > sound and lines > renders a syllable for every speaker 7ms\\n ✓ labs/game/audio.test.ts > sound and lines > keeps two hundred short lines, and Plumb never shouts 8ms\\n\\n Test Files  2 passed (2)\\n      Tests  5 passed (5)\\n   Start at  01:00:39\\n   Duration  6.13s (transform 8.00s, setup 141ms, import 10.84s, tests 309ms, environment 0ms)\\n\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"cd \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656\\\" && npx vitest run labs/game/island.test.ts labs/game/audio.test.ts --reporter=verbose 2>&1 | tail -40\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Run island and audio tests\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc%2Fwork/01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc/terminal/call-79f4547f-2ca5-4671-9abf-fb758ff6ab84-150.log\",\"total_bytes\":1426}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"02d6cea7-69c2-4a3e-9c0e-072c361b1c0b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_537","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Island and audio checks passed. Ghost seat check passed.\n\nSongs are non-silent and lines pass. I will write verify.mjs and browse.py next, then launch the ~3-minute retreat test in the background while writing scripts.\n\nI will wait for vitest to finish before launching browsers to avoid memory pressure. I am drafting verify.mjs now.\n\nverify.mjs is being written with Node.js child_process and fs modules. It will run vitest on retreat, island, and audio tests, with a --quick flag support.\n\nThe script parses vitest output to collect credit seed notes and failure lines. It flags a missing seed 1 credits line when the process exits successfully.\n\nverify.mjs now checks that seeds 2 and 3 also reach credits. It appends notes about songs and syllables rendering. The script skips replay and browser checks when --quick is used. Otherwise it runs the replay golden test and prepares to launch the Python browser script.\n\nverify.mjs now runs browse.py via python3 and prints the final failure count. A golden replay file is needed before the browser test can run, so I will generate it while writing browse.py. x replay already handles capture and restore.\n\nA golden replay file must exist before the browser test can run. I will generate one with x sim using 30 steps. The bench scene is instant in Node, but a Chromium replay of 60 steps may take 10–20 seconds. I am weighing whether to run the retreat vitest and x sim in parallel, since both are CPU-heavy and could contend for resources.\n\nI will run x sim first to generate the replay golden file, then start the retreat vitest in the background. I am beginning browse.py and verify.mjs now. After the retreat test finishes, I will update the goldens with x replay --update if it passes, then build HTML and run the browser script. I will also run npm test and npm check at the end.\n\nbrowse.py is being drafted with the Playwright Python sync API. It will launch Chromium, boot twice, and test glyphs, hover, attract, dev, about, fonts, menus, webkit messages, mobile views, the hub harness, and standalone client behavior.\n\nThe browser script will launch Chromium with sandbox and Vulkan flags. It navigates to a file URL and waits for the engine ready signal. Boot state and game state will be dumped as JSON. Screenshots will be saved. A custom init script will replace getGamepads so the engine can be polled frame by frame.\n\nThe scripted pad will expose a `window.__pad` object with 16 buttons and four axes. Standard mapping assigns button 0 to Cross, 1 to Circle, and the directional buttons to 12–15. The engine expects `mapping: 'standard'`, `connected: true`, and `id: 'Scripted Pad'`. A test can press Cross by setting `buttons[0].pressed = true`, waiting one frame, then clearing it.\n\nThe scripted pad now maps button values to pressed, value, and touched states. Menu accept is button 0 and uiDown is button 13. Both boots will press the same pad sequence and compare __game state. The glyph test will verify note text shows Cross instead of \" A confirms\", open settings via keyboard or pad, toggle icons to xbox, and expect all eight controller buttons.\n\nKeyboard navigation would switch lastDevice to keyboard before the xbox toggle, so the pad must handle settings navigation instead. The glyph test sequence is now: boot with playstation glyphs, pad down to Settings and press south, pad down to Icons and press south, then verify all eight controller buttons appear in the note text. After that, a keypress will switch glyphSet to keys and immediately evaluate __game.glyphSet.\n\nPlaywright waits for the keypress event before evaluating glyphSet, so no extra tick is needed. A canvas click will set glyphSet to mouse, and the note text should contain Mouse or Click. For hover, a pointermove with movementY on the second title menu item will be dispatched, then focus or data-value selected will be checked.\n\nThe attract test will reload the page, wait 10.2 seconds for the attract state to become true, record localStorage, then press a key and click to exit attract while verifying localStorage stays unchanged. The dev menu check is complicated because Escape from the title screen may trigger uiCancel instead of pause.\n\nTo reach the dev menu, the test will begin the game by pressing PadSouth on the title screen, wait for the play screen, then press Escape to pause. The keyboard device state is acceptable here. From the pause menu, it will navigate to More and select Dev Mode.\n\nThe dev menu will be reached by clicking the More and Dev items. Clicking sets the mouse device, which is acceptable.\n\nFor the slider test, `state().settings` may omit default values, so the script will query the DOM directly to read the slider before and after adjustment.\n\nThe slider test will set the range to 20 and dispatch an input event, then verify the setting equals 20. It will then click Reset and confirm the value returns to its default or is absent. The About screen will be checked for SOURCE fields and feedback answers. Font rendering will be tested by walking text nodes at 1920x1080. Menu items will be counted to ensure there are no more than six.\n\nThe title, pause, and settings menus will each be checked to contain exactly six items. WebKit tests will run in a separate browser and expect Chrome or Edge in the status message. Touch testing requires Chromium with the iPhone 13 device profile because the game needs WebGPU for attract mode; that profile includes SwiftShader flags. The script will launch Chromium using p.devices['iPhone 13'].\n\nThe iPhone 13 device context works with a custom executable. The touch test will tap the settings button, wait for the menu to appear, and verify no touch-stick element exists. After waiting eleven seconds, it will confirm attract mode is active. Tablet testing will use an iPad or iPad Pro 11 profile. For the standalone client check, the script will load the HTML directly without the hub, press Enter and Space twice, and confirm the client is present but inactive because Math.random remains unseeded. The client only seeds Math.random when an aihub-seed parameter is present.\n\nThe standalone client check will verify that window.AIHub exists with active set to false and seeded set to not true. The Enter Space Enter Space sequence must not throw or alter that state. Hub tests will run through a Python HTTP server started inside browse.py.\n\nThe Python HTTP server will serve the work root so both the game HTML and dev folder are accessible. The hub harness URL will pass the game path as a query parameter, with players set to two, latency to 150 ms, jitter to 50 ms, loss to 5 percent, auto mode enabled, and play time set to eight seconds. Each hub run is expected to take roughly sixty to ninety seconds.\n\nFour hub runs will take about six minutes, and the full browser script should finish in roughly ten minutes. To verify engine readiness during each run, the script will poll every iframe for `__engine.ready === true` and zero errors.\n\nThe script will poll every iframe for `__engine.ready` and error counts every 500 milliseconds during the harness run. It will record any frame where readiness drops after the first true state or where errors exceed zero. Boot frames are excluded from this check because `ready` is false until the first GPU frame.\n\nThe harness will poll after the initial ready event and fail only if readiness drops or errors appear after that point. The final state must show ready true and zero errors. Boot frames are included but will be logged as \"engine ready held\". A ghost test for two players is also being drafted.\n\nThe ghost test will inspect `__engine.state().entities` for entities with a `ghost` component. Console messages from the page and iframes will be captured to verify AIHub output.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9f9ca685-058d-4466-ba3e-965fd2713978-151","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/save.ts","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9f9ca685-058d-4466-ba3e-965fd2713978-152","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/app/store.ts","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":844,"output_tokens":4193,"cache_read_input_tokens":170752,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"d824965b-0209-4d08-919b-8c22293a3ff8"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9f9ca685-058d-4466-ba3e-965fd2713978-151","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The retreat save. The sim never reads the store. The page copies this in through game.begin.\\n * Outfits stay an empty list. Pebbles are kept and never spent.\\n */\\nimport type { Store } from '../../../engine';\\n\\n/** What the player turned in Settings. */\\nexport interface Prefs {\\n  music: number;\\n10→  effects: number;\\n  voices: number;\\n  icons: 'playstation' | 'xbox';\\n  assist: number;\\n  cpu: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** One saved week. */\\nexport interface Save {\\n  day: number;\\n20→  cursor: number;\\n  pebbles: number;\\n  age: number;\\n  prior: number;\\n  credits: number;\\n  result: number;\\n  seen: string;\\n  rank: string;\\n  bests: Record<string, number>;\\n  finds: string[];\\n30→  outfits: string[];\\n  settings: Prefs;\\n}\\n\\n/** The store key. */\\nexport const SAVE_KEY = 'save';\\n\\n/** Volumes and switches for a guest who has never saved. */\\nexport function freshPrefs(): Prefs {\\n  return { music: 0.1, effects: 1, voices: 1, icons: 'playstation', assist: 0, cpu: 1 };\\n40→}\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The retreat save. The sim never reads the store. The page copies this in through game.begin.\\n * Outfits stay an empty list. Pebbles are kept and never spent.\\n */\\nimport type { Store } from '../../../engine';\\n\\n/** What the player turned in Settings. */\\nexport interface Prefs {\\n  music: number;\\n10→  effects: number;\\n  voices: number;\\n  icons: 'playstation' | 'xbox';\\n  assist: number;\\n  cpu: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** One saved week. */\\nexport interface Save {\\n  day: number;\\n20→  cursor: number;\\n  pebbles: number;\\n  age: number;\\n  prior: number;\\n  credits: number;\\n  result: number;\\n  seen: string;\\n  rank: string;\\n  bests: Record<string, number>;\\n  finds: string[];\\n30→  outfits: string[];\\n  settings: Prefs;\\n}\\n\\n/** The store key. */\\nexport const SAVE_KEY = 'save';\\n\\n/** Volumes and switches for a guest who has never saved. */\\nexport function freshPrefs(): Prefs {\\n  return { music: 0.1, effects: 1, voices: 1, icons: 'playstation', assist: 0, cpu: 1 };\\n40→}\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/save.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The retreat save. The sim never reads the store. The page copies this in through game.begin.\\n * Outfits stay an empty list. Pebbles are kept and never spent.\\n */\\nimport type { Store } from '../../../engine';\\n\\n/** What the player turned in Settings. */\\nexport interface Prefs {\\n  music: number;\\n  effects: number;\\n  voices: number;\\n  icons: 'playstation' | 'xbox';\\n  assist: number;\\n  cpu: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** One saved week. */\\nexport interface Save {\\n  day: number;\\n  cursor: number;\\n  pebbles: number;\\n  age: number;\\n  prior: number;\\n  credits: number;\\n  result: number;\\n  seen: string;\\n  rank: string;\\n  bests: Record<string, number>;\\n  finds: string[];\\n  outfits: string[];\\n  settings: Prefs;\\n}\\n\\n/** The store key. */\\nexport const SAVE_KEY = 'save';\\n\\n/** Volumes and switches for a guest who has never saved. */\\nexport function freshPrefs(): Prefs {\\n  return { music: 0.1, effects: 1, voices: 1, icons: 'playstation', assist: 0, cpu: 1 };\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":70}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9f9ca685-058d-4466-ba3e-965fd2713978-152","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The store (PLAN.md WP 10.9, §9.1, ADR-0024): what a game keeps across sessions, outside the sim (high scores,\\n * progress, its settings). `createStore({ prefix, version, mode, backend, migrate })` reads and writes plain data as\\n * JSON under `prefix + key` in the page's `localStorage`, else in memory: in Node, where the page blocks storage\\n * (advice `APP_STORE_BLOCKED`, once), and in the modes that must leave a player's saves alone, `demo` (a replay or an\\n * attract loop), `sandbox` (a developer's throwaway play) and `gallery` (sheets and shots): their memory starts empty\\n * and dies with the page, so what they play is never kept over what the player played.\\n *\\n * Every value is written in its envelope, `{ format: 'my3dge-store/1', version, data }`, and checked when read (shardfall\\n10→ * writes a version and never checks it): a value of another format or version is not handed back as it is. With\\n * `migrate(data, version)` the store makes it the current version (and writes it back); without, the reader gets its\\n * fallback, the value stays until `set` replaces it, and the advice `APP_STORE_VERSION` names the key once.\\n *\\n * Invariants: storage never throws here (a full or refused write returns false; a value that is not JSON reads as its\\n * fallback); values go in and come out as copies (JSON), so a caller's object never aliases the store's; only keys\\n * under the prefix are listed or cleared, so games and pages sharing an origin keep apart (pick a prefix of the game's\\n * own, `my3dge-game:`). Sim-side code cannot import the app layer, so the sim never reads a store and nothing kept can\\n * change a replay. Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:196-200` (`store`: get with a fallback, set, remove,\\n * never throwing), the fixed `my3d2dge:` prefix made the store's own.\\n20→ *\\n * @example\\n * import { createLog } from '../core/log';\\n * const store = createStore({ prefix: 'demo-game:', backend: memoryBackend() });\\n * store.set('best', { seconds: 12.5 }); // true\\n * store.get('best', null); // { seconds: 12.5 }: a copy\\n * const log = createLog({ console: { warn: () => {}, error: () => {} } }); // advice kept, not printed\\n * const next = createStore({ prefix: 'demo-game:', version: 2, backend: store.backend, log });\\n * next.get('best', null); // null: written at version 1, until migrate or set\\n * log.advice[0].code; // 'APP_STORE_VERSION'\\n30→ * createStore({ mode: 'demo' }).persistent; // false: a replay's play is never kept\\n * @see engine/app/store.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, log as sharedLog, type Log } from '../core/log';\\nimport { isPlainObject, show } from '../core/schema';\\n\\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\\nexport const STORE_CODES = defineCodes('app', {\\n  APP_STORE_VERSION: {\\n    template: 'the store {prefix} holds {key} at {found}; this game reads version {version}',\\n40→    fix: 'give createStore a migrate(data, version) that turns the old value into the current one, or let the reader fall back to its default (the old value stays until set replaces it)',\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The store (PLAN.md WP 10.9, §9.1, ADR-0024): what a game keeps across sessions, outside the sim (high scores,\\n * progress, its settings). `createStore({ prefix, version, mode, backend, migrate })` reads and writes plain data as\\n * JSON under `prefix + key` in the page's `localStorage`, else in memory: in Node, where the page blocks storage\\n * (advice `APP_STORE_BLOCKED`, once), and in the modes that must leave a player's saves alone, `demo` (a replay or an\\n * attract loop), `sandbox` (a developer's throwaway play) and `gallery` (sheets and shots): their memory starts empty\\n * and dies with the page, so what they play is never kept over what the player played.\\n *\\n * Every value is written in its envelope, `{ format: 'my3dge-store/1', version, data }`, and checked when read (shardfall\\n10→ * writes a version and never checks it): a value of another format or version is not handed back as it is. With\\n * `migrate(data, version)` the store makes it the current version (and writes it back); without, the reader gets its\\n * fallback, the value stays until `set` replaces it, and the advice `APP_STORE_VERSION` names the key once.\\n *\\n * Invariants: storage never throws here (a full or refused write returns false; a value that is not JSON reads as its\\n * fallback); values go in and come out as copies (JSON), so a caller's object never aliases the store's; only keys\\n * under the prefix are listed or cleared, so games and pages sharing an origin keep apart (pick a prefix of the game's\\n * own, `my3dge-game:`). Sim-side code cannot import the app layer, so the sim never reads a store and nothing kept can\\n * change a replay. Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:196-200` (`store`: get with a fallback, set, remove,\\n * never throwing), the fixed `my3d2dge:` prefix made the store's own.\\n20→ *\\n * @example\\n * import { createLog } from '../core/log';\\n * const store = createStore({ prefix: 'demo-game:', backend: memoryBackend() });\\n * store.set('best', { seconds: 12.5 }); // true\\n * store.get('best', null); // { seconds: 12.5 }: a copy\\n * const log = createLog({ console: { warn: () => {}, error: () => {} } }); // advice kept, not printed\\n * const next = createStore({ prefix: 'demo-game:', version: 2, backend: store.backend, log });\\n * next.get('best', null); // null: written at version 1, until migrate or set\\n * log.advice[0].code; // 'APP_STORE_VERSION'\\n30→ * createStore({ mode: 'demo' }).persistent; // false: a replay's play is never kept\\n * @see engine/app/store.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, log as sharedLog, type Log } from '../core/log';\\nimport { isPlainObject, show } from '../core/schema';\\n\\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\\nexport const STORE_CODES = defineCodes('app', {\\n  APP_STORE_VERSION: {\\n    template: 'the store {prefix} holds {key} at {found}; this game reads version {version}',\\n40→    fix: 'give createStore a migrate(data, version) that turns the old value into the current one, or let the reader fall back to its default (the old value stays until set replaces it)',\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/app/store.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The store (PLAN.md WP 10.9, §9.1, ADR-0024): what a game keeps across sessions, outside the sim (high scores,\\n * progress, its settings). `createStore({ prefix, version, mode, backend, migrate })` reads and writes plain data as\\n * JSON under `prefix + key` in the page's `localStorage`, else in memory: in Node, where the page blocks storage\\n * (advice `APP_STORE_BLOCKED`, once), and in the modes that must leave a player's saves alone, `demo` (a replay or an\\n * attract loop), `sandbox` (a developer's throwaway play) and `gallery` (sheets and shots): their memory starts empty\\n * and dies with the page, so what they play is never kept over what the player played.\\n *\\n * Every value is written in its envelope, `{ format: 'my3dge-store/1', version, data }`, and checked when read (shardfall\\n * writes a version and never checks it): a value of another format or version is not handed back as it is. With\\n * `migrate(data, version)` the store makes it the current version (and writes it back); without, the reader gets its\\n * fallback, the value stays until `set` replaces it, and the advice `APP_STORE_VERSION` names the key once.\\n *\\n * Invariants: storage never throws here (a full or refused write returns false; a value that is not JSON reads as its\\n * fallback); values go in and come out as copies (JSON), so a caller's object never aliases the store's; only keys\\n * under the prefix are listed or cleared, so games and pages sharing an origin keep apart (pick a prefix of the game's\\n * own, `my3dge-game:`). Sim-side code cannot import the app layer, so the sim never reads a store and nothing kept can\\n * change a replay. Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:196-200` (`store`: get with a fallback, set, remove,\\n * never throwing), the fixed `my3d2dge:` prefix made the store's own.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createLog } from '../core/log';\\n * const store = createStore({ prefix: 'demo-game:', backend: memoryBackend() });\\n * store.set('best', { seconds: 12.5 }); // true\\n * store.get('best', null); // { seconds: 12.5 }: a copy\\n * const log = createLog({ console: { warn: () => {}, error: () => {} } }); // advice kept, not printed\\n * const next = createStore({ prefix: 'demo-game:', version: 2, backend: store.backend, log });\\n * next.get('best', null); // null: written at version 1, until migrate or set\\n * log.advice[0].code; // 'APP_STORE_VERSION'\\n * createStore({ mode: 'demo' }).persistent; // false: a replay's play is never kept\\n * @see engine/app/store.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, log as sharedLog, type Log } from '../core/log';\\nimport { isPlainObject, show } from '../core/schema';\\n\\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\\nexport const STORE_CODES = defineCodes('app', {\\n  APP_STORE_VERSION: {\\n    template: 'the store {prefix} holds {key} at {found}; this game reads version {version}',\\n    fix: 'give createStore a migrate(data, version) that turns the old value into the current one, or let the reader fall back to its default (the old value stays until set replaces it)',\\n\",\"total_lines\":258}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"8997ff35-e15b-41f0-a84b-ef5df5142813"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_538","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The localStorage key is `thumb-yoga:save`.\n\nI'll snapshot all localStorage. I'll write the files and start the retreat test in the background. I'll run the x simulation to create a replay. I'll check if eslint allows console.log in tests.\n\nI'll write browse.py and verify.mjs now. I'll fix a bug where applyPrefs sets note text during play before the menu opens.\n\nThe paint-overwrite bug is harmless. Key events trigger the capture listener immediately, before the next frame paints the prompt.\n\nThe scripts are long and need careful writing. The hub server will serve the work root, so verify.mjs must build the HTML first if it is missing.\n\nThe HTML output path is the parent of the dev folder. The onefile build may take 30 to 60 seconds. The verify sequence will run vitest first, then generate replays, then build the HTML, and finally start browse.py. Vitest will be launched in the background so the remaining steps can proceed while it runs.\n\nA pre-check run of vitest will catch failures early. The official verify will rerun it anyway, so the extra time is acceptable. Vitest will output to scratch for easy reading. The x simulation may run in parallel, though that could slow both processes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d8510ded-3631-4815-a18f-057c9351ac5d-153","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656\" && node x sim labs/game/scenes/bench.ts --steps 60 2>&1 | tail -30 && echo \"---OUT---\" && find out -name '*.replay.json' | head","description":"Record a short bench replay with x sim"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5387,"output_tokens":1041,"cache_read_input_tokens":171520,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_too