{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_542","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The .ui-panel element has pointer-events set to auto.\n\nMenu hover and clicks are confirmed working. The ui-panel position will be queried dynamically rather than assumed. Files are being written now. The browse.py gamepad init script must precede navigation. The dev slider's __engine.state is a function, so test assertions will print keys on failure for debugging. Unique strings from SOURCE and each feedback array will be used for about text. A font check function is also being prepared.\n\nThe font check script walks the document body to collect visible text nodes. It filters out empty text, hidden elements, and zero-opacity items. It also skips nodes with no bounding rectangle or minimal size.\n\nThe font check now flags text smaller than 28 pixels. SVG text is not a concern because the disc uses circles. Menu count will be verified with a locator on `[data-ui=item]`. The touch stick will be confirmed absent, and any stick-like elements will be excluded. Attract mode will wait for 11 seconds after the last input event.\n\nThe 11-second attract wait begins only after the engine is ready. Settings will be opened by tapping the center of the `[data-ui=touch-settings]` button. The test will wait for `window.__game.screen` to become `'settings'`. Webkit message handling is immediate when `!navigator.gpu`.\n\nA module import error could overwrite the inline script's GPU message. The gameFailed handler sets APP_START only when errors.length is zero, so a thrown import would erase the Chrome message. I need to guard index.html against this.\n\nThe `gameFailed` handler will return early when `!navigator.gpu`. This prevents a thrown import from overwriting the inline script's GPU message.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8079c363-0ef5-42c7-bb67-b64b9aea8dd8-158","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/index.html","old_string":"      function gameFailed(message) {\n        if (!window.__engine || typeof window.__engine.help === 'function') return;","new_string":"      function gameFailed(message) {\n        if (!navigator.gpu) return;\n        if (!window.__engine || typeof window.__engine.help === 'function') return;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8079c363-0ef5-42c7-bb67-b64b9aea8dd8-159","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/replay.test.ts","content":"/**\n * @file The shipped golden and a capture. Both go through the bench scene the game ships.\n * Restore continues from the captured step. The golden's hashes are the recording's.\n */\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\nimport { createHeadless } from '../../engine';\nimport { createAppHost } from '../../engine/app/headless';\nimport { bench } from './scenes/bench';\n\ndescribe('replay', () => {\n  it('restores a capture and continues the golden', async () => {\n    const run = createAppHost({ scene: bench, seed: 1 });\n    for (let i = 0; i < 30; i++) run.stepOnce({});\n    const world = run.session.world;\n    const snap = world.capture();\n    const hash = world.hash();\n    for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) run.stepOnce({ move: [1, 0] });\n    expect(world.hash()).not.toBe(hash);\n    world.restore(snap);\n    expect(world.hash()).toBe(hash);\n\n    const text = readFileSync(new URL('./replays/still.replay.json', import.meta.url), 'utf8');\n    const golden = JSON.parse(text) as { hashes: { 'linux-x64': Record<string, string> } };\n    const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: bench });\n    const played = await (\n      engine.replay as (body: string) => Promise<{ hashes: Record<string, string> }>\n    )(text);\n    expect(played.hashes).toEqual(golden.hashes['linux-x64']);\n  });\n});\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1078,"output_tokens":1576,"cache_read_input_tokens":180224,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"2a77026f-a2b8-4a0f-8b52-6ba1c7ac839c"}
