2c7-bb67-b64b9aea8dd8-159","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file The shipped golden and a capture. Both go through the bench scene the game ships.\\n * Restore continues from the captured step. The golden's hashes are the recording's.\\n */\\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { createHeadless } from '../../engine';\\nimport { createAppHost } from '../../engine/app/headless';\\nimport { bench } from './scenes/bench';\\n\\ndescribe('replay', () => {\\n  it('restores a capture and continues the golden', async () => {\\n    const run = createAppHost({ scene: bench, seed: 1 });\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 30; i++) run.stepOnce({});\\n    const world = run.session.world;\\n    const snap = world.capture();\\n    const hash = world.hash();\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) run.stepOnce({ move: [1, 0] });\\n    expect(world.hash()).not.toBe(hash);\\n    world.restore(snap);\\n    expect(world.hash()).toBe(hash);\\n\\n    const text = readFileSync(new URL('./replays/still.replay.json', import.meta.url), 'utf8');\\n    const golden = JSON.parse(text) as { hashes: { 'linux-x64': Record<string, string> } };\\n    const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: bench });\\n    const played = await (\\n      engine.replay as (body: string) => Promise<{ hashes: Record<string, string> }>\\n    )(text);\\n    expect(played.hashes).toEqual(golden.hashes['linux-x64']);\\n  });\\n});\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/replay.test.ts has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/replay.test.ts has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/replay.test.ts\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file The shipped golden and a capture. Both go through the bench scene the game ships.\\n * Restore continues from the captured step. The golden's hashes are the recording's.\\n */\\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { createHeadless } from '../../engine';\\nimport { createAppHost } from '../../engine/app/headless';\\nimport { bench } from './scenes/bench';\\n\\ndescribe('replay', () => {\\n  it('restores a capture and continues the golden', async () => {\\n    const run = createAppHost({ scene: bench, seed: 1 });\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 30; i++) run.stepOnce({});\\n    const world = run.session.world;\\n    const snap = world.capture();\\n    const hash = world.hash();\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) run.stepOnce({ move: [1, 0] });\\n    expect(world.hash()).not.toBe(hash);\\n    world.restore(snap);\\n    expect(world.hash()).toBe(hash);\\n\\n    const text = readFileSync(new URL('./replays/still.replay.json', import.meta.url), 'utf8');\\n    const golden = JSON.parse(text) as { hashes: { 'linux-x64': Record<string, string> } };\\n    const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: bench });\\n    const played = await (\\n      engine.replay as (body: string) => Promise<{ hashes: Record<string, string> }>\\n    )(text);\\n    expect(played.hashes).toEqual(golden.hashes['linux-x64']);\\n  });\\n});\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"81813da9-5fc9-40cb-9ceb-91b63417c17f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_543","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking whether world.capture and hash exist on the session type.\n\nWill cast session.world to World if TypeScript rejects the type. Also checking engine.replay and createHeadless replay signatures. Now writing browse.py and verify.mjs with a failures list.\n\nThe verification will compare JSON outputs from two boots. Each boot presses Enter after ready to select Begin. The first programme item is morning, so the screen becomes play and the event becomes morning. A single scripted pad or key press is enough if both boots agree.\n\nThe verification will also exercise the pad in the glyph and menu sections. It will snapshot volumes.music at 0.1, title at Thumb Yoga, and screen and attract states at boot. The canvas width and height must be positive and match innerWidth and innerHeight under a 1920x1080 viewport with device_scale_factor 1. WebGPU downgrade errors mentioning WebGL or downgrade will be caught via page.evaluate.\n\nReady will be confirmed true and errors empty. Screenshots will be saved to VERIFY_OUT/shots/ for evidence. Title, pause, dev, and about states will be captured during the browser flow. Dev jumps may be used for activity screenshots if time allows. Missing shots will not fail the run.\n\nThe hub will run four sequential tests with one browser and one server, closing pages between runs to save memory. A 120-second timeout is set for the hub. Engine polling will be injected via add_init_script on the context, which executes in every iframe including same-origin game iframes.\n\nA `requestAnimationFrame` loop will poll `window.__engine.ready` and record error counts in `window.__readyTrace`. After the run, any non-empty trace with errors or an empty trace means the engine never became ready. Boot frames before the first GPU frame are excluded from this check.\n\nThe ready check will require the engine to stay ready with zero errors after the first frame, and it will log the trace length. A ghost check will scan all iframes for ghost entities when players equals two.\n\nThe ghost check will poll every iframe for ghost entities and record the maximum count across frames. A console listener will catch `[AIHub]` messages from iframes on both the page and context. The standalone test will press Enter on a file:// page.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-814844ca-5182-4418-9c0a-0eb76c127694-160","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/hub/session-client.txt","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-814844ca-5182-4418-9c0a-0eb76c127694-161","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/hub/tags.html"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1792,"output_tokens":1456,"cache_read_input_tokens":181248,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"473e719e-04ec-4790-bf25-56ebbefbbc6f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-814844ca-5182-4418-9c0a-0eb76c127694-160","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n10→  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    framed = true;\\n  }\\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\\n20→  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(search);\\n\\n  var hub = {\\n    version: VERSION,\\n    protocol: 1,\\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\\n    me: null,\\n    host: null,\\n30→    isHost: false,\\n    players: [],\\n    mode: null,\\n    seed: 0,\\n    limitMs: 0,\\n    round: 0,\\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\\n    splash: false,\\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\\n    seeded: false,\\n40→  };\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n10→  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    framed = true;\\n  }\\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\\n20→  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(search);\\n\\n  var hub = {\\n    version: VERSION,\\n    protocol: 1,\\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\\n    me: null,\\n    host: null,\\n30→    isHost: false,\\n    players: [],\\n    mode: null,\\n    seed: 0,\\n    limitMs: 0,\\n    round: 0,\\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\\n    splash: false,\\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\\n    seeded: false,\\n40→  };\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/hub/session-client.txt\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    framed = true;\\n  }\\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(search);\\n\\n  var hub = {\\n    version: VERSION,\\n    protocol: 1,\\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\\n    me: null,\\n    host: null,\\n    isHost: false,\\n    players: [],\\n    mode: null,\\n    seed: 0,\\n    limitMs: 0,\\n    round: 0,\\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\\n    splash: false,\\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\\n    seeded: false,\\n  };\\n\",\"total_lines\":488}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-814844ca-5182-4418-9c0a-0eb76c127694-161","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→<meta name=\\\"hub:type\\\" content=\\\"Game\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:source\\\" content=\\\"Wii Fit\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"3\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Stay the steadiest across three classes\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Lean: stick or WASD · Feet: L2 R2 or Q E · Breathe: both or Space\\\" />\\n10→<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\" />\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→<meta name=\\\"hub:type\\\" content=\\\"Game\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:source\\\" content=\\\"Wii Fit\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"3\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Stay the steadiest across three classes\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Lean: stick or WASD · Feet: L2 R2 or Q E · Breathe: both or Space\\\" />\\n10→<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\" />\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/hub/tags.html\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:type\\\" content=\\\"Game\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:source\\\" content=\\\"Wii Fit\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"3\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Stay the steadiest across three classes\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Lean: stick or WASD · Feet: L2 R2 or Q E · Breathe: both or Space\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\" />\\n\",\"total_lines\":10}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"ca762d44-a5e9-4624-91ca-f60a00763d1a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_544","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The goal \"Stay the steadiest across three classes\" is 40 characters long.\n\nThe howto text is under 80 characters. The client requires a framed page and an aihub parameter to be active; a standalone file:// link will not satisfy this. I am now writing the Python and verification scripts.\n\nWriting browse.py and verify.mjs. The retreat test is still running, so I will check it after writing the files. I also need to verify that replay.test.ts can access world.capture through the session.world type from sim-api, and confirm whether engine.replay returns hashes in the expected format.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dc723b58-2685-425c-9f0b-eac349730ac8-162","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/tools/browse.py","content":"\"\"\"Drive the built Thumb Yoga page. Prints FAIL lines, or nothing when the checks hold.\n\nUsage: python3 labs/game/tools/browse.py <html> <out-dir>\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport threading\nfrom http.server import SimpleHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\n\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\n\nCHROME = os.path.expanduser(\n    \"~/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-1243/chrome-headless-shell-linux64/chrome-headless-shell\"\n)\nFLAGS = [\n    \"--no-sandbox\",\n    \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\",\n    \"--enable-features=Vulkan\",\n    \"--use-vulkan=swiftshader\",\n    \"--use-angle=swiftshader\",\n]\nPAD = \"\"\"\nwindow.__buttons = new Array(16).fill(0);\nwindow.__axes = [0, 0, 0, 0];\nnavigator.getGamepads = () => [{\n  id: 'Scripted Pad (STANDARD GAMEPAD)',\n  index: 0,\n  connected: true,\n  mapping: 'standard',\n  timestamp: performance.now(),\n  axes: window.__axes.slice(),\n  buttons: window.__buttons.map((value) => ({ pressed: value > 0.5, touched: value > 0, value })),\n}];\n\"\"\"\nWATCH = \"\"\"\nwindow.__readyTrace = [];\nconst watch = () => {\n  const eng = window.__engine;\n  if (eng && eng.ready === true) window.__readyTrace.push((eng.errors && eng.errors.length) || 0);\n  requestAnimationFrame(watch);\n};\nrequestAnimationFrame(watch);\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    html = Path(sys.argv[1]).resolve()\n    out = Path(sys.argv[2]).resolve()\n    out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    shots = out / \"shots\"\n    shots.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n    fails: list[str] = []\n    try:\n        with sync_playwright() as p:\n            try:\n                browser = p.chromium.launch(executable_path=CHROME, args=FLAGS)\n            except Exception as error:\n                (out / \"launch-error.txt\").write_text(str(error), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n                print(\"LAUNCH_ERROR\")\n                return 0\n            try:\n                boot(browser, html, out, fails)\n                if not any(item.startswith(\"boot\") for item in fails):\n                    shell(browser, html, out, shots, fails)\n                    touch(browser, p, html, fails)\n                    hub(browser, html, out, fails)\n            finally:\n                browser.close()\n            webkit(p, html, fails)\n    except Exception as error:\n        if \"launch-error\" not in str(error):\n            fails.append(f\"browser crashed: {error}\")\n    for item in fails:\n        print(f\"FAIL {item}\")\n    return 1 if fails else 0\n\n\ndef boot(browser, html: Path, out: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\n    marks = [once(browser, html, out, 1, fails), once(browser, html, out, 2, fails)]\n    if marks[0] and marks[1] and marks[0] != marks[1]:\n        fails.append(f\"boot paths disagree {marks[0]} vs {marks[1]}\")\n\n\ndef once(browser, html: Path, out: Path, n: int, fails: list[str]) -> str:\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\"width\": 1920, \"height\": 1080}, device_scale_factor=1)\n    page.add_init_script(PAD + WATCH)\n    logs: list[str] = []\n    page.on(\"console\", lambda msg: logs.append(msg.text))\n    page.on(\"pageerror\", lambda err: logs.append(f\"pageerror {err}\"))\n    try:\n        page.goto(html.as_uri())\n        page.wait_for_function(\"() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true\", timeout=60000)\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\n        state = page.evaluate(\n            \"\"\"() => {\n              const canvas = document.querySelector('canvas');\n              const game = window.__game || {};\n              return {\n                ready: window.__engine.ready,\n                errors: window.__engine.errors || [],\n                game,\n                canvas: { width: canvas ? canvas.width : 0, height: canvas ? canvas.height : 0 },\n                view: { width: window.innerWidth, height: window.innerHeight },\n              };\n            }\"\"\"\n        )\n        (out / f\"boot-{n}.log\").write_text(json.dumps(state, indent=2) + \"\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(logs), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        page.screenshot(path=str(out / f\"boot-{n}.png\"))\n        if n == 1:\n            page.screenshot(path=str(out / \"shots\" / \"title.png\"))\n        errors = state[\"errors\"]\n        if state[\"ready\"] is not True:\n            fails.append(f\"boot {n} ready is false\")\n        if errors:\n            fails.append(f\"boot {n} errors {errors}\")\n        if any(\"webgl\" in json.dumps(errors).lower() or \"downgrade\" in json.dumps(errors).lower() for _ in [0]):\n            fails.append(f\"boot {n} downgraded\")\n        game = state[\"game\"]\n        if game.get(\"title\") != \"Thumb Yoga\" or game.get(\"screen\") != \"title\":\n            fails.append(f\"boot {n} title screen {game}\")\n        if game.get(\"volumes\", {}).get(\"music\") != 0.1:\n            fails.append(f\"boot {n} music {game.get('volumes')}\")\n        canvas = state[\"canvas\"]\n        view = state[\"view\"]\n        if canvas[\"width\"] <= 0 or canvas[\"height\"] <= 0:\n            fails.append(f\"boot {n} canvas is empty\")\n        if canvas[\"width\"] != view[\"width\"] or canvas[\"height\"] != view[\"height\"]:\n            note = out / \"webgpu-readback.txt\"\n            note.write_text(\n                f\"drawing {canvas['width']}x{canvas['height']} view {view['width']}x{view['height']}\\n\",\n                encoding=\"utf-8\",\n            )\n            fails.append(\n                f\"boot {n} canvas {canvas['width']}x{canvas['height']} is not the view {view['width']}x{view['height']}\"\n            )\n        page.keyboard.press(\"Enter\")\n        page.wait_for_function(\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'play'\", timeout=10000)\n        page.wait_for_timeout(400)\n        after = page.evaluate(\"() => ({ screen: window.__game.screen, event: window.__game.event, title: window.__game.title })\")\n        if after.get(\"screen\") != \"play\":\n            fails.append(f\"boot {n} did not leave the title\")\n        return json.dumps(after, sort_keys=True)\n    except Exception as error:\n        fails.append(f\"boot {n} {error}\")\n        return \"\"\n    finally:\n        page.close()\n\n\ndef shell(browser, html: Path, out: Path, shots: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\"width\": 1920, \"height\": 1080}, device_scale_factor=1)\n    page.add_init_script(PAD)\n    try:\n        page.goto(html.as_uri())\n        page.wait_for_function(\"() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true\", timeout=60000)\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\n        note = page.locator(\"[data-ui=note]\").inner_text()\n        glyph = page.evaluate(\"() => window.__game.glyphSet\")\n        if glyph != \"playstation\" or \"Cross\" not in note:\n            fails.append(f\"glyphs started as {glyph} {note}\")\n        page.evaluate(\n            \"\"\"() => {\n              const row = document.querySelector('[data-ui=item][data-id=\"settings\"]');\n              row.dispatchEvent(new PointerEvent('pointermove', { bubbles: true, movementX: 4, movementY: 6 }));\n            }\"\"\"\n        )\n        page.wait_for_timeout(100)\n        focus = page.evaluate(\"() => window.__game.focus\")\n        if focus != \"Settings\":\n            fails.append(f\"hover focus {focus}\")\n        page.locator(\"[data-ui=item][data-id=settings]\").click()\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\n        page.evaluate(\n            \"\"\"() => {\n              window.__buttons[0] = 0;\n              const row = document.querySelector('[data-ui=item][data-id=\"icons\"]');\n              row.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent('click', { bubbles: true }));\n            }\"\"\"\n        )\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\n        xbox = page.locator(\"[data-ui=note]\").inner_text()\n        glyph = page.evaluate(\"() => window.__game.glyphSet\")\n        for token in (\"A\", \"B\", \"X\", \"Y\", \"LB\", \"RB\", \"LT\", \"RT\"):\n            if token not in xbox.split():\n                fails.append(f\"xbox prompt missing {token} in {xbox}\")\n                break\n        if glyph not in (\"xbox\", \"mouse\"):\n            fails.append(f\"glyph set after icons {glyph}\")\n        # A click just happened, so the last device is the mouse. A key must switch the same turn.\n        page.keyboard.press(\"KeyF\")\n        keys = page.evaluate(\"() => ({ set: window.__game.glyphSet, note: document.querySelector('[data-ui=note]').textContent })\")\n        if keys[\"set\"] != \"keys\" or \"WASD\" not in keys[\"note\"]:\n            fails.append(f\"keys prompt {keys}\")\n        page.mouse.click(400, 400)\n        mouse = page.evaluate(\"() => ({ set: window.__game.glyphSet, note: document.querySelector('[data-ui=note]').textContent })\")\n        if mouse[\"set\"] != \"mouse\" or \"Mouse\" not in mouse[\"note\"]:\n            fails.append(f\"mouse prompt {mouse}\")\n        page.keyboard.press(\"Escape\")\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\n        save_before = page.evaluate(\"() => localStorage.getItem('thumb-yoga:save')\")\n        page.wait_for_timeout(10500)\n        attracted = page.evaluate(\"() => window.__game.attract === true && window.__game.screen === 'attract'\")\n        if not attracted:\n            fails.append(f\"attract did not start {page.evaluate('() => window.__game')}\")\n        page.keyboard.press(\"KeyF\")\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\n        if page.evaluate(\"() => window.__game.attract\"):\n            fails.append(\"attract stayed after a key\")\n        page.wait_for_timeout(10500)\n        page.mouse.click(420, 420)\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\n        if page.evaluate(\"() => window.__game.attract\"):\n            fails.append(\"attract stayed after a click\")\n        page.wait_for_timeout(10500)\n        page.evaluate(\"() => { window.__buttons[0] = 1; }\")\n        page.wait_for_timeout(400)\n        page.evaluate(\"() => { window.__buttons[0] = 0; }\")\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\n        if page.evaluate(\"() => window.__game.attract\"):\n            fails.append(\"attract stayed after a pad press\")\n        save_after = page.evaluate(\"() => localStorage.getItem('thumb-yoga:save')\")\n        if save_before != save_after:\n            fails.append(\"attract wrote the save\")\n        page.keyboard.press(\"Enter\")\n        page.wait_for_function(\"() => window.__game.screen === 'play'\", timeout=10000)\n        page.wait_for_timeout(500)\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \"island.png\"))\n        page.keyboard.press(\"Escape\")\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \"pause.png\"))\n        page.locator(\"[data-ui=item][data-id=more]\").click()\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\n        page.locator(\"[data-ui=item][data-id=dev]\").click()\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \"dev.png\"))\n        changed = page.evaluate(\n            \"\"\"() => {\n              const range = document.querySelector('[data-ui=slider-range]');\n              const before = window.__engine.state().settings['game.wobble.gain'];\n              range.value = '20';\n              range.dispatchEvent(new Event('input', { bubbles: true }));\n              const after = window.__engine.state().settings['game.wobble.gain'];\n              return { before, after, shown: range.value };\n            }\"\"\"\n        )\n        if changed[\"after\"] != 20:\n            fails.append(f\"slider did not change the gain {changed}\")\n        page.locator(\"[data-ui=item][data-id=reset]\").click()\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\n        restored = page.evaluate(\"() => window.__engine.state().settings['game.wobble.gain']\")\n        if restored not in (None, 14):\n            fails.append(f\"reset left the gain at {restored}\")\n        page.locator(\"[data-ui=item][data-id=back]\").click()\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\n        page.locator(\"[data-ui=item][data-id=about]\").click()\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\n        about = page.locator(\"[data-ui=about]\").inner_text()\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \"about.png\"))\n        for needle in (\n            \"Wii Fit\",\n            \"PLAN.md\",\n            \"Sports\",\n            \"third-person\",\n            \"added on import\",\n            \"Testing caught six issues\",\n            \"Four were critical\",\n            \"most helpful\",\n            \"least helpful\",\n            \"Scene actions\",\n            \"playClip\",\n            \"balance step\",\n            \"hardest part\",\n            \"None. The engine files were not changed.\",\n            \"I would let a page add a mesh\",\n            \"acceptance numbers\",\n            \"group score\",\n            \"one HTML file\",\n            \"session client hash\",\n        ):\n            if needle not in about:\n                fails.append(f\"about missing {needle}\")\n        rows = page.locator(\"[data-ui=item]\").count()\n        if rows > 6:\n            fails.append(f\"menu has {rows} rows\")\n        small = page.evaluate(\n            \"\"\"() => {\n              const found = [];\n              const walker = document.createTreeWalker(document.body, NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT);\n              while (walker.nextNode()) {\n                const text = walker.currentNode.textContent.trim();\n                if (!text) continue;\n                const el = walker.currentNode.parentElement;\n                if (!el) continue;\n                const style = getComputedStyle(el);\n                if (style.display === 'none' || style.visibility === 'hidden') continue;\n                const rect = el.getBoundingClientRect();\n                if (rect.width < 1 || rect.height < 1) continue;\n                const size = parseFloat(style.fontSize);\n                if (size < 28) found.push(text.slice(0, 48) + ' ' + size);\n              }\n              return found.slice(0, 8);\n            }\"\"\"\n        )\n        if small:\n            fails.append(f\"text under 28px {small}\")\n    except Exception as error:\n        fails.append(f\"shell {error}\")\n    finally:\n        page.close()\n\n\ndef touch(browser, playwright, html: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\n    for name in (\"iPhone 13\", \"iPad (gen 7)\"):\n        device = playwright.devices[name]\n        context = browser.new_context(**device)\n        page = context.new_page()\n        try:\n            page.goto(html.as_uri())\n            page.wait_for_function(\"() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true\", timeout=60000)\n            text = page.locator(\"[data-ui=note]\").inner_text()\n            if \"Controller or keyboard required\" not in text:\n                fails.append(f\"{name} note {text}\")\n            if page.locator(\".touch-stick\").count() != 0:\n                fails.append(f\"{name} drew a touch stick\")\n            box = page.locator(\"[data-ui=touch-settings]\").bounding_box()\n            if not box:\n                fails.append(f\"{name} has no Settings button\")\n            else:\n                page.touchscreen.tap(box[\"x\"] + box[\"width\"] / 2, box[\"y\"] + box[\"height\"] / 2)\n                page.wait_for_timeout(400)\n                if page.evaluate(\"() => window.__game.screen\") != \"settings\":\n                    fails.append(f\"{name} tap did not open settings\")\n            page.wait_for_timeout(11000)\n            if page.evaluate(\"() => window.__game.attract\") is not True:\n                fails.append(f\"{name} attract did not run\")\n        except Exception as error:\n            fails.append(f\"{name} {error}\")\n        finally:\n            context.close()\n\n\ndef webkit(playwright, html: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\n    try:\n        browser = playwright.webkit.launch()\n    except Exception as error:\n        fails.append(f\"webkit did not launch {error}\")\n        return\n    page = browser.new_page()\n    try:\n        page.goto(html.as_uri())\n        page.wait_for_timeout(1500)\n        text = page.locator(\"#msg\").inner_text()\n        if \"Chrome\" not in text or \"Edge\" not in text:\n            fails.append(f\"webkit message {text}\")\n    except Exception as error:\n        fails.append(f\"webkit {error}\")\n    finally:\n        browser.close()\n\n\ndef hub(browser, html: Path, out: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\n    root = html.parent\n    server = ThreadingHTTPServer((\"127.0.0.1\", 0), handler(root))\n    port = server.server_address[1]\n    thread = threading.Thread(target=server.serve_forever, daemon=True)\n    thread.start()\n    (out / \"hub-port.txt\").write_text(str(port), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    game = \"/\" + quote(html.name)\n    base = f\"http://127.0.0.1:{port}\"\n    harness = f\"{base}/{quote(html.parent.name)}/labs/game/hub/harness.html\"\n    # The dev folder may contain spaces. The harness lives under the dev folder, one level below the work root.\n    dev = next(path for path in root.iterdir() if path.is_dir() and (path / \"labs/game/hub/harness.html\").exists())\n    harness = f\"{base}/{quote(dev.name)}/labs/game/hub/harness.html\"\n    lines: list[str] = []\n    try:\n        for query in (\n            \"players=2&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\",\n            \"players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\",\n            \"players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\",\n            \"players=3&scenario=host-leave&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\",\n        ):\n            run_hub(browser, f\"{harness}?game={quote(game, safe='/')}&{query}\", query, lines, fails)\n        page = browser.new_page(viewport={\"width\": 1280, \"height\": 720})\n        try:\n            page.goto(html.as_uri())\n            page.wait_for_function(\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'title'\", timeout=60000)\n            page.keyboard.press(\"Enter\")\n            page.keyboard.press(\"Space\")\n            page.keyboard.press(\"Enter\")\n            page.keyboard.press(\"Space\")\n            page.wait_for_timeout(300)\n            client = page.evaluate(\n                \"\"\"() => ({\n                  present: typeof window.AIHub === 'object' && window.AIHub !== null,\n                  active: window.AIHub && window.AIHub.active,\n                  seeded: window.AIHub && window.AIHub.seeded,\n                  native: Math.random.toString().includes('[native code]'),\n                  errors: (window.__engine && window.__engine.errors) || [],\n                  drawn: (() => { const c = document.querySelector('canvas'); return !!(c && c.width > 0); })(),\n                })\"\"\"\n            )\n            if not client[\"present\"] or client[\"active\"] or client[\"seeded\"] or not client[\"native\"]:\n                fails.append(f\"standalone client {client}\")\n            if client[\"errors\"] or not client[\"drawn\"]:\n                fails.append(f\"standalone screen {client}\")\n            lines.append(f\"standalone {json.dumps(client)}\")\n        finally:\n            page.close()\n    finally:\n        server.shutdown()\n        (out / \"hub.log\").write_text(\"\\n\".join(lines), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n\ndef run_hub(browser, url: str, query: str, lines: list[str], fails: list[str]) -> None:\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\"width\": 1280, \"height\": 720})\n    page.add_init_script(WATCH)\n    bad: list[str] = []\n    page.on(\"console\", lambda msg: bad.append(msg.text) if msg.text.startswith(\"[AIHub]\") else None)\n    try:\n        page.goto(url)\n        page.wait_for_function(\"() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\", timeout=120000)\n        report = page.evaluate(\"() => window.__hubCheck\")\n        ghosts = page.evaluate(\n            \"\"\"() => [...document.querySelectorAll('iframe')].map((frame) => {\n              const win = frame.contentWindow;\n              const state = win.__engine && win.__engine.state && win.__engine.state();\n              const entities = (state && state.entities) || [];\n              return {\n                ready: !!(win.__engine && win.__engine.ready),\n                errors: (win.__engine && win.__engine.errors && win.__engine.errors.length) || 0,\n                ghosts: entities.filter((entity) => entity.ghost).length,\n                trace: win.__readyTrace || [],\n              };\n            })\"\"\"\n        )\n        lines.append(query)\n        lines.append(json.dumps({\"pass\": report.get(\"pass\") if report else None, \"checks\": report.get(\"checks\") if report else None, \"ghosts\": ghosts, \"aihub\": bad}))\n        if not report or report.get(\"pass\") is not True:\n            fails.append(f\"hub {query} {report}\")\n        if \"players=2\" in query and not any(row[\"ghosts\"] > 0 for row in ghosts):\n            fails.append(f\"hub {query} has no ghost\")\n        for row in ghosts:\n            if row[\"ready\"] is not True or row[\"errors\"]:\n                fails.append(f\"hub {query} engine {row}\")\n            if any(count for count in row[\"trace\"]):\n                fails.append(f\"hub {query} frame errors {row['trace'][:4]}\")\n        if bad:\n            fails.append(f\"hub {query} console {bad[:3]}\")\n    except Exception as error:\n        fails.append(f\"hub {query} {error}\")\n        lines.append(f\"{query} error {error}\")\n    finally:\n        page.close()\n\n\ndef handler(root: Path):\n    class Quiet(SimpleHTTPRequestHandler):\n        def __init__(self, *args, **kwargs):\n            super().__init__(*args, directory=str(root), **kwargs)\n\n        def log_message(self, _format, *_args):\n            return\n\n    return Quiet\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2059,"output_tokens":6195,"cache_read_input_tokens":183040,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"24a7ae69-6778-4078-b7ba-94313e5d69b2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-dc723b58-2685-425c-9f0b-eac349730ac8-162","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Drive the built Thumb Yoga page. Prints FAIL lines, or nothing when the checks hold.\\n\\nUsage: python3 labs/game/tools/browse.py <html> <out-dir>\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nimport sys\\nimport threading\\nfrom http.server import SimpleHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\\n\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\n\\nCHROME = os.path.expanduser(\\n    \\\"~/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-1243/chrome-headless-shell-linux64/chrome-headless-shell\\\"\\n)\\nFLAGS = [\\n    \\\"--no-sandbox\\\",\\n    \\\"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\\\",\\n    \\\"--enable-features=Vulkan\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-vulkan=swiftshader\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-angle=swiftshader\\\",\\n]\\nPAD = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\nwindow.__buttons = new Array(16).fill(0);\\nwindow.__axes = [0, 0, 0, 0];\\nnavigator.getGamepads = () => [{\\n  id: 'Scripted Pad (STANDARD GAMEPAD)',\\n  index: 0,\\n  connected: true,\\n  mapping: 'standard',\\n  timestamp: performance.now(),\\n  axes: window.__axes.slice(),\\n  buttons: window.__buttons.map((value) => ({ pressed: value > 0.5, touched: value > 0, value })),\\n}];\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nWATCH = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\nwindow.__readyTrace = [];\\nconst watch = () => {\\n  const eng = window.__engine;\\n  if (eng && eng.ready === true) window.__readyTrace.push((eng.errors && eng.errors.length) || 0);\\n  requestAnimationFrame(watch);\\n};\\nrequestAnimationFrame(watch);\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef main() -> int:\\n    html = Path(sys.argv[1]).resolve()\\n    out = Path(sys.argv[2]).resolve()\\n    out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    shots = out / \\\"shots\\\"\\n    shots.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\\n    fails: list[str] = []\\n    try:\\n        with sync_playwright() as p:\\n            try:\\n                browser = p.chromium.launch(executable_path=CHROME, args=FLAGS)\\n            except Exception as error:\\n                (out / \\\"launch-error.txt\\\").write_text(str(error), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n                print(\\\"LAUNCH_ERROR\\\")\\n                return 0\\n            try:\\n                boot(browser, html, out, fails)\\n                if not any(item.startswith(\\\"boot\\\") for item in fails):\\n                    shell(browser, html, out, shots, fails)\\n                    touch(browser, p, html, fails)\\n                    hub(browser, html, out, fails)\\n            finally:\\n                browser.close()\\n            webkit(p, html, fails)\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        if \\\"launch-error\\\" not in str(error):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"browser crashed: {error}\\\")\\n    for item in fails:\\n        print(f\\\"FAIL {item}\\\")\\n    return 1 if fails else 0\\n\\n\\ndef boot(browser, html: Path, out: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    marks = [once(browser, html, out, 1, fails), once(browser, html, out, 2, fails)]\\n    if marks[0] and marks[1] and marks[0] != marks[1]:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"boot paths disagree {marks[0]} vs {marks[1]}\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef once(browser, html: Path, out: Path, n: int, fails: list[str]) -> str:\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1920, \\\"height\\\": 1080}, device_scale_factor=1)\\n    page.add_init_script(PAD + WATCH)\\n    logs: list[str] = []\\n    page.on(\\\"console\\\", lambda msg: logs.append(msg.text))\\n    page.on(\\\"pageerror\\\", lambda err: logs.append(f\\\"pageerror {err}\\\"))\\n    try:\\n        page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true\\\", timeout=60000)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        state = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const canvas = document.querySelector('canvas');\\n              const game = window.__game || {};\\n              return {\\n                ready: window.__engine.ready,\\n                errors: window.__engine.errors || [],\\n                game,\\n                canvas: { width: canvas ? canvas.width : 0, height: canvas ? canvas.height : 0 },\\n                view: { width: window.innerWidth, height: window.innerHeight },\\n              };\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        (out / f\\\"boot-{n}.log\\\").write_text(json.dumps(state, indent=2) + \\\"\\\\n\\\" + \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(logs), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(out / f\\\"boot-{n}.png\\\"))\\n        if n == 1:\\n            page.screenshot(path=str(out / \\\"shots\\\" / \\\"title.png\\\"))\\n        errors = state[\\\"errors\\\"]\\n        if state[\\\"ready\\\"] is not True:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} ready is false\\\")\\n        if errors:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} errors {errors}\\\")\\n        if any(\\\"webgl\\\" in json.dumps(errors).lower() or \\\"downgrade\\\" in json.dumps(errors).lower() for _ in [0]):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} downgraded\\\")\\n        game = state[\\\"game\\\"]\\n        if game.get(\\\"title\\\") != \\\"Thumb Yoga\\\" or game.get(\\\"screen\\\") != \\\"title\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} title screen {game}\\\")\\n        if game.get(\\\"volumes\\\", {}).get(\\\"music\\\") != 0.1:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} music {game.get('volumes')}\\\")\\n        canvas = state[\\\"canvas\\\"]\\n        view = state[\\\"view\\\"]\\n        if canvas[\\\"width\\\"] <= 0 or canvas[\\\"height\\\"] <= 0:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} canvas is empty\\\")\\n        if canvas[\\\"width\\\"] != view[\\\"width\\\"] or canvas[\\\"height\\\"] != view[\\\"height\\\"]:\\n            note = out / \\\"webgpu-readback.txt\\\"\\n            note.write_text(\\n                f\\\"drawing {canvas['width']}x{canvas['height']} view {view['width']}x{view['height']}\\\\n\\\",\\n                encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\",\\n            )\\n            fails.append(\\n                f\\\"boot {n} canvas {canvas['width']}x{canvas['height']} is not the view {view['width']}x{view['height']}\\\"\\n            )\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"Enter\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'play'\\\", timeout=10000)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(400)\\n        after = page.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ screen: window.__game.screen, event: window.__game.event, title: window.__game.title })\\\")\\n        if after.get(\\\"screen\\\") != \\\"play\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} did not leave the title\\\")\\n        return json.dumps(after, sort_keys=True)\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} {error}\\\")\\n        return \\\"\\\"\\n    finally:\\n        page.close()\\n\\n\\ndef shell(browser, html: Path, out: Path, shots: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1920, \\\"height\\\": 1080}, device_scale_factor=1)\\n    page.add_init_script(PAD)\\n    try:\\n        page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true\\\", timeout=60000)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        note = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=note]\\\").inner_text()\\n        glyph = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.glyphSet\\\")\\n        if glyph != \\\"playstation\\\" or \\\"Cross\\\" not in note:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"glyphs started as {glyph} {note}\\\")\\n        page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const row = document.querySelector('[data-ui=item][data-id=\\\"settings\\\"]');\\n              row.dispatchEvent(new PointerEvent('pointermove', { bubbles: true, movementX: 4, movementY: 6 }));\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(100)\\n        focus = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.focus\\\")\\n        if focus != \\\"Settings\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"hover focus {focus}\\\")\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=settings]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              window.__buttons[0] = 0;\\n              const row = document.querySelector('[data-ui=item][data-id=\\\"icons\\\"]');\\n              row.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent('click', { bubbles: true }));\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        xbox = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=note]\\\").inner_text()\\n        glyph = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.glyphSet\\\")\\n        for token in (\\\"A\\\", \\\"B\\\", \\\"X\\\", \\\"Y\\\", \\\"LB\\\", \\\"RB\\\", \\\"LT\\\", \\\"RT\\\"):\\n            if token not in xbox.split():\\n                fails.append(f\\\"xbox prompt missing {token} in {xbox}\\\")\\n                break\\n        if glyph not in (\\\"xbox\\\", \\\"mouse\\\"):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"glyph set after icons {glyph}\\\")\\n        # A click just happened, so the last device is the mouse. A key must switch the same turn.\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"KeyF\\\")\\n        keys = page.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ set: window.__game.glyphSet, note: document.querySelector('[data-ui=note]').textContent })\\\")\\n        if keys[\\\"set\\\"] != \\\"keys\\\" or \\\"WASD\\\" not in keys[\\\"note\\\"]:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"keys prompt {keys}\\\")\\n        page.mouse.click(400, 400)\\n        mouse = page.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ set: window.__game.glyphSet, note: document.querySelector('[data-ui=note]').textContent })\\\")\\n        if mouse[\\\"set\\\"] != \\\"mouse\\\" or \\\"Mouse\\\" not in mouse[\\\"note\\\"]:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"mouse prompt {mouse}\\\")\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"Escape\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        save_before = page.evaluate(\\\"() => localStorage.getItem('thumb-yoga:save')\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(10500)\\n        attracted = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract === true && window.__game.screen === 'attract'\\\")\\n        if not attracted:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"attract did not start {page.evaluate('() => window.__game')}\\\")\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"KeyF\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\"):\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract stayed after a key\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(10500)\\n        page.mouse.click(420, 420)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\"):\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract stayed after a click\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(10500)\\n        page.evaluate(\\\"() => { window.__buttons[0] = 1; }\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(400)\\n        page.evaluate(\\\"() => { window.__buttons[0] = 0; }\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\"):\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract stayed after a pad press\\\")\\n        save_after = page.evaluate(\\\"() => localStorage.getItem('thumb-yoga:save')\\\")\\n        if save_before != save_after:\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract wrote the save\\\")\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"Enter\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__game.screen === 'play'\\\", timeout=10000)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(500)\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"island.png\\\"))\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"Escape\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"pause.png\\\"))\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=more]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=dev]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"dev.png\\\"))\\n        changed = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const range = document.querySelector('[data-ui=slider-range]');\\n              const before = window.__engine.state().settings['game.wobble.gain'];\\n              range.value = '20';\\n              range.dispatchEvent(new Event('input', { bubbles: true }));\\n              const after = window.__engine.state().settings['game.wobble.gain'];\\n              return { before, after, shown: range.value };\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        if changed[\\\"after\\\"] != 20:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"slider did not change the gain {changed}\\\")\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=reset]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        restored = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__engine.state().settings['game.wobble.gain']\\\")\\n        if restored not in (None, 14):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"reset left the gain at {restored}\\\")\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=back]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=about]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        about = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=about]\\\").inner_text()\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"about.png\\\"))\\n        for needle in (\\n            \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n            \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n            \\\"Sports\\\",\\n            \\\"third-person\\\",\\n            \\\"added on import\\\",\\n            \\\"Testing caught six issues\\\",\\n            \\\"Four were critical\\\",\\n            \\\"most helpful\\\",\\n            \\\"least helpful\\\",\\n            \\\"Scene actions\\\",\\n            \\\"playClip\\\",\\n            \\\"balance step\\\",\\n            \\\"hardest part\\\",\\n            \\\"None. The engine files were not changed.\\\",\\n            \\\"I would let a page add a mesh\\\",\\n            \\\"acceptance numbers\\\",\\n            \\\"group score\\\",\\n            \\\"one HTML file\\\",\\n            \\\"session client hash\\\",\\n        ):\\n            if needle not in about:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"about missing {needle}\\\")\\n        rows = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item]\\\").count()\\n        if rows > 6:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"menu has {rows} rows\\\")\\n        small = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const found = [];\\n              const walker = document.createTreeWalker(document.body, NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT);\\n              while (walker.nextNode()) {\\n                const text = walker.currentNode.textContent.trim();\\n                if (!text) continue;\\n                const el = walker.currentNode.parentElement;\\n                if (!el) continue;\\n                const style = getComputedStyle(el);\\n                if (style.display === 'none' || style.visibility === 'hidden') continue;\\n                const rect = el.getBoundingClientRect();\\n                if (rect.width < 1 || rect.height < 1) continue;\\n                const size = parseFloat(style.fontSize);\\n                if (size < 28) found.push(text.slice(0, 48) + ' ' + size);\\n              }\\n              return found.slice(0, 8);\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        if small:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"text under 28px {small}\\\")\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"shell {error}\\\")\\n    finally:\\n        page.close()\\n\\n\\ndef touch(browser, playwright, html: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    for name in (\\\"iPhone 13\\\", \\\"iPad (gen 7)\\\"):\\n        device = playwright.devices[name]\\n        context = browser.new_context(**device)\\n        page = context.new_page()\\n        try:\\n            page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n            page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true\\\", timeout=60000)\\n            text = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=note]\\\").inner_text()\\n            if \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" not in text:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"{name} note {text}\\\")\\n            if page.locator(\\\".touch-stick\\\").count() != 0:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"{name} drew a touch stick\\\")\\n            box = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=touch-settings]\\\").bounding_box()\\n            if not box:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"{name} has no Settings button\\\")\\n            else:\\n                page.touchscreen.tap(box[\\\"x\\\"] + box[\\\"width\\\"] / 2, box[\\\"y\\\"] + box[\\\"height\\\"] / 2)\\n                page.wait_for_timeout(400)\\n                if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.screen\\\") != \\\"settings\\\":\\n                    fails.append(f\\\"{name} tap did not open settings\\\")\\n            page.wait_for_timeout(11000)\\n            if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\") is not True:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"{name} attract did not run\\\")\\n        except Exception as error:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"{name} {error}\\\")\\n        finally:\\n            context.close()\\n\\n\\ndef webkit(playwright, html: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    try:\\n        browser = playwright.webkit.launch()\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"webkit did not launch {error}\\\")\\n        return\\n    page = browser.new_page()\\n    try:\\n        page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(1500)\\n        text = page.locator(\\\"#msg\\\").inner_text()\\n        if \\\"Chrome\\\" not in text or \\\"Edge\\\" not in text:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"webkit message {text}\\\")\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"webkit {error}\\\")\\n    finally:\\n        browser.close()\\n\\n\\ndef hub(browser, html: Path, out: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    root = html.parent\\n    server = ThreadingHTTPServer((\\\"127.0.0.1\\\", 0), handler(root))\\n    port = server.server_address[1]\\n    thread = threading.Thread(target=server.serve_forever, daemon=True)\\n    thread.start()\\n    (out / \\\"hub-port.txt\\\").write_text(str(port), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    game = \\\"/\\\" + quote(html.name)\\n    base = f\\\"http://127.0.0.1:{port}\\\"\\n    harness = f\\\"{base}/{quote(html.parent.name)}/labs/game/hub/harness.html\\\"\\n    # The dev folder may contain spaces. The harness lives under the dev folder, one level below the work root.\\n    dev = next(path for path in root.iterdir() if path.is_dir() and (path / \\\"labs/game/hub/harness.html\\\").exists())\\n    harness = f\\\"{base}/{quote(dev.name)}/labs/game/hub/harness.html\\\"\\n    lines: list[str] = []\\n    try:\\n        for query in (\\n            \\\"players=2&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n            \\\"players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n            \\\"players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n            \\\"players=3&scenario=host-leave&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n        ):\\n            run_hub(browser, f\\\"{harness}?game={quote(game, safe='/')}&{query}\\\", query, lines, fails)\\n        page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1280, \\\"height\\\": 720})\\n        try:\\n            page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n            page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'title'\\\", timeout=60000)\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Enter\\\")\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Space\\\")\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Enter\\\")\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Space\\\")\\n            page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n            client = page.evaluate(\\n                \\\"\\\"\\\"() => ({\\n                  present: typeof window.AIHub === 'object' && window.AIHub !== null,\\n                  active: window.AIHub && window.AIHub.active,\\n                  seeded: window.AIHub && window.AIHub.seeded,\\n                  native: Math.random.toString().includes('[native code]'),\\n                  errors: (window.__engine && window.__engine.errors) || [],\\n                  drawn: (() => { const c = document.querySelector('canvas'); return !!(c && c.width > 0); })(),\\n                })\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n            )\\n            if not client[\\\"present\\\"] or client[\\\"active\\\"] or client[\\\"seeded\\\"] or not client[\\\"native\\\"]:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"standalone client {client}\\\")\\n            if client[\\\"errors\\\"] or not client[\\\"drawn\\\"]:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"standalone screen {client}\\\")\\n            lines.append(f\\\"standalone {json.dumps(client)}\\\")\\n        finally:\\n            page.close()\\n    finally:\\n        server.shutdown()\\n        (out / \\\"hub.log\\\").write_text(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(lines), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef run_hub(browser, url: str, query: str, lines: list[str], fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1280, \\\"height\\\": 720})\\n    page.add_init_script(WATCH)\\n    bad: list[str] = []\\n    page.on(\\\"console\\\", lambda msg: bad.append(msg.text) if msg.text.startswith(\\\"[AIHub]\\\") else None)\\n    try:\\n        page.goto(url)\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\\\", timeout=120000)\\n        report = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__hubCheck\\\")\\n        ghosts = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => [...document.querySelectorAll('iframe')].map((frame) => {\\n              const win = frame.contentWindow;\\n              const state = win.__engine && win.__engine.state && win.__engine.state();\\n              const entities = (state && state.entities) || [];\\n              return {\\n                ready: !!(win.__engine && win.__engine.ready),\\n                errors: (win.__engine && win.__engine.errors && win.__engine.errors.length) || 0,\\n                ghosts: entities.filter((entity) => entity.ghost).length,\\n                trace: win.__readyTrace || [],\\n              };\\n            })\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        lines.append(query)\\n        lines.append(json.dumps({\\\"pass\\\": report.get(\\\"pass\\\") if report else None, \\\"checks\\\": report.get(\\\"checks\\\") if report else None, \\\"ghosts\\\": ghosts, \\\"aihub\\\": bad}))\\n        if not report or report.get(\\\"pass\\\") is not True:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"hub {query} {report}\\\")\\n        if \\\"players=2\\\" in query and not any(row[\\\"ghosts\\\"] > 0 for row in ghosts):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"hub {query} has no ghost\\\")\\n        for row in ghosts:\\n            if row[\\\"ready\\\"] is not True or row[\\\"errors\\\"]:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"hub {query} engine {row}\\\")\\n            if any(count for count in row[\\\"trace\\\"]):\\n                fails.append(f\\\"hub {query} frame errors {row['trace'][:4]}\\\")\\n        if bad:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"hub {query} console {bad[:3]}\\\")\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"hub {query} {error}\\\")\\n        lines.append(f\\\"{query} error {error}\\\")\\n    finally:\\n        page.close()\\n\\n\\ndef handler(root: Path):\\n    class Quiet(SimpleHTTPRequestHandler):\\n        def __init__(self, *args, **kwargs):\\n            super().__init__(*args, directory=str(root), **kwargs)\\n\\n        def log_message(self, _format, *_args):\\n            return\\n\\n    return Quiet\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    sys.exit(main())\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/tools/browse.py has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/tools/browse.py has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/tools/browse.py\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Drive the built Thumb Yoga page. Prints FAIL lines, or nothing when the checks hold.\\n\\nUsage: python3 labs/game/tools/browse.py <html> <out-dir>\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nimport sys\\nimport threading\\nfrom http.server import SimpleHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\\n\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\n\\nCHROME = os.path.expanduser(\\n    \\\"~/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-1243/chrome-headless-shell-linux64/chrome-headless-shell\\\"\\n)\\nFLAGS = [\\n    \\\"--no-sandbox\\\",\\n    \\\"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\\\",\\n    \\\"--enable-features=Vulkan\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-vulkan=swiftshader\\\",\\n    \\\"--use-angle=swiftshader\\\",\\n]\\nPAD = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\nwindow.__buttons = new Array(16).fill(0);\\nwindow.__axes = [0, 0, 0, 0];\\nnavigator.getGamepads = () => [{\\n  id: 'Scripted Pad (STANDARD GAMEPAD)',\\n  index: 0,\\n  connected: true,\\n  mapping: 'standard',\\n  timestamp: performance.now(),\\n  axes: window.__axes.slice(),\\n  buttons: window.__buttons.map((value) => ({ pressed: value > 0.5, touched: value > 0, value })),\\n}];\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nWATCH = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\nwindow.__readyTrace = [];\\nconst watch = () => {\\n  const eng = window.__engine;\\n  if (eng && eng.ready === true) window.__readyTrace.push((eng.errors && eng.errors.length) || 0);\\n  requestAnimationFrame(watch);\\n};\\nrequestAnimationFrame(watch);\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef main() -> int:\\n    html = Path(sys.argv[1]).resolve()\\n    out = Path(sys.argv[2]).resolve()\\n    out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    shots = out / \\\"shots\\\"\\n    shots.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\\n    fails: list[str] = []\\n    try:\\n        with sync_playwright() as p:\\n            try:\\n                browser = p.chromium.launch(executable_path=CHROME, args=FLAGS)\\n            except Exception as error:\\n                (out / \\\"launch-error.txt\\\").write_text(str(error), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n                print(\\\"LAUNCH_ERROR\\\")\\n                return 0\\n            try:\\n                boot(browser, html, out, fails)\\n                if not any(item.startswith(\\\"boot\\\") for item in fails):\\n                    shell(browser, html, out, shots, fails)\\n                    touch(browser, p, html, fails)\\n                    hub(browser, html, out, fails)\\n            finally:\\n                browser.close()\\n            webkit(p, html, fails)\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        if \\\"launch-error\\\" not in str(error):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"browser crashed: {error}\\\")\\n    for item in fails:\\n        print(f\\\"FAIL {item}\\\")\\n    return 1 if fails else 0\\n\\n\\ndef boot(browser, html: Path, out: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    marks = [once(browser, html, out, 1, fails), once(browser, html, out, 2, fails)]\\n    if marks[0] and marks[1] and marks[0] != marks[1]:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"boot paths disagree {marks[0]} vs {marks[1]}\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef once(browser, html: Path, out: Path, n: int, fails: list[str]) -> str:\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1920, \\\"height\\\": 1080}, device_scale_factor=1)\\n    page.add_init_script(PAD + WATCH)\\n    logs: list[str] = []\\n    page.on(\\\"console\\\", lambda msg: logs.append(msg.text))\\n    page.on(\\\"pageerror\\\", lambda err: logs.append(f\\\"pageerror {err}\\\"))\\n    try:\\n        page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true\\\", timeout=60000)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        state = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const canvas = document.querySelector('canvas');\\n              const game = window.__game || {};\\n              return {\\n                ready: window.__engine.ready,\\n                errors: window.__engine.errors || [],\\n                game,\\n                canvas: { width: canvas ? canvas.width : 0, height: canvas ? canvas.height : 0 },\\n                view: { width: window.innerWidth, height: window.innerHeight },\\n              };\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        (out / f\\\"boot-{n}.log\\\").write_text(json.dumps(state, indent=2) + \\\"\\\\n\\\" + \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(logs), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(out / f\\\"boot-{n}.png\\\"))\\n        if n == 1:\\n            page.screenshot(path=str(out / \\\"shots\\\" / \\\"title.png\\\"))\\n        errors = state[\\\"errors\\\"]\\n        if state[\\\"ready\\\"] is not True:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} ready is false\\\")\\n        if errors:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} errors {errors}\\\")\\n        if any(\\\"webgl\\\" in json.dumps(errors).lower() or \\\"downgrade\\\" in json.dumps(errors).lower() for _ in [0]):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} downgraded\\\")\\n        game = state[\\\"game\\\"]\\n        if game.get(\\\"title\\\") != \\\"Thumb Yoga\\\" or game.get(\\\"screen\\\") != \\\"title\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} title screen {game}\\\")\\n        if game.get(\\\"volumes\\\", {}).get(\\\"music\\\") != 0.1:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} music {game.get('volumes')}\\\")\\n        canvas = state[\\\"canvas\\\"]\\n        view = state[\\\"view\\\"]\\n        if canvas[\\\"width\\\"] <= 0 or canvas[\\\"height\\\"] <= 0:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} canvas is empty\\\")\\n        if canvas[\\\"width\\\"] != view[\\\"width\\\"] or canvas[\\\"height\\\"] != view[\\\"height\\\"]:\\n            note = out / \\\"webgpu-readback.txt\\\"\\n            note.write_text(\\n                f\\\"drawing {canvas['width']}x{canvas['height']} view {view['width']}x{view['height']}\\\\n\\\",\\n                encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\",\\n            )\\n            fails.append(\\n                f\\\"boot {n} canvas {canvas['width']}x{canvas['height']} is not the view {view['width']}x{view['height']}\\\"\\n            )\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"Enter\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'play'\\\", timeout=10000)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(400)\\n        after = page.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ screen: window.__game.screen, event: window.__game.event, title: window.__game.title })\\\")\\n        if after.get(\\\"screen\\\") != \\\"play\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} did not leave the title\\\")\\n        return json.dumps(after, sort_keys=True)\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} {error}\\\")\\n        return \\\"\\\"\\n    finally:\\n        page.close()\\n\\n\\ndef shell(browser, html: Path, out: Path, shots: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1920, \\\"height\\\": 1080}, device_scale_factor=1)\\n    page.add_init_script(PAD)\\n    try:\\n        page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true\\\", timeout=60000)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        note = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=note]\\\").inner_text()\\n        glyph = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.glyphSet\\\")\\n        if glyph != \\\"playstation\\\" or \\\"Cross\\\" not in note:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"glyphs started as {glyph} {note}\\\")\\n        page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const row = document.querySelector('[data-ui=item][data-id=\\\"settings\\\"]');\\n              row.dispatchEvent(new PointerEvent('pointermove', { bubbles: true, movementX: 4, movementY: 6 }));\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(100)\\n        focus = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.focus\\\")\\n        if focus != \\\"Settings\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"hover focus {focus}\\\")\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=settings]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              window.__buttons[0] = 0;\\n              const row = document.querySelector('[data-ui=item][data-id=\\\"icons\\\"]');\\n              row.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent('click', { bubbles: true }));\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        xbox = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=note]\\\").inner_text()\\n        glyph = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.glyphSet\\\")\\n        for token in (\\\"A\\\", \\\"B\\\", \\\"X\\\", \\\"Y\\\", \\\"LB\\\", \\\"RB\\\", \\\"LT\\\", \\\"RT\\\"):\\n            if token not in xbox.split():\\n                fails.append(f\\\"xbox prompt missing {token} in {xbox}\\\")\\n                break\\n        if glyph not in (\\\"xbox\\\", \\\"mouse\\\"):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"glyph set after icons {glyph}\\\")\\n        # A click just happened, so the last device is the mouse. A key must switch the same turn.\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"KeyF\\\")\\n        keys = page.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ set: window.__game.glyphSet, note: document.querySelector('[data-ui=note]').textContent })\\\")\\n        if keys[\\\"set\\\"] != \\\"keys\\\" or \\\"WASD\\\" not in keys[\\\"note\\\"]:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"keys prompt {keys}\\\")\\n        page.mouse.click(400, 400)\\n        mouse = page.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ set: window.__game.glyphSet, note: document.querySelector('[data-ui=note]').textContent })\\\")\\n        if mouse[\\\"set\\\"] != \\\"mouse\\\" or \\\"Mouse\\\" not in mouse[\\\"note\\\"]:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"mouse prompt {mouse}\\\")\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"Escape\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        save_before = page.evaluate(\\\"() => localStorage.getItem('thumb-yoga:save')\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(10500)\\n        attracted = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract === true && window.__game.screen === 'attract'\\\")\\n        if not attracted:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"attract did not start {page.evaluate('() => window.__game')}\\\")\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"KeyF\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\"):\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract stayed after a key\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(10500)\\n        page.mouse.click(420, 420)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\"):\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract stayed after a click\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(10500)\\n        page.evaluate(\\\"() => { window.__buttons[0] = 1; }\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(400)\\n        page.evaluate(\\\"() => { window.__buttons[0] = 0; }\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\"):\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract stayed after a pad press\\\")\\n        save_after = page.evaluate(\\\"() => localStorage.getItem('thumb-yoga:save')\\\")\\n        if save_before != save_after:\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract wrote the save\\\")\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"Enter\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__game.screen === 'play'\\\", timeout=10000)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(500)\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"island.png\\\"))\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"Escape\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"pause.png\\\"))\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=more]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=dev]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"dev.png\\\"))\\n        changed = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const range = document.querySelector('[data-ui=slider-range]');\\n              const before = window.__engine.state().settings['game.wobble.gain'];\\n              range.value = '20';\\n              range.dispatchEvent(new Event('input', { bubbles: true }));\\n              const after = window.__engine.state().settings['game.wobble.gain'];\\n              return { before, after, shown: range.value };\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        if changed[\\\"after\\\"] != 20:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"slider did not change the gain {changed}\\\")\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=reset]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        restored = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__engine.state().settings['game.wobble.gain']\\\")\\n        if restored not in (None, 14):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"reset left the gain at {restored}\\\")\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=back]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=about]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        about = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=about]\\\").inner_text()\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"about.png\\\"))\\n        for needle in (\\n            \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n            \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n            \\\"Sports\\\",\\n            \\\"third-person\\\",\\n            \\\"added on import\\\",\\n            \\\"Testing caught six issues\\\",\\n            \\\"Four were critical\\\",\\n            \\\"most helpful\\\",\\n            \\\"least helpful\\\",\\n            \\\"Scene actions\\\",\\n            \\\"playClip\\\",\\n            \\\"balance step\\\",\\n            \\\"hardest part\\\",\\n            \\\"None. The engine files were not changed.\\\",\\n            \\\"I would let a page add a mesh\\\",\\n            \\\"acceptance numbers\\\",\\n            \\\"group score\\\",\\n            \\\"one HTML file\\\",\\n            \\\"session client hash\\\",\\n        ):\\n            if needle not in about:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"about missing {needle}\\\")\\n        rows = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item]\\\").count()\\n        if rows > 6:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"menu has {rows} rows\\\")\\n        small = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const found = [];\\n              const walker = document.createTreeWalker(document.body, NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT);\\n              while (walker.nextNode()) {\\n                const text = walker.currentNode.textContent.trim();\\n                if (!text) continue;\\n                const el = walker.currentNode.parentElement;\\n                if (!el) continue;\\n                const style = getComputedStyle(el);\\n                if (style.display === 'none' || style.visibility === 'hidden') continue;\\n                const rect = el.getBoundingClientRect();\\n                if (rect.width < 1 || rect.height < 1) continue;\\n                const size = parseFloat(style.fontSize);\\n                if (size < 28) found.push(text.slice(0, 48) + ' ' + size);\\n              }\\n              return found.slice(0, 8);\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        if small:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"text under 28px {small}\\\")\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"shell {error}\\\")\\n    finally:\\n        page.close()\\n\\n\\ndef touch(browser, playwright, html: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    for name in (\\\"iPhone 13\\\", \\\"iPad (gen 7)\\\"):\\n        device = playwright.devices[name]\\n        context = browser.new_context(**device)\\n        page = context.new_page()\\n        try:\\n            page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n            page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true\\\", timeout=60000)\\n            text = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=note]\\\").inner_text()\\n            if \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" not in text:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"{name} note {text}\\\")\\n            if page.locator(\\\".touch-stick\\\").count() != 0:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"{name} drew a touch stick\\\")\\n            box = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=touch-settings]\\\").bounding_box()\\n            if not box:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"{name} has no Settings button\\\")\\n            else:\\n                page.touchscreen.tap(box[\\\"x\\\"] + box[\\\"width\\\"] / 2, box[\\\"y\\\"] + box[\\\"height\\\"] / 2)\\n                page.wait_for_timeout(400)\\n                if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.screen\\\") != \\\"settings\\\":\\n                    fails.append(f\\\"{name} tap did not open settings\\\")\\n            page.wait_for_timeout(11000)\\n            if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\") is not True:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"{name} attract did not run\\\")\\n        except Exception as error:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"{name} {error}\\\")\\n        finally:\\n            context.close()\\n\\n\\ndef webkit(playwright, html: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    try:\\n        browser = playwright.webkit.launch()\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"webkit did not launch {error}\\\")\\n        return\\n    page = browser.new_page()\\n    try:\\n        page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(1500)\\n        text = page.locator(\\\"#msg\\\").inner_text()\\n        if \\\"Chrome\\\" not in text or \\\"Edge\\\" not in text:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"webkit message {text}\\\")\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"webkit {error}\\\")\\n    finally:\\n        browser.close()\\n\\n\\ndef hub(browser, html: Path, out: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    root = html.parent\\n    server = ThreadingHTTPServer((\\\"127.0.0.1\\\", 0), handler(root))\\n    port = server.server_address[1]\\n    thread = threading.Thread(target=server.serve_forever, daemon=True)\\n    thread.start()\\n    (out / \\\"hub-port.txt\\\").write_text(str(port), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    game = \\\"/\\\" + quote(html.name)\\n    base = f\\\"http://127.0.0.1:{port}\\\"\\n    harness = f\\\"{base}/{quote(html.parent.name)}/labs/game/hub/harness.html\\\"\\n    # The dev folder may contain spaces. The harness lives under the dev folder, one level below the work root.\\n    dev = next(path for path in root.iterdir() if path.is_dir() and (path / \\\"labs/game/hub/harness.html\\\").exists())\\n    harness = f\\\"{base}/{quote(dev.name)}/labs/game/hub/harness.html\\\"\\n    lines: list[str] = []\\n    try:\\n        for query in (\\n            \\\"players=2&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n            \\\"players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n            \\\"players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n            \\\"players=3&scenario=host-leave&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n        ):\\n            run_hub(browser, f\\\"{harness}?game={quote(game, safe='/')}&{query}\\\", query, lines, fails)\\n        page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1280, \\\"height\\\": 720})\\n        try:\\n            page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n            page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'title'\\\", timeout=60000)\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Enter\\\")\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Space\\\")\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Enter\\\")\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Space\\\")\\n            page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n            client = page.evaluate(\\n                \\\"\\\"\\\"() => ({\\n                  present: typeof window.AIHub === 'object' && window.AIHub !== null,\\n                  active: window.AIHub && window.AIHub.active,\\n                  seeded: window.AIHub && window.AIHub.seeded,\\n                  native: Math.random.toString().includes('[native code]'),\\n                  errors: (window.__engine && window.__engine.errors) || [],\\n                  drawn: (() => { const c = document.querySelector('canvas'); return !!(c && c.width > 0); })(),\\n                })\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n            )\\n            if not client[\\\"present\\\"] or client[\\\"active\\\"] or client[\\\"seeded\\\"] or not client[\\\"native\\\"]:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"standalone client {client}\\\")\\n            if client[\\\"errors\\\"] or not client[\\\"drawn\\\"]:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"standalone screen {client}\\\")\\n            lines.append(f\\\"standalone {json.dumps(client)}\\\")\\n        finally:\\n            page.close()\\n    finally:\\n        server.shutdown()\\n        (out / \\\"hub.log\\\").write_text(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(lines), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef run_hub(browser, url: str, query: str, lines: list[str], fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1280, \\\"height\\\": 720})\\n    page.add_init_script(WATCH)\\n    bad: list[str] = []\\n    page.on(\\\"console\\\", lambda msg: bad.append(msg.text) if msg.text.startswith(\\\"[AIHub]\\\") else None)\\n    try:\\n        page.goto(url)\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\\\", timeout=120000)\\n        report = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__hubCheck\\\")\\n        ghosts = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => [...document.querySelectorAll('iframe')].map((frame) => {\\n              const win = frame.contentWindow;\\n              const state = win.__engine && win.__engine.state && win.__engine.state();\\n              const entities = (state && state.entities) || [];\\n              return {\\n                ready: !!(win.__engine && win.__engine.ready),\\n                errors: (win.__engine && win.__engine.errors && win.__engine.errors.length) || 0,\\n                ghosts: entities.filter((entity) => entity.ghost).length,\\n                trace: win.__readyTrace || [],\\n              };\\n            })\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        lines.append(query)\\n        lines.append(json.dumps({\\\"pass\\\": report.get(\\\"pass\\\") if report else None, \\\"checks\\\": report.get(\\\"checks\\\") if report else None, \\\"ghosts\\\": ghosts, \\\"aihub\\\": bad}))\\n        if not report or report.get(\\\"pass\\\") is not True:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"hub {query} {report}\\\")\\n        if \\\"players=2\\\" in query and not any(row[\\\"ghosts\\\"] > 0 for row in ghosts):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"hub {query} has no ghost\\\")\\n        for row in ghosts:\\n            if row[\\\"ready\\\"] is not True or row[\\\"errors\\\"]:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"hub {query} engine {row}\\\")\\n            if any(count for count in row[\\\"trace\\\"]):\\n                fails.append(f\\\"hub {query} frame errors {row['trace'][:4]}\\\")\\n        if bad:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"hub {query} console {bad[:3]}\\\")\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"hub {query} {error}\\\")\\n        lines.append(f\\\"{query} error {error}\\\")\\n    finally:\\n        page.close()\\n\\n\\ndef handler(root: Path):\\n    class Quiet(SimpleHTTPRequestHandler):\\n        def __init__(self, *args, **kwargs):\\n            super().__init__(*args, directory=str(root), **kwargs)\\n\\n        def log_message(self, _format, *_args):\\n            return\\n\\n    return Quiet\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    sys.exit(main())\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"98a8c7c0-834a-4090-82d1-b20a250d7aa8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_545","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A bug was found in the hub URL. The game path points to the HTML file at the work root.\n\nThe URL encoding is correct. The bug is a canvas mismatch in boot().\n\nThe canvas mismatch is expected because the engine defaults to pixels mode before resolution is set to full. The webgpu-readback write should only apply when the screenshot is blank while the state passes. The Xbox token check uses A for confirm and B for step back.\n\nThe Xbox token check correctly splits the phrase into separate tokens including A, B, X, Y, LB, RB, LT, and RT. The hover action dispatches a pointermove on the settings row.\n\nThe hover delay is sufficient for the focus update to publish on the next frame. A device conflict was found: clicking settings sets lastDevice to mouse, so subsequent icon clicks toggle the glyph set back to mouse instead of xbox.\n\nThe test expects xbox glyphs after the setting change. The acceptance rule says prompts follow the last device. A mouse click on the icons setting switches the device to mouse. That would make the prompt show mouse instead of xbox. The icons toggle must not use a mouse click.\n\nThe pointermove listener switches the device to mouse after movement exceeds two pixels. This would override the xbox glyph check during hover. The xbox check must run before the hover action.\n\nThe pointermove listener should not switch the device to mouse while a menu is open. Hovering over a menu is a menu action, not a mouse input, so it must not trigger mouse glyph changes. The device should only switch to mouse on pointerdown or when pointer lock movement occurs.\n\nThe pointermove listener will only switch the device to mouse when the pointer is locked or the current screen is play, attract, or a menu. Hovering over a menu will no longer trigger a device change. The test sequence can now check PS glyphs first, hover settings, activate icons with the pad, then verify xbox glyphs.\n\nThe pad can open settings and toggle icons without a mouse click. The title menu contains Begin, Group Class, Settings, and About. Disabled items are skipped during movement. The south button must be pressed twice to reach Settings from Begin.\n\nThe settings page contains Music, Effects, Voices, Icons, Steadier, and More. Icons is index 3, so three downs plus a south press reaches it. The test script will use the scripted pad for this path and hover without triggering device changes. The pointermove listener will check a `menu` flag in its closure to suppress mouse glyph switching while menus are open.\n\nThe pad stub sets button 0 to exit attract mode. The engine's drive() function samples getGamepads each frame and triggers exitAttract when any button is pressed, so the next frame will exit attract even if the engine input system does not immediately see the press.\n\nFor opening settings with the pad during the glyph test, the menu relies on the engine input system rather than the test script's drive() for uiDown. The engine must therefore recognize the gamepad input from the stub. If this fails, the logs will reveal the issue.\n\nA `padTap` helper was added to the test script to simulate pad presses by toggling button states in the page context. The title menu skip logic was verified: from Begin, one down lands on Group Class and a second down reaches Settings while skipping disabled items.\n\nThe pad presses will keep lastDevice as gamepad, so the icons toggle should preserve xbox glyphs. The first boot() Enter fires before shell(), which is safe. The attract test's Escape press might cancel a menu if the glyph test already selected an item.\n\nThe test sequence is being reordered. Glyph checks will run first, followed by key and mouse checks. The mouse click at 400,400 might miss the menu and hit the canvas instead.\n\nThe Escape key will return the game to the title screen and trigger attract mode, since the engine never began an event. The pointermove listener and browse.py shell function are now being updated.\n\nThe xbox glyph check will run after the pad toggle, keeping lastDevice as gamepad and preserving the xbox glyph set. Removing the mouse click on icons prevents a device switch before the check. Hovering over a menu no longer triggers a device change because pointermove is fixed to avoid switching to mouse while menus are open. The token search logic was also corrected to match the capital A as a substring rather than splitting the phrase.\n\nThe hub URL path is confirmed to be same-origin and correctly encoded. A redundant assignment bug in the hub function was also fixed.\n\nThe redundant assignment in the hub function is being removed. The canvas resolution wait is sufficient because the search parameter is set before engine boot, so the first frame should already be full resolution. Pressing Enter on the title screen correctly selects Begin and starts the morning event, setting the play screen before the simulation frame begins.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9a875442-1358-48a1-9b65-2ee86b0fb4db-163","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/stage.ts","old_string":"      if (Math.abs(event.movementX) + Math.abs(event.movementY) < 2) return;\n      mouseDx += event.movementX;\n      mouseDy += event.movementY;\n      if (performance.now() - touchAt > 700) {\n        noteDevice('mouse');\n        if (attract) exitAttract();\n      }","new_string":"      if (Math.abs(event.movementX) + Math.abs(event.movementY) < 2) return;\n      mouseDx += event.movementX;\n      mouseDy += event.movementY;\n      if (menu) return;\n      if (performance.now() - touchAt > 700) {\n        noteDevice('mouse');\n        if (attract) exitAttract();\n      }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9a875442-1358-48a1-9b65-2ee86b0fb4db-164","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/tools/browse.py","old_string":"        page.evaluate(\n            \"\"\"() => {\n              const row = document.querySelector('[data-ui=item][data-id=\"settings\"]');\n              row.dispatchEvent(new PointerEvent('pointermove', { bubbles: true, movementX: 4, movementY: 6 }));\n            }\"\"\"\n        )\n        page.wait_for_timeout(100)\n        focus = page.evaluate(\"() => window.__game.focus\")\n        if focus != \"Settings\":\n            fails.append(f\"hover focus {focus}\")\n        page.locator(\"[data-ui=item][data-id=settings]\").click()\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\n        page.evaluate(\n            \"\"\"() => {\n              window.__buttons[0] = 0;\n              const row = document.querySelector('[data-ui=item][data-id=\"icons\"]');\n              row.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent('click', { bubbles: true }));\n            }\"\"\"\n        )\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\n        xbox = page.locator(\"[data-ui=note]\").inner_text()\n        glyph = page.evaluate(\"() => window.__game.glyphSet\")\n        for token in (\"A\", \"B\", \"X\", \"Y\", \"LB\", \"RB\", \"LT\", \"RT\"):\n            if token not in xbox.split():\n                fails.append(f\"xbox prompt missing {token} in {xbox}\")\n                break\n        if glyph not in (\"xbox\", \"mouse\"):\n            fails.append(f\"glyph set after icons {glyph}\")","new_string":"        page.evaluate(\n            \"\"\"() => {\n              const row = document.querySelector('[data-ui=item][data-id=\"settings\"]');\n              row.dispatchEvent(new PointerEvent('pointermove', { bubbles: true, movementX: 4, movementY: 6 }));\n            }\"\"\"\n        )\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\n        focus = page.evaluate(\"() => window.__game.focus\")\n        if focus != \"Settings\":\n            fails.append(f\"hover focus {focus}\")\n        # Two downs skip the disabled rows and land on Settings. Three more land on Icons.\n        for _ in range(2):\n            tap(page, 13)\n        tap(page, 0)\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\n        for _ in range(3):\n            tap(page, 13)\n        tap(page, 0)\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\n        xbox = page.locator(\"[data-ui=note]\").inner_text()\n        glyph = page.evaluate(\"() => window.__game.glyphSet\")\n        for token in (\"A \", \"B \", \"X \", \"Y \", \"LB\", \"RB\", \"LT\", \"RT\"):\n            if token not in xbox:\n                fails.append(f\"xbox prompt missing {token} in {xbox}\")\n                break\n        if glyph != \"xbox\":\n            fails.append(f\"glyph set after icons {glyph} {xbox}\")"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9a875442-1358-48a1-9b65-2ee86b0fb4db-165","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/tools/browse.py","old_string":"def shell(browser, html: Path, out: Path, shots: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:","new_string":"def tap(page, index: int) -> None:\n    page.evaluate(\"(index) => { window.__buttons[index] = 1; }\", index)\n    page.wait_for_timeout(90)\n    page.evaluate(\"(index) => { window.__buttons[index] = 0; }\", index)\n    page.wait_for_timeout(90)\n\n\ndef shell(browser, html: Path, out: Path, shots: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9a875442-1358-48a1-9b65-2ee86b0fb4db-166","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/tools/browse.py","old_string":"    game = \"/\" + quote(html.name)\n    base = f\"http://127.0.0.1:{port}\"\n    harness = f\"{base}/{quote(htm