0,100,32,116,119,111,32,99,111,110,115,105,115,116,101,110,116,32,98,111,111,116,115,32,119,105,116,104,32,108,111,103,115,32,117,110,100,101,114,32,96,123,83,67,82,65,84,67,72,125,96,46,10,53,52,58,35,35,32,82,105,115,107,115,32,47,32,67,111,110,116,114,97,100,105,99,116,105,111,110,115,10,53,54,58,45,32,84,104,101,32,108,105,118,101,32,99,108,105,101,110,116,32,102,101,116,99,104,101,100,32,119,104,105,108,101,32,119,114,105,116,105,110,103,32,116,104,105,115,32,112,108,97,110,32,105,115,32,98,97,110,110,101,114,32,96,49,46,52,46,48,96,44,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,80,76,65,78,46,109,100,226,128,153,115,32,112,105,110,46,32,73,102,32,116,104,101,32,117,112,115,116,114,101,97,109,32,102,105,108,101,32,109,111,118,101,115,44,32,116,104,101,32,117,110,109,111,100,105,102,105,101,100,32,102,101,116,99,104,101,100,32,98,121,116,101,115,32,119,105,110,32,111,118,101,114,32,116,104,101,32,111,108,100,32,104,97,115,104,44,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,101,32,110,101,119,32,104,97,115,104,32,103,111,101,115,32,105,110,32,96,80,82,79,71,82,69,83,83,46,109,100,96,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":23,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc%2Fwork/01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc/goal/plan.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":3,\"content\":\"## Goal kind\"},{\"line_number\":6,\"content\":\"## Acceptance criteria\"},{\"line_number\":7,\"content\":\"1. **Hand-in, title, and records.** The work root contains `PROGRESS.md`, `exit-interview.json`, and one self-contained HTML file. The HTML and the dev subfolder share the basename `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656` (SOURCE keeps the space in `Wii Fit`; `{Title}` is the on-screen title, with only OS-illegal characters sanitized, and that sanitization noted in `PROGRESS.md`). `{Title}` was chosen by executing a real RNG over a saved list of 50 playful riffs on “Wii Fit,” and that list plus the pick are in the dev folder. The page shows `{Title}` on the title screen. `exit-interview.json` is one JSON object in TASK.md’s exact shape, every value filled, `usage` exactly `added on import`, and its Source Information plus the three feedback lists match the in-game About/Credits screen in the same order. `aiHub.genre` is `Sports`, `aiHub.source` is `Wii Fit`, `aiHub.type` is `Game`, `aiHub.players` is `1–4`. The word `Wii` appears in-game only on that source line and the hub sou [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":15,\"content\":\"5. **Couch Group Class and AI Hub ghost sessions.** Up to four players join mats on one screen (pad, or keyboard and mouse for one seat). Empty seats become CPU guests unless Settings turns them off. A round is three short classes dealt from one seed, then a podium. In AI Hub the mode is ghost: meta tags `hub:session` 1, `hub:session-players` 1-4, `hub:session-mode` ghost, `hub:session-minutes` 3, goal at most 60 characters, how-to at most 80 characters, `hub:webgpu` required, `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` 1-4, `hub:source` Wii Fit. The fetched session client is pasted unmodified and is byte-identical in the HTML. Its SHA-256 is `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a` (client 1.4.0). If the fetched file’s own banner is a newer client, record the new hash in `PROGRESS.md` and still inject those exact bytes. `?aihub` query keys are stripped before engine boot so unknown keys do not kill the engine. A session skips title, attract, and dev mode; pause does not p [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":17,\"content\":\"## Verification plan\"},{\"line_number\":18,\"content\":\"1. **gating:** In the dev workspace, add or extend tests that call the shipped balance step and each shipped activity’s own setup, step, score, and bot from a fresh sim. Do not reimplement the model, mock the unit under test, or start past setup. Assert criterion 2’s bands, self-end, age range, Still Pond penalties, teardown, and no `NaN`. Run `node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs` from the dev folder (full run, not only `--quick`) and write stdout to `{SCRATCH}/verify.log`. Pass only if the exit code is 0 and the log has no failure lines and one final count line of zero failures. Also write `{SCRATCH}/npm-test.log` and `{SCRATCH}/npm-check.log` for `npm test` and `npm run check`, both passing. `npm run check` shows the engine matches its lock, or `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` lists the exact engine diff and why.\"},{\"line_number\":23,\"content\":\"6. **gating:** Static pass on the work root: HTML and folder names, `exit-interview.json` parses and matches About, `PROGRESS.md` exists, game README says what the game is and which judgment calls were made, `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` is specific, and a search of the game sources for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, and `stub` is clean except test wording. Audio proof (song and syllable render, music 0.1) is in `{SCRATCH}/verify.log` or `{SCRATCH}/audio.log`.\"},{\"line_number\":26,\"content\":\"## Non-goals\"},{\"line_number\":34,\"content\":\"## Assumed scope\"},{\"line_number\":35,\"content\":\"Work root is the folder that holds `STAGE.md`, `PLAN.md`, and `TASK.md`. The dev subfolder is a my-3dge full workspace created with that repo’s `new-game` tool (clone only for the generator, then delete it), then `npm ci` only. Game code lives on top of the read-only engine. Hub `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, and `round.js` are fetched from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/`, not from a clone. Deliverables in the work root: the one HTML file, `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`.\"},{\"line_number\":39,\"content\":\"## Implementation approach\"},{\"line_number\":42,\"content\":\"Keep the balance step, activity rules, bots, and day tables as pure sim code with no rendering or DOM, so node tests drive them directly. The page only reads sim state, plays code audio, and sends input or menu choices back through the engine’s recorded channels. One bot writer produces perfect, human-like, sloppy, idle, attract, and CPU-guest input. Days, poses, charts, trays, and lines stay data. Ship a smaller complete loop early (boot, one activity, one-file HTML, hub `ready`) and add activities without breaking that loop. Put the single verify command in front of the node tests, the three-seed auto playthrough, audio renders, and the browser and harness stages. Publish `window.__game` for those checks. Write About copy and `exit-interview.json` from the same answers before the final HTML build.\"},{\"line_number\":44,\"content\":\"## Task checklist\"},{\"line_number\":45,\"content\":\"- [ ] Save 50 titles, RNG-pick one, create the named dev folder with `new-game`, `npm ci`, and a work-root `PROGRESS.md`.\"},{\"line_number\":46,\"content\":\"- [ ] One-file HTML build, unmodified hub client and tags, tiny session scene, verify command skeleton, harness green with the engine actually ready.\"},{\"line_number\":47,\"content\":\"- [ ] Balance model, maps, disc, glyphs, Morning Check, four bots, dev sliders, and the score-band tests.\"},{\"line_number\":48,\"content\":\"- [ ] Scrubbed clips, Guest and Plumb, Pose Class, code voices, island, flow, saves, results.\"},{\"line_number\":49,\"content\":\"- [ ] Still Pond, The Line, Paddle Glide, Sand Garden, any later activities not cut, Great Tilt, and the 3-seed auto path to credits.\"},{\"line_number\":50,\"content\":\"- [ ] Same-screen Group Class and hub ghosts; harness 2, 3, 4, and host-leave.\"},{\"line_number\":51,\"content\":\"- [ ] Attract, settings, controls, About, touch-only and no-WebGPU pages, songs, and 200+ lines.\"},{\"line_number\":52,\"content\":\"- [ ] `exit-interview.json`, HTML copied to the work root, full verify, and two consistent boots with logs under `{SCRATCH}`.\"},{\"line_number\":54,\"content\":\"## Risks / Contradictions\"},{\"line_number\":56,\"content\":\"- The live client fetched while writing this plan is banner `1.4.0`, matching PLAN.md’s pin. If the upstream file moves, the unmodified fetched bytes win over the old hash, and the new hash goes in `PROGRESS.md`.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-510e40e2-8a20-4d6f-81b9-c4eb18666c9f-5","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,48,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,47,84,104,117,109,98,32,89,111,103,97,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,47,108,97,98,115,47,103,97,109,101,47,117,105,47,97,98,111,117,116,45,100,97,116,97,46,116,115,10,50,48,58,32,32,117,115,97,103,101,58,32,39,97,100,100,101,100,32,111,110,32,105,109,112,111,114,116,39,44,10,50,52,58,101,120,112,111,114,116,32,99,111,110,115,116,32,84,69,83,84,73,78,71,32,61,32,91,10,51,50,58,101,120,112,111,114,116,32,99,111,110,115,116,32,69,78,71,73,78,69,32,61,32,91,10,52,50,58,101,120,112,111,114,116,32,99,111,110,115,116,32,80,82,79,77,80,84,32,61,32,91,10,54,48,58,101,120,112,111,114,116,32,99,111,110,115,116,32,65,73,95,72,85,66,32,61,32,123,10,55,54,58,101,120,112,111,114,116,32,99,111,110,115,116,32,69,88,73,84,32,61,32,123,10,55