is one object whose fields `next()` rewrites, so a page's `navigator.getGamepads` can hand it\"},{\"line_number\":63,\"content\":\"/** The standard button index a script's name means, or -1. */\"},{\"line_number\":88,\"content\":\"    mapping: 'standard',\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/devices/gamepad.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":12,\"content\":\" * Invariants: buttons are read by the standard mapping's index (`PAD_BUTTONS`); a pad with another `mapping` is read\"},{\"line_number\":37,\"content\":\"/** Where pads come from: `navigator.getGamepads`, or a test's slots. */\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"840199eb-32a3-4e5f-b707-01bb8950594d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_563","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Menu movement uses input.\n\nNeed to verify the engine maps button 13 to uiDown and button 0 to uiAccept. The tap() helper holds a button for 90ms, which is roughly five frames at 60fps.\n\nThe engine polls getGamepads during the animation frame loop, so the 90ms button press should register as a single input. Need to check the repeat delay to avoid unintended repeats. Pressing button 0 triggers both the gamepad device note and the menu accept action.\n\nMenu.update runs before drive() each frame. The accept action therefore fires before the gamepad device note is recorded.\n\nHovering the settings row with a synthetic PointerEvent should trigger the engine listener because movementX is non-zero. Focus will be published next frame and should target the Settings label after a 200ms wait.\n\nThis hover step occurs before pad navigation.\n\nThe test plan assumes focus starts at Begin, but the script first hovers Settings. Two pad-down presses from Settings land on About and then wrap to Begin, so Settings never opens. This is a bug in the browse.py assumption.\n\nThe fix is to move the hover step after pad navigation, or navigate from the start before hovering. The intended sequence is: check PlayStation glyphs while focus is at Begin, then use pad-down and accept to open Settings, then verify Xbox glyphs appear.\n\nTwo pad-downs from Begin land on Settings, so the original assumption is correct. The hover test must therefore happen after returning to the title menu, or before pad navigation with focus reset to Begin.\n\nThe script should check glyphs first, then pad navigate to Settings from Begin. Hovering Settings afterward would leave focus there, so the next step would be to open Settings with a single accept press and then move three more times to Icons. This creates tension because the test requires the full pad navigation path.\n\nThe cleanest fix is to check glyphs first, hover Settings to assert focus, then press accept once to open it, and move three more times to Icons. Another option is to pad navigate from Begin to Settings, toggle Icons, escape back to the title, and then hover Settings for verification. The key and mouse tests currently run while Settings is already open.\n\nThe final test sequence is now fixed. Glyph checks come first. Then pad navigation opens Settings and toggles Icons. Key and mouse tests follow. Escape returns to the title menu. Hovering Settings there verifies focus. The attract sequence runs last. A mouse click at 400,400 risks hitting a menu item because the settings menu is centered.\n\nClicking at 400,400 risks hitting the centered settings menu and selecting an item. That would change the screen state before Escape runs. A safer approach is to click a corner such as (20, 20) or (1800, 20). This avoids the menu entirely so pointerdown notes the mouse device without picking anything.\n\nThe pointerdown listener fires during the capture phase, so it should record the mouse device before any click event bubbles to the menu. Even if the click selects a menu item and changes the screen, the glyph set and note text will still be captured correctly.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-07f4b77d-22f9-49d3-a0b7-87bd897ade1c-26","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/glyphs.ts","limit":70}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-07f4b77d-22f9-49d3-a0b7-87bd897ade1c-27","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/devices/gamepad.ts","limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-07f4b77d-22f9-49d3-a0b7-87bd897ade1c-28","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function createRepeat|delay|repeat","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/ui/widgets.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2357,"output_tokens":1908,"cache_read_input_tokens":69760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"5fda5812-6d06-41b4-945f-dd8be71efaa8"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-07f4b77d-22f9-49d3-a0b7-87bd897ade1c-26","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Prompts for the device used last. Pads start as PlayStation. Settings can ask for Xbox.\\n * Keys and mouse buttons replace the pad marks the frame those devices are used.\\n */\\nexport type GlyphSet = 'playstation' | 'xbox' | 'keys' | 'mouse';\\n\\n/** One row of marks for the verbs. */\\nconst MARKS: Record<GlyphSet, Record<string, string>> = {\\n  playstation: {\\n10→    accept: 'Cross',\\n    cancel: 'Circle',\\n    lean: 'Left stick',\\n    feet: 'L2 and R2',\\n    breathe: 'L2 and R2 together',\\n    act: 'Cross',\\n    pause: 'Options',\\n    spare: 'Square and Triangle',\\n    shoulders: 'L1 and R1',\\n  },\\n20→  xbox: {\\n    accept: 'A',\\n    cancel: 'B',\\n    lean: 'Left stick',\\n    feet: 'LT and RT',\\n    breathe: 'LT and RT together',\\n    act: 'A',\\n    pause: 'Menu',\\n    spare: 'X and Y',\\n    shoulders: 'LB and RB',\\n30→  },\\n  keys: {\\n    accept: 'Enter',\\n    cancel: 'Esc',\\n    lean: 'WASD',\\n    feet: 'Q and E',\\n    breathe: 'Space',\\n    act: 'F',\\n    pause: 'Esc',\\n    spare: '',\\n40→    shoulders: '',\\n  },\\n  mouse: {\\n    accept: 'Click',\\n    cancel: 'Esc',\\n    lean: 'Mouse',\\n    feet: 'Left and right buttons',\\n    breathe: 'Space',\\n    act: 'Click',\\n    pause: 'Esc',\\n50→    spare: '',\\n    shoulders: '',\\n  },\\n};\\n\\n/** The mark for one verb on this glyph set. */\\nexport function glyph(set: GlyphSet, verb: string): string {\\n  return MARKS[set][verb] ?? verb;\\n}\\n\\n60→/** One prompt line. Two clauses, one sentence. */\\nexport function promptLine(set: GlyphSet): string {\\n  const row = MARKS[set];\\n  if (set === 'playstation' || set === 'xbox') {\\n    return `${row.accept} confirms and ${row.cancel} steps back. ${row.spare} wait, ${row.shoulders} wait, and ${row.feet} are the feet.`;\\n  }\\n  return `${row.lean} leans, and ${row.feet} are the feet. ${row.breathe} breathes, and ${row.act} acts.`;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Prompts for the device used last. Pads start as PlayStation. Settings can ask for Xbox.\\n * Keys and mouse buttons replace the pad marks the frame those devices are used.\\n */\\nexport type GlyphSet = 'playstation' | 'xbox' | 'keys' | 'mouse';\\n\\n/** One row of marks for the verbs. */\\nconst MARKS: Record<GlyphSet, Record<string, string>> = {\\n  playstation: {\\n10→    accept: 'Cross',\\n    cancel: 'Circle',\\n    lean: 'Left stick',\\n    feet: 'L2 and R2',\\n    breathe: 'L2 and R2 together',\\n    act: 'Cross',\\n    pause: 'Options',\\n    spare: 'Square and Triangle',\\n    shoulders: 'L1 and R1',\\n  },\\n20→  xbox: {\\n    accept: 'A',\\n    cancel: 'B',\\n    lean: 'Left stick',\\n    feet: 'LT and RT',\\n    breathe: 'LT and RT together',\\n    act: 'A',\\n    pause: 'Menu',\\n    spare: 'X and Y',\\n    shoulders: 'LB and RB',\\n30→  },\\n  keys: {\\n    accept: 'Enter',\\n    cancel: 'Esc',\\n    lean: 'WASD',\\n    feet: 'Q and E',\\n    breathe: 'Space',\\n    act: 'F',\\n    pause: 'Esc',\\n    spare: '',\\n40→    shoulders: '',\\n  },\\n  mouse: {\\n    accept: 'Click',\\n    cancel: 'Esc',\\n    lean: 'Mouse',\\n    feet: 'Left and right buttons',\\n    breathe: 'Space',\\n    act: 'Click',\\n    pause: 'Esc',\\n50→    spare: '',\\n    shoulders: '',\\n  },\\n};\\n\\n/** The mark for one verb on this glyph set. */\\nexport function glyph(set: GlyphSet, verb: string): string {\\n  return MARKS[set][verb] ?? verb;\\n}\\n\\n60→/** One prompt line. Two clauses, one sentence. */\\nexport function promptLine(set: GlyphSet): string {\\n  const row = MARKS[set];\\n  if (set === 'playstation' || set === 'xbox') {\\n    return `${row.accept} confirms and ${row.cancel} steps back. ${row.spare} wait, ${row.shoulders} wait, and ${row.feet} are the feet.`;\\n  }\\n  return `${row.lean} leans, and ${row.feet} are the feet. ${row.breathe} breathes, and ${row.act} acts.`;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/glyphs.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":70,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file Prompts for the device used last. Pads start as PlayStation. Settings can ask for Xbox.\\n * Keys and mouse buttons replace the pad marks the frame those devices are used.\\n */\\nexport type GlyphSet = 'playstation' | 'xbox' | 'keys' | 'mouse';\\n\\n/** One row of marks for the verbs. */\\nconst MARKS: Record<GlyphSet, Record<string, string>> = {\\n  playstation: {\\n    accept: 'Cross',\\n    cancel: 'Circle',\\n    lean: 'Left stick',\\n    feet: 'L2 and R2',\\n    breathe: 'L2 and R2 together',\\n    act: 'Cross',\\n    pause: 'Options',\\n    spare: 'Square and Triangle',\\n    shoulders: 'L1 and R1',\\n  },\\n  xbox: {\\n    accept: 'A',\\n    cancel: 'B',\\n    lean: 'Left stick',\\n    feet: 'LT and RT',\\n    breathe: 'LT and RT together',\\n    act: 'A',\\n    pause: 'Menu',\\n    spare: 'X and Y',\\n    shoulders: 'LB and RB',\\n  },\\n  keys: {\\n    accept: 'Enter',\\n    cancel: 'Esc',\\n    lean: 'WASD',\\n    feet: 'Q and E',\\n    breathe: 'Space',\\n    act: 'F',\\n    pause: 'Esc',\\n    spare: '',\\n    shoulders: '',\\n  },\\n  mouse: {\\n    accept: 'Click',\\n    cancel: 'Esc',\\n    lean: 'Mouse',\\n    feet: 'Left and right buttons',\\n    breathe: 'Space',\\n    act: 'Click',\\n    pause: 'Esc',\\n    spare: '',\\n    shoulders: '',\\n  },\\n};\\n\\n/** The mark for one verb on this glyph set. */\\nexport function glyph(set: GlyphSet, verb: string): string {\\n  return MARKS[set][verb] ?? verb;\\n}\\n\\n/** One prompt line. Two clauses, one sentence. */\\nexport function promptLine(set: GlyphSet): string {\\n  const row = MARKS[set];\\n  if (set === 'playstation' || set === 'xbox') {\\n    return `${row.accept} confirms and ${row.cancel} steps back. ${row.spare} wait, ${row.shoulders} wait, and ${row.feet} are the feet.`;\\n  }\\n  return `${row.lean} leans, and ${row.feet} are the feet. ${row.breathe} breathes, and ${row.act} acts.`;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":67}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-07f4b77d-22f9-49d3-a0b7-87bd897ade1c-27","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The gamepad device (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24): polls the Gamepad API once per sample and writes its buttons and\\n * sticks as codes (engine/input/codes.ts). Any slot works: the active pad stays while it is connected, a pad in\\n * another slot takes over when it is used while the active one rests, and a pad that leaves (disconnected or\\n * replaced) releases everything it held at once.\\n *\\n * Sticks get a radial deadzone, rescaled so the stick still reaches 1: a lean of l ≤ d gives 0, otherwise the\\n * direction times min(1, (l − d) / (1 − d)), so there is no jump at the edge and no drift. The four direction codes of\\n * each stick carry how far it leans that way, so a half-pushed stick walks at half speed; they count as held from 0.5\\n10→ * and let go below 0.4, as the triggers do (analog, `value` 0 to 1). Other buttons are held as the browser reports.\\n *\\n * Invariants: buttons are read by the standard mapping's index (`PAD_BUTTONS`); a pad with another `mapping` is read\\n * the same way, as browsers expose it. `deadzone` is clamped to [0.05, 0.5]. Nothing here reads a clock.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:595-619` (`tick`: any slot, the radial deadzone, release on\\n * disconnect) and `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md` (slot 0 only, drift and stuck buttons were its bugs).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * radialDeadzone(0.1, 0, 0.18); // [0, 0]: inside the deadzone\\n20→ * radialDeadzone(0.59, 0, 0.18); // [0.5, 0]: rescaled, so half the travel past the deadzone is 0.5\\n * radialDeadzone(0, -1, 0.18); // [0, -1]: still reaches the edge\\n * @see engine/input/devices/devices.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { MathUtils } from '../../core/math';\\nimport { PAD_BUTTONS, padStyle, type InputSink, type PadStyle } from '../codes';\\n\\n/** The Gamepad API's `Gamepad`, as far as the device reads it (a test stub gives just this). */\\nexport interface GamepadLike {\\n  readonly id: string;\\n30→  readonly index: number;\\n  readonly connected: boolean;\\n  readonly mapping?: string;\\n  readonly axes: readonly number[];\\n  readonly buttons: readonly { readonly pressed: boolean; readonly value: number }[];\\n}\\n\\n/** Where pads come from: `navigator.getGamepads`, or a test's slots. */\\nexport type GamepadSource = () => readonly (GamepadLike | null)[];\\n\\n40→/** The stick deadzone by default (the prototype's). */\\nexport const DEADZONE = 0.18;\\n\\n/** An analog code is held from this strength… */\\nconst PRESS = 0.5;\\n/** …until it falls below this one. */\\nconst LET_GO = 0.4;\\n\\n/** A stick reading with a radial deadzone `d`, rescaled so the edge still reaches 1. */\\nexport function radialDeadzone(x: number, y: number, d: number): [number, number] {\\n50→  const length = Math.hypot(x, y);\\n  if (length <= d || length === 0) return [0, 0];\\n  const k = Math.min(1, (length - d) / (1 - d)) / length;\\n  return [x * k, y * k];\\n}\\n\\n/** The gamepad device: `poll()` once per sample; the right stick and the family for the camera and prompts. */\\nexport interface GamepadDevice {\\n  /** Reads the pads and writes the active one's codes. */\\n  poll(): void;\\n60→  /** The active pad's right stick after the deadzone, `[x, y]` with y down as the API gives it; `[0, 0]` without one. */\\n  rightStick(): [number, number];\\n  /** The active pad's slot, or null. */\\n  readonly index: number | null;\\n  /** The active pad's family, for labels. */\\n  readonly style: PadStyle;\\n  /** Lets go of the active pad (a `gamepaddisconnected`, or a page blur). */\\n  release(): void;\\n}\\n\\n70→/** Makes the gamepad device over `source`, writing to `sink`. */\\nexport function createGamepadDevice(sink: InputSink, source: GamepadSource, deadzone = DEADZONE): GamepadDevice {\\n  const d = MathUtils.clamp(deadzone, 0.05, 0.5);\\n  let active: { index: number; id: string } | null = null;\\n  let right: [number, number] = [0, 0];\\n  let style: PadStyle = 'xbox';\\n  const held = new Set<string>();\\n  const set = (code: string, value: number, down: boolean) => {\\n    if (down && !held.has(code)) {\\n      held.add(code);\\n80→      sink.press(code, 'gamepad');\\n    } else if (!down && held.delete(code)) sink.release(code);\\n    sink.analog(code, value);\\n  };\\n  const busy = (pad: GamepadLike) =>\\n    pad.buttons.some((button) => button.pressed) ||\\n    Math.hypot(pad.axes[0] ?? 0, pad.axes[1] ?? 0) > d ||\\n    Math.hypot(pad.axes[2] ?? 0, pad.axes[3] ?? 0) > d;\\n  const device: GamepadDevice = {\\n    get index() {\\n90→      return active?.index ?? null;\\n    },\\n    get style() {\\n      return style;\\n    },\\n    rightStick: () => [...right],\\n    release() {\\n      for (const code of held) sink.release(code);\\n      held.clear();\\n      right = [0, 0];\\n100→      active = null;\\n    },\\n    poll() {\\n      let pads: GamepadLike[] = [];\\n      try {\\n        pads = [...source()].filter((pad): pad is GamepadLike => !!pad && pad.connected !== false);\\n      } catch {\\n        pads = []; // a page in a frame may not read gamepads\\n      }\\n      let pad = pads.find((p) => active && p.index === active.index && p.id === active.id);\\n110→      const other = pads.find((p) => p !== pad && busy(p));\\n      if (!pad || (other && !busy(pad))) {\\n        if (active) device.release();\\n        pad = other ?? pads[0];\\n        if (!pad) return;\\n        active = { index: pad.index, id: pad.id };\\n        style = padStyle(pad.id);\\n      }\\n      read(pad);\\n    },\\n120→  };\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The gamepad device (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24): polls the Gamepad API once per sample and writes its buttons and\\n * sticks as codes (engine/input/codes.ts). Any slot works: the active pad stays while it is connected, a pad in\\n * another slot takes over when it is used while the active one rests, and a pad that leaves (disconnected or\\n * replaced) releases everything it held at once.\\n *\\n * Sticks get a radial deadzone, rescaled so the stick still reaches 1: a lean of l ≤ d gives 0, otherwise the\\n * direction times min(1, (l − d) / (1 − d)), so there is no jump at the edge and no drift. The four direction codes of\\n * each stick carry how far it leans that way, so a half-pushed stick walks at half speed; they count as held from 0.5\\n10→ * and let go below 0.4, as the triggers do (analog, `value` 0 to 1). Other buttons are held as the browser reports.\\n *\\n * Invariants: buttons are read by the standard mapping's index (`PAD_BUTTONS`); a pad with another `mapping` is read\\n * the same way, as browsers expose it. `deadzone` is clamped to [0.05, 0.5]. Nothing here reads a clock.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:595-619` (`tick`: any slot, the radial deadzone, release on\\n * disconnect) and `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md` (slot 0 only, drift and stuck buttons were its bugs).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * radialDeadzone(0.1, 0, 0.18); // [0, 0]: inside the deadzone\\n20→ * radialDeadzone(0.59, 0, 0.18); // [0.5, 0]: rescaled, so half the travel past the deadzone is 0.5\\n * radialDeadzone(0, -1, 0.18); // [0, -1]: still reaches the edge\\n * @see engine/input/devices/devices.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { MathUtils } from '../../core/math';\\nimport { PAD_BUTTONS, padStyle, type InputSink, type PadStyle } from '../codes';\\n\\n/** The Gamepad API's `Gamepad`, as far as the device reads it (a test stub gives just this). */\\nexport interface GamepadLike {\\n  readonly id: string;\\n30→  readonly index: number;\\n  readonly connected: boolean;\\n  readonly mapping?: string;\\n  readonly axes: readonly number[];\\n  readonly buttons: readonly { readonly pressed: boolean; readonly value: number }[];\\n}\\n\\n/** Where pads come from: `navigator.getGamepads`, or a test's slots. */\\nexport type GamepadSource = () => readonly (GamepadLike | null)[];\\n\\n40→/** The stick deadzone by default (the prototype's). */\\nexport const DEADZONE = 0.18;\\n\\n/** An analog code is held from this strength… */\\nconst PRESS = 0.5;\\n/** …until it falls below this one. */\\nconst LET_GO = 0.4;\\n\\n/** A stick reading with a radial deadzone `d`, rescaled so the edge still reaches 1. */\\nexport function radialDeadzone(x: number, y: number, d: number): [number, number] {\\n50→  const length = Math.hypot(x, y);\\n  if (length <= d || length === 0) return [0, 0];\\n  const k = Math.min(1, (length - d) / (1 - d)) / length;\\n  return [x * k, y * k];\\n}\\n\\n/** The gamepad device: `poll()` once per sample; the right stick and the family for the camera and prompts. */\\nexport interface GamepadDevice {\\n  /** Reads the pads and writes the active one's codes. */\\n  poll(): void;\\n60→  /** The active pad's right stick after the deadzone, `[x, y]` with y down as the API gives it; `[0, 0]` without one. */\\n  rightStick(): [number, number];\\n  /** The active pad's slot, or null. */\\n  readonly index: number | null;\\n  /** The active pad's family, for labels. */\\n  readonly style: PadStyle;\\n  /** Lets go of the active pad (a `gamepaddisconnected`, or a page blur). */\\n  release(): void;\\n}\\n\\n70→/** Makes the gamepad device over `source`, writing to `sink`. */\\nexport function createGamepadDevice(sink: InputSink, source: GamepadSource, deadzone = DEADZONE): GamepadDevice {\\n  const d = MathUtils.clamp(deadzone, 0.05, 0.5);\\n  let active: { index: number; id: string } | null = null;\\n  let right: [number, number] = [0, 0];\\n  let style: PadStyle = 'xbox';\\n  const held = new Set<string>();\\n  const set = (code: string, value: number, down: boolean) => {\\n    if (down && !held.has(code)) {\\n      held.add(code);\\n80→      sink.press(code, 'gamepad');\\n    } else if (!down && held.delete(code)) sink.release(code);\\n    sink.analog(code, value);\\n  };\\n  const busy = (pad: GamepadLike) =>\\n    pad.buttons.some((button) => button.pressed) ||\\n    Math.hypot(pad.axes[0] ?? 0, pad.axes[1] ?? 0) > d ||\\n    Math.hypot(pad.axes[2] ?? 0, pad.axes[3] ?? 0) > d;\\n  const device: GamepadDevice = {\\n    get index() {\\n90→      return active?.index ?? null;\\n    },\\n    get style() {\\n      return style;\\n    },\\n    rightStick: () => [...right],\\n    release() {\\n      for (const code of held) sink.release(code);\\n      held.clear();\\n      right = [0, 0];\\n100→      active = null;\\n    },\\n    poll() {\\n      let pads: GamepadLike[] = [];\\n      try {\\n        pads = [...source()].filter((pad): pad is GamepadLike => !!pad && pad.connected !== false);\\n      } catch {\\n        pads = []; // a page in a frame may not read gamepads\\n      }\\n      let pad = pads.find((p) => active && p.index === active.index && p.id === active.id);\\n110→      const other = pads.find((p) => p !== pad && busy(p));\\n      if (!pad || (other && !busy(pad))) {\\n        if (active) device.release();\\n        pad = other ?? pads[0];\\n        if (!pad) return;\\n        active = { index: pad.index, id: pad.id };\\n        style = padStyle(pad.id);\\n      }\\n      read(pad);\\n    },\\n120→  };\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/devices/gamepad.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The gamepad device (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24): polls the Gamepad API once per sample and writes its buttons and\\n * sticks as codes (engine/input/codes.ts). Any slot works: the active pad stays while it is connected, a pad in\\n * another slot takes over when it is used while the active one rests, and a pad that leaves (disconnected or\\n * replaced) releases everything it held at once.\\n *\\n * Sticks get a radial deadzone, rescaled so the stick still reaches 1: a lean of l ≤ d gives 0, otherwise the\\n * direction times min(1, (l − d) / (1 − d)), so there is no jump at the edge and no drift. The four direction codes of\\n * each stick carry how far it leans that way, so a half-pushed stick walks at half speed; they count as held from 0.5\\n * and let go below 0.4, as the triggers do (analog, `value` 0 to 1). Other buttons are held as the browser reports.\\n *\\n * Invariants: buttons are read by the standard mapping's index (`PAD_BUTTONS`); a pad with another `mapping` is read\\n * the same way, as browsers expose it. `deadzone` is clamped to [0.05, 0.5]. Nothing here reads a clock.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:595-619` (`tick`: any slot, the radial deadzone, release on\\n * disconnect) and `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md` (slot 0 only, drift and stuck buttons were its bugs).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * radialDeadzone(0.1, 0, 0.18); // [0, 0]: inside the deadzone\\n * radialDeadzone(0.59, 0, 0.18); // [0.5, 0]: rescaled, so half the travel past the deadzone is 0.5\\n * radialDeadzone(0, -1, 0.18); // [0, -1]: still reaches the edge\\n * @see engine/input/devices/devices.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { MathUtils } from '../../core/math';\\nimport { PAD_BUTTONS, padStyle, type InputSink, type PadStyle } from '../codes';\\n\\n/** The Gamepad API's `Gamepad`, as far as the device reads it (a test stub gives just this). */\\nexport interface GamepadLike {\\n  readonly id: string;\\n  readonly index: number;\\n  readonly connected: boolean;\\n  readonly mapping?: string;\\n  readonly axes: readonly number[];\\n  readonly buttons: readonly { readonly pressed: boolean; readonly value: number }[];\\n}\\n\\n/** Where pads come from: `navigator.getGamepads`, or a test's slots. */\\nexport type GamepadSource = () => readonly (GamepadLike | null)[];\\n\\n/** The stick deadzone by default (the prototype's). */\\nexport const DEADZONE = 0.18;\\n\\n/** An analog code is held from this strength… */\\nconst PRESS = 0.5;\\n/** …until it falls below this one. */\\nconst LET_GO = 0.4;\\n\\n/** A stick reading with a radial deadzone `d`, rescaled so the edge still reaches 1. */\\nexport function radialDeadzone(x: number, y: number, d: number): [number, number] {\\n  const length = Math.hypot(x, y);\\n  if (length <= d || length === 0) return [0, 0];\\n  const k = Math.min(1, (length - d) / (1 - d)) / length;\\n  return [x * k, y * k];\\n}\\n\\n/** The gamepad device: `poll()` once per sample; the right stick and the family for the camera and prompts. */\\nexport interface GamepadDevice {\\n  /** Reads the pads and writes the active one's codes. */\\n  poll(): void;\\n  /** The active pad's right stick after the deadzone, `[x, y]` with y down as the API gives it; `[0, 0]` without one. */\\n  rightStick(): [number, number];\\n  /** The active pad's slot, or null. */\\n  readonly index: number | null;\\n  /** The active pad's family, for labels. */\\n  readonly style: PadStyle;\\n  /** Lets go of the active pad (a `gamepaddisconnected`, or a page blur). */\\n  release(): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** Makes the gamepad device over `source`, writing to `sink`. */\\nexport function createGamepadDevice(sink: InputSink, source: GamepadSource, deadzone = DEADZONE): GamepadDevice {\\n  const d = MathUtils.clamp(deadzone, 0.05, 0.5);\\n  let active: { index: number; id: string } | null = null;\\n  let right: [number, number] = [0, 0];\\n  let style: PadStyle = 'xbox';\\n  const held = new Set<string>();\\n  const set = (code: string, value: number, down: boolean) => {\\n    if (down && !held.has(code)) {\\n      held.add(code);\\n      sink.press(code, 'gamepad');\\n    } else if (!down && held.delete(code)) sink.release(code);\\n    sink.analog(code, value);\\n  };\\n  const busy = (pad: GamepadLike) =>\\n    pad.buttons.some((button) => button.pressed) ||\\n    Math.hypot(pad.axes[0] ?? 0, pad.axes[1] ?? 0) > d ||\\n    Math.hypot(pad.axes[2] ?? 0, pad.axes[3] ?? 0) > d;\\n  const device: GamepadDevice = {\\n    get index() {\\n      return active?.index ?? null;\\n    },\\n    get style() {\\n      return style;\\n    },\\n    rightStick: () => [...right],\\n    release() {\\n      for (const code of held) sink.release(code);\\n      held.clear();\\n      right = [0, 0];\\n      active = null;\\n    },\\n    poll() {\\n      let pads: GamepadLike[] = [];\\n      try {\\n        pads = [...source()].filter((pad): pad is GamepadLike => !!pad && pad.connected !== false);\\n      } catch {\\n        pads = []; // a page in a frame may not read gamepads\\n      }\\n      let pad = pads.find((p) => active && p.index === active.index && p.id === active.id);\\n      const other = pads.find((p) => p !== pad && busy(p));\\n      if (!pad || (other && !busy(pad))) {\\n        if (active) device.release();\\n        pad = other ?? pads[0];\\n        if (!pad) return;\\n        active = { index: pad.index, id: pad.id };\\n        style = padStyle(pad.id);\\n      }\\n      read(pad);\\n    },\\n  };\\n\",\"total_lines\":150}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-07f4b77d-22f9-49d3-a0b7-87bd897ade1c-28","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,53,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114