{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_583","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"titles.json is located in the dev folder root.\n\nThe title pick is currently only in scratch. It needs to be moved to the dev folder so it is included in the hand-in.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-642ee79a-42c7-40e2-9e14-d5d631744bdc-66","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/titles.json","offset":45}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3227,"output_tokens":288,"cache_read_input_tokens":107136,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"85d68aba-a94e-4642-a15e-51c86c0d06c0"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-642ee79a-42c7-40e2-9e14-d5d631744bdc-66","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"45→    \\\"Least Wobbly\\\",\\n    \\\"The Gentle Topple\\\",\\n    \\\"Island on a Thumb\\\",\\n    \\\"Serene Enough\\\",\\n    \\\"The Courtesy Lean\\\",\\n50→    \\\"Quiet Feet\\\",\\n    \\\"Balance Brochure\\\",\\n    \\\"Rock Underneath\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"bytes\\\": \\\"b0306a24\\\",\\n  \\\"uint32\\\": 2955962916,\\n  \\\"index\\\": 16,\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Thumb Yoga\\\"\\n}\",\"content_concise\":\"45→    \\\"Least Wobbly\\\",\\n    \\\"The Gentle Topple\\\",\\n    \\\"Island on a Thumb\\\",\\n    \\\"Serene Enough\\\",\\n    \\\"The Courtesy Lean\\\",\\n50→    \\\"Quiet Feet\\\",\\n    \\\"Balance Brochure\\\",\\n    \\\"Rock Underneath\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"bytes\\\": \\\"b0306a24\\\",\\n  \\\"uint32\\\": 2955962916,\\n  \\\"index\\\": 16,\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Thumb Yoga\\\"\\n}\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/titles.json\",\"offset\":45,\"raw_output\":\"    \\\"Least Wobbly\\\",\\n    \\\"The Gentle Topple\\\",\\n    \\\"Island on a Thumb\\\",\\n    \\\"Serene Enough\\\",\\n    \\\"The Courtesy Lean\\\",\\n    \\\"Quiet Feet\\\",\\n    \\\"Balance Brochure\\\",\\n    \\\"Rock Underneath\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"bytes\\\": \\\"b0306a24\\\",\\n  \\\"uint32\\\": 2955962916,\\n  \\\"index\\\": 16,\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Thumb Yoga\\\"\\n}\",\"total_lines\":58}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"03430f49-2e69-471f-b178-498c91d8a0a2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_584","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The pick is in titles.json in the dev folder.\n\nPlanning six edits to stage.ts. Adding an exitPending flag and a finishExit function. Replacing exitAttract. Calling finishExit after remember. Returning early from remember. Preventing forced attract screen when the current screen is touch.\n\nThe pending exit version will show the title if armed, otherwise switch to touch. The frame override that forces attract must run after finishExit, not before.\n\nfinishExit must run after the attract screen override but before paint. The override still sees attract true and sets the screen to attract, then finishExit clears attract and shows the title.\n\nA problem emerged: if the current screen is settings, finishExit would close settings and show the title instead. Exiting attract from settings should not switch away from settings.\n\nA key press exiting attract to the title is acceptable even if the user was in settings. Touch input will not trigger exit, so the screen remains unchanged. The attract override and startAttract will both exclude touch and settings screens.\n\nstartAttract now only closes the title menu and sets the screen to attract when the current screen is title. Touch input no longer triggers this behavior, so it keeps its existing screen and message. The remember function is being updated next.\n\nThe remember function now returns early when attract, exitPending, or hub is active. This prevents stale attract data from being written to disk during the exit sequence.\n\nNext, browse.py needs a shell section rewrite with a hashlib import and a browser log trace list. The hub client hash will be added at the start of the hub() function.\n\nThe verify script must not print FAIL lines on success. The \"0 failures\" count line is acceptable because it is the final summary. LAUNCH_ERROR is a note, not a failure. A potential issue was spotted: x replay --browser sim launches Chromium, and browse may launch another browser instance.\n\nThe browser instances run sequentially, not in parallel. Chromium closes before WebKit launches, so only one browser is active at a time. The hub tests run four sessions sequentially and each can take up to two minutes. Total verify time should be roughly eight to fifteen minutes.\n\nA monitor script will poll the verify process until it exits. It stays silent during execution and prints DONE or FAILED with the final output once finished. The script will be placed in scratch for this session.\n\nA bash one-liner will poll the verify process and check the log for \"0 failures\". The PID is hard to capture because the tool returns a task ID rather than a shell PID. The command will write its own PID to a file so the monitor can track it.\n\nThe verify command will run in the background with block_until_ms 0. The shell PID will be captured from the tool result so the monitor can track it. Documentation updates can proceed while the process is running.\n\nThe exact sequence is now set: edit stage.ts and browse.py, run Prettier on stage.ts, write the docs and exit interview, start verify, then monitor. Documentation can be written in parallel with Prettier after the edits are done. The exit interview does not depend on HTML output because it does not change about-data. A quick TypeScript or Node syntax check may follow.\n\nGroup class begin resets preferences without touching them. The stage file will be checked for line length after editing. browse.py will remain evidence-only and skip writing missing shots to keep the run short. The dev slider test clicks More to reach page one, then Dev; the data-id=more selector is unique after pause. The slider query [data-ui=slider-range] targets the gain control in dev. Reset uses data-id=reset.\n\nThe reset test is verified: gain returns to 14 after reset, and the engine nulls the setting when it matches the default. A paint overwrite issue was spotted where noteDevice sets text immediately, but the same frame's paint routine may overwrite it with a prompt line or menu text.\n\nThe noteDevice paint overwrite concern is resolved. Key and mouse handlers set the note text synchronously before paint runs, so tests evaluate it immediately. Pad input sets the note during drive() and paint() updates it later in the same frame, which is consistent with the 200ms wait. Hover focus is published when the menu updates.\n\nHover focus requires a 200ms frame delay because the menu index updates synchronously while __game.focus only refreshes in frame(). Pad navigation will precede hover to ensure focus starts at Begin. The first pad press is counted as one movement since its 90ms repeat interval stays below the 350ms threshold.\n\nA potential bug was spotted in the tap() helper. It holds a button for 90 milliseconds between presses, but if the game drops to 10fps during WebGPU or SwiftShader, that interval may be shorter than one frame and the press could be missed entirely. Extending the hold to 400ms would risk triggering the 350ms repeat threshold and cause two moves per tap instead of one.\n\nA better tap strategy is to hold the button until the game confirms the press, then release it. The helper will poll `__game.focus` or a predicate JavaScript function to detect when the game observes the input. After releasing, it waits 150 milliseconds before the next press. This avoids relying on fixed hold times that could be shorter than one frame.\n\nThe tap helper will press a button and poll until focus changes. It releases the button, waits 200 milliseconds or one frame to ensure the release registers, then repeats. This prevents the engine from treating the next press as a held edge if the frame is slow.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fe8bcbfa-d34b-4adb-a34a-654cd38d34e3-67","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/ui/widgets.ts","offset":210,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":425,"output_tokens":2863,"cache_read_input_tokens":110336,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"aad4bf76-e701-4297-bc61-96a295022869"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fe8bcbfa-d34b-4adb-a34a-654cd38d34e3-67","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"210→  const body = uiElement(el, 'ui-box-body');\\n  el.append(body);\\n  parent.append(el);\\n  const set = (text: string) => setText(body, text);\\n  set(options.text ?? '');\\n  return { el, body, set, remove: () => el.remove() };\\n}\\n\\n/** How long a held direction waits before it repeats, then between repeats (s). */\\nexport const REPEAT = Object.freeze({ delay: 0.35, every: 0.1 });\\n220→\\n/** A held direction's repeat: `(input, action, dt)` is true on the press and on each repeat while held. */\\nexport function createRepeat(): (input: UiInput, action: string, dt: number) => boolean {\\n  const held = new Map<string, number>();\\n  const count = (t: number) => (t < REPEAT.delay ? 0 : 1 + Math.floor((t - REPEAT.delay) / REPEAT.every + 1e-9));\\n  return (input, action, dt) => {\\n    if (input.pressed(action)) return (held.set(action, 0), true);\\n    if (!input.held(action)) return (held.delete(action), false);\\n    const before = held.get(action) ?? 0;\\n    held.set(action, before + dt);\\n230→    return count(before + dt) > count(before);\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** A gamepad's cursor over a page (see the file comment). */\\nexport interface PadCursor {\\n  readonly el: HTMLElement;\\n  /** Where it is (CSS px from the root's top left), or null while it does not show. */\\n  readonly at: readonly [number, number] | null;\\n  /** Moves it for a frame of `dt` s while `open` (a panel is open); returns what its accept clicked, or null. */\\n240→  update(dt: number, open: boolean): Element | null;\\n  remove(): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** The pad's cursor over `root` (see the file comment), from `input`. */\\nexport function createPadCursor(root: HTMLElement, input: UiInput): PadCursor {\\n  widgetStyle(root.ownerDocument);\\n  const el = uiElement(root, 'ui-cursor ui-at', 'cursor');\\n  el.hidden = true;\\n  root.append(el);\",\"content_concise\":\"210→  const body = uiElement(el, 'ui-box-body');\\n  el.append(body);\\n  parent.append(el);\\n  const set = (text: string) => setText(body, text);\\n  set(options.text ?? '');\\n  return { el, body, set, remove: () => el.remove() };\\n}\\n\\n/** How long a held direction waits before it repeats, then between repeats (s). */\\nexport const REPEAT = Object.freeze({ delay: 0.35, every: 0.1 });\\n220→\\n/** A held direction's repeat: `(input, action, dt)` is true on the press and on each repeat while held. */\\nexport function createRepeat(): (input: UiInput, action: string, dt: number) => boolean {\\n  const held = new Map<string, number>();\\n  const count = (t: number) => (t < REPEAT.delay ? 0 : 1 + Math.floor((t - REPEAT.delay) / REPEAT.every + 1e-9));\\n  return (input, action, dt) => {\\n    if (input.pressed(action)) return (held.set(action, 0), true);\\n    if (!input.held(action)) return (held.delete(action), false);\\n    const before = held.get(action) ?? 0;\\n    held.set(action, before + dt);\\n230→    return count(before + dt) > count(before);\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** A gamepad's cursor over a page (see the file comment). */\\nexport interface PadCursor {\\n  readonly el: HTMLElement;\\n  /** Where it is (CSS px from the root's top left), or null while it does not show. */\\n  readonly at: readonly [number, number] | null;\\n  /** Moves it for a frame of `dt` s while `open` (a panel is open); returns what its accept clicked, or null. */\\n240→  update(dt: number, open: boolean): Element | null;\\n  remove(): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** The pad's cursor over `root` (see the file comment), from `input`. */\\nexport function createPadCursor(root: HTMLElement, input: UiInput): PadCursor {\\n  widgetStyle(root.ownerDocument);\\n  const el = uiElement(root, 'ui-cursor ui-at', 'cursor');\\n  el.hidden = true;\\n  root.append(el);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/ui/widgets.ts\",\"offset\":210,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"  const body = uiElement(el, 'ui-box-body');\\n  el.append(body);\\n  parent.append(el);\\n  const set = (text: string) => setText(body, text);\\n  set(options.text ?? '');\\n  return { el, body, set, remove: () => el.remove() };\\n}\\n\\n/** How long a held direction waits before it repeats, then between repeats (s). */\\nexport const REPEAT = Object.freeze({ delay: 0.35, every: 0.1 });\\n\\n/** A held direction's repeat: `(input, action, dt)` is true on the press and on each repeat while held. */\\nexport function createRepeat(): (input: UiInput, action: string, dt: number) => boolean {\\n  const held = new Map<string, number>();\\n  const count = (t: number) => (t < REPEAT.delay ? 0 : 1 + Math.floor((t - REPEAT.delay) / REPEAT.every + 1e-9));\\n  return (input, action, dt) => {\\n    if (input.pressed(action)) return (held.set(action, 0), true);\\n    if (!input.held(action)) return (held.delete(action), false);\\n    const before = held.get(action) ?? 0;\\n    held.set(action, before + dt);\\n    return count(before + dt) > count(before);\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** A gamepad's cursor over a page (see the file comment). */\\nexport interface PadCursor {\\n  readonly el: HTMLElement;\\n  /** Where it is (CSS px from the root's top left), or null while it does not show. */\\n  readonly at: readonly [number, number] | null;\\n  /** Moves it for a frame of `dt` s while `open` (a panel is open); returns what its accept clicked, or null. */\\n  update(dt: number, open: boolean): Element | null;\\n  remove(): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** The pad's cursor over `root` (see the file comment), from `input`. */\\nexport function createPadCursor(root: HTMLElement, input: UiInput): PadCursor {\\n  widgetStyle(root.ownerDocument);\\n  const el = uiElement(root, 'ui-cursor ui-at', 'cursor');\\n  el.hidden = true;\\n  root.append(el);\\n\",\"total_lines\":276}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"35655eb1-1ffe-46f8-b364-3a10df01271f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_585","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`input.pressed(action)` returns true on the edge. The function returns immediately and resets held time to zero.\n\nRepeats trigger on subsequent frames while held, once accumulated dt crosses 0.35s. The press frame itself fires once and resets held time to zero. A release before the next frame prevents repeats. The planned sequence is: press, wait for focus change, release immediately, wait two rAF, then press again.\n\nIf focus does not change, the test will time out and fail. For accept, which does not shift focus, the code will wait for a screen or label change instead. A `down_up` helper is being drafted to press a button and block until a specified condition becomes true.\n\nThe `down_up` helper now releases the button and waits for two animation frames before returning. A concrete `pad_down` function is being drafted: it records the current focus, presses button 13, waits for focus to change, then releases the button.\n\n`pad_down` now returns the new focus after waiting for two animation frames. A `pad_accept` helper is being drafted to press button 0 and block until a specified condition becomes true.\n\n`pad_accept` will wait for two animation frames after releasing the button. It will block until the screen becomes `'settings'` or the glyph set switches to `'xbox'`. From Music, three downs land on Icons, so the test will assert that focus contains `\"Icons\"` before accepting. To exit the attract pad, it will press button 0 while the menu is closed and wait for `attract` to become false.\n\nThe attract exit sequence is confirmed safe. `finishExit` opens the title menu at the end of the frame after `menu.update`, so the accept press is consumed as a menu close and does not reopen Begin. The button is released immediately once `attract` becomes false, preventing any repeat on the next frame.\n\nThe robust pad helper will replace fixed 90ms delays. It will also handle attract exit. I will update stage.ts with surgical replacements, then write the shell function changes and documentation. I still need to verify that `wait_for_function` accepts a string referencing a captured variable.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Attract was able to write the save on the frame it exited, and the pad script could miss a slow frame. I am fixing both before the full verifier run."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9edf6aa8-bf83-4c09-8d94-8b177739a655-68","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/stage.ts","old_string":"  let attract = false;\n  let armed = !touch;","new_string":"  let attract = false;\n  let exitPending = false;\n  let armed = !touch;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9edf6aa8-bf83-4c09-8d94-8b177739a655-69","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/stage.ts","old_string":"  const exitAttract = () => {\n    if (!attract) return;\n    attract = false;\n    lastInput = performance.now();\n    inspector()?.set('game.auto', 'off');\n    const seed = inspector()?.seed() ?? 1;\n    inspector()?.seed(seed);\n    if (armed) menus.showTitle();\n    else screen = 'touch';\n  };\n  const startAttract = () => {\n    attract = true;\n    inspector()?.set('game.auto', 'attract');\n    const seed = inspector()?.seed() ?? 1;\n    inspector()?.seed(seed);\n    if (screen === 'title' || screen === 'touch') close();\n    if (screen !== 'settings' && screen !== 'about' && screen !== 'controls' && screen !== 'programme')\n      screen = 'attract';\n    publish();\n  };","new_string":"  const exitAttract = () => {\n    if (!attract) return;\n    exitPending = true;\n    lastInput = performance.now();\n  };\n  /** Leaves the demo after this frame has decided not to store it. */\n  const finishExit = () => {\n    if (!exitPending) return;\n    exitPending = false;\n    attract = false;\n    lastInput = performance.now();\n    inspector()?.set('game.auto', 'off');\n    const seed = inspector()?.seed() ?? 1;\n    inspector()?.seed(seed);\n    if (armed) menus.showTitle();\n    else screen = 'touch';\n  };\n  const startAttract = () => {\n    attract = true;\n    inspector()?.set('game.auto', 'attract');\n    const seed = inspector()?.seed() ?? 1;\n    inspector()?.seed(seed);\n    if (screen === 'title') close();\n    if (screen === 'title') screen = 'attract';\n    publish();\n  };"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9edf6aa8-bf83-4c09-8d94-8b177739a655-70","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/stage.ts","old_string":"      if (attract && screen !== 'settings' && screen !== 'about' && screen !== 'controls' && screen !== 'programme')\n        screen = 'attract';","new_string":"      if (\n        attract &&\n        screen !== 'settings' &&\n        screen !== 'about' &&\n        screen !== 'controls' &&\n        screen !== 'programme' &&\n        screen !== 'touch'\n      )\n        screen = 'attract';"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9edf6aa8-bf83-4c09-8d94-8b177739a655-71","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/stage.ts","old_string":"      setLook(snap);\n      remember(snap);\n      paint(snap, drawn);","new_string":"      setLook(snap);\n      remember(snap);\n      finishExit();\n      paint(snap, drawn);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9edf6aa8-bf83-4c09-8d94-8b177739a655-72","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.bu