(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\nlabs/game/ui/stage.ts 297ms (unchanged)\\n576 labs/game/ui/stage.ts\\nPYOK\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"cd \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656\\\" && wc -l labs/game/ui/stage.ts && npx prettier --write labs/game/ui/stage.ts && wc -l labs/game/ui/stage.ts && python3 -m py_compile labs/game/tools/browse.py && echo PYOK\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Format stage.ts and syntax-check browse.py\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc%2Fwork/01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc/terminal/call-56792587-9175-4d7e-80dd-b877ad67cf86-89.log\",\"total_bytes\":427}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"55cd7e32-c6bf-46d6-b78c-3d5d03732267"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_592","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The file is 576 lines, under the 600-line limit. Prettier formatting is unchanged.\n\nPython compiles. I'll run eslint on stage.ts in parallel with writing the remaining files. The exit interview, PROGRESS.md, ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md, and README are next.\n\nThe exit interview will be generated via Node to guarantee exact alignment with the EXIT file. I am also checking whether the GOAL plan needs a Deviations section, per the system reminder.\n\nThe goal plan contains no Deviations section. I am checking STAGE.md and PLAN.md to see if deviations should be recorded elsewhere.\n\nI will add a ## Deviations section to the goal plan with one bullet. PLAN.md and TASK.md are off-limits, but the goal plan is fair game.\n\nThe exit interview will be generated by running Node in the dev folder to import EXIT from about-data.ts and write it to a JSON file. jq will verify the parse.\n\nENGINE-FEEDBACK.md will request that pages can add meshes or prop parts without registered geometry.\n\nThe feedback document now lists five concrete issues. The guest was built from the engine humanoid, so simple generated meshes could not be dropped in; the team stayed with engine puppets and props instead. The music bus defaults to 0.5, but the brief requires a fresh save at 0.1, so audio.volume('music', 0.1) must run before reading the save. playClip throws during scene setup, so clips are played at spawn time instead. spawnProp without yaw produces a NaN quaternion because yaw should default to zero; passing yaw explicitly fixes this.\n\nThe feedback document now lists eleven issues. The headless session.world is frozen, so the live world from createAppHost must be re-read after every inspector seed. Hub query keys are read as settings and can kill boot; aihub* keys are stripped from the URLSearchParams passed to createEngine. input.prompt defaults to Xbox glyphs even when the page uses PlayStation glyphs, so the team keeps their own glyph set. The touch stick appears unless touch=off is set. geometry:cylinder is missing, so a frustum was used instead. Prop parts use position rather than at. node x new prints labs/playground documentation noise.\n\nThe feedback document now lists fourteen issues. A pasted hub protocol file exceeded the 600-line hard cap, so its @file comment was shortened. gfx.resolution auto without a look resolution defaults to pixels rather than the view, so the team set gfx.resolution=full. There is no inspector.reset, so they described the setting and set a default. Import paths are inconsistent: scenes use ../../../engine/sim-api while events use one folder deeper, with no alias. createMenu does not enforce six rows, so the page slices its own menu.\n\nThe plan's pinned hash (529eac78...) does not match the fetched client 1.4.0 bytes (6ab6be43...). The banner still claims version 1.4.0. No engine files were patched. The README will be rewritten from scratch.\n\nThe fetched hub protocol file is confirmed to be the winning version. The plan's ordered cuts are: Great Tilt counterweights, expert variants and outfits, Hoop Patrol, Reps Hall, Island Jog's race (the walk stays), Cliff Plunge, and Step Class. Group Class uses only Heron as its middle class; its group score is the 0–1000 mean of the three classes, so a rank still fits. The plan also described a sum to 3000.\n\nThe island terrain is a 60 by 60 grid with cell size 4, so SwiftShader can boot it.\n\nTesting caught six issues. Four were critical: score bands, island boot, ghost seat, and event import depth. The other two were NaN prop yaw and over-long lines. Bot bands on ten seeds were the most helpful test. A headless screenshot was the least helpful.\n\nThe replay golden file is 60 steps of game:bench, seed 1, linux-x64. Capture, restore, and hash replay are in the node test.\n\nPROGRESS.md will be written now and updated after the test suite runs. The retreat suite passed sixteen tests earlier.\n\nThe feedback requests are open issues, not tree defects. The group.ts score comment is already present. Prettier formatting on stage.ts was unchanged, so edits matched the formatter. A potential exit bug was reviewed: finishExit runs every frame and showTitle reads the store, but the test waits 300 ms after exit so reseeding and title display should work.\n\nThe attract-mode save logic is sound. While the attract sequence runs, remember exits early because the attract flag is set, so the in-memory save stays unchanged and no attract snapshot is written. The test captures the state before the player presses Begin, which then replaces the save with a fresh game write. The code appears solid.\n\nThe pad_down race is safe. The wait function string uses json.dumps, so the focus comparison works correctly. Opening settings during a held button press is synchronous: open() calls publish(), updating __game.screen in the same frame before the final publish.\n\nI will write the documentation files and run eslint quietly. The verify script will be backgrounded and monitored because it is a long-running job. I also need to update the todos. I confirmed that spawnSync for vitest has no timeout, which is acceptable. Before starting the long run, I will check that Chrome exists, unset DISPLAY for the Python browser, and set PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE.\n\nThe verify script will export PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 directly, since non-interactive shells may not load ~/.bashrc. CHROMIUM_PATH is passed as executable_path in browse.py, so the platform override likely does not affect that browser.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2b8bcf87-d82a-4d39-98a9-4f5d888e0376-90","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/PROGRESS.md","content":"# Thumb Yoga\n\nThe on-screen title is Thumb Yoga. It was picked from the 50 names in `titles.json` in the dev folder. The RNG bytes were `b0306a24`, the uint32 was 2955962916, and the index was 16. The title has no characters a folder name cannot hold, so nothing was sanitized. The dev folder and the HTML share that basename with the source token left as `Wii Fit`.\n\nThe fetched session client still banners 1.4.0. Its SHA-256 is `6ab6be43898e2db069bc21a94757d77d9c3f2a0cb76f01186490d3bd88d8717a`. The plan pinned `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a`. The fetched bytes won, and those exact bytes are pasted into the HTML.\n\nCuts, in the plan's order: Great Tilt's counterweights, expert variants and outfits, Hoop Patrol, Reps Hall, Island Jog's race (the walk stays), Cliff Plunge, and Step Class. Group Class's middle class is Heron only. The group score is the 0–1000 mean of the three classes, so a rank still fits. The plan also described a sum to 3000. The island terrain is a 60 by 60 grid with cell size 4, which is 240 m, so SwiftShader can boot it.\n\nTesting caught six issues before hand-in. Four were critical: the score bands, the island boot, the ghost seat, and event imports one folder too high. The other two were a NaN prop yaw and lines that ran past two sentences. The four bot bands on ten seeds were the most helpful test. A headless screenshot was the least helpful, because the canvas can be blank while the sim is fine.\n\nThe shipped golden is `labs/game/replays/still.replay.json`: 60 steps of `game:bench`, seed 1, platform `linux-x64`. A node test captures, perturbs, restores, and checks the golden hashes. The engine files were not changed.\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2b8bcf87-d82a-4d39-98a9-4f5d888e0376-91","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md","content":"# Engine feedback: thumb-yoga\n\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at e7a1243) and did not get. The owner collects this file\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\n\n## Requests\n\n- Let a page add a mesh. The retreat needed a readable guest and a few simple solids. There is no public way to register a generated mesh, so the body stays on the engine humanoid and the props stay on the built-in parts. A `geometry:cylinder` is also missing. A frustum stood in for a post.\n- Start the music bus at 0.1, or let `createAudio` take a default. The bus comes up at 0.5. This game has to call `audio.volume('music', 0.1)` before a save can raise it, because a fresh stay must be a tenth.\n- `playClip` during `setup` throws. A rest pose queued from setup never starts. Clips are played at spawn instead. Setup should accept the same call, or the error should say to wait for spawn.\n- `spawnProp` with no yaw builds a NaN quaternion and the sim blows up. Yaw should default to 0. Every prop in this game passes one.\n- A prop part's offset field is `position`. Code that says `at`, which the rest of the engine uses, is ignored and the part sits on the origin. One name would do.\n- `headlessHost(engine).session.world` is a frozen recording. The live world is `createAppHost(...).session.world`, and `inspector.seed()` replaces that session, so a cached world goes stale. The frozen view should be named as a recording, and `seed` should say that old handles die.\n- Query keys the engine does not know fail the boot. An AI Hub page arrives with `?aihub=1` and friends. Those keys have to be stripped from the string passed to `createEngine` or the page never starts. Unknown keys could be ignored.\n- `input.prompt` is Xbox. A game whose default glyphs are PlayStation cannot use it. The prompt should follow the pad the browser reported, or the page should be able to set the family.\n- The touch stick is drawn unless the page sets `touch=off`. A 10-foot game that must refuse touch play has to know that secret. A `createEngine` flag would be the obvious place.\n- `gfx.resolution=auto`, when the look names no resolution, becomes `pixels` and caps the buffer around 330 lines. A check that the drawing buffer matches the view then fails on a correct page. `full` has to be set by hand.\n- There is no `inspector.reset`. Live sliders put the defaults back by reading `describe('setting', path)` and calling `set`. A reset that restores every `game.*` default would match the dev-mode job.\n- `node x new` prints `NEW_DOCS` lines about `labs/playground/…` even when the entry is written and its test passes. The docs check is tripping over its own guide. Those lines should not look like a failed command.\n\n## Friction\n\n- From `labs/game/scenes/*.ts` the sim API is `../../../engine/sim-api`. From `labs/game/scenes/events/*.ts` it is `../../../../engine/sim-api`. There is no alias. The first import, one folder short, typechecks as a missing module and the event never loads.\n- `createMenu` will show more than six rows. A 10-foot page has to slice the list itself.\n- The hard line cap is 600. The fetched hub round, plus the `@file` comment this repo requires, was 603 lines and `eslint` failed `hard-cap/max-lines`. The protocol file should be allowed to stay the file the hub shipped. The comment was shortened so the cap would pass. Behaviour was not changed.\n- The plan pinned session-client SHA-256 `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a`. The file fetched from the raw URL banners 1.4.0 and hashes to `6ab6be43898e2db069bc21a94757d77d9c3f2a0cb76f01186490d3bd88d8717a`. The banner did not move when the bytes did.\n\n## Local engine patches\n\nNone. No file under `engine/` was edited. `npm run check` should still match `engine-lock.json`.\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2b8bcf87-d82a-4d39-98a9-4f5d888e0376-92","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/README.md","content":"# Thumb Yoga\n\nA five-day balance retreat at Little Fulcrum, for one player or a couch of four. The only verb is where your weight sits inside a unit disc. Lean with the left stick, WASD, or a pointer-locked mouse. L2 and R2, or Q and E, are the feet. Both feet, or Space, breathe. Toppling recentres you. It is not a game over. Nothing here scores weight, size, or calories.\n\nThe days are a morning check, pose class, a pond, a sand garden, a paddle, a slackline, a group class, and a storm that tilts the island. Pebbles stack on a cairn. They are never spent. After the credits the ferry does not come back. Free play and a new morning remain.\n\n## See it\n\nFrom this workspace:\n\n```sh\nnpm run dev\nnode labs/game/tools/verify.mjs\nnpm test\nnpm run check\n```\n\n`verify.mjs` runs the balance bands, the three-seed walk to the credits, the song and syllable renders, and the golden replay. Without `--quick` it also builds `../Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656.html` and drives that file. The HTML opens from `file://` and fetches nothing.\n\nA hub session is the same file, served beside `labs/game/hub/harness.html`. The mode is ghost. Empty mats on a local Group Class are staff unless Settings turns them off.\n\n## Calls\n\n- The title was drawn from `titles.json` (50 names). The pick is Thumb Yoga, index 16.\n- Great Tilt's counterweights, expert variants, outfits, Hoop Patrol, Reps Hall, Island Jog's race, Cliff Plunge, and Step Class are cut. The walk around the island stays. The day list is the five days in `scenes/data/days.ts`.\n- Group Class is a still hold, Heron, and the pond. Its score is the mean of those three, from 0 to 1000, so the same ranks apply. The plan also described a sum to 3000. The mean is the one that fits a rank.\n- The island grid is 60 by 60 with cell size 4 (240 m). A finer cell made the SwiftShader boot too slow for a hub `ready()`.\n- The session client is pasted unmodified. Its hash does not match the older pin. The fetched bytes are the ones in the page. See `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`.\n- Music on a fresh save is a tenth. The engine's bus default is a half, so the page sets the volume before the save is applied.\n- The engine tree was not modified.\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2b8bcf87-d82a-4d39-98a9-4f5d888e0376-93","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/docs/PROGRESS.md","content":"# Progress\n\nThe engine in this workspace is unchanged. Thumb Yoga, the balance retreat, lives in labs/game.\n\nThe page, the five-day director, and the pavilion ghost round are the game's own code. ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md lists what the engine did not provide. Nothing under engine/ is patched.\n\nNext is to leave the engine as it is. The open items are requests in that feedback file, not defects in this tree.\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2b8bcf87-d82a-4d39-98a9-4f5d888e0376-94","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656\" && npx eslint --quiet labs/game/ui/stage.ts && node --experimental-strip-types --input-type=module -e '\nimport { writeFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { EXIT } from \"./labs/game/ui/about-data.ts\";\nconst file = new URL(\"../exit-interview.json\", import.meta.url);\nwriteFileSync(file, JSON.stringify(EXIT, null, 2) + \"\\n\");\n' && python3 -c 'import json; p=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/exit-interview.json\"; d=json.load(open(p)); assert d[\"sourceInformation\"][\"usage\"]==\"added on import\"; assert d[\"aiHub\"][\"genre\"]==\"Sports\" and d[\"aiHub\"][\"players\"]==\"1–4\"; assert len(d[\"testingFeedback\"])==4 and len(d[\"engineFeedback\"])==6 and len(d[\"promptFeedback\"])==4; print(\"exit ok\", d[\"aiHub\"][\"name\"])' && test -x \"$HOME/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-1243/chrome-headless-shell-linux64/chrome-headless-shell\" && echo CHROME_OK && wc -l docs/PROGRESS.md","description":"Lint stage, write exit interview, check Chrome"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":414,"output_tokens":5206,"cache_read_input_tokens":128000,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"3ebd2ccd-c6a8-4811-bd08-b9f58a984ca3"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2b8bcf87-d82a-4d39-98a9-4f5d888e0376-90","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"# Thumb Yoga\\n\\nThe on-screen title is Thumb Yoga. It was picked from the 50 names in `titles.json` in the dev folder. The RNG bytes were `b0306a24`, the uint32 was 2955962916, and the index was 16. The title has no characters a folder name cannot hold, so nothing was sanitized. The dev folder and the HTML share that basename with the source token left as `Wii Fit`.\\n\\nThe fetched session client still banners 1.4.0. Its SHA-256 is `6ab6be43898e2db069bc21a94757d77d9c3f2a0cb76f01186490d3bd88d8717a`. The plan pinned `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a`. The fetched bytes won, and those exact bytes are pasted into the HTML.\\n\\nCuts, in the plan's order: Great Tilt's counterweights, expert variants and outfits, Hoop Patrol, Reps Hall, Island Jog's race (the walk stays), Cliff Plunge, and Step Class. Group Class's middle class is Heron only. The group score is the 0–1000 mean of the three classes, so a rank still fits. The plan also described a sum to 3000. The island terrain is a 60 by 60 grid with cell size 4, which is 240 m, so SwiftShader can boot it.\\n\\nTesting caught six issues before hand-in. Four were critical: the score bands, the island boot, the ghost seat, and event imports one folder too high. The other two were a NaN prop yaw and lines that ran past two sentences. The four bot bands on ten seeds were the most helpful test. A headless screenshot was the least helpful, because the canvas can be blank while the sim is fine.\\n\\nThe shipped golden is `labs/game/replays/still.replay.json`: 60 steps of `game:bench`, seed 1, platform `linux-x64`. A node test captures, perturbs, restores, and checks the golden hashes. The engine files were not changed.\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/PROGRESS.md has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/PROGRESS.md has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"# Thumb Yoga\\n\\nThe on-screen title is Thumb Yoga. It was picked from the 50 names in `titles.json` in the dev folder. The RNG bytes were `b0306a24`, the uint32 was 2955962916, and the index was 16. The title has no characters a folder name cannot hold, so nothing was sanitized. The dev folder and the HTML share that basename with the source token left as `Wii Fit`.\\n\\nThe fetched session client still banners 1.4.0. Its SHA-256 is `6ab6be43898e2db069bc21a94757d77d9c3f2a0cb76f01186490d3bd88d8717a`. The plan pinned `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a`. The fetched bytes won, and those exact bytes are pasted into the HTML.\\n\\nCuts, in the plan's order: Great Tilt's counterweights, expert variants and outfits, Hoop Patrol, Reps Hall, Island Jog's race (the walk stays), Cliff Plunge, and Step Class. Group Class's middle class is Heron only. The group score is the 0–1000 mean of the three classes, so a rank still fits. The plan also described a sum to 3000. The island terrain is a 60 by 60 grid with cell size 4, which is 240 m, so SwiftShader can boot it.\\n\\nTesting caught six issues before hand-in. Four were critical: the score bands, the island boot, the ghost seat, and event imports one folder too high. The other two were a NaN prop yaw and lines that ran past two sentences. The four bot bands on ten seeds were the most helpful test. A headless screenshot was the least helpful, because the canvas can be blank while the sim is fine.\\n\\nThe shipped golden is `labs/game/replays/still.replay.json`: 60 steps of `game:bench`, seed 1, platform `linux-x64`. A node test captures, perturbs, restores, and checks the golden hashes. The engine files were not changed.\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2b8bcf87-d82a-4d39-98a9-4f5d888e0376-91","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"# Engine feedback: thumb-yoga\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at e7a1243) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n<!-- What the engine should add or fix, most costly first. -->\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n<!-- Docs, errors, templates or APIs that slowed you down or misled you, most costly first. -->\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\n<!--\\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\\n-->\\n\",\"new_string\":\"# Engine feedback: thumb-yoga\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at e7a1243) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n- Let a page add a mesh. The retreat needed a readable guest and a few simple solids. There is no public way to register a generated mesh, so the body stays on the engine humanoid and the props stay on the built-in parts. A `geometry:cylinder` is also missing. A frustum stood in for a post.\\n- Start the music bus at 0.1, or let `createAudio` take a default. The bus comes up at 0.5. This game has to call `audio.volume('music', 0.1)` before a save can raise it, because a fresh stay must be a tenth.\\n- `playClip` during `setup` throws. A rest pose queued from setup never starts. Clips are played at spawn instead. Setup should accept the same call, or the error should say to wait for spawn.\\n- `spawnProp` with no yaw builds a NaN quaternion and the sim blows up. Yaw should default to 0. Every prop in this game passes one.\\n- A prop part's offset field is `position`. Code that says `at`, which the rest of the engine uses, is ignored and the part sits on the origin. One name would do.\\n- `headlessHost(engine).session.world` is a frozen recording. The live world is `createAppHost(...).session.world`, and `inspector.seed()` replaces that session, so a cached world goes stale. The frozen view should be named as a recording, and `seed` should say that old handles die.\\n- Query keys the engine does not know fail the boot. An AI Hub page arrives with `?aihub=1` and friends. Those keys have to be stripped from the string passed to `createEngine` or the page never starts. Unknown keys could be ignored.\\n- `input.prompt` is Xbox. A game whose default glyphs are PlayStation cannot use it. The prompt should follow the pad the browser reported, or the page should be able to set the family.\\n- The touch stick is drawn unless the page sets `touch=off`. A 10-foot game that must refuse touch play has to know that secret. A `createEngine` flag would be the obvious place.\\n- `gfx.resolution=auto`, when the look names no resolution, becomes `pixels` and caps the buffer around 330 lines. A check that the drawing buffer matches the view then fails on a correct page. `full` has to be set by hand.\\n- There is no `inspector.reset`. Live sliders put the defaults back by reading `describe('setting', path)` and calling `set`. A reset that restores every `game.*` default would match the dev-mode job.\\n- `node x new` prints `NEW_DOCS` lines about `labs/playground/…` even when the entry is written and its test passes. The docs check is tripping over its own guide. Those lines should not look like a failed command.\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n- From `labs/game/scenes/*.ts` the sim API is `../../../engine/sim-api`. From `labs/game/scenes/events/*.ts` it is `../../../../engine/sim-api`. There is no alias. The first import, one folder short, typechecks as a missing module and the event never loads.\\n- `createMenu` will show more than six rows. A 10-foot page has to slice the list itself.\\n- The hard line cap is 600. The fetched hub round, plus the `@file` comment this repo requires, was 603 lines and `eslint` failed `hard-cap/max-lines`. The protocol file should be allowed to stay the file the hub shipped. The comment was shortened so the cap would pass. Behaviour was not changed.\\n- The plan pinned session-client SHA-256 `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a`. The file fetched from the raw URL banners 1.4.0 and hashes to `6ab6be43898e2db069bc21a94757d77d9c3f2a0cb76f01186490d3bd88d8717a`. The banner did not move when the bytes did.\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\nNone. No file under `engine/` was edited. `npm run check` should still match `engine-lock.json`.\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"Wrote file successfully to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"Wrote file successfully to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"# Engine feedback: thumb-yoga\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at e7a1243) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n<!-- What the engine should add or fix, most costly first. -->\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n<!-- Docs, errors, templates or APIs that slowed you down or misled you, most costly first. -->\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\n<!--\\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\\n-->\\n\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"# Engine feedback: thumb-yoga\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at e7a1243) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n- Let a page add a mesh. The retreat needed a readable guest and a few simple solids. There is no public way to register a generated mesh, so the body stays on the engine humanoid and the props stay on the built-in parts. A `geometry:cylinder` is also missing. A frustum stood in for a post.\\n- Start the music bus at 0.1, or let `createAudio` take a default. The bus comes up at 0.5. This game has to call `audio.volume('music', 0.1)` before a save can raise it, because a fresh stay must be a tenth.\\n- `playClip` during `setup` throws. A rest pose queued from setup never starts. Clips are played at spawn instead. Setup should accept the same call, or the error should say to wait for spawn.\\n- `spawnProp` with no yaw builds a NaN quaternion and the sim blows up. Yaw should default to 0. Every prop in this game passes one.\\n- A prop part's offset field is `position`. Code that says `at`, which the rest of the engine uses, is ignored and the part sits on the origin. One name would do.\\n- `headlessHost(engine).session.world` is a frozen recording. The live world is `createAppHost(...).session.world`, and `inspector.seed()` replaces that session, so a cached world goes stale. The frozen view should be named as a recording, and `seed` should say that old handles die.\\n- Query keys the engine does not know fail the boot. An AI Hub page arrives with `?aihub=1` and friends. Those keys have to be stripped from the string passed to `createEngine` or the page never starts. Unknown keys could be ignored.\\n- `input.prompt` is Xbox. A game whose default glyphs are PlayStation cannot use it. The prompt should follow the pad the browser reported, or the page should be able to set the family.\\n- The touch stick is drawn unless the page sets `touch=off`. A 10-foot game that must refuse touch play has to know that secret. A `createEngine` flag would be the obvious place.\\n- `gfx.resolution=auto`, when the look names no resolution, becomes `pixels` and caps the buffer around 330 lines. A check that the drawing buffer matches the view then fails on a correct page. `full` has to be set by hand.\\n- There is no `inspector.reset`. Live sliders put the defaults back by reading `describe('setting', path)` and calling `set`. A reset that restores every `game.*` default would match the dev-mode job.\\n- `node x new` prints `NEW_DOCS` lines about `labs/playground/…` even when the entry is written and its test passes. The docs check is tripping over its own guide. Those lines should not look like a failed command.\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n- From `labs/game/scenes/*.ts` the sim API is `../../../engine/sim-api`. From `labs/game/scenes/events/*.ts` it is `../../../../engine/sim-api`. There is no alias. The first import, one folder short, typechecks as a missing module and the event never loads.\\n- `createMenu` will show more than six rows. A 10-foot page has to slice the list itself.\\n- The hard line cap is 600. The fetched hub round, plus the `@file` comment this repo requires, was 603 lines and `eslint` failed `hard-cap/max-lines`. The protocol file should be allowed to stay the file the hub shipped. The comment was shortened so the cap would pass. Behaviour was not changed.\\n- The plan pinned session-client SHA-256 `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a`. The file fetched from the raw URL banners 1.4.0 and hashes to `6ab6be43898e2db069bc21a94757d77d9c3f2a0cb76f01186490d3bd88d8717a`. The banner did not move when the bytes did.\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\nNone. No file under `engine/` was edited. `npm run check` should still match `engine-lock.json`.\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2b8bcf87-d82a-4d39-98a9-4f5d888e0376-92","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"# The starter game\\n\\nEvery game made with my-3dge starts as this one (`node tools/game/new-game.mjs`), then becomes its own: rewrite this\\npage as the game grows. It is the game's page for the owner and the next agent: what the game is, how it plays, how to\\nsee it, and the calls made along the way.\\n\\n## The game\\n\\nRun round the arena collecting every gem before the clock runs out. WASD or the arrows run, Space jumps (over the low\\nwalls), Shift dashes. All the gems: won. The clock at 0: lost. Enter starts a new round on the next seed.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n| File                              | What it is                                                                    |\\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n| labs/game/scenes/play.ts          | The rules, sim-side: the arena's text, the settings, the gems, the round, the systems |\\n| labs/game/cast/player.ts          | The player: its character (run, jump, dash) and the body it is drawn as        |\\n| labs/game/bot.ts                  | The bot: plays through intents, down the flow field to the nearest gem         |\\n| labs/game/main.ts, index.html     | The page: the engine, the HUD, Enter to play again, the chase camera           |\\n| labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts     | The tests: the golden replay, capture and restore, the bot wins on 10 seeds, the clock |\\n| labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json | The bot's play from seed 1, with its golden hashes                             |\\n\\n## Settings\\n\\n`game.gems` (10), `game.seconds` (30) and `game.speed` (6 m/s), read when the round starts: `?game.gems=20` in the\\npage, `--set game.gems=20` for `node x sim` and `node x shot`.\\n\\n## See it\\n\\n```sh\\nnpm run dev                                         # http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (?replay=bot plays the bot's run)\\nnpm test                                            # the tests\\nnode x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --feel          # the rules in Node: hash, events, how the player handles\\nnode x shot labs/game                               # the page on WebGPU, as numbers\\nnode x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim       # the goldens, in Node and Chromium\\n```\\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n<!-- The calls made without the owner, newest first: the date, what was decided, why. -->\\n\",\"new_string\":\"# Thumb Yoga\\n\\nA five-day balance retreat at Little Fulcrum, for one player or a couch of four. The only verb is where your weight sits inside a unit disc. Lean with the left stick, WASD, or a pointer-locked mouse. L2 and R2, or Q and E, are the feet. Both feet, or Space, breathe. Toppling recentres you. It is not a game over. Nothing here scores weight, size, or calories.\\n\\nThe days are a morning check, pose class, a pond, a sand garden, a paddle, a slackline, a group class, and a storm that tilts the island. Pebbles stack on a cairn. They are never spent. After the credits the ferry does not come back. Free play and a new morning remain.\\n\\n## See it\\n\\nFrom this workspace:\\n\\n```sh\\nnpm run dev\\nnode labs/game/tools/verify.mjs\\nnpm test\\nnpm run check\\n```\\n\\n`verify.mjs` runs the balance bands, the three-seed walk to the credits, the song and syllable renders, and the golden replay. Without `--quick` it also builds `../Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656.html` and drives that file. The HTML opens from `file://` and fetches nothing.\\n\\nA hub session is the same file, served beside `labs/game/hub/harness.html`. The mode is ghost. Empty mats on a local Group Class are staff unless Settings turns them off.\\n\\n## Calls\\n\\n- The title was drawn from `titles.json` (50 names). The pick is Thumb Yoga, index 16.\\n- Great Tilt's counterweights, expert variants, outfits, Hoop Patrol, Reps Hall, Island Jog's race, Cliff Plunge, and Step Class are cut. The walk around the island stays. The day list is the five days in `scenes/data/days.ts`.\\n- Group Class is a still hold, Heron, and the pond. Its score is the mean of those three, from 0 to 1000, so the same ranks apply. The plan also described a sum to 3000. The mean is the one that fits a rank.\\n- The island grid is 60 by 60 with cell size 4 (240 m). A finer cell made the SwiftShader boot too slow for a hub `ready()`.\\n- The session client is pasted unmodified. Its hash does not match the older pin. The fetched bytes are the ones in the page. See `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`.\\n- Music on a fresh save is a tenth. The engine's bus default is a half, so the page sets the volume before the save is applied.\\n- The engine tree was not modified.\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"Wrote file successfully to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/README.md.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"Wrote file successfully to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/README.md.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/README.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"# The starter game\\n\\nEvery game made with my-3dge starts as this one (`node tools/game/new-game.mjs`), then becomes its own: rewrite this\\npage as the game grows. It is the game's page for the owner and the next agent: what the game is, how it plays, how to\\nsee it, and the calls made along the way.\\n\\n## The game\\n\\nRun round the arena collecting every gem before the clock runs out. WASD or the arrows run, Space jumps (over the low\\nwalls), Shift dashes. All the gems: won. The clock at 0: lost. Enter starts a new round on the next seed.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n| File                              | What it is                                                                    |\\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n| labs/game/scenes/play.ts          | The rules, sim-side: the arena's text, the settings, the gems, the round, the systems |\\n| labs/game/cast/player.ts          | The player: its character (run, jump, dash) and the body it is drawn as        |\\n| labs/game/bot.ts                  | The bot: plays through intents, down the flow field to the nearest gem         |\\n| labs/game/main.ts, index.html     | The page: the engine, the HUD, Enter to play again, the chase camera           |\\n| labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts     | The tests: the golden replay, capture and restore, the bot wins on 10 seeds, the clock |\\n| labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json | The bot's play from seed 1, with its golden hashes                             |\\n\\n## Settings\\n\\n`game.gems` (10), `game.seconds` (30) and `game.speed` (6 m/s), read when the round starts: `?game.gems=20` in the\\npage, `--set game.gems=20` for `node x sim` and `node x shot`.\\n\\n## See it\\n\\n```sh\\nnpm run dev                                         # http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (?replay=bot plays the bot's run)\\nnpm test                                            # the tests\\nnode x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --feel          # the rules in Node: hash, events, how the player handles\\nnode x shot labs/game                               # the page on WebGPU, as numbers\\nnode x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim       # the goldens, in Node and Chromium\\n```\\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n<!-- The calls made without the owner, newest first: the date, what was decided, why. -->\\n\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"# Thumb Yoga\\n\\nA five-day balance retreat at Little Fulcrum, for one player or a couch of four. The only verb is where your weight sits inside a unit disc. Lean with the left stick, WASD, or a pointer-locked mouse. L2 and R2, or Q and E, are the feet. Both feet, or Space, breathe. Toppling recentres you. It is not a game over. Nothing here scores weight, size, or calories.\\n\\nThe days are a morning check, pose class, a pond, a sand garden, a paddle, a slackline, a group class, and a storm that tilts the island. Pebbles stack on a cairn. They are never spent. After the credits the ferry does not come back. Free play and a new morning remain.\\n\\n## See it\\n\\nFrom this workspace:\\n\\n```sh\\nnpm run dev\\nnode labs/game/tools/verify.mjs\\nnpm test\\nnpm run check\\n```\\n\\n`verify.mjs` runs the balance bands, the three-seed walk to the credits, the song and syllable renders, and the golden replay. Without `--quick` it also builds `../Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656.html` and drives that file. The HTML opens from `file://` and fetches nothing.\\n\\nA hub session is the same file, served beside `labs/game/hub/harness.html`. The mode is ghost. Empty mats on a local Group Class are staff unless Settings turns them off.\\n\\n## Calls\\n\\n- The title was drawn from `titles.json` (50 names). The pick is Thumb Yoga, index 16.\\n- Great Tilt's counterweights, expert variants, outfits, Hoop Patrol, Reps Hall, Island Jog's race, Cliff Plunge, and Step Class are cut. The walk around the island stays. The day list is the five days in `scenes/data/days.ts`.\\n- Group Class is a still hold, Heron, and the pond. Its score is the mean of those three, from 0 to 1000, so the same ranks apply. The plan also described a sum to 3000. The mean is the one that fits a rank.\\n- The island grid is 60 by 60 with cell size 4 (240 m). A finer cell made the SwiftShader boot too slow for a hub `ready()`.\\n- The session client is pasted unmodified. Its hash does not match the older pin. The fetched bytes are the ones in the page. See `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`.\\n- Music on a fresh save is a tenth. The engine's bus default is a half, so the page sets the volume before the save is applied.\\n- The engine tree was not modified.\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2b8bcf87-d82a-4d39-98a9-4f5d888e0376-93","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"# Progress\\n\\nThe engine in this workspace is unchanged. Thumb Yoga, the balance retreat, lives in labs/game.\\n\\nThe page, the five-day director, and the pavilion ghost round are the game's own code. ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md lists what the engine did not provide. Nothing under engine/ is patched.\\n\\nNext is to leave the engine as it is. The open items are requests in that feedback file, not defects in this tree.\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/docs/PROGRESS.md has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/docs/PROGRESS.md has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/docs/PROGRESS.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"# Progress\\n\\nThe engine in this workspace is unchanged. Thumb Yoga, the balance retreat, lives in labs/game.\\n\\nThe page, the five-day director, and the pavilion ghost round are the game's own code. ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md lists what the engine did not provide. Nothing under engine/ is patched.\\n\\nNext is to leave the engine as it is. The open items are requests in that feedback file, not defects in this tree.\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2b8bcf87-d82a-4d39-98a9-4f5d888e0376-94","content":"{\"type\":\"Bash\",\"output\":[40,110,111,100,101,58,49,51,56,54,54,54,41,32,87,97,114,110,105,110,103,58,32,84,104,101,32,39,78,79,95,67,79,76,79,82,39,32,101,110,118,32,105,115,32,105,103,110,111,114,101,100,32,100,117,101,32,116,111,32,116,104,101,32,39,70,79,82,67,69,95,67,79,76,79,82,39,32,101,110,118,32,98,101,105,110,103,32,115,101,116,46,10,40,85,115,101,32,96,110,111,100,101,32,45,45,116,114,97,99,101,45,119,97,114,110,105,110,103,115,32,46,46,46,96,32,116,111,32,115,104,111,119,32,119,104,101,114,101,32,116,104,101,32,119,97,114,110,105,110,103,32,119,97,115,32,99,114,101,97,116,101,100,41,10,40,110,111,100,101,58,49,51,56,54,57,50,41,32,87,97,114,110,105,110,103,58,32,84,104,101,32,39,78,79,95,67,79,76,79,82,39,32,101,110,118,32,105,115,32,105,103,110,111,114,101,100,32,100,117,101,32,116,111,32,116,104,101,32,39,70,79,82,67,69,95,67,79,76,79,82,39,32,101,110,118,32,98,101,105,