{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_594","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Prettier ignores markdown files by default, except for specific documentation.\n\nVerify is starting in the background. It will run vitest and browser checks. npm test is deferred to avoid memory pressure.\n\nA pid file will be written to the scratch directory so the monitor can track the verify process reliably. This avoids a race condition where the monitor might start before the process ID is available.\n\nThe monitor will locate the verify process by searching for the node process directly, rather than relying on a pid file.\n\nThe monitor script waits for the verify log to appear, then polls every 30 seconds to see if the process is still running. It remains silent until the job finishes and prints a single DONE or FAILED line. If verification takes a long time, the system will sit idle until it completes.\n\nBoth tools return immediately, so this turn can end after launching them. I will be woken when the monitor reports verify's final result.\n\nI will read the hub code during the verify run to prepare for any likely failures. The monitor can find the verify process because spawnSync blocks the node process.\n\nThe monitor will poll for the verify process once per second for ten seconds, then switch to thirty-second intervals. It will only print a final DONE or FAILED line when the job ends. If verification fails early, the last forty lines of the log will be printed so I can see the error immediately.\n\nThe monitor script would match itself in pgrep because its own command line contains the verify filename. The verify command will write its bash process ID to a pid file instead. The monitor will check that file to know when verification finishes.\n\nThe monitor will wait silently for the pid file to appear, then watch that bash process ID with kill -0. It polls every thirty seconds until the process exits.\n\nThe monitor script will grep the verify log for exactly zero failures. If verification fails, it will print FAILED, tail the last fifty lines of the log, and exit with an error.\n\nBoth tools will launch in parallel with no block timeout. The verify command must write its pid file immediately at startup to avoid a race condition.\n\nThe monitor timeout is ten hours, which is more than enough for verify to run for twenty-plus minutes.\n\nI will update the task list to show that verification is in progress. I will also read round.go and the hub client code in parallel so I am ready to fix any issues if verification fails.\n\nI will launch verify now rather than reading the hub code first. The monitor will wake me with the log if verification fails, so I can fix hub issues then. I confirmed that VERIFY_OUT is set in the environment for spawnSync.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4cff0aae-f208-4abf-8e67-81af648dd37e-97","name":"todo_write","input":{"todos":[{"id":"ac1","content":"Hand-in records: PROGRESS, exit-interview, HTML, title","status":"in_progress"},{"id":"ac3","content":"Five-day retreat already in the sim; page shell wired","status":"completed"},{"id":"ac4","content":"10-foot shell: prove pad, attract, touch, and WebGPU fallback","status":"in_progress"},{"id":"ac5","content":"Group Class and AI Hub harness runs","status":"pending"},{"id":"verify","content":"Official verify, npm test, and npm run check","status":"in_progress"}],"merge":true}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4cff0aae-f208-4abf-8e67-81af648dd37e-98","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"SCRATCH=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer\"\nDEV=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656\"\necho $$ > \"$SCRATCH/verify.pid\"\ncd \"$DEV\"\nexport PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64\nexport VERIFY_OUT=\"$SCRATCH\"\nnode labs/game/tools/verify.mjs > \"$SCRATCH/verify.log\" 2>&1\necho \"EXIT:$?\" >> \"$SCRATCH/verify.log\"","description":"Run the full Thumb Yoga verifier","block_until_ms":0}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4cff0aae-f208-4abf-8e67-81af648dd37e-99","name":"monitor","input":{"command":"SCRATCH=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer\"\nPIDFILE=\"$SCRATCH/verify.pid\"\nLOG=\"$SCRATCH/verify.log\"\nfor _ in $(seq 1 60); do [ -f \"$PIDFILE\" ] && break; sleep 1; done\nPID=$(cat \"$PIDFILE\" 2>/dev/null || true)\nif [ -z \"$PID\" ]; then echo \"FAILED: verify pid missing\"; exit 1; fi\nwhile kill -0 \"$PID\" 2>/dev/null; do sleep 30; done\nif grep -qx '0 failures' \"$LOG\"; then echo \"DONE: verify 0 failures\"; else echo \"FAILED: verify\"; tail -60 \"$LOG\"; exit 1; fi","description":"Watch verifier until it exits"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":659,"output_tokens":2473,"cache_read_input_tokens":134016,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"7ae09646-9a3e-40d3-89e4-654bb78bbf4d"}
