{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_605","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The log is empty because vitest output is buffered by spawnSync until the process completes.\n\nverify.mjs only prints at the end of all stages, so the log stays empty until completion. The retreat tests take roughly 188 seconds, and the full process needs a long timeout.\n\nI'll wait 8 minutes for the process to finish. The worst-case estimate for all remaining stages is roughly 8 minutes, so this should cover everything.\n\nThe optimistic total is about 10 minutes and the worst case about 18. I'll wait 10 minutes. I can also run other tools in parallel while waiting.\n\nI'll scan for remaining bugs while the process runs. I have roughly three to four minutes before onefile builds, so any fixes would be picked up in time.\n\nI'll hold off on the long wait and do a quick review of risky page code first. I need to verify that the engine applies gfx.resolution=full correctly, since Playwright's viewport may not match the canvas size. I also want to check whether 16px overlay text is visible in the engine.\n\nOverlay visibility checks out: width and height are zero, so it is hidden. The about page text and menu row count match the requirements. Hover after escape dispatches a pointermove with movementX 4, but the stage's capture listener on window may also fire.\n\nMenu hover returns early without changing the device. Focus updates correctly and the frame publishes it after a 200ms wait. The engine polls gamepads every frame via navigator.getGamepads, so the pad navigation stub is safe. Playwright init scripts run before page scripts, preventing any startup caching issue with the getGamepads override.\n\nButton 13 is confirmed as D-pad down. The title menu skip logic correctly bypasses two disabled rows. WebKit devices without WebGPU are handled safely by the inline script and gameFailed guard. Playwright device emulation should provide the correct touch and coarse-pointer media queries.\n\nThe touch button visibility depends on the `touch` flag computed at boot from matchMedia. If the device descriptor omits `hover: none`, the button stays hidden and the controller note never appears.\n\nPlaywright's mobile device context likely sets `has_touch` and `is_mobile`, so the coarse-pointer media query should match. On touch devices, the attract flag becomes true while the screen stays on touch, keeping the controller note visible until settings are tapped.\n\nThe test taps settings while the controller note is still visible. The 11-second wait starts attract mode without switching screens, so the flag becomes true and the test passes. On desktop, the Escape key resets lastInput, but hover does not because the menu remains open.\n\nThe 10.5-second wait should trigger attract mode, switching the screen to attract and closing the menu. A 500ms margin is included for slow frames, though a stall could still cause a flake. The dev slider also works: pressing Enter to begin and Escape to pause.\n\nThe dev slider test clicks More, opens the dev menu, sets wobble.gain to 20, then resets. The pause menu item should be clickable. After attract mode exits via pad, the title screen is reached and Enter starts Begin. I am now checking resolution.ts to confirm that full resolution matches the inner canvas size including devicePixelRatio.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-aa02c912-d651-4ff3-aaa5-3e3af999c9aa-115","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/gfx/resolution.ts","offset":166,"limit":70}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-aa02c912-d651-4ff3-aaa5-3e3af999c9aa-116","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/index.html","limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":391,"output_tokens":2118,"cache_read_input_tokens":148992,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"322d74bd-6e65-414f-8d66-25806389f280"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-aa02c912-d651-4ff3-aaa5-3e3af999c9aa-115","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"166→/** Keeps `renderer`'s drawing buffer fitted to `canvas` and the `gfx.resolution` setting. */\\nexport function createResolution(options: ResolutionOptions): Resolution {\\n  const { renderer, canvas } = options;\\n  const settings = options.settings ?? createSettings();\\n170→  const pixelRatio = options.pixelRatio ?? (() => globalThis.devicePixelRatio ?? 1);\\n  let current: Fit | null = null;\\n  let key = '';\\n  let limit: PixelCap = {};\\n  let preferred: ResolutionMode | null = null;\\n  let offset: [number, number] = [0, 0];\\n  /** CSS pixels per drawn pixel. */\\n  const cssPixel = () => (current && current.width > 0 ? current.css.width / current.width : 1);\\n  const resolution: Resolution = {\\n    get current() {\\n180→      return current;\\n    },\\n    get offset() {\\n      return offset;\\n    },\\n    shift(x, y) {\\n      if (x === offset[0] && y === offset[1]) return;\\n      offset = [x, y];\\n      const k = cssPixel();\\n      canvas.style.transform = x === 0 && y === 0 ? '' : `translate(${x * k}px, ${y * k}px)`;\\n190→    },\\n    update() {\\n      const css = { width: canvas.clientWidth, height: canvas.clientHeight };\\n      const asked = settings.get<ResolutionSetting>('gfx.resolution');\\n      const mode = asked === 'auto' ? (preferred ?? 'pixels') : asked;\\n      const ratio = pixelRatio();\\n      const next = `${css.width}x${css.height}@${ratio}:${mode}<${limit.maxPixels ?? ''},${limit.maxPixelRatio ?? ''}`;\\n      if (next === key) return false;\\n      key = next;\\n      current = fitResolution(css, ratio, mode, limit);\\n200→      renderer.setPixelRatio(1);\\n      renderer.setSize(current.width, current.height, false);\\n      canvas.style.imageRendering = current.pixelated ? 'pixelated' : '';\\n      canvas.style.setProperty('--my3dge-pixel', `${cssPixel()}px`);\\n      return true;\\n    },\\n    cap(next) {\\n      limit = { maxPixels: next.maxPixels ?? null, maxPixelRatio: next.maxPixelRatio ?? null };\\n    },\\n    prefer(mode) {\\n210→      if (mode === preferred) return;\\n      preferred = mode;\\n      resolution.update();\\n    },\\n  };\\n  return resolution;\\n}\\n\\n/** The widest vertical field of view a portrait picture gets, in degrees. */\\nexport const MAX_PORTRAIT_FOV = 150;\\n220→\\n/** The vertical field of view (deg) that keeps `fov`'s width on a picture `aspect` (width / height) wide, below 1. */\\nexport function portraitFov(fov: number, aspect: number): number {\\n  if (!(aspect > 0 && aspect < 1)) return fov;\\n  return Math.min(MAX_PORTRAIT_FOV, (360 / Math.PI) * Math.atan(Math.tan((fov * Math.PI) / 360) / aspect));\\n}\\n\\n/** Widens a perspective camera placed for this frame when the picture is portrait (`portraitFov`); else no change. */\\nexport function keepWidth(camera: Camera, aspect: number): void {\\n  const lens = camera as PerspectiveCamera;\\n230→  if (!lens.isPerspectiveCamera) return;\\n  const fov = portraitFov(lens.fov, aspect);\\n  if (fov === lens.fov) return;\\n  lens.fov = fov;\\n  lens.updateProjectionMatrix();\\n}\",\"content_concise\":\"166→/** Keeps `renderer`'s drawing buffer fitted to `canvas` and the `gfx.resolution` setting. */\\nexport function createResolution(options: ResolutionOptions): Resolution {\\n  const { renderer, canvas } = options;\\n  const settings = options.settings ?? createSettings();\\n170→  const pixelRatio = options.pixelRatio ?? (() => globalThis.devicePixelRatio ?? 1);\\n  let current: Fit | null = null;\\n  let key = '';\\n  let limit: PixelCap = {};\\n  let preferred: ResolutionMode | null = null;\\n  let offset: [number, number] = [0, 0];\\n  /** CSS pixels per drawn pixel. */\\n  const cssPixel = () => (current && current.width > 0 ? current.css.width / current.width : 1);\\n  const resolution: Resolution = {\\n    get current() {\\n180→      return current;\\n    },\\n    get offset() {\\n      return offset;\\n    },\\n    shift(x, y) {\\n      if (x === offset[0] && y === offset[1]) return;\\n      offset = [x, y];\\n      const k = cssPixel();\\n      canvas.style.transform = x === 0 && y === 0 ? '' : `translate(${x * k}px, ${y * k}px)`;\\n190→    },\\n    update() {\\n      const css = { width: canvas.clientWidth, height: canvas.clientHeight };\\n      const asked = settings.get<ResolutionSetting>('gfx.resolution');\\n      const mode = asked === 'auto' ? (preferred ?? 'pixels') : asked;\\n      const ratio = pixelRatio();\\n      const next = `${css.width}x${css.height}@${ratio}:${mode}<${limit.maxPixels ?? ''},${limit.maxPixelRatio ?? ''}`;\\n      if (next === key) return false;\\n      key = next;\\n      current = fitResolution(css, ratio, mode, limit);\\n200→      renderer.setPixelRatio(1);\\n      renderer.setSize(current.width, current.height, false);\\n      canvas.style.imageRendering = current.pixelated ? 'pixelated' : '';\\n      canvas.style.setProperty('--my3dge-pixel', `${cssPixel()}px`);\\n      return true;\\n    },\\n    cap(next) {\\n      limit = { maxPixels: next.maxPixels ?? null, maxPixelRatio: next.maxPixelRatio ?? null };\\n    },\\n    prefer(mode) {\\n210→      if (mode === preferred) return;\\n      preferred = mode;\\n      resolution.update();\\n    },\\n  };\\n  return resolution;\\n}\\n\\n/** The widest vertical field of view a portrait picture gets, in degrees. */\\nexport const MAX_PORTRAIT_FOV = 150;\\n220→\\n/** The vertical field of view (deg) that keeps `fov`'s width on a picture `aspect` (width / height) wide, below 1. */\\nexport function portraitFov(fov: number, aspect: number): number {\\n  if (!(aspect > 0 && aspect < 1)) return fov;\\n  return Math.min(MAX_PORTRAIT_FOV, (360 / Math.PI) * Math.atan(Math.tan((fov * Math.PI) / 360) / aspect));\\n}\\n\\n/** Widens a perspective camera placed for this frame when the picture is portrait (`portraitFov`); else no change. */\\nexport function keepWidth(camera: Camera, aspect: number): void {\\n  const lens = camera as PerspectiveCamera;\\n230→  if (!lens.isPerspectiveCamera) return;\\n  const fov = portraitFov(lens.fov, aspect);\\n  if (fov === lens.fov) return;\\n  lens.fov = fov;\\n  lens.updateProjectionMatrix();\\n}\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/gfx/resolution.ts\",\"offset\":166,\"limit\":70,\"raw_output\":\"/** Keeps `renderer`'s drawing buffer fitted to `canvas` and the `gfx.resolution` setting. */\\nexport function createResolution(options: ResolutionOptions): Resolution {\\n  const { renderer, canvas } = options;\\n  const settings = options.settings ?? createSettings();\\n  const pixelRatio = options.pixelRatio ?? (() => globalThis.devicePixelRatio ?? 1);\\n  let current: Fit | null = null;\\n  let key = '';\\n  let limit: PixelCap = {};\\n  let preferred: ResolutionMode | null = null;\\n  let offset: [number, number] = [0, 0];\\n  /** CSS pixels per drawn pixel. */\\n  const cssPixel = () => (current && current.width > 0 ? current.css.width / current.width : 1);\\n  const resolution: Resolution = {\\n    get current() {\\n      return current;\\n    },\\n    get offset() {\\n      return offset;\\n    },\\n    shift(x, y) {\\n      if (x === offset[0] && y === offset[1]) return;\\n      offset = [x, y];\\n      const k = cssPixel();\\n      canvas.style.transform = x === 0 && y === 0 ? '' : `translate(${x * k}px, ${y * k}px)`;\\n    },\\n    update() {\\n      const css = { width: canvas.clientWidth, height: canvas.clientHeight };\\n      const asked = settings.get<ResolutionSetting>('gfx.resolution');\\n      const mode = asked === 'auto' ? (preferred ?? 'pixels') : asked;\\n      const ratio = pixelRatio();\\n      const next = `${css.width}x${css.height}@${ratio}:${mode}<${limit.maxPixels ?? ''},${limit.maxPixelRatio ?? ''}`;\\n      if (next === key) return false;\\n      key = next;\\n      current = fitResolution(css, ratio, mode, limit);\\n      renderer.setPixelRatio(1);\\n      renderer.setSize(current.width, current.height, false);\\n      canvas.style.imageRendering = current.pixelated ? 'pixelated' : '';\\n      canvas.style.setProperty('--my3dge-pixel', `${cssPixel()}px`);\\n      return true;\\n    },\\n    cap(next) {\\n      limit = { maxPixels: next.maxPixels ?? null, maxPixelRatio: next.maxPixelRatio ?? null };\\n    },\\n    prefer(mode) {\\n      if (mode === preferred) return;\\n      preferred = mode;\\n      resolution.update();\\n    },\\n  };\\n  return resolution;\\n}\\n\\n/** The widest vertical field of view a portrait picture gets, in degrees. */\\nexport const MAX_PORTRAIT_FOV = 150;\\n\\n/** The vertical field of view (deg) that keeps `fov`'s width on a picture `aspect` (width / height) wide, below 1. */\\nexport function portraitFov(fov: number, aspect: number): number {\\n  if (!(aspect > 0 && aspect < 1)) return fov;\\n  return Math.min(MAX_PORTRAIT_FOV, (360 / Math.PI) * Math.atan(Math.tan((fov * Math.PI) / 360) / aspect));\\n}\\n\\n/** Widens a perspective camera placed for this frame when the picture is portrait (`portraitFov`); else no change. */\\nexport function keepWidth(camera: Camera, aspect: number): void {\\n  const lens = camera as PerspectiveCamera;\\n  if (!lens.isPerspectiveCamera) return;\\n  const fov = portraitFov(lens.fov, aspect);\\n  if (fov === lens.fov) return;\\n  lens.fov = fov;\\n  lens.updateProjectionMatrix();\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":235}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-aa02c912-d651-4ff3-aaa5-3e3af999c9aa-116","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n  <head>\\n    <meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" />\\n    <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user