{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_647","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The game enters play mode, but a frame throws an error.\n\nThe frame crash reads `menu.selected` after the menu closes. The loop stops, but the screen is already play. This explains why the browse test times out at 10 seconds.\n\nThe frame code already guards `menu.selected` with a `menu` check. The null read must come from another unguarded access. I will search stage.ts and menus for other `.selected` references.\n\nThe browse test times out even though debug shows the screen becomes play. The loop may stop before publishing that state, so the test never sees it.\n\nThe crash is caused by `menu.update` calling `pickTitle`, which sets the screen to play and publishes it before the code later reads `menu.selected`. The null read happens after the state change, so the screen should already be 'play' when the error occurs.\n\nThe screen is already 'play' when the loop stops, so the browse timeout is puzzling. The error might crash the page or reset it before publish. I will check if APP_FRAME resets the page.\n\nThe browse timeout is confirmed to be the 10-second wait for screen play. The debug run succeeded because it skipped the WATCH script and used a longer pause. Browse writes logs, takes screenshots, checks state, and then presses Enter.\n\nI am re-examining the browse code to verify which wait triggers the 10-second timeout. The HTML is identical across runs, so the failure likely stems from a subtle difference in how the test interacts with the page.\n\nThe browse timeout is confirmed to be the 10-second wait for `window.__game.screen === 'play'`. The timeline shows HTML rebuilt, boot-debug succeeded, browse failed on both boots, then enter-debug showed Enter sets play before the frame throws. This isolates the failure to the Enter interaction.\n\nThe PAD init script is identical in both browse and enter-debug, so it cannot explain the difference. The boot log shows no errors before Enter, ruling out a crash during the earlier screenshot or evaluation. Once the loop stops after Enter, nothing can reset the screen back to title.\n\nThe engine's frame error handler might reset the page or replace `window.__engine`, which would explain why the browse timeout still occurs despite `__game.screen` already being `'play'`. I will check how the loop handles a thrown frame.\n\nThe engine loop catch block is being inspected to see if it reloads the page or resets state after a frame throws. The 10-second timeout is confirmed to be the play-screen wait, not the ready wait. A document reload on error seems unlikely.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ea6d2cea-e964-4026-b645-22a3daf7d24a-171","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"\\.selected","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ea6d2cea-e964-4026-b645-22a3daf7d24a-172","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"APP_FRAME|a frame threw","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/app"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":930,"output_tokens":1908,"cache_read_input_tokens":198528,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"fae60487-8b9c-4d1b-9fff-761dfc822804"}
