{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_648","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Line 169 is inside an open() function.\n\nThe bug is at line 376. The `if (menu)` guard only checks before `update()`. If the update callback calls `close()` and sets `menu` to null, the next line tries to read `menu.selected` and crashes. The fix is to add a second `if (menu)` check right after `update()`.\n\nTracing the menu callback chain confirms the crash path. `pickTitle` calls `close()`, which sets `menu` to null. This happens during `update()` before the second `if (menu)` guard runs.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-021f58d2-19c7-4c90-9687-eb40d3498e12-173","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/app/engine.ts","offset":330,"limit":55}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2279,"output_tokens":498,"cache_read_input_tokens":199424,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"ea0def79-1d55-4c67-b15e-bc83acbc9daa"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-021f58d2-19c7-4c90-9687-eb40d3498e12-173","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"330→  try {\\n    parts.gfx = await createRenderer(options.canvas, { settings: currentSettings(() => started), registry, log });\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    fail(error);\\n    return engine;\\n  }\\n  const gfx = parts.gfx;\\n  parts.numbers = createDamageNumbers((parts.ui = createUi({ canvas: options.canvas })));\\n  try {\\n    gfx.renderer.shadowMap.enabled = true;\\n340→    const styles = createStyleSet({ library: materials!, registry });\\n    const post = (parts.post = createPost(gfx, { settings: currentSettings(() => started), registry, log, styles }));\\n    const budget = () => parts.governor!.budget(settingsNow.get<QualitySetting>('quality'), input.touch?.active ?? false); // prettier-ignore\\n    parts.look = createPageLook({ post, styles, warmup: gfx.warmup, resolution: gfx.resolution, library: materials!, quality: budget, asked: () => warmsAsked(settingsNow) }); // prettier-ignore\\n    post.attach(gfx.warmup);\\n    viewNow().stage.register(gfx.warmup, gfx.features);\\n    await warmCameras();\\n    await settle(1, 0);\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    fail(error);\\n350→    return engine;\\n  }\\n  const step = (intents: Record<string, unknown>) => {\\n    if (playback && !playback.done) {\\n      playback.step(started.session);\\n      started.stepped(); // its hit-stops reach the clock as in live play\\n    } else {\\n      playback = null;\\n      started.stepOnce(intents);\\n    }\\n360→  };\\n  loop = createLoop({\\n    clock: () => started.clock,\\n    sample,\\n    step,\\n    draw: ({ alpha, dt }) => {\\n      // frozen in a reproducible run: a replay playing, or the governor turned off (engine/dev/governor.ts)\\n      parts.governor!.freeze((playback !== null && !playback.done) || !settingsNow.get<boolean>('gfx.governor'));\\n      if (warming) return;\\n      const report = frame(alpha, dt);\\n370→      if (!report.drawn && report.warming) warming = warmCameras().finally(() => (warming = null));\\n    },\\n    hold: () => started.playing,\\n    cap: () => input.touch?.active ?? false,\\n    onError: (error) => fail(error, 'APP_FRAME'),\\n  });\\n  parts.ready = true;\\n  overlay.hide();\\n  loop.start();\\n  const replay = asked?.playback;\\n380→  if (asked && !replay) fail(asked.error);\\n  else if (replay) {\\n    try {\\n      started.begin(replay.replay);\\n      playback = replay;\",\"content_concise\":\"330→  try {\\n    parts.gfx = await createRenderer(options.canvas, { settings: currentSettings(() => started), registry, log });\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    fail(error);\\n    return engine;\\n  }\\n  const gfx = parts.gfx;\\n  parts.numbers = createDamageNumbers((parts.ui = createUi({ canvas: options.canvas })));\\n  try {\\n    gfx.renderer.shadowMap.enabled = true;\\n340→    const styles = createStyleSet({ library: materials!, registry });\\n    const post = (parts.post = createPost(gfx, { settings: currentSettings(() => started), registry, log, styles }));\\n    const budget = () => parts.governor!.budget(settingsNow.get<QualitySetting>('quality'), input.touch?.active ?? false); // prettier-ignore\\n    parts.look = createPageLook({ post, styles, warmup: gfx.warmup, resolution: gfx.resolution, library: materials!, quality: budget, asked: () => warmsAsked(settingsNow) }); // prettier-ignore\\n    post.attach(gfx.warmup);\\n    viewNow().stage.register(gfx.warmup, gfx.features);\\n    await warmCameras();\\n    await settle(1, 0);\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    fail(error);\\n350→    return engine;\\n  }\\n  const step = (intents: Record<string, unknown>) => {\\n    if (playback && !playback.done) {\\n      playback.step(started.session);\\n      started.stepped(); // its hit-stops reach the clock as in live play\\n    } else {\\n      playback = null;\\n      started.stepOnce(intents);\\n    }\\n360→  };\\n