{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_660","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Beginning to outline the initial steps from STAGE.md.\n\nThe menu null error during the close-to-play transition is caught by the engine. The screen should already be 'play' at that point, so the browse timeout is puzzling. The Enter key may not reach the game because the menu uses input sampling and Enter is mapped to uiAccept.\n\nThe enter-debug output confirms the screen is 'play', so the timeout is unexpected. The actual browse log needs closer inspection.\n\nThe isolated browse run timed out after Enter, contradicting the enter-debug result where screen play was visible. The two runs may have used different HTML builds.\n\nThe throw should stop the frame loop and keep the screen as play. The timeout may instead come from the engine's fail() or page onError republishing title after the error overlay appears.\n\nChecking if __game is a snapshot object replaced on every publish, which could let the page reset the screen in a catch block after the error. Also examining whether keyboard.press timing or focus issues prevent the Enter key from reaching the window listener.\n\nThe APP_FRAME error might actually occur on a frame before Enter is pressed. If the throw happens during menu.update, the screen could stay stuck on title and never reach play. The menu should not close prematurely in this short window.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4bd2afad-ce63-4fc2-8f40-1ab47fbfbfc1-16","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"const publish|function publish|screen:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/stage.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1607,"output_tokens":1013,"cache_read_input_tokens":51968,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":