se answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"f4c4aa62-7622-4921-bf25-859926196035"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_672","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reviewing the plan's constraints.\n\nConfirmed the browser limit. Only two browsers run at once: one for verify and touch, another for webkit after the first closes. The play-debug chrome instance is already closed.\n\nEarlyoom kills are memory pressure, not game bugs. I will not retry forever if verify gets OOM-killed. I will check free memory before starting. verify.mjs does not pass CHROMIUM_PATH to browse.py, but the shell exports it so spawnSync picks it up.\n\nVitest song and syllable notes are pushed unconditionally when the test status is zero, matching the log requirement. A ## Deviations section with one bullet will be added after verify passes.\n\nThe deviations section belongs on the goal plan, not the game PLAN.md. I will run eslint first since it is fast and does not use Chrome, then launch verify.\n\nConfirmed the browser limit is strictly enforced. Verify runs sequentially and exits before the next browser starts, so only one Chromium process is active at a time. The hub iframe pages share that single browser tree. Vitest itself does not launch browsers; the browser replay is handled separately by the node script.\n\nThe verify launch command is ready. It sets the Playwright platform override, exports the cached Chromium path, and runs verify.mjs into a scratch log.\n\nThe monitor script needs the verify process ID to poll it. Since block_until_ms is zero, the command runs asynchronously and returns a task ID instead of the shell PID. I will write the actual process ID to a scratch file immediately so the monitor can read it without race conditions.\n\nThe monitor script polls for the verify PID file, then watches the process every 30 seconds. It checks the log for zero failures and exit code 0 before reporting success or failure.\n\nA 25-minute stall detector will be added to the monitor. If verify runs longer than that, it will print FAILED and exit without killing the process. The previous hang was caused by a missing CHROMIUM_PATH.\n\nI will check for a stale verify.pid before launching. I will read TASK.md after launch, since file reads do not compete with browsers.\n\nESLint and verify can run in parallel because ESLint does not modify source files, and verify rebuilds from stage.ts at startup. The menu guard is confirmed to be in the Vite-bundled source.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-35f62d3c-e4e4-4d98-bf2b-96432bb49412-38","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"free -h && cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656\" && npx eslint --quiet labs/game/ui/stage.ts; echo ESLINT:$?","description":"Check free memory and lint stage.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7028,"output_tokens":1795,"cache_read_input_tokens":67968,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"75efac14-65d5-4eb0-8aee-9b888eb3ba4b"}
