,54,58,101,120,112,111,114,116,32,99,111,110,115,116,32,69,88,73,84,32,61,32,123,10,55,55,58,32,32,115,111,117,114,99,101,73,110,102,111,114,109,97,116,105,111,110,58,32,83,79,85,82,67,69,44,10,55,56,58,32,32,116,101,115,116,105,110,103,70,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,58,32,91,46,46,46,84,69,83,84,73,78,71,93,44,10,55,57,58,32,32,101,110,103,105,110,101,70,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,58,32,91,46,46,46,69,78,71,73,78,69,93,44,10,56,48,58,32,32,112,114,111,109,112,116,70,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,58,32,91,46,46,46,80,82,79,77,80,84,93,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":5,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/about-data.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":76,\"content\":\"export const EXIT = {\"},{\"line_number\":77,\"content\":\"  sourceInformation: SOURCE,\"},{\"line_number\":78,\"content\":\"  testingFeedback: [...TESTING],\"},{\"line_number\":79,\"content\":\"  engineFeedback: [...ENGINE],\"},{\"line_number\":80,\"content\":\"  promptFeedback: [...PROMPT],\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-990ae87a-e924-4e7d-b650-59f848e9d806-47","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Progress\\n\\nThe engine in this workspace is unchanged. Thumb Yoga, the balance retreat, lives in labs/game.\\n\\nThe page, the five-day director, and the pavilion ghost round are the game's own code. ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md lists what the engine did not provide. Nothing under engine/ is patched.\\n\\nNext is to leave the engine as it is. The open items are requests in that feedback file, not defects in this tree.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Progress\\n\\nThe engine in this workspace is unchanged. Thumb Yoga, the balance retreat, lives in labs/game.\\n\\nThe page, the five-day director, and the pavilion ghost round are the game's own code. ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md lists what the engine did not provide. Nothing under engine/ is patched.\\n\\nNext is to leave the engine as it is. The open items are requests in that feedback file, not defects in this tree.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/docs/PROGRESS.md\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"# Progress\\n\\nThe engine in this workspace is unchanged. Thumb Yoga, the balance retreat, lives in labs/game.\\n\\nThe page, the five-day director, and the pavilion ghost round are the game's own code. ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md lists what the engine did not provide. Nothing under engine/ is patched.\\n\\nNext is to leave the engine as it is. The open items are requests in that feedback file, not defects in this tree.\\n\",\"total_lines\":7}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-990ae87a-e924-4e7d-b650-59f848e9d806-48","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Engine feedback: thumb-yoga\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at e7a1243) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n- Let a page add a mesh. The retreat needed a readable guest and a few simple solids. There is no public way to register a generated mesh, so the body stays on the engine humanoid and the props stay on the built-in parts. A `geometry:cylinder` is also missing. A frustum stood in for a post.\\n10→- Start the music bus at 0.1, or let `createAudio` take a default. The bus comes up at 0.5. This game has to call `audio.volume('music', 0.1)` before a save can raise it, because a fresh stay must be a tenth.\\n- `playClip` during `setup` throws. A rest pose queued from setup never starts. Clips are played at spawn instead. Setup should accept the same call, or the error should say to wait for spawn.\\n- `spawnProp` with no yaw builds a NaN quaternion and the sim blows up. Yaw should default to 0. Every prop in this game passes one.\\n- A prop part's offset field is `position`. Code that says `at`, which the rest of the engine uses, is ignored and the part sits on the origin. One name would do.\\n- `headlessHost(engine).session.world` is a frozen recording. The live world is `createAppHost(...).session.world`, and `inspector.seed()` replaces that session, so a cached world goes stale. The frozen view should be named as a recording, and `seed` should say that old handles die.\\n- Query keys the engine does not know fail the boot. An AI Hub page arrives with `?aihub=1` and friends. Those keys have to be stripped from the string passed to `createEngine` or the page never starts. Unknown keys could be ignored.\\n- `input.prompt` is Xbox. A game whose default glyphs are PlayStation cannot use it. The prompt should follow the pad the browser reported, or the page should be able to set the family.\\n- The touch stick is drawn unless the page sets `touch=off`. A 10-foot game that must refuse touch play has to know that secret. A `createEngine` flag would be the obvious place.\\n- `gfx.resolution=auto`, when the look names no resolution, becomes `pixels` and caps the buffer around 330 lines. A check that the drawing buffer matches the view then fails on a correct page. `full` has to be set by hand.\\n- There is no `inspector.reset`. Live sliders put the defaults back by reading `describe('setting', path)` and calling `set`. A reset that restores every `game.*` default would match the dev-mode job.\\n20→- `node x new` prints `NEW_DOCS` lines about `labs/playground/…` even when the entry is written and its test passes. The docs check is tripping over its own guide. Those lines should not look like a failed command.\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n- From `labs/game/scenes/*.ts` the sim API is `../../../engine/sim-api`. From `labs/game/scenes/events/*.ts` it is `../../../../engine/sim-api`. There is no alias. The first import, one folder short, typechecks as a missing module and the event never loads.\\n- `createMenu` will show more than six rows. A 10-foot page has to slice the list itself.\\n- The hard line cap is 600. The fetched hub round, plus the `@file` comment this repo requires, was 603 lines and `eslint` failed `hard-cap/max-lines`. The protocol file should be allowed to stay the file the hub shipped. The comment was shortened so the cap would pass. Behaviour was not changed.\\n- The plan pinned session-client SHA-256 `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a`. The file fetched from the raw URL banners 1.4.0 and hashes to `6ab6be43898e2db069bc21a94757d77d9c3f2a0cb76f01186490d3bd88d8717a`. The banner did not move when the bytes did.\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n30→\\nNone. No file under `engine/` was edited. `npm run check` should still match `engine-lock.json`.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Engine feedback: thumb-yoga\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at e7a1243) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n- Let a page add a mesh. The retreat needed a readable guest and a few simple solids. There is no public way to register a generated mesh, so the body stays on the engine humanoid and the props stay on the built-in parts. A `geometry:cylinder` is also missing. A frustum stood in for a post.\\n10→- Start the music bus at 0.1, or let `createAudio` take a default. The bus comes up at 0.5. This game has to call `audio.volume('music', 0.1)` before a save can raise it, because a fresh stay must be a tenth.\\n- `playClip` during `setup` throws. A rest pose queued from setup never starts. Clips are played at spawn instead. Setup should accept the same call, or the error should say to wait for spawn.\\n- `spawnProp` with no yaw builds a NaN quaternion and the sim blows up. Yaw should default to 0. Every prop in this game passes one.\\n- A prop part's offset field is `position`. Code that says `at`, which the rest of the engine uses, is ignored and the part sits on the origin. One name would do.\\n- `headlessHost(engine).session.world` is a frozen recording. The live world is `createAppHost(...).session.world`, and `inspector.seed()` replaces that session, so a cached world goes stale. The frozen view should be named as a recording, and `seed` should say that old handles die.\\n- Query keys the engine does not know fail the boot. An AI Hub page arrives with `?aihub=1` and friends. Those keys have to be stripped from the string passed to `createEngine` or the page never starts. Unknown keys could be ignored.\\n- `input.prompt` is Xbox. A game whose default glyphs are PlayStation cannot use it. The prompt should follow the pad the browser reported, or the page should be able to set the family.\\n- The touch stick is drawn unless the page sets `touch=off`. A 10-foot game that must refuse touch play has to know that secret. A `createEngine` flag would be the obvious place.\\n- `gfx.resolution=auto`, when the look names no resolution, becomes `pixels` and caps the buffer around 330 lines. A check that the drawing buffer matches the view then fails on a correct page. `full` has to be set by hand.\\n- There is no `inspector.reset`. Live sliders put the defaults back by reading `describe('setting', path)` and calling `set`. A reset that restores every `game.*` default would match the dev-mode job.\\n20→- `node x new` prints `NEW_DOCS` lines about `labs/playground/…` even when the entry is written and its test passes. The docs check is tripping over its own guide. Those lines should not look like a failed command.\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n- From `labs/game/scenes/*.ts` the sim API is `../../../engine/sim-api`. From `labs/game/scenes/events/*.ts` it is `../../../../engine/sim-api`. There is no alias. The first import, one folder short, typechecks as a missing module and the event never loads.\\n- `createMenu` will show more than six rows. A 10-foot page has to slice the list itself.\\n- The hard line cap is 600. The fetched hub round, plus the `@file` comment this repo requires, was 603 lines and `eslint` failed `hard-cap/max-lines`. The protocol file should be allowed to stay the file the hub shipped. The comment was shortened so the cap would pass. Behaviour was not changed.\\n- The plan pinned session-client SHA-256 `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a`. The file fetched from the raw URL banners 1.4.0 and hashes to `6ab6be43898e2db069bc21a94757d77d9c3f2a0cb76f01186490d3bd88d8717a`. The banner did not move when the bytes did.\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n30→\\nNone. No file under `engine/` was edited. `npm run check` should still match `engine-lock.json`.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"# Engine feedback: thumb-yoga\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at e7a1243) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n- Let a page add a mesh. The retreat needed a readable guest and a few simple solids. There is no public way to register a generated mesh, so the body stays on the engine humanoid and the props stay on the built-in parts. A `geometry:cylinder` is also missing. A frustum stood in for a post.\\n- Start the music bus at 0.1, or let `createAudio` take a default. The bus comes up at 0.5. This game has to call `audio.volume('music', 0.1)` before a save can raise it, because a fresh stay must be a tenth.\\n- `playClip` during `setup` throws. A rest pose queued from setup never starts. Clips are played at spawn instead. Setup should accept the same call, or the error should say to wait for spawn.\\n- `spawnProp` with no yaw builds a NaN quaternion and the sim blows up. Yaw should default to 0. Every prop in this game passes one.\\n- A prop part's offset field is `position`. Code that says `at`, which the rest of the engine uses, is ignored and the part sits on the origin. One name would do.\\n- `headlessHost(engine).session.world` is a frozen recording. The live world is `createAppHost(...).session.world`, and `inspector.seed()` replaces that session, so a cached world goes stale. The frozen view should be named as a recording, and `seed` should say that old handles die.\\n- Query keys the engine does not know fail the boot. An AI Hub page arrives with `?aihub=1` and friends. Those keys have to be stripped from the string passed to `createEngine` or the page never starts. Unknown keys could be ignored.\\n- `input.prompt` is Xbox. A game whose default glyphs are PlayStation cannot use it. The prompt should follow the pad the browser reported, or the page should be able to set the family.\\n- The touch stick is drawn unless the page sets `touch=off`. A 10-foot game that must refuse touch play has to know that secret. A `createEngine` flag would be the obvious place.\\n- `gfx.resolution=auto`, when the look names no resolution, becomes `pixels` and caps the buffer around 330 lines. A check that the drawing buffer matches the view then fails on a correct page. `full` has to be set by hand.\\n- There is no `inspector.reset`. Live sliders put the defaults back by reading `describe('setting', path)` and calling `set`. A reset that restores every `game.*` default would match the dev-mode job.\\n- `node x new` prints `NEW_DOCS` lines about `labs/playground/…` even when the entry is written and its test passes. The docs check is tripping over its own guide. Those lines should not look like a failed command.\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n- From `labs/game/scenes/*.ts` the sim API is `../../../engine/sim-api`. From `labs/game/scenes/events/*.ts` it is `../../../../engine/sim-api`. There is no alias. The first import, one folder short, typechecks as a missing module and the event never loads.\\n- `createMenu` will show more than six rows. A 10-foot page has to slice the list itself.\\n- The hard line cap is 600. The fetched hub round, plus the `@file` comment this repo requires, was 603 lines and `eslint` failed `hard-cap/max-lines`. The protocol file should be allowed to stay the file the hub shipped. The comment was shortened so the cap would pass. Behaviour was not changed.\\n- The plan pinned session-client SHA-256 `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a`. The file fetched from the raw URL banners 1.4.0 and hashes to `6ab6be43898e2db069bc21a94757d77d9c3f2a0cb76f01186490d3bd88d8717a`. The banner did not move when the bytes did.\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\nNone. No file under `engine/` was edited. `npm run check` should still match `engine-lock.json`.\\n\",\"total_lines\":31}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"0265a7c3-2539-406d-9686-4fe668dadb74"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_677","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No TODO comments were found in labs/game.\n\nI will verify exit-interview matches EXIT statically. I will check that README exists. I am comparing browse needles against the actual About text to catch missing items before verification starts.\n\nVitest is already running, so I can edit about-data.ts now without affecting it. Browse executes after vitest and replay, so any changes will be picked up before that stage begins.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9fb828d5-ccda-46c0-b482-65c2f05efac8-49","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/about-data.ts","offset":1,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9fb828d5-ccda-46c0-b482-65c2f05efac8-50","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"needles|Wii Fit|PLAN.md|most helpful","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/tools/browse.py"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2133,"output_tokens":487,"cache_read_input_tokens":80768,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"05e3dda1-520d-4691-9c1d-6e3878eb9bc3"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9fb828d5-ccda-46c0-b482-65c2f05efac8-49","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The words shared by the About screen and exit-interview.json.\\n * Each answer is at most two short sentences. The source name appears only in the source fields.\\n */\\nexport const SOURCE = {\\n  date: '2026-11-04 22:36:56',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n10→  perspective: 'third-person',\\n  tech: 'my-3dge at e7a1243, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite 7.3, TypeScript.',\\n  artDirection: 'The engine toon style, with a bright lawn, sand shore, and a flat sea.',\\n  animation: 'The engine clip layer. Original poses are scrubbed from the balance step. The rest pose is Mesh2Motion.',\\n  audio: 'Tracker songs, code-made effects, and gibberish syllable voices. A fresh save plays music at a tenth.',\\n  online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, and same-screen Group Class on its own.',\\n  testing: 'Bot bands on ten seeds, a three-seed walk to the credits, and browser checks of the built file.',\\n  research: 'none',\\n  environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\\n  model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\\n20→  usage: 'added on import',\\n} as const;\\n\\n/** Testing Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const TESTING = [\\n  'Testing caught six issues before hand-in. They were score bands, a NaN prop yaw, a missing boot setting, over-long lines, a ghost pack at the wrong offset, and event imports one folder too high.',\\n  'Four were critical. The bands, the island boot, the ghost seat, and the event imports each stopped a run.',\\n  'The most helpful test was the four bot bands on ten seeds for every shipped activity.',\\n  'The least helpful was a headless screenshot. The canvas can be blank while the sim state is fine.',\\n] as const;\\n30→\\n/** Engine Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const ENGINE = [\\n  'Scene actions, live settings, and a headless world you can step made the week testable without a browser.',\\n  'I got stuck on playClip during setup, props that need a yaw, a frozen recorded world, and hub query keys read as settings.',\\n  'The balance step, the day director, the songs, and the syllable voices are the game’s own.',\\n  'The hardest part was keeping the pavilion small enough for the hub ready deadline while the island stayed a place.',\\n  'None. The engine files were not changed.',\\n  'I would let a page add a mesh, and I would start the music bus at a tenth instead of a half.',\\n] as const;\\n40→\\n/** Prompt Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const PROMPT = [\\n  'The acceptance numbers, the cut line, and the bot bands made the scope checkable.',\\n  'The group score is described as a sum to 3000 and also has to fit a rank from 0 to 1000. Several seed lines are longer than two sentences.',\\n  'The hardest part was one HTML file that is a full retreat and also a ghost session the harness can drive.',\\n  'I would state the group score once, and pin the session client hash to the file the plan says to fetch.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Credits shown under the same About screen. */\\n50→export const CREDITS = [\\n  'my-3dge, MIT.',\\n  'three.js r182, MIT.',\\n  'Rapier 0.21, Apache-2.0.',\\n  '@stdlib, Apache-2.0.',\\n  'AI Hub session client 1.4.0, pasted unmodified.',\\n  'The rest pose follows Mesh2Motion. The pose clips themselves are original.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Catalogue fields. The source name is only here and in SOURCE.source. */\\n60→export const AI_HUB = {\\n  name: 'Thumb Yoga',\\n  tagline: 'A week of balance at Little Fulcrum',\\n  description:\\n    'Stand on the disc and keep the dot near the middle. Little Fulcrum runs five days of pose, pond, water, sand, and a storm.',\\n  type: 'Game',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  series: '',\\n  players: '1–4',\\n70→  controls:\\n    'Lean with the left stick, WASD or the mouse. L2 and R2, or Q and E, are the feet. Both feet or Space breathe.',\\n  tags: ['3d', 'sports', 'third-person', 'comedy', 'co-op'],\\n} as const;\\n\\n/** The exit-interview object. The screen and the file both read this. */\\nexport const EXIT = {\\n  sourceInformation: SOURCE,\\n  testingFeedback: [...TESTING],\\n  engineFeedback: [...ENGINE],\\n80→  promptFeedback: [...PROMPT],\\n  aiHub: AI_HUB,\\n};\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The words shared by the About screen and exit-interview.json.\\n * Each answer is at most two short sentences. The source name appears only in the source fields.\\n */\\nexport const SOURCE = {\\n  date: '2026-11-04 22:36:56',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n10→  perspective: 'third-person',\\n  tech: 'my-3dge at e7a1243, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite 7.3, TypeScript.',\\n  artDirection: 'The engine toon style, with a bright lawn, sand shore, and a flat sea.',\\n  animation: 'The engine clip layer. Original poses are scrubbed from the balance step. The rest pose is Mesh2Motion.',\\n  audio: 'Tracker songs, code-made effects, and gibberish syllable voices. A fresh save plays music at a tenth.',\\n  online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, and same-screen Group Class on its own.',\\n  testing: 'Bot bands on ten seeds, a three-seed walk to the credits, and browser checks of the built file.',\\n  research: 'none',\\n  environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\\n  model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\\n20→  usage: 'added on import',\\n} as const;\\n\\n/** Testing Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const TESTING = [\\n  'Testing caught six issues before hand-in. They were score bands, a NaN prop yaw, a missing boot setting, over-long lines, a ghost pack at the wrong offset, and event imports one folder too high.',\\n  'Four were critical. The bands, the island boot, the ghost seat, and the event imports each stopped a run.',\\n  'The most helpful test was the four bot bands on ten seeds for every shipped activity.',\\n  'The least helpful was a headless screenshot. The canvas can be blank while the sim state is fine.',\\n] as const;\\n30→\\n/** Engine Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const ENGINE = [\\n  'Scene actions, live settings, and a headless world you can step made the week testable without a browser.',\\n  'I got stuck on playClip during setup, props that need a yaw, a frozen recorded world, and hub query keys read as settings.',\\n  'The balance step, the day director, the songs, and the syllable voices are the game’s own.',\\n  'The hardest part was keeping the pavilion small enough for the hub ready deadline while the island stayed a place.',\\n  'None. The engine files were not changed.',\\n  'I would let a page add a mesh, and I would start the music bus at a tenth instead of a half.',\\n] as const;\\n40→\\n/** Prompt Feedback, in the order the brief asks. */\\nexport const PROMPT = [\\n  'The acceptance numbers, the cut line, and the bot bands made the scope checkable.',\\n  'The group score is described as a sum to 3000 and also has to fit a rank from 0 to 1000. Several seed lines are longer than two sentences.',\\n  'The hardest part was one HTML file that is a full retreat and also a ghost session the harness can drive.',\\n  'I would state the group score once, and pin the session client hash to the file the plan says to fetch.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Credits shown under the same About screen. */\\n50→export const CREDITS = [\\n  'my-3dge, MIT.',\\n  'three.js r182, MIT.',\\n  'Rapier 0.21, Apache-2.0.',\\n  '@stdlib, Apache-2.0.',\\n  'AI Hub session client 1.4.0, pasted unmodified.',\\n  'The rest pose follows Mesh2Motion. The pose clips themselves are original.',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** Catalogue fields. The source name is only here and in SOURCE.source. */\\n60→export const AI_HUB = {\\n  name: 'T