.ts) in Node, step by step, against its goldens, and reads its sound\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/tools/cmd/check.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":13,\"content\":\" * its fonts go anywhere in labs/game/ with their license beside them, and the engine's approvals stand as its\"},{\"line_number\":103,\"content\":\"const GAME_FONTS = 'labs/game/';\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/tools/lib/replayState.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":2,\"content\":\" * @file The state a replay reaches, for `x replay --state` and `--until n` (tools/cmd/replay.ts; gate G7's review):\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/tools/lib/docsGameApi.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":132,\"content\":\"    return [{ id: 'DOCS_STALE', message, file: GUIDE }];\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/tools/cmd/replay.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":14,\"content\":\" * same player (engine/sim/replay.ts). Every run must give the goldens of this platform (`linux-x64`): one set, valid\"},{\"line_number\":17,\"content\":\" * and loads after the animation library, as there (tools/anim/library.ts; the page: tests/pages/replay.ts).\"},{\"line_number\":60,\"content\":\"/** Where two runs part: the step, the runs, and what differs there (engine/sim/replay.ts `partingOf`). */\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/tools/cmd/engine.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":49,\"content\":\"          message: `${path} is in the engine's folders (my-3dge@${short}), read-only in a game: move it into labs/game/, where the game's files live, or ${patch}`,\"},{\"line_number\":129,\"content\":\"      ['sim', process.execPath, ['x', 'sim', 'labs/game/scenes/play.ts', '--steps', '600']],\"},{\"line_number\":130,\"content\":\"      ['replay', process.execPath, ['x', 'replay', 'labs/game/replays', '--browser', 'sim']],\"},{\"line_number\":131,\"content\":\"      ['shot', process.execPath, ['x', 'shot', 'labs/game']],\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/tools/cmd/sim.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":10,\"content\":\" * records it, so `run.replay.json` replays it (engine/sim/replay.ts), golden hashes for this platform included (copy\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/tools/lib/scenes.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":26,\"content\":\"/** Where scene modules live: `fixtures/scenes/` and every `labs/<name>/scenes/` (tests/pages/replay.ts globs the same). */\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"14da1ccc-51ea-4b42-a6b0-8dd1c5b538f4"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_688","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The npm run check command includes a simulation test for the play scene with 600 steps.\n\nThe check command also includes replay and shot tests. The missing play.ts file may cause the check to fail.\n\nThe verification plan requires both npm test and npm run check to pass. Restoring play.ts conflicts with the preference to avoid the starter gem, since the game now uses retreat scenes instead. I am weighing whether the check is configurable or if the failure should be documented.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5a57469f-994c-4310-bc14-68fef08a1a84-67","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/tools/cmd/engine.ts","offset":90,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5a57469f-994c-4310-bc14-68fef08a1a84-68","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"play\\.ts","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656","glob":"*.{ts,json,md}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1922,"output_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_tokens":101632,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"1a36e1b8-6b54-4e86-90fd-4cddbb1ab671"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5a57469f-994c-4310-bc14-68fef08a1a84-67","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"90→    },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** Runs a command in `cwd`, returning whether it passed, its time, its output and the output's tail. */\\nfunction step(cwd: string, command: string, args: string[]): { ok: boolean; ms: number; output: string; tail: string } {\\n  const started = performance.now();\\n  const env = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(process.env).filter(([key]) => !key.startsWith('VITEST')));\\n  const run = spawnSync(command, args, { cwd, env, encoding: 'utf8', timeout: STEP_MS, maxBuffer: 64 << 20 });\\n  const output = `${run.stdout ?? ''}${run.stderr ?? ''}${run.error ? String(run.error) : ''}`;\\n100→  const tail = output.trim().split('\\\\n').slice(-6).join(' | ');\\n  return { ok: run.status === 0, ms: performance.now() - started, output, tail };\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * The engine's own commands that a game's `x help` listed: none, when game mode works. Up to 18 commands, help prints\\n * them one a line, name first; past that, out/help/all/commands.txt holds the same lines (tools/cmd/help.ts).\\n */\\nexport function engineOnlyListed(game: string, output: string): string[] {\\n  const file = join(game, 'out', 'help', 'all', 'commands.txt');\\n110→  const listed = existsSync(file) ? readFileSync(file, 'utf8') : output;\\n  return ENGINE_ONLY_COMMANDS.filter((name) => new RegExp(`^\\\\\\\\s*${name}\\\\\\\\s{2,}`, 'm').test(listed));\\n}\\n\\n/** Makes a game from the checkout at `root` in a temporary folder and runs its gate (see the file comment). */\\nfunction testGame(root: string, keep: boolean): CommandResult {\\n  const folder = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'my3dge-game-'));\\n  const target = join(folder, 'game-test');\\n  const lines: string[] = [];\\n  const failures: Finding[] = [];\\n120→  const metrics: Record<string, number> = {};\\n  try {\\n    const made = createGame({ target, name: 'game-test', source: root });\\n    lines.push(`made: ${made.engineFiles} engine files and ${made.starterFiles} starter files in ${target}`);\\n    Object.assign(metrics, { engineFiles: made.engineFiles, starterFiles: made.starterFiles });\\n    const steps: [string, string, string[]][] = [\\n      ['install', 'npm', ['ci', '--prefer-offline', '--no-audit', '--no-fund']],\\n      ['check', 'npm', ['run', 'check']],\\n      ['test', 'npm', ['test']],\\n      ['sim', process.execPath, ['x', 'sim', 'labs/game/scenes/play.ts', '--steps', '600']],\\n130→      ['replay', process.execPath, ['x', 'replay', 'labs/game/replays', '--browser', 'sim']],\\n      ['shot', process.execPath, ['x', 'shot', 'labs/game']],\\n      ['qa', process.execPath, ['x', 'qa', ...qaFamilies(root)]],\\n      ['help', process.execPath, ['x', 'help']],\\n    ];\\n    for (const [name, command, args] of steps) {\\n      const done = step(target, command, args);\\n      const leaked = name === 'help' ? engineOnlyListed(target, done.output) : [];\\n      metrics[`${name}.ms`] = Math.round(done.ms);\\n      lines.push(`${name}: ${done.ok && leaked.length === 0 ? 'ok' : 'FAIL'} (${(done.ms / 1000).toFixed(1)} s)`);\\n140→      if (leaked.length > 0) failures.push({ id: 'ENGINE_TEST_HELP', message: `a game's x help lists the engine's own commands: ${leaked.join(', ')}` }); // prettier-ignore\\n      if (!done.ok) failures.push({ id: `ENGINE_TEST_${name.toUpperCase()}`, message: `${command} ${args.join(' ')} failed in the new game: ${done.tail}` }); // prettier-ignore\\n      if (!done.ok && name === 'install') break;\\n    }\\n  } finally {\\n    if (keep) lines.push(`kept: ${target}`);\\n    else rmSync(folder, { recursive: true, force: true });\\n  }\\n  return {\\n    ok: failures.length === 0,\\n150→    summary: failures.length === 0 ? 'a new game passes its own gate' : `a new game fails ${failures.length} step(s)`,\\n    target: 'test',\\n    lines,\\n    failures,\\n    metrics,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** Clones `repository` at `ref` (a branch, a tag or a commit) into `into`, shallow. */\\nfunction cloneEngine(repository: string, ref: string, into: string): void {\\n160→  const git = (...args: string[]) => {\\n    const run = spawnSync('git', args, { encoding: 'utf8', timeout: STEP_MS });\\n    if (run.status !== 0) throw new Error(`git ${args.join(' ')} failed: ${(run.stderr || String(run.error)).trim()}`);\\n  };\\n  if (/^[0-9a-f]{7,40}$/.test(ref)) {\\n    git('init', '--quiet', into);\\n    git('-C', into, 'fetch', '--quiet', '--depth', '1', repository, ref);\\n    git('-C', into, 'checkout', '--quiet', '--detach', 'FETCH_HEAD');\\n  } else git('clone', '--quiet', '--depth', '1', '--branch', ref, repository, into);\\n}\",\"content_concise\":\"90→    },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** Runs a command in `cwd`, returning whether it passed, its time, its output and the output's tail. */\\nfunction step(cwd: string, command: string, args: string[]): { ok: boolean; ms: number; output: string; tail: string } {\\n  const started = performance.now();\\n  const env = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(process.env).filter(([key]) => !key.startsWith('VITEST')));\\n  const run = spawnSync(command, args, { cwd, env, encoding: 'utf8', timeout: STEP_MS, maxBuffer: 64 << 20 });\\n  const output = `${run.stdout ?? ''}${run.stderr ?? ''}${run.error ? String(run.error) : ''}`;\\n100→  const tail = output.trim().split('\\\\n').slice(-6).join(' | ');\\n  return { ok: run.status === 0, ms: performance.now() - started, output, tail };\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * The engine's own commands that a game's `x help` listed: none, when game mode works. Up to 18 commands, help prints\\n * them one a line, name first; past that, out/help/all/commands.txt holds the same lines (tools/cmd/help.ts).\\n */\\nexport function engineOnlyListed(game: string, output: string): string[] {\\n  const file = join(game, 'out', 'help', 'all', 'commands.txt');\\n110→  const listed = existsSync(file) 