{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-16f24c58-79e4-45bc-b113-ff58571083e1-70","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→seed 1 credits\\nseed 2 credits\\nseed 3 credits\\nsongs render\\nsyllables render\\nreplay capture and restore continue\\nreplay goldens continue\\nFAIL boot 1 Page.wait_for_function: Timeout 10000ms exceeded.\\nFAIL boot 2 Page.wait_for_function: Timeout 10000ms exceeded.\\n10→2 failures\\nEXIT:1\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→seed 1 credits\\nseed 2 credits\\nseed 3 credits\\nsongs render\\nsyllables render\\nreplay capture and restore continue\\nreplay goldens continue\\nFAIL boot 1 Page.wait_for_function: Timeout 10000ms exceeded.\\nFAIL boot 2 Page.wait_for_function: Timeout 10000ms exceeded.\\n10→2 failures\\nEXIT:1\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/verify.log\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"seed 1 credits\\nseed 2 credits\\nseed 3 credits\\nsongs render\\nsyllables render\\nreplay capture and restore continue\\nreplay goldens continue\\nFAIL boot 1 Page.wait_for_function: Timeout 10000ms exceeded.\\nFAIL boot 2 Page.wait_for_function: Timeout 10000ms exceeded.\\n2 failures\\nEXIT:1\\n\",\"total_lines\":11}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"90d05016-5762-4cdd-9dd0-5ec829ad23cc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_691","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The 10-second wait for screen===play is still failing.\n\nplay-debug succeeded against the pre-verify HTML, so the source fix is present. The failure likely stems from a different cause, such as Enter not changing screen in browse's once(), or the rebuilt HTML omitting the guard.\n\nThe ready timeout succeeded, so the boot reached the play wait. The failure is isolated to that 10-second screen check.\n\nThe title checks passed. The log shows only the play wait timeout, so earlier asserts did not fail.\n\nThe rebuilt HTML should include the guard because onefile reads the source before running. The failure likely stems from differences between browse and play-debug: browse evaluates state and takes screenshots before pressing Enter, while play-debug only used PAD. These extra steps may prevent Enter from reaching the game screen.\n\nWATCH is just a rAF counter and should not block Enter. The gamepad might be intercepting the keyboard press, but play-debug used the same PAD and worked, so this seems unlikely. The rebuilt HTML from verify may differ from the tested version. I will check whether the built HTML contains the guard comment.\n\nThe guard comment may be stripped by terser during the Vite build, so a direct string search of the minified bundle is unreliable. I will inspect boot-1.log to see the pre-enter state and add a debug script that mirrors browse's once() exactly against the newly built HTML.\n\nBoot logs are written before Enter, so they cannot reveal the failure. The Enter press may be too fast for the engine's per-frame input sampling to catch it. Because both boots failed, this is systematic rather than a timing flake.\n\nThe screenshot step in browse may be the culprit. It could take enough time to let the 10-second attract timer expire and close the menu before Enter is pressed. Play-debug skips this step entirely.\n\nThe 10-second attract timer starts from the engine's bind() call, not from when ready becomes true. If lastInput was set before the ready signal, the menu could close before Enter is pressed.\n\nThe menu might accept Enter yet fail to reach the play screen. I will check the rebuilt HTML's file modification time and search for the guard snippet or PadLeftTrigger to confirm it is the updated build.\n\nI will grep the rebuilt HTML for \"PadLeftTrigger\" and \"menu.selected\" to confirm the guard is present. I will also read boot-1.log from scratch to check the pre-enter state. A debug script that mirrors browse's once() exactly will be run against the verify-built HTML, with a timeout that dumps __game, errors, and logs. The monitor process should be killed to prevent it from printing FAILED.\n\nI will kill the monitor process to avoid a stale wakeup. I am now reading boot-1.log and grepping the rebuilt HTML. I also spotted a potential race condition in the frame loop: menu.update runs before engine input is read, which could prevent Enter from registering.\n\nA new theory is that Enter is bound to both the menu and pause. If so, the frame that begins play would immediately see the pause key pressed and reopen the pause menu, resetting the screen back to pause before the frame ends. This would explain why browse fails while play-debug succeeds.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-05edd826-0b38-430b-b576-7e19ca2cf59b-71","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pause:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/actions.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-05edd826-0b38-430b-b576-7e19ca2cf59b-72","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"PadLeftTrigger|Begin closes the menu","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656.html"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-05edd826-0b38-430b-b576-7e19ca2cf59b-73","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/boot-1.log","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":288,"output_tokens":2080,"cache_read_input_tokens":110336,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"8331adcd-e144-4d86-902a-cd40c96a818c"}
