{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_697","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Enter key was detected, yet the title screen persisted for five seconds before attract mode began at sample 10.\n\nThe 5.5-second delay suggests the lastInput timestamp was set during boot, not at enter. That would make the total time from boot to attract roughly 7 seconds.\n\nThe Enter key did trigger the keyboard listener, which set lastInput and exited attract mode. The title screen delay must have another cause.\n\nThe game's keydown handler did not fire. If it had, Enter would have reset lastInput and delayed attract mode by another ten seconds. The fact that attract began at roughly 5.5 seconds confirms the game listener missed the keypress.\n\nThe init script's capture listener registered first and does not stop event propagation, so it should not block the game handler. The game listener should also still be active by the time Enter is pressed. The cause of its silence remains unclear.\n\nThe game's keyboard and stage listeners both missed the Enter key. The init script listener caught it, so the event reached the page. The game's listeners may have been removed.\n\nPlaywright's keyboard.press targets a specific element, but the window-level listeners should still catch the event. The game handler does not filter by key code. The 5.5-second attract delay is exactly eleven 500-millisecond samples after the press call returns.\n\nThe timing confirms lastInput was never reset. The screenshot likely took about four seconds, so the total from engine ready to sample 10 is roughly ten seconds. This proves the game's keydown handler did not fire. The stage listener is registered inside createStage at startup, so it should already be attached before the ready event.\n\nThe engine's keyboard listener may be the culprit. If it registered after the game's handler and called stopImmediatePropagation, it would block the game from ever receiving the Enter key.\n\nThe engine listener likely fired and blocked the stage handler with stopImmediatePropagation. The menu should still accept Enter if the engine recorded the key for uiAccept. The remaining question is whether the engine handler itself was suppressed.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-377f1d06-e927-49fd-9b74-2dbc30f9db3a-82","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/devices/keyboard.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":711,"output_tokens":1393,"cache_read_input_tokens":120320,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"843956e1-f61e-4ee6-b1a6-ffa4908fec93"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-377f1d06-e927-49fd-9b74-2dbc30f9db3a-82","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The keyboard device (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24): key events → codes by `KeyboardEvent.code`, the physical key, so\\n * bindings hold on every layout (engine/input/codes.ts). A key held down presses once (auto-repeat events are\\n * ignored), a key pressed and let go between two samples still counts as pressed (the sink keeps it), and a bound\\n * key's default is prevented, so Space does not scroll the page under the game.\\n *\\n * Invariants: keys typed into a text field, a text area, a select or editable content are the page's, not the game's;\\n * a key-up always releases, wherever it lands. `attachKeyboard` returns the function that removes its listeners.\\n *\\n10→ * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:491-499` (the typing filter, `preventDefault` on bound keys, `repeat`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * const target = new EventTarget();\\n * const presses: string[] = [];\\n * const sink = { press: (code: string) => presses.push(code), release() {}, analog() {}, used() {}, bound: () => true };\\n * const detach = attachKeyboard(target, sink);\\n * target.dispatchEvent(Object.assign(new Event('keydown'), { code: 'KeyW', repeat: false }));\\n * target.dispatchEvent(Object.assign(new Event('keydown'), { code: 'KeyW', repeat: true })); // auto-repeat: ignored\\n * presses; // ['KeyW']\\n20→ * detach();\\n * @see engine/input/devices/devices.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { deviceOf, type InputSink } from '../codes';\\n\\n/** The fields of a key event the device reads. */\\ninterface KeyEventLike extends Event {\\n  readonly code: string;\\n  readonly repeat?: boolean;\\n}\\n30→\\n/** Input types whose element still lets keys through to the game (no text goes into them). */\\nconst NOT_TYPING = new Set(['range', 'checkbox', 'radio', 'button', 'submit', 'reset', 'color', 'file', 'image']);\\n\\n/** Whether a key event's target is somewhere the player types. */\\nexport function isTyping(target: EventTarget | null): boolean {\\n  const element = target as { tagName?: string; type?: string; isContentEditable?: boolean } | null;\\n  if (!element?.tagName) return false;\\n  const tag = element.tagName.toUpperCase();\\n  if (tag === 'TEXTAREA' || tag === 'SELECT' || element.isContentEditable) return true;\\n40→  return tag === 'INPUT' && !NOT_TYPING.has((element.type ?? 'text').toLowerCase());\\n}\\n\\n/** Listens for keys on `target` (the window) and writes them to `sink`; returns the detach function. */\\nexport function attachKeyboard(target: EventTarget, sink: InputSink): () => void {\\n  const down = (event: Event) => {\\n    const { code, repeat } = event as KeyEventLike;\\n    if (!code || deviceOf(code) !== 'keyboard' || isTyping(event.target)) return;\\n    if (sink.bound(code)) event.preventDefault();\\n    if (!repeat) sink.press(code, 'keyboard');\\n50→  };\\n  const up = (event: Event) => {\\n    const { code } = event as KeyEventLike;\\n    if (code) sink.release(code);\\n  };\\n  target.addEventListener('keydown', down);\\n  target.addEventListener('keyup', up);\\n  return () => {\\n    target.removeEventListener('keydown', down);\\n    target.removeEventListener('keyup', up);\\n60→  };\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The keyboard device (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24): key events → codes by `KeyboardEvent.code`, the physical key, so\\n * bindings hold on every layout (engine/input/codes.ts). A key held down presses once (auto-repeat events are\\n * ignored), a key pressed and let go between two samples still counts as pressed (the sink keeps it), and a bound\\n * key's default is prevented, so Space does not scroll the page under the game.\\n *\\n * Invariants: keys typed into a text field, a text area, a select or editable content are the page's, not the game's;\\n * a key-up always releases, wherever it lands. `attachKeyboard` returns the function that removes its listeners.\\n *\\n10→ * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:491-499` (the typing filter, `preventDefault` on bound keys, `repeat`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * const target = new EventTarget();\\n * const presses: string[] = [];\\n * const sink = { press: (code: string) => presses.push(code), release() {}, analog() {}, used() {}, bound: () => true };\\n * const detach = attachKeyboard(target, sink);\\n * target.dispatchEvent(Object.assign(new Event('keydown'), { code: 'KeyW', repeat: false }));\\n * target.dispatchEvent(Object.assign(new Event('keydown'), { code: 'KeyW', repeat: true })); // auto-repeat: ignored\\n * presses; // ['KeyW']\\n20→ * detach();\\n * @see engine/input/devices/devices.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { deviceOf, type InputSink } from '../codes';\\n\\n/** The fields of a key event the device reads. */\\ninterface KeyEventLike extends Event {\\n  readonly code: string;\\n  readonly repeat?: boolean;\\n}\\n30→\\n/** Input types whose element still lets keys through to the game (no text goes into them). */\\nconst NOT_TYPING = new Set(['range', 'checkbox', 'radio', 'button', 'submit', 'reset', 'color', 'file', 'image']);\\n\\n/** Whether a key event's target is somewhere the player types. */\\nexport function isTyping(target: EventTarget | null): boolean {\\n  const element = target as { tagName?: string; type?: string; isContentEditable?: boolean } | null;\\n  if (!element?.tagName) return false;\\n  const tag = element.tagName.toUpperCase();\\n  if (tag === 'TEXTAREA' || tag === 'SELECT' || element.isContentEditable) return true;\\n40→  return tag === 'INPUT' && !NOT_TYPING.has((element.type ?? 'text').toLowerCase());\\n}\\n\\n/** Listens for keys on `target` (the window) and writes them to `sink`; returns the detach function. */\\nexport function attachKeyboard(target: EventTarget, sink: InputSink): () => void {\\n  const down = (event: Event) => {\\n    const { code, repeat } = event as KeyEventLike;\\n    if (!code || deviceOf(code) !== 'keyboard' || isTyping(event.target)) return;\\n    if (sink.bound(code)) event.preventDefault();\\n    if (!repeat) sink.press(code, 'keyboard');\\n50→  };\\n  const up = (event: Event) => {\\n    const { code } = event as KeyEventLike;\\n    if (code) sink.release(code);\\n  };\\n  target.addEventListener('keydown', down);\\n  target.addEventListener('keyup', up);\\n  return () => {\\n    target.removeEventListener('keydown', down);\\n    target.removeEventListener('keyup', up);\\n60→  };\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/devices/keyboard.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The keyboard device (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24): key events → codes by `KeyboardEvent.code`, the physical key, so\\n * bindings hold on every layout (engine/input/codes.ts). A key held down presses once (auto-repeat events are\\n * ignored), a key pressed and let go between two samples still counts as pressed (the sink keeps it), and a bound\\n * key's default is prevented, so Space does not scroll the page under the game.\\n *\\n * Invariants: keys typed into a text field, a text area, a select or editable content are the page's, not the game's;\\n * a key-up always releases, wherever it lands. `attachKeyboard` returns the function that removes its listeners.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:491-499` (the typing filter, `preventDefault` on bound keys, `repeat`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * const target = new EventTarget();\\n * const presses: string[] = [];\\n * const sink = { press: (code: string) => presses.push(code), release() {}, analog() {}, used() {}, bound: () => true };\\n * const detach = attachKeyboard(target, sink);\\n * target.dispatchEvent(Object.assign(new Event('keydown'), { code: 'KeyW', repeat: false }));\\n * target.dispatchEvent(Object.assign(new Event('keydown'), { code: 'KeyW', repeat: true })); // auto-repeat: ignored\\n * presses; // ['KeyW']\\n * detach();\\n * @see engine/input/devices/devices.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { deviceOf, type InputSink } from '../codes';\\n\\n/** The fields of a key event the device reads. */\\ninterface KeyEventLike extends Event {\\n  readonly code: string;\\n  readonly repeat?: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/** Input types whose element still lets keys through to the game (no text goes into them). */\\nconst NOT_TYPING = new Set(['range', 'checkbox', 'radio', 'button', 'submit', 'reset', 'color', 'file', 'image']);\\n\\n/** Whether a key event's target is somewhere the player types. */\\nexport function isTyping(target: EventTarget | null): boolean {\\n  const element = target as { tagName?: string; type?: string; isContentEditable?: boolean } | null;\\n  if (!element?.tagName) return false;\\n  const tag = element.tagName.toUpperCase();\\n  if (tag === 'TEXTAREA' || tag === 'SELECT' || element.isContentEditable) return true;\\n  return tag === 'INPUT' && !NOT_TYPING.has((element.type ?? 'text').toLowerCase());\\n}\\n\\n/** Listens for keys on `target` (the window) and writes them to `sink`; returns the detach function. */\\nexport function attachKeyboard(target: EventTarget, sink: InputSink): () => void {\\n  const down = (event: Event) => {\\n    const { code, repeat } = event as KeyEventLike;\\n    if (!code || deviceOf(code) !== 'keyboard' || isTyping(event.target)) return;\\n    if (sink.bound(code)) event.preventDefault();\\n    if (!repeat) sink.press(code, 'keyboard');\\n  };\\n  const up = (event: Event) => {\\n    const { code } = event as KeyEventLike;\\n    if (code) sink.release(code);\\n  };\\n  target.addEventListener('keydown', down);\\n  target.addEventListener('keyup', up);\\n  return () => {\\n    target.removeEventListener('keydown', down);\\n    target.removeEventListener('keyup', up);\\n  };\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":61}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"5d140b82-975d-4ec0-9719-7315ab0cff2a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_698","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The engine keyboard listener uses the bubble phase, not capture.\n\nStage's listener uses capture phase. It should fire before the engine records keys. It might return early. The source code has the listener. The running page might be stale.\n\nTiming data confirms stage's keydown never fired. If it had, attract would appear about ten seconds after the keypress rather than five. The init script listener definitely ran because Enter is present in keys. Stage's capture listener was not added, or it was added too late.\n\nThe listener is unconditional inside the stage factory, so it should exist if createStage ran. A realm mismatch is unlikely. I will probe the page to verify whether the listener is actually registered.\n\nI realized I never printed glyphSet, so I cannot confirm whether noteDevice ran. The attract timing proves lastInput was not reset, which means noteDevice definitely did not execute. Playwright does not set metaKey, and the event object is identical, so those are not the cause. I just had a sudden realization.\n\nThe init script runs in the page context, so it shares the window object. The stage listener does not check event.isTrusted. I will re-read the current stage.ts keydown block from disk and search the page for stopImmediatePropagation.\n\nThe \"Begin\" button might be intercepting the Enter key and triggering a click instead of letting the keydown reach the stage listener. I will inspect createMenu and the accept handler to see how the button processes the key.\n\nI considered whether a connected gamepad suppresses keyboard input. The sink receives the keypress regardless, so the menu should still detect it. I also checked if the focused element is an input field; the menu buttons are not inputs, so isTyping remains false.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-02a387d4-64a5-4312-825c-785c0a79d