{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_699","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The grep missed the keydown listener in stage.ts because the code is formatted across multiple lines.\n\nThe keydown listener is confirmed in stage.ts. The engine has no stopImmediatePropagation, so the stage handler should run. The real question is why lastInput did not reset. I am re-reading noteDevice and the keydown handler to verify. I suspect the 10-second attract timer may be from boot time rather than the Enter press.\n\nThe 5.5-second gap between Enter and attract proves noteDevice never ran. The stage listener likely failed to attach or returned early before reaching noteDevice.\n\nThe stage is clearly active because the title menu rendered. The keydown listener sits before the return and should be attached unconditionally. A JavaScript error in that listener would have produced a console warning, but only a GFX_GOVERNOR message appeared. I will re-read lines 296-320 to inspect the handler.\n\nI am now checking whether the HTML bundle is stale and lacks the keydown listener. I will search for unique strings like \"KeyT\" or \"Controller or keyboard required\" in the minified output to confirm the handler is actually present.\n\nPlaywright dispatches Enter correctly, and window capture should receive the event even inside a shadow root. I considered injecting a debug hook into EventTarget.prototype.addEventListener to inspect the listener chain, but that is too late because listeners are already registered.\n\nI will inject a synthetic KeyboardEvent via page.evaluate to test whether the stage listener fires. If glyphSet changes, the listener works for synthetic events. Playwright's Enter event is trusted, so if the synthetic one succeeds, the real event should too.\n\nI will patch the trace to override window.addEventListener and count capture listeners after the game is ready. I will also dispatch a synthetic KeyF event via page.evaluate to test whether the stage listener fires.\n\nThe listener-probe idea is abandoned because it would only reveal the new listeners. I will instead read glyphSet and lastDevice after Enter to confirm whether noteDevice ran. I am also preparing a synthetic keyboard dispatch from page.evaluate.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-572a7195-14e0-477c-b6e6-2bd6ef58edc3-85","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"KeyT","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656.html"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1489,"output_tokens":1302,"cache_read_input_tokens":123136,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"8fc489b2-9cd3-49e3-8eed-577cfd1c968e"}
