8,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":6,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/stage.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":91,\"content\":\"  let lastDevice = 'gamepad';\"},{\"line_number\":262,\"content\":\"  const noteDevice = (device: string) => {\"},{\"line_number\":305,\"content\":\"      noteDevice('keyboard');\"},{\"line_number\":322,\"content\":\"      noteDevice('mouse');\"},{\"line_number\":339,\"content\":\"        noteDevice('mouse');\"},{\"line_number\":421,\"content\":\"      noteDevice('gamepad');\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"07559838-e8a6-4ac3-b518-651b5f7fcaed"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_703","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"lastDevice starts as 'gamepad'.\n\nBoot shows gamepad before any input because glyphSet defaults to playstation. If Enter's noteDevice had run, glyph would have become keys and stayed there. The attract timing suggests noteDevice never fired. I'll add timestamps to the script and poll glyphSet to verify.\n\nThe menu's accept input path should still register Enter regardless of the last device. The title screen stayed for over five seconds, so the key was likely not recorded in the sink. Other possibilities include the menu not detecting the press or the screen changing and reverting before each sample.\n\nA throw during game.begin before the screen changes to play would leave the title screen in place. The trace shows no errors, so this is not the cause.\n\nA silent failure during game.begin that sets the screen to play and then immediately reverts it would also leave the title visible. No such code path exists.\n\nThe keyboard event likely reached the window listener but was blocked by the engine sink's isTyping check on the event target.\n\nThe stage listener runs during the capture phase, before the event reaches the target. It is not blocked by the engine sink's isTyping check. The stage listener should still fire and noteDevice regardless of which element is focused.\n\nThe 5.5-second gap between the Enter press and the attract screen appearing is inconsistent with a keys device. If noteDevice had fired, the attract timer would have started from that moment rather than from boot. This confirms glyphSet must still be playstation. I will verify this by printing the value.\n\nI will mark the exact moment before pressing Enter using `performance.now()`. A requestAnimationFrame callback inside the page will record when the attract screen flips. I will also log glyphSet and a flag from within the page to verify what happened.\n\nI will add a capture listener before pressing Enter to set a flag and read glyphSet after a rAF. I will also print the event target's outerHTML snippet.\n\nThe script's init listener will store target info. Each sample will print glyphSet, time since the mark, and time since ready.\n\nIf glyph becomes keys, noteDevice works and the menu is the problem. If it stays playstation, the stage listener did not run.\n\nA minification bug with the comma expression might be short-circuiting the event handler.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1bdc5917-02f0-4fd7-a77e-ca48f16813df-89","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"createElement|contentEditable|button","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/ui/menu.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":732,"output_tokens":1198,"cache_read_input_tokens":128384,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"b50fdf75-9a15-480c-8fc6-81aa6f07a007"}
