{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_712","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reviewing the sample() function in JavaScript.\n\nGamepad polling runs before keyboard taps. The fake pad stays connected with all buttons off. Enter and Space register as uiAccept presses. release() returns waiting codes to the taps set.\n\nrelease() does not remove codes from taps. A tap persists until sample() clears the set at the end of each frame. The concern is that Playwright's keyboard.press may trigger a blur or focus cycle, which could clear taps after keydown but before sample() runs.\n\nA blur event during keyboard.press would clear the taps set before the next sample, causing a missed uiAccept press. Play-debug worked once, possibly because blur did not fire or the page was fast enough to sample between keydown and blur.\n\nenter-trace and browse both failed. The screenshot step may leave the page blurred. That would clear taps before Enter is pressed.\n\nKeyDown still fires while the page is blurred, so a blur during keyboard.press should not prevent the tap from being recorded. The next sample should then detect it. A permanently blurred page or a visibilitychange loop seems unlikely. The focus is shifting to whether gamepad polling clears taps every frame.\n\nChecking if missing gamepad buttons are treated as keyboard releases. Enter is not a hold code. The menu reads pressedNow during sample, and its frame callback runs after that. If Enter arrives after the current sample, the next frame catches it. Many frames passed, so timing is unlikely to blame.\n\nThe game loop is confirmed running. Attract mode started at sample 10 in the first trace, and the second trace ran for seven seconds without errors. The menu updates every frame, so Enter should have been consumed on the next sample. The suspicion now shifts to whether the synthetic KeyF event reached the engine sink.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8f65a173-11ee-4d09-b108-eb342e74bce8-101","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/codes.ts","offset":80,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8f65a173-11ee-4d09-b108-eb342e74bce8-102","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/devices/gamepad.ts","offset":50,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2243,"output_tokens":1240,"cache_read_input_tokens":138752,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"1e130f8b-9a30-4932-871a-561de841a9e8"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8f65a173-11ee-4d09-b108-eb342e74bce8-101","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"80→  'PadLeftStickUp',\\n  'PadLeftStickDown',\\n  'PadLeftStickLeft',\\n  'PadLeftStickRight',\\n  'PadRightStickUp',\\n  'PadRightStickDown',\\n  'PadRightStickLeft',\\n  'PadRightStickRight',\\n] as const;\\n\\n90→/** Mouse buttons by `MouseEvent.button` (0 left, 1 middle, 2 right, 3 back, 4 forward). */\\nexport const MOUSE_BUTTONS = ['MouseLeft', 'MouseMiddle', 'MouseRight', 'MouseBack', 'MouseForward'] as const;\\n\\n/** The wheel's codes: a notch is a tap, never held. */\\nexport const WHEEL_CODES = ['WheelUp', 'WheelDown'] as const;\\n\\n/** `KeyboardEvent.code` values a binding may name. */\\nconst KEY =\\n  /^(Key[A-Z]|Digit[0-9]|Numpad([0-9]|Add|Subtract|Multiply|Divide|Decimal|Enter)|F([1-9]|1[0-9]|2[0-4])|Arrow(Up|Down|Left|Right)|(Shift|Control|Alt|Meta)(Left|Right)|Space|Enter|Tab|Escape|Backspace|Backquote|Minus|Equal|Bracket(Left|Right)|Backslash|Semicolon|Quote|Comma|Period|Slash|CapsLock|Insert|Delete|Home|End|PageUp|PageDown|ContextMenu|IntlBackslash)$/;\\n\\n100→/** Every non-keyboard code. */\\nconst OTHER: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set([...PAD_BUTTONS, ...PAD_STICKS, ...MOUSE_BUTTONS, ...WHEEL_CODES]);\\n\\n/** The prefix of a held binding: `Hold:PadWest` is X kept down `HOLD_TIME` (see the file comment). */\\nexport const HOLD_PREFIX = 'Hold:';\\n\\n/** How long a held binding's code stays down before its action presses, s (ours); let go sooner, it is a tap. */\\nexport const HOLD_TIME = 0.3;\\n\\n/** The held binding of `code`: `holdCode('PadWest')` is `Hold:PadWest`. */\\n110→export function holdCode(code: string): string {\\n  return `${HOLD_PREFIX}${code}`;\\n}\\n\\n/** The code a held binding waits on (`Hold:PadWest` → `PadWest`), or null for any other code. */\\nexport function heldBase(code: string): string | null {\\n  return code.startsWith(HOLD_PREFIX) ? code.slice(HOLD_PREFIX.length) : null;\\n}\\n\\n/** The digital codes a held binding may wait on: keys, mouse buttons and pad buttons, never a notch or a stick. */\\n120→const HOLDABLE: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set<string>([...PAD_BUTTONS, ...MOUSE_BUTTONS]);\\n\\n/** Whether `code` is one a binding may name. */\\nexport function isCode(code: unknown): code is string {\\n  if (typeof code !== 'string') return false;\\n  const base = heldBase(code);\\n  if (base !== null) return HOLDABLE.has(base) || KEY.test(base);\\n  return OTHER.has(code) || KEY.test(code);\\n}\\n\\n130→/** The prefix of the codes touch buttons write: `touch:jump` is the jump button (`touchCode`). */\\nexport const TOUCH_PREFIX = 'touch:';\\n\\n/** The code a touch button for `action` writes; every action binds its own (engine/input/input.ts). */\\nexport function touchCode(action: string): string {\\n  return `${TOUCH_PREFIX}${action}`;\\n}\\n\\n/** The device a code belongs to. */\\nexport function deviceOf(code: string): Exclude<DeviceKind, 'virtual'> {\\n140→  const base = heldBase(code);\\n  if (base !== null) return deviceOf(base);\\n  if (code.startsWith(TOUCH_PREFIX)) return 'touch';\\n  if (code.startsWith('Pad')) return 'gamepad';\\n  return code.startsWith('Mouse') || code.startsWith('Wheel') ? 'mouse' : 'keyboard';\\n}\\n\\n/** Pad button labels per family, in `PAD_BUTTONS` order. */\\nconst PAD_LABELS: Record<PadStyle, readonly string[]> = {\\n  xbox: ['A', 'B', 'X', 'Y', 'LB', 'RB', 'LT', 'RT', 'View', 'Menu', 'LS', 'RS', 'D-pad Up', 'D-pad Down', 'D-pad Left', 'D-pad Right', 'Guide'], // prettier-ignore\\n150→  playstation: ['Cross', 'Circle', 'Square', 'Triangle', 'L1', 'R1', 'L2', 'R2', 'Create', 'Options', 'L3', 'R3', 'D-pad Up', 'D-pad Down', 'D-pad Left', 'D-pad Right', 'PS'], // prettier-ignore\\n  nintendo: ['B', 'A', 'Y', 'X', 'L', 'R', 'ZL', 'ZR', '−', '+', 'L Stick', 'R Stick', 'D-pad Up', 'D-pad Down', 'D-pad Left', 'D-pad Right', 'Home'], // prettier-ignore\\n};\\n\\n/** Labels of codes whose name says too little or too much. */\\nconst NAMED: Readonly<Record<string, string>> = {\\n  MouseLeft: 'LMB',\\n  MouseMiddle: 'MMB',\\n  MouseRight: 'RMB',\\n  MouseBack: 'Mouse 4',\",\"content_concise\":\"80→  'PadLeftStickUp',\\n  'PadLeftStickDown',\\n  'PadLeftStickLeft',\\n  'PadLeftStickRight',\\n  'PadRightStickUp',\\n  'PadRightStickDown',\\n  'PadRightStickLeft',\\n  'PadRightStickRight',\\n] as const;\\n\\n90→/** Mouse buttons by `MouseEvent.button` (0 left, 1 middle, 2 right, 3 back, 4 forward). */\\nexport const MOUSE_BUTTONS = ['MouseLeft', 'MouseMiddle', 'MouseRight', 'MouseBack', 'MouseForward'] as const;\\n\\n/** The wheel's codes: a notch is a tap, never held. */\\nexport const WHEEL_CODES = ['WheelUp', 'WheelDown'] as const;\\n\\n/** `KeyboardEvent.code` values a binding may name. */\\nconst KEY =\\n  /^(Key[A-Z]|Digit[0-9]|Numpad([0-9]|Add|Subtract|Multiply|Divide|Decimal|Enter)|F([1-9]|1[0-9]|2[0-4])|Arrow(Up|Down|Left|Right)|(Shift|Control|Alt|Meta)(Left|Right)|Space|Enter|Tab|Escape|Backspace|Backquote|Minus|Equal|Bracket(Left|Right)|Backslash|Semicolon|Quote|Comma|Period|Slash|CapsLock|Insert|Delete|Home|End|PageUp|PageDown|ContextMenu|IntlBackslash)$/;\\n\\n100→/** Every non-keyboard code. */\\nconst OTHER: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set([...PAD_BUTTONS, ...PAD_STICKS, ...MOUSE_BUTTONS, ...WHEEL_CODES]);\\n\\n/** The prefix of a held binding: `Hold:PadWest` is X kept down `HOLD_TIME` (see the file comment). */\\nexport const HOLD_PREFIX = 'Hold:';\\n\\n/** How long a held binding's code stays down before its action presses, s (ours); let go sooner, it is a tap. */\\nexport const HOLD_TIME = 0.3;\\n\\n/** The held binding of `code`: `holdCode('PadWest')` is `Hold:PadWest`. */\\n110→export function holdCode(code: string): string {\\n  return `${HOLD_PREFIX}${code}`;\\n}\\n\\n/** The code a held binding waits on (`Hold:PadWest` → `PadWest`), or null for any other code. */\\nexport function heldBase(co