{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_715","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No stopPropagation calls were found in TypeScript or JavaScript files.\n\nPlaywright's keyboard events likely bubble through the DOM. The window capture listener already received them, so nothing in our code stops propagation. The engine's bubble listener should run unless Playwright dispatches the event at the window during capture only.\n\nThe event is confirmed to be a real bubbling keydown targeted at the body. The engine should fire sink.press('Enter') because the target is not a text input. I will monkeypatch EventTarget.prototype.addEventListener in the init script to log keydown events before the page loads.\n\nThe monkeypatch wraps every keydown listener to record the event target and code in a global array before the original handler runs.\n\nThe monkeypatch will be placed first in the init script so it wraps all keydown listeners, including our own. If the engine listener appears in the logs, the sink received the key and the bug is elsewhere. I will update the init script and rerun without synthetic input to keep the test clean.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f08fd8d6-8651-4c34-a482-c28bbbbdb30d-105","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/enter-trace.py","old_string":"PAD = \"\"\"\nwindow.__buttons = new Array(16).fill(0);\nwindow.__axes = [0, 0, 0, 0];\nwindow.__keys = [];\nwindow.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => window.__keys.push({\n  code: event.code, meta: event.metaKey, ctrl: event.ctrlKey, alt: event.altKey,\n  trusted: event.isTrusted, tag: event.target && event.target.tagName, type: event.target && event.target.type,\n}), true);\nnavigator.getGamepads = () => [{","new_string":"PAD = \"\"\"\nwindow.__buttons = new Array(16).fill(0);\nwindow.__axes = [0, 0, 0, 0];\nwindow.__listeners = [];\nconst origAdd = EventTarget.prototype.addEventListener;\nEventTarget.prototype.addEventListener = function (type, fn, opts) {\n  if (type === 'keydown' && typeof fn === 'function') {\n    const wrapped = function (event) {\n      const where = this === window ? 'win' : this === document ? 'doc' : (this && this.tagName) || 'other';\n      window.__listeners.push(where + ':' + (event.code || '') + ':phase' + event.eventPhase);\n      return fn.call(this, event);\n    };\n    return origAdd.call(this, type, wrapped, opts);\n  }\n  return origAdd.call(this, type, fn, opts);\n};\nnavigator.getGamepads = () => [{"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f08fd8d6-8651-4c34-a482-c28bbbbdb30d-106","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/enter-trace.py","old_string":"    synth = page.evaluate(\n        \"\"\"() => {\n          const before = window.__game.glyphSet;\n          window.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('keydown', { code: 'KeyF', key: 'f', bubbles: true, cancelable: true }));\n          return { before, after: window.__game.glyphSet, device: window.__game.lastDevice };\n        }\"\"\"\n    )\n    print(\"synth\", synth)\n    page.evaluate(\"() => { window.__t0 = performance.now(); }\")\n    page.keyboard.press(\"Enter\")\n    for i in range(8):\n        page.wait_for_timeout(400)\n        state = page.evaluate(\n            \"\"\"() => ({\n              dt: Math.round(performance.now() - window.__t0),\n              screen: window.__game && window.__game.screen,\n              focus: window.__game && window.__game.focus,\n              glyph: window.__game && window.__game.glyphSet,\n              device: window.__game && window.__game.lastDevice,\n              attract: window.__game && window.__game.attract,\n              errors: (window.__engine && window.__engine.errors || []).map((row) => row.message || row.code || row),\n              keys: window.__keys,\n              active: document.activeElement && document.activeElement.tagName,\n            })\"\"\"\n        )\n        print(i, state)\n        if state[\"screen\"] == \"play\" and not state[\"errors\"]:\n            break","new_string":"    page.keyboard.down(\"Enter\")\n    for i in range(6):\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\n        state = page.evaluate(\n            \"\"\"() => ({\n              screen: window.__game && window.__game.screen,\n              focus: window.__game && window.__game.focus,\n              glyph: window.__game && window.__game.glyphSet,\n              attract: window.__game && window.__game.attract,\n              errors: (window.__engine && window.__engine.errors || []).length,\n              listeners: window.__listeners.slice(-8),\n            })\"\"\"\n        )\n        print(i, state)\n        if state[\"screen\"] == \"play\":\n            break\n    page.keyboard.up(\"Enter\")"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1666,"output_tokens":1569,"cache_read_input_tokens":145664,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"e01e09fb-3150-4f4c-ba33-f5dfcb3e13ba"}
