{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_720","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A bug was spotted in the `codesOf` function.\n\nThe retreat action map defines `forward`, `back`, `left`, and `right` as game actions. These do not overwrite the UI navigation actions `uiUp`, `uiDown`, etc.\n\nShared keycodes between game and UI actions are harmless. Enter is bound to both `act` and `uiAccept`, so pressing it triggers both actions simultaneously. The `gated` function builds its held set from `heldBase`.\n\n`heldBase` only returns held codes for keys prefixed with `Hold:`, so Enter is not gated. The menu receives the real engine input object, not a stale stub. A new realization is forming.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8a48729e-b3c4-4726-8f57-31ad212c03ce-112","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/ui/menu.ts","offset":90,"limit":55}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1896,"output_tokens":612,"cache_read_input_tokens":152064,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"ca981500-edc7-497c-8273-d73c927cd578"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8a48729e-b3c4-4726-8f57-31ad212c03ce-112","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"90→  widgetStyle(parent.ownerDocument);\\n  const { input, sound = () => {} } = options;\\n  const el = uiElement(parent, 'ui-panel ui-menu', 'menu', options.id);\\n  el.dataset.place = options.place ?? 'center';\\n  if (options.title) el.append(Object.assign(uiElement(el, 'ui-menu-title', 'menu-title'), { textContent: options.title })); // prettier-ignore\\n  parent.append(el);\\n  const repeat = createRepeat();\\n  let list: MenuItem[] = [];\\n  let rows: HTMLElement[] = [];\\n  let index = 0;\\n100→\\n  /** `index` stepped by `dir` until an enabled item (or all the way round). */\\n  const skip = (from: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\\n    let at = from;\\n    for (let k = 0; k < list.length && off(list[at]); k++) at = (at + dir + list.length) % list.length;\\n    return at;\\n  };\\n  const draw = () => {\\n    if (el.dataset.value !== String(index)) el.dataset.value = String(index);\\n    rows.forEach((row, i) => {\\n110→      const value = off(list[i]) ? 'disabled' : i === index ? 'selected' : '';\\n      if (row.dataset.value !== value) row.dataset.value = value;\\n    });\\n  };\\n  const move = (to: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\\n    if (!list.length) return;\\n    const next = skip(((to % list.length) + list.length) % list.length, dir);\\n    if (next === index) return;\\n    index = next;\\n    sound('move');\\n120→    draw();\\n    options.onMove?.(index, list[index]);\\n  };\\n  const pick = () => {\\n    const item = list[index];\\n    if (item === undefined || off(item)) return false;\\n    sound('pick');\\n    if (typeof item === 'object' && item.id !== undefined) options.send?.(item.id);\\n    options.onPick?.(index, item);\\n    return true;\\n130→  };\\n  const setItems = (next: readonly MenuItem[]) => {\\n    for (const item of next) {\\n      const ok =\\n        typeof item === 'string' || (typeof item === 'object' && item !== null && typeof item.label === 'string');\\n      if (!ok) throw codeError('UI_BAD_MENU', { problem: `the item ${JSON.stringify(item)} is no string or { label }` }); // prettier-ignore\\n    }\\n    for (const row of rows) row.remove();\\n    list = [...next];\\n    rows = list.map((item, i) => {\\n140→      const row = uiElement(el, 'ui-menu-item', 'item', typeof item === 'object' && item.id !== undefined ? item.id : String(i)); // prettier-ignore\\n      row.dataset.index = String(i);\\n      setText(row, labelOf(item));\\n      row.addEventListener('pointermove', (event) => {\\n        const { movementX = 0, movementY = 0 } = event as PointerEvent; // a still pointer the page moved under moves none\",\"content_concise\":\"90→  widgetStyle(parent.ownerDocument);\\n  const { input, sound = () => {} } = options;\\n  const el = uiElement(parent, 'ui-panel ui-menu', 'menu', options.id);\\n  el.dataset.place = options.place ?? 'center';\\n  if (options.title) el.append(Object.assign(uiElement(el, 'ui-menu-title', 'menu-title'), { textContent: options.title })); // prettier-ignore\\n  parent.append(el);\\n  const repeat = createRepeat();\\n  let list: MenuItem[] = [];\\n  let rows: HTMLElement[] = [];\\n  let index = 0;\\n100→\\n  /** `index` stepped by `dir` until an enabled item (or all the way round). */\\n  const skip = (from: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\\n    let at = from;\\n    for (let k = 0; k < list.length && off(list[at]); k++) at = (at + dir + list.length) % list.length;\\n    return at;\\n  };\\n  const draw = () => {\\n    if (el.dataset.value !== String(index)) el.dataset.value = String(index);\\n    rows.forEach((row, i) => {\\n110→      const value = off(list[i]) ? 'disabled' : i === index ? 'selected' : '';\\n      if (row.dataset.value !== value) row.dataset.value = value;\\n    });\\n  };\\n  const move = (to: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\\n    if (!list.length) return;\\n    const next = skip(((to % list.length) + list.length) % list.length, dir);\\n    if (next === index) return;\\n    index = next;\\n    sound('move');\\n120→    draw();\\n    options.onMove?.(index, list[index]);\\n  };\\n  const pick = () => {\\n    const item = list[index];\\n    if (item === undefined || off(item)) return false;\\n    sound('pick');\\n    if (typeof item === 'object' && item.id !== undefined) options.send?.(item.id);\\n    options.onPick?.(index, item);\\n    return true;\\n130→  };\\n  const setItems = (next: readonly MenuItem[]) => {\\n    for (const item of next) {\\n      const ok =\\n        typeof item === 'string' || (typeof item === 'object' && item !== null && typeof item.label === 'string');\\n      if (!ok) throw codeError('UI_BAD_MENU', { problem: `the item ${JSON.stringify(item)} is no string or { label }` }); // prettier-ignore\\n    }\\n    for (const row of rows) row.remove();\\n    list = [...next];\\n    rows = list.map((item, i) => {\\n140→      const row = uiElement(el, 'ui-menu-item', 'item', typeof item === 'object' && item.id !== undefined ? item.id : String(i)); // prettier-ignore\\n      row.dataset.index = String(i);\\n      setText(row, labelOf(item));\\n      row.addEventListener('pointermove', (event) => {\\n        const { movementX = 0, movementY = 0 } = event as PointerEvent; // a still pointer the page moved under moves none\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/ui/menu.ts\",\"offset\":90,\"limit\":55,\"raw_output\":\"  widgetStyle(parent.ownerDocument);\\n  const { input, sound = () => {} } = options;\\n  const el = uiElement(parent, 'ui-panel ui-menu', 'menu', options.id);\\n  el.dataset.place = options.place ?? 'center';\\n  if (options.title) el.append(Object.assign(uiElement(el, 'ui-menu-title', 'menu-title'), { textContent: options.title })); // prettier-ignore\\n  parent.append(el);\\n  const repeat = createRepeat();\\n  let list: MenuItem[] = [];\\n  let rows: HTMLElement[] = [];\\n  let index = 0;\\n\\n  /** `index` stepped by `dir` until an enabled item (or all the way round). */\\n  const skip = (from: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\\n    let at = from;\\n    for (let k = 0; k < list.length && off(list[at]); k++) at = (at + dir + list.length) % list.length;\\n    return at;\\n  };\\n  const draw = () => {\\n    if (el.dataset.value !== String(index)) el.dataset.value = String(index);\\n    rows.forEach((row, i) => {\\n      const value = off(list[i]) ? 'disabled' : i === index ? 'selected' : '';\\n      if (row.dataset.value !== value) row.dataset.value = value;\\n    });\\n  };\\n  const move = (to: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\\n    if (!list.length) return;\\n    const next = skip(((to % list.length) + list.length) % list.length, dir);\\n    if (next === index) return;\\n    index = next;\\n    sound('move');\\n    draw();\\n    options.onMove?.(index, list[index]);\\n  };\\n  const pick = () => {\\n    const item = list[index];\\n    if (item === undefined || off(item)) return false;\\n    sound('pick');\\n    if (typeof item === 'object' && item.id !== undefined) options.send?.(item.id);\\n    options.onPick?.(index, item);\\n    return true;\\n  };\\n  const setItems = (next: readonly MenuItem[]) => {\\n    for (const item of next) {\\n      const ok =\\n        typeof item === 'string' || (typeof item === 'object' && item !== null && typeof item.label === 'string');\\n      if (!ok) throw codeError('UI_BAD_MENU', { problem: `the item ${JSON.stringify(item)} is no string or { label }` }); // prettier-ignore\\n    }\\n    for (const row of rows) row.remove();\\n    list = [...next];\\n    rows = list.map((item, i) => {\\n      const row = uiElement(el, 'ui-menu-item', 'item', typeof item === 'object' && item.id !== undefined ? item.id : String(i)); // prettier-ignore\\n      row.dataset.index = String(i);\\n      setText(row, labelOf(item));\\n      row.addEventListener('pointermove', (event) => {\\n        const { movementX = 0, movementY = 0 } = event as PointerEvent; // a still pointer the page moved under moves none\\n\",\"total_lines\":187}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"841bf96b-df00-4b24-b8f1-120ed01855a1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_721","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `onPick` function is being called. The `pickTitle` for \"begin\" should set the screen to play.\n\nA frame-order bug with held keyboard input is suspected. The menu's `update` call appears correct.\n\nThe held-keyboard theory is ruled out. If the menu had updated on that frame, the screen would be play. It remains title instead. The pick() edge must have failed to fire.\n\nThe menu variable might be null. The visible focus on Begin could be stale from the last publish. If the menu were closed, focus would remain stuck on Begin while the screen stays title.\n\nThe menu object is always truthy, so a null menu is not the cause. I will patch frame() to record pressed state, menu presence, and screen into a ring buffer each frame. Rebuilding and tracing in Chrome should reveal the exact failure. Keyboard auto-repeat might also be interfering.\n\nThe engine ignores repeat events for sink presses. The first keydown should have registered as a press. The glyph changed, so the stage handler ran. The bubble listener also completed without throwing an error, confirming it reached the sink.\n\nI will update the wrapper to log each listener's source code snippet. This avoids a rebuild and should reveal whether the bubble handler contains sink.press or repeat logic.\n\nThe minified sink function is the `down` handler. It checks `repeat` and calls `sink.press`. I will log 180 characters of each listener body. I will also log `event.repeat`, `isTrusted`, and `event.target` to check for typing interference.\n\nThe trace shows only one keydown event. The listener array length stays at three, so Playwright did not send a repeat event. The engine's repeat guard is not the cause.\n\nThe stage listener does not check `repeat`, so the glyph changed even if Playwright sent a repeated keydown. This matches the observed behavior: the glyph updated but the menu never accepted the input. The engine's `sink` ignores repeat events, which would prevent the press from registering. The trace still needs to log `event.repeat` to confirm this.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9e6b7299-8e80-4dd9-b5c8-48823cec3495-113","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/enter-trace.py","old_string":"      window.__listeners.push(where + ':' + (event.code || '') + ':phase' + event.eventPhase);","new_string":"      window.__listeners.push(where + ':' + (event.code || '') + ':phase' + event.eventPhase + ':repeat' + event.repeat);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9e6b7299-8e80-4dd9-b5c8-48823cec3495-114","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/enter-trace.py","old_string":"    page.keyboard.up(\"Enter\")","new_string":"    page.keyboard.up(\"Enter\")\n    page.wait_for_timeout(200)\n    manual = page.evaluate(\n        \"\"\"() => {\n          window.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('keydown', { code: 'Enter', key: 'Enter', bubbles: true, cancelable: true, repeat: false }));\n          return window.__listeners.slice(-4);\n        }\"\"\"\n    )\n    print(\"manual listeners\", manual)\n    page.wait_for_timeout(800)\n    print(\"after manual\", page.evaluate(\"() => ({ screen: window.__game.screen, focus: window.__game.focus, errors: window.__engine.errors.length })\"))"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1452,"output_tokens":1676,"cache_read_input_tokens":153856,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"a163b45a-5de9-45aa-a0de-92d38ad96acc"}
