Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/input.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":23,\"content\":\" * nothing stays held after alt-tab; a gamepad that disconnects lets go of its own. `listen(device)` serves rebinding.\"},{\"line_number\":138,\"content\":\"  listen(device: 'keyboard' | 'gamepad'): Promise<string | null>;\"},{\"line_number\":375,\"content\":\"    listen(device) {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"e68d06c9-b9aa-4b74-ab01-b52985d0ac05"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_734","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Listen is only triggered during controls rebind.\n\nAdding debug to check pressed state at frame time. The menu likely misses held input because pressed never triggers on draw frames, or the screen reverts after pick.\n\nThe multi-sample theory explains the held-key bug. If the loop samples twice before each draw, the first sample registers the edge and sets pressed true. The second sample sees the key is already held, so it clears pressed to false. The menu therefore sees pressed as false on every draw frame during a hold.\n\nThe loop is running slow, so it double-steps during catch-up and the menu misses every edge. The same bug would affect gamepad input. The fix must either let the menu see a held key across catch-up samples or stop the loop from dropping edges.\n\nThe fix is to track the held state across frames. When `uiAccept` is held but was not held on the previous drawn frame, the menu should pick. This lets the menu register a press even when the raw pressed flag drops during catch-up sampling.\n\nThe held-state fix works for simple menu closes, but settings toggles risk double action. If pick() spawns a new menu, the next update sees pressed and selects that new menu's first item too. Only begin avoids this because close() nulls the menu.\n\nThe held-edge fix still causes double action on settings toggles. When pick() spawns a new menu, the next update sees pressed and toggles the first item too. Updating before picking is hard because there is no way to tell if the update already acted. The current idea is to pick from held-edge before update, but this risks the same double action.\n\nA swallowed flag cannot block the menu's own update from checking pressed. Clearing all input would be too broad. The better approach is to wrap menu.update so it detects held-edge presses internally, using a local acceptHeld variable to track state across frames.\n\nThe held-edge fix is being implemented by checking `held && !was` before calling `menu.update`. If the accept key is held but was not held on the previous frame, the code picks immediately and skips update entirely. This prevents double action on settings toggles because the menu's own update loop will not see the edge again once the held flag is set.\n\nThe held-edge fix avoids double picks because menu repeat only applies to up and down, not accept. However, a tap that releases before the first draw is still lost. If the frame is slow, the entire press and release happen before the next draw, so held and pressed both read false and the edge is missed.\n\nThe engine should not be modified. The browse menu should use a held button instead of a quick tap, so the edge is detected on the draw frame.\n\nThe engine's tap set preserves the key after release, so a fully completed press can still register on the next draw. The game must therefore treat held input as an edge on the drawn frame.\n\nThe engine's tap set clears after the first sample, so a second sample sees no taps and pressed becomes false. A held key is equally lost because its edge only registers on the first sample. The menu therefore misses both quick taps and held keys when multiple samples occur before it reads input.\n\nThe shell's pad_down already holds the button until focus changes, so the page fix is needed to keep those holds working when the loop is slow. The implementation plan starts by tracking acceptHeld in the stage frame.\n\nThe implementation now checks `held('uiAccept')` before calling `menu.update`. If the accept key is held but was not held on the previous frame, it picks immediately and skips update entirely. This prevents the menu from picking again on the same frame when the raw pressed flag is still true.\n\nThe held-edge fix is refined to avoid double picks. The code now checks `held && !was` before picking, but only if the raw `pressed` flag is false. This prevents an extra pick on the fast path where the menu's own update loop would otherwise select again.\n\nThe held-edge fix works for Begin. The menu closes cleanly on both fast and slow paths. Navigation via uiDown is unaffected because the menu's repeat logic already checks held() internally.\n\nThe menu's repeat logic has a 0.35-second delay before it fires. If the press edge is missed on the first draw, the timer starts at zero and the first frame does not move. The pad_down helper already waits until focus changes, so the repeat will eventually fire once the delay expires.\n\nThe menu's repeat function uses a 0.35-second delay before firing, so missed d-pad edges still trigger after about 350 milliseconds. Accept buttons do not repeat at all, so a missed edge on uiAccept or PadSouth is permanently lost. This explains why Enter and button 0 fail when frames are slow, while the d-pad may still work once the delay expires.\n\nThe fix requires two changes. The page must pick from a held accept edge even when the raw pressed flag is false. The browse script should hold Enter down until the screen changes instead of using a zero-delay press.\n\nThe shell's final Enter and Escape presses also need to be held until the screen changes. Escape is a short press, so it would fail under load just like Enter. The page fix should apply to uiCancel as well, not just uiAccept.\n\nThe page fix will handle both uiAccept and uiCancel held-edges. However, the menu object does not expose a public cancel method, so the Escape key cannot be triggered from the stage frame.\n\nA held Escape key is also lost if its first sample is not drawn, so a cancel path is still needed. The page can call the menu's internal `onCancel` handler directly through the `cancelMenu` closure it already stores, avoiding any engine changes.\n\nThe page will store the menu's internal `onCancel` handler in a `cancelMenu` closure. During the frame loop, if `uiCancel` is held but was not held on the previous frame and the raw `pressed` flag is false, it calls `cancelMenu` directly. The `!input.pressed('uiCancel')` guard prevents double cancellation when the raw pressed flag is still true.\n\nThe title menu omits an onCancel handler, so Escape does nothing there. The settings menu passes backFromSettings, which the page can use for cancellation. Space is mapped to uiAccept, so holding it will pick the menu. Gamepad PadSouth also stays held across frames even if its initial edge is overwritten, because the sample set preserves the down state.\n\nThe edge condition fires once per drawn hold, so it handles both the pad-down helper and a held Enter key. The browse script will use the existing `hold()` helper for button 0 instead of a quick press, because the helper is defined after `once()` in the file.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-510af04d-6eff-4290-9e33-76d358c3a499-129","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/tools/browse.py","offset":250,"limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-510af04d-6eff-4290-9e33-76d358c3a499-130","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/stage.ts","offset":145,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":978,"output_tokens":4017,"cache_read_input_tokens":172544,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"6fe42b61-f6d7-4639-ab36-aa70eb565b6b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-510af04d-6eff-4290-9e33-76d358c3a499-129","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"250→        if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\"):\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract stayed after a click\\\")\\n        else:\\n            trace.append(\\\"attract left on a click\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(10500)\\n        hold(page, 0, \\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.attract === false\\\")\\n        if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\"):\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract stayed after a pad press\\\")\\n        else:\\n            trace.append(\\\"attract left on a pad press\\\")\\n260→        save_after = page.evaluate(\\\"() => localStorage.getItem('thumb-yoga:save')\\\")\\n        trace.append(\\\"save unchanged\\\" if save_before == save_after else \\\"save changed\\\")\\n        if save_before != save_after:\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract wrote the save\\\")\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"Enter\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__game.screen === 'play'\\\", timeout=10000)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(500)\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"island.png\\\"))\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"Escape\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n270→        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"pause.png\\\"))\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=more]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=dev]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"dev.png\\\"))\\n        changed = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const range = document.querySelector('[data-ui=slider-range]');\\n              const before = window.__engine.state().settings['game.wobble.gain'];\",\"content_concise\":\"250→        if page.evaluate(\\\"