{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2001ebc0-bfef-4376-a47c-c45b2d08f52b-151","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"70→  island.tiltX = base;\\n  island.tiltZ = 0;\\n}\\n\\n/** Starts one activity. Setup runs now, so its spawned guests exist before the next step. */\\nexport function startEvent(w: World, id: string): void {\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const previous = findActivity(flow.event);\\n  if (previous && flow.mode === 'event') previous.teardown(w);\\n  const activity = activityById(id);\\n80→  const act = actOf(w);\\n  resetAct(act);\\n  const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n  resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n  flow.mode = 'event';\\n  flow.event = id;\\n  visit(flow, id);\\n  if (id.startsWith('pose')) visit(flow, 'pose');\\n  activity.setup(w);\\n}\\n90→\\n/** Scores the activity that just ended, then results, the next demo slice, or nothing for attract pebbles. */\\nfunction finishEvent(w: World, rank?: string): void {\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const activity = activityById(flow.event);\\n  let value = activity.score(w);\\n  activity.teardown(w);\\n  if (rank !== undefined && Object.hasOwn(RANK_SCORE, rank)) value = RANK_SCORE[rank] ?? value;\\n  value = clampScore(value);\\n  flow.result = value;\\n100→  flow.rank = rank !== undefined && Object.hasOwn(RANK_SCORE, rank) ? rank : rankOf(value);\\n  const auto = autoOf(w);\\n  if (auto !== 'attract') flow.pebbles += pebblesOf(flow.rank, Number(w.settings.get('game.pebbles.mult')));\\n  if (flow.event === 'morning') {\\n    flow.prior = flow.age;\\n    flow.age = wobbleAge(value / 1000, Number(w.settings.get('game.age.k')));\\n  }\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  act.done = 0;\\n  act.wait = 0;\\n110→  if (auto === 'attract') {\\n    const at = SLICES.indexOf(flow.event);\\n    startEvent(w, SLICES[(at + 1) % SLICES.length] ?? 'pose-a');\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  flow.mode = 'results';\\n}\\n\\n/** The next programme row, when the one that just finished is the row the cursor is on. */\\nfunction advance(w: World): void {\\n120→  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const list = programme();\\n  const here = list[flow.cursor];\\n  if (!here || here.event !== flow.event) {\\n    flow.mode = 'roam';\",\"content_concise\":\"70→  island.tiltX = base;\\n  island.tiltZ = 0;\\n}\\n\\n/** Starts one activity. Setup runs now, so its spawned guests exist before the next step. */\\nexport function startEvent(w: World, id: string): void {\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const previous = findActivity(flow.event);\\n  if (previous && flow.mode === 'event') previous.teardown(w);\\n  const activity = activityById(id);\\n80→  const act = actOf(w);\\n  resetAct(act);\\n  const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n  resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n  flow.mode = 'event';\\n  flow.event = id;\\n  visit(flow, id);\\n  if (id.startsWith('pose')) visit(flow, 'pose');\\n  activity.setup(w);\\n}\\n90→\\n/** Scores the activity that just ended, then results, the next demo slice, or nothing for attract pebbles. */\\nfunction finishEvent(w: World, rank?: string): void {\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const activity = activityById(flow.event);\\n  let value = activity.score(w);\\n  activity.teardown(w);\\n  if (rank !== undefined && Object.hasOwn(RANK_SCORE, rank)) value = RANK_SCORE[rank] ?? value;\\n  value = clampScore(value);\\n  flow.result = value;\\n100→  flow.rank = rank !== undefined && Object.hasOwn(RANK_SCORE, rank) ? rank : rankOf(value);\\n  const auto = autoOf(w);\\n  if (auto !== 'attract') flow.pebbles += pebblesOf(flow.rank, Number(w.settings.get('game.pebbles.mult')));\\n  if (flow.event === 'morning') {\\n    flow.prior = flow.age;\\n    flow.age = wobbleAge(value / 1000, Number(w.settings.get('game.age.k')));\\n  }\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  act.done = 0;\\n  act.wait = 0;\\n110→  if (auto === 'attract') {\\n    const at = SLICES.indexOf(flow.event);\\n    startEvent(w, SLICES[(at + 1) % SLICES.length] ?? 'pose-a');\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  flow.mode = 'results';\\n}\\n\\n/** The next programme row, when the one that just finished is the row the cursor is on. */\\nfunction advance(w: World): void {\\n120→  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const list = programme();\\n  const here = list[flow.cursor];\\n  if (!here || here.event !== flow.event) {\\n    flow.mode = 'roam';\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/driver.ts\",\"offset\":70,\"limit\":55,\"raw_output\":\"  island.tiltX = base;\\n  island.tiltZ = 0;\\n}\\n\\n/** Starts one activity. Setup runs now, so its spawned guests exist before the next step. */\\nexport function startEvent(w: World, id: string): void {\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const previous = findActivity(flow.event);\\n  if (previous && flow.mode === 'event') previous.teardown(w);\\n  const activity = activityById(id);\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  resetAct(act);\\n  const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n  resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n  flow.mode = 'event';\\n  flow.event = id;\\n  visit(flow, id);\\n  if (id.startsWith('pose')) visit(flow, 'pose');\\n  activity.setup(w);\\n}\\n\\n/** Scores the activity that just ended, then results, the next demo slice, or nothing for attract pebbles. */\\nfunction finishEvent(w: World, rank?: string): void {\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const activity = activityById(flow.event);\\n  let value = activity.score(w);\\n  activity.teardown(w);\\n  if (rank !== undefined && Object.hasOwn(RANK_SCORE, rank)) value = RANK_SCORE[rank] ?? value;\\n  value = clampScore(value);\\n  flow.result = value;\\n  flow.rank = rank !== undefined && Object.hasOwn(RANK_SCORE, rank) ? rank : rankOf(value);\\n  const auto = autoOf(w);\\n  if (auto !== 'attract') flow.pebbles += pebblesOf(flow.rank, Number(w.settings.get('game.pebbles.mult')));\\n  if (flow.event === 'morning') {\\n    flow.prior = flow.age;\\n    flow.age = wobbleAge(value / 1000, Number(w.settings.get('game.age.k')));\\n  }\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  act.done = 0;\\n  act.wait = 0;\\n  if (auto === 'attract') {\\n    const at = SLICES.indexOf(flow.event);\\n    startEvent(w, SLICES[(at + 1) % SLICES.length] ?? 'pose-a');\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  flow.mode = 'results';\\n}\\n\\n/** The next programme row, when the one that just finished is the row the cursor is on. */\\nfunction advance(w: World): void {\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const list = programme();\\n  const here = list[flow.cursor];\\n  if (!here || here.event !== flow.event) {\\n    flow.mode = 'roam';\\n\",\"total_lines\":345}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"62031fba-0cdd-4e3b-a502-6f0dfe9b75ef"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_748","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"startEvent sets flow.event to the event ID immediately.\n\nThe event field stayed empty after 1.2 seconds, so game.begin likely never ran or the main loop stopped. The comment says actions run between steps, but the loop may have halted silently after menu.pick() without error.\n\nThe empty event matches the state left by pickTitle. If the frame callback stopped after that, the screen would freeze at the old publish and never update.\n\nI will inspect the engine state directly to see if the flow component was ever updated. I plan to add a short test that prints the flow data from __engine.state() after the hold.\n\nThe script will check the engine state directly. If flow.event is morning, the simulation started but frames stopped publishing. If it is still empty or title, game.begin never applied.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c6930338-2e4d-43bc-a311-6450eb9e8287-152","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/hold-debug.py","old_string":"    state = page.evaluate(\n        \"\"\"() => ({\n          screen: window.__game.screen,\n          event: window.__game.event,\n          focus: window.__game.focus,\n          errors: (window.__engine.errors || []).map((row) => row.message || row.code || JSON.stringify(row)),\n        })\"\"\"\n    )","new_string":"    state = page.evaluate(\n        \"\"\"() => {\n          const entities = (window.__engine.state() && window.__engine.state().entities) || [];\n          const flow = entities.map((entity) => entity.flow).find(Boolean);\n          return {\n            screen: window.__game.screen,\n            event: window.__game.event,\n            focus: window.__game.focus,\n            flow,\n            errors: (window.__engine.errors || []).map((r