{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_780","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The clock pauses only on menu taps.\n\nPaused clock advance may still draw. I'll run a diagnostic using __engine.state().\n\nThe diagnostic plan is to boot, record ticks and rAF counts, press a button, then log state every 100ms for two seconds. Tick growth with empty events means onFrame isn't publishing snaps. A flat tick means the simulation isn't stepping.\n\nI traced the frame-by-frame execution while HOLD is active. The menu closes and screen switches to play, but menu.update is skipped because menu becomes null. The note stays on the prompt. The next frame should publish the morning snap.\n\nI suspect the snap query misses mutations because of how components are stored. `game.begin` mutates the live component object directly, but `copyValue` might not capture those changes if the fields are on a prototype or getters. I need to check whether `part()` or `flowOf` mutate a copy instead of the entity's actual component.\n\nState() confirms the live entity was mutated, so copyValue should capture the change. The empty event string likely means later frames never publish a new handle. I'm also checking whether audio.update throws when the song switches from lobby to stillness.\n\nThe empty errors array means the loop did not crash. The HTML bundle includes the hold-edge fix because the play screen loaded successfully. If the first frame keeps the lobby song active, audio.music will not throw.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-939f232d-3ffc-4568-a126-5f6c0e62bf42-46","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"music\\(id|function music|play\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/audio","glob":"*.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-939f232d-3ffc-4568-a126-5f6c0e62bf42-47","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"song: