{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_783","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm examining the engine's audio.\n\nI'll run a diagnostic browser script to check for audio errors, but first I'll verify memory usage to avoid an out-of-memory crash. While that runs, I'm also designing a robust page fix: re-read the world snapshot after input handling and menu updates, before painting, so any state changes from game.begin are captured.\n\nRe-reading the snapshot before paint fixes the one-frame lag. If paint throws, the event never publishes. The hold-debug log showed no errors, so a paint exception is unlikely.\n\nI'm now investigating why later frames read an empty event even though the world should contain morning. I ruled out double buffering and stale snapshots. The current hypothesis is unstable query order from multiple flow entities, since state() returns the first match.\n\nI'm now checking whether frozen entities lose the flow component during snapshot copying. I also verified that the page's query function returns fresh data, not stale cached results.\n\nI ruled out readSnap exceptions and schema stripping. The current suspicion is that the page's world object is a stale closure from EngineFrame, since drawing.ts captures it from session.run.parts.run.session.\n\nI'm now tracing whether the `session` getter on the AppHost object is actually returning fresh data or a stale snapshot. I need to verify if `createEngine` receives the host object and if `drawing.ts` reads from that getter each frame.\n\nThe session getter tracks restarts, but act does not restart the run, so the world object stays the same across frames. I am now looking for a way to expose the raw session on the page or add a probe, because the inspector only shows entities and state() does not reveal the exact onFrame world contents.\n\nI'll add a `__dbg` counter to the page's global window object in stage.ts to track frame execution and snapshot state. Rebuilding and running hold-debug will reveal whether frames stopped, readSnap is blind, or the previous failure was a timing flake.\n\nThe persistent prompt after 1.2 seconds means paint never received a sentence, so frames were likely not running for that long. I'm now checking whether the hold-debug HTML was stale, or if the `ask.sleep` line exists in book.ts.\n\nFocus remaining on 'Begin' is expected behavior, not a bug. The real issue is that the note stayed as the prompt because paint received an empty sentence on the last completed frame.\n\nAn empty copy string does not prove the game is still in title mode. Event mode without a lure also leaves copy blank. The note element is the real discriminator: it shows the prompt when there is no sentence, or the actual sentence otherwise.\n\nThe note remaining as the prompt means either the sentence was empty or the menu was still open. Since the screen is already set to play, a lingering menu would be unexpected. If later frames show a null menu and an empty sentence, the note would revert to the prompt.\n\nThe page's snapshot and the engine's state disagree. The page read an empty event, while state() still shows morning. This confirms the page is reading stale data.\n\nI'm now examining why the animation loop might have stopped after the world change. The tick function only halts if `loop.frame` throws an error, so a silent death would mean the frame completed without crashing.\n\nI'm now considering whether the browser throttled requestAnimationFrame after the first frames, though Playwright headless usually keeps it running. The stronger possibility is an infinite loop in the begin frame's paint or audio code that never returns. If paint hangs, the screen would already have published to play before the hang, leaving the HUD frozen on the prompt.\n\nThe page remained responsive, so the begin frame did not hang. The loop is either stopped or failing to update the event. I will check if `clock.paused` is a member of `__engine`, run the diagnostic script, and sample the tick twice. I will also patch stage to re-read the snapshot after actions and fall back to a direct inspector state read for publishing.\n\nRe-reading the snapshot after begin would only fix the HUD for that single frozen frame. If later frames still read an empty event, the query itself is broken and the diagnostic script is needed to find why.\n\nI now suspect `freezeValue` caches frozen copies by entity identity. If the query's `frozen()` wrapper returns a cached copy after mutation, later frames would read stale data even though the live session is current. I will inspect that function.\n\nI inspected the `frozen()` wrapper and confirmed it calls `copyValue` before freezing. If `copyValue` deep-copies, each query returns a fresh snapshot rather than a cached frozen reference. This rules out `freezeValue` as the source of stale data.\n\nI considered whether freezeValue freezes live entities in place, which would break mutations. Since state() still shows morning, mutations succeeded and the live objects were not frozen. copyValue works correctly.\n\nI am now checking whether the page's readSnap query throws a SIM error because the 'flow' component is missing from its table. That would stop the animation loop on frame two, and hold-debug might have missed the error if it was recorded in an unexpected format.\n\nI will include pageerrors in the diagnostic script, since hold-debug only printed state output and may have missed a pageerror. I am also checking whether game.begin spawns entities that cause gfx.frame to throw before onFrame runs.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a667b23d-9540-42a2-92df-f8cab3970235-51","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/state.ts","offset":230,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a667b23d-9540-42a2-92df-f8cab3970235-52","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function copyValue|function freezeValue","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/core/schema.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1242,"output_tokens":3249,"cache_read_input_tokens":85376,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"2e933316-d273-4084-bee4-313e74e90608"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a667b23d-9540-42a2-92df-f8cab3970235-51","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"230→/** The component table of `registry` (the shared one by default). Kinds never change once declared, so it caches. */\\nexport function componentTable(registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): ComponentTable {\\n  componentKind(registry);\\n  const known = new Map<string, { schema: Schema; names: readonly string[] }>();\\n  const kindOf = (name: string) => {\\n    let kind = known.get(name);\\n    if (kind) return kind;\\n    if (typeof name !== 'string' || !registry.has('component', name)) {\\n      const ids = registry.list('component').map((entry) => entry.id);\\n      throw codeError('SIM_UNKNOWN_COMPONENT', { name: show(name), suggestion: didYouMean(String(name), ids) });\\n240→    }\\n    const schema = (registry.get('component', name) as unknown as ComponentKind).fields;\\n    kind = { schema, names: Object.keys(schema) };\\n    known.set(name, kind);\\n    return kind;\\n  };\\n  return {\\n    fields: (name) => kindOf(name).names,\\n    make(name, values, where) {\\n      const kind = kindOf(name);\\n250→      const label = `${where}: component ${show(name)}`;\\n      const made = parse(kind.schema, values, label) as ComponentData;\\n      for (const key of kind.names) {\\n        const bad = notData(made[key]);\\n        if (bad) throw codeError('SIM_NOT_DATA', { path: `${label}: ${key}${bad.path}`, what: bad.what });\\n      }\\n      return made;\\n    },\\n  };\\n}\\n260→\\n/** Feeds one entity: its id, then its components in name order, each with its declared fields in order. */\\nfunction feedEntity(h: Fnv64, entity: EntityData, table: ComponentTable, live: boolean): void {\\n  const names = componentNames(entity, table, live);\\n  h.number(entity.id).uint32(names.length);\\n  for (const name of names) {\\n    h.byte(TAG.string).text(name); // the bytes h.value(name) feeds\\n    eachField(\\n      entity,\\n      name,\",\"content_concise\":\"230→/** The component table of `registry` (the shared one by default). Kinds never change once declared, so it caches. */\\nexport function componentTable(registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): ComponentTable {\\n  componentKind(registry);\\n  const known = new Map<string, { schema: Schema; names: readonly string[] }>();\\n  const kindOf = (name: string) => {\\n    let kind = known.get(name);\\n    if (kind) return kind;\\n    if (typeof name !== 'string' || !registry.has('component', name)) {\\n      const ids = registry.list('component').map((entry) => entry.id);\\n      throw codeError('SIM_UNKNOWN_COMPONENT', { name: show(name), suggestion: didYouMean(String(name), ids) });\\n240→    }\\n    const schema = (registry.get('component', name) as unknown as ComponentKind).fields;\\n    kind = { schema, names: Object.keys(schema) };\\n    known.set(name, kind);\\n    return kind;\\n  };\\n  return {\\n    fields: (name) => kindOf(name).names,\\n    make(name, values, where) {\\n      const kind = kindOf(name);\\n250→      const label = `${where}: component ${show(name)}`;\\n      const made = parse(kind.schema, values, label) as ComponentData;\\n      for (const key of kind.names) {\\n        const bad = notData(made[key]);\\n        if (bad) throw codeError('SIM_NOT_DATA', { path: `${label}: ${key}${bad.path}`, what: bad.what });\\n      }\\n      return made;\\n    },\\n  };\\n}\\n260→\\n/** Feeds one entity: its id, then its components in name order, each with its declared fields in order. */\\nfunction feedEntity(h: Fnv64, entity: EntityData, table: ComponentTable, live: boolean): void {\\n  const names = componentNames(entity, table, live);\\n  h.number(entity.id).uint32(names.length);\\n  for (const name of names) {\\n    h.byte(TAG.string).text(name); // the bytes h.value(name) feeds\\n    eachField(\\n      entity,\\n      name,\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/state.ts\",\"offset\":230,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/** The component table of `registry` (the shared one by default). Kinds never change once declared, so it caches. */\\nexport function componentTable(registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): ComponentTable {\\n  componentKind(registry);\\n  const known = new Map<string, { schema: Schema; names: readonly string[] }>();\\n  const kindOf = (name: string) => {\\n    let kind = known.get(name);\\n    if (kind) return kind;\\n    if (typeof name !== 'string' || !registry.has('component', name)) {\\n      const ids = registry.list('component').map((entry) => entry.id);\\n      throw codeError('SIM_UNKNOWN_COMPONENT', { name: show(name), suggestion: didYouMean(String(name), ids) });\\n    }\\n    const schema = (registry.get('component', name) as unknown as ComponentKind).fields;\\n    kind = { schema, names: Object.keys(schema) };\\n    known.set(name, kind);\\n    return kind;\\n  };\\n  return {\\n    fields: (name) => kindOf(name).names,\\n    make(name, values, where) {\\n      const kind = kindOf(name);\\n      const label = `${where}: component ${show(name)}`;\\n      const made = parse(kind.schema, values, label) as ComponentData;\\n      for (const key of kind.names) {\\n        const bad = notData(made[key]);\\n        if (bad) throw codeError('SIM_NOT_DATA', { path: `${label}: ${key}${bad.path}`, what: bad.what });\\n      }\\n      return made;\\n    },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** Feeds one entity: its id, then its components in name order, each with its declared fields in order. */\\nfunction feedEntity(h: Fnv64, entity: EntityData, table: ComponentTable, live: boolean): void {\\n  const names = componentNames(entity, table, live);\\n  h.number(entity.id).uint32(names.length);\\n  for (const name of names) {\\n    h.byte(TAG.string).text(name); // the bytes h.value(name) feeds\\n    eachField(\\n      entity,\\n      name,\\n\",\"total_lines\":361}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a667b23d-9540-42a2-92df-f8cab3970235-52","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,47,84,104,117,109,98,32,89,111,103,97,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,99,111,114,101,47,115,99,104,101,109,97,46,116,115,10,50,50,50,58,101,120,112,111,114,116,32,102,117,110,99,116,105,111,110,32,99,111,112,121,86,97,108,117,101,60,84,62,40,118,97,108,117,101,58,32,84,41,58,32,84,32,123,10,50,51,49,58,101,120,112,111,114,116,32,102,117,110,99,116,105,111,110,32,102,114,101,101,122,101,86,97,108,117,101,60,84,62,40,118,97,108,117,101,58,32,84,41,58,32,84,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/core/schema.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":222,\"content\":\"export function copyValue<T>(value: T): T {\"},{\"line_number\":2