{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_784","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking the flow component definition to see if events are stored differently.\n\nChecking if string fields are non-enumerable in the page's world query. A diagnostic probe in stage.ts is being considered, but full HTML rebuilds are too slow and DevTools protocol is too heavy.\n\nA 4-line probe will be added and tested. Re-reading the snapshot after actions only fixes the begin frame. Later frames might overwrite live.event back to empty if they read stale data. The behavior of later frames needs to be understood.\n\nA frozen simulation would pass verification but break gameplay. The loop must keep drawing and the HUD must track live events.\n\nChecking whether the clock pauses during game.begin. Also investigating if NaN transforms in new entities cause view.restarted() to throw inside gfx.frame, though onFrame should still run. Will inspect the renderer frame's try/catch next.\n\nopenBeat and startAttract are not the issue on the first second. A new hypothesis is that `drawn.world.query` reads from a snapshot array while `state()` reads a different structure, causing act updates to miss the query. The `query()` function was already reviewed.\n\nConfirmed that `query()` and `state()` both read from the same live entity list, so they should agree unless called on different worlds. The focus is now on whether `__engine.state` and the frame's `parts.run.session.world.query` actually reference the same world object after `act`.\n\nRuled out inspector restarts from `applyPrefs` and `seed()` as causes for world replacement. Now comparing the inspector's world object against `parts.run.session` inside `createEngine`.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4676c2be-5a6f-48e1-8e7a-a1e122ece44d-53","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/app/headless.ts","offset":248,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4676c2be-5a6f-48e1-8e7a-a1e122ece44d-54","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"createInspector|inspector","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/app/headless.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3991,"output_tokens":1047,"cache_read_input_tokens":86528,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"911c2296-8cd3-412d-88ad-39fcae5ec6b5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4676c2be-5a6f-48e1-8e7a-a1e122ece44d-53","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"248→  const host: AppHost = {\\n    registry,\\n250→    members: sharedRegistry,\\n    log: options.log ?? sharedLog,\\n    get clock() {\\n      return run.clock;\\n    },\\n    get session() {\\n      return run.recorded;\\n    },\\n    runtime: typeof window === 'undefined' ? 'node' : 'browser',\\n    get renderer() {\\n260→      return drawing?.active() ?? false;\\n    },\\n    get adapter() {\\n      return drawing?.adapter ?? null;\\n    },\\n    get features() {\\n      return drawing?.features ?? [];\\n    },\\n    get downgrades() {\\n      return drawing?.downgrades ?? [];\\n270→    },\\n    get ready() {\\n      return drawing ? drawing.ready() : true;\\n    },\\n    view,\\n    meter,\\n    step(n, intents) {\\n      if (intents === undefined) {\\n        // No intents: what the virtual device holds (`__engine.input`), taken each step as the page's input is.\\n        const device = virtualDeviceOf(host);\\n280→        for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) stepOnce(virtualIntents(device.take()));\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      const script = Array.isArray(intents) ? intents : undefined;\\n      const later = isPlainObject(intents) ? { ...intents, p: undefined } : intents;\\n      for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) stepOnce(script ? (script[k] ?? {}) : k === 0 ? intents : later);\\n    },\\n    restart(next) {\\n      restart(run.session.scene, next, changedSettings(run.session, registry));\\n    },\\n290→    render: (frames) => drawing!.render(frames),\\n    shot: (shotOptions) => drawing!.shot(shotOptions),\\n    async replay(text: string, playOptions: PlayIntoOptions): Promise<PlayResult> {\\n      playing = true;\\n      try {\\n        return await playInto(\\n          {\\n            registry,\\n            begin,\\n            stepped: () => view?.stepped(),\\n300→            draw: drawing && (() => drawing.draw()),\\n            carry: drawing && view ? () => view.carry() : undefined,\\n            camera: view ? (code, blend) => void view.setCamera(code, { blend }) : undefined,\\n            setView: (path, value) => (drawing ? drawing.setView(path, value) : run.session.set(path, value)),\\n            shoot: drawing && ((shotOptions) => drawing.shot(shotOptions)),\\n          },\\n          text,\\n          playOptions,\\n        );\\n      } finally {\\n310→        playing = false;\\n        // The loop was held, so no frame passed for the stops its steps asked for: left in the outbox, they would\\n        // freeze the first live frame after it.\\n        takeHitStop(run.session.world);\\n      }\\n    },\\n  };\\n  const inspector = createInspector(host);\\n  hosts.set(inspector, host);\\n  return {\\n320→    inspector,\\n    host,\\n    get session() {\\n      return run.session;\\n    },\\n    get clock() {\\n      return run.clock;\\n    },\\n    view,\\n    stepOnce,\\n330→    stepped,\\n    get playing() {\\n      return playing;\\n    },\\n    begin,\\n    meter,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n340→ * Starts a scene headless, in this process, and returns its inspector: the members a page's `window.__engine` has\\n * (`step`, `hash`, `state`, `set`…; `help()` lists them all), minus a renderer. With `view: true` it also builds the\\n * scene's view, for `scene.dump()` and `camera`. Throws `CORE_NO_ENTRY` for an unknown scene id, `CORE_BAD_SETTING`\\n * for a bad setting, `SIM_BAD_SEED` for a seed a replay cannot hold, and with a view `APP_NO_LEVEL` for a level not\\n * registered.\\n */\\nexport async function createHeadless<C extends object = AnyComponents, E extends EventMap = EventMap>(\\n  options: HeadlessOptions<C, E>,\\n): Promise<Headless> {\\n  return createAppHost(options).inspector;\\n350→}\\n\\n/** The run behind a headless engine: its session (world, settings, recording) and clock. Tools only. */\\nexport function headlessHost(headless: Headless): InspectorHost {\\n  const host = hosts.get(headless);\\n  if (!host) throw codeError('APP_NOT_HEADLESS', { value: typeof headless });\\n  return host;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"248→  const host: AppHost = {\\n    registry,\\n250→    members: sharedRegistry,\\n    log: options.log ?? sharedLog,\\n    get clock() {\\n      return run.clock;\\n    },\\n    get session() {\\n      return run.recorded;\\n    },\\n    runtime: typeof window === 'undefined' ? 'node' : 'browser',\\n    get renderer() {\\n260→      return drawing?.active() ?? false;\\n    },\\n    get adapter() {\\n      return drawing?.adapter ?? null;\\n    },\\n    get features() {\\n      return drawing?.features ?? [];\\n    },\\n    get downgrades() {\\n      return drawing?.downgrades ?? [];\\n270→    },\\n    get ready() {\\n      return drawing ? drawing.ready() : true;\\n    },\\n    view,\\n    meter,\\n    step(n, intents) {\\n      if (intents === undefined) {\\n        // No intents: what the virtual device holds (`__engine.input`), taken each step as the page's input is.\\n        const device = virtualDeviceOf(host);\\n280→        for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) stepOnce(virtualIntents(device.take()));\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      const script = Array.isArray(intents) ? intents : undefined;\\n      const later = isPlainObject(intents) ? { ...intents, p: undefined } : intents;\\n      for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) stepOnce(script ? (script[k] ?? {}) : k === 0 ? intents : later);\\n    },\\n    restart(next) {\\n      restart(run.session.scene, next, changedSettings(run.session, registry));\\n    },\\n290→    render: (frames) => drawing!.render(frames),\\n    shot: (shotOptions) => drawing!.shot(shotOptions),\\n    async replay(text: string, playOptions: PlayIntoOptions): Promise<PlayResult> {\\n      playing = true;\\n      try {\\n        return await playInto(\\n          {\\n            registry,\\n            begin,\\n            stepped: () => view?.stepped(),\\n300→            draw: drawing && (() => drawing.draw()),\\n            carry: drawing && view ? () => view.carry() : undefined,\\n            camera: view ? (code, blend) => void view.setCamera(code, { blend }) : undefined,\\n            setView: (path, value) => (drawing ? drawing.setView(path, value) : run.session.set(path, value)),\\n            shoot: drawing && ((shotOptions) => drawing.shot(shotOptions)),\\n          },\\n          text,\\n          playOptions,\\n        );\\n      } finally {\\n310→        playing = false;\\n        // The loop was held, so no frame passed for the stops its steps asked for: left in the outbox, they would\\n        // freeze the first live frame after it.\\n        takeHitStop(run.session.world);\\n      }\\n    },\\n  };\\n  const inspector = createInspector(host);\\n  hosts.set(inspector, host);\\n  return {\\n320→    inspector,\\n    host,\\n    get session() {\\n      return run.session;\\n    },\\n    get clock() {\\n      return run.clock;\\n    },\\n    view,\\n    stepOnce,\\n330→    stepped,\\n    get playing() {\\n      return playing;\\n    },\\n    begin,\\n    meter,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n340→ * Starts a scene headless, in this process, and returns its inspector: the members a page's `window.__engine` has\\n * (`step`, `hash`, `state`, `set`…; `help()` lists them all), minus a renderer. With `view: true` it also builds the\\n * scene's view, for `scene.dump()` and `camera`. Throws `CORE_NO_ENTRY` for an unknown scene id, `CORE_BAD_SETTING`\\n * for a bad setting, `SIM_BAD_SEED` for a seed a replay cannot hold, and with a view `APP_NO_LEVEL` for a level not\\n * registered.\\n */\\nexport async function createHeadless<C extends object = AnyComponents, E extends EventMap = EventMap>(\\n  options: HeadlessOptions<C, E>,\\n): Promise<Headless> {\\n  return createAppHost(options).inspector;\\n350→}\\n\\n/** The run behind a headless engine: its session (world, settings, recording) and clock. Tools only. */\\nexport function headlessHost(headless: Headless): InspectorHost {\\n  const host = hosts.get(headless);\\n  if (!host) throw codeError('APP_NOT_HEADLESS', { value: typeof headless });\\n  return host;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/app/headless.ts\",\"offset\":248,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"  const host: AppHost = {\\n    registry,\\n    members: sharedRegistry,\\n    log: options.log ?? sharedLog,\\n    get clock() {\\n      return run.clock;\\n    },\\n    get session() {\\n      return run.recorded;\\n    },\\n    runtime: typeof window === 'undefined' ? 'node' : 'browser',\\n    get renderer() {\\n      return drawing?.active() ?? false;\\n    },\\n    get adapter() {\\n      return drawing?.adapter ?? null;\\n    },\\n    get features() {\\n      return drawing?.features ?? [];\\n    },\\n    get downgrades() {\\n      return drawing?.downgrades ?? [];\\n    },\\n    get ready() {\\n      return drawing ? drawing.ready() : true;\\n    },\\n    view,\\n    meter,\\n    step(n, intents) {\\n      if (intents === undefined) {\\n        // No intents: what the virtual device holds (`__engine.input`), taken each step as the page's input is.\\n        const device = virtualDeviceOf(host);\\n        for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) stepOnce(virtualIntents(device.take()));\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      const script = Array.isArray(intents) ? intents : undefined;\\n      const later = isPlainObject(intents) ? { ...intents, p: undefined } : intents;\\n      for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) stepOnce(script ? (script[k] ?? {}) : k === 0 ? intents : later);\\n    },\\n    restart(next) {\\n      restart(run.session.scene, next, changedSettings(run.session, registry));\\n    },\\n    render: (frames) => drawing!.render(frames),\\n    shot: (shotOptions) => drawing!.shot(shotOptions),\\n    async replay(text: string, playOptions: PlayIntoOptions): Promise<PlayResult> {\\n      playing = true;\\n      try {\\n        return await playInto(\\n          {\\n            registry,\\n            begin,\\n            stepped: () => view?.stepped(),\\n            draw: drawing && (() => drawing.draw()),\\n            carry: drawing && view ? () => view.carry() : undefined,\\n            camera: view ? (code, blend) => void view.setCamera(code, { blend }) : undefined,\\n            setView: (path, value) => (drawing ? drawing.setView(path, value) : run.session.set(path, value)),\\n            shoot: drawing && ((shotOptions) => drawing.shot(shotOptions)),\\n          },\\n          text,\\n          playOptions,\\n        );\\n      } finally {\\n        playing = false;\\n        // The loop was held, so no frame passed for the stops its steps asked for: left in the outbox, they would\\n        // freeze the first live frame after it.\\n        takeHitStop(run.session.world);\\n      }\\n    },\\n  };\\n  const inspector = createInspector(host);\\n  hosts.set(inspector, host);\\n  return {\\n    inspector,\\n    host,\\n    get session() {\\n      return run.session;\\n    },\\n    get clock() {\\n      return run.clock;\\n    },\\n    view,\\n    stepOnce,\\n    stepped,\\n    get playing() {\\n      return playing;\\n    },\\n    begin,\\n    meter,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Starts a scene headless, in this process, and returns its inspector: the members a page's `window.__engine` has\\n * (`step`, `hash`, `state`, `set`…; `help()` lists them all), minus a renderer. With `view: true` it also builds the\\n * scene's view, for `scene.dump()` and `camera`. Throws `CORE_NO_ENTRY` for an unknown scene id, `CORE_BAD_SETTING`\\n * for a bad setting, `SIM_BAD_SEED` for a seed a replay cannot hold, and with a view `APP_NO_LEVEL` for a level not\\n * registered.\\n */\\nexport async function createHeadless<C extends object = AnyComponents, E extends EventMap = EventMap>(\\n  options: HeadlessOptions<C, E>,\\n): Promise<Headless> {\\n  return createAppHost(options).inspector;\\n}\\n\\n/** The run behind a headless engine: its session (world, settings, recording) and clock. Tools only. */\\nexport function headlessHost(headless: Headless): InspectorHost {\\n  const host = hosts.get(headless);\\n  if (!host) throw codeError('APP_NOT_HEADLESS', { value: typeof headless });\\n  return host;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":357}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4676c2be-5a6f-48e1-8e7a-a1e122ece44d-54","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,47,84,104,117,109,98,32,89,111,103,97,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,97,112,112,47,104,101,97,100,108,101,115,115,46,116,115,10,52,58,32,42,32,105,110,115,112,101,99,116,111,114,44,32,116,104,101,32,115,97,109,101,32,111,98,106,101,99,116,32,97,32,112,97,103,101,32,112,117,98,108,105,115,104,101,115,32,97,115,32,96,119,105,110,100,111,119,46,95,95,101,110,103,105,110,101,96,32,109,105,110,117,115,32,97,32,114,101,110,100,101,114,101,114,58,32,96,114,101,110,100,101,114,96,32,97,110,100,32,96,115,104,111,116,96,32,11