2,48,58,32,42,32,83,116,97,114,116,115,32,97,32,115,99,101,110,101,32,104,101,97,100,108,101,115,115,44,32,105,110,32,116,104,105,115,32,112,114,111,99,101,115,115,44,32,97,110,100,32,114,101,116,117,114,110,115,32,105,116,115,32,105,110,115,112,101,99,116,111,114,58,32,116,104,101,32,109,101,109,98,101,114,115,32,97,32,112,97,103,101,39,115,32,96,119,105,110,100,111,119,46,95,95,101,110,103,105,110,101,96,32,104,97,115,10,51,52,57,58,32,32,114,101,116,117,114,110,32,99,114,101,97,116,101,65,112,112,72,111,115,116,40,111,112,116,105,111,110,115,41,46,105,110,115,112,101,99,116,111,114,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":11,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/app/headless.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":4,\"content\":\" * inspector, the same object a page publishes as `window.__engine` minus a renderer: `render` and `shot` throw\"},{\"line_number\":25,\"content\":\" * points); runs share nothing but the registry; the inspector holds only its members, so the run behind it is reached\"},{\"line_number\":46,\"content\":\"import { createInspector, type Inspector } from '../dev/inspector';\"},{\"line_number\":52,\"content\":\"import { virtualDeviceOf } from '../input/devices/inspector'; // registers `__engine.input` too\"},{\"line_number\":121,\"content\":\"/** The run behind an engine: the inspector, its host, and the live session (app code only, never members). */\"},{\"line_number\":123,\"content\":\"  readonly inspector: Inspector;\"},{\"line_number\":317,\"content\":\"  const inspector = createInspector(host);\"},{\"line_number\":318,\"content\":\"  hosts.set(inspector, host);\"},{\"line_number\":320,\"content\":\"    inspector,\"},{\"line_number\":340,\"content\":\" * Starts a scene headless, in this process, and returns its inspector: the members a page's `window.__engine` has\"},{\"line_number\":349,\"content\":\"  return createAppHost(options).inspector;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"f59b449f-526f-48df-81bf-c7ad4c56416a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_785","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A critical difference was identified.\n\nThe raw session exposes live entities, not frozen copies. The inspector and onFrame both read from the same underlying world, so their results should match.\n\nThe mutation becomes visible before paint, but readSnap already captured the old event. If no later onFrame runs, publish still emits the stale value. The investigation is now focused on why the animation loop might have stopped without an error.\n\nThe investigation now points to the `warming` flag. If the initial cold-frame promise never resolves, every subsequent draw exits early and `onFrame` never runs. This would leave the session stale without any error.\n\nThe warmedAt map is keyed by camera object, not shader key. Since view.restarted does not create new cameras, the warmup flag should persist across settings changes. This makes a dev action re-triggering warming unlikely. The focus is now shifting to whether the begin frame itself might be the first cold frame.\n\nThe title was already visible, so many frames had already run. The touch cap only throttles to 60fps and does not stop the loop. hold() is false because playing is false. The next step is to find any call to loop.stop(). An exception outside the try block could kill requestAnimationFrame, though Playwright usually keeps the document visible.\n\nBackground tab throttling is unlikely because the page is the only foreground tab. A begin-frame paint or audio schedule stopping the loop seems improbable. The next step is to inspect whether engine loop start, fail(), or audio.play throws asynchronously. The gfx governor dropping and warming state are also being checked. Cheap instrumentation will be added, the project rebuilt, and a diagnostic run performed.\n\nThe menu pick path was ruled out because the screen reached play. The frame completed without throwing errors, so the loop should have scheduled the next frame. A synchronous re-entrant frame stopping the loop is unlikely. The investigation is now shifting to whether errors are being cleared or logged, which could hide a failure in a later frame.\n\nfail() is being checked to see if it stops the loop and whether errors might omit APP_FRAME or get replaced by a second error. A scenario where a later frame reads the correct event but something resets it before publish was considered, but only the snap assignment could do that. A theory that a later frame threw and stopped the loop was dismissed because the page recovered. The hold-debug output still shows empty errors, an empty event, and a morning flow from state.\n\nMonkeypatching DOM methods like append or textContent would not reveal onFrame execution. Overriding requestAnimationFrame after navigation is also ineffective because the engine loop already captured the original function in its closure. The plan is to install a frame-counting override via add_init_script before navigation so it can track the engine loop directly.\n\nA frame-counting wrapper around requestAnimationFrame will be injected via add_init_script before navigation. The engine loop captures this wrapper, so __raf increments only when callbacks actually fire. If __raf freezes after begin while timers.ticks continues advancing, the animation loop has stopped. Because steps run inside the rAF callback, a stopped loop would freeze both steps and the event at its last value.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-888af204-b9fc-452f-9bac-a43e6f0269c3-55","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"tick:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/dev/inspector.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-888af204-b9fc-452f-9bac-a43e6f0269c3-56","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/world.ts","offset":200,"limit":70}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2418,"output_tokens":1523,"cache_read_input_tokens":90496,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"ad70ec22-1f31-4d10-857e-a7a5e5a23272"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-888af204-b9fc-452f-9bac-a43e6f0269c3-55","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,47,84,104,117,109,98,32,89,111,103,97,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,100,101,118,47,105,110,115,112,101,99,116,111,114,46,116,115,10,55,54,58,32,32,116,105,99,107,58,32,110,117,109,98,101,114,59,10,49,56,57,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,116,105,99,107,58,32,104,46,115,101,115,115,105,111,110,46,119,111,114,108,100,46,116,105,99,107,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/dev/inspector.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":76,\"content\":\"  tick: number;\"},{\"line_number\":189,\"content\":\"      tick: h.session.world.tick,\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-888af204-b9fc-452f-9bac-a43e6f0269c3-56","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"200→  const store = options.settings ?? createSettings({ registry });\\n  const firstSeed = options.seed ?? 0;\\n  check(Number.isFinite(firstSeed), 'createWorld({ seed })', firstSeed, 'a finite number');\\n  const hz = options.hz ?? (store.values({ view: false })['time.hz'] as number | undefined) ?? SIM_HZ;\\n  check(Number.isInteger(hz) && hz >= 1, 'createWorld({ hz })', hz, 'whole steps per second, 1 or more');\\n  const timers = createTimers({ hz });\\n  const emitter = createEvents<E>({ log: options.log ?? sharedLog });\\n  const systems = createSystems<World<C, E>>();\\n  const physics = options.physics;\\n  const { probe } = options;\\n210→  const streams = new RngStreams(firstSeed);\\n  const fx = new RngStreams(derive(firstSeed, 'fx'));\\n  const entities = createEntityTable();\\n  /** The queues an entry point fills and its boundary empties. */\\n  const spawns: LiveEntity[] = [];\\n  const despawns: number[] = [];\\n  const queued: [keyof E & string, unknown][] = [];\\n  let busy = false;\\n  const boundary = (): void => {\\n    for (let round = 0; spawns.length || despawns.length || queued.length; round++) {\\n220→      if (round >= MAX_ROUNDS) throw codeError('SIM_EVENT_STORM', { tick: timers.ticks, rounds: MAX_ROUNDS });\\n      spawns.splice(0).forEach(entities.insert);\\n      for (const id of entities.removeAll(despawns.splice(0))) streams.dropEntity(id);\\n      for (const [type, payload] of queued.splice(0)) emitter.emit(type, payload as E[typeof type]);\\n    }\\n  };\\n  /** Runs `fn` as an entry point: not inside another, inside withSimMath, the boundary after it. */\\n  const enter = <T>(what: string, fn: () => T): T => {\\n    if (busy) throw codeError('SIM_BUSY', { what });\\n    return withSimMath(() => {\\n230→      busy = true;\\n      try {\\n        const out = fn();\\n        boundary();\\n        return out;\\n      } catch (error) {\\n        spawns.length = despawns.length = queued.length = 0;\\n        throw error;\\n      } finally {\\n        busy = false;\\n240→      }\\n    });\\n  };\\n  const pending = (id: number) => spawns.some((entity) => entity.id === id);\\n  const live = (id: number): LiveEntity => entities.live(id, pending);\\n  const view = (): StateView => ({\\n    seed: streams.seed,\\n    nextId: entities.nextId,\\n    hz,\\n    entities: entities.order,\\n250→    timers: timers.state(),\\n    // Only what differs from its default: declaring another setting (any scene module does) never changes the hash.\\n    settings: Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(store.values({ view: false })).filter(([path]) => store.differs(path))),\\n    rng: streams.state(),\\n    ...(physics ? { physics: physics.state() } : {}),\\n  });\\n  const rng = Object.assign((...keys: readonly (string | number)[]) => streams.stream(...keys), {\\n    entity(id: number, ...keys: readonly (string | number)[]) {\\n      if (!entities.has(id) && !pending(id)) live(id); // a dropped stream never comes back\\n      return streams.entity(id, ...keys);\\n260→    },\\n  });\\n\\n  const world: World<C, E> = {\\n    get seed() {\\n      return streams.seed;\\n    },\\n    hz,\\n    dt: 1 / hz,\\n    get tick() {\",\"content_concise\":\"200→  const store = options.settings ?? createSettings({ registry });\\n  const firstSeed = options.seed ?? 0;\\n  check(Number.isFinite(firstSeed), 'createWorld({ seed })', firstSeed, 'a finite number');\\n  const hz = options.hz ?? (store.values({ view: false })['time.hz'] as number | undefined) ?? SIM_HZ;\\n  check(Number.isInteger(hz) && hz >= 1, 'createWorld({ hz })', hz, 'whole steps per second, 1 or more');\\n  const timers = createTimers({ hz });\\n  const emitter = createEvents<E>({ log: options.log ?? sharedLog });\\n  const systems = createSystems<World<C, E>>();\\n  const physics = options.physics;\\n  const { probe } = options;\\n210→  const streams = new RngStreams(firstSeed);\\n  const fx = new RngStreams(derive(firstSeed, 'fx'));\\n  const entities = createEntityTable();\\n  /** The queues an entry point fills and its boundary empties. */\\n  const spawns: LiveEntity[] = [];\\n  const despawns: number[] = [];\\n  const queued: [keyof E & string, unknown][] = [];\\n  let busy = false;\\n  const boundary = (): void => {\\n    for (let round = 0; spawns.length || despawns.length || queued.length; round++) {\\n220→      if (round >= MAX_ROUNDS) throw codeError('SIM_EVENT_STORM', { tick: timers.ticks, rounds: MAX_ROUNDS });\\n      spawns.splice(0).forEach(entities.insert);\\n      for (const id of entities.removeAll(despawns.splice(0))) streams.dropEntity(id);\\n      for (const [type, payload] of queued.splice(0)) emitter.emit(type, payload as E[typeof type]);\\n    }\\n  };\\n  /** Runs `fn` as an entry point: not inside another, inside withSimMath, the boundary after it. */\\n  const enter = <T>(what: string, fn: () => T): T => {\\n    if (busy) throw codeError('SIM_BUSY', { what });\\n    return withSimMath(() => {\\n230→      busy = true;\\n      try {\\n        const out = fn();\\n        boundary();\\n        return out;\\n      } catch (error) {\\n        spawns.length = despawns.length = queued.length = 0;\\n        throw error;\\n      } finally {\\n        busy = false;\\n240→      }\\n    });\\n  };\\n  const pending = (id: number) => spawns.some((entity) => entity.id === id);\\n  const live = (id: number): LiveEntity => entities.live(id, pending);\\n  const view = (): StateView => ({\\n    seed: streams.seed,\\n    nextId: entities.nextId,\\n    hz,\\n    entities: entities.order,\\n250→    timers: timers.state(),\\n    // Only what differs from its default: declaring another setting (any scene module does) never changes the hash.\\n    settings: Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(store.values({ view: false })).filter(([path]) => store.differs(path))),\\n    rng: streams.state(),\\n    ...(physics ? { physics: physics.state() } : {}),\\n  });\\n  const rng = Object.assign((...keys: r