{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4a13cba1-2d60-4e68-960b-cb90f4932d07-67","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"44→export function createOverlay(document: Document): Overlay {\\n  let element = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#msg');\\n  if (!element) {\\n    element = document.createElement('div');\\n    element.id = 'msg';\\n    element.setAttribute('role', 'status');\\n50→    element.setAttribute('style', STYLE);\\n    document.body.append(element);\\n  }\\n  const box = element;\\n  let first: OverlayRecord | null = null;\\n  let more = 0;\\n  const show = (text: string) => {\\n    box.textContent = text;\\n    box.hidden = text === '';\\n  };\\n60→  const errorText = () =>\\n    first\\n      ? `${first.code}: ${first.message}\\\\nFix: ${first.fix}${more ? `\\\\n(${more} more in __engine.errors)` : ''}`\\n      : '';\\n  return {\\n    status(text) {\\n      if (!first) show(text);\\n    },\\n    error(record) {\\n      if (first) more++;\\n70→      else first = { code: record.code, message: record.message, fix: record.fix };\\n      show(errorText());\\n    },\\n    hide() {\\n      if (!first) show('');\\n    },\\n    text: () => (box.hidden ? '' : (box.textContent ?? '')),\\n  };\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"44→export function createOverlay(document: Document): Overlay {\\n  let element = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#msg');\\n  if (!element) {\\n    element = document.createElement('div');\\n    element.id = 'msg';\\n    element.setAttribute('role', 'status');\\n50→    element.setAttribute('style', STYLE);\\n    document.body.append(element);\\n  }\\n  const box = element;\\n  let first: OverlayRecord | null = null;\\n  let more = 0;\\n  const show = (text: string) => {\\n    box.textContent = text;\\n    box.hidden = text === '';\\n  };\\n60→  const errorText = () =>\\n    first\\n      ? `${first.code}: ${first.message}\\\\nFix: ${first.fix}${more ? `\\\\n(${more} more in __engine.errors)` : ''}`\\n      : '';\\n  return {\\n    status(text) {\\n      if (!first) show(text);\\n    },\\n    error(record) {\\n      if (first) more++;\\n70→      else first = { code: record.code, message: record.message, fix: record.fix };\\n      show(errorText());\\n    },\\n    hide() {\\n      if (!first) show('');\\n    },\\n    text: () => (box.hidden ? '' : (box.textContent ?? '')),\\n  };\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/dev/overlay.ts\",\"offset\":44,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"export function createOverlay(document: Document): Overlay {\\n  let element = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#msg');\\n  if (!element) {\\n    element = document.createElement('div');\\n    element.id = 'msg';\\n    element.setAttribute('role', 'status');\\n    element.setAttribute('style', STYLE);\\n    document.body.append(element);\\n  }\\n  const box = element;\\n  let first: OverlayRecord | null = null;\\n  let more = 0;\\n  const show = (text: string) => {\\n    box.textContent = text;\\n    box.hidden = text === '';\\n  };\\n  const errorText = () =>\\n    first\\n      ? `${first.code}: ${first.message}\\\\nFix: ${first.fix}${more ? `\\\\n(${more} more in __engine.errors)` : ''}`\\n      : '';\\n  return {\\n    status(text) {\\n      if (!first) show(text);\\n    },\\n    error(record) {\\n      if (first) more++;\\n      else first = { code: record.code, message: record.message, fix: record.fix };\\n      show(errorText());\\n    },\\n    hide() {\\n      if (!first) show('');\\n    },\\n    text: () => (box.hidden ? '' : (box.textContent ?? '')),\\n  };\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":78}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"7f07a0fc-47bb-4ed6-9174-c41a33afc7fe"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_795","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing a diagnostic to capture messages, tick progress, animation frames, menu presence, and errors.\n\nAdding a requestAnimationFrame counter and document visibility checks. Verifying whether touch input is active and could stall frames. Running a memory check before launching Chrome.\n\nWriting hud-debug.py to the scratch path. The gamepad stub may not update timestamps, so the engine might miss button 0 as uiAccept after the first frame. The screen did switch to play, confirming the initial edge worked. pickTitle calls host.close() to clear the menu and set screen to play.\n\nRuled out a mid-run exception blocking the menu close. Confirmed begin completed and screen switched to play. Noted that only stage.ts writes __game, so publish is not being overwritten elsewhere.\n\nDrafting the diagnostic script to read the paused flag from state().settings and gather tick, animation frame, and screen data.\n\nThe diagnostic script now also captures event state, focus status, UI text from note and copy elements, the message box contents, menu presence, and flow or act entity data.\n\nThe diagnostic will sample errors and document visibility. It will run at ready, after play, and five times every 400 milliseconds. Menu element counts will be captured via querySelectorAll. The gamepad stub already updates timestamps on every poll. The init script will combine the gamepad hook and the rAF counter.\n\nThe diagnostic will run for 90 seconds to cover boot and sampling. It will check for existing Chrome processes before launching to respect the two-browser limit. The script will also export PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE. No rebuild is needed for the diagnostic.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2a41880e-48ca-4fb7-8bfc-ebf894420cf6-68","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/hud-debug.py","content":"\"\"\"See whether drawn frames keep publishing the morning snap after Begin.\"\"\"\n\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\n\nHTML = Path(\n    \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656.html\"\n)\nCHROME = os.path.expanduser(\n    \"~/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-1243/chrome-headless-shell-linux64/chrome-headless-shell\"\n)\nFLAGS = [\n    \"--no-sandbox\",\n    \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\",\n    \"--enable-features=Vulkan\",\n    \"--use-vulkan=swiftshader\",\n    \"--use-angle=swiftshader\",\n]\nINIT = \"\"\"\nwindow.__buttons = new Array(16).fill(0);\nwindow.__axes = [0, 0, 0, 0];\nwindow.__raf = 0;\nconst orig = window.requestAnimationFrame.bind(window);\nwindow.requestAnimationFrame = (cb) => orig((t) => { window.__raf += 1; return cb(t); });\nnavigator.getGamepads = () => [{\n  id: 'Scripted Pad (STANDARD GAMEPAD)',\n  index: 0, connected: true, mapping: 'standard', timestamp: performance.now(),\n  axes: window.__axes.slice(),\n  buttons: window.__buttons.map((value) => ({ pressed: value > 0.5, touched: value > 0, value })),\n}];\n\"\"\"\nSAMPLE = \"\"\"() => {\n  const engine = window.__engine;\n  const st = engine.state();\n  const flow = (st.entities || []).map((e) => e.flow).find(Boolean) || null;\n  const act = (st.entities || []).map((e) => e.act).find(Boolean) || null;\n  const msg = document.querySelector('#msg');\n  return {\n    raf: window.__raf,\n    tick: engine.info().tick,\n    paused: st.settings ? st.settings['time.paused'] : null,\n    screen: window.__game && window.__game.screen,\n    event: window.__game && window.__game.event,\n    focus: window.__game && window.__game.focus,\n    note: (document.querySelector('[data-ui=note]') || {}).textContent || '',\n    copy: (document.querySelector('[data-ui=copy]') || {}).textContent || '',\n    msg: msg && !msg.hidden ? (msg.textContent || '').slice(0, 240) : '',\n    menus: document.querySelectorAll('#shell [data-menu], #shell button, #shell [role=menu]').length,\n    flow: flow && { mode: flow.mode, event: flow.event, line: flow.line, tick: flow.age },\n    actTick: act && act.tick,\n    errors: (engine.errors || []).map((e) => (e.code || '') + ' ' + (e.message || '')),\n    hidden: document.hidden,\n  };\n}\"\"\"\n\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\n    browser = p.chromium.launch(executable_path=CHROME, args=FLAGS)\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\"width\": 1280, \"height\": 720}, device_scale_factor=1)\n    page.add_init_script(INIT)\n    logs = []\n    page.on(\"console\", lambda msg: logs.append(msg.type + \" \" + msg.text[:300]))\n    page.on(\"pageerror\", lambda err: logs.append(\"pageerror \" + str(err)[:300]))\n    page.goto(HTML.as_uri())\n    page.wait_for_function(\"() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true\", timeout=60000)\n    page.wait_for_timeout(400)\n    print(\"READY\", page.evaluate(SAMPLE))\n    page.evaluate(\"() => { window.__buttons[0] = 1; }\")\n    page.wait_for_function(\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'play'\", timeout=8000)\n    print(\"PLAY\", page.evaluate(SAMPLE))\n    page.evaluate(\"() => { window.__buttons[0] = 0; }\")\n    for i in range(6):\n        page.wait_for_timeout(400)\n        print(f\"T{i}\", page.evaluate(SAMPLE))\n    print(\"LOGS\", len(logs))\n    for line in logs[-12:]:\n        print(\"LOG\", line)\n    browser.close()\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":490,"output_tokens":2161,"cache_read_input_tokens":107136,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"ef5347e0-1176-4cd0-b95f-4aaedf6d09a8"}
