version downloads its own.\\n  Playwright runs here with PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 (already set for runs): this OS isn't one it supports by name.\\n- **Tools:** node 24.22.1, npm 11.19.1, python3 3.14.8, pip3 26.2.1, git 2.56.0, gh 2.46.0, curl 8.22.0, wget 1.25.0, jq 1.8.1, ffmpeg 9.0.2, ffprobe 9.0.2, sqlite3 3.53.4, zip 3.0, unzip 6.00, rustc 1.99.0, cargo 1.99.0, go 1.27.1, java 27, lighthouse 13.5.0, shot-scraper 1.12, xvfb-run, magick 7.1.2, esbuild 0.28.2, uv 0.12.23, tsc 7.0.2, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129.\\n- **Rust:** rustup's toolchains 1.96.0, 1.98.1, stable; the wasm32-unknown-unknown target on 1.98.1.\\n- **Not installed:** sox, bun, deno.\\n- **Network:** internet works (github.com, registry.npmjs.org).\\n- **Memory:** earlyoom is on: when memory runs out it ends the biggest browser, so \\\"Target closed\\\", \\\"page crashed\\\" or \\\"browser has been closed\\\" means memory ran out, not a bug in your game. Run fewer browsers at once rather than retrying.\\n\\n### What this computer doesn't have\\n\\n50→No script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\\n\\n- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\\n- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\\n- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\\n- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\\n- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\\n- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\\n\\n### Sharing this computer\\n60→\\n- Other agents run here at the same time. Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\\n- Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\\n- The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\\n- The system Python has Playwright and nothing else. For one (Pillow, numpy …), use uv: `uv run --with pillow python script.py`, adding `--with playwright==1.63.0` when the script drives a browser too (a newer Playwright can't find the browsers here).\\n\\n## Goal\\n\\nBuild an original game inspired by the source.\\n\\n70→Scope\\n\\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\\n\\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\\n\\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\\n\\nMultiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\\n\\n80→Narrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/TASK.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"SOURCE: Wii Fit\\n\\nGenre: Pick the game genre(s) that best fit the source and would make the best game.\\n\\nPerspective: Pick the camera perspective(s) that best fit the genre and source and would make the best game.\\n\\nGame Title: A playful riff on SOURCE's name. Silently brainstorm 50 titles, then pick one with a real random number generator (e.g., run code).\\n\\nResearch: Whether and how much to research is your choice.\\n\\nPackage: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656].html. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the html file if that is easier.\\n\\nTech Stack: Build on https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3dge#make-a-game-with-my-3dge, in the engine's full workspace. The engine stays read-only, as the AGENTS.md it gives your game says: add whatever systems, art assets and animations the game needs on top of it. The rest of the tech stack is your choice.\\n\\nArt Direction: Use the engine’s native style as the base. Make new art assets for whatever makes the game feel like the source; the engine’s asset library is fine for generic props.\\n\\nAnimation: Use the engine’s native animation system as the base. Make new animations for whatever makes the game feel like the source.\\n\\nAudio: All music, sound effects and voices are written in code, with no audio files. Voices are Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. Music is to be set to 10% volume by default.\\n\\nOnline: https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub\\n\\nWorking Environment and deliverable:\\nCreate a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\\n\\nPerformance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited. Add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights, and shadows as the scene needs. Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\\n\\nTesting: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\\n\\nEffort: Spend effort however you see fit.\\n\\n## This computer\\nChecked 2026-11-04 20:05 (America/Vancouver) by node check-environment.mjs.\\n\\n- **Computer:** Worki9: 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900K, 32 cores, 20 GB RAM, 8 GB swap. Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS on WSL2 (Linux 6.18.33.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2).\\n- **Space:** 850 GB free in the home folder. /tmp: 9.8 GB, in memory (tmpfs), 8.2 GB free when checked.\\n- **Display:** none for runs (they run with DISPLAY unset), so a headed browser needs xvfb-run.\\n- **Browsers:** Playwright 1.63.0 for Python (from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright), with Chromium 153.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered; WebGPU, software-rendered, when started with --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader), Firefox 155.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered), WebKit 26.6 (WebGL 2) already downloaded. Phone and tablet device profiles are built in.\\n  WebGPU only works on a secure page: file:// or http://127.0.0.1. A WebGPU canvas can come out blank in a headless screenshot, so check the game's state instead.\\n  For Node, `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in your folder uses the browsers already downloaded; another version downloads its own.\\n  Playwright runs here with PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 (already set for runs): this OS isn't one it supports by name.\\n- **Tools:** node 24.22.1, npm 11.19.1, python3 3.14.8, pip3 26.2.1, git 2.56.0, gh 2.46.0, curl 8.22.0, wget 1.25.0, jq 1.8.1, ffmpeg 9.0.2, ffprobe 9.0.2, sqlite3 3.53.4, zip 3.0, unzip 6.00, rustc 1.99.0, cargo 1.99.0, go 1.27.1, java 27, lighthouse 13.5.0, shot-scraper 1.12, xvfb-run, magick 7.1.2, esbuild 0.28.2, uv 0.12.23, tsc 7.0.2, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129.\\n- **Rust:** rustup's toolchains 1.96.0, 1.98.1, stable; the wasm32-unknown-unknown target on 1.98.1.\\n- **Not installed:** sox, bun, deno.\\n- **Network:** internet works (github.com, registry.npmjs.org).\\n- **Memory:** earlyoom is on: when memory runs out it ends the biggest browser, so \\\"Target closed\\\", \\\"page crashed\\\" or \\\"browser has been closed\\\" means memory ran out, not a bug in your game. Run fewer browsers at once rather than retrying.\\n\\n### What this computer doesn't have\\n\\nNo script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\\n\\n- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\\n- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\\n- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\\n- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\\n- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\\n- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\\n\\n### Sharing this computer\\n\\n- Other agents run here at the same time. Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\\n- Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\\n- The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\\n- The system Python has Playwright and nothing else. For one (Pillow, numpy …), use uv: `uv run --with pillow python script.py`, adding `--with playwright==1.63.0` when the script drives a browser too (a newer Playwright can't find the browsers here).\\n\\n## Goal\\n\\nBuild an original game inspired by the source.\\n\\nScope\\n\\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\\n\\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\\n\\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\\n\\nMultiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\\n\\nNarrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\\n\",\"total_lines\":151}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"1dff360b-bfc0-415d-ada2-221925f87686"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_799","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The HUD works. Launching the official verification now.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-409db427-fdf6-4c19-93bb-f55909570313-75","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/tools/browse.py","offset":90,"limit":400}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10009,"output_tokens":269,"cache_read_input_tokens":113664,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"c321a344-3223-4b67-9656-0e6a1dbb6d51"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-409db427-fdf6-4c19-93bb-f55909570313-75","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"90→\\ndef once(browser, html: Path, out: Path, n: int, fails: list[str]) -> str:\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1920, \\\"height\\\": 1080}, device_scale_factor=1)\\n    page.add_init_script(PAD + WATCH)\\n    logs: list[str] = []\\n    page.on(\\\"console\\\", lambda msg: logs.append(msg.text))\\n    page.on(\\\"pageerror\\\", lambda err: logs.append(f\\\"pageerror {err}\\\"))\\n    try:\\n        page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true\\\", timeout=60000)\\n100→        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        state = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const canvas = document.querySelector('canvas');\\n              const game = window.__game || {};\\n              return {\\n                ready: window.__engine.ready,\\n                errors: window.__engine.errors || [],\\n                game,\\n                canvas: { width: canvas ? canvas.width : 0, height: canvas ? canvas.height : 0 },\\n110→                view: { width: window.innerWidth, height: window.innerHeight },\\n              };\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        (out / f\\\"boot-{n}.log\\\").write_text(json.dumps(state, indent=2) + \\\"\\\\n\\\" + \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(logs), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(out / f\\\"boot-{n}.png\\\"))\\n        if n == 1:\\n            page.screenshot(path=str(out / \\\"shots\\\" / \\\"title.png\\\"))\\n        errors = state[\\\"errors\\\"]\\n        if state[\\\"ready\\\"] is not True:\\n120→            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} ready is false\\\")\\n        if errors:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} errors {errors}\\\")\\n        if any(\\\"webgl\\\" in json.dumps(errors).lower() or \\\"downgrade\\\" in json.dumps(errors).lower() for _ in [0]):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} downgraded\\\")\\n        game = state[\\\"game\\\"]\\n        if game.get(\\\"title\\\") != \\\"Thumb Yoga\\\" or game.get(\\\"screen\\\") != \\\"title\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} title screen {game}\\\")\\n        if game.get(\\\"volumes\\\", {}).get(\\\"music\\\") != 0.1:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} music {game.get('volumes')}\\\")\\n130→        canvas = state[\\\"canvas\\\"]\\n        view = state[\\\"view\\\"]\\n        if canvas[\\\"width\\\"] <= 0 or canvas[\\\"height\\\"] <= 0:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} canvas is empty\\\")\\n        if canvas[\\\"width\\\"] != view[\\\"width\\\"] or canvas[\\\"height\\\"] != view[\\\"height\\\"]:\\n            note = out / \\\"webgpu-readback.txt\\\"\\n            note.write_text(\\n                f\\\"drawing {canvas['width']}x{canvas['height']} view {view['width']}x{view['height']}\\\\n\\\",\\n                encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\",\\n            )\\n140→            fails.append(\\n                f\\\"boot {n} canvas {canvas['width']}x{canvas['height']} is not the view {view['width']}x{view['height']}\\\"\\n            )\\n        # A short key tap can be sampled by a catch-up step and never reach the menu. Hold Cross.\\n        hold(page, 0, \\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'play'\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(400)\\n        after = page.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ screen: window.__game.screen, event: window.__game.event, title: window.__game.title })\\\")\\n        if after.get(\\\"screen\\\") != \\\"play\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} did not leave the title\\\")\\n        return json.dumps(after, sort_keys=True)\\n150→    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} {error}\\\")\\n        return \\\"\\\"\\n    finally:\\n        page.close()\\n\\n\\ndef frames(page) -> None:\\n    page.evaluate(\\\"() => new Promise((resolve) => requestAnimationFrame(() => requestAnimationFrame(resolve)))\\\")\\n\\n160→\\ndef hold(page, index: int, until: str) -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Holds one standard-mapping button until `until` is true, then lets it go for a frame.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    page.evaluate(\\\"(index) => { window.__buttons[index] = 1; }\\\", index)\\n    page.wait_for_function(until, timeout=8000)\\n    page.evaluate(\\\"(index) => { window.__buttons[index] = 0; }\\\", index)\\n    frames(page)\\n\\n\\ndef pad_down(page) -> str:\\n170→    before = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.focus\\\")\\n    hold(page, 13, f\\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.focus !== {json.dumps(before)}\\\")\\n    return page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.focus\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef shell(browser, html: Path, out: Path, shots: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1920, \\\"height\\\": 1080}, device_scale_factor=1)\\n    page.add_init_script(PAD)\\n    trace: list[str] = []\\n    try:\\n180→        page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true\\\", timeout=60000)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        note = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=note]\\\").inner_text()\\n        glyph = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.glyphSet\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"start {glyph} {note}\\\")\\n        if glyph != \\\"playstation\\\" or \\\"Cross\\\" not in note:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"glyphs started as {glyph} {note}\\\")\\n        # Focus starts on Begin. Two downs skip the disabled rows and land on Settings.\\n        for _ in range(2):\\n190→            pad_down(page)\\n        focus = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.focus\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"pad focus {focus}\\\")\\n        if focus != \\\"Settings\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"pad did not reach Settings {focus}\\\")\\n        hold(page, 0, \\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'settings'\\\")\\n        for _ in range(3):\\n            pad_down(page)\\n        focus = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.focus\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"icons row {focus}\\\")\\n200→        if \\\"Icons\\\" not in focus:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"pad did not reach Icons {focus}\\\")\\n        hold(page, 0, \\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.glyphSet === 'xbox'\\\")\\n        xbox = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=note]\\\").inner_text()\\n        glyph = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.glyphSet\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"xbox {glyph} {xbox}\\\")\\n        for token in (\\\"A \\\", \\\"B \\\", \\\"X \\\", \\\"Y \\\", \\\"LB\\\", \\\"RB\\\", \\\"LT\\\", \\\"RT\\\"):\\n            if token not in xbox:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"xbox prompt missing {token} in {xbox}\\\")\\n                break\\n210→        if glyph != \\\"xbox\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"glyph set after icons {glyph} {xbox}\\\")\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"f\\\")\\n        keys = page.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ set: window.__game.glyphSet, note: document.querySelector('[data-ui=note]').textContent })\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"keys {keys}\\\")\\n        if keys[\\\"set\\\"] != \\\"keys\\\" or \\\"WASD\\\" not in keys[\\\"note\\\"]:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"keys prompt {keys}\\\")\\n        page.mouse.click(12, 12)\\n        mouse = page.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ set: window.__game.glyphSet, note: document.querySelector('[data-ui=note]').textContent })\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"mouse {mouse}\\\")\\n220→        if mouse[\\\"set\\\"] != \\\"mouse\\\" or \\\"Mouse\\\" not in mouse[\\\"note\\\"]:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"mouse prompt {mouse}\\\")\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"Escape\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'title'\\\", timeout=5000)\\n        page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const row = document.querySelector('[data-ui=item][data-id=\\\"settings\\\"]');\\n              row.dispatchEvent(new PointerEvent('pointermove', { bubbles: true, movementX: 4, movementY: 6 }));\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n230→        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        focus = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.focus\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"hover focus {focus}\\\")\\n        if focus != \\\"Settings\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"hover focus {focus}\\\")\\n        save_before = page.evaluate(\\\"() => localStorage.getItem('thumb-yoga:save')\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(10500)\\n        attracted = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract === true && window.__game.screen === 'attract'\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"attract after 10.5s {attracted}\\\")\\n        if not attracted:\\n240→            fails.append(f\\\"attract did not start {page.evaluate('() => window.__game')}\\\")\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"f\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\"):\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract stayed after a key\\\")\\n        else:\\n            trace.append(\\\"attract left on a key\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(10500)\\n        page.mouse.click(420, 420)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n250→        if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\"):\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract stayed after a click\\\")\\n        else:\\n            trace.append(\\\"attract left on a click\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(10500)\\n        hold(page, 0, \\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.attract === false\\\")\\n        if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\"):\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract stayed after a pad press\\\")\\n        else:\\n            trace.append(\\\"attract left on a pad press\\\")\\n260→        save_after = page.evaluate(\\\"() => localStorage.getItem('thumb-yoga:save')\\\")\\n        trace.append(\\\"save unchanged\\\" if save_before == save_after else \\\"save changed\\\")\\n        if save_before != save_after:\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract wrote the save\\\")\\n        hold(page, 0, \\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'play'\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(500)\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"island.png\\\"))\\n        hold(page, 9, \\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'pause'\\\")\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"pause.png\\\"))\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=more]\\\").click()\\n270→        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=dev]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"dev.png\\\"))\\n        changed = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const range = document.querySelector('[data-ui=slider-range]');\\n              const before = window.__engine.state().settings['game.wobble.gain'];\\n              range.value = '20';\\n              range.dispatchEvent(new Event('input', { bubbles: true }));\\n280→              const after = window.__engine.state().settings['game.wobble.gain'];\\n              return { before, after, shown: range.value };\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        trace.append(f\\\"slider {changed}\\\")\\n        if changed[\\\"after\\\"] != 20:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"slider did not change the gain {changed}\\\")\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=reset]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        restored = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__engine.state().settings['game.wobble.gain']\\\")\\n290→        trace.append(f\\\"reset gain {restored}\\\")\\n        if restored not in (None, 14):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"reset left the gain at {restored}\\\")\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=back]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=about]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        about = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=about]\\\").inner_text()\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"about.png\\\"))\\n        for needle in (\\n300→            \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n            \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n            \\\"Sports\\\",\\n            \\\"third-person\\\",\\n            \\\"added on import\\\",\\n            \\\"Testing caught six issues\\\",\\n            \\\"Four were critical\\\",\\n            \\\"most helpful\\\",\\n            \\\"least helpful\\\",\\n            \\\"Scene actions\\\",\\n310→            \\\"playClip\\\",\\n            \\\"balance step\\\",\\n            \\\"hardest part\\\",\\n            \\\"None. The engine files were not changed.\\\",\\n            \\\"I would let a page add a mesh\\\",\\n            \\\"acceptance numbers\\\",\\n            \\\"group score\\\",\\n            \\\"one HTML file\\\",\\n            \\\"session client hash\\\",\\n        ):\\n320→            if needle not in about:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"about missing {needle}\\\")\\n        rows = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item]\\\").count()\\n        if rows > 6:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"menu has {rows} rows\\\")\\n        small = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const found = [];\\n              const walker = document.createTreeWalker(document.body, NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT);\\n              while (walker.nextNode()) {\\n330→                const text = walker.currentNode.textContent.trim();\\n                if (!text) continue;\\n                const el = walker.currentNode.parentElement;\\n                if (!el) continue;\\n                const style = getComputedStyle(el);\\n                if (style.display === 'none' || style.visibility === 'hidden') continue;\\n                const rect = el.getBoundingClientRect();\\n                if (rect.width < 1 || rect.height < 1) continue;\\n                const size = parseFloat(style.fontSize);\\n                if (size < 28) found.push(text.slice(0, 48) + ' ' + size);\\n340→              }\\n              return found.slice(0, 8);\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        if small:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"text under 28px {small}\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"menu rows {rows}\\\")\\n        trace.append(\\\"font ok\\\" if not small else f\\\"font {small}\\\")\\n        trace.append(\\\"about ok\\\" if not any(item.startswith(\\\"about missing\\\") for item in fails) else \\\"about incomplete\\\")\\n    except Exception as error:\\n350→        fails.append(f\\\"shell {error}\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"shell {error}\\\")\\n    finally:\\n        (out / \\\"browser.log\\\").write_text(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(trace) + \\\"\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n        page.close()\\n\\n\\ndef touch(browser, playwright, html: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    for name in (\\\"iPhone 13\\\", \\\"iPad (gen 7)\\\"):\\n        device = playwright.devices[name]\\n360→        context = browser.new_context(**device)\\n        page = context.new_page()\\n        try:\\n            page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n            page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true\\\", timeout=60000)\\n            text = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=note]\\\").inner_text()\\n            if \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" not in text:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"{name} note {text}\\\")\\n            if page.locator(\\\".touch-stick\\\").count() != 0:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"{name} drew a touch stick\\\")\\n370→            box = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=touch-settings]\\\").bounding_box()\\n            if not box:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"{name} has no Settings button\\\")\\n            else:\\n                page.touchscreen.tap(box[\\\"x\\\"] + box[\\\"width\\\"] / 2, box[\\\"y\\\"] + box[\\\"height\\\"] / 2)\\n                page.wait_for_timeout(400)\\n                if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.screen\\\") != \\\"settings\\\":\\n                    fails.append(f\\\"{name} tap did not open settings\\\")\\n            page.wait_for_timeout(11000)\\n            if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\") is not True:\\n380→                fails.append(f\\\"{name} attract did not run\\\")\\n        except Exception as error:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"{name} {error}\\\")\\n        finally:\\n            context.close()\\n\\n\\ndef webkit(playwright, html: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    try:\\n        browser = playwright.webkit.launch()\\n390→    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"webkit did not launch {error}\\\")\\n        return\\n    page = browser.new_page()\\n    try:\\n        page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(1500)\\n        text = page.locator(\\\"#msg\\\").inner_text()\\n        if \\\"Chrome\\\" not in text or \\\"Edge\\\" not in text:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"webkit message {text}\\\")\\n400→    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"webkit {error}\\\")\\n    finally:\\n        browser.close()\\n\\n\\ndef hub(browser, html: Path, out: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    root = html.parent\\n    server = ThreadingHTTPServer((\\\"127.0.0.1\\\", 0), handler(root))\\n    port = server.server_address[1]\\n410→    thread = threading.Thread(target=server.serve_forever, daemon=True)\\n    thread.start()\\n    (out / \\\"hub-port.txt\\\").write_text(str(port), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    game = \\\"/\\\" + quote(html.name)\\n    base = f\\\"http://127.0.0.1:{port}\\\"\\n    dev = next(path for path in root.iterdir() if path.is_dir() and (path / \\\"labs/game/hub/harness.html\\\").exists())\\n    client = (dev / \\\"labs/game/hub/session-client.txt\\\").read_bytes()\\n    digest = hashlib.sha256(client).hexdigest()\\n    (out / \\\"hub-client.sha\\\").write_text(digest + \\\"\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    if client not in html.read_bytes():\\n420→        fails.append(\\\"session client bytes are not in the html\\\")\\n    harness = f\\\"{base}/{quote(dev.name)}/labs/game/hub/harness.html\\\"\\n    lines: list[str] = []\\n    try:\\n        for query in (\\n            \\\"players=2&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n            \\\"players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n            \\\"players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n            \\\"players=3&scenario=host-leave&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n        ):\\n430→            run_hub(browser, f\\\"{harness}?game={quote(game, safe='/')}&{query}\\\", query, lines, fails)\\n        page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1280, \\\"height\\\": 720})\\n        try:\\n            page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n            page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'title'\\\", timeout=60000)\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Enter\\\")\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Space\\\")\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Enter\\\")\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Space\\\")\\n            page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n440→            client = page.evaluate(\\n                \\\"\\\"\\\"() => ({\\n                  present: typeof window.AIHub === 'object' && window.AIHub !== null,\\n                  active: window.AIHub && window.AIHub.active,\\n                  seeded: window.AIHub && window.AIHub.seeded,\\n                  native: Math.random.toString().includes('[native code]'),\\n                  errors: (window.__engine && window.__engine.errors) || [],\\n                  drawn: (() => { const c = document.querySelector('canvas'); return !!(c && c.width > 0); })(),\\n                })\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n            )\\n450→            if not client[\\\"present\\\"] or client[\\\"active\\\"] or client[\\\"seeded\\\"] or not client[\\\"native\\\"]:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"standalone client {client}\\\")\\n            if client[\\\"errors\\\"] or not client[\\\"drawn\\\"]:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"standalone screen {client}\\\")\\n            lines.append(f\\\"standalone {json.dumps(client)}\\\")\\n        finally:\\n            page.close()\\n    finally:\\n        server.shutdown()\\n        (out / \\\"hub.log\\\").write_text(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(lines), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n460→\\n\\ndef run_hub(browser, url: str, query: str, lines: list[str], fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1280, \\\"height\\\": 720})\\n    page.add_init_script(WATCH)\\n    bad: list[str] = []\\n    page.on(\\\"console\\\", lambda msg: bad.append(msg.text) if msg.text.startswith(\\\"[AIHub]\\\") else None)\\n    try:\\n        page.goto(url)\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\\\", timeout=120000)\\n470→        report = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__hubCheck\\\")\\n        ghosts = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => [...document.querySelectorAll('iframe')].map((frame) => {\\n              const win = frame.contentWindow;\\n              const state = win.__engine && win.__engine.state && win.__engine.state();\\n              const entities = (state && state.entities) || [];\\n              return {\\n                ready: !!(win.__engine && win.__engine.ready),\\n                errors: (win.__engine && win.__engine.errors && win.__engine.errors.length) || 0,\\n                ghosts: entities.filter((entity) => entity.ghost).length,\\n480→                trace: win.__readyTrace || [],\\n              };\\n            })\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        lines.append(query)\\n        lines.append(json.dumps({\\\"pass\\\": report.get(\\\"pass\\\") if report else None, \\\"checks\\\": report.get(\\\"checks\\\") if report else None, \\\"ghosts\\\": ghosts, \\\"aihub\\\": bad}))\\n        if not report or report.get(\\\"pass\\\") is not True:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"hub {query} {report}\\\")\\n        if \\\"players=2\\\" in query and not any(row[\\\"ghosts\\\"] > 0 for row in ghosts):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"hub {query} has no ghost\\\")\",\"content_concise\":\"90→\\ndef once(browser, html: Path, out: Path, n: int, fails: list[str]) -> str:\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1920, \\\"height\\\": 1080}, device_scale_factor=1)\\n    page.add_init_script(PAD + WATCH)\\n    logs: list[str] = []\\n    page.on(\\\"console\\\", lambda msg: logs.append(msg.text))\\n    page.on(\\\"pageerror\\\", lambda err: logs.append(f\\\"pageerror {err}\\\"))\\n    try:\\n        page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true\\\", timeout=60000)\\n100→        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        state = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const canvas = document.querySelector('canvas');\\n              const game = window.__game || {};\\n              return {\\n                ready: window.__engine.ready,\\n                errors: window.__engine.errors || [],\\n                game,\\n                canvas: { width: canvas ? canvas.width : 0, height: canvas ? canvas.height : 0 },\\n110→                view: { width: window.innerWidth, height: window.innerHeight },\\n              };\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        (out / f\\\"boot-{n}.log\\\").write_text(json.dumps(state, indent=2) + \\\"\\\\n\\\" + \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(logs), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(out / f\\\"boot-{n}.png\\\"))\\n        if n == 1:\\n            page.screenshot(path=str(out / \\\"shots\\\" / \\\"title.png\\\"))\\n        errors = state[\\\"errors\\\"]\\n        if state[\\\"ready\\\"] is not True:\\n120→            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} ready is false\\\")\\n        if errors:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} errors {errors}\\\")\\n        if any(\\\"webgl\\\" in json.dumps(errors).lower() or \\\"downgrade\\\" in json.dumps(errors).lower() for _ in [0]):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} downgraded\\\")\\n        game = state[\\\"game\\\"]\\n        if game.get(\\\"title\\\") != \\\"Thumb Yoga\\\" or game.get(\\\"screen\\\") != \\\"title\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} title screen {game}\\\")\\n        if game.get(\\\"volumes\\\", {}).get(\\\"music\\\") != 0.1:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} music {game.get('volumes')}\\\")\\n130→        canvas = state[\\\"canvas\\\"]\\n        view = state[\\\"view\\\"]\\n        if canvas[\\\"width\\\"] <= 0 or canvas[\\\"height\\\"] <= 0:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} canvas is empty\\\")\\n        if canvas[\\\"width\\\"] != view[\\\"width\\\"] or canvas[\\\"height\\\"] != view[\\\"height\\\"]:\\n            note = out / \\\"webgpu-readback.txt\\\"\\n            note.write_text(\\n                f\\\"drawing {canvas['width']}x{canvas['height']} view {view['width']}x{view['height']}\\\\n\\\",\\n                encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\",\\n            )\\n140→            fails.append(\\n                f\\\"boot {n} canvas {canvas['width']}x{canvas['height']} is not the view {view['width']}x{view['height']}\\\"\\n            )\\n        # A short key tap can be sampled by a catch-up step and never reach the menu. Hold Cross.\\n        hold(page, 0, \\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'play'\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(400)\\n        after = page.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ screen: window.__game.screen, event: window.__game.event, title: window.__game.title })\\\")\\n        if after.get(\\\"screen\\\") != \\\"play\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} did not leave the title\\\")\\n        return json.dumps(after, sort_keys=True)\\n150→    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} {error}\\\")\\n        return \\\"\\\"\\n    finally:\\n        page.close()\\n\\n\\ndef frames(page) -> None:\\n    page.evaluate(\\\"() => new Promise((resolve) => requestAnimationFrame(() => requestAnimationFrame(resolve)))\\\")\\n\\n160→\\ndef hold(page, index: int, until: str) -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Holds one standard-mapping button until `until` is true, then lets it go for a frame.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    page.evaluate(\\\"(index) => { window.__buttons[index] = 1; }\\\", index)\\n    page.wait_for_function(until, timeout=8000)\\n    page.evaluate(\\\"(index) => { window.__buttons[index] = 0; }\\\", index)\\n    frames(page)\\n\\n\\ndef pad_down(page) -> str:\\n170→    before = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.focus\\\")\\n    hold(page, 13, f\\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.focus !== {json.dumps(before)}\\\")\\n    return page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.focus\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef shell(browser, html: Path, out: Path, shots: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1920, \\\"height\\\": 1080}, device_scale_factor=1)\\n    page.add_init_script(PAD)\\n    trace: list[str] = []\\n    try:\\n180→        page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true\\\", timeout=60000)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        note = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=note]\\\").inner_text()\\n        glyph = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.glyphSet\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"start {glyph} {note}\\\")\\n        if glyph != \\\"playstation\\\" or \\\"Cross\\\" not in note:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"glyphs started as {glyph} {note}\\\")\\n        # Focus starts on Begin. Two downs skip the disabled rows and land on Settings.\\n        for _ in range(2):\\n190→            pad_down(page)\\n        focus = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.focus\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"pad focus {focus}\\\")\\n        if focus != \\\"Settings\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"pad did not reach Settings {focus}\\\")\\n        hold(page, 0, \\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'settings'\\\")\\n        for _ in range(3):\\n            pad_down(page)\\n        focus = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.focus\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"icons row {focus}\\\")\\n200→        if \\\"Icons\\\" not in focus:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"pad did not reach Icons {focus}\\\")\\n        hold(page, 0, \\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.glyphSet === 'xbox'\\\")\\n        xbox = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=note]\\\").inner_text()\\n        glyph = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.glyphSet\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"xbox {glyph} {xbox}\\\")\\n        for token in (\\\"A \\\", \\\"B \\\", \\\"X \\\", \\\"Y \\\", \\\"LB\\\", \\\"RB\\\", \\\"LT\\\", \\\"RT\\\"):\\n            if token not in xbox:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"xbox prompt missing {token} in {xbox}\\\")\\n                break\\n210→        if glyph != \\\"xbox\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"glyph set after icons {glyph} {xbox}\\\")\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"f\\\")\\n        keys = page.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ set: window.__game.glyphSet, note: document.querySelector('[data-ui=note]').textContent })\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"keys {keys}\\\")\\n        if keys[\\\"set\\\"] != \\\"keys\\\" or \\\"WASD\\\" not in keys[\\\"note\\\"]:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"keys prompt {keys}\\\")\\n        page.mouse.click(12, 12)\\n        mouse = page.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ set: window.__game.glyphSet, note: document.querySelector('[data-ui=note]').textContent })\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"mouse {mouse}\\\")\\n220→        if mouse[\\\"set\\\"] != \\\"mouse\\\" or \\\"Mouse\\\" not in mouse[\\\"note\\\"]:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"mouse prompt {mouse}\\\")\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"Escape\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'title'\\\", timeout=5000)\\n        page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const row = document.querySelector('[data-ui=item][data-id=\\\"settings\\\"]');\\n              row.dispatchEvent(new PointerEvent('pointermove', { bubbles: true, movementX: 4, movementY: 6 }));\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n230→        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        focus = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.focus\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"hover focus {focus}\\\")\\n        if focus != \\\"Settings\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"hover focus {focus}\\\")\\n        save_before = page.evaluate(\\\"() => localStorage.getItem('thumb-yoga:save')\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(10500)\\n        attracted = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract === true && window.__game.screen === 'attract'\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"attract after 10.5s {attracted}\\\")\\n        if not attracted:\\n240→            fails.append(f\\\"attract did not start {page.evaluate('() => window.__game')}\\\")\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"f\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\"):\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract stayed after a key\\\")\\n        else:\\n            trace.append(\\\"attract left on a key\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(10500)\\n        page.mouse.click(420, 420)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n250→        if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\"):\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract stayed after a click\\\")\\n        else:\\n            trace.append(\\\"attract left on a click\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(10500)\\n        hold(page, 0, \\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.attract === false\\\")\\n        if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\"):\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract stayed after a pad press\\\")\\n        else:\\n            trace.append(\\\"attract left on a pad press\\\")\\n260→        save_after = page.evaluate(\\\"() => localStorage.getItem('thumb-yoga:save')\\\")\\n        trace.append(\\\"save unchanged\\\" if save_before == save_after else \\\"save changed\\\")\\n        if save_before != save_after:\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract wrote the save\\\")\\n        hold(page, 0, \\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'play'\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(500)\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"island.png\\\"))\\n        hold(page, 9, \\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'pause'\\\")\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"pause.png\\\"))\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=more]\\\").click()\\n270→        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=dev]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"dev.png\\\"))\\n        changed = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const range = document.querySelector('[data-ui=slider-range]');\\n              const before = window.__engine.state().settings['game.wobble.gain'];\\n              range.value = '20';\\n              range.dispatchEvent(new Event('input', { bubbles: true }));\\n280→              const after = window.__engine.state().settings['game.wobble.gain'];\\n              return { before, after, shown: range.value };\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        trace.append(f\\\"slider {changed}\\\")\\n        if changed[\\\"after\\\"] != 20:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"slider did not change the gain {changed}\\\")\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=reset]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        restored = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__engine.state().settings['game.wobble.gain']\\\")\\n290→        trace.append(f\\\"reset gain {restored}\\\")\\n        if restored not in (None, 14):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"reset left the gain at {restored}\\\")\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=back]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=about]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        about = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=about]\\\").inner_text()\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"about.png\\\"))\\n        for needle in (\\n300→            \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n            \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n            \\\"Sports\\\",\\n            \\\"third-person\\\",\\n            \\\"added on import\\\",\\n            \\\"Testing caught six issues\\\",\\n            \\\"Four were critical\\\",\\n            \\\"most helpful\\\",\\n            \\\"least helpful\\\",\\n            \\\"Scene actions\\\",\\n310→            \\\"playClip\\\",\\n            \\\"balance step\\\",\\n            \\\"hardest part\\\",\\n            \\\"None. The engine files were not changed.\\\",\\n            \\\"I would let a page add a mesh\\\",\\n            \\\"acceptance numbers\\\",\\n            \\\"group score\\\",\\n            \\\"one HTML file\\\",\\n            \\\"session client hash\\\",\\n        ):\\n320→            if needle not in about:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"about missing {needle}\\\")\\n        rows = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item]\\\").count()\\n        if rows > 6:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"menu has {rows} rows\\\")\\n        small = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const found = [];\\n              const walker = document.createTreeWalker(document.body, NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT);\\n              while (walker.nextNode()) {\\n330→                const text = walker.currentNode.textContent.trim();\\n                if (!text) continue;\\n                const el = walker.currentNode.parentElement;\\n                if (!el) continue;\\n                const style = getComputedStyle(el);\\n                if (style.display === 'none' || style.visibility === 'hidden') continue;\\n                const rect = el.getBoundingClientRect();\\n                if (rect.width < 1 || rect.height < 1) continue;\\n                const size = parseFloat(style.fontSize);\\n                if (size < 28) found.push(text.slice(0, 48) + ' ' + size);\\n340→              }\\n              return found.slice(0, 8);\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        if small:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"text under 28px {small}\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"menu rows {rows}\\\")\\n        trace.append(\\\"font ok\\\" if not small else f\\\"font {small}\\\")\\n        trace.append(\\\"about ok\\\" if not any(item.startswith(\\\"about missing\\\") for item in fails) else \\\"about incomplete\\\")\\n    except Exception as error:\\n350→        fails.append(f\\\"shell {error}\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"shell {error}\\\")\\n    finally:\\n        (out / \\\"browser.log\\\").write_text(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(trace) + \\\"\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n        page.close()\\n\\n\\ndef touch(browser, playwright, html: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    for name in (\\\"iPhone 13\\\", \\\"iPad (gen 7)\\\"):\\n        device = playwright.devices[name]\\n360→        context = browser.new_context(**device)\\n        page = context.new_page()\\n        try:\\n            page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n            page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true\\\", timeout=60000)\\n            text = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=note]\\\").inner_text()\\n            if \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" not in text:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"{name} note {text}\\\")\\n            if page.locator(\\\".touch-stick\\\").count() != 0:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"{name} drew a touch stick\\\")\\n370→            box = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=touch-settings]\\\").bounding_box()\\n            if not box:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"{name} has no Settings button\\\")\\n            else:\\n                page.touchscreen.tap(box[\\\"x\\\"] + box[\\\"width\\\"] / 2, box[\\\"y\\\"] + box[\\\"height\\\"] / 2)\\n                page.wait_for_timeout(400)\\n                if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.screen\\\") != \\\"settings\\\":\\n                    fails.append(f\\\"{name} tap did not open settings\\\")\\n            page.wait_for_timeout(11000)\\n            if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\") is not True:\\n380→                fails.append(f\\\"{name} attract did not run\\\")\\n        except Exception as error:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"{name} {error}\\\")\\n        finally:\\n            context.close()\\n\\n\\ndef webkit(playwright, html: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    try:\\n        browser = playwright.webkit.launch()\\n390→    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"webkit did not launch {error}\\\")\\n        return\\n    page = browser.new_page()\\n    try:\\n        page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(1500)\\n        text = page.locator(\\\"#msg\\\").inner_text()\\n        if \\\"Chrome\\\" not in text or \\\"Edge\\\" not in text:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"webkit message {text}\\\")\\n400→    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"webkit {error}\\\")\\n    finally:\\n        browser.close()\\n\\n\\ndef hub(browser, html: Path, out: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    root = html.parent\\n    server = ThreadingHTTPServer((\\\"127.0.0.1\\\", 0), handler(root))\\n    port = server.server_address[1]\\n410→    thread = threading.Thread(target=server.serve_forever, daemon=True)\\n    thread.start()\\n    (out / \\\"hub-port.txt\\\").write_text(str(port), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    game = \\\"/\\\" + quote(html.name)\\n    base = f\\\"http://127.0.0.1:{port}\\\"\\n    dev = next(path for path in root.iterdir() if path.is_dir() and (path / \\\"labs/game/hub/harness.html\\\").exists())\\n    client = (dev / \\\"labs/game/hub/session-client.txt\\\").read_bytes()\\n    digest = hashlib.sha256(client).hexdigest()\\n    (out / \\\"hub-client.sha\\\").write_text(digest + \\\"\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    if client not in html.read_bytes():\\n420→        fails.append(\\\"session client bytes are not in the html\\\")\\n    harness = f\\\"{base}/{quote(dev.name)}/labs/game/hub/harness.html\\\"\\n    lines: list[str] = []\\n    try:\\n        for query in (\\n            \\\"players=2&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n            \\\"players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n            \\\"players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n            \\\"players=3&scenario=host-leave&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n        ):\\n430→            run_hub(browser, f\\\"{harness}?game={quote(game, safe='/')}&{query}\\\", query, lines, fails)\\n        page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1280, \\\"height\\\": 720})\\n        try:\\n            page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n            page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'title'\\\", timeout=60000)\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Enter\\\")\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Space\\\")\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Enter\\\")\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Space\\\")\\n            page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n440→            client = page.evaluate(\\n                \\\"\\\"\\\"() => ({\\n                  present: typeof window.AIHub === 'object' && window.AIHub !== null,\\n                  active: window.AIHub && window.AIHub.active,\\n                  seeded: window.AIHub && window.AIHub.seeded,\\n                  native: Math.random.toString().includes('[native code]'),\\n                  errors: (window.__engine && window.__engine.errors) || [],\\n                  drawn: (() => { const c = document.querySelector('canvas'); return !!(c && c.width > 0); })(),\\n                })\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n            )\\n450→            if not client[\\\"present\\\"] or client[\\\"active\\\"] or client[\\\"seeded\\\"] or not client[\\\"native\\\"]:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"standalone client {client}\\\")\\n            if client[\\\"errors\\\"] or not client[\\\"drawn\\\"]:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"standalone screen {client}\\\")\\n            lines.append(f\\\"standalone {json.dumps(client)}\\\")\\n        finally:\\n            page.close()\\n    finally:\\n        server.shutdown()\\n        (out / \\\"hub.log\\\").write_text(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(lines), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n460→\\n\\ndef run_hub(browser, url: str, query: str, lines: list[str], fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1280, \\\"height\\\": 720})\\n    page.add_init_script(WATCH)\\n    bad: list[str] = []\\n    page.on(\\\"console\\\", lambda msg: bad.append(msg.text) if msg.text.startswith(\\\"[AIHub]\\\") else None)\\n    try:\\n        page.goto(url)\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\\\", timeout=120000)\\n470→        report = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__hubCheck\\\")\\n        ghosts = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => [...document.querySelectorAll('iframe')].map((frame) => {\\n              const win = frame.contentWindow;\\n              const state = win.__engine && win.__engine.state && win.__engine.state();\\n              const entities = (state && state.entities) || [];\\n              return {\\n                ready: !!(win.__engine && win.__engine.ready),\\n                errors: (win.__engine && win.__engine.errors && win.__engine.errors.length) || 0,\\n                ghosts: entities.filter((entity) => entity.ghost).length,\\n480→                trace: win.__readyTrace || [],\\n              };\\n            })\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        lines.append(query)\\n        lines.append(json.dumps({\\\"pass\\\": report.get(\\\"pass\\\") if report else None, \\\"checks\\\": report.get(\\\"checks\\\") if report else None, \\\"ghosts\\\": ghosts, \\\"aihub\\\": bad}))\\n        if not report or report.get(\\\"pass\\\") is not True:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"hub {query} {report}\\\")\\n        if \\\"players=2\\\" in query and not any(row[\\\"ghosts\\\"] > 0 for row in ghosts):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"hub {query} has no ghost\\\")\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/tools/browse.py\",\"offset\":90,\"limit\":400,\"raw_output\":\"\\ndef once(browser, html: Path, out: Path, n: int, fails: list[str]) -> str:\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1920, \\\"height\\\": 1080}, device_scale_factor=1)\\n    page.add_init_script(PAD + WATCH)\\n    logs: list[str] = []\\n    page.on(\\\"console\\\", lambda msg: logs.append(msg.text))\\n    page.on(\\\"pageerror\\\", lambda err: logs.append(f\\\"pageerror {err}\\\"))\\n    try:\\n        page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true\\\", timeout=60000)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        state = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const canvas = document.querySelector('canvas');\\n              const game = window.__game || {};\\n              return {\\n                ready: window.__engine.ready,\\n                errors: window.__engine.errors || [],\\n                game,\\n                canvas: { width: canvas ? canvas.width : 0, height: canvas ? canvas.height : 0 },\\n                view: { width: window.innerWidth, height: window.innerHeight },\\n              };\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        (out / f\\\"boot-{n}.log\\\").write_text(json.dumps(state, indent=2) + \\\"\\\\n\\\" + \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(logs), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(out / f\\\"boot-{n}.png\\\"))\\n        if n == 1:\\n            page.screenshot(path=str(out / \\\"shots\\\" / \\\"title.png\\\"))\\n        errors = state[\\\"errors\\\"]\\n        if state[\\\"ready\\\"] is not True:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} ready is false\\\")\\n        if errors:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} errors {errors}\\\")\\n        if any(\\\"webgl\\\" in json.dumps(errors).lower() or \\\"downgrade\\\" in json.dumps(errors).lower() for _ in [0]):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} downgraded\\\")\\n        game = state[\\\"game\\\"]\\n        if game.get(\\\"title\\\") != \\\"Thumb Yoga\\\" or game.get(\\\"screen\\\") != \\\"title\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} title screen {game}\\\")\\n        if game.get(\\\"volumes\\\", {}).get(\\\"music\\\") != 0.1:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} music {game.get('volumes')}\\\")\\n        canvas = state[\\\"canvas\\\"]\\n        view = state[\\\"view\\\"]\\n        if canvas[\\\"width\\\"] <= 0 or canvas[\\\"height\\\"] <= 0:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} canvas is empty\\\")\\n        if canvas[\\\"width\\\"] != view[\\\"width\\\"] or canvas[\\\"height\\\"] != view[\\\"height\\\"]:\\n            note = out / \\\"webgpu-readback.txt\\\"\\n            note.write_text(\\n                f\\\"drawing {canvas['width']}x{canvas['height']} view {view['width']}x{view['height']}\\\\n\\\",\\n                encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\",\\n            )\\n            fails.append(\\n                f\\\"boot {n} canvas {canvas['width']}x{canvas['height']} is not the view {view['width']}x{view['height']}\\\"\\n            )\\n        # A short key tap can be sampled by a catch-up step and never reach the menu. Hold Cross.\\n        hold(page, 0, \\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'play'\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(400)\\n        after = page.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ screen: window.__game.screen, event: window.__game.event, title: window.__game.title })\\\")\\n        if after.get(\\\"screen\\\") != \\\"play\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} did not leave the title\\\")\\n        return json.dumps(after, sort_keys=True)\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"boot {n} {error}\\\")\\n        return \\\"\\\"\\n    finally:\\n        page.close()\\n\\n\\ndef frames(page) -> None:\\n    page.evaluate(\\\"() => new Promise((resolve) => requestAnimationFrame(() => requestAnimationFrame(resolve)))\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef hold(page, index: int, until: str) -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Holds one standard-mapping button until `until` is true, then lets it go for a frame.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    page.evaluate(\\\"(index) => { window.__buttons[index] = 1; }\\\", index)\\n    page.wait_for_function(until, timeout=8000)\\n    page.evaluate(\\\"(index) => { window.__buttons[index] = 0; }\\\", index)\\n    frames(page)\\n\\n\\ndef pad_down(page) -> str:\\n    before = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.focus\\\")\\n    hold(page, 13, f\\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.focus !== {json.dumps(before)}\\\")\\n    return page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.focus\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef shell(browser, html: Path, out: Path, shots: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1920, \\\"height\\\": 1080}, device_scale_factor=1)\\n    page.add_init_script(PAD)\\n    trace: list[str] = []\\n    try:\\n        page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true\\\", timeout=60000)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        note = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=note]\\\").inner_text()\\n        glyph = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.glyphSet\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"start {glyph} {note}\\\")\\n        if glyph != \\\"playstation\\\" or \\\"Cross\\\" not in note:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"glyphs started as {glyph} {note}\\\")\\n        # Focus starts on Begin. Two downs skip the disabled rows and land on Settings.\\n        for _ in range(2):\\n            pad_down(page)\\n        focus = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.focus\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"pad focus {focus}\\\")\\n        if focus != \\\"Settings\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"pad did not reach Settings {focus}\\\")\\n        hold(page, 0, \\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'settings'\\\")\\n        for _ in range(3):\\n            pad_down(page)\\n        focus = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.focus\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"icons row {focus}\\\")\\n        if \\\"Icons\\\" not in focus:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"pad did not reach Icons {focus}\\\")\\n        hold(page, 0, \\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.glyphSet === 'xbox'\\\")\\n        xbox = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=note]\\\").inner_text()\\n        glyph = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.glyphSet\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"xbox {glyph} {xbox}\\\")\\n        for token in (\\\"A \\\", \\\"B \\\", \\\"X \\\", \\\"Y \\\", \\\"LB\\\", \\\"RB\\\", \\\"LT\\\", \\\"RT\\\"):\\n            if token not in xbox:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"xbox prompt missing {token} in {xbox}\\\")\\n                break\\n        if glyph != \\\"xbox\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"glyph set after icons {glyph} {xbox}\\\")\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"f\\\")\\n        keys = page.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ set: window.__game.glyphSet, note: document.querySelector('[data-ui=note]').textContent })\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"keys {keys}\\\")\\n        if keys[\\\"set\\\"] != \\\"keys\\\" or \\\"WASD\\\" not in keys[\\\"note\\\"]:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"keys prompt {keys}\\\")\\n        page.mouse.click(12, 12)\\n        mouse = page.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ set: window.__game.glyphSet, note: document.querySelector('[data-ui=note]').textContent })\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"mouse {mouse}\\\")\\n        if mouse[\\\"set\\\"] != \\\"mouse\\\" or \\\"Mouse\\\" not in mouse[\\\"note\\\"]:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"mouse prompt {mouse}\\\")\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"Escape\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'title'\\\", timeout=5000)\\n        page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const row = document.querySelector('[data-ui=item][data-id=\\\"settings\\\"]');\\n              row.dispatchEvent(new PointerEvent('pointermove', { bubbles: true, movementX: 4, movementY: 6 }));\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        focus = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.focus\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"hover focus {focus}\\\")\\n        if focus != \\\"Settings\\\":\\n            fails.append(f\\\"hover focus {focus}\\\")\\n        save_before = page.evaluate(\\\"() => localStorage.getItem('thumb-yoga:save')\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(10500)\\n        attracted = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract === true && window.__game.screen === 'attract'\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"attract after 10.5s {attracted}\\\")\\n        if not attracted:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"attract did not start {page.evaluate('() => window.__game')}\\\")\\n        page.keyboard.press(\\\"f\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\"):\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract stayed after a key\\\")\\n        else:\\n            trace.append(\\\"attract left on a key\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(10500)\\n        page.mouse.click(420, 420)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\"):\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract stayed after a click\\\")\\n        else:\\n            trace.append(\\\"attract left on a click\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(10500)\\n        hold(page, 0, \\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.attract === false\\\")\\n        if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\"):\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract stayed after a pad press\\\")\\n        else:\\n            trace.append(\\\"attract left on a pad press\\\")\\n        save_after = page.evaluate(\\\"() => localStorage.getItem('thumb-yoga:save')\\\")\\n        trace.append(\\\"save unchanged\\\" if save_before == save_after else \\\"save changed\\\")\\n        if save_before != save_after:\\n            fails.append(\\\"attract wrote the save\\\")\\n        hold(page, 0, \\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'play'\\\")\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(500)\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"island.png\\\"))\\n        hold(page, 9, \\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'pause'\\\")\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"pause.png\\\"))\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=more]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=dev]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"dev.png\\\"))\\n        changed = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const range = document.querySelector('[data-ui=slider-range]');\\n              const before = window.__engine.state().settings['game.wobble.gain'];\\n              range.value = '20';\\n              range.dispatchEvent(new Event('input', { bubbles: true }));\\n              const after = window.__engine.state().settings['game.wobble.gain'];\\n              return { before, after, shown: range.value };\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        trace.append(f\\\"slider {changed}\\\")\\n        if changed[\\\"after\\\"] != 20:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"slider did not change the gain {changed}\\\")\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=reset]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        restored = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__engine.state().settings['game.wobble.gain']\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"reset gain {restored}\\\")\\n        if restored not in (None, 14):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"reset left the gain at {restored}\\\")\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=back]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(200)\\n        page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item][data-id=about]\\\").click()\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        about = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=about]\\\").inner_text()\\n        page.screenshot(path=str(shots / \\\"about.png\\\"))\\n        for needle in (\\n            \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n            \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n            \\\"Sports\\\",\\n            \\\"third-person\\\",\\n            \\\"added on import\\\",\\n            \\\"Testing caught six issues\\\",\\n            \\\"Four were critical\\\",\\n            \\\"most helpful\\\",\\n            \\\"least helpful\\\",\\n            \\\"Scene actions\\\",\\n            \\\"playClip\\\",\\n            \\\"balance step\\\",\\n            \\\"hardest part\\\",\\n            \\\"None. The engine files were not changed.\\\",\\n            \\\"I would let a page add a mesh\\\",\\n            \\\"acceptance numbers\\\",\\n            \\\"group score\\\",\\n            \\\"one HTML file\\\",\\n            \\\"session client hash\\\",\\n        ):\\n            if needle not in about:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"about missing {needle}\\\")\\n        rows = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=item]\\\").count()\\n        if rows > 6:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"menu has {rows} rows\\\")\\n        small = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => {\\n              const found = [];\\n              const walker = document.createTreeWalker(document.body, NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT);\\n              while (walker.nextNode()) {\\n                const text = walker.currentNode.textContent.trim();\\n                if (!text) continue;\\n                const el = walker.currentNode.parentElement;\\n                if (!el) continue;\\n                const style = getComputedStyle(el);\\n                if (style.display === 'none' || style.visibility === 'hidden') continue;\\n                const rect = el.getBoundingClientRect();\\n                if (rect.width < 1 || rect.height < 1) continue;\\n                const size = parseFloat(style.fontSize);\\n                if (size < 28) found.push(text.slice(0, 48) + ' ' + size);\\n              }\\n              return found.slice(0, 8);\\n            }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        if small:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"text under 28px {small}\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"menu rows {rows}\\\")\\n        trace.append(\\\"font ok\\\" if not small else f\\\"font {small}\\\")\\n        trace.append(\\\"about ok\\\" if not any(item.startswith(\\\"about missing\\\") for item in fails) else \\\"about incomplete\\\")\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"shell {error}\\\")\\n        trace.append(f\\\"shell {error}\\\")\\n    finally:\\n        (out / \\\"browser.log\\\").write_text(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(trace) + \\\"\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n        page.close()\\n\\n\\ndef touch(browser, playwright, html: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    for name in (\\\"iPhone 13\\\", \\\"iPad (gen 7)\\\"):\\n        device = playwright.devices[name]\\n        context = browser.new_context(**device)\\n        page = context.new_page()\\n        try:\\n            page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n            page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true\\\", timeout=60000)\\n            text = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=note]\\\").inner_text()\\n            if \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" not in text:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"{name} note {text}\\\")\\n            if page.locator(\\\".touch-stick\\\").count() != 0:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"{name} drew a touch stick\\\")\\n            box = page.locator(\\\"[data-ui=touch-settings]\\\").bounding_box()\\n            if not box:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"{name} has no Settings button\\\")\\n            else:\\n                page.touchscreen.tap(box[\\\"x\\\"] + box[\\\"width\\\"] / 2, box[\\\"y\\\"] + box[\\\"height\\\"] / 2)\\n                page.wait_for_timeout(400)\\n                if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.screen\\\") != \\\"settings\\\":\\n                    fails.append(f\\\"{name} tap did not open settings\\\")\\n            page.wait_for_timeout(11000)\\n            if page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__game.attract\\\") is not True:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"{name} attract did not run\\\")\\n        except Exception as error:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"{name} {error}\\\")\\n        finally:\\n            context.close()\\n\\n\\ndef webkit(playwright, html: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    try:\\n        browser = playwright.webkit.launch()\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"webkit did not launch {error}\\\")\\n        return\\n    page = browser.new_page()\\n    try:\\n        page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(1500)\\n        text = page.locator(\\\"#msg\\\").inner_text()\\n        if \\\"Chrome\\\" not in text or \\\"Edge\\\" not in text:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"webkit message {text}\\\")\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"webkit {error}\\\")\\n    finally:\\n        browser.close()\\n\\n\\ndef hub(browser, html: Path, out: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    root = html.parent\\n    server = ThreadingHTTPServer((\\\"127.0.0.1\\\", 0), handler(root))\\n    port = server.server_address[1]\\n    thread = threading.Thread(target=server.serve_forever, daemon=True)\\n    thread.start()\\n    (out / \\\"hub-port.txt\\\").write_text(str(port), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    game = \\\"/\\\" + quote(html.name)\\n    base = f\\\"http://127.0.0.1:{port}\\\"\\n    dev = next(path for path in root.iterdir() if path.is_dir() and (path / \\\"labs/game/hub/harness.html\\\").exists())\\n    client = (dev / \\\"labs/game/hub/session-client.txt\\\").read_bytes()\\n    digest = hashlib.sha256(client).hexdigest()\\n    (out / \\\"hub-client.sha\\\").write_text(digest + \\\"\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    if client not in html.read_bytes():\\n        fails.append(\\\"session client bytes are not in the html\\\")\\n    harness = f\\\"{base}/{quote(dev.name)}/labs/game/hub/harness.html\\\"\\n    lines: list[str] = []\\n    try:\\n        for query in (\\n            \\\"players=2&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n            \\\"players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n            \\\"players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n            \\\"players=3&scenario=host-leave&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\\",\\n        ):\\n            run_hub(browser, f\\\"{harness}?game={quote(game, safe='/')}&{query}\\\", query, lines, fails)\\n        page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1280, \\\"height\\\": 720})\\n        try:\\n            page.goto(html.as_uri())\\n            page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => window.__game && window.__game.screen === 'title'\\\", timeout=60000)\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Enter\\\")\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Space\\\")\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Enter\\\")\\n            page.keyboard.press(\\\"Space\\\")\\n            page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n            client = page.evaluate(\\n                \\\"\\\"\\\"() => ({\\n                  present: typeof window.AIHub === 'object' && window.AIHub !== null,\\n                  active: window.AIHub && window.AIHub.active,\\n                  seeded: window.AIHub && window.AIHub.seeded,\\n                  native: Math.random.toString().includes('[native code]'),\\n                  errors: (window.__engine && window.__engine.errors) || [],\\n                  drawn: (() => { const c = document.querySelector('canvas'); return !!(c && c.width > 0); })(),\\n                })\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n            )\\n            if not client[\\\"present\\\"] or client[\\\"active\\\"] or client[\\\"seeded\\\"] or not client[\\\"native\\\"]:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"standalone client {client}\\\")\\n            if client[\\\"errors\\\"] or not client[\\\"drawn\\\"]:\\n                fails.append(f\\\"standalone screen {client}\\\")\\n            lines.append(f\\\"standalone {json.dumps(client)}\\\")\\n        finally:\\n            page.close()\\n    finally:\\n        server.shutdown()\\n        (out / \\\"hub.log\\\").write_text(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(lines), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef run_hub(browser, url: str, query: str, lines: list[str], fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1280, \\\"height\\\": 720})\\n    page.add_init_script(WATCH)\\n    bad: list[str] = []\\n    page.on(\\\"console\\\", lambda msg: bad.append(msg.text) if msg.text.startswith(\\\"[AIHub]\\\") else None)\\n    try:\\n        page.goto(url)\\n        page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\\\", timeout=120000)\\n        report = page.evaluate(\\\"() => window.__hubCheck\\\")\\n        ghosts = page.evaluate(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"() => [...document.querySelectorAll('iframe')].map((frame) => {\\n              const win = frame.contentWindow;\\n              const state = win.__engine && win.__engine.state && win.__engine.state();\\n              const entities = (state && state.entities) || [];\\n              return {\\n                ready: !!(win.__engine && win.__engine.ready),\\n                errors: (win.__engine && win.__engine.errors && win.__engine.errors.length) || 0,\\n                ghosts: entities.filter((entity) => entity.ghost).length,\\n                trace: win.__readyTrace || [],\\n              };\\n            })\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        lines.append(query)\\n        lines.append(json.dumps({\\\"pass\\\": report.get(\\\"pass\\\") if report else None, \\\"checks\\\": report.get(\\\"checks\\\") if report else None, \\\"ghosts\\\": ghosts, \\\"aihub\\\": bad}))\\n        if not report or report.get(\\\"pass\\\") is not True:\\n            fails.append(f\\\"hub {query} {report}\\\")\\n        if \\\"players=2\\\" in query and not any(row[\\\"ghosts\\\"] > 0 for row in ghosts):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"hub {query} has no ghost\\\")\\n\",\"total_lines\":516}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"169392cc-abe8-4c2d-82da-3b10adb7a3ae"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_800","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A potential bug exists in the shell flow after attract.\n\nThe hold on Cross to exit attract releases the button after attract ends. The next screen depends on finishExit and startAttract. A Begin input might trigger once the menu returns.\n\nThe held Cross might trigger Begin before release, sending the game to play. The next hold for play is safe if already active. pad_down holds Down for focus changes with a 0.35s menu repeat.\n\nThe hold-edge fix only covers uiAccept, uiCancel, and pause. It does not cover uiDown. If the initial down edge is eaten by catch-up, holding Down should still repeat after 0.35s via menu.update(). This allows focus to move even when the first press is missed.\n\nThe Xbox toggle hold works correctly. If the accept edge is missed, the hold-edge fix calls pick() once when the hold starts, toggling the icons.\n\nKeyboard presses go directly through the stage keydown listener and noteDevice immediately, bypassing the simulated input edge entirely.\n\nAttract mode lasts 10.5 seconds idle. lastInput updates via noteDevice. A hover pointermove on settings may also update lastInput if movement is sufficient while no menu is active.\n\nThe stage pointermove listener returns early when a menu is active. It does not update lastInput during that time. This means a hover pointermove on the settings row cannot reset the attract idle timer while the menu remains open.\n\nThe menu's own pointermove handler might move focus to Settings without calling noteDevice. If so, lastInput stays from the Escape keypress and attract mode starts 10.5 seconds later. The test expects focus to reach Settings.\n\nThe attract timer check runs at roughly 10.7 seconds after the Escape keypress. At 2.5 fps, a frame must land between 10.0 and 10.7 seconds to catch the transition. A single 800ms delay could miss the window entirely. This makes the test flaky under load.\n\nDiagnostic frames ran at roughly 400ms with 11Gi of memory available, so the timing window should be adequate. The test samples attract mode at exactly 10.5 seconds. If no frame lands in that narrow window, the test fails even when attract begins slightly later, which is within the stated 10–11 second criterion.\n\nA timer-based attract check outside onFrame would be more reliable than frame-dependent sampling. The current frame timing should still satisfy the 10–11 second criterion, since 400 ms intervals place attract start between 10 and 10.4 seconds.\n\nThe wait_for_function call for the title screen can take up to five seconds. If it runs slowly, lastInput becomes stale and attract mode may begin before the hover pointermove resets it. If the screen is already on title, the wait returns immediately and the menu-open state preserves lastInput until the 10.5 second check.\n\nPressing F to exit attract calls noteDevice and sets exitPending. finishExit then executes on the following frame.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b960d4bd-b3fc-45e4-9884-f2277b81108a-76","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/stage.ts","offset":268,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5600,"output_tokens":1773,"cache_read_input_tokens":123648,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"af371826-e163-48c3-a103-770f96c40fbe"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b960d4bd-b3fc-45e4-9884-f2277b81108a-76","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"268→  const noteDevice = (device: string) => {\\n    lastDevice = device;\\n270→    glyphSet = device === 'keyboard' ? 'keys' : device === 'mouse' ? 'mouse' : icons;\\n    lastInput = performance.now();\\n    if (screen !== 'touch') note.textContent = promptLine(glyphSet);\\n    publish();\\n  };\\n  const exitAttract = () => {\\n    if (!attract) return;\\n    exitPending = true;\\n    lastInput = performance.now();\\n  };\\n280→  /** Leaves the demo after this frame has decided not to store it. */\\n  const finishExit = () => {\\n    if (!exitPending) return;\\n    exitPending = false;\\n    attract = false;\\n    lastInput = performance.now();\\n    inspector()?.set('game.auto', 'off');\\n    const seed = inspector()?.seed() ?? 1;\\n    inspector()?.seed(seed);\\n    if (armed) menus.showTitle();\\n290→    else screen = 'touch';\\n  };\\n  const startAttract = () => {\\n    attract = true;\\n    inspector()?.set('game.auto', 'attract');\\n    const seed = inspector()?.seed() ?? 1;\\n    inspector()?.seed(seed);\\n    if (screen === 'title') close();\\n    if (screen === 'title') screen = 'attract';\\n    publish();\\n300→  };\\n\\n  touchBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {\\n    touchAt = performance.now();\\n    menus.showSettings(0);\\n  });\\n  window.addEventListener(\\n    'keydown',\\n    (event) => {\\n      if (event.metaKey || event.ctrlKey || event.altKey) return;\\n310→      armed = true;\\n      noteDevice('keyboard');\\n      if (attract) exitAttract();\\n      else if (screen === 'touch') menus.showTitle();\\n      if (hub && screen === 'card') {\\n        if (event.code === 'Enter' || event.code === 'NumpadEnter') client?.answer('ready');\\n        if (event.code === 'KeyT') client?.answer('more');\\n      }\",\"content_concise\":\"268→  const noteDevice = (device: string) => {\\n    lastDevice = device;\\n270→    glyphSet = device === 'keyboard' ? 'keys' : device === 'mouse' ? 'mouse' : icons;\\n    lastInput = performance.now();\\n    if (screen !== 'touch') note.textContent = promptLine(glyphSet);\\n    publish();\\n  };\\n  const exitAttract = () => {\\n    if (!attract) return;\\n    exitPending = true;\\n    lastInput = performance.now();\\n  };\\n280→  /** Leaves the demo after this frame has decided not to store it. */\\n  const finishExit = () => {\\n    if (!exitPending) return;\\n    exitPending = false;\\n    attract = false;\\n    lastInput = performance.now();\\n    inspector()?.set('game.auto', 'off');\\n    const seed = inspector()?.seed() ?? 1;\\n    inspector()?.seed(seed);\\n    if (armed) menus.showTitle();\\n290→    else screen = 'touch';\\n  };\\n  const startAttract = () => {\\n    attract = true;\\n    inspector()?.set('game.auto', 'attract');\\n    const seed = inspector()?.seed() ?? 1;\\n    inspector()?.seed(seed);\\n    if (screen === 'title') close();\\n    if (screen === 'title') screen = 'attract';\\n    publish();\\n300→  };\\n\\n  touchBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {\\n    touchAt = performance.now();\\n    menus.showSettings(0);\\n  });\\n  window.addEventListener(\\n    'keydown',\\n    (event) => {\\n      if (event.metaKey || event.ctrlKey || event.altKey) return;\\n310→      armed = true;\\n      noteDevice('keyboard');\\n      if (attract) exitAttract();\\n      else if (screen === 'touch') menus.showTitle();\\n      if (hub && screen === 'card') {\\n        if (event.code === 'Enter' || event.code === 'NumpadEnter') client?.answer('ready');\\n        if (event.code === 'KeyT') client?.answer('more');\\n      }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/stage.ts\",\"offset\":268,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"  const noteDevice = (device: string) => {\\n    lastDevice = device;\\n    glyphSet = device === 'keyboard' ? 'keys' : device === 'mouse' ? 'mouse' : icons;\\n    lastInput = performance.now();\\n    if (screen !== 'touch') note.textContent = promptLine(glyphSet);\\n    publish();\\n  };\\n  const exitAttract = () => {\\n    if (!attract) return;\\n    exitPending = true;\\n    lastInput = performance.now();\\n  };\\n  /** Leaves the demo after this frame has decided not to store it. */\\n  const finishExit = () => {\\n    if (!exitPending) return;\\n    exitPending = false;\\n    attract = false;\\n    lastInput = performance.now();\\n    inspector()?.set('game.auto', 'off');\\n    const seed = inspector()?.seed() ?? 1;\\n    inspector()?.seed(seed);\\n    if (armed) menus.showTitle();\\n    else screen = 'touch';\\n  };\\n  const startAttract = () => {\\n    attract = true;\\n    inspector()?.set('game.auto', 'attract');\\n    const seed = inspector()?.seed() ?? 1;\\n    inspector()?.seed(seed);\\n    if (screen === 'title') close();\\n    if (screen === 'title') screen = 'attract';\\n    publish();\\n  };\\n\\n  touchBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {\\n    touchAt = performance.now();\\n    menus.showSettings(0);\\n  });\\n  window.addEventListener(\\n    'keydown',\\n    (event) => {\\n      if (event.metaKey || event.ctrlKey || event.altKey) return;\\n      armed = true;\\n      noteDevice('keyboard');\\n      if (attract) exitAttract();\\n      else if (screen === 'touch') menus.showTitle();\\n      if (hub && screen === 'card') {\\n        if (event.code === 'Enter' || event.code === 'NumpadEnter') client?.answer('ready');\\n        if (event.code === 'KeyT') client?.answer('more');\\n      }\\n\",\"total_lines\":592}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"64d54703-0bbc-4f4d-9ac0-929f500f1e6d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_801","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The attract exit is deferred to finishExit so remember() does not save the demo.\n\nA keydown between frames could let remember() run before attract is cleared. That would save the demo instead of skipping it.\n\nThe test waits 300ms for attract to end. If the next frame is later, remember() runs and saves the demo. Calling finishExit immediately in the input handler avoids this, but remember() might still run before reseed completes.\n\nfinishExit is synchronous. It sets attract false, then calls seed() to replace the world and return to title mode.\n\nThere is a risk of session mismatch. The loop steps the original `started` run from engine.ts. Drawing uses the current session via `parts.run!.session`. Both paths call `inspector.seed()`.\n\nThe next step is to determine what `inspector.seed()` actually does.\n\n`inspector.seed()` calls `host.restart()`, which reassigns the `run` variable. The simulation loop's `stepOnce` closure captures this reassigned `run.session`, so steps correctly target the new session after restart. Drawing also reads from the updated session, so there is no mismatch.\n\nCalling finishExit directly from the event handler fixes the 300ms race. Attract becomes false immediately, so remember() skips title mode and does not save the demo.\n\nexitAttract now calls finishExit immediately after setting exitPending. The next frame's remember sees attract false and title mode, so it skips saving. The interaction between startAttract and finishExit seeds is still being checked.\n\nThe demo world is discarded. The exit handler runs in the capture phase before the engine's bubble-phase listener, so it cannot be re-entrant with world.run.\n\nThe attract pad exit is handled inside onFrame before remember and finishExit. If exitAttract immediately calls finishExit, the world is restarted and the title menu opens before the frame ends.\n\nCalling finishExit before remember inside the frame would let remember run with the old demo snap while attract is already false. That would write the demo save. The pad exit must defer finishExit until after remember.\n\nImmediate finishExit is safe for keydown because the next frame's remember sees title mode. The pad path defers exit and polls attract for up to eight seconds, so slow frames are fine there. The actual failures are the 300ms waits after key and click.\n\nThe 300ms waits in browse.py sample attract once after a fixed timeout. If no frame runs, attract remains true and the test fails.\n\nThe fix is to wait for attract === false with a timeout instead of using a fixed delay. The game exits on the next frame, so the criterion only requires exit after key, click, or pad input, not within 300ms.\n\nThe test should use `wait_for_function` with an 8-second timeout to poll for `attract === false` after both key and click. This is a test robustness fix, not a game change. The glyph checks that follow the input are synchronous evaluations.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c8bedc30-4e22-4f6c-8145-deda09cb14ed-77","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pointermove|mousemove|hover","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/ui/menu.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2336,"output_tokens":1949,"cache_read_input_tokens":129152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"4a17580e-5971-4213-a017-c5701a97c7b7"}
