{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a7c55ed9-fe95-4ab7-a532-49f6d93ccbe3-85","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"53→def main() -> int:\\n    html = Path(sys.argv[1]).resolve()\\n    out = Path(sys.argv[2]).resolve()\\n    out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    shots = out / \\\"shots\\\"\\n    shots.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\\n    fails: list[str] = []\\n60→    try:\\n        with sync_playwright() as p:\\n            try:\\n                browser = p.chromium.launch(executable_path=CHROME, args=FLAGS)\\n            except Exception as error:\\n                (out / \\\"launch-error.txt\\\").write_text(str(error), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n                print(\\\"LAUNCH_ERROR\\\")\\n                return 0\\n            try:\\n                boot(browser, html, out, fails)\\n70→                if not any(item.startswith(\\\"boot\\\") for item in fails):\\n                    shell(browser, html, out, shots, fails)\\n                    touch(browser, p, html, fails)\\n                    hub(browser, html, out, fails)\\n            finally:\\n                browser.close()\\n            webkit(p, html, fails)\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        if \\\"launch-error\\\" not in str(error):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"browser crashed: {error}\\\")\\n80→    for item in fails:\\n        print(f\\\"FAIL {item}\\\")\\n    return 1 if fails else 0\\n\\n\\ndef boot(browser, html: Path, out: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    marks = [once(browser, html, out, 1, fails), once(browser, html, out, 2, fails)]\\n    if marks[0] and marks[1] and marks[0] != marks[1]:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"boot paths disagree {marks[0]} vs {marks[1]}\\\")\\n\\n90→\\ndef once(browser, html: Path, out: Path, n: int, fails: list[str]) -> str:\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1920, \\\"height\\\": 1080}, device_scale_factor=1)\",\"content_concise\":\"53→def main() -> int:\\n    html = Path(sys.argv[1]).resolve()\\n    out = Path(sys.argv[2]).resolve()\\n    out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    shots = out / \\\"shots\\\"\\n    shots.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\\n    fails: list[str] = []\\n60→    try:\\n        with sync_playwright() as p:\\n            try:\\n                browser = p.chromium.launch(executable_path=CHROME, args=FLAGS)\\n            except Exception as error:\\n                (out / \\\"launch-error.txt\\\").write_text(str(error), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n                print(\\\"LAUNCH_ERROR\\\")\\n                return 0\\n            try:\\n                boot(browser, html, out, fails)\\n70→                if not any(item.startswith(\\\"boot\\\") for item in fails):\\n                    shell(browser, html, out, shots, fails)\\n                    touch(browser, p, html, fails)\\n                    hub(browser, html, out, fails)\\n            finally:\\n                browser.close()\\n            webkit(p, html, fails)\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        if \\\"launch-error\\\" not in str(error):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"browser crashed: {error}\\\")\\n80→    for item in fails:\\n        print(f\\\"FAIL {item}\\\")\\n    return 1 if fails else 0\\n\\n\\ndef boot(browser, html: Path, out: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    marks = [once(browser, html, out, 1, fails), once(browser, html, out, 2, fails)]\\n    if marks[0] and marks[1] and marks[0] != marks[1]:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"boot paths disagree {marks[0]} vs {marks[1]}\\\")\\n\\n90→\\ndef once(browser, html: Path, out: Path, n: int, fails: list[str]) -> str:\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1920, \\\"height\\\": 1080}, device_scale_factor=1)\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/tools/browse.py\",\"offset\":53,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"def main() -> int:\\n    html = Path(sys.argv[1]).resolve()\\n    out = Path(sys.argv[2]).resolve()\\n    out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    shots = out / \\\"shots\\\"\\n    shots.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\\n    fails: list[str] = []\\n    try:\\n        with sync_playwright() as p:\\n            try:\\n                browser = p.chromium.launch(executable_path=CHROME, args=FLAGS)\\n            except Exception as error:\\n                (out / \\\"launch-error.txt\\\").write_text(str(error), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n                print(\\\"LAUNCH_ERROR\\\")\\n                return 0\\n            try:\\n                boot(browser, html, out, fails)\\n                if not any(item.startswith(\\\"boot\\\") for item in fails):\\n                    shell(browser, html, out, shots, fails)\\n                    touch(browser, p, html, fails)\\n                    hub(browser, html, out, fails)\\n            finally:\\n                browser.close()\\n            webkit(p, html, fails)\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        if \\\"launch-error\\\" not in str(error):\\n            fails.append(f\\\"browser crashed: {error}\\\")\\n    for item in fails:\\n        print(f\\\"FAIL {item}\\\")\\n    return 1 if fails else 0\\n\\n\\ndef boot(browser, html: Path, out: Path, fails: list[str]) -> None:\\n    marks = [once(browser, html, out, 1, fails), once(browser, html, out, 2, fails)]\\n    if marks[0] and marks[1] and marks[0] != marks[1]:\\n        fails.append(f\\\"boot paths disagree {marks[0]} vs {marks[1]}\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef once(browser, html: Path, out: Path, n: int, fails: list[str]) -> str:\\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\\\"width\\\": 1920, \\\"height\\\": 1080}, device_scale_factor=1)\\n\",\"total_lines\":516}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"41bb3712-971a-43db-8510-628b0826b36d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_810","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Webkit launches after the Chromium browser closes.\n\nOnly one browser process is needed. Hub and touch use sequential pages and contexts within that single process. Two fixes are planned before verification: stage.ts will publish focus immediately on move, and browse.py will wait for attract to become false instead of a fixed delay.\n\nBoot path comparison is flaky. A boot that runs the next frame includes an event, while one that does not leaves it empty. This causes the two boot paths to disagree and fail.\n\nThe 400ms boot wait is unstable because a frame can slip in during that window. I will make the comparison stable by either waiting for the event to become non-empty or comparing only screen and title.\n\nThe correct fix is to snap the event in the same frame as begin, so both boots see event morning before hold() returns. This satisfies the criterion that the menu path changes __game identically each time.\n\nThe re-read fix has a sequencing problem. publish() fires before the frame function can re-read snap and publish again, so event still reads as empty when screen becomes play.\n\nWait_for_function can return mid-frame while event is still empty. The frame then re-reads and publishes morning. Playwright polls cannot interleave inside a synchronous frame. The test evaluates after the frame finishes.\n\nThe synchronous publish inside pickTitle completes before the frame ends. Re-reading snap before the final publish ensures event is morning when wait_for_function returns. Without that re-read, the event stays empty until the next frame, so the 400ms boot wait can slip past it and cause disagreement between boots. This fix must be applied before verification.\n\nThe synchronous frame callback means observers only see the final publish, so re-reading snap before the final publish is safe. I will also make show() compact.\n\nTouch settings will use wait_for_function for safety, though the 400ms check is likely sufficient. The touch attract timeout stays at eleven seconds. Focus is excluded from the boot comparison, so only screen, event, and title are checked. Re-reading snap before publish ensures both boots see the same event value.\n\nThe seed() path in attract is separate. I will replace the snap assignment block with a helper function to keep show() under 600 lines, then run eslint on stage.ts and launch the official verify.\n\nThe verify script buffers vitest output until completion, so verify.log stays empty until the process ends. The monitor should poll the process PID and report DONE or FAILED once it exits.\n\nThe verify run is expected to take ten to twenty minutes. It covers vitest, replay browser, onefile, and the full browse suite with multiple boots and attract waits.\n\nThe browse suite alone takes about six minutes. Total verify time is roughly fifteen to twenty minutes. I will export CHROMIUM_PATH and PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE, set VERIFY_OUT to scratch, and avoid parallel npm test runs. I am also considering tightening the boot comparison in browse.py to screen and title only as an extra safeguard.\n\nThe event stays morning even if the next simulation step runs before the draw callback, so both boots remain aligned. I will now implement the code changes and start verify. The hud-debug file will be deleted after the goal ends.\n\nI will declare `snap` as a mutable variable near `shownFrame` and import `emptySnap`. The `show()` function will be placed just before the return object, declared after the `live` object so it can assign `follow` and `live.event` directly.\n\nThe `frame` function will call `show(readSnap(drawn))` twice: once before `drive(input, snap)` and again after it. This second call catches any state change from `game.start` inside `drive`.\n\nThe `if` check after `wait_for_function` in browse.py is redundant because the call throws an exception on timeout, which fails the shell step.\n\nThe redundant `if` after `wait_for_function` in browse.py is acceptable because a timeout raises an exception that the shell catches. The 400ms check in touch settings will be removed and replaced by `wait_for_function` to wait for the settings screen. Hover delays can also be tightened with `wait_for_function` on focus.\n\nThe 200ms hover delay is unnecessary because the synchronous evaluate dispatches the move event and publishes focus before returning. The pad_down focus path is also safe: menu.update sets the index, the frame callback updates focus from the selected item, and hold waits for that change to register before yielding.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1bba0e36-7987-49d3-a5b9-9001eba0bfc7-86","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"onMove","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/ui/menu.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":608,"output_tokens":3328,"cache_read_input_tokens":139904,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"aeeaa5de-78ab-4a37-9ba8-fbd9945de4a4"}
