{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_820","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md is located in the dev folder, which the engine check monitors.\n\nThe static pass checks the work root and game folder. TASK.md hand-in items belong in the work root. ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md belongs in the dev folder.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-50bd96a8-baba-467f-a42a-6e5b631461d3-105","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md","limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-50bd96a8-baba-467f-a42a-6e5b631461d3-106","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"TODO|FIXME|placeholder|stub","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game","glob":"*.{ts,js,mjs,py,md,json}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3911,"output_tokens":444,"cache_read_input_tokens":155648,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"33338338-62a2-4f59-9f50-b9e37a2f1f25"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-50bd96a8-baba-467f-a42a-6e5b631461d3-105","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Engine feedback: thumb-yoga\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at e7a1243) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n- Let a page add a mesh. The retreat needed a readable guest and a few simple solids. There is no public way to register a generated mesh, so the body stays on the engine humanoid and the props stay on the built-in parts. A `geometry:cylinder` is also missing. A frustum stood in for a post.\\n10→- Start the music bus at 0.1, or let `createAudio` take a default. The bus comes up at 0.5. This game has to call `audio.volume('music', 0.1)` before a save can raise it, because a fresh stay must be a tenth.\\n- `playClip` during `setup` throws. A rest pose queued from setup never starts. Clips are played at spawn instead. Setup should accept the same call, or the error should say to wait for spawn.\\n- `spawnProp` with no yaw builds a NaN quaternion and the sim blows up. Yaw should default to 0. Every prop in this game passes one.\\n- A prop part's offset field is `position`. Code that says `at`, which the rest of the engine uses, is ignored and the part sits on the origin. One name would do.\\n- `headlessHost(engine).session.world` is a frozen recording. The live world is `createAppHost(...).session.world`, and `inspector.seed()` replaces that session, so a cached world goes stale. The frozen view should be named as a recording, and `seed` should say that old handles die.\\n- Query keys the engine does not know fail the boot. An AI Hub page arrives with `?aihub=1` and friends. Those keys have to be stripped from the string passed to `createEngine` or the page never starts. Unknown keys could be ignored.\\n- `input.prompt` is Xbox. A game whose default glyphs are PlayStation cannot use it. The prompt should follow the pad the browser reported, or the page should be able to set the family.\\n- The touch stick is drawn unless the page sets `touch=off`. A 10-foot game that must refuse touch play has to know that secret. A `createEngine` flag would be the obvious place.\\n- `gfx.resolution=auto`, when the look names no resolution, becomes `pixels` and caps the buffer around 330 lines. A check that the drawing buffer matches the view then fails on a correct page. `full` has to be set by hand.\\n- There is no `inspector.reset`. Live sliders put the defaults back by reading `describe('setting', path)` and calling `set`. A reset that restores every `game.*` default would match the dev-mode job.\\n20→- `node x new` prints `NEW_DOCS` lines about `labs/playground/…` even when the entry is written and its test passes. The docs check is tripping over its own guide. Those lines should not look like a failed command.\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n- From `labs/game/scenes/*.ts` the sim API is `../../../engine/sim-api`. From `labs/game/scenes/events/*.ts` it is `../../../../engine/sim-api`. There is no alias. The first import, one folder short, typechecks as a missing module and the event never loads.\\n- `createMenu` will show more than six rows. A 10-foot page has to slice the list itself.\\n- The hard line cap is 600. The fetched hub round, plus the `@file` comment this repo requires, was 603 lines and `eslint` failed `hard-cap/max-lines`. The protocol file should be allowed to stay the file the hub shipped. The comment was shortened so the cap would pass. Behaviour was not changed.\\n- The plan pinned session-client SHA-256 `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a`. The file fetched from the raw URL banners 1.4.0 and hashes to `6ab6be43898e2db069bc21a94757d77d9c3f2a0cb76f01186490d3bd88d8717a`. The banner did not move when the bytes did.\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n30→\\nNone. No file under `engine/` was edited. `npm run check` should still match `engine-lock.json`.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Engine feedback: thumb-yoga\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at e7a1243) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n- Let a page add a mesh. The retreat needed a readable guest and a few simple solids. There is no public way to register a generated mesh, so the body stays on the engine humanoid and the props stay on the built-in parts. A `geometry:cylinder` is also missing. A frustum stood in for a post.\\n10→- Start the music bus at 0.1, or let `createAudio` take a default. The bus comes up at 0.5. This game has to call `audio.volume('music', 0.1)` before a save can raise it, because a fresh stay must be a tenth.\\n- `playClip` during `setup` throws. A rest pose queued from setup never starts. Clips are played at spawn instead. Setup should accept the same call, or the error should say to wait for spawn.\\n- `spawnProp` with no yaw builds a NaN quaternion and the sim blows up. Yaw should default to 0. Every prop in this game passes one.\\n- A prop part's offset field is `position`. Code that says `at`, which the rest of the engine uses, is ignored and the part sits on the origin. One name would do.\\n- `headlessHost(engine).session.world` is a frozen recording. The live world is `createAppHost(...).session.world`, and `inspector.seed()` replaces that session, so a cached world goes stale. The frozen view should be named as a recording, and `seed` should say that old handles die.\\n- Query keys the engine does not know fail the boot. An AI Hub page arrives with `?aihub=1` and friends. Those keys have to be stripped from the string passed to `createEngine` or the page never starts. Unknown keys could be ignored.\\n- `input.prompt` is Xbox. A game whose default glyphs are PlayStation cannot use it. The prompt should follow the pad the browser reported, or the page should be able to set the family.\\n- The touch stick is drawn unless the page sets `touch=off`. A 10-foot game that must refuse touch play has to know that secret. A `createEngine` flag would be the obvious place.\\n- `gfx.resolution=auto`, when the look names no resolution, becomes `pixels` and caps the buffer around 330 lines. A check that the drawing buffer matches the view then fails on a correct page. `full` has to be set by hand.\\n- There is no `inspector.reset`. Live sliders put the defaults back by reading `describe('setting', path)` and calling `set`. A reset that restores every `game.*` default would match the dev-mode job.\\n20→- `node x new` prints `NEW_DOCS` lines about `labs/playground/…` even when the entry is written and its test passes. The docs check is tripping over its own guide. Those lines should not look like a failed command.\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n- From `labs/game/scenes/*.ts` the sim API is `../../../engine/sim-api`. From `labs/game/scenes/events/*.ts` it is `../../../../engine/sim-api`. There is no alias. The first import, one folder short, typechecks as a missing module and the event never loads.\\n- `createMenu` will show more than six rows. A 10-foot page has to slice the list itself.\\n- The hard line cap is 600. The fetched hub round, plus the `@file` comment this repo requires, was 603 lines and `eslint` failed `hard-cap/max-lines`. The protocol file should be allowed to stay the file the hub shipped. The comment was shortened so the cap would pass. Behaviour was not changed.\\n- The plan pinned session-client SHA-256 `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a`. The file fetched from the raw URL banners 1.4.0 and hashes to `6ab6be43898e2db069bc21a94757d77d9c3f2a0cb76f01186490d3bd88d8717a`. The banner did not move when the bytes did.\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n30→\\nNone. No file under `engine/` was edited. `npm run check` should still match `engine-lock.json`.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"# Engine feedback: thumb-yoga\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at e7a1243) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n- Let a page add a mesh. The retreat needed a readable guest and a few simple solids. There is no public way to register a generated mesh, so the body stays on the engine humanoid and the props stay on the built-in parts. A `geometry:cylinder` is also missing. A frustum stood in for a post.\\n- Start the music bus at 0.1, or let `createAudio` take a default. The bus comes up at 0.5. This game has to call `audio.volume('music', 0.1)` before a save can raise it, because a fresh stay must be a tenth.\\n- `playClip` during `setup` throws. A rest pose queued from setup never starts. Clips are played at spawn instead. Setup should accept the same call, or the error should say to wait for spawn.\\n- `spawnProp` with no yaw builds a NaN quaternion and the sim blows up. Yaw should default to 0. Every prop in this game passes one.\\n- A prop part's offset field is `position`. Code that says `at`, which the rest of the engine uses, is ignored and the part sits on the origin. One name would do.\\n- `headlessHost(engine).session.world` is a frozen recording. The live world is `createAppHost(...).session.world`, and `inspector.seed()` replaces that session, so a cached world goes stale. The frozen view should be named as a recording, and `seed` should say that old handles die.\\n- Query keys the engine does not know fail the boot. An AI Hub page arrives with `?aihub=1` and friends. Those keys have to be stripped from the string passed to `createEngine` or the page never starts. Unknown keys could be ignored.\\n- `input.prompt` is Xbox. A game whose default glyphs are PlayStation cannot use it. The prompt should follow the pad the browser reported, or the page should be able to set the family.\\n- The touch stick is drawn unless the page sets `touch=off`. A 10-foot game that must refuse touch play has to know that secret. A `createEngine` flag would be the obvious place.\\n- `gfx.resolution=auto`, when the look names no resolution, becomes `pixels` and caps the buffer around 330 lines. A check that the drawing buffer matches the view then fails on a correct page. `full` has to be set by hand.\\n- There is no `inspector.reset`. Live sliders put the defaults back by reading `describe('setting', path)` and calling `set`. A reset that restores every `game.*` default would match the dev-mode job.\\n- `node x new` prints `NEW_DOCS` lines about `labs/playground/…` even when the entry is written and its test passes. The docs check is tripping over its own guide. Those lines should not look like a failed command.\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n- From `labs/game/scenes/*.ts` the sim API is `../../../engine/sim-api`. From `labs/game/scenes/events/*.ts` it is `../../../../engine/sim-api`. There is no alias. The first import, one folder short, typechecks as a missing module and the event never loads.\\n- `createMenu` will show more than six rows. A 10-foot page has to slice the list itself.\\n- The hard line cap is 600. The fetched hub round, plus the `@file` comment this repo requires, was 603 lines and `eslint` failed `hard-cap/max-lines`. The protocol file should be allowed to stay the file the hub shipped. The comment was shortened so the cap would pass. Behaviour was not changed.\\n- The plan pinned session-client SHA-256 `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a`. The file fetched from the raw URL banners 1.4.0 and hashes to `6ab6be43898e2db069bc21a94757d77d9c3f2a0cb76f01186490d3bd88d8717a`. The banner did not move when the bytes did.\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\nNone. No file under `engine/` was edited. `npm run check` should still match `engine-lock.json`.\\n\",\"total_lines\":31}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-50bd96a8-baba-467f-a42a-6e5b631461d3-106","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"91978f0a-99fe-4891-8ea4-3bc34ba8d9c9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_821","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"ENGINE-FEEDBACK looks solid. The TODO search is clean.\n\nHand-in docs exist. I will add the menu press-edge issue to ENGINE-FEEDBACK as a short bullet. This records a real engine surprise without affecting verification.\n\nThe press-edge issue will be added under Friction. The page treats a new hold of `uiAccept`, `uiCancel`, and `pause` as the edge when `pressed` is false. The menu's own repeat already covers Up and Down after 0.35 s.\n\nI will add the friction bullet while verify runs. I will review the goal plan deviations text next so I can write it quickly after verify. I will not flip boxes yet. I am waiting for the monitor to wake me. I am also checking if anything else could fail check that I can preflight without browsers.\n\nI will not run `npm run check` until verify's browsers finish, to avoid memory contention. I also verified the new `onMove` callback types against `MenuItem`; they look correct.\n\nI will update the todos to mark the HUD complete and verify running. I will not poll the verify log while it is empty. After the monitor signals DONE, I will read the log to confirm seeds, songs, syllables, replay, zero failures, and exit code 0. Then I will run npm test and npm run check sequentially once browsers are gone. Finally I will flip the plan checkboxes with evidence and add the deviations section.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-88a030a5-153b-4902-96b7-7247fed69493-107","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md","old_string":"## Friction\n\n- From `labs/game/scenes/*.ts` the sim API is `../../../engine/sim-api`.","new_string":"## Friction\n\n- `input.pressed` is one sample for the whole drawn frame, and a catch-up step can take that sampl