{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_825","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Boot 1 timed out after 8000ms while waiting for a function.\n\nThe 8-second hold timeout likely failed because the official 1920x1080 browse is slower than the debug 1280x720 version. Heavy GPU load may delay the first frames and prevent input from being sampled within the window.\n\nThe canvas size check runs before the hold begins, so it cannot explain the timeout. The failure is purely the 8-second wait_for_function exception. I am now comparing the working debug run against the failing official browse to find the real cause.\n\nThe official browse includes a WATCH init script plus PAD. Memory pressure from the prior replay browser may be slowing frame processing. A bug in hold() combined with WATCH is also possible. The menu might not be focused or button 0 might not be uiAccept. The boot 1 screenshot and state check could add extra delay before the hold begins. I will read boot-1.log, browser.log, the WATCH script, and boot-1.png to find the cause.\n\nThe exception is caught inside once() and returned as a failure string. This prevents the shell from running. Only boot 1 failed. Boot 2 may have succeeded, or it was never reached.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-50ff891a-e242-4d68-ba79-26f8e8d871bf-113","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/boot-1.log","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-50ff891a-e242-4d68-ba79-26f8e8d871bf-114","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/boot-2.log","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-50ff891a-e242-4d68-ba79-26f8e8d871bf-115","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104