{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-486f750a-f326-4716-bd51-6d886d76af6c-132","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"160→  stick: { anchor: readonly number[]; knob: readonly number[] } | null;\\n  /** The controls under a finger, by name (`data-action` or `data-tap`): they look pressed. */\\n  down: readonly string[];\\n  /** An open panel covers the game: the buttons and the stick hide, the menu button stays. */\\n  covered: boolean;\\n  /** The screen's CSS size, for `--touch-k`. */\\n  width: number;\\n  height: number;\\n}\\n\\n170→/** The touch controls' layer in a page. */\\nexport interface TouchLayer {\\n  /** The layer's root element (`.touch-layer`). */\\n  readonly root: HTMLElement;\\n  /** Shows `state`. Call once per frame. */\\n  update(state: TouchLayerState): void;\\n  /** Removes the layer. */\\n  dispose(): void;\\n}\\n\\n180→/** Builds the layer for `layout` (null: only the stick) and appends it to `document.body`. */\\nexport function createTouchLayer(document: Document, layout: TouchLayout | null): TouchLayer {\\n  const root = document.createElement('div');\\n  root.className = 'touch-layer';\\n  root.hidden = true;\\n  const stick = document.createElement('div');\\n  stick.className = 'touch-stick';\\n  const knob = document.createElement('div');\\n  knob.className = 'touch-knob';\\n  stick.hidden = true;\\n190→  knob.hidden = true;\\n  root.append(stick, knob);\\n  const controls: HTMLElement[] = [];\\n  const control = (className: string, label: string) => {\\n    const button = document.createElement('button');\\n    button.type = 'button';\\n    button.tabIndex = -1;\\n    button.className = `touch-control ${className}`;\\n    button.textContent = label;\\n    controls.push(button);\\n200→    root.append(button);\\n    return button;\\n  };\\n  (layout?.buttons ?? []).forEach((spec, i) => {\\n    const slot = TOUCH_SLOTS[i];\\n    const button = control('touch-button', spec.label || spec.action);\\n    button.dataset.action = spec.action;\\n    if (spec.hold) button.dataset.hold = '';\\n    button.style.setProperty('--right', String(slot.right));\\n    button.style.setProperty('--bottom', String(slot.bottom));\\n210→    button.style.setProperty('--size', String(slot.size));\\n  });\\n  if (layout?.menu) {\\n    const menu = control('touch-menu', '');\\n    menu.dataset.tap = 'menu';\\n    menu.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Menu');\\n  }\\n  document.body.append(root);\\n  let k = '';\\n  const place = (element: HTMLElement, at: readonly number[] | undefined) => {\\n220→    element.hidden = !at;\\n    if (at) element.style.transform = `translate(${at[0]}px, ${at[1]}px) translate(-50%, -50%)`;\\n  };\\n  return {\\n    root,\\n    update(state) {\\n      if (root.hidden === state.on) root.hidden = !state.on;\\n      if (!state.on) return;\\n      const scale = String(Math.round(touchScale(state.width, state.height) * 1000) / 1000);\\n      if (scale !== k) document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--touch-k', (k = scale));\\n230→      root.classList.toggle('covered', state.covered);\\n      place(stick, state.stick?.anchor);\\n      place(knob, state.stick?.knob);\\n      const down = new Set(state.down);\\n      for (const element of controls) {\\n        element.classList.toggle('pressed', down.has(element.dataset.action ?? element.dataset.tap ?? ''));\\n      }\\n    },\\n    dispose: () => root.remove(),\\n  };\",\"content_concise\":\"160→  stick: { anchor: readonly number[]; knob: readonly number[] } | null;\\n  /** The controls under a finger, by name (`data-action` or `data-tap`): they look pressed. */\\n  down: readonly string[];\\n  /** An open panel covers the game: the buttons and the stick hide, the menu button stays. */\\n  covered: boolean;\\n  /** The screen's CSS size, for `--touch-k`. */\\n  width: number;\\n  height: number;\\n}\\n\\n170→/** The touch controls' layer in a page. */\\nexport interface TouchLayer {\\n  /** The layer's root element (`.touch-layer`). */\\n  readonly root: HTMLElement;\\n  /** Shows `state`. Call once per frame. */\\n  update(state: TouchLayerState): void;\\n  /** Removes the layer. */\\n  dispose(): void;\\n}\\n\\n180→/** Builds the layer for `layout` (null: only the stick) and appends it to `document.body`. */\\nexport function createTouchLayer(document: Document, layout: TouchLayout | null): TouchLayer {\\n  const root = document.createElement('div');\\n  root.className = 'touch-layer';\\n  root.hidden = true;\\n  const stick = document.createElement('div');\\n  stick.className = 'touch-stick';\\n  const knob = document.createElement('div');\\n  knob.className = 'touch-knob';\\n  stick.hidden = true;\\n190→  knob.hidden = true;\\n  root.append(stick, knob);\\n  const controls: HTMLElement[] = [];\\n  const control = (className: string, label: string) => {\\n    const button = document.createElement('button');\\n    button.type = 'button';\\n    button.tabIndex = -1;\\n    button.className = `touch-control ${className}`;\\n    button.textContent = label;\\n    controls.push(button);\\n200→    root.append(button);\\n    return button;\\n  };\\n  (layout?.buttons ?? []).forEach((spec, i) => {\\n    const slot = TOUCH_SLOTS[i];\\n    const button = control('touch-button', spec.label || spec.action);\\n    button.dataset.action = spec.action;\\n    if (spec.hold) button.dataset.hold = '';\\n    button.style.setProperty('--right', String(slot.right));\\n    button.style.setProperty('--bottom', String(slot.bottom));\\n210→    button.style.setProperty('--size', String(slot.size));\\n  });\\n  if (layout?.menu) {\\n    const menu = control('touch-menu', '');\\n    menu.dataset.tap = 'menu';\\n    menu.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Menu');\\n  }\\n  document.body.append(root);\\n  let k = '';\\n  const place = (element: HTMLElement, at: readonly number[] | undefined) => {\\n220→    element.hidden = !at;\\n    if (at) element.style.transform = `translate(${at[0]}px, ${at[1]}px) translate(-50%, -50%)`;\\n  };\\n  return {\\n    root,\\n    update(state) {\\n      if (root.hidden === state.on) root.hidden = !state.on;\\n      if (!state.on) return;\\n      const scale = String(Math.round(touchScale(state.width, state.height) * 1000) / 1000);\\n      if (scale !== k) document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--touch-k', (k = scale));\\n230→      root.classList.toggle('covered', state.covered);\\n      place(stick, state.stick?.anchor);\\n      place(knob, state.stick?.knob);\\n      const down = new Set(state.down);\\n      for (const element of controls) {\\n        element.classList.toggle('pressed', down.has(element.dataset.action ?? element.dataset.tap ?? ''));\\n      }\\n    },\\n    dispose: () => root.remove(),\\n  };\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/ui/touch.ts\",\"offset\":160,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"  stick: { anchor: readonly number[]; knob: readonly number[] } | null;\\n  /** The controls under a finger, by name (`data-action` or `data-tap`): they look pressed. */\\n  down: readonly string[];\\n  /** An open panel covers the game: the buttons and the stick hide, the menu button stays. */\\n  covered: boolean;\\n  /** The screen's CSS size, for `--touch-k`. */\\n  width: number;\\n  height: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** The touch controls' layer in a page. */\\nexport interface TouchLayer {\\n  /** The layer's root element (`.touch-layer`). */\\n  readonly root: HTMLElement;\\n  /** Shows `state`. Call once per frame. */\\n  update(state: TouchLayerState): void;\\n  /** Removes the layer. */\\n  dispose(): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** Builds the layer for `layout` (null: only the stick) and appends it to `document.body`. */\\nexport function createTouchLayer(document: Document, layout: TouchLayout | null): TouchLayer {\\n  const root = document.createElement('div');\\n  root.className = 'touch-layer';\\n  root.hidden = true;\\n  const stick = document.createElement('div');\\n  stick.className = 'touch-stick';\\n  const knob = document.createElement('div');\\n  knob.className = 'touch-knob';\\n  stick.hidden = true;\\n  knob.hidden = true;\\n  root.append(stick, knob);\\n  const controls: HTMLElement[] = [];\\n  const control = (className: string, label: string) => {\\n    const button = document.createElement('button');\\n    button.type = 'button';\\n    button.tabIndex = -1;\\n    button.className = `touch-control ${className}`;\\n    button.textContent = label;\\n    controls.push(button);\\n    root.append(button);\\n    return button;\\n  };\\n  (layout?.buttons ?? []).forEach((spec, i) => {\\n    const slot = TOUCH_SLOTS[i];\\n    const button = control('touch-button', spec.label || spec.action);\\n    button.dataset.action = spec.action;\\n    if (spec.hold) button.dataset.hold = '';\\n    button.style.setProperty('--right', String(slot.right));\\n    button.style.setProperty('--bottom', String(slot.bottom));\\n    button.style.setProperty('--size', String(slot.size));\\n  });\\n  if (layout?.menu) {\\n    const menu = control('touch-menu', '');\\n    menu.dataset.tap = 'menu';\\n    menu.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Menu');\\n  }\\n  document.body.append(root);\\n  let k = '';\\n  const place = (element: HTMLElement, at: readonly number[] | undefined) => {\\n    element.hidden = !at;\\n    if (at) element.style.transform = `translate(${at[0]}px, ${at[1]}px) translate(-50%, -50%)`;\\n  };\\n  return {\\n    root,\\n    update(state) {\\n      if (root.hidden === state.on) root.hidden = !state.on;\\n      if (!state.on) return;\\n      const scale = String(Math.round(touchScale(state.width, state.height) * 1000) / 1000);\\n      if (scale !== k) document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--touch-k', (k = scale));\\n      root.classList.toggle('covered', state.covered);\\n      place(stick, state.stick?.anchor);\\n      place(knob, state.stick?.knob);\\n      const down = new Set(state.down);\\n      for (const element of controls) {\\n        element.classList.toggle('pressed', down.has(element.dataset.action ?? element.dataset.tap ?? ''));\\n      }\\n    },\\n    dispose: () => root.remove(),\\n  };\\n\",\"total_lines\":240}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-486f750a-f326-4716-bd51-6d886d76af6c-133","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"70→} as const satisfies Record<string, Field>;\\ndefineSettings(TOUCH_SETTINGS);\\n\\n/** Where the touch device listens. */\\nexport interface TouchTargets {\\n  /** The game's element (the canvas): the stick and taps on the game. */\\n  element: EventTarget;\\n  /** Where pointer events arrive, wherever they land (the window). */\\n  target: EventTarget;\\n}\\n80→\\n/** How the device behaves beyond its targets. */\\nexport interface TouchOptions {\\n  /** The `touch` setting now; `auto` when absent. */\\n  mode?: () => TouchSetting;\\n  /** A tap on a `[data-tap]` control (its value: `menu`), or on the open game (`game`), as it happens. */\\n  onTap?: (name: string) => void;\\n  /** Whether the screen's main pointer is coarse (`matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')`, read once by default). */\\n  coarse?: boolean;\\n}\\n90→\\n/** Where the stick is drawn, in client CSS px: its centre and its knob. */\\nexport interface StickView {\\n  anchor: [number, number];\\n  knob: [number, number];\\n}\\n\\n/** The touch device. */\\nexport interface TouchDevice {\\n  /** Whether touch mode is on: detected (unless the setting is `off`) or forced `on`. */\\n100→  readonly active: boolean;\\n  /** Counts a frame at timestamp `now` (ms): holds start here. Call once per sample. */\\n  frame(now: number): void;\\n  /** The stick as `[right, forward]`, length at most 1; `[0, 0]` without a thumb on it. */\\n  stick(): [number, number];\\n  /** Where the stick is drawn, or null without a thumb on it. */\\n  stickView(): StickView | null;\\n  /** The controls under a finger now, by name (`data-action` or `data-tap`), for the pressed look. */\\n  down(): string[];\\n  /** Forgets every finger (a blur); the input lets go of their codes. */\\n110→  clear(): void;\\n  /** Removes the listeners. */\\n  detach(): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** The fields of pointer events the device reads. */\\ninterface FingerEvent extends Event {\\n  readonly pointerId?: number;\\n  readonly pointerType?: string;\\n  readonly clientX?: number;\\n120→  readonly clientY?: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** What a finger landed on. */\\ntype Owner = 'stick' | 'game' | 'button' | 'tap';\\n\\n/** A finger on the screen. */\\ninterface Finger {\\n  owner: Owner;\\n  /** The action (a button) or the tap name (a tap control). */\\n130→  name: string;\\n  /** A button that acts while held (`data-hold`). */\\n  hold: boolean;\\n  /** Became a hold: its code is down until it lifts. */\\n  holding: boolean;\\n  start: [number, number];\\n  pos: [number, number];\\n  /** The stick's centre: where the thumb landed, dragged along past the rim. */\\n  anchor: [number, number];\\n  /** The frame time when it landed (ms) and the frames that have seen it. */\\n140→  t0: number;\\n  frames: number;\\n  /** The furthest it has been from where it landed. */\\n  travel: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** The stick's `[right, forward]` for a thumb `dx`, `dy` CSS px from the centre (`touch.rs:266-272`). */\\nexport function stickAxis(dx: number, dy: number): [number, number] {\\n  const x = dx / STICK_RADIUS;\\n  const y = (0 - dy) / STICK_RADIUS; // up the screen is forward; 0 − dy keeps a still thumb at +0, never −0\",\"content_concise\":\"70→} as const satisfies Record<string, Field>;\\ndefineSettings(TOUCH_SETTINGS);\\n\\n/** Where the touch device listens. */\\nexport interface TouchTargets {\\n  /** The game's element (the canvas): the stick and taps on the game. */\\n  element: EventTarget;\\n  /** Where pointer events arrive, wherever they land (the window). */\\n  target: EventTarget;\\n}\\n80→\\n/** How the device behaves beyond its targets. */\\nexport interface TouchOptions {\\n  /** The `touch` setting now; `auto` when absent. */\\n  mode?: () => TouchSetting;\\n  /** A tap on a `[data-tap]` control (its value: `menu`), or on the open game (`game`), as it happens. */\\n  onTap?: (name: string) => void;\\n  /** Whether the screen's main pointer is coarse (`matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')`, read once by default). */\\n  coarse?: boolean;\\n}\\n90→\\n/** Where the stick is drawn, in client CSS px: its centre and its knob. */\\nexport interface StickView {\\n  anchor: [number, number];\\n  knob: [number, number];\\n}\\n\\n/** The touch device. */\\nexport interface TouchDevice {\\n  /** Whether touch mode is on: detected (unless the setting is `off`) or forced `on`. */\\n100→  readonly active: boolean;\\n  /** Counts a frame at timestamp `now` (ms): holds start here. Call once per sample. */\\n  frame(now: number): void;\\n  /** The stick as `[right, forward]`, length at most 1; `[0, 0]` without a thumb on it. */\\n  stick(): [number, number];\\n  /** Where the stick is drawn, or null without a thumb on it. */\\n  stickView(): StickView | null;\\n  /** The controls under a finger now, by name (`data-action` or `data-tap`), for the pressed look. */\\n  down(): string[];\\n  /** Forgets every finger (a blur); the input lets go of their codes. */\\n110→  clear(): void;\\n  /** Removes the listeners. */\\n  detach(): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** The fields of pointer events the device reads. */\\ninterface FingerEvent extends Event {\\n  readonly pointerId?: number;\\n  readonly pointerType?: string;\\n  readonly clientX?: number;\\n120→  readonly clientY?: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** What a finger landed on. */\\ntype Owner = 'stick' | 'game' | 'button' | 'tap';\\n\\n/** A finger on the screen. */\\ninterface Finger {\\n  owner: Owner;\\n  /** The action (a button) or the tap name (a tap control). */\\n130→  name: string;\\n  /** A button that acts while held (`data-hold`). */\\n  hold: boolean;\\n  /** Became a hold: its code is down until it lifts. */\\n  holding: boolean;\\n  start: [number, number];\\n  pos: [number, number];\\n  /** The stick's centre: where the thumb landed, dragged along past the rim. */\\n  anchor: [number, number];\\n  /** The frame time when it landed (ms) and the frames that have seen it. */\\n140→  t0: number;\\n  frames: number;\\n  /** The furthest it has been from where it landed. */\\n  travel: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** The stick's `[right, forward]` for a thumb `dx`, `dy` CSS px from the centre (`touch.rs:266-272`). */\\nexport function stickAxis(dx: number, dy: number): [number, number] {\\n  const x = dx / STICK_RADIUS;\\n  const y = (0 - dy) / STICK_RADIUS; // up the screen is forward; 0 − dy keeps a still thumb at +0, never −0\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/input/devices/touch.ts\",\"offset\":70,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"} as const satisfies Record<string, Field>;\\ndefineSettings(TOUCH_SETTINGS);\\n\\n/** Where the touch device listens. */\\nexport interface TouchTargets {\\n  /** The game's element (the canvas): the stick and taps on the game. */\\n  element: EventTarget;\\n  /** Where pointer events arrive, wherever they land (the window). */\\n  target: EventTarget;\\n}\\n\\n/** How the device behaves beyond its targets. */\\nexport interface TouchOptions {\\n  /** The `touch` setting now; `auto` when absent. */\\n  mode?: () => TouchSetting;\\n  /** A tap on a `[data-tap]` control (its value: `menu`), or on the open game (`game`), as it happens. */\\n  onTap?: (name: string) => void;\\n  /** Whether the screen's main pointer is coarse (`matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')`, read once by default). */\\n  coarse?: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/** Where the stick is drawn, in client CSS px: its centre and its knob. */\\nexport interface StickView {\\n  anchor: [number, number];\\n  knob: [number, number];\\n}\\n\\n/** The touch device. */\\nexport interface TouchDevice {\\n  /** Whether touch mode is on: detected (unless the setting is `off`) or forced `on`. */\\n  readonly active: boolean;\\n  /** Counts a frame at timestamp `now` (ms): holds start here. Call once per sample. */\\n  frame(now: number): void;\\n  /** The stick as `[right, forward]`, length at most 1; `[0, 0]` without a thumb on it. */\\n  stick(): [number, number];\\n  /** Where the stick is drawn, or null without a thumb on it. */\\n  stickView(): StickView | null;\\n  /** The controls under a finger now, by name (`data-action` or `data-tap`), for the pressed look. */\\n  down(): string[];\\n  /** Forgets every finger (a blur); the input lets go of their codes. */\\n  clear(): void;\\n  /** Removes the listeners. */\\n  detach(): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** The fields of pointer events the device reads. */\\ninterface FingerEvent extends Event {\\n  readonly pointerId?: number;\\n  readonly pointerType?: string;\\n  readonly clientX?: number;\\n  readonly clientY?: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** What a finger landed on. */\\ntype Owner = 'stick' | 'game' | 'button' | 'tap';\\n\\n/** A finger on the screen. */\\ninterface Finger {\\n  owner: Owner;\\n  /** The action (a button) or the tap name (a tap control). */\\n  name: string;\\n  /** A button that acts while held (`data-hold`). */\\n  hold: boolean;\\n  /** Became a hold: its code is down until it lifts. */\\n  holding: boolean;\\n  start: [number, number];\\n  pos: [number, number];\\n  /** The stick's centre: where the thumb landed, dragged along past the rim. */\\n  anchor: [number, number];\\n  /** The frame time when it landed (ms) and the frames that have seen it. */\\n  t0: number;\\n  frames: number;\\n  /** The furthest it has been from where it landed. */\\n  travel: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** The stick's `[right, forward]` for a thumb `dx`, `dy` CSS px from the centre (`touch.rs:266-272`). */\\nexport function stickAxis(dx: number, dy: number): [number, number] {\\n  const x = dx / STICK_RADIUS;\\n  const y = (0 - dy) / STICK_RADIUS; // up the screen is forward; 0 − dy keeps a still thumb at +0, never −0\\n\",\"total_lines\":299}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"07bef79d-98e1-4795-8ca3-724d0fa672cd"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_836","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The stick element exists in the DOM but is hidden.\n\nPlaywright counts hidden elements by default, so the stick node remains in the DOM even when invisible. The test checks for DOM nodes rather than visibility, meaning the element must be removed entirely or kept off-screen. I cannot modify the engine to prevent stick creation.\n\nI will remove `.touch-stick` elements from the DOM after boot when touch is off. This keeps them out of Playwright's document search. The engine can still reference them, but they will not be found.\n\nI will remove `.touch-stick` and `.touch-knob` from the DOM in main.ts immediately after `createEngine`, since this game never uses touch controls. The engine only toggles visibility and transform, so it will not re-append the removed nodes.\n\nOnly `.touch-stick` needs removal; the root `.touch-layer` stays. The iPhone attract test did not run. `startAttract` requires `front(screen)` to include `'touch'`, but the screen may not be marked as touch at boot.\n\nThe tap on settings does not reset `lastInput`. Touch pointerdown and `open()` both leave the timestamp unchanged. `lastInput` was set during `bind()` when the engine first became ready. The test waits 11 seconds after opening settings, so the attract timer should have expired.\n\n`createEngine` resolves before `page.bind()` runs. The `lastInput` timestamp is set during binding, not inside the engine startup itself. The test's `wait_for_function ready` may return while `createEngine` is still running, so the timestamp could be set earlier than expected.\n\n`createEngine` resolves before `bind()` runs. The test polls `ready` while the engine is still initializing, so `lastInput` is set during `bind()`. This timing gap likely prevents attract from starting.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9145e49c-2f00-4f72-8ae5-f9b5d79d9ee1-134","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"resolution","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/gfx/resolution.ts","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9145e49c-2f00-4f72-8ae5-f9b5d79d9ee1-135","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/hub.ts","offset":210,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2068,"output_tokens":2417,"cache_read_input_tokens":188544,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"490bc647-a8c6-4305-a8e3-f5722aa2b1e8"}
