8,97,109,101,32,61,32,39,116,111,117,99,104,45,115,116,105,99,107,39,59,10,49,56,57,58,32,32,115,116,105,99,107,46,104,105,100,100,101,110,32,61,32,116,114,117,101,59,10,49,57,48,58,32,32,107,110,111,98,46,104,105,100,100,101,110,32,61,32,116,114,117,101,59,10,50,50,48,58,32,32,32,32,101,108,101,109,101,110,116,46,104,105,100,100,101,110,32,61,32,33,97,116,59,10,50,50,54,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,105,102,32,40,114,111,111,116,46,104,105,100,100,101,110,32,61,61,61,32,115,116,97,116,101,46,111,110,41,32,114,111,111,116,46,104,105,100,100,101,110,32,61,32,33,115,116,97,116,101,46,111,110,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":8,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/ui/touch.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":27,\"content\":\" * // const layer = createTouchLayer(document, getTouchLayout('touchlayout:box'));\"},{\"line_number\":181,\"content\":\"export function createTouchLayer(document: Document, layout: TouchLayout | null): TouchLayer {\"},{\"line_number\":184,\"content\":\"  root.hidden = true;\"},{\"line_number\":186,\"content\":\"  stick.className = 'touch-stick';\"},{\"line_number\":189,\"content\":\"  stick.hidden = true;\"},{\"line_number\":190,\"content\":\"  knob.hidden = true;\"},{\"line_number\":220,\"content\":\"    element.hidden = !at;\"},{\"line_number\":226,\"content\":\"      if (root.hidden === state.on) root.hidden = !state.on;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"d152697f-e563-4c37-9763-e1ff2f30ec26"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_845","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to investigate the iPhone attract failure more carefully.\n\nThe touch test taps the settings button. Playwright's touchscreen.tap generates touch events. These do not update lastInput. The attract timer should continue counting down.\n\nThe settings menu keeps snap.mode as 'title'. The screen is front. startAttract should fire after 10 seconds of idle.\n\nThe test waits for engine.ready before tapping settings. lastInput is set at bind time, so the tap does not reset it. By the 11-second mark, the idle timer should have expired. The attract failure likely has another cause.\n\nThe browser may synthesize mouse events alongside touch events during the tap. A mouse pointerdown would call noteDevice and reset lastInput, preventing attract from starting.\n\nThe iPad passed attract while the iPhone failed. The iPhone 13 has a deviceScaleFactor of 3, creating a roughly 3-megapixel drawing buffer. The iPad gen 7 uses a deviceScaleFactor of 2. This higher resolution on the iPhone may be causing the GPU to stall and prevent attract from starting.\n\nThe iPad actually has more total pixels than the iPhone, so resolution alone does not explain the attract failure. The iPad passed because its frames rendered quickly enough. The iPhone likely stalls for a different reason.\n\nThe test checks the `attract` flag directly, not the screen state. The per-frame override only forces a screen change when attract is active and the current screen is not settings or touch. It does not clear attract while settings is open.\n\nIf frames never run after engine.ready, the attract flag stays false. This suggests the iPhone may stall rendering immediately after ready, while the iPad continues drawing.\n\nThe iPhone failure is specific: engine.ready passed, the note text was correct, the settings tap succeeded, and the screen changed to settings. Only the attract flag remained false after 11 seconds. This suggests frames were running during the wait, since the settings transition happened synchronously on the click rather than on a frame boundary.\n\nThe settings wait returns immediately because the click handler is synchronous. The 11-second window begins right after that tap. If the first frame after engine.ready takes longer than 11 seconds on the iPhone, attract never starts. The iPad may have drawn a frame within that window by chance.\n\nThe iPhone may be stuck drawing its first boot frame when the 11-second wait begins, so onFrame never fires. Playwright's tap generates only a single touch event, not continuous pointer moves that would reset lastInput repeatedly. The quality auto-on-touch setting is also being considered as a possible factor.\n\nThe engine's touch setting is off, so quality auto stays high and the iPhone buffer remains huge. Using gfx.resolution=pixels caps the buffer at 330 lines regardless of device scale factor. That should make iPhone frames cheap. I considered lowering quality for coarse and hub screens, but the boot desktop canvas must stay full resolution to match the viewport.\n\nI will set coarse and hub screens to `gfx.resolution=pixels`, `quality=low`, and `gfx.warmUp=asked`. This should keep the iPhone buffer small enough for attract. The test only checks the attract flag, note text, stick state, and settings button, so a pixel resolution change should not break anything. I also need to verify whether starting the hub screen as 'card' before the engine exists causes any issues.\n\nThe initial screen should be 'card' for hub builds instead of 'title'. The keydown handler already answers ready when the screen is 'card'. However, if createEngine blocks the main thread, the Enter key sent by the harness at 14 seconds will not be processed until createEngine yields. This is a critical timing issue.\n\nIf createEngine blocks the main thread during GPU initialization, the 14-second watchdog timer cannot fire until that blocking code yields. The harness then sends the card and Enter while the screen is still title or touch. This would prevent the ready signal from reaching the engine.\n\nThe card was sent, so ready() fired. The failure is a missing answer('ready') within 3 seconds after Enter. This means createEngine likely blocked the main thread for over 20 seconds without yielding.\n\nThe synchronous ready() call fires immediately after createEngine returns, before bind() sets the screen to card. The harness therefore receives the card and sends Enter while the screen is still title or touch. This timing mismatch would prevent the ready signal from reaching the engine.\n\nThe root cause is now clear. The harness sends Enter while the screen is still title or touch, so the keydown handler ignores it. When createEngine finally returns and bind sets the screen to card, the ready signal has already been lost.\n\nThe fix is to start the hub screen as 'card' before the engine exists. This lets the warmup Enter key answer ready immediately.\n\nHowever, if createEngine blocks the main thread during GPU initialization, the Enter keydown itself may not be processed until that blocking code yields.\n\nThe 14-second watchdog can fire while createEngine is still running, but only if the engine yields at an await point. If it blocks the main thread with a long synchronous chunk, the keydown is queued and delayed past the 3-second window.\n\nThe 14-second watchdog fires while the main thread is still running, so the card is sent. The Enter key arrives after the harness waits for the card, but if createEngine blocks the thread again during that wait, the keydown is queued and delayed past the 3-second window. Starting the screen as 'card' does not fix this; the race is simply between the harness sending Enter and createEngine yielding back to the event loop.\n\nFaster GPU initialization should let createEngine return before the 14-second watchdog fires. The card would then be sent while the engine is already ready, and the harness Enter would be answered immediately. If createEngine never finishes, the frame loop cannot run and ghost sends and progress will not appear.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e03894a-2ba4-4409-b463-552e78578a2f-13","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/app/engine.ts","offset":280,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e03894a-2ba4-4409-b463-552e78578a2f-14","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/stage.ts","offset":500,"limit":100}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e03894a-2ba4-4409-b463-552e78578a2f-15","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ready-without|card Enter|answer\\('ready'\\)|function poke|cardSent","glob":"**/labs/game/hub/harness.html"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e03894a-2ba4-4409-b463-552e78578a2f-16","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/hub.ts","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5483,"output_tokens":3485,"cache_read_input_tokens":43648,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"1c17e26a-8817-4e02-9491-2751c654bd08"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3e03894a-2ba4-4409-b463-552e78578a2f-13","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"280→      const scene = asked.playback?.replay.scene;\\n      if (scene && !new URLSearchParams(search).has('scene') && options.scenes.includes(scene)) {\\n        routes = { ...routes, scene };\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (options.touchLayout !== undefined) layout = getTouchLayout(options.touchLayout, registry);\\n    materials = createMaterialLibrary({ registry });\\n    const { scene, seed, settings, cam } = routes;\\n    parts.run = createAppHost({ scene, seed, settings, cam, registry, log, drawing, materials });\\n    if (routes.gallery) gallery = createGalleryDriver(routes.gallery, () => parts.run!, registry);\\n290→  } catch (error) {\\n    fail(error);\\n    return engine;\\n  }\\n  const started = parts.run;\\n  Object.assign(window, { __engine: started.inspector });\\n  const onTap = (name: string) => {\\n    if (name === 'game') chrome.closeTopPanel();\\n    if (name !== 'menu') return;\\n    started.clock.pause();\\n300→    options.onMenu?.();\\n  };\\n  const touchMode = () => settingsNow.get<TouchSetting>('touch');\\n  const mapFor = () => {\\n    const asked = options.actionMap;\\n    return (typeof asked === 'function' ? asked(viewNow().camera.code()) : asked) ?? 'actionMap:thirdPerson';\\n  };\\n  const declared = (path: string) => registry.kinds().includes('setting') && registry.has('setting', path);\\n  const look = () => lookOptions((path) => (declared(path) ? settingsNow.get(path) : undefined));\\n  const input = (parts.input = createInput({ window, document, element: options.canvas, registry, log, touchMode, onTap, map: mapFor(), look, onView: options.onView, storage: options.store && textStorage(options.store) })); // prettier-ignore\\n310→  /** The camera the devices read: its heading, its look, and the aim from the view (engine/input/aim.ts). */\\n  const camera: CameraLike = {\\n    yaw: () => viewNow().camera.yaw(),\\n    pose: () => viewNow().camera.pose(),\\n    aim: (rule, devices) => viewNow().aim(rule, devices),\\n  };\\n  /** The map for the camera now, and the pointer lock: a click takes it where the map's mouse looks; pause gives it back. */ // prettier-ignore\\n  const sample = (now: number) => {\\n    const id = mapFor();\\n    if (id !== input.bindings.map.id) input.use(id);\\n320→    if (input.mouse?.locked && (!input.bindings.map.lock || started.clock.paused)) input.mouse.unlock();\\n    const intents = input.sample(camera, now);\\n    return options.modal?.() ? {} : intents;\\n  };\\n  options.canvas.addEventListener('click', () => {\\n    if (input.bindings.map.lock && !started.clock.paused && !input.mouse?.locked) input.mouse?.lock();\\n  });\\n  parts.layer = createTouchLayer(document, layout);\\n  attachSwipes(document);\\n  connectVirtualDevice(started.host, input.virtual);\\n330→  try {\\n    parts.gfx = await createRenderer(options.canvas, { settings: currentSettings(() => started), registry, log });\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    fail(error);\\n    return engine;\\n  }\\n  const gfx = parts.gfx;\\n  parts.numbers = createDamageNumbers((parts.ui = createUi({ canvas: options.canvas })));\\n  try {\\n    gfx.renderer.shadowMap.enabled = true;\\n340→    const styles = createStyleSet({ library: materials!, registry });\\n    const post = (parts.post = createPost(gfx, { settings: currentSettings(() => started), registry, log, styles }));\\n    const budget = () => parts.governor!.budget(settingsNow.get<QualitySetting>('quality'), input.touch?.active ?? false); // prettier-ignore\\n    parts.look = createPageLook({ post, styles, warmup: gfx.warmup, resolution: gfx.resolution, library: materials!, quality: budget, asked: () => warmsAsked(settingsNow) }); // prettier-ignore\\n    post.attach(gfx.warmup);\\n    viewNow().stage.register(gfx.warmup, gfx.features);\\n    await warmCameras();\\n    await settle(1, 0);\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    fail(error);\\n350→    return engine;\\n  }\\n  const step = (intents: Record<string, unknown>) => {\\n    if (playback && !playback.done) {\\n      playback.step(started.session);\\n      started.stepped(); // its hit-stops reach the clock as in live play\\n    } else {\\n      playback = null;\\n      started.stepOnce(intents);\\n    }\\n360→  };\\n  loop = createLoop({\\n    clock: () => started.clock,\\n    sample,\\n    step,\\n    draw: ({ alpha, dt }) => {\\n      // frozen in a reproducible run: a replay playing, or the governor turned off (engine/dev/governor.ts)\\n      parts.governor!.freeze((playback !== null && !playback.done) || !settingsNow.get<boolean>('gfx.governor'));\\n      if (warming) return;\\n      const report = frame(alpha, dt);\\n370→      if (!report.drawn && report.warming) warming = warmCameras().finally(() => (warming = null));\\n    },\\n    hold: () => started.playing,\\n    cap: () => input.touch?.active ?? false,\\n    onError: (error) => fail(error, 'APP_FRAME'),\\n  });\\n  parts.ready = true;\\n  overlay.hide();\\n  loop.start();\\n  const replay = asked?.playback;\\n380→  if (asked && !replay) fail(asked.error);\\n  else if (replay) {\\n    try {\\n      started.begin(replay.replay);\\n      playback = replay;\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      fail(error);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return engine;\\n390→}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"280→      const scene = asked.playback?.replay.scene;\\n      if (scene && !new URLSearchParams(search).has('scene') && options.scenes.includes(scene)) {\\n        routes = { ...routes, scene };\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (options.touchLayout !== undefined) layout = getTouchLayout(options.touchLayout, registry);\\n    materials = createMaterialLibrary({ registry });\\n    const { scene, seed, settings, cam } = routes;\\n    parts.run = createAppHost({ scene, seed, settings, cam, registry, log, drawing, materials });\\n    if (routes.gallery) gallery = createGalleryDriver(routes.gallery, () => parts.run!, registry);\\n290→  } catch (error) {\\n    fail(error);\\n    return engine;\\n  }\\n  const started = parts.run;\\n  Object.assign(window, { __engine: started.inspector });\\n  const onTap = (name: string) => {\\n    if (name === 'game') chrome.closeTopPanel();\\n    if (name !== 'menu') return;\\n    started.clock.pause();\\n300→    options.onMenu?.();\\n  };\\n  const touchMode = () => settingsNow.get<TouchSetting>('touch');\\n  const mapFor = () => {\\n    const asked = options.actionMap;\\n    return (typeof asked === 'function' ? asked(viewNow().camera.code()) : asked) ?? 'actionMap:thirdPerson';\\n  };\\n  const declared = (path: string) => registry.kinds().includes('setting') && registry.has('setting', path);\\n  const look = () => lookOptions((path) => (declared(path) ? settingsNow.get(path) : undefined));\\n  const input = (parts.input = createInput({ window, document, element: options.canvas, registry, log, touchMode, onTap, map: mapFor(), look, onView: options.onView, storage: options.store && textStorage(options.store) })); // prettier-ignore\\n310→  /** The camera the devices read: its heading, its look, and the aim from the view (engine/input/aim.ts). */\\n  const camera: CameraLike = {\\n    yaw: () => viewNow().camera.yaw(),\\n    pose: () => viewNow().camera.pose(),\\n    aim: (rule, devices) => viewNow().aim(rule, devices),\\n  };\\n  /** The map for the camera now, and the pointer lock: a click takes it where the map's mouse looks; pause gives it back. */ // prettier-ignore\\n  const sample = (now: number) => {\\n    const id = mapFor();\\n    if (id !== input.bindings.map.id) input.use(id);\\n320→    if (input.mouse?.locked && (!input.bindings.map.lock || started.clock.paused)) input.mouse.unlock();\\n    const intents = input.sample(camera, now);\\n    return options.modal?.() ? {} : intents;\\n  };\\n  options.canvas.addEventListener('click', () => {\\n    if (input.bindings.map.lock && !started.clock.paused && !input.mouse?.locked) input.mouse?.lock();\\n  });\\n  parts.layer = createTouchLayer(document, layout);\\n  attachSwipes(document);\\n  connectVirtualDevice(started.host, input.virtual);\\n330→  try {\\n    parts.gfx = await createRenderer(options.canvas, { settings: currentSettings(() => started), registry, log });\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    fail(error);\\n    return engine;\\n  }\\n  const gfx = parts.gfx;\\n  parts.numbers = createDamageNumbers((parts.ui = createUi({ canvas: options.canvas })));\\n  try {\\n    gfx.renderer.shadowMap.enabled = true;\\n340→    const styles = createStyleSet({ library: materials!, registry });\\n    const post = (parts.post = createPost(gfx, { settings: currentSettings(() => started), registry, log, styles }));\\n    const budget = () => parts.governor!.budget(settingsNow.get<QualitySetting>('quality'), input.touch?.active ?? false); // prettier-ignore\\n    parts.look = createPageLook({ post, styles, warmup: gfx.warmup, resolution: gfx.resolution, library: materials!, quality: budget, asked: () => warmsAsked(settingsNow) }); // prettier-ignore\\n    post.attach(gfx.warmup);\\n    viewNow().stage.register(gfx.warmup, gfx.features);\\n    await warmCameras();\\n    await settle(1, 0);\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    fail(error);\\n350→    return engine;\\n  }\\n  const step = (intents: Record<string, unknown>) => {\\n    if (playback && !playback.done) {\\n      playback.step(started.session);\\n      started.stepped(); // its hit-stops reach the clock as in live play\\n    } else {\\n      playback = null;\\n      started.stepOnce(intents);\\n    }\\n360→  };\\n  loop = createLoop({\\n    clock: () => started.clock,\\n    sample,\\n    step,\\n    draw: ({ alpha, dt }) => {\\n      // frozen in a reproducible run: a replay playing, or the governor turned off (engine/dev/governor.ts)\\n      parts.governor!.freeze((playback !== null && !playback.done) || !settingsNow.get<boolean>('gfx.governor'));\\n      if (warming) return;\\n      const report = frame(alpha, dt);\\n370→      if (!report.drawn && report.warming) warming = warmCameras().finally(() => (warming = null));\\n    },\\n    hold: () => started.playing,\\n    cap: () => input.touch?.active ?? false,\\n    onError: (error) => fail(error, 'APP_FRAME'),\\n  });\\n  parts.ready = true;\\n  overlay.hide();\\n  loop.start();\\n  const replay = asked?.playback;\\n380→  if (asked && !replay) fail(asked.error);\\n  else if (replay) {\\n    try {\\n      started.begin(replay.replay);\\n      playback = replay;\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      fail(error);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return engine;\\n390→}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/app/engine.ts\",\"offset\":280,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"      const scene = asked.playback?.replay.scene;\\n      if (scene && !new URLSearchParams(search).has('scene') && options.scenes.includes(scene)) {\\n        routes = { ...routes, scene };\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (options.touchLayout !== undefined) layout = getTouchLayout(options.touchLayout, registry);\\n    materials = createMaterialLibrary({ registry });\\n    const { scene, seed, settings, cam } = routes;\\n    parts.run = createAppHost({ scene, seed, settings, cam, registry, log, drawing, materials });\\n    if (routes.gallery) gallery = createGalleryDriver(routes.gallery, () => parts.run!, registry);\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    fail(error);\\n    return engine;\\n  }\\n  const started = parts.run;\\n  Object.assign(window, { __engine: started.inspector });\\n  const onTap = (name: string) => {\\n    if (name === 'game') chrome.closeTopPanel();\\n    if (name !== 'menu') return;\\n    started.clock.pause();\\n    options.onMenu?.();\\n  };\\n  const touchMode = () => settingsNow.get<TouchSetting>('touch');\\n  const mapFor = () => {\\n    const asked = options.actionMap;\\n    return (typeof asked === 'function' ? asked(viewNow().camera.code()) : asked) ?? 'actionMap:thirdPerson';\\n  };\\n  const declared = (path: string) => registry.kinds().includes('setting') && registry.has('setting', path);\\n  const look = () => lookOptions((path) => (declared(path) ? settingsNow.get(path) : undefined));\\n  const input = (parts.input = createInput({ window, document, element: options.canvas, registry, log, touchMode, onTap, map: mapFor(), look, onView: options.onView, storage: options.store && textStorage(options.store) })); // prettier-ignore\\n  /** The camera the devices read: its heading, its look, and the aim from the view (engine/input/aim.ts). */\\n  const camera: CameraLike = {\\n    yaw: () => viewNow().camera.yaw(),\\n    pose: () => viewNow().camera.pose(),\\n    aim: (rule, devices) => viewNow().aim(rule, devices),\\n  };\\n  /** The map for the camera now, and the pointer lock: a click takes it where the map's mouse looks; pause gives it back. */ // prettier-ignore\\n  const sample = (now: number) => {\\n    const id = mapFor();\\n    if (id !== input.bindings.map.id) input.use(id);\\n    if (input.mouse?.locked && (!input.bindings.map.lock || started.clock.paused)) input.mouse.unlock();\\n    const intents = input.sample(camera, now);\\n    return options.modal?.() ? {} : intents;\\n  };\\n  options.canvas.addEventListener('click', () => {\\n    if (input.bindings.map.lock && !started.clock.paused && !input.mouse?.locked) input.mouse?.lock();\\n  });\\n  parts.layer = createTouchLayer(document, layout);\\n  attachSwipes(document);\\n  connectVirtualDevice(started.host, input.virtual);\\n  try {\\n    parts.gfx = await createRenderer(options.canvas, { settings: currentSettings(() => started), registry, log });\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    fail(error);\\n    return engine;\\n  }\\n  const gfx = parts.gfx;\\n  parts.numbers = createDamageNumbers((parts.ui = createUi({ canvas: options.canvas })));\\n  try {\\n    gfx.renderer.shadowMap.enabled = true;\\n    const styles = createStyleSet({ library: materials!, registry });\\n    const post = (parts.post = createPost(gfx, { settings: currentSettings(() => started), registry, log, styles }));\\n    const budget = () => parts.governor!.budget(settingsNow.get<QualitySetting>('quality'), input.touch?.active ?? false); // prettier-ignore\\n    parts.look = createPageLook({ post, styles, warmup: gfx.warmup, resolution: gfx.resolution, library: materials!, quality: budget, asked: () => warmsAsked(settingsNow) }); // prettier-ignore\\n    post.attach(gfx.warmup);\\n    viewNow().stage.register(gfx.warmup, gfx.features);\\n    await warmCameras();\\n    await settle(1, 0);\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    fail(error);\\n    return engine;\\n  }\\n  const step = (intents: Record<string, unknown>) => {\\n    if (playback && !playback.done) {\\n      playback.step(started.session);\\n      started.stepped(); // its hit-stops reach the clock as in live play\\n    } else {\\n      playback = null;\\n      started.stepOnce(intents);\\n    }\\n  };\\n  loop = createLoop({\\n    clock: () => started.clock,\\n    sample,\\n    step,\\n    draw: ({ alpha, dt }) => {\\n      // frozen in a reproducible run: a replay playing, or the governor turned off (engine/dev/governor.ts)\\n      parts.governor!.freeze((playback !== null && !playback.done) || !settingsNow.get<boolean>('gfx.governor'));\\n      if (warming) return;\\n      const report = frame(alpha, dt);\\n      if (!report.drawn && report.warming) warming = warmCameras().finally(() => (warming = null));\\n    },\\n    hold: () => started.playing,\\n    cap: () => input.touch?.active ?? false,\\n    onError: (error) => fail(error, 'APP_FRAME'),\\n  });\\n  parts.ready = true;\\n  overlay.hide();\\n  loop.start();\\n  const replay = asked?.playback;\\n  if (asked && !replay) fail(asked.error);\\n  else if (replay) {\\n    try {\\n      started.begin(replay.replay);\\n      playback = replay;\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      fail(error);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return engine;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":390}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3e03894a-2ba4-4409-b463-552e78578a2f-14","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"500→      pebbles: snap.pebbles,\\n      age: snap.age,\\n      credits: snap.credits,\\n      result: snap.result,\\n      seen: snap.seen,\\n      rank: snap.rank,\\n      settings: { ...prefs, icons },\\n      outfits: [],\\n    };\\n    if (snap.line === 'find.pebble' && !save.finds.includes('find.pebble')) save.finds = [...save.finds, 'find.pebble'];\\n510→    if (snap.mode === 'results' && snap.event) {\\n      const best = save.bests[snap.event] ?? -1;\\n      if (snap.result > best) save.bests = { ...save.bests, [snap.event]: snap.result };\\n    }\\n    const key = `${snap.mode}:${snap.event}:${snap.result}:${snap.pebbles}:${snap.cursor}:${snap.credits}`;\\n    if (key !== savedKey && snap.mode !== 'title' && !attract && !hub) {\\n      savedKey = key;\\n      writeSave(store, save);\\n    }\\n  }\\n520→\\n  function paint(snap: Snap, drawn: EngineFrame): void {\\n    const lure = LURE_IDS.has(snap.text) ? LURES.find((row) => row.id === snap.text) : undefined;\\n    const sentence = lure ? (LINES[`lure.${lure.id}`] ?? lure.line) : (LINES[snap.line] ?? '');\\n    if (sentence && sentence !== said && screen !== 'title' && screen !== 'touch' && screen !== 'card') {\\n      said = sentence;\\n      say(audio, speakerFor(snap.line || 'tare.welcome'), sentence, prefs.voices);\\n    }\\n    if (screen === 'touch') note.textContent = 'Controller or keyboard required.';\\n    else if (menu || !sentence) note.textContent = promptLine(glyphSet);\\n530→    else note.textContent = sentence;\\n    banner.textContent = attract ? 'Thumb Yoga. DEMO. Press any button.' : '';\\n    disc.hidden = (snap.mode === 'title' && !attract) || screen === 'card';\\n    const dot = disc.querySelector('#dot');\\n    if (dot) {\\n      dot.setAttribute('cx', String(50 + snap.ax * 40));\\n      dot.setAttribute('cy', String(50 - snap.ay * 40));\\n    }\\n    copy.hidden = screen === 'about' || screen === 'card';\\n    if (snap.mode === 'results')\\n540→      copy.textContent = `${snap.rank}. ${Math.round(snap.result)}. ${LINES[`rank.${snap.rank}`] ?? ''}`;\\n    else if (snap.mode === 'evening') copy.textContent = LINES['evening.close'] ?? '';\\n    else if (snap.mode === 'credits')\\n      copy.textContent = `${LINES['credits.roll'] ?? ''} ${LINES['credits.walk'] ?? ''}`;\\n    else if (lure) copy.textContent = lure.line;\\n    else copy.textContent = snap.mode === 'roam' ? `Day ${snap.day}. Pebbles ${Math.round(snap.pebbles)}.` : '';\\n    touchBtn.hidden = !touch || (armed && screen !== 'touch');\\n    about.hidden = screen !== 'about';\\n    if (screen !== 'dev') sliders.hidden = true;\\n    const nextSong = songFor(attract ? { ...snap, mode: snap.mode === 'title' ? 'event' : snap.mode } : snap);\\n550→    if (nextSong !== song) {\\n      song = nextSong;\\n      audio.music(nextSong);\\n    }\\n    audio.update(drawn.camera, drawn.queries ?? undefined);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Title and the other front screens, where ten quiet seconds starts the demo. */\\nfunction front(screen: string): boolean {\\n560→  return (\\n    screen === 'title' ||\\n    screen === 'touch' ||\\n    screen === 'settings' ||\\n    screen === 'about' ||\\n    screen === 'controls' ||\\n    screen === 'programme'\\n  );\\n}\\n\\n570→/** The label under the menu cursor. */\\nfunction labelOf(item: MenuItem | undefined): string {\\n  return typeof item === 'string' ? item : (item?.label ?? '');\\n}\\n\\n/** Extra pads fill seats 1 to 3. Seat 0 stays on the balance map. */\\nfunction sendSeats(input: NonNullable<Engine['input']>, pads: readonly (Gamepad | null)[]): void {\\n  const claim = [0, 0, 0, 0];\\n  const seats = Array.from({ length: 16 }, () => 0);\\n  for (let seat = 1; seat <= 3; seat += 1) {\\n580→    const pad = pads[seat];\\n    if (!pad) continue;\\n    claim[seat] = 1;\\n    seats[seat * 4] = pad.axes[0] ?? 0;\\n    seats[seat * 4 + 1] = -(pad.axes[1] ?? 0);\\n    seats[seat * 4 + 2] = pad.buttons[6]?.value || (pad.buttons[6]?.pressed ? 1 : 0);\\n    seats[seat * 4 + 3] = pad.buttons[7]?.value || (pad.buttons[7]?.pressed ? 1 : 0);\\n  }\\n  input.virtual.axis('game:claim', claim);\\n  input.virtual.axis('game:seats', seats);\\n590→}\\n\\n/** A line in the shell. */\\nfunction para(kind: string): HTMLElement {\\n  const node = document.createElement('p');\\n  node.dataset.ui = kind;\\n  return node;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"500→      pebbles: snap.pebbles,\\n      age: snap.age,\\n      credits: snap.credits,\\n      result: snap.result,\\n      seen: snap.seen,\\n      rank: snap.rank,\\n      settings: { ...prefs, icons },\\n      outfits: [],\\n    };\\n    if (snap.line === 'find.pebble' && !save.finds.includes('find.pebble')) save.finds = [...save.finds, 'find.pebble'];\\n510→    if (snap.mode === 'results' && snap.event) {\\n      const best = save.bests[snap.event] ?? -1;\\n      if (snap.result > best) save.bests = { ...save.bests, [snap.event]: snap.result };\\n    }\\n    const key = `${snap.mode}:${snap.event}:${snap.result}:${snap.pebbles}:${snap.cursor}:${snap.credits}`;\\n    if (key !== savedKey && snap.mode !== 'title' && !attract && !hub) {\\n      savedKey = key;\\n      writeSave(store, save);\\n    }\\n  }\\n520→\\n  function paint(snap: Snap, drawn: EngineFrame): void {\\n    const lure = LURE_IDS.has(snap.text) ? LURES.find((row) => row.id === snap.text) : undefined;\\n    const sentence = lure ? (LINES[`lure.${lure.id}`] ?? lure.line) : (LINES[snap.line] ?? '');\\n    if (sentence && sentence !== said && screen !== 'title' && screen !== 'touch' && screen !== 'card') {\\n      said = sentence;\\n      say(audio, speakerFor(snap.line || 'tare.welcome'), sentence, prefs.voices);\\n    }\\n    if (screen === 'touch') note.textContent = 'Controller or keyboard required.';\\n    else if (menu || !sentence