{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_848","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to find where tick() is called from stage.ts drive().\n\nChecking whether hub frames need the loop. The browse.py harness runs for 8 seconds of play plus countdown, a 20-second ready wait, and grace. Engine readiness during this window determines the final check.\n\nThe failure occurred because createEngine never returned during the entire harness run. The engine loads both island and round scenes, so warmup compiles the full island and pavilion at high resolution inside each iframe. Even though game:round is active, the warmup still processes the retreat sky and post-look for the current view.\n\nBoth scene modules load at import time. The GPU work is limited to the current scene. Four iframes compiling the retreat look in SwiftShader could contend for minutes. gfx.warmUp=asked should reduce upfront compilation. quality=low disables shadows, GI, god rays, bloom, and halos. resolution=pixels uses smaller targets. The retreat post-look stays. I am checking whether the hub can skip island scene registration.\n\nThe hub only needs the round scene. Excluding the island from createEngine's scenes array should prevent its terrain from loading into the world. The active scene is set via search scene=game:round, so defineScene still registers both scenes without necessarily initializing the island.\n\nI decided not to change the hub scene list. The stall is GPU-related, so removing the island would add unnecessary risk. The warmup card already handles ready signals via keydown and pointerdown.\n\nFront and attract are correctly skipped in hub mode. The screen resets to card via bind(). createPage runs after the client connects, so createHub executes inside a valid session. The 14-second watchdog triggers ready() before the card UI binds, but enter still works because the screen is already set to card. A double ready answer from both watchdog and keydown should be harmless. One remaining concern: during load, what element is focused when the harness dispatches keydown?\n\nThe harness dispatches keydown on the iframe body or canvas. The window capture listener catches it even if the event bubbles from the canvas. The handler checks for Enter, matching the dispatched code.\n\nThe dispatched keydown event does not need to be trusted. The handler ignores isTyping. Setting armed and noteDevice on the card screen is harmless for the hub. createPage publishes the screen as card before the engine starts, but hub tests do not check that early state. The touch stick must be removed immediately after createEngine returns, before the ready check.\n\nThe game loop starts before createEngine returns, so the first frames may run while the touch stick is still present. Removing it synchronously after createEngine resolves is safe because the test polls for ready before checking the count.\n\ncreateEngine sets ready and starts the loop before returning. The await resumes as a microtask, so the touch stick is removed synchronously in that same turn. Playwright polls from the browser side, and the removal happens before the browser yields control back to the test. This ensures the stick is already gone when the test checks its count.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-94f4bff5-2c92-46a0-8f9c-e19c8cad2e0c-24","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"canvas|resolution|width","glob":"**/labs/game/tools/browse.py"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-94f4bff5-2c92-46a0-8f9c-e19c8cad2e0c-25","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"hubView\\?\\.tick|tick\\(","glob":"**/labs/game/ui/stage.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-94f4bff5-2c92-46a0-8f9c-e19c8cad2e0c-26","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/app/drawing.ts","offset":160,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4761,"output_tokens":1537,"cache_read_input_tokens":60416,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"04ad7a75-35a0-4c70-97f0-2bd76aefb0ec"}
