{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_876","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking renderer shadow settings and iframe durations.\n\nFixing the 4-wide init timeout is the priority. A probe will log performance.now when ready fires. The harness timing of ready() calls relative to send windows also needs review.\n\nThe harness waits until the last player is ready. Then it pauses for two seconds. It then waits up to 1500 milliseconds. It then waits up to four seconds. Only then does it check sends.\n\nThe send check happens 5.5 seconds after the round starts, once engines are already looping. For two players this works because they finish initialization before the 20-second ready deadline. Four players exceed that limit, so the ready check fails. The plan is to reduce initialization time below 20 seconds and skip island scene registration for the hub to avoid terrain setup.\n\nOnly the active scene runs setup, so island terrain is not in the round scene. The warmup cost is the pavilion retreat look. A bare look will be defined and used only for the hub.\n\nThe warm-up camera pass is still required before ready. A bare look keeps that warm-up to a single simple pass, which should stay fast even with four players. The phone stays on the retreat look so the game looks correct on both devices. The hub pavilion can be flatter because it does not need to match the retreat; the local group class uses the island scene with the retreat look instead.\n\nA no-filter look will be defined for the hub pavilion to test whether removing the toon and outline pipeline fixes the four-player timeout. The current 240p resolution and low quality are already in place.\n\nThe new `look:pavilion` uses the same retreat sky but no filters. `main.ts` will set this look for hub sessions and keep the retreat look for local ones. A 15-second ready fallback is also being added as a safety net if engines still fail to finish in time.\n\nThe 15-second ready fallback is being reconsidered because it risks send failures. The simpler look will be tested first without the fallback.\n\nHub sessions only need one camera warm-up, not two.\n\nA new hypothesis is that SwiftShader serializes four WebGPU device initializations, making them inherently slow even after shader compilation finishes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-238e6b25-5b91-44c5-aca1-6c54edb62f04-72","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"TIMINGS|countdownMs|graceMs|helloMs","glob":"**/labs/game/hub/**/*.{html,js,txt}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3205,"output_tokens":1346,"cache_read_input_tokens":114944,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"0ebd9e45-6a95-47c9-b230-49b927fb8c2a"}
