{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7daad9ec-c64c-4057-9289-e9f495533c71-97","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"125→      day: save.day,\\n      event: live.event,\\n      focus,\\n    };\\n    (window as unknown as { __game?: GameHandle }).__game = handle;\\n130→  };\\n  const inspector = (): Inspector | null => engine?.inspector ?? null;\\n  const run = (name: string, args?: Record<string, unknown>) => {\\n    const actions = inspector()?.actions as\\n      { run?: (id: string, body?: Record<string, unknown>) => unknown } | undefined;\\n    if (typeof actions?.run === 'function') actions.run(name, args);\\n  };\\n  const applyPrefs = () => {\\n    audio.volume('music', prefs.music);\\n    audio.volume('effects', prefs.effects);\\n140→    audio.volume('ui', prefs.voices);\\n    inspector()?.set('game.assist', prefs.assist);\\n    inspector()?.set('game.cpu', prefs.cpu);\\n    glyphSet = lastDevice === 'keyboard' ? 'keys' : lastDevice === 'mouse' ? 'mouse' : icons;\\n    if (screen !== 'touch') note.textContent = promptLine(glyphSet);\\n  };\\n  const persist = () => {\\n    save = { ...save, outfits: [], settings: { ...prefs, icons } };\\n    if (attract || hub) return;\\n    writeSave(store, save);\\n150→  };\\n  const close = () => {\\n    menu?.remove();\\n    menu = null;\\n    menuCancel = undefined;\",\"content_concise\":\"125→      day: save.day,\\n      event: live.event,\\n      focus,\\n    };\\n    (window as unknown as { __game?: GameHandle }).__game = handle;\\n130→  };\\n  const inspector = (): Inspector | null => engine?.inspector ?? null;\\n  const run = (name: string, args?: Record<string, unknown>) => {\\n    const actions = inspector()?.actions as\\n      { run?: (id: string, body?: Record<string, unknown>) => unknown } | undefined;\\n    if (typeof actions?.run === 'function') actions.run(name, args);\\n  };\\n  const applyPrefs = () => {\\n    audio.volume('music', prefs.music);\\n    audio.volume('effects', prefs.effects);\\n140→    audio.volume('ui', prefs.voices);\\n    inspector()?.set('game.assist', prefs.assist);\\n    inspector()?.set('game.cpu', prefs.cpu);\\n    glyphSet = lastDevice === 'keyboard' ? 'keys' : lastDevice === 'mouse' ? 'mouse' : icons;\\n    if (screen !== 'touch') note.textContent = promptLine(glyphSet);\\n  };\\n  const persist = () => {\\n    save = { ...save, outfits: [], settings: { ...prefs, icons } };\\n    if (attract || hub) return;\\n    writeSave(store, save);\\n150→  };\\n  const close = () => {\\n    menu?.remove();\\n    menu = null;\\n    menuCancel = undefined;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/stage.ts\",\"offset\":125,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"      day: save.day,\\n      event: live.event,\\n      focus,\\n    };\\n    (window as unknown as { __game?: GameHandle }).__game = handle;\\n  };\\n  const inspector = (): Inspector | null => engine?.inspector ?? null;\\n  const run = (name: string, args?: Record<string, unknown>) => {\\n    const actions = inspector()?.actions as\\n      { run?: (id: string, body?: Record<string, unknown>) => unknown } | undefined;\\n    if (typeof actions?.run === 'function') actions.run(name, args);\\n  };\\n  const applyPrefs = () => {\\n    audio.volume('music', prefs.music);\\n    audio.volume('effects', prefs.effects);\\n    audio.volume('ui', prefs.voices);\\n    inspector()?.set('game.assist', prefs.assist);\\n    inspector()?.set('game.cpu', prefs.cpu);\\n    glyphSet = lastDevice === 'keyboard' ? 'keys' : lastDevice === 'mouse' ? 'mouse' : icons;\\n    if (screen !== 'touch') note.textContent = promptLine(glyphSet);\\n  };\\n  const persist = () => {\\n    save = { ...save, outfits: [], settings: { ...prefs, icons } };\\n    if (attract || hub) return;\\n    writeSave(store, save);\\n  };\\n  const close = () => {\\n    menu?.remove();\\n    menu = null;\\n    menuCancel = undefined;\\n\",\"total_lines\":598}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"e00665a8-2eea-4546-bb8e-50d7fd405265"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_896","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"run() is safe when the inspector is null. It does nothing.\n\nThe pump's `lastSend` guard prevents `round.go` from running once the engine starts. The class never begins. I need to trigger `round.go` only when the engine exists.\n\nA `began` flag replaces the `lastSend` guard. It ensures `round.go` runs exactly once the engine exists. The pump still sends and reports while the engine is absent.\n\nThe pump starts on the 'start' event. It no-ops while `client.time()` is negative during countdown, then sends once time becomes non-negative. The answer screen is the card from the start.\n\nCards are already being sent during the splash screen because `showsCard` is set on hello. When `ready()` fires, the card should already be present. The Enter key then triggers the answer because the screen is still the card.\n\nA key timing risk remains. If `ready()` is called immediately before `createEngine`, the engine may block the main thread with a long synchronous chunk before its first `await`. The Enter keydown could then sit in the queue and miss the three-second window. Because `createEngine` uses `await`, it yields, so the key should be processed at the next yield if the card screen is still active.\n\nThe harness must see the card within two seconds and then press Enter. If createEngine blocks the main thread with a long synchronous chunk before its first await, that keypress is delayed. The timing probe showed the engine was not ready for ten seconds, yet the event loop kept yielding enough for the harness to poll. While the iframe main thread awaits the GPU, it can still process Enter events. The code should call ready() before starting createEngine.\n\nThe await on createEngine allows Enter to be processed while the engine loads. The pump also needs no frames at startup.\n\nHowever, ready() should not fire immediately. If it does, the round ends around t=21 seconds. Engines in slow runs may finish after that point, so engine.ready will not be seen by the harness check at the end.\n\nA slow run finishes engines at t=25. The shortened round ends at t=21. The harness check sees engine.ready as false. A fast run at t=16 passes. The official verify uses the slow environment.\n\nThe engine.ready check is separate from the harness pass. It runs only after the harness finishes, so it does not wait for engines to finish. The previous official failure occurred because the round ended before engines were ready. With cheap graphics, the hub4 probe showed engine.ready as true at the end because the round waited long enough for slow boots to complete. Early-ready shortens that wait and risks the same failure.\n\nThe round lasts roughly sixteen seconds after release. Engines must finish before that point. The timing probe reached sixteen seconds, but the fail probe hit over twenty seconds for client readiness while engines were already done in a longer test. I should not change browse.py timeouts to hide slow boots; the test is the specification.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cbc01537-0b4e-4bfd-bfd2-8b17fb06d7ec-98","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"play=8000|players=4|engine.ready","glob":"**/{TASK.md,PLAN.md,STAGE.md,labs/game/**/*.md}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":538,"output_tokens":1642,"cache_read_input_tokens":145408,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"d7252cd1-4c96-4b0c-8e94-b00f128ab781"}
