{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_903","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The 4-player test passed with the pavilion look.\n\nThe flat look fixed the 4-player timeout. The 2-player and touch tests still pass. I will now run the full official verify.\n\nThe full verify will run with CHROMIUM_PATH and PLAYWRIGHT overrides. It targets one browser and uses scratch output. After passing, I will run npm test and npm run check. Then I will update the goal plan and confirm hand-in files. The 4-player case is the hardest hub scenario.\n\nI will write a monitor script to poll the verify process and report once when it finishes. I will check that stage.ts stays under 600 lines. The goal plan will be reviewed after verify completes so I can flip the right boxes.\n\nThe monitor script will wait for a pid file written by the verify command before polling it. This avoids a race condition with the shell wrapper.\n\nI will start the verify and monitor now, then read the goal plan and TASK requirements in parallel. This prepares the checklist flips before the monitor wakes me.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8ffe8c8c-3397-4e0a-83ee-adcb1f8a09a4-107","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/watch-verify.sh","content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Wake once when the official verifier exits. Diagnostics go to the watch log.\nPIDFILE=$1\nLOG=$2\nWATCH=$3\necho \"watching $(date -Is)\" >>\"$WATCH\"\nfor _ in $(seq 1 60); do\n  [ -f \"$PIDFILE\" ] && break\n  sleep 1\ndone\nPID=$(cat \"$PIDFILE\" 2>/dev/null || true)\nif [ -z \"$PID\" ]; then\n  echo \"FAILED: no verify pid\"\n  exit 1\nfi\nwhile kill -0 \"$PID\" 2>/dev/null; do\n  echo \"alive $PID $(date -Is)\" >>\"$WATCH\"\n  sleep 30\ndone\necho \"exited $PID $(date -Is)\" >>\"$WATCH\"\ntail -20 \"$LOG\" >>\"$WATCH\" 2>/dev/null || true\nif grep -qx '0 failures' \"$LOG\" && grep -qx 'EXIT:0' \"$LOG\"; then\n  echo \"DONE: verify 0 failures EXIT:0\"\n  exit 0\nfi\necho \"FAILED: $(tail -8 \"$LOG\" 2>/dev/null | tr '\\n' ' | ')\"\nexit 1\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8ffe8c8c-3397-4e0a-83ee-adcb1f8a09a4-108","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"SCRATCH=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer\"\nDEV=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656\"\ncd \"$DEV\"\nexport PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64\nexport CHROMIUM_PATH=\"$HOME/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-1243/chrome-headless-shell-linux64/chrome-headless-shell\"\nexport VERIFY_OUT=\"$SCRATCH\"\necho $$ > \"$SCRATCH/verify.pid\"\nnode labs/game/tools/verify.mjs > \"$SCRATCH/verify.log\" 2>&1\necho EXIT:$? >> \"$SCRATCH/verify.log\"","description":"Run the official full Thumb Yoga verifier","block_until_ms":0}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8ffe8c8c-3397-4e0a-83ee-adcb1f8a09a4-109","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^- \\[[ x]\\]|## Deviations|## Verification","path":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc%2Fwork/01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc/goal/plan.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":298,"output_tokens":2204,"cache_read_input_tokens":152576,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"993b6417-ac39-4cf3-bf8e-24e0e13b0d67"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8ffe8c8c-3397-4e0a-83ee-adcb1f8a09a4-107","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Silent until the official verify process exits, or until it has run 25 minutes.\\nSCRATCH=\\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer\\\"\\nPIDFILE=\\\"$SCRATCH/verify.pid\\\"\\nLOG=\\\"$SCRATCH/verify.log\\\"\\nTRACE=\\\"$SCRATCH/watch-verify.trace\\\"\\nfor _ in $(seq 1 60); do\\n  [ -f \\\"$PIDFILE\\\" ] && break\\n  sleep 1\\ndone\\nif [ ! -f \\\"$PIDFILE\\\" ]; then\\n  echo \\\"FAILED: verify.pid never appeared\\\"\\n  exit 1\\nfi\\nPID=$(cat \\\"$PIDFILE\\\")\\necho \\\"pid $PID start $(date -Is)\\\" >>\\\"$TRACE\\\"\\nstart=$(date +%s)\\nwarned=0\\nwhile kill -0 \\\"$PID\\\" 2>/dev/null; do\\n  now=$(date +%s)\\n  if [ \\\"$warned\\\" -eq 0 ] && [ $((now - start)) -ge 1500 ]; then\\n    warned=1\\n    echo \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: verify pid $PID still running after 25m\\\"\\n  fi\\n  sleep 30\\ndone\\nsleep 1\\ntail=$(tail -n 8 \\\"$LOG\\\" 2>/dev/null | tr '\\\\n' ' | ')\\necho \\\"exit $(date -Is) $tail\\\" >>\\\"$TRACE\\\"\\nif grep -qx '0 failures' \\\"$LOG\\\" && grep -qx 'EXIT:0' \\\"$LOG\\\"; then\\n  echo \\\"DONE: $tail\\\"\\n  exit 0\\nfi\\necho \\\"FAILED: $tail\\\"\\nexit 1\\n\",\"new_string\":\"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Wake once when the official verifier exits. Diagnostics go to the watch log.\\nPIDFILE=$1\\nLOG=$2\\nWATCH=$3\\necho \\\"watching $(date -Is)\\\" >>\\\"$WATCH\\\"\\nfor _ in $(seq 1 60); do\\n  [ -f \\\"$PIDFILE\\\" ] && break\\n  sleep 1\\ndone\\nPID=$(cat \\\"$PIDFILE\\\" 2>/dev/null || true)\\nif [ -z \\\"$PID\\\" ]; then\\n  echo \\\"FAILED: no verify pid\\\"\\n  exit 1\\nfi\\nwhile kill -0 \\\"$PID\\\" 2>/dev/null; do\\n  echo \\\"alive $PID $(date -Is)\\\" >>\\\"$WATCH\\\"\\n  sleep 30\\ndone\\necho \\\"exited $PID $(date -Is)\\\" >>\\\"$WATCH\\\"\\ntail -20 \\\"$LOG\\\" >>\\\"$WATCH\\\" 2>/dev/null || true\\nif grep -qx '0 failures' \\\"$LOG\\\" && grep -qx 'EXIT:0' \\\"$LOG\\\"; then\\n  echo \\\"DONE: verify 0 failures EXIT:0\\\"\\n  exit 0\\nfi\\necho \\\"FAILED: $(tail -8 \\\"$LOG\\\" 2>/dev/null | tr '\\\\n' ' | ')\\\"\\nexit 1\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"Wrote file successfully to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/watch-verify.sh.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"Wrote file successfully to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/watch-verify.sh.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/watch-verify.sh\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Silent until the official verify process exits, or until it has run 25 minutes.\\nSCRATCH=\\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer\\\"\\nPIDFILE=\\\"$SCRATCH/verify.pid\\\"\\nLOG=\\\"$SCRATCH/verify.log\\\"\\nTRACE=\\\"$SCRATCH/watch-verify.trace\\\"\\nfor _ in $(seq 1 60); do\\n  [ -f \\\"$PIDFILE\\\" ] && break\\n  sleep 1\\ndone\\nif [ ! -f \\\"$PIDFILE\\\" ]; then\\n  echo \\\"FAILED: verify.pid never appeared\\\"\\n  exit 1\\nfi\\nPID=$(cat \\\"$PIDFILE\\\")\\necho \\\"pid $PID start $(date -Is)\\\" >>\\\"$TRACE\\\"\\nstart=$(date +%s)\\nwarned=0\\nwhile kill -0 \\\"$PID\\\" 2>/dev/null; do\\n  now=$(date +%s)\\n  if [ \\\"$warned\\\" -eq 0 ] && [ $((now - start)) -ge 1500 ]; then\\n    warned=1\\n    echo \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: verify pid $PID still running after 25m\\\"\\n  fi\\n  sleep 30\\ndone\\nsleep 1\\ntail=$(tail -n 8 \\\"$LOG\\\" 2>/dev/null | tr '\\\\n' ' | ')\\necho \\\"exit $(date -Is) $tail\\\" >>\\\"$TRACE\\\"\\nif grep -qx '0 failures' \\\"$LOG\\\" && grep -