{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_929","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Two Prettier failures appeared on 14 files. These may be pre-existing and unrelated to recent edits.\n\nPrettier passes on main.ts and retreat.ts. The 14 files need formatting to satisfy the full-tree check. The generated browse.py pycache must be deleted rather than approved as a binary.\n\nChecking for other pyc files I created. The 14 Prettier failures likely predate my edits. I will format them to satisfy the check.\n\nPrettier only changes whitespace, so it will not alter shipped HTML or verify behavior. I will format the 14 files and delete the generated __pycache__ before rerunning the check.\n\nPrettier changes to JSON files like titles.json could alter the title RNG bytes. The summary noted those bytes are b0306a24, so reformatting must be avoided.\n\nThe title was already fixed by the prior RNG pick, so reformatting titles.json will not change the game state. However, a test that hashes the file bytes could fail. I will inspect the prettier diff for titles.json before writing.\n\nI will run prettier --write on the 14 files and inspect the diff. If titles.json content changes, I will revert it. The engine lock was already fine, so only the formatting and pycache fixes should remain.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-51364f5e-96cd-4f14-92ac-155dad6c7f1a-147","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/tools/checkAll.ts","limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-51364f5e-96cd-4f14-92ac-155dad6c7f1a-148","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"find \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656\" -type d -name '__pycache__' -o -name '*.pyc' | head -40","description":"Find Python bytecode that check rejects"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1575,"output_tokens":1034,"cache_read_input_tokens":186368,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"5acf4ad6-8c73-4836-ac05-ed102d0d8f04"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-51364f5e-96cd-4f14-92ac-155dad6c7f1a-147","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file `npm run check` (T0, PLAN.md §8.1–§8.2): runs `tsc`, ESLint, Prettier and `node x check` at the same time and\\n * fails if any fails. Run one after another they took about 9 s of T0's 10 s budget at G0, `tsc` alone about 4 s; in\\n * parallel T0 takes as long as the slowest. Node runs this file directly (type stripping, as the hooks do; ADR-0014\\n * amendment 4), so it needs nothing installed beyond the tools it starts.\\n *\\n * `tsc` is `npm run typecheck`'s command: `tsc -b` over the projects of tsconfig.check.json, which together hold\\n * tsconfig.json's files. It reuses what the last run checked (node_modules/.cache/tsc/), so it costs what a change\\n * reaches: measured 0.2 s unchanged, 1.5–3 s after a typical edit, about 6 s when an export of a module every file\\n10→ * reaches changes, against 6 s every time for `tsc --noEmit` (ADR-0014 amendment 7).\\n *\\n * Invariants: every tool runs to the end, so one run names every failure; each tool's output is printed whole, in\\n * the fixed order below, after all have finished (never interleaved); the exit code is 0 only when all four pass,\\n * else 1. Caches live under node_modules/.cache/, which `x ci --local` keeps across `npm ci`; a new checkout or\\n * worktree has none, so its first run fills them (measured after G5: 13.9 s cold, Prettier 13.7 s of it; 5.8 s warm).\\n *\\n * Usage: `npm run check` (package.json: `\\\"check\\\": \\\"node tools/checkAll.ts\\\"`). Importing the module runs nothing.\\n *\\n * @see package.json, docs/TESTING.md\\n20→ */\\nimport { spawn } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { mkdirSync } from 'node:fs';\\n\\n/** One T0 tool: its name and its command line, run from the repository root. */\\nexport interface CheckTool {\\n  name: string;\\n  command: string;\\n}\\n\\n30→/** The T0 tools, in the order their output is printed; `tsc` runs package.json's `typecheck` command. */\\nexport const CHECK_TOOLS: CheckTool[] = [\\n  { name: 'tsc', command: 'npx tsc -b tsconfig.check.json' },\\n  { name: 'eslint', command: 'npx eslint --cache --cache-location node_modules/.cache/eslint/ .' },\\n  { name: 'prettier', command: 'npx prettier --check --cache .' },\\n  { name: 'x check', command: 'node x check' },\\n];\\n\\n/** The outcome of one tool: its exit code, combined output and time taken. */\\ninterface ToolResult {\\n40→  tool: CheckTool;\\n  code: number;\\n  output: string;\\n  ms: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** Runs one tool through the shell, collecting stdout and stderr together. */\\nfunction run(tool: CheckTool): Promise<ToolResult> {\\n  const started = performance.now();\\n  return new Promise((resolve) => {\\n50→    const child = spawn(tool.command, { shell: true, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'] });\\n    let output = '';\\n    child.stdout.on('data', (chunk: Buffer) => (output += chunk));\\n    child.stderr.on('data', (chunk: Buffer) => (output += chunk));\\n    child.on('close', (code) => resolve({ tool, code: code ?? 1, output, ms: performance.now() - started }));\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * The cache directories ESLint and Prettier create on a cold run. They are made first, because `x check`'s docs\\n60→ * plugin, running at the same time, checks that the paths the docs cite exist.\\n */\\nexport const CACHE_DIRS = ['node_modules/.cache/eslint', 'node_modules/.cache/prettier'];\\n\\n/** Runs every tool in parallel, prints their output in order, and returns the exit code (0 only if all pass). */\\nexport async function checkAll(tools: CheckTool[] = CHECK_TOOLS): Promise<number> {\\n  for (const dir of CACHE_DIRS) mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });\\n  const started = performance.now();\\n  const results = await Promise.all(tools.map(run));\\n  for (const { tool, code, output, ms } of results) {\\n70→    const text = output.trimEnd();\\n    console.log(`${code === 0 ? 'ok  ' : 'FAIL'} ${tool.name} (${(ms / 1000).toFixed(1)} s)${text ? `\\\\n${text}` : ''}`);\\n  }\\n  const failed = results.filter((result) => result.code !== 0).map((result) => result.tool.name);\\n  const seconds = ((performance.now() - started) / 1000).toFixed(1);\\n  console.log(failed.length ? `check: FAIL (${failed.join(', ')})` : `check: ok in ${seconds} s`);\\n  return failed.length ? 1 : 0;\\n}\\n\\nif (import.meta.main) process.exitCode = await checkAll();\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file `npm run check` (T0, PLAN.md §8.1–§8.2): runs `tsc`, ESLint, Prettier and `node x check` at the same time and\\n * fails if any fails. Run one after another they took about 9 s of T0's 10 s budget at G0, `tsc` alone about 4 s; in\\n * parallel T0 takes as long as the slowest. Node runs this file directly (type stripping, as the hooks do; ADR-0014\\n * amendment 4), so it needs nothing installed beyond the tools it starts.\\n *\\n * `tsc` is `npm run typecheck`'s command: `tsc -b` over the projects of tsconfig.check.json, which together hold\\n * tsconfig.json's files. It reuses what the last run checked (node_modules/.cache/tsc/), so it costs what a change\\n * reaches: measured 0.2 s unchanged, 1.5–3 s after a typical edit, about 6 s when an export of a module every file\\n10→ * reaches changes, against 6 s every time for `tsc --noEmit` (ADR-0014 amendment 7).\\n *\\n * Invariants: every tool runs to the end, so one run names every failure; each tool's output is printed whole, in\\n * the fixed order below, after all have finished (never interleaved); the exit code is 0 only when all four pass,\\n * else 1. Caches live under node_modules/.cache/, which `x ci --local` keeps across `npm ci`; a new checkout or\\n * worktree has none, so its first run fills them (measured after G5: 13.9 s cold, Prettier 13.7 s of it; 5.8 s warm).\\n *\\n * Usage: `npm run check` (package.json: `\\\"check\\\": \\\"node tools/checkAll.ts\\\"`). Importing the module runs nothing.\\n *\\n * @see package.json, docs/TESTING.md\\n20→ */\\nimport { spawn } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { mkdirSync } from 'node:fs';\\n\\n/** One T0 tool: its name and its command line, run from the repository root. */\\nexport interface CheckTool {\\n  name: string;\\n  command: string;\\n}\\n\\n30→/** The T0 tools, in the order their output is printed; `tsc` runs package.json's `typecheck` command. */\\nexport const CHECK_TOOLS: CheckTool[] = [\\n  { name: 'tsc', command: 'npx tsc -b tsconfig.check.json' },\\n  { name: 'eslint', command: 'npx eslint --cache --cache-location node_modules/.cache/eslint/ .' },\\n  { name: 'prettier', command: 'npx prettier --check --cache .' },\\n  { name: 'x check', command: 'node x check' },\\n];\\n\\n/** The outcome of one tool: its exit code, combined output and time taken. */\\ninterface ToolResult {\\n40→  tool: CheckTool;\\n  code: number;\\n  output: string;\\n  ms: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** Runs one tool through the shell, collecting stdout and stderr together. */\\nfunction run(tool: CheckTool): Promise<ToolResult> {\\n  const started = performance.now();\\n  return new Promise((resolve) => {\\n50→    const child = spawn(tool.command, { shell: true, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'] });\\n    let output = '';\\n    child.stdout.on('data', (chunk: Buffer) => (output += chunk));\\n    child.stderr.on('data', (chunk: Buffer) => (output += chunk));\\n    child.on('close', (code) => resolve({ tool, code: code ?? 1, output, ms: performance.now() - started }));\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * The cache directories ESLint and Prettier create on a cold run. They are made first, because `x check`'s docs\\n60→ * plugin, running at the same time, checks that the paths the docs cite exist.\\n */\\nexport const CACHE_DIRS = ['node_modules/.cache/eslint', 'node_modules/.cache/prettier'];\\n\\n/** Runs every tool in parallel, prints their output in order, and returns the exit code (0 only if all pass). */\\nexport async function checkAll(tools: CheckTool[] = CHECK_TOOLS): Promise<number> {\\n  for (const dir of CACHE_DIRS) mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });\\n  const started = performance.now();\\n  const results = await Promise.all(tools.map(run));\\n  for (const { tool, code, output, ms } of results) {\\n70→    const text = output.trimEnd();\\n    console.log(`${code === 0 ? 'ok  ' : 'FAIL'} ${tool.name} (${(ms / 1000).toFixed(1)} s)${text ? `\\\\n${text}` : ''}`);\\n  }\\n  const failed = results.filter((result) => result.code !== 0).map((result) => result.tool.name);\\n  const seconds = ((performance.now() - started) / 1000).toFixed(1);\\n  console.log(failed.length ? `check: FAIL (${failed.join(', ')})` : `check: ok in ${seconds} s`);\\n  return failed.length ? 1 : 0;\\n}\\n\\nif (import.meta.main) process.exitCode = await checkAll();\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/tools/checkAll.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file `npm run check` (T0, PLAN.md §8.1–§8.2): runs `tsc`, ESLint, Prettier and `node x check` at the same time and\\n * fails if any fails. Run one after another they took about 9 s of T0's 10 s budget at G0, `tsc` alone about 4 s; in\\n * parallel T0 takes as long as the slowest. Node runs this file directly (type stripping, as the hooks do; ADR-0014\\n * amendment 4), so it needs nothing installed beyond the tools it starts.\\n *\\n * `tsc` is `npm run typecheck`'s command: `tsc -b` over the projects of tsconfig.check.json, which together hold\\n * tsconfig.json's files. It reuses what the last run checked (node_modules/.cache/tsc/), so it costs what a change\\n * reaches: measured 0.2 s unchanged, 1.5–3 s after a typical edit, about 6 s when an export of a module every file\\n * reaches changes, against 6 s every time for `tsc --noEmit` (ADR-0014 amendment 7).\\n *\\n * Invariants: every tool runs