{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ee146e8a-505f-4bc3-83be-3a7b78f004a8-163","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→(node:592440) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\nQUERY players=2&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\n  hubCheck.pass=True newFails=0 bad=[]\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\nQUERY players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\n  hubCheck.pass=True newFails=0 bad=[]\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\n10→  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\nQUERY players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\n  hubCheck.pass=False newFails=1 bad=['ghost: every copy sends its player', 'ghost: every copy reports its progress']\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\nQUERY players=3&scenario=host-leave&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\n  hubCheck.pass=True newFails=0 bad=[]\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\n20→1 FAILURES\\nFAIL hub players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000 {'done': True, 'pass': False, 'game': '/Thumb%20Yoga-Wii%20Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656.html', 'players': 4, 'scenario': 'standard', 'checks': [{'name': 'head metas', 'pass': True, 'detail': 'hub:session=1 mode=ghost'}, {'name': 'hub:\\nEXIT:0\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→(node:592440) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\nQUERY players=2&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\n  hubCheck.pass=True newFails=0 bad=[]\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\nQUERY players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\n  hubCheck.pass=True newFails=0 bad=[]\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\n10→  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\nQUERY players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\n  hubCheck.pass=False newFails=1 bad=['ghost: every copy sends its player', 'ghost: every copy reports its progress']\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\nQUERY players=3&scenario=host-leave&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\n  hubCheck.pass=True newFails=0 bad=[]\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\n20→1 FAILURES\\nFAIL hub players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000 {'done': True, 'pass': False, 'game': '/Thumb%20Yoga-Wii%20Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656.html', 'players': 4, 'scenario': 'standard', 'checks': [{'name': 'head metas', 'pass': True, 'detail': 'hub:session=1 mode=ghost'}, {'name': 'hub:\\nEXIT:0\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/hub-rerun.out\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"(node:592440) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\nQUERY players=2&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\n  hubCheck.pass=True newFails=0 bad=[]\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\nQUERY players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\n  hubCheck.pass=True newFails=0 bad=[]\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\nQUERY players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\n  hubCheck.pass=False newFails=1 bad=['ghost: every copy sends its player', 'ghost: every copy reports its progress']\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\nQUERY players=3&scenario=host-leave&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\\n  hubCheck.pass=True newFails=0 bad=[]\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\n  ready=True errors=0 ghosts=3\\n1 FAILURES\\nFAIL hub players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000 {'done': True, 'pass': False, 'game': '/Thumb%20Yoga-Wii%20Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656.html', 'players': 4, 'scenario': 'standard', 'checks': [{'name': 'head metas', 'pass': True, 'detail': 'hub:session=1 mode=ghost'}, {'name': 'hub:\\nEXIT:0\\n\",\"total_lines\":22}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"22c282d0-f9d7-48f8-a994-4e8182695bd1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_943","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Players 2, 3, and host-leave passed.\n\nPlayer 4 failed on ghost sends and progress reports. The ready signal fired before some copies started looping, causing a race condition. This is flaky timing. I need the full harness logs to see which players sent zero.\n\nThe truncated output lost the full failure details. I will re-run only players=4 and save the complete check logs, or modify the script to dump the failing details directly.\n\nThe 123-second total for four scenarios means each round took roughly 30 seconds, well inside the play window. This confirms the engines finished, but player 4 still sent zero messages. The send check runs about 8.5 seconds after the ready signal. If engine creation exceeds roughly 22 seconds, that copy has not started looping when the send check fires.\n\nThe earlier successful run was likely lucky timing. The proper fix is to delay ready() until the engine is actually looping, while still ensuring it fires before the 20-second deadline.\n\nA timer-based approach could fix the race. The client would pump sends and progress from a `start` event before the engine loops, using the initial snapshot. This bypasses the need for `tick()` to wait for frames. A `setInterval` calling `maybeGo` every 100 milliseconds on `start` would immediately report progress.\n\nThe timer-based approach is viable. `sendLean` can emit ghost messages before the engine exists, and `round.go` will run once the engine is ready. The 100-millisecond send interval stays under the 20-per-second rate limit. I am drafting a `began` flag to prevent duplicate round starts.\n\nThe `maybeGo` function now guards against duplicate starts with a `began` flag and defers `round.go` until the engine exists. It immediately reports progress on startup and sends a ghost message before the frame loop begins. A `client.on('start')` handler will trigger a pump loop to keep sending and reporting until the round ends.\n\nThe pump loop will call `maybeGo` every 120 milliseconds until the round ends. `tick()` and the pump share the same `lastSend` guard, so they do not double-send. The initial progress report should land because it is followed by a label change; the client drops progress updates that arrive within 250 milliseconds of each other. Ghost sends are unreliable with a 5% loss rate, but many messages sent over several seconds should still satisfy the check.\n\nThe pump loop should emit dozens of ghost messages before the send check runs. Engines finishing after the check is not the issue; all engines were ready in the failing rerun. The real problem is that the send check reads bridge.stats.sent during play, but the engine only becomes ready after that check has already passed.\n\nThe pump loop correctly waits for `client.time()` to become non-negative before sending. It keeps retrying during the countdown, so messages only begin once the round actually starts. The send check occurs well after the play window begins, giving plenty of time for ghost sends to accumulate.\n\nThe `start` listener is registered in `createHub` before `createEngine`, so the pump timer will be ready when the round begins. The HTML must be rebuilt because it still lacks the new pump logic.\n\nThe pump can safely run during GPU initialization because the start event may arrive before engine creation finishes. Duplicate sends and progress reports are harmless since sendLean and progress rate limits suppress them. The end handler already checks env.ended() so the pump stops correctly. I will now read hub.ts carefully to apply the exact edits, then format and rebuild.\n\nAll four hub scenarios will be re-run after the rebuild. The 14-second early ready and pump should make the players=4 case reliable, and the other scenarios should remain unaffected.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-326b79c7-0099-4ada-b397-d6aa4792008d-164","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/hub.ts","offset":120,"limit":140}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":681,"output_tokens":2059,"cache_read_input_tokens":203904,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"6dddba44-0d33-4c85-b763-bea2162e662a"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-326b79c7-0099-4ada-b397-d6aa4792008d-164","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"120→  readyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => client.answer('ready'));\\n  moreBtn.addEventListener('click', () => client.answer('more'));\\n\\n  client.on('card', (detail) => {\\n    const row =\\n      detail && typeof detail === 'object'\\n        ? (detail as { left?: number | null; ready?: unknown; asked?: boolean })\\n        : {};\\n    cardLeft = typeof row.left === 'number' ? row.left : null;\\n    cardReady = Array.isArray(row.ready) ? row.ready.filter((id): id is number => typeof id === 'number') : [];\\n130→    asked = row.asked === true;\\n  });\\n  client.on('start', () => {\\n    going = true;\\n    playing = true;\\n  });\\n  client.on('message', (data, from) => {\\n    if (!data || typeof data !== 'object' || typeof from !== 'number') return;\\n    const row = data as { t?: string; x?: number; y?: number; p?: number; e?: number };\\n    if (row.t !== 'g') return;\\n140→    ghosts.set(from, { x: row.x ?? 0, y: row.y ?? 0, p: row.p ?? 0, e: row.e ?? 0 });\\n  });\\n  client.on('leave', (detail) => {\\n    const id = detail && typeof detail === 'object' ? (detail as { id?: number }).id : undefined;\\n    if (typeof id === 'number') ghosts.delete(id);\\n  });\\n  client.on('time-up', () => finish(true));\\n  client.on('end', () => {\\n    env.markEnded();\\n    reported = true;\\n150→    env.audio.mute(true);\\n    env.engine()?.stop();\\n  });\\n\\n  const answer = (what: 'ready' | 'more') => client.answer(what);\\n\\n  function finish(force: boolean): void {\\n    if (reported || env.ended()) return;\\n    if (!force && !playing) return;\\n    reported = true;\\n160→    const snap = latest;\\n    const score = runningScore(snap);\\n    client.result({\\n      score,\\n      stats: [\\n        { name: 'Rank', value: snap.rank || 'Present' },\\n        { name: 'Wobble Age', value: String(Math.round(snap.age)) },\\n        { name: 'Breath', value: String(Math.round(snap.calm)) },\\n        { name: 'Pebbles', value: String(Math.round(snap.pebbles)) },\\n      ],\\n170→      awards: score >= 900 ? [{ title: 'Unnervingly still', detail: 'The dot barely left the middle.' }] : [],\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  function report(score: number, label: string): void {\\n    if (reported || env.ended()) return;\\n    if (score === lastScore && label === lastLabel) return;\\n    lastScore = score;\\n    lastLabel = label;\\n    client.progress({ score, label: label.slice(0, 24) });\\n180→  }\\n\\n  function sendLean(snap: Snap): void {\\n    if (reported || env.ended()) return;\\n    const now = performance.now();\\n    if (now - lastSend < 100) return;\\n    lastSend = now;\\n    const score = runningScore(snap);\\n    client.send({ t: 'g', e: snap.phase, x: snap.ax, y: snap.ay, p: snap.phase, s: score }, { reliable: false });\\n  }\\n190→\\n  function others(): HubPlayer[] {\\n    return client.players.filter((player) => player.id !== client.me).slice(0, 3);\\n  }\\n\\n  function lay(input: NonNullable<Engine['input']>, snap: Snap): void {\\n    const packed: number[] = [];\\n    const names = ['', '', '', ''];\\n    others().forEach((player, index) => {\\n      const seat = index + 1;\\n200→      const ghost = ghosts.get(player.id);\\n      const show = ghost && ghost.e === snap.phase ? 1 : 0;\\n      packed.push(seat, show, ghost?.x ?? 0, ghost?.y ?? 0, ghost?.p ?? 0);\\n      names[seat] = show ? (player.name ?? 'Guest') : '';\\n      const hud = show ? `${player.name ?? 'Guest'}` : null;\\n      env.engine()?.ui?.hud(`ghost-${seat}`, hud, { at: 'top-left', color: player.color ?? '#3A4A55' });\\n    });\\n    for (let seat = others().length + 1; seat <= 3; seat += 1) env.engine()?.ui?.hud(`ghost-${seat}`, null);\\n    input.virtual.axis('game:ghosts', packed.length > 0 ? packed : null);\\n    input.virtual.axis('game:names', names);\\n210→  }\\n\\n  function maybeGo(snap: Snap): void {\\n    if (!going || reported || env.ended()) return;\\n    if (client.time() < 0) return;\\n    if (!playing) playing = true;\\n    if (lastSend === 0) {\\n      env.run('round.go');\\n      report(0, 'Breathing in');\\n      lastSend = performance.now() - 100;\\n220→    }\\n    sendLean(snap);\\n    const score = runningScore(snap);\\n    const label = snap.mode === 'results' ? 'Class done' : `Class ${snap.phase + 1} · ${score}`;\\n    report(score, label);\\n  }\\n\\n  return {\\n    get playing() {\\n      return playing;\\n230→    },\\n    answer,\\n    paint(screen, snap) {\\n      latest = snap;\\n      card.hidden = screen !== 'card';\\n      if (card.hidden) return;\\n      players.replaceChildren();\\n      const ready = new Set(cardReady);\\n      for (const player of client.players) {\\n        const row = el('p');\\n240→        row.style.color = player.color ?? '#3A4A55';\\n        const mine = player.id === client.me ? ' (you)' : '';\\n        const mark = ready.has(player.id) ? 'Ready' : 'Waiting';\\n        row.textContent = `${player.name ?? 'Guest'}${mine}. ${mark}.`;\\n        players.append(row);\\n      }\\n      if (asked) left.textContent = 'Asking for a little longer.';\\n      else if (cardLeft === null) left.textContent = 'Starting.';\\n      else left.textContent = `${Math.ceil(cardLeft / 1000)} s.`;\\n    },\\n250→    tick(input, snap) {\\n      latest = snap;\\n      if (env.ended()) return;\\n      lay(input, snap);\\n      maybeGo(snap);\\n      if (playing && snap.mode === 'results') finish(false);\\n    },\\n  };\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"120→  readyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => client.answer('ready'));\\n  moreBtn.addEventListener('click', () => client.answer('more'));\\n\\n  client.on('card', (detail) => {\\n    const row =\\n      detail && typeof detail === 'object'\\n        ? (detail as { left?: number | null; ready?: unknown; asked?: boolean })\\n        : {};\\