{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_957","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Applying the hub.ts edit carefully.\n\nConfirmed the pump interval and sendLean timing won't race. `playing` is set in both the start handler and maybeGo, which stage.ts checks before switching screens.\n\nConfirmed the card screen stays visible until frame() runs, since paint only executes from there. Also considering clearing the pump interval in finish() for prompt cleanup.\n\nNo need to clear the pump interval in finish(). Confirmed window.setInterval works in modules and the type is correct. The stopPump variable will be used, so no unused-variable warning. Will watch for prettier comment length issues. Will not send progress and lean when time is slightly negative near the end; following the spec.\n\nThe pump beat can trigger round.go before the first tick. The simulation starts immediately when the clock begins. This is correct because the class should start with the clock, not wait for the GPU.\n\nRealized that round.go cannot fire before the engine exists, because the pump calls maybeGo before createEngine returns. The simulation start is therefore still synchronized with the loop, not premature.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-866986d8-9ae8-43cb-8ef3-e0721a319a3a-34","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"loop\\.start|ready = true|return \\{","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/app/engine.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-866986d8-9ae8-43cb-8ef3-e0721a319a3a-35","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/stage.ts","offset":380,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":905,"output_tokens":970,"cache_read_input_to