{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_958","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"loop.start() runs before createEngine returns, and bind happens after.\n\nFrames can render before bind, but drive and tick are skipped while engine is null. Snaps still update because readSnap uses the drawn argument. Need to check if onFrame provides input.\n\nPaint updates the latest snap before bind, so the pump can send leans immediately. round.go and the pump both wait for env.engine(), which is set only after bind. The first frames therefore skip tick and round.go entirely.\n\nAfter bind, the next pump beat or tick will call round.go. The harness intentionally skips round.go during the pre-bind window. This matches the old maybeGo behavior.\n\nThe new behavior sends leans and progress before bind, using the latest snap. If no frames have rendered yet, the title snap provides a valid starting state with score 0 and phase 0. Real lean data arrives once paint updates the latest snap during pre-bind frames. This is the correct fix.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a01c3ad5-3708-479e-a319-6c281d72fecf-36","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/eslint.config.js","offset":50,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1670,"output_tokens":725,"cache_read_input_tokens":71040,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"ebc8502f-cd49-422c-bdaa-3b61b74efe2b"}
