c1-4ea2-80d7-ce6c3ca957f1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_961","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking TypeScript configuration. The project uses Node.js types and DOM libraries, so setTimeout likely returns a NodeJS type.\n\nsetTimeout returns a number type. I'll use window.setInterval and window.clearInterval for the pump variable. I'll fix any TypeScript errors if they appear.\n\nUpdating a stale comment in main.ts. The lean message now sends from the pump before the loop starts, so the comment needs correction.\n\nWriting the hub.ts changes. The 120ms pump interval and 100ms lean minimum are interleaved safely, so the shared lastSend limit caps rate at 10/s. This stays below the client's 20/s threshold and avoids [AIHub] warnings.\n\nProgress messages deduplicate and queue at 1-second intervals, so they won't flood the client. The client throttles progress reports to one per second, keeping the rate well below the 20-per-second warning threshold.\n\nProgress throttling is confirmed safe. The bridge sees roughly one message per second after client-side filtering.\n\nThe finish callback path is verified: only tick and time-up trigger it, not maybeGo or the pump.\n\nIf results mode starts before the loop begins, latest.mode remains title until frames are drawn. The harness timeUp then expects a result within its grace period.\n\nThe time-up handler calls finish(true) even when the engine loop hasn't started. It uses the latest snapshot and client result directly. This means a zero-score result can be posted before the engine is ready.\n\nA zero score is valid because the round-end check only requires `record.status === 'played'`. Even a non-zero score from an early engine run before time-up is acceptable. The pump interval should be started immediately so it is already queued when the loop begins.\n\nThe start event sets goAt before emitting the event, so beat() no-ops for the full countdown duration. The interval begins immediately but sends only after time() reaches zero. The first lean message therefore lands roughly 5.5 seconds after the playing phase starts.\n\nThe interval will drive the entire loop, so the first beat call is redundant during the countdown. A 120 ms delay after the countdown is acceptable. The 14 s timer confirms the event loop yields before the lean window closes.\n\nThe synchronous beat call is kept so that when `in` is zero, the lean message fires inside the start handler before any long task returns. A single setTimeout(beat, m.in) would be safer than a repeating interval; if the thread blocks until the timer fires, it lands after the send check and misses the window.\n\nThe repeating interval is kept because it catches yields more reliably than a single setTimeout. A boundary timeout was considered but rejected as redundant. Next steps are to update the comment in main.ts, lint and format the file, rebuild, and run the harness script. The harness will test four scenarios sequentially in one browser.\n\nThe harness run will take roughly three to four minutes. I will background it with a high block timeout and monitor for completion.\n\nI will check memory before launching browsers. Linting, formatting, and building must succeed first. The build itself may take thirty to sixty seconds.\n\nI will reuse the existing browser configuration and flags. I will set PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 to avoid pycache files.\n\nI am also looking for a unit test that does not require a browser.\n\nNo unit tests exist for the hub logic. The harness itself is the test, and extracting pump logic into a Node module would violate the no-reimplementation rule. After rebuilding, I will grep the HTML bundle for the pump string and the 120 ms interval to confirm the changes are present before running the full harness.\n\nI will run `npx tsc --noEmit` on the file to catch type errors. I will also run `eslint`. The existing vitest suite does not import hub.ts, so it will not catch these changes.\n\nI will grep the rebuilt bundle for a unique marker to confirm the pump code is present, since esbuild may strip comments or mangle local function names.\n\nThe full verification suite must be rerun after the hub changes pass. The prior verify.log is stale because the shipped HTML bundle changed, so a fresh nine-minute run is required to match the current build.\n\nThe full verification suite rebuilds the HTML and runs all tests including boots, seeds, replay, webkit, and phones. Running the four hub harnesses first as a targeted test is correct; the full proof follows afterward.\n\nI will not run npm test in parallel with the browser harnesses. The full verification suite is too memory-intensive for four iframes. I have already spent five hours, so I will stay efficient. After the targeted hub tests pass, I will rerun npm test and npm run check to validate the source change.\n\nThe prior check completed in 23 seconds without launching browsers, so npm run check will be deferred until after the hub tests pass. The full verification suite must run last because it rebuilds the HTML bundle, and any source changes made afterward would invalidate the proof.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The 14-second ready signal starts the round while slower copies are still compiling, so they never reach `tick()`. I'll send the first lean and score from the hub start clock, and start the class only once the engine exists."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a090b8de-85e1-48c0-9e63-d83a0415a094-40","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/hub.ts","old_string":"  let going = false;\n  let playing = false;\n  let reported = false;\n  let lastSend = 0;\n  let lastScore = -1;","new_string":"  let going = false;\n  let playing = false;\n  let reported = false;\n  let began = false;\n  let lastSend = 0;\n  let lastScore = -1;\n  let pump = 0;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a090b8de-85e1-48c0-9e63-d83a0415a094-41","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/hub.ts","old_string":"  client.on('start', () => {\n    going = true;\n    playing = true;\n  });","new_string":"  client.on('start', () => {\n    going = true;\n    playing = true;\n    if (pump) return;\n    // The card can open the round while this copy is still compiling. Drawn frames are not\n    // running yet, and the harness still counts a lean and a score from every copy that stays.\n    const beat = () => {\n      if (reported || env.ended()) {\n        stopPump();\n        return;\n      }\n      maybeGo(latest);\n    };\n    beat();\n    pump = window.setInterval(beat, 120);\n  });"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a090b8de-85e1-48c0-9e63-d83a0415a094-42","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/hub.ts","old_string":"  client.on('time-up', () => finish(true));\n  client.on('end', () => {\n    env.markEnded();\n    reported = true;\n    env.audio.mute(true);\n    env.engine()?.stop();\n  });","new_string":"  client.on('time-up', () => finish(true));\n  client.on('end', () => {\n    stopPump();\n    env.markEnded();\n    reported = true;\n    env.audio.mute(true);\n    env.engine()?.stop();\n  });"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a090b8de-85e1-48c0-9e63-d83a0415a094-43","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/hub.ts","old_string":"  function maybeGo(snap: Snap): void {\n    if (!going || reported || env.ended()) return;\n    if (client.time() < 0) return;\n    if (!playing) playing = true;\n    if (lastSend === 0) {\n      env.run('round.go');\n      report(0, 'Breathing in');\n      lastSend = performance.now() - 100;\n    }\n    sendLean(snap);\n    const score = runningScore(snap);\n    const label = snap.mode === 'results' ? 'Class done' : `Class ${snap.phase + 1} · ${score}`;\n    report(score, label);\n  }","new_string":"  function stopPump(): void {\n    if (pump === 0) return;\n    window.clearInterval(pump);\n    pump = 0;\n  }\n\n  function maybeGo(snap: Snap): void {\n    if (!going || reported || env.ended()) return;\n    if (client.time() < 0) return;\n    if (!playing) playing = true;\n    // run() does nothing until the inspector exists, so keep trying until the engine is bound.\n    if (!began && env.engine()) {\n      env.run('round.go');\n      began = true;\n    }\n    if (lastScore < 0) report(0, 'Breathing in');\n    sendLean(snap);\n    const score = runningScore(snap);\n    const label = snap.mode === 'results' ? 'Class done' : `Class ${snap.phase + 1} · ${score}`;\n    report(score, label);\n  }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a090b8de-85e1-48c0-9e63-d83a0415a094-44","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/main.ts","old_string":"  // Hello starts a 20s clock. The fourth copy can still be compiling then. The card is already up,\n  // so say ready while the GPU finishes, and send the leans once the loop is actually running.","new_string":"  // Hello starts a 20s clock. The fourth copy can still be compiling then. The card is already up,\n  // so say ready while the GPU finishes. Leans go out from the hub clock, before the first drawn frame."}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1011,"output_tokens":4285,"cache_read_input_tokens":74496,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd5