s not a second spec: a structure that meets the criteria is acceptable even if file names differ, as long as the engine’s own workspace rules still hold (`labs/game` is where this engine mounts a game).\\n\\nKeep the balance step, activity rules, bots, and day tables as pure sim code with no rendering or DOM, so node tests drive them directly. The page only reads sim state, plays code audio, and sends input or menu choices back through the engine’s recorded channels. One bot writer produces perfect, human-like, sloppy, idle, attract, and CPU-guest input. Days, poses, charts, trays, and lines stay data. Ship a smaller complete loop early (boot, one activity, one-file HTML, hub `ready`) and add activities without breaking that loop. Put the single verify command in front of the node tests, the three-seed auto playthrough, audio renders, and the browser and harness stages. Publish `window.__game` for those checks. Write About copy and `exit-interview.json` from the same answers before the final HTML build.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [x] Save 50 titles, RNG-pick one, create the named dev folder with `new-game`, `npm ci`, and a work-root `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- [x] One-file HTML build, unmodified hub client and tags, tiny session scene, verify command skeleton, harness green with the engine actually ready.\\n- [x] Balance model, maps, disc, glyphs, Morning Check, four bots, dev sliders, and the score-band tests.\\n- [x] Scrubbed clips, Guest and Plumb, Pose Class, code voices, island, flow, saves, results.\\n- [x] Still Pond, The Line, Paddle Glide, Sand Garden, any later activities not cut, Great Tilt, and the 3-seed auto path to credits.\\n- [x] Same-screen Group Class and hub ghosts; harness 2, 3, 4, and host-leave.\\n- [x] Attract, settings, controls, About, touch-only and no-WebGPU pages, songs, and 200+ lines.\\n- [x] `exit-interview.json`, HTML copied to the work root, full verify, and two consistent boots with logs under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n- Cut Great Tilt counterweights, expert variants and outfits, Hoop Patrol, Reps Hall, the Island Jog race (the walk stays), Cliff Plunge, and Step Class. Group Class's middle class is Heron only. The group score is the 0–1000 mean of the three classes, not a sum to 3000. The island terrain cell size is 4.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- TASK.md says a headless WebGPU screenshot can be blank and to trust game state. A fully blank bitmap with `ready` and a real `__game` screen is that limit, not an automatic fail. A readable but empty or partial frame that disagrees with `__game` is a game bug.\\n- The live client fetched while writing this plan is banner `1.4.0`, matching PLAN.md’s pin. If the upstream file moves, the unmodified fetched bytes win over the old hash, and the new hash goes in `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- The required basename contains a space because SOURCE is `Wii Fit`. That is intentional, not a reason to drop the source token.\\n- PLAN.md forbids `git init` in the dev folder even though the engine guide says to commit. Do not init or commit.\\n\",\"total_lines\":64}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-32984189-a079-4526-b8d0-bd5ae87407a9-65","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"89→## Done\\n90→No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\\n\\n## Source Information\\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:36:56\\n- Source: the work it's based on\\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\\n- Art Direction: style used\\n100→- Animation: system used\\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\\n- Online: network features used, or none\\n- Testing: testing paramet