{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6c5f173c-6f14-44cc-b6f7-d860d01ceda4-68","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→seed 1 credits\\nseed 2 credits\\nseed 3 credits\\nsongs render\\nsyllables render\\nreplay capture and restore continue\\nreplay goldens continue\\n0 failures\\nEXIT:0\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→seed 1 credits\\nseed 2 credits\\nseed 3 credits\\nsongs render\\nsyllables render\\nreplay capture and restore continue\\nreplay goldens continue\\n0 failures\\nEXIT:0\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/verify-before-pump.log\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"seed 1 credits\\nseed 2 credits\\nseed 3 credits\\nsongs render\\nsyllables render\\nreplay capture and restore continue\\nreplay goldens continue\\n0 failures\\nEXIT:0\\n\",\"total_lines\":9}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6c5f173c-6f14-44cc-b6f7-d860d01ceda4-69","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Thumb Yoga\\n\\nA five-day balance retreat at Little Fulcrum, for one player or a couch of four. The only verb is where your weight sits inside a unit disc. Lean with the left stick, WASD, or a pointer-locked mouse. L2 and R2, or Q and E, are the feet. Both feet, or Space, breathe. Toppling recentres you. It is not a game over. Nothing here scores weight, size, or calories.\\n\\nThe days are a morning check, pose class, a pond, a sand garden, a paddle, a slackline, a group class, and a storm that tilts the island. Pebbles stack on a cairn. They are never spent. After the credits the ferry does not come back. Free play and a new morning remain.\\n\\n## See it\\n\\nFrom this workspace:\\n10→\\n```sh\\nnpm run dev\\nnode labs/game/tools/verify.mjs\\nnpm test\\nnpm run check\\n```\\n\\n`verify.mjs` runs the balance bands, the three-seed walk to the credits, the song and syllable renders, and the golden replay. Without `--quick` it also builds `../Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656.html` and drives that file. The HTML opens from `file://` and fetches nothing.\\n\\n20→A hub session is the same file, served beside `labs/game/hub/harness.html`. The mode is ghost. Empty mats on a local Group Class are staff unless Settings turns them off.\\n\\n## Calls\\n\\n- The title was drawn from `titles.json` (50 names). The pick is Thumb Yoga, index 16.\\n- Great Tilt's counterweights, expert variants, outfits, Hoop Patrol, Reps Hall, Island Jog's race, Cliff Plunge, and Step Class are cut. The walk around the island stays. The day list is the five days in `scenes/data/days.ts`.\\n- Group Class is a still hold, Heron, and the pond. Its score is the mean of those three, from 0 to 1000, so the same ranks apply. The plan also described a sum to 3000. The mean is the one that fits a rank.\\n- The island grid is 60 by 60 with cell size 4 (240 m). A finer cell made the SwiftShader boot too slow for a hub `ready()`.\\n- The session client is pasted unmodified. Its hash does not match the older pin. The fetched bytes are the ones in the page. See `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`.\\n- Music on a fresh save is a tenth. The engine's bus default is a half, so the page sets the volume before the save is applied.\\n30→- The engine tree was not modified.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Thumb Yoga\\n\\nA five-day balance retreat at Little Fulcrum, for one player or a couch of four. The only verb is where your weight sits inside a unit disc. Lean with the left stick, WASD, or a pointer-locked mouse. L2 and R2, or Q and E, are the feet. Both feet, or Space, breathe. Toppling recentres you. It is not a game over. Nothing here scores weight, size, or calories.\\n\\nThe days are a morning check, pose class, a pond, a sand garden, a paddle, a slackline, a group class, and a storm that tilts the island. Pebbles stack on a cairn. They are never spent. After the credits the ferry does not come back. Free play and a new morning remain.\\n\\n## See it\\n\\nFrom this workspace:\\n10→\\n```sh\\nnpm run dev\\nnode labs/game/tools/verify.mjs\\nnpm test\\nnpm run check\\n```\\n\\n`verify.mjs` runs the balance bands, the three-seed walk to the credits, the song and syllable renders, and the golden replay. Without `--quick` it also builds `../Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656.html` and drives that file. The HTML opens from `file://` and fetches nothing.\\n\\n20→A hub session is the same file, served beside `labs/game/hub/harness.html`. The mode is ghost. Empty mats on a local Group Class are staff unless Settings turns them off.\\n\\n## Calls\\n\\n- The title was drawn from `titles.json` (50 names). The pick is Thumb Yoga, index 16.\\n- Great Tilt's counterweights, expert variants, outfits, Hoop Patrol, Reps Hall, Island Jog's race, Cliff Plunge, and Step Class are cut. The walk around the island stays. The day list is the five days in `scenes/data/days.ts`.\\n- Group Class is a still hold, Heron, and the pond. Its score is the mean of those three, from 0 to 1000, so the same ranks apply. The plan also described a sum to 3000. The mean is the one that fits a rank.\\n- The island grid is 60 by 60 with cell size 4 (240 m). A finer cell made the SwiftShader boot too slow for a hub `ready()`.\\n- The session client is pasted unmodified. Its hash does not match the older pin. The fetched bytes are the ones in the page. See `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`.\\n- Music on a fresh save is a tenth. The engine's bus default is a half, so the page sets the volume before the save is applied.\\n30→- The engine tree was not modified.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/README.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"# Thumb Yoga\\n\\nA five-day balance retreat at Little Fulcrum, for one player or a couch of four. The only verb is where your weight sits inside a unit disc. Lean with the left stick, WASD, or a pointer-locked mouse. L2 and R2, or Q and E, are the feet. Both feet, or Space, breathe. Toppling recentres you. It is not a game over. Nothing here scores weight, size, or calories.\\n\\nThe days are a morning check, pose class, a pond, a sand garden, a paddle, a slackline, a group class, and a storm that tilts the island. Pebbles stack on a cairn. They are never spent. After the credits the ferry does not come back. Free play and a new morning remain.\\n\\n## See it\\n\\nFrom this workspace:\\n\\n```sh\\nnpm run dev\\nnode labs/game/tools/verify.mjs\\nnpm test\\nnpm run check\\n```\\n\\n`verify.mjs` runs the balance bands, the three-seed walk to the credits, the song and syllable renders, and the golden replay. Without `--quick` it also builds `../Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656.html` and drives that file. The HTML opens from `file://` and fetches nothing.\\n\\nA hub session is the same file, served beside `labs/game/hub/harness.html`. The mode is ghost. Empty mats on a local Group Class are staff unless Settings turns them off.\\n\\n## Calls\\n\\n- The title was drawn from `titles.json` (50 names). The pick is Thumb Yoga, index 16.\\n- Great Tilt's counterweights, expert variants, outfits, Hoop Patrol, Reps Hall, Island Jog's race, Cliff Plunge, and Step Class are cut. The walk around the island stays. The day list is the five days in `scenes/data/days.ts`.\\n- Group Class is a still hold, Heron, and the pond. Its score is the mean of those three, from 0 to 1000, so the same ranks apply. The plan also described a sum to 3000. The mean is the one that fits a rank.\\n- The island grid is 60 by 60 with cell size 4 (240 m). A finer cell made the SwiftShader boot too slow for a hub `ready()`.\\n- The session client is pasted unmodified. Its hash does not match the older pin. The fetched bytes are the ones in the page. See `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`.\\n- Music on a fresh save is a tenth. The engine's bus default is a half, so the page sets the volume before the save is applied.\\n- The engine tree was not modified.\\n\",\"total_lines\":30}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6c5f173c-6f14-44cc-b6f7-d860d01ceda4-70","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:36:56\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"third-person\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"my-3dge at e7a1243, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite 7.3, TypeScript.\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine toon style, with a bright lawn, sand shore, and a flat sea.\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine clip layer. Original poses are scrubbed from the balance step. The rest pose is Mesh2Motion.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Tracker songs, code-made effects, and gibberish syllable voices. A fresh save plays music at a tenth.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, and same-screen Group Class on its own.\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Bot bands on ten seeds, a three-seed walk to the credits, and browser checks of the built file.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"none\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Testing caught six issues before hand-in. They were score bands, a NaN prop yaw, a missing boot setting, over-long lines, a ghost pack at the wrong offset, and event imports one folder too high.\\\",\\n    \\\"Four were critical. The bands, the island boot, the ghost seat, and the event imports each stopped a run.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the four bot bands on ten seeds for every shipped activity.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful was a headless screenshot. The canvas can be blank while the sim state is fine.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Scene actions, live settings, and a headless world you can step made the week testable without a browser.\\\",\\n    \\\"I got stuck on playClip during setup, props that need a yaw, a frozen recorded world, and hub query keys read as settings.\\\",\\n    \\\"The balance step, the day director, the songs, and the syllable voices are the game’s own.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest part was keeping the pavilion small enough for the hub ready deadline while the island stayed a place.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"None. The engine files were not changed.\\\",\",\"content_concise\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:36:56\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"third-person\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"my-3dge at e7a1243, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite 7.3, TypeScript.\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine toon style, with a bright lawn, sand shore, and a flat sea.\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine clip layer. Original poses are scrubbed from the balance step. The rest pose is Mesh2Motion.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Tracker songs, code-made effects, and gibberish syllable voices. A fresh save plays music at a tenth.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, and same-screen Group Class on its own.\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Bot bands on ten seeds, a three-seed walk to the credits, and browser checks of the built file.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"none\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Testing caught six issues before hand-in. They were score bands, a NaN prop yaw, a missing boot setting, over-long lines, a ghost pack at the wrong offset, and event imports one folder too high.\\\",\\n    \\\"Four were critical. The bands, the island boot, the ghost seat, and the event imports each stopped a run.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the four bot bands on ten seeds for every shipped activity.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful was a headless screenshot. The canvas can be blank while the sim state is fine.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Scene actions, live settings, and a headless world you can step made the week testable without a browser.\\\",\\n    \\\"I got stuck on playClip during setup, props that need a yaw, a frozen recorded world, and hub query keys read as settings.\\\",\\n    \\\"The balance step, the day director, the songs, and the syllable voices are the game’s own.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest part was keeping the pavilion small enough for the hub ready deadline while the island stayed a place.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"None. The engine files were not changed.\\\",\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/exit-interview.json\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:36:56\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"third-person\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"my-3dge at e7a1243, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite 7.3, TypeScript.\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine toon style, with a bright lawn, sand shore, and a flat sea.\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine clip layer. Original poses are scrubbed from the balance step. The rest pose is Mesh2Motion.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Tracker songs, code-made effects, and gibberish syllable voices. A fresh save plays music at a tenth.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, and same-screen Group Class on its own.\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Bot bands on ten seeds, a three-seed walk to the credits, and browser checks of the built file.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"none\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Testing caught six issues before hand-in. They were score bands, a NaN prop yaw, a missing boot setting, over-long lines, a ghost pack at the wrong offset, and event imports one folder too high.\\\",\\n    \\\"Four were critical. The bands, the island boot, the ghost seat, and the event imports each stopped a run.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the four bot bands on ten seeds for every shipped activity.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful was a headless screenshot. The canvas can be blank while the sim state is fine.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Scene actions, live settings, and a headless world you can step made the week testable without a browser.\\\",\\n    \\\"I got stuck on playClip during setup, props that need a yaw, a frozen recorded world, and hub query keys read as settings.\\\",\\n    \\\"The balance step, the day director, the songs, and the syllable voices are the game’s own.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest part was keeping the pavilion small enough for the hub ready deadline while the island stayed a place.\\\",\\n    \\\"None. The engine files were not changed.\\\",\\n\",\"total_lines\":57}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"f5b40f18-eee9-462e-88ca-483c9e01636d"}
