;\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/hub.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":70,\"content\":\"  card.hidden = true;\"},{\"line_number\":257,\"content\":\"      card.hidden = screen !== 'card';\"},{\"line_number\":258,\"content\":\"      if (card.hidden) return;\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/lines/book.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":20,\"content\":\"  'tare.ferry': 'The ferry has gone. You may keep the lawn.',\"},{\"line_number\":85,\"content\":\"  'tilt.dawn': 'Dawn, and the ferry does not return. You may stay for the light.',\"},{\"line_number\":91,\"content\":\"  'plaque.want': 'Did you know. The average person leans two degrees toward the things they want.',\"},{\"line_number\":92,\"content\":\"  'plaque.moved': 'Did you know. This plaque was four centimetres to the left on Tuesday.',\"},{\"line_number\":93,\"content\":\"  'plaque.flamingo': 'Did you know. A flamingo stands on one leg because it has been told it is being watched.',\"},{\"line_number\":94,\"content\":\"  'plaque.gulls': 'Did you know that gulls have no Wobble Age. They have been asked.',\"},{\"line_number\":143,\"content\":\"  'pier.note': 'The pier is empty. The ferry was a rumour with a timetable.',\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/menus.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":216,\"content\":\"        } else void rebind(id);\"},{\"line_number\":222,\"content\":\"  const rebind = async (action: string) => {\"},{\"line_number\":229,\"content\":\"      const result = input.bindings.rebind(action, code);\"},{\"line_number\":236,\"content\":\"    host.about.hidden = false;\"},{\"line_number\":265,\"content\":\"    host.about.hidden = true;\"},{\"line_number\":430,\"content\":\"    host.sliders.hidden = false;\"},{\"line_number\":481,\"content\":\"          host.sliders.hidden = true;\"},{\"line_number\":488,\"content\":\"        host.sliders.hidden = true;\"},{\"line_number\":534,\"content\":\"          host.sliders.hidden = true;\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/stage.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":68,\"content\":\"    '<svg viewBox=\\\"0 0 100 100\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"><circle cx=\\\"50\\\" cy=\\\"50\\\" r=\\\"46\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#FF8A70\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><circle id=\\\"dot\\\" cx=\\\"50\\\" cy=\\\"50\\\" r=\\\"5\\\" fill=\\\"#3A4A55\\\"/></svg>';\"},{\"line_number\":73,\"content\":\"  about.hidden = true;\"},{\"line_number\":76,\"content\":\"  sliders.hidden = true;\"},{\"line_number\":147,\"content\":\"    save = { ...save, outfits: [], settings: { ...prefs, icons } };\"},{\"line_number\":508,\"content\":\"      outfits: [],\"},{\"line_number\":533,\"content\":\"    disc.hidden = (snap.mode === 'title' && !attract) || screen === 'card';\"},{\"line_number\":539,\"content\":\"    copy.hidden = screen === 'about' || screen === 'card';\"},{\"line_number\":547,\"content\":\"    touchBtn.hidden = !touch || (armed && screen !== 'touch');\"},{\"line_number\":548,\"content\":\"    about.hidden = screen !== 'about';\"},{\"line_number\":549,\"content\":\"    if (screen !== 'dev') sliders.hidden = true;\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-78e94308-233a-40c4-a107-d6bec39f2607-41","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Songs, syllables and the line book. Each one has to make a sound, or be a real sentence.\\n */\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { renderSfx, renderSong } from '../../engine';\\nimport { syllableId } from './audio/voice';\\nimport { dawn, lobby, rake, stamp, stillness, tilt, water } from './sounds/songs';\\nimport { LINES } from './ui/lines/book';\\n\\n10→const SONGS = [lobby, stillness, water, rake, tilt, dawn, stamp];\\n\\ndescribe('sound and lines', () => {\\n  it('renders every song with samples', () => {\\n    for (const song of SONGS) {\\n      const samples = renderSong(song.id);\\n      expect(samples.length, song.id).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n      let loud = 0;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < samples.length; i += 32) loud = Math.max(loud, Math.abs(samples[i] ?? 0));\\n      expect(loud, song.id).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n20→    }\\n  });\\n\\n  it('renders a syllable for every speaker', () => {\\n    for (const speaker of ['tare', 'plumb', 'gerald', 'bex', 'nan', 'pa'] as const) {\\n      const samples = renderSfx(syllableId(speaker, 0));\\n      expect(samples.length, speaker).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n      let loud = 0;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < samples.length; i += 8) loud = Math.max(loud, Math.abs(samples[i] ?? 0));\\n      expect(loud, speaker).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n30→    }\\n  });\\n\\n  it('keeps two hundred short lines, and Plumb never shouts', () => {\\n    const entries = Object.entries(LINES);\\n    expect(entries.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(200);\\n    for (const [id, line] of entries) {\\n      const stops = line.match(/[.!?]/g)?.length ?? 0;\\n      expect(stops, id).toBeLessThanOrEqual(2);\\n      expect(line.length, id).toBeGreaterThan(8);\\n40→      if (id.startsWith('plumb')) expect(line.includes('!'), id).toBe(false);\\n    }\\n  });\\n});\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Songs, syllables and the line book. Each one has to make a sound, or be a real sentence.\\n */\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { renderSfx, renderSong } from '../../engine';\\nimport { syllableId } from './audio/voice';\\nimport { dawn, lobby, rake, stamp, stillness, tilt, water } from './sounds/songs';\\nimport { LINES } from './ui/lines/book';\\n\\n10→const SONGS = [lobby, stillness, water, rake, tilt, dawn, stamp];\\n\\ndescribe('sound and lines', () => {\\n  it('renders every song with samples', () => {\\n    for (const song of SONGS) {\\n      const samples = renderSong(song.id);\\n      expect(samples.length, song.id).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n      let loud = 0;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < samples.length; i += 32) loud = Math.max(loud, Math.abs(samples[i] ?? 0));\\n      expect(loud, song.id).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n20→    }\\n  });\\n\\n  it('renders a syllable for every speaker', () => {\\n    for (const speaker of ['tare', 'plumb', 'gerald', 'bex', 'nan', 'pa'] as const) {\\n      const samples = renderSfx(syllableId(speaker, 0));\\n      expect(samples.length, speaker).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n      let loud = 0;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < samples.length; i += 8) loud = Math.max(loud, Math.abs(samples[i] ?? 0));\\n      expect(loud, speaker).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n30→    }\\n  });\\n\\n  it('keeps two hundred short lines, and Plumb never shouts', () => {\\n    const entries = Object.entries(LINES);\\n    expect(entries.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(200);\\n    for (const [id, line] of entries) {\\n      const stops = line.match(/[.!?]/g)?.length ?? 0;\\n      expect(stops, id).toBeLessThanOrEqual(2);\\n      expect(line.length, id).toBeGreaterThan(8);\\n40→      if (id.startsWith('plumb')) expect(line.includes('!'), id).toBe(false);\\n    }\\n  });\\n});\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/audio.test.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file Songs, syllables and the line book. Each one has to make a sound, or be a real sentence.\\n */\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { renderSfx, renderSong } from '../../engine';\\nimport { syllableId } from './audio/voice';\\nimport { dawn, lobby, rake, stamp, stillness, tilt, water } from './sounds/songs';\\nimport { LINES } from './ui/lines/book';\\n\\nconst SONGS = [lobby, stillness, water, rake, tilt, dawn, stamp];\\n\\ndescribe('sound and lines', () => {\\n  it('renders every song with samples', () => {\\n    for (const song of SONGS) {\\n      const samples = renderSong(song.id);\\n      expect(samples.length, song.id).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n      let loud = 0;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < samples.length; i += 32) loud = Math.max(loud, Math.abs(samples[i] ?? 0));\\n      expect(loud, song.id).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  it('renders a syllable for every speaker', () => {\\n    for (const speaker of ['tare', 'plumb', 'gerald', 'bex', 'nan', 'pa'] as const) {\\n      const samples = renderSfx(syllableId(speaker, 0));\\n      expect(samples.length, speaker).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n      let loud = 0;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < samples.length; i += 8) loud = Math.max(loud, Math.abs(samples[i] ?? 0));\\n      expect(loud, speaker).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  it('keeps two hundred short lines, and Plumb never shouts', () => {\\n    const entries = Object.entries(LINES);\\n    expect(entries.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(200);\\n    for (const [id, line] of entries) {\\n      const stops = line.match(/[.!?]/g)?.length ?? 0;\\n      expect(stops, id).toBeLessThanOrEqual(2);\\n      expect(line.length, id).toBeGreaterThan(8);\\n      if (id.startsWith('plumb')) expect(line.includes('!'), id).toBe(false);\\n    }\\n  });\\n});\\n\",\"total_lines\":43}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-78e94308-233a-40c4-a107-d6bec39f2607-42","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The island and the pavilion boot through the shipped scenes and take a few steps.\\n */\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { createAppHost } from '../../engine/app/headless';\\nimport { island } from './scenes/island';\\nimport { round } from './scenes/round';\\n\\ndescribe('places', () => {\\n10→  it('boots the island and walks a step', () => {\\n    const run = createAppHost({ scene: island, seed: 1 });\\n    run.stepOnce({ move: [0, 1] });\\n    run.stepOnce({ move: [0, 1] });\\n    const world = run.session.world;\\n    expect(world.query('flow').length).toBe(1);\\n    expect(world.query('actor').length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    expect(world.query('mark').length).toBeGreaterThan(4);\\n  });\\n\\n20→  it('boots the pavilion and keeps a ghost seat', () => {\\n    const run = createAppHost({ scene: round, seed: 2 });\\n    run.stepOnce({ 'game:ghosts': [1, 1, 0.2, -0.1, 0, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0] });\\n    const world = run.session.world;\\n    const ghosts = world.query('ghost') as unknown as { ghost: { on: number; seat: number } }[];\\n    expect(ghosts.length).toBe(3);\\n    expect(ghosts.some((row) => row.ghost.seat === 1 && row.ghost.on === 1)).toBe(true);\\n  });\\n});\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The island and the pavilion boot through the shipped scenes and take a few steps.\\n */\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { createAppHost } from '../../engine/app/headless';\\nimport { island } from './scenes/island';\\nimport { round } from './scenes/round';\\n\\ndescribe('places', () => {\\n10→  it('boots the island and walks a step', () => {\\n    const run = createAppHost({ scene: island, seed: 1 });\\n    run.stepOnce({ move: [0, 1] });\\n    run.stepOnce({ move: [0, 1] });\\n    const world = run.session.world;\\n    expect(world.query('flow').length).toBe(1);\\n    expect(world.query('actor').length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    expect(world.query('mark').length).toBeGreaterThan(4);\\n  });\\n\\n20→  it('boots the pavilion and keeps a ghost seat', () => {\\n    const run = createAppHost({ scene: round, seed: 2 });\\n    run.stepOnce({ 'game:ghosts': [1, 1, 0.2, -0.1, 0, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0] });\\n    const world = run.session.world;\\n    const ghosts = world.query('ghost') as unknown as { ghost: { on: number; seat: number } }[];\\n    expect(ghosts.length).toBe(3);\\n    expect(ghosts.some((row) => row.ghost.seat === 1 && row.ghost.on === 1)).toBe(true);\\n  });\\n});\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/island.test.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The island and the pavilion boot through the shipped scenes and take a few steps.\\n */\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { createAppHost } from '../../engine/app/headless';\\nimport { island } from './scenes/island';\\nimport { round } from './scenes/round';\\n\\ndescribe('places', () => {\\n  it('boots the island and walks a step', () => {\\n    const run = createAppHost({ scene: island, seed: 1 });\\n    run.stepOnce({ move: [0, 1] });\\n    run.stepOnce({ move: [0, 1] });\\n    const world = run.session.world;\\n    expect(world.query('flow').length).toBe(1);\\n    expect(world.query('actor').length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    expect(world.query('mark').length).toBeGreaterThan(4);\\n  });\\n\\n  it('boots the pavilion and keeps a ghost seat', () => {\\n    const run = createAppHost({ scene: round, seed: 2 });\\n    run.stepOnce({ 'game:ghosts': [1, 1, 0.2, -0.1, 0, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0] });\\n    const world = run.session.world;\\n    const ghosts = world.query('ghost') as unknown as { ghost: { on: number; seat: number } }[];\\n    expect(ghosts.length).toBe(3);\\n    expect(ghosts.some((row) => row.ghost.seat === 1 && row.ghost.on === 1)).toBe(true);\\n  });\\n});\\n\",\"total_lines\":28}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-78e94308-233a-40c4-a107-d6bec39f2607-43","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The Great Tilt. A storm, a walk to the east terrace, the centre stone, then dawn.\\n * The island's geometry stays put. Your centre of balance is what leans it, once you are on the stone.\\n * There is no fail state. The clock moves every part on.\\n */\\nimport type { Intents, World } from '../../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { type Band, seek, stickIntents, wantBreath } from '../bot';\\nimport { clampScore } from '../score';\\nimport { resetAct, visit } from '../state';\\n10→import { resetBalance } from '../wobble';\\nimport { actOf, apply, cfgOf, flowOf, rowOf, sweep } from './kit';\\n\\nconst NAMES = ['Nan', 'Gerald', 'Bex', 'A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'E', 'F', 'G', 'H', 'I'];\\n\\n/** Guests, the storm, and a still balance. Attract begins on the stone. */\\nexport function setup(w: World): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  resetAct(act);\\n  const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n20→  resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n  const attract = String(w.settings.get('game.auto')) === 'attract';\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 12; i++) {\\n    const nan = i === 0;\\n    const col = (i - 1) % 4;\\n    const row = Math.floor((i - 1) / 4);\\n    w.spawn({\\n      made: { tag: 'guest' },\\n      mark: {\\n        x: nan ? 64 : 1 + col * 2.2,\\n30→        y: 0,\\n        z: nan ? 8 : (row - 1) * 2.2,\\n        kind: 'guest',\\n        text: NAMES[i] ?? 'guest',\\n        taken: nan ? 1 : 0,\\n        follow: nan ? 1 : 0,\\n      },\\n    });\\n  }\\n  flowOf(w).line = 'tilt.storm';\\n40→  visit(flowOf(w), 'tilt:storm');\\n  if (attract) {\\n    act.phase = 2;\\n    act.a = 1;\\n    act.b = 1;\\n    visit(flowOf(w), 'tilt:east');\\n    visit(flowOf(w), 'tilt:stone');\\n    flowOf(w).line = 'tilt.stone';\\n  }\\n}\\n50→\\nfunction delivered(w: World): number {\\n  let n = 0;\\n  for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as { mark: { kind: string; taken: number } }[]) {\\n    if (row.mark.kind === 'guest' && row.mark.taken > 0.5) n += 1;\\n  }\\n  return n;\\n}\\n\\n/** The four parts. Each one ends itself. */\\n60→export function step(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  if (act.done) return;\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const phase = act.phase;\\n  const inst = phase === 2 ? 1 : 1;\\n  const wave = phase === 2 ? Math.sin(w.time * 1.4) * 0.55 : 0;\\n  const { body, seat } = apply(w, intents, { dx: wave, inst, noise: phase === 2 ? 1 : 0.4 });\\n  act.tick += 1;\\n  act.left += 1;\\n70→  if (phase === 0) {\\n    const island = w.query('island') as unknown as { island: { tiltX: number } }[];\\n    const tilt = island[0]?.island;\\n    if (tilt) tilt.tiltX = 0.4 + (act.left / 60) * 0.28;\\n    if (act.left >= 20 * 60) {\\n      act.a = 1;\\n      act.phase = 1;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n      flow.line = 'tilt.east';\\n      visit(flow, 'tilt:east');\\n80→    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (phase === 1) {\\n    act.px += Math.max(0, body.y) * 6 * w.dt;\\n    if (seat.both) act.hold += 1;\\n    else {\\n      if (act.hold >= 50) pulse(w);\\n      act.hold = 0;\\n    }\\n90→    for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as {\\n      mark: { kind: string; x: number; z: number; follow: number; taken: number };\\n    }[]) {\\n      const mark = row.mark;\\n      if (mark.kind !== 'guest') continue;\\n      if (mark.follow > 0.5) mark.x += (act.px - mark.x) * Math.min(1, 4 * w.dt);\\n      else mark.x -= 0.3 * w.dt;\\n      if (mark.x > 58) mark.taken = 1;\\n    }\\n    if (act.left >= 75 * 60) {\\n100→      act.b = delivered(w) / 12;\\n      act.phase = 2;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n      act.samples = 0;\\n      act.acc = 0;\\n      act.acc2 = 0;\\n      resetBalance(rowOf(w, 0).wobble, rowOf(w, 0).hist);\\n      flow.line = 'tilt.stone';\\n      visit(flow, 'tilt:stone');\\n    }\\n110→    return;\\n  }\\n  if (phase === 2) {\\n    const ring = 0.3 - 0.14 * Math.min(1, act.left / (60 * 60));\\n    act.samples += 1;\\n    if (Math.hypot(body.x, body.y) <= ring) act.acc += 1;\\n    act.acc2 += body.sync;\\n    const island = w.query('island') as unknown as { island: { tiltX: number; tiltZ: number } }[];\\n    const tilt = island[0]?.island;\\n    if (tilt) {\\n120→      tilt.tiltX = body.x * 6;\\n      tilt.tiltZ = body.y * 6;\\n    }\\n    if (act.left >= 60 * 60) {\\n      act.c = act.samples ? act.acc / act.samples : 0;\\n      act.hz = act.samples ? act.acc2 / act.samples : 0;\\n      act.phase = 3;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n      if (tilt) {\\n        tilt.tiltX = 0;\\n130→        tilt.tiltZ = 0;\\n      }\\n      flow.line = 'tilt.dawn';\\n      visit(flow, 'tilt:dawn');\\n    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (act.left >= 15 * 60) act.done = 1;\\n}\\n\\n140→/** A calm wave. Guests close enough come with you. Nan is already there. */\\nfunction pulse(w: World): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as { mark: { kind: string; x: number; z: number; follow: number } }[]) {\\n    const mark = row.mark;\\n    if (mark.kind !== 'guest') continue;\\n    if (Math.hypot(mark.x - act.px, mark.z) < 8) mark.follow = 1;\\n  }\\n  act.falls += 1;\\n}\\n150→\\n/** Storm, guests, the stone, and the breath on it. */\\nexport function score(w: World): number {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  return clampScore(1000 * (0.15 * act.a + 0.35 * act.b + 0.4 * act.c + 0.1 * act.hz));\\n}\\n\\n/** Breathes in the storm, walks east, then holds the stone. */\\nexport function bot(w: World, band: Band): Intents {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n160→  const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n  const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n  const breathe = wantBreath(band, w.time, cfg.period);\\n  if (band === 'idle') return stickIntents({ x: 0, y: 0 }, {});\\n  if (act.phase === 1) {\\n    const stick = seek(band, 0, 0.55, row.wobble, row.hist, cfg, w.tick);\\n    const call = act.left % 240 < 100;\\n    return stickIntents(stick, { both: call });\\n  }\\n  const stick = seek(band, 0, 0, row.wobble, row.hist, cfg, w.tick);\\n170→  return stickIntents(stick, { both: breathe });\\n}\\n\\n/** The crowd markers leave. The island stays. */\\nexport function teardown(w: World): void {\\n  sweep(w);\\n}\\n\\n/** The activity record. */\\nexport const tilt = {\\n180→  id: 'tilt',\\n  title: 'The Great Tilt',\\n  seconds: 170,\\n  setup,\\n  step,\\n  teardown,\\n  score,\\n  bot,\\n};\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The Great Tilt. A storm, a walk to the east terrace, the centre stone, then dawn.\\n * The island's geometry stays put. Your centre of balance is what leans it, once you are on the stone.\\n * There is no fail state. The clock moves every part on.\\n */\\nimport type { Intents, World } from '../../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { type Band, seek, stickIntents, wantBreath } from '../bot';\\nimport { clampScore } from '../score';\\nimport { resetAct, visit } from '../state';\\n10→import { resetBalance } from '../wobble';\\nimport { actOf, apply, cfgOf, flowOf, rowOf, sweep } from './kit';\\n\\nconst NAMES = ['Nan', 'Gerald', 'Bex', 'A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'E', 'F', 'G', 'H', 'I'];\\n\\n/** Guests, the storm, and a still balance. Attract begins on the stone. */\\nexport function setup(w: World): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  resetAct(act);\\n  const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n20→  resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n  const attract = String(w.settings.get('game.auto')) === 'attract';\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 12; i++) {\\n    const nan = i === 0;\\n    const col = (i - 1) % 4;\\n    const row = Math.floor((i - 1) / 4);\\n    w.spawn({\\n      made: { tag: 'guest' },\\n      mark: {\\n        x: nan ? 64 : 1 + col * 2.2,\\n30→        y: 0,\\n        z: nan ? 8 : (row - 1) * 2.2,\\n        kind: 'guest',\\n        text: NAMES[i] ?? 'guest',\\n        taken: nan ? 1 : 0,\\n        follow: nan ? 1 : 0,\\n      },\\n    });\\n  }\\n  flowOf(w).line = 'tilt.storm';\\n40→  visit(flowOf(w), 'tilt:storm');\\n  if (attract) {\\n    act.phase = 2;\\n    act.a = 1;\\n    act.b = 1;\\n    visit(flowOf(w), 'tilt:east');\\n    visit(flowOf(w), 'tilt:stone');\\n    flowOf(w).line = 'tilt.stone';\\n  }\\n}\\n50→\\nfunction delivered(w: World): number {\\n  let n = 0;\\n  for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as { mark: { kind: string; taken: number } }[]) {\\n    if (row.mark.kind === 'guest' && row.mark.taken > 0.5) n += 1;\\n  }\\n  return n;\\n}\\n\\n/** The four parts. Each one ends itself. */\\n60→export function step(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  if (act.done) return;\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const phase = act.phase;\\n  const inst = phase === 2 ? 1 : 1;\\n  const wave = phase === 2 ? Math.sin(w.time * 1.4) * 0.55 : 0;\\n  const { body, seat } = apply(w, intents, { dx: wave, inst, noise: phase === 2 ? 1 : 0.4 });\\n  act.tick += 1;\\n  act.left += 1;\\n70→  if (phase === 0) {\\n    const island = w.query('island') as unknown as { island: { tiltX: number } }[];\\n    const tilt = island[0]?.island;\\n    if (tilt) tilt.tiltX = 0.4 + (act.left / 60) * 0.28;\\n    if (act.left >= 20 * 60) {\\n      act.a = 1;\\n      act.phase = 1;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n      flow.line = 'tilt.east';\\n      visit(flow, 'tilt:east');\\n80→    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (phase === 1) {\\n    act.px += Math.max(0, body.y) * 6 * w.dt;\\n    if (seat.both) act.hold += 1;\\n    else {\\n      if (act.hold >= 50) pulse(w);\\n      act.hold = 0;\\n    }\\n90→    for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as {\\n      mark: { kind: string; x: number; z: number; follow: number; taken: number };\\n    }[]) {\\n      const mark = row.mark;\\n      if (mark.kind !== 'guest') continue;\\n      if (mark.follow > 0.5) mark.x += (act.px - mark.x) * Math.min(1, 4 * w.dt);\\n      else mark.x -= 0.3 * w.dt;\\n      if (mark.x > 58) mark.taken = 1;\\n    }\\n    if (act.left >= 75 * 60) {\\n100→      act.b = delivered(w) / 12;\\n      act.phase = 2;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n      act.samples = 0;\\n      act.acc = 0;\\n      act.acc2 = 0;\\n      resetBalance(rowOf(w, 0).wobble, rowOf(w, 0).hist);\\n      flow.line = 'tilt.stone';\\n      visit(flow, 'tilt:stone');\\n    }\\n110→    return;\\n  }\\n  if (phase === 2) {\\n    const ring = 0.3 - 0.14 * Math.min(1, act.left / (60 * 60));\\n    act.samples += 1;\\n    if (Math.hypot(body.x, body.y) <= ring) act.acc += 1;\\n    act.acc2 += body.sync;\\n    const island = w.query('island') as unknown as { island: { tiltX: number; tiltZ: number } }[];\\n    const tilt = island[0]?.island;\\n    if (tilt) {\\n120→      tilt.tiltX = body.x * 6;\\n      tilt.tiltZ = body.y * 6;\\n    }\\n    if (act.left >= 60 * 60) {\\n      act.c = act.samples ? act.acc / act.samples : 0;\\n      act.hz = act.samples ? act.acc2 / act.samples : 0;\\n      act.phase = 3;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n      if (tilt) {\\n        tilt.tiltX = 0;\\n130→        tilt.tiltZ = 0;\\n      }\\n      flow.line = 'tilt.dawn';\\n      visit(flow, 'tilt:dawn');\\n    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (act.left >= 15 * 60) act.done = 1;\\n}\\n\\n140→/** A calm wave. Guests close enough come with you. Nan is already there. */\\nfunction pulse(w: World): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as { mark: { kind: string; x: number; z: number; follow: number } }[]) {\\n    const mark = row.mark;\\n    if (mark.kind !== 'guest') continue;\\n    if (Math.hypot(mark.x - act.px, mark.z) < 8) mark.follow = 1;\\n  }\\n  act.falls += 1;\\n}\\n150→\\n/** Storm, guests, the stone, and the breath on it. */\\nexport function score(w: World): number {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  return clampScore(1000 * (0.15 * act.a + 0.35 * act.b + 0.4 * act.c + 0.1 * act.hz));\\n}\\n\\n/** Breathes in the storm, walks east, then holds the stone. */\\nexport function bot(w: World, band: Band): Intents {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n160→  const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n  const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n  const breathe = wantBreath(band, w.time, cfg.period);\\n  if (band === 'idle') return stickIntents({ x: 0, y: 0 }, {});\\n  if (act.phase === 1) {\\n    const stick = seek(band, 0, 0.55, row.wobble, row.hist, cfg, w.tick);\\n    const call = act.left % 240 < 100;\\n    return stickIntents(stick, { both: call });\\n  }\\n  const stick = seek(band, 0, 0, row.wobble, row.hist, cfg, w.tick);\\n170→  return stickIntents(stick, { both: breathe });\\n}\\n\\n/** The crowd markers leave. The island stays. */\\nexport function teardown(w: World): void {\\n  sweep(w);\\n}\\n\\n/** The activity record. */\\nexport const tilt = {\\n180→  id: 'tilt',\\n  title: 'The Great Tilt',\\n  seconds: 170,\\n  setup,\\n  step,\\n  teardown,\\n  score,\\n  bot,\\n};\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/events/tilt.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":220,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The Great Tilt. A storm, a walk to the east terrace, the centre stone, then dawn.\\n * The island's geometry stays put. Your centre of balance is what leans it, once you are on the stone.\\n * There is no fail state. The clock moves every part on.\\n */\\nimport type { Intents, World } from '../../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { type Band, seek, stickIntents, wantBreath } from '../bot';\\nimport { clampScore } from '../score';\\nimport { resetAct, visit } from '../state';\\nimport { resetBalance } from '../wobble';\\nimport { actOf, apply, cfgOf, flowOf, rowOf, sweep } from './kit';\\n\\nconst NAMES = ['Nan', 'Gerald', 'Bex', 'A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'E', 'F', 'G', 'H', 'I'];\\n\\n/** Guests, the storm, and a still balance. Attract begins on the stone. */\\nexport function setup(w: World): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  resetAct(act);\\n  const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n  resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n  const attract = String(w.settings.get('game.auto')) === 'attract';\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 12; i++) {\\n    const nan = i === 0;\\n    const col = (i - 1) % 4;\\n    const row = Math.floor((i - 1) / 4);\\n    w.spawn({\\n      made: { tag: 'guest' },\\n      mark: {\\n        x: nan ? 64 : 1 + col * 2.2,\\n        y: 0,\\n        z: nan ? 8 : (row - 1) * 2.2,\\n        kind: 'guest',\\n        text: NAMES[i] ?? 'guest',\\n        taken: nan ? 1 : 0,\\n        follow: nan ? 1 : 0,\\n      },\\n    });\\n  }\\n  flowOf(w).line = 'tilt.storm';\\n  visit(flowOf(w), 'tilt:storm');\\n  if (attract) {\\n    act.phase = 2;\\n    act.a = 1;\\n    act.b = 1;\\n    visit(flowOf(w), 'tilt:east');\\n    visit(flowOf(w), 'tilt:stone');\\n    flowOf(w).line = 'tilt.stone';\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction delivered(w: World): number {\\n  let n = 0;\\n  for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as { mark: { kind: string; taken: number } }[]) {\\n    if (row.mark.kind === 'guest' && row.mark.taken > 0.5) n += 1;\\n  }\\n  return n;\\n}\\n\\n/** The four parts. Each one ends itself. */\\nexport function step(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  if (act.done) return;\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const phase = act.phase;\\n  const inst = phase === 2 ? 1 : 1;\\n  const wave = phase === 2 ? Math.sin(w.time * 1.4) * 0.55 : 0;\\n  const { body, seat } = apply(w, intents, { dx: wave, inst, noise: phase === 2 ? 1 : 0.4 });\\n  act.tick += 1;\\n  act.left += 1;\\n  if (phase === 0) {\\n    const island = w.query('island') as unknown as { island: { tiltX: number } }[];\\n    const tilt = island[0]?.island;\\n    if (tilt) tilt.tiltX = 0.4 + (act.left / 60) * 0.28;\\n    if (act.left >= 20 * 60) {\\n      act.a = 1;\\n      act.phase = 1;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n      flow.line = 'tilt.east';\\n      visit(flow, 'tilt:east');\\n    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (phase === 1) {\\n    act.px += Math.max(0, body.y) * 6 * w.dt;\\n    if (seat.both) act.hold += 1;\\n    else {\\n      if (act.hold >= 50) pulse(w);\\n      act.hold = 0;\\n    }\\n    for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as {\\n      mark: { kind: string; x: number; z: number; follow: number; taken: number };\\n    }[]) {\\n      const mark = row.mark;\\n      if (mark.kind !== 'guest') continue;\\n      if (mark.follow > 0.5) mark.x += (act.px - mark.x) * Math.min(1, 4 * w.dt);\\n      else mark.x -= 0.3 * w.dt;\\n      if (mark.x > 58) mark.taken = 1;\\n    }\\n    if (act.left >= 75 * 60) {\\n      act.b = delivered(w) / 12;\\n      act.phase = 2;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n      act.samples = 0;\\n      act.acc = 0;\\n      act.acc2 = 0;\\n      resetBalance(rowOf(w, 0).wobble, rowOf(w, 0).hist);\\n      flow.line = 'tilt.stone';\\n      visit(flow, 'tilt:stone');\\n    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (phase === 2) {\\n    const ring = 0.3 - 0.14 * Math.min(1, act.left / (60 * 60));\\n    act.samples += 1;\\n    if (Math.hypot(body.x, body.y) <= ring) act.acc += 1;\\n    act.acc2 += body.sync;\\n    const island = w.query('island') as unknown as { island: { tiltX: number; tiltZ: number } }[];\\n    const tilt = island[0]?.island;\\n    if (tilt) {\\n      tilt.tiltX = body.x * 6;\\n      tilt.tiltZ = body.y * 6;\\n    }\\n    if (act.left >= 60 * 60) {\\n      act.c = act.samples ? act.acc / act.samples : 0;\\n      act.hz = act.samples ? act.acc2 / act.samples : 0;\\n      act.phase = 3;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n      if (tilt) {\\n        tilt.tiltX = 0;\\n        tilt.tiltZ = 0;\\n      }\\n      flow.line = 'tilt.dawn';\\n      visit(flow, 'tilt:dawn');\\n    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (act.left >= 15 * 60) act.done = 1;\\n}\\n\\n/** A calm wave. Guests close enough come with you. Nan is already there. */\\nfunction pulse(w: World): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as { mark: { kind: string; x: number; z: number; follow: number } }[]) {\\n    const mark = row.mark;\\n    if (mark.kind !== 'guest') continue;\\n    if (Math.hypot(mark.x - act.px, mark.z) < 8) mark.follow = 1;\\n  }\\n  act.falls += 1;\\n}\\n\\n/** Storm, guests, the stone, and the breath on it. */\\nexport function score(w: World): number {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  return clampScore(1000 * (0.15 * act.a + 0.35 * act.b + 0.4 * act.c + 0.1 * act.hz));\\n}\\n\\n/** Breathes in the storm, walks east, then holds the stone. */\\nexport function bot(w: World, band: Band): Intents {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n  const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n  const breathe = wantBreath(band, w.time, cfg.period);\\n  if (band === 'idle') return stickIntents({ x: 0, y: 0 }, {});\\n  if (act.phase === 1) {\\n    const stick = seek(band, 0, 0.55, row.wobble, row.hist, cfg, w.tick);\\n    const call = act.left % 240 < 100;\\n    return stickIntents(stick, { both: call });\\n  }\\n  const stick = seek(band, 0, 0, row.wobble, row.hist, cfg, w.tick);\\n  return stickIntents(stick, { both: breathe });\\n}\\n\\n/** The crowd markers leave. The island stays. */\\nexport function teardown(w: World): void {\\n  sweep(w);\\n}\\n\\n/** The activity record. */\\nexport const tilt = {\\n  id: 'tilt',\\n  title: 'The Great Tilt',\\n  seconds: 170,\\n  setup,\\n  step,\\n  teardown,\\n  score,\\n  bot,\\n};\\n\",\"total_lines\":188}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"feaafe3c-3a88-41d7-8a4e-cb3ef55c38e6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_994","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to look for real bugs more carefully.\n\nGuests in the \"everyone east\" phase drift west because non-followers move left while the player moves right. The bot should seek y=0.55 to walk east and deliver them, but idle mode does not.\n\nThe westward drift for non-following guests might be intentional. The score component is delivered/12. The plan specifies 20 hidden pebbles and 12 plaques, but the goal criterion only requires existence.\n\nThe plan requires plaques to creep downhill. I will check island.ts for pebble counts and plaque movement. Day 2 after cuts includes Reps Hall, Sand Garden, and Pose Class B.\n\nDay 4 contains only morning and pose-c because all other activities were cut. The walk to the noticeboard on day one is not a programme event, but the island roam must remain intact.\n\nThe pose list needs eight poses. A reset gain bug exists in the read menus reset and settings. I need to check cast/clips.ts for scrub clips, plus group class and session query strip functionality. The line length rule allows two punctuation marks, so a single sentence could still be very long despite the plan's \"two short sentences\" limit. All seed lines from the plan must be included. The hub client also requires modification.\n\nWobble model correctness against the specification needs verification. Morning check structure, sand garden, line, and paddle mechanics require review. The hub pause button does not stop the simulation. Numeric game settings need dev sliders. Music volume is confirmed at 0.1. Voice babbling must be deterministic so identical lines repeat identically. Group score logic needs checking. The built HTML file must include the pump interval.\n\nI will also verify the driver director step actually plays events rather than skipping them. The test `play()` double-teardown is harmless if teardown is idempotent, since the second call matches the boot count. I am now examining the `play()` function for a potential bug.\n\nThe director runs stepOnce with game.auto. The simulation must apply the bot internally. I need to inspect the driver step function. Activity scores might be gamed so bots always produce high scores regardless of input quality.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5b9fa960-8399-40f3-afa0-dd0a5ce13cbe-44","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/PLAN.md","offset":108,"limit":70}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5b9fa960-8399-40f3-afa0-dd0a5ce13cbe-45","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/wobble.ts","limit":220}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5b9fa960-8399-40f3-afa0-dd0a5ce13cbe-46","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/bot.ts","limit":180}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5b9fa960-8399-40f3-afa0-dd0a5ce13cbe-47","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/island.ts","offset":90,"limit":180}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6167,"output_tokens":1463,"cache_read_input_tokens":92160,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"a1b4322c-7fc6-4404-a5ae-eaa83c2af285"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5b9fa960-8399-40f3-afa0-dd0a5ce13cbe-44","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"108→## 3. The one verb: the Wobble Model\\n\\n110→This is the game's core. Build it first, tune it in dev mode, and reuse it everywhere. It lives in the sim as a\\ncomponent `wobble` on each balancing body, one per seat.\\n\\n**The centre of balance (CoB)** is a point in a unit disc: `x` left to right, `y` back to forward. `r = 1` is the edge:\\npast it you topple.\\n\\nEach step (1/60 s), for each axis:\\n\\n```\\ntarget  = slew(stick + mouse, 4 units/s) × (gentle ? 0.4 : 1) × reach      // clamped to the disc\\n120→accel   = gain × (target − cob) + instability × cob + noise(t) × (1 − calmEffect × calm) + disturbance\\nvel    += accel × dt;   vel *= exp(−damping × dt);   cob += vel × dt\\n```\\n\\n| Setting | Default | Range | What it does |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `game.wobble.gain` | 14 /s² | 4–30 | How fast your weight follows your thumb |\\n| `game.wobble.instability` | 3 /s² | 0–10 | How hard you fall away from the centre |\\n| `game.wobble.damping` | 5 /s | 1–12 | How heavy the body feels |\\n| `game.wobble.noise` | 3.5 /s² | 0–8 | Sway strength |\\n130→| `game.wobble.noiseRate` | 0.15 Hz | 0.05–0.4 | Sway speed: a slow push you lean against |\\n| `game.wobble.reach` | 0.9 | 0.5–1 | Full stick's target; a held full stick topples, on purpose |\\n| `game.breath.period` | 8 s | 4–14 | One breath, half in, half out |\\n| `game.breath.calmEffect` | 0.5 | 0–1 | How much full calm quiets the sway |\\n\\nSway per axis, phases and small rate ratios `m` drawn once per seat from a named stream (`w.rng('sway')`), never\\n`Math.random`, and written with plain `Math.sin` so the sim's math swap reaches it:\\n\\n```\\nnoise(t) = ( sin(2π·rate·m1·t + p1) + 0.6·sin(2π·rate·1.7·m2·t + p2) + 0.3·sin(2π·rate·3.1·m3·t + p3) ) / 1.3      // mi in 0.8–1.25\\n140→```\\n\\n**These numbers are modelled, and the slow sway matters [tested in a small simulation of this exact model, 20 s, 10 seeds,\\nstaying in a ring of 0.22]:** no input 38%; a human-like thumb (250 ms reaction, proportional gain 1.2, a little jitter) 90%;\\na sloppy thumb (350 ms, gain 0.8) 72%; a no-delay bot 100%. A ring of 0.16 drops the thumb to 65%. Off-centre seats out to\\n0.35 hold at 87%, and 0.6 starts to topple (so keep seats within 0.5). **At the 0.45 Hz sway first tried, doing nothing beat\\nthe human thumb,** because a 250 ms reaction turns correction into amplification, so keep the sway slow. Nobody can play by\\nhand here: the delayed-thumb bot (section 16) is how you judge feel.\\n\\nThe universal 4 units/s slew is what makes keyboard feel analog: a quick tap is a small nudge, a held key is a full lean.\\n150→Sticks barely notice it. Mouse adds its own target with a slow decay (section 4).\\n\\n**Topple.** `r > 1` for 6 steps: the body stumbles (`reactTo` flinch, a stumble clip, a creak), the activity decides the\\nprice, and the CoB returns to centre over a second. It is never a game over.\\n\\n**Breath.** The third input is both feet held. A guide ring swells and shrinks with `breath.period`. Holding both feet\\nfills `lungs`; letting go empties them. `sync` is a running match between your lungs and the guide. Good sync raises\\n`calm` (0–1), which quiets the sway, warms the picture slightly, softens the sound, and pays a bonus. Breath is used in\\nstill activities and is the charge mechanic in fast ones. Being out of sync has no penalty beyond losing the help.\\n\\n160→**Feet.** Left and right foot are the two triggers (analog) or shoulders. Used for steps, rhythm, paddling, jogging and\\none-leg holds. Both together is breath, or a jump in Step Class. That is every input the activities need: **Lean, Left\\nFoot, Right Foot, Both Feet.**\\n\\n**Scoring.** Every activity yields 0–1000 and a rank: 0 **Present**, 300 **Adequate**, 550 **Composed**, 750 **Serene**,\\n900 **Unsettling**. Pebbles earned: 1 to 5 by rank.\\n\\n**No softlocks.** Every activity and every finale step ends by itself: each step has a time box, after which it moves on with\\na remark (\\\"We will call that a start.\\\"). A player who puts the pad down reaches the results screen.\\n\\n170→**Balance targets the tests enforce** (section 16) on 10 seeds at default settings, in every activity: the perfect bot\\nscores ≥ 750, the human-like delayed thumb ≥ 550, the sloppy thumb ≥ 300, no input at all ≤ 500 and below the human-like\\nthumb. Random mashing never crashes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Controls\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"108→## 3. The one verb: the Wobble Model\\n\\n110→This is the game's core. Build it first, tune it in dev mode, and reuse it everywhere. It lives in the sim as a\\ncomponent `wobble` on each balancing body, one per seat.\\n\\n**The centre of balance (CoB)** is a point in a unit disc: `x` left to right, `y` back to forward. `r = 1` is the edge:\\npast it you topple.\\n\\nEach step (1/60 s), for each axis:\\n\\n```\\ntarget  = slew(stick + mouse, 4 units/s) × (gentle ? 0.4 : 1) × reach      // clamped to the disc\\n120→accel   = gain × (target − cob) + instability × cob + noise(t) × (1 − calmEffect × calm) + disturbance\\nvel    += accel × dt;   vel *= exp(−damping × dt);   cob += vel × dt\\n```\\n\\n| Setting | Default | Range | What it does |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `game.wobble.gain` | 14 /s² | 4–30 | How fast your weight follows your thumb |\\n| `game.wobble.instability` | 3 /s² | 0–10 | How hard you fall away from the centre |\\n| `game.wobble.damping` | 5 /s | 1–12 | How heavy the body feels |\\n| `game.wobble.noise` | 3.5 /s² | 0–8 | Sway strength |\\n130→| `game.wobble.noiseRate` | 0.15 Hz | 0.05–0.4 | Sway speed: a slow push you lean against |\\n| `game.wobble.reach` | 0.9 | 0.5–1 | Full stick's target; a held full stick topples, on purpose |\\n| `game.breath.period` | 8 s | 4–14 | One breath, half in, half out |\\n| `game.breath.calmEffect` | 0.5 | 0–1 | How much full calm quiets the sway |\\n\\nSway per axis, phases and small rate ratios `m` drawn once per seat from a named stream (`w.rng('sway')`), never\\n`Math.random`, and written with plain `Math.sin` so the sim's math swap reaches it:\\n\\n```\\nnoise(t) = ( sin(2π·rate·m1·t + p1) + 0.6·sin(2π·rate·1.7·m2·t + p2) + 0.3·sin(2π·rate·3.1·m3·t + p3) ) / 1.3      // mi in 0.8–1.25\\n140→```\\n\\n**These numbers are modelled, and the slow sway matters [tested in a small simulation of this exact model, 20 s, 10 seeds,\\nstaying in a ring of 0.22]:** no input 38%; a human-like thumb (250 ms reaction, proportional gain 1.2, a little jitter) 90%;\\na sloppy thumb (350 ms, gain 0.8) 72%; a no-delay bot 100%. A ring of 0.16 drops the thumb to 65%. Off-centre seats out to\\n0.35 hold at 87%, and 0.6 starts to topple (so keep seats within 0.5). **At the 0.45 Hz sway first tried, doing nothing beat\\nthe human thumb,** because a 250 ms reaction turns correction into amplification, so keep the sway slow. Nobody can play by\\nhand here: the delayed-thumb bot (section 16) is how you judge feel.\\n\\nThe universal 4 units/s slew is what makes keyboard feel analog: a quick tap is a small nudge, a held key is a full lean.\\n150→Sticks barely notice it. Mouse adds its own target with a slow decay (section 4).\\n\\n**Topple.** `r > 1` for 6 steps: the body stumbles (`reactTo` flinch, a stumble clip, a creak), the activity decides the\\nprice, and the CoB returns to centre over a second. It is never a game over.\\n\\n**Breath.** The third input is both feet held. A guide ring swells and shrinks with `breath.period`. Holding both feet\\nfills `lungs`; letting go empties them. `sync` is a running match between your lungs and the guide. Good sync raises\\n`calm` (0–1), which quiets the sway, warms the picture slightly, softens the sound, and pays a bonus. Breath is used in\\nstill activities and is the charge mechanic in fast ones. Being out of sync has no penalty beyond losing the help.\\n\\n160→**Feet.** Left and right foot are the two triggers (analog) or shoulders. Used for steps, rhythm, paddling, jogging and\\none-leg holds. Both together is breath, or a jump in Step Class. That is every input the activities need: **Lean, Left\\nFoot, Right Foot, Both Feet.**\\n\\n**Scoring.** Every activity yields 0–1000 and a rank: 0 **Present**, 300 **Adequate**, 550 **Composed**, 750 **Serene**,\\n900 **Unsettling**. Pebbles earned: 1 to 5 by rank.\\n\\n**No softlocks.** Every activity and every finale step ends by itself: each step has a time box, after which it moves on with\\na remark (\\\"We will call that a start.\\\"). A player who puts the pad down reaches the results screen.\\n\\n170→**Balance targets the tests enforce** (section 16) on 10 seeds at default settings, in every activity: the perfect bot\\nscores ≥ 750, the human-like delayed thumb ≥ 550, the sloppy thumb ≥ 300, no input at all ≤ 500 and below the human-like\\nthumb. Random mashing never crashes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Controls\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":108,\"limit\":70,\"raw_output\":\"## 3. The one verb: the Wobble Model\\n\\nThis is the game's core. Build it first, tune it in dev mode, and reuse it everywhere. It lives in the sim as a\\ncomponent `wobble` on each balancing body, one per seat.\\n\\n**The centre of balance (CoB)** is a point in a unit disc: `x` left to right, `y` back to forward. `r = 1` is the edge:\\npast it you topple.\\n\\nEach step (1/60 s), for each axis:\\n\\n```\\ntarget  = slew(stick + mouse, 4 units/s) × (gentle ? 0.4 : 1) × reach      // clamped to the disc\\naccel   = gain × (target − cob) + instability × cob + noise(t) × (1 − calmEffect × calm) + disturbance\\nvel    += accel × dt;   vel *= exp(−damping × dt);   cob += vel × dt\\n```\\n\\n| Setting | Default | Range | What it does |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `game.wobble.gain` | 14 /s² | 4–30 | How fast your weight follows your thumb |\\n| `game.wobble.instability` | 3 /s² | 0–10 | How hard you fall away from the centre |\\n| `game.wobble.damping` | 5 /s | 1–12 | How heavy the body feels |\\n| `game.wobble.noise` | 3.5 /s² | 0–8 | Sway strength |\\n| `game.wobble.noiseRate` | 0.15 Hz | 0.05–0.4 | Sway speed: a slow push you lean against |\\n| `game.wobble.reach` | 0.9 | 0.5–1 | Full stick's target; a held full stick topples, on purpose |\\n| `game.breath.period` | 8 s | 4–14 | One breath, half in, half out |\\n| `game.breath.calmEffect` | 0.5 | 0–1 | How much full calm quiets the sway |\\n\\nSway per axis, phases and small rate ratios `m` drawn once per seat from a named stream (`w.rng('sway')`), never\\n`Math.random`, and written with plain `Math.sin` so the sim's math swap reaches it:\\n\\n```\\nnoise(t) = ( sin(2π·rate·m1·t + p1) + 0.6·sin(2π·rate·1.7·m2·t + p2) + 0.3·sin(2π·rate·3.1·m3·t + p3) ) / 1.3      // mi in 0.8–1.25\\n```\\n\\n**These numbers are modelled, and the slow sway matters [tested in a small simulation of this exact model, 20 s, 10 seeds,\\nstaying in a ring of 0.22]:** no input 38%; a human-like thumb (250 ms reaction, proportional gain 1.2, a little jitter) 90%;\\na sloppy thumb (350 ms, gain 0.8) 72%; a no-delay bot 100%. A ring of 0.16 drops the thumb to 65%. Off-centre seats out to\\n0.35 hold at 87%, and 0.6 starts to topple (so keep seats within 0.5). **At the 0.45 Hz sway first tried, doing nothing beat\\nthe human thumb,** because a 250 ms reaction turns correction into amplification, so keep the sway slow. Nobody can play by\\nhand here: the delayed-thumb bot (section 16) is how you judge feel.\\n\\nThe universal 4 units/s slew is what makes keyboard feel analog: a quick tap is a small nudge, a held key is a full lean.\\nSticks barely notice it. Mouse adds its own target with a slow decay (section 4).\\n\\n**Topple.** `r > 1` for 6 steps: the body stumbles (`reactTo` flinch, a stumble clip, a creak), the activity decides the\\nprice, and the CoB returns to centre over a second. It is never a game over.\\n\\n**Breath.** The third input is both feet held. A guide ring swells and shrinks with `breath.period`. Holding both feet\\nfills `lungs`; letting go empties them. `sync` is a running match between your lungs and the guide. Good sync raises\\n`calm` (0–1), which quiets the sway, warms the picture slightly, softens the sound, and pays a bonus. Breath is used in\\nstill activities and is the charge mechanic in fast ones. Being out of sync has no penalty beyond losing the help.\\n\\n**Feet.** Left and right foot are the two triggers (analog) or shoulders. Used for steps, rhythm, paddling, jogging and\\none-leg holds. Both together is breath, or a jump in Step Class. That is every input the activities need: **Lean, Left\\nFoot, Right Foot, Both Feet.**\\n\\n**Scoring.** Every activity yields 0–1000 and a rank: 0 **Present**, 300 **Adequate**, 550 **Composed**, 750 **Serene**,\\n900 **Unsettling**. Pebbles earned: 1 to 5 by rank.\\n\\n**No softlocks.** Every activity and every finale step ends by itself: each step has a time box, after which it moves on with\\na remark (\\\"We will call that a start.\\\"). A player who puts the pad down reaches the results screen.\\n\\n**Balance targets the tests enforce** (section 16) on 10 seeds at default settings, in every activity: the perfect bot\\nscores ≥ 750, the human-like delayed thumb ≥ 550, the sloppy thumb ≥ 300, no input at all ≤ 500 and below the human-like\\nthumb. Random mashing never crashes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Controls\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":1059}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5b9fa960-8399-40f3-afa0-dd0a5ce13cbe-45","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The one verb. Centre of balance is a point in the unit disc. Each step slews the stick, then\\n * accelerates toward it with instability, slow sway and breath. Past the rim for six steps the body topples,\\n * stumbles, and recentres. It is never a game over.\\n */\\nimport { defineComponent, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\n\\n/** Numbers the balance step reads. Sliders change them between steps. */\\nexport interface BalanceCfg {\\n10→  gain: number;\\n  instability: number;\\n  damping: number;\\n  noise: number;\\n  noiseRate: number;\\n  reach: number;\\n  calmEffect: number;\\n  period: number;\\n  sens: number;\\n}\\n20→\\n/** What the thumb, the feet and the activity are doing this step. */\\nexport interface Stick {\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  gentle: boolean;\\n  both: boolean;\\n  mdx: number;\\n  mdy: number;\\n  disturbX: number;\\n30→  disturbY: number;\\n  noiseScale: number;\\n  instabilityScale: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** The centre of balance and the sway drawn once for the seat. */\\nexport interface Wobble {\\n  seat: number;\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n40→  vx: number;\\n  vy: number;\\n  sx: number;\\n  sy: number;\\n  mx: number;\\n  my: number;\\n  calm: number;\\n  lungs: number;\\n  sync: number;\\n  over: number;\\n50→  recover: number;\\n  topples: number;\\n  guide: number;\\n  m1: number;\\n  m2: number;\\n  m3: number;\\n  p1: number;\\n  p2: number;\\n  p3: number;\\n  n1: number;\\n60→  n2: number;\\n  n3: number;\\n  q1: number;\\n  q2: number;\\n  q3: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** A ring buffer of recent centres, so a late thumb sees an old one. */\\nexport interface Hist {\\n  i: number;\\n70→  n: number;\\n  xs: number[];\\n  ys: number[];\\n}\\n\\nconst field = (description: string, unit = '1') => ({ type: 'number' as const, default: 0, unit, description });\\n\\n/** The component `wobble`: one balancing body. */\\nexport const WOBBLE = defineComponent('wobble', {\\n  description: 'A seat’s centre of balance, its breath and the sway drawn for it.',\\n80→  fields: {\\n    seat: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Which mat this body stands on.' },\\n    x: field('Centre of balance, left to right. Past 1 is the rim.'),\\n    y: field('Centre of balance, back to forward.'),\\n    vx: field('Velocity along x.', '1/s'),\\n    vy: field('Velocity along y.', '1/s'),\\n    sx: field('The stick after the slew, left to right.'),\\n    sy: field('The stick after the slew, back to forward.'),\\n    mx: field('Mouse lean, decaying.'),\\n    my: field('Mouse lean, decaying.'),\\n90→    calm: field('How settled the breath is, 0 to 1.'),\\n    lungs: field('How full the breath is, 0 to 1.'),\\n    sync: field('How well the breath matches the guide, 0 to 1.'),\\n    over: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Steps in a row spent outside the disc.' },\\n    recover: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Steps left in a topple’s recentre.' },\\n    topples: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Topples since the count was cleared.' },\\n    guide: field('The breath guide, 0 empty to 1 full.'),\\n    m1: field('Sway rate ratio, x, first voice.'),\\n    m2: field('Sway rate ratio, x, second voice.'),\\n    m3: field('Sway rate ratio, x, third voice.'),\\n100→    p1: field('Sway phase, x, first voice.', 'rad'),\\n    p2: field('Sway phase, x, second voice.', 'rad'),\\n    p3: field('Sway phase, x, third voice.', 'rad'),\\n    n1: field('Sway rate ratio, y, first voice.'),\\n    n2: field('Sway rate ratio, y, second voice.'),\\n    n3: field('Sway rate ratio, y, third voice.'),\\n    q1: field('Sway phase, y, first voice.', 'rad'),\\n    q2: field('Sway phase, y, second voice.', 'rad'),\\n    q3: field('Sway phase, y, third voice.', 'rad'),\\n  },\\n110→});\\n\\n/** The component `hist`: the centres a delayed thumb can still see. */\\nexport const HIST = defineComponent('hist', {\\n  description: 'Recent centres of balance for one seat, oldest first in the ring.',\\n  fields: {\\n    i: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Where the next sample is written once the ring is full.' },\\n    n: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'How many samples have been kept.' },\\n    xs: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Recent centres, left to right.' },\\n    ys: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Recent centres, back to forward.' },\\n120→  },\\n});\\n\\n/** A number kept between lo and hi. */\\nexport function clamp(n: number, lo: number, hi: number): number {\\n  return Math.max(lo, Math.min(hi, n));\\n}\\n\\n/** Moves `current` toward `target` by at most `maxDelta`. */\\nexport function slew(current: number, target: number, maxDelta: number): number {\\n130→  const d = target - current;\\n  if (Math.abs(d) <= maxDelta) return target;\\n  return current + Math.sign(d) * maxDelta;\\n}\\n\\n/** The slow sway on one axis. Phases come from the seat, never from Math.random. */\\nexport function swayNoise(\\n  t: number,\\n  rate: number,\\n  m1: number,\\n140→  m2: number,\\n  m3: number,\\n  p1: number,\\n  p2: number,\\n  p3: number,\\n): number {\\n  const a = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * m1 * t + p1);\\n  const b = 0.6 * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * 1.7 * m2 * t + p2);\\n  const c = 0.3 * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * 3.1 * m3 * t + p3);\\n  return (a + b + c) / 1.3;\\n150→}\\n\\n/** Draws the six ratios and phases for a seat from the stream `sway`. */\\nexport function drawSway(w: World): void {\\n  const rng = w.rng('sway');\\n  const ratio = () => rng.range(0.8, 1.25);\\n  const phase = () => rng.range(0, Math.PI * 2);\\n  const body = w.spawn({\\n    wobble: {\\n      m1: ratio(),\\n160→      m2: ratio(),\\n      m3: ratio(),\\n      p1: phase(),\\n      p2: phase(),\\n      p3: phase(),\\n      n1: ratio(),\\n      n2: ratio(),\\n      n3: ratio(),\\n      q1: phase(),\\n      q2: phase(),\\n170→      q3: phase(),\\n    },\\n    hist: { xs: [], ys: [] },\\n  });\\n  void body;\\n}\\n\\n/** Clears the motion and the breath, and keeps the sway. A new activity starts here. */\\nexport function resetBalance(b: Wobble, hist: Hist): void {\\n  b.x = 0;\\n180→  b.y = 0;\\n  b.vx = 0;\\n  b.vy = 0;\\n  b.sx = 0;\\n  b.sy = 0;\\n  b.mx = 0;\\n  b.my = 0;\\n  b.calm = 0;\\n  b.lungs = 0;\\n  b.sync = 0;\\n190→  b.over = 0;\\n  b.recover = 0;\\n  b.topples = 0;\\n  b.guide = 0;\\n  hist.i = 0;\\n  hist.n = 0;\\n  hist.xs.length = 0;\\n  hist.ys.length = 0;\\n}\\n\\n200→/** Remembers a centre. The ring holds 24, which covers the sloppy thumb’s delay. */\\nexport function remember(hist: Hist, x: number, y: number): void {\\n  const cap = 24;\\n  if (hist.xs.length < cap) {\\n    hist.xs.push(x);\\n    hist.ys.push(y);\\n  } else {\\n    hist.xs[hist.i] = x;\\n    hist.ys[hist.i] = y;\\n    hist.i = (hist.i + 1) % cap;\\n210→  }\\n  hist.n += 1;\\n}\\n\\n/** The centre `delay` steps ago, or the oldest one we have. */\\nexport function recall(hist: Hist, delay: number): { x: number; y: number } {\\n  const len = hist.xs.length;\\n  if (len === 0) return { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n  const age = Math.min(Math.max(0, delay), len - 1);\\n  const newest = len < 24 ? len - 1 : (hist.i + 24 - 1) % 24;\\n220→  const at = (newest - age + len) % len;\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The one verb. Centre of balance is a point in the unit disc. Each step slews the stick, then\\n * accelerates toward it with instability, slow sway and breath. Past the rim for six steps the body topples,\\n * stumbles, and recentres. It is never a game over.\\n */\\nimport { defineComponent, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\n\\n/** Numbers the balance step reads. Sliders change them between steps. */\\nexport interface BalanceCfg {\\n10→  gain: number;\\n  instability: number;\\n  damping: number;\\n  noise: number;\\n  noiseRate: number;\\n  reach: number;\\n  calmEffect: number;\\n  period: number;\\n  sens: number;\\n}\\n20→\\n/** What the thumb, the feet and the activity are doing this step. */\\nexport interface Stick {\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  gentle: boolean;\\n  both: boolean;\\n  mdx: number;\\n  mdy: number;\\n  disturbX: number;\\n30→  disturbY: number;\\n  noiseScale: number;\\n  instabilityScale: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** The centre of balance and the sway drawn once for the seat. */\\nexport interface Wobble {\\n  seat: number;\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n40→  vx: number;\\n  vy: number;\\n  sx: number;\\n  sy: number;\\n  mx: number;\\n  my: number;\\n  calm: number;\\n  lungs: number;\\n  sync: number;\\n  over: number;\\n50→  recover: number;\\n  topples: number;\\n  guide: number;\\n  m1: number;\\n  m2: number;\\n  m3: number;\\n  p1: number;\\n  p2: number;\\n  p3: number;\\n  n1: number;\\n60→  n2: number;\\n  n3: number;\\n  q1: number;\\n  q2: number;\\n  q3: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** A ring buffer of recent centres, so a late thumb sees an old one. */\\nexport interface Hist {\\n  i: number;\\n70→  n: number;\\n  xs: number[];\\n  ys: number[];\\n}\\n\\nconst field = (description: string, unit = '1') => ({ type: 'number' as const, default: 0, unit, description });\\n\\n/** The component `wobble`: one balancing body. */\\nexport const WOBBLE = defineComponent('wobble', {\\n  description: 'A seat’s centre of balance, its breath and the sway drawn for it.',\\n80→  fields: {\\n    seat: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Which mat this body stands on.' },\\n    x: field('Centre of balance, left to right. Past 1 is the rim.'),\\n    y: field('Centre of balance, back to forward.'),\\n    vx: field('Velocity along x.', '1/s'),\\n    vy: field('Velocity along y.', '1/s'),\\n    sx: field('The stick after the slew, left to right.'),\\n    sy: field('The stick after the slew, back to forward.'),\\n    mx: field('Mouse lean, decaying.'),\\n    my: field('Mouse lean, decaying.'),\\n90→    calm: field('How settled the breath is, 0 to 1.'),\\n    lungs: field('How full the breath is, 0 to 1.'),\\n    sync: field('How well the breath matches the guide, 0 to 1.'),\\n    over: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Steps in a row spent outside the disc.' },\\n    recover: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Steps left in a topple’s recentre.' },\\n    topples: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Topples since the count was cleared.' },\\n    guide: field('The breath guide, 0 empty to 1 full.'),\\n    m1: field('Sway rate ratio, x, first voice.'),\\n    m2: field('Sway rate ratio, x, second voice.'),\\n    m3: field('Sway rate ratio, x, third voice.'),\\n100→    p1: field('Sway phase, x, first voice.', 'rad'),\\n    p2: field('Sway phase, x, second voice.', 'rad'),\\n    p3: field('Sway phase, x, third voice.', 'rad'),\\n    n1: field('Sway rate ratio, y, first voice.'),\\n    n2: field('Sway rate ratio, y, second voice.'),\\n    n3: field('Sway rate ratio, y, third voice.'),\\n    q1: field('Sway phase, y, first voice.', 'rad'),\\n    q2: field('Sway phase, y, second voice.', 'rad'),\\n    q3: field('Sway phase, y, third voice.', 'rad'),\\n  },\\n110→});\\n\\n/** The component `hist`: the centres a delayed thumb can still see. */\\nexport const HIST = defineComponent('hist', {\\n  description: 'Recent centres of balance for one seat, oldest first in the ring.',\\n  fields: {\\n    i: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Where the next sample is written once the ring is full.' },\\n    n: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'How many samples have been kept.' },\\n    xs: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Recent centres, left to right.' },\\n    ys: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Recent centres, back to forward.' },\\n120→  },\\n});\\n\\n/** A number kept between lo and hi. */\\nexport function clamp(n: number, lo: number, hi: number): number {\\n  return Math.max(lo, Math.min(hi, n));\\n}\\n\\n/** Moves `current` toward `target` by at most `maxDelta`. */\\nexport function slew(current: number, target: number, maxDelta: number): number {\\n130→  const d = target - current;\\n  if (Math.abs(d) <= maxDelta) return target;\\n  return current + Math.sign(d) * maxDelta;\\n}\\n\\n/** The slow sway on one axis. Phases come from the seat, never from Math.random. */\\nexport function swayNoise(\\n  t: number,\\n  rate: number,\\n  m1: number,\\n140→  m2: number,\\n  m3: number,\\n  p1: number,\\n  p2: number,\\n  p3: number,\\n): number {\\n  const a = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * m1 * t + p1);\\n  const b = 0.6 * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * 1.7 * m2 * t + p2);\\n  const c = 0.3 * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * 3.1 * m3 * t + p3);\\n  return (a + b + c) / 1.3;\\n150→}\\n\\n/** Draws the six ratios and phases for a seat from the stream `sway`. */\\nexport function drawSway(w: World): void {\\n  const rng = w.rng('sway');\\n  const ratio = () => rng.range(0.8, 1.25);\\n  const phase = () => rng.range(0, Math.PI * 2);\\n  const body = w.spawn({\\n    wobble: {\\n      m1: ratio(),\\n160→      m2: ratio(),\\n      m3: ratio(),\\n      p1: phase(),\\n      p2: phase(),\\n      p3: phase(),\\n      n1: ratio(),\\n      n2: ratio(),\\n      n3: ratio(),\\n      q1: phase(),\\n      q2: phase(),\\n170→      q3: phase(),\\n    },\\n    hist: { xs: [], ys: [] },\\n  });\\n  void body;\\n}\\n\\n/** Clears the motion and the breath, and keeps the sway. A new activity starts here. */\\nexport function resetBalance(b: Wobble, hist: Hist): void {\\n  b.x = 0;\\n180→  b.y = 0;\\n  b.vx = 0;\\n  b.vy = 0;\\n  b.sx = 0;\\n  b.sy = 0;\\n  b.mx = 0;\\n  b.my = 0;\\n  b.calm = 0;\\n  b.lungs = 0;\\n  b.sync = 0;\\n190→  b.over = 0;\\n  b.recover = 0;\\n  b.topples = 0;\\n  b.guide = 0;\\n  hist.i = 0;\\n  hist.n = 0;\\n  hist.xs.length = 0;\\n  hist.ys.length = 0;\\n}\\n\\n200→/** Remembers a centre. The ring holds 24, which covers the sloppy thumb’s delay. */\\nexport function remember(hist: Hist, x: number, y: number): void {\\n  const cap = 24;\\n  if (hist.xs.length < cap) {\\n    hist.xs.push(x);\\n    hist.ys.push(y);\\n  } else {\\n    hist.xs[hist.i] = x;\\n    hist.ys[hist.i] = y;\\n    hist.i = (hist.i + 1) % cap;\\n210→  }\\n  hist.n += 1;\\n}\\n\\n/** The centre `delay` steps ago, or the oldest one we have. */\\nexport function recall(hist: Hist, delay: number): { x: number; y: number } {\\n  const len = hist.xs.length;\\n  if (len === 0) return { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n  const age = Math.min(Math.max(0, delay), len - 1);\\n  const newest = len < 24 ? len - 1 : (hist.i + 24 - 1) % 24;\\n220→  const at = (newest - age + len) % len;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/wobble.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":220,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The one verb. Centre of balance is a point in the unit disc. Each step slews the stick, then\\n * accelerates toward it with instability, slow sway and breath. Past the rim for six steps the body topples,\\n * stumbles, and recentres. It is never a game over.\\n */\\nimport { defineComponent, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\n\\n/** Numbers the balance step reads. Sliders change them between steps. */\\nexport interface BalanceCfg {\\n  gain: number;\\n  instability: number;\\n  damping: number;\\n  noise: number;\\n  noiseRate: number;\\n  reach: number;\\n  calmEffect: number;\\n  period: number;\\n  sens: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** What the thumb, the feet and the activity are doing this step. */\\nexport interface Stick {\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  gentle: boolean;\\n  both: boolean;\\n  mdx: number;\\n  mdy: number;\\n  disturbX: number;\\n  disturbY: number;\\n  noiseScale: number;\\n  instabilityScale: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** The centre of balance and the sway drawn once for the seat. */\\nexport interface Wobble {\\n  seat: number;\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  vx: number;\\n  vy: number;\\n  sx: number;\\n  sy: number;\\n  mx: number;\\n  my: number;\\n  calm: number;\\n  lungs: number;\\n  sync: number;\\n  over: number;\\n  recover: number;\\n  topples: number;\\n  guide: number;\\n  m1: number;\\n  m2: number;\\n  m3: number;\\n  p1: number;\\n  p2: number;\\n  p3: number;\\n  n1: number;\\n  n2: number;\\n  n3: number;\\n  q1: number;\\n  q2: number;\\n  q3: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** A ring buffer of recent centres, so a late thumb sees an old one. */\\nexport interface Hist {\\n  i: number;\\n  n: number;\\n  xs: number[];\\n  ys: number[];\\n}\\n\\nconst field = (description: string, unit = '1') => ({ type: 'number' as const, default: 0, unit, description });\\n\\n/** The component `wobble`: one balancing body. */\\nexport const WOBBLE = defineComponent('wobble', {\\n  description: 'A seat’s centre of balance, its breath and the sway drawn for it.',\\n  fields: {\\n    seat: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Which mat this body stands on.' },\\n    x: field('Centre of balance, left to right. Past 1 is the rim.'),\\n    y: field('Centre of balance, back to forward.'),\\n    vx: field('Velocity along x.', '1/s'),\\n    vy: field('Velocity along y.', '1/s'),\\n    sx: field('The stick after the slew, left to right.'),\\n    sy: field('The stick after the slew, back to forward.'),\\n    mx: field('Mouse lean, decaying.'),\\n    my: field('Mouse lean, decaying.'),\\n    calm: field('How settled the breath is, 0 to 1.'),\\n    lungs: field('How full the breath is, 0 to 1.'),\\n    sync: field('How well the breath matches the guide, 0 to 1.'),\\n    over: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Steps in a row spent outside the disc.' },\\n    recover: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Steps left in a topple’s recentre.' },\\n    topples: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Topples since the count was cleared.' },\\n    guide: field('The breath guide, 0 empty to 1 full.'),\\n    m1: field('Sway rate ratio, x, first voice.'),\\n    m2: field('Sway rate ratio, x, second voice.'),\\n    m3: field('Sway rate ratio, x, third voice.'),\\n    p1: field('Sway phase, x, first voice.', 'rad'),\\n    p2: field('Sway phase, x, second voice.', 'rad'),\\n    p3: field('Sway phase, x, third voice.', 'rad'),\\n    n1: field('Sway rate ratio, y, first voice.'),\\n    n2: field('Sway rate ratio, y, second voice.'),\\n    n3: field('Sway rate ratio, y, third voice.'),\\n    q1: field('Sway phase, y, first voice.', 'rad'),\\n    q2: field('Sway phase, y, second voice.', 'rad'),\\n    q3: field('Sway phase, y, third voice.', 'rad'),\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** The component `hist`: the centres a delayed thumb can still see. */\\nexport const HIST = defineComponent('hist', {\\n  description: 'Recent centres of balance for one seat, oldest first in the ring.',\\n  fields: {\\n    i: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'Where the next sample is written once the ring is full.' },\\n    n: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'How many samples have been kept.' },\\n    xs: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Recent centres, left to right.' },\\n    ys: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Recent centres, back to forward.' },\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** A number kept between lo and hi. */\\nexport function clamp(n: number, lo: number, hi: number): number {\\n  return Math.max(lo, Math.min(hi, n));\\n}\\n\\n/** Moves `current` toward `target` by at most `maxDelta`. */\\nexport function slew(current: number, target: number, maxDelta: number): number {\\n  const d = target - current;\\n  if (Math.abs(d) <= maxDelta) return target;\\n  return current + Math.sign(d) * maxDelta;\\n}\\n\\n/** The slow sway on one axis. Phases come from the seat, never from Math.random. */\\nexport function swayNoise(\\n  t: number,\\n  rate: number,\\n  m1: number,\\n  m2: number,\\n  m3: number,\\n  p1: number,\\n  p2: number,\\n  p3: number,\\n): number {\\n  const a = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * m1 * t + p1);\\n  const b = 0.6 * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * 1.7 * m2 * t + p2);\\n  const c = 0.3 * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * rate * 3.1 * m3 * t + p3);\\n  return (a + b + c) / 1.3;\\n}\\n\\n/** Draws the six ratios and phases for a seat from the stream `sway`. */\\nexport function drawSway(w: World): void {\\n  const rng = w.rng('sway');\\n  const ratio = () => rng.range(0.8, 1.25);\\n  const phase = () => rng.range(0, Math.PI * 2);\\n  const body = w.spawn({\\n    wobble: {\\n      m1: ratio(),\\n      m2: ratio(),\\n      m3: ratio(),\\n      p1: phase(),\\n      p2: phase(),\\n      p3: phase(),\\n      n1: ratio(),\\n      n2: ratio(),\\n      n3: ratio(),\\n      q1: phase(),\\n      q2: phase(),\\n      q3: phase(),\\n    },\\n    hist: { xs: [], ys: [] },\\n  });\\n  void body;\\n}\\n\\n/** Clears the motion and the breath, and keeps the sway. A new activity starts here. */\\nexport function resetBalance(b: Wobble, hist: Hist): void {\\n  b.x = 0;\\n  b.y = 0;\\n  b.vx = 0;\\n  b.vy = 0;\\n  b.sx = 0;\\n  b.sy = 0;\\n  b.mx = 0;\\n  b.my = 0;\\n  b.calm = 0;\\n  b.lungs = 0;\\n  b.sync = 0;\\n  b.over = 0;\\n  b.recover = 0;\\n  b.topples = 0;\\n  b.guide = 0;\\n  hist.i = 0;\\n  hist.n = 0;\\n  hist.xs.length = 0;\\n  hist.ys.length = 0;\\n}\\n\\n/** Remembers a centre. The ring holds 24, which covers the sloppy thumb’s delay. */\\nexport function remember(hist: Hist, x: number, y: number): void {\\n  const cap = 24;\\n  if (hist.xs.length < cap) {\\n    hist.xs.push(x);\\n    hist.ys.push(y);\\n  } else {\\n    hist.xs[hist.i] = x;\\n    hist.ys[hist.i] = y;\\n    hist.i = (hist.i + 1) % cap;\\n  }\\n  hist.n += 1;\\n}\\n\\n/** The centre `delay` steps ago, or the oldest one we have. */\\nexport function recall(hist: Hist, delay: number): { x: number; y: number } {\\n  const len = hist.xs.length;\\n  if (len === 0) return { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n  const age = Math.min(Math.max(0, delay), len - 1);\\n  const newest = len < 24 ? len - 1 : (hist.i + 24 - 1) % 24;\\n  const at = (newest - age + len) % len;\\n\",\"total_lines\":292}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5b9fa960-8399-40f3-afa0-dd0a5ce13cbe-46","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The four thumbs. Nobody here can hold a pad, so these write the same lean a player would.\\n * Perfect is immediate. Human-like is 250 ms late. Sloppy is 350 ms late. Idle holds nothing.\\n * Off-centre seats need a feedforward term, or a late thumb settles short of the ring.\\n */\\nimport type { Intents } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { type BalanceCfg, type Hist, type Wobble, clamp, recall } from './wobble';\\n\\n/** Which thumb is playing. */\\n10→export type Band = 'perfect' | 'human' | 'sloppy' | 'idle';\\n\\n/** Delay in steps, proportional gain, and jitter width. */\\nexport function bandTune(band: Band): { delay: number; k: number; jitter: number } {\\n  if (band === 'perfect') return { delay: 0, k: 3, jitter: 0 };\\n  if (band === 'human') return { delay: 15, k: 1.2, jitter: 0.04 };\\n  if (band === 'sloppy') return { delay: 21, k: 0.8, jitter: 0.06 };\\n  return { delay: 0, k: 0, jitter: 0 };\\n}\\n\\n20→/** The breath guide at sim time `t`, the same triangle the balance step draws. */\\nexport function guideAt(t: number, period: number): number {\\n  const p = Math.max(0.25, period);\\n  const phase = (((t % p) + p) % p) / p;\\n  return phase < 0.5 ? phase * 2 : (1 - phase) * 2;\\n}\\n\\n/** True while this thumb means to be breathing in. Idle never does. Delay is the late thumb. */\\nexport function wantBreath(band: Band, t: number, period: number): boolean {\\n  if (band === 'idle') return false;\\n30→  const tune = bandTune(band);\\n  const when = Math.max(0, t - tune.delay / 60);\\n  const p = Math.max(0.25, period);\\n  const phase = (when % p) / p;\\n  return phase < 0.5;\\n}\\n\\n/** A deterministic wobble so the same step always jitters the same way. Not Math.random. */\\nfunction jitter(amount: number, tick: number, axis: number): number {\\n  if (amount === 0) return 0;\\n40→  return amount * Math.sin(tick * 1.7 + axis * 4.1);\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * The stick that holds `desired` on this seat. `instScale` matches the activity's instability.\\n * The hold term is zero at the centre, so the still-ring model is unchanged.\\n */\\nexport function seek(\\n  band: Band,\\n  desiredX: number,\\n50→  desiredY: number,\\n  body: Wobble,\\n  hist: Hist,\\n  cfg: BalanceCfg,\\n  tick: number,\\n  instScale = 1,\\n): { x: number; y: number } {\\n  if (band === 'idle') return { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n  const tune = bandTune(band);\\n  const seen = recall(hist, tune.delay);\\n60→  const inst = cfg.instability * instScale;\\n  const denom = cfg.gain * cfg.reach;\\n  const hold = denom === 0 ? 0 : (cfg.gain - inst) / denom;\\n  const x = hold * desiredX + tune.k * (desiredX - seen.x) + jitter(tune.jitter, tick, 0);\\n  const y = hold * desiredY + tune.k * (desiredY - seen.y) + jitter(tune.jitter, tick, 1);\\n  return { x: clamp(x, -1, 1), y: clamp(y, -1, 1) };\\n}\\n\\n/** Turns a stick and the feet into the intents the balance map reads. */\\nexport function stickIntents(\\n70→  stick: { x: number; y: number },\\n  feet: { l?: boolean; r?: boolean; both?: boolean },\\n): Intents {\\n  const out: Record<string, number> = {};\\n  if (stick.x >= 0) out['game:r'] = clamp(stick.x, 0, 1);\\n  else out['game:l'] = clamp(-stick.x, 0, 1);\\n  if (stick.y >= 0) out['game:f'] = clamp(stick.y, 0, 1);\\n  else out['game:b'] = clamp(-stick.y, 0, 1);\\n  if (feet.both || (feet.l && feet.r)) {\\n    out['game:fl'] = 1;\\n80→    out['game:fr'] = 1;\\n  } else {\\n    if (feet.l) out['game:fl'] = 1;\\n    if (feet.r) out['game:fr'] = 1;\\n  }\\n  return out as Intents;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The four thumbs. Nobody here can hold a pad, so these write the same lean a player would.\\n * Perfect is immediate. Human-like is 250 ms late. Sloppy is 350 ms late. Idle holds nothing.\\n * Off-centre seats need a feedforward term, or a late thumb settles short of the ring.\\n */\\nimport type { Intents } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { type BalanceCfg, type Hist, type Wobble, clamp, recall } from './wobble';\\n\\n/** Which thumb is playing. */\\n10→export type Band = 'perfect' | 'human' | 'sloppy' | 'idle';\\n\\n/** Delay in steps, proportional gain, and jitter width. */\\nexport function bandTune(band: Band): { delay: number; k: number; jitter: number } {\\n  if (band === 'perfect') return { delay: 0, k: 3, jitter: 0 };\\n  if (band === 'human') return { delay: 15, k: 1.2, jitter: 0.04 };\\n  if (band === 'sloppy') return { delay: 21, k: 0.8, jitter: 0.06 };\\n  return { delay: 0, k: 0, jitter: 0 };\\n}\\n\\n20→/** The breath guide at sim time `t`, the same triangle the balance step draws. */\\nexport function guideAt(t: number, period: number): number {\\n  const p = Math.max(0.25, period);\\n  const phase = (((t % p) + p) % p) / p;\\n  return phase < 0.5 ? phase * 2 : (1 - phase) * 2;\\n}\\n\\n/** True while this thumb means to be breathing in. Idle never does. Delay is the late thumb. */\\nexport function wantBreath(band: Band, t: number, period: number): boolean {\\n  if (band === 'idle') return false;\\n30→  const tune = bandTune(band);\\n  const when = Math.max(0, t - tune.delay / 60);\\n  const p = Math.max(0.25, period);\\n  const phase = (when % p) / p;\\n  return phase < 0.5;\\n}\\n\\n/** A deterministic wobble so the same step always jitters the same way. Not Math.random. */\\nfunction jitter(amount: number, tick: number, axis: number): number {\\n  if (amount === 0) return 0;\\n40→  return amount * Math.sin(tick * 1.7 + axis * 4.1);\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * The stick that holds `desired` on this seat. `instScale` matches the activity's instability.\\n * The hold term is zero at the centre, so the still-ring model is unchanged.\\n */\\nexport function seek(\\n  band: Band,\\n  desiredX: number,\\n50→  desiredY: number,\\n  body: Wobble,\\n  hist: Hist,\\n  cfg: BalanceCfg,\\n  tick: number,\\n  instScale = 1,\\n): { x: number; y: number } {\\n  if (band === 'idle') return { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n  const tune = bandTune(band);\\n  const seen = recall(hist, tune.delay);\\n60→  const inst = cfg.instability * instScale;\\n  const denom = cfg.gain * cfg.reach;\\n  const hold = denom === 0 ? 0 : (cfg.gain - inst) / denom;\\n  const x = hold * desiredX + tune.k * (desiredX - seen.x) + jitter(tune.jitter, tick, 0);\\n  const y = hold * desiredY + tune.k * (desiredY - seen.y) + jitter(tune.jitter, tick, 1);\\n  return { x: clamp(x, -1, 1), y: clamp(y, -1, 1) };\\n}\\n\\n/** Turns a stick and the feet into the intents the balance map reads. */\\nexport function stickIntents(\\n70→  stick: { x: number; y: number },\\n  feet: { l?: boolean; r?: boolean; both?: boolean },\\n): Intents {\\n  const out: Record<string, number> = {};\\n  if (stick.x >= 0) out['game:r'] = clamp(stick.x, 0, 1);\\n  else out['game:l'] = clamp(-stick.x, 0, 1);\\n  if (stick.y >= 0) out['game:f'] = clamp(stick.y, 0, 1);\\n  else out['game:b'] = clamp(-stick.y, 0, 1);\\n  if (feet.both || (feet.l && feet.r)) {\\n    out['game:fl'] = 1;\\n80→    out['game:fr'] = 1;\\n  } else {\\n    if (feet.l) out['game:fl'] = 1;\\n    if (feet.r) out['game:fr'] = 1;\\n  }\\n  return out as Intents;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/bot.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":180,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The four thumbs. Nobody here can hold a pad, so these write the same lean a player would.\\n * Perfect is immediate. Human-like is 250 ms late. Sloppy is 350 ms late. Idle holds nothing.\\n * Off-centre seats need a feedforward term, or a late thumb settles short of the ring.\\n */\\nimport type { Intents } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { type BalanceCfg, type Hist, type Wobble, clamp, recall } from './wobble';\\n\\n/** Which thumb is playing. */\\nexport type Band = 'perfect' | 'human' | 'sloppy' | 'idle';\\n\\n/** Delay in steps, proportional gain, and jitter width. */\\nexport function bandTune(band: Band): { delay: number; k: number; jitter: number } {\\n  if (band === 'perfect') return { delay: 0, k: 3, jitter: 0 };\\n  if (band === 'human') return { delay: 15, k: 1.2, jitter: 0.04 };\\n  if (band === 'sloppy') return { delay: 21, k: 0.8, jitter: 0.06 };\\n  return { delay: 0, k: 0, jitter: 0 };\\n}\\n\\n/** The breath guide at sim time `t`, the same triangle the balance step draws. */\\nexport function guideAt(t: number, period: number): number {\\n  const p = Math.max(0.25, period);\\n  const phase = (((t % p) + p) % p) / p;\\n  return phase < 0.5 ? phase * 2 : (1 - phase) * 2;\\n}\\n\\n/** True while this thumb means to be breathing in. Idle never does. Delay is the late thumb. */\\nexport function wantBreath(band: Band, t: number, period: number): boolean {\\n  if (band === 'idle') return false;\\n  const tune = bandTune(band);\\n  const when = Math.max(0, t - tune.delay / 60);\\n  const p = Math.max(0.25, period);\\n  const phase = (when % p) / p;\\n  return phase < 0.5;\\n}\\n\\n/** A deterministic wobble so the same step always jitters the same way. Not Math.random. */\\nfunction jitter(amount: number, tick: number, axis: number): number {\\n  if (amount === 0) return 0;\\n  return amount * Math.sin(tick * 1.7 + axis * 4.1);\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * The stick that holds `desired` on this seat. `instScale` matches the activity's instability.\\n * The hold term is zero at the centre, so the still-ring model is unchanged.\\n */\\nexport function seek(\\n  band: Band,\\n  desiredX: number,\\n  desiredY: number,\\n  body: Wobble,\\n  hist: Hist,\\n  cfg: BalanceCfg,\\n  tick: number,\\n  instScale = 1,\\n): { x: number; y: number } {\\n  if (band === 'idle') return { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n  const tune = bandTune(band);\\n  const seen = recall(hist, tune.delay);\\n  const inst = cfg.instability * instScale;\\n  const denom = cfg.gain * cfg.reach;\\n  const hold = denom === 0 ? 0 : (cfg.gain - inst) / denom;\\n  const x = hold * desiredX + tune.k * (desiredX - seen.x) + jitter(tune.jitter, tick, 0);\\n  const y = hold * desiredY + tune.k * (desiredY - seen.y) + jitter(tune.jitter, tick, 1);\\n  return { x: clamp(x, -1, 1), y: clamp(y, -1, 1) };\\n}\\n\\n/** Turns a stick and the feet into the intents the balance map reads. */\\nexport function stickIntents(\\n  stick: { x: number; y: number },\\n  feet: { l?: boolean; r?: boolean; both?: boolean },\\n): Intents {\\n  const out: Record<string, number> = {};\\n  if (stick.x >= 0) out['game:r'] = clamp(stick.x, 0, 1);\\n  else out['game:l'] = clamp(-stick.x, 0, 1);\\n  if (stick.y >= 0) out['game:f'] = clamp(stick.y, 0, 1);\\n  else out['game:b'] = clamp(-stick.y, 0, 1);\\n  if (feet.both || (feet.l && feet.r)) {\\n    out['game:fl'] = 1;\\n    out['game:fr'] = 1;\\n  } else {\\n    if (feet.l) out['game:fl'] = 1;\\n    if (feet.r) out['game:fr'] = 1;\\n  }\\n  return out as Intents;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":86}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5b9fa960-8399-40f3-afa0-dd0a5ce13cbe-47","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"90→      name: 'c',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:roundedBox',\\n      params: { width: 0.32, height: 0.18, depth: 0.26, radius: 0.06 },\\n      material: 'material:sand',\\n      position: [-0.02, 0.48, 0.02],\\n    },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\n/** A place a guest can walk up to and begin. */\\n100→const STATIONS: readonly { id: string; x: number; z: number }[] = [\\n  { id: 'morning', x: 0, z: 8 },\\n  { id: 'pose-a', x: 10, z: 2 },\\n  { id: 'pond', x: 24, z: 16 },\\n  { id: 'garden', x: -18, z: 12 },\\n  { id: 'paddle', x: 0, z: -36 },\\n  { id: 'line', x: -26, z: 6 },\\n  { id: 'group', x: -8, z: -6 },\\n  { id: 'tilt', x: 40, z: 8 },\\n];\\n110→\\n/** Plaques. They creep nowhere. They only say they did. */\\nconst PLAQUES: readonly { x: number; z: number; text: string }[] = [\\n  { x: 6, z: -4, text: 'plaque.want' },\\n  { x: -6, z: 14, text: 'plaque.moved' },\\n  { x: 16, z: -8, text: 'plaque.flamingo' },\\n  { x: -12, z: -12, text: 'plaque.gulls' },\\n  { x: 8, z: 12, text: 'notice.even' },\\n  { x: -4, z: -16, text: 'notice.lawn' },\\n];\\n120→\\n/** Hidden pebbles. They join the cairn. They are not a shop. */\\nconst PEBBLES: readonly { x: number; z: number }[] = [\\n  { x: 18, z: -14 },\\n  { x: -22, z: -8 },\\n  { x: 8, z: 22 },\\n  { x: -30, z: 18 },\\n];\\n\\n/** An actor row the pilot can push. */\\n130→defineComponent('posed', {\\n  description: '1 once the guest is wearing the lean clips.',\\n  fields: { on: { type: 'number', default: 0, description: '1 after the leans are playing.' } },\\n});\\n\\ninterface Body {\\n  id: number;\\n  actor: { x: number; y: number; z: number; intents: { move?: readonly [number, number] } };\\n  role?: { who: string };\\n  posed?: { on: number };\\n140→  clips?: { state?: { slots?: { clip: string; t: number }[] } };\\n}\\n\\n/** A placed thing. */\\ninterface Spot {\\n  id: number;\\n  mark: { x: number; y: number; z: number; kind: string; text: string; taken: number; follow: number };\\n}\\n\\n/** The sea's drawn position. */\\n150→interface Sea {\\n  sceneProp: { x: number; y: number; z: number; prop: string };\\n}\\n\\n/** Distance on the lawn. */\\nfunction flat(ax: number, az: number, bx: number, bz: number): number {\\n  const dx = ax - bx;\\n  const dz = az - bz;\\n  return Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dz * dz);\\n}\\n160→\\n/** The guest, if the cast has spawned. */\\nfunction guest(w: World): Body | undefined {\\n  const rows = w.query('actor') as unknown as Body[];\\n  return rows.find((row) => row.role?.who === 'guest');\\n}\\n\\n/** Stands one still person. No clips. The mat is the performance. */\\nfunction person(w: World, who: string, x: number, z: number, yaw: number): void {\\n  spawnActor(w, {\\n170→    at: [x, 40, z],\\n    yaw,\\n    player: false,\\n    character: createCharacter({ speed: 0 }),\\n    components: { role: { who } },\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/** Puts the island, the sea, the cast and the hidden pebbles into the world. */\\nfunction furnish(w: World): void {\\n180→  addTerrainBody(physicsOf(w), getTerrain('terrain:fulcrum'));\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:sea', at: [0, 2, 0], yaw: 0 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:cairn', at: [-3, 0, 3], yaw: 0 });\\n  for (const spot of [\\n    [0, 2],\\n    [3, 2],\\n    [-3, 2],\\n    [0, 5],\\n  ] as const) {\\n    spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:mat', at: [spot[0], 0, spot[1]], yaw: 0 });\\n190→  }\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:pillar', at: [-6, 0, -4], yaw: 0 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:pillar', at: [6, 0, -4], yaw: 0 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:bench', at: [4, 0, -8], yaw: 0.2 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:bench', at: [-4, 0, 14], yaw: -0.2 });\\n  for (const station of STATIONS) {\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: station.x, y: 1.2, z: station.z, kind: 'station', text: station.id, taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n  }\\n  for (const plaque of PLAQUES) {\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: plaque.x, y: 1.1, z: plaque.z, kind: 'plaque', text: plaque.text, taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n200→  }\\n  for (const pebble of PEBBLES) {\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: pebble.x, y: 0.3, z: pebble.z, kind: 'pebble', text: 'find.pebble', taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n  }\\n  spawnActor(w, {\\n    at: [0, 40, 6],\\n    player: false,\\n    yaw: Math.PI,\\n    character: createCharacter({ speed: 5.5 }),\\n    anim: { build: 'build:retreat' },\\n210→    clips: {\\n      sets: ['clipset:retreat'],\\n      play: { clip: 'RETREAT/Nothing', speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, loop: false },\\n    },\\n    components: { role: { who: 'guest' }, posed: { on: 0 } },\\n  });\\n  person(w, 'plumb', 2.2, 4, Math.PI);\\n  person(w, 'tare', -2.2, 5, 0);\\n  person(w, 'gerald', 8, -2, 1);\\n  person(w, 'bex', -8, 0, 0.4);\\n220→  person(w, 'nan', 5, 10, 2);\\n  w.systems.add('retreat.dress', dress, { phase: 'rules' });\\n}\\n\\n/** Sea bob, pebble pickup, and the pose scrub. Runs after the clips have stepped. */\\nfunction dress(w: World): void {\\n  for (const row of w.query('sceneProp') as unknown as Sea[]) {\\n    if (row.sceneProp.prop === 'prop:sea') row.sceneProp.y = 2 + 0.06 * Math.sin(w.time * 0.35);\\n  }\\n  const who = guest(w);\\n230→  if (!who) return;\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  if (flow.mode === 'roam') {\\n    for (const spot of w.query('mark') as unknown as Spot[]) {\\n      if (spot.mark.kind !== 'pebble' || spot.mark.taken) continue;\\n      if (flat(who.actor.x, who.actor.z, spot.mark.x, spot.mark.z) < 1.5) {\\n        spot.mark.taken = 1;\\n        flow.pebbles += 1;\\n        flow.line = 'find.pebble';\\n      }\\n240→    }\\n  }\\n  scrub(w, who);\\n}\\n\\n/** Writes the lean and the pose onto the clip slots. */\\nfunction scrub(w: World, who: Body): void {\\n  const slots = who.clips?.state?.slots;\\n  if (!who.posed?.on) {\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanR', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n250→    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanL', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanF', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanB', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    if (who.posed) who.posed.on = 1;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (!slots) return;\\n  const rows = w.query('wobble') as unknown as { wobble: { x: number; y: number; seat: number } }[];\\n  const body = rows.find((row) => row.wobble.seat === 0)?.wobble;\\n  const x = body?.x ?? 0;\\n260→  const y = body?.y ?? 0;\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  const pose = flowOf(w).event.startsWith('pose') ? Math.min(1, act.hold / (12 * 60)) : 0;\\n  for (const slot of slots) {\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanR') slot.t = Math.max(0, x);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanL') slot.t = Math.max(0, -x);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanF') slot.t = Math.max(0, y);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanB') slot.t = Math.max(0, -y);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/Heron') slot.t = pose;\\n  }\",\"content_concise\":\"90→      name: 'c',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:roundedBox',\\n      params: { width: 0.32, height: 0.18, depth: 0.26, radius: 0.06 },\\n      material: 'material:sand',\\n      position: [-0.02, 0.48, 0.02],\\n    },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\n/** A place a guest can walk up to and begin. */\\n100→const STATIONS: readonly { id: string; x: number; z: number }[] = [\\n  { id: 'morning', x: 0, z: 8 },\\n  { id: 'pose-a', x: 10, z: 2 },\\n  { id: 'pond', x: 24, z: 16 },\\n  { id: 'garden', x: -18, z: 12 },\\n  { id: 'paddle', x: 0, z: -36 },\\n  { id: 'line', x: -26, z: 6 },\\n  { id: 'group', x: -8, z: -6 },\\n  { id: 'tilt', x: 40, z: 8 },\\n];\\n110→\\n/** Plaques. They creep nowhere. They only say they did. */\\nconst PLAQUES: readonly { x: number; z: number; text: string }[] = [\\n  { x: 6, z: -4, text: 'plaque.want' },\\n  { x: -6, z: 14, text: 'plaque.moved' },\\n  { x: 16, z: -8, text: 'plaque.flamingo' },\\n  { x: -12, z: -12, text: 'plaque.gulls' },\\n  { x: 8, z: 12, text: 'notice.even' },\\n  { x: -4, z: -16, text: 'notice.lawn' },\\n];\\n120→\\n/** Hidden pebbles. They join the cairn. They are not a shop. */\\nconst PEBBLES: readonly { x: number; z: number }[] = [\\n  { x: 18, z: -14 },\\n  { x: -22, z: -8 },\\n  { x: 8, z: 22 },\\n  { x: -30, z: 18 },\\n];\\n\\n/** An actor row the pilot can push. */\\n130→defineComponent('posed', {\\n  description: '1 once the guest is wearing the lean clips.',\\n  fields: { on: { type: 'number', default: 0, description: '1 after the leans are playing.' } },\\n});\\n\\ninterface Body {\\n  id: number;\\n  actor: { x: number; y: number; z: number; intents: { move?: readonly [number, number] } };\\n  role?: { who: string };\\n  posed?: { on: number };\\n140→  clips?: { state?: { slots?: { clip: string; t: number }[] } };\\n}\\n\\n/** A placed thing. */\\ninterface Spot {\\n  id: number;\\n  mark: { x: number; y: number; z: number; kind: string; text: string; taken: number; follow: number };\\n}\\n\\n/** The sea's drawn position. */\\n150→interface Sea {\\n  sceneProp: { x: number; y: number; z: number; prop: string };\\n}\\n\\n/** Distance on the lawn. */\\nfunction flat(ax: number, az: number, bx: number, bz: number): number {\\n  const dx = ax - bx;\\n  const dz = az - bz;\\n  return Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dz * dz);\\n}\\n160→\\n/** The guest, if the cast has spawned. */\\nfunction guest(w: World): Body | undefined {\\n  const rows = w.query('actor') as unknown as Body[];\\n  return rows.find((row) => row.role?.who === 'guest');\\n}\\n\\n/** Stands one still person. No clips. The mat is the performance. */\\nfunction person(w: World, who: string, x: number, z: number, yaw: number): void {\\n  spawnActor(w, {\\n170→    at: [x, 40, z],\\n    yaw,\\n    player: false,\\n    character: createCharacter({ speed: 0 }),\\n    components: { role: { who } },\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/** Puts the island, the sea, the cast and the hidden pebbles into the world. */\\nfunction furnish(w: World): void {\\n180→  addTerrainBody(physicsOf(w), getTerrain('terrain:fulcrum'));\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:sea', at: [0, 2, 0], yaw: 0 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:cairn', at: [-3, 0, 3], yaw: 0 });\\n  for (const spot of [\\n    [0, 2],\\n    [3, 2],\\n    [-3, 2],\\n    [0, 5],\\n  ] as const) {\\n    spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:mat', at: [spot[0], 0, spot[1]], yaw: 0 });\\n190→  }\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:pillar', at: [-6, 0, -4], yaw: 0 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:pillar', at: [6, 0, -4], yaw: 0 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:bench', at: [4, 0, -8], yaw: 0.2 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:bench', at: [-4, 0, 14], yaw: -0.2 });\\n  for (const station of STATIONS) {\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: station.x, y: 1.2, z: station.z, kind: 'station', text: station.id, taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n  }\\n  for (const plaque of PLAQUES) {\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: plaque.x, y: 1.1, z: plaque.z, kind: 'plaque', text: plaque.text, taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n200→  }\\n  for (const pebble of PEBBLES) {\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: pebble.x, y: 0.3, z: pebble.z, kind: 'pebble', text: 'find.pebble', taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n  }\\n  spawnActor(w, {\\n    at: [0, 40, 6],\\n    player: false,\\n    yaw: Math.PI,\\n    character: createCharacter({ speed: 5.5 }),\\n    anim: { build: 'build:retreat' },\\n210→    clips: {\\n      sets: ['clipset:retreat'],\\n      play: { clip: 'RETREAT/Nothing', speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, loop: false },\\n    },\\n    components: { role: { who: 'guest' }, posed: { on: 0 } },\\n  });\\n  person(w, 'plumb', 2.2, 4, Math.PI);\\n  person(w, 'tare', -2.2, 5, 0);\\n  person(w, 'gerald', 8, -2, 1);\\n  person(w, 'bex', -8, 0, 0.4);\\n220→  person(w, 'nan', 5, 10, 2);\\n  w.systems.add('retreat.dress', dress, { phase: 'rules' });\\n}\\n\\n/** Sea bob, pebble pickup, and the pose scrub. Runs after the clips have stepped. */\\nfunction dress(w: World): void {\\n  for (const row of w.query('sceneProp') as unknown as Sea[]) {\\n    if (row.sceneProp.prop === 'prop:sea') row.sceneProp.y = 2 + 0.06 * Math.sin(w.time * 0.35);\\n  }\\n  const who = guest(w);\\n230→  if (!who) return;\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  if (flow.mode === 'roam') {\\n    for (const spot of w.query('mark') as unknown as Spot[]) {\\n      if (spot.mark.kind !== 'pebble' || spot.mark.taken) continue;\\n      if (flat(who.actor.x, who.actor.z, spot.mark.x, spot.mark.z) < 1.5) {\\n        spot.mark.taken = 1;\\n        flow.pebbles += 1;\\n        flow.line = 'find.pebble';\\n      }\\n240→    }\\n  }\\n  scrub(w, who);\\n}\\n\\n/** Writes the lean and the pose onto the clip slots. */\\nfunction scrub(w: World, who: Body): void {\\n  const slots = who.clips?.state?.slots;\\n  if (!who.posed?.on) {\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanR', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n250→    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanL', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanF', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanB', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    if (who.posed) who.posed.on = 1;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (!slots) return;\\n  const rows = w.query('wobble') as unknown as { wobble: { x: number; y: number; seat: number } }[];\\n  const body = rows.find((row) => row.wobble.seat === 0)?.wobble;\\n  const x = body?.x ?? 0;\\n260→  const y = body?.y ?? 0;\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  const pose = flowOf(w).event.startsWith('pose') ? Math.min(1, act.hold / (12 * 60)) : 0;\\n  for (const slot of slots) {\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanR') slot.t = Math.max(0, x);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanL') slot.t = Math.max(0, -x);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanF') slot.t = Math.max(0, y);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanB') slot.t = Math.max(0, -y);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/Heron') slot.t = pose;\\n  }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/island.ts\",\"offset\":90,\"limit\":180,\"raw_output\":\"      name: 'c',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:roundedBox',\\n      params: { width: 0.32, height: 0.18, depth: 0.26, radius: 0.06 },\\n      material: 'material:sand',\\n      position: [-0.02, 0.48, 0.02],\\n    },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\n/** A place a guest can walk up to and begin. */\\nconst STATIONS: readonly { id: string; x: number; z: number }[] = [\\n  { id: 'morning', x: 0, z: 8 },\\n  { id: 'pose-a', x: 10, z: 2 },\\n  { id: 'pond', x: 24, z: 16 },\\n  { id: 'garden', x: -18, z: 12 },\\n  { id: 'paddle', x: 0, z: -36 },\\n  { id: 'line', x: -26, z: 6 },\\n  { id: 'group', x: -8, z: -6 },\\n  { id: 'tilt', x: 40, z: 8 },\\n];\\n\\n/** Plaques. They creep nowhere. They only say they did. */\\nconst PLAQUES: readonly { x: number; z: number; text: string }[] = [\\n  { x: 6, z: -4, text: 'plaque.want' },\\n  { x: -6, z: 14, text: 'plaque.moved' },\\n  { x: 16, z: -8, text: 'plaque.flamingo' },\\n  { x: -12, z: -12, text: 'plaque.gulls' },\\n  { x: 8, z: 12, text: 'notice.even' },\\n  { x: -4, z: -16, text: 'notice.lawn' },\\n];\\n\\n/** Hidden pebbles. They join the cairn. They are not a shop. */\\nconst PEBBLES: readonly { x: number; z: number }[] = [\\n  { x: 18, z: -14 },\\n  { x: -22, z: -8 },\\n  { x: 8, z: 22 },\\n  { x: -30, z: 18 },\\n];\\n\\n/** An actor row the pilot can push. */\\ndefineComponent('posed', {\\n  description: '1 once the guest is wearing the lean clips.',\\n  fields: { on: { type: 'number', default: 0, description: '1 after the leans are playing.' } },\\n});\\n\\ninterface Body {\\n  id: number;\\n  actor: { x: number; y: number; z: number; intents: { move?: readonly [number, number] } };\\n  role?: { who: string };\\n  posed?: { on: number };\\n  clips?: { state?: { slots?: { clip: string; t: number }[] } };\\n}\\n\\n/** A placed thing. */\\ninterface Spot {\\n  id: number;\\n  mark: { x: number; y: number; z: number; kind: string; text: string; taken: number; follow: number };\\n}\\n\\n/** The sea's drawn position. */\\ninterface Sea {\\n  sceneProp: { x: number; y: number; z: number; prop: string };\\n}\\n\\n/** Distance on the lawn. */\\nfunction flat(ax: number, az: number, bx: number, bz: number): number {\\n  const dx = ax - bx;\\n  const dz = az - bz;\\n  return Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dz * dz);\\n}\\n\\n/** The guest, if the cast has spawned. */\\nfunction guest(w: World): Body | undefined {\\n  const rows = w.query('actor') as unknown as Body[];\\n  return rows.find((row) => row.role?.who === 'guest');\\n}\\n\\n/** Stands one still person. No clips. The mat is the performance. */\\nfunction person(w: World, who: string, x: number, z: number, yaw: number): void {\\n  spawnActor(w, {\\n    at: [x, 40, z],\\n    yaw,\\n    player: false,\\n    character: createCharacter({ speed: 0 }),\\n    components: { role: { who } },\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/** Puts the island, the sea, the cast and the hidden pebbles into the world. */\\nfunction furnish(w: World): void {\\n  addTerrainBody(physicsOf(w), getTerrain('terrain:fulcrum'));\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:sea', at: [0, 2, 0], yaw: 0 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:cairn', at: [-3, 0, 3], yaw: 0 });\\n  for (const spot of [\\n    [0, 2],\\n    [3, 2],\\n    [-3, 2],\\n    [0, 5],\\n  ] as const) {\\n    spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:mat', at: [spot[0], 0, spot[1]], yaw: 0 });\\n  }\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:pillar', at: [-6, 0, -4], yaw: 0 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:pillar', at: [6, 0, -4], yaw: 0 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:bench', at: [4, 0, -8], yaw: 0.2 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:bench', at: [-4, 0, 14], yaw: -0.2 });\\n  for (const station of STATIONS) {\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: station.x, y: 1.2, z: station.z, kind: 'station', text: station.id, taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n  }\\n  for (const plaque of PLAQUES) {\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: plaque.x, y: 1.1, z: plaque.z, kind: 'plaque', text: plaque.text, taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n  }\\n  for (const pebble of PEBBLES) {\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: pebble.x, y: 0.3, z: pebble.z, kind: 'pebble', text: 'find.pebble', taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n  }\\n  spawnActor(w, {\\n    at: [0, 40, 6],\\n    player: false,\\n    yaw: Math.PI,\\n    character: createCharacter({ speed: 5.5 }),\\n    anim: { build: 'build:retreat' },\\n    clips: {\\n      sets: ['clipset:retreat'],\\n      play: { clip: 'RETREAT/Nothing', speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, loop: false },\\n    },\\n    components: { role: { who: 'guest' }, posed: { on: 0 } },\\n  });\\n  person(w, 'plumb', 2.2, 4, Math.PI);\\n  person(w, 'tare', -2.2, 5, 0);\\n  person(w, 'gerald', 8, -2, 1);\\n  person(w, 'bex', -8, 0, 0.4);\\n  person(w, 'nan', 5, 10, 2);\\n  w.systems.add('retreat.dress', dress, { phase: 'rules' });\\n}\\n\\n/** Sea bob, pebble pickup, and the pose scrub. Runs after the clips have stepped. */\\nfunction dress(w: World): void {\\n  for (const row of w.query('sceneProp') as unknown as Sea[]) {\\n    if (row.sceneProp.prop === 'prop:sea') row.sceneProp.y = 2 + 0.06 * Math.sin(w.time * 0.35);\\n  }\\n  const who = guest(w);\\n  if (!who) return;\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  if (flow.mode === 'roam') {\\n    for (const spot of w.query('mark') as unknown as Spot[]) {\\n      if (spot.mark.kind !== 'pebble' || spot.mark.taken) continue;\\n      if (flat(who.actor.x, who.actor.z, spot.mark.x, spot.mark.z) < 1.5) {\\n        spot.mark.taken = 1;\\n        flow.pebbles += 1;\\n        flow.line = 'find.pebble';\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n  scrub(w, who);\\n}\\n\\n/** Writes the lean and the pose onto the clip slots. */\\nfunction scrub(w: World, who: Body): void {\\n  const slots = who.clips?.state?.slots;\\n  if (!who.posed?.on) {\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanR', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanL', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanF', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanB', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    if (who.posed) who.posed.on = 1;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (!slots) return;\\n  const rows = w.query('wobble') as unknown as { wobble: { x: number; y: number; seat: number } }[];\\n  const body = rows.find((row) => row.wobble.seat === 0)?.wobble;\\n  const x = body?.x ?? 0;\\n  const y = body?.y ?? 0;\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  const pose = flowOf(w).event.startsWith('pose') ? Math.min(1, act.hold / (12 * 60)) : 0;\\n  for (const slot of slots) {\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanR') slot.t = Math.max(0, x);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanL') slot.t = Math.max(0, -x);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanF') slot.t = Math.max(0, y);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanB') slot.t = Math.max(0, -y);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/Heron') slot.t = pose;\\n  }\\n\",\"total_lines\":321}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"ec3c3819-7c14-40ef-b2e4-f2309e538307"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_995","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"An important finding was identified at line 111 of island.ts.\n\nThe plan claims plaques creep downhill, but the code comment explicitly states they do not. The actual counts are far lower than planned: only 4 \"did you know\" plaques and 2 notice plaques instead of 12, plus only 4 hidden pebbles rather than 20. These items were not included in the cut line, so it is unclear whether they are core requirements or optional polish.\n\nThe acceptance criterion explicitly requires creeping plaques. The code only implements static plaques that claim to move. This appears to be a direct contradiction of the requirement.\n\nThe instructions explicitly require refuting when a feature is a stub, placeholder, or dead code. The code comment is an admission that plaques creep nowhere. This raises the question of whether creeping plaques is a core objective or merely optional polish.\n\nThe objective is to complete everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer. Creeping plaques are in the plan and executable here, but they were excluded from the cut line.\n\nThe skeptic instructions caution against inventing requirements beyond the contract. The derived checklist criterion is passed because hidden pebbles and plaques do exist; they simply do not creep. Refuting this for missing edge cases would be a false refutation.\n\nThe contract is OBJECTIVE, defined by STAGE.md, PLAN.md, and TASK.md. PLAN.md explicitly requires plaques that creep downhill and 20 pebbles with 12 plaques. The acceptance criteria may clarify but cannot narrow or override the objective. I must judge core requirements in PLAN.md directly rather than relying solely on the shortened acceptance criteria. I also need to determine the core intent before deciding whether a plan gap actually misses it.\n\nThe core intent is a complete Wii Fit-inspired balance retreat with activities, the balance verb, and the five-day structure. Hidden pebbles and creeping plaques are exploration flavor in section 5. The \"creep nowhere\" comment is a deliberate omission rather than an oversight. Criterion 3 only requires their existence, not movement.\n\nThe word \"creeping\" is an adjective, so a static plaque cannot satisfy it. The user's instruction to implement everything in PLAN.md that can be done creates a very broad bar. If I were to refute every unmet detail in the plan, I would find many more issues than just plaques and pebbles.\n\nThe search for refutable gaps continues across the plan. Cast lines, bench meditation, and wave interactions are missing. Tilt mechanics, group classes, Day 4 depth, pose classes, morning checks, pond lures, sand garden trays, The Line, paddle glide, songs, and total line count all appear unimplemented or cut.\n\nCredits include licenses. Dev sliders are all tunables. Keyboard rebind is present. The ferry line cannot be called again. Outfits always save as empty arrays.\n\nThe focus is shifting from missing content counts to hunting for actual logic bugs that make the game wrong.\n\nThe cut line never explicitly removes plaques or pebbles, so their absence is an unimplemented plan feature. This is the first verification round, so raising it is appropriate. The instructions forbid refuting missing edge cases or extra scope, and require returning Not Refuted when every criterion is met. Criterion 3 explicitly demands creeping plaques, which the code contradicts.\n\nThe static plaques are a direct miss of both the acceptance criterion and PLAN.md. I am now hunting for clearer functional bugs in stepBalance, morning checks, pond lures, group classes, pose poses, save/restore, settings reset, query strips, and line seed quotes. I confirmed the HTML rebuild included the hub.ts pump. The browser log shows `reset gain None`.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-51b4b888-a8c8-40dd-adb7-ac72ea49a339-48","nam