{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3f75f6ee-0cee-4556-bb5e-4fc0123bf8e3-79","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3f75f6ee-0cee-4556-bb5e-4fc0123bf8e3-80","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3f75f6ee-0cee-4556-bb5e-4fc0123bf8e3-81","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n10→  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n10→  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/hub/session-client.txt\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":15,\"raw_output\":\"/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n\",\"total_lines\":488}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3f75f6ee-0cee-4556-bb5e-4fc0123bf8e3-82","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Engine feedback: thumb-yoga\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at e7a1243) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n- Let a page add a mesh. The retreat needed a readable guest and a few simple solids. There is no public way to register a generated mesh, so the body stays on the engine humanoid and the props stay on the built-in parts. A `geometry:cylinder` is also missing. A frustum stood in for a post.\\n10→- Start the music bus at 0.1, or let `createAudio` take a default. The bus comes up at 0.5. This game has to call `audio.volume('music', 0.1)` before a save can raise it, because a fresh stay must be a tenth.\\n- `playClip` during `setup` throws. A rest pose queued from setup never starts. Clips are played at spawn instead. Setup should accept the same call, or the error should say to wait for spawn.\\n- `spawnProp` with no yaw builds a NaN quaternion and the sim blows up. Yaw should default to 0. Every prop in this game passes one.\\n- A prop part's offset field is `position`. Code that says `at`, which the rest of the engine uses, is ignored and the part sits on the origin. One name would do.\\n- `headlessHost(engine).session.world` is a frozen recording. The live world is `createAppHost(...).session.world`, and `inspector.seed()` replaces that session, so a cached world goes stale. The frozen view should be named as a recording, and `seed` should say that old handles die.\\n- Query keys the engine does not know fail the boot. An AI Hub page arrives with `?aihub=1` and friends. Those keys have to be stripped from the string passed to `createEngine` or the page never starts. Unknown keys could be ignored.\\n- `input.prompt` is Xbox. A game whose default glyphs are PlayStation cannot use it. The prompt should follow the pad the browser reported, or the page should be able to set the family.\\n- `touch=off` hides the touch layer but `createTouchLayer` still appends `.touch-stick`. A count of that class is 1 on a page that never draws a stick. The page removes `.touch-layer` after `createEngine`. A flag on `createEngine`, or skipping the node when touch is off, would match the setting.\\n- `gfx.resolution=auto`, when the look names no resolution, becomes `pixels` and caps the buffer around 330 lines. A check that the drawing buffer matches the view then fails on a correct page. `full` has to be set by hand.\\n- There is no `inspector.reset`. Live sliders put the defaults back by reading `describe('setting', path)` and calling `set`. A reset that restores every `game.*` default would match the dev-mode job.\\n20→- `node x new` prints `NEW_DOCS` lines about `labs/playground/…` even when the entry is written and its test passes. The docs check is tripping over its own guide. Those lines should not look like a failed command.\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n- `input.pressed` is one sample for the whole drawn frame, and a catch-up step can take that sample before `onFrame` reads it. `uiAccept` does not repeat, so holding Cross never confirms if the edge was already consumed. A short Enter tap then leaves the title on Begin with an empty `__engine.errors`. The page treats a new hold of `uiAccept`, `uiCancel`, or `pause`, when `pressed` is false, as that edge. Up and Down already repeat after 0.35 s.\\n- From `labs/game/scenes/*.ts` the sim API is `../../../engine/sim-api`. From `labs/game/scenes/events/*.ts` it is `../../../../engine/sim-api`. There is no alias. The first import, one folder short, typechecks as a missing module and the event never loads.\\n- `createMenu` will show more than six rows. A 10-foot page has to slice the list itself.\\n- The hard line cap is 600. The fetched hub round, plus the `@file` comment this repo requires, was 603 lines and `eslint` failed `hard-cap/max-lines`. The protocol file should be allowed to stay the file the hub shipped. The comment was shortened so the cap would pass. Behaviour was not changed.\\n- The plan pinned session-client SHA-256 `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a`. The file fetched from the raw URL banners 1.4.0 and hashes to `6ab6be43898e2db069bc21a94757d77d9c3f2a0cb76f01186490d3bd88d8717a`. The banner did not move when the bytes did.\\n\\n30→## Local engine patches\\n\\nNone. No file under `engine/` was edited. `npm run check` should still match `engine-lock.json`.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Engine feedback: thumb-yoga\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at e7a1243) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n- Let a page add a mesh. The retreat needed a readable guest and a few simple solids. There is no public way to register a generated mesh, so the body stays on the engine humanoid and the props stay on the built-in parts. A `geometry:cylinder` is also missing. A frustum stood in for a post.\\n10→- Start the music bus at 0.1, or let `createAudio` take a default. The bus comes up at 0.5. This game has to call `audio.volume('music', 0.1)` before a save can raise it, because a fresh stay must be a tenth.\\n- `playClip` during `setup` throws. A rest pose queued from setup never starts. Clips are played at spawn instead. Setup should accept the same call, or the error should say to wait for spawn.\\n- `spawnProp` with no yaw builds a NaN quaternion and the sim blows up. Yaw should default to 0. Every prop in this game passes one.\\n- A prop part's offset field is `position`. Code that says `at`, which the rest of the engine uses, is ignored and the part sits on the origin. One name would do.\\n- `headlessHost(engine).session.world` is a frozen recording. The live world is `createAppHost(...).session.world`, and `inspector.seed()` replaces that session, so a cached world goes stale. The frozen view should be named as a recording, and `seed` should say that old handles die.\\n- Query keys the engine does not know fail the boot. An AI Hub page arrives with `?aihub=1` and friends. Those keys have to be stripped from the string passed to `createEngine` or the page never starts. Unknown keys could be ignored.\\n- `input.prompt` is Xbox. A game whose default glyphs are PlayStation cannot use it. The prompt should follow the pad the browser reported, or the page should be able to set the family.\\n- `touch=off` hides the touch layer but `createTouchLayer` still appends `.touch-stick`. A count of that class is 1 on a page that never draws a stick. The page removes `.touch-layer` after `createEngine`. A flag on `createEngine`, or skipping the node when touch is off, would match the setting.\\n- `gfx.resolution=auto`, when the look names no resolution, becomes `pixels` and caps the buffer around 330 lines. A check that the drawing buffer matches the view then fails on a correct page. `full` has to be set by hand.\\n- There is no `inspector.reset`. Live sliders put the defaults back by reading `describe('setting', path)` and calling `set`. A reset that restores every `game.*` default would match the dev-mode job.\\n20→- `node x new` prints `NEW_DOCS` lines about `labs/playground/…` even when the entry is written and its test passes. The docs check is tripping over its own guide. Those lines should not look like a failed command.\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n- `input.pressed` is one sample for the whole drawn frame, and a catch-up step can take that sample before `onFrame` reads it. `uiAccept` does not repeat, so holding Cross never confirms if the edge was already consumed. A short Enter tap then leaves the title on Begin with an empty `__engine.errors`. The page treats a new hold of `uiAccept`, `uiCancel`, or `pause`, when `pressed` is false, as that edge. Up and Down already repeat after 0.35 s.\\n- From `labs/game/scenes/*.ts` the sim API is `../../../engine/sim-api`. From `labs/game/scenes/events/*.ts` it is `../../../../engine/sim-api`. There is no alias. The first import, one folder short, typechecks as a missing module and the event never loads.\\n- `createMenu` will show more than six rows. A 10-foot page has to slice the list itself.\\n- The hard line cap is 600. The fetched hub round, plus the `@file` comment this repo requires, was 603 lines and `eslint` failed `hard-cap/max-lines`. The protocol file should be allowed to stay the file the hub shipped. The comment was shortened so the cap would pass. Behaviour was not changed.\\n- The plan pinned session-client SHA-256 `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a`. The file fetched from the raw URL banners 1.4.0 and hashes to `6ab6be43898e2db069bc21a94757d77d9c3f2a0cb76f01186490d3bd88d8717a`. The banner did not move when the bytes did.\\n\\n30→## Local engine patches\\n\\nNone. No file under `engine/` was edited. `npm run check` should still match `engine-lock.json`.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"# Engine feedback: thumb-yoga\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at e7a1243) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n- Let a page add a mesh. The retreat needed a readable guest and a few simple solids. There is no public way to register a generated mesh, so the body stays on the engine humanoid and the props stay on the built-in parts. A `geometry:cylinder` is also missing. A frustum stood in for a post.\\n- Start the music bus at 0.1, or let `createAudio` take a default. The bus comes up at 0.5. This game has to call `audio.volume('music', 0.1)` before a save can raise it, because a fresh stay must be a tenth.\\n- `playClip` during `setup` throws. A rest pose queued from setup never starts. Clips are played at spawn instead. Setup should accept the same call, or the error should say to wait for spawn.\\n- `spawnProp` with no yaw builds a NaN quaternion and the sim blows up. Yaw should default to 0. Every prop in this game passes one.\\n- A prop part's offset field is `position`. Code that says `at`, which the rest of the engine uses, is ignored and the part sits on the origin. One name would do.\\n- `headlessHost(engine).session.world` is a frozen recording. The live world is `createAppHost(...).session.world`, and `inspector.seed()` replaces that session, so a cached world goes stale. The frozen view should be named as a recording, and `seed` should say that old handles die.\\n- Query keys the engine does not know fail the boot. An AI Hub page arrives with `?aihub=1` and friends. Those keys have to be stripped from the string passed to `createEngine` or the page never starts. Unknown keys could be ignored.\\n- `input.prompt` is Xbox. A game whose default glyphs are PlayStation cannot use it. The prompt should follow the pad the browser reported, or the page should be able to set the family.\\n- `touch=off` hides the touch layer but `createTouchLayer` still appends `.touch-stick`. A count of that class is 1 on a page that never draws a stick. The page removes `.touch-layer` after `createEngine`. A flag on `createEngine`, or skipping the node when touch is off, would match the setting.\\n- `gfx.resolution=auto`, when the look names no resolution, becomes `pixels` and caps the buffer around 330 lines. A check that the drawing buffer matches the view then fails on a correct page. `full` has to be set by hand.\\n- There is no `inspector.reset`. Live sliders put the defaults back by reading `describe('setting', path)` and calling `set`. A reset that restores every `game.*` default would match the dev-mode job.\\n- `node x new` prints `NEW_DOCS` lines about `labs/playground/…` even when the entry is written and its test passes. The docs check is tripping over its own guide. Those lines should not look like a failed command.\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n- `input.pressed` is one sample for the whole drawn frame, and a catch-up step can take that sample before `onFrame` reads it. `uiAccept` does not repeat, so holding Cross never confirms if the edge was already consumed. A short Enter tap then leaves the title on Begin with an empty `__engine.errors`. The page treats a new hold of `uiAccept`, `uiCancel`, or `pause`, when `pressed` is false, as that edge. Up and Down already repeat after 0.35 s.\\n- From `labs/game/scenes/*.ts` the sim API is `../../../engine/sim-api`. From `labs/game/scenes/events/*.ts` it is `../../../../engine/sim-api`. There is no alias. The first import, one folder short, typechecks as a missing module and the event never loads.\\n- `createMenu` will show more than six rows. A 10-foot page has to slice the list itself.\\n- The hard line cap is 600. The fetched hub round, plus the `@file` comment this repo requires, was 603 lines and `eslint` failed `hard-cap/max-lines`. The protocol file should be allowed to stay the file the hub shipped. The comment was shortened so the cap would pass. Behaviour was not changed.\\n- The plan pinned session-client SHA-256 `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a`. The file fetched from the raw URL banners 1.4.0 and hashes to `6ab6be43898e2db069bc21a94757d77d9c3f2a0cb76f01186490d3bd88d8717a`. The banner did not move when the bytes did.\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\nNone. No file under `engine/` was edited. `npm run check` should still match `engine-lock.json`.\\n\",\"total_lines\":32}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3f75f6ee-0cee-4556-bb5e-4fc0123bf8e3-83","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Thumb Yoga\\n\\nA five-day balance retreat at Little Fulcrum, for one player or a couch of four. The only verb is where your weight sits inside a unit disc. Lean with the left stick, WASD, or a pointer-locked mouse. L2 and R2, or Q and E, are the feet. Both feet, or Space, breathe. Toppling recentres you. It is not a game over. Nothing here scores weight, size, or calories.\\n\\nThe days are a morning check, pose class, a pond, a sand garden, a paddle, a slackline, a group class, and a storm that tilts the island. Pebbles stack on a cairn. They are never spent. After the credits the ferry does not come back. Free play and a new morning remain.\\n\\n## See it\\n\\nFrom this workspace:\\n10→\\n```sh\\nnpm run dev\\nnode labs/game/tools/verify.mjs\\nnpm test\\nnpm run check\\n```\\n\\n`verify.mjs` runs the balance bands, the three-seed walk to the credits, the song and syllable renders, and the golden replay. Without `--quick` it also builds `../Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656.html` and drives that file. The HTML opens from `file://` and fetches nothing.\\n\\n20→A hub session is the same file, served beside `labs/game/hub/harness.html`. The mode is ghost. Empty mats on a local Group Class are staff unless Settings turns them off.\\n\\n## Calls\\n\\n- The title was drawn from `titles.json` (50 names). The pick is Thumb Yoga, index 16.\\n- Great Tilt's counterweights, expert variants, outfits, Hoop Patrol, Reps Hall, Island Jog's race, Cliff Plunge, and Step Class are cut. The walk around the island stays. The day list is the five days in `scenes/data/days.ts`.\\n- Group Class is a still hold, Heron, and the pond. Its score is the mean of those three, from 0 to 1000, so the same ranks apply. The plan also described a sum to 3000. The mean is the one that fits a rank.\\n- The island grid is 60 by 60 with cell size 4 (240 m). A finer cell made the SwiftShader boot too slow for a hub `ready()`.\\n- The session client is pasted unmodified. Its hash does not match the older pin. The fetched bytes are the ones in the page. See `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`.\\n- Music on a fresh save is a tenth. The engine's bus default is a half, so the page sets the volume before the save is applied.\\n30→- The engine tree was not modified.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Thumb Yoga\\n\\nA five-day balance retreat at Little Fulcrum, for one player or a couch of four. The only verb is where your weight sits inside a unit disc. Lean with the left stick, WASD, or a pointer-locked mouse. L2 and R2, or Q and E, are the feet. Both feet, or Space, breathe. Toppling recentres you. It is not a game over. Nothing here scores weight, size, or calories.\\n\\nThe days are a morning check, pose class, a pond, a sand garden, a paddle, a slackline, a group class, and a storm that tilts the island. Pebbles stack on a cairn. They are never spent. After the credits the ferry does not come back. Free play and a new morning remain.\\n\\n## See it\\n\\nFrom this workspace:\\n10→\\n```sh\\nnpm run dev\\nnode labs/game/tools/verify.mjs\\nnpm test\\nnpm run check\\n```\\n\\n`verify.mjs` runs the balance bands, the three-seed walk to the credits, the song and syllable renders, and the golden replay. Without `--quick` it also builds `../Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656.html` and drives that file. The HTML opens from `file://` and fetches nothing.\\n\\n20→A hub session is the same file, served beside `labs/game/hub/harness.html`. The mode is ghost. Empty mats on a local Group Class are staff unless Settings turns them off.\\n\\n## Calls\\n\\n- The title was drawn from `titles.json` (50 names). The pick is Thumb Yoga, index 16.\\n- Great Tilt's counterweights, expert variants, outfits, Hoop Patrol, Reps Hall, Island Jog's race, Cliff Plunge, and Step Class are cut. The walk around the island stays. The day list is the five days in `scenes/data/days.ts`.\\n- Group Class is a still hold, Heron, and the pond. Its score is the mean of those three, from 0 to 1000, so the same ranks apply. The plan also described a sum to 3000. The mean is the one that fits a rank.\\n- The island grid is 60 by 60 with cell size 4 (240 m). A finer cell made the SwiftShader boot too slow for a hub `ready()`.\\n- The session client is pasted unmodified. Its hash does not match the older pin. The fetched bytes are the ones in the page. See `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`.\\n- Music on a fresh save is a tenth. The engine's bus default is a half, so the page sets the volume before the save is applied.\\n30→- The engine tree was not modified.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/README.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"# Thumb Yoga\\n\\nA five-day balance retreat at Little Fulcrum, for one player or a couch of four. The only verb is where your weight sits inside a unit disc. Lean with the left stick, WASD, or a pointer-locked mouse. L2 and R2, or Q and E, are the feet. Both feet, or Space, breathe. Toppling recentres you. It is not a game over. Nothing here scores weight, size, or calories.\\n\\nThe days are a morning check, pose class, a pond, a sand garden, a paddle, a slackline, a group class, and a storm that tilts the island. Pebbles stack on a cairn. They are never spent. After the credits the ferry does not come back. Free play and a new morning remain.\\n\\n## See it\\n\\nFrom this workspace:\\n\\n```sh\\nnpm run dev\\nnode labs/game/tools/verify.mjs\\nnpm test\\nnpm run check\\n```\\n\\n`verify.mjs` runs the balance bands, the three-seed walk to the credits, the song and syllable renders, and the golden replay. Without `--quick` it also builds `../Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656.html` and drives that file. The HTML opens from `file://` and fetches nothing.\\n\\nA hub session is the same file, served beside `labs/game/hub/harness.html`. The mode is ghost. Empty mats on a local Group Class are staff unless Settings turns them off.\\n\\n## Calls\\n\\n- The title was drawn from `titles.json` (50 names). The pick is Thumb Yoga, index 16.\\n- Great Tilt's counterweights, expert variants, outfits, Hoop Patrol, Reps Hall, Island Jog's race, Cliff Plunge, and Step Class are cut. The walk around the island stays. The day list is the five days in `scenes/data/days.ts`.\\n- Group Class is a still hold, Heron, and the pond. Its score is the mean of those three, from 0 to 1000, so the same ranks apply. The plan also described a sum to 3000. The mean is the one that fits a rank.\\n- The island grid is 60 by 60 with cell size 4 (240 m). A finer cell made the SwiftShader boot too slow for a hub `ready()`.\\n- The session client is pasted unmodified. Its hash does not match the older pin. The fetched bytes are the ones in the page. See `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`.\\n- Music on a fresh save is a tenth. The engine's bus default is a half, so the page sets the volume before the save is applied.\\n- The engine tree was not modified.\\n\",\"total_lines\":30}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"da4fe8a0-80a6-4f4b-ab37-410a01c0ae52"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1005","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The HTML grep for the pump comment found nothing.\n\nThe \"still compiling\" comment is absent from the HTML because bundlers strip comments. I am now searching for a surviving string like \"Breathing in\" to locate the pump code.\n\nThe \"Breathing in\" string might predate the pump fix. I will check the hub.ts patch or git diff to confirm the change. The verify script already built the HTML that passed the hub test, so the pump is present in that bundle.\n\nI will check the HTML file timestamp to confirm it matches the verify log. I am also searching for a setInterval pattern or \"Breathing in\" to locate the pump code. The pose scrub check is being reviewed once more to make the finding airtight. In island.ts, setting speed to 0 on the RETREAT/Nothing clip prevents it from advancing.\n\nThe engine semantics for speed 0 and hold true are ambiguous. If the clip freezes at the first keyframe, the body remains in a static rest pose and never advances. In that case, pose clips would never play and lean additives would scrub. If the engine snaps to the end instead, the Nothing pose becomes a fixed seated squat that ignores pose progress.\n\nEither engine interpretation leaves the body frozen as a single squat pose. This violates the scrub-following-criterion for all eight poses.\n\nThe Heron slot is never started. Its progress formula divides by 720.\n\nCreeping plaques are inactive code. Island tilt is hardcoded and ignores delivered guests.\n\nThe everyone-east step is real because guests move and score deliveries. The tilt reduction is a separate PLAN section bug because game.tilt.rate is wired to nothing. The pose scrub remains the decisive core issue. Hidden pebbles are 4, not 20.\n\nThe 20-pebble count is in PLAN.md section 5. The OBJECTIVE done condition is \"Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done.\" This is very broad. A skeptic could dispute dozens of missing PLAN details.\n\nThe guidance restricts refutations to gaps that miss the objective's core intent. Acceptance criteria form the derived checklist for judging met or unmet status. Pose scrub is explicitly required by acceptance criteria 2 and 3, so it qualifies as a core omission.\n\nCreeping plaques are explicitly named in criterion 3, so that no-op counts as a bug. The tilt.rate control is a shipped feature with no effect; the everyone-east deed also fails to reduce tilt, which PLAN.md promises it should do. I will limit the final findings to actionable gaps and avoid listing every PLAN detail.\n\nThe pose scrub test never checks that clip time advances. This missing coverage is a valid refutation because the repository can test animation.\n\nThe pose scrub bug is confirmed by the formula itself. During pose entry, act.hold rises from 0 to 1, but the progress value divides by 720, so it stays near zero even if a clip were playing. This makes the bug demonstrable without running the simulation.\n\nA save bug prevents pebble finds from persisting. The `remember()` function only records finds for line type `find.pebble`, and `applySave` never restores the taken state. On reload, the four pebbles respawn as untaken, so the player can collect them again and double-count them.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5eade83f-d19e-46bb-b328-275a8e33809c-84","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/menus.ts","offset":80,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5eade83f-d19e-46bb-b328-275a8e33809c-85","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"prior","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui","glob":"*.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,