{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1013","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wobble Age is calculated and stored in __game but never displayed in the UI.\n\nThe age is never spoken or displayed during the Morning Check. The distinctive Wii Fit Age parody is invisible despite being a named feature. This is a completeness bug. It is unclear whether showing it on screen is required.\n\nThe plan requires a dial, remark, calendar stamp, and graph for the Morning Check. The age is computed and saved but never revealed. Players see only the 0-1000 score. This makes the feature unplayable.\n\nThe prior Wobble Age is also absent from the snap. The simulation stores it but never displays it.\n\nPose scrubbing in island.ts is broken. Pose clips are not scrubbed. The guest remains stuck on RETREAT/Nothing at speed zero. The Heron slot write targets a clip that is never played. The hold duration calculation yields roughly zero. This violates criteria two and three.\n\nPlaques in island.ts:111 remain motionless. This violates the creeping plaques criterion.\n\nThe save routine omits prior Wobble Age entirely. Yesterday's age cannot survive a reload.\n\nThe morning.ts script never sets an age line. The stage.ts results copy only carries rank, score, and sentence.\n\nScore.ts line 53 is dead code.\n\nThe Wobble Age display gap may be treated as polish rather than a core bug.\n\nThe Wobble Age display gap will be cited as a primary flow bug because the player-facing reveal is missing.\n\nTilt rate is hardcoded in tilt.ts and settings.ts. The Phase 1 delivery never writes to it. PLAN section 7 covers this.\n\nThe everyone-east and centre-stone following CoB behaviors are working correctly.\n\nThe tilt rate slider is a dead control. Criterion 4 requires dev sliders to change live game behavior for numeric `game.*` tunables. Moving the slider does nothing even though its description claims it alters storm lean. This violates the live-control requirement.\n\nPebble count is not a separate nit. It is folded into the plaques finding.\n\nOnly four pebbles exist. The save stores them as one generic id. The driver ignores finds during applySave. Pebble marks respawn and can be collected again.\n\nThis is a shipped behavior defect, not an untested edge case. Criterion 3 explicitly requires finds to be restored into the world alongside pebbles and outfits.\n\nOutfits are always empty because the feature was cut. This is correct behavior.\n\nThe verdict will be refuted with concrete findings.\n\nBands tests drive real code. They are not dishonest.\n\nThe pose scrub bug has no test coverage. I will ask them to fix it and add a test that plays a pose on the island scene. The test should assert the active pose clip time advances with hold progress and the clip id matches the pose. If the test cannot drive the unit directly, they should refactor into a callable unit.\n\nThe scrub function is internal to island.ts and unexported. A test can boot the island scene, start a pose, step with a bot, and read the guest's clip slots directly. If those slots are not observable, the scrub selection should be refactored into a pure function.\n\nThe HTML client check passed with zero failures. The hash mismatch is documented and PLAN.md allows fetched bytes to win, so it does not constitute a refute. Boot evidence matches the latest log. Hub and tests passed. The pose hold duration is confirmed to reset to zero at phase transitions and never increment during phase one.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-798fae21-1ce4-4096-bf35-9a608bce5d17-97","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"tiltX|tiltZ|island\\.base","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game","glob":"*.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":879,"output_tokens":1729,"cache_read_input_tokens":166272,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"9ff8a7ad-7c72-4581-aa95-0c315613701a"}
