{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1024","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to understand how marks are drawn so that moving plaques remain visible.\n\nI am weighing four ways to consume tilt: slope push, camera roll, prop knock, or sea counter-rotation. The centre stone writes tiltX and tiltZ from body position. I need a visible consumer so non-zero CoB changes the output. I will pick the best one for headless testing.\n\nSea prop rotation, slope push on guest moves, and prop drift are the three visible consumers under consideration. The bench scene lacks the island's sea and guest actor, so the test must target the island scene.\n\nBench.ts needs checking to confirm the sea prop exists there. The slope push in roam() is blocked during tilt because the mode switches to event and movement zeroes out. This leaves sea counter-rotation as the only viable visible consumer for the test.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fde9e77e-ccaa-4e7c-9a43-96535a8cf79e-103","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"sceneProp","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine","glob":"*.ts","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fde9e77e-ccaa-4e7c-9a43-96535a8cf79e-104","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/bench.ts","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fde9e77e-ccaa-4e7c-9a43-96535a8cf79e-105","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"mark\\.|kind === 'plaque'|drawMark|prop:plaque","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game","glob":"*.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fde9e77e-ccaa-4e7c-9a43-96535a8cf79e-106","name":"read_file","input":{"target_