18-3308a1dd51dc/terminal/call-c2a580e2-d008-4cf1-b0b3-e2016bb90e53-127.log\",\"total_bytes\":984}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"1ae49fbb-d564-4a14-bb2d-035ff7fff40d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1033","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"stage.ts is 598 lines, just under the 600-line hard cap. Any additions must be matched one-for-one or the file must shrink.\n\nLogic will move from remember into save.ts to reduce stage.ts. Island scrub needs care because playClip might throw before clips are ready. The first day age remark in score.ts and the finishEvent logic in driver.ts are also being updated.\n\ntilt.ts will handle rate and delivery. island.ts needs plaques, pebble IDs, pose scrub, sea quaternion, and slope. snap.ts needs prior state, finds, and resultCopy. save.ts needs noteProgress. stage.ts will integrate all of this while staying under 600 lines. Tests are next. A helper will let island.ts query the Island component for slope in roam. The Sea interface is gaining a q field, and a seaTurn quaternion function is being added.\n\nThe seaTurn quaternion is being derived from the sea's tilt angles. It applies a counter-rotation around the Z axis to offset the ground's roll, ensuring the sea stays level beneath the island.\n\nThe sea quaternion is being corrected to use the proper axes. tiltX maps to rotation around Z, and tiltZ maps to rotation around X. The sea's counter-rotation is the negative of both angles, applied in the order Z then X.\n\nThe sea quaternion will be set by querying the island's tiltX and tiltZ, then calling seaTurn. Plaques are being positioned with west offset calculated from the current day.\n\nPlaques are placed by matching mark text to the home list and offsetting west. Pebbles will use unique text. The scrub logic is being rewritten. In roam, slope is derived from tiltX as a downhill force that subtracts from movement; title mode skips this so the guest stays still.\n\ndriver.ts will store the prior age before wobbling in finishEvent, then compute the age line with a new ageLine helper. That helper compares yesterday's age to today's and returns an id such as 'age.first', 'age.down', or 'age.same'. The first line of score.ts's ageRemark will also include the age number.\n\nThe existing bounds test does not verify the age remark string. The morning event check in finishEvent runs before the mode switches to results, so the line update will take effect. The remember block in stage.ts will import noteProgress from save.ts.\n\nsnap.ts will import ageRemark from ../scenes/score. noteProgress will accept a Snap type from snap.ts to avoid circular dependencies. stage.ts will import noteProgress from save.ts and resultCopy from snap.ts.\n\nThe save key does not need to change because pebbles are already included. Prior must be set on the save object before writing, since the morning finish updates mode and result.\n\nThe save key will include finds so a restored pebble paired with a new find is not missed. The remember block returns early for hub and attract modes. game.begin spreads kept state, which now carries prior and finds, and applySave handles both fields.\n\napplyFinds reads the restored finds array. During continue, marks are already taken, so a restored pebble cannot be picked up again while the player is still in an event; pickup only happens once they enter roam. The test will follow the same sequence: fresh furnish, then begin. Pickup will use the unique pebble ID instead of text.\n\nA compact poseClip helper is being drafted for island.ts scrub. It builds a clip name from the current pose ID. A matching poseProgress helper will return the actor's pose index.\n\nposeProgress now returns 0 while the actor is idle, 1 during the pose hold phase scaled by the pose duration, and 1 once the pose ends. The posesFor lookup is acceptable for clarity. A play options constant is being added, and the Body interface path for clip state slots is being verified.\n\nplayClip mutates the component in place, so who.clips is the correct target. If slots is undefined after playback, the scrub will skip and be fixed later. A lean pose and a pose change can occur on the same frame. When a pose clip is missing from slots, it is played and its time is scrubbed; the layer may blend underneath, but the top clip should remain active.\n\nThe scrub logic will only set the time on the current clip, so a lingering idle pose underneath does not interfere. A mismatch between the expected slot name and the actual clip string could restart the pose every frame; the test will log the real names to diagnose this.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-36980934-552c-455c-8b08-f769df0f5cb9-128","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"clip:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/anim/clip","glob":"*layer*"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2804,"output_tokens":2826,"cache_read_input_tokens":197376,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"3bd038f7-9ce9-4b86-9e55-27f0791ce3c7"}
