,"is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"262b7894-8123-4d23-bc7e-0f186af97c0b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1043","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"An island.test.ts file already exists in the current folder.\n\nReading island.test.ts now. Need to verify how move direction maps to axes so downhill push uses negative x for westward tilt. The sea counter-rotation is the visible tilt consumer; slope is an additional effect. The test should confirm that a non-zero CoB changes the consumed tilt.\n\nThe primary test compares consumed sea quaternion between zero and full stick during the stone phase. Delivery -0.5 also shifts tilt. Storm uses game.tilt.rate. Sea quaternion is the chosen design; it avoids engine edits. The sea counter-rotates while island geometry stays fixed, so the horizon appears level and only the sea tilts.\n\nThe PLAN explicitly states the island mesh never moves. Counter-rotating the sea alone would make the sea look tilted relative to the fixed island, not the island itself. The camera must roll with the island for the horizon to stay level while the island appears to tip.\n\nThe sea quaternion will be built from half angles using `ax = -tiltZ` and `az = -tiltX`, then multiplied as `qz * qx`. The test compares sea quaternion differences against tiltX changes across zero and full stick. Both sea counter-rotation and slope effects will be implemented.\n\nThe quaternion multiplication qZ * qx yields [cz*sx, -sz*sx, sz*cx, cz*cx].\n\nThe quaternion multiplication was corrected. The y component is positive sz*sx, so the sea quaternion is [cz*sx, sz*sx, sz*cx, cz*cx].\n\nThe sea quaternion is stored in Three.js order [x, y, z, w]. The base tilt of 0.4° means the sea is not perfectly level at rest; the test compares two runs to isolate the change from a non-zero CoB. Slope push is gated to roam mode or the stone phase of a tilt event.\n\nThe move-zeroing logic now allows tilt phase 1. Slope push subtracts `Math.sin(tiltX * π / 180)` from the horizontal move. Station naming is skipped during title and tilt events.\n\nDuring tilt phase 1, the player character drifts west because balance intents override move intents. Title mode must skip slope to prevent the player from drifting off-screen. Roam mode keeps the slope push.\n\nThe delivery test will use a jump tilt:east with one untaken guest set to follow=1 and x=59, then step once. TiltX should drop by 0.5, so it becomes -0.1 from the base 0.4°. Phase 1 does not write tiltX, and storm only affects phase 0, so the starting value is fixed at boot.\n\nThe delivery test needs act.px near the guest. Otherwise the mark lerps west before the x > 58 check and never delivers.\n\nThe delivery test will set act.px to 64 and mark.x to 59 so the guest lands within the 58 threshold. The island reference is needed in phase 1 to access tiltX. Storm tilt rate is read from game.tilt.rate.\n\nThe storm tilt formula is `base + (act.left / 60) * speed`, with a fallback rate of 0.15 and base 0.4°. The island type will include `base` and `tiltZ`. Changing the storm rate from 0.28 to 0.15 does not affect the score, since scoring depends on `act.a = 1` at storm end rather than the angle. Deed relief during storm is safe because deeds run in phase 1 while storm runs in phase 0.\n\nPhase 2 overwrites tilt from CoB every frame, so deed relief is intentionally lost during the stone phase; dawn zeroes it. Plaque marks shift west by `(day - 1) * 0.04` each day, but this is idempotent and harmless on day one. The test will set `flow.day` directly to three before stepping to verify the creep.\n\nThe test can either set flow.day directly and step once, or use game.jump to day 3. Both paths run the dress code and move plaques. The direct approach is simpler; the jump path is more realistic.\n\nThe test will set `flow.day` to 5 and step once. The dress code reads that value directly, so `game.jump` is unnecessary. A day-3 creep of 0.08 would place plaques at 5.92.\n\nThe Wobble Age system is being added to score.ts. ageRemark returns a first-time greeting when yesterday is zero, and ageLine compares today against yesterday to return 'age.first', 'age.down', 'age.up', or 'age.same'. finishEvent will store the prior day in flow.prior during the morning event.\n\nfinishEvent now stores the prior day and computes the age line. The first morning yields age 0 and line 'age.first', so existing tests remain valid. snap.ts is being extended to hold a prior field, and readSnap will populate it from the flow object.\n\nreadSnap now collects pebble finds by scanning marks for text starting with 'pebble:'. resultCopy prepends the Wobble Age remark to the score when the event is morning, then appends the rank line. The stage paint code renders this combined string in results mode.\n\nsave.ts is being updated to persist the new snap fields. noteProgress now copies day, cursor, pebbles, age, prior, credits, result, seen, rank, and finds into the save object.\n\nsave.ts now deduplicates pebble IDs in `finds` and updates the best score for the current event when the mode is results. The stage's `remember` function calls `noteProgress` to persist the snap before saving settings.\n\nThe save key now includes prior and finds. noteProgress preserves existing settings by spreading the save object before overwriting them. The remember function shrinks slightly because resultCopy replaces the old inline string. Stage.ts will be about 598 lines after these edits.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1873fc41-8887-45b0-acfb-c4279dcfbc0a-29","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/stage.ts","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1873fc41-8887-45b0-acfb-c4279dcfbc0a-30","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/island.test.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1873fc41-8887-45b0-acfb-c4279dcfbc0a-31","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/driver.ts","offset":1,"limit":60}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1873fc41-8887-45b0-acfb-c4279dcfbc0a-32","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"stickIntents","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/bot.ts","-A":25}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3081,"output_tokens":4456,"cache_read_input_tokens":64000,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"05160d07-af77-4b02-b65a-e8b1f8e614e3"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1873fc41-8887-45b0-acfb-c4279dcfbc0a-29","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The 10-foot shell. Attract, the touch gate, and the hub card sit over the sim.\\n * The sim stays in the scene. Menus and ghosts live in their own files.\\n */\\nimport {\\n  createMenu,\\n  type Audio,\\n  type Engine,\\n  type EngineFrame,\\n10→  type Inspector,\\n  type Menu,\\n  type MenuItem,\\n  type Store,\\n} from '../../../engine';\\nimport { say, speakerFor } from '../audio/voice';\\nimport { LURES } from '../scenes/data/lures';\\nimport { type GlyphSet, promptLine } from './glyphs';\\nimport { createHub, type HubClient, type HubView } from './hub';\\nimport { LINES } from './lines/book';\\n20→import { createMenus, type Host, type Live, type Menus } from './menus';\\nimport { freshPrefs, freshSave, readSave, writeSave, type Prefs } from './save';\\nimport { readSnap, runningScore, songFor, type Snap } from './snap';\\n\\n/** What tests read. The page fills it in the same frame as the input. */\\nexport interface GameHandle {\\n  title: 'Thumb Yoga';\\n  screen: string;\\n  attract: boolean;\\n  lastDevice: string;\\n30→  glyphSet: GlyphSet;\\n  volumes: { music: number; effects: number; voices: number };\\n  day: number;\\n  event: string;\\n  focus: string;\\n}\\n\\n/** How the page is built. */\\nexport interface PageOptions {\\n  audio: Audio;\\n40→  store: Store;\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The 10-foot shell. Attract, the touch gate, and the hub card sit over the sim.\\n * The sim stays in the scene. Menus and ghosts live in their own files.\\n */\\nimport {\\n  createMenu,\\n  type Audio,\\n  type Engine,\\n  type EngineFrame,\\n10→  type Inspector,\\n  type Menu,\\n  type MenuItem,\\n  type Store,\\n} from '../../../engine';\\nimport { say, speakerFor } from '../audio/voice';\\nimport { LURES } from '../scenes/data/lures';\\nimport { type GlyphSet, promptLine } from './glyphs';\\nimport { createHub, type HubClient, type HubView } from './hub';\\nimport { LINES } from './lines/book';\\n20→import { createMenus, type Host, type Live, type Menus } from './menus';\\nimport { freshPrefs, freshSave, readSave, writeSave, type Prefs } from './save';\\nimport { readSnap, runningScore, songFor, type Snap } from './snap';\\n\\n/** What tests read. The page fills it in the same frame as the input. */\\nexport interface GameHandle {\\n  title: 'Thumb Yoga';\\n  screen: string;\\n  attract: boolean;\\n  lastDevice: string;\\n30→  glyphSet: GlyphSet;\\n  volumes: { music: number; effects: number; voices: number };\\n  day: number;\\n  event: string;\\n  focus: string;\\n}\\n\\n/** How the page is built. */\\nexport interface PageOptions {\\n  audio: Audio;\\n40→  store: Store;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/stage.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The 10-foot shell. Attract, the touch gate, and the hub card sit over the sim.\\n * The sim stays in the scene. Menus and ghosts live in their own files.\\n */\\nimport {\\n  createMenu,\\n  type Audio,\\n  type Engine,\\n  type EngineFrame,\\n  type Inspector,\\n  type Menu,\\n  type MenuItem,\\n  type Store,\\n} from '../../../engine';\\nimport { say, speakerFor } from '../audio/voice';\\nimport { LURES } from '../scenes/data/lures';\\nimport { type GlyphSet, promptLine } from './glyphs';\\nimport { createHub, type HubClient, type HubView } from './hub';\\nimport { LINES } from './lines/book';\\nimport { createMenus, type Host, type Live, type Menus } from './menus';\\nimport { freshPrefs, freshSave, readSave, writeSave, type Prefs } from './save';\\nimport { readSnap, runningScore, songFor, type Snap } from './snap';\\n\\n/** What tests read. The page fills it in the same frame as the input. */\\nexport interface GameHandle {\\n  title: 'Thumb Yoga';\\n  screen: string;\\n  attract: boolean;\\n  lastDevice: string;\\n  glyphSet: GlyphSet;\\n  volumes: { music: number; effects: number; voices: number };\\n  day: number;\\n  event: string;\\n  focus: string;\\n}\\n\\n/** How the page is built. */\\nexport interface PageOptions {\\n  audio: Audio;\\n  store: Store;\\n\",\"total_lines\":598}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1873fc41-8887-45b0-acfb-c4279dcfbc0a-30","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The island and the pavilion boot through the shipped scenes and take a few steps.\\n */\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { createAppHost } from '../../engine/app/headless';\\nimport { island } from './scenes/island';\\nimport { round } from './scenes/round';\\n\\ndescribe('places', () => {\\n10→  it('boots the island and walks a step', () => {\\n    const run = createAppHost({ scene: island, seed: 1 });\\n    run.stepOnce({ move: [0, 1] });\\n    run.stepOnce({ move: [0, 1] });\\n    const world = run.session.world;\\n    expect(world.query('flow').length).toBe(1);\\n    expect(world.query('actor').length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    expect(world.query('mark').length).toBeGreaterThan(4);\\n  });\\n\\n20→  it('boots the pavilion and keeps a ghost seat', () => {\\n    const run = createAppHost({ scene: round, seed: 2 });\\n    run.stepOnce({ 'game:ghosts': [1, 1, 0.2, -0.1, 0, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0] });\\n    const world = run.session.world;\\n    const ghosts = world.query('ghost') as unknown as { ghost: { on: number; seat: number } }[];\\n    expect(ghosts.length).toBe(3);\\n    expect(ghosts.some((row) => row.ghost.seat === 1 && row.ghost.on === 1)).toBe(true);\\n  });\\n});\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The island and the pavilion boot through the shipped scenes and take a few steps.\\n */\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { createAppHost } from '../../engine/app/headless';\\nimport { island } from './scenes/island';\\nimport { round } from './scenes/round';\\n\\ndescribe('places', () => {\\n10→  it('boots the island and walks a step', () => {\\n    const run = createAppHost({ scene: island, seed: 1 });\\n    run.stepOnce({ move: [0, 1] });\\n    run.stepOnce({ move: [0, 1] });\\n    const world = run.session.world;\\n    expect(world.query('flow').length).toBe(1);\\n    expect(world.query('actor').length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    expect(world.query('mark').length).toBeGreaterThan(4);\\n  });\\n\\n20→  it('boots the pavilion and keeps a ghost seat', () => {\\n    const run = createAppHost({ scene: round, seed: 2 });\\n    run.stepOnce({ 'game:ghosts': [1, 1, 0.2, -0.1, 0, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0] });\\n    const world = run.session.world;\\n    const ghosts = world.query('ghost') as unknown as { ghost: { on: number; seat: number } }[];\\n    expect(ghosts.length).toBe(3);\\n    expect(ghosts.some((row) => row.ghost.seat === 1 && row.ghost.on === 1)).toBe(true);\\n  });\\n});\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/island.test.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The island and the pavilion boot through the shipped scenes and take a few steps.\\n */\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { createAppHost } from '../../engine/app/headless';\\nimport { island } from './scenes/island';\\nimport { round } from './scenes/round';\\n\\ndescribe('places', () => {\\n  it('boots the island and walks a step', () => {\\n    const run = createAppHost({ scene: island, seed: 1 });\\n    run.stepOnce({ move: [0, 1] });\\n    run.stepOnce({ move: [0, 1] });\\n    const world = run.session.world;\\n    expect(world.query('flow').length).toBe(1);\\n    expect(world.query('actor').length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    expect(world.query('mark').length).toBeGreaterThan(4);\\n  });\\n\\n  it('boots the pavilion and keeps a ghost seat', () => {\\n    const run = createAppHost({ scene: round, seed: 2 });\\n    run.stepOnce({ 'game:ghosts': [1, 1, 0.2, -0.1, 0, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0] });\\n    const world = run.session.world;\\n    const ghosts = world.query('ghost') as unknown as { ghost: { on: number; seat: number } }[];\\n    expect(ghosts.length).toBe(3);\\n    expect(ghosts.some((row) => row.ghost.seat === 1 && row.ghost.on === 1)).toBe(true);\\n  });\\n});\\n\",\"total_lines\":28}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1873fc41-8887-45b0-acfb-c4279dcfbc0a-31","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The day. Boot puts a seat and a programme on the world. Each step runs the activity, or the thumb\\n * that stands in for a player when `game.auto` is director or attract. Menus arrive as scene actions.\\n */\\nimport type { Intents, World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport './settings';\\nimport { activityById, findActivity } from './catalog';\\nimport { programme, type ProgrammeItem } from './data/days';\\nimport { actOf, flowOf, rowOf } from './events/kit';\\n10→import { clampScore, pebblesOf, rankOf, wobbleAge } from './score';\\nimport { type Act, type Flow, type Island, emptyAct, part, resetAct, visit } from './state';\\nimport { drawSway, resetBalance } from './wobble';\\n\\n/** How long a result or an evening stays up when the director is walking. */\\nconst BEAT = 45;\\n\\n/** Attract shows each slice for about fifteen seconds, then the next. */\\nconst SLICE = 15 * 60;\\n\\n20→/** The demo loop. The Great Tilt slice opens on the centre stone. */\\nconst SLICES = ['pose-a', 'pond', 'line', 'paddle', 'garden', 'tilt'];\\n\\n/** A rank a dev jump can stamp without playing the hold. */\\nconst RANK_SCORE: Readonly<Record<string, number>> = {\\n  Present: 0,\\n  Adequate: 300,\\n  Composed: 550,\\n  Serene: 750,\\n  Unsettling: 900,\\n30→};\\n\\n/** The island lean. */\\nfunction islandOf(w: World): Island {\\n  return part<Island>(w, 'island');\\n}\\n\\n/** A plain object of action arguments, or an empty one. */\\nfunction rec(args: unknown): Record<string, unknown> {\\n  if (typeof args === 'object' && args !== null && !Array.isArray(args)) return args as Record<string, unknown>;\\n40→  return {};\\n}\\n\\n/** A finite number argument. */\\nfunction numArg(args: Record<string, unknown>, key: string): number | undefined {\\n  const value = args[key];\\n  return typeof value === 'number' && Number.isFinite(value) ? value : undefined;\\n}\\n\\n/** A string argument. */\\n50→function strArg(args: Record<string, unknown>, key: string): string | undefined {\\n  const value = args[key];\\n  return typeof value === 'string' ? value : undefined;\\n}\\n\\n/** Who is driving this step. */\\nfunction autoOf(w: World): string {\\n  return String(w.settings.get('game.auto'));\\n}\\n\\n60→/** Story lean for a residency day. Day 1 is 0.4 degrees, and each day adds half a degree. */\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The day. Boot puts a seat and a programme on the world. Each step runs the activity, or the thumb\\n * that stands in for a player when `game.auto` is director or attract. Menus arrive as scene actions.\\n */\\nimport type { Intents, World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport './settings';\\nimport { activityById, findActivity } from './catalog';\\nimport { programme, type ProgrammeItem } from './data/days';\\nimport { actOf, flowOf, rowOf } from './events/kit';\\n10→import { clampScore, pebblesOf, rankOf, wobbleAge } from './score';\\nimport { type Act, type Flow, type Island, emptyAct, part, resetAct, visit } from './state';\\nimport { drawSway, resetBalance } from './wobble';\\n\\n/** How long a result or an evening stays up when the director is walking. */\\nconst BEAT = 45;\\n\\n/** Attract shows each slice for about fifteen seconds, then the next. */\\nconst SLICE = 15 * 60;\\n\\n20→/** The demo loop. The Great Tilt slice opens on the centre stone. */\\nconst SLICES = ['pose-a', 'pond', 'line', 'paddle', 'garden', 'tilt'];\\n\\n/** A rank a dev jump can stamp without playing the hold. */\\nconst RANK_SCORE: Readonly<Record<string, number>> = {\\n  Present: 0,\\n  Adequate: 300,\\n  Composed: 550,\\n  Serene: 750,\\n  Unsettling: 900,\\n30→};\\n\\n/** The island lean. */\\nfunction islandOf(w: World): Island {\\n  return part<Island>(w, 'island');\\n}\\n\\n/** A plain object of action arguments, or an empty one. */\\nfunction rec(args: unknown): Record<string, unknown> {\\n  if (typeof args === 'object' && args !== null && !Array.isArray(args)) return args as Record<string, unknown>;\\n40→  return {};\\n}\\n\\n/** A finite number argument. */\\nfunction numArg(args: Record<string, unknown>, key: string): number | undefined {\\n  const value = args[key];\\n  return typeof value === 'number' && Number.isFinite(value) ? value : undefined;\\n}\\n\\n/** A string argument. */\\n50→function strArg(args: Record<string, unknown>, key: string): string | undefined {\\n  const value = args[key];\\n  return typeof value === 'string' ? value : undefined;\\n}\\n\\n/** Who is driving this step. */\\nfunction autoOf(w: World): string {\\n  return String(w.settings.get('game.auto'));\\n}\\n\\n60→/** Story lean for a residency day. Day 1 is 0.4 degrees, and each day adds half a degree. */\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/driver.ts\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":60,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The day. Boot puts a seat and a programme on the world. Each step runs the activity, or the thumb\\n * that stands in for a player when `game.auto` is director or attract. Menus arrive as scene actions.\\n */\\nimport type { Intents, World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport './settings';\\nimport { activityById, findActivity } from './catalog';\\nimport { programme, type ProgrammeItem } from './data/days';\\nimport { actOf, flowOf, rowOf } from './events/kit';\\nimport { clampScore, pebblesOf, rankOf, wobbleAge } from './score';\\nimport { type Act, type Flow, type Island, emptyAct, part, resetAct, visit } from './state';\\nimport { drawSway, resetBalance } from './wobble';\\n\\n/** How long a result or an evening stays up when the director is walking. */\\nconst BEAT = 45;\\n\\n/** Attract shows each slice for about fifteen seconds, then the next. */\\nconst SLICE = 15 * 60;\\n\\n/** The demo loop. The Great Tilt slice opens on the centre stone. */\\nconst SLICES = ['pose-a', 'pond', 'line', 'paddle', 'garden', 'tilt'];\\n\\n/** A rank a dev jump can stamp without playing the hold. */\\nconst RANK_SCORE: Readonly<Record<string, number>> = {\\n  Present: 0,\\n  Adequate: 300,\\n  Composed: 550,\\n  Serene: 750,\\n  Unsettling: 900,\\n};\\n\\n/** The island lean. */\\nfunction islandOf(w: World): Island {\\n  return part<Island>(w, 'island');\\n}\\n\\n/** A plain object of action arguments, or an empty one. */\\nfunction rec(args: unknown): Record<string, unknown> {\\n  if (typeof args === 'object' && args !== null && !Array.isArray(args)) return args as Record<string, unknown>;\\n  return {};\\n}\\n\\n/** A finite number argument. */\\nfunction numArg(args: Record<string, unknown>, key: string): number | undefined {\\n  const value = args[key];\\n  return typeof value === 'number' && Number.isFinite(value) ? value : undefined;\\n}\\n\\n/** A string argument. */\\nfunction strArg(args: Record<string, unknown>, key: string): string | undefined {\\n  const value = args[key];\\n  return typeof value === 'string' ? value : undefined;\\n}\\n\\n/** Who is driving this step. */\\nfunction autoOf(w: World): string {\\n  return String(w.settings.get('game.auto'));\\n}\\n\\n/** Story lean for a residency day. Day 1 is 0.4 degrees, and each day adds half a degree. */\\n\",\"total_lines\":345}}