{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1046","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Beginning immediate action on the morning tasks.\n\nConfirmed the finish and start flow correctly overwrites the line to the age line. The resultCopy and noteProgress tests can be pure functions without simulation. Also checking eslint import order.\n\nVerified no circular imports exist between snap, score, and save. Confirmed noteProgress safely clones bests and finds arrays without mutating the original state.\n\nConfirmed noteProgress preserves settings from the original save. The save key includes prior and finds, so updates to either trigger a new write. Morning results with different priors generate distinct keys.\n\nPose clip names are derived from lowercase pose IDs with the first letter capitalized. Group events are excluded from pose scrubbing because they use a different event prefix. The scrub implementation must initialize time on the first frame. playClip returns state and also writes to clips.state.\n\nThe scrub function must re-read the clips state after playClip because the local slots constant was captured before. Leaning clips may be additive and leave the base Nothing pose active.\n\nposeName returns an empty string for non-pose events. The scrub function updates lean clips on every frame but only advances the pose clip's time when a pose is active. If a pose clip was never played, it does not need to be zeroed. When a pose ends and the event changes, the pose clip can remain at its last progress value.\n\nThe hold duration for a pose should fall back to the global `game.pose.hold` setting when the pose record itself has no hold value. A new `poseProgress` helper is being drafted to return the active pose clip and its current time, using the same lookup logic as `pose.ts`.\n\nThe `poseProgress` helper is now fully implemented. It returns the pose clip name and current time based on the act phase. Phase 0 maps to the opening animation using `act.left / (4 * 60)`. Phase 2 maps to a fixed rest at full progress. The remaining phases use the pose hold duration or the global `game.pose.hold` setting, converted to steps.\n\nThe test timing was verified. The first chair frame reaches progress 1/240 immediately after the nothing hold and 20 rest steps. The full pose sequence takes roughly 380 steps: about 120 frames to enter the ring, 240 for the hold phase, then 20 rest steps before advancing to pose 1. The test will loop until act.pose reaches 1 or stop at 800 steps.\n\nThe 800-step test limit is sufficient for the 5280-step pose hold.\n\nA timing issue was found at the phase boundary. When the nothing pose finishes, the act phase increments and `left` resets to zero within the same step before dress begins. This means sampling progress at step 25 could hit the transition and read zero instead of the opening animation.\n\nThe test should sample the Nothing pose clip time before that reset occurs.\n\nSampling the Nothing pose clip within the first 30 steps is safe because progress strictly increases during phase 0. The transition to the next pose resets `left` to zero at the end of that step, so the following frame immediately starts with `left = 1` and the new pose clip begins at positive progress.\n\nThe test will wait until the pose reaches 1, then run a few extra steps to confirm the Chair clip time is positive and increasing. It will assert specifically on the Chair pose rather than the Nothing pose, since the transition frame may leave the new clip at zero.\n\nThe test will verify the Nothing pose clip time rises over 20 steps. It will also confirm the Chair clip time is positive and increasing after the pose advances.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-068334a0-a41c-4f99-b85a-62ce6d04c422-39","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"intents\\.move|move\\[0\\]","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine","glob":"*.ts","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-068334a0-a41c-4f99-b85a-62ce6d04c422-40","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"'game:r'|axis.*move|virtual.*move","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game","glob":"*.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1705,"output_tokens":2497,"cache_read_input_tokens":77312,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"5a7d86dd-7844-407f-860d-664b4d9b6e0d"}
