aracter({ move })', input.move, 'a direction [x, z]');\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/physics/feel.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":244,\"content\":\"  const [mx, mz] = input.move ?? [0, 0];\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"fb913874-109b-4a0d-a7b6-9e6fb1a3bc97"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1053","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Move[0] is x (east). Move[1] is z (south).\n\nWest is negative x. Downhill lean west subtracts sin(tiltX) from mx. Scene step writes intents first. Then the actors system moves the character. Roam applies slope before movement. If the actors system ran in the same phase as scene step, the slope would lag one frame.\n\nSlope drift is detectable over 120 frames. The test must exit title mode first, since slope is skipped there and the guest would stay put.\n\nA test will step the guest for 180 frames and assert it drifts west by at least 0.02 meters. Zeroing tiltX will confirm the guest stays put, isolating slope as the cause. Both CoB and sea q consumers should be tested, since delivery changes tiltX and affects both.\n\nA concrete test will jump east and deliver, dropping tiltX by 0.5. Both the updated tilt and the sea quaternion should change in the same step. The trace begins at boot with tiltX at 0.4.\n\nThe trace now covers the delivery step. The guest starts at x=59 with act.px=70, so it moves east before the tiltX drop. During that step, taken flips and tiltX falls to -0.1, which updates the sea quaternion in the same frame. Other guests near x=1–8 drift west unless they are following.\n\nThe test will assert that tiltX drops by exactly 0.5 after the first step, then stays flat on the next step since the guest is already taken. A sea quaternion read helper is needed to verify the quaternion updates. An optional storm-rate test could set game.tilt.rate to 1 and step for 60 frames to confirm a one-degree increase.\n\nThe storm-rate test will compare two islands: one with rate 0 and one with rate 1. After 60 steps, the fast island should read tiltX near 1.4 while the slow one stays near 0.4. This confirms the rate is read and the tilt accumulates correctly.\n\nStorm sets tiltX from base plus time times rate, not by adding to the current value. The score stays unchanged because the test does not finish the event.\n\nHosts will be reused across tests to avoid slow physics boot-up. Pose needs its own host with pose hold 4. Tilt, plaque, and pebble can share one or two hosts. Age can use the bench host from retreat.test since it does not need an island.\n\nA double finish will be added to existing tests so they do not boot another physics world. noteProgress and resultCopy unit tests need no world. Sea and CoB tests require an island. The sea prop likely has no physics body, so its quaternion will not be overwritten by readback.\n\nPhysics readback runs before rules, so dress writes the quaternion after readback and it persists until the next frame. The test reads component state after stepOnce, which is safe even if the sea prop has a physics body. The skeptic wants something visible to the player, but these headless tests only inspect internal state.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-929d5734-97a8-4627-ba4c-6c30e6cd33ef-48","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"phase:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/systems.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-929d5734-97a8-4627-ba4c-6c30e6cd33ef-49","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"systems\\.step|phase","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/app","glob":"*.ts","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":480,"output_tokens":1925,"cache_read_input_tokens":86528,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"56b1a994-11aa-4a8f-a5bc-b05c8b81a6ee"}
