{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1085","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"verify.mjs runs vitest on retreat.test.ts, which includes director seeds and band tests.\n\nFull verification takes roughly 15 minutes. It covers all tests including browser and hub tests. I will launch it in the background and monitor its output.\n\nNode buffers stdout when redirected, so the log stays empty until the process exits. A small watcher will poll the process every 30 seconds and print the final result once it finishes.\n\nI will block for up to 20 minutes so the verification completes before I claim done. The existing verify log does not need to be preserved separately.\n\nThe new verify.log will overwrite the old one as the official evidence. I am setting environment variables for Playwright and Chromium before launching verification.\n\nI will delete the Python cache first. The shell command must capture the node exit code so it fails if verification fails.\n\nI will check available memory before launching to avoid an out-of-memory crash. The verification block is set to 15 minutes instead of 20, and I will monitor for backgrounding.\n\nI will launch verification with block_until_ms set to 0 so I can continue working while it runs. I will also read TASK.md to confirm the hand-in files are ready.\n\nI will check PROGRESS.md and exit-interview.json for the hub sentence and any documentation changes. I also want to review the goal plan verification steps so I know what remains after verification finishes.\n\nI will not rebuild HTML manually because verify already handles that, and running onefile separately would race. I must keep the monitor active so I know when verification finishes, and I must not claim completion before it ends.\n\nThe new tests passed in isolation, but director scores might be affected by the code changes. Tilt score no longer uses angle, and storm now uses rate 0.15 instead of 0.28.\n\nDirector score logic is unaffected by the recent changes. Storm ending sets act.a to 1 regardless of angle. Delivery changes tiltX but score uses delivered count, not tilt. Pose scrub, plaques, and age line do not affect score. Pebble collection is handled by frame() walking activities rather than the guest moving to pebbles, so flow.pebbles from rank pebbles remains correct. During director mode, slope is zeroed outside event mode and during tilt phase 1.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d2cc7aa8-dc43-4051-ad50-6f120d25653f-119","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"free -h && ls -d \"$HOME/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-1243/chrome-headless-shell-linux64/chrome-headless-shell\" && rm -rf \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/tools/__pycache__\"","description":"Check memory and Chromium before verify"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1658,"output_tokens":1724,"cache_read_input_tokens":143744,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"db97f436-39d4-48e5-a979-3b69f3fb8326"}
