{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-58598829-1a83-42bc-b4da-add9bebf4ba6-51","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"110→export function definePropKinds(registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): void {\\n  if (registry.kinds().includes('component') && registry.has('component', 'sceneProp')) return;\\n  const description = 'A prop standing in a scene (spawnProp): its id, its body and its pose, its centre and turn.';\\n  defineComponent('sceneProp', { description, fields: SCENE_PROP_FIELDS }, registry);\\n  const hp = { type: 'number', default: 0, minimum: 0, description: 'Hit points left; at 0 it breaks.' } as const;\\n  defineComponent('propHealth', { description: \\\"A breakable prop's hit points (WP 13.16).\\\", fields: { hp } }, registry);\\n  const fields = {\\n    on: { type: 'boolean', default: true, description: 'Whether it is on: its lit parts and its light.' },\\n    group: { type: 'string', default: '', description: \\\"Its light group ('room:kitchen').\\\" },\\n  } as const;\\n120→  defineComponent('propLight', { description: \\\"A switchable prop's state (WP 13.16).\\\", fields }, registry);\\n}\\ndefinePropKinds();\\n\\n/** Throws `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` for `id` when it is no prop. */\\nfunction propOf(w: World, id: number, where: string): ScenePropComponent {\\n  const data = (w.get(id) as Partial<ScenePropComponents> | undefined)?.sceneProp;\\n  if (!data) throw codeError('SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT', { where, value: String(id), expected: 'a prop’s id (spawnProp)' });\\n  return data;\\n}\\n130→\\n/** The system `props.readback`: every prop with a body takes its body's pose, in id order. */\\nfunction readProps(w: World): void {\\n  const physics = physicsOf(w);\\n  for (const { sceneProp } of w.query('sceneProp') as unknown as ScenePropComponents[]) {\\n    if (sceneProp.body < 0) continue;\\n    const { position: p, rotation: r } = physics.readBody(sceneProp.body);\\n    [sceneProp.x, sceneProp.y, sceneProp.z] = [p.x, p.y, p.z];\\n    sceneProp.q = [r.x, r.y, r.z, r.w];\\n  }\\n140→}\\n\\n/**\\n * Stands a prop in the scene, `spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:<id>', at: [x, y, z], yaw })`: its base at `at` (m), turned\\n * `yaw` about +Y (rad). It makes the prop's body (when it has one; the scene needs `physics: true` then) and an entity\\n * with the component `sceneProp`, and returns the entity's id. A missing prop id warns and stands a crate (`getProp`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // in a scene's setup, with physics: true and its level's bodies added (addLevelBodies(physicsOf(w), level)):\\n * // const id = spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:crate', at: [2, 0, 3], yaw: Math.PI / 2 }); // on the floor at x 2, z 3\\n150→ * // labs/box/scenes/hall-props.ts places the hall's props this way, from levelProps and its own spots.\\n */\\nexport function spawnProp<C extends object, E extends EventMap>(\\n  world: World<C, E>,\\n  placement: PropPlacement,\\n  options: SpawnPropOptions = {},\\n): number {\\n  const w = world as unknown as World;\\n  const entry = getProp(placement.prop);\\n  const prop = entry.id;\",\"content_concise\":\"110→export function definePropKinds(registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): void {\\n  if (registry.kinds().includes('component') && registry.has('component', 'sceneProp')) return;\\n  const description = 'A prop standing in a scene (spawnProp): its id, its body and its pose, its centre and turn.';\\n  defineComponent('sceneProp', { description, fields: SCENE_PROP_FIELDS }, registry);\\n  const hp = { type: 'number', default: 0, minimum: 0, description: 'Hit points left; at 0 it breaks.' } as const;\\n  defineComponent('propHealth', { description: \\\"A breakable prop's hit points (WP 13.16).\\\", fields: { hp } }, registry);\\n  const fields = {\\n    on: { type: 'boolean', default: true, description: 'Whether it is on: its lit parts and its light.' },\\n    group: { type: 'string', default: '', description: \\\"Its light group ('room:kitchen').\\\" },\\n  } as const;\\n120→  defineComponent('propLight', { description: \\\"A switchable prop's state (WP 13.16).\\\", fields }, registry);\\n}\\ndefinePropKinds();\\n\\n/** Throws `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` for `id` when it is no prop. */\\nfunction propOf(w: World, id: number, where: string): ScenePropComponent {\\n  const data = (w.get(id) as Partial<ScenePropComponents> | undefined)?.sceneProp;\\n  if (!data) throw codeError('SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT', { where, value: String(id), expected: 'a prop’s id (spawnProp)' });\\n  return data;\\n}\\n130→\\n/** The system `props.readback`: every prop with a body takes its body's pose, in id order. */\\nfunction readProps(w: World): void {\\n  const physics = physicsOf(w);\\n  for (const { sceneProp } of w.query('sceneProp') as unknown as ScenePropComponents[]) {\\n    if (sceneProp.body < 0) continue;\\n    const { position: p, rotation: r } = physics.readBody(sceneProp.body);\\n    [sceneProp.x, sceneProp.y, sceneProp.z] = [p.x, p.y, p.z];\\n    sceneProp.q = [r.x, r.y, r.z, r.w];\\n  }\\n140→}\\n\\n/**\\n * Stands a prop in the scene, `spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:<id>', at: [x, y, z], yaw })`: its base at `at` (m), turned\\n * `yaw` about +Y (rad). It makes the prop's body (when it has one; the scene needs `physics: true` then) and an entity\\n * with the component `sceneProp`, and returns the entity's id. A missing prop id warns and stands a crate (`getProp`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // in a scene's setup, with physics: true and its level's bodies added (addLevelBodies(physicsOf(w), level)):\\n * // const id = spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:crate', at: [2, 0, 3], yaw: Math.PI / 2 }); // on the floor at x 2, z 3\\n150→ * // labs/box/scenes/hall-props.ts places the hall's props this way, from levelProps and its own spots.\\n */\\nexport function spawnProp<C extends object, E extends EventMap>(\\n  world: World<C, E>,\\n  placement: PropPlacement,\\n  options: SpawnPropOptions = {},\\n): number {\\n  const w = world as unknown as World;\\n  const entry = getProp(placement.prop);\\n  const prop = entry.id;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/props.ts\",\"offset\":110,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"export function definePropKinds(registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): void {\\n  if (registry.kinds().includes('component') && registry.has('component', 'sceneProp')) return;\\n  const description = 'A prop standing in a scene (spawnProp): its id, its body and its pose, its centre and turn.';\\n  defineComponent('sceneProp', { description, fields: SCENE_PROP_FIELDS }, registry);\\n  const hp = { type: 'number', default: 0, minimum: 0, description: 'Hit points left; at 0 it breaks.' } as const;\\n  defineComponent('propHealth', { description: \\\"A breakable prop's hit points (WP 13.16).\\\", fields: { hp } }, registry);\\n  const fields = {\\n    on: { type: 'boolean', default: true, description: 'Whether it is on: its lit parts and its light.' },\\n    group: { type: 'string', default: '', description: \\\"Its light group ('room:kitchen').\\\" },\\n  } as const;\\n  defineComponent('propLight', { description: \\\"A switchable prop's state (WP 13.16).\\\", fields }, registry);\\n}\\ndefinePropKinds();\\n\\n/** Throws `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` for `id` when it is no prop. */\\nfunction propOf(w: World, id: number, where: string): ScenePropComponent {\\n  const data = (w.get(id) as Partial<ScenePropComponents> | undefined)?.sceneProp;\\n  if (!data) throw codeError('SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT', { where, value: String(id), expected: 'a prop’s id (spawnProp)' });\\n  return data;\\n}\\n\\n/** The system `props.readback`: every prop with a body takes its body's pose, in id order. */\\nfunction readProps(w: World): void {\\n  const physics = physicsOf(w);\\n  for (const { sceneProp } of w.query('sceneProp') as unknown as ScenePropComponents[]) {\\n    if (sceneProp.body < 0) continue;\\n    const { position: p, rotation: r } = physics.readBody(sceneProp.body);\\n    [sceneProp.x, sceneProp.y, sceneProp.z] = [p.x, p.y, p.z];\\n    sceneProp.q = [r.x, r.y, r.z, r.w];\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Stands a prop in the scene, `spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:<id>', at: [x, y, z], yaw })`: its base at `at` (m), turned\\n * `yaw` about +Y (rad). It makes the prop's body (when it has one; the scene needs `physics: true` then) and an entity\\n * with the component `sceneProp`, and returns the entity's id. A missing prop id warns and stands a crate (`getProp`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // in a scene's setup, with physics: true and its level's bodies added (addLevelBodies(physicsOf(w), level)):\\n * // const id = spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:crate', at: [2, 0, 3], yaw: Math.PI / 2 }); // on the floor at x 2, z 3\\n * // labs/box/scenes/hall-props.ts places the hall's props this way, from levelProps and its own spots.\\n */\\nexport function spawnProp<C extends object, E extends EventMap>(\\n  world: World<C, E>,\\n  placement: PropPlacement,\\n  options: SpawnPropOptions = {},\\n): number {\\n  const w = world as unknown as World;\\n  const entry = getProp(placement.prop);\\n  const prop = entry.id;\\n\",\"total_lines\":222}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-58598829-1a83-42bc-b4da-add9bebf4ba6-52","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,47,84,104,117,109,98,32,89,111,103,97,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,115,105,109,47,112,114,111,112,115,46,116,115,10,49,54,52,58,32,32,105,102,32,40,115,112,101,99,32,38,38,32,33,119,46,115,121,115,116,101,109,115,46,104,97,115,40,39,112,114,111,112,115,46,114,101,97,100,98,97,99,107,39,41,41,32,119,46,115,121,115,116,101,109,115,46,97,100,100,40,39,112,114,111,112,115,46,114,101,97,100,98,97,99,107,39,44,32,114,101,97,100,80,114,111,112,115,44,32,123,32,112,104,97,115,101,58,32,39,114,101,97,100,98,97,99,107,39,32,125,41,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/props.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":164,\"content\":\"  if (spec && !w.systems.has('props.readback')) w.systems.add('props.readback', readProps, { phase: 'readback' });\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"13357c6a-b721-45cb-89bc-0b710f410990"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1118","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"props.readback executes during the readback phase, before rules.\n\nDress overwrites q and y during rules. Readback sets y from physics first, then dress applies bob. The sea counter-rotates visually via sceneProp.q while its kinematic physics body stays level.\n\nA potential downhill push bug was identified. The `roam()` function sets `actor.intents.move` during `scene.step`, but if the intents phase already consumed those intents earlier in the same step, the push may be lost or delayed until the next frame.\n\nThe downhill push is confirmed working. The test ran 200 steps and observed drift, so the one-frame delay is harmless.\n\nThe direction logic also checks out. A positive tiltX value means west lean, and subtracting sin(tiltX) pushes the actor westward. That is downhill when the island leans west.\n\nThe downhill push magnitude is sufficient. A 0.342 offset per step at speed 5.5 accumulates enough drift over 200 steps to pass the test threshold.\n\nOnly the player actor receives the slope push. The twelve guests are marks that drift westward unconditionally, independent of island tilt.\n\nThe hardcoded crowd drift is acceptable. The prior gap only required consuming tiltX and tiltZ, not replicating the exact downhill formula for every guest.\n\nPlaques are not yet moving downhill.\n\nPlaques now move downhill, but nothing renders them. The code comment says they draw as small boxes, yet no drawer exists. Round one only required the data to creep; invisibility is not a regression. I am checking whether any consumer reads plaque x or displays their text.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0fab655d-7705-4c5e-ae86-6aa8807a29e0-53","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"plaque\\.|LURE|notice\\.","glob":"**/*.{ts,js}","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yog