{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d5731531-15bb-4621-87e9-a7f1a9ddf0c0-69","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"100→  const { clip, ...play } = typeof spec.play === 'string' ? { clip: spec.play } : spec.play;\\n  const layer = new ClipLayer({ library, build, dt: w.dt, ik: data.ik, blade: data.blade }).play(clip, play);\\n  return { ...data, state: layer.save() };\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Gives the live animated actor `id` the component `clips` (`clipsFor`); an actor spawned in the same step takes\\n * them from `spawnActor`'s `clips`. Throws `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` for an entity without an animator.\\n */\\nexport function addClips<C extends object>(world: World<C>, id: number, spec: ClipsSpec): ClipsData {\\n110→  const w = world as unknown as World;\\n  const entity = w.get(id) as Partial<ClipActor> | undefined;\\n  if (!entity?.actor || !entity.animator)\\n    throw codeError('SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT', { where: 'addClips(w, id, spec)', value: String(id), expected: 'a live animated actor’s id' }); // prettier-ignore\\n  return w.add(id, 'clips', clipsFor(w, spec, entity.animator.build) as never) as unknown as ClipsData;\\n}\\n\\n/** Changes the clip layer of `id` with `change` and writes its state back; returns the state. */\\nfunction change(w: World, id: number, where: string, how: (layer: ClipLayer) => void): ClipLayerState {\\n  const { animator, clips } = clipActor(w, id, where);\\n120→  const layer = poolOf(w).get(id, clips, animator.build, w.dt);\\n  how(layer);\\n  return (clips.state = layer.save());\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Plays `clip` (`SET/Clip`, or bare) on actor `id`, fading in over what plays (the layer's `play`). Throws\\n * `ANIM_UNKNOWN_CLIP` naming the closest clips, and `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` for an actor without clips.\\n */\\nexport function playClip<C extends object>(world: World<C>, id: number, clip: string, play?: ClipPlay): ClipLayerState {\\n130→  return change(world as unknown as World, id, 'playClip(w, id, clip)', (layer) => layer.play(clip, play));\\n}\\n\\n/** Fades out the clip on top of actor `id` over `fade` seconds (its `out`), with what it covers. */\\nexport function stopClip<C extends object>(world: World<C>, id: number, fade?: number): ClipLayerState {\\n  return change(world as unknown as World, id, 'stopClip(w, id)', (layer) => layer.stop(fade));\\n}\\n\\n/** Plays `loops.idle`, `walk` or `run` on actor `id` by its ground speed, each at that speed; null stops them. */\\nexport function locomoteClips<C extends object>(\\n140→  world: World<C>,\\n  id: number,\\n  loops: ClipLayerState['moving'],\\n): ClipLayerState {\\n  return change(world as unknown as World, id, 'locomoteClips(w, id, loops)', (layer) => layer.locomote(loops));\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Puts the clip on top of actor `id` at `t` clip seconds (kept within 0 and its length), its fade done: a frame step\\n * is `seekClip(w, id, frame / BAKE_FPS)`. Nothing playing, it changes nothing.\\n150→ */\\nexport function seekClip<C extends object>(world: World<C>, id: number, t: number): ClipLayerState {\\n  return change(world as unknown as World, id, 'seekClip(w, id, t)', (layer) => {\\n    const top = layer.current;\\n    if (!top) return;\\n    const [library, name] = layer.resolve(top.clip);\\n    const { dur } = library.clip(name);\\n    [top.t, top.w, top.stopping] = [Math.min(Math.max(0, t), dur), 1, 0];\\n  });\\n}\\n160→\\n/** The clip layer of actor `id`, loaded from its component, to read (`current`, `inspect()`); changes are not kept. */\\nexport function clipLayerOf<C extends object>(world: World<C>, id: number): ClipLayer {\\n  const w = world as unknown as World;\\n  const { animator, clips } = clipActor(w, id, 'clipLayerOf(w, id)');\\n  return poolOf(w).get(id, clips, animator.build, w.dt);\\n}\\n\\n/** The system `actors.clips`: each layer's tick at its actor's ground speed, in id order; emits its events. */\\nfunction stepClips(w: World): void {\\n170→  const pool = poolOf(w);\\n  for (const { id, actor, animator, clips } of w.query('actor', 'animator', 'clips') as unknown as ClipActor[]) {\\n    const layer = pool.get(id, clips, animator.build, w.dt);\\n    const events = layer.step({ groundSpeed: Math.hypot(actor.vx, actor.vz) });\\n    clips.state = layer.save();\\n    for (const { type, ...event } of events) w.emit('clip', { id, type, ...event });\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"100→  const { clip, ...play } = typeof spec.play === 'string' ? { clip: spec.play } : spec.play;\\n  const layer = new ClipLayer({ library, build, dt: w.dt, ik: data.ik, blade: data.blade }).play(clip, play);\\n  return { ...data, state: layer.save() };\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Gives the live animated actor `id` the component `clips` (`clipsFor`); an actor spawned in the same step takes\\n * them from `spawnActor`'s `clips`. Throws `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` for an entity without an animator.\\n */\\nexport function addClips<C extends object>(world: World<C>, id: number, spec: ClipsSpec): ClipsData {\\n110→  const w = world as unknown as World;\\n  const entity = w.get(id) as Partial<ClipActor> | undefined;\\n  if (!entity?.actor || !entity.animator)\\n    throw codeError('SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT', { where: 'addClips(w, id, spec)', value: String(id), expected: 'a live animated actor’s id' }); // prettier-ignore\\n  return w.add(id, 'clips', clipsFor(w, spec, entity.animator.build) as never) as unknown as ClipsData;\\n}\\n\\n/** Changes the clip layer of `id` with `change` and writes its state back; returns the state. */\\nfunction change(w: World, id: number, where: string, how: (layer: ClipLayer) => void): ClipLayerState {\\n  const { animator, clips } = clipActor(w, id, where);\\n120→  const layer = poolOf(w).get(id, clips, animator.build, w.dt);\\n  how(layer);\\n  return (clips.state = layer.save());\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Plays `clip` (`SET/Clip`, or bare) on actor `id`, fading in over what plays (the layer's `play`). Throws\\n * `ANIM_UNKNOWN_CLIP` naming the closest clips, and `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` for an actor without clips.\\n */\\nexport function playClip<C extends object>(world: World<C>, id: number, clip: string, play?: ClipPlay): ClipLayerState {\\n130→  return change(world as unknown as World, id, 'playClip(w, id, clip)', (layer) => layer.play(clip, play));\\n}\\n\\n/** Fades out the clip on top of actor `id` over `fade` seconds (its `out`), with what it covers. */\\nexport function stopClip<C extends object>(world: World<C>, id: number, fade?: number): ClipLayerState {\\n  return change(world as unknown as World, id, 'stopClip(w, id)', (layer) => layer.stop(fade));\\n}\\n\\n/** Plays `loops.idle`, `walk` or `run` on actor `id` by its ground speed, each at that speed; null stops them. */\\nexport function locomoteClips<C extends object>(\\n140→  world: World<C>,\\n  id: number,\\n  loops: ClipLayerState['moving'],\\n): ClipLayerState {\\n  return change(world as unknown as World, id, 'locomoteClips(w, id, loops)', (layer) => layer.locomote(loops));\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Puts the clip on top of actor `id` at `t` clip seconds (kept within 0 and its length), its fade done: a frame step\\n * is `seekClip(w, id, frame / BAKE_FPS)`. Nothing playing, it changes nothing.\\n150→ */\\nexport function seekClip<C extends object>(world: World<C>, id: number, t: number): ClipLayerState {\\n  return change(world as unknown as World, id, 'seekClip(w, id, t)', (layer) => {\\n    const top = layer.current;\\n    if (!top) return;\\n    const [library, name] = layer.resolve(top.clip);\\n    const { dur } = library.clip(name);\\n    [top.t, top.w, top.stopping] = [Math.min(Math.max(0, t), dur), 1, 0];\\n  });\\n}\\n160→\\n/** The clip layer of actor `id`, loaded from its component, to read (`current`, `inspect()`); changes are not kept. */\\nexport function clipLayerOf<C extends object>(world: World<C>, id: number): ClipLayer {\\n  const w = world as unknown as World;\\n  const { animator, clips } = clipActor(w, id, 'clipLayerOf(w, id)');\\n  return poolOf(w).get(id, clips, animator.build, w.dt);\\n}\\n\\n/** The system `actors.clips`: each layer's tick at its actor's ground speed, in id order; emits its events. */\\nfunction stepClips(w: World): void {\\n170→  const pool = poolOf(w);\\n  for (const { id, actor, animator, clips } of w.query('actor', 'animator', 'clips') as unknown as ClipActor[]) {\\n    const layer = pool.get(id, clips, animator.build, w.dt);\\n    const events = layer.step({ groundSpeed: Math.hypot(actor.vx, actor.vz) });\\n    clips.state = layer.save();\\n    for (const { type, ...event } of events) w.emit('clip', { id, type, ...event });\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/actorClips.ts\",\"offset\":100,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"  const { clip, ...play } = typeof spec.play === 'string' ? { clip: spec.play } : spec.play;\\n  const layer = new ClipLayer({ library, build, dt: w.dt, ik: data.ik, blade: data.blade }).play(clip, play);\\n  return { ...data, state: layer.save() };\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Gives the live animated actor `id` the component `clips` (`clipsFor`); an actor spawned in the same step takes\\n * them from `spawnActor`'s `clips`. Throws `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` for an entity without an animator.\\n */\\nexport function addClips<C extends object>(world: World<C>, id: number, spec: ClipsSpec): ClipsData {\\n  const w = world as unknown as World;\\n  const entity = w.get(id) as Partial<ClipActor> | undefined;\\n  if (!entity?.actor || !entity.animator)\\n    throw codeError('SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT', { where: 'addClips(w, id, spec)', value: String(id), expected: 'a live animated actor’s id' }); // prettier-ignore\\n  return w.add(id, 'clips', clipsFor(w, spec, entity.animator.build) as never) as unknown as ClipsData;\\n}\\n\\n/** Changes the clip layer of `id` with `change` and writes its state back; returns the state. */\\nfunction change(w: World, id: number, where: string, how: (layer: ClipLayer) => void): ClipLayerState {\\n  const { animator, clips } = clipActor(w, id, where);\\n  const layer = poolOf(w).get(id, clips, animator.build, w.dt);\\n  how(layer);\\n  return (clips.state = layer.save());\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Plays `clip` (`SET/Clip`, or bare) on actor `id`, fading in over what plays (the layer's `play`). Throws\\n * `ANIM_UNKNOWN_CLIP` naming the closest clips, and `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` for an actor without clips.\\n */\\nexport function playClip<C extends object>(world: World<C>, id: number, clip: string, play?: ClipPlay): ClipLayerState {\\n  return change(world as unknown as World, id, 'playClip(w, id, clip)', (layer) => layer.play(clip, play));\\n}\\n\\n/** Fades out the clip on top of actor `id` over `fade` seconds (its `out`), with what it covers. */\\nexport function stopClip<C extends object>(world: World<C>, id: number, fade?: number): ClipLayerState {\\n  return change(world as unknown as World, id, 'stopClip(w, id)', (layer) => layer.stop(fade));\\n}\\n\\n/** Plays `loops.idle`, `walk` or `run` on actor `id` by its ground speed, each at that speed; null stops them. */\\nexport function locomoteClips<C extends object>(\\n  world: World<C>,\\n  id: number,\\n  loops: ClipLayerState['moving'],\\n): ClipLayerState {\\n  return change(world as unknown as World, id, 'locomoteClips(w, id, loops)', (layer) => layer.locomote(loops));\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Puts the clip on top of actor `id` at `t` clip seconds (kept within 0 and its length), its fade done: a frame step\\n * is `seekClip(w, id, frame / BAKE_FPS)`. Nothing playing, it changes nothing.\\n */\\nexport function seekClip<C extends object>(world: World<C>, id: number, t: number): ClipLayerState {\\n  return change(world as unknown as World, id, 'seekClip(w, id, t)', (layer) => {\\n    const top = layer.current;\\n    if (!top) return;\\n    const [library, name] = layer.resolve(top.clip);\\n    const { dur } = library.clip(name);\\n    [top.t, top.w, top.stopping] = [Math.min(Math.max(0, t), dur), 1, 0];\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/** The clip layer of actor `id`, loaded from its component, to read (`current`, `inspect()`); changes are not kept. */\\nexport function clipLayerOf<C extends object>(world: World<C>, id: number): ClipLayer {\\n  const w = world as unknown as World;\\n  const { animator, clips } = clipActor(w, id, 'clipLayerOf(w, id)');\\n  return poolOf(w).get(id, clips, animator.build, w.dt);\\n}\\n\\n/** The system `actors.clips`: each layer's tick at its actor's ground speed, in id order; emits its events. */\\nfunction stepClips(w: World): void {\\n  const pool = poolOf(w);\\n  for (const { id, actor, animator, clips } of w.query('actor', 'animator', 'clips') as unknown as ClipActor[]) {\\n    const layer = pool.get(id, clips, animator.build, w.dt);\\n    const events = layer.step({ groundSpeed: Math.hypot(actor.vx, actor.vz) });\\n    clips.state = layer.save();\\n    for (const { type, ...event } of events) w.emit('clip', { id, type, ...event });\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":177}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"e1c552bc-6121-403c-8ae0-96b32900fe32"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1125","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `play()` function fades in over what plays.\n\nThe scrub writes `slot.t` after `playClip`, but `stepClips` runs earlier in the animation phase. The saved state therefore advances before the scrub can overwrite it. If speed is zero, the time value still gets reset on the next frame.\n\nThe fade-in is correct crossfade behavior. A potential bug remains: `seekClip` expects seconds, but the scrub writes a 0–1 normalized value to `slot.t`. This mismatch could make poses jump or barely move through long clips.\n\n`slot.t` is in seconds, not 0–1. The scrub writes a 0–1 fraction, so it only reaches the first second of a long clip. Short pose strips might hide this bug. The old code had the same flaw: it also used a 0–1 fraction over 720 frames.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a720727e-3184-486b-ab1c-930b8c05e1e9-70","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function strip|dur:|duration","glob":"**/clips.ts","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/cast"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a720727e-3184-486b-ab1c-930b8c05e1e9-71","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/cast/clips.ts","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1521,"output_tokens":723,"cache_read_input_tokens":119296,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"39b28773-bdf4-4dea-9999-580b0f0bac2e"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a720727e-3184-486b-ab1c-930b8c05e1e9-70","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,95,95,120,53,52,102,97,99,99,47,119,111,114,107,47,84,104,117,109,98,32,89,111,103,97,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,54,53,54,47,108,97,98,115,47,103,97,109,101,47,99,97,115,116,47,99,108,105,112,115,46,116,115,10,51,48,58,102,117,110,99,116,105,111,110,32,115,116,114,105,112,40,111,118,101,114,58,32,111,98,106,101,99,116,41,58,32,111,98,106,101,99,116,32,123,10,51,49,58,32,32,114,101,116,117,114,110,32,123,32,115,114,99,58,32,39,82,69,84,82,69,65,84,39,44,32,100,117,114,58,32,49,44,32,108,111,111,112,58,32,102,97,108,115,101,44,32,107,101,121,115,58,32,91,107,101,121,40,48,44,32,123,125,41,44,32,107,101,121,40,49,44,32,111,118,101,114,41,93,32,125,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/cast/clips.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":30,\"content\":\"function strip(over: object): object {\"},{\"line_number\":31,\"content\":\"  return { src: 'RETREAT', dur: 1, loop: false, keys: [key(0, {}), key(1, over)] };\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a720727e-3184-486b-ab1c-930b8c05e1e9-71","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Pose strips for the retreat. Each clip stands, then arrives. The page scrubs the time.\\n * The rest body is Mesh2Motion's, so the poses share a body the engine already draws.\\n */\\nimport { defineClipSet, defineSetBuild } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { REST } from './rest';\\n\\n/** A standing key. Up is 100. The arms hang. The knees are soft. */\\nconst STAND = {\\n10→  hips: [0, 0, 100],\\n  body: [0, 0, 0],\\n  chest: [0, 0, 0],\\n  head: [0, 0, 0],\\n  shL: [0, 0],\\n  shR: [0, 0],\\n  armL: [0, 20, -100, 8, 0],\\n  armR: [0, 20, -100, 8, 0],\\n  legL: [0, 6, -100, 4, 0],\\n  legR: [0, 6, -100, 4, 0],\\n20→  footL: [0, 6, 0],\\n  footR: [0, 6, 0],\\n};\\n\\n/** One key at time `t`, with `over` laid on the stand. */\\nfunction key(t: number, over: object): object {\\n  return { t, ...STAND, ...over };\\n}\\n\\n/** A two-key strip. The first key is neutral so an additive lean starts at nothing. */\\n30→function strip(over: object): object {\\n  return { src: 'RETREAT', dur: 1, loop: false, keys: [key(0, {}), key(1, over)] };\\n}\\n\\n/** The retreat clip set. Play a clip as `RETREAT/Name`. */\\nexport const SET = defineClipSet({\\n  set: 'RETREAT',\\n  title: 'Retreat poses',\\n  format: 2,\\n  fps: 30,\\n40→  credit: 'Original poses. Rest body from Mesh2Motion.',\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Pose strips for the retreat. Each clip stands, then arrives. The page scrubs the time.\\n * The rest body is Mesh2Motion's, so the poses share a body the engine already draws.\\n */\\nimport { defineClipSet, defineSetBuild } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { REST } from './rest';\\n\\n/** A standing key. Up is 100. The arms hang. The knees are soft. */\\nconst STAND = {\\n10→  hips: [0, 0, 100],\\n  body: [0, 0, 0],\\n  chest: [0, 0, 0],\\n  head: [0, 0, 0],\\n  shL: [0, 0],\\n  shR: [0, 0],\\n  armL: [0, 20, -100, 8, 0],\\n  armR: [0, 20, -100, 8, 0],\\n  legL: [0, 6, -100, 4, 0],\\n  legR: [0, 6, -100, 4, 0],\\n20→  footL: [0, 6, 0],\\n  footR: [0, 6, 0],\\n};\\n\\n/** One key at time `t`, with `over` laid on the stand. */\\nfunction key(t: number, over: object): object {\\n  return { t, ...STAND, ...over };\\n}\\n\\n/** A two-key strip. The first key is neutral so an additive lean starts at nothing. */\\n30→function strip(over: object): object {\\n  return { src: 'RETREAT', dur: 1, loop: false, keys: [key(0, {}), key(1, over)] };\\n}\\n\\n/** The retreat clip set. Play a clip as `RETREAT/Name`. */\\nexport const SET = defineClipSet({\\n  set: 'RETREAT',\\n  title: 'Retreat poses',\\n  format: 2,\\n  fps: 30,\\n40→  credit: 'Original poses. Rest body from Mesh2Motion.',\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/cast/clips.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file Pose strips for the retreat. Each clip stands, then arrives. The page scrubs the time.\\n * The rest body is Mesh2Motion's, so the poses share a body the engine already draws.\\n */\\nimport { defineClipSet, defineSetBuild } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { REST } from './rest';\\n\\n/** A standing key. Up is 100. The arms hang. The knees are soft. */\\nconst STAND = {\\n  hips: [0, 0, 100],\\n  body: [0, 0, 0],\\n  chest: [0, 0, 0],\\n  head: [0, 0, 0],\\n  shL: [0, 0],\\n  shR: [0, 0],\\n  armL: [0, 20, -100, 8, 0],\\n  armR: [0, 20, -100, 8, 0],\\n  legL: [0, 6, -100, 4, 0],\\n  legR: [0, 6, -100, 4, 0],\\n  footL: [0, 6, 0],\\n  footR: [0, 6, 0],\\n};\\n\\n/** One key at time `t`, with `over` laid on the stand. */\\nfunction key(t: number, over: object): object {\\n  return { t, ...STAND, ...over };\\n}\\n\\n/** A two-key strip. The first key is neutral so an additive lean starts at nothing. */\\nfunction strip(over: object): object {\\n  return { src: 'RETREAT', dur: 1, loop: false, keys: [key(0, {}), key(1, over)] };\\n}\\n\\n/** The retreat clip set. Play a clip as `RETREAT/Name`. */\\nexport const SET = defineClipSet({\\n  set: 'RETREAT',\\n  title: 'Retreat poses',\\n  format: 2,\\n  fps: 30,\\n  credit: 'Original poses. Rest body from Mesh2Motion.',\\n\",\"total_lines\":128}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"c1c5882a-712f-4aa4-bd36-eee2fee7b9ab"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1126","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A duration of 1 second is noted, with keys at t=0 and t=1.\n\nPose scrub timing checks out. Enter and hold durations map to t=0→1 correctly. The pebble `taken` truthiness test passed. Plaque shifts are accepted as visibly fixed.\n\nA potential bug in `finishEvent` was considered: if it sets `prior = age` before computing, a same-day reload might show yesterday's result on the morning screen. The scenario was traced through save and continue logic, but the next activity starts after a save, so the same-day result is not reloaded.\n\nThe prior-age bug is ruled out. Day-one results correctly show the first age, and day-two morning results correctly show both ages. The test file was edited after the run but passed and matches the source. PLAN changes only reflect checked boxes and existing deviations, so they do not weaken the criteria.\n\nThe PLAN diff only checks task boxes and adds deviations matching the allowed cut. No criteria were deleted. Blocking issues are none. The verdict is Not Refuted with high confidence.\n\nThe JSON and markdown output paths are confirmed. Findings will be an empty array and evidence a one-line citation. Boot logs from the same pass are still available.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e49e66a1-3a80-4d28-92df-05e21010e3a9-72","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ready|error|Error|__game|EXIT","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/boot-1.log"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e49e66a1-3a80-4d28-92df-05e21010e3a9-73","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ready|error|Error|EXIT|fail","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/boot-2.log"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e49e66a1-3a80-4d28-92df-05e21010e3a9-74","name":"grep","input"