ii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/retreat.test.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":17,\"content\":\"import { freshSave, noteProgress } from './ui/save';\"},{\"line_number\":242,\"content\":\"    const next = noteProgress(freshSave(), {\"},{\"line_number\":255,\"content\":\"    const kept = noteProgress(next, {\"},{\"line_number\":276,\"content\":\"    expect(noteProgress(freshSave(), snap).prior).toBe(0);\"},{\"line_number\":286,\"content\":\"    expect(noteProgress(freshSave(), again).prior).toBe(82);\"},{\"line_number\":287,\"content\":\"    menu('game.begin', { day: 1, cursor: 0, age: 40, prior: 82 });\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/island.test.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":14,\"content\":\"import { freshSave, noteProgress } from './ui/save';\"},{\"line_number\":191,\"content\":\"    expect(noteProgress(freshSave(), snap).finds).toEqual(['pebble:0']);\"},{\"line_number\":193,\"content\":\"    menu('game.begin', { day: 1, cursor: 0, pebbles: 1, finds: ['pebble:0'] });\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/driver.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":232,\"content\":\"function applySave(w: World, args: Record<string, unknown>): void {\"},{\"line_number\":299,\"content\":\"  'game.begin': (w: World, args: unknown) => {\"},{\"line_number\":301,\"content\":\"    applySave(w, given);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"3b410543-1042-4cce-8134-a4a90b1f9ee9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1136","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to examine potential bugs more carefully.\n\nAnalyzing the `poseScrub` function. Phase 0 maps `act.left` to a normalized time value. Phase 1 increments `act.left` each step to reach the hold duration. The test expects `later > held` after 15 steps, which depends on the clip actually playing.\n\nTracing the pose transition logic. Phase 2 lasts 20 frames before the pose increments and phase resets to 0. The held value is captured when the pose reaches 1, but the exact timing of that capture relative to the reset is unclear. The step function increments the pose once act.left reaches 20.\n\nThe phase reset happens in the same step as the pose increment. The key question is whether the dress system runs before or after activity.step. If dress runs first, scrub may execute on stale state when the test checks pose >= 1.\n\nThe test runs stepOnce, then checks pose >= 1. If dress executes before activity.step, it sees pose 0 and left at 20. After the reset, the Chair clip may not have started yet, so slotT returns -1. The held capture would be invalid.\n\nThe test still validates that the clip time advances during the pose even if the held capture is -1. The phase 2 logic returns t: 1 for the current pose.\n\nPhase 2 holds the clip time at 1, which is acceptable for the pose's end. The hold progress scrubbing uses `act.left` divided by steps during the scored hold. All poses default to `pose.hold = 0`, so the settings fallback works correctly. The test sets `game.pose.hold` to 4. I should verify that the clip set includes Nothing, Chair, and Heron, and that `playClip` can actually play them.\n\nThe test suite passing confirms playClip works correctly. Now examining the tilt system: dress writes sea quaternion values from tilt angles, and stone phase sets tiltX and tiltZ based on body position. A positive tiltX produces a negative seaZ component, which the test expects to be non-zero. The island also boots with a small initial tiltX of 0.4.\n\nStone phase overwrites tiltX each frame rather than adding to the base. The initial 0.4 tilt may persist briefly before stone takes over, so seaZ could be non-zero from residual sway or that starting value. After 120 frames of stone, tiltX equals body.x times 6. If the still body is near zero, seaZ might approach zero, but float noise could still satisfy the non-zero assertion.\n\nThe storm tilt calculation adds rate times elapsed steps to the base tilt of 0.4. After 60 steps at rate 1, tiltX reaches 1.4, matching the test expectation.\n\nRate 0 leaves tiltX at the base value of 0.4.\n\nThe east delivery test teleports a guest to trigger the real step() path with positioned state. The stone phase already validates that non-zero CoB changes consume tilt, so the deed part is extra. Setting mark state and stepping is reasonable for testing the delivery threshold.\n\nA potential bug exists in the east phase guest follow drift logic. The code interpolates mark.x toward act.px using a capped delta factor.\n\nThe east delivery test correctly triggers a single tilt decrement because the guest is already past the 58-unit threshold. The downhill walk test expects a westward drift of at least 0.2 over 200 frames, driven by the sine of the 20-degree tilt angle. If the character controller applies move intents in headless mode, this should pass.\n\nTilt is confirmed visible and deed-tunable. It drives sea rotation, storm rate, and guest delivery.\n\nPlaques shift west by 4 cm per day after the first. Day 4 should place them 12 cm further west. The test jumps to day 4 and steps. I need to verify that game.jump sets the day and dress runs afterward.\n\nThe jump-to-day test is sound. The stepOnce call after the menu action lets dress apply its westward offset to plaques that respawn at home.\n\nAge data flows through resultCopy into stage paint for results mode. Prior ages are stored via noteProgress and restored by applySave.\n\nThe age test exercises the real morning finish path and asserts that resultCopy contains today's age alongside yesterday's. It reads resultCopy directly rather than querying the DOM, but stage.ts:526 uses that same object for painting results. This validates the live wiring instead of a dead function.\n\nThe spoken age line omits the numeric value. The visible results copy includes it via resultCopy. This satisfies the prior requirement to show today's age against yesterday on the morning result.\n\nThe continue menu passes the full Save object, which includes prior age data. A potential bug exists in noteProgress: it stores snap.prior rather than snap.age. Morning results set flow.prior to yesterday and flow.age to today, so the save captures both values. On the next morning, finishEvent promotes today's age to yesterday, but this only works if game.begin restores the saved prior before that step.\n\nDuring a continuous session, flow.age persists in memory and the second morning uses that value. After reload, game.begin restores the saved age and prior, but finishEvent immediately overwrites prior with the restored today's age before computing the new age. This means yesterday is correctly set to the restored age even if the saved prior was stale.\n\nThe age restoration logic is sound. A concrete example confirms that restoring age 40 and prior 82 makes the next morning use 40 as yesterday. The remaining question is whether reloading while the results screen is still visible correctly restores results mode.\n\napplySave may not restore the game mode, so game.begin needs full verification. The first morning correctly handles age zero because the prior defaults to zero and the age remark logic falls back to the first-age sentence.\n\nThe pebble test validates that applyFinds marks taken items, so dress pickup skips them. After a respawn and game.begin restore, the first pebble is marked as taken and stays at one. Walking over it again leaves the count unchanged. A second pebble then increments the total to two.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5595617d-2940-4e37-be25-ac4a9541724a-22","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/driver.ts","offset":290,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5595617d-2940-4e37-be25-ac4a9541724a-23","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/ui/menus.ts","offset":60,"limit":70}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5595617d-2940-4e37-be25-ac4a9541724a-24","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"failures|EXIT|Tests |passed|failed","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/npm-test.log"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5595617d-2940-4e37-be25-ac4a9541724a-25","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"failures|EXIT|seed |error|FAIL","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/tmp/grok-goal-ed8f613011b3/implementer/verify.log"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5579,"output_tokens":3284,"cache_read_input_tokens":66048,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"4fc6f37e-3ec0-477a-ac41-3004ab8c770f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5595617d-2940-4e37-be25-ac4a9541724a-22","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"290→    if (act.wait >= BEAT) {\\n      if (flow.mode === 'results') advance(w);\\n      else sleep(w);\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Menu picks. Each one runs between steps. */\\nexport const retreatActions = {\\n  'game.begin': (w: World, args: unknown) => {\\n300→    const given = rec(args);\\n    applySave(w, given);\\n    const flow = flowOf(w);\\n    applyLean(w, flow.day);\\n    if (flow.credits) {\\n      flow.mode = 'roam';\\n      flow.event = '';\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    openItem(w, programme()[flow.cursor]);\\n310→  },\\n  'game.start': (w: World, args: unknown) => {\\n    const event = strArg(rec(args), 'event');\\n    if (!event) return;\\n    if (event === 'evening') openEvening(w);\\n    else if (event === 'credits') openCredits(w);\\n    else startEvent(w, event);\\n  },\\n  'game.carry': (w: World) => {\\n    if (flowOf(w).mode === 'results') advance(w);\\n320→  },\\n  'game.sleep': (w: World) => {\\n    if (flowOf(w).mode === 'evening') sleep(w);\\n  },\\n  'game.leave': (w: World) => {\\n    const flow = flowOf(w);\\n    const activity = findActivity(flow.event);\\n    if (activity && flow.mode === 'event') activity.teardown(w);\\n    flow.mode = 'roam';\\n    flow.event = '';\\n330→  },\\n  'game.jump': (w: World, args: unknown) => {\\n    const given = rec(args);\\n    const step = strArg(given, 'step');\\n    const event = strArg(given, 'event');\\n    const day = numArg(given, 'day');\\n    if (step) {\\n      jumpTilt(w, step);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n340→    if (event) {\\n      startEvent(w, event);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (day === undefined) return;\\n    const list = programme();\\n    const at = list.findIndex((item) => item.day === day);\\n    if (at < 0) return;\\n    const flow = flowOf(w);\\n    flow.cursor = at;\\n350→    flow.day = day;\\n    applyLean(w, day);\\n    openItem(w, list[at]);\\n  },\\n  'game.finish': (w: World, args: unknown) => {\\n    if (flowOf(w).mode !== 'event') return;\\n    finishEvent(w, strArg(rec(args), 'rank'));\\n  },\\n};\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"290→    if (act.wait >= BEAT) {\\n      if (flow.mode === 'results') advance(w);\\n      else sleep(w);\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Menu picks. Each one runs between steps. */\\nexport const retreatActions = {\\n  'game.begin': (w: World, args: unknown) => {\\n300→    const given = rec(args);\\n    applySave(w, given);\\n    const flow = flowOf(w);\\n    applyLean(w, flow.day);\\n    if (flow.credits) {\\n      flow.mode = 'roam';\\n      flow.event = '';\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    openItem(w, programme()[flow.cursor]);\\n310→  },\\n  'game.start': (w: World, args: unknown) => {\\n    const event = strArg(rec(args), 'event');\\n    if (!event) return;\\n    if (event === 'evening') openEvening(w);\\n    else if (event === 'credits') openCredits(w);\\n    else startEvent(w, event);\\n  },\\n  'game.carry': (w: World) => {\\n    if (flowOf(w).mode === 'results') advance(w);\\n320→  },\\n  'game.sleep': (w: World) => {\\n    if (flowOf(w).mode === 'evening') sleep(w);\\n  },\\n  'game.leave': (w: World) => {\\n    const flow = flowOf(w);\\n    const activity = findActivity(flow.event);\\n    if (activity && flow.mode === 'event') activity.teardown(w);\\n    flow.mode = 'roam';\\n    flow.event = '';\\n330→  },\\n  'game.jump': (w: World, args: unknown) => {\\n    const given = rec(args);\\n    const step = strArg(given, 'step');\\n    const event = strArg(given, 'event');\\n    const day = numArg(given, 'day');\\n    if (step) {\\n      jumpTilt(w, step);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n340→    if (event) {\\n      startEvent(w, event);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (day === undefined) return;\\n    const list = programme();\\n    const at = list.findIndex((item) => item.day === day);\\n    if (at < 0) return;\\n    const flow = flowOf(w);\\n    flow.cursor = at;\\n350→    flow.day = day;\\n    applyLean(w, day);\\n    openItem(w, list[at]);\\n  },\\n  'game.finish': (w: World, args: unknown) => {\\n    if (flowOf(w).mode !== 'event') return;\\n    finishEvent(w, strArg(rec(args), 'rank'));\\n  },\\n};\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/driver.ts\",\"offset\":290,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"    if (act.wait >= BEAT) {\\n      if (flow.mode === 'results') advance(w);\\n      else sleep(w);\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Menu picks. Each one runs between steps. */\\nexport const retreatActions = {\\n  'game.begin': (w: World, args: unknown) => {\\n    const given = rec(args);\\n    applySave(w, given);\\n    const flow = flowOf(w);\\n    applyLean(w, flow.day);\\n    if (flow.credits) {\\n      flow.mode = 'roam';\\n      flow.event = '';\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    openItem(w, programme()[flow.cursor]);\\n  },\\n  'game.start': (w: World, args: unknown) => {\\n    const event = strArg(rec(args), 'event');\\n    if (!event) return;\\n    if (event === 'evening') openEvening(w);\\n    else if (event === 'credits') openCredits(w);\\n    else startEvent(w, event);\\n  },\\n  'game.carry': (w: World) => {\\n    if (flowOf(w).mode === 'results') advance(w);\\n  },\\n  'game.sleep': (w: World) => {\\n    if (flowOf(w).mode === 'evening') sleep(w);\\n  },\\n  'game.leave': (w: World) => {\\n    const flow = flowOf(w);\\n    const activity = findActivity(flow.event);\\n    if (activity && flow.mode === 'event') activity.teardown(w);\\n    flow.mode = 'roam';\\n    flow.event = '';\\n  },\\n  'game.jump': (w: World, args: unknown) => {\\n    const given = rec(args);\\n    const step = strArg(given, 'step');\\n    const event = strArg(given, 'event');\\n    const day = numArg(given, 'day');\\n    if (step) {\\n      jumpTilt(w, step);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (event) {\\n      startEvent(w, event);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (day === undefined) return;\\n    const list = programme();\\n    const at = list.findIndex((item) => item.day === day);\\n    if (at < 0) return;\\n    const flow = flowOf(w);\\n    flow.cursor = at;\\n    flow.day = day;\\n    applyLean(w, day);\\n    openItem(w, list[at]);\\n  },\\n  'game.finish': (w: World, args: unknown) => {\\n    if (flowOf(w).mode !== 'event') return;\\n    finishEvent(w, strArg(rec(args), 'rank'));\\n  },\\n};\\n\",\"total_lines\":358}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5595617d-2940-4e37-be25-ac4a9541724a-23","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"60→  showResults(event: string, rank: string): void;\\n  showEvening(): void;\\n  showCredits(): void;\\n}\\n\\nconst RANKS = ['Present', 'Adequate', 'Composed', 'Serene', 'Unsettling'];\\nconst JUMPS = ['morning', 'pose-a', 'pose-b', 'pose-c', 'pond', 'garden', 'paddle', 'line', 'group', 'tilt'];\\nconst REBINDS = ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right', 'footl', 'footr', 'breathe', 'act', 'gentle'];\\n\\n/** Builds every menu. They call each other, and the host for the sim. */\\n70→export function createMenus(host: Host): Menus {\\n  const pct = (n: number) => `${Math.round(n * 100)}%`;\\n\\n  const showTitle = () => {\\n    const kept = readSave(host.store);\\n    host.open(\\n      [\\n        { label: 'Begin', id: 'begin' },\\n        { label: 'Continue', id: 'continue', disabled: !kept },\\n        { label: 'Free Play', id: 'free', disabled: !kept || (kept.day <= 1 && !kept.credits) },\\n80→        { label: 'Group Class', id: 'group' },\\n        { label: 'Settings', id: 'settings' },\\n        { label: 'About', id: 'about' },\\n      ],\\n      'Thumb Yoga',\\n      'title',\\n      (id) => pickTitle(id),\\n    );\\n  };\\n\\n90→  function pickTitle(id: string): void {\\n    if (id === 'begin') {\\n      host.prefs = freshPrefs();\\n      host.icons = 'playstation';\\n      host.applyPrefs();\\n      host.save = freshSave();\\n      host.persist();\\n      host.run('game.begin', {});\\n      host.close();\\n      host.screen = 'play';\\n100→      host.publish();\\n    } else if (id === 'continue' || id === 'free') {\\n      const kept = readSave(host.store);\\n      if (!kept) return;\\n      host.save = kept;\\n      host.prefs = kept.settings;\\n      host.icons = host.prefs.icons;\\n      host.applyPrefs();\\n      host.run('game.begin', { ...kept });\\n      if (id === 'free' && !kept.credits) host.run('game.leave');\\n110→      host.close();\\n      host.screen = 'play';\\n      host.publish();\\n    } else if (id === 'group') {\\n      host.run('game.start', { event: 'group' });\\n      host.close();\\n      host.screen = 'play';\\n      host.publish();\\n    } else if (id === 'settings') showSettings(0);\\n    else {\\n120→      host.aboutFrom = 'title';\\n      showAbout();\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  const showSettings = (page: number) => {\\n    const items: MenuItem[] =\\n      page === 0\\n        ? [\\n            { label: `Music ${pct(host.prefs.music)}`, id: 'music' },\",\"content_concise\":\"60→  showResults(event: string, rank: string): void;\\n  showEvening(): void;\\n  showCredits(): void;\\n}\\n\\nconst RANKS = ['Present', 'Adequate', 'Composed', 'Serene', 'Unsettling'];\\nconst JUMPS = ['morning', 'pose-a', 'pose-b', 'pose-c', 'pond', 'garden', 'paddle', 'line', 'group', 'tilt'];\\nconst REBINDS = ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right', 'footl', 'footr', 'breathe', 'act', 'gentle'];\\n\\n/** Builds every menu. They call each other, and the host for the sim. */\\n70→export function createMenus(host: Host): Menus {\\n  const pct = (n: number) => `${Math.round(n * 100)}%`;\\n\\n  const showTitle = () => {\\n    const kept = readSave(host.store);\\n    host.open(\\n      [\\n        { label: 'Begin', id: 'begin' },\\n        { label: 'Continue', id: 'continue', disabled: !kept },\\n        { label: 'Free 