{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-89fec25b-cfdf-4b96-b043-afdfd1c52404-3","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Plan: Build PLAN.md’s original Wii Fit–inspired balance retreat and hand in TASK.md’s files\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. **Hand-in, title, and records.** The work root contains `PROGRESS.md`, `exit-interview.json`, and one self-contained HTML file. The HTML and the dev subfolder share the basename `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656` (SOURCE keeps the space in `Wii Fit`; `{Title}` is the on-screen title, with only OS-illegal characters sanitized, and that sanitization noted in `PROGRESS.md`). `{Title}` was chosen by executing a real RNG over a saved list of 50 playful riffs on “Wii Fit,” and that list plus the pick are in the dev folder. The page shows `{Title}` on the title screen. `exit-interview.json` is one JSON object in TASK.md’s exact shape, every value filled, `usage` exactly `added on import`, and its Source Information plus the three feedback lists match the in-game About/Credits screen in the same order. `aiHub.genre` is `Sports`, `aiHub.source` is `Wii Fit`, `aiHub.type` is `Game`, `aiHub.players` is `1–4`. The word `Wii` appears in-game only on that source line and the hub source field. There is no weight, BMI, calorie, or body-size scoring, and none of these source names: Fit Age, Fit Credits, Fit Piggy Bank, Body Test, Wuhu, or the source’s minigame, menu, or melody names. Opening the HTML does not need the network. It contains no `data:audio`, `.mp3`, `.wav`, or `.ogg` payload.\\n\\n2. **One balance verb, every shipped activity.** Lean (left stick or D-pad, WASD or arrows, pointer-locked mouse), left foot, right foot, and both feet are the only activity inputs, and a new activity changes what the weight moves, not how it is moved. Centre-of-balance is a point in a unit disc. With no input, time inside radius 0.22 is well under half (sway stays slow). A held full lean topples. Calm from breathing with the guide reduces sway. Topple stumbles and recentres; it is never a game over. Each activity, started from its own fresh state, scores 0–1000, maps to Present / Adequate / Composed / Serene / Unsettling (thresholds 0 / 300 / 550 / 750 / 900), awards 1–5 pebbles by rank, ends itself on a time box if the pad is put down, and leaves no stray bodies. On 10 seeds the perfect bot scores at least 750, the human-like bot (about 250 ms late, gain about 1.2) at least 550, the sloppy bot (about 350 ms, gain about 0.8) at least 300, and idle at most 500 and below the human-like bot. Random input does not throw. These are present and playable: Morning Check (still ring, reach, one-foot, Wobble Age from 18 to 82), Pose Class for Seated Nothing, Patient Chair, Heron, Archer, Sideways Comma, Folded Napkin, Polite Bridge, and Lighthouse (enter, hold, release; the body scrub follows the thumb), Still Pond (only matched breathing is correct; other input costs composure; a lure is not a real pause; doing nothing is Adequate), The Line, Paddle Glide, Sand Garden, and Great Tilt steps storm, everyone-east, centre-stone (island tilt follows centre-of-balance), and dawn. Reps Hall, Step Class, Hoop Patrol, Cliff Plunge, Island Jog’s race, Great Tilt counterweights, expert variants, and outfits are either fully playable or removed in that cut order with the day list reflowed and no leftover mention.\\n10→\\n3. **Five-day retreat you can finish.** A third-person island hub has the stations and the cast Tare, Plumb, Gerald, Bex, Old Nan, the Gull, and the Frog. Walking is allowed, and every programme or noticeboard entry can also “Go” without crossing the island. Five days each do a Morning Check plus their activities, then sleep, stamps, and a short remark. Pebbles are never spent; they stack on a cairn. Hidden pebbles and creeping plaques exist. Saves restore day, results, pebbles, finds, outfits, bests, and settings; erase asks inside the game, not `confirm()`. A shipped auto playthrough from a fresh save, on 3 seeds, visits every shipped day, activity, and finale step and reaches credits without throwing or a softlock. After credits, free play and a new daily check remain, and the ferry does not come back. At least 200 lines, none longer than two short sentences, include PLAN.md’s seed lines; Plumb has no exclamation marks. All music, effects, and voices are code. Fresh-save music volume is 0.1. The same line always babbles the same way. Songs and syllables render non-silent. Pose and lean clips are scrubbed from balance or pose progress, not played as a canned squat at the player.\\n\\n4. **10-foot shell.** The same screens serve a standard-mapped pad, keyboard, and mouse. Prompts follow the last device in the same frame: PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox glyphs (A B X Y, LB RB LT RT) after the Settings switch, key caps and mouse buttons after those inputs. Hover moves menu focus; click selects. Body text at 1920×1080 is at least 28 px; menus have at most six rows; results are one rank, one number, one sentence, not a dense data page. Pause opens Resume, Restart, Back to the island, Settings, Controls, Dev Mode, About/Credits, and Quit. Dev Mode, absent in a hub session, has live sliders for the numeric `game.*` tunables in PLAN.md (including wobble, breath, and pebble multiplier) and a reset to defaults, plus jumps to a day, activity, or finale step. Attract mode starts after 10 seconds without input on a front-end menu, loops through several activities (the driver may cheat), exits on key, click, or pad, and does not write the save. A touch-only profile shows “Controller or keyboard required” and a Settings control that opens by tap, with no on-screen touch play, while attract still runs. Without WebGPU the page shows a plain message naming current Chrome or Edge, not a blank page. Keyboard bindings can be rebound in Controls.\\n\\n5. **Couch Group Class and AI Hub ghost sessions.** Up to four players join mats on one screen (pad, or keyboard and mouse for one seat). Empty seats become CPU guests unless Settings turns them off. A round is three short classes dealt from one seed, then a podium. In AI Hub the mode is ghost: meta tags `hub:session` 1, `hub:session-players` 1-4, `hub:session-mode` ghost, `hub:session-minutes` 3, goal at most 60 characters, how-to at most 80 characters, `hub:webgpu` required, `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` 1-4, `hub:source` Wii Fit. The fetched session client is pasted unmodified and is byte-identical in the HTML. Its SHA-256 is `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a` (client 1.4.0). If the fetched file’s own banner is a newer client, record the new hash in `PROGRESS.md` and still inject those exact bytes. `?aihub` query keys are stripped before engine boot so unknown keys do not kill the engine. A session skips title, attract, and dev mode; pause does not pause the sim; `ready()` is reached with the engine actually running. Ghosts show the other players’ leans and do not affect local play. The hub harness passes for 2, 3, and 4 players and for host-leave: `__hubCheck.pass`, `body[data-complete=\\\"true\\\"]`, every frame `__engine.ready === true` and zero engine errors, a ghost present at 2 players, and no console line starting with `[AIHub]`. With no hub, the game is the full single-player build.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. **gating:** In the dev workspace, add or extend tests that call the shipped balance step and each shipped activity’s own setup, step, score, and bot from a fresh sim. Do not reimplement the model, mock the unit under test, or start past setup. Assert criterion 2’s bands, self-end, age range, Still Pond penalties, teardown, and no `NaN`. Run `node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs` from the dev folder (full run, not only `--quick`) and write stdout to `{SCRATCH}/verify.log`. Pass only if the exit code is 0 and the log has no failure lines and one final count line of zero failures. Also write `{SCRATCH}/npm-test.log` and `{SCRATCH}/npm-check.log` for `npm test` and `npm run check`, both passing. `npm run check` shows the engine matches its lock, or `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` lists the exact engine diff and why.\\n2. **gating:** The same verify command (or a node test it runs) drives the shipped auto/director path from a fresh save on 3 seeds, not a hand-rolled copy of the day table. `{SCRATCH}/verify.log` must show each seed reaching credits. Replay capture/restore of the shipped goldens continues exactly; that result is in the same log.\\n20→3. **gating:** Launch the handed-in HTML twice, from `file://`, in headless Chromium (`CHROMIUM_PATH` = the headless shell, flags `--no-sandbox --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`). Both runs must agree: `__engine.ready === true`, `__engine.errors` empty, no WebGPU downgrade error, `window.__game` (screen, attract, last device, glyph set, volumes, day, event, focus) shows the title screen and `{Title}`, and the music volume is 0.1. The canvas’s drawing width and height equal the requested view and are non-zero. A scripted standard-mapping pad or a key, applied through the real menu path, changes `__game` the same way both times. Save `{SCRATCH}/boot-1.log`, `{SCRATCH}/boot-2.log`, `{SCRATCH}/boot-1.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/boot-2.png`. Primary observable is that state, not the bitmap. If the screenshot is fully blank or uncleared while those state checks pass, write `{SCRATCH}/webgpu-readback.txt` and do not fail the launch for pixels alone (known SwiftShader limit). If a readback shows a partial scene that disagrees with `__game`, that is a failure. If Chromium cannot start, save the error as `{SCRATCH}/launch-error.txt`; node checks in steps 1–2 and the static checks in step 5 are then the bar. A started page with `ready` false or a blank state is never that fallback.\\n4. **gating:** Browser-drive the built page (same Chromium) and record `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`. Must show: PlayStation glyphs before any Xbox setting, Xbox glyphs after the setting, prompts switching to keys and to mouse in the same frame as those inputs, hover moving focus, attract beginning at 10–11 s of idle and leaving on a key, a click, and a pad press with the save unchanged, a dev slider changing live behaviour and Reset restoring the default, About text containing every Source Information field and each feedback answer, and at 1920×1080 every visible text node at least 28 px and no menu over six rows. WebKit (no WebGPU here) shows the Chrome-or-Edge message. An iPhone and a tablet Chromium profile show the controller-or-keyboard line, open Settings by `touchscreen.tap`, draw no touch stick, and still run attract.\\n5. **gating:** Serve the built HTML and the fetched harness files with a single `127.0.0.1` process on an OS-picked port; stop only that PID. Run the harness for `players=2`, `3`, `4`, and `players=3&scenario=host-leave` (latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5). Write `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`. Pass only if each run has `__hubCheck.pass`, `data-complete=\\\"true\\\"`, per-frame engine ready and zero engine errors, a ghost at 2 players, and no `[AIHub]` console line. `{SCRATCH}/hub-client.sha` is the injected client hash and matches criterion 5. A no-session load still reaches the title. Standalone client check: Enter, Space, Enter, Space leaves the client present and inactive, leaves `Math.random` unseeded, draws the screen, and adds no errors.\\n6. **gating:** Static pass on the work root: HTML and folder names, `exit-interview.json` parses and matches About, `PROGRESS.md` exists, game README says what the game is and which judgment calls were made, `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` is specific, and a search of the game sources for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, and `stub` is clean except test wording. Audio proof (song and syllable render, music 0.1) is in `{SCRATCH}/verify.log` or `{SCRATCH}/audio.log`.\\n7. **evidence:** 1920×1080 screenshots under `{SCRATCH}/shots/` of title, island, Pose Class HUD, Still Pond with a lure, The Line, Great Tilt wide shot, results, pause, Dev Mode, and About. Missing shots do not fail when steps 1–6 passed, including an honest launch fallback.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- Recreating Wii Fit’s BMI or weight test, trainer look, Balance Board, Miis, Wuhu Island, Fit Bank, logos, fonts, or melodies.\\n- Frame-rate optimization, except the hub’s 20-second `ready()` deadline.\\n- Cloning the ai-hub repository, adding npm dependencies, or `git init` / commits in the dev folder.\\n30→- Shared-world or more than four players, real gamepads, iOS Safari, and listening tests by ear.\\n- A second desktop-only layout, or touch controls beyond the required message and Settings button.\\n- A half-built cut-line activity left in the menu.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\nWork root is the folder that holds `STAGE.md`, `PLAN.md`, and `TASK.md`. The dev subfolder is a my-3dge full workspace created with that repo’s `new-game` tool (clone only for the generator, then delete it), then `npm ci` only. Game code lives on top of the read-only engine. Hub `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, and `round.js` are fetched from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/`, not from a clone. Deliverables in the work root: the one HTML file, `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`.\\n\\nWii Fit (Nintendo, 2007) was checked against public guides: daily Body Test (weight, BMI, centre-of-balance, Wii Fit Age), yoga holds with a breath guide, strength reps, aerobics (step, hoop, jog), lean-steered balance minigames, a trainer, and a time bank. PLAN.md already maps those into an original wobble game and bans body-size metrics and source names. Do not add activities the plan does not list.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\n40→Follow PLAN.md for design detail. This section is not a second spec: a structure that meets the criteria is acceptable even if file names differ, as long as the engine’s own workspace rules still hold (`labs/game` is where this engine mounts a game).\\n\\nKeep the balance step, activity rules, bots, and day tables as pure sim code with no rendering or DOM, so node tests drive them directly. The page only reads sim state, plays code audio, and sends input or menu choices back through the engine’s recorded channels. One bot writer produces perfect, human-like, sloppy, idle, attract, and CPU-guest input. Days, poses, charts, trays, and lines stay data. Ship a smaller complete loop early (boot, one activity, one-file HTML, hub `ready`) and add activities without breaking that loop. Put the single verify command in front of the node tests, the three-seed auto playthrough, audio renders, and the browser and harness stages. Publish `window.__game` for those checks. Write About copy and `exit-interview.json` from the same answers before the final HTML build.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [x] Save 50 titles, RNG-pick one, create the named dev folder with `new-game`, `npm ci`, and a work-root `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- [x] One-file HTML build, unmodified hub client and tags, tiny session scene, verify command skeleton, harness green with the engine actually ready.\\n- [x] Balance model, maps, disc, glyphs, Morning Check, four bots, dev sliders, and the score-band tests.\\n- [x] Scrubbed clips, Guest and Plumb, Pose Class, code voices, island, flow, saves, results.\\n- [x] Still Pond, The Line, Paddle Glide, Sand Garden, any later activities not cut, Great Tilt, and the 3-seed auto path to credits.\\n50→- [x] Same-screen Group Class and hub ghosts; harness 2, 3, 4, and host-leave.\\n- [x] Attract, settings, controls, About, touch-only and no-WebGPU pages, songs, and 200+ lines.\\n- [x] `exit-interview.json`, HTML copied to the work root, full verify, and two consistent boots with logs under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n- Cut Great Tilt counterweights, expert variants and outfits, Hoop Patrol, Reps Hall, the Island Jog race (the walk stays), Cliff Plunge, and Step Class. Group Class's middle class is Heron only. The group score is the 0–1000 mean of the three classes, not a sum to 3000. The island terrain cell size is 4.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- TASK.md says a headless WebGPU screenshot can be blank and to trust game state. A fully blank bitmap with `ready` and a real `__game` screen is that limit, not an automatic fail. A readable but empty or partial frame that disagrees with `__game` is a game bug.\\n- The live client fetched while writing this plan is banner `1.4.0`, matching PLAN.md’s pin. If the upstream file moves, the unmodified fetched bytes win over the old hash, and the new hash goes in `PROGRESS.md`.\\n60→- The required basename contains a space because SOURCE is `Wii Fit`. That is intentional, not a reason to drop the source token.\\n- PLAN.md forbids `git init` in the dev folder even though the engine guide says to commit. Do not init or commit.\\n- Other agents share ports and memory. Do not bind 5173, do not kill processes you did not start, and do not run more than two browsers. `earlyoom` killing a browser is memory pressure, not a game bug to retry in a loop.\\n- Great Tilt’s session scene must stay small: SwiftShader has needed most of the harness’s 20 s just to boot. The island must not load in a hub session.\\n- Firefox has no WebGPU here. Only Chromium can run the game; WebKit is only for the no-WebGPU message.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Plan: Build PLAN.md’s original Wii Fit–inspired balance retreat and hand in TASK.md’s files\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. **Hand-in, title, and records.** The work root contains `PROGRESS.md`, `exit-interview.json`, and one self-contained HTML file. The HTML and the dev subfolder share the basename `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656` (SOURCE keeps the space in `Wii Fit`; `{Title}` is the on-screen title, with only OS-illegal characters sanitized, and that sanitization noted in `PROGRESS.md`). `{Title}` was chosen by executing a real RNG over a saved list of 50 playful riffs on “Wii Fit,” and that list plus the pick are in the dev folder. The page shows `{Title}` on the title screen. `exit-interview.json` is one JSON object in TASK.md’s exact shape, every value filled, `usage` exactly `added on import`, and its Source Information plus the three feedback lists match the in-game About/Credits screen in the same order. `aiHub.genre` is `Sports`, `aiHub.source` is `Wii Fit`, `aiHub.type` is `Game`, `aiHub.players` is `1–4`. The word `Wii` appears in-game only on that source line and the hub source field. There is no weight, BMI, calorie, or body-size scoring, and none of these source names: Fit Age, Fit Credits, Fit Piggy Bank, Body Test, Wuhu, or the source’s minigame, menu, or melody names. Opening the HTML does not need the network. It contains no `data:audio`, `.mp3`, `.wav`, or `.ogg` payload.\\n\\n2. **One balance verb, every shipped activity.** Lean (left stick or D-pad, WASD or arrows, pointer-locked mouse), left foot, right foot, and both feet are the only activity inputs, and a new activity changes what the weight moves, not how it is moved. Centre-of-balance is a point in a unit disc. With no input, time inside radius 0.22 is well under half (sway stays slow). A held full lean topples. Calm from breathing with the guide reduces sway. Topple stumbles and recentres; it is never a game over. Each activity, started from its own fresh state, scores 0–1000, maps to Present / Adequate / Composed / Serene / Unsettling (thresholds 0 / 300 / 550 / 750 / 900), awards 1–5 pebbles by rank, ends itself on a time box if the pad is put down, and leaves no stray bodies. On 10 seeds the perfect bot scores at least 750, the human-like bot (about 250 ms late, gain about 1.2) at least 550, the sloppy bot (about 350 ms, gain about 0.8) at least 300, and idle at most 500 and below the human-like bot. Random input does not throw. These are present and playable: Morning Check (still ring, reach, one-foot, Wobble Age from 18 to 82), Pose Class for Seated Nothing, Patient Chair, Heron, Archer, Sideways Comma, Folded Napkin, Polite Bridge, and Lighthouse (enter, hold, release; the body scrub follows the thumb), Still Pond (only matched breathing is correct; other input costs composure; a lure is not a real pause; doing nothing is Adequate), The Line, Paddle Glide, Sand Garden, and Great Tilt steps storm, everyone-east, centre-stone (island tilt follows centre-of-balance), and dawn. Reps Hall, Step Class, Hoop Patrol, Cliff Plunge, Island Jog’s race, Great Tilt counterweights, expert variants, and outfits are either fully playable or removed in that cut order with the day list reflowed and no leftover mention.\\n10→\\n3. **Five-day retreat you can finish.** A third-person island hub has the stations and the cast Tare, Plumb, Gerald, Bex, Old Nan, the Gull, and the Frog. Walking is allowed, and every programme or noticeboard entry can also “Go” without crossing the island. Five days each do a Morning Check plus their activities, then sleep, stamps, and a short remark. Pebbles are never spent; they stack on a cairn. Hidden pebbles and creeping plaques exist. Saves restore day, results, pebbles, finds, outfits, bests, and settings; erase asks inside the game, not `confirm()`. A shipped auto playthrough from a fresh save, on 3 seeds, visits every shipped day, activity, and finale step and reaches credits without throwing or a softlock. After credits, free play and a new daily check remain, and the ferry does not come back. At least 200 lines, none longer than two short sentences, include PLAN.md’s seed lines; Plumb has no exclamation marks. All music, effects, and voices are code. Fresh-save music volume is 0.1. The same line always babbles the same way. Songs and syllables render non-silent. Pose and lean clips are scrubbed from balance or pose progress, not played as a canned squat at the player.\\n\\n4. **10-foot shell.** The same screens serve a standard-mapped pad, keyboard, and mouse. Prompts follow the last device in the same frame: PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox glyphs (A B X Y, LB RB LT RT) after the Settings switch, key caps and mouse buttons after those inputs. Hover moves menu focus; click selects. Body text at 1920×1080 is at least 28 px; menus have at most six rows; results are one rank, one number, one sentence, not a dense data page. Pause opens Resume, Restart, Back to the island, Settings, Controls, Dev Mode, About/Credits, and Quit. Dev Mode, absent in a hub session, has live sliders for the numeric `game.*` tunables in PLAN.md (including wobble, breath, and pebble multiplier) and a reset to defaults, plus jumps to a day, activity, or finale step. Attract mode starts after 10 seconds without input on a front-end menu, loops through several activities (the driver may cheat), exits on key, click, or pad, and does not write the save. A touch-only profile shows “Controller or keyboard required” and a Settings control that opens by tap, with no on-screen touch play, while attract still runs. Without WebGPU the page shows a plain message naming current Chrome or Edge, not a blank page. Keyboard bindings can be rebound in Controls.\\n\\n5. **Couch Group Class and AI Hub ghost sessions.** Up to four players join mats on one screen (pad, or keyboard and mouse for one seat). Empty seats become CPU guests unless Settings turns them off. A round is three short classes dealt from one seed, then a podium. In AI Hub the mode is ghost: meta tags `hub:session` 1, `hub:session-players` 1-4, `hub:session-mode` ghost, `hub:session-minutes` 3, goal at most 60 characters, how-to at most 80 characters, `hub:webgpu` required, `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` 1-4, `hub:source` Wii Fit. The fetched session client is pasted unmodified and is byte-identical in the HTML. Its SHA-256 is `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a` (client 1.4.0). If the fetched file’s own banner is a newer client, record the new hash in `PROGRESS.md` and still inject those exact bytes. `?aihub` query keys are stripped before engine boot so unknown keys do not kill the engine. A session skips title, attract, and dev mode; pause does not pause the sim; `ready()` is reached with the engine actually running. Ghosts show the other players’ leans and do not affect local play. The hub harness passes for 2, 3, and 4 players and for host-leave: `__hubCheck.pass`, `body[data-complete=\\\"true\\\"]`, every frame `__engine.ready === true` and zero engine errors, a ghost present at 2 players, and no console line starting with `[AIHub]`. With no hub, the game is the full single-player build.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. **gating:** In the dev workspace, add or extend tests that call the shipped balance step and each shipped activity’s own setup, step, score, and bot from a fresh sim. Do not reimplement the model, mock the unit under test, or start past setup. Assert criterion 2’s bands, self-end, age range, Still Pond penalties, teardown, and no `NaN`. Run `node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs` from the dev folder (full run, not only `--quick`) and write stdout to `{SCRATCH}/verify.log`. Pass only if the exit code is 0 and the log has no failure lines and one final count line of zero failures. Also write `{SCRATCH}/npm-test.log` and `{SCRATCH}/npm-check.log` for `npm test` and `npm run check`, both passing. `npm run check` shows the engine matches its lock, or `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` lists the exact engine diff and why.\\n2. **gating:** The same verify command (or a node test it runs) drives the shipped auto/director path from a fresh save on 3 seeds, not a hand-rolled copy of the day table. `{SCRATCH}/verify.log` must show each seed reaching credits. Replay capture/restore of the shipped goldens continues exactly; that result is in the same log.\\n20→3. **gating:** Launch the handed-in HTML twice, from `file://`, in headless Chromium (`CHROMIUM_PATH` = the headless shell, flags `--no-sandbox --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`). Both runs must agree: `__engine.ready === true`, `__engine.errors` empty, no WebGPU downgrade error, `window.__game` (screen, attract, last device, glyph set, volumes, day, event, focus) shows the title screen and `{Title}`, and the music volume is 0.1. The canvas’s drawing width and height equal the requested view and are non-zero. A scripted standard-mapping pad or a key, applied through the real menu path, changes `__game` the same way both times. Save `{SCRATCH}/boot-1.log`, `{SCRATCH}/boot-2.log`, `{SCRATCH}/boot-1.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/boot-2.png`. Primary observable is that state, not the bitmap. If the screenshot is fully blank or uncleared while those state checks pass, write `{SCRATCH}/webgpu-readback.txt` and do not fail the launch for pixels alone (known SwiftShader limit). If a readback shows a partial scene that disagrees with `__game`, that is a failure. If Chromium cannot start, save the error as `{SCRATCH}/launch-error.txt`; node checks in steps 1–2 and the static checks in step 5 are then the bar. A started page with `ready` false or a blank state is never that fallback.\\n4. **gating:** Browser-drive the built page (same Chromium) and record `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`. Must show: PlayStation glyphs before any Xbox setting, Xbox glyphs after the setting, prompts switching to keys and to mouse in the same frame as those inputs, hover moving focus, attract beginning at 10–11 s of idle and leaving on a key, a click, and a pad press with the save unchanged, a dev slider changing live behaviour and Reset restoring the default, About text containing every Source Information field and each feedback answer, and at 1920×1080 every visible text node at least 28 px and no menu over six rows. WebKit (no WebGPU here) shows the Chrome-or-Edge message. An iPhone and a tablet Chromium profile show the controller-or-keyboard line, open Settings by `touchscreen.tap`, draw no touch stick, and still run attract.\\n5. **gating:** Serve the built HTML and the fetched harness files with a single `127.0.0.1` process on an OS-picked port; stop only that PID. Run the harness for `players=2`, `3`, `4`, and `players=3&scenario=host-leave` (latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5). Write `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`. Pass only if each run has `__hubCheck.pass`, `data-complete=\\\"true\\\"`, per-frame engine ready and zero engine errors, a ghost at 2 players, and no `[AIHub]` console line. `{SCRATCH}/hub-client.sha` is the injected client hash and matches criterion 5. A no-session load still reaches the title. Standalone client check: Enter, Space, Enter, Space leaves the client present and inactive, leaves `Math.random` unseeded, draws the screen, and adds no errors.\\n6. **gating:** Static pass on the work root: HTML and folder names, `exit-interview.json` parses and matches About, `PROGRESS.md` exists, game README says what the game is and which judgment calls were made, `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` is specific, and a search of the game sources for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, and `stub` is clean except test wording. Audio proof (song and syllable render, music 0.1) is in `{SCRATCH}/verify.log` or `{SCRATCH}/audio.log`.\\n7. **evidence:** 1920×1080 screenshots under `{SCRATCH}/shots/` of title, island, Pose Class HUD, Still Pond with a lure, The Line, Great Tilt wide shot, results, pause, Dev Mode, and About. Missing shots do not fail when steps 1–6 passed, including an honest launch fallback.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- Recreating Wii Fit’s BMI or weight test, trainer look, Balance Board, Miis, Wuhu Island, Fit Bank, logos, fonts, or melodies.\\n- Frame-rate optimization, except the hub’s 20-second `ready()` deadline.\\n- Cloning the ai-hub repository, adding npm dependencies, or `git init` / commits in the dev folder.\\n30→- Shared-world or more than four players, real gamepads, iOS Safari, and listening tests by ear.\\n- A second desktop-only layout, or touch controls beyond the required message and Settings button.\\n- A half-built cut-line activity left in the menu.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\nWork root is the folder that holds `STAGE.md`, `PLAN.md`, and `TASK.md`. The dev subfolder is a my-3dge full workspace created with that repo’s `new-game` tool (clone only for the generator, then delete it), then `npm ci` only. Game code lives on top of the read-only engine. Hub `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, and `round.js` are fetched from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/`, not from a clone. Deliverables in the work root: the one HTML file, `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`.\\n\\nWii Fit (Nintendo, 2007) was checked against public guides: daily Body Test (weight, BMI, centre-of-balance, Wii Fit Age), yoga holds with a breath guide, strength reps, aerobics (step, hoop, jog), lean-steered balance minigames, a trainer, and a time bank. PLAN.md already maps those into an original wobble game and bans body-size metrics and source names. Do not add activities the plan does not list.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\n40→Follow PLAN.md for design detail. This section is not a second spec: a structure that meets the criteria is acceptable even if file names differ, as long as the engine’s own workspace rules still hold (`labs/game` is where this engine mounts a game).\\n\\nKeep the balance step, activity rules, bots, and day tables as pure sim code with no rendering or DOM, so node tests drive them directly. The page only reads sim state, plays code audio, and sends input or menu choices back through the engine’s recorded channels. One bot writer produces perfect, human-like, sloppy, idle, attract, and CPU-guest input. Days, poses, charts, trays, and lines stay data. Ship a smaller complete loop early (boot, one activity, one-file HTML, hub `ready`) and add activities without breaking that loop. Put the single verify command in front of the node tests, the three-seed auto playthrough, audio renders, and the browser and harness stages. Publish `window.__game` for those checks. Write About copy and `exit-interview.json` from the same answers before the final HTML build.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [x] Save 50 titles, RNG-pick one, create the named dev folder with `new-game`, `npm ci`, and a work-root `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- [x] One-file HTML build, unmodified hub client and tags, tiny session scene, verify command skeleton, harness green with the engine actually ready.\\n- [x] Balance model, maps, disc, glyphs, Morning Check, four bots, dev sliders, and the score-band tests.\\n- [x] Scrubbed clips, Guest and Plumb, Pose Class, code voices, island, flow, saves, results.\\n- [x] Still Pond, The Line, Paddle Glide, Sand Garden, any later activities not cut, Great Tilt, and the 3-seed auto path to credits.\\n50→- [x] Same-screen Group Class and hub ghosts; harness 2, 3, 4, and host-leave.\\n- [x] Attract, settings, controls, About, touch-only and no-WebGPU pages, songs, and 200+ lines.\\n- [x] `exit-interview.json`, HTML copied to the work root, full verify, and two consistent boots with logs under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n- Cut Great Tilt counterweights, expert variants and outfits, Hoop Patrol, Reps Hall, the Island Jog race (the walk stays), Cliff Plunge, and Step Class. Group Class's middle class is Heron only. The group score is the 0–1000 mean of the three classes, not a sum to 3000. The island terrain cell size is 4.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- TASK.md says a headless WebGPU screenshot can be blank and to trust game state. A fully blank bitmap with `ready` and a real `__game` screen is that limit, not an automatic fail. A readable but empty or partial frame that disagrees with `__game` is a game bug.\\n- The live client fetched while writing this plan is banner `1.4.0`, matching PLAN.md’s pin. If the upstream file moves, the unmodified fetched bytes win over the old hash, and the new hash goes in `PROGRESS.md`.\\n60→- The required basename contains a space because SOURCE is `Wii Fit`. That is intentional, not a reason to drop the source token.\\n- PLAN.md forbids `git init` in the dev folder even though the engine guide says to commit. Do not init or commit.\\n- Other agents share ports and memory. Do not bind 5173, do not kill processes you did not start, and do not run more than two browsers. `earlyoom` killing a browser is memory pressure, not a game bug to retry in a loop.\\n- Great Tilt’s session scene must stay small: SwiftShader has needed most of the harness’s 20 s just to boot. The island must not load in a hub session.\\n- Firefox has no WebGPU here. Only Chromium can run the game; WebKit is only for the no-WebGPU message.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc%2Fwork/01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc/goal/plan.md\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"# Plan: Build PLAN.md’s original Wii Fit–inspired balance retreat and hand in TASK.md’s files\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. **Hand-in, title, and records.** The work root contains `PROGRESS.md`, `exit-interview.json`, and one self-contained HTML file. The HTML and the dev subfolder share the basename `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656` (SOURCE keeps the space in `Wii Fit`; `{Title}` is the on-screen title, with only OS-illegal characters sanitized, and that sanitization noted in `PROGRESS.md`). `{Title}` was chosen by executing a real RNG over a saved list of 50 playful riffs on “Wii Fit,” and that list plus the pick are in the dev folder. The page shows `{Title}` on the title screen. `exit-interview.json` is one JSON object in TASK.md’s exact shape, every value filled, `usage` exactly `added on import`, and its Source Information plus the three feedback lists match the in-game About/Credits screen in the same order. `aiHub.genre` is `Sports`, `aiHub.source` is `Wii Fit`, `aiHub.type` is `Game`, `aiHub.players` is `1–4`. The word `Wii` appears in-game only on that source line and the hub source field. There is no weight, BMI, calorie, or body-size scoring, and none of these source names: Fit Age, Fit Credits, Fit Piggy Bank, Body Test, Wuhu, or the source’s minigame, menu, or melody names. Opening the HTML does not need the network. It contains no `data:audio`, `.mp3`, `.wav`, or `.ogg` payload.\\n\\n2. **One balance verb, every shipped activity.** Lean (left stick or D-pad, WASD or arrows, pointer-locked mouse), left foot, right foot, and both feet are the only activity inputs, and a new activity changes what the weight moves, not how it is moved. Centre-of-balance is a point in a unit disc. With no input, time inside radius 0.22 is well under half (sway stays slow). A held full lean topples. Calm from breathing with the guide reduces sway. Topple stumbles and recentres; it is never a game over. Each activity, started from its own fresh state, scores 0–1000, maps to Present / Adequate / Composed / Serene / Unsettling (thresholds 0 / 300 / 550 / 750 / 900), awards 1–5 pebbles by rank, ends itself on a time box if the pad is put down, and leaves no stray bodies. On 10 seeds the perfect bot scores at least 750, the human-like bot (about 250 ms late, gain about 1.2) at least 550, the sloppy bot (about 350 ms, gain about 0.8) at least 300, and idle at most 500 and below the human-like bot. Random input does not throw. These are present and playable: Morning Check (still ring, reach, one-foot, Wobble Age from 18 to 82), Pose Class for Seated Nothing, Patient Chair, Heron, Archer, Sideways Comma, Folded Napkin, Polite Bridge, and Lighthouse (enter, hold, release; the body scrub follows the thumb), Still Pond (only matched breathing is correct; other input costs composure; a lure is not a real pause; doing nothing is Adequate), The Line, Paddle Glide, Sand Garden, and Great Tilt steps storm, everyone-east, centre-stone (island tilt follows centre-of-balance), and dawn. Reps Hall, Step Class, Hoop Patrol, Cliff Plunge, Island Jog’s race, Great Tilt counterweights, expert variants, and outfits are either fully playable or removed in that cut order with the day list reflowed and no leftover mention.\\n\\n3. **Five-day retreat you can finish.** A third-person island hub has the stations and the cast Tare, Plumb, Gerald, Bex, Old Nan, the Gull, and the Frog. Walking is allowed, and every programme or noticeboard entry can also “Go” without crossing the island. Five days each do a Morning Check plus their activities, then sleep, stamps, and a short remark. Pebbles are never spent; they stack on a cairn. Hidden pebbles and creeping plaques exist. Saves restore day, results, pebbles, finds, outfits, bests, and settings; erase asks inside the game, not `confirm()`. A shipped auto playthrough from a fresh save, on 3 seeds, visits every shipped day, activity, and finale step and reaches credits without throwing or a softlock. After credits, free play and a new daily check remain, and the ferry does not come back. At least 200 lines, none longer than two short sentences, include PLAN.md’s seed lines; Plumb has no exclamation marks. All music, effects, and voices are code. Fresh-save music volume is 0.1. The same line always babbles the same way. Songs and syllables render non-silent. Pose and lean clips are scrubbed from balance or pose progress, not played as a canned squat at the player.\\n\\n4. **10-foot shell.** The same screens serve a standard-mapped pad, keyboard, and mouse. Prompts follow the last device in the same frame: PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox glyphs (A B X Y, LB RB LT RT) after the Settings switch, key caps and mouse buttons after those inputs. Hover moves menu focus; click selects. Body text at 1920×1080 is at least 28 px; menus have at most six rows; results are one rank, one number, one sentence, not a dense data page. Pause opens Resume, Restart, Back to the island, Settings, Controls, Dev Mode, About/Credits, and Quit. Dev Mode, absent in a hub session, has live sliders for the numeric `game.*` tunables in PLAN.md (including wobble, breath, and pebble multiplier) and a reset to defaults, plus jumps to a day, activity, or finale step. Attract mode starts after 10 seconds without input on a front-end menu, loops through several activities (the driver may cheat), exits on key, click, or pad, and does not write the save. A touch-only profile shows “Controller or keyboard required” and a Settings control that opens by tap, with no on-screen touch play, while attract still runs. Without WebGPU the page shows a plain message naming current Chrome or Edge, not a blank page. Keyboard bindings can be rebound in Controls.\\n\\n5. **Couch Group Class and AI Hub ghost sessions.** Up to four players join mats on one screen (pad, or keyboard and mouse for one seat). Empty seats become CPU guests unless Settings turns them off. A round is three short classes dealt from one seed, then a podium. In AI Hub the mode is ghost: meta tags `hub:session` 1, `hub:session-players` 1-4, `hub:session-mode` ghost, `hub:session-minutes` 3, goal at most 60 characters, how-to at most 80 characters, `hub:webgpu` required, `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` 1-4, `hub:source` Wii Fit. The fetched session client is pasted unmodified and is byte-identical in the HTML. Its SHA-256 is `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a` (client 1.4.0). If the fetched file’s own banner is a newer client, record the new hash in `PROGRESS.md` and still inject those exact bytes. `?aihub` query keys are stripped before engine boot so unknown keys do not kill the engine. A session skips title, attract, and dev mode; pause does not pause the sim; `ready()` is reached with the engine actually running. Ghosts show the other players’ leans and do not affect local play. The hub harness passes for 2, 3, and 4 players and for host-leave: `__hubCheck.pass`, `body[data-complete=\\\"true\\\"]`, every frame `__engine.ready === true` and zero engine errors, a ghost present at 2 players, and no console line starting with `[AIHub]`. With no hub, the game is the full single-player build.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. **gating:** In the dev workspace, add or extend tests that call the shipped balance step and each shipped activity’s own setup, step, score, and bot from a fresh sim. Do not reimplement the model, mock the unit under test, or start past setup. Assert criterion 2’s bands, self-end, age range, Still Pond penalties, teardown, and no `NaN`. Run `node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs` from the dev folder (full run, not only `--quick`) and write stdout to `{SCRATCH}/verify.log`. Pass only if the exit code is 0 and the log has no failure lines and one final count line of zero failures. Also write `{SCRATCH}/npm-test.log` and `{SCRATCH}/npm-check.log` for `npm test` and `npm run check`, both passing. `npm run check` shows the engine matches its lock, or `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` lists the exact engine diff and why.\\n2. **gating:** The same verify command (or a node test it runs) drives the shipped auto/director path from a fresh save on 3 seeds, not a hand-rolled copy of the day table. `{SCRATCH}/verify.log` must show each seed reaching credits. Replay capture/restore of the shipped goldens continues exactly; that result is in the same log.\\n3. **gating:** Launch the handed-in HTML twice, from `file://`, in headless Chromium (`CHROMIUM_PATH` = the headless shell, flags `--no-sandbox --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`). Both runs must agree: `__engine.ready === true`, `__engine.errors` empty, no WebGPU downgrade error, `window.__game` (screen, attract, last device, glyph set, volumes, day, event, focus) shows the title screen and `{Title}`, and the music volume is 0.1. The canvas’s drawing width and height equal the requested view and are non-zero. A scripted standard-mapping pad or a key, applied through the real menu path, changes `__game` the same way both times. Save `{SCRATCH}/boot-1.log`, `{SCRATCH}/boot-2.log`, `{SCRATCH}/boot-1.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/boot-2.png`. Primary observable is that state, not the bitmap. If the screenshot is fully blank or uncleared while those state checks pass, write `{SCRATCH}/webgpu-readback.txt` and do not fail the launch for pixels alone (known SwiftShader limit). If a readback shows a partial scene that disagrees with `__game`, that is a failure. If Chromium cannot start, save the error as `{SCRATCH}/launch-error.txt`; node checks in steps 1–2 and the static checks in step 5 are then the bar. A started page with `ready` false or a blank state is never that fallback.\\n4. **gating:** Browser-drive the built page (same Chromium) and record `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`. Must show: PlayStation glyphs before any Xbox setting, Xbox glyphs after the setting, prompts switching to keys and to mouse in the same frame as those inputs, hover moving focus, attract beginning at 10–11 s of idle and leaving on a key, a click, and a pad press with the save unchanged, a dev slider changing live behaviour and Reset restoring the default, About text containing every Source Information field and each feedback answer, and at 1920×1080 every visible text node at least 28 px and no menu over six rows. WebKit (no WebGPU here) shows the Chrome-or-Edge message. An iPhone and a tablet Chromium profile show the controller-or-keyboard line, open Settings by `touchscreen.tap`, draw no touch stick, and still run attract.\\n5. **gating:** Serve the built HTML and the fetched harness files with a single `127.0.0.1` process on an OS-picked port; stop only that PID. Run the harness for `players=2`, `3`, `4`, and `players=3&scenario=host-leave` (latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5). Write `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`. Pass only if each run has `__hubCheck.pass`, `data-complete=\\\"true\\\"`, per-frame engine ready and zero engine errors, a ghost at 2 players, and no `[AIHub]` console line. `{SCRATCH}/hub-client.sha` is the injected client hash and matches criterion 5. A no-session load still reaches the title. Standalone client check: Enter, Space, Enter, Space leaves the client present and inactive, leaves `Math.random` unseeded, draws the screen, and adds no errors.\\n6. **gating:** Static pass on the work root: HTML and folder names, `exit-interview.json` parses and matches About, `PROGRESS.md` exists, game README says what the game is and which judgment calls were made, `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` is specific, and a search of the game sources for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, and `stub` is clean except test wording. Audio proof (song and syllable render, music 0.1) is in `{SCRATCH}/verify.log` or `{SCRATCH}/audio.log`.\\n7. **evidence:** 1920×1080 screenshots under `{SCRATCH}/shots/` of title, island, Pose Class HUD, Still Pond with a lure, The Line, Great Tilt wide shot, results, pause, Dev Mode, and About. Missing shots do not fail when steps 1–6 passed, including an honest launch fallback.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- Recreating Wii Fit’s BMI or weight test, trainer look, Balance Board, Miis, Wuhu Island, Fit Bank, logos, fonts, or melodies.\\n- Frame-rate optimization, except the hub’s 20-second `ready()` deadline.\\n- Cloning the ai-hub repository, adding npm dependencies, or `git init` / commits in the dev folder.\\n- Shared-world or more than four players, real gamepads, iOS Safari, and listening tests by ear.\\n- A second desktop-only layout, or touch controls beyond the required message and Settings button.\\n- A half-built cut-line activity left in the menu.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\nWork root is the folder that holds `STAGE.md`, `PLAN.md`, and `TASK.md`. The dev subfolder is a my-3dge full workspace created with that repo’s `new-game` tool (clone only for the generator, then delete it), then `npm ci` only. Game code lives on top of the read-only engine. Hub `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, and `round.js` are fetched from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/`, not from a clone. Deliverables in the work root: the one HTML file, `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`.\\n\\nWii Fit (Nintendo, 2007) was checked against public guides: daily Body Test (weight, BMI, centre-of-balance, Wii Fit Age), yoga holds with a breath guide, strength reps, aerobics (step, hoop, jog), lean-steered balance minigames, a trainer, and a time bank. PLAN.md already maps those into an original wobble game and bans body-size metrics and source names. Do not add activities the plan does not list.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nFollow PLAN.md for design detail. This section is not a second spec: a structure that meets the criteria is acceptable even if file names differ, as long as the engine’s own workspace rules still hold (`labs/game` is where this engine mounts a game).\\n\\nKeep the balance step, activity rules, bots, and day tables as pure sim code with no rendering or DOM, so node tests drive them directly. The page only reads sim state, plays code audio, and sends input or menu choices back through the engine’s recorded channels. One bot writer produces perfect, human-like, sloppy, idle, attract, and CPU-guest input. Days, poses, charts, trays, and lines stay data. Ship a smaller complete loop early (boot, one activity, one-file HTML, hub `ready`) and add activities without breaking that loop. Put the single verify command in front of the node tests, the three-seed auto playthrough, audio renders, and the browser and harness stages. Publish `window.__game` for those checks. Write About copy and `exit-interview.json` from the same answers before the final HTML build.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [x] Save 50 titles, RNG-pick one, create the named dev folder with `new-game`, `npm ci`, and a work-root `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- [x] One-file HTML build, unmodified hub client and tags, tiny session scene, verify command skeleton, harness green with the engine actually ready.\\n- [x] Balance model, maps, disc, glyphs, Morning Check, four bots, dev sliders, and the score-band tests.\\n- [x] Scrubbed clips, Guest and Plumb, Pose Class, code voices, island, flow, saves, results.\\n- [x] Still Pond, The Line, Paddle Glide, Sand Garden, any later activities not cut, Great Tilt, and the 3-seed auto path to credits.\\n- [x] Same-screen Group Class and hub ghosts; harness 2, 3, 4, and host-leave.\\n- [x] Attract, settings, controls, About, touch-only and no-WebGPU pages, songs, and 200+ lines.\\n- [x] `exit-interview.json`, HTML copied to the work root, full verify, and two consistent boots with logs under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n- Cut Great Tilt counterweights, expert variants and outfits, Hoop Patrol, Reps Hall, the Island Jog race (the walk stays), Cliff Plunge, and Step Class. Group Class's middle class is Heron only. The group score is the 0–1000 mean of the three classes, not a sum to 3000. The island terrain cell size is 4.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- TASK.md says a headless WebGPU screenshot can be blank and to trust game state. A fully blank bitmap with `ready` and a real `__game` screen is that limit, not an automatic fail. A readable but empty or partial frame that disagrees with `__game` is a game bug.\\n- The live client fetched while writing this plan is banner `1.4.0`, matching PLAN.md’s pin. If the upstream file moves, the unmodified fetched bytes win over the old hash, and the new hash goes in `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- The required basename contains a space because SOURCE is `Wii Fit`. That is intentional, not a reason to drop the source token.\\n- PLAN.md forbids `git init` in the dev folder even though the engine guide says to commit. Do not init or commit.\\n- Other agents share ports and memory. Do not bind 5173, do not kill processes you did not start, and do not run more than two browsers. `earlyoom` killing a browser is memory pressure, not a game bug to retry in a loop.\\n- Great Tilt’s session scene must stay small: SwiftShader has needed most of the harness’s 20 s just to boot. The island must not load in a hub session.\\n- Firefox has no WebGPU here. Only Chromium can run the game; WebKit is only for the no-WebGPU message.\\n\",\"total_lines\":64}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-89fec25b-cfdf-4b96-b043-afdfd1c52404-4","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Little Fulcrum. A lawn on a sand dome, a pond, a cove, and a guest who can walk.\\n * Activities still run on the balance step. The ground mesh stays put. The sea tips against the lean,\\n * plaques creep west, and the guest walks downhill.\\n */\\nimport {\\n  addTerrainBody,\\n  createCharacter,\\n  defineComponent,\\n10→  defineProp,\\n  defineScene,\\n  defineTerrain,\\n  getTerrain,\\n  physicsOf,\\n  playClip,\\n  spawnActor,\\n  spawnProp,\\n  type Intents,\\n  type World,\\n20→} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport '../cast/clips';\\nimport { boot, frame, retreatActions } from './driver';\\nimport { actOf, flowOf } from './events/kit';\\nimport { posesFor } from './events/pose';\\n\\ndefineTerrain('terrain:fulcrum', {\\n  size: [60, 60],\\n  cell: 4,\\n  origin: [-120, 0, -120],\\n30→  seed: 4,\\n  height: 0,\\n  ridges: 0,\\n  high: 7,\\n  materials: ['material:sand', 'material:sand', 'material:lawn'],\\n  hills: [\\n    { at: [0, 0], radius: 110, height: 11 },\\n    { at: [10, -6], radius: 22, height: 4 },\\n    { at: [24, 18], radius: 16, height: -3.2 },\\n    { at: [0, -78], radius: 30, height: -6 },\\n40→  ],\\n  flats: [\\n    { rect: [-14, -14, 14, 14], height: 9.2, margin: 8 },\\n    { rect: [-34, -2, -16, 16], height: 8.4, margin: 6 },\\n    { rect: [16, 8, 34, 28], height: 7.6, margin: 6 },\\n    { rect: [-8, -48, 10, -28], height: 6.2, margin: 6 },\\n    { rect: [32, 0, 52, 16], height: 8.8, margin: 5 },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\n50→defineProp('prop:sea', {\\n  description: 'The sea. It is flat, and it pretends to breathe.',\\n  parts: [\\n    {\\n      name: 'water',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:box',\\n      params: { width: 280, height: 0.35, depth: 280 },\\n      material: 'material:sea',\\n    },\\n  ],\\n60→});\\n\\ndefineProp('prop:mat', {\\n  description: 'A round mat.',\\n  parts: [\\n    {\\n      name: 'disc',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:frustum',\\n      params: { radiusTop: 1.15, radiusBottom: 1.2, height: 0.08, radialSegments: 16, smooth: true },\\n      material: 'material:sand',\\n70→    },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\ndefineProp('prop:cairn', {\\n  description: 'Pebbles that are not spent.',\\n  parts: [\\n    {\\n      name: 'a',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:roundedBox',\\n80→      params: { width: 0.7, height: 0.28, depth: 0.5, radius: 0.08 },\\n      material: 'material:sand',\\n    },\\n    {\\n      name: 'b',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:roundedBox',\\n      params: { width: 0.5, height: 0.22, depth: 0.38, radius: 0.08 },\\n      material: 'material:lawn',\\n      position: [0.05, 0.28, 0],\\n    },\\n90→    {\\n      name: 'c',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:roundedBox',\\n      params: { width: 0.32, height: 0.18, depth: 0.26, radius: 0.06 },\\n      material: 'material:sand',\\n      position: [-0.02, 0.48, 0.02],\\n    },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\n100→/** A place a guest can walk up to and begin. */\\nconst STATIONS: readonly { id: string; x: number; z: number }[] = [\\n  { id: 'morning', x: 0, z: 8 },\\n  { id: 'pose-a', x: 10, z: 2 },\\n  { id: 'pond', x: 24, z: 16 },\\n  { id: 'garden', x: -18, z: 12 },\\n  { id: 'paddle', x: 0, z: -36 },\\n  { id: 'line', x: -26, z: 6 },\\n  { id: 'group', x: -8, z: -6 },\\n  { id: 'tilt', x: 40, z: 8 },\\n110→];\\n\\n/** Plaques. Each day past the first they sit four centimetres further west. */\\nconst PLAQUES: readonly { x: number; z: number; text: string }[] = [\\n  { x: 6, z: -4, text: 'plaque.want' },\\n  { x: -6, z: 14, text: 'plaque.moved' },\\n  { x: 16, z: -8, text: 'plaque.flamingo' },\\n  { x: -12, z: -12, text: 'plaque.gulls' },\\n  { x: 8, z: 12, text: 'notice.even' },\\n  { x: -4, z: -16, text: 'notice.lawn' },\\n120→];\\n\\n/** Hidden pebbles. They join the cairn. They are not a shop. */\\nconst PEBBLES: readonly { x: number; z: number }[] = [\\n  { x: 18, z: -14 },\\n  { x: -22, z: -8 },\\n  { x: 8, z: 22 },\\n  { x: -30, z: 18 },\\n];\\n\\n130→/** An actor row the pilot can push. */\\ndefineComponent('posed', {\\n  description: '1 once the guest is wearing the lean clips.',\\n  fields: { on: { type: 'number', default: 0, description: '1 after the leans are playing.' } },\\n});\\n\\ninterface Body {\\n  id: number;\\n  actor: { x: number; y: number; z: number; intents: { move?: readonly [number, number] } };\\n  role?: { who: string };\\n140→  posed?: { on: number };\\n  clips?: { state?: { slots?: { clip: string; t: number }[] } };\\n}\\n\\n/** A placed thing. */\\ninterface Spot {\\n  id: number;\\n  mark: { x: number; y: number; z: number; kind: string; text: string; taken: number; follow: number };\\n}\\n\\n150→/** The sea's drawn position. `q` is the counter-rotation the dress writes. */\\ninterface Sea {\\n  sceneProp: { x: number; y: number; z: number; prop: string; q: [number, number, number, number] };\\n}\\n\\n/** The island lean the sea and the slope both read. */\\ninterface Lean {\\n  island: { tiltX: number; tiltZ: number; base: number };\\n}\\n\\n160→/** Distance on the lawn. */\\nfunction flat(ax: number, az: number, bx: number, bz: number): number {\\n  const dx = ax - bx;\\n  const dz = az - bz;\\n  return Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dz * dz);\\n}\\n\\n/** The island lean, if the day has spawned. */\\nfunction leanOf(w: World): Lean['island'] | undefined {\\n  const rows = w.query('island') as unknown as Lean[];\\n170→  return rows[0]?.island;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Sea quaternion for a lean in degrees. tiltX rotates about Z (west), tiltZ about X.\\n * q = qz * qx. tiltX > 0 and tiltZ = 0 leaves q[2] negative.\\n */\\nfunction seaTurn(tiltX: number, tiltZ: number): [number, number, number, number] {\\n  const ax = (-tiltZ * Math.PI) / 180;\\n  const az = (-tiltX * Math.PI) / 180;\\n180→  const sx = Math.sin(ax / 2);\\n  const cx = Math.cos(ax / 2);\\n  const sz = Math.sin(az / 2);\\n  const cz = Math.cos(az / 2);\\n  return [cz * sx, sz * sx, sz * cx, cz * cx];\\n}\\n\\n/** The pose clip and how far through it the class is. Enter and the scored hold both move `t`. */\\nfunction poseScrub(w: World): { clip: string; t: number } | undefined {\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n190→  if (!flow.event.startsWith('pose')) return undefined;\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  const poses = posesFor(act.text || flow.event);\\n  const pose = poses[act.pose] ?? poses[0];\\n  if (!pose) return undefined;\\n  const clip = `RETREAT/${pose.id.charAt(0).toUpperCase()}${pose.id.slice(1)}`;\\n  if (act.phase >= 2) return { clip, t: 1 };\\n  if (act.phase === 0) return { clip, t: Math.min(1, act.left / (4 * 60)) };\\n  const seconds = pose.hold || Number(w.settings.get('game.pose.hold')) || 12;\\n  const steps = Math.max(1, Math.round(seconds * 60));\\n200→  return { clip, t: Math.min(1, act.left / steps) };\\n}\\n\\n/** The guest, if the cast has spawned. */\\nfunction guest(w: World): Body | undefined {\\n  const rows = w.query('actor') as unknown as Body[];\\n  return rows.find((row) => row.role?.who === 'guest');\\n}\\n\\n/** Stands one still person. No clips. The mat is the performance. */\\n210→function person(w: World, who: string, x: number, z: number, yaw: number): void {\\n  spawnActor(w, {\\n    at: [x, 40, z],\\n    yaw,\\n    player: false,\\n    character: createCharacter({ speed: 0 }),\\n    components: { role: { who } },\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n220→/** Puts the island, the sea, the cast and the hidden pebbles into the world. */\\nfunction furnish(w: World): void {\\n  addTerrainBody(physicsOf(w), getTerrain('terrain:fulcrum'));\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:sea', at: [0, 2, 0], yaw: 0 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:cairn', at: [-3, 0, 3], yaw: 0 });\\n  for (const spot of [\\n    [0, 2],\\n    [3, 2],\\n    [-3, 2],\\n    [0, 5],\\n230→  ] as const) {\\n    spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:mat', at: [spot[0], 0, spot[1]], yaw: 0 });\\n  }\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:pillar', at: [-6, 0, -4], yaw: 0 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:pillar', at: [6, 0, -4], yaw: 0 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:bench', at: [4, 0, -8], yaw: 0.2 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:bench', at: [-4, 0, 14], yaw: -0.2 });\\n  for (const station of STATIONS) {\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: station.x, y: 1.2, z: station.z, kind: 'station', text: station.id, taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n  }\\n240→  for (const plaque of PLAQUES) {\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: plaque.x, y: 1.1, z: plaque.z, kind: 'plaque', text: plaque.text, taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n  }\\n  for (let i = 0; i < PEBBLES.length; i += 1) {\\n    const pebble = PEBBLES[i];\\n    if (!pebble) continue;\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: pebble.x, y: 0.3, z: pebble.z, kind: 'pebble', text: `pebble:${i}`, taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n  }\\n  spawnActor(w, {\\n    at: [0, 40, 6],\\n250→    player: false,\\n    yaw: Math.PI,\\n    character: createCharacter({ speed: 5.5 }),\\n    anim: { build: 'build:retreat' },\\n    clips: {\\n      sets: ['clipset:retreat'],\\n      play: { clip: 'RETREAT/Nothing', speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, loop: false },\\n    },\\n    components: { role: { who: 'guest' }, posed: { on: 0 } },\\n  });\\n260→  person(w, 'plumb', 2.2, 4, Math.PI);\\n  person(w, 'tare', -2.2, 5, 0);\\n  person(w, 'gerald', 8, -2, 1);\\n  person(w, 'bex', -8, 0, 0.4);\\n  person(w, 'nan', 5, 10, 2);\\n  w.systems.add('retreat.dress', dress, { phase: 'rules' });\\n}\\n\\n/** Sea bob, plaque creep, pebble pickup, and the pose scrub. Runs after the clips have stepped. */\\nfunction dress(w: World): void {\\n270→  const lean = leanOf(w);\\n  const q = seaTurn(lean?.tiltX ?? 0, lean?.tiltZ ?? 0);\\n  for (const row of w.query('sceneProp') as unknown as Sea[]) {\\n    if (row.sceneProp.prop !== 'prop:sea') continue;\\n    row.sceneProp.y = 2 + 0.06 * Math.sin(w.time * 0.35);\\n    row.sceneProp.q = q;\\n  }\\n  const day = Math.max(1, flowOf(w).day);\\n  const west = (day - 1) * 0.04;\\n  for (const spot of w.query('mark') as unknown as Spot[]) {\\n280→    if (spot.mark.kind !== 'plaque') continue;\\n    const home = PLAQUES.find((plaque) => plaque.text === spot.mark.text);\\n    if (home) spot.mark.x = home.x - west;\\n  }\\n  const who = guest(w);\\n  if (!who) return;\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  if (flow.mode === 'roam') {\\n    for (const spot of w.query('mark') as unknown as Spot[]) {\\n      if (spot.mark.kind !== 'pebble' || spot.mark.taken) continue;\\n290→      if (flat(who.actor.x, who.actor.z, spot.mark.x, spot.mark.z) < 1.5) {\\n        spot.mark.taken = 1;\\n        flow.pebbles += 1;\\n        flow.line = 'find.pebble';\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n  scrub(w, who);\\n}\\n\\n300→/** Writes the lean and the current pose onto the clip slots. The scored hold lives in `left`, not `hold`. */\\nfunction scrub(w: World, who: Body): void {\\n  if (!who.posed?.on) {\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanR', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanL', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanF', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanB', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    if (who.posed) who.posed.on = 1;\\n  }\\n  const pose = poseScrub(w);\\n310→  let slots = who.clips?.state?.slots;\\n  if (pose && !slots?.some((slot) => slot.clip === pose.clip)) {\\n    playClip(w, who.id, pose.clip, { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, loop: false });\\n    slots = who.clips?.state?.slots;\\n  }\\n  if (!slots) return;\\n  const rows = w.query('wobble') as unknown as { wobble: { x: number; y: number; seat: number } }[];\\n  const body = rows.find((row) => row.wobble.seat === 0)?.wobble;\\n  const x = body?.x ?? 0;\\n  const y = body?.y ?? 0;\\n320→  for (const slot of slots) {\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanR') slot.t = Math.max(0, x);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanL') slot.t = Math.max(0, -x);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanF') slot.t = Math.max(0, y);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanB') slot.t = Math.max(0, -y);\\n    if (pose && slot.clip === pose.clip) slot.t = pose.t;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Walks the guest while the day is open, and names the station underfoot. */\\n330→function roam(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const who = guest(w);\\n  if (!who) return;\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  const onTerrace = flow.event === 'tilt' && act.phase === 1;\\n  if (flow.mode !== 'roam' && flow.mode !== 'title' && !onTerrace) {\\n    who.actor.intents = { move: [0, 0] };\\n    return;\\n  }\\n340→  const move = intents.move;\\n  let mx = move?.[0] ?? 0;\\n  let my = move?.[1] ?? 0;\\n  if (flow.mode === 'roam' || onTerrace) {\\n    const tiltX = leanOf(w)?.tiltX ?? 0;\\n    mx -= Math.sin((tiltX * Math.PI) / 180);\\n  }\\n  const reach = Math.hypot(who.actor.x, who.actor.z);\\n  if (reach > 78) {\\n    mx = -who.actor.x / reach;\\n350→    my = -who.actor.z / reach;\\n  }\\n  who.actor.intents = { move: [mx, my] };\\n  if (flow.mode !== 'roam') return;\\n  let near = '';\\n  let best = 3.2;\\n  for (const spot of w.query('mark') as unknown as Spot[]) {\\n    if (spot.mark.kind !== 'station') continue;\\n    const d = flat(who.actor.x, who.actor.z, spot.mark.x, spot.mark.z);\\n    if (d < best) {\\n360→      best = d;\\n      near = spot.mark.text;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  act.text = near;\\n}\\n\\n/** The island scene. The page boots this. Tests that score the week boot the bench instead. */\\nexport const island = defineScene('game:island', {\\n  description: 'Little Fulcrum. Walk the lawn. Begin the day from a mat, a plaque, or the programme.',\\n370→  terrain: 'terrain:fulcrum',\\n  physics: true,\\n  setup(w) {\\n    boot(w);\\n    furnish(w);\\n  },\\n  step(w, intents) {\\n    frame(w, intents);\\n    roam(w, intents);\\n  },\\n380→  actions: retreatActions,\\n});\\n\\nexport default island;\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Little Fulcrum. A lawn on a sand dome, a pond, a cove, and a guest who can walk.\\n * Activities still run on the balance step. The ground mesh stays put. The sea tips against the lean,\\n * plaques creep west, and the guest walks downhill.\\n */\\nimport {\\n  addTerrainBody,\\n  createCharacter,\\n  defineComponent,\\n10→  defineProp,\\n  defineScene,\\n  defineTerrain,\\n  getTerrain,\\n  physicsOf,\\n  playClip,\\n  spawnActor,\\n  spawnProp,\\n  type Intents,\\n  type World,\\n20→} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport '../cast/clips';\\nimport { boot, frame, retreatActions } from './driver';\\nimport { actOf, flowOf } from './events/kit';\\nimport { posesFor } from './events/pose';\\n\\ndefineTerrain('terrain:fulcrum', {\\n  size: [60, 60],\\n  cell: 4,\\n  origin: [-120, 0, -120],\\n30→  seed: 4,\\n  height: 0,\\n  ridges: 0,\\n  high: 7,\\n  materials: ['material:sand', 'material:sand', 'material:lawn'],\\n  hills: [\\n    { at: [0, 0], radius: 110, height: 11 },\\n    { at: [10, -6], radius: 22, height: 4 },\\n    { at: [24, 18], radius: 16, height: -3.2 },\\n    { at: [0, -78], radius: 30, height: -6 },\\n40→  ],\\n  flats: [\\n    { rect: [-14, -14, 14, 14], height: 9.2, margin: 8 },\\n    { rect: [-34, -2, -16, 16], height: 8.4, margin: 6 },\\n    { rect: [16, 8, 34, 28], height: 7.6, margin: 6 },\\n    { rect: [-8, -48, 10, -28], height: 6.2, margin: 6 },\\n    { rect: [32, 0, 52, 16], height: 8.8, margin: 5 },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\n50→defineProp('prop:sea', {\\n  description: 'The sea. It is flat, and it pretends to breathe.',\\n  parts: [\\n    {\\n      name: 'water',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:box',\\n      params: { width: 280, height: 0.35, depth: 280 },\\n      material: 'material:sea',\\n    },\\n  ],\\n60→});\\n\\ndefineProp('prop:mat', {\\n  description: 'A round mat.',\\n  parts: [\\n    {\\n      name: 'disc',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:frustum',\\n      params: { radiusTop: 1.15, radiusBottom: 1.2, height: 0.08, radialSegments: 16, smooth: true },\\n      material: 'material:sand',\\n70→    },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\ndefineProp('prop:cairn', {\\n  description: 'Pebbles that are not spent.',\\n  parts: [\\n    {\\n      name: 'a',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:roundedBox',\\n80→      params: { width: 0.7, height: 0.28, depth: 0.5, radius: 0.08 },\\n      material: 'material:sand',\\n    },\\n    {\\n      name: 'b',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:roundedBox',\\n      params: { width: 0.5, height: 0.22, depth: 0.38, radius: 0.08 },\\n      material: 'material:lawn',\\n      position: [0.05, 0.28, 0],\\n    },\\n90→    {\\n      name: 'c',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:roundedBox',\\n      params: { width: 0.32, height: 0.18, depth: 0.26, radius: 0.06 },\\n      material: 'material:sand',\\n      position: [-0.02, 0.48, 0.02],\\n    },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\n100→/** A place a guest can walk up to and begin. */\\nconst STATIONS: readonly { id: string; x: number; z: number }[] = [\\n  { id: 'morning', x: 0, z: 8 },\\n  { id: 'pose-a', x: 10, z: 2 },\\n  { id: 'pond', x: 24, z: 16 },\\n  { id: 'garden', x: -18, z: 12 },\\n  { id: 'paddle', x: 0, z: -36 },\\n  { id: 'line', x: -26, z: 6 },\\n  { id: 'group', x: -8, z: -6 },\\n  { id: 'tilt', x: 40, z: 8 },\\n110→];\\n\\n/** Plaques. Each day past the first they sit four centimetres further west. */\\nconst PLAQUES: readonly { x: number; z: number; text: string }[] = [\\n  { x: 6, z: -4, text: 'plaque.want' },\\n  { x: -6, z: 14, text: 'plaque.moved' },\\n  { x: 16, z: -8, text: 'plaque.flamingo' },\\n  { x: -12, z: -12, text: 'plaque.gulls' },\\n  { x: 8, z: 12, text: 'notice.even' },\\n  { x: -4, z: -16, text: 'notice.lawn' },\\n120→];\\n\\n/** Hidden pebbles. They join the cairn. They are not a shop. */\\nconst PEBBLES: readonly { x: number; z: number }[] = [\\n  { x: 18, z: -14 },\\n  { x: -22, z: -8 },\\n  { x: 8, z: 22 },\\n  { x: -30, z: 18 },\\n];\\n\\n130→/** An actor row the pilot can push. */\\ndefineComponent('posed', {\\n  description: '1 once the guest is wearing the lean clips.',\\n  fields: { on: { type: 'number', default: 0, description: '1 after the leans are playing.' } },\\n});\\n\\ninterface Body {\\n  id: number;\\n  actor: { x: number; y: number; z: number; intents: { move?: readonly [number, number] } };\\n  role?: { who: string };\\n140→  posed?: { on: number };\\n  clips?: { state?: { slots?: { clip: string; t: number }[] } };\\n}\\n\\n/** A placed thing. */\\ninterface Spot {\\n  id: number;\\n  mark: { x: number; y: number; z: number; kind: string; text: string; taken: number; follow: number };\\n}\\n\\n150→/** The sea's drawn position. `q` is the counter-rotation the dress writes. */\\ninterface Sea {\\n  sceneProp: { x: number; y: number; z: number; prop: string; q: [number, number, number, number] };\\n}\\n\\n/** The island lean the sea and the slope both read. */\\ninterface Lean {\\n  island: { tiltX: number; tiltZ: number; base: number };\\n}\\n\\n160→/** Distance on the lawn. */\\nfunction flat(ax: number, az: number, bx: number, bz: number): number {\\n  const dx = ax - bx;\\n  const dz = az - bz;\\n  return Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dz * dz);\\n}\\n\\n/** The island lean, if the day has spawned. */\\nfunction leanOf(w: World): Lean['island'] | undefined {\\n  const rows = w.query('island') as unknown as Lean[];\\n170→  return rows[0]?.island;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Sea quaternion for a lean in degrees. tiltX rotates about Z (west), tiltZ about X.\\n * q = qz * qx. tiltX > 0 and tiltZ = 0 leaves q[2] negative.\\n */\\nfunction seaTurn(tiltX: number, tiltZ: number): [number, number, number, number] {\\n  const ax = (-tiltZ * Math.PI) / 180;\\n  const az = (-tiltX * Math.PI) / 180;\\n180→  const sx = Math.sin(ax / 2);\\n  const cx = Math.cos(ax / 2);\\n  const sz = Math.sin(az / 2);\\n  const cz = Math.cos(az / 2);\\n  return [cz * sx, sz * sx, sz * cx, cz * cx];\\n}\\n\\n/** The pose clip and how far through it the class is. Enter and the scored hold both move `t`. */\\nfunction poseScrub(w: World): { clip: string; t: number } | undefined {\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n190→  if (!flow.event.startsWith('pose')) return undefined;\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  const poses = posesFor(act.text || flow.event);\\n  const pose = poses[act.pose] ?? poses[0];\\n  if (!pose) return undefined;\\n  const clip = `RETREAT/${pose.id.charAt(0).toUpperCase()}${pose.id.slice(1)}`;\\n  if (act.phase >= 2) return { clip, t: 1 };\\n  if (act.phase === 0) return { clip, t: Math.min(1, act.left / (4 * 60)) };\\n  const seconds = pose.hold || Number(w.settings.get('game.pose.hold')) || 12;\\n  const steps = Math.max(1, Math.round(seconds * 60));\\n200→  return { clip, t: Math.min(1, act.left / steps) };\\n}\\n\\n/** The guest, if the cast has spawned. */\\nfunction guest(w: World): Body | undefined {\\n  const rows = w.query('actor') as unknown as Body[];\\n  return rows.find((row) => row.role?.who === 'guest');\\n}\\n\\n/** Stands one still person. No clips. The mat is the performance. */\\n210→function person(w: World, who: string, x: number, z: number, yaw: number): void {\\n  spawnActor(w, {\\n    at: [x, 40, z],\\n    yaw,\\n    player: false,\\n    character: createCharacter({ speed: 0 }),\\n    components: { role: { who } },\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n220→/** Puts the island, the sea, the cast and the hidden pebbles into the world. */\\nfunction furnish(w: World): void {\\n  addTerrainBody(physicsOf(w), getTerrain('terrain:fulcrum'));\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:sea', at: [0, 2, 0], yaw: 0 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:cairn', at: [-3, 0, 3], yaw: 0 });\\n  for (const spot of [\\n    [0, 2],\\n    [3, 2],\\n    [-3, 2],\\n    [0, 5],\\n230→  ] as const) {\\n    spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:mat', at: [spot[0], 0, spot[1]], yaw: 0 });\\n  }\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:pillar', at: [-6, 0, -4], yaw: 0 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:pillar', at: [6, 0, -4], yaw: 0 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:bench', at: [4, 0, -8], yaw: 0.2 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:bench', at: [-4, 0, 14], yaw: -0.2 });\\n  for (const station of STATIONS) {\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: station.x, y: 1.2, z: station.z, kind: 'station', text: station.id, taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n  }\\n240→  for (const plaque of PLAQUES) {\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: plaque.x, y: 1.1, z: plaque.z, kind: 'plaque', text: plaque.text, taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n  }\\n  for (let i = 0; i < PEBBLES.length; i += 1) {\\n    const pebble = PEBBLES[i];\\n    if (!pebble) continue;\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: pebble.x, y: 0.3, z: pebble.z, kind: 'pebble', text: `pebble:${i}`, taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n  }\\n  spawnActor(w, {\\n    at: [0, 40, 6],\\n250→    player: false,\\n    yaw: Math.PI,\\n    character: createCharacter({ speed: 5.5 }),\\n    anim: { build: 'build:retreat' },\\n    clips: {\\n      sets: ['clipset:retreat'],\\n      play: { clip: 'RETREAT/Nothing', speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, loop: false },\\n    },\\n    components: { role: { who: 'guest' }, posed: { on: 0 } },\\n  });\\n260→  person(w, 'plumb', 2.2, 4, Math.PI);\\n  person(w, 'tare', -2.2, 5, 0);\\n  person(w, 'gerald', 8, -2, 1);\\n  person(w, 'bex', -8, 0, 0.4);\\n  person(w, 'nan', 5, 10, 2);\\n  w.systems.add('retreat.dress', dress, { phase: 'rules' });\\n}\\n\\n/** Sea bob, plaque creep, pebble pickup, and the pose scrub. Runs after the clips have stepped. */\\nfunction dress(w: World): void {\\n270→  const lean = leanOf(w);\\n  const q = seaTurn(lean?.tiltX ?? 0, lean?.tiltZ ?? 0);\\n  for (const row of w.query('sceneProp') as unknown as Sea[]) {\\n    if (row.sceneProp.prop !== 'prop:sea') continue;\\n    row.sceneProp.y = 2 + 0.06 * Math.sin(w.time * 0.35);\\n    row.sceneProp.q = q;\\n  }\\n  const day = Math.max(1, flowOf(w).day);\\n  const west = (day - 1) * 0.04;\\n  for (const spot of w.query('mark') as unknown as Spot[]) {\\n280→    if (spot.mark.kind !== 'plaque') continue;\\n    const home = PLAQUES.find((plaque) => plaque.text === spot.mark.text);\\n    if (home) spot.mark.x = home.x - west;\\n  }\\n  const who = guest(w);\\n  if (!who) return;\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  if (flow.mode === 'roam') {\\n    for (const spot of w.query('mark') as unknown as Spot[]) {\\n      if (spot.mark.kind !== 'pebble' || spot.mark.taken) continue;\\n290→      if (flat(who.actor.x, who.actor.z, spot.mark.x, spot.mark.z) < 1.5) {\\n        spot.mark.taken = 1;\\n        flow.pebbles += 1;\\n        flow.line = 'find.pebble';\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n  scrub(w, who);\\n}\\n\\n300→/** Writes the lean and the current pose onto the clip slots. The scored hold lives in `left`, not `hold`. */\\nfunction scrub(w: World, who: Body): void {\\n  if (!who.posed?.on) {\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanR', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanL', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanF', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanB', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    if (who.posed) who.posed.on = 1;\\n  }\\n  const pose = poseScrub(w);\\n310→  let slots = who.clips?.state?.slots;\\n  if (pose && !slots?.some((slot) => slot.clip === pose.clip)) {\\n    playClip(w, who.id, pose.clip, { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, loop: false });\\n    slots = who.clips?.state?.slots;\\n  }\\n  if (!slots) return;\\n  const rows = w.query('wobble') as unknown as { wobble: { x: number; y: number; seat: number } }[];\\n  const body = rows.find((row) => row.wobble.seat === 0)?.wobble;\\n  const x = body?.x ?? 0;\\n  const y = body?.y ?? 0;\\n320→  for (const slot of slots) {\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanR') slot.t = Math.max(0, x);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanL') slot.t = Math.max(0, -x);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanF') slot.t = Math.max(0, y);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanB') slot.t = Math.max(0, -y);\\n    if (pose && slot.clip === pose.clip) slot.t = pose.t;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Walks the guest while the day is open, and names the station underfoot. */\\n330→function roam(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const who = guest(w);\\n  if (!who) return;\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  const onTerrace = flow.event === 'tilt' && act.phase === 1;\\n  if (flow.mode !== 'roam' && flow.mode !== 'title' && !onTerrace) {\\n    who.actor.intents = { move: [0, 0] };\\n    return;\\n  }\\n340→  const move = intents.move;\\n  let mx = move?.[0] ?? 0;\\n  let my = move?.[1] ?? 0;\\n  if (flow.mode === 'roam' || onTerrace) {\\n    const tiltX = leanOf(w)?.tiltX ?? 0;\\n    mx -= Math.sin((tiltX * Math.PI) / 180);\\n  }\\n  const reach = Math.hypot(who.actor.x, who.actor.z);\\n  if (reach > 78) {\\n    mx = -who.actor.x / reach;\\n350→    my = -who.actor.z / reach;\\n  }\\n  who.actor.intents = { move: [mx, my] };\\n  if (flow.mode !== 'roam') return;\\n  let near = '';\\n  let best = 3.2;\\n  for (const spot of w.query('mark') as unknown as Spot[]) {\\n    if (spot.mark.kind !== 'station') continue;\\n    const d = flat(who.actor.x, who.actor.z, spot.mark.x, spot.mark.z);\\n    if (d < best) {\\n360→      best = d;\\n      near = spot.mark.text;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  act.text = near;\\n}\\n\\n/** The island scene. The page boots this. Tests that score the week boot the bench instead. */\\nexport const island = defineScene('game:island', {\\n  description: 'Little Fulcrum. Walk the lawn. Begin the day from a mat, a plaque, or the programme.',\\n370→  terrain: 'terrain:fulcrum',\\n  physics: true,\\n  setup(w) {\\n    boot(w);\\n    furnish(w);\\n  },\\n  step(w, intents) {\\n    frame(w, intents);\\n    roam(w, intents);\\n  },\\n380→  actions: retreatActions,\\n});\\n\\nexport default island;\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/island.ts\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":400,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file Little Fulcrum. A lawn on a sand dome, a pond, a cove, and a guest who can walk.\\n * Activities still run on the balance step. The ground mesh stays put. The sea tips against the lean,\\n * plaques creep west, and the guest walks downhill.\\n */\\nimport {\\n  addTerrainBody,\\n  createCharacter,\\n  defineComponent,\\n  defineProp,\\n  defineScene,\\n  defineTerrain,\\n  getTerrain,\\n  physicsOf,\\n  playClip,\\n  spawnActor,\\n  spawnProp,\\n  type Intents,\\n  type World,\\n} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport '../cast/clips';\\nimport { boot, frame, retreatActions } from './driver';\\nimport { actOf, flowOf } from './events/kit';\\nimport { posesFor } from './events/pose';\\n\\ndefineTerrain('terrain:fulcrum', {\\n  size: [60, 60],\\n  cell: 4,\\n  origin: [-120, 0, -120],\\n  seed: 4,\\n  height: 0,\\n  ridges: 0,\\n  high: 7,\\n  materials: ['material:sand', 'material:sand', 'material:lawn'],\\n  hills: [\\n    { at: [0, 0], radius: 110, height: 11 },\\n    { at: [10, -6], radius: 22, height: 4 },\\n    { at: [24, 18], radius: 16, height: -3.2 },\\n    { at: [0, -78], radius: 30, height: -6 },\\n  ],\\n  flats: [\\n    { rect: [-14, -14, 14, 14], height: 9.2, margin: 8 },\\n    { rect: [-34, -2, -16, 16], height: 8.4, margin: 6 },\\n    { rect: [16, 8, 34, 28], height: 7.6, margin: 6 },\\n    { rect: [-8, -48, 10, -28], height: 6.2, margin: 6 },\\n    { rect: [32, 0, 52, 16], height: 8.8, margin: 5 },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\ndefineProp('prop:sea', {\\n  description: 'The sea. It is flat, and it pretends to breathe.',\\n  parts: [\\n    {\\n      name: 'water',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:box',\\n      params: { width: 280, height: 0.35, depth: 280 },\\n      material: 'material:sea',\\n    },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\ndefineProp('prop:mat', {\\n  description: 'A round mat.',\\n  parts: [\\n    {\\n      name: 'disc',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:frustum',\\n      params: { radiusTop: 1.15, radiusBottom: 1.2, height: 0.08, radialSegments: 16, smooth: true },\\n      material: 'material:sand',\\n    },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\ndefineProp('prop:cairn', {\\n  description: 'Pebbles that are not spent.',\\n  parts: [\\n    {\\n      name: 'a',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:roundedBox',\\n      params: { width: 0.7, height: 0.28, depth: 0.5, radius: 0.08 },\\n      material: 'material:sand',\\n    },\\n    {\\n      name: 'b',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:roundedBox',\\n      params: { width: 0.5, height: 0.22, depth: 0.38, radius: 0.08 },\\n      material: 'material:lawn',\\n      position: [0.05, 0.28, 0],\\n    },\\n    {\\n      name: 'c',\\n      geometry: 'geometry:roundedBox',\\n      params: { width: 0.32, height: 0.18, depth: 0.26, radius: 0.06 },\\n      material: 'material:sand',\\n      position: [-0.02, 0.48, 0.02],\\n    },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\n/** A place a guest can walk up to and begin. */\\nconst STATIONS: readonly { id: string; x: number; z: number }[] = [\\n  { id: 'morning', x: 0, z: 8 },\\n  { id: 'pose-a', x: 10, z: 2 },\\n  { id: 'pond', x: 24, z: 16 },\\n  { id: 'garden', x: -18, z: 12 },\\n  { id: 'paddle', x: 0, z: -36 },\\n  { id: 'line', x: -26, z: 6 },\\n  { id: 'group', x: -8, z: -6 },\\n  { id: 'tilt', x: 40, z: 8 },\\n];\\n\\n/** Plaques. Each day past the first they sit four centimetres further west. */\\nconst PLAQUES: readonly { x: number; z: number; text: string }[] = [\\n  { x: 6, z: -4, text: 'plaque.want' },\\n  { x: -6, z: 14, text: 'plaque.moved' },\\n  { x: 16, z: -8, text: 'plaque.flamingo' },\\n  { x: -12, z: -12, text: 'plaque.gulls' },\\n  { x: 8, z: 12, text: 'notice.even' },\\n  { x: -4, z: -16, text: 'notice.lawn' },\\n];\\n\\n/** Hidden pebbles. They join the cairn. They are not a shop. */\\nconst PEBBLES: readonly { x: number; z: number }[] = [\\n  { x: 18, z: -14 },\\n  { x: -22, z: -8 },\\n  { x: 8, z: 22 },\\n  { x: -30, z: 18 },\\n];\\n\\n/** An actor row the pilot can push. */\\ndefineComponent('posed', {\\n  description: '1 once the guest is wearing the lean clips.',\\n  fields: { on: { type: 'number', default: 0, description: '1 after the leans are playing.' } },\\n});\\n\\ninterface Body {\\n  id: number;\\n  actor: { x: number; y: number; z: number; intents: { move?: readonly [number, number] } };\\n  role?: { who: string };\\n  posed?: { on: number };\\n  clips?: { state?: { slots?: { clip: string; t: number }[] } };\\n}\\n\\n/** A placed thing. */\\ninterface Spot {\\n  id: number;\\n  mark: { x: number; y: number; z: number; kind: string; text: string; taken: number; follow: number };\\n}\\n\\n/** The sea's drawn position. `q` is the counter-rotation the dress writes. */\\ninterface Sea {\\n  sceneProp: { x: number; y: number; z: number; prop: string; q: [number, number, number, number] };\\n}\\n\\n/** The island lean the sea and the slope both read. */\\ninterface Lean {\\n  island: { tiltX: number; tiltZ: number; base: number };\\n}\\n\\n/** Distance on the lawn. */\\nfunction flat(ax: number, az: number, bx: number, bz: number): number {\\n  const dx = ax - bx;\\n  const dz = az - bz;\\n  return Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dz * dz);\\n}\\n\\n/** The island lean, if the day has spawned. */\\nfunction leanOf(w: World): Lean['island'] | undefined {\\n  const rows = w.query('island') as unknown as Lean[];\\n  return rows[0]?.island;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Sea quaternion for a lean in degrees. tiltX rotates about Z (west), tiltZ about X.\\n * q = qz * qx. tiltX > 0 and tiltZ = 0 leaves q[2] negative.\\n */\\nfunction seaTurn(tiltX: number, tiltZ: number): [number, number, number, number] {\\n  const ax = (-tiltZ * Math.PI) / 180;\\n  const az = (-tiltX * Math.PI) / 180;\\n  const sx = Math.sin(ax / 2);\\n  const cx = Math.cos(ax / 2);\\n  const sz = Math.sin(az / 2);\\n  const cz = Math.cos(az / 2);\\n  return [cz * sx, sz * sx, sz * cx, cz * cx];\\n}\\n\\n/** The pose clip and how far through it the class is. Enter and the scored hold both move `t`. */\\nfunction poseScrub(w: World): { clip: string; t: number } | undefined {\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  if (!flow.event.startsWith('pose')) return undefined;\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  const poses = posesFor(act.text || flow.event);\\n  const pose = poses[act.pose] ?? poses[0];\\n  if (!pose) return undefined;\\n  const clip = `RETREAT/${pose.id.charAt(0).toUpperCase()}${pose.id.slice(1)}`;\\n  if (act.phase >= 2) return { clip, t: 1 };\\n  if (act.phase === 0) return { clip, t: Math.min(1, act.left / (4 * 60)) };\\n  const seconds = pose.hold || Number(w.settings.get('game.pose.hold')) || 12;\\n  const steps = Math.max(1, Math.round(seconds * 60));\\n  return { clip, t: Math.min(1, act.left / steps) };\\n}\\n\\n/** The guest, if the cast has spawned. */\\nfunction guest(w: World): Body | undefined {\\n  const rows = w.query('actor') as unknown as Body[];\\n  return rows.find((row) => row.role?.who === 'guest');\\n}\\n\\n/** Stands one still person. No clips. The mat is the performance. */\\nfunction person(w: World, who: string, x: number, z: number, yaw: number): void {\\n  spawnActor(w, {\\n    at: [x, 40, z],\\n    yaw,\\n    player: false,\\n    character: createCharacter({ speed: 0 }),\\n    components: { role: { who } },\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/** Puts the island, the sea, the cast and the hidden pebbles into the world. */\\nfunction furnish(w: World): void {\\n  addTerrainBody(physicsOf(w), getTerrain('terrain:fulcrum'));\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:sea', at: [0, 2, 0], yaw: 0 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:cairn', at: [-3, 0, 3], yaw: 0 });\\n  for (const spot of [\\n    [0, 2],\\n    [3, 2],\\n    [-3, 2],\\n    [0, 5],\\n  ] as const) {\\n    spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:mat', at: [spot[0], 0, spot[1]], yaw: 0 });\\n  }\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:pillar', at: [-6, 0, -4], yaw: 0 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:pillar', at: [6, 0, -4], yaw: 0 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:bench', at: [4, 0, -8], yaw: 0.2 });\\n  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:bench', at: [-4, 0, 14], yaw: -0.2 });\\n  for (const station of STATIONS) {\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: station.x, y: 1.2, z: station.z, kind: 'station', text: station.id, taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n  }\\n  for (const plaque of PLAQUES) {\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: plaque.x, y: 1.1, z: plaque.z, kind: 'plaque', text: plaque.text, taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n  }\\n  for (let i = 0; i < PEBBLES.length; i += 1) {\\n    const pebble = PEBBLES[i];\\n    if (!pebble) continue;\\n    w.spawn({ mark: { x: pebble.x, y: 0.3, z: pebble.z, kind: 'pebble', text: `pebble:${i}`, taken: 0, follow: 0 } });\\n  }\\n  spawnActor(w, {\\n    at: [0, 40, 6],\\n    player: false,\\n    yaw: Math.PI,\\n    character: createCharacter({ speed: 5.5 }),\\n    anim: { build: 'build:retreat' },\\n    clips: {\\n      sets: ['clipset:retreat'],\\n      play: { clip: 'RETREAT/Nothing', speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, loop: false },\\n    },\\n    components: { role: { who: 'guest' }, posed: { on: 0 } },\\n  });\\n  person(w, 'plumb', 2.2, 4, Math.PI);\\n  person(w, 'tare', -2.2, 5, 0);\\n  person(w, 'gerald', 8, -2, 1);\\n  person(w, 'bex', -8, 0, 0.4);\\n  person(w, 'nan', 5, 10, 2);\\n  w.systems.add('retreat.dress', dress, { phase: 'rules' });\\n}\\n\\n/** Sea bob, plaque creep, pebble pickup, and the pose scrub. Runs after the clips have stepped. */\\nfunction dress(w: World): void {\\n  const lean = leanOf(w);\\n  const q = seaTurn(lean?.tiltX ?? 0, lean?.tiltZ ?? 0);\\n  for (const row of w.query('sceneProp') as unknown as Sea[]) {\\n    if (row.sceneProp.prop !== 'prop:sea') continue;\\n    row.sceneProp.y = 2 + 0.06 * Math.sin(w.time * 0.35);\\n    row.sceneProp.q = q;\\n  }\\n  const day = Math.max(1, flowOf(w).day);\\n  const west = (day - 1) * 0.04;\\n  for (const spot of w.query('mark') as unknown as Spot[]) {\\n    if (spot.mark.kind !== 'plaque') continue;\\n    const home = PLAQUES.find((plaque) => plaque.text === spot.mark.text);\\n    if (home) spot.mark.x = home.x - west;\\n  }\\n  const who = guest(w);\\n  if (!who) return;\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  if (flow.mode === 'roam') {\\n    for (const spot of w.query('mark') as unknown as Spot[]) {\\n      if (spot.mark.kind !== 'pebble' || spot.mark.taken) continue;\\n      if (flat(who.actor.x, who.actor.z, spot.mark.x, spot.mark.z) < 1.5) {\\n        spot.mark.taken = 1;\\n        flow.pebbles += 1;\\n        flow.line = 'find.pebble';\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n  scrub(w, who);\\n}\\n\\n/** Writes the lean and the current pose onto the clip slots. The scored hold lives in `left`, not `hold`. */\\nfunction scrub(w: World, who: Body): void {\\n  if (!who.posed?.on) {\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanR', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanL', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanF', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    playClip(w, who.id, 'RETREAT/LeanB', { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, additive: true, loop: false });\\n    if (who.posed) who.posed.on = 1;\\n  }\\n  const pose = poseScrub(w);\\n  let slots = who.clips?.state?.slots;\\n  if (pose && !slots?.some((slot) => slot.clip === pose.clip)) {\\n    playClip(w, who.id, pose.clip, { speed: 0, hold: true, walk: true, loop: false });\\n    slots = who.clips?.state?.slots;\\n  }\\n  if (!slots) return;\\n  const rows = w.query('wobble') as unknown as { wobble: { x: number; y: number; seat: number } }[];\\n  const body = rows.find((row) => row.wobble.seat === 0)?.wobble;\\n  const x = body?.x ?? 0;\\n  const y = body?.y ?? 0;\\n  for (const slot of slots) {\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanR') slot.t = Math.max(0, x);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanL') slot.t = Math.max(0, -x);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanF') slot.t = Math.max(0, y);\\n    if (slot.clip === 'RETREAT/LeanB') slot.t = Math.max(0, -y);\\n    if (pose && slot.clip === pose.clip) slot.t = pose.t;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Walks the guest while the day is open, and names the station underfoot. */\\nfunction roam(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const who = guest(w);\\n  if (!who) return;\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  const onTerrace = flow.event === 'tilt' && act.phase === 1;\\n  if (flow.mode !== 'roam' && flow.mode !== 'title' && !onTerrace) {\\n    who.actor.intents = { move: [0, 0] };\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  const move = intents.move;\\n  let mx = move?.[0] ?? 0;\\n  let my = move?.[1] ?? 0;\\n  if (flow.mode === 'roam' || onTerrace) {\\n    const tiltX = leanOf(w)?.tiltX ?? 0;\\n    mx -= Math.sin((tiltX * Math.PI) / 180);\\n  }\\n  const reach = Math.hypot(who.actor.x, who.actor.z);\\n  if (reach > 78) {\\n    mx = -who.actor.x / reach;\\n    my = -who.actor.z / reach;\\n  }\\n  who.actor.intents = { move: [mx, my] };\\n  if (flow.mode !== 'roam') return;\\n  let near = '';\\n  let best = 3.2;\\n  for (const spot of w.query('mark') as unknown as Spot[]) {\\n    if (spot.mark.kind !== 'station') continue;\\n    const d = flat(who.actor.x, who.actor.z, spot.mark.x, spot.mark.z);\\n    if (d < best) {\\n      best = d;\\n      near = spot.mark.text;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  act.text = near;\\n}\\n\\n/** The island scene. The page boots this. Tests that score the week boot the bench instead. */\\nexport const island = defineScene('game:island', {\\n  description: 'Little Fulcrum. Walk the lawn. Begin the day from a mat, a plaque, or the programme.',\\n  terrain: 'terrain:fulcrum',\\n  physics: true,\\n  setup(w) {\\n    boot(w);\\n    furnish(w);\\n  },\\n  step(w, intents) {\\n    frame(w, intents);\\n    roam(w, intents);\\n  },\\n  actions: retreatActions,\\n});\\n\\nexport default island;\\n\",\"total_lines\":383}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-89fec25b-cfdf-4b96-b043-afdfd1c52404-5","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The Great Tilt. A storm, a walk to the east terrace, the centre stone, then dawn.\\n * The island's geometry stays put. Your centre of balance is what leans it, once you are on the stone.\\n * There is no fail state. The clock moves every part on.\\n */\\nimport type { Intents, World } from '../../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { type Band, seek, stickIntents, wantBreath } from '../bot';\\nimport { clampScore } from '../score';\\nimport { resetAct, visit } from '../state';\\n10→import { resetBalance } from '../wobble';\\nimport { actOf, apply, cfgOf, flowOf, rowOf, sweep } from './kit';\\n\\nconst NAMES = ['Nan', 'Gerald', 'Bex', 'A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'E', 'F', 'G', 'H', 'I'];\\n\\n/** Guests, the storm, and a still balance. Attract begins on the stone. */\\nexport function setup(w: World): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  resetAct(act);\\n  const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n20→  resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n  const attract = String(w.settings.get('game.auto')) === 'attract';\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 12; i++) {\\n    const nan = i === 0;\\n    const col = (i - 1) % 4;\\n    const row = Math.floor((i - 1) / 4);\\n    w.spawn({\\n      made: { tag: 'guest' },\\n      mark: {\\n        x: nan ? 64 : 1 + col * 2.2,\\n30→        y: 0,\\n        z: nan ? 8 : (row - 1) * 2.2,\\n        kind: 'guest',\\n        text: NAMES[i] ?? 'guest',\\n        taken: nan ? 1 : 0,\\n        follow: nan ? 1 : 0,\\n      },\\n    });\\n  }\\n  flowOf(w).line = 'tilt.storm';\\n40→  visit(flowOf(w), 'tilt:storm');\\n  if (attract) {\\n    act.phase = 2;\\n    act.a = 1;\\n    act.b = 1;\\n    visit(flowOf(w), 'tilt:east');\\n    visit(flowOf(w), 'tilt:stone');\\n    flowOf(w).line = 'tilt.stone';\\n  }\\n}\\n50→\\n/** The lean the storm, the deeds and the centre stone all write. */\\nfunction islandTilt(w: World): { tiltX: number; tiltZ: number; base: number } | undefined {\\n  const island = w.query('island') as unknown as { island: { tiltX: number; tiltZ: number; base: number } }[];\\n  return island[0]?.island;\\n}\\n\\nfunction delivered(w: World): number {\\n  let n = 0;\\n  for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as { mark: { kind: string; taken: number } }[]) {\\n60→    if (row.mark.kind === 'guest' && row.mark.taken > 0.5) n += 1;\\n  }\\n  return n;\\n}\\n\\n/** The four parts. Each one ends itself. */\\nexport function step(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  if (act.done) return;\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n70→  const phase = act.phase;\\n  const inst = phase === 2 ? 1 : 1;\\n  const wave = phase === 2 ? Math.sin(w.time * 1.4) * 0.55 : 0;\\n  const { body, seat } = apply(w, intents, { dx: wave, inst, noise: phase === 2 ? 1 : 0.4 });\\n  act.tick += 1;\\n  act.left += 1;\\n  if (phase === 0) {\\n    const tilt = islandTilt(w);\\n    if (tilt) {\\n      const rate = Number(w.settings.get('game.tilt.rate'));\\n80→      const speed = Number.isFinite(rate) ? rate : 0.15;\\n      tilt.tiltX = tilt.base + (act.left / 60) * speed;\\n    }\\n    if (act.left >= 20 * 60) {\\n      act.a = 1;\\n      act.phase = 1;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n      flow.line = 'tilt.east';\\n      visit(flow, 'tilt:east');\\n    }\\n90→    return;\\n  }\\n  if (phase === 1) {\\n    act.px += Math.max(0, body.y) * 6 * w.dt;\\n    if (seat.both) act.hold += 1;\\n    else {\\n      if (act.hold >= 50) pulse(w);\\n      act.hold = 0;\\n    }\\n    const tilt = islandTilt(w);\\n100→    for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as {\\n      mark: { kind: string; x: number; z: number; follow: number; taken: number };\\n    }[]) {\\n      const mark = row.mark;\\n      if (mark.kind !== 'guest') continue;\\n      if (mark.follow > 0.5) mark.x += (act.px - mark.x) * Math.min(1, 4 * w.dt);\\n      else mark.x -= 0.3 * w.dt;\\n      if (mark.x > 58 && mark.taken < 0.5) {\\n        mark.taken = 1;\\n        if (tilt) tilt.tiltX -= 0.5;\\n110→      }\\n    }\\n    if (act.left >= 75 * 60) {\\n      act.b = delivered(w) / 12;\\n      act.phase = 2;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n      act.samples = 0;\\n      act.acc = 0;\\n      act.acc2 = 0;\\n      resetBalance(rowOf(w, 0).wobble, rowOf(w, 0).hist);\\n120→      flow.line = 'tilt.stone';\\n      visit(flow, 'tilt:stone');\\n    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (phase === 2) {\\n    const ring = 0.3 - 0.14 * Math.min(1, act.left / (60 * 60));\\n    act.samples += 1;\\n    if (Math.hypot(body.x, body.y) <= ring) act.acc += 1;\\n    act.acc2 += body.sync;\\n130→    const tilt = islandTilt(w);\\n    if (tilt) {\\n      tilt.tiltX = body.x * 6;\\n      tilt.tiltZ = body.y * 6;\\n    }\\n    if (act.left >= 60 * 60) {\\n      act.c = act.samples ? act.acc / act.samples : 0;\\n      act.hz = act.samples ? act.acc2 / act.samples : 0;\\n      act.phase = 3;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n140→      if (tilt) {\\n        tilt.tiltX = 0;\\n        tilt.tiltZ = 0;\\n      }\\n      flow.line = 'tilt.dawn';\\n      visit(flow, 'tilt:dawn');\\n    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (act.left >= 15 * 60) act.done = 1;\\n150→}\\n\\n/** A calm wave. Guests close enough come with you. Nan is already there. */\\nfunction pulse(w: World): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as { mark: { kind: string; x: number; z: number; follow: number } }[]) {\\n    const mark = row.mark;\\n    if (mark.kind !== 'guest') continue;\\n    if (Math.hypot(mark.x - act.px, mark.z) < 8) mark.follow = 1;\\n  }\\n160→  act.falls += 1;\\n}\\n\\n/** Storm, guests, the stone, and the breath on it. */\\nexport function score(w: World): number {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  return clampScore(1000 * (0.15 * act.a + 0.35 * act.b + 0.4 * act.c + 0.1 * act.hz));\\n}\\n\\n/** Breathes in the storm, walks east, then holds the stone. */\\n170→export function bot(w: World, band: Band): Intents {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n  const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n  const breathe = wantBreath(band, w.time, cfg.period);\\n  if (band === 'idle') return stickIntents({ x: 0, y: 0 }, {});\\n  if (act.phase === 1) {\\n    const stick = seek(band, 0, 0.55, row.wobble, row.hist, cfg, w.tick);\\n    const call = act.left % 240 < 100;\\n    return stickIntents(stick, { both: call });\\n180→  }\\n  const stick = seek(band, 0, 0, row.wobble, row.hist, cfg, w.tick);\\n  return stickIntents(stick, { both: breathe });\\n}\\n\\n/** The crowd markers leave. The island stays. */\\nexport function teardown(w: World): void {\\n  sweep(w);\\n}\\n\\n190→/** The activity record. */\\nexport const tilt = {\\n  id: 'tilt',\\n  title: 'The Great Tilt',\\n  seconds: 170,\\n  setup,\\n  step,\\n  teardown,\\n  score,\\n  bot,\\n200→};\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The Great Tilt. A storm, a walk to the east terrace, the centre stone, then dawn.\\n * The island's geometry stays put. Your centre of balance is what leans it, once you are on the stone.\\n * There is no fail state. The clock moves every part on.\\n */\\nimport type { Intents, World } from '../../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { type Band, seek, stickIntents, wantBreath } from '../bot';\\nimport { clampScore } from '../score';\\nimport { resetAct, visit } from '../state';\\n10→import { resetBalance } from '../wobble';\\nimport { actOf, apply, cfgOf, flowOf, rowOf, sweep } from './kit';\\n\\nconst NAMES = ['Nan', 'Gerald', 'Bex', 'A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'E', 'F', 'G', 'H', 'I'];\\n\\n/** Guests, the storm, and a still balance. Attract begins on the stone. */\\nexport function setup(w: World): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  resetAct(act);\\n  const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n20→  resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n  const attract = String(w.settings.get('game.auto')) === 'attract';\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 12; i++) {\\n    const nan = i === 0;\\n    const col = (i - 1) % 4;\\n    const row = Math.floor((i - 1) / 4);\\n    w.spawn({\\n      made: { tag: 'guest' },\\n      mark: {\\n        x: nan ? 64 : 1 + col * 2.2,\\n30→        y: 0,\\n        z: nan ? 8 : (row - 1) * 2.2,\\n        kind: 'guest',\\n        text: NAMES[i] ?? 'guest',\\n        taken: nan ? 1 : 0,\\n        follow: nan ? 1 : 0,\\n      },\\n    });\\n  }\\n  flowOf(w).line = 'tilt.storm';\\n40→  visit(flowOf(w), 'tilt:storm');\\n  if (attract) {\\n    act.phase = 2;\\n    act.a = 1;\\n    act.b = 1;\\n    visit(flowOf(w), 'tilt:east');\\n    visit(flowOf(w), 'tilt:stone');\\n    flowOf(w).line = 'tilt.stone';\\n  }\\n}\\n50→\\n/** The lean the storm, the deeds and the centre stone all write. */\\nfunction islandTilt(w: World): { tiltX: number; tiltZ: number; base: number } | undefined {\\n  const island = w.query('island') as unknown as { island: { tiltX: number; tiltZ: number; base: number } }[];\\n  return island[0]?.island;\\n}\\n\\nfunction delivered(w: World): number {\\n  let n = 0;\\n  for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as { mark: { kind: string; taken: number } }[]) {\\n60→    if (row.mark.kind === 'guest' && row.mark.taken > 0.5) n += 1;\\n  }\\n  return n;\\n}\\n\\n/** The four parts. Each one ends itself. */\\nexport function step(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  if (act.done) return;\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n70→  const phase = act.phase;\\n  const inst = phase === 2 ? 1 : 1;\\n  const wave = phase === 2 ? Math.sin(w.time * 1.4) * 0.55 : 0;\\n  const { body, seat } = apply(w, intents, { dx: wave, inst, noise: phase === 2 ? 1 : 0.4 });\\n  act.tick += 1;\\n  act.left += 1;\\n  if (phase === 0) {\\n    const tilt = islandTilt(w);\\n    if (tilt) {\\n      const rate = Number(w.settings.get('game.tilt.rate'));\\n80→      const speed = Number.isFinite(rate) ? rate : 0.15;\\n      tilt.tiltX = tilt.base + (act.left / 60) * speed;\\n    }\\n    if (act.left >= 20 * 60) {\\n      act.a = 1;\\n      act.phase = 1;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n      flow.line = 'tilt.east';\\n      visit(flow, 'tilt:east');\\n    }\\n90→    return;\\n  }\\n  if (phase === 1) {\\n    act.px += Math.max(0, body.y) * 6 * w.dt;\\n    if (seat.both) act.hold += 1;\\n    else {\\n      if (act.hold >= 50) pulse(w);\\n      act.hold = 0;\\n    }\\n    const tilt = islandTilt(w);\\n100→    for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as {\\n      mark: { kind: string; x: number; z: number; follow: number; taken: number };\\n    }[]) {\\n      const mark = row.mark;\\n      if (mark.kind !== 'guest') continue;\\n      if (mark.follow > 0.5) mark.x += (act.px - mark.x) * Math.min(1, 4 * w.dt);\\n      else mark.x -= 0.3 * w.dt;\\n      if (mark.x > 58 && mark.taken < 0.5) {\\n        mark.taken = 1;\\n        if (tilt) tilt.tiltX -= 0.5;\\n110→      }\\n    }\\n    if (act.left >= 75 * 60) {\\n      act.b = delivered(w) / 12;\\n      act.phase = 2;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n      act.samples = 0;\\n      act.acc = 0;\\n      act.acc2 = 0;\\n      resetBalance(rowOf(w, 0).wobble, rowOf(w, 0).hist);\\n120→      flow.line = 'tilt.stone';\\n      visit(flow, 'tilt:stone');\\n    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (phase === 2) {\\n    const ring = 0.3 - 0.14 * Math.min(1, act.left / (60 * 60));\\n    act.samples += 1;\\n    if (Math.hypot(body.x, body.y) <= ring) act.acc += 1;\\n    act.acc2 += body.sync;\\n130→    const tilt = islandTilt(w);\\n    if (tilt) {\\n      tilt.tiltX = body.x * 6;\\n      tilt.tiltZ = body.y * 6;\\n    }\\n    if (act.left >= 60 * 60) {\\n      act.c = act.samples ? act.acc / act.samples : 0;\\n      act.hz = act.samples ? act.acc2 / act.samples : 0;\\n      act.phase = 3;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n140→      if (tilt) {\\n        tilt.tiltX = 0;\\n        tilt.tiltZ = 0;\\n      }\\n      flow.line = 'tilt.dawn';\\n      visit(flow, 'tilt:dawn');\\n    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (act.left >= 15 * 60) act.done = 1;\\n150→}\\n\\n/** A calm wave. Guests close enough come with you. Nan is already there. */\\nfunction pulse(w: World): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as { mark: { kind: string; x: number; z: number; follow: number } }[]) {\\n    const mark = row.mark;\\n    if (mark.kind !== 'guest') continue;\\n    if (Math.hypot(mark.x - act.px, mark.z) < 8) mark.follow = 1;\\n  }\\n160→  act.falls += 1;\\n}\\n\\n/** Storm, guests, the stone, and the breath on it. */\\nexport function score(w: World): number {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  return clampScore(1000 * (0.15 * act.a + 0.35 * act.b + 0.4 * act.c + 0.1 * act.hz));\\n}\\n\\n/** Breathes in the storm, walks east, then holds the stone. */\\n170→export function bot(w: World, band: Band): Intents {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n  const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n  const breathe = wantBreath(band, w.time, cfg.period);\\n  if (band === 'idle') return stickIntents({ x: 0, y: 0 }, {});\\n  if (act.phase === 1) {\\n    const stick = seek(band, 0, 0.55, row.wobble, row.hist, cfg, w.tick);\\n    const call = act.left % 240 < 100;\\n    return stickIntents(stick, { both: call });\\n180→  }\\n  const stick = seek(band, 0, 0, row.wobble, row.hist, cfg, w.tick);\\n  return stickIntents(stick, { both: breathe });\\n}\\n\\n/** The crowd markers leave. The island stays. */\\nexport function teardown(w: World): void {\\n  sweep(w);\\n}\\n\\n190→/** The activity record. */\\nexport const tilt = {\\n  id: 'tilt',\\n  title: 'The Great Tilt',\\n  seconds: 170,\\n  setup,\\n  step,\\n  teardown,\\n  score,\\n  bot,\\n200→};\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/events/tilt.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The Great Tilt. A storm, a walk to the east terrace, the centre stone, then dawn.\\n * The island's geometry stays put. Your centre of balance is what leans it, once you are on the stone.\\n * There is no fail state. The clock moves every part on.\\n */\\nimport type { Intents, World } from '../../../../engine/sim-api';\\nimport { type Band, seek, stickIntents, wantBreath } from '../bot';\\nimport { clampScore } from '../score';\\nimport { resetAct, visit } from '../state';\\nimport { resetBalance } from '../wobble';\\nimport { actOf, apply, cfgOf, flowOf, rowOf, sweep } from './kit';\\n\\nconst NAMES = ['Nan', 'Gerald', 'Bex', 'A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'E', 'F', 'G', 'H', 'I'];\\n\\n/** Guests, the storm, and a still balance. Attract begins on the stone. */\\nexport function setup(w: World): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  resetAct(act);\\n  const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n  resetBalance(row.wobble, row.hist);\\n  const attract = String(w.settings.get('game.auto')) === 'attract';\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 12; i++) {\\n    const nan = i === 0;\\n    const col = (i - 1) % 4;\\n    const row = Math.floor((i - 1) / 4);\\n    w.spawn({\\n      made: { tag: 'guest' },\\n      mark: {\\n        x: nan ? 64 : 1 + col * 2.2,\\n        y: 0,\\n        z: nan ? 8 : (row - 1) * 2.2,\\n        kind: 'guest',\\n        text: NAMES[i] ?? 'guest',\\n        taken: nan ? 1 : 0,\\n        follow: nan ? 1 : 0,\\n      },\\n    });\\n  }\\n  flowOf(w).line = 'tilt.storm';\\n  visit(flowOf(w), 'tilt:storm');\\n  if (attract) {\\n    act.phase = 2;\\n    act.a = 1;\\n    act.b = 1;\\n    visit(flowOf(w), 'tilt:east');\\n    visit(flowOf(w), 'tilt:stone');\\n    flowOf(w).line = 'tilt.stone';\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** The lean the storm, the deeds and the centre stone all write. */\\nfunction islandTilt(w: World): { tiltX: number; tiltZ: number; base: number } | undefined {\\n  const island = w.query('island') as unknown as { island: { tiltX: number; tiltZ: number; base: number } }[];\\n  return island[0]?.island;\\n}\\n\\nfunction delivered(w: World): number {\\n  let n = 0;\\n  for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as { mark: { kind: string; taken: number } }[]) {\\n    if (row.mark.kind === 'guest' && row.mark.taken > 0.5) n += 1;\\n  }\\n  return n;\\n}\\n\\n/** The four parts. Each one ends itself. */\\nexport function step(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  if (act.done) return;\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const phase = act.phase;\\n  const inst = phase === 2 ? 1 : 1;\\n  const wave = phase === 2 ? Math.sin(w.time * 1.4) * 0.55 : 0;\\n  const { body, seat } = apply(w, intents, { dx: wave, inst, noise: phase === 2 ? 1 : 0.4 });\\n  act.tick += 1;\\n  act.left += 1;\\n  if (phase === 0) {\\n    const tilt = islandTilt(w);\\n    if (tilt) {\\n      const rate = Number(w.settings.get('game.tilt.rate'));\\n      const speed = Number.isFinite(rate) ? rate : 0.15;\\n      tilt.tiltX = tilt.base + (act.left / 60) * speed;\\n    }\\n    if (act.left >= 20 * 60) {\\n      act.a = 1;\\n      act.phase = 1;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n      flow.line = 'tilt.east';\\n      visit(flow, 'tilt:east');\\n    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (phase === 1) {\\n    act.px += Math.max(0, body.y) * 6 * w.dt;\\n    if (seat.both) act.hold += 1;\\n    else {\\n      if (act.hold >= 50) pulse(w);\\n      act.hold = 0;\\n    }\\n    const tilt = islandTilt(w);\\n    for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as {\\n      mark: { kind: string; x: number; z: number; follow: number; taken: number };\\n    }[]) {\\n      const mark = row.mark;\\n      if (mark.kind !== 'guest') continue;\\n      if (mark.follow > 0.5) mark.x += (act.px - mark.x) * Math.min(1, 4 * w.dt);\\n      else mark.x -= 0.3 * w.dt;\\n      if (mark.x > 58 && mark.taken < 0.5) {\\n        mark.taken = 1;\\n        if (tilt) tilt.tiltX -= 0.5;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (act.left >= 75 * 60) {\\n      act.b = delivered(w) / 12;\\n      act.phase = 2;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n      act.samples = 0;\\n      act.acc = 0;\\n      act.acc2 = 0;\\n      resetBalance(rowOf(w, 0).wobble, rowOf(w, 0).hist);\\n      flow.line = 'tilt.stone';\\n      visit(flow, 'tilt:stone');\\n    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (phase === 2) {\\n    const ring = 0.3 - 0.14 * Math.min(1, act.left / (60 * 60));\\n    act.samples += 1;\\n    if (Math.hypot(body.x, body.y) <= ring) act.acc += 1;\\n    act.acc2 += body.sync;\\n    const tilt = islandTilt(w);\\n    if (tilt) {\\n      tilt.tiltX = body.x * 6;\\n      tilt.tiltZ = body.y * 6;\\n    }\\n    if (act.left >= 60 * 60) {\\n      act.c = act.samples ? act.acc / act.samples : 0;\\n      act.hz = act.samples ? act.acc2 / act.samples : 0;\\n      act.phase = 3;\\n      act.left = 0;\\n      if (tilt) {\\n        tilt.tiltX = 0;\\n        tilt.tiltZ = 0;\\n      }\\n      flow.line = 'tilt.dawn';\\n      visit(flow, 'tilt:dawn');\\n    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (act.left >= 15 * 60) act.done = 1;\\n}\\n\\n/** A calm wave. Guests close enough come with you. Nan is already there. */\\nfunction pulse(w: World): void {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as { mark: { kind: string; x: number; z: number; follow: number } }[]) {\\n    const mark = row.mark;\\n    if (mark.kind !== 'guest') continue;\\n    if (Math.hypot(mark.x - act.px, mark.z) < 8) mark.follow = 1;\\n  }\\n  act.falls += 1;\\n}\\n\\n/** Storm, guests, the stone, and the breath on it. */\\nexport function score(w: World): number {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  return clampScore(1000 * (0.15 * act.a + 0.35 * act.b + 0.4 * act.c + 0.1 * act.hz));\\n}\\n\\n/** Breathes in the storm, walks east, then holds the stone. */\\nexport function bot(w: World, band: Band): Intents {\\n  const act = actOf(w);\\n  const row = rowOf(w, 0);\\n  const cfg = cfgOf(w);\\n  const breathe = wantBreath(band, w.time, cfg.period);\\n  if (band === 'idle') return stickIntents({ x: 0, y: 0 }, {});\\n  if (act.phase === 1) {\\n    const stick = seek(band, 0, 0.55, row.wobble, row.hist, cfg, w.tick);\\n    const call = act.left % 240 < 100;\\n    return stickIntents(stick, { both: call });\\n  }\\n  const stick = seek(band, 0, 0, row.wobble, row.hist, cfg, w.tick);\\n  return stickIntents(stick, { both: breathe });\\n}\\n\\n/** The crowd markers leave. The island stays. */\\nexport function teardown(w: World): void {\\n  sweep(w);\\n}\\n\\n/** The activity record. */\\nexport const tilt = {\\n  id: 'tilt',\\n  title: 'The Great Tilt',\\n  seconds: 170,\\n  setup,\\n  step,\\n  teardown,\\n  score,\\n  bot,\\n};\\n\",\"total_lines\":200}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-89fec25b-cfdf-4b96-b043-afdfd1c52404-6","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Ranks, pebbles and Wobble Age. Every activity ends as a number from 0 to 1000. The words and the\\n * pebbles hang off that number. Age is the morning check only, and it never talks about a body.\\n */\\nimport { clamp } from './wobble';\\n\\n/** The rank words, from a quiet morning to a result the staff will not discuss. */\\nexport const RANKS = ['Present', 'Adequate', 'Composed', 'Serene', 'Unsettling'] as const;\\n\\n10→/** Pebbles a rank is worth before the multiplier. One is the least. Five is the most. */\\nconst PEBBLES: Readonly<Record<string, number>> = {\\n  Present: 1,\\n  Adequate: 2,\\n  Composed: 3,\\n  Serene: 4,\\n  Unsettling: 5,\\n};\\n\\n/** A score kept inside 0 to 1000. Anything that is not a finite number becomes 0. */\\n20→export function clampScore(n: number): number {\\n  if (!Number.isFinite(n)) return 0;\\n  return clamp(n, 0, 1000);\\n}\\n\\n/** The rank word for a score. Thresholds are 300, 550, 750 and 900. */\\nexport function rankOf(score: number): string {\\n  const s = clampScore(score);\\n  if (s >= 900) return 'Unsettling';\\n  if (s >= 750) return 'Serene';\\n30→  if (s >= 550) return 'Composed';\\n  if (s >= 300) return 'Adequate';\\n  return 'Present';\\n}\\n\\n/** Pebbles for a rank, scaled, and never fewer than one. They are not spent. */\\nexport function pebblesOf(rank: string, mult: number): number {\\n  const base = PEBBLES[rank] ?? 1;\\n  const m = Number.isFinite(mult) ? mult : 1;\\n  return Math.max(1, Math.round(base * m));\\n40→}\\n\\n/**\\n * Wobble Age from a morning share `s` (0 to 1). `k` is `game.age.k`.\\n * A perfect morning is 18. A morning with no share is 82.\\n */\\nexport function wobbleAge(s: number, k: number): number {\\n  const t = clamp(Number.isFinite(s) ? s : 0, 0, 1);\\n  const exp = Number.isFinite(k) ? k : 1.3;\\n  return Math.round(18 + 64 * Math.pow(1 - t, exp));\\n50→}\\n\\n/** How today's age sits next to yesterday. The same number is still news. Today's number is always in the sentence. */\\nexport function ageRemark(today: number, yesterday: number): string {\\n  if (!(yesterday > 0)) {\\n    return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Your first Wobble Age. We will pretend to be surprised tomorrow.`;\\n  }\\n  const d = yesterday - today;\\n  if (d > 0)\\n    return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Yesterday it was ${yesterday}. You stood still and time went backwards.`;\\n60→  if (d < 0) return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Yesterday it was ${yesterday}. The island has noted the difference.`;\\n  return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Yesterday it was ${today}. Consistency is a kind of wobble.`;\\n}\\n\\n/** The book id for today's age beside yesterday. The page says the words. The number lives in `ageRemark`. */\\nexport function ageLine(today: number, yesterday: number): string {\\n  if (!(yesterday > 0)) return 'age.first';\\n  if (yesterday > today) return 'age.down';\\n  if (yesterday < today) return 'age.up';\\n  return 'age.same';\\n70→}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Ranks, pebbles and Wobble Age. Every activity ends as a number from 0 to 1000. The words and the\\n * pebbles hang off that number. Age is the morning check only, and it never talks about a body.\\n */\\nimport { clamp } from './wobble';\\n\\n/** The rank words, from a quiet morning to a result the staff will not discuss. */\\nexport const RANKS = ['Present', 'Adequate', 'Composed', 'Serene', 'Unsettling'] as const;\\n\\n10→/** Pebbles a rank is worth before the multiplier. One is the least. Five is the most. */\\nconst PEBBLES: Readonly<Record<string, number>> = {\\n  Present: 1,\\n  Adequate: 2,\\n  Composed: 3,\\n  Serene: 4,\\n  Unsettling: 5,\\n};\\n\\n/** A score kept inside 0 to 1000. Anything that is not a finite number becomes 0. */\\n20→export function clampScore(n: number): number {\\n  if (!Number.isFinite(n)) return 0;\\n  return clamp(n, 0, 1000);\\n}\\n\\n/** The rank word for a score. Thresholds are 300, 550, 750 and 900. */\\nexport function rankOf(score: number): string {\\n  const s = clampScore(score);\\n  if (s >= 900) return 'Unsettling';\\n  if (s >= 750) return 'Serene';\\n30→  if (s >= 550) return 'Composed';\\n  if (s >= 300) return 'Adequate';\\n  return 'Present';\\n}\\n\\n/** Pebbles for a rank, scaled, and never fewer than one. They are not spent. */\\nexport function pebblesOf(rank: string, mult: number): number {\\n  const base = PEBBLES[rank] ?? 1;\\n  const m = Number.isFinite(mult) ? mult : 1;\\n  return Math.max(1, Math.round(base * m));\\n40→}\\n\\n/**\\n * Wobble Age from a morning share `s` (0 to 1). `k` is `game.age.k`.\\n * A perfect morning is 18. A morning with no share is 82.\\n */\\nexport function wobbleAge(s: number, k: number): number {\\n  const t = clamp(Number.isFinite(s) ? s : 0, 0, 1);\\n  const exp = Number.isFinite(k) ? k : 1.3;\\n  return Math.round(18 + 64 * Math.pow(1 - t, exp));\\n50→}\\n\\n/** How today's age sits next to yesterday. The same number is still news. Today's number is always in the sentence. */\\nexport function ageRemark(today: number, yesterday: number): string {\\n  if (!(yesterday > 0)) {\\n    return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Your first Wobble Age. We will pretend to be surprised tomorrow.`;\\n  }\\n  const d = yesterday - today;\\n  if (d > 0)\\n    return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Yesterday it was ${yesterday}. You stood still and time went backwards.`;\\n60→  if (d < 0) return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Yesterday it was ${yesterday}. The island has noted the difference.`;\\n  return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Yesterday it was ${today}. Consistency is a kind of wobble.`;\\n}\\n\\n/** The book id for today's age beside yesterday. The page says the words. The number lives in `ageRemark`. */\\nexport function ageLine(today: number, yesterday: number): string {\\n  if (!(yesterday > 0)) return 'age.first';\\n  if (yesterday > today) return 'age.down';\\n  if (yesterday < today) return 'age.up';\\n  return 'age.same';\\n70→}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/labs/game/scenes/score.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file Ranks, pebbles and Wobble Age. Every activity ends as a number from 0 to 1000. The words and the\\n * pebbles hang off that number. Age is the morning check only, and it never talks about a body.\\n */\\nimport { clamp } from './wobble';\\n\\n/** The rank words, from a quiet morning to a result the staff will not discuss. */\\nexport const RANKS = ['Present', 'Adequate', 'Composed', 'Serene', 'Unsettling'] as const;\\n\\n/** Pebbles a rank is worth before the multiplier. One is the least. Five is the most. */\\nconst PEBBLES: Readonly<Record<string, number>> = {\\n  Present: 1,\\n  Adequate: 2,\\n  Composed: 3,\\n  Serene: 4,\\n  Unsettling: 5,\\n};\\n\\n/** A score kept inside 0 to 1000. Anything that is not a finite number becomes 0. */\\nexport function clampScore(n: number): number {\\n  if (!Number.isFinite(n)) return 0;\\n  return clamp(n, 0, 1000);\\n}\\n\\n/** The rank word for a score. Thresholds are 300, 550, 750 and 900. */\\nexport function rankOf(score: number): string {\\n  const s = clampScore(score);\\n  if (s >= 900) return 'Unsettling';\\n  if (s >= 750) return 'Serene';\\n  if (s >= 550) return 'Composed';\\n  if (s >= 300) return 'Adequate';\\n  return 'Present';\\n}\\n\\n/** Pebbles for a rank, scaled, and never fewer than one. They are not spent. */\\nexport function pebblesOf(rank: string, mult: number): number {\\n  const base = PEBBLES[rank] ?? 1;\\n  const m = Number.isFinite(mult) ? mult : 1;\\n  return Math.max(1, Math.round(base * m));\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Wobble Age from a morning share `s` (0 to 1). `k` is `game.age.k`.\\n * A perfect morning is 18. A morning with no share is 82.\\n */\\nexport function wobbleAge(s: number, k: number): number {\\n  const t = clamp(Number.isFinite(s) ? s : 0, 0, 1);\\n  const exp = Number.isFinite(k) ? k : 1.3;\\n  return Math.round(18 + 64 * Math.pow(1 - t, exp));\\n}\\n\\n/** How today's age sits next to yesterday. The same number is still news. Today's number is always in the sentence. */\\nexport function ageRemark(today: number, yesterday: number): string {\\n  if (!(yesterday > 0)) {\\n    return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Your first Wobble Age. We will pretend to be surprised tomorrow.`;\\n  }\\n  const d = yesterday - today;\\n  if (d > 0)\\n    return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Yesterday it was ${yesterday}. You stood still and time went backwards.`;\\n  if (d < 0) return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Yesterday it was ${yesterday}. The island has noted the difference.`;\\n  return `Your Wobble Age is ${today}. Yesterday it was ${today}. Consistency is a kind of wobble.`;\\n}\\n\\n/** The book id for today's age beside yesterday. The page says the words. The number lives in `ageRemark`. */\\nexport function ageLine(today: number, yesterday: number): string {\\n  if (!(yesterday > 0)) return 'age.first';\\n  if (yesterday > today) return 'age.down';\\n  if (yesterday < today) return 'age.up';\\n  return 'age.same';\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":70}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-89fec25b-cfdf-4b96-b043-afdfd1c52404-7","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"180→  applyLean(w, next.day);\\n  if (next.event === 'credits') openCredits(w);\\n  else if (next.event === 'evening') openEvening(w);\\n  else startEvent(w, next.event);\\n}\\n\\n/** Puts the finale on a named step. Storm is where the activity already starts. */\\nfunction jumpTilt(w: World, step: string): void {\\n  startEvent(w, 'tilt');\\n  const act: Act = actOf(w);\\n190→  const flow: Flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const name = step.startsWith('tilt:') ? step : `tilt:${step}`;\\n  if (name === 'tilt:east') {\\n    act.phase = 1;\\n    act.a = 1;\\n    act.left = 0;\\n    flow.line = 'tilt.east';\\n    visit(flow, 'tilt:east');\\n  } else if (name === 'tilt:stone') {\\n    act.phase = 2;\\n200→    act.a = 1;\\n    act.b = 1;\\n    act.left = 0;\\n    flow.line = 'tilt.stone';\\n    visit(flow, 'tilt:east');\\n    visit(flow, 'tilt:stone');\\n  } else if (name === 'tilt:dawn') {\\n    act.phase = 3;\\n    act.a = 1;\\n    act.b = 1;\\n210→    act.c = 1;\\n    act.hz = 1;\\n    act.left = 0;\\n    flow.line = 'tilt.dawn';\\n    visit(flow, 'tilt:east');\\n    visit(flow, 'tilt:stone');\\n    visit(flow, 'tilt:dawn');\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n220→/** Marks pebbles the save already found. The count is restored separately, so this does not add any. */\\nfunction applyFinds(w: World, args: Record<string, unknown>): void {\\n  const raw = args.finds;\\n  if (!Array.isArray(raw)) return;\\n  const found = new Set(raw.filter((id) => typeof id === 'string'));\\n  if (found.size === 0) return;\\n  for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as { mark: { kind: string; text: string; taken: number } }[]) {\\n    if (row.mark.kind === 'pebble' && found.has(row.mark.text)) row.mark.taken = 1;\\n  }\\n}\\n230→\\n/** Copies a save the page handed in. The sim never reads the store itself. */\\nfunction applySave(w: World, args: Record<string, unknown>): void {\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const day = numArg(args, 'day');\\n  const cursor = numArg(args, 'cursor');\\n  const pebbles = numArg(args, 'pebbles');\\n  const age = numArg(args, 'age');\\n  const prior = numArg(args, 'prior');\\n  const credits = numArg(args, 'credits');\\n240→  const result = numArg(args, 'result');\\n  const seen = strArg(args, 'seen');\\n  const rank = strArg(args, 'rank');\\n  if (day !== undefined) flow.day = day;\\n  if (cursor !== undefined) flow.cursor = cursor;\\n  if (pebbles !== undefined) flow.pebbles = pebbles;\\n  if (age !== undefined) flow.age = age;\\n  if (prior !== undefined) flow.prior = prior;\\n  if (credits !== undefined) flow.credits = credits;\\n  if (result !== undefined) flow.result = result;\\n250→  if (seen !== undefined) flow.seen = seen;\\n  if (rank !== undefined) flow.rank = rank;\\n  applyFinds(w, args);\\n}\\n\\n/** One seat, the day, and the island. The first step starts a director or a demo. */\\nexport function boot(w: World): void {\\n  drawSway(w);\\n  w.spawn({\\n    flow: { mode: 'title', day: 1 },\\n260→    act: emptyAct() as unknown as Record<string, unknown>,\\n    island: { tiltX: 0.4, tiltZ: 0, base: 0.4 },\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/** One step of whatever the day is doing. */\\nexport function frame(w: World, intents: Intents): void {\\n  const flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const auto = autoOf(w);\\n  if (flow.mode === 'title' && auto === 'director') {\\n270→    openItem(w, programme()[flow.cursor]);\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (flow.mode === 'title' && auto === 'attract') {\\n    startEvent(w, 'pose-a');\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (flow.mode === 'event') {\\n    const activity = activityById(flow.event);\\n    let use = intents;\\n280→    if (auto === 'director') use = activity.bot(w, 'human');\\n    else if (auto === 'attract') use = activity.bot(w, 'perfect');\\n    activity.step(w, use);\\n    const act = actOf(w);\\n    if (act.done === 1 || (auto === 'attract' && act.tick >= SLICE)) finishEvent(w);\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if ((flow.mode === 'results' || flow.mode === 'evening') && (auto === 'director' || auto === 'attract')) {\\n    const act = actOf(w);\\n    act.wait += 1;\\n290→    if (act.wait >= BEAT) {\\n      if (flow.mode === 'results') advance(w);\\n      else sleep(w);\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Menu picks. Each one runs between steps. */\\nexport const retreatActions = {\\n  'game.begin': (w: World, args: unknown) => {\",\"content_concise\":\"180→  applyLean(w, next.day);\\n  if (next.event === 'credits') openCredits(w);\\n  else if (next.event === 'evening') openEvening(w);\\n  else startEvent(w, next.event);\\n}\\n\\n/** Puts the finale on a named step. Storm is where the activity already starts. */\\nfunction jumpTilt(w: World, step: string): void {\\n  startEvent(w, 'tilt');\\n  const act: Act = actOf(w);\\n190→  const flow: Flow = flowOf(w);\\n  const name = step.startsWith('tilt:') ? step : `tilt:${step}`;\\n  if (name === 'tilt:east') {\\n    act.phase = 1;\\n    act.a = 1;\\n    act.left = 0;\\n    flow.line = 'tilt.east';\\n    visit(flow, 'tilt:east');\\n  } else if (name === 'tilt:stone') {\\n    act.phase = 2;\\n200→    act.a = 1;\\n    act.b = 1;\\n    act.left = 0;\\n    flow.line = 'tilt.stone';\\n    visit(flow, 'tilt:east');\\n    visit(flow, 'tilt:stone');\\n  } else if (name === 'tilt:dawn') {\\n    act.phase = 3;\\n    act.a = 1;\\n    act.b = 1;\\n210→    act.c = 1;\\n    act.hz = 1;\\n    act.left = 0;\\n    flow.line = 'tilt.dawn';\\n    visit(flow, 'tilt:east');\\n    visit(flow, 'tilt:stone');\\n    visit(flow, 'tilt:dawn');\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n220→/** Marks pebbles the save already found. The count is restored separately, so this does not add any. */\\nfunction applyFinds(w: World, args: Record<string, unknown>): void {\\n  const raw = args.finds;\\n  if (!Array.isArray(raw)) return;\\n  const found = new Set(raw.filter((id) => typeof id === 'string'));\\n  if (found.size === 0) return;\\n  for (const row of w.query('mark') as unknown as { mark: { kind: string; text: string; taken: number } }[]) {\\n    if (row.mark.kind === 'pebble' && found.has(row.mark.text)) row.mark.taken = 1;\\n  }\\n}\\n230→\\n/** Copies a save the page handed in. The sim ne