{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1159","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The prior gaps are specifically about wiring dead features.I need to look more carefully for real bugs in the shipped behavior related to prior gaps.\n\nPose scrub is verified and working. Tilt logic is implemented with sea counter-rotation, storm tilt rate, delivery offset, and slope push. Dynamic props still need knock impulse. Camera banking with roll remains unimplemented.\n\nCamera roll and prop knock were not required. Sea counter-rotation,\n\nI'm analyzing the  slope push, and tilt rate are sufficient.poseScrub function. \n\nPlaques shift westIt returns t=1 for phase downhill each day. Age displays on the  2, interpolates fromresults paint. 0 to 1 over 4 seconds in phase 0, and scales the hold duration by 60fps.\n\nI need to verify the pose IDs are \"nothing\"\n\nAll 28 tests passed and \"chair\" so the clip names resolve to with zero failures. RETREAT/Nothing and The verify log confirms RETREAT/Chair. I also need to check when  the new tests are includedthe clip system steps and the process exited relative to the rules successfully. phase, since dress() runs during that phase.\n\nThe test passed, so\n\nA potential real bug the scrubbed t values was found in pose scrub. persisted through the step. This suggests When the guest reaches dress() either runs the pose quickly, phase after clip advancement 1 resets the timer  or the clip system preserves a held speed-0to zero and the body clip. I need to verify enters the pose twice. whether the island tests were included in that 28-test run.\n\nThe pose scrub bug is confirmed. The body\n\nThe 28-test count  enters the pose twiceconfirms the new island because the timer resets tests are included. to zero when the guest Phase transitions reset reaches it quickly. correctly. A potential The plan requires the bug was spotted: scrub body to stay at the only plays a clip if pose during hold, not it is not already in re-scrub from zero. slots.\n\nThe Nothing pose is\n\nThe pose scrub behavior already playing as the spawn clip, so its is correct. The plan slot.t is set immediately. explicitly requested When switching to Chair, scrubbing from hold playClip adds the new progress, so animating slot before the function through the clip during re-reads slots, and the hold is the intended tests confirm the scrubbed behavior. A snap at time advances. I still the phase boundary  need to verify whetheris acceptable.\n\nThe  the dress phase runs before or after thepose clip only switches clip system updates when playClip is called. t.\n\nThe passed tests confirm that scrubbed clip times survive the full step, so any later overwrite would have failed them. I am now investigating whether centre-stone tilt is\n\nA potential defect was found in pose transitions. When the pose changes, the old clip remains at its final time while the new clip scrubs. If the clip system blends all playing clips, the guest could appear stuck in a blend of the previous and current poses instead of cleanly following the current one. written before the sea system updates in the same frame, which could cause a one-frame lag. I am checking the execution order of the systems.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-beac8241-ae96-4be6-82a9-04445f2ea807-50","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"slots|weight|blend","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/anim","glob":"**/*layer*","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-beac8241-ae96-4be6-82a9-04445f2ea807-51","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"play\\(clip|slots","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine","glob":"**/*clip*Layer*"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2860,"output_tok