{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1165","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nThe implementation shifts plaques uniformly west by 4cm per day. This matches the \"four centimetres to the left\" note, but it is not downhill for every plaque on the dome-shaped island.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b73b1d79-214e-4aa8-9674-3d2efce890c9-27","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/PLAN.md","offset":250,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b73b1d79-214e-4aa8-9674-3d2efce890c9-28","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/PLAN.md","offset":420,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b73b1d79-214e-4aa8-9674-3d2efce890c9-29","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/props.ts","offset":100,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b73b1d79-214e-4aa8-9674-3d2efce890c9-30","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"syncProps|sceneProp\\.q|phase: 'rules'|readBodies","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine","glob":"*.ts","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4982,"output_tokens":1090,"cache_read_input_tokens":72704,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"d2a50ada-82cd-4c55-a25b-ae6cd99e3117"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b73b1d79-214e-4aa8-9674-3d2efce890c9-27","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"250→activities, from a data table in `labs/game/scenes/data/days.ts`:\\n\\n| Day | Activities |\\n|---|---|\\n| 1 | Morning Check (tutorial) · Pose Class A (Seated Nothing, Patient Chair, Heron) · Still Pond · a walk to find the Noticeboard |\\n| 2 | Morning Check · Reps Hall · Sand Garden · Pose Class B (Archer, Comma, Napkin) |\\n| 3 | Morning Check · Paddle Glide · The Line · Step Class |\\n| 4 | Morning Check · Hoop Patrol · Cliff Plunge · Island Jog with Gerald |\\n| 5 | Morning Check · Group Class (you and CPU guests) · Pose Class C (Bridge, Lighthouse) · The Great Tilt |\\n| After | Final Morning Check, credits, then Free Play with every activity and daily checks |\\n260→\\nFinishing all of a day lets you sleep at your hut (walk there, or pick it from the Programme). Every activity can also be\\nreplayed from the Noticeboard once met. Activities have no fail state: finishing at any rank counts.\\n\\n**Getting around.** You may walk everywhere, and the island rewards it, but nothing requires it: every Programme and\\nNoticeboard item has \\\"Go\\\", which fades to the station. A controller player on a sofa never has to cross the island.\\n\\n**Wobble Age.** The Morning Check's result, from 18 to 82: `age = round(18 + 64 × (1 − s)^k)`, `k` is `game.age.k` (1.3).\\nOne big number, a remark, a stamp on the calendar, and a line graph of at most seven points. Always compared with yesterday,\\nin a tone of mild scientific surprise.\\n270→\\n**Pebbles and your Cairn.** Pebbles are the currency: 1 to 5 per activity by rank, plus 20 hidden around the island. You\\nnever spend them. They stack, one by one, on a physical cairn in the Plaza, with a satisfying clack. The cairn leans\\nslightly according to your last Wobble Age and stands true at 18. Thresholds unlock things, shown on the Noticeboard:\\n10 Expert variants (a smaller ring, more sway), 20 and 30 tracksuit colours and a headband, 40 the \\\"Unsettling\\\" stamp set.\\n\\n**Exploration.** 20 pebbles, 12 \\\"Did you know?\\\" plaques, and each cast member has 3–5 new lines each day. Sit on a bench\\nto watch the view with the Meditate clip. Wave at Gerald. Plaques visibly creep downhill across the days.\\n\\n**Tilt as story.** A value `island.tilt` starts at 0.4° on Day 1 and rises by 0.5° a day, so drinks slide, marbles roll,\\n280→loose props drift and the sea sits fractionally wrong at the horizon. Only the Great Tilt gives it weight in play.\\n\\n**Saves** go in the page store (`createStore`, prefix unique to your game): day, done list, ages, pebbles, finds,\\noutfits, bests, settings. The sim never reads them: the page hands the sim its starting state through a scene action\\n(`game.begin`, section 14). Settings has Erase with an in-game confirmation, never `confirm()`.\\n\\n**Built to grow.** Days, poses, charts, trays, courses, lines, lures and settings are all data tables, one file each, so\\nlater content is adding rows. Keep it that way: it is part of the brief.\\n\\n---\\n290→\\n## 6. Activities\\n\\nEvery activity is a module exposing the same shape: `{ id, title, station, camera, map, setup, step, teardown, score,\\nbot, attract, short? }` in `labs/game/scenes/events/`. `step` emits sim events; the page turns them into text, sound and\\nHUD. `bot` writes the same seat input a player does, and is used by tests, attract mode and dev auto-play. `short` is the\\n45-second form for rounds (section 9).\\n\\n| Activity | Station | Camera | Verbs |\\n|---|---|---|---|\",\"content_concise\":\"250→activities, from a data table in `labs/game/scenes/data/days.ts`:\\n\\n| Day | Activities |\\n|---|---|\\n| 1 | Morning Check (tutorial) · Pose Class A (Seated Nothing, Patient Chair, Heron) · Still Pond · a walk to find the Noticeboard |\\n| 2 | Morning Check · Reps Hall · Sand Garden · Pose Class B (Archer, Comma, Napkin) |\\n| 3 | Morning Check · Paddle Glide · The Line · Step Class |\\n| 4 | Morning Check · Hoop Patrol · Cliff Plunge · Island Jog with Gerald |\\n| 5 | Morning Check · Group Class (you and CPU guests) · Pose Class C (Bridge, Lighthouse) · The Great Tilt |\\n| After | Final Morning Check, credits, then Free Play with every activity and daily checks |\\n260→\\nFinishing all of a day lets you sleep at your hut (walk there, or pick it from the Programme). Every activity can also be\\nreplayed from the Noticeboard once met. Activities have no fail state: finishing at any rank counts.\\n\\n**Getting around.** You may walk everywhere, and the island rewards it, but nothing requires it: every Programme and\\nNoticeboard item has \\\"Go\\\", which fades to the station. A controller player on a sofa never has to cross the island.\\n\\n**Wobble Age.** The Morning Check's result, from 18 to 82: `age = round(18 + 64 × (1 − s)^k)`, `k` is `game.age.k` (1.3).\\nOne big number, a remark, a stamp on the calendar, and a line graph of at most seven points. Always compared with yesterday,\\nin a tone of mild scientific surprise.\\n270→\\n**Pebbles and your Cairn.** Pebbles are the currency: 1 to 5 per activity by rank, plus 20 hidden around the island. You\\nnever spend them. They stack, one by one, on a physical cairn in the Plaza, with a satisfying clack. The cairn leans\\nslightly according to your last Wobble Age and stands true at 18. Thresholds unlock things, shown on the Noticeboard:\\n10 Expert variants (a smaller ring, more sway), 20 and 30 tracksuit colours and a headband, 40 the \\\"Unsettling\\\" stamp set.\\n\\n**Exploration.** 20 pebbles, 12 \\\"Did you know?\\\" plaques, and each cast member has 3–5 new lines each day. Sit on a bench\\nto watch the view with the Meditate clip. Wave at Gerald. Plaques visibly creep downhill across the days.\\n\\n**Tilt as story.** A value `island.tilt` starts at 0.4° on Day 1 and rises by 0.5° a day, so drinks slide, marbles roll,\\n280→loose props drift and the sea sits fractionally wrong at the horizon. Only the Great Tilt gives it weight in play.\\n\\n**Saves** go in the page store (`createStore`, prefix unique to your game): day, done list, ages, pebbles, finds,\\noutfits, bests, settings. The sim never reads them: the page hands the sim its starting state through a scene action\\n(`game.begin`, section 14). Settings has Erase with an in-game confirmation, never `confirm()`.\\n\\n**Built to grow.** Days, poses, charts, trays, courses, lines, lures and settings are all data tables, one file each, so\\nlater content is adding rows. Keep it that way: it is part of the brief.\\n\\n---\\n290→\\n## 6. Activities\\n\\nEvery activity is a module exposing the same shape: `{ id, title, station, camera, map, setup, step, teardown, score,\\nbot, attract, short? }` in `labs/game/scenes/events/`. `step` emits sim events; the page turns them into text, sound and\\nHUD. `bot` writes the same seat input a player does, and is used by tests, attract mode and dev auto-play. `short` is the\\n45-second form for rounds (section 9).\\n\\n| Activity | Station | Camera | Verbs |\\n|---|---|---|---|\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":250,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"activities, from a data table in `labs/game/scenes/data/days.ts`:\\n\\n| Day | Activities |\\n|---|---|\\n| 1 | Morning Check (tutorial) · Pose Class A (Seated Nothing, Patient Chair, Heron) · Still Pond · a walk to find the Noticeboard |\\n| 2 | Morning Check · Reps Hall · Sand Garden · Pose Class B (Archer, Comma, Napkin) |\\n| 3 | Morning Check · Paddle Glide · The Line · Step Class |\\n| 4 | Morning Check · Hoop Patrol · Cliff Plunge · Island Jog with Gerald |\\n| 5 | Morning Check · Group Class (you and CPU guests) · Pose Class C (Bridge, Lighthouse) · The Great Tilt |\\n| After | Final Morning Check, credits, then Free Play with every activity and daily checks |\\n\\nFinishing all of a day lets you sleep at your hut (walk there, or pick it from the Programme). Every activity can also be\\nreplayed from the Noticeboard once met. Activities have no fail state: finishing at any rank counts.\\n\\n**Getting around.** You may walk everywhere, and the island rewards it, but nothing requires it: every Programme and\\nNoticeboard item has \\\"Go\\\", which fades to the station. A controller player on a sofa never has to cross the island.\\n\\n**Wobble Age.** The Morning Check's result, from 18 to 82: `age = round(18 + 64 × (1 − s)^k)`, `k` is `game.age.k` (1.3).\\nOne big number, a remark, a stamp on the calendar, and a line graph of at most seven points. Always compared with yesterday,\\nin a tone of mild scientific surprise.\\n\\n**Pebbles and your Cairn.** Pebbles are the currency: 1 to 5 per activity by rank, plus 20 hidden around the island. You\\nnever spend them. They stack, one by one, on a physical cairn in the Plaza, with a satisfying clack. The cairn leans\\nslightly according to your last Wobble Age and stands true at 18. Thresholds unlock things, shown on the Noticeboard:\\n10 Expert variants (a smaller ring, more sway), 20 and 30 tracksuit colours and a headband, 40 the \\\"Unsettling\\\" stamp set.\\n\\n**Exploration.** 20 pebbles, 12 \\\"Did you know?\\\" plaques, and each cast member has 3–5 new lines each day. Sit on a bench\\nto watch the view with the Meditate clip. Wave at Gerald. Plaques visibly creep downhill across the days.\\n\\n**Tilt as story.** A value `island.tilt` starts at 0.4° on Day 1 and rises by 0.5° a day, so drinks slide, marbles roll,\\nloose props drift and the sea sits fractionally wrong at the horizon. Only the Great Tilt gives it weight in play.\\n\\n**Saves** go in the page store (`createStore`, prefix unique to your game): day, done list, ages, pebbles, finds,\\noutfits, bests, settings. The sim never reads them: the page hands the sim its starting state through a scene action\\n(`game.begin`, section 14). Settings has Erase with an in-game confirmation, never `confirm()`.\\n\\n**Built to grow.** Days, poses, charts, trays, courses, lines, lures and settings are all data tables, one file each, so\\nlater content is adding rows. Keep it that way: it is part of the brief.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Activities\\n\\nEvery activity is a module exposing the same shape: `{ id, title, station, camera, map, setup, step, teardown, score,\\nbot, attract, short? }` in `labs/game/scenes/events/`. `step` emits sim events; the page turns them into text, sound and\\nHUD. `bot` writes the same seat input a player does, and is used by tests, attract mode and dev auto-play. `short` is the\\n45-second form for rounds (section 9).\\n\\n| Activity | Station | Camera | Verbs |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n\",\"total_lines\":1059}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b73b1d79-214e-4aa8-9674-3d2efce890c9-28","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"420→**Air** (about 2 s): lean y spins you, lean x twists, scrubbing a rotation strip. Enter the water within 15° of vertical.\\nThree Gulls hold up score cards, 0 to 10. Sum of all cards, scaled to 1000. Huge splash, water-level camera, one judge\\nalways scores 4. Wait too long at the lip and you slip off anyway, a small splash, low cards. This is the attract mode's best shot.\\n\\n### Hoop Patrol (60 s)\\n\\nHoops fly in from Tare. Spin your stick in circles: angular speed in the band (`game.hoop.bandMin` 5, `bandMax` 9 rad/s)\\nkeeps every hoop up; outside it they sink and fall. A new hoop every 8 s from a telegraphed side: lean that way within 0.6 s\\nto catch it. Up to eight at once. Score: hoops × seconds, scaled. The hip-circle strip scrubs with your stick's angle, so\\nthe character's hips follow your thumb, with increasing dignity. Keyboard and accessibility: alternate Q and E at 2.5 Hz or\\n430→more counts as spinning. Mouse: circle it.\\n\\n### Island Jog (about 150 s)\\n\\nFollow Gerald round the coast path, a ring of flags past every landmark. Stick steers; alternating feet at about 2.5 Hz gives\\n+35% speed (swap `actor.character` for another `createCharacter` with the new speed **[tested]**). Stay within 8 m of him (\\\"the Pace Ribbon\\\").\\nScore: share of time in the ribbon. Tare hops beside you and talks, the plaques go by. At the end Gerald says: \\\"Nice weather\\nfor it.\\\" It is the longest thing Gerald will ever say.\\n\\n### Group Class\\n440→\\nSee section 9.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. The finale: The Great Tilt (about 4 minutes)\\n\\nDay 5, evening. It uses every verb at the scale of the world. There is no fail state, only remarks.\\n\\n**How the tilt works.** `island.tiltX, tiltZ` are sim values. The island's geometry never moves. Instead:\\n450→\\n- Actors get a slope push: the pilot system (section 14) adds `slope × sin(tilt)`, downhill, to the move it writes.\\n- Dynamic props (sun loungers, crates, drinks) get a per-step impulse with `knock`. Rapier's own gravity stays straight\\n  down: `physics.gravity` has no sideways part **[source]**.\\n- A custom camera banks with `makePose({ roll })` **[source]**. The sea prop, on a kinematic body, counter-rotates\\n  so the horizon stays level on screen while the island visibly tips. Use a sky with no silhouette backdrop for this.\\n\\nTilt grows by `game.tilt.rate`, and each deed below takes some off.\\n\\n1. **Storm (20 s, cutscene).** The sky darkens, rain falls (`frame.emit`), the ferry horn sounds far away. Close-up: Plumb's\\n460→   plait swings. Plumb, flat as ever: \\\"The island is now six degrees out of true. Please remain calm. Calm is mandatory.\\\"\\n2. **Everyone East (75 s).** Slope push is on. Twelve guests (crowd agents; Gerald, Bex and Nan among them) drift downhill\\n   politely. **Calm Call:** hold both feet 2 s, release: a calm wave (radius 8 m) makes nearby guests follow you. Lead them to\\n   the East Terrace (a sensor): each one delivered takes off 0.5°. Loungers slide through. Nan walks up on her own and is\\n   already there.\\n3. **Counterweights (45 s).** Two pebble carts on rails, cranked by alternating feet while you lean into the slope with the\\n   Wobble Model: your whole Cairn is on one of them. (First part to cut if the budget runs short.)\\n4. **The Centre Stone (60 s).** You climb to the summit and stand on the plate that says \\\"Do not\\\". The camera pulls back to the\\n   whole island. **Now the tilt is your CoB:** the stick moves your weight, and your weight moves the island. Waves are the\\n   disturbance, breathing quiets them, the ring shrinks as the storm peaks, the lighthouse beam sweeps. Topple: the island lurches\",\"content_concise\":\"420→**Air** (about 2 s): lean y spins you, lean x twists, scrubbing a rotation strip. Enter the water within 15° of vertical.\\nThree Gulls hold up score cards, 0 to 10. Sum of all cards, scaled to 1000. Huge splash, water-level camera, one judge\\nalways scores 4. Wait too long at the lip and you slip off anyway, a small splash, low cards. This is the attract mode's best shot.\\n\\n### Hoop Patrol (60 s)\\n\\nHoops fly in from Tare. Spin your stick in circles: angular speed in the band (`game.hoop.bandMin` 5, `bandMax` 9 rad/s)\\nkeeps every hoop up; outside it they sink and fall. A new hoop every 8 s from a telegraphed side: lean that way within 0.6 s\\nto catch it. Up to eight at once. Score: hoops × seconds, scaled. The hip-circle strip scrubs with your stick's angle, so\\nthe character's hips follow your thumb, with increasing dignity. Keyboard and accessibility: alternate Q and E at 2.5 Hz or\\n430→more counts as spinning. Mouse: circle it.\\n\\n### Island Jog (about 150 s)\\n\\nFollow Gerald round the coast path, a ring of flags past every landmark. Stick steers; alternating feet at about 2.5 Hz gives\\n+35% speed (swap `actor.character` for another `createCharacter` with the new speed **[tested]**). Stay within 8 m of him (\\\"the Pace Ribbon\\\").\\nScore: share of time in the ribbon. Tare hops beside you and talks, the plaques go by. At the end Gerald says: \\\"Nice weather\\nfor it.\\\" It is the longest thing Gerald will ever say.\\n\\n### Group Class\\n440→\\nSee section 9.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. The finale: The Great Tilt (about 4 minutes)\\n\\nDay 5, evening. It uses every verb at the scale of the world. There is no fail state, only remarks.\\n\\n**How the tilt works.** `island.tiltX, tiltZ` are sim values. The island's geometry never moves. Instead:\\n450→\\n- Actors get a slope push: the pilot system (section 14) adds `slope × sin(tilt)`, downhill, to the move it writes.\\n- Dynamic props (sun loungers, crates, drinks) get a per-step impulse with `knock`. Rapier's own gravity stays straight\\n  down: `physics.gravity` has no sideways part **[source]**.\\n- A custom camera banks with `makePose({ roll })` **[source]**. The sea prop, on a kinematic body, counter-rotates\\n  so the horizon stays level on screen while the island visibly tips. Use a sky with no silhouette backdrop for this.\\n\\nTilt grows by `game.tilt.rate`, and each deed below takes some off.\\n\\n1. **Storm (20 s, cutscene).** The sky darkens, rain falls (`frame.emit`), the ferry horn sounds far away. Close-up: Plumb's\\n460→   plait swings. Plumb, flat as ever: \\\"The island is now six degrees out of true. Please remain calm. Calm is mandatory.\\\"\\n2. **Everyone East (75 s).** Slope push is on. Twelve guests (crowd agents; Gerald, Bex and Nan among them) drift downhill\\n   politely. **Calm Call:** hold both feet 2 s, release: a calm wave (radius 8 m) makes nearby guests follow you. Lead them to\\n   the East Terrace (a sensor): each one delivered takes off 0.5°. Loungers slide through. Nan walks up on her own and is\\n   already there.\\n3. **Counterweights (45 s).** Two pebble carts on rails, cranked by alternating feet while you lean into the slope with the\\n   Wobble Model: your whole Cairn is on one of them. (First part to cut if the budget runs short.)\\n4. **The Centre Stone (60 s).** You climb to the summit and stand on the plate that says \\\"Do not\\\". The camera pulls back to the\\n   whole island. **Now the tilt is your CoB:** the stick moves your weight, and your weight moves the island. Waves are the\\n   disturbance, breathing quiets them, the ring shrinks as the storm peaks, the lighthouse beam sweeps. Topple: the island lurches\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":420,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"**Air** (about 2 s): lean y spins you, lean x twists, scrubbing a rotation strip. Enter the water within 15° of vertical.\\nThree Gulls hold up score cards, 0 to 10. Sum of all cards, scaled to 1000. Huge splash, water-level camera, one judge\\nalways scores 4. Wait too long at the lip and you slip off anyway, a small splash, low cards. This is the attract mode's best shot.\\n\\n### Hoop Patrol (60 s)\\n\\nHoops fly in from Tare. Spin your stick in circles: angular speed in the band (`game.hoop.bandMin` 5, `bandMax` 9 rad/s)\\nkeeps every hoop up; outside it they sink and fall. A new hoop every 8 s from a telegraphed side: lean that way within 0.6 s\\nto catch it. Up to eight at once. Score: hoops × seconds, scaled. The hip-circle strip scrubs with your stick's angle, so\\nthe character's hips follow your thumb, with increasing dignity. Keyboard and accessibility: alternate Q and E at 2.5 Hz or\\nmore counts as spinning. Mouse: circle it.\\n\\n### Island Jog (about 150 s)\\n\\nFollow Gerald round the coast path, a ring of flags past every landmark. Stick steers; alternating feet at about 2.5 Hz gives\\n+35% speed (swap `actor.character` for another `createCharacter` with the new speed **[tested]**). Stay within 8 m of him (\\\"the Pace Ribbon\\\").\\nScore: share of time in the ribbon. Tare hops beside you and talks, the plaques go by. At the end Gerald says: \\\"Nice weather\\nfor it.\\\" It is the longest thing Gerald will ever say.\\n\\n### Group Class\\n\\nSee section 9.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. The finale: The Great Tilt (about 4 minutes)\\n\\nDay 5, evening. It uses every verb at the scale of the world. There is no fail state, only remarks.\\n\\n**How the tilt works.** `island.tiltX, tiltZ` are sim values. The island's geometry never moves. Instead:\\n\\n- Actors get a slope push: the pilot system (section 14) adds `slope × sin(tilt)`, downhill, to the move it writes.\\n- Dynamic props (sun loungers, crates, drinks) get a per-step impulse with `knock`. Rapier's own gravity stays straight\\n  down: `physics.gravity` has no sideways part **[source]**.\\n- A custom camera banks with `makePose({ roll })` **[source]**. The sea prop, on a kinematic body, counter-rotates\\n  so the horizon stays level on screen while the island visibly tips. Use a sky with no silhouette backdrop for this.\\n\\nTilt grows by `game.tilt.rate`, and each deed below takes some off.\\n\\n1. **Storm (20 s, cutscene).** The sky darkens, rain falls (`frame.emit`), the ferry horn sounds far away. Close-up: Plumb's\\n   plait swings. Plumb, flat as ever: \\\"The island is now six degrees out of true. Please remain calm. Calm is mandatory.\\\"\\n2. **Everyone East (75 s).** Slope push is on. Twelve guests (crowd agents; Gerald, Bex and Nan among them) drift downhill\\n   politely. **Calm Call:** hold both feet 2 s, release: a calm wave (radius 8 m) makes nearby guests follow you. Lead them to\\n   the East Terrace (a sensor): each one delivered takes off 0.5°. Loungers slide through. Nan walks up on her own and is\\n   already there.\\n3. **Counterweights (45 s).** Two pebble carts on rails, cranked by alternating feet while you lean into the slope with the\\n   Wobble Model: your whole Cairn is on one of them. (First part to cut if the budget runs short.)\\n4. **The Centre Stone (60 s).** You climb to the summit and stand on the plate that says \\\"Do not\\\". The camera pulls back to the\\n   whole island. **Now the tilt is your CoB:** the stick moves your weight, and your weight moves the island. Waves are the\\n   disturbance, breathing quiets them, the ring shrinks as the storm peaks, the lighthouse beam sweeps. Topple: the island lurches\\n\",\"total_lines\":1059}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b73b1d79-214e-4aa8-9674-3d2efce890c9-29","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"100→  /** Whether it is on at first, and its light group: either makes it switchable (`propLight`). */\\n  on?: boolean;\\n  group?: string;\\n  /** More components its entity holds from the start (a door's `door`, a switch's `switch`). */\\n  components?: Readonly<Record<string, object>>;\\n  /** Its body knocked away from `from` as it is made (a broken prop's pieces: engine/physics/bodies.ts's `knock`). */\\n  knock?: PropKnock & { from: readonly [number, number, number] };\\n}\\n\\n/** Declares the component `sceneProp` on `registry` (once). */\\n110→export function definePropKinds(registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): void {\\n  if (registry.kinds().includes('component') && registry.has('component', 'sceneProp')) return;\\n  const description = 'A prop standing in a scene (spawnProp): its id, its body and its pose, its centre and turn.';\\n  defineComponent('sceneProp', { description, fields: SCENE_PROP_FIELDS }, registry);\\n  const hp = { type: 'number', default: 0, minimum: 0, description: 'Hit points left; at 0 it breaks.' } as const;\\n  defineComponent('propHealth', { description: \\\"A breakable prop's hit points (WP 13.16).\\\", fields: { hp } }, registry);\\n  const fields = {\\n    on: { type: 'boolean', default: true, description: 'Whether it is on: its lit parts and its light.' },\\n    group: { type: 'string', default: '', description: \\\"Its light group ('room:kitchen').\\\" },\\n  } as const;\\n120→  defineComponent('propLight', { description: \\\"A switchable prop's state (WP 13.16).\\\", fields }, registry);\\n}\\ndefinePropKinds();\\n\\n/** Throws `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` for `id` when it is no prop. */\\nfunction propOf(w: World, id: number, where: string): ScenePropComponent {\\n  const data = (w.get(id) as Partial<ScenePropComponents> | undefined)?.sceneProp;\\n  if (!data) throw codeError('SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT', { where, value: String(id), expected: 'a prop’s id (spawnProp)' });\\n  return data;\\n}\\n130→\\n/** The system `props.readback`: every prop with a body takes its body's pose, in id order. */\\nfunction readProps(w: World): void {\\n  const physics = physicsOf(w);\\n  for (const { sceneProp } of w.query('sceneProp') as unknown as ScenePropComponents[]) {\\n    if (sceneProp.body < 0) continue;\\n    const { position: p, rotation: r } = physics.readBody(sceneProp.body);\\n    [sceneProp.x, sceneProp.y, sceneProp.z] = [p.x, p.y, p.z];\\n    sceneProp.q = [r.x, r.y, r.z, r.w];\\n  }\\n140→}\\n\\n/**\\n * Stands a prop in the scene, `spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:<id>', at: [x, y, z], yaw })`: its base at `at` (m), turned\\n * `yaw` about +Y (rad). It makes the prop's body (when it has one; the scene needs `physics: true` then) and an entity\\n * with the component `sceneProp`, and returns the entity's id. A missing prop id warns and stands a crate (`getProp`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // in a scene's setup, with physics: true and its level's bodies added (addLevelBodies(physicsOf(w), level)):\\n * // const id = spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:crate', at: [2, 0, 3], yaw: Math.PI / 2 }); // on the floor at x 2, z 3\\n150→ * // labs/box/scenes/hall-props.ts places the hall's props this way, from levelProps and its own spots.\\n */\\nexport function spawnProp<C extends object, E extends EventMap>(\\n  world: World<C, E>,\\n  placement: PropPlacement,\\n  options: SpawnPropOptions = {},\\n): number {\\n  const w = world as unknown as World;\\n  const entry = getProp(placement.prop);\\n  const prop = entry.id;\\n160→  const spec = propBody({ ...placement, prop }, undefined, options.as);\\n  const { position, rotation } = spec ?? propPose({ ...placement, prop });\\n  const body = spec ? physicsOf(w).addBody(spec) : -1;\\n  if (options.knock && body >= 0) knock(physicsOf(w), body, [...options.knock.from], options.knock);\\n  if (spec && !w.systems.has('props.readback')) w.systems.add('props.readback', readProps, { phase: 'readback' });\\n  const [x, y, z] = position;\\n  const health = entry.health > 0 ? { propHealth: { hp: entry.health } } : {};\\n  const switchable = options.on !== undefined || options.group !== undefined;\\n  const light = switchable ? { propLight: { on: options.on ?? true, group: options.group ?? '' } } : {};\\n  return w.spawn({ ...options.components, sceneProp: { prop, body, x, y, z, q: rotation }, ...health, ...light });\\n170→}\\n\\n/** The entity whose prop `body` is (a `sceneProp`'s), or −1: the body-to-entity lookup uses and hits read (WP 13.16). */\\nexport function propOfBody<C extends object, E extends EventMap>(world: World<C, E>, body: number): number {\\n  if (body < 0) return -1;\\n  const props = (world as unknown as World).query('sceneProp') as unknown as (ScenePropComponents & { id: number })[];\\n  return props.find((e) => e.sceneProp.body === body)?.id ?? -1;\\n}\\n\\n/** The entity whose body is `body` (a body id; −1 for none): a prop's (`propOfBody`), else an actor's; −1 for neither. */\",\"content_concise\":\"100→  /** Whether it is on at first, and its light group: either makes it switchable (`propLight`). */\\n  on?: boolean;\\n  group?: string;\\n  /** More components its entity holds from the start (a door's `door`, a switch's `switch`). */\\n  components?: Readonly<Record<string, object>>;\\n  /** Its body knocked away from `from` as it is made (a broken prop's pieces: engine/physics/bodies.ts's `knock`). */\\n  knock?: PropKnock & { from: readonly [number, number, number] };\\n}\\n\\n/** Declares the component `sceneProp` on `registry` (once). */\\n110→export function definePropKinds(registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): void {\\n  if (registry.kinds().includes('component') && registry.has('component', 'sceneProp')) return;\\n  const description = 'A prop standing in a scene (spawnProp): its id, its body and its pose, its centre and turn.';\\n  defineComponent('sceneProp', { description, fields: SCENE_PROP_FIELDS }, registry);\\n  const hp = { type: 'number', default: 0, minimum: 0, description: 'Hit points left; at 0 it breaks.' } as const;\\n  defineComponent('propHealth', { description: \\\"A breakable prop's hit points (WP 13.16).\\\", fields: { hp } }, registry);\\n  const fields = {\\n    on: { type: 'boolean', default: true, description: 'Whether it is on: its lit parts and its light.' },\\n    group: { type: 'string', default: '', description: \\\"Its light group ('room:kitchen').\\\" },\\n  } as const;\\n120→  defineComponent('propLight', { description: \\\"A switchable prop's state (WP 13.16).\\\", fields }, registry);\\n}\\ndefinePropKinds();\\n\\n/** Throws `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` for `id` when it is no prop. */\\nfunction propOf(w: World, id: number, where: string): ScenePropComponent {\\n  const data = (w.get(id) as Partial<ScenePropComponents> | undefined)?.sceneProp;\\n  if (!data) throw codeError('SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT', { where, value: String(id), expected: 'a prop’s id (spawnProp)' });\\n  return data;\\n}\\n130→\\n/** The system `props.readback`: every prop with a body takes its body's pose, in id order. */\\nfunction readProps(w: World): void {\\n  const physics = physicsOf(w);\\n  for (const { sceneProp } of w.query('sceneProp') as unknown as ScenePropComponents[]) {\\n    if (sceneProp.body < 0) continue;\\n    const { position: p, rotation: r } = physics.readBody(sceneProp.body);\\n    [sceneProp.x, sceneProp.y, sceneProp.z] = [p.x, p.y, p.z];\\n    sceneProp.q = [r.x, r.y, r.z, r.w];\\n  }\\n140→}\\n\\n/**\\n * Stands a prop in the scene, `spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:<id>', at: [x, y, z], yaw })`: its base at `at` (m), turned\\n * `yaw` about +Y (rad). It makes the prop's body (when it has one; the scene needs `physics: true` then) and an entity\\n * with the component `sceneProp`, and returns the entity's id. A missing prop id warns and stands a crate (`getProp`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // in a scene's setup, with physics: true and its level's bodies added (addLevelBodies(physicsOf(w), level)):\\n * // const id = spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:crate', at: [2, 0, 3], yaw: Math.PI / 2 }); // on the floor at x 2, z 3\\n150→ * // labs/box/scenes/hall-props.ts places the hall's props this way, from levelProps and its own spots.\\n */\\nexport function spawnProp<C extends object, E extends EventMap>(\\n  world: World<C, E>,\\n  placement: PropPlacement,\\n  options: SpawnPropOptions = {},\\n): number {\\n  const w = world as unknown as World;\\n  const entry = getProp(placement.prop);\\n  const prop = entry.id;\\n160→  const spec = propBody({ ...placement, prop }, undefined, options.as);\\n  const { position, rotation } = spec ?? propPose({ ...placement, prop });\\n  const body = spec ? physicsOf(w).addBody(spec) : -1;\\n  if (options.knock && body >= 0) knock(physicsOf(w), body, [...options.knock.from], options.knock);\\n  if (spec && !w.systems.has('props.readback')) w.systems.add('props.readback', readProps, { phase: 'readback' });\\n  const [x, y, z] = position;\\n  const health = entry.health > 0 ? { propHealth: { hp: entry.health } } : {};\\n  const switchable = options.on !== undefined || options.group !== undefined;\\n  const light = switchable ? { propLight: { on: options.on ?? true, group: options.group ?? '' } } : {};\\n  return w.spawn({ ...options.components, sceneProp: { prop, body, x, y, z, q: rotation }, ...health, ...light });\\n170→}\\n\\n/** The entity whose prop `body` is (a `sceneProp`'s), or −1: the body-to-entity lookup uses and hits read (WP 13.16). */\\nexport function propOfBody<C extends object, E extends EventMap>(world: World<C, E>, body: number): num