},{\"line_number\":882,\"content\":\"**Key components** (plain data): `flow` (mode: front, roam, event, cutscene, results; event, phase, tick; day), `wobble` (per seat), `seat` (input per seat), `island` (tilt), `round`, `pebble`, `plaque`, `ghost`, plus one per activity. Time in whole steps, randomness from named streams, loops in `w.query` order, `Math.pow` not `**`.\"},{\"line_number\":996,\"content\":\"5. **The joke.** Still Pond. Then Cairn, plaques, day cycle.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"bd2a5954-677a-40c4-a14d-582e656d26b3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1169","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nTests passed. GatingThe phase order is intents, ai, anim, physics,  criteria were verifiedreadback, and rules. in prior rounds and captured in logs.\n\nThe HTML hand-in file is present in CHANGED_FILES. The code-review lens defaults to refuted, but the evidence supports Not Refuted.\n\nThe sea counter-rotation is visible because the renderer reads q after rules apply it. Prior gap 2 is fixed. Now considering plaques as marks versus props.\n\nA subtle bug remains in poseScrub phase 1. The scrub uses act.left, which includes elapsed time rather than hold progress. This may conflict with the body\n\nPlaques are invisible scrub following the `mark` components,  thumb.not visible props. The implementation shifts `mark.x` to move them downhill as the day advances, and positions will be asserted from the island step.\n\nPlaques are invisible\n\nThe prior gap was  marks, so shifting their x coordinate would not make them visiblythe clip not playing, leaving t near zero. creep downhill. The The fix plays the clip design calls for visible and scrubs t from elapsed movement, and the prior time rather than thumb skeptic explicitly  position. Criterionrequested this. I need to verify whether plaques 2 requires the body have a visual representation scrub to follow the or if they only act thumb. as text triggers.\n\nThe anti-ratchet rule\n\nThe old bug was `slot.t` limits refutation to using `act.hold/(12*60)`, demonstrable defects or unmet gating criteria. which stayed near zero The prior gap only required plaques to  because enter hold move downhill, not tois 0–1 and scored hold become visible props. The skeptic accepted resets it to 0. The shifting mark positions and asserting island-step fix scrubs from elapsed positions. They did time instead. not demand a visual representation.\n\nThe prior fix already satisfies the acceptance criterion that creeping\n\n\"Follows the thumb\" plaques exist. I should likely means the body not raise a new objection scrub should track  about their invisibilitythe thumb's position unless it is a core or balance inside the defect. I need to verify ring, not merely elapsed whether marks are rendered time. The current fix visually. The current implementation shifts scrubs from the hold plaques uniformly west timer, which may not rather than along the satisfy that requirement. slope gradient.\n\nThe implementer followed the skeptic's exact prescription. The test asserts that clip time advances, which the current fix satisfies.\n\nMoving plaques uniformly Raising the bar to  west is only downhillrequire thumb position for those already on the west side of the tracking would exceed the prior request. dome center. East-side plaques would creep uphill toward center, so the shift direction must vary by position.\n\nThe uniform westward shift is a reasonable interpretation of the \"four centimetres to the left\" copy line, but it is not downhill for plaques on the east side of the dome.\n\nThe pose scrub design The prior gap explicitly is confirmed as intentional. required plaques to The body follows the shift downhill as the guide timer, which  day advances. This raises the question is the intended \"followof whether that specific the thumb\" metaphor. wording creates a demonstrable\n\nThe slope push calculation defect. adds sin(tilt) with an implicit slope of 1. At a tilt of 0.4° this produces a very small push.\n\nThe island's tilt rises by 0.5 degrees daily, so westward creep follows the island's lean rather than the terrain mesh. The implementer's 4cm west shift matches the design's concrete number and the test assertion. Treating the non-geometric downhill\n\nThe slope push feature behavior as a defect would raise the bar works correctly. At beyond the prior gap's 20° tilt the push is requirements. noticeable, while at 2.4° it produces a small but visible drift over time. During storms the guest remains in event mode and is not pushed; the push only applies during the east phase. The sea quaternion order is \n\nThe island's westwardnow being examined. tilt confirms plaques creep downhill by moving west. The prior gap is resolved.\n\nNow examining pose scrub clip naming. The function builds names from pose IDs like `RETREAT/Chair` and `RETREAT/Heron`.\n\nPose IDs match the expected clip names. The Chair and Nothing clips exist in the set, so slotT returns valid timestamps and the tests pass.\n\nRecomputing the sea quaternion multiplication qz * qx with the full Hamilton product formula. The initial manual calculation produced a sign error in the z component, so the correct result is being derived.\n\nPose scrub timing has a minor jump at the start of the hold phase. The clip resets to act.left/steps once enter completes, so t jumps backward from roughly 0.35 seconds. This is janky but acceptable\n\nThe sea quaternion since the prior request multiplication is now was to scrub from hold confirmed correct. The array order matches progress.\n\nThe hold phase correctly uses act.left instead of act.hold. During scored the proper qz * qx Hamilton product. A  holds act.hold resetsnew issue was spotted: the age line contains to zero, so act.left is the proper value numbers in the spoken for scrubbing. line but not in the results copy.\n\nThe results panel now includes age numbers in the copy, fixing the prior gap that restricted results to rank, score, and sentence. The remember function correctly skips saving during title mode. A potential issue with noteProgress during title mode was noted but not pursued.\n\nThe pose scrub timing is sound. When the pose threshold triggers, the clip timestamp is already near zero and grows correctly\n\nThe title-mode save over the next fifteen flow is confirmed safe. steps.\n\nA potential noteProgress updates age persistence bug the in-memory save  was spotted in the during title, but themorning finishEvent: write to storage is skipped; clicking Begin it stores the current age in prior before then persists a fresh save, while Continue updating age and line. reads from storage.\n\nA potential bug was spotted: prior could be lost because noteProgress copies snap.prior, which is zero before the first result is saved and overwrites any loaded save.\n\nThe suspected prior-loss bug is harmless. Continue re-reads the save from disk, so the in-memory mutation during title mode cannot overwrite the stored prior.\n\nThe age persistence logic is sound. On the first morning, age initializes to zero and prior captures it correctly. Subsequent mornings compare the stored prior against the newly computed age. Save and continue operations preserve both fields through snap storage and stage remember. When resuming, game.begin restores the saved values without resetting them.\n\nThe prior-loss concern is resolved. The hand-in HTML must contain the fixes, since tests \n\nA bug was found inrun against source rather the age persistence than the built file. logic. When the second morning starts, `startEvent` does not clear `age` or `prior`. The previous day's saved `prior` remains in memory while `age` is still at its old value. This causes the next morning's finish event to compare against stale data.\n\nThe age persistence logic is sound. The second morning's finish event correctly stores","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e62f9f5c-e514-4fb3-ae5f-55b37e57b3eb-62","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Your Wobble Age|seaTurn|applyFinds|home\\.x - west|poseScrub","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656.html"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e62f9f5c-e514-4fb3-ae5f-55b37e57b3eb-63","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Your Wobble Age is","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/exit-interview.json"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e62f