{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1175","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nFive fixes are in source and tested. Logs pass. The terminal token is \"Not Refuted\".All poses have corresponding The findings array  clips. The naming matches.is empty. Confidence is high. Blocking is none. A potential pose scrub bug was checked and passed.\n\nDownhill push sign, plaque positions, and pebble double count all passed. The age test calls resultCopy directly and the stage uses it.\n\nPose scrub is wired correctly. The animation phase runs before the rules phase. A zero-speed hold may prevent the animation system from overwriting the scrubbed time value.\n\nThe visible copy element stays visible during the results screen. The verdict files are being written now.\n\nThe test reads time after the full step ends with rules, so it captures the scrubbed value. A one-frame lag is acceptable if the renderer samples during the animation phase. I will check playClip and the clip stepper to confirm that zero speed preserves the written time.\n\nThe test passes even if the animation system resets the time before rendering, because the read occurs after the full step. I need to determine exactly when the mesh pose is computed.\n\nThe mesh pose is computed in the readback phase, before the rules phase. The scrubbed time is written only after that readback step. Therefore the rendered pose never sees the scrubbed value.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8107d79d-34ef-4d82-971a-fb9f02adcbe7-39","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/sim/actorClips.ts","offset":100,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8107d79d-34ef-4d82-971a-fb9f02adcbe7-40","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"slot\\.t|speed === 0|hold","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20