{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1191","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Sweep only removes entities with the `made` component.\n\nPebbles persist because they lack the `made` component. Tilt guests carry `made: { tag: 'guest' }`. The five prior gaps are fixed. verify.log and npm-test.log confirm 28 passing tests with zero failures. I am double-checking that the new island tests are included in those 28.\n\nThe test count checks out: 22 old tests plus 6 new ones equals 28. I am now hunting for a genuine bug to demonstrate from the code.\n\nThe age display is not a bug. The spoken line omits the number, but the results copy includes it. Both can appear together because the copy updates every frame while the menu stays separate.\n\nThe morning result sentence may violate the \"one sentence\" criterion. The age remark contains multiple sentences, and the rank line adds another. Criterion 4 requires one rank, one number, and one sentence. The prior gap explicitly required showing today's age against yesterday.\n\nThe morning result sentence is not a new defect. The prior round explicitly required that age comparison text, so the multi-sentence format is intentional.\n\nThe pebble generic id bug is fixed with `pebble:i`. The taken check prevents double increment, and tests confirm pebbles stay at one.\n\nI am leaning toward returning Not Refuted, though the instructions bias toward refuted.\n\nTilt stone jumps skip the storm phase, so tilt stays at base 0.4 until the centre stone overwrites it from CoB. The sea quaternion math for tiltX=0.4 correctly yields a nonzero seaZ even with a still stick, and a pushed stick creates the expected gap. Downhill tilt is 20 degrees with guest speed 5.5.\n\nDownhill drift tests passed. The character controller applies the small move intent correctly, so the expected negative tippedDrift is achieved. The dress sea y overwrite bug is resolved by rules after readback. HTML strings are present. Hand-in files PROGRESS.md, exit-interview.json, and HTML are confirmed in the folder.\n\nI will not re-audit the entire game unless a fix breaks something. The PLAN_CHANGES diff may be cumulative from baseline rather than reflecting only this round.\n\nThe deviations section does not weaken acceptance criteria. It simply records cuts that the existing rules already permit. The verdict is Not Refuted.\n\nI am checking a potential pose scrub bug. The `#advance` function might reset the animation time if the loaded state steps while the clip ends, even at speed zero. I verified that when `t` is exactly 1 at the end of a hold, the duration clamp does not trigger.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e5331fae-e8bc-438d-993a-554611b77516-68","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/anim/clip/layer.ts","offset":190,"limit":35}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e5331fae-e8bc-438d-993a-554611b77516-69","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"poseOf|function poseOf","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223656__x54facc/work/Thumb Yoga-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223656/engine/gfx/stageProps.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":276,"output_tokens":1656,"cache_read_input_tokens":126720,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa35-d4ff-74f0-9f18-3308a1dd51dc","uuid":"451a89fb-b217-47a7-a65b-5c03bfff0633"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e5331fae-e8bc-438d-993a-554611b77516-68","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"190→        pose.rootPos.applyQuaternion(yaw).add(body.position);\\n        pose.rootRot.copy(yaw);\\n        return pose;\\n      };\\n      place(retargetPose(loopedAs(baked, slot), slot.t, body.skeleton, clipPose, options));\\n      const mask = slot.play.mask ? boneMask(slot.play.mask) : undefined;\\n      if (!slot.play.additive) blendPoses(body.pose, clipPose, smooth(slot.w), body.pose, { mask });\\n      else {\\n        place(retargetPose(baked, 0, body.skeleton, reference, options));\\n        addPose(body.pose, makeAdditive(clipPose, reference, delta), smooth(slot.w), body.pose, mask);\\n200→      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  /** The layer as plain JSON: each slot, bottom first, the locomotion loops, the ground speed, the root motion. */\\n  inspect(): Record<string, unknown> {\\n    const r = (x: number) => Math.round(x * 1e4) / 1e4 || 0;\\n    const slot = (s: ClipSlot) => ({ clip: s.clip, t: r(s.t), w: r(s.w), rate: r(s.rate), stopping: s.stopping > 0, loco: s.loco, ...s.play }); // prettier-ignore\\n    const { slots, moving, running, ground, root } = this.state;\\n    return { slots: slots.map(slot), moving, running, ground: r(ground), root: root.map(r) };\\n210→  }\\n\\n  /** A copy of `state`, plain data. */\\n  save(): ClipLayerState {\\n    return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(this.state)) as ClipLayerState;\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Reads `state` (copied, never kept). */\\n  load(state: Readonly<ClipLayerState>): this {\\n    Object.assign(this.state, JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(state)) as ClipLayerState);\\n220→    return this;\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Starts `clip` in a new slot at `at` in the stack (the top: `slots.length`). */\\n  #start(clip: string, play: ClipPlay, loco: boolean, at: number): void {\",\"content_concise\":\"190→        pose.rootPos.applyQuaternion(yaw).add(b